Ico_mk_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.endpoint_ident", "description": "The relation identifying the endpoints of `Icc a (a + p)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.endpoint_ident.mk", "description": "The relation identifying the endpoints of `Icc a (a + p)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.finite_set_of_add_order_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.coe_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle", "description": "The \"additive circle\": `\ud835\udd5c \u29f8 (\u2124 \u2219 p)`. See also `circle` and `real.angle`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_right_to_Ico_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.exists_gcd_eq_one_of_is_of_fin_add_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.set_add_order_of_equiv", "description": " The natural bijection between points of order `n` and natural numbers less than and coprime to\n`n`. The inverse of the map sends `m \u21a6 (m/n * p : add_circle p)` where `m` is coprime to `n` and\nsatisfies `0 \u2264 m < n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.lift_Ioc", "description": " Given a function on `\ud835\udd5c`, return the unique function on `add_circle p` agreeing with `f` on\n`(a, a + p]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.real.properly_discontinuous_vadd", "description": " The action on `\u211d` by right multiplication of its the subgroup `zmultiples p` (the multiples of\n`p:\u211d`) is properly discontinuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.equiv_Ico", "description": " The equivalence between `add_circle p` and the half-open interval `[a, a + p)`, whose inverse\nis the natural quotient map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.add_order_of_coe_rat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.equiv_Icc_quot", "description": " The equivalence between `add_circle p` and the quotient of `[a, a + p]` by the relation\nidentifying the endpoints.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"na