": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.homeo_Icc_quot", "description": " The natural map from `[a, a + p] \u2282 \ud835\udd5c` with endpoints identified to `\ud835\udd5c / \u2124 \u2022 p`, as a\nhomeomorphism of topological spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unit_add_circle.second_countable_topology", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.add_order_of_div_of_gcd_eq_one'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.continuous_at_equiv_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.lift_Ico_coe_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.coe_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.coe_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.coe_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.add_order_of_eq_pos_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.continuous_at_equiv_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.coe_eq_coe_iff_of_mem_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.normal_space", "description": "The \"additive circle\" `\u211d \u29f8 (\u2124 \u2219 p)` is normal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.add_order_of_div_of_gcd_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.circular_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.coe_eq_zero_of_pos_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.equiv_add_circle_apply_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.coe_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unit_add_circle", "description": "The unit circle `\u211d \u29f8 \u2124`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.topological_space.second_countable_topology", "description": "The \"additive circle\" `\u211d \u29f8 (\u2124 \u2219 p)` is second-countable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.topological_add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.continuous_equiv_Ico_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.equiv_Icc_quot_comp_mk_eq_to_Ico_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.lift_Ioc_coe_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_Ico_mod_eventually_eq_to_Ioc_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.lift_Ico", "description": " Given a function on `\ud835\udd5c`, return the unique function on `add_circle p` agreeing with `f` on\n`[a, a + p)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.liminf_right_slope_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at_iff_tendsto_slope'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at_filter_iff_tendsto_slope", "description": " If the domain has dimension one, then Fr\u00e9chet derivative is equivalent to the classical\ndefinition with a limit. In this version we have to take the limit along the subset `-{x}`,\nbecause for `y=x` the slope equals zero due to the convention `0\u207b\u00b9=0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.limsup_slope_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at_iff_tendsto_slope", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.liminf_right_norm_slope_le", "description": " If `f` has derivative `f'` within `(x, +\u221e)` at `x`, then for any `r > \u2016f'\u2016` the ratio\n`\u2016f z - f x\u2016 / \u2016z - x\u2016` is frequently less than `r` as `z \u2192 x+0`.\nIn other words, the limit inferior of this ratio as `z` tends to `x+0`\nis less than or equal to `\u2016f'\u2016`. See also `has_deriv_within_at.limsup_norm_slope_le`\nfor a stronger version using limit superior and any set `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.limsup_slope_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at_iff_tendsto_slope", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.limsup_norm_slope_le", "description": " If `f` has derivative `f'` within `s` at `x`, then for any `r > \u2016f'\u2016` the ratio\n`\u2016f z - f x\u2016 / \u2016z - x\u2016` is less than `r` in some neighborhood of `x` within `s`.\nIn other words, the limit superior of this ratio as `z` tends to `x` along `s`\nis less than or equal to `\u2016f'\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.liminf_right_slope_norm_le", "description": " If `f` has derivative `f'` within `(x, +\u221e)` at `x`, then for any `r > \u2016f'\u2016` the ratio\n`(\u2016f z\u2016 - \u2016f x\u2016) / (z - x)` is frequently less than `r` as `z \u2192 x+0`.\nIn other words, the limit inferior of this ratio as `z` tends to `x+0`\nis less than or equal to `\u2016f'\u2016`.\n\nSee also\n\n* `has_deriv_within_at.limsup_norm_slope_le` for a stronger version using\n  limit superior and any set `s`;\n* `has_deriv_within_at.liminf_right_norm_slope_le` for a stronger version using\n  `\u2016f z - f x\u2016` instead of `\u2016f z\u2016 - \u2016f x\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.limsup_slope_norm_le", "description": " If `f` has derivative `f'` within `s` at `x`, then for any `r > \u2016f'\u2016` the ratio\n`(\u2016f z\u2016 - \u2016f x\u2016) / \u2016z - x\u2016` is less than `r` in some neighborhood of `x` within `s`.\nIn other words, the limit superior of this ratio as `z` tends to `x` along `s`\nis less than or equal to `\u2016f'\u2016`.\n\nThis lemma is a weaker version of `has_deriv_within_at.limsup_norm_slope_le`\nwhere `\u2016f z\u2016 - \u2016f x\u2016` is replaced by `\u2016f z - f x\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_units.eq_neg_of_add_eq_zero_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.is_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_units.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_units.add_zero_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit_of_mul_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit", "description": " An element `a : M` of a monoid is a unit if it has a two-sided inverse.\nThe actual definition says that `a` is equal to some `u : M\u02e3`, where\n`M\u02e3` is a bundled version of `is_unit`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_units.is_add_unit_add_units_add", "description": "Addition of a `u : add_units M` on the left doesn't affect `is_add_unit`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_units.add_neg_cancel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_unit.add_unit_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "divp_mul_eq_mul_divp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.mul_one_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_units.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_one_of_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_divp_iff_mul_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.coe_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.mul_eq_one_iff_inv_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_units.neg_add_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.has_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.inv_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_units.add_eq_zero_iff_neg_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.exists_left_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.simps.coe", "description": "See Note [custom simps projection]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_units.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "divp_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.mul_inv_eq_iff_eq_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.coe_mk_of_mul_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "math