s may be anything,\nalthough many usages of `lift_on'` assume `f p 0 = f 0 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.lift_ring_hom_apply_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.mk_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.of_fraction_ring_comp_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.num_div_dvd'", "description": "A version of `num_div_dvd` with the LHS in simp normal form", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.of_fraction_ring_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.lift_on_condition_of_lift_on'_condition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.to_fraction_ring_ring_equiv", "description": " `ratfunc K` is isomorphic to the field of fractions of `K[X]`, as rings.\n\nThis is an auxiliary definition; `simp`-normal form is `is_localization.alg_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.div_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.X", "description": "`ratfunc.X` is the polynomial variable (aka indeterminate).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.eval_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.sub", "description": "Subtraction of rational functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.int_degree_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.nat_degree_num_mul_right_sub_nat_degree_denom_mul_left_eq_int_degree", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.coe_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.of_fraction_ring_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.mk_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.algebra_map_eq_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.map_apply_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.neg", "description":