", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.has_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.smul_eq_C_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.of_fraction_ring_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.coe_map_alg_hom_eq_coe_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.to_fraction_ring_ring_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.lift_monoid_with_zero_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.lift_alg_hom", "description": " Lift an injective algebra homomorphism `K[X] \u2192\u2090[S] L` to a `ratfunc K \u2192\u2090[S] L`\nby mapping both the numerator and denominator and quotienting them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.lift_monoid_with_zero_hom_apply_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.coe_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.lift_ring_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.algebra_map_apply_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.int_degree_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.map_apply_div_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.lift_alg_hom_apply_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.of_fraction_ring_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.of_fraction_ring_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.num_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.smul_tac", "description": "Solve equations for `ratfunc K` by applying `ratfunc.induction_on`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.mk_one'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.to_fraction_ring_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.is_coprime_num_denom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.num_div_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.lift_alg_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.laurent_series.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.lift_monoid_with_zero_hom_apply_of_fraction_ring_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.int_degree_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.mk_eq_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.eval", "description": " Evaluate a rational function `p` given a ring hom `f` from the scalar field\nto the target and a value `x` for the variable in the target.\n\nFractions are reduced by clearing common denominators before evaluating:\n`eval id 1 ((X^2 - 1) / (X - 1)) = eval id 1 (X + 1) = 2`, not `0 / 0 = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.coe_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.eval_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.inv", "description": "Multiplicative inverse of a rational function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.algebra_map_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.to_fraction_ring_ring_equiv_symm_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.denom_add_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.num_mul_eq_mul_denom_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.coe_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.has_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.mk_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.zero", "description": "The zero rational function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.laurent_series.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.lift_on_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.X_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.algebra_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.div", "description": "Division of rational functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.smul_eq_C_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.int_degree", "description": " `int_degree x` is the degree of the rational function `x`, defined as the difference between\nthe `nat_degree` of its numerator and the `nat_degree` of its denominator. In particular,\n`int_degree 0 = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.mk_eq_localization_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.num_denom_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.eval_eq_zero_of_eval\u2082_denom_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.algebra_map_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.induction_on", "description": " Induction principle for `ratfunc K`: if `f p q : P (p / q)` for all `p q : K[X]`,\nthen `P` holds on all elements of `ratfunc K`.\n\nSee also `induction_on'`, which is a recursion principle defined in terms of `ratfunc.mk`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.num_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.mk_eq_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.denom_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc", "description": " `ratfunc K` is `K(x)`, the field of rational functions over `K`.\n\nThe inclusion of polynomials into `ratfunc` is `algebra_map K[X] (ratfunc K)`,\nthe maps between `ratfunc K` and another field of fractions of `K[X]`,\nespecially `fraction_ring K[X]`, are given by `is_localization.algebra_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.to_fraction_ring", "description": " `ratfunc K` is `K(x)`, the field of rational functions over `K`.\n\nThe inclusion of polynomials into `ratfunc` is `algebra_map K[X] (ratfunc K)`,\nthe maps between `ratfunc K` and another field of fractions of `K[X]`,\nespecially `fraction_ring K[X]`, are given by `is_localization.algebra_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.lift_on'_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.frac_tac", "description": "Solve equations for `ratfunc K` by working in `fraction_ring K[X]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.int_degree_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.num_denom_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.lift_ring_hom_apply_of_fraction_ring_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.num_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.denom_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.of_fraction_ring_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.mul_inv_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.coe_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.lift_monoid_with_zero_hom", "description": " Lift an monoid with zero homomorphism `R[X] \u2192*\u2080 G\u2080` to a `ratfunc R \u2192*\u2080 G\u2080`\non the condition that `\u03c6` maps non zero divisors to non zero divisors,\nby mapping both the numerator and denominator and quotienting them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.lift_ring_hom", "description": " Lift an injective ring homomorphism `R[X] \u2192+* L` to a `ratfunc R \u2192+* L`\nby mapping both the numerator and denominator and quotienting them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.num_div_denom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.mk_eq_div'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.lift_alg_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.coe_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.denom_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.coe_num_denom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.eval_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.of_fraction_ring_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.one", "description": "The multiplicative unit of rational functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.int_degree_polynomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.denom_div_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.eval_mul", "description": " `eval` is a multiplicative homomorphism except when a denominator evaluates to `0`.\n\nCounterexample: `eval _ 0 X * eval _ 0 (1/X) = 0 \u2260 1 = eval _ 0 1 = eval _ 0 (X * 1/X)`.\n\nSee also `ratfunc.eval\u2082_denom_ne_zero` to make the hypotheses simpler but less general.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.coe_map_ring_hom_eq_coe_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.denom_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.num_denom_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.num_mul_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.eval_add", "description": " `eval` is an additive homomorphism except when a denominator evaluates to `0`.\n\nCounterexample: `eval _ 1 (X / (X-1)) + eval _ 1 (-1 / (X-1)) = 0`\n`... \u2260 1 = eval _ 1 ((X-1) / (X-1))`.\n\nSee also `ratfunc.eval\u2082_denom_ne_zero` to make the hypotheses simpler but less general.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.int_degree_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.of_fraction_ring_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.has_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.to_fraction_ring_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.lift_on'_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.num_denom_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.lift_on_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.denom_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.map_ring_hom", "description": " Lift a ring homomorphism that maps polynomials `\u03c6 : R[X] \u2192+* S[X]`\nto a `ratfunc R \u2192+* ratfunc S`,\non the condition that `\u03c6` maps non zero divisors to non zero divisors,\nby mapping both the numerator and denominator and quotienting them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.num_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.of_fraction_ring_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.of_fraction_ring_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.denom_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.is_fraction_ring", "description": "`ratfunc K` is the field of fractions of the polynomials over `K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.lift_monoid_with_zero_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.mk_def_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.int_degree_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.algebra_map_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.map", "description": " Lift a monoid homomorphism that maps polynomials `\u03c6 : R[X] \u2192* S[X]`\nto a `ratfunc R \u2192* ratfunc S`,\non the condition that `\u03c6` maps non zero divisors to non zero divisors,\nby mapping both the numerator and denominator and quotienting them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.lift_on", "description": " Non-dependent recursion principle for `ratfunc K`:\nTo construct a term of `P : Sort*` out of `x : ratfunc K`,\nit suffices to provide a constructor `f : \u03a0 (p q : K[X]), P`\nand a proof that `f p q = f p' q'` for all `p q p' q'` such that `q' * p = q * p'` where\nboth `q` and `q'` are not zero divisors, stated as `q \u2209 K[X]\u2070`, `q' \u2209 K[X]\u2070`.\n\nIf considering `K` as an integral domain, this is the same as saying that\nwe construct a value of `P` for such elements of `ratfunc K` by setting\n`lift_on (p / q) f _ = f p q`.\n\nWhen `[is_domain K]`, one can use `ratfunc.lift_on'`, which has the stronger requirement\nof `\u2200 {p q a : K[X]} (hq : q \u2260 0) (ha : a \u2260 0), f (a * p) (a * q) = f p q)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.induction_on'", "description": " Induction principle for `ratfunc K`: if `f p q : P (ratfunc.mk p q)` for all `p q`,\nthen `P` holds on all elements of `ratfunc K`.\n\nSee also `induction_on`, which is a recursion principle defined in terms of `algebra_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.monic_denom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.add", "description": "Addition of rational functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.of_fraction_ring_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.mk_def_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.C", "description": "`ratfunc.C a` is the constant rational function `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.algebra_map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.num_mul_denom_add_denom_mul_num_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.smul", "description": "Scalar multiplication of rational functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.coe_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.mk", "description": " `ratfunc.mk (p q : K[X])` is `p / q` as a rational function.\n\nIf `q = 0`, then `mk` returns 0.\n\nThis is an auxiliary definition used to define an `algebra` structure on `ratfunc`;\nthe `simp` normal form of `mk p q` is `algebra_map _ _ p / algebra_map _ _ q`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ratfunc.coe_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform.tendsto_nhds_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_comp_of_mem_b