"description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.of_fun", "description": " Define a `uniform_space` using a \"distance\" function. The function can be, e.g., the distance in\na (usual or extended) metric space or an absolute value on a ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "empty.uniform_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.uniformity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod_mk_mem_comp_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_ball_symmetry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_continuous\u2082.bicompl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.has_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infi_uniformity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_le_uniformity", "description": "Entourages are neighborhoods of the diagonal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_topological_space_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_uniformity_iterate_comp_subset", "description": " If `s \u2208 \ud835\udce4 \u03b1`, then for any natural `n`, for a subset `t` of a sufficiently small set in `\ud835\udce4 \u03b1`,\nwe have `t \u25cb t \u25cb ... \u25cb t \u2286 s` (`n` compositions).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comp_rel_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.uniformity_trans", "description": "Relation `\u03bb f g, tendsto (\u03bb x, (f x, g x)) l (\ud835\udce4 \u03b1)` is transitive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "symmetric_rel", "description": "The relation is invariant under swapping factors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comp_open_symm_mem_uniformity_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_continuous_comap'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.has_basis_nhds_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "disjoint.exists_uniform_thickening", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.has_basis_symmetric", "description": "Symmetric entourages form a basis of `\