s_uniformity_iff_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_topological_space_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniformity_multiplicative", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_continuous_of_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_iff_uniform_continuous_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_set_diagonal_le_uniformity", "description": "Entourages are neighborhoods of the diagonal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniformity_set_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.mem_nhds_iff_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ball_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_prod_uniformity_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_uniformity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.uniform_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.ball", "description": " The ball around `(x : \u03b2)` with respect to `(V : set (\u03b2 \u00d7 \u03b2))`. Intended to be\nused for `V \u2208 \ud835\udce4 \u03b2`, but this is not needed for the definition. Recovers the\nnotions of metric space ball when `V = {p | dist p.1 p.2 < r }`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_iterate_comp_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "symmetric_rel.inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_continuous_Inf_dom\u2082", "description": "A version of `uniform_continuous_Inf_dom` for binary functions", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "symmetrize_rel_subset_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comp_rel", "description": "The composition of relations", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform.tendsto_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniformity_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.comap", "description": "Given `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` and a uniformity `u` on `\u03b2`, the inverse image of `u` under `f`\n is the inverse image in the filter sense of the induced function `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u00d7 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_topological_space_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.mem_nhds_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_uniformity_is_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comp_le_uniformity3", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_nhds_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_uniformity_comp_subset", "description": " If `s \u2208 \ud835\udce4 \u03b1`, then for any natural `n`, for a subset `t` of a sufficiently small set in `\ud835\udce4 \u03b1`,\nwe have `t \u25cb t \u2286 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_topological_space_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_basis.uniformity_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_continuous_on.continuous_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_eq_uniformity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniformity_add_opposite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lebesgue_number_lemma_sUnion", "description": " Let `c : set (set \u03b1)` be an open cover of a compact set `s`. Then there exists an entourage\n`n` such that for each `x \u2208 s` its `n`-neighborhood is contained in some `t \u2208 c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bool.uniform_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.congr_uniformity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_iff_open_ball_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_uniformity_of_uniform_continuous_invariant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform.continuous_on_iff'_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.core_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_uniform_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_subset_comp_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lebesgue_number_lemma", "description": " Let `c : \u03b9 \u2192 set \u03b1` be an open cover of a compact set `s`. Then there exists an entourage\n`n` such that for each `x \u2208 s` its `n`-neighborhood is contained in some `c i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inhabited_uniform_space_core", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "disjoint.exists_uniform_thickening_of_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_continuous_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "refl_mem_uniformity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_nhds_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.core.sum", "description": " Uniformity on a disjoint union. Entourages of the diagonal in the union are obtained\nby taking independently an entourage of the diagonal in the first part, and an entourage of\nthe diagonal in the second part.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.uniform_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniformity_lift_le_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_comp_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_continuous_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_continuous_Inf_dom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniformity_has_basis_open_symmetric", "description": " Open elements `s : set (\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b1)` of `\ud835\udce4 \u03b1` such that `(x, y) \u2208 s \u2194 (y, x) \u2208 s` form a basis\nof `\ud835\udce4 \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lebesgue_number_of_compact_open", "description": " A useful consequence of the Lebesgue number lemma: given any compact set `K` contained in an\nopen set `U`, we can find an (open) entourage `V` such that the ball of size `V` about any point of\n`K` is contained in `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.mk'", "description": "Alternative constructor for `uniform_space \u03b1` when a topology is already given.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name"