re", "description": "Closed entourages form a basis of the uniformity filter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_continuous_infi_rng", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_continuous_to_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.core.mk'", "description": " An alternative constructor for `uniform_space.core`. This version unfolds various\n`filter`-related definitions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_topological_space_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_basis.uniform_continuous_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "open_of_uniformity_sum_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.core", "description": "This core description of a uniform space is outside of the type class hierarchy. It is useful\n for constructions of uniform spaces, when the topology is derived from the uniform space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.core.uniformity", "description": "This core description of a uniform space is outside of the type class hierarchy. It is useful\n for constructions of uniform spaces, when the topology is derived from the uniform space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.core.refl", "description": "This core description of a uniform space is outside of the type class hierarchy. It is useful\n for constructions of uniform spaces, when the topology is derived from the uniform space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.core.symm", "description": "This core description of a uniform space is outside of the type class hierarchy. It is useful\n for constructions of uniform spaces, when the topology is derived from the uniform space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.core.comp", "description": "This core description of a uniform space is outside of the type class hierarchy. It is useful\n for constructions of uniform spaces, when the topology is derived from the uniform space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniformity_has_basis_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.mem_closure_iff_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_iff_ball_subset", "description": "See also `is_open_iff_open_ball_subset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.of_core_eq", "description": " Construct a `uniform_space` from a `u : uniform_space.core` and a `topological_space` structure\nthat is equal to `u.to_topological_space`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space_comap_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_continuous_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ball_inter_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.bUnion_uniformity_ball", "description": "The uniform neighborhoods of all points of a dense set cover the whole space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_continuous\u2082.uniform_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_mem_nhds_ball_subset_of_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_continuous_on", "description": " A function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is *uniformly continuous* on `s : set \u03b1` if `(f x, f y)` tends to\nthe diagonal as `(x, y)` tends to the diagonal while remaining in `s \u00d7\u02e2 s`.\nIn other words, if `x` is sufficiently close to `y`, then `f x` is close to\n`f y` no matter where `x` and `y` are located in `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_ball_comp", "description": "The triangle inequality for `uniform_space.ball`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.mem_closure_iff_symm_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_uniformity_of_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inf_uniformity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_nhds_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ball_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform.continuous_at_iff_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lift_nhds_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.core.to_topological_space", "description": "A uniform space generates a topological space", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space", "description": "A uniform space is a generalization of the \"uniform\" topological aspects of a\n metric space. It consists of a filter on `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b1` called the \"uniformity\", which\n satisfies properties analogous to the reflexivity, symmetry, and triangle properties\n of a metric.\n\n A metric space has a natural uniformity, and a uniform space has a natural topology.\n A topological group also has a natural uniformity, even when it is not metrizable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.to_topological_space", "description": "A uniform space is a generalization of the \"uniform\" topological aspects of a\n metric space. It consists of a filter on `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b1` called the \"uniformity\", which\n satisfies properties analogous to the reflexivity, symmetry, and triangle properties\n of a metric.\n\n A metric space has a natural uniformity, and a uniform space has a natural topology.\n A topological group also has a natural uniformity, even when it is not metrizable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.to_core", "description": "A uniform space is a generalization of the \"uniform\" topological aspects of a\n metric space. It consists of a filter on `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b1` called the \"uniformity\", which\n satisfies properties analogous to the reflexivity, symmetry, and triangle properties\n of a metric.\n\n A metric space has a natural uniformity, and a uniform space has a natural topology.\n A topological group also has a natural uniformity, even when it is not metrizable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.is_open_uniformity", "description": "A uniform space is a generalization of the \"uniform\" topological aspects of a\n metric space. It consists of a filter on `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b1` called the \"uniformity\", which\n satisfies properties analogous to the reflexivity, symmetry, and triangle properties\n of a metric.\n\n A metric space has a natural uniformity, and a uniform space has a natural topology.\n A topological group also has a natural uniformity, even when it is not metrizable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comp_symm_of_uniformity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.comp_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "symmetrize_mem_uniformity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.core.mk_of_basis", "description": "Defining an `uniform_space.core` from a filter basis satisfying some uniformity-like axioms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_continuous_Inf_rng", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_continuous_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_basis_uniformity'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_continuous.prod_mk_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_topological_space_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.is_open_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.context.mk_app", "description": " Apply the function `n : \u2200 {\u03b1} [inst \u03b1], _` to the implicit parameters in the\ncontext, and the given list of arguments.\n\nCompared to `context.app`, this takes the name of the typeclass, rather than an\ninferred typeclass instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.term_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.term_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.zero_termg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.term_add_term", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.int_smul_instg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.zero_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.smulg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.normal_expr.refl_conv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.eval_atom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.normal_expr.to_list", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.normalize_mode.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.unfold_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.subst_into_smul_upcast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.unfold_zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.abel", "description": "Evaluate expressions in the language of *additive*, commutative monoids and groups.\nIt attempts to prove the goal outright if there is no `at`\nspecifier and the target is an equality, but if this\nfails, it falls back to rewriting all monoid expressions into a normal form.\nIf there is an `at` specifier, it rewrites the given target into a normal form.\n\n`abel!` will use a more aggressive reducibility setting to identify atoms.\nThis can prove goals that `abel` cannot, but is more expensive.\n```lean\nexample {\u03b1 : Type*} {a b : \u03b1} [add_comm_monoid \u03b1] : a + (b + a) = a + a + b := by abel\nexample {\u03b1 : Type*} {a b : \u03b1} [add_comm_group \u03b1] : (a + b) - ((b + a) + a) = -a := by abel\nexample {\u03b1 : Type*} {a b : \u03b1} [add_comm_group \u03b1] (hyp : a + a - a = b - b) : a = 0 :=\nby { abel at hyp, exact hyp }\nexample {\u03b1 : Type*} {a b : \u03b1} [add_comm_group \u03b1] : (a + b) - (id a + b) = 0 := by abel!\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.add_g", "description": " Add the letter \"g\" to the end of the name, e.g. turning `term` into `termg`.\n\nThis is used to choose between declarations taking `add_comm_monoid` and those\ntaking `add_comm_group` instances.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.subst_into_smulg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.term_atom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.normalize", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.term_add_termg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.unfold_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.context.int_to_expr", "description": "Interpret an integer as a coefficient to a term.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.termg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.abel1", "description": " Tactic for solving equations in the language of\n*additive*, commutative monoids and groups.\nThis version of `abel` fails if the target is not an equality\nthat is provable by the axioms of commutative monoids/groups.\n\n`abel1!` will use a more aggressive reducibility setting to identify atoms.\nThis can prove goals that `abel` cannot, but is more expensive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.normal_expr.term'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.context.iapp", "description": " Apply the function `n : \u2200 {\u03b1} [add_comm_{monoid,group} \u03b1]` to the given\nlist of arguments.\n\nWill use the `add_comm_{monoid,group}` instance that has been cached in the context.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.subst_into_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.term_smulg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.normalize_mode", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.normalize_mode.raw", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.normalize_mode.term", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.tactic.abel", "description": "Evaluate expressions in the language of *additive*, commutative monoids and groups.\nIt attempts to prove the goal outright if there is no `at`\nspecifier and the target is an equality, but if this\nfails, it falls back to rewriting all monoid expressions into a normal form.\nIf there is an `at` specifier, it rewrites the given target into a normal form.\n\n`abel!` will use a more aggressive reducibility setting to identify atoms.\nThis can prove goals that `abel` cannot, but is more expensive.\n```lean\nexample {\u03b1 : Type*} {a b : \u03b1} [add_comm_monoid \u03b1] : a + (b + a) = a + a + b := by abel\nexample {\u03b1 : Type*} {a b : \u03b1} [add_comm_group \u03b1] : (a + b) - ((b + a) + a) = -a := by abel\nexample {\u03b1 : Type*} {a b : \u03b1} [add_comm_group \u03b1] (hyp : a + a - a = b - b) : a = 0 :=\nby { abel at hyp, exact hyp }\nexample {\u03b1 : Type*} {a b : \u03b1} [add_comm_group \u03b1] : (a + b) - (id a + b) = 0 := by abel!\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.const_add_termg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.normal_expr.to_string", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.term_add_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.eval'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.context", "description": " The `context` for a call to `abel`.\n\nStores a few options for this call, and caches some common subexpressions\nsuch as typeclass instances and `0 : \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.context.red", "description": " The `context` for a call to `abel`.\n\nStores a few options for this call, and caches some common subexpressions\nsuch as typeclass instances and `0 : \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.context.\u03b1", "description": " The `context` for a call to `abel`.\n\nStores a few options for this call, and caches some common subexpressions\nsuch as typeclass instances and `0 : \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.context.univ", "description": " The `context` for a call to `abel`.\n\nStores a few options for this call, and caches some common subexpressions\nsuch as typeclass instances and `0 : \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.context.\u03b10", "description": " The `context` for a call to `abel`.\n\nStores a few options for this call, and caches some common subexpressions\nsuch as typeclass instances and `0 : \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.context.is_group", "description": " The `context` for a call to `abel`.\n\nStores a few options for this call, and caches some common subexpressions\nsuch as typeclass instances and `0 : \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.context.inst", "description": " The `context` for a call to `abel`.\n\nStores a few options for this call, and caches some common subexpressions\nsuch as typeclass instances and `0 : \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.nat_smul_instg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.zero_term", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.expr.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.nat_smul_inst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.context.app", "description": " Apply the function `n : \u2200 {\u03b1} [inst : add_whatever \u03b1], _` to the\nimplicit parameters in the context, and the given list of arguments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.abel.mode", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.mk_context", "description": "Populate a `context` object for evaluating `e`, up to reducibility level `red`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.eval_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.normal_expr.has_to_tactic_format", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.normal_expr.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.eval_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.eval_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.normal_expr.zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.term_add_constg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.context.mk_term", "description": "Evaluate a term with coefficient `n`, atom `x` and successor terms `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.normal_expr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.normal_expr.zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.normal_expr.nterm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.term_atomg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.const_add_term", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.eval_smul'", "description": "Normalize a term `orig` of the form `smul e\u2081 e\u2082` or `smulg e\u2081 e\u2082`.\n Normalized terms use `smul` for monoids and `smulg` for groups,\n so there are actually four cases to handle:\n * Using `smul` in a monoid just simplifies the pieces using `subst_into_smul`\n * Using `smulg` in a group just simplifies the pieces using `subst_into_smulg`\n * Using `smul a b` in a group requires converting `a` from a nat to an int and\n   then simplifying `smulg \u2191a b` using `subst_into_smul_upcast`\n * Using `smulg` in a monoid is impossible (or at least out of scope),\n   because you need a group argument to write a `smulg` term", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.zero_smulg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.term", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.normal_expr.pp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.normal_expr.e", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.unfold_smulg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abel.normalize_mode.has_reflect", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.to_signed_measure_eq_to_signed_measure_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.map_range_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.zero_le_restrict_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.ennreal_to_measure_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.restrict_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.mutually_singular.zero_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.restrict_le_restrict_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.to_signed_measure_apply_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.neg_le_neg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.absolutely_continuous.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.le_restrict_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.to_measure_of_zero_le", "description": " Given a signed measure `s` and a positive measurable set `i`, `to_measure_of_zero_le`\nprovides the measure, mapping measurable sets `j` to `s (i \u2229 j)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.trim", "description": "Restriction of a vector measure onto a sub-\u03c3-algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.map_range_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.nonneg_of_zero_le_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.restrict_le_zero_of_not_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.map_range\u2097", "description": " Given a continuous linear map `f : M \u2192 N`, `map_range\u2097` is the linear map mapping the\nvector measure `v` on `M` to the vector measure `f \u2218 v` on `N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.map_gm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.equiv_measure_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.to_signed_measure_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.absolutely_continuous.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.add_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.measurable_of_not_zero_le_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.absolutely_continuous.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.restrict_gm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.to_ennreal_vector_measure_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.mutually_singular.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.trim_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.ennreal_to_measure", "description": "A vector measure over `\u211d\u22650\u221e` is a measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.has_sum_of_disjoint_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.of_nonneg_disjoint_union_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.absolutely_continuous.zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.to_measure_of_zero_le'", "description": "The underlying function for `signed_measure.to_measure_of_zero_le`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.restrict_trim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.to_signed_measure_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.coe_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.map_range_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.absolutely_continuous.neg_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.measure_of_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.to_ennreal_vector_measure_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.of_add_of_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.not_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.of_disjoint_Union_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.le_restrict_univ_iff_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.coe_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.to_ennreal_vector_measure_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.nonpos_of_restrict_le_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.to_measure_of_le_zero_to_signed_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.coe_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.restrict_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.sub_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.partial_order", "description": " Vector measures over a partially ordered monoid is partially ordered.\n\nThis definition is consistent with `measure.partial_order`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.to_measure_of_zero_le_to_signed_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.restrict_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.le_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.restrict_le_restrict_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.to_signed_measure", "description": "A finite measure coerced into a real function is a signed measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.restrict_gm", "description": "`vector_measure.restrict` as an additive monoid homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.map_not_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.subset_le_of_restrict_le_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.to_measure_of_le_zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.absolutely_continuous", "description": " A vector measure `v` is absolutely continuous with respect to a measure `\u03bc` if for all sets\n`s`, `\u03bc s = 0`, we have `v s = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.restrict\u2097_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.of_Union_nonpos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.to_measure_of_zero_le_finite", "description": "`signed_measure.to_measure_of_zero_le` is a finite measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.restrict_le_restrict_countable_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.map_range", "description": " Given a vector measure `v` on `M` and a continuous add_monoid_hom `f : M \u2192 N`, `f \u2218 v` is a\nvector measure on `N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.vector_measure.measurable_of_not_restrict_le_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {