, "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "ne.symm", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "mk_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "or.left_comm", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "or.comm", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "non_contradictory_em", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "ne.irrefl", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "subsingleton_prop", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "plift", "description": "Universe lifting operation from Sort to Type", "p": "core"}, {"name": "plift.down", "description": "Universe lifting operation from Sort to Type", "p": "core"}, {"name": "dif_ctx_congr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nonempty", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nonempty.intro", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "implies_true_iff", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "iff.trans", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "true_or", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "ne_self_iff_false", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "eq_self_iff_true", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nonempty_of_inhabited", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "and_congr_right", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "forall_congr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "let_value_eq", "description": "Equalities for rewriting let-expressions", "p": "core"}, {"name": "not_or", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "not_true", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "inv_image.trans", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "not_false", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "not_congr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "empty_relation", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "irreflexive", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "or_false", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "iff", "description": " `iff P Q`, with notation `P \u2194 Q`, is the proposition asserting that `P` and `Q` are equivalent,\nthat is, have the same truth value.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "iff.mp", "description": " `iff P Q`, with notation `P \u2194 Q`, is the proposition asserting that `P` and `Q` are equivalent,\nthat is, have the same truth value.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "iff.mpr", "description": " `iff P Q`, with notation `P \u2194 Q`, is the proposition asserting that `P` and `Q` are equivalent,\nthat is, have the same truth value.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "exists_unique.elim", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "ulift.down_up", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "ne", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "iff_true", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "xor", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "unique_of_exists_unique", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "of_eq_true", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "Exists", "description": "The existential quantifier.\n\nTo prove a goal of the form `\u22a2 \u2203 x, p x`, you can provide a witness `y` with the tactic `existsi y`.\nIf you are working in a project that depends on mathlib, then we recommend the `use` tactic\ninstead.\nYou'll then be left with the goal `\u22a2 p y`.\n\nTo extract a witness `x` and proof `hx : p x` from a hypothesis `h : \u2203 x, p x`,\nuse the tactic `cases h with x hx`. See also the mathlib tactics `obtain` and `rcases`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "Exists.intro", "description": "The existential quantifier.\n\nTo prove a goal of the form `\u22a2 \u2203 x, p x`, you can provide a witness `y` with the tactic `existsi y`.\nIf you are working in a project that depends on mathlib, then we recommend the `use` tactic\ninstead.\nYou'll then be left with the goal `\u22a2 p y`.\n\nTo extract a witness `x` and proof `hx : p x` from a hypothesis `h : \u2203 x, p x`,\nuse the tactic `cases h with x hx`. See also the mathlib tactics `obtain` and `rcases`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "dif_eq_if", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "inv_image", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cast_proof_irrel", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "type_eq_of_heq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "iff_iff_implies_and_implies", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "heq.symm", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "and_iff_right", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "ne.intro", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "right_identity", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "ite", "description": "if-then-else", "p": "core"}, {"name": "neq_of_not_iff", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "subrelation", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "or.neg_resolve_right", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "let_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "if_false", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "ne.def", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "of_iff_true", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "not_iff_self", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "trans_rel_left", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "dif_neg", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "if_neg", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "or_true", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "forall_not_of_not_exists", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "not_false_iff", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "iff.elim_left", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "not_not_intro", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "decidable.true", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "not_iff_not_of_iff", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "false.elim", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "dif_ctx_simp_congr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "decidable_eq_of_bool_pred", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "proof_irrel", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "iff.decidable", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "bool.ff_ne_tt", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "decidable.em", "description": "Law of Excluded Middle.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "decidable.not_and_iff_or_not", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "and_self", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "heq.subst", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "heq_of_eq_rec_right", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "decidable.not_or_iff_and_not", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "prop.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "and_not_self", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "iff.comm", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "heq_self_iff_true", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "or.imp_left", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "decidable.not_not_iff", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "pi.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "or_assoc", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "implies.trans", "description": "Implication `\u2192` is transitive. If `P \u2192 Q` and `Q \u2192 R` then `P \u2192 R`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "and.assoc", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "decidable_of_decidable_of_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "symmetric", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "eq_rec_heq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "decidable.by_cases", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "heq.trans", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "ne.elim", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "or.elim", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "and.decidable", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "iff_congr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cast_heq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "or_congr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "plift.down_up", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "if_congr_prop", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "exists.intro", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "or_comm", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "and.elim", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "decidable_eq_inr_neg", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "iff.elim_right", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "forall_prop_decidable", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "right_cancelative", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "absurd", "description": "We can't have `a` and `\u00aca`, that would be absurd!", "p": "core"}, {"name": "iff.elim", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "iff_false", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "or.symm", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cast_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "dite", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "decidable.false", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "inhabited", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "inhabited.default", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "and_false", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "implies_of_if_neg", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "eq.to_iff", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "congr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "heq_of_heq_of_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "or.resolve_left", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "or.decidable", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "iff_not_self", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "heq_of_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "rec_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "false_and", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "decidable.to_bool", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "or_self", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "mt", "description": "Modus tollens. If an implication is true, then so is its contrapositive.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "false_of_true_iff_false", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "total", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "exists_imp_exists", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "exists_congr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "left_comm", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "exists_unique_congr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "plift.up_down", "description": "Bijection between \u03b1 and plift \u03b1", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.paren", "description": "Surround with \"()\".", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.join", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "name.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.of_options", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.sbracket", "description": "Surround with \"[]\".", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.when", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "sigma.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "string_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "sum_has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "trace_fmt", "description": "Traces the given format to the output window, then performs the given continuation.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.highlight", "description": "Make the given format be displayed a particular color.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.to_string", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "subtype.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.color", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.color.red", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.color.green", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.color.orange", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.color.blue", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.color.pink", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.color.cyan", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.color.grey", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.indent", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.space", "description": "The whitespace character `\" \"`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.color.to_string", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.flatten", "description": "Flattening removes all of the `format.nest` items from the format tree.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "char.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "options.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "list.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "decidable.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.has_append", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.of_string", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.compose", "description": "Concatenate the given format strings.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "prod.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "option.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "bool.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "list.to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "has_to_format", "description": " Use this instead of `has_to_string` to enable prettier formatting.\nSee docstring for `format` for more on the differences between `format` and `string`.\nNote that `format` is `meta` while `string` is not.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "has_to_format.to_format", "description": " Use this instead of `has_to_string` to enable prettier formatting.\nSee docstring for `format` for more on the differences between `format` and `string`.\nNote that `format` is `meta` while `string` is not.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.cbrace", "description": "Surround with \"{}\".", "p": "core"}, {"name": "unsigned.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.line", "description": "Indicate that it is ok to put a linebreak in here if the line is too long.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.of_nat", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "to_fmt", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.bracket", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.nest", "description": " `format.nest n f` tells the formatter that `f` is nested inside something with length `n`\nso that it is pretty-printed with the correct tabs on a line break.\nFor example, in `list.to_format` we have:\n\n```lean\n(nest 1 $ format.join $ list.intersperse (\",\" ++ line) $ xs.map to_fmt)\n```\n\nThis will be written all on one line, but when the list is too large, it will put in linebreaks after the comma and indent later lines by 1.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.nil", "description": "= `\"\"`", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.is_nil", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.group", "description": "When printing the given format `f`, if `f.flatten` fits without need for linebreaks then print the `f.flatten`, else print `f` unflattened with linebreaks.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "string.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format", "description": "Format is a rich string with highlighting and information about how tabs should be put in if linebreaks are needed. A 'pretty string'.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.has_to_string", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "format.dcbrace", "description": "Surround with \"\u2983\u2984\".", "p": "core"}, {"name": "unit.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact_kernel_subobject_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.exact_of_exact_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact_comp_hom_inv_comp_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact", "description": "Two morphisms `f : A \u27f6 B`, `g : B \u27f6 C` are called exact if `w : f \u226b g = 0` and the natural map\n`image_to_kernel f g w : image_subobject f \u27f6 kernel_subobject g` is an epimorphism.\n\nIn any preadditive category, this is equivalent to `w : f \u226b g = 0` and `homology f g w \u2245 0`.\n\nIn an abelian category, this is equivalent to `image_to_kernel f g w` being an isomorphism,\nand hence equivalent to the usual definition,\n`image_subobject f = kernel_subobject g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact.w", "description": "Two morphisms `f : A \u27f6 B`, `g : B \u27f6 C` are called exact if `w : f \u226b g = 0` and the natural map\n`image_to_kernel f g w : image_subobject f \u27f6 kernel_subobject g` is an epimorphism.\n\nIn any preadditive category, this is equivalent to `w : f \u226b g = 0` and `homology f g w \u2245 0`.\n\nIn an abelian category, this is equivalent to `image_to_kernel f g w` being an isomorphism,\nand hence equivalent to the usual definition,\n`image_subobject f = kernel_subobject g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact.epi", "description": "Two morphisms `f : A \u27f6 B`, `g : B \u27f6 C` are called exact if `w : f \u226b g = 0` and the natural map\n`image_to_kernel f g w : image_subobject f \u27f6 kernel_subobject g` is an epimorphism.\n\nIn any preadditive category, this is equivalent to `w : f \u226b g = 0` and `homology f g w \u2245 0`.\n\nIn an abelian category, this is equivalent to `image_to_kernel f g w` being an isomorphism,\nand hence equivalent to the usual definition,\n`image_subobject f = kernel_subobject g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.kernel_\u03b9_eq_zero_of_exact_zero_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact_zero_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact.w_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel.lift.epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.factor_thru_kernel_subobject.epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.kernel_subobject_arrow_eq_zero_of_exact_zero_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.epi_iff_exact_zero_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comp_eq_zero_of_image_eq_kernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact_iso_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact_kernel_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.kernel_comp_cokernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preadditive.exact_of_iso_of_exact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact_of_image_eq_kernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact_comp_mono_iff", "description": "The dual of this lemma is only true when `V` is abelian, see `abelian.exact_epi_comp_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.fork_\u03b9_comp_cofork_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preadditive.exact_of_iso_of_exact'", "description": " A reformulation of `preadditive.exact_of_iso_of_exact` that does not involve the arrow\ncategory.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comp_eq_zero_of_exact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preadditive.exact_iff_exact_of_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.reflects_exact_sequences", "description": "A functor reflects exact sequences if any composable pair of morphisms that is mapped to an\n   exact pair is itself exact.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.reflects_exact_sequences.reflects", "description": "A functor reflects exact sequences if any composable pair of morphisms that is mapped to an\n   exact pair is itself exact.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.kernel_comp_cokernel_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact_epi_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact_comp_hom_inv_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact_comp_inv_hom_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact_comp_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.fork_\u03b9_comp_cofork_\u03c0_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact_epi_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.image_to_kernel_is_iso_of_image_eq_kernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact_comp_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_iff_exact_zero_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preadditive.exact_iff_homology_zero", "description": "In any preadditive category,\ncomposable morphisms `f g` are exact iff they compose to zero and the homology vanishes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact_zero_left_of_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact_of_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group.exists_list_of_mem_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_subgroup.mem_add_center", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_subgroup.neg_mem_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_group_hom.zero_iff_ker_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_group_hom.zero_ker_neg'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_subgroup.trivial", "description": "the trivial additive subgroup", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.of", "description": "Create a bundled subgroup from a set `s` and `[is_subgroup s]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group.normal_closure.is_normal", "description": "The normal closure of s is a normal subgroup.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_subgroup.add_center_normal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.mem_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_group_hom.one_iff_ker_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_group_hom.mem_ker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_group_hom.injective_iff_trivial_ker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_subgroup.inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_group_hom.range_add_subgroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_subgroup.eq_trivial_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_subgr