ar_map.to_is_linear_map", "description": " A function `f` satisfies `is_bounded_linear_map \ud835\udd5c f` if it is linear and satisfies the\ninequality `\u2016f x\u2016 \u2264 M * \u2016x\u2016` for some positive constant `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_linear_map.bound", "description": " A function `f` satisfies `is_bounded_linear_map \ud835\udd5c f` if it is linear and satisfies the\ninequality `\u2016f x\u2016 \u2264 M * \u2016x\u2016` for some positive constant `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.map_smul\u209b\u2097\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_linear_map.snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_bilinear_map.is_bounded_linear_map_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_linear_map.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_bilinear_map.map_sub_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.map_smul\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.map_add\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_linear_map.is_O_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_bilinear_map.linear_deriv", "description": " Definition of the derivative of a bilinear map `f`, given at a point `p` by\n`q \u21a6 f(p.1, q.2) + f(q.1, p.2)` as in the standard formula for the derivative of a product.\nWe define this function here as a linear map `E \u00d7 F \u2192\u2097[\ud835\udd5c] G`, then `is_bounded_bilinear_map.deriv`\nstrengthens it to a continuous linear map `E \u00d7 F \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] G`.\n``.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_linear_map.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.map_sub\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_linear_map.tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_bilinear_map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_linear_map_prod_multilinear", "description": " Taking the cartesian product of two continuous multilinear maps\nis a bounded linear operation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_bilinear_map.deriv", "description": " The derivative of a bounded bilinear map at a point `p : E \u00d7 F`, as a continuous linear map\nfrom `E \u00d7 F` to `G`. The statement that this is indeed the derivative of `f` is\n`is_bounded_bilinear_map.has_fderiv_at` in `analysis.calculus.fderiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_bilinear_map_deriv_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_bilinear_map_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_bilinear_map.continuous_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_bilinear_map", "description": " A map `f : E \u00d7 F \u2192 G` satisfies `is_bounded_bilinear_map \ud835\udd5c f` if it is bilinear and\ncontinuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_bilinear_map.add_left", "description": " A map `f : E \u00d7 F \u2192 G` satisfies `is_bounded_bilinear_map \ud835\udd5c f` if it is bilinear and\ncontinuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_bilinear_map.smul_left", "description": " A map `f : E \u00d7 F \u2192 G` satisfies `is_bounded_bilinear_map \ud835\udd5c f` if it is bilinear and\ncontinuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_bilinear_map.add_right", "description": " A map `f : E \u00d7 F \u2192 G` satisfies `is_bounded_bilinear_map \ud835\udd5c f` if it is bilinear and\ncontinuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_bilinear_map.smul_right", "description": " A map `f : E \u00d7 F \u2192 G` satisfies `is_bounded_bilinear_map \ud835\udd5c f` if it is bilinear and\ncontinuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_bilinear_map.bound", "description": " A map `f : E \u00d7 F \u2192 G` satisfies `is_bounded_bilinear_map \ud835\udd5c f` if it is bilinear and\ncontinuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"nam