llows us to write `{x \u2208 s | p x}` for `finset.filter p s`.\n Since the former notation requires us to define this for all propositions `p`, and `finset.filter`\n only works for decidable propositions, the notation `{x \u2208 s | p x}` is only compatible with\n classical logic because it uses `classical.prop_decidable`.\n We don't want to redo all lemmas of `finset.filter` for `has_sep.sep`, so we make sure that `simp`\n unfolds the notation `{x \u2208 s | p x}` to `finset.filter p s`. If `p` happens to be decidable, the\n simp-lemma `finset.filter_congr_decidable` will make sure that `finset.filter` uses the right\n instance for decidability.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.disjoint_filter_filter_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.to_finset_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.subset_union_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.union_subset_union_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.union_eq_right_iff_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.filter_true", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nonempty.not_disjoint", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `finset.not_disjoint_iff_nonempty_inter`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mem_range_succ_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.not_nonempty_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mem_insert_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.ssubset_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.union_distrib_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.choose_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inter_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.coe_eq_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.range_filter_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inter_subset_inter_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"