 of\n`l` satisfying `p` this unique element, as an element of the ambient type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.const_mul_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.localization_to_stalk_stalk_specializes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.stalk_specializes_stalk_to_fiber", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.stalk_to_fiber_ring_hom.category_theory.is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.is_locally_fraction_pred", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.stalk_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_open_res", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_basic_open_to_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.localization_to_stalk_stalk_specializes_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.open_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.as_ideal.is_localization.at_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.localization_to_stalk_stalk_to_fiber_ring_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.is_iso_to_basic_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.stalk_to_fiber_ring_hom_to_stalk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.const_mul_rev", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.global_sections_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_global_factors_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_stalk_comp_stalk_to_fiber_ring_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.comm_ring_structure_sheaf_in_Type_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_presheaf_comp_forget", "description": "Some glue, verifying that that structure presheaf valued in `CommRing` agrees\nwith the `Type` valued structure presheaf.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.open_to_localization_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.is_localization.to_stalk", "description": "Stalk of the structure sheaf at a prime p as localization of R", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_open_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.const_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.is_fraction.eq_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_open_eq_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_stalk_stalk_specializes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.is_unit_to_stalk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.localizations.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.germ_comp_stalk_to_fiber_ring_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.stalk_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.const_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.locally_const_basic_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.coe_open_to_localization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.germ_to_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.localization_to_stalk", "description": " The canonical ring homomorphism from the localization of `R` at `p` to the stalk\nof the structure sheaf at the point `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.is_locally_fraction", "description": "We will define the structure sheaf as\nthe subsheaf of all dependent functions in `\u03a0 x : U, localizations R x`\nconsisting of those functions which can locally be expressed as a ratio of\n(the images in the localization of) elements of `R`.\n\nQuoting Hartshorne:\n\nFor an open set $U \u2286 Spec A$, we define $\ud835\udcaa(U)$ to be the set of functions\n$s : U \u2192 \u2a06_{\ud835\udd2d \u2208 U} A_\ud835\udd2d$, such that $s(\ud835\udd2d) \u2208 A_\ud835\udd2d$ for each $\ud835\udd2d$,\nand such that $s$ is locally a quotient of elements of $A$:\nto be precise, we require that for each $\ud835\udd2d \u2208 U$, there is a neighborhood $V$ of $\ud835\udd2d$,\ncontained in $U$, and elements $a, f \u2208 A$, such that for each $\ud835\udd2e \u2208 V, f \u2209 \ud835\udd2e$,\nand $s(\ud835\udd2e) = a/f$ in $A_\ud835\udd2e$.\n\nNow Hartshorne had the disadvantage of not knowing about dependent functions,\nso we replace his circumlocution about functions into a disjoint union with\n`\u03a0 x : U, localizations x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.prime_spectrum.Top", "description": "The prime spectrum, just as a topological space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.const_mul_cancel'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_presheaf_in_CommRing_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.sections_subring", "description": "The functions satisfying `is_locally_fraction` form a subring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.comap_fun_is_locally_fraction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.comap_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.stalk_specializes_stalk_to_fiber_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.open_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.stalk_specializes_stalk_to_fiber_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.stalk_to_fiber_ring_hom_localization_to_stalk_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.localization_to_stalk_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.res_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.const_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_presheaf_in_CommRing", "description": "The structure presheaf, valued in `CommRing`, constructed by dressing up the `Type` valued\nstructure presheaf.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.comap_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.const_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_basic_open_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_open_comp_comap_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.is_localization.to_basic_open", "description": "Sections of the structure sheaf of Spec R on a basic open as localization of R", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.global_sections_iso_hom_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.comap_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.localizations.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.normalize_finite_fraction_representation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_basic_open", "description": " The canonical ring homomorphism interpreting `s \u2208 R_f` as a section of the structure sheaf\non the basic open defined by `f \u2208 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.global_sections_iso", "description": "The ring isomorphism between the ring `R` and the global sections `\u0393(X, \ud835\udcaa\u2093)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.res_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.const_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.stalk_iso", "description": " The ring isomorphism between the stalk of the structure sheaf of `R` at a point `p`\ncorresponding to a prime ideal in `R` and the localization of `R` at `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.localizations.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.localization_to_stalk_stalk_specializes_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.open_to_localization", "description": " The ring homomorphism that takes a section of the structure sheaf of `R` on the open set `U`,\nimplemented as a subtype of dependent functions to localizations at prime ideals, and evaluates\nthe section on the point corresponding to a given prime ideal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.comap_id'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.const_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.germ_to_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_open", "description": " The canonical ring homomorphism interpreting an element of `R` as\na section of the structure sheaf.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.exists_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.stalk_to_fiber_ring_hom", "description": " The ring homomorphism from the stalk of the structure sheaf of `R` at a point corresponding to\na prime ideal `p` to the localization of `R` at `p`,\nformed by gluing the `open_to_localization` maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.const_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.is_fraction_prelocal", "description": "The predicate `is_fraction` is \"prelocal\",\nin the sense that if it holds on `U` it holds on any open subset `V` of `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_stalk_stalk_specializes_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.comap", "description": "For a ring homomorphism `f : R \u2192+* S` and open sets `U` and `V` of the prime spectra of `R` and\n`S` such that `V \u2286 (comap f) \u207b\u00b9 U`, the induced ring homomorphism from the structure sheaf of `R`\nat `U` to the structure sheaf of `S` at `V`.\n\nExplicitly, this map is given as follows: For a point `p : V`, if the section `s` evaluates on `p`\nto the fraction `a / b`, its image on `V` evaluates on `p` to the fraction `f(a) / f(b)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_stalk_stalk_specializes_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.structure_sheaf", "description": "The structure sheaf on $Spec R$, valued in `CommRing`.\n\nThis is provided as a bundled `SheafedSpace` as `Spec.SheafedSpace R` later.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.localizations.local_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.global_sections_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.comap_id_eq_map", "description": "For an inclusion `i : V \u27f6 U` between open sets of the prime spectrum of `R`, the comap of the\nidentity from OO_X(U) to OO_X(V) equals as the restriction map of the structure sheaf.\n\nThis is a generalization of the fact that, for fixed `U`, the comap of the identity from OO_X(U)\nto OO_X(U) is the identity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.const_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_stalk", "description": " The canonical ring homomorphism interpreting an element of `R` as an element of\nthe stalk of `structure_sheaf R` at `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.stalk_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_open_germ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.comap_id", "description": "The comap of the identity is the identity. In this variant of the lemma, two open subsets `U` and\n`V` are given as arguments, together with a proof that `U = V`. This is be useful when `U` and `V`\nare not definitionally equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.const_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_basic_open_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.localization_to_stalk_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_presheaf_in_CommRing_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_basic_open_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_open_comp_comap_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.res_const'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.localization_to_stalk_stalk_to_fiber_ring_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.localizations", "description": "The type family over `prime_spectrum R` consisting of the localization over each point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_basic_open_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.stalk_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.stalk_to_fiber_ring_hom_localization_to_stalk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.is_iso_to_global", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_open_comp_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.localization_to_stalk.category_theory.is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_global_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.stalk_to_fiber_ring_hom_germ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.const", "description": " The section of `structure_sheaf R` on an open `U` sending each `x \u2208 U` to the element\n`f/g` in the localization of `R` at `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.localization_to_basic_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.stalk_to_fiber_ring_hom_germ'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf_in_Type", "description": "The structure sheaf (valued in `Type`, not yet `CommRing`) is the subsheaf consisting of\nfunctions satisfying `is_locally_fraction`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.is_fraction", "description": "The predicate saying that a dependent function on an open `U` is realised as a fixed fraction\n`r / s` in each of the stalks (which are localizations at various prime ideals).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.comap_fun", "description": "Given a ring homomorphism `f : R \u2192+* S`, an open set `U` of the prime spectrum of `R` and an open\nset `V` of the prime spectrum of `S`, such that `V \u2286 (comap f) \u207b\u00b9' U`, we can push a section `s`\non `U` to a section on `V`, by composing with `localization.local_ring_hom _ _ f` from the left and\n`comap f` from the right. Explicitly, if `s` evaluates on `comap f p` to `a / b`, its image on `V`\nevaluates on `p` to `f(a) / f(b)`.\n\nAt the moment, we work with arbitrary dependent functions `s : \u03a0 x : U, localizations R x`. Below,\nwe prove the predicate `is_locally_fraction` is preserved by this map, hence it can be extended to\na morphism between the structure sheaves of `R` and `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.basic_open_iso", "description": " The ring isomorphism between the structure sheaf on `basic_open f` and the localization of `R`\nat the submonoid of powers of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.is_unit_to_basic_open_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_fn_abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.norm_lt_iff_of_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.nnreal.upper_bound", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.dist_extend_extend", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.eval_clm", "description": "The evaluation at a point, as a continuous linear map from `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d47 \u03b2` to `\u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_of_normed_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.comp", "description": " Composition (in the target) of a bounded continuous function with a Lipschitz map again\ngives a bounded continuous function", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.has_int_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.mk_of_discrete_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.dist_set_exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.const_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.mk_of_compact_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.semilattice_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.bounded_continuous_map_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.self_eq_nnreal_part_sub_nnreal_part_neg", "description": "Decompose a bounded continuous function to its positive and negative parts.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.to_continuous_map_add_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.uniform_continuous_comp", "description": "The composition operator (in the target) with a Lipschitz map is uniformly continuous", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.sub_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.nsmul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.simps.apply", "description": "See Note [custom simps projection]. We need to specify this projection explicitly in this case,\n because it is a composition of multiple projections.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.dist_lt_of_nonempty_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.of_normed_add_comm_group", "description": " Constructing a bounded continuous function from a uniformly bounded continuous\nfunction taking values in a normed group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.dist_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.has_nat_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.normed_comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.has_dist", "description": "The uniform distance between two bounded continuous functions", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.eval_clm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.dist_le", "description": "The distance between two functions is controlled by the supremum of the pointwise distances", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.has_nat_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.pow_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.mk_of_compact", "description": "A continuous function on a compact space is automatically a bounded continuous function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.norm_comp_continuous_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.nnnorm_coe_fun_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.non_unital_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.dist_le_two_norm'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_map_class.to_continuous_map_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.complete_space", "description": "Bounded continuous functions taking values in a complete space form a complete space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.norm_coe_le_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.bdd_above_range_norm_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.mk_of_compact_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.algebra_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.continuous_eval_const", "description": "When `x` is fixed, `(f : \u03b1 \u2192\u1d47 \u03b2) \u21a6 f x` is continuous", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function", "description": " `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d47 \u03b2` is the type of bounded continuous functions `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` from a topological space to a\nmetric space.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : \u03b1 \u2192\u1d47 \u03b2)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [bounded_continuous_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `bounded_continuous_map_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.to_continuous_map", "description": " `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d47 \u03b2` is the type of bounded continuous functions `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` from a topological space to a\nmetric space.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : \u03b1 \u2192\u1d47 \u03b2)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [bounded_continuous_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `bounded_continuous_map_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.map_bounded'", "description": " `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d47 \u03b2` is the type of bounded continuous functions `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` from a topological space to a\nmetric space.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : \u03b1 \u2192\u1d47 \u03b2)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [bounded_continuous_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `bounded_continuous_map_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.arzela_ascoli\u2082", "description": "Second version, with pointwise equicontinuity and range in a compact subset", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.norm_of_normed_add_comm_group_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.dist_le_iff_of_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.has_coe_to_fun", "description": " Helper instance for when there's too many metavariables to apply `fun_like.has_coe_to_fun`\ndirectly.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.pseudo_metric_space", "description": "The type of bounded continuous functions, with the uniform distance, is a pseudometric space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.forall_coe_one_iff_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_comp_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.normed_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.extend_of_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.mk_of_discrete_to_continuous_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.norm_eq_of_nonempty", "description": " When the domain is non-empty, we do not need the `0 \u2264 C` condition in the formula for \u2016f\u2016 as an\n`Inf`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.semi_normed_comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.dist_le_two_norm", "description": "Distance between the images of any two points is at most twice the norm of the function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.abs_self_eq_nnreal_part_add_nnreal_part_neg", "description": " Express the absolute value of a bounded continuous function in terms of its\npositive and negative parts.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.zero_comp_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.star_module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.norm_const_le", "description": " Norm of `const \u03b1 b` is less than or equal to `\u2016b\u2016`. If `\u03b1` is nonempty,\nthen it is equal to `\u2016b\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.nnnorm_const_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.nndist_coe_le_nndist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.non_unital_normed_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.norm_le", "description": "The norm of a function is controlled by the supremum of the pointwise norms", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.module'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.norm_const_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.nndist_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_fn_add_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.norm_smul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.normed_star_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.star_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.has_lipschitz_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.star_add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_le_coe_add_dist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.norm_one_class", "description": "If `\u2016(1 : \u03b2)\u2016 = 1`, then `\u2016(1 : \u03b1 \u2192\u1d47 \u03b2)\u2016 = 1` if `\u03b1` is nonempty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.continuous_comp_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.nndist_le_two_nnnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.semilattice_inf", "description": "Continuous normed lattice group valued functions form a meet-semilattice", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.nnnorm_coe_le_nnnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.nnnorm", "description": " The absolute value of a bounded continuous `\u211d`-valued function as a bounded\ncontinuous `\u211d\u22650`-valued function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.mk_of_discrete", "description": " If a function is bounded on a discrete space, it is automatically continuous,\nand therefore gives rise to an element of the type of bounded continuous functions", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.nnreal_part", "description": " The nonnegative part of a bounded continuous `\u211d`-valued function as a bounded\ncontinuous `\u211d\u22650`-valued function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.add_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.dist_zero_of_empty", "description": "On an empty space, bounded continuous functions are at distance 0", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.has_sub", "description": "The pointwise difference of two bounded continuous functions is again bounded continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.has_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.norm_eq_zero_of_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.C", "description": "`bounded_continuous_function.const` as a `ring_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.dist_lt_iff_of_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.extend_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.has_add", "description": "The pointwise sum of two bounded continuous functions is again bounded continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.bounded_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.abs_diff_coe_le_dist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.norm_comp", "description": " Taking the pointwise norm of a bounded continuous function with values in a\n`seminormed_add_comm_group` yields a bounded continuous function with values in \u211d.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.bounded_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.mk_of_bound", "description": "A continuous function with an explicit bound is a bounded continuous function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.to_continuous_map_add_hom", "description": "The additive map forgetting that a bounded continuous function is bounded.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.comp_left_continuous_bounded", "description": "Postcomposition of bounded continuous functions into a normed module by a continuous linear map is\na continuous linear map.\nUpgraded version of `continuous_linear_map.comp_left_continuous`, similar to\n`linear_map.comp_left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.mk_of_bound_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.nnnorm_eq_supr_nnnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.norm_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.continuous_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.sum_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.nnnorm_le", "description": "The nnnorm of a function is controlled by the supremum of the pointwise nnnorms", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.is_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.norm_eq_supr_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.dist_eq_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.nnnorm_const_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.nndist_eq_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.one_comp_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_npow_rec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_map_class", "description": " `bounded_continuous_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of bounded continuous maps.\n\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `bounded_continuous_function`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_map_class.coe", "description": " `bounded_continuous_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of bounded continuous maps.\n\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `bounded_continuous_function`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_map_class.coe_injective'", "description": " `bounded_continuous_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of bounded continuous maps.\n\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `bounded_continuous_function`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_map_class.map_continuous", "description": " `bounded_continuous_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of bounded continuous maps.\n\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `bounded_continuous_function`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_map_class.map_bounded", "description": " `bounded_continuous_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of bounded continuous maps.\n\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `bounded_continuous_function`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.nnreal_part_coe_fun_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.comp_continuous", "description": "Composition of a bounded continuous function and a continuous function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.of_normed_add_comm_group_discrete", "description": " Constructing a bounded continuous function from a uniformly bounded\nfunction on a discrete space, taking values in a normed group", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.normed_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_norm_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.has_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.forall_coe_zero_iff_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.has_smul'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.nnnorm_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.comp_continuous_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.star_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.restrict_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.const_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_nsmul_rec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.inhabited", "description": "If the target space is inhabited, so is the space of bounded continuous functions", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.const_to_continuous_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_fn_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.seminormed_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.lipschitz_comp_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.restrict", "description": "Restrict a bounded continuous function to a set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.norm_lt_iff_of_nonempty_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.lipschitz_comp", "description": "The composition operator (in the target) with a Lipschitz map is Lipschitz", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.normed_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.has_bounded_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.const", "description": "Constant as a continuous bounded function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.norm_eq", "description": " The norm of a bounded continuous function is the supremum of `\u2016f x\u2016`.\nWe use `Inf` to ensure that the definition works if `\u03b1` has no elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.inducing_coe_fn", "description": "The topology on `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d47 \u03b2` is exactly the topology induced by the natural map to `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.mk_of_compact_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_star", "description": " The right-hand side of this equality can be parsed `star \u2218 \u21d1f` because of the\ninstance `pi.has_star`. Upon inspecting the goal, one sees `\u22a2 \u21d1(star f) = star \u21d1f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.add_add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.non_unital_semi_normed_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.isometry_extend", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.mul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.zsmul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.metric_space", "description": "The type of bounded continuous functions, with the uniform distance, is a metric space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.lipschitz_evalx", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_to_continuous_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.norm_norm_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.extend", "description": " A version of `function.extend` for bounded continuous maps. We assume that the domain has\ndiscrete topology, so we only need to verify boundedness.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.to_continuous_map_linear_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.continuous_comp", "description": "The composition operator (in the target) with a Lipschitz map is continuous", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.extend_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.cstar_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.has_neg", "description": "The pointwise opposite of a bounded continuous function is again bounded continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.to_continuous_map_linear_map", "description": "The linear map forgetting that a bounded continuous function is bounded.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_of_normed_add_comm_group_discrete", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.dist_lt_iff_of_nonempty_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.add_comp_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.continuous_eval", "description": "The evaluation map is continuous, as a joint function of `u` and `x`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.neg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.comp_left_continuous_bounded_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.tendsto_iff_tendsto_uniformly", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.dist_coe_le_dist", "description": "The pointwise distance is controlled by the distance between functions, by definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.cod_restrict", "description": "Restriction (in the target) of a bounded continuous function taking values in a subset", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.semi_normed_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.normed_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.arzela_ascoli", "description": " Third (main) version, with pointwise equicontinuity and range in a compact subset, but\nwithout closedness. The closure is then compact", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.mk_of_compact_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.mk_of_compact_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_fn_add_hom", "description": " Coercion of a `normed_add_group_hom` is an `add_monoid_hom`. Similar to\n`add_monoid_hom.coe_fn`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.nndist_set_exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.mk_of_compact_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.uniform_continuous_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.arzela_ascoli\u2081", "description": "First version, with pointwise equicontinuity and range in a compact space", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.bounded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.eq_of_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.norm_le_of_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.extend_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.has_coe_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.embedding_coe_fn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.normed_lattice_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.coe_zsmul_rec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.has_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.hom_orthogonal.matrix_decomposition", "description": " Morphisms between two direct sums over a hom orthogonal family `s : \u03b9 \u2192 C`\nare equivalent to block diagonal matrices,\nwith blocks indexed by `\u03b9`,\nand matrix entries in `i`-th block living in the endomorphisms of `s i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.hom_orthogonal.eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.hom_orthogonal.matrix_decomposition_add_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.hom_orthogonal", "description": " A family of objects is \"hom orthogonal\" if\nthere is at most one morphism between distinct objects.\n\n(In a category with zero morphisms, that must be the zero morphism.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.hom_orthogonal.matrix_decomposition_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.hom_orthogonal.matrix_decomposition_add_equiv", "description": "`hom_orthogonal.matrix_decomposition` as an additive equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.hom_orthogonal.equiv_of_iso", "description": "Given a hom orthogonal family `s : \u03b9 \u2192 C`\nfor which each `End (s i)` is a ring with invariant basis number (e.g. if each `s i` is simple),\nif two direct sums over `s` are isomorphic, then they have the same multiplicities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.hom_orthogonal.matrix_decomposition_linear_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.hom_orthogonal.matrix_decomposition_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.hom_orthogonal.matrix_decomposition_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.hom_orthogonal.matrix_decomposition_add_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.hom_orthogonal.matrix_decomposition_linear_equiv", "description": "`hom_orthogonal.matrix_decomposition` as an `R`-linear equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.hom_orthogonal.matrix_decomposition_linear_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.hom_orthogonal.matrix_decomposition_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.tr_normal", "description": " Translate a normal instruction. For the `write` command, we use a `goto` indirection so that\nwe can access the current value of the tape.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.stmt.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0to1.tr_cfg", "description": "The configuration translation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.move_right_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.tr_supports", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.blank_rel.above", "description": "Given two `blank_rel` lists, there exists (constructively) a common join.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.append_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.st_act.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.tr_respects", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.mem_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.step_aux", "description": "The semantics of TM1 evaluation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.write", "description": "Replace the current value of the head on the tape.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.tr_tape_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.write_move_right_n", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.step_supports", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.stmts_supports_stmt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.eval", "description": "Evaluates a TM2 program to completion, with the output on the same stack as the input.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.stmts\u2081_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.stmt", "description": "The TM1 model is a simplification and extension of TM0\n (Post-Turing model) in the direction of Wang B-machines. The machine's\n internal state is extended with a (finite) store `\u03c3` of variables\n that may be accessed and updated at any time.\n A machine is given by a `\u039b` indexed set of procedures or functions.\n Each function has a body which is a `stmt`, which can either be a\n `move` or `write` command, a `branch` (if statement based on the\n current tape value), a `load` (set the variable value),\n a `goto` (call another function), or `halt`. Note that here\n most statements do not have labels; `goto` commands can only\n go to a new function. All commands have access to the variable value\n and current tape value.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.stmt.move", "description": "The TM1 model is a simplification and extension of TM0\n (Post-Turing model) in the direction of Wang B-machines. The machine's\n internal state is extended with a (finite) store `\u03c3` of variables\n that may be accessed and updated at any time.\n A machine is given by a `\u039b` indexed set of procedures or functions.\n Each function has a body which is a `stmt`, which can either be a\n `move` or `write` command, a `branch` (if statement based on the\n current tape value), a `load` (set the variable value),\n a `goto` (call another function), or `halt`. Note that here\n most statements do not have labels; `goto` commands can only\n go to a new function. All commands have access to the variable value\n and current tape value.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.stmt.write", "description": "The TM1 model is a simplification and extension of TM0\n (Post-Turing model) in the direction of Wang B-machines. The machine's\n internal state is extended with a (finite) store `\u03c3` of variables\n that may be accessed and updated at any time.\n A machine is given by a `\u039b` indexed set of procedures or functions.\n Each function has a body which is a `stmt`, which can either be a\n `move` or `write` command, a `branch` (if statement based on the\n current tape value), a `load` (set the variable value),\n a `goto` (call another function), or `halt`. Note that here\n most statements do not have labels; `goto` commands can only\n go to a new function. All commands have access to the variable value\n and current tape value.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.stmt.load", "description": "The TM1 model is a simplification and extension of TM0\n (Post-Turing model) in the direction of Wang B-machines. The machine's\n internal state is extended with a (finite) store `\u03c3` of variables\n that may be accessed and updated at any time.\n A machine is given by a `\u039b` indexed set of procedures or functions.\n Each function has a body which is a `stmt`, which can either be a\n `move` or `write` command, a `branch` (if statement based on the\n current tape value), a `load` (set the variable value),\n a `goto` (call another function), or `halt`. Note that here\n most statements do not have labels; `goto` commands can only\n go to a new function. All commands have access to the variable value\n and current tape value.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.stmt.branch", "description": "The TM1 model is a simplification and extension of TM0\n (Post-Turing model) in the direction of Wang B-machines. The machine's\n internal state is extended with a (finite) store `\u03c3` of variables\n that may be accessed and updated at any time.\n A machine is given by a `\u039b` indexed set of procedures or functions.\n Each function has a body which is a `stmt`, which can either be a\n `move` or `write` command, a `branch` (if statement based on the\n current tape value), a `load` (set the variable value),\n a `goto` (call another function), or `halt`. Note that here\n most statements do not have labels; `goto` commands can only\n go to a new function. All commands have access to the variable value\n and current tape value.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.stmt.goto", "description": "The TM1 model is a simplification and extension of TM0\n (Post-Turing model) in the direction of Wang B-machines. The machine's\n internal state is extended with a (finite) store `\u03c3` of variables\n that may be accessed and updated at any time.\n A machine is given by a `\u039b` indexed set of procedures or functions.\n Each function has a body which is a `stmt`, which can either be a\n `move` or `write` command, a `branch` (if statement based on the\n current tape value), a `load` (set the variable value),\n a `goto` (call another function), or `halt`. Note that here\n most statements do not have labels; `goto` commands can only\n go to a new function. All commands have access to the variable value\n and current tape value.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.stmt.halt", "description": "The TM1 model is a simplification and extension of TM0\n (Post-Turing model) in the direction of Wang B-machines. The machine's\n internal state is extended with a (finite) store `\u03c3` of variables\n that may be accessed and updated at any time.\n A machine is given by a `\u039b` indexed set of procedures or functions.\n Each function has a body which is a `stmt`, which can either be a\n `move` or `write` command, a `branch` (if statement based on the\n current tape value), a `load` (set the variable value),\n a `goto` (call another function), or `halt`. Note that here\n most statements do not have labels; `goto` commands can only\n go to a new function. All commands have access to the variable value\n and current tape value.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.stmt.map", "description": " Map a TM statement across a function. This does nothing to move statements and maps the write\nvalues.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.tr_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.cons_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.eval", "description": "Evaluate a Turing machine on initial input to a final state,\n if it terminates.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.st_act", "description": " A stack action is a command that interacts with the top of a stack. Our default position\nis at the bottom of all the stacks, so we have to hold on to this action while going to the end\nto modify the stack.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.st_act.push", "description": " A stack action is a command that interacts with the top of a stack. Our default position\nis at the bottom of all the stacks, so we have to hold on to this action while going to the end\nto modify the stack.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.st_act.peek", "description": " A stack action is a command that interacts with the top of a stack. Our default position\nis at the bottom of all the stacks, so we have to hold on to this action while going to the end\nto modify the stack.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.st_act.pop", "description": " A stack action is a command that interacts with the top of a stack. Our default position\nis at the bottom of all the stacks, so we have to hold on to this action while going to the end\nto modify the stack.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.eval_maximal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.tr", "description": "The top level program.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.pointed_map.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.mk\u2082", "description": "Construct a tape from a left side and an inclusive right side.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.append_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.\u039b'.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank", "description": " A `list_blank \u0393` is a quotient of `list \u0393` by extension by blanks at the end. This is used to\nrepresent half-tapes of a Turing machine, so that we can pretend that the list continues\ninfinitely with blanks.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.add_bottom_modify_nth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.step_run", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.tail_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.init", "description": "The initial state of the TM2 model. The input is provided on a designated stack.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.blank_extends.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.tr_st_act", "description": " The program corresponding to state transitions at the end of a stack. Here we start out just\nafter the top of the stack, and should end just after the new top of the stack.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.machine.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.supports_stmt_write", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.st_run", "description": "The TM2 statement corresponding to a stack action.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.tr_tape'_move_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.step", "description": "The step function for the TM2 model.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.stmt.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.map_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.stmts_supports_stmt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.modify_nth", "description": "Apply a function to a value stored at the nth position of the list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.step_supports", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tr_reaches\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.tail_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.frespects", "description": "A simpler version of `respects` when the state transition relation `tr` is a function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.exists_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.supports", "description": "A set `S` of labels supports machine `M` if all the `goto`\n statements in the functions in `S` refer only to other functions\n in `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.cfg.map", "description": " Map a configuration across a function, given `f : \u0393 \u2192 \u0393'` a map of the alphabets and\n`g : \u039b \u2192 \u039b'` a map of the machine states.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.proj", "description": "The `i`-th projection as a pointed map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.bind", "description": " The `bind` function on lists is well defined on `list_blank`s provided that the default element\nis sent to a sequence of default elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.step_aux_write", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.st_write", "description": "The effect of a stack action on the stack.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.append", "description": "Append a list on the left side of a list_blank.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.writes", "description": "The set of accessible `\u039b'.write` machine states.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.exists_cons", "description": " The `cons` and `head`/`tail` functions are mutually inverse, unlike in the case of `list` where\nthis only holds for nonempty lists.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.map_write", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.supports_stmt_move", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.bind_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.reaches\u2080.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.has_emptyc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tr_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.stmts\u2081", "description": "The set of subtree statements in a statement.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.nth_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.move_right_n_head", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.reaches", "description": " The reflexive transitive closure of a state transition function. `reaches f a b` means\nthere is a finite sequence of steps `f a = some a\u2081`, `f a\u2081 = some a\u2082`, ... such that `a\u2099 = b`.\nThis relation permits zero steps of the state transition function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.head", "description": "The head of a `list_blank` is well defined.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.nth_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.reaches\u2081", "description": " The transitive closure of a state transition function. `reaches\u2081 f a b` means there is a\nnonempty finite sequence of steps `f a = some a\u2081`, `f a\u2081 = some a\u2082`, ... such that `a\u2099 = b`.\nThis relation does not permit zero steps of the state transition function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.right\u2080_nth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.machine.map_step", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.head_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.blank_rel.below", "description": "Given two `blank_rel` lists, there exists (constructively) a common meet.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.blank_extends.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.reaches_total", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.tr_normal", "description": " The translation of TM2 statements to TM1 statements. regular actions have direct equivalents,\nbut stack actions are deferred by going to the corresponding `go` state, so that we can find the\nappropriate stack top.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.tr_cfg", "description": "The machine configuration translation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to0.tr_respects", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.reaches", "description": "The (reflexive) reachability relation for the TM2 model.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.\u039b'", "description": " The machine states of the TM2 emulator. We can either be in a normal state when waiting for the\nnext TM2 action, or we can be in the \"go\" and \"return\" states to go to the top of the stack and\nreturn to the bottom, respectively.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.\u039b'.normal", "description": " The machine states of the TM2 emulator. We can either be in a normal state when waiting for the\nnext TM2 action, or we can be in the \"go\" and \"return\" states to go to the top of the stack and\nreturn to the bottom, respectively.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.\u039b'.go", "description": " The machine states of the TM2 emulator. We can either be in a normal state when waiting for the\nnext TM2 action, or we can be in the \"go\" and \"return\" states to go to the top of the stack and\nreturn to the bottom, respectively.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.\u039b'.ret", "description": " The machine states of the TM2 emulator. We can either be in a normal state when waiting for the\nnext TM2 action, or we can be in the \"go\" and \"return\" states to go to the top of the stack and\nreturn to the bottom, respectively.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.fun_respects", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.nth_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.blank_extends.above_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.step_supports", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.move_right_nth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.map_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.stmts", "description": "The set of statements accessible from initial set `S` of labels.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.init", "description": "The initial configuration.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.st_var", "description": "The effect of a stack action on the local variables, given the value of the stack.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.mk'", "description": "Construct a tape from a left side and an inclusive right side.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.mk'_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.cfg", "description": "The configuration state of a Turing machine during operation\n consists of a label (machine state), and a tape, represented in\n the form `(a, L, R)` meaning the tape looks like `L.rev ++ [a] ++ R`\n with the machine currently reading the `a`. The lists are\n automatically extended with blanks as the machine moves around.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.cfg.q", "description": "The configuration state of a Turing machine during operation\n consists of a label (machine state), and a tape, represented in\n the form `(a, L, R)` meaning the tape looks like `L.rev ++ [a] ++ R`\n with the machine currently reading the `a`. The lists are\n automatically extended with blanks as the machine moves around.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.cfg.tape", "description": "The configuration state of a Turing machine during operation\n consists of a label (machine state), and a tape, represented in\n the form `(a, L, R)` meaning the tape looks like `L.rev ++ [a] ++ R`\n with the machine currently reading the `a`. The lists are\n automatically extended with blanks as the machine moves around.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.tr_supports", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.tr_tape", "description": "The low level tape corresponding to the given tape over alphabet `\u0393`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.stmts\u2081_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0to1.\u039b'", "description": " The machine states for a TM1 emulating a TM0 machine. States of the TM0 machine are embedded\nas `normal q` states, but the actual operation is split into two parts, a jump to `act s q`\nfollowed by the action and a jump to the next `normal` state.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0to1.\u039b'.normal", "description": " The machine states for a TM1 emulating a TM0 machine. States of the TM0 machine are embedded\nas `normal q` states, but the actual operation is split into two parts, a jump to `act s q`\nfollowed by the action and a jump to the next `normal` state.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0to1.\u039b'.act", "description": " The machine states for a TM1 emulating a TM0 machine. States of the TM0 machine are embedded\nas `normal q` states, but the actual operation is split into two parts, a jump to `act s q`\nfollowed by the action and a jump to the next `normal` state.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.move_right_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.stmts_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.map_modify_nth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.blank_rel.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.tr_cfg", "description": "The relation between TM2 configurations and TM1 configurations of the TM2 emulator.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.tr_cfg.mk", "description": "The relation between TM2 configurations and TM1 configurations of the TM2 emulator.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.tr_respects_aux\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.step_aux", "description": "The step function for the TM2 model.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.add_bottom_nth_succ_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.tr_stmts\u2081_run", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.stmt", "description": "A Turing machine \"statement\" is just a command to either move\n left or right, or write a symbol on the tape.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.stmt.move", "description": "A Turing machine \"statement\" is just a command to either move\n left or right, or write a symbol on the tape.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.stmt.write", "description": "A Turing machine \"statement\" is just a command to either move\n left or right, or write a symbol on the tape.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.tail", "description": "The tail of a `list_blank` is well defined (up to the tail of blanks).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.move", "description": " Move the tape in response to a motion of the Turing machine. Note that `T.move dir.left` makes\n`T.left` smaller; the Turing machine is moving left and the tape is moving right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.nth", "description": "The n-th element of a `list_blank` is well defined for all `n : \u2115`, unlike in a `list`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.pointed_map", "description": "A pointed map of `inhabited` types is a map that sends one default value to the other.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.pointed_map.f", "description": "A pointed map of `inhabited` types is a map that sends one default value to the other.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.pointed_map.map_pt'", "description": "A pointed map of `inhabited` types is a map that sends one default value to the other.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.cfg.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.step_aux_read", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.move_left_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.stmts\u2081_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.reaches\u2081.to\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.stmts\u2081", "description": "The subterm closure of a statement.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.reaches\u2080.tail", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.dir.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.mk'_right\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.blank_rel.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.blank_rel.setoid", "description": "Construct a setoid instance for `blank_rel`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.map_init", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.mk'_nth_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to0.tr_aux", "description": " The core TM1 \u2192 TM0 translation function. Here `s` is the current value on the tape, and the\n`stmt\u2081` is the TM1 statement to translate, with local state `v : \u03c3`. We evaluate all regular\ninstructions recursively until we reach either a `move` or `write` command, or a `goto`; in the\nlatter case we emit a dummy `write s` step and transition to the new target location.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.step", "description": "The state transition function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.tr_cfg_init", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.tr_tape'", "description": "The low level tape corresponding to the given tape over alphabet `\u0393`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.left\u2080", "description": "The \"inclusive\" left side of the tape, including both `left` and `head`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.eval", "description": " Run a state transition function `\u03c3 \u2192 option \u03c3` \"to completion\". The return value is the last\nstate returned before a `none` result. If the state transition function always returns `some`,\nthen the computation diverges, returning `part.none`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.mk", "description": "The quotient map turning a `list` into a `list_blank`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.reaches_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.tr", "description": " The TM2 emulator machine states written as a TM1 program.\nThis handles the `go` and `ret` states, which shuttle to and from a stack top.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tr_reaches_rev", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.reaches\u2080.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.step_aux_move", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.cons", "description": "We can cons an element onto a `list_blank`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.pointed_map.mk_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.stmts\u2081_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.machine.map", "description": " Because the state transition function uses the alphabet and machine states in both the input\nand output, to map a machine from one alphabet and machine state space to another we need functions\nin both directions, essentially an `equiv` without the laws.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.read_aux", "description": "Read a vector of length `n` from the tape.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.head_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.nth_modify_nth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.write_nth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tr_eval_dom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0to1.tr", "description": "The program.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.tr_respects_aux\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.induction_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.stmt_st_rec", "description": " We have partitioned the TM2 statements into \"stack actions\", which require going to the end\nof the stack, and all other actions, which do not. This is a modified recursor which lumps the\nstack actions into one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.map", "description": "Apply a pointed map to a tape to change the alphabet.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.step", "description": "Execution semantics of the Turing machine.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.proj_map_nth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.blank_extends", "description": " The `blank_extends` partial order holds of `l\u2081` and `l\u2082` if `l\u2082` is obtained by adding\nblanks (`default : \u0393`) to the end of `l\u2081`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to0.\u039b'", "description": " The base machine state space is a pair of an `option stmt\u2081` representing the current program\nto be executed, or `none` for the halt state, and a `\u03c3` which is the local state (stored in the TM,\nnot the tape). Because there are an infinite number of programs, this state space is infinite, but\nfor a finitely supported TM1 machine and a finite type `\u03c3`, only finitely many of these states are\nreachable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.reaches.to\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to0.tr_cfg", "description": "Translate configurations from TM1 to TM0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.reaches\u2080", "description": " A variation on `reaches`. `reaches\u2080 f a b` holds if whenever `reaches\u2081 f b c` then\n`reaches\u2081 f a c`. This is a weaker property than `reaches` and is useful for replacing states with\nequivalent states without taking a step.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.\u0393'.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to0.\u039b'.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.cons_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.eval_maximal\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.reaches\u2080_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.eval", "description": " Evaluate a TM to completion, resulting in an output list on the tape (with an indeterminate\nnumber of blanks on the end).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.tr_stmts\u2081", "description": "The set of machine states accessible from an initial TM2 statement.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.map_mk\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0to1.tr_respects", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to0.tr_stmts", "description": " Given a finite set of accessible `\u039b` machine states, there is a finite set of accessible\nmachine states in the target (even though the type `\u039b'` is infinite).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.supports", "description": " Given a TM2 machine `M` and a set `S` of states, `supports M S` means that all states in\n`S` jump only to other states in `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.dir.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.reaches\u2081_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.add_bottom_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.frespects_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.stmts_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.nth_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.pointed_map.map_pt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.supports_stmt", "description": "A set `S` of labels supports the statement `q` if all the `goto`\n statements in `q` refer only to other functions in `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.cfg", "description": "The configuration of a TM1 machine is given by the currently\n evaluating statement, the variable store value, and the tape.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.cfg.l", "description": "The configuration of a TM1 machine is given by the currently\n evaluating statement, the variable store value, and the tape.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.cfg.var", "description": "The configuration of a TM1 machine is given by the currently\n evaluating statement, the variable store value, and the tape.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.cfg.tape", "description": "The configuration of a TM1 machine is given by the currently\n evaluating statement, the variable store value, and the tape.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.univ_supports", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tr_reaches", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.tr_eval_dom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.stmts", "description": " The set of all statements in a turing machine, plus one extra value `none` representing the\nhalt state. This is used in the TM1 to TM0 reduction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.reaches", "description": "The statement `reaches M s\u2081 s\u2082` means that `s\u2082` is obtained\n starting from `s\u2081` after a finite number of steps from `s\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.lift_on", "description": " A modified version of `quotient.lift_on'` specialized for `list_blank`, with the stronger\nprecondition `blank_extends` instead of `blank_rel`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.cons_head_tail", "description": " The `cons` and `head`/`tail` functions are mutually inverse, unlike in the case of `list` where\nthis only holds for nonempty lists.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.right\u2080", "description": "The \"inclusive\" right side of the tape, including both `right` and `head`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.mk'_head", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.\u0393'", "description": " The alphabet of the TM2 simulator on TM1 is a marker for the stack bottom,\nplus a vector of stack elements for each stack, or none if the stack does not extend this far.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.pointed_map.head_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.add_bottom_nth_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.dir", "description": "A direction for the turing machine `move` command, either\n left or right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.dir.left", "description": "A direction for the turing machine `move` command, either\n left or right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.dir.right", "description": "A direction for the turing machine `move` command, either\n left or right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.blank_rel", "description": " `blank_rel` is the symmetric closure of `blank_extends`, turning it into an equivalence\nrelation. Two lists are related by `blank_rel` if one extends the other by blanks.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.add_bottom", "description": " The bottom marker is fixed throughout the calculation, so we use the `add_bottom` function\nto express the program state in terms of a tape with only the stacks themselves.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.stmt.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.cfg", "description": " A configuration in the TM2 model is a label (or `none` for the halt state), the state of\nlocal variables, and the stacks. (Note that the stacks are not `list_blank`s, they have a definite\nsize.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.cfg.l", "description": " A configuration in the TM2 model is a label (or `none` for the halt state), the state of\nlocal variables, and the stacks. (Note that the stacks are not `list_blank`s, they have a definite\nsize.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.cfg.var", "description": " A configuration in the TM2 model is a label (or `none` for the halt state), the state of\nlocal variables, and the stacks. (Note that the stacks are not `list_blank`s, they have a definite\nsize.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.cfg.stk", "description": " A configuration in the TM2 model is a label (or `none` for the halt state), the state of\nlocal variables, and the stacks. (Note that the stacks are not `list_blank`s, they have a definite\nsize.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.reaches\u2080.single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.stmt", "description": "The TM2 model removes the tape entirely from the TM1 model,\n replacing it with an arbitrary (finite) collection of stacks.\n The operation `push` puts an element on one of the stacks,\n and `pop` removes an element from a stack (and modifying the\n internal state based on the result). `peek` modifies the\n internal state but does not remove an element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.stmt.push", "description": "The TM2 model removes the tape entirely from the TM1 model,\n replacing it with an arbitrary (finite) collection of stacks.\n The operation `push` puts an element on one of the stacks,\n and `pop` removes an element from a stack (and modifying the\n internal state based on the result). `peek` modifies the\n internal state but does not remove an element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.stmt.peek", "description": "The TM2 model removes the tape entirely from the TM1 model,\n replacing it with an arbitrary (finite) collection of stacks.\n The operation `push` puts an element on one of the stacks,\n and `pop` removes an element from a stack (and modifying the\n internal state based on the result). `peek` modifies the\n internal state but does not remove an element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.stmt.pop", "description": "The TM2 model removes the tape entirely from the TM1 model,\n replacing it with an arbitrary (finite) collection of stacks.\n The operation `push` puts an element on one of the stacks,\n and `pop` removes an element from a stack (and modifying the\n internal state based on the result). `peek` modifies the\n internal state but does not remove an element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.stmt.load", "description": "The TM2 model removes the tape entirely from the TM1 model,\n replacing it with an arbitrary (finite) collection of stacks.\n The operation `push` puts an element on one of the stacks,\n and `pop` removes an element from a stack (and modifying the\n internal state based on the result). `peek` modifies the\n internal state but does not remove an element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.stmt.branch", "description": "The TM2 model removes the tape entirely from the TM1 model,\n replacing it with an arbitrary (finite) collection of stacks.\n The operation `push` puts an element on one of the stacks,\n and `pop` removes an element from a stack (and modifying the\n internal state based on the result). `peek` modifies the\n internal state but does not remove an element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.stmt.goto", "description": "The TM2 model removes the tape entirely from the TM1 model,\n replacing it with an arbitrary (finite) collection of stacks.\n The operation `push` puts an element on one of the stacks,\n and `pop` removes an element from a stack (and modifying the\n internal state based on the result). `peek` modifies the\n internal state but does not remove an element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.stmt.halt", "description": "The TM2 model removes the tape entirely from the TM1 model,\n replacing it with an arbitrary (finite) collection of stacks.\n The operation `push` puts an element on one of the stacks,\n and `pop` removes an element from a stack (and modifying the\n internal state based on the result). `peek` modifies the\n internal state but does not remove an element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape", "description": " The tape of a Turing machine is composed of a head element (which we imagine to be the\ncurrent position of the head), together with two `list_blank`s denoting the portions of the tape\ngoing off to the left and right. When the Turing machine moves right, an element is pulled from the\nright side and becomes the new head, while the head element is consed onto the left side.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.head", "description": " The tape of a Turing machine is composed of a head element (which we imagine to be the\ncurrent position of the head), together with two `list_blank`s denoting the portions of the tape\ngoing off to the left and right. When the Turing machine moves right, an element is pulled from the\nright side and becomes the new head, while the head element is consed onto the left side.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.left", "description": " The tape of a Turing machine is composed of a head element (which we imagine to be the\ncurrent position of the head), together with two `list_blank`s denoting the portions of the tape\ngoing off to the left and right. When the Turing machine moves right, an element is pulled from the\nright side and becomes the new head, while the head element is consed onto the left side.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.right", "description": " The tape of a Turing machine is composed of a head element (which we imagine to be the\ncurrent position of the head), together with two `list_blank`s denoting the portions of the tape\ngoing off to the left and right. When the Turing machine moves right, an element is pulled from the\nright side and becomes the new head, while the head element is consed onto the left side.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.map_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0to1.\u039b'.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.write_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.tr_respects_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.tr_respects", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.stmts\u2081_supports_stmt_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.reaches\u2081_fwd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.mk'_left_right\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.blank_extends.above", "description": " Any two extensions by blank `l\u2081,l\u2082` of `l` have a common join (which can be taken to be the\nlonger of `l\u2081` and `l\u2082`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.map_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.tr_tape'_move_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.cfg.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.nth_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.\u0393'.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.respects", "description": " Given a relation `tr : \u03c3\u2081 \u2192 \u03c3\u2082 \u2192 Prop` between state spaces, and state transition functions\n`f\u2081 : \u03c3\u2081 \u2192 option \u03c3\u2081` and `f\u2082 : \u03c3\u2082 \u2192 option \u03c3\u2082`, `respects f\u2081 f\u2082 tr` means that if `tr a\u2081 a\u2082` holds\ninitially and `f\u2081` takes a step to `a\u2082` then `f\u2082` will take one or more steps before reaching a\nstate `b\u2082` satisfying `tr a\u2082 b\u2082`, and if `f\u2081 a\u2081` terminates then `f\u2082 a\u2082` also terminates.\nSuch a relation `tr` is also known as a refinement.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.exists_enc_dec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tr_eval'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.cfg.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.blank_rel.equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.stmts\u2081_supports_stmt_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.tr_supp", "description": " The set of accessible machine states, assuming that the input machine is supported on `S`,\nare the normal states embedded from `S`, plus all write states accessible from these states.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.supports", "description": "The raw definition of a Turing machine does not require that\n `\u0393` and `\u039b` are finite, and in practice we will be interested\n in the infinite `\u039b` case. We recover instead a notion of\n \"effectively finite\" Turing machines, which only make use of a\n finite subset of their states. We say that a set `S \u2286 \u039b`\n supports a Turing machine `M` if `S` is closed under the\n transition function and contains the initial state.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.pointed_map.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.\u039b'.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2.supports_stmt", "description": "Given a set `S` of states, `support_stmt S q` means that `q` only jumps to states in `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tr_eval_rev", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.move", "description": "A move left or right corresponds to `n` moves across the super-cell.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.move_left_nth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to0.tr", "description": "The translated TM0 machine (given the TM1 machine input).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.blank_extends.below_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.tr_respects_aux\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.move_left_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.machine.map_respects", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1.init", "description": " The initial state, given a finite input that is placed on the tape starting at the TM head and\ngoing to the right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.map_mk\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.supports_run", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.tail_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.tr_supp", "description": "The support of a set of TM2 states in the TM2 emulator.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.head_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.stk_nth_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.tr_normal_run", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.reaches\u2080.head", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.reaches\u2080.tail'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.mk'_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.\u039b'", "description": "The configuration state of the TM.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.\u039b'.normal", "description": "The configuration state of the TM.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.\u039b'.write", "description": "The configuration state of the TM.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.supports_stmt_read", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.eval_induction", "description": " (co-)Induction principle for `eval`. If a property `C` holds of any point `a` evaluating to `b`\nwhich is either terminal (meaning `a = b`) or where the next point also satisfies `C`, then it\nholds of any point where `eval f a` evaluates to `b`. This formalizes the notion that if\n`eval f a` evaluates to `b` then it reaches terminal state `b` in finitely many steps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.list_blank.map", "description": " The `map` function on lists is well defined on `list_blank`s provided that the map is\npointed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.tr_init", "description": " The initial state for the TM2 emulator, given an initial TM2 state. All stacks start out empty\nexcept for the input stack, and the stack bottom mark is set at the head.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.blank_rel.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to0.tr_supports", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.map_move", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.nth", "description": " The `nth` function of a tape is integer-valued, with index `0` being the head, negative indexes\non the left and positive indexes on the right. (Picture a number line.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.mk\u2081", "description": " Construct a tape from a list, with the head of the list at the TM head and the rest going\nto the right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM2to1.add_bottom_head_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to0.tr_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tape.write_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM0.machine", "description": "A Post-Turing machine with symbol type `\u0393` and label type `\u039b`\n is a function which, given the current state `q : \u039b` and\n the tape head `a : \u0393`, either halts (returns `none`) or returns\n a new state `q' : \u039b` and a `stmt` describing what to do,\n either a move left or right, or a write command.\n\n Both `\u039b` and `\u0393` are required to be inhabited; the default value\n for `\u0393` is the \"blank\" tape value, and the default value of `\u039b` is\n the initial state.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.read", "description": " To read a symbol from the tape, we use `read_aux` to traverse the symbol,\nthen return to the original position with `n` moves to the left.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.TM1to1.write", "description": "Write a list of bools on the tape.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_multiset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multiset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_mul", "description": " Basic hypothesis to talk about a topological monoid or a topological semigroup.\nA topological monoid over `M`, for example, is obtained by requiring both the instances `monoid M`\nand `has_continuous_mul M`.\n\nContinuity in only the left/right argument can be stated using\n`has_continuous_const_smul \u03b1 \u03b1`/`has_continuous_const_smul \u03b1\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_mul.continuous_mul", "description": " Basic hypothesis to talk about a topological monoid or a topological semigroup.\nA topological monoid over `M`, for example, is obtained by requiring both the instances `monoid M`\nand `has_continuous_mul M`.\n\nContinuity in only the left/right argument can be stated using\n`has_continuous_const_smul \u03b1 \u03b1`/`has_continuous_const_smul \u03b1\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.mul_right", "description": "The continuous map `\u03bb y, y * x`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.topological_closure", "description": " The (topological-space) closure of a submonoid of a space `M` with `has_continuous_mul` is\nitself a submonoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_mul_of_comm_of_nhds_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.coe_inv_units", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.top_closure_add_self_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_nhds_one_split4", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_scalar_tower.has_continuous_const_smul", "description": " If `R` acts on `A` via `A`, then continuous multiplication implies continuous scalar\nmultiplication by constants.\n\nNotably, this instances applies when `R = A`, or when `[algebra R A]` is available.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_set_of_map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_add_of_comm_of_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_mul_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_list_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.has_continuous_mul", "description": "If multiplication is continuous in `\u03b1`, then it also is in `\u03b1\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.exists_finset_mul_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smul_comm_class.has_continuous_const_smul", "description": " If the action of `R` on `A` commutes with left-multiplication, then continuous multiplication\nimplies continuous scalar multiplication by constants.\n\nNotably, this instances applies when `R = A\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_list_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom_of_mem_closure_range_coe", "description": " Construct a bundled monoid homomorphism `M\u2081 \u2192* M\u2082` from a function `f` and a proof that it\nbelongs to the closure of the range of the coercion from `M\u2081 \u2192* M\u2082` (or another type of bundled\nhomomorphisms that has a `monoid_hom_class` instance) to `M\u2081 \u2192 M\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.has_continuous_add", "description": "If addition is continuous in `\u03b1`, then it also is in `\u03b1\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom_of_tendsto_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.mul_left", "description": "The continuous map `\u03bb y, x * y`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_nhds_zero_quarter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.comm_monoid_topological_closure", "description": "If a submonoid of a topological monoid is commutative, then so is its topological closure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_mul_nhds_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.add_units", "description": "Construct an additive unit from limits of additive units\nand their negatives.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.add_left", "description": "The continuous map `\u03bb y, x + y", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_nhds_within_Iio.mul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.mul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsum_eventually_eq_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_set_of_map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_mul_induced", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_add.of_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.coe_add_units", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.has_continuous_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_mul_of_discrete_topology", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_nhds_within_Iio.const_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.mem_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_eq_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_mul_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.coe_neg_add_units", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.const_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_multiset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.top_closure_add_self_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemigroup.has_continuous_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_set_of_map_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.top_closure_mul_self_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_open_nhds_zero_add_subset", "description": "Given a open neighborhood `U` of `0` there is a open neighborhood `V` of `0`\n  such that `V + V \u2286 U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_add.to_has_continuous_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.has_continuous_mul'", "description": " A version of `pi.has_continuous_mul` for non-dependent functions. It is needed because sometimes\nLean fails to use `pi.has_continuous_mul` for non-dependent functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.has_continuous_add'", "description": "A version of `pi.has_continuous_add` for non-dependent functions. It is needed\nbecause sometimes Lean fails to use `pi.has_continuous_add` for non-dependent functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom_of_tendsto_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.add_right", "description": "The continuous map `\u03bb y, y + x", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.units", "description": "Construct a unit from limits of units and their inverses.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.top_closure_mul_self_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.has_continuous_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_nhds_within_Ioi.mul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_list_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_mul.to_has_continuous_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_nhds_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom_of_mem_closure_range_coe_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom_of_mem_closure_range_coe", "description": "Construct a bundled additive monoid homomorphism `M\u2081 \u2192+ M\u2082` from a function `f`\nand a proof that it belongs to the closure of the range of the coercion from `M\u2081 \u2192+ M\u2082` (or another\ntype of bundled homomorphisms that has a `add_monoid_hom_class` instance) to `M\u2081 \u2192 M\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.mem_nhds_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_finprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_list_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_add_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_add.to_has_continuous_vadd_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multiset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_finset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_nhds_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.units_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.is_closed_range_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_nhds_zero_half", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vadd_assoc_class.has_continuous_const_vadd", "description": "If `R` acts on `A` via `A`, then continuous addition implies\ncontinuous affine addition by constants.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_eq_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.topological_closure_minimal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.has_continuous_mul", "description": " If multiplication on a monoid is continuous, then multiplication on the units of the monoid,\nwith respect to the induced topology, is continuous.\n\nInversion is also continuous, but we register this in a later file, `topology.algebra.group`,\nbecause the predicate `has_continuous_inv` has not yet been defined.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_add_induced", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.has_continuous_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_cocompact_mul_left", "description": " Left-multiplication by a left-invertible element of a topological monoid is proper, i.e.,\ninverse images of compact sets are compact.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.has_continuous_smul_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.topological_closure_minimal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_open_nhds_one_split", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.add_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_mul_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inducing.has_continuous_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.exists_finset_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_units.has_continuous_add", "description": "If addition on an additive monoid is continuous, then addition on the additive units\nof the monoid, with respect to the induced topology, is continuous.\n\nNegation is also continuous, but we register this in a later file, `topology.algebra.group`, because\nthe predicate `has_continuous_neg` has not yet been defined.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inducing.has_continuous_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_finprod_cond", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vadd_comm_class.has_continuous_const_vadd", "description": "If the action of `R` on `A` commutes with left-addition, then\ncontinuous addition implies continuous affine addition by constants.\n\nNotably, this instances applies when `R = A\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.topological_closure", "description": "The (topological-space) closure of an additive submonoid of a space `M` with\n`has_continuous_add` is itself an additive submonoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_list_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_open_nhds_zero_half", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom_of_mem_closure_range_coe_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_set_of_map_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.has_continuous_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.has_continuous_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_finsum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_multiset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_finset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom_of_tendsto", "description": "Construct a bundled monoid homomorphism from a pointwise limit of monoid homomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_mul.of_nhds_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at.nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_add_of_discrete_topology", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_finset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.is_closed_topological_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_add", "description": " Basic hypothesis to talk about a topological additive monoid or a topological additive\nsemigroup. A topological additive monoid over `M`, for example, is obtained by requiring both the\ninstances `add_monoid M` and `has_continuous_add M`.\n\nContinuity in only the left/right argument can be stated using\n`has_continuous_const_vadd \u03b1 \u03b1`/`has_continuous_const_vadd \u03b1\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_add.continuous_add", "description": " Basic hypothesis to talk about a topological additive monoid or a topological additive\nsemigroup. A topological additive monoid over `M`, for example, is obtained by requiring both the\ninstances `add_monoid M` and `has_continuous_add M`.\n\nContinuity in only the left/right argument can be stated using\n`has_continuous_const_vadd \u03b1 \u03b1`/`has_continuous_const_vadd \u03b1\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u03b1`.", "p"