en a neighborhood `U` of `1` there is an open neighborhood `V` of `1`\nsuch that `VV \u2286 U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.has_continuous_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.is_closed_topological_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_add_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_list_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_nhds_one_split", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.has_continuous_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subsemigroup.has_continuous_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.has_continuous_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.coe_units", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.has_continuous_const_smul_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.add_comm_monoid_topological_closure", "description": "If a submonoid of an additive topological monoid is commutative, then so is its\ntopological closure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.le_topological_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.const_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.map_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient_map_add_subgroup_of_of_le_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.mk'_eq_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.map_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.map_id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient.group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.range_ker_lift_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient_quotient_equiv_quotient_aux_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.ker_lift_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.map", "description": "An `add_group` homomorphism `f : G \u2192+ H` induces a map `G/N \u2192+ H/M` if\n`N \u2286 f\u207b\u00b9(M)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient_inf_equiv_prod_normal_quotient", "description": " **Noether's second isomorphism theorem**: given two subgroups `H` and `N` of a group `G`, where\n`N` is normal, defines an isomorphism between `H/(H \u2229 N)` and `(HN)/N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient_map_subgroup_of_of_le_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient_quotient_equiv_quotient_aux_coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.fintype_of_ker_eq_range", "description": "If `F` and `H` are finite such that `ker(G \u2192+ H) = im(F \u2192+ G)`, then `G` is finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.map_comp_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient_bot_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient.add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.coe_zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.equiv_quotient_zpow_of_equiv_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.mk'_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.comap_comap_center", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.map_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.coe_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient_add_equiv_of_eq_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.coe_zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.lift_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.fintype_of_dom_of_coker", "description": "If `F` and `coker(F \u2192+ G)` are finite, then `G` is finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient_quotient_equiv_quotient", "description": "**Noether's third isomorphism theorem** for groups: `(G / N) / (M / N) \u2243* G / M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.ker_lift_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.add_subgroup_eq_top_of_subsingleton", "description": "If the quotient by an additive subgroup gives a singleton then the additive subgroup\nis the whole additive group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.mk'", "description": "The group homomorphism from `G` to `G/N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.ker_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.hom_quotient_zpow_of_hom", "description": "The map of quotients by powers of an integer induced by a group homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.lift", "description": " A group homomorphism `\u03c6 : G \u2192* H` with `N \u2286 ker(\u03c6)` descends (i.e. `lift`s) to a\ngroup homomorphism `G/N \u2192* H`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse", "description": " The canonical isomorphism `G/(ker \u03c6) \u2243* H` induced by a homomorphism `\u03c6 : G \u2192* H`\nwith a right inverse `\u03c8 : H \u2192 G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.equiv_quotient_zpow_of_equiv_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.lift_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient_map_add_subgroup_of_of_le", "description": "Let `A', A, B', B` be subgroups of `G`. If `A' \u2264 B'` and `A \u2264 B`,\nthen there is a map `A / (A' \u2293 A) \u2192+ B / (B' \u2293 B)` induced by the inclusions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient_ker_equiv_range", "description": " **Noether's first isomorphism theorem** (a definition): the canonical isomorphism between\n`G/(ker \u03c6)` to `range \u03c6`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse", "description": "The canonical isomorphism `G/(ker \u03c6) \u2243+ H` induced by a homomorphism `\u03c6 : G \u2192+ H`\nwith a right inverse `\u03c8 : H \u2192 G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.range_ker_lift", "description": "The induced map from the quotient by the kernel to the range.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group.fintype_of_ker_eq_range", "description": "If `F` and `H` are finite such that `ker(G \u2192* H) = im(F \u2192* G)`, then `G` is finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient_ker_equiv_range", "description": "The first isomorphism theorem (a definition): the canonical isomorphism between\n`G/(ker \u03c6)` to `range \u03c6`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.fintype_of_ker_of_codom", "description": "If `ker(G \u2192+ H)` and `H` are finite, then `G` is finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient_mul_equiv_of_eq_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.map_comp_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.hom_quotient_zpow_of_hom_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.equiv_quotient_zpow_of_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.subsingleton_quotient_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.ker_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.equiv_quotient_subgroup_of_of_eq", "description": " Let `A', A, B', B` be subgroups of `G`.\nIf `A' = B'` and `A = B`, then the quotients `A / (A' \u2293 A)` and `B / (B' \u2293 B)` are isomorphic.\n\nApplying this equiv is nicer than rewriting along the equalities, since the type of\n`(A'.subgroup_of A : subgroup A)` depends on on `A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.coe_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.map_normal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.mk'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.range_ker_lift_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient_bot", "description": "The canonical isomorphism `G/\u22a5 \u2243+ G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.hom_quotient_zpow_of_hom_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group.fintype_of_ker_le_range", "description": "If `F` and `H` are finite such that `ker(G \u2192* H) \u2264 im(F \u2192* G)`, then `G` is finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.lift_quot_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.ker_lift_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.map_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.con", "description": "The congruence relation generated by a normal subgroup.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.map_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient_quotient_equiv_quotient", "description": "**Noether's third isomorphism theorem** for additive groups:\n`(A / N) / (M / N) \u2243+ A / M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient_bot", "description": "The canonical isomorphism `G/\u22a5 \u2243* G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.coe_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.eq_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.add_monoid_hom_ext", "description": " Two `add_monoid_hom`s from an additive quotient group are equal if their\ncompositions with `add_quotient_group.mk'` are equal.\n\nSee note [partially-applied ext lemmas].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.equiv_quotient_zsmul_of_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.mk'", "description": "The additive group homomorphism from `G` to `G/N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient_quotient_equiv_quotient_aux", "description": "The map from the third isomorphism theorem for additive groups:\n`(A / N) / (M / N) \u2192 A / M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.hom_quotient_zpow_of_hom_comp_of_right_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient_add_equiv_of_eq", "description": "If two normal subgroups `M` and `N` of `G` are the same, their quotient groups are\nisomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.congr", "description": "`quotient_add_group.congr` lifts the isomorphism `e : G \u2243 H` to `G \u29f8 G' \u2243 H \u29f8 H'`,\ngiven that `e` maps `G` to `H`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.map_normal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.coe_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.congr", "description": " `quotient_group.congr` lifts the isomorphism `e : G \u2243 H` to `G \u29f8 G' \u2243 H \u29f8 H'`,\ngiven that `e` maps `G` to `H`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.map_id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.congr_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group.fintype_of_ker_of_codom", "description": "If `ker(G \u2192* H)` and `H` are finite, then `G` is finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient_ker_equiv_of_surjective", "description": "The canonical isomorphism `G/(ker \u03c6) \u2243+ H` induced by a surjection `\u03c6 : G \u2192+ H`.\n\nFor a `computable` version, see `quotient_add_group.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.hom_quotient_zsmul_of_hom", "description": "The map of quotients by multiples of an integer induced by an additive group\nhomomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.con", "description": "The additive congruence relation generated by a normal additive subgroup.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.fintype_of_ker_le_range", "description": "If `F` and `H` are finite such that `ker(G \u2192+ H) \u2264 im(F \u2192+ G)`, then `G` is finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.ker_lift_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.equiv_quotient_zsmul_of_equiv_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.congr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.lift_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient_bot_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.comap_comap_center", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.mk'_eq_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.map", "description": "A group homomorphism `f : G \u2192* H` induces a map `G/N \u2192* H/M` if `N \u2286 f\u207b\u00b9(M)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.lift_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient_inf_equiv_sum_normal_quotient", "description": "The second isomorphism theorem: given two subgroups `H` and `N` of a group `G`,\nwhere `N` is normal, defines an isomorphism between `H/(H \u2229 N)` and `(H + N)/N`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.ker_lift", "description": "The induced map from the quotient by the kernel to the codomain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient_quotient_equiv_quotient_aux_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.coe_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.equiv_quotient_zsmul_of_equiv_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.lift", "description": "An `add_group` homomorphism `\u03c6 : G \u2192+ H` with `N \u2286 ker(\u03c6)` descends (i.e. `lift`s)\nto a group homomorphism `G/N \u2192* H`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.coe_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.equiv_quotient_zpow_of_equiv", "description": "The equivalence of quotients by powers of an integer induced by a group isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient_map_subgroup_of_of_le", "description": " Let `A', A, B', B` be subgroups of `G`. If `A' \u2264 B'` and `A \u2264 B`,\nthen there is a map `A / (A' \u2293 A) \u2192* B / (B' \u2293 B)` induced by the inclusions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.range_ker_lift", "description": "The induced map from the quotient by the kernel to the range.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.subgroup_eq_top_of_subsingleton", "description": "If the quotient by a subgroup gives a singleton then the subgroup is the whole group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.equiv_quotient_zsmul_of_equiv", "description": "The equivalence of quotients by multiples of an integer induced by an additive group\nisomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.ker_lift_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.eq_iff_div_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.subsingleton_quotient_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.eq_iff_sub_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.hom_quotient_zsmul_of_hom_comp_of_right_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.lift_quot_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.monoid_hom_ext", "description": " Two `monoid_hom`s from a quotient group are equal if their compositions with\n`quotient_group.mk'` are equal.\n\nSee note [partially-applied ext lemmas].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.mk'_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient_ker_equiv_of_surjective", "description": " The canonical isomorphism `G/(ker \u03c6) \u2243* H` induced by a surjection `\u03c6 : G \u2192* H`.\n\nFor a `computable` version, see `quotient_group.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.hom_quotient_zsmul_of_hom_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.ker_lift_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient_bot_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.equiv_quotient_add_subgroup_of_of_eq", "description": "Let `A', A, B', B` be subgroups of `G`.\nIf `A' = B'` and `A = B`, then the quotients `A / (A' \u2293 A)` and `B / (B' \u2293 B)` are isomorphic.\n\nApplying this equiv is nicer than rewriting along the equalities, since the type of\n`(A'.add_subgroup_of A : add_subgroup A)` depends on on `A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient_bot_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.coe_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.ker_lift", "description": "The induced map from the quotient by the kernel to the codomain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.hom_quotient_zsmul_of_hom_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient.comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.congr_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.coe_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.congr_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.mk'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.congr_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient_quotient_equiv_quotient_aux", "description": "The map from the third isomorphism theorem for groups: `(G / N) / (M / N) \u2192 G / M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.range_ker_lift_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient_mul_equiv_of_eq", "description": " If two normal subgroups `M` and `N` of `G` are the same, their quotient groups are\nisomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.map_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient_quotient_equiv_quotient_aux_coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.range_ker_lift_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.coe_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group.fintype_of_dom_of_coker", "description": "If `F` and `coker(F \u2192* G)` are finite, then `G` is finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.Inf_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.mk_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.Sup_of_not_bdd_above", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.star_ring", "description": "The real numbers are a `*`-ring, with the trivial `*`-structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.mul_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.distrib_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.Inf_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.comm_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.mk_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.is_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real", "description": " The type `\u211d` of real numbers constructed as equivalence classes of Cauchy sequences of rational\nnumbers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cauchy", "description": " The type `\u211d` of real numbers constructed as equivalence classes of Cauchy sequences of rational\nnumbers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.ind_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.Inf_nonneg", "description": "As `0` is the default value for `real.Inf` of the empty set, it suffices to show that `S` is\nbounded below by `0` to show that `0 \u2264 Inf S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.of_cauchy_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cauchy_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cauchy_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cauchy_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.mk_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.Inf_nonpos", "description": "As `0` is the default value for `real.Inf` of the empty set or sets which are not bounded below, it\nsuffices to show that `S` is bounded above by `0` to show that `Inf S \u2264 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.Sup_le", "description": "As `0` is the default value for `real.Sup` of the empty set or sets which are not bounded above, it\nsuffices to show that all elements of `S` are bounded by a nonnagative number to show that `Sup S`\nis bounded by this number.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.of_cauchy_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.of_cauchy_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {