bove, it\nsuffices to show that `S` is bounded below by `0` to show that `0 \u2264 Sup S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.Sup_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.mk_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cau_seq_converges", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.linear_ordered_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.Inf_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cinfi_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.of_cauchy_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.mk_near_of_forall_near", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.comm_monoid_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_repr", "description": " Show an underlying cauchy sequence for real numbers.\n\nThe representative chosen is the one passed in the VM to `quot.mk`, so two cauchy sequences\nconverging to the same number may be printed differently.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.supr_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.Inf_of_not_bdd_below", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.strict_ordered_comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.strict_ordered_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.zero_lt_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cauchy_rat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.le_mk_of_forall_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.exists_floor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.mk_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.exists_is_lub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.semilattice_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.of_cauchy_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.ext_cauchy_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.ordered_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_rat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.add_left_cancel_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.ordered_add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.ordered_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.semilattice_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.Sup_nonpos", "description": "As `0` is the default value for `real.Sup` of the empty set, it suffices to show that `S` is\nbounded above by `0` to show that `Sup S \u2264 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.equiv_Cauchy", "description": "The real numbers are isomorphic to the quotient of Cauchy sequences on the rationals.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.fact_zero_lt_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.linear_ordered_comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cauchy_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.is_limit_whisker_equiv", "description": "When `F : C \u2964 D` is initial, and `t : cone G` for some `G : D \u2964 E`,\n`t.whisker F` is a limit cone exactly when `t` is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.limit_iso", "description": "When `F : C \u2964 D` is initial, and `G : D \u2964 E` has a limit, then `F \u22d9 G` has a limit also and\n`limit (F \u22d9 G) \u2245 limit G`\n\nhttps://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04E7", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.is_limit_extend_cone_equiv", "description": "When `F` is initial, and `t : cone (F \u22d9 G)`,\n`extend_cone.obj t` is a limit cone exactly when `t` is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.colimit_cocone_comp_is_colimit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.colimit_comp_coyoneda_iso", "description": "If the universal morphism `colimit (F \u22d9 coyoneda.obj (op d)) \u27f6 colimit (coyoneda.obj (op d))`\nis an isomorphism (as it always is when `F` is cofinal),\nthen `colimit (F \u22d9 coyoneda.obj (op d)) \u2245 punit`\n(simply because `colimit (coyoneda.obj (op d)) \u2245 punit`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial_of_is_left_adjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.limit_cone_of_comp_cone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.extend_cocone_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.cocones_equiv_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.induction", "description": "We provide an induction principle for reasoning about `lift` and `hom_to_lift`.\nWe want to perform some construction (usually just a proof) about\nthe particular choices `lift F d` and `hom_to_lift F d`,\nit suffices to perform that construction for some other pair of choices\n(denoted `X\u2080 : C` and `k\u2080 : F.obj X\u2080 \u27f6 d` below),\nand to show how to transport such a construction\n*both* directions along a morphism between such choices.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial_of_final_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.category_theory.costructured_arrow.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.limit_cone_of_comp_is_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.extend_cocone_obj_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.limit_cone_comp_cone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.comp_has_colimit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.colimit_pre_is_iso_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.is_colimit_whisker_equiv", "description": "When `F : C \u2964 D` is cofinal, and `t : cocone G` for some `G : D \u2964 E`,\n`t.whisker F` is a colimit cocone exactly when `t` is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.cones_equiv_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.limit_cone_comp", "description": "Given a limit cone over `G : D \u2964 E` we can construct a limit cone over `F \u22d9 G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.extend_cocone", "description": "Given a cocone over `F \u22d9 G`, we can construct a `cocone G` with the same cocone point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.cones_equiv", "description": "If `F` is initial,\nthe category of cones on `F \u22d9 G` is equivalent to the category of cones on `G`,\nfor any `G : D \u2964 E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial", "description": "A functor `F : C \u2964 D` is initial if for every `d : D`, the comma category of morphisms\n`F.obj c \u27f6 d` is connected.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.out", "description": "A functor `F : C \u2964 D` is initial if for every `d : D`, the comma category of morphisms\n`F.obj c \u27f6 d` is connected.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.colimit_cocone_comp", "description": "Given a colimit cocone over `G : D \u2964 E` we can construct a colimit cocone over `F \u22d9 G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.cocones_equiv", "description": "If `F` is cofinal,\nthe category of cocones on `F \u22d9 G` is equivalent to the category of cocones on `G`,\nfor any `G : D \u2964 E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.category_theory.structured_arrow.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.limit_pre_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.extend_cone_map_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.colimit_cocone_comp_cocone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.extend_cocone_map_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.zigzag_of_eqv_gen_quot_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.extend_cone", "description": "Given a cone over `F \u22d9 G`, we can construct a `cone G` with the same cocone point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.has_limit_of_comp", "description": "When `F` is initial, and `F \u22d9 G` has a limit, then `G` has a limit also.\n\nWe can't make this an instance, because `F` is not determined by the goal.\n(Even if this weren't a problem, it would cause a loop with `comp_has_limit`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.lift", "description": "When `F : C \u2964 D` is cofinal, we denote by `lift F d` an arbitrary choice of object in `C` such that\nthere exists a morphism `d \u27f6 F.obj (lift F d)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.cones_equiv_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final", "description": "A functor `F : C \u2964 D` is final if for every `d : D`, the comma category of morphisms `d \u27f6 F.obj c`\nis connected.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04E6>", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.out", "description": "A functor `F : C \u2964 D` is final if for every `d : D`, the comma category of morphisms `d \u27f6 F.obj c`\nis connected.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04E6>", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.colimit_cocone_of_comp_is_colimit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final_of_is_right_adjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.limit_cone_of_comp", "description": "Given a limit cone over `F \u22d9 G` we can construct a limit cone over `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.is_colimit_extend_cocone_equiv", "description": "When `F` is cofinal, and `t : cocone (F \u22d9 G)`,\n`extend_cocone.obj t` is a colimit coconne exactly when `t` is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.extend_cone_obj_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.colimit_cocone_of_comp_cocone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.limit_iso'", "description": "When `F` is initial, and `F \u22d9 G` has a limit, then `G` has a limit also and\n`limit (F \u22d9 G) \u2245 limit G`\n\nhttps://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04E7", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.colimit_cocone_of_comp", "description": "Given a colimit cocone over `F \u22d9 G` we can construct a colimit cocone over `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final_of_adjunction", "description": "If a functor `R : D \u2964 C` is a right adjoint, it is final.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.colimit_cocone_comp_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.lift", "description": "When `F : C \u2964 D` is initial, we denote by `lift F d` an arbitrary choice of object in `C` such that\nthere exists a morphism `F.obj (lift F d) \u27f6 d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.limit_cone_comp_is_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.cones_equiv_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final_of_initial_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.has_colimit_of_comp", "description": "When `F` is cofinal, and `F \u22d9 G` has a colimit, then `G` has a colimit also.\n\nWe can't make this an instance, because `F` is not determined by the goal.\n(Even if this weren't a problem, it would cause a loop with `comp_has_colimit`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial_of_adjunction", "description": "If a functor `L : C \u2964 D` is a left adjoint, it is initial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.limit_pre_is_iso_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.cocones_equiv_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.hom_to_lift", "description": "When `F : C \u2964 D` is cofinal, we denote by `hom_to_lift` an arbitrary choice of morphism\n`d \u27f6 F.obj (lift F d)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.extend_cone_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial_op_of_final", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.cocones_equiv_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.cones_equiv_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.cofinal_of_colimit_comp_coyoneda_iso_punit", "description": "If `colimit (F \u22d9 coyoneda.obj (op d)) \u2245 punit` for all `d : D`, then `F` is cofinal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.comp_has_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.limit_cone_comp_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final_op_of_initial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.cocones_equiv_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.initial.hom_to_lift", "description": "When `F : C \u2964 D` is initial, we denote by `hom_to_lift` an arbitrary choice of morphism\n`F.obj (lift F d) \u27f6 d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.colimit_pre_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.colimit_iso'", "description": "When `F` is cofinal, and `F \u22d9 G` has a colimit, then `G` has a colimit also and\n`colimit (F \u22d9 G) \u2245 colimit G`\n\nhttps://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04E7", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.colimit_iso", "description": "When `F : C \u2964 D` is cofinal, and `G : D \u2964 E` has a colimit, then `F \u22d9 G` has a colimit also and\n`colimit (F \u22d9 G) \u2245 colimit G`\n\nhttps://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04E7", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.final.induction", "description": "We provide an induction principle for reasoning about `lift` and `hom_to_lift`.\nWe want to perform some construction (usually just a proof) about\nthe particular choices `lift F d` and `hom_to_lift F d`,\nit suffices to perform that construction for some other pair of choices\n(denoted `X\u2080 : C` and `k\u2080 : d \u27f6 F.obj X\u2080` below),\nand to show how to transport such a construction\n*both* directions along a morphism between such choices.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.coe_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.map_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.mul_action_with_zero", "description": "The action by a subsemiring is the action by the underlying semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.centralizer_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.map_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.center_to_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.copy", "description": " Copy of a subsemiring with a new `carrier` equal to the old one. Useful to fix definitional\nequalities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.has_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.closure_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.range_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.closure_induction\u2082", "description": "An induction principle for closure membership for predicates with two arguments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.mem_to_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.nsmul_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.mem_map_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.coe_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.centralizer_to_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.mem_centralizer_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pos_submonoid", "description": "Submonoid of positive elements of an ordered semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.to_strict_ordered_comm_semiring", "description": "A subsemiring of a `strict_ordered_comm_semiring` is a `strict_ordered_comm_semiring`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.subtype", "description": "The natural ring hom from a subsemiring of semiring `R` to `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.to_submonoid_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.top_prod_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.to_submonoid_strict_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.map", "description": "The image of a subsemiring along a ring homomorphism is a subsemiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.closure", "description": "The `subsemiring` generated by a set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.comap_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.copy_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.top_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring_class.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.has_inf", "description": "The inf of two subsemirings is their intersection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.cod_restrict", "description": "Restriction of a ring homomorphism to a subsemiring of the codomain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.mem_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.not_mem_of_not_mem_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.eq_of_eq_on_stop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.comap_equiv_eq_map_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.coe_closure_eq", "description": " The elements of the subsemiring closure of `M` are exactly the elements of the additive closure\nof a multiplicative submonoid `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.mem_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.multiset_prod_mem", "description": "Product of a multiset of elements in a `subsemiring` of a `comm_semiring`\n   is in the `subsemiring`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.to_add_submonoid", "description": "Reinterpret a `subsemiring` as an `add_submonoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.coe_to_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.comap_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.closure_mono", "description": " Subsemiring closure of a set is monotone in its argument: if `s \u2286 t`,\nthen `closure s \u2264 closure t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring_class.subtype", "description": "The natural ring hom from a subsemiring of semiring `R` to `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid_with_one_class", "description": " `add_submonoid_with_one_class S R` says `S` is a type of subsets `s \u2264 R` that contain `0`, `1`,\nand are closed under `(+)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid_with_one_class.to_add_submonoid_class", "description": " `add_submonoid_with_one_class S R` says `S` is a type of subsets `s \u2264 R` that contain `0`, `1`,\nand are closed under `(+)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid_with_one_class.to_one_mem_class", "description": " `add_submonoid_with_one_class S R` says `S` is a type of subsets `s \u2264 R` that contain `0`, `1`,\nand are closed under `(+)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_pos_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring_class.to_semiring", "description": "A subsemiring of a `semiring` is a `semiring`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.subsemiring_closure_to_add_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring_class.to_comm_semiring", "description": "A subsemiring of a `comm_semiring` is a `comm_semiring`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.coe_restrict_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.mem_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.centralizer_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.center_le_centralizer", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.module", "description": "The action by a subsemiring is the action by the underlying semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.coe_copy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.center.smul_comm_class_left", "description": "The center of a semiring acts commutatively on that semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.mul_semiring_action", "description": "The action by a subsemiring is the action by the underlying semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.srange_restrict_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.zero_mem", "description": "A subsemiring contains the semiring's 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.center_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.to_add_submonoid_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.fintype_srange", "description": " The range of a morphism of semirings is a fintype, if the domain is a fintype.\nNote: this instance can form a diamond with `subtype.fintype` in the\n  presence of `fintype S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring_class.coe_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.eq_slocus", "description": "The subsemiring of elements `x : R` such that `f x = g x`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.prod_mem", "description": "Product of elements of a subsemiring of a `comm_semiring` indexed by a `finset` is in the\n   subsemiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.has_top", "description": "The subsemiring `R` of the semiring `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.coe_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.prod", "description": " Given `subsemiring`s `s`, `t` of semirings `R`, `S` respectively, `s.prod t` is `s \u00d7 t`\nas a subsemiring of `R \u00d7 S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.coe_center", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.closure_induction", "description": " An induction principle for closure membership. If `p` holds for `0`, `1`, and all elements\nof `s`, and is preserved under addition and multiplication, then `p` holds for all elements\nof the closure of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid_with_one_class.to_add_monoid_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.coe_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_equiv.subsemiring_map", "description": " Given an equivalence `e : R \u2243+* S` of semirings and a subsemiring `s` of `R`,\n`subsemiring_map e s` is the induced equivalence between `s` and `s.map e`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.restrict_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.to_semiring", "description": "A subsemiring of a `semiring` is a `semiring`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.set_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.comap", "description": "The preimage of a subsemiring along a ring homomorphism is a subsemiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.to_strict_ordered_semiring", "description": "A subsemiring of a `strict_ordered_semiring` is a `strict_ordered_semiring`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_equiv.sof_left_inverse_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.gi", "description": "`closure` forms a Galois insertion with the coercion to set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.prod_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.comap_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.eq_on_sclosure", "description": "If two ring homomorphisms are equal on a set, then they are equal on its subsemiring closure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.mem_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.subsemiring_closure_eq_closure", "description": " The `subsemiring` generated by a multiplicative submonoid coincides with the\n`subsemiring.closure` of the submonoid itself .", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.to_add_submonoid_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.centralizer_eq_top_iff_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.mem_Sup_of_directed_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.prod_top", "description": "", "p