al.smul_Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnreal.summable_sigma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_lt_tsum_of_nonneg", "description": " If a sequence `f` with non-negative terms is dominated by a sequence `g` with summable\nseries and at least one term of `f` is strictly smaller than the corresponding term in `g`,\nthen the series of `f` is strictly smaller than the series of `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.mul_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.tsum_const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.finset_sum_supr_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.exists_frequently_lt_of_liminf_ne_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.tendsto_to_real_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.sub_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.normal_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.has_sum_to_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.topological_space", "description": " Topology on `\u211d\u22650\u221e`.\n\nNote: this is different from the `emetric_space` topology. The `emetric_space` topology has\n`is_open {\u22a4}`, while this topology doesn't have singleton elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_le_tsum_of_edist_le_of_tendsto\u2080", "description": " If `edist (f n) (f (n+1))` is bounded above by a function `d : \u2115 \u2192 \u211d\u22650\u221e`,\nthen the distance from `f 0` to the limit is bounded by `\u2211'_{k=0}^\u221e d k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.eventually_eq_of_to_real_eventually_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.diam_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.tendsto_of_real_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_ne_top_of_mem_ball", "description": "In an emetric ball, the distance between points is everywhere finite", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.tsum_union_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.tendsto_nat_nhds_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.to_nnreal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.coe_tsum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric_space_emetric_ball", "description": " Each ball in an extended metric space gives us a metric space, as the edist\nis everywhere finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.pullback_p1_iso_inv_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.pullback_p1_iso_inv_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.cocycle_snd_fst_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.pullback_p1_iso_inv_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t'_fst_fst_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.pullback_p1_iso_hom_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.gluing_to_glue_data_U", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t'_snd_fst_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.gluing_to_glue_data_V", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t'_fst_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.open_cover_of_left_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.left_affine_comp_pullback_has_pullback", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t'_fst_fst_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.glued_lift_pullback_map_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.open_cover_of_base_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.has_pullback_of_cover", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.open_cover_of_base'", "description": "(Implementation). Use `open_cover_of_base` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.cocycle_fst_fst_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t'_fst_fst_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t_fst_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t'", "description": "The map `((X\u1d62 \u00d7[Z] Y) \u00d7[X] X\u2c7c) \u00d7[X\u1d62 \u00d7[Z] Y] ((X\u1d62 \u00d7[Z] Y) \u00d7[X] X\u2096)` \u27f6\n `((X\u2c7c \u00d7[Z] Y) \u00d7[X] X\u2096) \u00d7[X\u2c7c \u00d7[Z] Y] ((X\u2c7c \u00d7[Z] Y) \u00d7[X] X\u1d62)` needed for gluing", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.pullback_p1_iso", "description": " The canonical isomorphism between `W \u00d7[X] U\u1d62` and `U\u1d62 \u00d7[X] Y`. That is, the preimage of `U\u1d62` in\n`W` along `p1` is indeed `U\u1d62 \u00d7[X] Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t_fst_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.p1", "description": "The first projection from the glued scheme into `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.glued_lift_pullback_map_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.open_cover_of_base_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.open_cover_of_left_right_J", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.category_theory.limits.pullback.algebraic_geometry.is_affine", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.glued_lift", "description": "The lifted map `s.X \u27f6 (gluing \ud835\udcb0 f g).glued` in order to show that `(gluing \ud835\udcb0 f g).glued` is\nindeed the pullback.\n\nGiven a pullback cone `s`, we have the maps `s.fst \u207b\u00b9' U\u1d62 \u27f6 U\u1d62` and\n`s.fst \u207b\u00b9' U\u1d62 \u27f6 s.X \u27f6 Y` that we may lift to a map `s.fst \u207b\u00b9' U\u1d62 \u27f6 U\u1d62 \u00d7[Z] Y`.\n\nto glue these into a map `s.X \u27f6 U\u1d62 \u00d7[Z] Y`, we need to show that the maps agree on\n`(s.fst \u207b\u00b9' U\u1d62) \u00d7[s.X] (s.fst \u207b\u00b9' U\u2c7c) \u27f6 U\u1d62 \u00d7[Z] Y`. This is achieved by showing that both of these\nmaps factors through `glued_lift_pullback_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.affine_affine_has_pullback", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.open_cover_of_base", "description": "Given an open cover `{ Z\u1d62 }` of `Z`, then `X \u00d7[Z] Y` is covered by `X\u1d62 \u00d7[Z\u1d62] Y\u1d62`, where\n `X\u1d62 = X \u00d7[Z] Z\u1d62` and `Y\u1d62 = Y \u00d7[Z] Z\u1d62` is the preimage of `Z\u1d62` in `X` and `Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.gluing", "description": "Given `U\u1d62 \u00d7[Z] Y`, this is the glued fibered product `X \u00d7[Z] Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.open_cover_of_left_right_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.open_cover_of_right_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t'_snd_fst_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.pullback_p1_iso_hom_\u03b9_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.gluing_to_glue_data_t'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.affine_has_pullback", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t'_snd_fst_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.cocycle_fst_fst_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.pullback_fst_\u03b9_to_V", "description": " (Implementation)\nThe canonical map `(W \u00d7[X] U\u1d62) \u00d7[W] (U\u2c7c \u00d7[Z] Y) \u27f6 (U\u2c7c \u00d7[Z] Y) \u00d7[X] U\u1d62 = V j i` where `W` is\nthe glued fibred product.\n\nThis is used in `lift_comp_\u03b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t'_snd_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.p_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t'_snd_fst_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.pullback_p1_iso_hom_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.base_affine_has_pullback", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.pullback_p1_iso_hom_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.p2", "description": "The second projection from the glued scheme into `Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.cocycle_snd_fst_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.open_cover_of_right_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.fV", "description": "The inclusion map of `V i j = (U\u1d62 \u00d7[Z] Y) \u00d7[X] U\u2c7c \u27f6 U\u1d62 \u00d7[Z] Y`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.pullback_p1_iso_inv_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.pullback_fst_\u03b9_to_V_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.gluing_to_glue_data_J", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.cocycle_fst_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.cocycle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.open_cover_of_right_J", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.category_theory.limits.has_pullback", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.open_cover_of_left_J", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t'_fst_fst_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.glued_lift_p1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.pullback_p1_iso_hom_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.pullback_fst_\u03b9_to_V_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.algebraic_geometry.Scheme.category_theory.limits.has_pullbacks", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.open_cover_of_left_right", "description": " Given an open cover `{ X\u1d62 }` of `X` and an open cover `{ Y\u2c7c }` of `Y`, then\n`X \u00d7[Z] Y` is covered by `X\u1d62 \u00d7[Z] Y\u2c7c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t_fst_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.glued_is_limit", "description": "The glued scheme (`(gluing \ud835\udcb0 f g).glued`) is indeed the pullback of `f` and `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.glued_lift_pullback_map", "description": " (Implementation)\nThe canonical map `(s.X \u00d7[X] U\u1d62) \u00d7[s.X] (s.X \u00d7[X] U\u2c7c) \u27f6 (U\u1d62 \u00d7[Z] Y) \u00d7[X] U\u2c7c`\n\nThis is used in `glued_lift`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.open_cover_of_left", "description": "Given an open cover `{ X\u1d62 }` of `X`, then `X \u00d7[Z] Y` is covered by `X\u1d62 \u00d7[Z] Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t", "description": " The canonical transition map `(U\u1d62 \u00d7[Z] Y) \u00d7[X] U\u2c7c \u27f6 (U\u2c7c \u00d7[Z] Y) \u00d7[X] U\u1d62` given by the fact\nthat pullbacks are associative and symmetric.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.open_cover_of_left_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t'_fst_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t'_snd_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.open_cover_of_right", "description": "Given an open cover `{ Y\u1d62 }` of `Y`, then `X \u00d7[Z] Y` is covered by `X \u00d7[Z] Y\u1d62`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.lift_comp_\u03b9", "description": " We show that the map `W \u00d7[X] U\u1d62 \u27f6 U\u1d62 \u00d7[Z] Y \u27f6 W` is the first projection, where the\nfirst map is given by the lift of `W \u00d7[X] U\u1d62 \u27f6 U\u1d62` and `W \u00d7[X] U\u1d62 \u27f6 W \u27f6 Y`.\n\nIt suffices to show that the two map agrees when restricted onto `U\u2c7c \u00d7[Z] Y`. In this case,\nboth maps factor through `V j i` via `pullback_fst_\u03b9_to_V`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.pullback_fst_\u03b9_to_V_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.pullback_fst_\u03b9_to_V_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.gluing_to_glue_data_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.gluing_to_glue_data_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.open_cover_of_left_right_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.cocycle_snd_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.category_theory.limits.pullback.map.is_open_immersion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.t_fst_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.glued_lift_p2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.V", "description": "The intersection of `U\u1d62 \u00d7[Z] Y` and `U\u2c7c \u00d7[Z] Y` is given by (U\u1d62 \u00d7[Z] Y) \u00d7[X] U\u2c7c", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.pullback_p1_iso_hom_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.glued_lift_pullback_map_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.glued_lift_pullback_map_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.pullback.open_cover_of_base_J", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cau_seq.completion.mk_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cau_seq.completion.of_rat_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cau_seq.completion.Cauchy.has_rat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cau_seq.completion.inv_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cau_seq.completion.of_rat_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cau_seq.lim_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cau_seq.lim_eq_lim_of_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cau_seq.completion.Cauchy.has_repr", "description": " Show the first 10 items of a representative of this equivalence class of cauchy sequences.\n\nThe representative chosen is the one passed in the VM to `quot.mk`, so two cauchy sequences\nconverging to t