e morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.refl", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.symm", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.trans", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.comp", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.tensor", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.comp_id", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.id_comp", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.assoc", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.tensor_id", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.tensor_comp", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.\u03b1_hom_inv", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.\u03b1_inv_hom", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.associator_naturality", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.\u03c1_hom_inv", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.\u03c1_inv_hom", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.\u03c1_naturality", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.l_hom_inv", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.l_inv_hom", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.l_naturality", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.pentagon", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom_equiv.triangle", "description": "The morphisms of the free monoidal category satisfy 21 relations ensuring that the resulting\n   category is in fact a category and that it is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category", "description": "Given a type `C`, the free monoidal category over `C` has as objects formal expressions built from\n(formal) tensor products of terms of `C` and a formal unit. Its morphisms are compositions and\ntensor products of identities, unitors and associators.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.of", "description": "Given a type `C`, the free monoidal category over `C` has as objects formal expressions built from\n(formal) tensor products of terms of `C` and a formal unit. Its morphisms are compositions and\ntensor products of identities, unitors and associators.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.unit", "description": "Given a type `C`, the free monoidal category over `C` has as objects formal expressions built from\n(formal) tensor products of terms of `C` and a formal unit. Its morphisms are compositions and\ntensor products of identities, unitors and associators.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.tensor", "description": "Given a type `C`, the free monoidal category over `C` has as objects formal expressions built from\n(formal) tensor products of terms of `C` and a formal unit. Its morphisms are compositions and\ntensor products of identities, unitors and associators.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.setoid_hom", "description": "We say that two formal morphisms in the free monoidal category are equivalent if they become\n   equal if we apply the relations that are true in a monoidal category. Note that we will prove\n   that there is only one equivalence class -- this is the monoidal coherence theorem.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.category_free_monoidal_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.project_map_aux", "description": "Auxiliary definition for `free_monoidal_category.project`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.project_obj", "description": "Auxiliary definition for `free_monoidal_category.project`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.mk_\u03b1_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.mk_\u03c1_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.mk_l_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.mk_\u03b1_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.mk_\u03c1_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.project_map", "description": "Auxiliary definition for `free_monoidal_category.project`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.project", "description": "If `D` is a monoidal category and we have a function `C \u2192 D`, then we have a functor from the\n   free monoidal category over `C` to the category `D`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom", "description": "Formal compositions and tensor products of identities, unitors and associators. The morphisms\n   of the free monoidal category are obtained as a quotient of these formal morphisms by the\n   relations defining a monoidal category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom.id", "description": "Formal compositions and tensor products of identities, unitors and associators. The morphisms\n   of the free monoidal category are obtained as a quotient of these formal morphisms by the\n   relations defining a monoidal category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom.\u03b1_hom", "description": "Formal compositions and tensor products of identities, unitors and associators. The morphisms\n   of the free monoidal category are obtained as a quotient of these formal morphisms by the\n   relations defining a monoidal category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom.\u03b1_inv", "description": "Formal compositions and tensor products of identities, unitors and associators. The morphisms\n   of the free monoidal category are obtained as a quotient of these formal morphisms by the\n   relations defining a monoidal category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom.l_hom", "description": "Formal compositions and tensor products of identities, unitors and associators. The morphisms\n   of the free monoidal category are obtained as a quotient of these formal morphisms by the\n   relations defining a monoidal category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom.l_inv", "description": "Formal compositions and tensor products of identities, unitors and associators. The morphisms\n   of the free monoidal category are obtained as a quotient of these formal morphisms by the\n   relations defining a monoidal category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom.\u03c1_hom", "description": "Formal compositions and tensor products of identities, unitors and associators. The morphisms\n   of the free monoidal category are obtained as a quotient of these formal morphisms by the\n   relations defining a monoidal category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom.\u03c1_inv", "description": "Formal compositions and tensor products of identities, unitors and associators. The morphisms\n   of the free monoidal category are obtained as a quotient of these formal morphisms by the\n   relations defining a monoidal category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom.comp", "description": "Formal compositions and tensor products of identities, unitors and associators. The morphisms\n   of the free monoidal category are obtained as a quotient of these formal morphisms by the\n   relations defining a monoidal category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.hom.tensor", "description": "Formal compositions and tensor products of identities, unitors and associators. The morphisms\n   of the free monoidal category are obtained as a quotient of these formal morphisms by the\n   relations defining a monoidal category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.of_restrict", "description": "The canonical map from the restriction to the supspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.to_RingedSpace", "description": "An alias for `to_SheafedSpace`, where the result type is a `RingedSpace`.\nThis allows us to use dot-notation for the `RingedSpace` namespace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.comp_val_c_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.comp_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.restrict", "description": "The restriction of a locally ringed space along an open embedding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.forget_to_SheafedSpace.category_theory.faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.comp_val_c", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.is_SheafedSpace_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.to_Top", "description": "The underlying topological space of a locally ringed space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.restrict_to_SheafedSpace", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.\u0393", "description": "The global sections, notated Gamma.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.component_nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.forget_to_SheafedSpace_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace", "description": " A `LocallyRingedSpace` is a topological space equipped with a sheaf of commutative rings\nsuch that all the stalks are local rings.\n\nA morphism of locally ringed spaces is a morphism of ringed spaces\nsuch that the morphisms induced on stalks are local ring homomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.to_SheafedSpace", "description": " A `LocallyRingedSpace` is a topological space equipped with a sheaf of commutative rings\nsuch that all the stalks are local rings.\n\nA morphism of locally ringed spaces is a morphism of ringed spaces\nsuch that the morphisms induced on stalks are local ring homomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.local_ring", "description": " A `LocallyRingedSpace` is a topological space equipped with a sheaf of commutative rings\nsuch that all the stalks are local rings.\n\nA morphism of locally ringed spaces is a morphism of ringed spaces\nsuch that the morphisms induced on stalks are local ring homomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.\u0393_obj_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.forget_to_SheafedSpace_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.id", "description": "The identity morphism on a locally ringed space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.\ud835\udcaa", "description": "The structure sheaf of a locally ringed space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.forget_to_Top_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.\u0393_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.stalk", "description": "The stalk of a locally ringed space, just as a `CommRing`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.category_theory.category", "description": "The category of locally ringed spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.forget_to_Top", "description": "The forgetful functor from `LocallyRingedSpace` to `Top`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.preimage_basic_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.hom_of_SheafedSpace_hom_of_is_iso", "description": "Given two locally ringed spaces `X` and `Y`, an isomorphism between `X` and `Y` as _sheafed_\nspaces can be lifted to a morphism `X \u27f6 Y` as locally ringed spaces.\n\nSee also `iso_of_SheafedSpace_iso`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.stalk_map.is_local_ring_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.forget_to_SheafedSpace", "description": "The forgetful functor from `LocallyRingedSpace` to `SheafedSpace CommRing`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.\u0393_map_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.hom", "description": "A morphism of locally ringed spaces is a morphism of ringed spaces\nsuch that the morphims induced on stalks are local ring homomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.hom.val", "description": "A morphism of locally ringed spaces is a morphism of ringed spaces\nsuch that the morphims induced on stalks are local ring homomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.hom.prop", "description": "A morphism of locally ringed spaces is a morphism of ringed spaces\nsuch that the morphims induced on stalks are local ring homomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.forget_to_Top_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.stalk_map", "description": "A morphism of locally ringed spaces `f : X \u27f6 Y` induces\na local ring homomorphism from `Y.stalk (f x)` to `X.stalk x` for any `x : X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.comp", "description": "Composition of morphisms of locally ringed spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.\u0393_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.iso_of_SheafedSpace_iso", "description": "Given two locally ringed spaces `X` and `Y`, an isomorphism between `X` and `Y` as _sheafed_\nspaces can be lifted to an isomorphism `X \u27f6 Y` as locally ringed spaces.\n\nThis is related to the property that the functor `forget_to_SheafedSpace` reflects isomorphisms.\nIn fact, it is slightly stronger as we do not require `f` to come from a morphism between\n_locally_ ringed spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.has_coe_to_sort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.basic_open_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.quiver", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.hom.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.hom_of_SheafedSpace_hom_of_is_iso_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.id_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.algebraic_geometry.PresheafedSpace.stalk_map.is_local_ring_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.\u0393_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.restrict_top_iso", "description": "The restriction of a locally ringed space `X` to the top subspace is isomorphic to `X` itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.forget_to_SheafedSpace.category_theory.refle