 "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.zero_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.comap_injective_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.map_sup_comap_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.sum_map_comap_sum'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.mker_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.mrange_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.map_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.inclusion", "description": "The `add_monoid` hom associated to an inclusion of submonoids.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.submonoid_comap", "description": "The `monoid_hom` from the preimage of a submonoid to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.add_submonoid_map", "description": "An `add_equiv` `\u03c6` between two additive monoids `M` and `N` induces an `add_equiv`\nbetween a submonoid `S \u2264 M` and the submonoid `\u03c6(S) \u2264 N`. See `add_monoid_hom.add_submonoid_map`\nfor a variant for `add_monoid_hom`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.sum_eq_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.comap_map_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.mem_mker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.mrange_inl'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.prod", "description": "Given `add_submonoid`s `s`, `t` of `add_monoid`s `A`, `B` respectively, `s \u00d7 t`\nas an `add_submonoid` of `A \u00d7 B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.comap_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.mker_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_mem_class.coe_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid_class.to_linear_ordered_cancel_add_comm_monoid", "description": "An `add_submonoid` of a `linear_ordered_cancel_add_comm_monoid` is\na `linear_ordered_cancel_add_comm_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.mrange_inl_sup_mrange_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.smul_comm_class_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid_class.to_ordered_cancel_comm_monoid", "description": "A submonoid of an `ordered_cancel_comm_monoid` is an `ordered_cancel_comm_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.add_submonoid_comap_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.top_equiv", "description": "The top additive submonoid is isomorphic to the additive monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.equiv_map_of_injective_coe_mul_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.bot_or_nontrivial", "description": "An additive submonoid is either the trivial additive submonoid or nontrivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.mrange_inr'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.submonoid_map", "description": " A `mul_equiv` `\u03c6` between two monoids `M` and `N` induces a `mul_equiv` between\na submonoid `S \u2264 M` and the submonoid `\u03c6(S) \u2264 N`.\nSee `monoid_hom.submonoid_map` for a variant for `monoid_hom`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.coe_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.prod_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.mem_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.coe_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.top_prod_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.comap_injective_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid_class.coe_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.coe_mker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.map_comap_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.refl'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.decidable_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient.eq_rel", "description": "A version of `quotient.eq'` compatible with `setoid.rel`, to make rewriting possible.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.injective_iff_ker_bot", "description": "A function from \u03b1 to \u03b2 is injective iff its kernel is the bottom element of the complete lattice\n   of equivalence relations on \u03b1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.Sup_def", "description": "The supremum of a set of equivalence relations is the equivalence closure of the\n   supremum of the set's image under the map to the underlying binary operation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.eqv_gen_mono", "description": "Equivalence closure of binary relations is monotone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.map_of_surjective", "description": "Given a surjective function f whose kernel is contained in an equivalence relation r, the\n   equivalence relation on f's codomain defined by x \u2248 y \u2194 the elements of f\u207b\u00b9(x) are related to\n   the elements of f\u207b\u00b9(y) by r.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.comm'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.ker_iff_mem_preimage", "description": "The elements related to x \u2208 \u03b1 by the kernel of f are those in the preimage of f(x) under f.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.symm'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.Inf_def", "description": "The underlying binary operation of the infimum of a set of equivalence relations\n   is the infimum of the set's image under the map to the underlying binary operation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.ker_lift_injective", "description": "Given a map f from \u03b1 to \u03b2, the natural map from the quotient of \u03b1 by the kernel of f is\n   injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.eq_top_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.Sup_eq_eqv_gen", "description": "The supremum of a set S of equivalence relations is the equivalence closure of the binary\n   relation `there exists r \u2208 S relating x and y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.le_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.lift_equiv", "description": " Equivalence between functions `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` such that `r x y \u2192 f x = f y` and functions\n`quotient r \u2192 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.ker_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.ker_mk_eq", "description": "The kernel of the quotient map induced by an equivalence relation r equals r.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.inf_def", "description": "The infimum of 2 equivalence relations r and s is the same relation as the infimum\n   of the underlying binary operations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.inf_iff_and", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.rel", "description": "A version of `setoid.r` that takes the equivalence relation as an explicit argument.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.quotient_ker_equiv_of_surjective", "description": " The quotient of \u03b1 by the kernel of a surjective function f bijects with f's codomain.\n\nIf a specific right-inverse of `f` is known, `setoid.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse` can be\ndefinitionally more useful.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.has_inf", "description": "The infimum of two equivalence relations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.sup_def", "description": "The supremum of 2 equivalence relations r and s is the equivalence closure of the\n   supremum of the underlying binary operations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.ker_apply_mk_out'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.complete_lattice", "description": "The complete lattice of equivalence relations on a type, with bottom element `=`\n   and top element the trivial equivalence relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.ker", "description": "The kernel of a function is an equivalence relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.correspondence", "description": " Given an equivalence relation `r` on `\u03b1`, the order-preserving bijection between the set of\nequivalence relations containing `r` and the equivalence relations on the quotient of `\u03b1` by `r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.prod", "description": "Given types `\u03b1`, `\u03b2`, the product of two equivalence relations `r` on `\u03b1` and `s` on `\u03b2`:\n   `(x\u2081, x\u2082), (y\u2081, y\u2082) \u2208 \u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2` are related by `r.prod s` iff `x\u2081` is related to `y\u2081`\n   by `r` and `x\u2082` is related to `y\u2082` by `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.comap_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient.subsingleton_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.map_of_surjective_eq_map", "description": "A special case of the equivalence closure of an equivalence relation r equalling r.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.ext'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.comap_eq", "description": "Given a map `f : N \u2192 M` and an equivalence relation `r` on `\u03b2`, the equivalence relation\n   induced on `\u03b1` by `f` equals the kernel of `r`'s quotient map composed with `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.bot_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.eqv_gen_idem", "description": "Equivalence closure is idempotent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.gi", "description": "There is a Galois insertion of equivalence relations on \u03b1 into binary relations\n   on \u03b1, with equivalence closure the lower adjoint.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.comap", "description": " Given a function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2`, an equivalence relation `r` on `\u03b2` induces an equivalence\nrelation on `\u03b1` defined by '`x \u2248 y` iff `f(x)` is related to `f(y)` by `r`'.\n\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.eqv_gen_le", "description": "The equivalence closure of a binary relation r is contained in any equivalence\n   relation containing r.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.comap_quotient_equiv", "description": "The second isomorphism theorem for sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quot.subsingleton_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.sup_eq_eqv_gen", "description": "The supremum of two equivalence relations r and s is the equivalence closure of the binary\n   relation `x is related to y by r or s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.quotient_ker_equiv_range", "description": "The first isomorphism theorem for sets: the quotient of \u03b1 by the kernel of a function f\n   bijects with f's image.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.quotient_quotient_equiv_quotient", "description": "The third isomorphism theorem for sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.eqv_gen_of_setoid", "description": "The equivalence closure of an equivalence relation r is r.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse", "description": " If `f` has a computable right-inverse, then the quotient by its kernel is equivalent to its\ndomain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.has_le", "description": "Defining `\u2264` for equivalence relations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.has_Inf", "description": "The infimum of a set of equivalence relations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.map", "description": "Given a function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` and equivalence relation `r` on `\u03b1`, the equivalence\n   closure of the relation on `f`'s image defined by '`x \u2248 y` iff the elements of `f\u207b\u00b9(x)` are\n   related to the elements of `f\u207b\u00b9(y)` by `r`.'", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.ker_eq_lift_of_injective", "description": "Given a map f from \u03b1 to \u03b2, the kernel of f is the unique equivalence relation on \u03b1 whose\n   induced map from the quotient of \u03b1 to \u03b2 is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.top_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.eqv_gen_eq", "description": "The inductively defined equivalence closure of a binary relation r is the infimum\n   of the set of all equivalence relations containing r.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.lift_unique", "description": "The uniqueness part of the universal property for quotients of an arbitrary type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.trans'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.ker_apply_mk_out", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.eq_iff_rel_eq", "description": "Two equivalence relations are equal iff their underlying binary operations are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.whisker_left_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.pentagon_hom_hom_inv_inv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.whisker_right_comp_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.pentagon_inv_inv_hom_hom_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.whisker_right_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.associator_naturality_left_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.triangle_assoc_comp_left_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.pentagon_hom_inv_inv_inv_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.whisker_right_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.pentagon_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.whisker_assoc_symm", "description": "", "p": "