ry_theory.bicategory.right_unitor_naturality_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.pentagon_inv_inv_hom_inv_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.id_whisker_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.triangle_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.pentagon_hom_hom_inv_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.whisker_left_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.whisker_left_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.associator_naturality_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.triangle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.whisker_left_iso", "description": "The left whiskering of a 2-isomorphism is a 2-isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.right_unitor_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.triangle_assoc_comp_right_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.inv_whisker_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.right_unitor_inv_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.pentagon_hom_inv_inv_inv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.associator_naturality_middle_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.hom_inv_whisker_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.whisker_left_right_unitor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.pentagon_hom_inv_inv_inv_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.associator_inv_naturality_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.associator_inv_naturality_middle_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.triangle_assoc_comp_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.left_unitor_whisker_right", "description": "We state it as a simp lemma, which is regarded as an involved version of\n`id_whisker_right f g : \ud835\udfd9 f \u25b7 g = \ud835\udfd9 (f \u226b g)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.left_unitor_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.pentagon_hom_hom_inv_inv_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.pentagon_inv_inv_hom_inv_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.comp_whisker_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.left_unitor_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.id_whisker_left_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.inv_hom_whisker_right_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.pentagon_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.hom_inv_whisker_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.whisker_assoc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.hom_inv_whisker_right_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory", "description": "In a bicategory, we can compose the 1-morphisms `f : a \u27f6 b` and `g : b \u27f6 c` to obtain\na 1-morphism `f \u226b g : a \u27f6 c`. This composition does not need to be strictly associative,\nbut there is a specified associator, `\u03b1_ f g h : (f \u226b g) \u226b h \u2245 f \u226b (g \u226b h)`.\nThere is an identity 1-morphism `\ud835\udfd9 a : a \u27f6 a`, with specified left and right unitor\nisomorphisms `\u03bb_ f : \ud835\udfd9 a \u226b f \u2245 f` and `\u03c1_ f : f \u226b \ud835\udfd9 a \u2245 f`.\nThese associators and unitors satisfy the pentagon and triangle equations.\n\nSee https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/bicategory.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.to_category_struct", "description": "In a bicategory, we can compose the 1-morphisms `f : a \u27f6 b` and `g : b \u27f6 c` to obtain\na 1-morphism `f \u226b g : a \u27f6 c`. This composition does not need to be strictly associative,\nbut there is a specified associator, `\u03b1_ f g h : (f \u226b g) \u226b h \u2245 f \u226b (g \u226b h)`.\nThere is an identity 1-morphism `\ud835\udfd9 a : a \u27f6 a`, with specified left and right unitor\nisomorphisms `\u03bb_ f : \ud835\udfd9 a \u226b f \u2245 f` and `\u03c1_ f : f \u226b \ud835\udfd9 a \u2245 f`.\nThese associators and unitors satisfy the pentagon and triangle equations.\n\nSee https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/bicategory.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.hom_category", "description": "In a bicategory, we can compose the 1-morphisms `f : a \u27f6 b` and `g : b \u27f6 c` to obtain\na 1-morphism `f \u226b g : a \u27f6 c`. This composition does not need to be strictly associative,\nbut there is a specified associator, `\u03b1_ f g h : (f \u226b g) \u226b h \u2245 f \u226b (g \u226b h)`.\nThere is an identity 1-morphism `\ud835\udfd9 a : a \u27f6 a`, with specified left and right unitor\nisomorphisms `\u03bb_ f : \ud835\udfd9 a \u226b f \u2245 f` and `\u03c1_ f : f \u226b \ud835\udfd9 a \u2245 f`.\nThese associators and unitors satisfy the pentagon and triangle equations.\n\nSee https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/bicategory.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.whisker_left", "description": "In a bicategory, we can compose the 1-morphisms `f : a \u27f6 b` and `g : b \u27f6 c` to obtain\na 1-morphism `f \u226b g : a \u27f6 c`. This composition does not need to