egory.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.whisker_exchange'", "description": "In a bicategory, we can compose the 1-morphisms `f : a \u27f6 b` and `g : b \u27f6 c` to obtain\na 1-morphism `f \u226b g : a \u27f6 c`. This composition does not need to be strictly associative,\nbut there is a specified associator, `\u03b1_ f g h : (f \u226b g) \u226b h \u2245 f \u226b (g \u226b h)`.\nThere is an identity 1-morphism `\ud835\udfd9 a : a \u27f6 a`, with specified left and right unitor\nisomorphisms `\u03bb_ f : \ud835\udfd9 a \u226b f \u2245 f` and `\u03c1_ f : f \u226b \ud835\udfd9 a \u2245 f`.\nThese associators and unitors satisfy the pentagon and triangle equations.\n\nSee https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/bicategory.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.pentagon'", "description": "In a bicategory, we can compose the 1-morphisms `f : a \u27f6 b` and `g : b \u27f6 c` to obtain\na 1-morphism `f \u226b g : a \u27f6 c`. This composition does not need to be strictly associative,\nbut there is a specified associator, `\u03b1_ f g h : (f \u226b g) \u226b h \u2245 f \u226b (g \u226b h)`.\nThere is an identity 1-morphism `\ud835\udfd9 a : a \u27f6 a`, with specified left and right unitor\nisomorphisms `\u03bb_ f : \ud835\udfd9 a \u226b f \u2245 f` and `\u03c1_ f : f \u226b \ud835\udfd9 a \u2245 f`.\nThese associators and unitors satisfy the pentagon and triangle equations.\n\nSee https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/bicategory.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.triangle'", "description": "In a bicategory, we can compose the 1-morphisms `f : a \u27f6 b` and `g : b \u27f6 c` to obtain\na 1-morphism `f \u226b g : a \u27f6 c`. This composition does not need to be strictly associative,\nbut there is a specified associator, `\u03b1_ f g h : (f \u226b g) \u226b h \u2245 f \u226b (g \u226b h)`.\nThere is an identity 1-morphism `\ud835\udfd9 a : a \u27f6 a`, with specified left and right unitor\nisomorphisms `\u03bb_ f : \ud835\udfd9 a \u226b f \u2245 f` and `\u03c1_ f : f \u226b \ud835\udfd9 a \u2245 f`.\nThese associators and unitors satisfy the pentagon and triangle equations.\n\nSee https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/bicategory.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.whisker_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.whisker_left_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.right_unitor_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.pentagon_inv_hom_hom_hom_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.left_unitor_comp_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.inv_whisker_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.triangle_assoc_comp_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.pentagon_hom_inv_inv_inv_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.whisker_right_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.triangle_assoc_comp_right_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.pentagon_inv_hom_hom_hom_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.whisker_exchange", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.associator_naturality_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.associator_inv_naturality_left_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.pentagon_hom_hom_inv_hom_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.left_unitor_inv_naturality_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.unitors_equal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.left_unitor_comp_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.triangle_assoc_comp_right_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.associator_naturality_right_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.left_unitor_inv_whisker_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.inv_hom_whisker_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.right_unitor_comp_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.pentagon_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.associator_inv_naturality_middle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.right_unitor_inv_naturality_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.comp_whisker_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.pentagon_inv_inv_hom_hom_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicategory.left_unitor_inv_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_card_inter_le", "description": " If every element belongs to at most `n` finsets, then the sum of their sizes is at most `n`\ntimes how many they are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_nonneg'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.one_le_prod''", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_le_univ_sum_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_eq_one_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_le_prod_of_subset_of_one_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_top.sum_lt_top_iff", "description": "A sum of finite numbers is still finite", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_mono_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_le_sum", "description": " In an ordered additive commutative monoid, if each summand `f i` of one finite sum is less than\nor equal to the corresponding summand `g i` of another finite sum, then\n`\u2211 i in s, f i \u2264 \u2211 i in s, g i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_le_sum_of_subset_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "absolute_value.map_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_le_prod", "description": " If all `f i`, `i \u2208 s`, are nonnegative and each `f i` is less than or equal to `g i`, then the\nproduct of `f i` is less than or equal to the product of `g i`. See also `finset.prod_le_prod'` for\nthe case of an ordered commutative multiplicative monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_add_prod_le", "description": "If `g, h \u2264 f` and `g i + h i \u2264 f i`, then the product of `f` over `s` is at least the\n sum of the products of `g` and `h`. This is the version for `ordered_comm_semiring`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_le_card_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_eq_sum_iff_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_sum_card_inter", "description": " If every element belongs to at least `n` finsets, then the sum of their sizes is at least `n`\ntimes how many they are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_prod_of_submultiplicative", "description": " If `f : M \u2192 N` is a submultiplicative function, `f (x * y) \u2264 f x * f y`, `f 1 = 1`, and `g i`,\n`i \u2208 s`, is a finite family of elements of `M`, then `f (\u220f i in s, g i) \u2264 \u220f i in s, f (g i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_le_prod'", "description": " In an ordered commutative monoid, if each factor `f i` of one finite product is less than or\nequal to the corresponding factor `g i` of another finite product, then\n`\u220f i in s, f i \u2264 \u220f i in s, g i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.abs_sum_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_fiberwise_le_sum_of_sum_fiber_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_mono'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.single_lt_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_absolute_value.abv_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_pos'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.exists_le_of_prod_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_le_card_bUnion_add_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_le_prod_of_ne_one'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_top.sum_eq_top_iff", "description": "A sum of numbers is infinite iff one of them is infinite", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_sum_of_subadditive", "description": " If `f : M \u2192 N` is a subadditive function, `f (x + y) \u2264 f x + f y`, `f 0 = 0`, and `g i`,\n`i \u2208 s`, is a finite family of elements of `M`, then `f (\u2211 i in s, g i) \u2264 \u2211 i in s, f (g i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_le_one", "description": " If each `f i`, `i \u2208 s` belongs to `[0, 1]`, then their product is less than or equal to one.\nSee also `finset.prod_le_one'` for the case of an ordered commutative multiplicative monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_card_le", "description": " If every element belongs to at most `n` finsets, then the sum of their sizes is at most `n`\ntimes how many they are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_le_prod_fiberwise_of_prod_fiber_le_one'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_absolute_value.map_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.exists_lt_of_sum_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_sum_nonempty_of_subadditive_on_pred", "description": " Let `{x | p x}` be an additive subsemigroup of an additive commutative monoid `M`. Let\n`f : M \u2192 N` be a map subadditive on `{x | p x}`, i.e., `p x \u2192 p y \u2192 f (x + y) \u2264 f x + f y`. Let\n`g i`, `i \u2208 s`, be a nonempty finite family of elements of `M` such that `\u2200 i \u2208 s, p (g i)`. Then\n`f (\u2211 i in s, g i) \u2264 \u2211 i in s, f (g i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_bUnion_le_card_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_prod_nonempty_of_submultiplicative", "description": " If `f : M \u2192 N` is a submultiplicative function, `f (x * y) \u2264 f x * f y` and `g i`, `i \u2208 s`, is a\nnonempty finite family of elements of `M`, then `f (\u220f i in s, g i) \u2264 \u220f i in s, f (g i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_le_sum_of_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_sum_nonempty_of_subadditive", "description": " If `f : M \u2192 N` is a subadditive function, `f (x + y) \u2264 f x + f y` and `g i`, `i \u2208 s`, is a\nnonempty finite family of elements of `M`, then `f (\u2211 i in s, g i) \u2264 \u2211 i in s, f (g i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.abs_sum_le_sum_abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.single_lt_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_nonpos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.abs_sum_of_nonneg'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_lt_prod_of_subset'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "absolute_value.sum_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_le_prod_of_subset'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_le_card_bUnion_add_card_fiber", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_le_card_bUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_mono_set_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_eq_zero_iff_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_eq_prod_iff_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_lt_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_lt_prod_of_nonempty'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.exists_pos_of_sum_zero_of_exists_nonzero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.exists_le_of_sum_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_le_mul_card_image_of_maps_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_lt_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mul_card_image_le_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.exists_one_lt_of_prod_one_of_exists_ne_one'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_sum_of_subadditive_on_pred", "description": " Let `{x | p x}` be a subsemigroup of a commutative additive monoid `M`. Let `f : M \u2192 N` be a map\nsuch that `f 0 = 0` and `f` is subadditive on `{x | p x}`, i.e. `p x \u2192 p y \u2192 f (x + y) \u2264 f x + f y`.\nLet `g i`, `i \u2208 s`, be a finite family of elements of `M` such that `\u2200 i \u2208 s, p (g i)`. Then\n`f (\u2211 x in s, g x) \u2264 \u2211 x in s, f (g x)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_le_sum_of_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.one_lt_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_mono_set_of_one_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.abs_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.single_le_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_le_one'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_le_mul_card_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_eq_one_iff_of_one_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.one_lt_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_strict_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_prod_of_submultiplicative_on_pred", "description": " Let `{x | p x}` be a subsemigroup of a commutative monoid `M`. Let `f : M \u2192 N` be a map\nsuch that `f 1 = 1` and `f` is submultiplicative on `{x | p x}`, i.e.,\n`p x \u2192 p y \u2192 f (x * y) \u2264 f x * f y`. Let `g i`, `i \u2208 s`, be a finite family of elements of `M` such\nthat `\u2200 i \u2208 s, p (g i)`. Then `f (\u220f i in s, g i) \u2264 \u220f i in s, f (g i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.prod_pos", "description": "Note that the name is to match `canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.mul_pos`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_le_pow_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_top.sum_lt_top", "description": "A sum of finite numbers is still finite", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_le_sum_fiberwise_of_sum_fiber_nonpos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_fiberwise_le_prod_of_one_le_prod_fiber'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_card_inter", "description": " If every element belongs to exactly `n` finsets, then the sum of their sizes is `n` times how\nmany they are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_lt_sum_of_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_neg'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.exists_lt_of_prod_lt'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.multiset_prod_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.pow_card_le_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_mono_set'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_lt_one'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_top.prod_lt_top", "description": "A product of finite numbers is still finite", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_lt_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_eq_one_iff_of_le_one'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_prod_nonempty_of_submultiplicative_on_pred", "description": " Let `{x | p x}` be a subsemigroup of a commutative monoid `M`. Let `f : M \u2192 N` be a map\nsubmultiplicative on `{x | p x}`, i.e., `p x \u2192 p y \u2192 f (x * y) \u2264 f x * f y`. Let `g i`, `i \u2208 s`, be\na nonempty finite family of elements of `M` such that `\u2200 i \u2208 s, p (g i)`. Then\n`f (\u220f x in s, g x) \u2264 \u220f x in s, f (g x)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.one_le_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_lt_sum_of_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_le_univ_prod_of_one_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.single_le_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mul_card_image_le_card_of_maps_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_sum_card", "description": " If every element belongs to at least `n` finsets, then the sum of their sizes is at least `n`\ntimes how many they are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_nsmul_le_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_card", "description": " If every element belongs to exactly `n` finsets, then the sum of their sizes is `n` times how\nmany they are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_strict_mono'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_add_prod_le'", "description": "If `g, h \u2264 f` and `g i + h i \u2264 f i`, then the product of `f` over `s` is at least the\n sum of the products of `g` and `h`. This is the version for `canonically_ordered_comm_semiring`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.moebius_apply_prime_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.is_multiplicative.map_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.id", "description": "The identity on `\u2115` as an `arithmetic_function`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.card_factors_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.is_multiplicative_moebius", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.pmul_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.is_multiplicative_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.int_coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.sum_eq_iff_sum_mul_moebius_eq", "description": "M\u00f6bius inversion for functions to a `ring`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.is_multiplicative", "description": "Multiplicative functions", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.moebius_ne_zero_iff_eq_or", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.moebius_mul_coe_zeta", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.sigma", "description": "`\u03c3 k n` is the sum of the `k`th powers of the divisors of `n`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.card_factors_apply_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.is_multiplicative.iff_ne_zero", "description": "A recapitulation of the definition of multiplicative that is simpler for proofs", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.pow_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.is_multiplicative.multiplicative_factorization", "description": " For any multiplicative function `f` and any `n > 0`,\nwe can evaluate `f n` by evaluating `f` at `p ^ k` over the factorization of `n`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.ppow_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.card_factors_apply", 