"description": " A distributive lattice is a lattice that satisfies any of four\nequivalent distributive properties (of `sup` over `inf` or `inf` over `sup`,\non the left or right).\n\nThe definition here chooses `le_sup_inf`: `(x \u2294 y) \u2293 (x \u2294 z) \u2264 x \u2294 (y \u2293 z)`. To prove distributivity\nfrom the dual law, use `distrib_lattice.of_inf_sup_le`.\n\nA classic example of a distributive lattice\nis the lattice of subsets of a set, and in fact this example is\ngeneric in the sense that every distributive lattice is realizable\nas a sublattice of a powerset lattice.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "distrib_lattice.le_inf", "description": " A distributive lattice is a lattice that satisfies any of four\nequivalent distributive properties (of `sup` over `inf` or `inf` over `sup`,\non the left or right).\n\nThe definition here chooses `le_sup_inf`: `(x \u2294 y) \u2293 (x \u2294 z) \u2264 x \u2294 (y \u2293 z)`. To prove distributivity\nfrom the dual law, use `distrib_lattice.of_inf_sup_le`.\n\nA classic example of a distributive lattice\nis the lattice of subsets of a set, and in fact this example is\ngeneric in the sense that every distributive lattice is realizable\nas a sublattice of a powerset lattice.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "distrib_lattice.le_sup_inf", "description": " A distributive lattice is a lattice that satisfies any of four\nequivalent distributive properties (of `sup` over `inf` or `inf` over `sup`,\non the left or right).\n\nThe definition here chooses `le_sup_inf`: `(x \u2294 y) \u2293 (x \u2294 z) \u2264 x \u2294 (y \u2293 z)`. To prove distributivity\nfrom the dual law, use `distrib_lattice.of_inf_sup_le`.\n\nA classic example of a distributive lattice\nis the lattice of subsets of a set, and in fact this example is\ngeneric in the sense that every distributive lattice is realizable\nas a sublattice of a powerset lattice.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sup_eq_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilattice_inf.mk'", "description": "A type with a commutative, associative and idempotent binary `inf` operation has the structure of a\nmeet-semilattice.\n\nThe partial order is defined so that `a \u2264 b` unfolds to `b \u2293 a = a`; cf. `inf_eq_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lattice.mk'", "description": "A type with a pair of commutative and associative binary operations which satisfy two absorption\nlaws relating the two operations has the structure of a lattice.\n\nThe partial order is defined so that `a \u2264 b` unfolds to `a \u2294 b = b`; cf. `sup_eq_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.distrib_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilattice_sup_mk'_partial_order_eq_semilattice_inf_mk'_partial_order", "description": " The partial orders from `semilattice_sup_mk'` and `semilattice_inf_mk'` agree\nif `sup` and `inf` satisfy the lattice absorption laws `sup_inf_self` (`a \u2294 a \u2293 b = a`)\nand `inf_sup_self` (`a \u2293 (a \u2294 b) = a`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone_on.min", "description": "Pointwise minimum of two monotone functions is a monotone function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sup_eq_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lt_inf_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lattice.to_linear_order", "description": " A lattice with total order is a linear order.\n\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lt_sup_of_lt_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone_on.map_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_order.to_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_dual_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.update_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_sup_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.of_map_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "distrib_lattice.of_inf_sup_le", "description": "Prove distributivity of an existing lattice from the dual distributive