2294 a`.\n\nThis generalizes `coheyting_algebra` by not requiring a top element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "generalized_coheyting_algebra.sdiff", "description": " A generalized co-Heyting algebra is a lattice with an additional binary difference operation `\\`\nsuch that `\\ a` is right adjoint to `\u2294 a`.\n\nThis generalizes `coheyting_algebra` by not requiring a top element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "generalized_coheyting_algebra.bot_le", "description": " A generalized co-Heyting algebra is a lattice with an additional binary difference operation `\\`\nsuch that `\\ a` is right adjoint to `\u2294 a`.\n\nThis generalizes `coheyting_algebra` by not requiring a top element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "generalized_coheyting_algebra.sdiff_le_iff", "description": " A generalized co-Heyting algebra is a lattice with an additional binary difference operation `\\`\nsuch that `\\ a` is right adjoint to `\u2294 a`.\n\nThis generalizes `coheyting_algebra` by not requiring a top element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "compl_compl_inf_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fst_sdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "compl_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.generalized_heyting_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.section_ext", "description": "Let `F` be a sheaf valued in a concrete category, whose forgetful functor reflects isomorphisms,\npreserves limits and filtered colimits. Then two sections who agree on every stalk must be equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_congr", "description": "The stalks are isomorphic on inseparable points", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.germ", "description": "The germ of a section of a presheaf over an open at a point of that open.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_specializes_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_functor_preserves_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_open_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_congr_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_functor", "description": "Stalks are functorial with respect to morphisms of presheaves over a fixed `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.germ_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.germ_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_pushforward", "description": "For a presheaf `F` on a space `X`, a continuous map `f : X \u27f6 Y` induces a morphisms between the\nstalk of `f _ * F` at `f x` and the stalk of `F` at `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.germ_res_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.app_surjective_of_injective_of_locally_surjective", "description": " For surjectivity, we are given an arbitrary section `t` and need to find a preimage for it.\nWe claim that it suffices to find preimages *locally*. That is, for each `x : U` we construct\na neighborhood `V \u2264 U` and a section `s : F.obj (op V))` such that `f.app (op V) s` and `t`\nagree on `V`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_pullback_iso", "description": "The isomorphism `\u2131_{f(x)} \u2245 (f\u207b\u00b9\u2131)\u2093`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_specializes_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.germ_stalk_specializes_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_functor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.is_iso_iff_stalk_functor_map_iso", "description": "Let `F` and `G` be sheaves valued in a concrete category, whose forgetful functor reflects\nisomorphisms, preserves limits and filtered colimits. Then a morphism `f : F \u27f6 G` is an\nisomorphism if and only if all of its stalk maps are isomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_pushforward.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_pullback_inv", "description": "The morphism `(f\u207b\u00b9\u2131)\u2093 \u27f6 \u2131_{f(x)}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_specializes_stalk_functor_map_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.is_iso_of_stalk_functor_map_iso", "description": "Let `F` and `G` be sheaves valued in a concrete category, whose forgetful functor reflects\nisomorphisms, preserves limits and filtered colimits. Then if the stalk maps of a morphism\n`f : F \u27f6 G` are all isomorphisms, `f` must be an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_mono_of_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_pushforward_germ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_specializes_stalk_pushforward_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.germ_to_pullback_stalk", "description": "The morphism `(f\u207b\u00b9\u2131)(U) \u27f6 \u2131_{f(x)}` for some `U \u220b x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.mono_iff_stalk_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.germ_stalk_specializes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_pushforward_germ_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.germ_stalk_specializes'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_specializes", "description": "If `x` specializes to `y`, then there is a natural map `F.stalk y \u27f6 F.stalk x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_specializes_stalk_pushforward", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.app_bijective_of_stalk_functor_map_bijective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.app_injective_of_stalk_functor_map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.mono_of_stalk_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_specializes_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk", "description": "The stalk of a presheaf `F` at a point `x` is calculated as the colimit of the functor\nnbhds x \u2964 opens F.X \u2964 C", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_specializes_comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_functor_map_germ_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.germ_exist", "description": "For presheaves valued in a concrete category whose forgetful functor preserves filtered colimits,\nevery element of the stalk is the germ of a section.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_specializes_stalk_pushforward_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.germ_stalk_specializes'_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_functor_map_germ_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_congr_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_pullback_hom", "description": "The morphism `\u2131_{f x} \u27f6 (f\u207b\u00b9\u2131)\u2093` that factors through `(f_*f\u207b\u00b9\u2131)_{f x}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.germ_stalk_specializes'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_hom_ext", "description": "A morphism from the stalk of `F` at `x` to some object `Y` is completely determined by its\ncomposition with the `germ` morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_specializes_stalk_functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_pushforward_germ_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_functor_map_germ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_pushforward.stalk_pushforward_iso_of_open_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_functor_map_injective_of_app_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_pushforward.id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.app_is_iso_of_stalk_functor_map_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.germ_res", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.app_surjective_of_stalk_functor_map_bijective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.app_injective_iff_stalk_functor_map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.germ_stalk_specializes_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_specializes_stalk_functor_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "forall_apply_eq_imp_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iff_not_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_unique_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "and_congr_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "decidable.not_imp_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ite_eq_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "opt_param.out", "description": " If `x : \u03b1 := d` then `x.out : \u03b1`. These are definitionally equal, but this can\nnevertheless be useful for various reasons, e.g. to apply further projection notation or in an\nargument to `simp`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_imp_of_and_not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "or.rotate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "em'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "forall_imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_or_eq_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "decidable.imp_iff_not_or", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pempty.elim", "description": "Ex falso, the nondependent eliminator for the `pempty` type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "or_or_distrib_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne_of_mem_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imp_or_distrib'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "and_imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "coe_sort_coe_base", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtype.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imp_iff_right_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "and_or_distrib_left", "description": "`\u2227` distributes over `\u2228` (on the left).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "forall\u2084_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "or_and_distrib_right", "description": "`\u2227` distributes over `\u2228` (on the right).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_and_of_not_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "and_not_self_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "forall_prop_of_true", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proof_irrel_heq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imp_forall_iff", "description": " We intentionally restrict the type of `\u03b1` in this lemma so that this is a safer to use in simp\nthan `forall_swap`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dite_eq_ite", "description": "A `dite` whose results do not actually depend on the condition may be reduced to an `ite`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_prop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "or_and_distrib_left", "description": "`\u2228` distributes over `\u2227` (on the left).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "xor_iff_iff_not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ball_true_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "decidable_of_bool", "description": " Prove that `a` is decidable by constructing a boolean `b` and a proof that `b \u2194 a`.\n(This is sometimes taken as an alternate definition of decidability.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "coe_fn_coe_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "decidable.iff_iff_not_or_and_or_not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "congr_fun_congr_arg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dec_em'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_exists_of_forall_not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bex.elim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iff.is_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "forall\u2082_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imp_intro", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "or_self_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "and_rotate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_rec_constant", "description": "Transport through trivial families is the identity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "by_contra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "congr_arg2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "decidable.or_congr_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "or_of_or_of_imp_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "and_iff_left_of_imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imp_iff_not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bex_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "xor.or", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "empty.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ite_eq_or_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "library_note.decidable arguments", "description": "As mathlib is primarily classical,\nif the type signature of a `def` or `lemma` does not require any `decidable` instances to state,\nit is preferable not to introduce any `decidable` instances that are needed in the proof\nas arguments, but rather to use the `classical` tactic as needed.\n\nIn the other direction, when `decidable` instances do appear in the type signature,\nit is better to use explicitly introduced ones rather than allowing Lean to automatically infer\nclassical ones, as these may cause instance mismatch errors later.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bex_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "decidable.or_iff_not_imp_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "classical.cases", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_imp_exists'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq.congr_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "library_note.function coercion", "description": "Many structures such as bundled morphisms coerce to functions so that you can\ntransparently apply them to arguments. For example, if `e : \u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2` and `a : \u03b1`\nthen you can write `e a` and this is elaborated as `\u21d1e a`. This type of\ncoercion is implemented using the `has_coe_to_fun` type class. There is one\nimportant consideration:\n\nIf a type coerces to another type which in turn coerces to a function,\nthen it **must** implement `has_coe_to_fun` directly:\n```lean\nstructure sparkling_equiv (\u03b1 \u03b2) extends \u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2\n\n-- if we add a `has_coe` instance,\ninstance {\u03b1 \u03b2} : has_coe (sparkling_equiv \u03b1 \u03b2) (\u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2) :=\n\u27e8sparkling_equiv.to_equiv\u27e9\n\n-- then a `has_coe_to_fun` instance **must** be added as well:\ninstance {\u03b1 \u03b2} : has_coe_to_fun (sparkling_equiv \u03b1 \u03b2) :=\n\u27e8\u03bb _, \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2, \u03bb f, f.to_equiv.to_fun\u27e9\n```\n\n(Rationale: if we do not declare the direct coercion, then `\u21d1e a` is not in\nsimp-normal form. The lemma `coe_fn_coe_base` will unfold it to `\u21d1\u2191e a`. This\noften causes loops in the simplifier.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_iff_not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not.elim", "description": " Ex falso for negation. From `\u00ac a` and `a` anything follows. This is the same as `absurd` with\nthe arguments flipped, but it is in the `not` namespace so that projection notation can be used.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_unique.exists2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "and_or_imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "peirce'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "congr_arg_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imp_not_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dite_ne_right_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_or_eq_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imp_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_or_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "decidable.not_imp_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "decidable.imp_or_distrib'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "xor_not_not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "congr_arg_heq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ite_apply", "description": " A 'ite' producing a `Pi` type `\u03a0 a, \u03c3 a`, applied to a value `a : \u03b1` is a `ite` that applies\neither branch to `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iff.or", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne.ite_ne_right_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "congr_fun\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "or_of_or_of_imp_of_imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "classical.some_spec2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iff.ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "forall_eq_or_imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_and'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "forall_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "and_self_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "decidable.iff_not_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "xor_false", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "auto_param.out", "description": " If `x : \u03b1 . tac_name` then `x.out : \u03b1`. These are definitionally equal, but this can\nnevertheless be useful for various reasons, e.g. to apply further projection notation or in an\nargument to `simp`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Exists.some_spec", "description": "Show that an element extracted from `P : \u2203 a, p a` using `P.some` satisfies `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "decidable.not_not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ball.imp_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_or_of_imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ball_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "library_note.decidable namespace", "description": "In most of mathlib, we use the law of excluded middle (LEM) and the axiom of choice (AC) freely.\nThe `decidable` namespace contains versions of lemmas from the root namespace that explicitly\nattempt to avoid the axiom of choice, usually by adding decidability assumptions on the inputs.\n\nYou can check if a lemma uses the axiom of choice by using `#print axioms foo` and seeing if\n`classical.choice` appears in the list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_and_self_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "apply_dite", "description": "A function applied to a `dite` is a `dite` of that function applied to each of the branches.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iff_true_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iff_false_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsingleton.prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "forall\u2082_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "false_ne_true", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "forall_exists_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dite_apply", "description": " A 'dite' producing a `Pi` type `\u03a0 a, \u03c3 a`, applied to a value `a : \u03b1` is a `dite` that applies\neither branch to `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "and_congr_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "coe_fn_coe_trans'", "description": "Non-dependent version of `coe_fn_coe_trans`, helps `rw` figure out the argument.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "congr_refl_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "or_congr_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_forall_not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "apply_dite2", "description": " A two-argument function applied to two `dite`s is a `dite` of that two-argument function\napplied to each of the branches.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iff_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iff_iff_not_or_and_or_not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "funext\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "or_rotate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "and.imp_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rec_heq_iff_heq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "decidable.not_and_not_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_apply_eq_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "decidable.not_and_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_unique_prop_of_true", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iff_and_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imp_false", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_and_not_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bex.imp_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "and_congr_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iff_mpr_iff_true_intro", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Exists.fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "or_self_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bex_imp_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "decidable.peirce", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Exists.imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq.congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne.ite_eq_left_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "decidable.not_iff_not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "and_and_distrib_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "decidable.iff_iff_and_or_not_and_not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imp_iff_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "classical.dec_rel", "description": "Any relation `p` is decidable classically.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.swap\u2082", "description": "Swaps two pairs of arguments to a function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ite_ne_right_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "and_self_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bex_or_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "plift.down_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cast_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "decidable_of_iff'", "description": " Transfer decidability of `b` to decidability of `a`, if the propositions are equivalent.\nThis is the same as `decidable_of_iff` but the iff is flipped.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne.ite_ne_left_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imp_iff_or_not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "or_imp_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iff_self_and", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "decidable.and_or_imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "forall_prop_of_false", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "or_congr_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_or_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "and_and_and_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iff.not_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_and", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "or_iff_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsingleton_iff_forall_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iff_of_true", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "classical.dec_eq", "description": "Any type `\u03b1` has decidable equality classically.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "and_iff_right_iff_imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "psum.inhabited_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "classi