ed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stone_cech_equivalence", "description": "(Implementation) The bijection of homsets to establish the reflective adjunction of compact\nHausdorff spaces in topological spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CompHaus_to_Top_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CompHaus.has_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CompHaus_to_Top.faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CompHaus.limit_cone", "description": " An explicit limit cone for a functor `F : J \u2964 CompHaus`, defined in terms of\n`Top.limit_cone`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CompHaus_to_Top.creates_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CompHaus.is_iso_of_bijective", "description": "Any continuous bijection of compact Hausdorff spaces is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CompHaus.compact_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CompHaus.concrete_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CompHaus_to_Top_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CompHaus_to_Top.full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CompHaus.is_closed_map", "description": "Any continuous function on compact Hausdorff spaces is a closed map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CompHaus.coe_to_Top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CompHaus.epi_iff_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CompHaus.limit_cone_is_limit", "description": "The limit cone `CompHaus.limit_cone F` is indeed a limit cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CompHaus.coe_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "StoneCech_obj_to_Top_str_is_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "StoneCech_obj_to_Top_\u03b1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CompHaus.forget_reflects_isomorphisms", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CompHaus.iso_of_bijective", "description": "Any continuous bijection of compact Hausdorff spaces induces an isomorphism.", "p":