_products.cones_equiv_inverse_obj_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.construct_products.cones_equiv_functor", "description": "(Impl) A preliminary definition to avoid timeouts.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.construct_products.cones_equiv_unit_iso_2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.construct_products.cones_equiv_functor_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.over_has_terminal", "description": "Construct terminal object in the over category. This isn't an instance as it's not typically the\nway we want to define terminal objects.\n(For instance, this gives a terminal object which is different from the generic one given by\n`over_product_of_wide_pullback` above.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.construct_products.cones_equiv_inverse_obj_2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.construct_products.cones_equiv_functor_2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.construct_products.cones_equiv_functor_obj_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.construct_products.over_finite_products_of_finite_wide_pullbacks", "description": "Given all finite wide pullbacks in `C`, construct finite products in `C/B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.construct_products.cones_equiv_counit_iso", "description": "(Impl) A preliminary definition to avoid timeouts.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.construct_products.over_binary_product_of_pullback", "description": "Given a pullback in `C`, construct a binary product in `C/B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.construct_products.has_over_limit_discrete_of_wide_pullback_limit", "description": "Use the above equivalence to prove we have a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.construct_products.cones_equiv_inverse_obj", "description": "(Impl) A preliminary definition to avoid timeouts.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.construct_products.cones_equiv_inverse_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.construct_products.over_product_of_wide_pullback", "description": "Given a wide pullback in `C`, construct a product in `C/B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.construct_products.over_products_of_wide_pullbacks", "description": "Given all wide pullbacks in `C`, construct products in `C/B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.construct_products.cones_equiv_inverse_map_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.comap", "description": " Pullback of a `measure`. If `f` sends each measurable set to a null-measurable set,\nthen for each measurable set `s` we have `comap f \u03bc s = \u03bc (f '' s)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.one_le_prob_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_finset_bUnion_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map\u2097", "description": " The pushforward of a measure as a linear map. It is defined to be `0` if `f` is not\na measurable function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.ae_sum_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.tsum_meas_le_meas_Union_of_disjoint", "description": " The measure of a disjoint union (even uncountable) of measurable sets is at least the sum of\nthe measures of the sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.exists_ne_forall_mem_nhds_pos_measure_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.restrict_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Ioo_ae_eq_Ico'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.le_count_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.eventually_mem_spanning_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_union_add_inter\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.self_mem_ae_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.trim_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_Ico_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.null_of_locally_null", "description": " If a set has zero measure in a neighborhood of each of its points, then it has zero measure\nin a second-countable space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.tendsto_measure_bInter_gt", "description": " The measure of the intersection of a decreasing sequence of measurable\nsets indexed by a linear order with first countable topology is the limit of the measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_restrict\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_union'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_embedding.restrict_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.sigma_finite.out", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sum_apply_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_ne_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.le_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_smul_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.sigma_finite_of_locally_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sum_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_closed_ball_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_sUnion_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_spanning_sets_in.of_le", "description": " Given measures `\u03bc`, `\u03bd` where `\u03bd \u2264 \u03bc`, `finite_spanning_sets_in.of_le` provides the induced\n`finite_spanning_set` with respect to `\u03bd` from a `finite_spanning_set` with respect to `\u03bc`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_set_of_frequently_eq_zero", "description": " A version of the **Borel-Cantelli lemma**: if `p\u1d62` is a sequence of predicates such that\n`\u2211 \u03bc {x | p\u1d62 x}` is finite, then the measure of `x` such that `p\u1d62 x` holds frequently as `i \u2192 \u221e` (or\nequivalently, `p\u1d62 x` holds for infinitely many `i`) is equal to zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.comap\u2097_eq_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_eq_measure_of_between_null_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_probability_measure.ae_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.ext_of_generate_from_of_Union", "description": "Two measures are equal if they are equal on the \u03c0-system generating the \u03c3-algebra,\n and they are both finite on a increasing spanning sequence of sets in the \u03c0-system.\n This lemma is formulated using `Union`.\n `finite_spanning_sets_in.ext` is a reformulation of this lemma.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_union_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_bUnion_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.exists_pos_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_spanning_sets_in.mono'", "description": " If `\u03bc` has finite spanning sets in `C` and `C \u2229 {s | \u03bc s < \u221e} \u2286 D` then `\u03bc` has finite spanning\nsets in `D`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_restrict_ae_le_map_indicator_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.countable.ae_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_bUnion_finset\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_eq_dirac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.subtype.volume_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.map_apply_eq_iff_map_symm_apply_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_Union_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count_apply_finite'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.comap_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.le_ae_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.exists_nonempty_inter_of_measure_univ_lt_tsum_measure", "description": " Pigeonhole principle for measure spaces: if `\u2211' i, \u03bc (s i) > \u03bc univ`, then\none of the intersections `s i \u2229 s j` is not empty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sum_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.eq_zero_of_is_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.coe_measure_univ_nnreal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.map_symm_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_of_ae_trim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_eventually_not_mem", "description": " A version of the **Borel-Cantelli lemma**: if `s\u1d62` is a sequence of sets such that\n`\u2211 \u03bc s\u1d62` exists, then for almost all `x`, `x` does not belong to almost all `s\u1d62`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.Inf_caratheodory", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ite_ae_eq_of_measure_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_filter.exists_mem_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.le_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_eq_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_Icc_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.subtype.volume_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.le_measure_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_set.map_coe_volume", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_spanning_sets_in.sigma_finite", "description": "If `\u03bc` has finite spanning sets in the collection of measurable sets `C`, then `\u03bc` is \u03c3-finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count", "description": "Counting measure on any measurable space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_inter_add_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_diff_null", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.mem_ae_dirac_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Ioo_ae_eq_Icc'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict", "description": "Restrict a measure `\u03bc` to a set `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.zero_trim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "piecewise_ae_eq_restrict_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.null_measurable_set.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_le.le.absolutely_continuous_of_ae", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `measure_theory.measure.ae_le_iff_absolutely_continuous`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.trim_measurable_set_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.union_ae_eq_right_iff_ae_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_union_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.absolutely_continuous.is_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.to_outer_measure_to_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.to_outer_measure_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.complete_semilattice_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "piecewise_ae_eq_of_ae_eq_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count_injective_image'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_liminf_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.ext_iff_of_sUnion_eq_univ", "description": "Two measures are equal if they have equal restrictions on a spanning collection of sets\n (formulated using `sUnion`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.ae_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_bUnion\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_locally_finite_measure", "description": "A measure is called locally finite if it is finite in some neighborhood of each point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_locally_finite_measure.finite_at_nhds", "description": "A measure is called locally finite if it is finite in some neighborhood of each point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.absolutely_continuous_of_le_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indicator_ae_eq_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.sigma_finite_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.bounded.measure_lt_top", "description": " A bounded subset has finite measure for a measure which is finite on compact sets, in a\nproper space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_eq_of_ae_subset_of_measure_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_map", "description": " The restriction of the pushforward measure is the pushforward of the restriction. For a version\nassuming only `ae_measurable`, see `restrict_map_of_ae_measurable`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_eq_restrict_iff_indicator_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_congr_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sum_bool", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_embedding.map_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set_coe.measure_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.prob_compl_eq_one_sub", "description": " Note that this is not quite as useful as it looks because the measure takes values in `\u211d\u22650\u221e`.\nThus the subtraction appearing is the truncated subtraction of `\u211d\u22650\u221e`, rather than the\nbetter-behaved subtraction of `\u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_spanning_sets_in.disjointed", "description": " Given `S : \u03bc.finite_spanning_sets_in {s | measurable_set s}`,\n`finite_spanning_sets_in.disjointed` provides a `finite_spanning_sets_in {s | measurable_set s}`\nsuch that its underlying sets are pairwise disjoint.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.map_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.restrict_trim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_finite_measure_on_compacts_of_is_locally_finite_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_spanning_sets_in.ext", "description": " An extensionality for measures. It is `ext_of_generate_from_of_Union` formulated in terms of\n`finite_spanning_sets_in`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_to_measurable_inter_of_cover", "description": " If a set `t` is covered by a countable family of finite measure sets, then its measurable\nsuperset `to_measurable \u03bc t` (which has the same measure as `t`) satisfies,\nfor any measurable set `s`, the equality `\u03bc (to_measurable \u03bc t \u2229 s) = \u03bc (t \u2229 s)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.ae_eq_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_sUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_apply_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_singleton'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.ae_map_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.eventually_cofinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.exists_measure_inter_spanning_sets_pos", "description": " A set in a \u03c3-finite space has positive measure if and only if its intersection with\nsome member of the countable family of finite measure spanning sets has positive measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_Inf_eq_Inf_restrict", "description": "This lemma shows that `Inf` and `restrict` commute for measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_filter", "description": " A measure is called finite at filter `f` if it is finite at some set `s \u2208 f`.\nEquivalently, it is eventually finite at `s` in `f.small_sets`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.le_sum_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.ae_smul_measure_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.lt_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.mem_spanning_sets_of_index_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_univ_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count_apply_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_union'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_iff_measure_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.mem_spanning_sets_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_of_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.is_locally_finite_measure_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.preimage_null", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_Ioo_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_eq_zero_of_trim_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.outer_measure.to_measure_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.exists_open_superset_measure_lt_top", "description": " If `s` is a compact set and `\u03bc` is a locally finite measure, then `s` admits an open superset of\nfinite measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indicator_ae_eq_restrict_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.le_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_probability_measure_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.sigma_finite.of_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.measure_lt_top_of_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.mem_ae_of_mem_ae_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.le_trim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.spanning_sets_index", "description": "`spanning_sets_index \u03bc x` is the least `n : \u2115` such that `x \u2208 spanning_sets \u03bc n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_probability_measure.to_is_finite_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measurable_spanning_sets_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_eq_measure_larger_of_between_null_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_eq_of_subset_of_measure_ge", "description": "If `s \u2286 t`, `\u03bc t \u2264 \u03bc s`, `\u03bc t \u2260 \u221e`, and `s` is measurable, then `s =\u1d50[\u03bc] t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.coe_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_Union_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.outer_measure.to_measure_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comap_subtype_coe_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.ext_of_bUnion_eq_univ", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `measure_theory.measure.ext_iff_of_bUnion_eq_univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_Union_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_apply", "description": "If `t` is a measurable set, then the measure of `t` with respect to the restriction of\n the measure to `s` equals the outer measure of `t \u2229 s`. An alternate version requiring that `s`\n be measurable instead of `t` exists as `measure.restrict_apply'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.ext_iff_of_Union_eq_univ", "description": "Two measures are equal if they have equal restrictions on a spanning collection of sets\n (formulated using `Union`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.le_of_add_le_add_left", "description": " `le_of_add_le_add_left` is normally applicable to `ordered_cancel_add_comm_monoid`,\nbut it holds for measures with the additional assumption that \u03bc is finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_union_add_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_eq.restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sum_coe_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.prob_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_spanning_sets_in.mono", "description": "If `\u03bc` has finite spanning sets in `C` and `C \u2286 D` then `\u03bc` has finite spanning sets in `D`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.ext_of_generate_from_of_cover", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.exists_mem_of_measure_ne_zero_of_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Ico_ae_eq_Ioc'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.exists_subset_measure_lt_top", "description": " In a \u03c3-finite space, any measurable set of measure `> r` contains a measurable subset of\nfinite measure `> r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.ae_sum_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ext_on_measurable_space_of_generate_finite", "description": " If two finite measures give the same mass to the whole space and coincide on a \u03c0-system made\nof measurable sets, then they coincide on all sets in the \u03c3-algebra generated by the \u03c0-system.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map\u2097_mk_apply_of_ae_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_Union_eq_supr", "description": " Continuity from below: the measure of the union of a directed sequence of (not necessarily\n-measurable) sets is the supremum of the measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.covariant_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_union_add_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.add.sigma_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_finite_measure_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.supr_restrict_spanning_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Ico_ae_eq_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_union_congr_of_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indicator_meas_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.pairwise_ae_disjoint_of_ae_disjoint_forall_ne_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.le_lift_linear_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.spanning_sets_index_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.exists_nonempty_inter_of_measure_univ_lt_sum_measure", "description": " Pigeonhole principle for measure spaces: if `s` is a `finset` and\n`\u2211 i in s, \u03bc (t i) > \u03bc univ`, then one of the intersections `t i \u2229 t j` is not empty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sigma_finite_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_trim_to_measurable_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_add_measure_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_spanning_sets_in_open'", "description": " A locally finite measure on a second countable topological space admits a finite spanning\nsequence of open sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.ae_sum_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_filter.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.absolutely_continuous.mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_finite_measure_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.subtype.measure_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_smul_nnreal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_filter.filter_mono_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_eq_restrict_bUnion_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.exists_open_superset_measure_lt_top'", "description": " If `s` is a compact set and `\u03bc` is finite at `\ud835\udcdd x` for every `x \u2208 s`, then `s` admits an open\nsuperset of finite measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_const_le_meas_of_disjoint_Union", "description": " If the union of disjoint measurable sets has finite measure, then there are only\nfinitely many members of the union whose measure exceeds any given positive number.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_map_indicator_ae_iff_of_zero_nmem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.insert_ae_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.sum_measure_le_measure_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.absolutely_continuous.ae_le", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `measure_theory.measure.ae_le_iff_absolutely_continuous`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count_eq_zero_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sum_smul_dirac", "description": "A measure on a countable type is a sum of Dirac measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.tendsto_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_to_measurable_add_inter_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_bUnion_finset_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_add_measure_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_of_not_ae_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_union_add_inter'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.smul_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_univ_nnreal_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.to_measure_to_outer_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.null_measurable_set.image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_finite_measure", "description": "A measure `\u03bc` is called finite if `\u03bc univ < \u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_finite_measure.measure_univ_lt_top", "description": "A measure `\u03bc` is called finite if `\u03bc univ < \u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_apply\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Union_spanning_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.nonempty_inter_of_measure_lt_add", "description": " If two sets `s` and `t` are included in a set `u`, and `\u03bc s + \u03bc t > \u03bc u`,\nthen `s` intersects `t`. Version assuming that `t` is measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.preimage_spanning_sets_index_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_to_outer_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.dirac_apply_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.nonpos_iff_eq_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.countable.measure_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.dirac_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_spanning_sets_in_open", "description": " A locally finite measure on a `\u03c3`-compact topological space admits a finite spanning sequence\nof open sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.image_zpow_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_id'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_of_forall_measure_lt_top_ae_restrict", "description": "To prove something for almost all `x` w.r.t. a \u03c3-finite measure, it is sufficient to show that\n this holds almost everywhere in sets where the measure has finite value.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_restrict\u2080'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_spanning_sets_in", "description": "`\u03bc` has finite spanning sets in `C` if there is a countable sequence of sets in `C` that have\n finite measures. This structure is a type, which is useful if we want to record extra properties\n about the sets, such as that they are monotone.\n `sigma_finite` is defined in terms of this: `\u03bc` is \u03c3-finite if there exists a sequence of\n finite spanning sets in the collection of all measurable sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_spanning_sets_in.set", "description": "`\u03bc` has finite spanning sets in `C` if there is a countable sequence of sets in `C` that have\n finite measures. This structure is a type, which is useful if we want to record extra properties\n about the sets, such as that they are monotone.\n `sigma_finite` is defined in terms of this: `\u03bc` is \u03c3-finite if there exists a sequence of\n finite spanning sets in the collection of all measurable sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_spanning_sets_in.set_mem", "description": "`\u03bc` has finite spanning sets in `C` if there is a countable sequence of sets in `C` that have\n finite measures. This structure is a type, which is useful if we want to record extra properties\n about the sets, such as that they are monotone.\n `sigma_finite` is defined in terms of this: `\u03bc` is \u03c3-finite if there exists a sequence of\n finite spanning sets in the collection of all measurable sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_spanning_sets_in.finite", "description": "`\u03bc` has finite spanning sets in `C` if there is a countable sequence of sets in `C` that have\n finite measures. This structure is a type, which is useful if we want to record extra properties\n about the sets, such as that they are monotone.\n `sigma_finite` is defined in terms of this: `\u03bc` is \u03c3-finite if there exists a sequence of\n finite spanning sets in the collection of all measurable sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_spanning_sets_in.spanning", "description": "`\u03bc` has finite spanning sets in `C` if there is a countable sequence of sets in `C` that have\n finite measures. This structure is a type, which is useful if we want to record extra properties\n about the sets, such as that they are monotone.\n `sigma_finite` is defined in terms of this: `\u03bc` is \u03c3-finite if there exists a sequence of\n finite spanning sets in the collection of all measurable sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.smul_ae_eq_of_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_diff_add_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_to_measurable_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map", "description": " The pushforward of a measure. It is defined to be `0` if `f` is not an almost everywhere\nmeasurable function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.dirac", "description": "The dirac measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_eq_univ_iff_measure_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.lift_linear_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_univ_nnreal", "description": "The measure of the whole space with respect to a finite measure, considered as `\u211d\u22650`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.smul_to_outer_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_bUnion_to_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.limsup_ae_eq_of_forall_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_mono", "description": "Restriction of a measure to a subset is monotone both in set and in measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count_apply_eq_top'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_diff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_eq_sum", "description": "If `f` is a map with countable codomain, then `\u03bc.map f` is a sum of Dirac measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable.quasi_measure_preserving", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_le_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.le_to_measure_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq.absolutely_continuous", "description": "**Alias** of `measure_theory.measure.absolutely_continuous_of_eq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.preimage_mono_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_Union_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_compl_le_add_of_le_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.ae_eq_image_of_ae_eq_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.to_finite_spanning_sets_in", "description": "If `\u03bc` is \u03c3-finite it has finite spanning sets in the collection of all measurable sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_of_ae_restrict_of_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_apply_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.absolutely_continuous.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_filter.inf_of_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_map_indicator_ae_iff_mem_map_restrict_ae_of_zero_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_mono'", "description": "Restriction of a measure to a subset is monotone both in set and in measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.tsum_measure_le_measure_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.liminf_preimage_iterate_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.absolutely_continuous.ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_spanning_sets_in_compact", "description": " Compact covering of a `\u03c3`-compact topological space as\n`measure_theory.measure.finite_spanning_sets_in`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.absolutely_continuous", "description": "We say that `\u03bc` is absolutely continuous with respect to `\u03bd`, or that `\u03bc` is dominated by `\u03bd`,\n if `\u03bd(A) = 0` implies that `\u03bc(A) = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.ae_le_iff_absolutely_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_spanning_sets_in.disjointed_set_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.cofinite", "description": "The filter of sets `s` such that `s\u1d9c` has finite measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_to_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_dirac_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_of_ae_eq_of_ae_restrict", "description": " If two measurable sets are ae_eq then any proposition that is almost everywhere true on one\nis almost everywhere true on the other", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.le_map_apply", "description": "Even if `s` is not measurable, we can bound `map f \u03bc s` from below.\n See also `measurable_equiv.map_apply`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_Union_apply_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.comap_apply\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_finite_measure.to_sigma_finite", "description": "Every finite measure is \u03c3-finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.ext_of_Union_eq_univ", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `measure_theory.measure.ext_iff_of_Union_eq_univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_filter.inf_of_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_imp_of_ae_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_filter.eventually", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.tendsto_measure_Union", "description": " Continuity from below: the measure of the union of an increasing sequence of measurable sets\nis the limit of the measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.sigma_finite_trim_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.countable_meas_level_set_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.exists_preimage_eq_of_preimage_ae", "description": " By replacing a measurable set that is almost invariant with the `limsup` of its preimages, we\nobtain a measurable set that is almost equal and strictly invariant.\n\n(The `liminf` would work just as well.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_univ_nnreal_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_mem\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.to_measure_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_iff'\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_countably_spanning_spanning_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.empty_of_count_eq_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_union_congr", "description": " If two measures agree on all measurable subsets of `s` and `t`, then they agree on all\nmeasurable subsets of `s \u222a t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count_injective_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_filter.of_inf_ae", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `measure_theory.measure.finite_at_filter.inf_ae_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_finite_measure_trim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_diff_lt_of_lt_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_image_eq_zero_of_comap_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.exists_eq_disjoint_finite_spanning_sets_in", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_eq_measure_of_null_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_union\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "volume_set_coe_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map\u2097_apply_of_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.exists_pos_measure_of_cover", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.absolutely_continuous_of_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_subtype_coe_eq_zero_of_comap_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_finite_measure_smul_of_nnreal_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.trim_trim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_embedding.comap_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.pairwise_ae_disjoint_of_ae_disjoint_forall_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.measure_lt_top", "description": "A compact subset has finite measure for a measure which is finite on compacts.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Ico_ae_eq_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.vadd_ae_eq_of_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.to_measure_apply\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.countable_meas_pos_of_disjoint_Union", "description": " In a \u03c3-finite space, among disjoint measurable sets, only countably many can have positive\nmeasure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_union_to_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_to_measurable_of_cover", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.absolutely_continuous.rfl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_compl_add_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_inter_add_diff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_Union_to_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Ioo_ae_eq_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_restrict_of_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.volume_subtype_coe_eq_zero_of_volume_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite.measure_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.empty_of_count_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_bUnion_finset_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.comap\u2097_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Ioo_ae_eq_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_bUnion_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.ext_of_generate_from_of_cover_subset", "description": "Two measures are equal if they are equal on the \u03c0-system generating the \u03c3-algebra,\n and they are both finite on a increasing spanning sequence of sets in the \u03c0-system.\n This lemma is formulated using `sUnion`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.map_apply", "description": "If we map a measure along a measurable equivalence, we can compute the measure on all sets\n (not just the measurable ones).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_Union_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_of_forall_measure_lt_top_ae_restrict'", "description": "Similar to `ae_of_forall_measure_lt_top_ae_restrict`, but where you additionally get the\n hypothesis that another \u03c3-finite measure has finite values on `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_eq_restrict_bUnion_finset_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_mono_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_finite_measure_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sigma_finite_of_countable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.map_measurable_equiv_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_of_ae_restrict_of_ae_restrict_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.compact_space.is_finite_measure", "description": " Note this cannot be an instance because it would form a typeclass loop with\n`is_finite_measure_on_compacts_of_is_locally_finite_measure`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finset_sum_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_bUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_embedding.comap_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_Ioc_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_apply\u2080'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.limsup_preimage_iterate_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_eq_left_of_subset_of_measure_add_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.monotone_spanning_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_subtype_coe_le_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_inter_eq_of_measure_eq", "description": " If `u` is a superset of `t` with the same (finite) measure (both sets possibly non-measurable),\nthen for any measurable set `s` one also has `\u03bc (t \u2229 s) = \u03bc (u \u2229 s)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_to_outer_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_congr_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_compl_le_add_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.zero_to_outer_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_map_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Ioi_ae_eq_Ici'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.mem_disjointed_spanning_sets_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.prob_compl_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.is_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_is_measurably_generated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_eq_restrict_Union_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.restrict.sigma_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.bsupr_measure_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_union_add_inter'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_mem_iff_measure_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_probability_measure.ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sum", "description": "Sum of an indexed family of measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.comap_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.bounded_by_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_eq_self_of_ae_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sum_apply_eq_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.has_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.ext_of_sUnion_eq_univ", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `measure_theory.measure.ext_iff_of_sUnion_eq_univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.absolutely_continuous.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.is_topological_basis_is_open_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_spanning_sets_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.coe_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.liminf_ae_eq_of_forall_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_filter.filter_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.le_restrict_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.sum_measure_preimage_singleton", "description": " If `s` is a `finset`, then the measure of its preimage can be found as the sum of measures\nof the fibers `f \u207b\u00b9' {y}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.mem_map_restrict_ae_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_apply_of_ae_measurable", "description": "We can evaluate the pushforward on measurable sets. For non-measurable sets, see\n `measure_theory.measure.le_map_apply` and `measurable_equiv.map_apply`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict.has_no_atoms", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count_apply_finset'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.exists_mem_forall_mem_nhds_within_pos_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.spanning_sets", "description": "A noncomputable way to get a monotone collection of sets that span `univ` and have finite\n measure using `classical.some`. This definition satisfies monotonicity in addition to all other\n properties in `sigma_finite`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_Inter_eq_infi", "description": " Continuity from above: the measure of the intersection of a decreasing sequence of measurable\nsets is the infimum of the measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_locally_finite_measure_of_is_finite_measure_on_compacts", "description": " A measure which is finite on compact sets in a locally compact space is locally finite.\nNot registered as an instance to avoid a loop with the other direction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.partial_order", "description": " Measures are partially ordered.\n\nThe definition of less equal here is equivalent to the definition without the\nmeasurable set condition, and this is shown by `measure.le_iff'`. It is defined\nthis way since, to prove `\u03bc \u2264 \u03bd`, we may simply `intros s hs` instead of rewriting followed\nby `intros s hs`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sum_add_sum_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_restrict_iff_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.mem_cofinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_filter.inf_ae_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.Inf_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.countable_meas_pos_of_disjoint_of_meas_Union_ne_top", "description": " If the union of disjoint measurable sets has finite measure, then there are only\ncountably many members of the union whose measure is positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.exists_pos_preimage_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Ioo_ae_eq_Ioc'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.not_is_finite_measure_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.measure_zero_of_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_spanning_sets_in.is_countably_spanning", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_eq_dirac'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.punit.measure_theory.measure_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.sigma_finite_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_filter.measure_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_to_measurable_of_sigma_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.summable_measure_to_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.to_outer_measure_trim_eq_trim_to_outer_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_zero_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_eq_right_of_subset_of_measure_add_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.is_finite_measure_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.comap\u2097", "description": " Pullback of a `measure` as a linear map. If `f` sends each measurable set to a measurable\nset, then for each measurable set `s` we have `comap\u2097 f \u03bc s = \u03bc (f '' s)`.\n\nIf the linearity is not needed, please use `comap` instead, which works for a larger class of\nfunctions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.tsum_measure_preimage_singleton", "description": " If `s` is a countable set, then the measure of its preimage can be found as the sum of measures\nof the fibers `f \u207b\u00b9' {y}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving", "description": " A map `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is said to be *quasi measure preserving* (a.k.a. non-singular) w.r.t. measures\n`\u03bca` and `\u03bcb` if it is measurable and `\u03bcb s = 0` implies `\u03bca (f \u207b\u00b9' s) = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.measurable", "description": " A map `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is said to be *quasi measure preserving* (a.k.a. non-singular) w.r.t. measures\n`\u03bca` and `\u03bcb` if it is measurable and `\u03bcb s = 0` implies `\u03bca (f \u207b\u00b9' s) = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.absolutely_continuous", "description": " A map `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is said to be *quasi measure preserving* (a.k.a. non-singular) w.r.t. measures\n`\u03bca` and `\u03bcb` if it is measurable and `\u03bcb s = 0` implies `\u03bca (f \u207b\u00b9' s) = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.outer_measure.to_measure", "description": "Obtain a measure by giving an outer measure where all sets in the \u03c3-algebra are\n Carath\u00e9odory measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count_apply_infinite", "description": "`count` measure evaluates to infinity at infinite sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_add_restrict_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.dirac.is_probability_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_univ_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_to_measurable_inter_of_sigma_finite", "description": " The measurable superset `to_measurable \u03bc t` of `t` (which has the same measure as `t`)\nsatisfies, for any measurable set `s`, the equality `\u03bc (to_measurable \u03bc t \u2229 s) = \u03bc (t \u2229 s)`.\nThis only holds when `\u03bc` is \u03c3-finite. For a version without this assumption (but requiring\nthat `t` has finite measure), see `measure_to_measurable_inter`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.uIoc_ae_eq_interval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_univ_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.top_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.tendsto_measure_Inter", "description": " Continuity from above: the measure of the intersection of a decreasing sequence of measurable\nsets is the limit of the measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indicator_ae_eq_of_ae_eq_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_to_measurable_add_inter_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.trim", "description": " Restriction of a measure to a sub-sigma algebra.\nIt is common to see a measure `\u03bc` on a measurable space structure `m0` as being also a measure on\nany `m \u2264 m0`. Since measures in mathlib have to be trimmed to the measurable space, `\u03bc` itself\ncannot be a measure on `m`, hence the definition of `\u03bc.trim hm`.\n\nThis notion is related to `outer_measure.trim`, see the lemma\n`to_outer_measure_trim_eq_trim_to_outer_measure`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.coe_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_inter_add_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count_singleton'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count_ne_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.map_map_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.nonempty_inter_of_measure_lt_add'", "description": " If two sets `s` and `t` are included in a set `u`, and `\u03bc s + \u03bc t > \u03bc u`,\nthen `s` intersects `t`. Version assuming that `s` is measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_add_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measurable_set.null_measurable_set_subtype_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_apply_eq_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Iio_ae_eq_Iic'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sum_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_embedding.ae_map_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_uIoc_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Iio_ae_eq_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_dirac_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.forall_measure_inter_spanning_sets_eq_zero", "description": " A set in a \u03c3-finite space has zero measure if and only if its intersection with\nall members of the countable family of finite measure spanning sets has zero measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_comap_subtype_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_inter_eq_zero_of_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.coe_nnreal_smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_finite_measure_on_compacts", "description": "A measure `\u03bc` is finite on compacts if any compact set `K` satisfies `\u03bc K < \u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_finite_measure_on_compacts.lt_top_of_is_compact", "description": "A measure `\u03bc` is finite on compacts if any compact set `K` satisfies `\u03bc K < \u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.preimage_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Ioi_ae_eq_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.null_measurable_set.mono_ac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count.is_finite_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "piecewise_ae_eq_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.volume_subtype_coe_le_volume", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.sigma_finite", "description": "A measure `\u03bc` is called \u03c3-finite if there is a countable collection of sets\n`{ A i | i \u2208 \u2115 }` such that `\u03bc (A i) < \u221e` and `\u22c3 i, A i = s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.sigma_finite.out'", "description": "A measure `\u03bc` is called \u03c3-finite if there is a countable collection of sets\n`{ A i | i \u2208 \u2115 }` such that `\u03bc (A i) < \u221e` and `\u22c3 i, A i = s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count_apply_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.lt_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_ball_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indicator_ae_eq_zero_of_restrict_ae_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.mono_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measurable_spanning_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_eq_comp'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map\u2097_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_eq_of_ae_eq_trim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sum_of_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.absolutely_continuous.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_sUnion\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ext_of_generate_finite", "description": "Two finite measures are equal if they are equal on the \u03c0-system generating the \u03c3-algebra\n (and `univ`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_bUnion_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_uIoc_iff", "description": "See also `measure_theory.ae_restrict_uIoc_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count_apply_lt_top'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_union_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.preimage_null_of_map_null", "description": "Even if `s` is not measurable, `map f \u03bc s = 0` implies that `\u03bc (f \u207b\u00b9' s) = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_eq_measure_smaller_of_between_null_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.le_comap_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.sum.sigma_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_finite_measure_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_to_measurable_inter", "description": " The measurable superset `to_measurable \u03bc t` of `t` (which has the same measure as `t`)\nsatisfies, for any measurable set `s`, the equality `\u03bc (to_measurable \u03bc t \u2229 s) = \u03bc (u \u2229 s)`.\nHere, we require that the measure of `t` is finite. The conclusion holds without this assumption\nwhen the measure is sigma_finite, see `measure_to_measurable_inter_of_sigma_finite`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.quasi_measure_preserving_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_probability_measure", "description": "A measure `\u03bc` is called a probability measure if `\u03bc univ = 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_probability_measure.measure_univ", "description": "A measure `\u03bc` is called a probability measure if `\u03bc univ = 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.le_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.subsingleton.measure_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_dirac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_of_ae_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.mono_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_restrict'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_map_mem_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.compl_mem_cofinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.tsum_indicator_apply_singleton", "description": " Given that `\u03b1` is a countable, measurable space with all singleton sets measurable,\nwrite the measure of a set `s` as the sum of the measure of `{x}` for all `x \u2208 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_apply'", "description": " If `s` is a measurable set, then the outer measure of `t` with respect to the restriction of\nthe measure to `s` equals the outer measure of `t \u2229 s`. This is an alternate version of\n`measure.restrict_apply`, requiring that `s` is measurable instead of `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count_apply_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_congr_set", "description": " If two measurable sets are ae_eq then any proposition that is almost everywhere true on one\nis almost everywhere true on the other", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.ae_mono'", "description": "**Alias** of `measure_theory.measure.absolutely_continuous.ae_le`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Ioo_ae_eq_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "volume_preimage_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sum_add_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_finite_measure_smul_nnreal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_locally_finite_measure_smul_nnreal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_disjoint.preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_Union_congr_of_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.union_ae_eq_left_iff_ae_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_to_outer_measure_eq_to_outer_measure_restrict", "description": " This lemma shows that `restrict` and `to_outer_measure` commute. Note that the LHS has a\nrestrict on measures and the RHS has a restrict on outer measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ite_ae_eq_of_measure_compl_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.prob_add_prob_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_diff_null'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.exists_is_open_measure_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "volume_image_subtype_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.zero_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.ext_iff_of_bUnion_eq_univ", "description": "Two measures are equal if they have equal restrictions on a spanning collection of sets\n (formulated using `bUnion`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict\u2097", "description": "Restrict a measure `\u03bc` to a set `s` as an `\u211d\u22650\u221e`-linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.to_outer_measure_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_apply_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_embedding.map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.sub_ae_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indicator_ae_eq_of_restrict_compl_ae_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_probability_measure_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_le_of_ae_le_trim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_finite_measure_iff_is_finite_measure_on_compacts_of_compact_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_apply_superset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Ioc_ae_eq_Icc'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.absolutely_continuous.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.restrict.is_finite_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_filter.filter_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.null_measurable_set.subtype_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.sigma_finite_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_principal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_bUnion_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.sigma_finite_trim_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.measure_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_le.le.absolutely_continuous", "description": "**Alias** of `measure_theory.measure.absolutely_continuous_of_le`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Ico_ae_eq_Icc'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.smul_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.dirac_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.coe_add_hom", "description": "Coercion to function as an additive monoid homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_filter_of_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_finite_measure.to_is_locally_finite_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.le_dirac_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.lift_linear", "description": " Lift a linear map between `outer_measure` spaces such that for each measure `\u03bc` every measurable\nset is caratheodory-measurable w.r.t. `f \u03bc` to a linear map between `measure` spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.absolutely_continuous_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sum_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_limsup_eq_zero", "description": " One direction of the **Borel-Cantelli lemma**: if (s\u1d62) is a sequence of sets such\nthat `\u2211 \u03bc s\u1d62` is finite, then the limit superior of the `s\u1d62` is a null set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_uIoc_iff", "description": "See also `measure_theory.ae_uIoc_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.mem_ae_map_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict\u2097_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_congr_meas", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_univ_nnreal_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_diff_le_iff_le_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_finite_measure_on_compacts.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sum_cond", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.count_apply_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.null_measurable_set.preimage", "description": " The preimage of a null measurable set under a (quasi) measure preserving map is a null\nmeasurable set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.prob_compl_eq_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.has_no_atoms", "description": " Measure `\u03bc` *has no atoms* if the measure of each singleton is zero.\n\nNB: Wikipedia assumes that for any measurable set `s` with positive `\u03bc`-measure,\nthere exists a measurable `t \u2286 s` such that `0 < \u03bc t < \u03bc s`. While this implies `\u03bc {x} = 0`,\nthe converse is not true.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.has_no_atoms.measure_singleton", "description": " Measure `\u03bc` *has no atoms* if the measure of each singleton is zero.\n\nNB: Wikipedia assumes that for any measurable set `s` with positive `\u03bc`-measure,\nthere exists a measurable `t \u2286 s` such that `0 < \u03bc t < \u03bc s`. While this implies `\u03bc {x} = 0`,\nthe converse is not true.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.le_to_outer_measure_caratheodory", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_if", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.tendsto_ae_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_restrict_Union_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Ioc_ae_eq_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.quasi_measure_preserving.preimage_iterate_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_bUnion_eq_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.complete_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.restrict_Union_apply_eq_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_finite_measure_of_is_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.psigma_equiv_sigma_plift", "description": "A `psigma`-type is equivalent to the corresponding `sigma`-type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.symm_apply_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.symm_trans_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.comp_bijective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.psigma_equiv_sigma", "description": "A `psigma`-type is equivalent to the corresponding `sigma`-type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.cast_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.conj", "description": "Conjugate a map `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1` by an equivalence `\u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.punit_arrow_equiv", "description": "The sort of maps from `punit` is equivalent to the codomain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.equiv_congr", "description": " If `\u03b1` is equivalent to `\u03b2` and `\u03b3` is equivalent to `\u03b4`, then the type of equivalences `\u03b1 \u2243 \u03b3`\nis equivalent to the type of equivalences `\u03b2 \u2243 \u03b4`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sigma_congr_right_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.forall_congr_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.to_fun_as_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.forall_congr'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.cast_eq_iff_heq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.exists_congr_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.self_trans_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.congr_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_assoc", "description": "Dependent product of types is associative up to an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.simps.symm_apply", "description": "See Note [custom simps projection]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.arrow_congr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.arrow_congr'_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.prop_equiv_pempty", "description": "The `Sort` of proofs of a false proposition is equivalent to `pempty`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.conj_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm", "description": "`perm \u03b1` is the type of bijections from `\u03b1` to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.equiv_of_is_empty", "description": "Two empty types are equivalent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_equiv_prod", "description": "`sigma` type with a constant fiber is equivalent to the product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.has_coe_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.inhabited'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.fun_unique", "description": "If `\u03b1` has a unique term, then the type of function `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is equivalent to `\u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.comp_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.equiv_congr_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quot.congr_right", "description": " Quotients are congruent on equivalences under equality of their relation.\nAn alternative is just to use rewriting with `eq`, but then computational proofs get stuck.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.symm_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.equiv_subsingleton_dom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.left_inverse_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.apply_eq_iff_eq_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.forall_congr_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.plift_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.subsingleton_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.eq_comp_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quot.congr_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.apply_eq_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.symm_trans_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.cast_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.equiv_congr_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.coe_fn_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_congr_right_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_congr_right_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_iff", "description": "equivalence of propositions is the same as iff", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient.congr_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.fun_unique_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_congr_right_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.self_comp_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.forall\u2083_congr'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.arrow_congr_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm_congr_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.prop_equiv_punit", "description": "The `Sort` of proofs of a true proposition is equivalent to `punit`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_congr_left_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.fun_unique_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.eq_symm_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.psigma_congr_right_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sigma_congr_right", "description": "A family of permutations `\u03a0 a, perm (\u03b2 a)` generates a permuation `perm (\u03a3 a, \u03b2\u2081 a)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.symm_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.arrow_congr'", "description": "A version of `equiv.arrow_congr` in `Type`, rather than `Sort`.\n\nThe `equiv_rw` tactic is not able to use the default `Sort` level `equiv.arrow_congr`,\nbecause Lean's universe rules will not unify `?l_1` with `imax (1 ?m_1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.comp_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.equiv_punit", "description": "If `\u03b1` has a unique element, then it is equivalent to any `punit`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.psigma_congr_right_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.coe_fn_symm_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.comp_symm_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.equiv_of_unique", "description": "If both `\u03b1` and `\u03b2` have a unique element, then `\u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.psigma_congr_right_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.psigma_equiv_sigma_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.Prop_equiv_bool", "description": "`Prop` is noncomputably equivalent to `bool`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.psigma_equiv_subtype", "description": "A `psigma` with `Prop` fibers is equivalent to the subtype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.conj_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.equiv_congr_refl_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.exists_unique_congr_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.congr_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.congr_arg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.arrow_congr_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.forall_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.arrow_congr'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.subsingleton.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.equiv_pempty", "description": "If `\u03b1` is an empty type, then it is equivalent to the `pempty` type in any universe.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm_congr_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.plift", "description": "`plift \u03b1` is equivalent to `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_congr_right", "description": " A family of equivalences `\u03a0 a, \u03b2\u2081 a \u2243 \u03b2\u2082 a` generates an equivalence between `\u03a3 a, \u03b2\u2081 a` and\n`\u03a3 a, \u03b2\u2082 a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient.congr", "description": " An equivalence `e : \u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2` generates an equivalence between quotient spaces,\nif `ra a\u2081 a\u2082 \u2194 rb (e a\u2081) (e a\u2082).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.psigma_equiv_sigma_plift_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.forall\u2083_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.cast_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.psigma_equiv_sigma_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.refl_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.equiv_congr_refl_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.trans_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_plift_equiv_subtype", "description": "A `sigma` with `plift` fibers is equivalent to the subtype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.forall\u2082_congr'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.equiv_congr_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.plift_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.equiv_empty_equiv", "description": "`\u03b1` is equivalent to an empty type iff `\u03b1` is empty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.apply_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.cast", "description": "Equivalence between equal types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.exists_unique_congr_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.symm", "description": "Inverse of an equivalence `e : \u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.arrow_congr'_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_congr_left'", "description": "Transporting a sigma type through an equivalence of the base", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.ulift_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.punit_equiv_punit", "description": "`punit` sorts in any two universes are equivalent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.nonempty_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm_congr_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm_congr_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.psigma_equiv_sigma_plift_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm_congr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.decidable_eq", "description": "Transfer `decidable_eq` across an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.bijective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quot.congr", "description": " An equivalence `e : \u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2` generates an equivalence between quotient spaces,\nif `ra a\u2081 a\u2082 \u2194 rb (e a\u2081) (e a\u2082).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.Pi_subsingleton", "description": " If `\u03b1` is `subsingleton` and `a : \u03b1`, then the type of dependent functions `\u03a0 (i : \u03b1), \u03b2\ni` is equivalent to `\u03b2 i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.refl_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.arrow_congr", "description": " If `\u03b1\u2081` is equivalent to `\u03b1\u2082` and `\u03b2\u2081` is equivalent to `\u03b2\u2082`, then the type of maps `\u03b1\u2081 \u2192 \u03b2\u2081`\nis equivalent to the type of maps `\u03b1\u2082 \u2192 \u03b2\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.equiv_congr_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_ulift_plift_equiv_subtype", "description": "A `sigma` with `\u03bb i, ulift (plift (P i))` fibers is equivalent to `{ x // P x }`.\nVariant of `sigma_plift_equiv_subtype`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.conj_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_equiv_prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.forall\u2082_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.refl_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.Pi_subsingleton_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.subsingleton_eq_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.Pi_subsingleton_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sigma_congr_right_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.false_arrow_equiv_punit", "description": "The sort of maps from `false` is equivalent to `punit`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.arrow_punit_of_is_empty", "description": "The sort of maps from a type that `is_empty` is equivalent to `punit`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.coe_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.inhabited", "description": "If `\u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2` and `\u03b2` is inhabited, then so is `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.pempty_arrow_equiv_punit", "description": "The sort of maps from `pempty` is equivalent to `punit`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.arrow_congr'_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.symm_comp_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.psigma_congr_right_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.arrow_punit_equiv_punit", "description": "The sort of maps to `punit.{v}` is equivalent to `punit.{w}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.ulift", "description": "`ulift \u03b1` is equivalent to `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.coe_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.surjective_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.equiv_empty", "description": "If `\u03b1` is an empty type, then it is equivalent to the `empty` type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.injective_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.trans", "description": "Composition of equivalences `e\u2081 : \u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2` and `e\u2082 : \u03b2 \u2243 \u03b3`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.coe_fn_injective", "description": "The map `coe_fn : (r \u2243 s) \u2192 (r \u2192 s)` is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quot.congr_left", "description": " An equivalence `e : \u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2` generates an equivalence between the quotient space of `\u03b1`\nby a relation `ra` and the quotient space of `\u03b2` by the image of this relation under `e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.congr_arg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm_congr_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.right_inverse_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_congr_left", "description": "An equivalence `f : \u03b1\u2081 \u2243 \u03b1\u2082` generates an equivalence between `\u03a3 a, \u03b2 (f a)` and `\u03a3 a, \u03b2 a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_equiv_prod_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.trans_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.refl", "description": "Any type is equivalent to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.equiv_subsingleton_cod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.equiv_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.arrow_congr_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.ulift_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_equiv_prod_of_equiv", "description": " If each fiber of a `sigma` type is equivalent to a fixed type, then the sigma type\nis equivalent to the product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.unique", "description": "If `\u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2` and `\u03b2` is a singleton type, then so is `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv", "description": "`\u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2` is the type of functions from `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` with a two-sided inverse.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.to_fun", "description": "`\u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2` is the type of functions from `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` with a two-sided inverse.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.inv_fun", "description": "`\u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2` is the type of functions from `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` with a two-sided inverse.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.left_inv", "description": "`\u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2` is the type of functions from `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` with a two-sided inverse.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.right_inv", "description": "`\u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2` is the type of functions from `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` with a two-sided inverse.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.psigma_congr_right", "description": " A family of equivalences `\u03a0 a, \u03b2\u2081 a \u2243 \u03b2\u2082 a` generates an equivalence between `\u03a3' a, \u03b2\u2081 a` and\n`\u03a3' a, \u03b2\u2082 a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient.congr_right", "description": " Quotients are congruent on equivalences under equality of their relation.\nAn alternative is just to use rewriting with `eq`, but then computational proofs get stuck.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.coe_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.trans_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.symm_comp_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.arrow_congr_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.cast_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_congr", "description": " Transporting a sigma type through an equivalence of the base and a family of equivalences\nof matching fibers", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm_congr", "description": "If `\u03b1` is equivalent to `\u03b2`, then `perm \u03b1` is equivalent to `perm \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_congr_right_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.inv_fun_as_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.bijective_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.eq_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.conj_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.true_arrow_equiv", "description": "The sort of maps from `true` is equivalent to the codomain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.conj_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.empty_arrow_equiv_punit", "description": "The sort of maps from `empty` is equivalent to `punit`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sigma_congr_right_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.exists_unique_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.coe_subsingleton", "description": " This cannot be a `simp` lemmas as it incorrectly matches against `e : \u03b1 \u2243 synonym \u03b1`, when\n`synonym \u03b1` is semireducible. This makes a mess of `multiplicative.of_add` etc.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_group", "description": " A topological group is a group in which the multiplication and inversion operations are\ncontinuous.\n\nWhen you declare an instance that does not already have a `uniform_space` instance,\nyou should also provide an instance of `uniform_space` and `uniform_group` using\n`topological_group.to_uniform_space` and `topological_comm_group_is_uniform`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_group.to_has_continuous_mul", "description": " A topological group is a group in which the multiplication and inversion operations are\ncontinuous.\n\nWhen you declare an instance that does not already have a `uniform_space` instance,\nyou should also provide an instance of `uniform_space` and `uniform_group` using\n`topological_group.to_uniform_space` and `topological_comm_group_is_uniform`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_group.to_has_continuous_inv", "description": " A topological group is a group in which the multiplication and inversion operations are\ncontinuous.\n\nWhen you declare an instance that does not already have a `uniform_space` instance,\nyou should also provide an instance of `uniform_space` and `uniform_group` using\n`topological_group.to_uniform_space` and `topological_comm_group_is_uniform`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.add_left", "description": "Addition from the left in a topological additive group as a homeomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map_div_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_topology.ext'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_add_group.t2_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.has_continuous_neg'", "description": "A version of `pi.has_continuous_neg` for non-dependent functions. It is needed\nbecause sometimes Lean fails to 