n\nThis is currently only available for commutative groups, but it can be extended to\nnon-commutative groups too.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_zero_nhd.zero_Z", "description": " additive group with a neighbourhood around 0.\nOnly used to construct a topology and uniform space.\n\nThis is currently only available for commutative groups, but it can be extended to\nnon-commutative groups too.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_zero_nhd.sub_Z", "description": " additive group with a neighbourhood around 0.\nOnly used to construct a topology and uniform space.\n\nThis is currently only available for commutative groups, but it can be extended to\nnon-commutative groups too.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_interior_smul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_disjoint_vadd_of_is_compact", "description": "Given two compact sets in a noncompact additive topological group, there is a\ntranslate of the second one that is disjoint from the first one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_neg_nhds_within_Iio_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_interior_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_topology.to_topological_space_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_topology.to_topological_space_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_topology.to_topological_space_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_one_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_interior_sub_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_group_induced", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_add_group.continuous_conj_sum", "description": "Conjugation is jointly continuous on `G \u00d7 G` when both `mul` and `inv` are\ncontinuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_inv.of_nhds_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_neg", "description": " Basic hypothesis to talk about a topological additive group. A topological additive group\nover `M`, for example, is obtained by requiring the instances `add_group M` and\n`has_continuous_add M` and `has_continuous_neg M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_neg.continuous_neg", "description": " Basic hypothesis to talk about a topological additive group. A topological additive group\nover `M`, for example, is obtained by requiring the instances `add_group M` and\n`has_continuous_add M` and `has_continuous_neg M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_singleton_mem_nhds_of_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_neg_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_group.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.sub_right_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_group.continuous_conj'", "description": " Conjugation acting on fixed element of the group is continuous when both `mul` and\n`inv` are continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map_div_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_topology.to_topological_space_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.properly_discontinuous_smul_of_tendsto_cofinite", "description": " A subgroup `S` of a topological group `G` acts on `G` properly discontinuously on the left, if\nit is discrete in the sense that `S \u2229 K` is finite for all compact `K`. (See also\n`discrete_topology`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.div_left_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_group.of_nhds_one'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.topological_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.sub_left_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.sub_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_add_group.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_inv", "description": " Basic hypothesis to talk about a topological group. A topological group over `M`, for example,\nis obtained by requiring the instances `group M` and `has_continuous_mul M` and\n`has_continuous_inv M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_inv.continuous_inv", "description": " Basic hypothesis to talk about a topological group. A topological group over `M`, for example,\nis obtained by requiring the instances `group M` and `has_continuous_mul M` and\n`has_continuous_inv M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inducing.topological_add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.shear_mul_right", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (x, xy)` as a homeomorphism. This is a shear mapping.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "discrete_topology_of_open_singleton_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_inv_of_discrete_topology", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at.zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_topology", "description": " A group topology on a group `\u03b1` is a topology for which multiplication and inversion\nare continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_topology.to_topological_space", "description": " A group topology on a group `\u03b1` is a topology for which multiplication and inversion\nare continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_topology.to_topological_group", "description": " A group topology on a group `\u03b1` is a topology for which multiplication and inversion\nare continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_topology.has_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "neg_mem_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.comm_group_topological_closure", "description": "If a subgroup of a topological group is commutative, then so is its topological closure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_topology.ext'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.is_open_map_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.div_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.has_continuous_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.sub_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_add_group.of_comm_of_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.topological_closure_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_one_symm'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_topology.to_topological_space_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_interior_vadd_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.sub_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_mem_nhds_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_mem_connected_component_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_add_group_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_neg.of_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_topology.has_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.smul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_neg_nhds_within_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.shear_add_right_symm_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_topology.has_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_singleton_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_inv_nhds_within_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_units.homeomorph.sum_add_units", "description": "The topological group isomorphism between the additive units of a product of two\nadditive monoids, and the product of the additive units of each additive monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_add_group.to_has_continuous_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_topology.semilattice_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inducing.has_continuous_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_topology.to_topological_space_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_neg_nhds_within_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.nhds_one_is_countably_generated", "description": " In a first countable topological group `G` with normal subgroup `N`, `1 : G \u29f8 N` has a\ncountable neighborhood basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_interior_div_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.sub_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_topology.coinduced", "description": "  Given `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` and a topology on `\u03b1`, the coinduced group topology on `\u03b2` is the finest\ntopology such that `f` is continuous and `\u03b2` is a topological group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_inv_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.topological_add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_neg_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.shear_mul_right_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_topology.coinduced_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_inv_nhds_within_Ici_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "discrete_topology_iff_open_singleton_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.has_continuous_const_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_topology.complete_semilattice_Inf", "description": " Group topologies on `\u03b3` form a complete lattice, with `\u22a5` the discrete topology and `\u22a4` the\nindiscrete topology.\n\nThe infimum of a collection of group topologies is the topology generated by all their open sets\n(which is a group topology).\n\nThe supremum of two group topologies `s` and `t` is the infimum of the family of all group\ntopologies contained in the intersection of `s` and `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smul_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "compact_covered_by_mul_left_translates", "description": "A compact set is covered by finitely many left multiplicative translates of a set\n with non-empty interior.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_zero_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.add_comm_group_topological_closure", "description": "If a subgroup of an additive topological group is commutative, then so is its\ntopological closure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.t3_quotient_of_is_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "singleton_mul_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.div_right_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "singleton_add_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_mem_connected_component_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_topology.has_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_add_left_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_group.t3_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_group.to_has_continuous_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_topology.has_Inf", "description": "Infimum of a collection of additive group topologies", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_add_group_induced", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_is_compact_is_closed_nhds_of_add_group", "description": "In a locally compact additive group, any neighborhood of the identity contains a\ncompact closed neighborhood of the identity, even without separation assumptions on the space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.topological_closure_minimal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_topology.partial_order", "description": " The ordering on group topologies on the group `\u03b3`. `t \u2264 s` if every set open in `s` is also open\nin `t` (`t` is finer than `s`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.coe_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_topology.partial_order", "description": "The ordering on group topologies on the group `\u03b3`. `t \u2264 s` if every set open in `s`\nis also open in `t` (`t` is finer than `s`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_group_quotient", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_closure_iff_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_topology.complete_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.le_topological_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_units.topological_add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.add_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_nhds_split_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.topological_add_group", "description": "If addition is continuous in `\u03b1`, then it also is in `\u03b1\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.left_coset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_interior_add'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_interior_div_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.properly_discontinuous_vadd_opposite_of_tendsto_cofinite", "description": "A subgroup `S` of an additive topological group `G` acts on `G` properly\ndiscontinuously on the right, if it is discrete in the sense that `S \u2229 K` is finite for all compact\n`K`. (See also `discrete_topology`.)\n\nIf `G` is Hausdorff, this can be combined with `t2_space_of_properly_discontinuous_vadd_of_t2_space`\nto show that the quotient group `G \u29f8 S` is Hausdorff.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.properly_discontinuous_smul_opposite_of_tendsto_cofinite", "description": " A subgroup `S` of a topological group `G` acts on `G` properly discontinuously on the right, if\nit is discrete in the sense that `S \u2229 K` is finite for all compact `K`. (See also\n`discrete_topology`.)\n\nIf `G` is Hausdorff, this can be combined with `t2_space_of_properly_discontinuous_smul_of_t2_space`\nto show that the quotient group `G \u29f8 S` is Hausdorff.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at.div'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_topology.continuous_neg'", "description": "A version of the global `continuous_neg` suitable for dot notation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_interior_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_group.t1_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.div_left_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_add_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.continuous_smul\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separable_locally_compact_add_group.sigma_compact_space", "description": "Every locally\ncompact separable topological group is \u03c3-compact.\nNote: this is not true if we drop the topological group hypothesis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.const_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.properly_discontinuous_vadd_of_tendsto_cofinite", "description": "A subgroup `S` of an additive topological group `G` acts on `G` properly\ndiscontinuously on the left, if it is discrete in the sense that `S \u2229 K` is finite for all compact\n`K`. (See also `discrete_topology`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_basis.nhds_of_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "singleton_mul_mem_nhds_of_nhds_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.div_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_interior_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.add_right_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.inv", "description": " If a function converges to a value in a multiplicative topological group, then its inverse\nconverges to the inverse of this value. For the version in normed fields assuming additionally\nthat the limit is nonzero, use `tendsto.inv'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at.zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.right_coset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.neg", "description": "If a function converges to a value in an additive topological group, then its\nnegation converges to the negation of this value.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_map_sub_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_add_group.exists_antitone_basis_nhds_zero", "description": "Any first countable topological additive group has an antitone neighborhood basis\n`u : \u2115 \u2192 set G` for which `u (n + 1) + u (n + 1) \u2286 u n`. The existence of such a neighborhood basis\nis a key tool for `quotient_add_group.complete_space`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.shear_add_right_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.has_continuous_inv'", "description": " A version of `pi.has_continuous_inv` for non-dependent functions. It is needed because sometimes\nLean fails to use `pi.has_continuous_inv` for non-dependent functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_zero_symm'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_singleton_mem_nhds_of_nhds_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "neg_mem_connected_component_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.div'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_topology.coinduced_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.has_continuous_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inducing.has_continuous_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_is_compact_is_closed_nhds_of_group", "description": " In a locally compact group, any neighborhood of the identity contains a compact closed\nneighborhood of the identity, even without separation assumptions on the space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.right_add_coset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "compact_open_separated_add_right", "description": "Given a compact set `K` inside an open set `U`, there is a open neighborhood `V` of\n`0` such that `K + V \u2286 U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_add_group_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.neg", "description": "Negation in a topological group as a homeomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_group.regular_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.div_right", "description": "A version of `homeomorph.mul_right a\u207b\u00b9 b` that is defeq to `b / a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_topology.to_topological_space_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_group_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.has_continuous_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.coe_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_set_of_map_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "discrete_topology_iff_open_singleton_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.mul_left_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "compact_open_separated_mul_left", "description": "Given a compact set `K` inside an open set `U`, there is a open neighborhood `V` of `1`\n such that `V * K \u2286 U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_disjoint_smul_of_is_compact", "description": " Given two compact sets in a noncompact topological group, there is a translate of the second\none that is disjoint from the first one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_div", "description": " A typeclass saying that `\u03bb p : G \u00d7 G, p.1 / p.2` is a continuous function. This property\nautomatically holds for topological groups. Lemmas using this class have primes.\nThe unprimed version is for `group_with_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_div.continuous_div'", "description": " A typeclass saying that `\u03bb p : G \u00d7 G, p.1 / p.2` is a continuous function. This property\nautomatically holds for topological groups. Lemmas using this class have primes.\nThe unprimed version is for `group_with_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_interior_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_topology.continuous_inv'", "description": "A version of the global `continuous_inv` suitable for dot notation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_map_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separable_locally_compact_group.sigma_compact_space", "description": "Every locally compact separable topological group is \u03c3-compact.\n Note: this is not true if we drop the topological group hypothesis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.shear_add_right", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (x, x + y)` as a homeomorphism.\nThis is a shear mapping.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.right_add_coset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.div'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_group.of_comm_of_nhds_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_interior_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.has_continuous_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_topology.complete_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_neg_nhds_within_Iio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.nhds_eq", "description": "Neighborhoods in the quotient are precisely the map of neighborhoods in the prequotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.topological_group", "description": "If multiplication is continuous in `\u03b1`, then it also is in `\u03b1\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_of_continuous_at_one", "description": " A monoid homomorphism (a bundled morphism of a type that implements `monoid_hom_class`) from a\ntopological group to a topological monoid is continuous provided that it is continuous at one. See\nalso `uniform_continuous_of_continuous_at_one`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_map_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_topology.complete_semilattice_Inf", "description": "Group topologies on `\u03b3` form a complete lattice, with `\u22a5` the discrete topology and\n`\u22a4` the indiscrete topology.\n\nThe infimum of a collection of group topologies is the topology generated by all their open sets\n(which is a group topology).\n\nThe supremum of two group topologies `s` and `t` is the infimum of the family of all group\ntopologies contained in the intersection of `s` and `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_neg_nhds_within_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.inv", "description": "Inversion in a topological group as a homeomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.topological_closure", "description": "The (topological-space) closure of an additive subgroup of a space `M` with\n`has_continuous_add` is itself an additive subgroup.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.t3_quotient_of_is_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.has_continuous_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_add_group.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_add_group.of_nhds_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.topological_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.const_div'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_basis.nhds_of_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conj_act.units_has_continuous_const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_sub_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_div_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.is_closed_topological_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_map_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_mul_hom", "description": "On a topological group, `\ud835\udcdd : G \u2192 filter G` can be promoted to a `mul_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.sub_right", "description": "A version of `homeomorph.add_right (-a) b` that is defeq to `b - a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_group.continuous_conj", "description": "Conjugation by a fixed element is continuous when `mul` is continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.connected_component_of_zero", "description": "The connected component of 0 is a subgroup of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.is_normal_topological_closure", "description": "The topological closure of a normal subgroup is normal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_topology.continuous_add'", "description": "A version of the global `continuous_add` suitable for dot notation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_add_units_homeomorph", "description": " If `G` is an additive group with topological negation, then it is homeomorphic to\nits additive units.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_closure_iff_nhds_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.continuous_smul\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_topology.has_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.closure_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_topology.bounded_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_group.exists_antitone_basis_nhds_one", "description": " Any first countable topological group has an antitone neighborhood basis `u : \u2115 \u2192 set G` for\nwhich `(u (n + 1)) ^ 2 \u2286 u n`. The existence of such a neighborhood basis is a key tool for\n`quotient_group.complete_space`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_interior_sub_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_map_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "singleton_add_mem_nhds_of_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_div_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_mul_left_nhds_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient.topological_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_map_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_of_continuous_at_zero", "description": "An additive monoid homomorphism (a bundled morphism of a type that implements\n`add_monoid_hom_class`) from an additive topological group to an additive topological monoid is\ncontinuous provided that it is continuous at zero. See also\n`uniform_continuous_of_continuous_at_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_topology", "description": "An additive group topology on an additive group `\u03b1` is a topology for which addition and\n negation are continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_topology.to_topological_space", "description": "An additive group topology on an additive group `\u03b1` is a topology for which addition and\n negation are continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_topology.to_topological_add_group", "description": "An additive group topology on an additive group `\u03b1` is a topology for which addition and\n negation are continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_topology.semilattice_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.topological_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_mul_right_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_topology.continuous_mul'", "description": "A version of the global `continuo