_geometry.Scheme.restrict_functor_obj_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.restrict_functor_\u0393_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_pullback_morphism_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.bind_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.restrict_functor_map_of_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.hom.inv_app", "description": "The isomorphism `\u0393(X, U) \u27f6 \u0393(Y, f(U))` induced by an open immersion `f : X \u27f6 Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.affine_basis_cover_of_affine", "description": "The basic open sets form an affine open cover of `Spec R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_open_immersion.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_open_immersion", "description": "A morphism of Schemes is an open immersion if it is an open immersion as a morphism\nof LocallyRingedSpaces", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_open_immersion.iso_restrict", "description": "A open immersion induces an isomorphism from the domain onto the image", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_open_immersion.app_eq_inv_app_app_of_comp_eq_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.morphism_restrict_base_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.of_restrict_val_c_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_open_immersion.lift_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.J.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.bind_J", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.finite_subcover_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.bind", "description": " Given an open cover `{ U\u1d62 }` of `X`, and for each `U\u1d62` an open cover, we may combine these\nopen covers to form an open cover of `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_open_immersion.forget_to_Top_preserves_of_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.restrict_functor_map_base", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.\u0393_map_morphism_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.supr_opens_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.morphism_restrict_c_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.morphism_restrict_eq", "description": " The restrictions onto two equal open sets are isomorphic. This currently has bad defeqs when\nunfolded, but it should not matter for now. Replace this definition if better defeqs are needed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_open_immersion.iso_of_range_eq_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_open_immersion.open_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.copy", "description": " We construct an open cover from another, by providing the needed fields and showing that the\nprovided fields are isomorphic with the original open cover.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.pullback_cover", "description": " Given an open cover on `X`, we may pull them back along a morphism `W \u27f6 X` to obtain\nan open cover of `W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.pushforward_iso_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.compact_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_open_immersion.forget_to_Top_preserves_of_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover_of_supr_eq_top", "description": "If `U` is a family of open sets that covers `X`, then `X.restrict U` forms an `X.open_cover`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.morphism_restrict.is_open_immersion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_open_immersion.range_pullback_to_base_of_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_open_immersion.lift", "description": "The universal property of open immersions:\nFor an open immersion `f : X \u27f6 Z`, given any morphism of schemes `g : Y \u27f6 Z` whose topological\nimage is contained in the image of `f`, we can lift this morphism to a unique `Y \u27f6 X` that\ncommutes with these maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.morphism_restrict_stalk_map", "description": "The stalk map of a restriction of a morphism is isomorphic to the stalk map of the original map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.PresheafedSpace.is_open_immersion.to_Scheme", "description": "If `X \u27f6 Y` is an open immersion, and `Y` is a scheme, then so is `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_open_immersion.iso_of_range_eq_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_iso_iff_is_open_immersion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_open_immersion.range_pullback_fst_of_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover", "description": " An open cover of `X` consists of a family of open immersions into `X`,\nand for each `x : X` an open immersion (indexed by `f x`) that covers `x`.\n\nThis is merely a coverage in the Zariski pretopology, and it would be optimal\nif we could reuse the existing API about pretopologies, However, the definitions of sieves and\ngrothendieck topologies uses `Prop`s, so that the actual open sets and immersions are hard to\nobtain. Also, since such a coverage in the pretopology usually contains a proper class of\nimmersions, it is quite hard to glue them, reason about finite covers, etc.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.J", "description": " An open cover of `X` consists of a family of open immersions into `X`,\nand for each `x : X` an open immersion (indexed by `f x`) that covers `x`.\n\nThis is merely a coverage in the Zariski pretopology, and it would be optimal\nif we could reuse the existing API about pretopologies, However, the definitions of sieves and\ngrothendieck topologies uses `Prop`s, so that the actual open sets and immersions are hard to\nobtain. Also, since such a coverage in the pretopology usually contains a proper class of\nimmersions, it is quite hard to glue them, reason about finite covers, etc.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.obj", "description": " An open cover of `X` consists of a family of open immersions into `X`,\nand for each `x : X` an open immersion (indexed by `f x`) that covers `x`.\n\nThis is merely a coverage in the Zariski pretopology, and it would be optimal\nif we could reuse the existing API about pretopologies, However, the definitions of sieves and\ngrothendieck topologies uses `Prop`s, so that the actual open sets and immersions are hard to\nobtain. Also, since such a coverage in the pretopology usually contains a proper class of\nimmersions, it is quite hard to glue them, reason about finite covers, etc.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.map", "description": " An open cover of `X` consists of a family of open immersions into `X`,\nand for each `x : X` an open immersion (indexed by `f x`) that covers `x`.\n\nThis is merely a coverage in the Zariski pretopology, and it would be optimal\nif we could reuse the existing API about pretopologies, However, the definitions of sieves and\ngrothendieck topologies uses `Prop`s, so that the actual open sets and immersions are hard to\nobtain. Also, since such a coverage in the pretopology usually contains a proper class of\nimmersions, it is quite hard to glue them, reason about finite covers, etc.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.f", "description": " An open cover of `X` consists of a family of open immersions into `X`,\nand for each `x : X` an open immersion (indexed by `f x`) that covers `x`.\n\nThis is merely a coverage in the Zariski pretopology, and it would be optimal\nif we could reuse the existing API about pretopologies, However, the definitions of sieves and\ngrothendieck topologies uses `Prop`s, so that the actual open sets and immersions are hard to\nobtain. Also, since such a coverage in the pretopology usually contains a proper class of\nimmersions, it is quite hard to glue them, reason about finite covers, etc.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.covers", "description": " An open cover of `X` consists of a family of open immersions into `X`,\nand for each `x : X` an open immersion (indexed by `f x`) that covers `x`.\n\nThis is merely a coverage in the Zariski pretopology, and it would be optimal\nif we could reuse the existing API about pretopologies, However, the definitions of sieves and\ngrothendieck topologies uses `Prop`s, so that the actual open sets and immersions are hard to\nobtain. Also, since such a coverage in the pretopology usually contains a proper class of\nimmersions, it is quite hard to glue them, reason about finite covers, etc.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.is_open", "description": " An open cover of `X` consists of a family of open immersions into `X`,\nand for each `x : X` an open immersion (indexed by `f x`) that covers `x`.\n\nThis is merely a coverage in the Zariski pretopology, and it would be optimal\nif we could reuse the existing API about pretopologies, However, the definitions of sieves and\ngrothendieck topologies uses `Prop`s, so that the actual open sets and immersions are hard to\nobtain. Also, since such a coverage in the pretopology usually contains a proper class of\nimmersions, it is quite hard to glue them, reason about finite covers, etc.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.pullback_restrict_iso_restrict_inv_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_open_immersion.range_pullback_to_base_of_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.PresheafedSpace.is_open_immersion.to_Scheme_hom_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.pullback_restrict_iso_restrict_hom_restrict_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.pullback_restrict_iso_restrict", "description": "Given a morphism `f : X \u27f6 Y` and an open set `U \u2286 Y`, we have `X \u00d7[Y] U \u2245 X |_{f \u207b\u00b9 U}`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.restrict_to_LocallyRingedSpace_to_SheafedSpace_to_PresheafedSpace", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.morphism_restrict_restrict_basic_open", "description": "Restricting a morphism twice onto a basic open set is isomorphic to one restriction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.pushforward_iso_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_open_immersion.range_pullback_snd_of_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.Union_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.pullback_cover_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_open_immersion.has_pullback_of_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.image_morphism_restrict_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.pullback_cover_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.open_cover.copy_J", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebrai