ormed_add_group_hom.completion_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_comm_group.to_compl", "description": "The map from a normed group to its completion, as a normed group hom.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.ker_le_ker_completion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_comm_group.dense_range_to_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.completion_to_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.completion", "description": "The normed group hom induced between completions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_comm_group.norm_to_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.norm_completion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.extension_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.zero_completion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.extension", "description": " If `H` is complete, the extension of `f : normed_add_group_hom G H` to a\n`normed_add_group_hom (completion G) H`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.extension_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.completion_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.completion_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_units.has_continuous_const_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t2_space_of_properly_discontinuous_smul_of_t2_space", "description": "The quotient by a discontinuous group action of a locally compact t2 space is t2.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.is_closed_map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smul_closure_orbit_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_smul\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at_const_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map_quotient_mk_add", "description": "The quotient map by a group action is open, i.e. the quotient by a group\naction is an open quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.const_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smul_closure_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_const_smul", "description": " Class `has_continuous_const_smul \u0393 T` says that the scalar multiplication `(\u2022) : \u0393 \u2192 T \u2192 T`\nis continuous in the second argument. We use the same class for all kinds of multiplicative\nactions, including (semi)modules and algebras.\n\nNote that both `has_continuous_const_smul \u03b1 \u03b1` and `has_continuous_const_smul \u03b1\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u03b1` are\nweaker versions of `has_continuous_mul \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_const_smul.continuous_const_smul", "description": " Class `has_continuous_const_smul \u0393 T` says that the scalar multiplication `(\u2022) : \u0393 \u2192 T \u2192 T`\nis continuous in the second argument. We use the same class for all kinds of multiplicative\nactions, including (semi)modules and algebras.\n\nNote that both `has_continuous_const_smul \u03b1 \u03b1` and `has_continuous_const_smul \u03b1\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u03b1` are\nweaker versions of `has_continuous_mul \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_const_smul.op", "description": "If a scalar is central, then its right action is continuous when its left action is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map_smul\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_const_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.vadd", "description": "The homeomorphism given by affine-addition by an element of an additive group `\u0393` acting on\n `T` is a homeomorphism from `T` to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vadd_closure_orbit_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.has_continuous_const_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_const_vadd.op", "description": "If an additive action is central, then its right action is continuous when its left\naction is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_map_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_const_smul_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.to_properly_discontinuous_vadd", "description": "A finite group action is always properly discontinuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_const_smul_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_const_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_const_vadd_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.has_continuous_const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set_smul_mem_nhds_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_const_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.is_open_map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t2_space_of_properly_discontinuous_vadd_of_t2_space", "description": "The quotient by a discontinuous group action of a locally compact t2\nspace is t2.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.to_properly_discontinuous_smul", "description": "A finite group action is always properly discontinuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map_quotient_mk_mul", "description": "The quotient map by a group action is open, i.e. the quotient by a group action is an open\n quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_const_vadd_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.const_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at_const_smul_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at_const_vadd_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.continuous_within_at_const_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.continuous_const_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.smul\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.has_continuous_const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_const_vadd.second_countable_topology", "description": "The quotient of a second countable space by an additive group action is second\ncountable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.smul_of_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.has_continuous_const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "properly_discontinuous_smul", "description": " Class `properly_discontinuous_smul \u0393 T` says that the scalar multiplication `(\u2022) : \u0393 \u2192 T \u2192 T`\nis properly discontinuous, that is, for any pair of compact sets `K, L` in `T`, only finitely many\n`\u03b3:\u0393` move `K` to have nontrivial intersection with `L`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "properly_discontinuous_smul.finite_disjoint_inter_image", "description": " Class `properly_discontinuous_smul \u0393 T` says that the scalar multiplication `(\u2022) : \u0393 \u2192 T \u2192 T`\nis properly discontinuous, that is, for any pair of compact sets `K, L` in `T`, only finitely many\n`\u03b3:\u0393` move `K` to have nontrivial intersection with `L`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.smul", "description": "The homeomorphism given by scalar multiplication by a given element of a group `\u0393` acting on\n `T` is a homeomorphism from `T` to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_const_smul_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.has_continuous_const_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_const_vadd_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_const_vadd", "description": " Class `has_continuous_const_vadd \u0393 T` says that the additive action `(+\u1d65) : \u0393 \u2192 T \u2192 T`\nis continuous in the second argument. We use the same class for all kinds of additive actions,\nincluding (semi)modules and algebras.\n\nNote that both `has_continuous_const_vadd \u03b1 \u03b1` and `has_continuous_const_vadd \u03b1\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u03b1` are\nweaker versions of `has_continuous_add \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_const_vadd.continuous_const_vadd", "description": " Class `has_continuous_const_vadd \u0393 T` says that the additive action `(+\u1d65) : \u0393 \u2192 T \u2192 T`\nis continuous in the second argument. We use the same class for all kinds of additive actions,\nincluding (semi)modules and algebras.\n\nNote that both `has_continuous_const_vadd \u03b1 \u03b1` and `has_continuous_const_vadd \u03b1\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u03b1` are\nweaker versions of `has_continuous_add \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.continuous_at_const_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.has_continuous_const_smul'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_map_smul_of_ne_zero", "description": " `smul` is a closed map in the second argument.\n\nThe lemma that `smul` is a closed map in the first argument (for a normed space over a complete\nnormed field) is `is_closed_map_smul_left` in `analysis.normed_space.finite_dimension`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "properly_discontinuous_vadd", "description": " Class `properly_discontinuous_vadd \u0393 T` says that the additive action `(+\u1d65) : \u0393 \u2192 T \u2192 T`\nis properly discontinuous, that is, for any pair of compact sets `K, L` in `T`, only finitely many\n`\u03b3:\u0393` move `K` to have nontrivial intersection with `L`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "properly_discontinuous_vadd.finite_disjoint_inter_image", "description": " Class `properly_discontinuous_vadd \u0393 T` says that the additive action `(+\u1d65) : \u0393 \u2192 T \u2192 T`\nis properly discontinuous, that is, for any pair of compact sets `K, L` in `T`, only finitely many\n`\u03b3:\u0393` move `K` to have nontrivial intersection with `L`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.has_continuous_const_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.const_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_smul\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_compact_mul_support.comp_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_const_vadd_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_map_smul\u2080", "description": " `smul` is a closed map in the second argument.\n\nThe lemma that `smul` is a closed map in the first argument (for a normed space over a complete\nnormed field) is `is_closed_map_smul_left` in `analysis.normed_space.finite_dimension`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.has_continuous_const_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.has_continuous_const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.smul_of_ne_zero", "description": " Scalar multiplication by a non-zero element of a group with zero acting on `\u03b1` is a\nhomeomorphism from `\u03b1` onto itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.continuous_on_const_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at.const_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.has_continuous_const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_compact_support.comp_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_const_smul_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.has_continuous_const_vadd'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set_smul_mem_nhds_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at.const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_const_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_const_smul.second_countable_topology", "description": "The quotient of a second countable space by a group action is second countable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.tendsto_const_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.const_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.smul\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vadd_closure_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set_smul_mem_nhds_smul", "description": "Scalar multiplication preserves neighborhoods.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_op_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.is_colimit.mk'", "description": "This is another convenient method to verify that a fork is a limit cone. It\n   only asks for a proof of facts that carry any mathematical content, and allows access to the\n   same `s` for all parts.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.app_one_eq_\u03b9_comp_right_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.eq_of_epi_equalizer", "description": "If the equalizer of two morphisms is an epimorphism, then the two morphisms are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_hom.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.is_colimit.exists_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.hom_comp_\u03b9_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_hom_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_op_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer_comparison", "description": "The comparison morphism for the coequalizer of `f,g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.is_limit.exists_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_op", "description": "The functor `walking_parallel_pair \u2964 walking_parallel_pair\u1d52\u1d56` sending left to left and right to\nright.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer.\u03c0_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.of_cocone_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_op_equiv_counit_iso_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.condition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_of_is_split_mono_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer_comparison", "description": "The comparison morphism for the equalizer of `f,g`.\nThis is an isomorphism iff `G` preserves the equalizer of `f,g`; see\n`category_theory/limits/preserves/shapes/equalizers.lean`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_equalizers", "description": "`has_equalizers` represents a choice of equalizer for every pair of morphisms", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagram_iso_parallel_pair_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.is_limit.hom_iso", "description": "Given a limit cone for the pair `f g : X \u27f6 Y`, for any `Z`, morphisms from `Z` to its point are in\nbijection with morphisms `h : Z \u27f6 X` such that `h \u226b f = h \u226b g`.\nFurther, this bijection is natural in `Z`: see `fork.is_limit.hom_iso_natural`.\nThis is a special case of `is_limit.hom_iso'`, often useful to construct adjunctions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.of_cofork_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.id_fork", "description": "The identity determines a cone on the equalizer diagram of `f` and `g` if `f = g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_coequalizer_epi_comp", "description": " The cofork obtained by precomposing a coequalizer cofork with an epimorphism is\na coequalizer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.eq_of_epi_fork_\u03b9", "description": "Two morphisms are equal if there is a fork whose inclusion is epi.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer.fork_\u03c0_app_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_coequalizers_of_has_colimit_parallel_pair", "description": "If `C` has all colimits of diagrams `parallel_pair f g`, then it has all coequalizers", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_equalizer", "description": "`has_equalizer f g` represents a particular choice of limiting cone\nfor the parallel pair of morphisms `f` and `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer.iso_source_of_self_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_split_epi_coequalizes", "description": "A split epi `f` coequalizes `(f \u226b section_ f)` and `(\ud835\udfd9 X)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.split_epi_of_idempotent_of_is_colimit_cofork", "description": "A coequalizer of an idempotent morphism and the identity is split epi.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.is_colimit.hom_iso", "description": "Given a colimit cocone for the pair `f g : X \u27f6 Y`, for any `Z`, morphisms from the cocone point\nto `Z` are in bijection with morphisms `h : Y \u27f6 Z` such that `f \u226b h = g \u226b h`.\nFurther, this bijection is natural in `Z`: see `cofork.is_colimit.hom_iso_natural`.\nThis is a special case of `is_colimit.hom_iso'`, often useful to construct adjunctions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.of_cone", "description": "Given `F : walking_parallel_pair \u2964 C`, which is really the same as\n   `parallel_pair (F.map left) (F.map right)` and a cone on `F`, we get a fork on\n   `F.map left` and `F.map right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_coequalizer_epi_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.is_limit.mk'", "description": "This is another convenient method to verify that a fork is a limit cone. It\n   only asks for a proof of facts that carry any mathematical content, and allows access to the\n   same `s` for all parts.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_split_mono_equalizes", "description": "A split mono `f` equalizes `(retraction f \u226b f)` and `(\ud835\udfd9 Y)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_hom", "description": "The type family of morphisms for the diagram indexing a (co)equalizer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_hom.left", "description": "The type family of morphisms for the diagram indexing a (co)equalizer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_hom.right", "description": "The type family of morphisms for the diagram indexing a (co)equalizer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_hom.id", "description": "The type family of morphisms for the diagram indexing a (co)equalizer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.of_fork", "description": "This is a helper construction that can be useful when verifying that a category has all\n   equalizers. Given `F : walking_parallel_pair \u2964 C`, which is really the same as\n   `parallel_pair (F.map left) (F.map right)`, and a fork on `F.map left` and `F.map right`,\n   we get a cone on `F`.\n\n   If you're thinking about using this, have a look at `has_equalizers_of_has_limit_parallel_pair`,\n   which you may find to be an easier way of achieving your goal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer_comparison_map_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_op_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_hom.comp", "description": "Composition of morphisms in the indexing diagram for (co)equalizers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.mk_hom", "description": "Helper function for constructing morphisms between coequalizer coforks.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.is_colimit.hom_iso_natural", "description": "The bijection of `cofork.is_colimit.hom_iso` is natural in `Z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer.hom_ext", "description": "Two maps into an equalizer are equal if they are are equal when composed with the equalizer\n   map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.split_mono_of_equalizer", "description": " We show that the converse to `is_split_mono_equalizes` is true:\nWhenever `f` equalizes `(r \u226b f)` and `(\ud835\udfd9 Y)`, then `r` is a retraction of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer_comparison_comp_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.map_lift_equalizer_comparison", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.\u03c0_precompose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_of_is_split_mono", "description": "A split mono `f` equalizes `(retraction f \u226b f)` and `(\ud835\udfd9 Y)`.\nHere we build the cone, and show in `is_split_mono_equalizes` that it is a limit cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_limit_cone_parallel_pair_of_self", "description": "Every equalizer of `(f, f)` is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer.fork", "description": "An equalizer cone for a parallel pair `f` and `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork", "description": "A cofork on `f` and `g` is just a `cocone (parallel_pair f g)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer.iso_source_of_self", "description": "The equalizer of a morphism with itself is isomorphic to the source.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_coequalizer", "description": "`has_coequalizer f g` represents a particular choice of colimiting cocone\nfor the parallel pair of morphisms `f` and `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer.cofork", "description": "An arbitrary choice of coequalizer cocone for a parallel pair `f` and `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.iso_fork_of_\u03b9", "description": "Every fork is isomorphic to one of the form `fork.of_\u03b9 _ _`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_op_equiv_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.eq_of_mono_cofork_\u03c0", "description": "Two morphisms are equal if there is a cofork whose projection is mono.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.mk_hom", "description": "Helper function for constructing morphisms between equalizer forks.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.app_one_eq_\u03b9_comp_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.\u03c0", "description": "A cofork `t` on the parallel_pair `f g : X \u27f6 Y` consists of two morphisms\n   `t.\u03b9.app zero : X \u27f6 t.X` and `t.\u03b9.app one : Y \u27f6 t.X`. Of these, only the second one is\n   interesting, and we give it the shorter name `cofork.\u03c0 t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.parallel_pair_map_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer.condition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.epi_of_is_colimit_cofork", "description": "The coequalizer morphism in any colimit cocone is an epimorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer.cofork_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.split_epi_of_coequalizer", "description": " We show that the converse to `is_split_epi_equalizes` is true:\nWhenever `f` coequalizes `(f \u226b s)` and `(\ud835\udfd9 X)`, then `s` is a section of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.is_limit.lift'", "description": "If `s` is a limit fork over `f` and `g`, then a morphism `k : W \u27f6 X` satisfying\n   `k \u226b f = k \u226b g` induces a morphism `l : W \u27f6 s.X` such that `l \u226b fork.\u03b9 s = k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer.desc", "description": "Any morphism `k : Y \u27f6 W` satisfying `f \u226b k = g \u226b k` factors through the coequalizer of `f`\n   and `g` via `coequalizer.desc : coequalizer f g \u27f6 W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer.\u03c0_colim_map_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer.iso_source_of_self_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.of_cone_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_colimit_cocone_parallel_pair_of_self", "description": "Every coequalizer of `(f, f)` is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.parallel_pair.ext", "description": " Construct a natural isomorphism between functors out of the walking parallel pair from\nits components.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.coequalizer_ext", "description": "To check whether two maps are coequalized by both maps of a cofork, it suffices to check it for\n   the second map", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_of_is_split_epi_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer_is_equalizer", "description": "The equalizer built from `equalizer.\u03b9 f g` is limiting.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.ext_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.parallel_pair.ext_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.parallel_pair_hom_app_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.is_limit.lift_\u03b9_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.iso_cofork_of_\u03c0", "description": "Every cofork is isomorphic to one of the form `cofork.of_\u03c0 _ _`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_coequalizers", "description": "`has_coequalizers` represents a choice of coequalizer for every pair of morphisms", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer.lift", "description": "A morphism `k : W \u27f6 X` satisfying `k \u226b f = k \u226b g` factors through the equalizer of `f` and `g`\n   via `equalizer.lift : W \u27f6 equalizer f g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer", "description": "If a coequalizer of `f` and `g` exists, we can access an arbitrary choice of such by\n   saying `coequalizer f g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.parallel_pair_obj_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer", "description": "If an equalizer of `f` and `g` exists, we can access an arbitrary choice of such by\n   saying `equalizer f g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.\u03c0_of_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_of_is_split_mono_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.parallel_pair_hom", "description": "Construct a morphism between parallel pairs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer.lift'", "description": "A morphism `k : W \u27f6 X` satisfying `k \u226b f = k \u226b g` induces a morphism `l : W \u27f6 equalizer f g`\n   satisfying `l \u226b equalizer.\u03b9 f g = k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.parallel_pair_functor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer.fork_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.parallel_pair.eq_of_hom_eq_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.parallel_pair", "description": "`parallel_pair f g` is the diagram in `C` consisting of the two morphisms `f` and `g` with\n   common domain and codomain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer.iso_target_of_self_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.is_limit.lift_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_of_is_split_mono_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer_comparison_comp_\u03c0_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagram_iso_parallel_pair_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.mk_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer.condition_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_coequalizer_of_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.split_mono_of_idempotent_of_is_limit_fork", "description": "An equalizer of an idempotent morphism and the identity is split mono.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagram_iso_parallel_pair", "description": "Every functor indexing a (co)equalizer is naturally isomorphic (actually, equal) to a\n   `parallel_pair`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.is_colimit.of_exists_unique", "description": "Noncomputably make a colimit cocone from the existence of unique factorizations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.of_\u03c0", "description": "A cofork on `f g : X \u27f6 Y` is determined by the morphism `\u03c0 : Y \u27f6 P` satisfying\n   `f \u226b \u03c0 = g \u226b \u03c0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.ext_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer.\u03c0_of_self", "description": "The coequalizer projection for `(f, f)` is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.\u03b9_comp_coequalizer_comparison_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.app_one_eq_\u03b9_comp_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_op_equiv_counit_iso_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.app_one_eq_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_of_is_split_epi", "description": "A split epi `f` coequalizes `(f \u226b section_ f)` and `(\ud835\udfd9 X)`.\nHere we build the cocone, and show in `is_split_epi_coequalizes` that it is a colimit cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.app_zero_eq_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.\u03b9_of_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.\u03c0_comp_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer.\u03c0", "description": "If a coequalizer of `f` and `g` exists, we can access the corresponding projection by\n  saying `coequalizer.\u03c0 f g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_op_equiv_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_equalizer_comp_mono", "description": "The fork obtained by postcomposing an equalizer fork with a monomorphism is an equalizer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.parallel_pair.eq_of_hom_eq", "description": " Construct a natural isomorphism between `parallel_pair f g` and `parallel_pair f' g'` given\nequalities `f = f'` and `g = g'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_op_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer.desc'", "description": "Any morphism `k : Y \u27f6 W` satisfying `f \u226b k = g \u226b k` induces a morphism\n   `l : coequalizer f g \u27f6 W` satisfying `coequalizer.\u03c0 \u226b g = l`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.equalizer_ext", "description": "To check whether two maps are equalized by both maps of a fork, it suffices to check it for the\n   first map", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer.condition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.is_colimit.hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_op_equiv", "description": "The equivalence `walking_parallel_pair \u2964 walking_parallel_pair\u1d52\u1d56` sending left to left and right to\nright.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_of_is_split_epi_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.of_\u03b9_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer.exists_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair", "description": "The type of objects for the diagram indexing a (co)equalizer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair.zero", "description": "The type of objects for the diagram indexing a (co)equalizer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair.one", "description": "The type of objects for the diagram indexing a (co)equalizer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.hom_comp_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.eq_of_mono_coequalizer", "description": "If the coequalizer of two morphisms is a monomorphism, then the two morphisms are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.\u03b9", "description": "A fork `t` on the parallel pair `f g : X \u27f6 Y` consists of two morphisms `t.\u03c0.app zero : t.X \u27f6 X`\n   and `t.\u03c0.app one : t.X \u27f6 Y`. Of these, only the first one is interesting, and we give it the\n   shorter name `fork.\u03b9 t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.split_mono_of_idempotent_equalizer", "description": "The equalizer of an idempotent morphism and the identity is split mono.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer.\u03b9_mono", "description": "An equalizer morphism is a monomorphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_hom_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer.\u03b9_of_self", "description": "The equalizer inclusion for `(f, f)` is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_op_equiv_unit_iso_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.is_limit.hom_iso_natural", "description": "The bijection of `fork.is_limit.hom_iso` is natural in `Z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer.\u03c0_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer_comparison_map_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.is_limit.of_exists_unique", "description": "Noncomputably make a limit cone from the existence of unique factorizations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.of_\u03c0_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_hom.inhabited", "description": "Satisfying the inhabited linter", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.app_zero_eq_comp_\u03c0_right_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer.\u03b9_of_eq", "description": "The equalizer of `(f, g)`, where `f = g`, is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer.lift_\u03b9_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.is_limit.mk", "description": "This is a slightly more convenient method to verify that a fork is a limit cone. It\n   only asks for a proof of facts that carry any mathematical content", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.mk_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer.lift_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.split_epi_of_idempotent_coequalizer", "description": "The coequalizer of an idempotent morphism and the identity is split epi.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.of_cofork", "description": "This is a helper construction that can be useful when verifying that a category has all\n   coequalizers. Given `F : walking_parallel_pair \u2964 C`, which is really the same as\n   `parallel_pair (F.map left) (F.map right)`, and a cofork on `F.map left` and `F.map right`,\n   we get a cocone on `F`.\n\n   If you're thinking about using this, have a look at\n   `has_coequalizers_of_has_colimit_parallel_pair`, which you may find to be an easier way of\n   achieving your goal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork", "description": "A fork on `f` and `g` is just a `cone (parallel_pair f g)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.is_colimit.desc'", "description": "If `s` is a colimit cofork over `f` and `g`, then a morphism `k : Y \u27f6 W` satisfying\n   `f \u226b k = g \u226b k` induces a morphism `l : s.X \u27f6 W` such that `cofork.\u03c0 s \u226b l = k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.is_colimit.hom_iso_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.of_cocone", "description": "Given `F : walking_parallel_pair \u2964 C`, which is really the same as\n   `parallel_pair (F.map left) (F.map right)` and a cocone on `F`, we get a cofork on\n   `F.map left` and `F.map right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.app_zero_eq_comp_\u03c0_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.parallel_pair.eq_of_hom_eq_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_equalizer_of_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.parallel_pair_map_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.id_cofork", "description": "The identity determines a cocone on the coequalizer diagram of `f` and `g`, if `f = g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.map_lift_equalizer_comparison_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.ext_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_of_is_split_epi_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.of_\u03b9_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.\u03c0_comp_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_limit_cone_parallel_pair_of_epi", "description": "An equalizer that is an epimorphism is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer_is_coequalizer", "description": "The cofork built from `coequalizer.\u03c0 f g` is colimiting.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.of_\u03c0_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.is_colimit.hom_iso_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_equalizers_of_has_limit_parallel_pair", "description": "If `C` has all limits of diagrams `parallel_pair f g`, then it has all equalizers", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.\u03b9_postcompose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.parallel_pair_hom_app_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_of_is_limit_fork", "description": "The equalizer morphism in any limit cone is a monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.ext", "description": "To construct an isomorphism between coforks,\nit suffices to give an isomorphism between the cocone points\nand check that it commutes with the `\u03c0` morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.is_limit.hom_iso_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.parallel_pair_obj_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.condition_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer.iso_target_of_self_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_limit_cone_parallel_pair_of_eq", "description": "Every equalizer of `(f, g)`, where `f = g`, is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.parallel_pair.ext_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer.exists_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.condition_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer.\u03c0_of_eq", "description": "The coequalizer of `(f, g)`, where `f = g`, is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer.\u03c0_epi", "description": "A coequalizer morphism is an epimorphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.is_limit.mk_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit_id_cofork", "description": "The identity on `Y` is a coequalizer of `(f, g)`, where `f = g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.ext_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer.condition_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.of_\u03b9", "description": "A fork on `f g : X \u27f6 Y` is determined by the morphism `\u03b9 : P \u27f6 X` satisfying `\u03b9 \u226b f = \u03b9 \u226b g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.is_colimit.mk", "description": "This is a slightly more convenient method to verify that a cofork is a colimit cocone. It\n   only asks for a proof of facts that carry any mathematical content", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.ext", "description": "To construct an isomorphism between forks,\nit suffices to give an isomorphism between the cone points\nand check that it commutes with the `\u03b9` morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_limit_cocone_parallel_pair_of_epi", "description": "A coequalizer that is a monomorphism is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.of_fork_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.\u03b9_comp_coequalizer_comparison", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.is_limit.hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_parallel_pair_op_equiv_unit_iso_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer.cofork_\u03b9_app_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer.hom_ext", "description": "Two maps from a coequalizer are equal if they are equal when composed with the coequalizer\n   map", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.split_mono_of_idempotent_of_is_limit_fork_retraction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.condition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_colimit_cocone_parallel_pair_of_eq", "description": "Every coequalizer of `(f, g)`, where `f = g`, is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.app_zero_eq_comp_\u03c0_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.is_colimit.\u03c0_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit_id_fork", "description": "The identity on `X` is an equalizer of `(f, g)`, if `f = g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coequalizer.iso_target_of_self", "description": "The coequalizer of a morphism with itself is isomorphic to the target.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer.\u03b9", "description": "If an equalizer of `f` and `g` exists, we can access the inclusion\n   `equalizer f g \u27f6 X` by saying `equalizer.\u03b9 f g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fork.is_limit.hom_iso_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.split_epi_of_idempotent_of_is_colimit_cofork_section_", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_equalizer_comp_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofork.is_colimit.\u03c0_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.of_finsupp_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.smul_zero_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.support_update_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.sum_add'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.support_monomial'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.not_mem_support_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.support_binomial'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.support_X_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.exists_iff_exists_finsupp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.has_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.of_finsupp_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.X_pow_mul_C", "description": " Prefer putting constants to the left of `X ^ n`.\n\nThis lemma is the loop-avoiding `simp` version of `X_pow_mul`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.of_finsupp_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.support_C_mul_X_pow'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.is_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial", "description": " `polynomial R` is the type of univariate polynomials over `R`.\n\nPolynomials should be seen as (semi-)rings with the additional constructor `X`.\nThe embedding from `R` is called `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.to_finsupp", "description": " `polynomial R` is the type of univariate polynomials over `R`.\n\nPolynomials should be seen as (semi-)rings with the additional constructor `X`.\nThe embedding from `R` is called `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.monomial_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.support_X_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.to_finsupp_X_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.support_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.monomial_one_one_eq_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.support_erase", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_update", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.to_finsupp_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.to_finsupp_C_mul_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_update_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.monomial_mul_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.to_finsupp_erase", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_erase", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_C_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.commute_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.smul_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.X_mul_monomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.monomial_mul_X_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.C_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.has_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"