orphisms in\n`Algebra`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.free", "description": "The \"free algebra\" functor, sending a type `S` to the free algebra on `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.free_obj_is_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.of_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.has_forget_to_Module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.category_theory.concrete_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.coe_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.adj", "description": "The free/forget adjunction for `R`-algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.free_obj_carrier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_equiv.to_Algebra_iso", "description": "Build an isomorphism in the category `Algebra R` from a `alg_equiv` between `algebra`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.free_obj_is_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.category_theory.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.of_self_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.free_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso.to_alg_equiv", "description": "Build a `alg_equiv` from an isomorphism in the category `Algebra R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_equiv.to_Algebra_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.has_coe_to_sort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.category_theory.forget.category_theory.is_right_adjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso.to_alg_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra", "description": "The category of R-algebras and their morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.carrier", "description": "The category of R-algebras and their morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.is_ring", "description": "The category of R-algebras and their morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.is_algebra", "description": "The category of R-algebras and their morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.of_self_iso", "description": " Forgetting to the underlying type and then building the bundled object returns the original\nalgebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.of", "description": " The object in the category of R-algebras associated to a type equipped with the appropriate\ntypeclasses.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.forget_reflects_isos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_equiv_iso_Algebra_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_drop_succ", "description": "Counterpart to `list.sum_take_succ` when we have an negation operation", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.alternating_prod_cons_cons'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_take_add_sum_drop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.alternating_sum_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_neg", "description": "This is the `list.sum` version of `add_neg`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_commute.list_sum_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_list_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.length_pos_of_one_lt_prod", "description": "A list with product greater than one must have positive length.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_drop_succ", "description": "Counterpart to `list.prod_take_succ` when we have an inverse operation", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.length_pos_of_prod_ne_one", "description": "A list with product not one must have positive length.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_hom\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_is_unit_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.single_le_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.head_add_tail_sum_of_ne_nil", "description": "Same as `nth_zero_add_tail_sum`, but avoiding the `list.head` garbage complication\nby requiring the list to be nonempty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.forall\u2082.sum_le_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_hom_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.alternating_prod_cons'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.exists_mem_ne_one_of_prod_ne_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.length_pos_of_prod_lt_one", "description": "A list with product less than one must have positive length.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.list_prod_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_eq_pow_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.alternating_sum_cons'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_lt_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_concat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.all_zero_of_le_zero_le_of_sum_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.length_pos_of_sum_ne_zero", "description": "A list with sum not zero must have positive length.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_map_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.monotone_sum_take", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.one_le_prod_of_one_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sublist_forall\u2082.sum_le_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_take_mul_prod_drop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_lt_sum_of_ne_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_hom\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.alternating_prod_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_erase", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_commute.list_sum_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.alternating_sum_cons_cons'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.alternating_sum_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.nth_zero_add_tail_sum", "description": "We'd like to state this as `L.head + L.tail.sum = L.sum`, but because `L.head`\nrelies on an inhabited instance to return a garbage value on the empty list, this is not possible.\nInstead, we write the statement in terms of `(L.nth 0).get_or_else 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_update_nth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.map_list_prod", "description": "Deprecated, use `_root_.map_list_prod` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_map_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.length_pos_of_sum_neg", "description": "A list with negative sum must have positive length.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.eq_of_sum_take_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_hom_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_const_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_eq_zero", "description": "Slightly more general version of `list.sum_eq_zero_iff`\n  for a non-ordered `add_monoid`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_inv_reverse", "description": "This is the `list.prod` version of `mul_inv_rev`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_map_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_le_foldr_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sublist.sum_le_sum", "description": "If `l\u2081` is a sublist of `l\u2082` and all elements of `l\u2082` are nonnegative,\nthen `l\u2081.sum \u2264 l\u2082.sum`. One can prove a stronger version assuming `\u2200 a \u2208 l\u2082.diff l\u2081, 0 \u2264 a` instead\nof `\u2200 a \u2208 l\u2082, 0 \u2264 a` but this lemma is not yet in `mathlib`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.single_le_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_lt_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_take_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.forall\u2082.prod_le_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_pos", "description": " The product of a list of positive natural numbers is positive,\nand likewise for any nontrivial ordered semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.alternating_prod_cons_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_le_pow_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_int_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_le_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sublist.prod_le_prod'", "description": " If `l\u2081` is a sublist of `l\u2082` and all elements of `l\u2082` are greater than or equal to one, then\n`l\u2081.prod \u2264 l\u2082.prod`. One can prove a stronger version assuming `\u2200 a \u2208 l\u2082.diff l\u2081, 1 \u2264 a` instead\nof `\u2200 a \u2208 l\u2082, 1 \u2264 a` but this lemma is not yet in `mathlib`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_eq_foldr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.exists_le_of_sum_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.alternating_prod_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.tail_sum", "description": "This relies on `default \u2115 = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.list_prod_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_map_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "