n": "The constant filtration which is equal to `m` for all `i : \u03b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.sigma_finite_filtration", "description": " A measure is \u03c3-finite with respect to filtration if it is \u03c3-finite with respect\nto all the sub-\u03c3-algebra of the filtration.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.sigma_finite_filtration.sigma_finite", "description": " A measure is \u03c3-finite with respect to filtration if it is \u03c3-finite with respect\nto all the sub-\u03c3-algebra of the filtration.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.filtration_of_set_eq_natural", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.strongly_measurable_limit_process'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measurable_set_of_filtration", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measurable_set_filtration_of_set'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measurable_set_filtration_of_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.has_Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.Sup_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.complete_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.limit_process", "description": " Given a process `f` and a filtration `\u2131`, if `f` converges to some `g` almost everywhere and\n`g` is `\u2a06 n, \u2131 n`-measurable, then `limit_process f \u2131 \u03bc` chooses said `g`, else it returns 0.\n\nThis definition is used to phrase the a.e. martingale convergence theorem\n`submartingale.ae_tendsto_limit_process` where an L\u00b9-bounded submartingale `f` adapted to `\u2131`\nconverges to `limit_process f \u2131 \u03bc` `\u03bc`-almost everywhere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration", "description": " A `filtration` on a measurable space `\u03a9` with \u03c3-algebra `m` is a monotone\nsequence of sub-\u03c3-algebras of `m`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.seq", "description": " A `filtration` on a measurable space `\u03a9` with \u03c3-algebra `m` is a monotone\nsequence of sub-\u03c3-algebras of `m`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.mono'", "description": " A `filtration` on a measurable space `\u03a9` with \u03c3-algebra `m` is a monotone\nsequence of sub-\u03c3-algebras of `m`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.le'", "description": " A `filtration` on a measurable space `\u03a9` with \u03c3-algebra `m` is a monotone\nsequence of sub-\u03c3-algebras of `m`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.has_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.has_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.mem_\u2112p_limit_process_of_snorm_bdd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.const_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.coe_fn_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.strongly_measurable_limit_process", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.has_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.sigma_finite_of_sigma_finite_filtration", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.Inf_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.uniform_integrable_condexp_filtration", "description": " Given a integrable function `g`, the conditional expectations of `g` with respect to a\nfiltration is uniformly integrable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration_of_set", "description": " Given a sequence of measurable sets `(s\u2099)`, `filtration_of_set` is the smallest filtration\nsuch that `s\u2099` is measurable with respect to the `n`-the sub-\u03c3-algebra in `filtration_of_set`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_finite_measure.sigma_finite_filtration", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.has_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.natural", "description": " Given a sequence of functions, the natural filtration is the smallest sequence\nof \u03c3-algebras such that that sequence of functions is measurable with respect to\nthe filtration.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.has_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.coe_fn_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.filtration.has_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne_zero_of_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.has_one", "description": "`1` is the multiplicative homomorphism sending all elements to `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.one_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.comp", "description": "Composition of monoid morphisms as a monoid morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom", "description": " `one_hom M N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve one.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : one_hom M N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [one_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to also extend `one_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.to_fun", "description": " `one_hom M N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve one.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : one_hom M N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [one_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to also extend `one_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.map_one'", "description": " `one_hom M N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve one.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : one_hom M N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [one_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to also extend `one_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.congr_fun", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.congr_fun` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.congr_fun", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.congr_fun` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.cancel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.cancel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.add_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.congr_arg", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.congr_arg` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.mul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.coe_inj", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.coe_injective` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.has_neg", "description": " If `f` is an additive monoid homomorphism to an additive commutative group, then `-f` is the\nhomomorphism sending `x` to `-(f x)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom_class.to_fun_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.coe_eq_to_mul_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom_class", "description": " `add_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of addition-preserving homomorphisms.\nYou should declare an instance of this typeclass when you extend `add_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom_class.coe", "description": " `add_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of addition-preserving homomorphisms.\nYou should declare an instance of this typeclass when you extend `add_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom_class.coe_injective'", "description": " `add_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of addition-preserving homomorphisms.\nYou should declare an instance of this typeclass when you extend `add_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom_class.map_add", "description": " `add_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of addition-preserving homomorphisms.\nYou should declare an instance of this typeclass when you extend `add_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.congr_arg", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.congr_arg` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.map_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.map_zsmul", "description": "Additive group homomorphisms preserve integer scaling.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.add_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_zsmul", "description": "Additive group homomorphisms preserve integer scaling.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.cancel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom", "description": " `M \u2192* N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve the `monoid` structure.\n`monoid_hom` is also used for group homomorphisms.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : M \u2192+ N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [monoid_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `monoid_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.to_fun", "description": " `M \u2192* N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve the `monoid` structure.\n`monoid_hom` is also used for group homomorphisms.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : M \u2192+ N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [monoid_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `monoid_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.map_one'", "description": " `M \u2192* N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve the `monoid` structure.\n`monoid_hom` is also used for group homomorphisms.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : M \u2192+ N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [monoid_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `monoid_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.map_mul'", "description": " `M \u2192* N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve the `monoid` structure.\n`monoid_hom` is also used for group homomorphisms.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : M \u2192+ N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [monoid_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `monoid_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.copy", "description": "Copy of a `zero_hom` with a new `to_fun` equal to the old one. Useful to fix\ndefinitional equalities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.map_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom_class", "description": " `monoid_with_zero_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of\n`monoid_with_zero`-preserving homomorphisms.\n\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `monoid_with_zero_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom_class.coe", "description": " `monoid_with_zero_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of\n`monoid_with_zero`-preserving homomorphisms.\n\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `monoid_with_zero_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom_class.coe_injective'", "description": " `monoid_with_zero_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of\n`monoid_with_zero`-preserving homomorphisms.\n\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `monoid_with_zero_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom_class.map_mul", "description": " `monoid_with_zero_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of\n`monoid_with_zero`-preserving homomorphisms.\n\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `monoid_with_zero_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom_class.map_one", "description": " `monoid_with_zero_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of\n`monoid_with_zero`-preserving homomorphisms.\n\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `monoid_with_zero_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom_class.map_zero", "description": " `monoid_with_zero_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of\n`monoid_with_zero`-preserving homomorphisms.\n\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `monoid_with_zero_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom_class", "description": " `add_monoid_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of `add_zero_class`-preserving\nhomomorphisms.\n\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `add_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom_class.coe", "description": " `add_monoid_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of `add_zero_class`-preserving\nhomomorphisms.\n\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `add_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom_class.coe_injective'", "description": " `add_monoid_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of `add_zero_class`-preserving\nhomomorphisms.\n\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `add_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom_class.map_add", "description": " `add_monoid_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of `add_zero_class`-preserving\nhomomorphisms.\n\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `add_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom_class.map_zero", "description": " `add_monoid_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of `add_zero_class`-preserving\nhomomorphisms.\n\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `add_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.cancel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.End.monoid_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom", "description": " `zero_hom M N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve zero.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : zero_hom M N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [zero_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to also extend `zero_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.to_fun", "description": " `zero_hom M N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve zero.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : zero_hom M N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [zero_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to also extend `zero_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.map_zero'", "description": " `zero_hom M N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve zero.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : zero_hom M N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [zero_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to also extend `zero_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "injective_iff_map_eq_zero'", "description": "A homomorphism from an additive group to an additive monoid is injective iff its\nkernel is trivial, stated as an iff on the triviality of the kernel. For the implication, see\n`injective_iff_map_eq_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.of_map_div", "description": "Define a morphism of additive groups given a map which respects ratios.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_zero_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.coe_inj", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.coe_injective` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "neg_add_monoid_hom", "description": "Negation on a commutative additive group, considered as an additive monoid\nhomomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.has_one", "description": "`1` is the homomorphism sending all elements to `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne_zero.of_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.has_coe_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.map_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.map_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.has_add", "description": " Given two additive morphisms `f`, `g` to an additive commutative semigroup, `f + g` is the\nadditive morphism sending `x` to `f x + g x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.comp_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.copy_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.has_mul", "description": " Given two monoid with zero morphisms `f`, `g` to a commutative monoid, `f * g` is the monoid\nwith zero morphism sending `x` to `f x * g x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.zero_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.congr_arg", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.congr_arg` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.one_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.cancel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.coe_copy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.to_mul_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.map_div", "description": "Group homomorphisms preserve division.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.cancel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.comp_assoc", "description": "Composition of monoid homomorphisms is associative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.add_monoid_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.mk'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.has_coe_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom_class", "description": " `monoid_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of `monoid`-preserving homomorphisms.\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom_class.coe", "description": " `monoid_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of `monoid`-preserving homomorphisms.\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom_class.coe_injective'", "description": " `monoid_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of `monoid`-preserving homomorphisms.\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom_class.map_mul", "description": " `monoid_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of `monoid`-preserving homomorphisms.\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom_class.map_one", "description": " `monoid_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of `monoid`-preserving homomorphisms.\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.comp", "description": "Composition of `zero_hom`s as a `zero_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.zero_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_mul_inv", "description": "Group homomorphisms preserve division.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.ext_iff", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.ext_iff` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_add_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.coe_of_map_mul_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.coe_copy_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.has_one", "description": "`1` is the monoid homomorphism sending all elements to `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.neg_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_add_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.has_coe_to_zero_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.to_zero_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "injective_iff_map_eq_one'", "description": " A homomorphism from a group to a monoid is injective iff its kernel is trivial,\nstated as an iff on the triviality of the kernel.\nFor the implication, see `injective_iff_map_eq_one`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.comp_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.map_mul", "description": "If `f` is a monoid homomorphism then `f (a * b) = f a * f b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.map_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.coe_inj", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.coe_injective` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_zpow'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.has_coe_to_zero_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom", "description": " `M \u2192+ N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve the `add_zero_class` structure.\n\n`add_monoid_hom` is also used for group homomorphisms.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : M \u2192+ N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [add_monoid_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `add_monoid_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_fun", "description": " `M \u2192+ N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve the `add_zero_class` structure.\n\n`add_monoid_hom` is also used for group homomorphisms.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : M \u2192+ N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [add_monoid_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `add_monoid_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.map_zero'", "description": " `M \u2192+ N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve the `add_zero_class` structure.\n\n`add_monoid_hom` is also used for group homomorphisms.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : M \u2192+ N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [add_monoid_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `add_monoid_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.map_add'", "description": " `M \u2192+ N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve the `add_zero_class` structure.\n\n`add_monoid_hom` is also used for group homomorphisms.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : M \u2192+ N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [add_monoid_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `add_monoid_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.map_add", "description": "If `f` is an additive monoid homomorphism then `f (a + b) = f a + f b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.has_coe_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom_class.to_one_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.of_map_sub", "description": "Define a morphism of additive groups given a map which respects difference.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom", "description": " `add_hom M N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve addition.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : add_hom M N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [add_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `add_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.to_fun", "description": " `add_hom M N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve addition.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : add_hom M N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [add_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `add_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.map_add'", "description": " `add_hom M N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve addition.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : add_hom M N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [add_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `add_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom_class.to_add_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.End.monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.comp", "description": "Composition of `mul_hom`s as a `mul_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.ext_iff", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.ext_iff` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom_class.to_fun_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.ext_iff", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.ext_iff` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.monoid_with_zero_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_zero_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.comp_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.coe_of_map_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_inv", "description": "Group homomorphisms preserve inverse.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.id", "description": "The identity map from an type with zero to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.sub_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_mul_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom_class.to_mul_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.comp_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.map_exists_right_inv", "description": " Given a monoid homomorphism `f : M \u2192* N` and an element `x : M`, if `x` has a right inverse,\nthen `f x` has a right inverse too. For elements invertible on both sides see `is_unit.map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.congr_arg", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.congr_arg` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_add_hom_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom", "description": " `M \u2192\u2099* N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve multiplication. The `\u2099` in the notation\nstands for \"non-unital\" because it is intended to match the notation for `non_unital_alg_hom` and\n`non_unital_ring_hom`, so a `mul_hom` is a non-unital monoid hom.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : M \u2192\u2099* N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [mul_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `mul_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.to_fun", "description": " `M \u2192\u2099* N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve multiplication. The `\u2099` in the notation\nstands for \"non-unital\" because it is intended to match the notation for `non_unital_alg_hom` and\n`non_unital_ring_hom`, so a `mul_hom` is a non-unital monoid hom.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : M \u2192\u2099* N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [mul_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `mul_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.map_mul'", "description": " `M \u2192\u2099* N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve multiplication. The `\u2099` in the notation\nstands for \"non-unital\" because it is intended to match the notation for `non_unital_alg_hom` and\n`non_unital_ring_hom`, so a `mul_hom` is a non-unital monoid hom.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : M \u2192\u2099* N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [mul_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `mul_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.cancel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.div_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_monoid_hom", "description": "Inversion on a commutative group, considered as a monoid homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.End.add_monoid_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_add_neg", "description": "Additive group homomorphisms preserve subtraction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.comp", "description": "Composition of `one_hom`s as a `one_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_zpow", "description": "Group homomorphisms preserve integer power.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.has_coe_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.coe_copy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom_class.to_monoid_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "injective_iff_map_eq_one", "description": " A homomorphism from a group to a monoid is injective iff its kernel is trivial.\nFor the iff statement on the triviality of the kernel, see `injective_iff_map_eq_one'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom_class", "description": " `mul_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of multiplication-preserving homomorphisms.\n\nYou should declare an instance of this typeclass when you extend `mul_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom_class.coe", "description": " `mul_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of multiplication-preserving homomorphisms.\n\nYou should declare an instance of this typeclass when you extend `mul_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom_class.coe_injective'", "description": " `mul_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of multiplication-preserving homomorphisms.\n\nYou should declare an instance of this typeclass when you extend `mul_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom_class.map_mul", "description": " `mul_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of multiplication-preserving homomorphisms.\n\nYou should declare an instance of this typeclass when you extend `mul_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.End.monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.map_zpow", "description": "Group homomorphisms preserve integer power.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.has_zero", "description": "`0` is the additive homomorphism sending all elements to `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.map_neg", "description": "Additive group homomorphisms preserve negation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom", "description": " `M \u2192*\u2080 N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve\nthe `monoid_with_zero` structure.\n\n`monoid_with_zero_hom` is also used for group homomorphisms.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : M \u2192*\u2080 N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [monoid_with_zero_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `monoid_with_zero_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.to_fun", "description": " `M \u2192*\u2080 N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve\nthe `monoid_with_zero` structure.\n\n`monoid_with_zero_hom` is also used for group homomorphisms.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : M \u2192*\u2080 N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [monoid_with_zero_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `monoid_with_zero_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.map_zero'", "description": " `M \u2192*\u2080 N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve\nthe `monoid_with_zero` structure.\n\n`monoid_with_zero_hom` is also used for group homomorphisms.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : M \u2192*\u2080 N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [monoid_with_zero_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `monoid_with_zero_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.map_one'", "description": " `M \u2192*\u2080 N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve\nthe `monoid_with_zero` structure.\n\n`monoid_with_zero_hom` is also used for group homomorphisms.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : M \u2192*\u2080 N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [monoid_with_zero_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `monoid_with_zero_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.map_mul'", "description": " `M \u2192*\u2080 N` is the type of functions `M \u2192 N` that preserve\nthe `monoid_with_zero` structure.\n\n`monoid_with_zero_hom` is also used for group homomorphisms.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : M \u2192*\u2080 N)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [monoid_with_zero_hom_class F M N] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `monoid_with_zero_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.id", "description": "The identity map from a type with multiplication to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.coe_copy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.coe_copy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.congr_fun", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.congr_fun` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.has_mul", "description": " Given two monoid morphisms `f`, `g` to a commutative monoid, `f * g` is the monoid morphism\nsending `x` to `f x * g x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_zsmul.aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.coe_inj", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.coe_injective` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.neg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.coe_inj", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.coe_injective` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.coe_copy_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.one_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.of_map_add_neg", "description": "Makes an additive group homomorphism from a proof that the map preserves\nthe operation `\u03bb a b, a + -b`. See also `add_monoid_hom.of_map_sub` for a version using\n`\u03bb a b, a - b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.coe_copy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "injective_iff_map_eq_zero", "description": "A homomorphism from an additive group to an additive monoid is injective iff\nits kernel is trivial. For the iff statement on the triviality of the kernel,\nsee `injective_iff_map_eq_zero'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_div", "description": "Group homomorphisms preserve division.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.map_sub", "description": "Additive group homomorphisms preserve subtraction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.cancel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.of_map_mul_inv", "description": " Makes a group homomorphism from a proof that the map preserves right division `\u03bb x y, x * y\u207b\u00b9`.\nSee also `monoid_hom.of_map_div` for a version using `\u03bb x y, x / y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.End.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.to_zero_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.copy", "description": "Copy of an `add_hom` with a new `to_fun` equal to the old one. Useful to fix\ndefinitional equalities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.End", "description": "The monoid of endomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.map_exists_right_neg", "description": "Given an add_monoid homomorphism `f : M \u2192+ N` and an element `x : M`, if `x` has\na right inverse, then `f x` has a right inverse too.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.congr_fun", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.congr_fun` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.comp_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.congr_arg", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.congr_arg` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.mul_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.ext_iff", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.ext_iff` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.coe_inj", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.coe_injective` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.copy", "description": " Copy of a `monoid_hom` with a new `to_fun` equal to the old one. Useful to fix\ndefinitional equalities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.cancel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.add_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.id", "description": "The identity map from a monoid to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.coe_eq_to_add_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.map_add_neg", "description": "Additive group homomorphisms preserve subtraction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.to_monoid_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.id", "description": "The identity map from a monoid_with_zero to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.coe_of_map_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.has_mul", "description": " Given two mul morphisms `f`, `g` to a commutative semigroup, `f * g` is the mul morphism\nsending `x` to `f x * g x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.coe_eq_to_zero_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.map_zsmul'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.comp_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_add_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.has_coe_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.add_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne_one_of_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.coe_inj", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.coe_injective` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.ext_iff", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.ext_iff` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.coe_of_map_add_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.cancel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.coe_eq_to_monoid_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.ext_iff", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.ext_iff` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.map_mul_inv", "description": "Group homomorphisms preserve division.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.congr_arg", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.congr_arg` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.map_exists_left_neg", "description": "Given an add_monoid homomorphism `f : M \u2192+ N` and an element `x : M`, if `x` has\na left inverse, then `f x` has a left inverse too. For elements invertible on both sides see\n`is_add_unit.map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.copy_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.mk'", "description": "Makes an additive group homomorphism from a proof that the map preserves addition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.to_mul_hom_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.copy_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_zero_hom_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_div'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.congr_fun", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.congr_fun` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne_zero.of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.copy", "description": "Copy of an `add_monoid_hom` with a new `to_fun` equal to the old one. Useful to fix\ndefinitional equalities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.coe_eq_to_zero_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.comp", "description": "Composition of `monoid_with_zero_hom`s as a `monoid_with_zero_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.copy", "description": " Copy of a `monoid_hom` with a new `to_fun` equal to the old one. Useful to fix\ndefinitional equalities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.mk'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_ne_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.coe_copy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.cancel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.coe_eq_to_one_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.one_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.mul_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.coe_copy_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.to_one_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom_class", "description": " `one_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of one-preserving homomorphisms.\nYou should extend this typeclass when you extend `one_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom_class.coe", "description": " `one_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of one-preserving homomorphisms.\nYou should extend this typeclass when you extend `one_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom_class.coe_injective'", "description": " `one_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of one-preserving homomorphisms.\nYou should extend this typeclass when you extend `one_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom_class.map_one", "description": " `one_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of one-preserving homomorphisms.\nYou should extend this typeclass when you extend `one_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.cancel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.to_one_hom_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.has_coe_to_one_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_sub'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.has_zero", "description": "`0` is the homomorphism sending all elements to `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.has_sub", "description": " If `f` and `g` are monoid homomorphisms to an additive commutative group, then `f - g`\nis the homomorphism sending `x` to `(f x) - (g x)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.has_coe_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.map_inv", "description": "Group homomorphisms preserve inverse.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.comp_assoc", "description": "Composition of additive monoid homomorphisms is associative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.coe_copy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom_class", "description": " `zero_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of zero-preserving homomorphisms.\n\nYou should extend this typeclass when you extend `zero_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom_class.coe", "description": " `zero_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of zero-preserving homomorphisms.\n\nYou should extend this typeclass when you extend `zero_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom_class.coe_injective'", "description": " `zero_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of zero-preserving homomorphisms.\n\nYou should extend this typeclass when you extend `zero_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom_class.map_zero", "description": " `zero_hom_class F M N` states that `F` is a type of zero-preserving homomorphisms.\n\nYou should extend this typeclass when you extend `zero_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.comp_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.congr_fun", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.congr_fun` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.map_exists_left_inv", "description": " Given a monoid homomorphism `f : M \u2192* N` and an element `x : M`, if `x` has a left inverse,\nthen `f x` has a left inverse too. For elements invertible on both sides see `is_unit.map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_neg", "description": "Additive group homomorphisms preserve negation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.to_monoid_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_eq_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.id", "description": "The identity map from an additive monoid to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.mk'", "description": "Makes a group homomorphism from a proof that the map preserves multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.has_add", "description": " Given two additive monoid morphisms `f`, `g` to an additive commutative monoid, `f + g` is the\nadditive monoid morphism sending `x` to `f x + g x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.to_mul_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_hom.one_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.has_div", "description": " If `f` and `g` are monoid homomorphisms to a commutative group, then `f / g` is the homomorphism\nsending `x` to `(f x) / (g x)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.comp", "description": "Composition of additive monoid morphisms as an additive monoid morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.cancel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.comp_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.to_one_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.comp_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_monoi