_fun", "description": "Deprecated: use `fun_like.congr_fun` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.to_monoid_hom_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom_class.to_zero_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.map_zpow'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.has_coe_to_mul_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.map_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.orientation_ne_iff_eq_neg", "description": " Given a basis, an orientation equals the negation of that given by that basis if and only\nif it does not equal that given by that basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.orientation", "description": "The orientation given by a basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.ne_iff_eq_neg", "description": " If the index type has cardinality equal to the finite dimension, an orientation equals the\nnegation of another orientation if and only if they are not equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.orientation_comp_linear_equiv_eq_iff_det_pos", "description": " Composing a basis with a linear equiv gives the same orientation if and only if the\ndeterminant is positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.reindex_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.orientation_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.oriented", "description": "A type class fixing an orientation of a module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.oriented.positive_orientation", "description": "A type class fixing an orientation of a module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.abs_det_adjust_to_orientation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.eq_or_eq_neg", "description": " If the index type has cardinality equal to the finite dimension, any two orientations are\nequal or negations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation", "description": " An orientation of a module, intended to be used when `\u03b9` is a `fintype` with the same\ncardinality as a basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.map", "description": "An equivalence between modules implies an equivalence between orientations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.some_basis_orientation", "description": "`some_basis` gives a basis with the required orientation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.orientation_comp_linear_equiv_eq_neg_iff_det_neg", "description": " Composing a basis with a linear equiv gives the negation of that orientation if and only if\nthe determinant is negative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.orientation_units_smul", "description": " The orientation given by a basis derived using `units_smul`, in terms of the product of those\nunits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.orientation_eq_or_eq_neg", "description": "Given a basis, any orientation equals the orientation given by that basis or its negation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.adjust_to_orientation_apply_eq_or_eq_neg", "description": " Every basis vector from `adjust_to_orientation` is either that from the original basis or its\nnegation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.map_eq_det_inv_smul", "description": " The value of `orientation.map` when the index type has cardinality equal to the finite\ndimension, in terms of `f.det`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.map_eq_iff_det_pos", "description": " If the index type has cardinality equal to the finite dimension, composing an alternating\nmap with the same linear equiv on each argument gives the same orientation if and only if the\ndeterminant is positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_empty.oriented", "description": "A module is canonically oriented with respect to an empty index type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.reindex", "description": "An