 "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "symm_diff_triangle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "symm_diff_eq_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "symm_diff_le_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bihimp_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sup_himp_bihimp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bihimp_hnot_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sup_sdiff_symm_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_eq_integral_of_forall_compl_eq_zero", "description": " If a function vanishes on `s\u1d9c`, then its integral on `s` coincides with its integral on the\nwhole space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_Ioc_eq_integral_Ioo'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integral_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integral_with_density_eq_integral_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_eq_zero_of_ae_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_pos_iff_support_of_nonneg_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_indicator_const_Lp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.integral_sub_linear_is_o_ae", "description": " Fundamental theorem of calculus for set integrals, `nhds_within` version: if `\u03bc` is a locally\nfinite measure, `f` is continuous on a measurable set `t`, and `a \u2208 t`, then `\u222b x in (s i), f x \u2202\u03bc =\n\u03bc (s i) \u2022 f a + o(\u03bc (s i))` at `li` provided that `s i` tends to `(\ud835\udcdd[t] a).small_sets` along `li`.\nSince `\u03bc (s i)` is an `\u211d\u22650\u221e` number, we use `(\u03bc (s i)).to_real` in the actual statement.\n\nOften there is a good formula for `(\u03bc (s i)).to_real`, so the formalization can take an optional\nargument `m` with this formula and a proof `of `(\u03bb i, (\u03bc (s i)).to_real) =\u1da0[li] m`. Without these\narguments, `m i = (\u03bc (s i)).to_real` is used in the output.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_Union_of_summable_integral_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.norm_set_integral_le_of_norm_le_const'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_union_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving.set_integral_preimage_emb", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_Ici_eq_integral_Ioi'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integral_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_indicator_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_le_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at.integral_sub_linear_is_o_ae", "description": " Fundamental theorem of calculus for set integrals, `nhds_within` version: if `\u03bc` is a locally\nfinite measure and `f` is an almost everywhere measurable function that is continuous at a point `a`\nwithin a measurable set `t`, then `\u222b x in s i, f x \u2202\u03bc = \u03bc (s i) \u2022 f a + o(\u03bc (s i))` at a filter `li`\nprovided that `s i` tends to `(\ud835\udcdd[t] a).small_sets` along `li`.  Since `\u03bc (s i)` is an `\u211d\u22650\u221e`\nnumber, we use `(\u03bc (s i)).to_real` in the actual statement.\n\nOften there is a good formula for `(\u03bc (s i)).to_real`, so the formalization can take an optional\nargument `m` with this formula and a proof `of `(\u03bb i, (\u03bc (s i)).to_real) =\u1da0[li] m`. Without these\narguments, `m i = (\u03bc (s i)).to_real` is used in the output.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_Ico_eq_integral_Ioo'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Lp_to_Lp_restrict_smul", "description": " For `f : Lp E p \u03bc`, we can define an element of `Lp E p (\u03bc.restrict s)` by\n`(Lp.mem_\u2112p f).restrict s).to_Lp f`. This map commutes with scalar multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_nonneg_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_Union_of_summable_norm_restrict", "description": " If `s` is a countable family of compact sets, `f` is a continuous function, and the sequence\n`\u2016f.restrict (s i)\u2016 * \u03bc (s i)` is summable, then `f` is integrable on the union of the `s i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_eq_of_subset_of_forall_diff_eq_zero", "description": " If a function vanishes on `t \\ s` with `s \u2286 t`, then its integrals on `s`\nand `t` coincide if `t` is measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_Icc_eq_integral_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_union_eq_left_of_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integral_re_add_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integral_coe_re_add_coe_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_map_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_embedding.set_integral_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.of_real_set_integral_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.integral_sub_linear_is_o_ae", "description": " Fundamental theorem of calculus for set integrals, `nhds` version: if `\u03bc` is a locally finite\nmeasure and `f` is an almost everywhere measurable function that is continuous at a point `a`, then\n`\u222b x in s i, f x \u2202\u03bc = \u03bc (s i) \u2022 f a + o(\u03bc (s i))` at `li` provided that `s` tends to\n`(\ud835\udcdd a).small_sets` along `li.  Since `\u03bc (s i)` is an `\u211d\u22650\u221e` number, we use `(\u03bc (s i)).to_real` in\nthe actual statement.\n\nOften there is a good formula for `(\u03bc (s i)).to_real`, so the formalization can take an optional\nargument `m` with this formula and a proof `of `(\u03bb i, (\u03bc (s i)).to_real) =\u1da0[li] m`. Without these\narguments, `m i = (\u03bc (s i)).to_real` is used in the output.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closed_embedding.set_integral_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.has_sum_integral_Union_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_Ico_eq_integral_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_inter_add_diff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_eq_zero_of_forall_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_of_summable_norm_restrict", "description": " If `s` is a countable family of compact sets covering `\u03b1`, `f` is a continuous function, and\nthe sequence `\u2016f.restrict (s i)\u2016 * \u03bc (s i)` is summable, then `f` is integrable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_union_eq_left_of_ae_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_Icc_eq_integral_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_Ioc_eq_integral_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_nonpos_of_ae_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.integral_comp_L1_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.simple_func_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_eq_of_subset_of_ae_diff_eq_zero", "description": " If a function vanishes almost everywhere on `t \\ s` with `s \u2286 t`, then its integrals on `s`\nand `t` coincide if `t` is null-measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_nonneg_of_ae_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_finset_bUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.tendsto_set_integral_of_monotone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.integral_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_inter_add_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set_integral_with_density_eq_set_integral_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.integral_comp_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.integral_comp_Lp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_indicator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_add_compl\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_trim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_nonpos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integral_conj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_Ici_eq_integral_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Lp_to_Lp_restrict_add", "description": " For `f : Lp E p \u03bc`, we can define an element of `Lp E p (\u03bc.restrict s)` by\n`(Lp.mem_\u2112p f).restrict s).to_Lp f`. This map is additive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_congr\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_congr_set_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_union_eq_left_of_forall\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.set_integral_comp_Lp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.norm_set_integral_le_of_norm_le_const_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.of_real_set_integral_one_of_measure_ne_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_gt_gt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_nonpos_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_congr_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integral_of_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_ge_of_const_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_mono_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving.set_integral_image_emb", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Lp_to_Lp_restrict_clm", "description": " Continuous linear map sending a function of `Lp F p \u03bc` to the same function in\n`Lp F p (\u03bc.restrict s)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_eq_integral_of_ae_compl_eq_zero", "description": " If a function vanishes almost everywhere on `s\u1d9c`, then its integral on `s`\ncoincides with its integral on the whole space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_eq_of_subset_of_ae_diff_eq_zero_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_norm_eq_pos_sub_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_Iic_eq_integral_Iio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_neg_eq_set_integral_nonpos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set_integral_re_add_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_le_lintegral_thickened_indicator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.Lp_to_Lp_restrict_clm_coe_fn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_nonpos_of_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.norm_Lp_to_Lp_restrict_le", "description": " For `f : Lp E p \u03bc`, we can define an element of `Lp E p (\u03bc.restrict s)` by\n`(Lp.mem_\u2112p f).restrict s).to_Lp f`. This map is non-expansive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone.tendsto_set_integral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fst_integral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_eq_zero_iff_of_nonneg_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_le_lintegral_thickened_indicator_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.integral_comp_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_piecewise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set_integral_with_density_eq_set_integral_smul\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.integral_sub_linear_is_o_ae", "description": " Fundamental theorem of calculus for set integrals: if `\u03bc` is a measure that is finite at a\nfilter `l` and `f` is a measurable function that has a finite limit `b` at `l \u2293 \u03bc.ae`, then `\u222b x in\ns i, f x \u2202\u03bc = \u03bc (s i) \u2022 b + o(\u03bc (s i))` at a filter `li` provided that `s i` tends to `l.small_sets`\nalong `li`. Since `\u03bc (s i)` is an `\u211d\u22650\u221e` number, we use `(\u03bc (s i)).to_real` in the actual statement.\n\nOften there is a good formula for `(\u03bc (s i)).to_real`, so the formalization can take an optional\nargument `m` with this formula and a proof `of `(\u03bb i, (\u03bc (s i)).to_real) =\u1da0[li] m`. Without these\narguments, `m i = (\u03bc (s i)).to_real` is used in the output.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integral_with_density_eq_integral_smul\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_Union_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_add_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathli