niform_on_fun.has_basis_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.uniform_group", "description": "If `G` is a uniform group, then `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 G` is a uniform group as well.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.has_basis_nhds_one_of_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.has_basis_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.has_basis_nhds_zero_of_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.uniform_add_group", "description": "If `G` is a uniform additive group, then `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 G` is a uniform additive group\nas well.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.uniform_add_group", "description": "Let `\ud835\udd16 : set (set \u03b1)`. If `G` is a uniform additive group, then `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] G` is a\nuniform additive group as well.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.uniform_group", "description": " Let `\ud835\udd16 : set (set \u03b1)`. If `G` is a uniform group, then `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] G` is a uniform group as\nwell.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.has_basis_nhds_zero_of_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.has_continuous_smul_induced_of_image_bounded", "description": " Let `E` be a TVS, `\ud835\udd16 : set (set \u03b1)` and `H` a submodule of `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] E`. If the image of any\n`S \u2208 \ud835\udd16` by any `u \u2208 H` is bounded (in the sense of `bornology.is_vonN_bounded`), then `H`,\nequipped with the topology of `\ud835\udd16`-convergence, is a TVS.\n\nFor convenience, we don't literally ask for `H : submodule (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] E)`. Instead, we prove the\nresult for any vector space `H` equipped with a linear inducing to `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] E`, which is often\neasier to use. We also state the `submodule` version as\n`uniform_on_fun.has_continuous_smul_submodule_of_image_bounded`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.has_basis_nhds_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.Sup_convergence_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Inf_convergence_class", "description": " We say that `\u03b1` is an `Inf_convergence_class` if the following holds. Let `f : \u03b9 \u2192 \u03b1` be a\nmonotone function, let `a : \u03b1` be a greatest lower bound of `set.range f`. Then `f x` tends to `\ud835\udcdd a`\nas `x \u2192 -\u221e` (formally, at the filter `filter.at_bot`). We require this for `\u03b9 = (s : set \u03b1)`,\n`f = coe` in the definition, then prove it for any `f` in `tendsto_at_bot_is_glb`.\n\nThis property holds for linear orders with order topology as well as their products.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Inf_convergence_class.tendsto_coe_at_bot_is_glb", "description": " We say that `\u03b1` is an `Inf_convergence_class` if the following holds. Let `f : \u03b9 \u2192 \u03b1` be a\nmonotone function, let `a : \u03b1` be a greatest lower bound of `set.range f`. Then `f x` tends to `\ud835\udcdd a`\nas `x \u2192 -\u221e` (formally, at the filter `filter.at_bot`). We require this for `\u03b9 = (s : set \u03b1)`,\n`f = coe` in the definition, then prove it for any `f` in `tendsto_at_bot_is_glb`.\n\nThis property holds for linear orders with order topology as well as their products.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Sup_convergence_class", "description": " We say that `\u03b1` is a `Sup_convergence_class` if the following holds. Let `f : \u03b9 \u2192 \u03b1` be a\nmonotone function, let `a : \u03b1` be a least upper bound of `set.range f`. Then `f x` tends to `\ud835\udcdd a` as\n`x \u2192 \u221e` (formally, at the filter `filter.at_top`). We require this for `\u03b9 = (s : set \u03b1)`, `f = coe`\nin the definition, then prove it for any `f` in `tendsto_at_top_is_lub`.\n\nThis property holds for linear orders with order topology as well as their products.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Sup_convergence_class.tendsto_coe_at_top_is_lub", "description": " We say that `\u03b1` is a `Sup_convergence_class` if the following holds. Let `f : \u03b9 \u2192 \u03b1` be a\nmonotone function, let `a : \u03b1` be a least upper bound of `set.range f`. Then `f x` tends to `\ud835\udcdd a` as\n`x \u2192 \u221e` (formally, at the filter `filter.at_top`). We require this for `\u03b9 = (s : set \u03b1)`, `f = coe`\nin the definition, then prove it for any `f` in `tendsto_at_top_is_lub`.\n\nThis property holds for linear orders with order topology as well as their products.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_glb_of_tendsto_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.Inf_convergence_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_order.Inf_convergence_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_at_top_is_lub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_at_bot_csupr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_at_bot_is_glb", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_order.Sup_convergence_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_lub_of_tendsto_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_lub_of_tendsto_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_at_top_csupr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infi_eq_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_of_monotone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_at_bot_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_at_bot_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_at_top_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_iff_tendsto_subseq_of_monotone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.Inf_convergence_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_at_top_is_glb", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_at_top_cinfi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.ge_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infi_eq_infi_subseq_of_monotone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.Sup_convergence_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "supr_eq_supr_subseq_of_monotone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "supr_eq_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.le_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone.le_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_glb_of_tendsto_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_at_top_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone.ge_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.Inf_convergence_class'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.Sup_convergence_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.Inf_convergence_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_at_bot_is_lub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.Sup_convergence_class'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_at_bot_cinfi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.left_coset_equiv_subgroup", "description": "The natural bijection between a left coset `g * s` and `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_left_add_coset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_coset_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_add_coset_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.card_dvd_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.quotient_equiv_prod_of_le'_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.exists_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.quotient_add_subgroup_of_embedding_of_le", "description": "If `s \u2264 t`, then there is an embedding\n  `s \u29f8 H.add_subgroup_of s \u21aa t \u29f8 H.add_subgroup_of t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.quotient_equiv_prod_of_le'", "description": " If `H \u2264 K`, then `G/H \u2243 G/K \u00d7 K/H` constructively, using the provided right inverse\nof the quotient map `G \u2192 G/K`. The classical version is `quotient_equiv_prod_of_le`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.group_equiv_quotient_times_subgroup", "description": "A (non-canonical) bijection between a group `\u03b1` and the product `(\u03b1/s) \u00d7 s`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_left_add_coset_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.eq_class_eq_left_coset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.subgroup.has_quotient", "description": "`\u03b1 \u29f8 s` is the quotient type representing the left cosets of `s`.  If `s` is a\nnormal subgroup, `\u03b1 \u29f8 s` is a group", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_add_coset_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.exists_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.card_quotient_right_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.left_rel_decidable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.quotient_equiv_prod_of_le_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.mk", "description": "The canonical map from an `add_group` `\u03b1` to the quotient `\u03b1 \u29f8 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.mk_out'_eq_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.left_coset_equiv_add_subgroup", "description": "The natural bijection between the cosets `g + s` and `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_coset_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.right_rel_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.quotient_infi_embedding_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_left_coset_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.right_rel", "description": " The equivalence relation corresponding to the partition of a group by right cosets of a\nsubgroup.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.right_coset_equiv_subgroup", "description": "The natural bijection between a right coset `s * g` and `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.card_quotient_dvd_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.right_coset_equiv_add_subgroup", "description": "The natural bijection between the cosets `s + g` and `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_coset_mem_left_coset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.mk", "description": "The canonical map from a group `\u03b1` to the quotient `\u03b1 \u29f8 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.preimage_image_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.quotient_infi_embedding_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.card_dvd_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.induction_on'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.left_rel_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.preimage_mk_equiv_subgroup_times_set", "description": " If `s` is a subgroup of the group `\u03b1`, and `t` is a subset of `\u03b1 \u29f8 s`, then there is a\n(typically non-canonical) bijection between the preimage of `t` in `\u03b1` and the product `s \u00d7 t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normal_iff_eq_add_cosets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normal_of_eq_cosets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orbit_add_subgroup_zero_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_own_right_coset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.has_quotient.quotient.has_coe_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "library_note.use has_coe_t", "description": "We use the class `has_coe_t` instead of `has_coe` if the first argument is a variable,\nor if the second argument is a variable not occurring in the first.\nUsing `has_coe` would cause looping of type-class inference. See\n<https://leanprover.zulipchat.com/#narrow/stream/113488-general/topic/remove.20all.20instances.20with.20variable.20domain>", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.left_rel_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_add_coset_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.mk_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.quotient_add_subgroup_of_map_of_le_apply_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_add_coset_equivalence_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.quotient_infi_add_subgroup_of_embedding_apply_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_add_coset", "description": "The left coset `a+s` for an element `a : \u03b1`\nand a subset `s : set \u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.quotient_subgroup_of_map_of_le_apply_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_coset_equivalence", "description": "Equality of two left cosets `a * s` and `b * s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_right_coset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.add_group_equiv_quotient_times_add_subgroup", "description": "A (non-canonical) bijection between an add_group `\u03b1` and the product `(\u03b1/s) \u00d7 s`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_right_coset_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_add_coset_mem_left_add_coset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_coset_right_coset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_left_coset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_coset", "description": "The left coset `a * s` for an element `a : \u03b1` and a subset `s : set \u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.right_rel_decidable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.preimage_mk_equiv_add_subgroup_times_set", "description": "If `s` is a subgroup of the additive group `\u03b1`, and `t` is a subset of `\u03b1 \u29f8 s`, then\nthere is a (typically non-canonical) bijection between the preimage of `t` in `\u03b1` and the product\n`s \u00d7 t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_coset", "description": "The right coset `s * a` for an element `a : \u03b1` and a subset `s : set \u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normal_of_eq_add_cosets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_right_coset_right_coset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.quotient_right_rel_equiv_quotient_left_rel", "description": "Right cosets are in bijection with left cosets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.card_quotient_dvd_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.card_dvd_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.quotient_subgroup_of_embedding_of_le_apply_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.right_rel_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.quotient_equiv_of_eq", "description": "If two subgroups `M` and `N` of `G` are equal, their quotients are in bijection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_add_coset_right_add_coset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.quotient_lift_on_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_cosets_of_normal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.quotient_map_of_le_apply_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.left_rel", "description": "The equivalence relation corresponding to the partition of a group by left cosets\nof a subgroup.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.quotient_infi_subgroup_of_embedding_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_right_add_coset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_own_left_coset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.out_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.left_rel_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.quotient_equiv_sum_of_le'_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.card_quotient_right_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.quotient_infi_embedding_apply_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orbit_add_subgroup_eq_right_coset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.quotient_infi_subgroup_of_embedding", "description": "The natural embedding `H \u29f8 (\u2a05 i, f i).subgroup_of H \u21aa \u03a0 i, H \u29f8 (f i).subgroup_of H`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_left_add_coset_left_add_coset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.induction_on'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.quotient_equiv_sum_of_le", "description": "If `H \u2264 K`, then `G/H \u2243 G/K \u00d7 K/H` nonconstructively.\nThe cons