"", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module_hom.add_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module_equiv.to_equiv", "description": "View an equivalence of Lie modules as a type level equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module_equiv.to_equiv_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_skew", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_hom.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.X_pow_sub_one_dvd_prod_cyclotomic", "description": " If `m` is a proper divisor of `n`, then `X ^ m - 1` divides\n`\u220f i in nat.proper_divisors n, cyclotomic i R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.map_cyclotomic", "description": "The definition of `cyclotomic n R` commutes with any ring homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic'_ne_zero", "description": "`cyclotomic' n R` is different from `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.X_pow_sub_one_mul_prod_cyclotomic_eq_X_pow_sub_one_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_prime_pow_eq_geom_sum", "description": " If `p ^ k` is a prime power, then\n`cyclotomic (p ^ (n + 1)) R = \u2211 i in range p, (X ^ (p ^ n)) ^ i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic'_eq_X_pow_sub_one_div", "description": " If there is a primitive `n`-th root of unity in `K`, then\n`cyclotomic' n K = (X ^ k - 1) /\u2098 (\u220f i in nat.proper_divisors k, cyclotomic' i K)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.degree_cyclotomic'", "description": "The degree of `cyclotomic' n R` is `totient n` if there is a primitive root of unity in `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_eq_X_pow_sub_one_div", "description": " We have\n`cyclotomic n R = (X ^ k - 1) /\u2098 (\u220f i in nat.proper_divisors k, cyclotomic i K)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_ne_zero", "description": "`cyclotomic n R` is different from `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.int_cyclotomic_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.roots_of_cyclotomic", "description": "The roots of `cyclotomic' n R` are the primitive `n`-th roots of unity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.unique_int_coeff_of_cycl", "description": " If `K` is of characteristic `0` and there is a primitive `n`-th root of unity in `K`,\nthen `cyclotomic n K` comes from a unique polynomial with integer coefficients.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_dvd_geom_sum_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coprime_of_root_cyclotomic", "description": " If `(a : \u2115)` is a root of `cyclotomic n (zmod p)`, where `p` is a prime, then `a` and `p` are\ncoprime.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_prime_mul_X_sub_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic.monic", "description": "`cyclotomic n` is monic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.int_cyclotomic_rw", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic'_two", "description": "The second modified cyclotomic polyomial is `X + 1` if the characteristic of `R` is not `2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic", "description": "The `n`-th cyclotomic polynomial with coefficients in `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_coeff_zero", "description": "The constant term of `cyclotomic n R` is `1` if `2 \u2264 n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.prod_cyclotomic'_eq_X_pow_sub_one", "description": " If there is a primitive `n`-th root of unity in `K`, then\n`\u220f i in nat.divisors n, cyclotomic' i K = X ^ n - 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic.is_primitive", "description": "`cyclotomic n` is primitive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic'_one", "description": "The first modified cyclotomic polyomial is `X - 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.X_pow_sub_one_eq_prod", "description": " If there is a primitive `n`th root of unity in `K`, then `X ^ n - 1 = \u220f (X - \u03bc)`, where `\u03bc`\nvaries over the `n`-th roots of unity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.int_cyclotomic_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_cyclotomic'", "description": " The natural degree of `cyclotomic' n R` is `totient n` if there is a primitive root of\nunity in `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic'_zero", "description": "The zeroth modified cyclotomic polyomial is `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic'.monic", "description": "`cyclotomic' n R` is monic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic.eval_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_zero", "description": "The zeroth cyclotomic polyomial is `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_eq_prod_X_pow_sub_one_pow_moebius", "description": "`cyclotomic n R` can be expressed as a product in a fraction field of `R[X]`\n using M\u00f6bius inversion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_three", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.X_pow_sub_one_splits", "description": "If there is a primitive `n`-th root of unity in `K`, then `X ^ n - 1`splits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.order_of_root_cyclotomic_dvd", "description": " If `(a : \u2115)` is a root of `cyclotomic n (zmod p)`, then the multiplicative order of `a` modulo\n`p` divides `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.degree_cyclotomic_pos", "description": "The degree of `cyclotomic n R` is positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic'", "description": " The modified `n`-th cyclotomic polynomial with coefficients in `R`, it is the usual cyclotomic\npolynomial if there is a primitive `n`-th root of unity in `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.X_pow_sub_one_mul_cyclotomic_dvd_X_pow_sub_one_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic.dvd_X_pow_sub_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.eq_cyclotomic_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.prod_cyclotomic_eq_X_pow_sub_one", "description": "`\u220f i in nat.divisors n, cyclotomic i R = X ^ n - 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.int_coeff_of_cyclotomic'", "description": " If there is a primitive `n`-th root of unity in `K`, then `cyclotomic' n K` comes from a\nmonic polynomial with integer coefficients.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_eq_prod_X_sub_primitive_roots", "description": " If there is a primitive `n`-th root of unity in `K`, then\n`cyclotomic n K = \u220f \u03bc in primitive_roots n R, (X - C \u03bc)`. In particular,\n`cyclotomic n K = cyclotomic' n K`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_prime", "description": "If `p` is prime, then `cyclotomic p R = \u2211 i in range p, X ^ i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.degree_cyclotomic", "description": "The degree of `cyclotomic n` is `totient n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_prime_pow_mul_X_pow_sub_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_one", "description": "The first cyclotomic polyomial is `X - 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.prod_cyclotomic_eq_geom_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic'_splits", "description": "`cyclotomic' n K` splits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_cyclotomic", "description": "The natural degree of `cyclotomic n` is `totient n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.map_cyclotomic_int", "description": "`cyclotomic n R` comes from `cyclotomic n \u2124`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.norm_set_to_L1s_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.set_to_simple_func_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.set_to_L1s_clm_smul_left'", "description": "", "p