tion": "Lebesgue dominated convergence theorem provides sufficient conditions under which almost\n everywhere convergence of a sequence of functions implies the convergence of their image by\n `set_to_fun`.\n We could weaken the condition `bound_integrable` to require `has_finite_integral bound \u03bc` instead\n (i.e. not requiring that `bound` is measurable), but in all applications proving integrability\n is easier.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.set_to_L1_zero_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.set_to_simple_func_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.norm_set_to_L1_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.set_to_L1s_clm_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.set_to_simple_func_zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.set_to_L1_add_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.set_to_L1s_smul_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_to_fun_to_L1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.continuous_on_set_to_fun_of_dominated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.set_to_simple_func_mono_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.set_to_L1_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_to_fun_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.fin_meas_additive.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_to_fun_congr_measure_of_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.set_to_L1s_add_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.dominated_fin_meas_additive.eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.set_to_L1_zero_left", "description"