relation `pre_envel_group_rel` is the `Prop`-valued version,\nwhich is used to define `envel_group` itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group_rel'.symm", "description": "Relations for the enveloping group. This is a type-valued relation because\n`to_envel_group.map_aux.well_def` inducts on it to show `to_envel_group.map`\nis well-defined.  The relation `pre_envel_group_rel` is the `Prop`-valued version,\nwhich is used to define `envel_group` itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group_rel'.trans", "description": "Relations for the enveloping group. This is a type-valued relation because\n`to_envel_group.map_aux.well_def` inducts on it to show `to_envel_group.map`\nis well-defined.  The relation `pre_envel_group_rel` is the `Prop`-valued version,\nwhich is used to define `envel_group` itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group_rel'.congr_mul", "description": "Relations for the enveloping group. This is a type-valued relation because\n`to_envel_group.map_aux.well_def` inducts on it to show `to_envel_group.map`\nis well-defined.  The relation `pre_envel_group_rel` is the `Prop`-valued version,\nwhich is used to define `envel_group` itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group_rel'.congr_inv", "description": "Relations for the enveloping group. This is a type-valued relation because\n`to_envel_group.map_aux.well_def` inducts on it to show `to_envel_group.map`\nis well-defined.  The relation `pre_envel_group_rel` is the `Prop`-valued version,\nwhich is used to define `envel_group` itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group_rel'.assoc", "description": "Relations for the enveloping group. This is a type-valued relation because\n`to_envel_group.map_aux.well_def` inducts on it to show `to_envel_group.map`\nis well-defined.  The relation `pre_envel_group_rel` is the `Prop`-valued version,\nwhich is used to define `envel_group` itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group_rel'.one_mul", "description": "Relations for the enveloping group. This is a type-valued relation because\n`to_envel_group.map_aux.well_def` inducts on it to show `to_envel_group.map`\nis well-defined.  The relation `pre_envel_group_rel` is the `Prop`-valued version,\nwhich is used to define `envel_group` itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group_rel'.mul_one", "description": "Relations for the enveloping group. This is a type-valued relation because\n`to_envel_group.map_aux.well_def` inducts on it to show `to_envel_group.map`\nis well-defined.  The relation `pre_envel_group_rel` is the `Prop`-valued version,\nwhich is used to define `envel_group` itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group_rel'.mul_left_inv", "description": "Relations for the enveloping group. This is a type-valued relation because\n`to_envel_group.map_aux.well_def` inducts on it to show `to_envel_group.map`\nis well-defined.  The relation `pre_envel_group_rel` is the `Prop`-valued version,\nwhich is used to define `envel_group` itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group_rel'.act_incl", "description": "Relations for the enveloping group. This is a type-valued relation because\n`to_envel_group.map_aux.well_def` inducts on it to show `to_envel_group.map`\nis well-defined.  The relation `pre_envel_group_rel` is the `Prop`-valued version,\nwhich is used to define `envel_group` itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.to_envel_group.univ", "description": "Given a homomorphism from a rack to a group, it factors through the enveloping group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.to_envel_group.univ_uniq", "description": "The homomorphism `to_envel_group.map f` is the unique map that fits into the commutative\ntriangle in `to_envel_group.univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group_rel.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.inv_act_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.envel_action", "description": "The induced group homomorphism from the enveloping group into bijections of the rack,\nusing `rack.to_conj`. Satisfies the property `envel_action_prop`.\n\nThis gives the rack `R` the structure of an augmented rack over `envel_group R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.to_envel_group.map_aux", "description": "The preliminary definition of the induced map from the enveloping group.\nSee `to_envel_group.map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.self_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.left_cancel_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.to_envel_group.map", "description": "Given a map from a rack to a group, lift it to being a map from the enveloping group.\nMore precisely, the `envel_group` functor is left adjoint to `quandle.conj`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unital_shelf.act_act_self_eq", "description": "A monoid is *graphic* if, for all `x` and `y`, the *graphic identity*\n`(x * y) * x = x * y` holds.  For a unital shelf, this graphic\nidentity holds.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.self_inv_act_inv_act_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.op_act_op_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.opposite_rack", "description": "The opposite rack, swapping the roles of `\u25c3` and `\u25c3\u207b\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group_rel'.rel", "description": "A quick way to convert a `pre_envel_group_rel'` to a `pre_envel_group_rel`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.self_act_act_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.self_act_eq_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quandle.opposite_quandle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group_rel.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quandle.conj.quandle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group_rel", "description": "The `pre_envel_group_rel` relation as a `Prop`.  Used as the relation for `pre_envel_group.setoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group_rel.rel", "description": "The `pre_envel_group_rel` relation as a `Prop`.  Used as the relation for `pre_envel_group.setoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shelf_hom", "description": "The type of homomorphisms between shelves.\nThis is also the notion of rack and quandle homomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shelf_hom.to_fun", "description": "The type of homomorphisms between shelves.\nThis is also the notion of rack and quandle homomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shelf_hom.map_act'", "description": "The type of homomorphisms between shelves.\nThis is also the notion of rack and quandle homomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unital_shelf.assoc", "description": "The associativity of a unital shelf comes for free.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.assoc_iff_id", "description": "Associative racks are uninteresting.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group_rel.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.envel_group.group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.self_inv_act_act_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.ad_conj", "description": "The *adjoint action* of a rack on itself is `op'`, and the adjoint\naction of `x \u25c3 y` is the conjugate of the action of `y` by the action\nof `x`. It is another way to understand the self-distributivity axiom.\n\nThis is used in the natural rack homomorphism `to_conj` from `R` to\n`conj (R \u2243 R)` defined by `op'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shelf", "description": "A *shelf* is a structure with a self-distributive binary operation.\nThe binary operation is regarded as a left action of the type on itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shelf.act", "description": "A *shelf* is a structure with a self-distributive binary operation.\nThe binary operation is regarded as a left action of the type on itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shelf.self_distrib", "description": "A *shelf* is a structure with a self-distributive binary operation.\nThe binary operation is regarded as a left action of the type on itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.self_distrib_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quandle.shelf_hom.has_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quandle.dihedral", "description": "The dihedral quandle. This is the conjugation quandle of the dihedral group restrict to flips.\n\nUsed for Fox n-colorings of knots.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shelf_hom.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.is_involutory", "description": "An involutory rack is one for which `rack.op R x` is an involution for every x.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quandle.conj.map", "description": "`conj` is functorial", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group", "description": "Free generators of the enveloping group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group.unit", "description": "Free generators of the enveloping group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group.incl", "description": "Free generators of the enveloping group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group.mul", "description": "Free generators of the enveloping group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group.inv", "description": "Free generators of the enveloping group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.envel_action_prop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quandle", "description": "A quandle is a rack such that each automorphism fixes its corresponding element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quandle.to_rack", "description": "A quandle is a rack such that each automorphism fixes its corresponding element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quandle.fix", "description": "A quandle is a rack such that each automorphism fixes its corresponding element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group.setoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.to_envel_group", "description": "The canonical homomorphism from a rack to its enveloping group.\nSatisfies universal properties given by `to_envel_group.map` and `to_envel_group.univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.to_conj", "description": "This is the natural rack homomorphism to the conjugation quandle of the group `R \u2243 R`\nthat acts on the rack.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.act_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.self_inv_act_eq_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.self_act_inv_act_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.pre_envel_group_rel'.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shelf_hom.id", "description": "The identity homomorphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unital_shelf", "description": "A *unital shelf* is a shelf equipped with an element `1` such that, for all elements `x`,\nwe have both `x \u25c3 1` and `1 \u25c3 x` equal `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unital_shelf.to_shelf", "description": "A *unital shelf* is a shelf equipped with an element `1` such that, for all elements `x`,\nwe have both `x \u25c3 1` and `1 \u25c3 x` equal `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unital_shelf.to_has_one", "description": "A *unital shelf* is a shelf equipped with an element `1` such that, for all elements `x`,\nwe have both `x \u25c3 1` and `1 \u25c3 x` equal `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unital_shelf.one_act", "description": "A *unital shelf* is a shelf equipped with an element `1` such that, for all elements `x`,\nwe have both `x \u25c3 1` and `1 \u25c3 x` equal `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unital_shelf.act_one", "description": "A *unital shelf* is a shelf equipped with an element `1` such that, for all elements `x`,\nwe have both `x \u25c3 1` and `1 \u25c3 x` equal `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.to_envel_group.map_aux.well_def", "description": "Show that `to_envel_group.map_aux` sends equivalent expressions to equal terms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shelf_hom.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shelf_hom.map_act", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.left_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unital_shelf.act_idem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quandle.dihedral.quandle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.envel_group.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shelf_hom.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unital_shelf.act_self_act_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.act_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.involutory_inv_act_eq_act", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shelf_hom.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack", "description": "A *rack* is an automorphic set (a set with an action on itself by\nbijections) that is self-distributive.  It is a shelf such that each\nelement's action is invertible.\n\nThe notations `x \u25c3 y` and `x \u25c3\u207b\u00b9 y` denote the action and the\ninverse action, respectively, and they are right associative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.to_shelf", "description": "A *rack* is an automorphic set (a set with an action on itself by\nbijections) that is self-distributive.  It is a shelf such that each\nelement's action is invertible.\n\nThe notations `x \u25c3 y` and `x \u25c3\u207b\u00b9 y` denote the action and the\ninverse action, respectively, and they are right associative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.inv_act", "description": "A *rack* is an automorphic set (a set with an action on itself by\nbijections) that is self-distributive.  It is a shelf such that each\nelement's action is invertible.\n\nThe notations `x \u25c3 y` and `x \u25c3\u207b\u00b9 y` denote the action and the\ninverse action, respectively, and they are right associative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.left_inv", "description": "A *rack* is an automorphic set (a set with an action on itself by\nbijections) that is self-distributive.  It is a shelf such that each\nelement's action is invertible.\n\nThe notations `x \u25c3 y` and `x \u25c3\u207b\u00b9 y` denote the action and the\ninverse action, respectively, and they are right associative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rack.right_inv", "description": "A *rack* is an automorphic set (a set with an action on itself by\nbijections) that is self-distributive.  It is a shelf such that each\nelement's action is invertible.\n\nThe notations `x \u25c3 y` and `x \u25c3\u207b\u00b9 y` denote the action and the\ninverse action, respectively, and they are right associative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shelf_hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quandle.fix_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.equiv_lim_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.equiv_real_prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.sub_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.one_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.conj_neg_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.of_real_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.bit1_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.re_eq_add_conj", "description": "A complex number `z` plus its conjugate `conj z` is `2` times its real part.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.add_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.I_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.abs_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.I_sq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.of_real_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.of_real_mul_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.abs_zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.strict_ordered_comm_ring", "description": "With `z \u2264 w` iff `w - z` is real and nonnegative, `\u2102` is a strictly ordered ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.decidable_eq", 