equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.formula.realize_not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.elementarily_equivalent.Theory_model", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.neg_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.expand'", "description": "A fraction is equal to its expansion by an factor from s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.right_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.ore_div_mul_ore_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.has_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.add_ore_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.universal_hom_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.add_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.localization_map", "description": "The morphism `numerator_hom` is a monoid localization map in the case of commutative `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.universal_hom_commutes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.ore_div_add_ore_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.equiv_monoid_localization", "description": "If `R` is commutative, Ore localization and monoid localization are isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.ore_div_mul_char", "description": " A characterization lemma for the multiplication on the Ore localization, allowing for a choice\nof Ore numerator and Ore denominator.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.zero_div_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.mul_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.ind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.mul_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.ore_div_add_char'", "description": " Another characterization of the addition on the Ore localization, bundling up all witnesses\nand conditions into a sigma type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.numerator_is_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.div_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.eq_of_num_factor_eq", "description": " Fractions which differ by a factor of the numerator can be proven equal if\nthose factors expand to equal elements of `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.numerator_hom", "description": " The multiplicative homomorphism from `R` to `R[S\u207b\u00b9]`, mapping `r : R` to the\nfraction `r /\u2092 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.lift\u2082_expand_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.expand", "description": "A fraction `r /\u2092 s` is equal to its expansion by an arbitrary factor `t` if `s * t \u2208 S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.universal_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.div_eq_one'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.universal_mul_hom", "description": " The universal lift from a morphism `R \u2192* T`, which maps elements of `S` to units of `T`,\nto a morphism `R[S\u207b\u00b9] \u2192* T`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.mul_cancel'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.numerator_hom_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.inv", "description": " The inversion of Ore fractions for a ring without zero divisors, satisying `0\u207b\u00b9 = 0` and\n`(r /\u2092 r')\u207b\u00b9 = r' /\u2092 r` for `r \u2260 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.mul_one_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.mul_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.add_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.universal_mul_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.add_left_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.inv_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.one_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.mul_inv_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.zero_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.div_one_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.ore_div_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.ore_div", "description": "The division in the ore localization `R[S\u207b\u00b9]`, as a fraction of an element of `R` and `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.mul_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.ore_div_add_char", "description": " A characterization of the addition on the Ore localizaion, allowing for arbitrary Ore\nnumerator and Ore denominator.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.universal_mul_hom_unique", "description": "The universal morphism `universal_mul_hom` is unique.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.lift_expand_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.universal_mul_hom_commutes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.left_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.numerator_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.mul", "description": "The multiplication on the Ore localization of monoids.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.one_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.neg", "description": "Negation on the Ore localization is defined via negation on the numerator.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.lift_expand", "description": " A function or predicate over `R` and `S` can be lifted to `R[S\u207b\u00b9]` if it is invariant\nunder expansion on the right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.lift\u2082_expand", "description": " A version of `lift_expand` used to simultaneously lift functions with two arguments\nin ``R[S\u207b\u00b9]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.ore_div_mul_char'", "description": " Another characterization lemma for the multiplication on the Ore localizaion delivering\nOre witnesses and conditions bundled in a sigma type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.division_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.numerator_unit", "description": "The fraction `s /\u2092 1` as a unit in `R[S\u207b\u00b9]`, where `s : S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.mul_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.zero_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.ore_eqv", "description": "The setoid on `R \u00d7 S` used for the Ore localization.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.ore_div_mul_ore_div_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.universal_hom", "description": " The universal lift from a ring homomorphism `f : R \u2192+* T`, which maps elements in `S` to\nunits of `T`, to a ring homomorphism `R[S\u207b\u00b9] \u2192+* T`. This extends the construction on\nmonoids.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.inv_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization", "description": "The ore localization of a monoid and a submonoid fulfilling the ore condition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.zero_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ore_localization.nontrivial_of_non_zero_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.preconnected_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.comap_nhds_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_embedding.dense_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_property", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.extend_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.dense_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.extend_eq_at'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.extend_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_range.induction_on\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_embedding.prod", "description": "The product of two dense embeddings is a dense embedding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.closure_image_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.extend", "description": "If `i : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is a dense inducing, then any function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b3` \"extends\"\n to a function `g = extend di f : \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b3`. If `\u03b3` is Hausdorff and `f` has a\n continuous extension, then `g` is the unique such extension. In general,\n `g` might not be continuous or even extend `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_basis.has_basis_of_dense_inducing", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_range.induction_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.extend_eq_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.dense_embedding_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.extend_eq'", "description": " Variation of `extend_eq` where we ask that `f` has a limit along `comap i (\ud835\udcdd b)` for each\n`b : \u03b2`. This is a strictly stronger assumption than continuity of `f`, but in a lot of cases\nyou'd have to prove it anyway to use `continuous_extend`, so this avoids doing the work twice.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_property3", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.tendsto_comap_nhds_nhds", "description": "```lean\n \u03b3 -f\u2192 \u03b1\ng\u2193     \u2193e\n \u03b4 -h\u2192 \u03b2\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.separable_space", "description": "If the domain of a `dense_inducing` map is a separable space, then so is the codomain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_embedding.subtype_emb_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_embedding.separable_space", "description": "If the domain of a `dense_embedding` is a separable space, then so is its codomain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_embedding", "description": "A dense embedding is an embedding with dense image.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_embedding.to_dense_inducing", "description": "A dense embedding is an embedding with dense image.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_embedding.inj", "description": "A dense embedding is an embedding with dense image.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing", "description": "`i : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is \"dense inducing\" if it has dense range and the topology on `\u03b1`\n is the one induced by `i` from the topology on `\u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.to_inducing", "description": "`i : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is \"dense inducing\" if it has dense range and the topology on `\u03b1`\n is the one induced by `i` from the topology on `\u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.dense", "description": "`i : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is \"dense inducing\" if it has dense range and the topology on `\u03b1`\n is the one induced by `i` from the topology on `\u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_embedding.to_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.extend_eq_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.nhds_within_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.continuous_extend", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_range.induction_on\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.nhds_eq_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_embedding.subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_embedding.inj_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_embedding.mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_property2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_embedding.subtype_emb", "description": "The dense embedding of a subtype inside its closure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.prod", "description": "The product of two dense inducings is a dense inducing", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.interior_compact_eq_empty", "description": " If `i : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is a dense embedding with dense complement of the range, then any compact set in\n`\u03b1` has empty interior.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_range.equalizer", "description": "Two continuous functions to a t2-space that agree on the dense range of a function are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_embedding_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.closure_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.extend_unique_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_inducing.continuous_at_extend", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.count_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.decidable_eq_ring_hom_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_image_univ_iff_mem_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Prop.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.decidable_bijective_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.decidable_mem_range_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.subset_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_strict_mono", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `set.to_finset_ssubset_to_finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bool.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.of_multiset", "description": "Construct a proof of `fintype \u03b1` from a universal multiset", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.choose", "description": " Given a fintype `\u03b1` and a predicate `p`, associate to a proof that there is a unique element of\n`\u03b1` satisfying `p` this unique element, as an element of `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.inv_of_mem_range", "description": "The inverse of an `hf : injective` function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2`, of the type `\u21a5(set.range f) \u2192 \u03b1`.\nThis is the computable version of `function.inv_fun` that requires `fintype \u03b1` and `decidable_eq \u03b2`,\nor the function version of applying `(equiv.of_injective f hf).symm`.\nThis function should not usually be used for actual computation because for most cases,\nan explicit inverse can be stated that has better computational properties.\nThis function computes by checking all terms `a : \u03b1` to find the `f a = b`, so it is O(N) where\n`N = fintype.card \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.bounded_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.compl_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.decidable_exists_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.compl_eq_univ_sdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.decidable_eq_one_hom_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units_equiv_ne_zero_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.univ", "description": "`univ` is the universal finite set of type `finset \u03b1` implied from\n the assumption `fintype \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype", "description": "`fintype \u03b1` means that `\u03b1` is finite, i.e. there are only\n finitely many distinct elements of type `\u03b1`. The evidence of this\n is a finset `elems` (a list up to permutation without duplicates),\n together with a proof that everything of type `\u03b1` is in the list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.elems", "description": "`fintype \u03b1` means that `\u03b1` is finite, i.e. there are only\n finitely many distinct elements of type `\u03b1`. The evidence of this\n is a finset `elems` (a list up to permutation without duplicates),\n together with a proof that everything of type `\u03b1` is in the list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.complete", "description": "`fintype \u03b1` means that `\u03b1` is finite, i.e. there are only\n finitely many distinct elements of type `\u03b1`. The evidence of this\n is a finset `elems` (a list up to permutation without duplicates),\n together with a proof that everything of type `\u03b1` is in the list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.decidable_eq_add_monoid_hom_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.univ_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.inv_of_mem_range_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.finset_equiv_set_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unit.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.decidable_codisjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.right_inv_of_inv_of_mem_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.image_succ_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.ssubset_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset", "description": "Construct a finset enumerating a set `s`, given a `fintype` instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_symm_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.univ_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.codisjoint_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.eq_univ_of_forall", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.disjoint_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.boolean_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image_univ_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inter_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.univ_filter_exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "coe_units_equiv_prod_subtype_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "psigma.fintype_prop_prop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.univ_filter_mem_range", "description": "Note this is a special case of `(finset.image_preimage f univ _).symm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.univ_eq_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.compl_ne_univ_iff_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.univ_pempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.decidable_eq_embedding_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units_equiv_prod_subtype_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mem_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.univ_cast_succ", "description": "Embed `fin n` into `fin (n + 1)` by appending a new `fin.last n` to the `univ`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.univ_Prop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_ssubset_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.piecewise_erase_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.image_cast_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.compl_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.decidable_eq_mul_hom_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mem_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_mono", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `set.to_finset_subset_to_finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.subtype_eq", "description": " Short-circuit instance to decrease search for `unique.fintype`,\nsince that relies on a subsingleton elimination for `unique`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units_equiv_ne_zero", "description": " In a `group_with_zero` `\u03b1`, the unit group `\u03b1\u02e3` is equivalent to the subtype of nonzero\nelements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.choose_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "plift.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.subtype.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_eq_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.compl_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.univ_punit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset_coe.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.not_mem_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.bij_inv", "description": "`bij_inv f` is the unique inverse to a bijection `f`. This acts\n  as a computable alternative to `function.inv_fun`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.subtype.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.decidable_eq_add_hom_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.of_equiv", "description": "If `f : \u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2` and `\u03b1` is a fintype, then `\u03b2` is also a fintype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.of_is_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.subtype.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.decidable_eq_equiv_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_eq_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.finset_equiv_set", "description": " Given `fintype \u03b1`, `finset_equiv_set` is the equiv between `finset \u03b1` and `set \u03b1`. (All\nsets on a finite type are finite.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.right_inverse_bij_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trunc_of_nonempty_fintype", "description": "A `nonempty` `fintype` constructively contains an element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inter_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.mem_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.right_inv_of_inv_of_mem_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_right", "description": "Given that `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2` is a fintype, `\u03b2` is also a fintype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_seq_of_forall_finset_exists", "description": " Induction principle to build a sequence, by adding one point at a time satisfying a given\nrelation with respect to all the previously chosen points.\n\nMore precisely, Assume that, for any finite set `s`, one can find another point satisfying\nsome relation `r` with respect to all the points in `s`. Then one may construct a\nfunction `f : \u2115 \u2192 \u03b1` such that `r (f m) (f n)` holds whenever `m < n`.\nWe also ensure that all constructed points satisfy a given predicate `P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.univ_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfun_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.left_inverse_bij_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.inv_fun_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "psigma.fintype_prop_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.union_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.of_bijective", "description": "If `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is a bijection and `\u03b1` is a fintype, then `\u03b2` is also a fintype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.decidable_pi_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.compl_eq_univ_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "punit.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.decidable_eq_zero_hom_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.bijective_bij_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.finset_equiv_set_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_set_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.to_finset_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.decidable_injective_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtype.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "psigma.fintype_prop_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"