p` this unique element, as an element of the corresponding subtype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.of_injective", "description": " Given an injective function to a fintype, the domain is also a\nfintype. This is noncomputable because injectivity alone cannot be\nused to construct preimages.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.piecewise_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.decidable_left_inverse_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.univ_eq_attach", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_ssubset_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.piecewise_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.choose_subtype_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mem_univ_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fintype_coe_sort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.eq_univ_iff_forall", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.univ_bool", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.compl_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.univ_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.top_eq_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.coe_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.subtype_eq'", "description": " Short-circuit instance to decrease search for `unique.fintype`,\nsince that relies on a subsingleton elimination for `unique`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_ssubset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.coe_filter_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_subset_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.coe_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.decidable_eq_monoid_hom_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.subtype", "description": " Given a predicate that can be represented by a finset, the subtype\nassociated to the predicate is a fintype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.image_succ_above_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_of_finset", "description": " Many `fintype` instances for sets are defined using an extensionally equal `finset`.\nRewriting `s.to_finset` with `set.to_finset_of_finset` replaces the term with such a `finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.univ_eq_empty_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.decidable_eq_monoid_with_zero_hom_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.map_univ_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.filter_mem_univ_eq_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.insert_inj_on'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_left", "description": "Given that `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2` is a fintype, `\u03b1` is also a fintype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.decidable_is_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sdiff_eq_inter_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.inv_of_mem_range_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.coe_eq_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.coe_image_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.univ_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units_equiv_ne_zero_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nonempty.eq_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.left_inv_of_inv_of_mem_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.map_univ_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units_equiv_prod_subtype", "description": "The `\u03b1\u02e3` type is equivalent to a subtype of `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.univ_succ_above", "description": " Embed `fin n` into `fin (n + 1)` by inserting\naround a specified pivot `p : fin (n + 1)` into the `univ`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set_fintype", "description": "A set on a fintype, when coerced to a type, is a fintype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.univ_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.attach_eq_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.decidable_surjective_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.decidable_forall_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lex.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_seq_of_forall_finset_exists'", "description": " Induction principle to build a sequence, by adding one point at a time satisfying a given\nsymmetric relation with respect to all the previously chosen points.\n\nMore precisely, Assume that, for any finite set `s`, one can find another point satisfying\nsome relation `r` with respect to all the points in `s`. Then one may construct a\nfunction `f : \u2115 \u2192 \u03b1` such that `r (f m) (f n)` holds whenever `m \u2260 n`.\nWe also ensure that all constructed points satisfy a given predicate `P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.decidable_mem_of_fintype", "description": " Membership of a set with a `fintype` instance is decidable.\n\nUsing this as an instance leads to potential loops with `subtype.fintype` under certain decidability\nassumptions, so it should only be declared a local instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.subset_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.compl_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trunc_of_multiset_exists_mem", "description": "For `s : multiset \u03b1`, we can lift the existential statement that `\u2203 x, x \u2208 s` to a `trunc \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.inv_of_mem_range", "description": "The inverse of an embedding `f : \u03b1 \u21aa \u03b2`, of the type `\u21a5(set.range f) \u2192 \u03b1`.\nThis is the computable version of `function.inv_fun` that requires `fintype \u03b1` and `decidable_eq \u03b2`,\nor the function version of applying `(equiv.of_injective f f.injective).symm`.\nThis function should not usually be used for actual computation because for most cases,\nan explicit inverse can be stated that has better computational properties.\nThis function computes by checking all terms `a : \u03b1` to find the `f a = b`, so it is O(N) where\n`N = fintype.card \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.coe_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.univ_succ", "description": "Embed `fin n` into `fin (n + 1)` by prepending zero to the `univ`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.univ_of_is_empty", "description": " Note: this lemma is specifically about `fintype.of_is_empty`. For a statement about\narbitrary `fintype` instances, use `finset.univ_eq_empty`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trunc_sigma_of_exists", "description": "By iterating over the elements of a fintype, we can lift an existential statement `\u2203 a, P a`\nto `trunc (\u03a3' a, P a)`, containing data.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.insert_compl_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.univ_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.inv_fun_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.lift_kaehler_differential_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.submodule_span_range_eq_ideal", "description": "The kernel of `S \u2297[R] S \u2192\u2090[R] S` is generated by `1 \u2297 s - s \u2297 1` as a `S`-module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.End_equiv", "description": "The endomorphisms of `\u03a9[S\u2044R]` corresponds to sections of the surjection `S \u2297[R] S \u29f8 J ^ 2 \u2192\u2090[R] S`,\nwith `J` being the kernel of the multiplication map `S \u2297[R] S \u2192\u2090[R] S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.tensor_product_to_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.ker_total_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.ker_total_mkq_single_algebra_map_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.tensor_product_to", "description": "For a `R`-derivation `S \u2192 M`, this is the map `S \u2297[R] S \u2192\u2097[S] M` sending `s \u2297\u209c t \u21a6 s \u2022 D t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.total_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.map_D", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.module'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.tensor_product_to_tmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.quot_ker_total_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.map_base_change_tmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.lift_kaehler_differential_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.quotient_cotangent_ideal_ring_equiv", "description": "The quotient ring of `S \u2297 S \u29f8 J ^ 2` by `\u03a9[S\u2044R]` is isomorphic to `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.lift_kaehler_differential_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.map_comp_der", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.End_equiv_derivation'", "description": " Derivations into `\u03a9[S\u2044R]` is equivalent to derivations\ninto `(kaehler_differential.ideal R S).cotangent_ideal`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.quotient_cotangent_ideal", "description": "The quotient ring of `S \u2297 S \u29f8 J ^ 2` by `\u03a9[S\u2044R]` is isomorphic to `S` as an `S`-algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.End_equiv_aux_equiv", "description": " (Implementation) An `equiv` version of `kaehler_differential.End_equiv_aux`.\nUsed in `kaehler_differential.End_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.derivation_quot_ker_total_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.comp_algebra_map", "description": " For a tower `R \u2192 A \u2192 B` and an `R`-derivation `B \u2192 M`, we may compose with `A \u2192 B` to obtain an\n`R`-derivation `A \u2192 M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.is_scalar_tower'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.tensor_product_to_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.span_range_derivation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.D", "description": "The universal derivation into `\u03a9[S\u2044R]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.End_equiv_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.linear_map_equiv_derivation", "description": " The `S`-linear maps from `\u03a9[S\u2044R]` to `M` are (`S`-linearly) equivalent to `R`-derivations\nfrom `S` to `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.is_scalar_tower_of_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.span_range_eq_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.D_linear_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.ker_total_mkq_single_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.map_base_change", "description": " The lift of the map `\u03a9[A\u2044R] \u2192\u2097[A] \u03a9[B\u2044R]` to the base change along `A \u2192 B`.\nThis is the first map in the exact sequence `B \u2297[A] \u03a9[A\u2044R] \u2192 \u03a9[B\u2044R] \u2192 \u03a9[B\u2044A] \u2192 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.ker_total_mkq_single_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.quot_ker_total_equiv_symm_comp_D", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.ker_total_mkq_single_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.D_tensor_product_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.map", "description": " The map `\u03a9[A\u2044R] \u2192\u2097[A] \u03a9[B\u2044R]` given a square\nA --\u2192 B\n\u2191     \u2191\n|     |\nR --\u2192 S", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.ker_total_mkq_single_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.derivation_quot_ker_total", "description": "The (universal) derivation into `(S \u2192\u2080 S) \u29f8 kaehler_differential.ker_total R S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.map_surjective_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.D_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.ideal", "description": "The kernel of the multiplication map `S \u2297[R] S \u2192\u2090[R] S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.lift_kaehler_differential_comp_D", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.quot_ker_total_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.derivation_quot_ker_total_lift_comp_total", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.ker_total", "description": " The `S`-submodule of `S \u2192\u2080 S` (the direct sum of copies of `S` indexed by `S`) generated by\nthe relations:\n1. `dx + dy = d(x + y)`\n2. `x dy + y dx = d(x * y)`\n3. `dr = 0` for `r \u2208 R`\nwhere `db` is the unit in the copy of `S` with index `b`.\n\nThis is the kernel of the surjection `finsupp.total S \u03a9[S\u2044R] S (kaehler_differential.D R S)`.\nSee `kaehler_differential.ker_total_eq` and `kaehler_differential.total_surjective`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.ker_total_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.from_ideal", "description": "The quotient map `I \u2192 \u03a9[S\u2044R]` with `I` being the kernel of `S \u2297[R] S \u2192 S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.quot_ker_total_equiv", "description": "`\u03a9[S\u2044R]` is isomorphic to `S` copies of `S` with kernel `kaehler_differential.ker_total`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential", "description": "The module of K\u00e4hler differentials (Kahler differentials, Kaehler differentials).\nThis is implemented as `I / I ^ 2` with `I` the kernel of the multiplication map `S \u2297[R] S \u2192\u2090[R] S`.\nTo view elements as a linear combination of the form `s \u2022 D s'`, use\n`kaehler_differential.tensor_product_to_surjective` and `derivation.tensor_product_to_tmul`.\n\nWe also provide the notation `\u03a9[S\u2044R]` for `kaehler_differential R S`.\nNote that the slash is `\\textfractionsolidus`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.D_linear_map", "description": "(Implementation) The underlying linear map of the derivation into `\u03a9[S\u2044R]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.one_smul_sub_smul_one_mem_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.lift_kaehler_differential_D", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kaehler_differential.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.lift_kaehler_differential", "description": "The linear map from `\u03a9[S\u2044R]`, associated with a derivation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_strict_deriv_at_rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at.const_rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_within_at.const_cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cont_diff_at_rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.has_strict_fderiv_at_cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_strict_fderiv_at_rpow_of_pos", "description": "`(x, y) \u21a6 x ^ y` is strictly differentiable at `p : \u211d \u00d7 \u211d` such that `0 < p.fst`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff.rpow_const_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.cpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cont_diff_at_rpow_of_ne", "description": "The function `\u03bb (x, y), x ^ y` is infinitely smooth at `(x, y)` unless `x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cont_diff_at_rpow_const_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_at.cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_on.rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.has_strict_deriv_at_const_cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_within_at.const_rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_deriv_at_rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_at.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at.const_cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at.const_cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_at.rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.differentiable_rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at.cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_within_rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.rpow_const_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable.rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at.cpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_within_at.cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_strict_fderiv_at_rpow_of_neg", "description": "`(x, y) \u21a6 x ^ y` is strictly differentiable at `p : \u211d \u00d7 \u211d` such that `p.fst < 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at.cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.deriv_rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.const_rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_within_at.rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_at.const_cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_at.rpow_const_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_within_at.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_strict_deriv_at_const_rpow_of_neg", "description": " This lemma says that `\u03bb x, a ^ x` is strictly differentiable for `a < 0`. Note that these\nvalues of `a` are outside of the \"official\" domain of `a ^ x`, and we may redefine `a ^ x`\nfor negative `a` if some other definition will be more convenient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_within_at.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.differentiable_at_rpow_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_one_plus_div_pow_exp", "description": "The function `(1 + t/x) ^ x` tends to `exp t` at `+\u221e` for naturals `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_strict_deriv_at_rpow_const_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at.rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cont_diff_rpow_const_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cont_diff_at_rpow_const_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.const_cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.rpow_const_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at.cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff.rpow_const_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_within_at.const_cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.deriv_rpow_const'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_at.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_strict_deriv_at_const_rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at.rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.const_cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.has_strict_deriv_at_cpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_within_at.cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_within_at.rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.rpow_const_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_one_plus_div_rpow_exp", "description": "The function `(1 + t/x) ^ x` tends to `exp t` at `+\u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.has_strict_fderiv_at_cpow'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.rpow_const_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at.cpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at.const_cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.has_fderiv_at_cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_on.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at_of_real_cpow", "description": " Although `\u03bb x, x ^ r` for fixed `r` is *not* complex-differentiable along the negative real\nline, it is still real-differentiable, and the derivative is what one would formally expect.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_at.rpow_const_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag_of_subsingleton", "description": "Every matrix indexed by a subsingleton is diagonal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag.diagonal_diag", "description": "Diagonal matrices are generated by the `matrix.diagonal` of their `matrix.diag`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag_from_blocks_iff", "description": "This is the `iff` version of `matrix.is_diag.from_blocks`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag.transpose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag_transpose_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag_one", "description": "Every identity matrix is diagonal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag.submatrix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag.is_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.mul_transpose_self_is_diag_iff_has_orthogonal_rows", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag.from_blocks", "description": "The block matrix `A.from_blocks 0 0 D` is diagonal if `A` and `D` are diagonal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.transpose_mul_self_is_diag_iff_has_orthogonal_cols", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag_neg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag.from_blocks_of_is_symm", "description": "A symmetric block matrix `A.from_blocks B C D` is diagonal\n   if  `A` and `D` are diagonal and `B` is `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag_diagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag", "description": "`A.is_diag` means square matrix `A` is a diagonal matrix.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag.kronecker", "description": "`(A \u2297 B).is_diag` if both `A` and `B` are diagonal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag_iff_diagonal_diag", "description": "`matrix.is_diag.diagonal_diag` as an iff.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag.conj_transpose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag_zero", "description": "Every zero matrix is diagonal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag_smul_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_diag_conj_transpose_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.to_freiman_hom_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.one_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.freiman_hom_class", "description": " A monoid homomorphism is naturally a `freiman_hom` on its entire domain.\n\nWe can't leave the domain `A : set \u03b1` of the `freiman_hom` a free variable, since it wouldn't be\ninferrable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.mul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.const_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.cancel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.cancel_left_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.const", "description": "`freiman_hom.const A n b` is the Freiman homomorphism sending everything to `b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.comp", "description": "Composition of Freiman homomorphisms as a Freiman homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.freiman_hom_class", "description": " An additive monoid homomorphism is naturally an `add_freiman_hom` on its entire\ndomain.\n\nWe can't leave the domain `A : set \u03b1` of the `freiman_hom` a free variable, since it wouldn't be\ninferrable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_sum_eq_map_sum_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.has_inv", "description": " If `f` is a Freiman homomorphism to a commutative group, then `f\u207b\u00b9` is the Freiman homomorphism\nsending `x` to `(f x)\u207b\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.div_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.const", "description": "`add_freiman_hom.const n b` is the Freiman homomorphism sending everything to `b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom", "description": "An additive `n`-Freiman homomorphism is a map which preserves sums of `n` elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.to_fun", "description": "An additive `n`-Freiman homomorphism is a map which preserves sums of `n` elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.map_sum_eq_map_sum'", "description": "An additive `n`-Freiman homomorphism is a map which preserves sums of `n` elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.mul_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.to_add_freiman_hom", "description": "`\u03b1 \u2192+[n] \u03b2` is naturally included in  `\u03b1 \u2192+[m] \u03b2`\nfor any `m \u2264 n`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_freiman_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.has_coe_to_fun", "description": " Helper instance for when there's too many metavariables to apply `fun_like.has_coe_to_fun`\ndirectly.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.const_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.id", "description": "The identity map from a commutative monoid to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom_class", "description": " `add_freiman_hom_class F s \u03b2 n` states that `F` is a type of `n`-ary sums-preserving morphisms.\nYou should extend this class when you extend `add_freiman_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom_class.map_sum_eq_map_sum'", "description": " `add_freiman_hom_class F s \u03b2 n` states that `F` is a type of `n`-ary sums-preserving morphisms.\nYou should extend this class when you extend `add_freiman_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.has_one", "description": "`1` is the Freiman homomorphism sending everything to `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.div_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.freiman_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_freiman_hom_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_add_map_eq_map_add_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.add_comm_monoid", "description": "`\u03b1 \u2192+[n] \u03b2` is an `add_comm_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.to_freiman_hom", "description": "`\u03b1 \u2192*[n] \u03b2` is naturally included in  `A \u2192*[m] \u03b2` for any `m \u2264 n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.add_freiman_hom_class_of_le", "description": "An additive `n`-Freiman homomorphism is\nalso an additive `m`-Freiman homomorphism for any `m \u2264 n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.has_mul", "description": "`f * g` is the Freiman homomorphism  sends `x` to `f x * g x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.fun_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.freiman_hom_class_of_le", "description": "A `n`-Freiman homomorphism is also a `m`-Freiman homomorphism for any `m \u2264 n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.to_freiman_hom", "description": "A `monoid_hom` is naturally a `freiman_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.fun_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.neg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.has_zero", "description": "`0` is the Freiman homomorphism sending everything to `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.zero_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom_class", "description": " `freiman_hom_class F A \u03b2 n` states that `F` is a type of `n`-ary products-preserving morphisms.\nYou should extend this class when you extend `freiman_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom_class.map_prod_eq_map_prod'", "description": " `freiman_hom_class F A \u03b2 n` states that `F` is a type of `n`-ary products-preserving morphisms.\nYou should extend this class when you extend `freiman_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.neg_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.add_comm_group", "description": "If `\u03b2` is an additive commutative group, then `A \u2192*[n] \u03b2` is an additive commutative\ngroup too.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.cancel_left_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_mul_map_eq_map_mul_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.to_freiman_hom_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.to_add_freiman_hom_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.one_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.inv_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.has_neg", "description": "If `f` is a Freiman homomorphism to an additive commutative group, then `-f` is the\nFreiman homomorphism sending `x` to `-f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "Helper instance for when there's too many metavariables to apply\n`fun_like.has_coe_to_fun` directly.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.to_freiman_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.cancel_right_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.has_add", "description": "`f + g` is the Freiman homomorphism sending `x` to `f x + g x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.id", "description": "The identity map from an additive commutative monoid to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.comm_group", "description": "If `\u03b2` is a commutative group, then `A \u2192*[n] \u03b2` is a commutative group too.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.comp", "description": "Composition of additive Freiman homomorphisms as an additive Freiman homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_add_freiman_hom", "description": "An `add_monoid_hom` is naturally an\n`add_freiman_hom`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.has_div", "description": " If `f` and `g` are Freiman homomorphisms to a commutative group, then `f / g` is the Freiman\nhomomorphism sending `x` to `f x / g x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.to_freiman_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.freiman_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom", "description": "A `n`-Freiman homomorphism on a set `A` is a map which preserves products of `n` elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.to_fun", "description": "A `n`-Freiman homomorphism on a set `A` is a map which preserves products of `n` elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.map_prod_eq_map_prod'", "description": "A `n`-Freiman homomorphism on a set `A` is a map which preserves products of `n` elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_prod_eq_map_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.sub_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.comm_monoid", "description": "`A \u2192*[n] \u03b2` is a `comm_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_sum_eq_map_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.add_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.to_freiman_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.has_sub", "description": "If `f` and `g` are additive Freiman homomorphisms to an additive commutative group,\nthen `f - g` is the additive Freiman homomorphism sending `x` to `f x - g x`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.const_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.const_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.cancel_right_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.sub_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_prod_eq_map_prod_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_freiman_hom.add_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "freiman_hom.cancel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_range_sub", "description": "A telescoping sum along `{0, ..., n - 1}` of an additive commutative group valued\nfunction reduces to the difference of the last and first terms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_const_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum", "description": "`\u2211 x in s, f x` is the sum of `f x` as `x` ranges over the elements\nof the finite set `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.coe_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_add_multiset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "library_note.operator precedence of big operators", "description": "There is no established mathematical convention\nfor the operator precedence of big operators like `\u220f` and `\u2211`.\nWe will have to make a choice.\n\nOnline discussions, such as https://math.stackexchange.com/q/185538/30839\nseem to suggest that `\u220f` and `\u2211` should have the same precedence,\nand that this should be somewhere between `*` and `+`.\nThe latter have precedence levels `70` and `65` respectively,\nand we therefore choose the level `67`.\n\nIn practice, this means that parentheses should be placed as follows:\n```lean\n\u2211 k in K, (a k + b k) = \u2211 k in K, a k + \u2211 k in K, b k \u2192\n  \u220f k in K, a k * b k = (\u220f k in K, a k) * (\u220f k in K, b k)\n```\n(Example taken from page 490 of Knuth's *Concrete Mathematics*.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_finset_product", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_mul_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_attach", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_subtype_of_mem", "description": " If all elements of a `finset` satisfy the predicate `p`, a product\nover `s.subtype p` equals that product over `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_dite_of_true", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_sigma", "description": " Product over a sigma type equals the product of fiberwise products. For rewriting\nin the reverse direction, use `finset.prod_sigma'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_to_list", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.sum_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_ite_one", "description": "See also `finset.prod_boole`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_apply_ite_of_false", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.finset_sum_eq_sup_iff_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sum_comp'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_sdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_sdiff_div_prod_sdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_eq_prod_compl_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_equiv", "description": " `fintype.prod_equiv` is a specialization of `finset.prod_bij` that\nautomatically fills in most arguments.\n\nSee `equiv.prod_comp` for a version without `h`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_filter_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_flip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_map_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_apply_ite_of_true", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compl.sum_add_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_update_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_ite_zero", "description": "See also `finset.sum_boole`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_eq_prod_diff_singleton_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.disjoint_finset_sum_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_equiv", "description": "`fintype.sum_equiv` is a specialization of `finset.sum_bij` that\nautomatically fills in most arguments.\n\nSee `equiv.sum_comp` for a version without `h`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_subtype_map_embedding", "description": "A sum of a function over a `finset` in a subtype equals a\nsum in the main type of a function that agrees with the first\nfunction on that `finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_multiset_count", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_dite_of_false", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.add_sum_erase", "description": "Taking a sum over `s : finset \u03b1` is the same as adding the value on a single element\n`f a` to the sum over `s.erase a`.\n\nSee `multiset.sum_map_erase` for the `multiset` version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.to_finset_prod_dvd_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_cancels_of_partition_cancels", "description": "If we can partition a product into subsets that cancel out, then the whole product cancels.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_eq_single_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_range_tsub", "description": "A telescoping sum along `{0, ..., n-1}` of an `\u2115`-valued function\nreduces to the difference of the last and first terms\nwhen the function we are summing is monotone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_product_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_dite_of_false", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_apply_ite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_range_add_sub_sum_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_finset_product_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_boole", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.equiv.prod_comp_finset", "description": " Reindexing a product over a finset along an equivalence.\nSee `equiv.prod_comp` for the version where `s` and `s'` are `univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_to_list", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_dite_irrel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_partition", "description": "A sum can be partitioned into a sum of sums, each equivalent under a setoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_list_map_count", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_range_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_eq_mul_prod_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.sup_powerset_len", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_filter_count_eq_countp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_pi_mul_single'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_partition", "description": "A product can be partitioned into a product of products, each equivalent under a setoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_range_induction", "description": " For any product along `{0, ..., n - 1}` of a commutative-monoid-valued function, we can verify\nthat it's equal to a different function just by checking ratios of adjacent terms.\n\nThis is a multiplicative discrete analogue of the fundamental theorem of calculus.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.eq_prod_range_div'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_sdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.add_eq_union_left_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_finset_product_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_add_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_erase_lt_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.eq_zero_of_sum_eq_zero", "description": "If a sum is 0 and the function is 0 except possibly at one\npoint, it is 0 everywhere on the `finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_sub_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_erase", "description": " If a function applied at a point is 1, a product is unchanged by\nremoving that point, if present, from a `finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_pair", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.sum_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_eq_card_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_eq_sum_card_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_insert_of_eq_zero_if_not_mem", "description": "The sum of `f` over `insert a s` is the same as\nthe sum over `s`, as long as `a` is in `s` or `f a = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_mul_prod", "description": "", "p": "