comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_sigma'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_union_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.prod_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_eq_add_sum_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_image'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_inv_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_comm'", "description": " Generalization of `finset.prod_comm` to the case when the inner `finset`s depend on the outer\nvariable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_div_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_list_count_of_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_subtype_map_embedding", "description": " A product of a function over a `finset` in a subtype equals a\nproduct in the main type of a function that agrees with the first\nfunction on that `finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.equiv.sum_comp_finset", "description": " Reindexing a sum over a finset along an equivalence.\nSee `equiv.sum_comp` for the version where `s` and `s'` are `univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nonempty_of_prod_ne_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_add_multiset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_multiset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_ite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_bij'", "description": "Reorder a sum.\n\nThe difference with `sum_bij` is that the bijection is specified with an inverse, rather than\nas a surjective injection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_eq_multiset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_mem_multiset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat_abs_sum_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mul_prod_erase", "description": " Taking a product over `s : finset \u03b1` is the same as multiplying the value on a single element\n`f a` by the product of `s.erase a`.\n\nSee `multiset.prod_map_erase` for the `multiset` version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_ite_eq'", "description": " A product taken over a conditional whose condition is an equality test on the index and whose\nalternative is `1` has value either the term at that index or `1`.\n\nThe difference with `finset.prod_ite_eq` is that the arguments to `eq` are swapped.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.sum_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_product_right'", "description": "An uncurried version of `finset.prod_product_right`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_pow_boole", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_induction", "description": "To prove a property of a product, it suffices to prove that\nthe property is multiplicative and holds on factors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_involution", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_eq_pow_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.mk0_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_subset_zero_on_sdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_list_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.unop_map_list_prod", "description": " A morphism into the opposite ring acts on the product by acting on the reversed elements.\n\nDeprecated: use `_root_.unop_map_list_prod` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_add_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_finset_product_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_of_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_bijective", "description": " `fintype.prod_bijective` is a variant of `finset.prod_bij` that accepts `function.bijective`.\n\nSee `function.bijective.prod_comp` for a version without `h`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_finset_product", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.map_prod", "description": "Deprecated: use `_root_.map_prod` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_of_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_eq_add_sum_diff_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_map_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_induction", "description": "To prove a property of a sum, it suffices to prove that\nthe property is additive and holds on summands.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_compl_mul_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_piecewise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_union_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_finset_product_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_filter_ne_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.map_prod", "description": "Deprecated: use `_root_.map_prod` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_coe_sort_eq_attach", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_eq_add_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod", "description": "`\u220f x in s, f x` is the product of `f x`\nas `x` ranges over the elements of the finite set `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_subset_one_on_sdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_coe_sort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_list_count_of_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_sum_elim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_apply_ite_of_false", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_finset_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_add_prod_eq", "description": "If `f = g = h` everywhere but at `i`, where `f i = g i + h i`, then the product of `f` over `s`\n is the sum of the products of `g` and `h`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.eq_sum_range_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_range_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_list_count", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_disj_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.eventually_constant_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_filter_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_mul_prod_compl", "description": " Multiplying the products of a function over `s` and over `s\u1d9c` gives the whole product.\nFor a version expressed with subtypes, see `fintype.prod_subtype_mul_prod_subtype`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_erase_eq_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_ite_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_dite_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_bij'", "description": "Reorder a product.\n\nThe difference with `prod_bij` is that the bijection is specified with an inverse, rather than\nas a surjective injection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.disjoint_list_sum_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_comp", "description": "The sum of the composition of functions `f` and `g`, is the sum over `b \u2208 s.image g`\nof `f b` times of the cardinality of the fibre of `b`. See also `finset.sum_image`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_bij_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_compl_add_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_sigma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_multiset_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_list_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_range_succ'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_dite_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.map_prod", "description": "Deprecated: use `_root_.map_prod` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.to_finset_sum_count_nsmul_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_ite_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_ite_of_false", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.fundamental_domain_bounded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.vadd_mem_fundamental_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.fract_fract", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.fundamental_domain", "description": " The fundamental domain of the \u2124-lattice spanned by `b`. See `zspan.is_add_fundamental_domain`\nfor the proof that it is the fundamental domain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.fract", "description": " The map that sends a vector `E` to the fundamental domain of the lattice,\nsee `zspan.fract_mem_fundamental_domain`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.fract_add_zspan", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.ceil", "description": " The map that sends a vector of `E` to the element of the \u2124-lattice spanned by `b` obtained\nby rounding up its coordinates on the basis `b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.fract_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.coe_floor_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.repr_fract_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.fract_mem_fundamental_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.norm_fract_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.repr_ceil_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.floor", "description": " The map that sends a vector of `E` to the element of the \u2124-lattice spanned by `b` obtained\nby rounding down its coordinates on the basis `b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.floor_eq_self_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.is_add_fundamental_domain", "description": " For a \u2124-lattice `submodule.span \u2124 (set.range b)`, proves that the set defined\nby `zspan.fundamental_domain` is a fundamental domain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.fract_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.repr_floor_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.mem_fundamental_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.ceil_eq_self_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.fract_zspan_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.fundamental_domain_measurable_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.fract_eq_fract", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.exist_unique_vadd_mem_fundamental_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zspan.coe_fract_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_functor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_stalk_of_specializes", "description": "If `y \u2208 closure {p\u2080}`, then the stalk of `skyscraper_presheaf p\u2080 A` at `y` is `A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stalk_skyscraper_presheaf_adjunction_auxs.unit_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_stalk_of_not_specializes", "description": "If `y \u2209 closure {p\u2080}`, then the stalk of `skyscraper_presheaf p\u2080 A` at `y` is isomorphic to a\nterminal object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_cocone", "description": "The cocone at `*` for the stalk functor of `skyscraper_presheaf p\u2080 A` when `y \u2209 closure {p\u2080}`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_functor.map'_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stalk_skyscraper_presheaf_adjunction_auxs.from_stalk", "description": "If `f : \ud835\udcd5 \u27f6 skyscraper_presheaf p\u2080 c` is a natural transformation, then there is a morphism\n`\ud835\udcd5.stalk p\u2080 \u27f6 c` defined as the morphism from colimit to cocone at `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_functor", "description": "Taking skyscraper presheaf at a point is functorial: `c \u21a6 skyscraper p\u2080 c` defines a functor by\nsending every `f : a \u27f6 b` to the natural transformation `\u03b1` defined as: `\u03b1(U) = f : a \u27f6 b` if\n`p\u2080 \u2208 U` and the unique morphism to a terminal object in `C` if `p\u2080 \u2209 U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stalk_skyscraper_presheaf_adjunction_auxs.from_stalk_to_skyscraper", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_functor.category_theory.is_left_adjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stalk_skyscraper_presheaf_adjunction_auxs.counit_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stalk_skyscraper_presheaf_adjunction_auxs.to_skyscraper_presheaf", "description": "If `f : \ud835\udcd5.stalk p\u2080 \u27f6 c`, then a natural transformation `\ud835\udcd5 \u27f6 skyscraper_presheaf p\u2080 c` can be\ndefined by: `\ud835\udcd5.germ p\u2080 \u226b f : \ud835\udcd5(U) \u27f6 c` if `p\u2080 \u2208 U` and the unique morphism to a terminal object\nif `p\u2080 \u2209 U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_cocone_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stalk_skyscraper_presheaf_adjunction_auxs.unit", "description": "The unit in `presheaf.stalk \u22a3 skyscraper_presheaf_functor`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_cocone_is_colimit_of_not_specializes", "description": "The cocone at `*` for the stalk functor of `skyscraper_presheaf p\u2080 A` when `y \u2209 closure {p\u2080}` is a\ncolimit", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_cocone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_functor.map'_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_cocone_of_specializes_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_stalk_of_not_specializes_is_terminal", "description": "If `y \u2209 closure {p\u2080}`, then the stalk of `skyscraper_presheaf p\u2080 A` at `y` is a terminal object", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_stalk_adjunction", "description": "`skyscraper_presheaf_functor` is the right adjoint of `presheaf.stalk_functor`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stalk_skyscraper_presheaf_adjunction_auxs.to_skyscraper_from_stalk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_sheaf", "description": "The skyscraper presheaf supported at `p\u2080` with value `A` is the sheaf that assigns `A` to all opens\n`U` that contain `p\u2080` and assigns `*` otherwise.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_functor.map'_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_is_sheaf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_eq_pushforward", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_functor.map'", "description": "Taking skyscraper presheaf at a point is functorial: `c \u21a6 skyscraper p\u2080 c` defines a functor by\nsending every `f : a \u27f6 b` to the natural transformation `\u03b1` defined as: `\u03b1(U) = f : a \u27f6 b` if\n`p\u2080 \u2208 U` and the unique morphism to a terminal object in `C` if `p\u2080 \u2209 U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_sheaf_functor", "description": "Taking skyscraper sheaf at a point is functorial: `c \u21a6 skyscraper p\u2080 c` defines a functor by\nsending every `f : a \u27f6 b` to the natural transformation `\u03b1` defined as: `\u03b1(U) = f : a \u27f6 b` if\n`p\u2080 \u2208 U` and the unique morphism to a terminal object in `C` if `p\u2080 \u2209 U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stalk_skyscraper_presheaf_adjunction_auxs.to_skyscraper_presheaf_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_functor.category_theory.is_right_adjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf", "description": "A skyscraper presheaf is a presheaf supported at a single point: if `p\u2080 \u2208 X` is a specified\npoint, then the skyscraper presheaf `\ud835\udcd5` with value `A` is defined by `U \u21a6 A` if `p\u2080 \u2208 U` and\n`U \u21a6 *` if `p\u2080 \u2209 A` where `*` is some terminal object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stalk_skyscraper_presheaf_adjunction_auxs.counit", "description": "The counit in `presheaf.stalk \u22a3 skyscraper_presheaf_functor`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_sheaf_functor.category_theory.is_right_adjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_cocone_is_colimit_of_specializes", "description": "The cocone at `A` for the stalk functor of `skyscraper_presheaf p\u2080 A` when `y \u2208 closure {p\u2080}` is a\ncolimit", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_cocone_of_specializes_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skyscraper_presheaf_cocone_of_specializes", "description": "The cocone at `A` for the stalk functor of `skyscraper_presheaf p\u2080 A` when `y \u2208 closure {p\u2080}`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stalk_skyscraper_sheaf_adjunction", "description": "Taking stalks of a sheaf is the left adjoint functor to `skyscraper_sheaf_functor`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.has_coe_t", "description": "The canonical inclusion `A \u2192 unitization R A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.add_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.algebra_map_eq_inl_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.inl_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.coe_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.fst", "description": "The canonical projection `unitization R A \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.inl_mul_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.fst_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.mul_one_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.inl_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.snd_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.fst_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.lift_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.lift_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.fst_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.snd_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.snd", "description": "The canonical projection `unitization R A \u2192 A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.inl", "description": "The canonical inclusion `R \u2192 unitization R A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.coe_mul_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.alg_hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.inl_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.coe_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.is_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.fst_hom", "description": "The canonical `R`-algebra projection `unitization R A \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.algebra_map_eq_inl_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.snd_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.snd_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.snd_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.snd_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.snd_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.star_add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.inl_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.fst_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.coe_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.linear_map_ext", "description": " This cannot be marked `@[ext]` as it ends up being used instead of `linear_map.prod_ext` when\nworking with `R \u00d7 A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.lift", "description": " Non-unital algebra homomorphisms from `A` into a unital `R`-algebra `C` lift uniquely to\n`unitization R A \u2192\u2090[R] C`. This is the universal property of the unitization.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.star_module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.non_assoc_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.inl_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.inl_fst_add_coe_snd_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.coe_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.ind", "description": " To show a property hold on all `unitization R A` it suffices to show it holds\non terms of the form `inl r + a`.\n\nThis can be used as `induction x using unitization.ind`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.fst_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.alg_hom_ext'", "description": "See note [partially-applied ext lemmas]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.coe_non_unital_alg_hom", "description": " The coercion from a non-unital `R`-algebra `A` to its unitization `unitization R A`\nrealized as a non-unital algebra homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.inl_mul_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.inl_ring_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.inl_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.coe_non_unital_alg_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.snd_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.coe_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.coe_hom", "description": "The canonical `R`-linear inclusion `A \u2192 unitization R A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.snd_hom", "description": "The canonical `R`-linear projection `unitization R A \u2192 A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.fst_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.coe_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.add_zero_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.fst_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.fst_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization", "description": " The minimal unitization of a non-unital `R`-algebra `A`. This is just a type synonym for\n`R \u00d7 A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.snd_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.inl_ring_hom", "description": "The canonical inclusion of rings `R \u2192+* unitization R A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.snd_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.smul_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.algebra_map_eq_inl_ring_hom_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.inl_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.fst_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.inl_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.add_comm_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.star_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.algebra_map_eq_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.fst_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unitization.has_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.inversion_vsub_center", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.inversion_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.inversion_dist_center", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.dist_inversion_inversion", "description": "Distance between the images of two points under an inversion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.inversion_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.dist_inversion_center", "description": " Distance from the image of a point under inversion to the center. This formula accidentally\nworks for `x = c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.inversion_involutive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.inversion_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.inversion_bijective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.dist_center_inversion", "description": " Distance from the center of an inversion to the image of a point under the inversion. This\nformula accidentally works for `x = c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.mul_dist_le_mul_dist_add_mul_dist", "description": " **Ptolemy's inequality**: in a quadrangle `ABCD`, `|AC| * |BD| \u2264 |AB| * |CD| + |BC| * |AD|`. If\n`ABCD` is a convex cyclic polygon, then this inequality becomes an equality, see\n`euclidean_geometry.mul_dist_add_mul_dist_eq_mul_dist_of_cospherical`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.inversion_of_mem_sphere", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.inversion_inversion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.inversion", "description": " Inversion in a sphere in an affine space. This map sends each point `x` to the point `y` such\nthat `y -\u1d65 c = (R / dist x c) ^ 2 \u2022 (x -\u1d65 c)`, where `c` and `R` are the center and the radius the\nsphere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.sec_fst_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.lift_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.map_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.map_units_map_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.algebra_map_apply_eq_map_map_submonoid", "description": " If the square below commutes, the bottom map is uniquely specified:\n```lean\nR  \u2192  S\n\u2193     \u2193\nR\u2098 \u2192 S\u2098\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_eq_mul_mk'_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_add_eq_iff_add_mul_eq_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.alg_equiv", "description": " If `S`, `Q` are localizations of `R` at the submonoid `M` respectively,\nthere is an isomorphism of localizations `S \u2243\u2090[R] Q`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_eq_mk'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_spec'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.to_localization_map_to_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.sec_spec'", "description": " Given `z : S`, `is_localization.sec M z` is defined to be a pair `(x, y) : R \u00d7 M` such\nthat `z * f y = f x`, so this lemma is just an application of `S`'s commutativity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.lift_injective_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.ring_equiv_of_ring_equiv_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.unique", "description": "The localization of a singleton is a singleton. Cannot be an instance due to metavariables.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.alg_equiv_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.add", "description": " Addition in a ring localization is defined as `\u27e8a, b\u27e9 + \u27e8c, d\u27e9 = \u27e8b * c + d * a, b * d\u27e9`.\n\nShould not be confused with `add_localization.add`, which is defined as\n`\u27e8a, b\u27e9 + \u27e8c, d\u27e9 = \u27e8a + c, b + d\u27e9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.alg_equiv_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.alg_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.add_mk_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.ring_equiv_of_ring_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.to_map_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_self''", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.to_localization_with_zero_map", "description": " `is_localization.to_localization_with_zero_map M S` shows `S` is the monoid localization of\n`R` at `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization_algebra_injective", "description": "Injectivity of the underlying `algebra_map` descends to the algebra induced by localization.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.map_map", "description": " If `comm_semiring` homs `g : R \u2192+* P, l : P \u2192+* A` induce maps of localizations, the composition\nof the induced maps equals the map of localizations induced by `l \u2218 g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_list_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.ext", "description": " To show `j` and `k` agree on the whole localization, it suffices to show they agree\non the image of the base ring, if they preserve `1` and `*`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.sec_spec", "description": " Given `z : S`, `is_localization.sec M z` is defined to be a pair `(x, y) : R \u00d7 M` such\nthat `z * f y = f x` (so this lemma is true by definition).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.sec", "description": " Given a localization map `f : M \u2192* N`, a section function sending `z : N` to some\n`(x, y) : M \u00d7 S` such that `f x * (f y)\u207b\u00b9 = z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.monoid_hom_ext", "description": "See note [partially-applied ext lemmas]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_eq_iff_mk'_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization", "description": " The typeclass `is_localization (M : submodule R) S` where `S` is an `R`-algebra\nexpresses that `S` is isomorphic to the localization of `R` at `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.map_units", "description": " The typeclass `is_localization (M : submodule R) S` where `S` is an `R`-algebra\nexpresses that `S` is isomorphic to the localization of `R` at `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.surj", "description": " The typeclass `is_localization (M : submodule R) S` where `S` is an `R`-algebra\nexpresses that `S` is isomorphic to the localization of `R` at `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.eq_iff_exists", "description": " The typeclass `is_localization (M : submodule R) S` where `S` is an `R`-algebra\nexpresses that `S` is isomorphic to the localization of `R` at `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.eq_mk'_iff_mul_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.map_injective_of_injective", "description": "Injectivity of a map descends to the map induced on localizations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.alg_hom_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.sec_snd_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.lift_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.lift_mk'_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.lift", "description": " Given a localization map `f : R \u2192+* S` for a submonoid `M \u2286 R` and a map of `comm_semiring`s\n`g : R \u2192+* P` such that `g y` is invertible for all `y : M`, the homomorphism induced from\n`S` to `P` sending `z : S` to `g x * (g y)\u207b\u00b9`, where `(x, y) : R \u00d7 M` are such that\n`z = f x * (f y)\u207b\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.is_localization_iff_of_base_ring_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.is_localization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.is_domain_of_le_non_zero_divisors", "description": " A `comm_ring` `S` which is the localization of an integral domain `R` at a subset of\nnon-zero elements is an integral domain.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.alg_equiv_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.lift_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_eq_iff_eq_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_eq_of_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.algebra_map_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.neg_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mul_add_inv_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.lift_surjective_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.unique_of_zero_mem", "description": "Localizing at a submonoid with 0 inside it leads to the trivial ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.map_right_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_eq_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mul_semiring_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_mul_cancel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.ring_equiv_of_ring_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.lift_mk'", "description": " Given a localization map `f : R \u2192+* S` for a submonoid `M \u2286 R` and a map of `comm_semiring`s\n`g : R \u2192* P` such that `g y` is invertible for all `y : M`, the homomorphism induced from\n`S` to `P` maps `f x * (f y)\u207b\u00b9` to `g x * (g y)\u207b\u00b9` for all `x : R, y \u2208 M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.localization_map_bijective", "description": "If `R` is a field, then localizing at a submonoid not containing `0` adds no new elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization_algebra", "description": " Definition of the natural algebra induced by the localization of an algebra.\nGiven an algebra `R \u2192 S`, a submonoid `R` of `M`, and a localization `R\u2098` for `M`,\nlet `S\u2098` be the localization of `S` to the image of `M` under `algebra_map R S`.\nThen this is the natural algebra structure on `R\u2098 \u2192 S\u2098`, such that the entire square commutes,\nwhere `localization_map.map_comp` gives the commutativity of the underlying maps.\n\nThis instance can be helpful if you define `S\u2098 := localization (algebra.algebra_map_submonoid S M)`,\nhowever we will instead use the hypotheses `[algebra R\u2098 S\u2098] [is_scalar_tower R R\u2098 S\u2098]` in lemmas\nsince the algebra structure may arise in different ways.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_eq_of_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.map_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_sec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.neg", "description": "Negation in a ring localization is defined as `-\u27e8a, b\u27e9 = \u27e8-a, b\u27e9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.to_localization_map_eq_monoid_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.sub_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.lift_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.map_non_zero_divisors_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.alg_equiv", "description": "The localization of `R` at `M` as a quotient type is isomorphic to any other localization.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.to_localization_map", "description": "`is_localization.to_localization_map M S` shows `S` is the monoid localization of `R` at `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.map_comp_map", "description": " If `comm_semiring` homs `g : R \u2192+* P, l : P \u2192+* A` induce maps of localizations, the composition\nof the induced maps equals the map of localizations induced by `l \u2218 g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_spec_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_spec'_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_field.localization_map_bijective", "description": "If `R` is a field, then localizing at a submonoid not containing `0` adds no new elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.alg_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_multiset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.is_domain_localization", "description": " The localization at of an integral domain to a set of non-zero elements is an integral domain.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mul_mk'_eq_mk'_of_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.alg_equiv_symm_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_self'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_one_eq_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.lift_spec_mul_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.fintype'", "description": "The localization of a `fintype` is a `fintype`. Cannot be an instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_mul_mk'_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.to_localization_map_sec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_add_monoid_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.to_map_ne_zero_of_mem_non_zero_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.algebra_map_eq_map_map_submonoid", "description": " If the square below commutes, the bottom map is uniquely specified:\n```lean\nR  \u2192  S\n\u2193     \u2193\nR\u2098 \u2192 S\u2098\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.is_localization_iff_of_alg_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.ring_equiv_of_ring_equiv", "description": " If `S`, `Q` are localizations of `R` and `P` at submonoids `M, T` respectively, an\nisomorphism `j : R \u2243+* P` such that `j(M) = T` induces an isomorphism of localizations\n`S \u2243+* Q`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.is_unit_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.is_localization_iff_of_ring_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.to_localization_map_to_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.eq_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.to_localization_with_zero_map_to_localization_map_to_monoid_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'", "description": " `is_localization.mk' S` is the surjection sending `(x, y) : R \u00d7 M` to\n`f x * (f y)\u207b\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.map_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.eq_of_eq", "description": " Given a localization map `f : R \u2192+* S` for a submonoid `M \u2286 R` and a map of `comm_semiring`s\n`g : R \u2192+* P` such that `g(M) \u2286 units P`, `f x = f y \u2192 g x = g y` for all `x y : R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.ring_equiv_of_ring_equiv_eq_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.lift_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.map_left_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.no_zero_divisors_of_le_non_zero_divisors", "description": " A `comm_ring` `S` which is the localization of a ring `R` without zero divisors at a subset of\nnon-zero elements does not have zero divisors.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_add_monoid_hom", "description": "For any given denominator `b : M`, the map `a \u21a6 a / b` is an `add_monoid_hom` from `R` to\n  `localization M`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.ring_hom_ext", "description": "See note [partially-applied ext lemmas]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_mul_mk'_eq_one'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.eq_zero_of_fst_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.lift_of_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.lift_algebra_map_eq_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.monoid_of_eq_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_eq_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.map_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.alg_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.is_localization_of_alg_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.alg_equiv_symm_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.alg_equiv_symm_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_mem_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.map", "description": " Map a homomorphism `g : R \u2192+* P` to `S \u2192+* Q`, where `S` and `Q` are\nlocalizations of `R` and `P` at `M` and `T` respectively,\nsuch that `g(M) \u2286 T`.\n\nWe send `z : S` to `algebra_map P Q (g x) * (algebra_map P Q (g y))\u207b\u00b9`, where\n`(x, y) : R \u00d7 M` are such that `z = f x * (f y)\u207b\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.ne_zero_of_mk'_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.non_zero_divisors_le_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.is_localization_of_base_ring_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.add_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.alg_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_mul_cancel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.ring_equiv_of_ring_equiv_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.mk'_eq_iff_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.is_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.eq_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.of_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.to_zero_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.zero_is_terminal", "description": "A zero object is in particular terminal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.category_theory.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.eq_of_src", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.is_terminal", "description": "A zero object is in particular terminal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.from_zero_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.zero_iso_terminal", "description": "The (unique) isomorphism between the chosen terminal object and the chosen zero object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso.is_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.category_theory.iso.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.has_zero", "description": "Construct a `has_zero C` for a category with a zero object.\nThis can not be a global instance as it will trigger for every `has_zero C` typeclass search.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.has_strict_initial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.to_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.has_initial", "description": "A zero object is in particular initial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.is_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.category_theory.epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.to", "description": "If `h : is_zero X`, then `h.to Y` is a choice of unique morphism `X \u2192 Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object", "description": "A category \"has a zero object\" if it has an object which is both initial and terminal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.zero", "description": "A category \"has a zero object\" if it has an object which is both initial and terminal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.eq_of_tgt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.is_initial", "description": "A zero object is in particular initial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.zero_iso_is_initial", "description": "The (unique) isomorphism between any initial object and the zero object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.zero_iso_initial", "description": "The (unique) isomorphism between the chosen initial object and the chosen zero object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.from", "description": "If `h : is_zero X`, then `h.from Y` is a choice of unique morphism `Y \u2192 X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.zero_is_initial", "description": "A zero object is in particular initial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.iso_is_terminal", "description": "The (unique) isomorphism between any terminal object and the zero object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.has_zero_object", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.from_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.zero_to_zero_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.iso_is_initial", "description": "The (unique) isomorphism between any initial object and the zero object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object_punit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.iso", "description": "Any two zero objects are isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.unique_from", "description": "There is a unique morphism from any object `X` to the zero object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.zero_iso_is_terminal", "description": "The (unique) isomorphism between any terminal object and the zero object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object_unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.unique_to", "description": "There is a unique morphism from the zero object to any object `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero", "description": " An object `X` in a category is a *zero object* if for every object `Y`\nthere is a unique morphism `to : X \u2192 Y` and a unique morphism `from : Y \u2192 X`.\n\nThis is a characteristic predicate for `has_zero_object`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.unique_to", "description": " An object `X` in a category is a *zero object* if for every object `Y`\nthere is a unique morphism `to : X \u2192 Y` and a unique morphism `from : Y \u2192 X`.\n\nThis is a characteristic predicate for `has_zero_object`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.unique_from", "description": " An object `X` in a category is a *zero object* if for every object `Y`\nthere is a unique morphism `to : X \u2192 Y` and a unique morphism `from : Y \u2192 X`.\n\nThis is a characteristic predicate for `has_zero_object`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.iso_zero", "description": "Every zero object is isomorphic to *the* zero object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.has_terminal", "description": "A zero object is in particular terminal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.eq_from", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsingleton.strict_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone_on", "description": "A function `f` is monotone on `s` if, for all `a, b \u2208 s`, `a \u2264 b` implies `f a \u2264 f b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone.ne_of_lt_of_lt_int", "description": " If `f` is an antitone function from `\u2124` to a preorder and `x` lies between `f (n + 1)` and\n`f n`, then `x` doesn't lie in the range of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strict_mono.maximal_of_maximal_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsingleton.antitone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strict_anti.lt_iff_lt", "descripti