iption": "Construct an isomorphism of spans from components.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_right_pullback_fst_iso_hom_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_ext_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_ext_hom_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.mk_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_snd_iso_of_right_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.mk_\u03b9_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inl_pushout_left_pushout_inr_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_comparison_map_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.epi_inr_of_is_pushout_of_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone_of_left_iso_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_comp_iso_hom_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.coequalizer_ext", "description": "To check whether a morphism is coequalized by the maps of a pushout cocone, it suffices to check\n it for `inl t` and `inr t`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_comparison_comp_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.fst_colimit_cocone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_span", "description": "The type of objects for the diagram indexing a pushout, defined as a special case of\n`wide_pushout_shape`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_assoc_hom_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.iso_mk", "description": " A diagram `walking_span \u2964 C` is isomorphic to some `pushout_cocone.mk` after composing with\n`diagram_iso_span`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout.inr_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.base_change_obj_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.of_pullback_cone", "description": "This is a helper construction that can be useful when verifying that a category has all\n   pullbacks. Given `F : walking_cospan \u2964 C`, which is really the same as\n   `cospan (F.map inl) (F.map inr)`, and a pullback cone on `F.map inl` and `F.map inr`, we\n   get a cone on `F`.\n\n   If you're thinking about using this, have a look at `has_pullbacks_of_has_limit_cospan`,\n   which you may find to be an easier way of achieving your goal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.of_cocone_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.map_lift_pullback_comparison_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone_of_right_iso_\u03c0_app_none", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_snd_iso_of_left_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.epi_inl_of_is_pushout_of_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inr_comp_pushout_symmetry_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_is_pullback", "description": "The pullback cone built from the pullback projections is a pullback.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_assoc_hom_snd_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.condition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_comparison_comp_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.is_colimit.desc'", "description": "If `t` is a colimit pushout cocone over `f` and `g` and `h : Y \u27f6 W` and `k : Z \u27f6 W` are\n   morphisms satisfying `f \u226b h = g \u226b k`, then we have a factorization `l : t.X \u27f6 W` such that\n   `inl t \u226b l = h` and `inr t \u226b l = k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_ext_inv_app_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.is_limit_of_comp_mono", "description": " If `W` is the pullback of `f, g`,\nit is also the pullback of `f \u226b i, g \u226b i` for any mono `i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inr_pushout_left_pushout_inr_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inl_inl_pushout_assoc_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_symmetry_inv_comp_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone_of_left_iso_\u03c0_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.mk", "description": "A pullback cone on `f` and `g` is determined by morphisms `fst : W \u27f6 X` and `snd : W \u27f6 Y`\n   such that `fst \u226b f = snd \u226b g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout.hom_ext", "description": "Two morphisms out of a pushout are equal if their compositions with the pushout morphisms are\n   equal", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_cospan.one", "description": "The central point of the walking cospan.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.of_cocone", "description": "Given `F : walking_span \u2964 C`, which is really the same as `span (F.map fst) (F.map snd)`,\n   and a cocone on `F`, we get a pushout cocone on `F.map fst` and `F.map snd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.is_colimit.hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_ext_hom_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.iso_mk_inv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone_of_left_iso", "description": "If `f : X \u27f6 Y` is iso, then `Y \u2a3f[X] Z \u2245 Z`. This is the explicit colimit cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_symmetry_inv_comp_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_symmetry_hom_of_epi_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout.inr", "description": "The second inclusion into the pushout of `f` and `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.of_cone", "description": "Given `F : walking_cospan \u2964 C`, which is really the same as `cospan (F.map inl) (F.map inr)`,\n   and a cone on `F`, we get a pullback cone on `F.map inl` and `F.map inr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_comp_iso_hom_app_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.of_cone_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_is_pushout_of_epi_comp", "description": "The pushout of `f, g` is also the pullback of `h \u226b f, h \u226b g` for any epi `h`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone_of_right_iso_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout.map_lift_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.lift", "description": "A pair of morphisms `h : W \u27f6 X` and `k : W \u27f6 Y` satisfying `h \u226b f = k \u226b g` induces a morphism\n   `pullback.lift : W \u27f6 pullback f g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_right_pullback_fst_iso_hom_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.base_change_obj_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_inl_iso_of_left_factors_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout.desc", "description": "A pair of morphisms `h : Y \u27f6 W` and `k : Z \u27f6 W` satisfying `f \u226b h = g \u226b k` induces a morphism\n   `pushout.desc : pushout f g \u27f6 W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone_of_left_iso_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.inl", "description": "The first inclusion of a pushout cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_pullback_to_prod", "description": "The map `X \u00d7[Z] Y \u27f6 X \u00d7 Y` is mono.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_span.hom.fst", "description": "The left arrow of the walking span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_assoc_hom_snd_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inl_comp_pushout_symmetry_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.desc'", "description": "A pair of morphisms `h : Y \u27f6 W` and `k : Z \u27f6 W` satisfying `f \u226b h = g \u226b k` induces a morphism\n   `l : pushout f g \u27f6 W` such that `pushout.inl \u226b l = h` and `pushout.inr \u226b l = k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_span_op_equiv_counit_iso_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inr_comp_pushout_comparison", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_assoc_hom_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_right_pullback_fst_iso_hom_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.inl_colimit_cocone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.lift'", "description": "A pair of morphisms `h : W \u27f6 X` and `k : W \u27f6 Y` satisfying `h \u226b f = k \u226b g` induces a morphism\n   `l : W \u27f6 pullback f g` such that `l \u226b pullback.fst = h` and `l \u226b pullback.snd = k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone_of_left_iso_is_limit", "description": "Verify that the constructed cocone is indeed a colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.is_limit_aux'", "description": "This is another convenient method to verify that a pullback cone is a limit cone. It\n   only asks for a proof of facts that carry any mathematical content, and allows access to the\n   same `s` for all parts.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.iso_mk_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_assoc", "description": "The canonical isomorphism `(X\u2081 \u00d7[Y\u2081] X\u2082) \u00d7[Y\u2082] X\u2083 \u2245 X\u2081 \u00d7[Y\u2081] (X\u2082 \u00d7[Y\u2082] X\u2083)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout.inr_of_epi", "description": "The pushout of an epimorphism is an epimorphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_comparison", "description": "The comparison morphism for the pushout of `f,g`.\nThis is an isomorphism iff `G` preserves the pushout of `f,g`; see\n`category_theory/limits/preserves/shapes/pullbacks.lean`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.is_limit_aux", "description": "This is a slightly more convenient method to verify that a pullback cone is a limit cone. It\n   only asks for a proof of facts that carry any mathematical content", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_comp_iso_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_assoc_inv_fst_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.map", "description": "Given such a diagram, then there is a natural morphism `W \u00d7\u209b X \u27f6 Y \u00d7\u209c Z`.\n\n    W  \u27f6  Y\n      \u2198      \u2198\n        S  \u27f6  T\n      \u2197      \u2197\n    X  \u27f6  Z", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.mk", "description": "A pushout cocone on `f` and `g` is determined by morphisms `inl : Y \u27f6 W` and `inr : Z \u27f6 W` such\n   that `f \u226b inl = g \u21a0 inr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pullback_of_left_factors_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inl_comp_pushout_symmetry_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_ext_inv_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_comp_iso_app_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_left_pushout_inr_iso", "description": "The canonical isomorphism `(Y \u2a3f[X] Z) \u2a3f[Z] W \u2245 Y \u00d7[X] W`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout.condition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.mk_\u03c0_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.\u03b9_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_comp_iso_hom_app_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout.condition_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pushout_of_left_factors_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_right_pullback_fst_iso", "description": "The canonical isomorphism `W \u00d7[X] (X \u00d7[Z] Y) \u2245 W \u00d7[Z] Y`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout.congr_hom_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.iso_mk_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone_of_right_iso_\u03c0_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.inr", "description": "The second inclusion of a pushout cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inl_comp_pushout_symmetry_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone_of_right_iso", "description": "If `g : Y \u27f6 Z` is iso, then `X \u00d7[Z] Y \u2245 X`. This is the explicit limit cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.equalizer_ext", "description": "To check whether a morphism is equalized by the maps of a pullback cone, it suffices to check\n it for `fst t` and `snd t`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pullback", "description": "`has_pullback f g` represents a particular choice of limiting cone\nfor the pair of morphisms `f : X \u27f6 Z` and `g : Y \u27f6 Z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout.inl_of_epi", "description": "The pushout of an epimorphism is an epimorphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_comparison_comp_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.map_desc", "description": "The canonical map `X \u00d7\u209b Y \u27f6 X \u00d7\u209c Y` given `S \u27f6 T`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.snd", "description": "The second projection of the pullback of `f` and `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_cospan.left", "description": "The left point of the walking cospan.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_assoc_is_pullback", "description": "`(X\u2081 \u00d7[Y\u2081] X\u2082) \u00d7[Y\u2082] X\u2083` is the pullback `X\u2081 \u00d7[Y\u2081] (X\u2082 \u00d7[Y\u2082] X\u2083)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pullback_of_right_factors_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inl_comp_pushout_comparison", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.right_square_is_pushout", "description": "Given\n\nX\u2081 - f\u2081 -> X\u2082 - f\u2082 -> X\u2083\n|          |          |\ni\u2081         i\u2082         i\u2083\n\u2228          \u2228          \u2228\nY\u2081 - g\u2081 -> Y\u2082 - g\u2082 -> Y\u2083\n\nThen the right square is a pushout if the left square and the big square are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.map_desc_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone_of_left_iso_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_span_op_equiv_inverse_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inr_pushout_assoc_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.epi_of_is_colimit_mk_id_id", "description": "`f` is an epi if the pushout cocone `(\ud835\udfd9 X, \ud835\udfd9 X)` is a colimit for the pair `(f, f)`.\nThe converse is given in `pushout_cocone.is_colimit_mk_id_id`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_comp_iso_inv_app_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_comparison", "description": "The comparison morphism for the pullback of `f,g`.\nThis is an isomorphism iff `G` preserves the pullback of `f,g`; see\n`category_theory/limits/preserves/shapes/pullbacks.lean`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout.map", "description": "Given such a diagram, then there is a natural morphism `W \u2a3f\u209b X \u27f6 Y \u2a3f\u209c Z`.\n\n        W  \u27f6  Y\n      \u2197      \u2197\n    S  \u27f6  T\n      \u2198      \u2198\n        X  \u27f6  Z", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.is_limit_mk_id_id", "description": "The pullback cone `(\ud835\udfd9 X, \ud835\udfd9 X)` for the pair `(f, f)` is a limit if `f` is a mono. The converse is\nshown in `mono_of_pullback_is_id`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_snd_iso_of_left_factors_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.mk_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_right_pullback_fst_iso_inv_snd_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_cospan.hom", "description": "The type of arrows for the diagram indexing a pullback.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout.inl_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.snd_colimit_cocone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_cospan.ext", "description": " To construct an isomorphism of cones over the walking cospan,\nit suffices to construct an isomorphism\nof the cone points and check it commutes with the legs to `left` and `right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_pushout_left_is_pushout", "description": "`(X\u2081 \u2a3f[Z\u2081] X\u2082) \u2a3f[Z\u2082] X\u2083` is the pushout `(X\u2081 \u2a3f[Z\u2081] X\u2082) \u00d7[X\u2082] (X\u2082 \u2a3f[Z\u2082] X\u2083)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone_of_left_iso_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_symmetry_inv_comp_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.is_limit_of_factors", "description": "Suppose `f` and `g` are two morphisms with a common codomain and `s` is a limit cone over the\n   diagram formed by `f` and `g`. Suppose `f` and `g` both factor through a monomorphism `h` via\n   `x` and `y`, respectively.  Then `s` is also a limit cone over the diagram formed by `x` and\n   `y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_ext_inv_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_cospan_op_equiv", "description": "The duality equivalence `walking_cospan\u1d52\u1d56 \u224c walking_span`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pushout_assoc_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_comp_iso_inv_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.\u03c0_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.mk_\u03c0_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.fst_of_mono", "description": "The pullback of a monomorphism is a monomorphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_ext_inv_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span", "description": "`span f g` is the functor from the walking span hitting `f` and `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout.congr_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_cospan.quiver.hom.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone_of_left_iso_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_comp_iso_app_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_comp_iso_hom_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_assoc_inv_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone_of_right_iso_is_limit", "description": "Verify that the constructed cocone is indeed a colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inr_inl_pushout_assoc_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_assoc_symm_is_pullback", "description": "`X\u2081 \u00d7[Y\u2081] (X\u2082 \u00d7[Y\u2082] X\u2083)` is the pullback `(X\u2081 \u00d7[Y\u2081] X\u2082) \u00d7[Y\u2082] X\u2083`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone_of_right_iso_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_cospan_op_equiv_inverse_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inr_inr_pushout_assoc_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.ext", "description": " To construct an isomorphism of pushout cocones, it suffices to construct an isomorphism\nof the cocone points and check it commutes with `inl` and `inr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_comp_iso_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_span.zero", "description": "The central point of the walking span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_pushout_right_is_pushout", "description": "`X\u2081 \u2a3f[Z\u2081] (X\u2082 \u2a3f[Z\u2082] X\u2083)` is the pushout `(X\u2081 \u2a3f[Z\u2081] X\u2082) \u00d7[X\u2082] (X\u2082 \u2a3f[Z\u2082] X\u2083)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_symmetry_hom_comp_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inr_comp_pushout_comparison_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_cospan", "description": "The type of objects for the diagram indexing a pullback, defined as a special case of\n`wide_pullback_shape`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagram_iso_cospan", "description": "Every diagram indexing an pullback is naturally isomorphic (actually, equal) to a `cospan`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_assoc_inv_fst_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.mono_of_is_limit_mk_id_id", "description": "`f` is a mono if the pullback cone `(\ud835\udfd9 X, \ud835\udfd9 X)` is a limit for the pair `(f, f)`. The converse is\ngiven in `pullback_cone.is_id_of_mono`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inr_inl_pushout_assoc_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout.map_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.congr_hom", "description": " If `f\u2081 = f\u2082` and `g\u2081 = g\u2082`, we may construct a canonical\nisomorphism `pullback f\u2081 g\u2081 \u2245 pullback f\u2082 g\u2082`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_assoc", "description": "The canonical isomorphism `(X\u2081 \u2a3f[Z\u2081] X\u2082) \u2a3f[Z\u2082] X\u2083 \u2245 X\u2081 \u2a3f[Z\u2081] (X\u2082 \u2a3f[Z\u2082] X\u2083)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inl_inr_pushout_assoc_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_comp_iso_inv_app_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.\u03b9_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_right_pullback_fst_iso_inv_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pushout_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.big_square_is_pullback", "description": "Given\n\nX\u2081 - f\u2081 -> X\u2082 - f\u2082 -> X\u2083\n|          |          |\ni\u2081         i\u2082         i\u2083\n\u2228          \u2228          \u2228\nY\u2081 - g\u2081 -> Y\u2082 - g\u2082 -> Y\u2083\n\nThen the big square is a pullback if both the small squares are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone_of_left_iso_\u03b9_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.hom_ext", "description": "Two morphisms into a pullback are equal if their compositions with the pullback morphisms are\n   equal", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.inr_colimit_cocone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_comp_iso_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_ext_hom_app_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.is_colimit.mk", "description": "This is a more convenient formulation to show that a `pushout_cocone` constructed using\n`pushout_cocone.mk` is a colimit cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.mono_snd_of_is_pullback_of_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_comp_iso_hom_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone_of_right_iso_\u03b9_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_map_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.of_pullback_cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inr_inl_pushout_left_pushout_inr_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_cospan.hom.id", "description": "The identity arrows of the walking cospan.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_span.right", "description": "The right point of the walking span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_span_op_equiv_functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone", "description": "A pullback cone is just a cone on the cospan formed by two morphisms `f : X \u27f6 Z` and\n   `g : Y \u27f6 Z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.iso_mk_inv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.is_colimit_mk_id_id", "description": "The pushout cocone `(\ud835\udfd9 X, \ud835\udfd9 X)` for the pair `(f, f)` is a colimit if `f` is an epi. The converse is\nshown in `epi_of_is_colimit_mk_id_id`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout.congr_hom", "description": " If `f\u2081 = f\u2082` and `g\u2081 = g\u2082`, we may construct a canonical\nisomorphism `pushout f\u2081 g\u2081 \u2245 pullback f\u2082 g\u2082`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.mono_fst_of_is_pullback_of_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.condition_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_assoc_is_pushout", "description": "`(X\u2081 \u2a3f[Z\u2081] X\u2082) \u2a3f[Z\u2082] X\u2083` is the pushout `X\u2081 \u2a3f[Z\u2081] (X\u2082 \u2a3f[Z\u2082] X\u2083)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inl_pushout_left_pushout_inr_iso_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone_of_right_iso_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inr_pushout_left_pushout_inr_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.base_change", "description": " Given a morphism `f : X \u27f6 Y`, we can take morphisms over `Y` to morphisms over `X` via\npullbacks. This is right adjoint to `over.map` (TODO)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.condition_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_is_pullback_of_comp_mono", "description": "The pullback of `f, g` is also the pullback of `f \u226b i, g \u226b i` for any mono `i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_cospan_op_equiv_unit_iso_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.of_pushout_cocone_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagram_iso_span_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inr_pushout_left_pushout_inr_iso_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.flip_is_colimit", "description": "The flip of a pushout square is a pushout square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone_of_right_iso_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_comp_iso", "description": "A functor applied to a cospan is a cospan.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_span.ext", "description": " To construct an isomorphism of cocones over the walking span,\nit suffices to construct an isomorphism\nof the cocone points and check it commutes with the legs from `left` and `right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone_of_right_iso_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pushout_of_right_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_comp_iso_inv_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pullbacks", "description": "`has_pullbacks` represents a choice of pullback for every pair of morphisms\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/001W>", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inl_inl_pushout_assoc_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.flip_is_limit", "description": "The flip of a pullback square is a pullback square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pushouts_of_has_colimit_span", "description": "If `C` has all colimits of diagrams `span f g`, then it has all pushouts", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_cospan.hom.inl", "description": "The left arrow of the walking cospan.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout", "description": "`pushout f g` computes the pushout of a pair of morphisms with the same source.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_comp_iso_inv_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_span_op_equiv_unit_iso_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_assoc_inv_fst_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.mk_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_ext_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_assoc_hom_snd_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_ext_inv_app_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_right_pullback_fst_iso_inv_snd_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pullback_symmetry", "description": "Making this a global instance would make the typeclass seach go in an infinite loop.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone_of_right_iso_\u03b9_app_none", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fst_iso_of_mono_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.fst", "description": "The first projection of the pullback of `f` and `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_snd_iso_of_right_factors_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_symmetry_hom_of_mono_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inr_pushout_assoc_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_map_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.base_change_map_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.epi_coprod_to_pushout", "description": "The map ` X \u2a3f Y \u27f6 X \u2a3f[Z] Y` is epi.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_symmetry_inv_comp_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_ext_inv_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pushout_of_epi_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagram_iso_span_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.fst", "description": "The first projection of a pullback cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_comp_iso_hom_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pushout_of_right_factors_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_ext_app_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pushouts", "description": "`has_pushouts` represents a choice of pushout for every pair of morphisms", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.mk_\u03b9_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_span_op_equiv_functor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone_of_left_iso_is_limit", "description": "Verify that the constructed limit cone is indeed a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.mk_\u03b9_app_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout.inl", "description": "The first inclusion into the pushout of `f` and `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.iso_mk", "description": " A diagram `walking_cospan \u2964 C` is isomorphic to some `pullback_cone.mk` after\ncomposing with `diagram_iso_cospan`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.condition_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback", "description": "`pullback f g` computes the pullback of a pair of morphisms with the same target.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_comp_iso_inv_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_span.hom.snd", "description": "The right arrow of the walking span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_span.quiver.hom.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_comparison_comp_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone_of_right_iso_is_limit", "description": "Verify that the constructed limit cone is indeed a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_assoc_inv_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.condition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.mk_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_span.hom.id", "description": "The identity arrows of the walking span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagram_iso_cospan_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pullback_assoc_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.lift_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan", "description": "`cospan f g` is the functor from the walking cospan hitting `f` and `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inr_iso_of_epi_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.mk_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inl_eq_inr_of_epi_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.condition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_cospan.hom.inr", "description": "The right arrow of the walking cospan.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_span.left", "description": "The left point of the walking span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inr_comp_pushout_symmetry_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone_of_right_iso_\u03c0_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagram_iso_cospan_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_map_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_symmetry_hom_comp_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.ext", "description": " To construct an isomorphism of pullback cones, it suffices to construct an isomorphism\nof the cone points and check it commutes with `fst` and `snd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_inr_iso_of_right_factors_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_assoc_inv_fst_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone_of_left_iso_\u03b9_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_comp_iso", "description": "A functor applied to a span is a span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pullbacks_of_has_limit_cospan", "description": "If `C` has all limits of diagrams `cospan f g`, then it has all pullbacks", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.left_square_is_pullback", "description": "Given\n\nX\u2081 - f\u2081 -> X\u2082 - f\u2082 -> X\u2083\n|          |          |\ni\u2081         i\u2082         i\u2083\n\u2228          \u2228          \u2228\nY\u2081 - g\u2081 -> Y\u2082 - g\u2082 -> Y\u2083\n\nThen the left square is a pullback if the right square and the big square are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.condition_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_span.hom", "description": "The type of arrows for the diagram indexing a pushout.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_cospan_op_equiv_functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone_of_left_iso_\u03c0_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_cokernel_pair_of_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pullback_of_comp_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pullbacks_of_has_wide_pullbacks", "description": "Having wide pullback at any universe level implies having binary pullbacks.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.is_colimit_of_factors", "description": "Suppose `f` and `g` are two morphisms with a common domain and `s` is a colimit cocone over the\n   diagram formed by `f` and `g`. Suppose `f` and `g` both factor through an epimorphism `h` via\n   `x` and `y`, respectively. Then `s` is also a colimit cocone over the diagram formed by `x` and\n   `y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.mk_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inr_comp_pushout_symmetry_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_comp_iso_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.of_cocone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pushout_of_left_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone_of_right_iso_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.map_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.big_square_is_pushout", "description": "Given\n\nX\u2081 - f\u2081 -> X\u2082 - f\u2082 -> X\u2083\n|          |          |\ni\u2081         i\u2082         i\u2083\n\u2228          \u2228          \u2228\nY\u2081 - g\u2081 -> Y\u2082 - g\u2082 -> Y\u2083\n\nThen the big square is a pushout if both the small squares are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inr_inr_pushout_assoc_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_ext_hom_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pullback_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_symmetry", "description": "The isomorphism `X \u00d7[Z] Y \u2245 Y \u00d7[Z] X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_comparison_map_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout.inr_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_symmetry_hom_comp_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_span_op_equiv", "description": "The duality equivalence `walking_span\u1d52\u1d56 \u224c walking_cospan`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_ext_app_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.of_pushout_cocone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone_of_left_iso_\u03c0_app_none", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_map_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inl_inl_pushout_left_pushout_inr_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_cospan_op_equiv_counit_iso_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout.inl_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.is_limit.mk", "description": "This is a more convenient formulation to show that a `pullback_cone` constructed using\n`pullback_cone.mk` is a limit cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.lift_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.snd_of_mono", "description": "The pullback of a monomorphism is a monomorphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_right_pullback_fst_iso_hom_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_is_pushout", "description": "The pushout cocone built from the pushout coprojections is a pushout.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.condition_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_right_pullback_fst_iso_inv_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.snd", "description": "The second projection of a pullback cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.mk_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pushout", "description": "`has_pushout f g` represents a particular choice of colimiting cocone\nfor the pair of morphisms `f : X \u27f6 Y` and `g : X \u27f6 Z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone", "description": "A pushout cocone is just a cocone on the span formed by two morphisms `f : X \u27f6 Y` and\n   `g : X \u27f6 Z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone_of_right_iso", "description": "If `f : X \u27f6 Z` is iso, then `Y \u2a3f[X] Z \u2245 Y`. This is the explicit colimit cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_right_pullback_fst_iso_inv_snd_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pushout_symmetry", "description": "Making this a global instance would make the typeclass seach go in an infinite loop.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.\u03c0_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_span_op_equiv_counit_iso_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.is_colimit_of_epi_comp", "description": " If `W` is the pushout of `f, g`,\nit is also the pushout of `h \u226b f, h \u226b g` for any epi `h`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_inl_iso_of_right_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.mk_\u03c0_app_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.mk_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_pullback_left_is_pullback", "description": "`(X\u2081 \u00d7[Y\u2081] X\u2082) \u00d7[Y\u2082] X\u2083` is the pullback `(X\u2081 \u00d7[Y\u2081] X\u2082) \u00d7[X\u2082] (X\u2082 \u00d7[Y\u2082] X\u2083)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_ext_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inr_comp_pushout_symmetry_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_cospan_op_equiv_counit_iso_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.congr_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagram_iso_span", "description": "Every diagram indexing a pushout is naturally isomorphic (actually, equal) to a `span`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_cospan.right", "description": "The right point of the walking cospan.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_ext_hom_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_assoc_symm_is_pushout", "description": "`X\u2081 \u2a3f[Z\u2081] (X\u2082 \u2a3f[Z\u2082] X\u2083)` is the pushout `(X\u2081 \u2a3f[Z\u2081] X\u2082) \u2a3f[Z\u2082] X\u2083`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone_of_left_iso_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.lift_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.of_pullback_cone_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_span_op_equiv_inverse_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.is_colimit_aux", "description": "This is a slightly more convenient method to verify that a pushout cocone is a colimit cocone.\n   It only asks for a proof of facts that carry any mathematical content", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inl_inl_pushout_left_pushout_inr_iso_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_symmetry_hom_comp_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.of_cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.of_pushout_cocone", "description": "This is a helper construction that can be useful when verifying that a category has all\n   pushout. Given `F : walking_span \u2964 C`, which is really the same as\n   `span (F.map fst) (F.mal snd)`, and a pushout cocone on `F.map fst` and `F.map snd`,\n   we get a cocone on `F`.\n\n   If you're thinking about using this, have a look at `has_pushouts_of_has_colimit_span`, which\n   you may find to be an easiery way of achieving your goal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout.map_lift", "description": "The canonical map `X \u2a3f\u209b Y \u27f6 X \u2a3f\u209c Y` given `S \u27f6 T`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_ext_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone.is_colimit_aux'", "description": "This is another convenient method to verify that a pushout cocone is a colimit cocone. It\n   only asks for a proof of facts that carry any mathematical content, and allows access to the\n   same `s` for all parts.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.congr_hom_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_cospan_op_equiv_unit_iso_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.is_limit.lift'", "description": "If `t` is a limit pullback cone over `f` and `g` and `h : W \u27f6 X` and `k : W \u27f6 Y` are such that\n   `h \u226b f = k \u226b g`, then we have `l : W \u27f6 t.X` satisfying `l \u226b fst t = h` and `l \u226b snd t = k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_right_pullback_fst_iso_inv_snd_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inl_iso_of_epi_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inl_comp_pushout_symmetry_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.map_lift_pullback_comparison", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cospan_ext", "description": "Construct an isomorphism of cospans from components.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_cospan_op_equiv_inverse_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_cospan_op_equiv_functor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.snd_iso_of_mono_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inr_pushout_left_pushout_inr_iso_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pullback_of_left_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inl_pushout_assoc_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_assoc_hom_snd_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inl_pushout_assoc_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inl_inr_pushout_assoc_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_symmetry", "description": "The isomorphism `Y \u2a3f[X] Z \u2245 Z \u2a3f[X] Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone.is_limit.hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_pullback_right_is_pullback", "description": "`X\u2081 \u00d7[Y\u2081] (X\u2082 \u00d7[Y\u2082] X\u2083)` is the pullback `(X\u2081 \u00d7[Y\u2081] X\u2082) \u00d7[X\u2082] (X\u2082 \u00d7[Y\u2082] X\u2083)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_inr_iso_of_left_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inr_inl_pushout_left_pushout_inr_iso_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_pullback_of_right_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_cone_of_left_iso", "description": "If `f : X \u27f6 Z` is iso, then `X \u00d7[Z] Y \u2245 Y`. This is the explicit limit cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.lift_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inl_comp_pushout_comparison_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fst_eq_snd_of_mono_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.span_ext_hom_app_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_span_op_equiv_unit_iso_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_kernel_pair_of_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pushout_cocone_of_right_iso_\u03b9_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.measurable_set_mul_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_fin_strongly_measurable.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.of_uncurry_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.fin_strongly_measurable_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.mono_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.fin_strongly_measurable.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.const_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.ae_strongly_measurable_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_fin_strongly_measurable.ae_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strongly_measurable_iff_measurable", "description": "In a space with second countable topology, strongly measurable and measurable are equivalent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_fin_strongly_measurable_iff_ae_measurable", "description": "In a space with second countable topology and a sigma-finite measure,\n `ae_fin_strongly_measurable` and `ae_measurable` are equivalent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_strongly_measurable_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.approx", "description": " A sequence of simple functions such that `\u2200 x, tendsto (\u03bb n, hf.approx n x) at_top (\ud835\udcdd (f x))`.\nThat property is given by `strongly_measurable.tendsto_approx`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.strongly_measurable_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.ae_strongly_measurable_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.ae_strongly_measurable_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.indicator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.measurable_set_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.smul_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.comp_quasi_measure_preserving", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.subsingleton.strongly_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.approx_bounded", "description": " Similar to `strongly_measurable.approx`, but enforces that the norm of every function in the\nsequence is less than `c` everywhere. If `\u2016f x\u2016 \u2264 c` this sequence of simple functions verifies\n`tendsto (\u03bb n, hf.approx_bounded n x) at_top (\ud835\udcdd (f x))`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.vadd_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.is_separable_ae_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.fin_strongly_measurable_iff_strongly_measurable_and_exists_set_sigma_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_fin_strongly_measurable.ae_eq_zero_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.fin_strongly_measurable.inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strongly_measurable_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "second_countable_topology_either_of_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.ae_strongly_measurable_uIoc_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable", "description": "A function is `strongly_measurable` if it is the limit of simple functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.comp_ae_strongly_measurable", "description": " The composition of a continuous function and an ae strongly measurable function is ae strongly\nmeasurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.prod_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.fin_strongly_measurable.sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.ae_mem_imp_eq_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_strongly_measurable_of_tendsto_ae", "description": " An almost everywhere sequential limit of almost everywhere strongly measurable functions is\nalmost everywhere strongly measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.subsingleton.ae_strongly_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.strongly_measurable_of_measurable_space_le_on", "description": " If the restriction to a set `s` of a \u03c3-algebra `m` is included in the restriction to `s` of\nanother \u03c3-algebra `m\u2082` (hypothesis `hs`), the set `s` is `m` measurable and a function `f` supported\non `s` is `m`-strongly-measurable, then `f` is also `m\u2082`-strongly-measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_fin_strongly_measurable.mk", "description": " A `fin_strongly_measurable` function such that `f =\u1d50[\u03bc] hf.mk f`. See lemmas\n`fin_strongly_measurable_mk` and `ae_eq_mk`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.fin_strongly_measurable.tendsto_approx", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.fin_strongly_measurable.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strongly_measurable.apply_continuous_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.is_separable_range", "description": "The range of a strongly measurable function is separable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_fin_strongly_measurable.measurable_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.fin_strongly_measurable.measurable", "description": "A finitely strongly measurable function is measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.ae_strongly_measurable", "description": " A continuous function from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2` is ae strongly measurable when one of the two spaces is\nsecond countable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_strongly_measurable_indicator_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_strongly_measurable_smul_const_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.strongly_measurable_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.strongly_measurable_sum'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.fin_strongly_measurable.exists_set_sigma_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "second_countable_topology_either_of_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.tendsto_approx", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.strongly_measurable_sum'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.strongly_measurable_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"n