urable.mk", "description": " A `strongly_measurable` function such that `f =\u1d50[\u03bc] hf.mk f`. See lemmas\n`strongly_measurable_mk` and `ae_eq_mk`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.strongly_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.add_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.real_to_nnreal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_strongly_measurable_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_fin_strongly_measurable.inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strongly_measurable_iff_measurable_separable", "description": " A function is strongly measurable if and only if it is measurable and has separable\nrange.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.fin_strongly_measurable.strongly_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.measurable_set_eq_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_strongly_measurable_with_density_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.ae_strongly_measurable_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.ae_strongly_measurable_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.comp_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.ae_strongly_measurable_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.ite", "description": " this is slightly different from `strongly_measurable.piecewise`. It can be used to show\n`strongly_measurable (ite (x=0) 0 1)` by\n`exact strongly_measurable.ite (measurable_set_singleton 0) strongly_measurable_const\nstrongly_measurable_const`, but replacing `strongly_measurable.ite` by\n`strongly_measurable.piecewise` in that example proof does not work.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable", "description": " A function is `ae_strongly_measurable` with respect to a measure `\u03bc` if it is almost everywhere\nequal to the limit of a sequence of simple functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.fin_strongly_measurable.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.comp_ae_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.fin_strongly_measurable_iff_measurable", "description": "In a space with second countable topology and a sigma-finite measure, `fin_strongly_measurable`\n and `measurable` are equivalent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_fin_strongly_measurable.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_strongly_measurable_Union_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable_zero_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.comp_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.fin_strongly_measurable", "description": "A function is `fin_strongly_measurable` with respect to a measure if it is the limit of simple\n functions with support with finite measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.prod_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.fin_strongly_measurable.ae_fin_strongly_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.ae_strongly_measurable_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.ae_strongly_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.edist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_fin_strongly_measurable_zer