ts norm in `E` is equal to its\nnorm in `s`.\n\nThis is a reversed version of the `simp` lemma `submodule.coe_norm` for use by `norm_cast`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_of_norm_sub_eq_zero", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `norm_div_eq_zero_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_self_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_norm_lt_iff'", "description": " The seminorm of an element in a product space is `< r` if and only if the norm of each\ncomponent is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "seminormed_group.to_has_nnnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnnorm_le_insert", "description": "**Alias** of `nnnorm_le_nnnorm_add_nnnorm_sub`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_one_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_add_self_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom_class.lipschitz_of_bound", "description": " A homomorphism `f` of seminormed groups is Lipschitz, if there exists a constant `C` such that\nfor all `x`, one has `\u2016f x\u2016 \u2264 C * \u2016x\u2016`. The analogous condition for a linear map of\n(semi)normed spaces is in `normed_space.operator_norm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_norm_nhds_within_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.nnnorm_abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.normed_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.exists_bound_of_continuous_on'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.norm_coe", "description": "If `x` is an element of a subgroup `s` of a seminormed group `E`, its norm\nin `s` is equal to its norm in `E`.\n\nThis is a reversed version of the `simp` lemma `add_subgroup.coe_norm` for use by `norm_cast`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom_class.continuous_of_bound", "description": " A homomorphism `f` of seminormed groups is continuous, if there exists a constant `C` such that\nfor all `x`, one has `\u2016f x\u2016 \u2264 C * \u2016x\u