`x` is an element of a subgroup `s` of a seminormed group `E`, its norm in `s` is equal to\nits norm in `E`.\n\nThis is a reversed version of the `simp` lemma `subgroup.coe_norm` for use by `norm_cast`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_mem_closed_ball_add_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_compact_support.exists_pos_le_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_group", "description": " A normed group is a group endowed with a norm for which `dist x y = \u2016x / y\u2016` defines a metric\nspace structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_group.to_has_norm", "description": " A normed group is a group endowed with a norm for which `dist x y = \u2016x / y\u2016` defines a metric\nspace structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_group.to_group", "description": " A normed group is a group endowed with a norm for which `dist x y = \u2016x / y\u2016` defines a metric\nspace structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_group.to_metric_space", "description": " A normed group is a group endowed with a norm for which `dist x y = \u2016x / y\u2016` defines a metric\nspace structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_group.dist_eq", "description": " A normed group is a group endowed with a norm for which `dist x y = \u2016x / y\u2016` defines a metric\nspace structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ball_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "seminormed_comm_group.to_seminormed_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_le_norm_add_norm_sub'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_zero_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_nnnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group.of_separation", "description": "Construct a `normed_add_group` from a `seminormed_add_group` satisfying\n`\u2200 x, \u2016x\u2016 = 0 \u2192 x = 0`. This avoids having to go back to the `(pseudo_)metric_space` level when\ndeclaring a `normed_add_group` instance as a special case of a more general `seminormed_add_group`\ninstance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.has_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_le_of_mem_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.seminormed_add_group", "description": "Finite product of seminormed groups, using the sup norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.seminormed_add_group", "description": " The (additive) norm on the multiplicative opposite is the same as the norm on the original type.\n\nNote that we do not provide this more generally as `has_norm E\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`, as this is not always a good\nchoice of norm in the multiplicative `seminormed_group E` case.\n\nWe could repeat this instance to provide a `[seminormed_group E] : seminormed_group E\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56` instance,\nbut that case would likely never be used.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.coe_norm", "description": " If `x` is an element of a subgroup `s` of a seminormed group `E`, its norm in `s` is equal to\nits norm in `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_of_dual", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.ennnorm_eq_of_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.seminormed_group", "description": "Product of seminormed groups, using the sup norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_comm_group.uniformity_basis_dist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_group.of_mul_dist'", "description": "Construct a normed group from a multiplication-invariant pseudodistance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_pow_le_mul_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_mem_closed_ball_mul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smul_closed_ball''", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_compact_support.norm", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `has_compact_support_norm_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "seminormed_add_group.to_has_nnnorm", "de