lso known as the **Huang degree theorem**", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.Q.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.V.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.f_succ_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.Q.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.f_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.g_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.f_squared", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.epsilon_total", "description": "Any vector in `V n` annihilated by all `\u03b5 p`'s is zero.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.Q", "description": "The hypercube in dimension `n`.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.Q.adj_iff_proj_eq", "description": " If `p` and `q` in `Q (n+1)` have different values at zero then they are adjacent\niff their projections to `Q n` are equal.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.V.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.dim_V", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.Q.card", "description": "`Q n` has 2^n elements.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.exists_eigenvalue", "description": " If a subset `H` of `Q (m+1)` has cardinal at least `2^m + 1` then the\nsubspace of `V (m+1)` spanned by the corresponding basis vectors non-trivially\nintersects the range of `g m`.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.Q.unique", "description": "`Q 0` has a unique element.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.Q.adjacent", "description": " The adjacency relation defining the graph structure on `Q n`:\n`p.adjacent q` if there is an edge from `p` to `q` in `Q n`.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.f_image_g", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.\u03b5", "description": "The dual basis to `e`, defined inductively.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.V.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.Q.adjacent.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.f", "description": " The linear operator $f_n$ corresponding to Huang's matrix $A_n$,\ndefined inductively as a \u211d-linear map from `V n` to `V n`.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.g", "description": "The linear operator $g_m$ corresponding to Knuth's matrix $B_m$.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.duality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.Q.adj_iff_proj_adj", "description": " If `p` and `q` in `Q (n+1)` have the same value at zero then they are adjacent\niff their projections to `Q n` are adjacent.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.\u03c0", "description": " The projection from `Q (n + 1)` to `Q n` forgetting the first value\n(ie. the image of zero).", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.Q.not_adjacent_zero", "description": "In `Q 0`, no two vertices are adjacent.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.dual_bases_e_\u03b5", "description": " `e` and `\u03b5` are dual families of vectors. It implies that `e` is indeed a basis\nand `\u03b5` computes coefficients of decompositions of vectors on that basis.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.e_zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sensitivity.V.finite_dimensional", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "sym_alg.unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym_alg.unsym_ne_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym_alg.unsym_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym_alg.mul_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym_alg.unsym_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym_alg.sym", "description": "The element of `sym_