"", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym_alg.unsym", "description": "The element of `\u03b1` represented by `x : \u03b1\u02e2\u02b8\u1d50`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym_alg.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym_alg.unsym_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym_alg.unsym_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym_alg.unsym_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym_alg.sym_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym_alg.unsym_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.small.functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.nat_gt.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.small.sampleable_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.list.one_le_sizeof", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.list.shrink_one", "description": "`list.shrink_one xs` shrinks list `xs` by shrinking only one item in\nthe list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.large.functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.bool.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.nat.shrink'", "description": " `nat.shrink' k n` creates a list of smaller natural numbers by\nsuccessively dividing `n` by 2 and subtracting the difference from\n`k`. For example, `nat.shrink 100 = [50, 75, 88, 94, 97, 99]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable.mk_trivial_interp", "description": " This function helps infer the proxy representation and\ninterpretation in `sampleable_ext` instances.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable.lift", "description": "Transport a `sampleable` instance from a type `\u03b1` to a type `\u03b2` using\nfunctions between the two, going in both directions.\n\nFunction `g` is used to define the well-founded order that\n`shrink` is expected to follow.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.perm.slim_check", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_tree", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.small", "description": "Type tag that signals to `slim_check` to use small values for a given type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_char", "description": " `sampleable_char` can be specialized into customized `sampleable char` instances.\n\nThe resulting instance has `1 / length` chances of making an unrestricted choice of characters\nand it otherwise chooses a character from `characters` with uniform probabilities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.ge.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.list.sizeof_drop_lt_sizeof_of_lt_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.rec_shrink", "description": " `rec_shrink x f_rec` takes the recursive call `f_rec` introduced\nby `well_founded.fix` and turns it into a shrinking function whose\nresult is adequate to use in a recursive call.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.int_ge.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.iterate_shrink", "description": " `iterate_shrink p x` takes a decidable predicate `p` and a\nvalue `x` of some sampleable type and recursively shrinks `x`.\nIt first calls `shrink x` to get a list of candidate sample,\nfinds the first that satisfies `p` and recursively tries\nto shrink that one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.no_shrink.mk", "description": "Introduction of the `no_shrink` type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.pnat.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.int.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.Prop.sampleable_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.large", "description": "Type tag that signals to `slim_check` to use large values for a given type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.large.sampleable_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.shrink_fn", "description": " `shrink_fn \u03b1` is the type of functions that shrink an\nargument of type `\u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.print_samples", "description": "Print (at most) 10 samples of a given type to stdout for debugging.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.tree.sample", "description": "implementation of `sampleable (tree \u03b1)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.list.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.list.sizeof_append_lt_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.int_lt.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sum.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sum.shrink", "description": "shrinking function for sum types", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.large.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.list.sizeof_cons_lt_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.prod.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.rat.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.mk_generator", "description": "Create a `gen \u03b1` expression from the argument of `#sample`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.list.sizeof_cons_lt_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.char.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.perm'.slim_check", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.int.has_sizeof", "description": "Redefine `sizeof` for `int` to make it easier to use with `nat`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_ext.functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.rec_shrink_with_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.int_gt.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.small.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.tree.one_le_sizeof", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.ulift.sampleable_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.list.shrink_with", "description": " `list.shrink_with shrink_f xs` shrinks `xs` by first\nconsidering `xs` with chunks removed in the middle (starting with\nchunks of size `xs.length` and halving down to `1`) and then\nshrinks only one element of the list.\n\nThis strategy is taken directly from Haskell's QuickCheck", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.list.shrink_removes", "description": "`list.shrink_removes` shrinks a list by removing chunks of size `k` in\nthe middle of the list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.no_shrink.get", "description": "Selector of the `no_shrink` type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_ext.of_sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.large.mk", "description": "Add the `large` type tag", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.int_le.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.no_shrink.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.le.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.nat.shrink", "description": " `nat.shrink n` creates a list of smaller natural numbers by\nsuccessively dividing by 2 and subtracting the difference from\n`n`. For example, `nat.shrink 100 = [50, 75, 88, 94, 97, 99]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sample_cmd", "description": "`#sample my_type`, where `my_type` has an instance of `sampleable`, prints ten random\nvalues of type `my_type` of using an increasing size parameter.\n\n```lean\n#sample nat\n-- prints\n-- 0\n-- 0\n-- 2\n-- 24\n-- 64\n-- 76\n-- 5\n-- 132\n-- 8\n-- 449\n-- or some other sequence of numbers\n\n#sample list int\n-- prints\n-- []\n-- [1, 1]\n-- [-7, 9, -6]\n-- [36]\n-- [-500, 105, 260]\n-- [-290]\n-- [17, 156]\n-- [-2364, -7599, 661, -2411, -3576, 5517, -3823, -968]\n-- [-643]\n-- [11892, 16329, -15095, -15461]\n-- or whatever\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.nat_le.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.no_shrink.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.nat_ge.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.fin.sampleable'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_ext.bifunctor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.fin.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable.bifunctor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.tree.functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_ext", "description": " `sampleable_ext` generalizes the behavior of `sampleable`\nand makes it possible to express instances for types that\ndo not lend themselves to introspection, such as `\u2115 \u2192 \u2115`.\nIf we test a quantification over functions the\ncounter-examples cannot be shrunken or printed meaningfully.\n\nFor that purpose, `sampleable_ext` provides a proxy representation\n`proxy_repr` that can be printed and shrunken as well\nas interpreted (using `interp`) as an object of the right type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_ext.proxy_repr", "description": " `sampleable_ext` generalizes the behavior of `sampleable`\nand makes it possible to express instances for types that\ndo not lend themselves to introspection, such as `\u2115 \u2192 \u2115`.\nIf we test a quantification over functions the\ncounter-examples cannot be shrunken or printed meaningfully.\n\nFor that purpose, `sampleable_ext` provides a proxy representation\n`proxy_repr` that can be printed and shrunken as well\nas interpreted (using `interp`) as an object of the right type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_ext.wf", "description": " `sampleable_ext` generalizes the behavior of `sampleable`\nand makes it possible to express instances for types that\ndo not lend themselves to introspection, such as `\u2115 \u2192 \u2115`.\nIf we test a quantification over functions the\ncounter-examples cannot be shrunken or printed meaningfully.\n\nFor that purpose, `sampleable_ext` provides a proxy representation\n`proxy_repr` that can be printed and shrunken as well\nas interpreted (using `interp`) as an object of the right type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_ext.interp", "description": " `sampleable_ext` generalizes the behavior of `sampleable`\nand makes it possible to express instances for types that\ndo not lend themselves to introspection, such as `\u2115 \u2192 \u2115`.\nIf we test a quantification over functions the\ncounter-examples cannot be shrunken or printed meaningfully.\n\nFor that purpose, `sampleable_ext` provides a proxy representation\n`proxy_repr` that can be printed and shrunken as well\nas interpreted (using `interp`) as an object of the right type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_ext.p_repr", "description": " `sampleable_ext` generalizes the behavior of `sampleable`\nand makes it possible to express instances for types that\ndo not lend themselves to introspection, such as `\u2115 \u2192 \u2115`.\nIf we test a quantification over functions the\ncounter-examples cannot be shrunken or printed meaningfully.\n\nFor that purpose, `sampleable_ext` provides a proxy representation\n`proxy_repr` that can be printed and shrunken as well\nas interpreted (using `interp`) as an object of the right type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_ext.sample", "description": " `sampleable_ext` generalizes the behavior of `sampleable`\nand makes it possible to express instances for types that\ndo not lend themselves to introspection, such as `\u2115 \u2192 \u2115`.\nIf we test a quantification over functions the\ncounter-examples cannot be shrunken or printed meaningfully.\n\nFor that purpose, `sampleable_ext` provides a proxy representation\n`proxy_repr` that can be printed and shrunken as well\nas interpreted (using `interp`) as an object of the right type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_ext.shrink", "description": " `sampleable_ext` generalizes the behavior of `sampleable`\nand makes it possible to express instances for types that\ndo not lend themselves to introspection, such as `\u2115 \u2192 \u2115`.\nIf we test a quantification over functions the\ncounter-examples cannot be shrunken or printed meaningfully.\n\nFor that purpose, `sampleable_ext` provides a proxy representation\n`proxy_repr` that can be printed and shrunken as well\nas interpreted (using `interp`) as an object of the right type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable", "description": " `sampleable \u03b1` provides ways of creating examples of type `\u03b1`,\nand given such an example `x : \u03b1`, gives us a way to shrink it\nand find simpler examples.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable.wf", "description": " `sampleable \u03b1` provides ways of creating examples of type `\u03b1`,\nand given such an example `x : \u03b1`, gives us a way to shrink it\nand find simpler examples.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable.sample", "description": " `sampleable \u03b1` provides ways of creating examples of type `\u03b1`,\nand given such an example `x : \u03b1`, gives us a way to shrink it\nand find simpler examples.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable.shrink", "description": " `sampleable \u03b1` provides ways of creating examples of type `\u03b1`,\nand given such an example `x : \u03b1`, gives us a way to shrink it\nand find simpler examples.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable.functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.rec_shrink_with", "description": "Recursion principle for shrinking tree-like structures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.nat.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_functor", "description": " `sampleable_functor F` makes it possible to create samples of and\nshrink `F \u03b1` given a sampling function and a shrinking function for\narbitrary `\u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_functor.wf", "description": " `sampleable_functor F` makes it possible to create samples of and\nshrink `F \u03b1` given a sampling function and a shrinking function for\narbitrary `\u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_functor.sample", "description": " `sampleable_functor F` makes it possible to create samples of and\nshrink `F \u03b1` given a sampling function and a shrinking function for\narbitrary `\u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_functor.shrink", "description": " `sampleable_functor F` makes it possible to create samples of and\nshrink `F \u03b1` given a sampling function and a shrinking function for\narbitrary `\u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_functor.p_repr", "description": " `sampleable_functor F` makes it possible to create samples of and\nshrink `F \u03b1` given a sampling function and a shrinking function for\narbitrary `\u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sigma.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sizeof_lt", "description": "`sizeof_lt x y` compares the sizes of `x` and `y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_bifunctor", "description": " `sampleable_bifunctor F` makes it possible to create samples of\nand shrink `F \u03b1 \u03b2` given a sampling function and a shrinking function\nfor arbitrary `\u03b1` and `\u03b2`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_bifunctor.wf", "description": " `sampleable_bifunctor F` makes it possible to create samples of\nand shrink `F \u03b1 \u03b2` given a sampling function and a shrinking function\nfor arbitrary `\u03b1` and `\u03b2`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_bifunctor.sample", "description": " `sampleable_bifunctor F` makes it possible to create samples of\nand shrink `F \u03b1 \u03b2` given a sampling function and a shrinking function\nfor arbitrary `\u03b1` and `\u03b2`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_bifunctor.shrink", "description": " `sampleable_bifunctor F` makes it possible to create samples of\nand shrink `F \u03b1 \u03b2` given a sampling function and a shrinking function\nfor arbitrary `\u03b1` and `\u03b2`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.sampleable_bifunctor.p_repr", "description": " `sampleable_bifunctor F` makes it possible to create samples of\nand shrink `F \u03b1 \u03b2` given a sampling function and a shrinking function\nfor arbitrary `\u03b1` and `\u03b2`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.no_shrink", "description": " `no_shrink` is a type annotation to signal that\na certain type is not to be shrunk. It can be useful in\ncombination with other types: e.g. `xs : list (no_shrink \u2124)`\nwill result in the list being cut down but individual\nintegers being kept as is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.prod.shrink", "description": "Provided two shrinking functions `prod.shrink` shrinks a pair `(x, y)` by\nfirst shrinking `x` and pairing the results with `y` and then shrinking\n`y` and pairing the results with `x`.\n\nAll pairs either contain `x` untouched or `y` untouched. We rely on\nshrinking being repeated for `x` to get maximally shrunken and then\nfor `y` to get shrunken too.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.string.sampleable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.small.mk", "description": "Add the `small` type tag", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.tree.shrink_with", "description": " `tree.shrink_with shrink_f t` shrinks `xs` by using the empty tree,\neach subtrees, and by shrinking the subtree to recombine them.\n\nThis strategy is taken directly from Haskell's QuickCheck", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.induction_on_rank", "description": " If `N` is a submodule in a free, finitely generated module,\ndo induction on adjoining a linear independent element to a submodule.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal_le_rank_of_linear_independent'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.rank_sup_add_rank_inf_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.rank_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.nonempty_equiv_iff_rank_eq", "description": "Two vector spaces are isomorphic if and only if they have the same dimension.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.le_span", "description": "If `R` satisfies the rank condition,\nthen the cardinality of any basis is bounded by the cardinality of any spanning set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.rank_le_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.index_equiv", "description": " Given two bases indexed by `\u03b9` and `\u03b9'` of an `R`-module, where `R` satisfies the invariant\nbasis number property, an equiv `\u03b9 \u2243 \u03b9' `.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_span_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_add_rank_split", "description": "This is mostly an auxiliary lemma for `submodule.rank_sup_add_rank_inf_eq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.rank_comp_le_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infinite_basis_le_maximal_linear_independent'", "description": "Over any ring `R`, if `b` is an infinite basis for a module `M`,\nand `s` is a maximal linearly independent set,\nthen the cardinality of `b` is bounded by the cardinality of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_fun'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_submodule_le_one_iff", "description": " A submodule has dimension at most `1` if and only if there is a\nsingle vector in the submodule such that the submodule is contained in\nits span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_quotient_add_rank", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.of_lift_rank_eq", "description": "Two vector spaces are isomorphic if they have the same dimension.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.rank_eq", "description": "Two linearly equivalent vector spaces have the same dimension.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.of_rank_eq", "description": "Two vector spaces are isomorphic if they have the same dimension.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lift_rank_range_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.lift_rank_le_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_le_of_submodule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal_le_rank_of_linear_independent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.rank_le_one_iff_is_principal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.finite_index_of_rank_lt_aleph_0", "description": "If a module has a finite dimension, all bases are indexed by a finite set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.rank_le_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_eq_card_basis", "description": " If a vector space has a finite basis, then its dimension (seen as a cardinal) is equal to the\ncardinality of the basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_mem_ne_zero_of_rank_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.mk_eq_rank", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.rank_comp_le_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_prod", "description": "The rank of `M \u00d7 N` is `(module.rank R M).lift + (module.rank R N).lift`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_submodule_le_one_iff'", "description": " A submodule has dimension at most `1` if and only if there is a\nsingle vector, not necessarily in the submodule, such that the\nsubmodule is contained in its span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonempty_linear_equiv_of_rank_eq", "description": "Two vector spaces are isomorphic if they have the same dimension.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_eq_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.rank_le_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.rank_map_eq", "description": "Pushforwards of submodules along a `linear_equiv` have the same dimension.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_fin_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal_lift_le_rank_of_linear_independent'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "maximal_linear_independent_eq_infinite_basis", "description": "Over any ring `R` satisfying the strong rank condition,\nif `b` is an infinite basis for a module `M`,\nthen every maximal linearly independent set has the same cardinality as `b`.\n\nThis proof (along with some of the lemmas above) comes from\n[Les familles libres maximales d'un module ont-elles le meme cardinal?][lazarus1973]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.of_rank_eq_zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.rank_le_one_iff_top_is_principal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.nonempty_equiv_iff_lift_rank_eq", "description": "Two vector spaces are isomorphic if and only if they have the same dimension.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_rank_iff_exists_linear_independent_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_pos_iff_exists_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.card_le_card_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.le_rank_iff_exists_linear_independent_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.rank", "description": " The rank of a module, defined as a term of type `cardinal`.\n\nWe define this as the supremum of the cardinalities of linearly independent subsets.\n\nFor a free module over any ring satisfying the strong rank condition\n(e.g. left-noetherian rings, commutative rings, and in particular division rings and fields),\nthis is the same as the dimension of the space (i.e. the cardinality of any basis).\n\nIn particular this agrees with the usual notion of the dimension of a vector space.\n\nThe definition is marked as protected to avoid conflicts with `_root_.rank`,\nthe rank of a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_le_one_iff", "description": " A vector space has dimension at most `1` if and only if there is a\nsingle vector of which all vectors are multiples.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_fun_eq_lift_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.lift_rank_eq", "description": " Two linearly equivalent vector spaces have the same dimension, a version with different\nuniverses.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_zero_iff_forall_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_pos_iff_nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis_le_span'", "description": "Another auxiliary lemma for `basis.le_span`, which does not require assuming the basis is finite,\nbut still assumes we have a finite spanning set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_quotient_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis_fintype_of_finite_spans", "description": "Over any nontrivial ring, the existence of a finite spanning set implies that any basis is finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_prod'", "description": "If `M` and `N` lie in the same universe, the rank of `M \u00d7 N` is\n `(module.rank R M) + (module.rank R N)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent.finite_of_is_noetherian", "description": " A linearly-independent family of vectors in a module over a non-trivial ring must be finite if\nthe module is Noetherian.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_punit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_le_basis", "description": "Over any ring `R` satisfying the strong rank condition,\nif `b` is a basis for a module `M`,\nand `s` is a linearly independent set,\nthen the cardinality of `s` is bounded by the cardinality of `b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "union_support_maximal_linear_independent_eq_range_basis", "description": "Over any ring `R`, if `b` is a basis for a module `M`,\nand `s` is a maximal linearly independent set,\nthen the union of the supports of `x \u2208 s` (when written out in the basis `b`) is all of `b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.card_le_card_of_linear_independent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_le_infinite_basis", "description": "An auxiliary lemma for `linear_independent_le_basis`:\nwe handle the case where the basis `b` is infinite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.fintype_index_of_rank_lt_aleph_0", "description": "If a module has a finite dimension, all bases are indexed by a finite type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.rank", "description": "`rank f` is the rank of a `linear_map` `f`, defined as the dimension of `f.range`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.rank_eq", "description": " If `S` a finite-dimensional ring extension of `R` which is free as an `R`-module,\nthen the rank of an ideal `I` of `S` over `R` is the same as the rank of `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_le_span'", "description": "If `R` satisfies the strong rank condition,\nthen for any linearly independent family `v : \u03b9 \u2192 M`\ncontained in the span of some finite `w : set M`,\nthe cardinality of `\u03b9` is bounded by the cardinality of `w`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.of_rank_eq_zero", "description": " The `\u03b9` indexed basis on `V`, where `\u03b9` is an empty type and `V` is zero-dimensional.\n\nSee also `finite_dimensional.fin_basis`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.independent.subtype_ne_bot_le_rank", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.mk_eq_rank'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_zero_iff", "description": "See `rank_subsingleton` for the reason that `nontrivial R` is needed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_fintype_of_le_span_fintype", "description": "If `R` satisfies the strong rank condition,\nthen any linearly independent family `v : \u03b9 \u2192 M`\ncontained in the span of some finite `w : set M`,\nis itself finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonempty_linear_equiv_of_lift_rank_eq", "description": "Two vector spaces are isomorphic if they have the same dimension.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.lift_rank_comp_le_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.le_span''", "description": "An auxiliary lemma for `basis.le_span`.\n\nIf `R` satisfies the rank condition,\nthen for any finite basis `b : basis \u03b9 R M`,\nand any finite spanning set `w : set M`,\nthe cardinality of `\u03b9` is bounded by the cardinality of `w`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.rank_add_le_rank_add_rank", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infinite_basis_le_maximal_linear_independent", "description": "Over any ring `R`, if `b` is an infinite basis for a module `M`,\nand `s` is a maximal linearly independent set,\nthen the cardinality of `b` is bounded by the cardinality of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_map_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.mk_eq_rank''", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.card_le_card_of_linear_independent_aux", "description": "In an `n`-dimensional space, the rank is at most `m`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent.set_finite_of_is_noetherian", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_submodule_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal_lift_le_rank_of_linear_independent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_eq_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.free.rank_eq_card_choose_basis_index", "description": "The rank of a free module `M` over `R` is the cardinality of `choose_basis_index R M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_le_span_finset", "description": "A version of `linear_independent_le_span` for `finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mk_eq_mk_of_basis", "description": " The dimension theorem: if `v` and `v'` are two bases, their index types\nhave the same cardinalities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.rank_comp_le", "description": " The rank of the composition of two maps is less than the minimum of their ranks.\n\nSee `lift_rank_comp_le` for the universe-polymorphic version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_span_of_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_pi", "description": "The rank of a finite product is the sum of the ranks.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.rank_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_range_add_rank_ker", "description": "rank-nullity theorem", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_le_span_aux'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.finite_of_vector_space_index_of_rank_lt_aleph_0", "description": "If a vector space has a finite dimension, the index set of `basis.of_vector_space` is finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_le_span", "description": "If `R` satisfies the strong rank condition,\nthen for any linearly independent family `v : \u03b9 \u2192 M`\nand any finite spanning set `w : set M`,\nthe cardinality of `\u03b9` is bounded by the cardinality of `w`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.rank_finset_sum_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.lift_rank_comp_le", "description": "The rank of the composition of two maps is less than the minimum of their ranks.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.mk_range_eq_rank", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.rank_le_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.card_le_card_of_submodule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_span_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_rank_iff_exists_linear_independent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mk_eq_mk_of_basis'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin_dim_vectorspace_equiv", "description": "An `n`-dimensional `K`-vector space is equivalent to `fin n \u2192 K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lift_rank_map_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.le_rank_iff_exists_linear_independent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_range_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_range_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.nonempty_fintype_index_of_rank_lt_aleph_0", "description": "If a module has a finite dimension, all bases are indexed by a finite type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Ioc_eq_range'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.range_add_eq_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_Iio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Ico_eq_range'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Ioc_succ_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cauchy_induction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Icc_eq_range'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.image_Ico_mod", "description": " Note that while this lemma cannot be easily generalized to a type class, it holds for \u2124 as\nwell. See `int.image_Ico_mod` for the \u2124 version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cauchy_induction_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Ioo_eq_range'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_fintype_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Ico_succ_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.uIcc_eq_range'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.multiset_Ico_map_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.decreasing_induction_of_not_bdd_above", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Ico_succ_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Ico_succ_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_fintype_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.range_eq_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Iio_eq_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_uIcc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Ico_succ_left_eq_erase_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Ico_zero_eq_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.image_sub_const_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.mod_inj_on_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Icc_pred_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Ico_insert_succ_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Ico_image_const_sub_eq_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Ico_pred_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cauchy_induction_two_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cauchy_induction'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.decreasing_induction_of_infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Ico_succ_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_fintype_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_fintype_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Icc_succ_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.locally_finite_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_fintype_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.range_image_pred_top_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_fintype_Iio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Ico_succ_right_eq_insert_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.smul_comm_class_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.coe_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.to_subsemiring_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.is_domain", "description": "A subring of a domain is a domain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.mem_to_add_subgroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring_class.to_ordered_comm_ring", "description": "A subring of an `ordered_comm_ring` is an `ordered_comm_ring`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_equiv.subring_map_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.eq_locus_same", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.no_zero_divisors", "description": "A subring of a ring with no zero divisors has no zero divisors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.closure_induction", "description": " An induction principle for closure membership. If `p` holds for `0`, `1`, and all elements\nof `s`, and is preserved under addition, negation, and multiplication, then `p` holds for all\nelements of the closure of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.center_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.map_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.nontrivial", "description": "A subring of a non-trivial ring is non-trivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.to_subsemiring_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.mul_distrib_mul_action", "description": "The action by a subring is the action by the underlying ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.map_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.int_mul_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.to_add_subgroup", "description": "Reinterpret a `subring` as an `add_subgroup`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.mk'_to_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.Inf_to_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.multiset_sum_mem", "description": " Sum of a multiset of elements in an `subring` of a `ring` is\nin the `subring`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.has_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.closure_preimage_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.mem_supr_of_directed", "description": "The underlying set of a non-empty directed Sup of subrings is just a union of the subrings.\n Note that this fails without the directedness assumption (the union of two subrings is\n typically not a subring)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.coe_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring_class", "description": " `subring_class S R` states that `S` is a type of subsets `s \u2286 R` that\nare both a multiplicative submonoid and an additive subgroup.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring_class.to_subsemiring_class", "description": " `subring_class S R` states that `S` is a type of subsets `s \u2286 R` that\nare both a multiplicative submonoid and an additive subgroup.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring_class.to_neg_mem_class", "description": " `subring_class S R` states that `S` is a type of subsets `s \u2286 R` that\nare both a multiplicative submonoid and an additive subgroup.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_equiv.of_left_inverse_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.coe_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.closure_induction\u2082", "description": "An induction principle for closure membership, for predicates with two arguments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_equiv.subring_congr", "description": "Makes the identity isomorphism from a proof two subrings of a multiplicative\n   monoid are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.sub_mem", "description": "A subring is closed under subtraction", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.zsmul_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.mem_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.module", "description": "The action by a subring is the action by the underlying ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.center_to_subsemiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring", "description": "`subring R` is the type of subrings of `R`. A subring of `R` is a subset `s` that is a\n multiplicative submonoid and an additive subgroup. Note in particular that it shares the\n same 0 and 1 as R.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.carrier", "description": "`subring R` is the type of subrings of `R`. A subring of `R` is a subset `s` that is a\n multiplicative submonoid and an additive subgroup. Note in particular that it shares the\n same 0 and 1 as R.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.mul_mem'", "description": "`subring R` is the type of subrings of `R`. A subring of `R` is a subset `s` that is a\n multiplicative submonoid and an additive subgroup. Note in particular that it shares the\n same 0 and 1 as R.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.one_mem'", "description": "`subring R` is the type of subrings of `R`. A subring of `R` is a subset `s` that is a\n multiplicative submonoid and an additive subgroup. Note in particular that it shares the\n same 0 and 1 as R.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.add_mem'", "description": "`subring R` is the type of subrings of `R`. A subring of `R` is a subset `s` that is a\n multiplicative submonoid and an additive subgroup. Note in particular that it shares the\n same 0 and 1 as R.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.zero_mem'", "description": "`subring R` is the type of subrings of `R`. A subring of `R` is a subset `s` that is a\n multiplicative submonoid and an additive subgroup. Note in particular that it shares the\n same 0 and 1 as R.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.neg_mem'", "description": "`subring R` is the type of subr