"name": "category_theory.center.forget", "description": "The forgetful monoidal functor from the Drinfeld center to the original category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.tensor_hom_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.tensor_hom", "description": "Auxiliary definition for the `monoidal_category` instance on `center C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.braiding", "description": "Auxiliary definition for the `braided_category` instance on `center C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.of_braided", "description": "The functor lifting a braided category to its center, using the braiding as the half-braiding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.of_braided_to_lax_monoidal_functor_\u03b5_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.tensor_obj", "description": "Auxiliary definition for the `monoidal_category` instance on `center C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.tensor_unit", "description": "Auxiliary definition for the `monoidal_category` instance on `center C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center", "description": "The Drinfeld center of a monoidal category `C` has as objects pairs `\u27e8X, b\u27e9`, where `X : C`\nand `b` is a half-braiding on `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.iso_mk_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.of_braided_obj", "description": "Auxiliary construction for `of_braided`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.tensor_unit_\u03b2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.of_braided_to_lax_monoidal_functor_\u03bc_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.tensor_obj_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.associator", "description": "Auxiliary definition for the `monoidal_category` instance on `center C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.of_braided_to_lax_monoidal_functor_to_functor_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.half_braiding.naturality_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.is_iso_of_f_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.left_unitor_inv_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.of_braided_to_lax_monoidal_functor_to_functor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.hom.comm_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.of_braided_obj_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.of_braided_obj_snd_\u03b2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.forget_to_lax_monoidal_functor_to_functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.left_unitor_hom_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.tensor_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.comp_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.category_theory.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.tensor_unit_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.forget_to_lax_monoidal_functor_\u03b5", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.half_braiding", "description": "A half-braiding on `X : C` is a family of isomorphisms `X \u2297 U \u2245 U \u2297 X`,\nmonoidally natural in `U : C`.\n\nThinking of `C` as a 2-category with a single `0`-morphism, these are the same as natural\ntransformations (in the pseudo- sense) of the identity 2-functor on `C`, which send the unique\n`0`-morphism to `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.half_braiding.\u03b2", "description": "A half-braiding on `X : C` is a family of isomorphisms `X \u2297 U \u2245 U \u2297 X`,\nmonoidally natural in `U : C`.\n\nThinking of `C` as a 2-category with a single `0`-morphism, these are the same as natural\ntransformations (in the pseudo- sense) of the identity 2-functor on `C`, which send the unique\n`0`-morphism to `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.half_braiding.monoidal'", "description": "A half-braiding on `X : C` is a family of isomorphisms `X \u2297 U \u2245 U \u2297 X`,\nmonoidally natural in `U : C`.\n\nThinking of `C` as a 2-category with a single `0`-morphism, these are the same as natural\ntransformations (in the pseudo- sense) of the identity 2-functor on `C`, which send the unique\n`0`-morphism to `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.half_braiding.naturality'", "description": "A half-braiding on `X : C` is a family of isomorphisms `X \u2297 U \u2245 U \u2297 X`,\nmonoidally natural in `U : C`.\n\nThinking of `C` as a 2-category with a single `0`-morphism, these are the same as natural\ntransformations (in the pseudo- sense) of the identity 2-functor on `C`, which send the unique\n`0`-morphism to `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.category_theory.monoidal_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.right_unitor_hom_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.half_braiding.monoidal_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.iso_mk", "description": "Construct an isomorphism in the Drinfeld center from\na morphism whose underlying morphism is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.forget_to_lax_monoidal_functor_to_functor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.right_unitor", "description": "Auxiliary definition for the `monoidal_category` instance on `center C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.tensor_unit_snd_\u03b2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.forget_to_lax_monoidal_functor_\u03bc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.left_unitor", "description": "Auxiliary definition for the `monoidal_category` instance on `center C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.to_functor.category_theory.reflects_isomorphisms", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.associator_inv_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.iso_mk_inv_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.hom", "description": "A morphism in the Drinfeld center of `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.hom.f", "description": "A morphism in the Drinfeld center of `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.hom.comm'", "description": "A morphism in the Drinfeld center of `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.half_braiding.monoidal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.hom.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.braided_category_center", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.hom.comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.tensor_obj_snd_\u03b2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.associator_hom_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.half_braiding.naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.id_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.braiding_inv_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.right_unitor_inv_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.center.tensor_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.adjointify_\u03b7", "description": " If `\u03b7 : \ud835\udfed C \u2245 F \u22d9 G` is part of a (not necessarily half-adjoint) equivalence, we can upgrade it\nto a refined natural isomorphism `adjointify_\u03b7 \u03b7 : \ud835\udfed C \u2245 F \u22d9 G` which exhibits the properties\nrequired for a half-adjoint equivalence. See `equivalence.mk`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.cancel_comp_right", "description": "If `G` and `F \u22d9 G` are equivalence of categories, then `F` is also an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.equiv_of_iso", "description": "When `F` and `G` are two isomorphic functors, then `F` is an equivalence iff `G` is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.of_iso", "description": " When a functor `F` is an equivalence of categories, and `G` is isomorphic to `F`, then\n`G` is also an equivalence of categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.functor_map_inj_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.pow_neg_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.faithful_of_equivalence", "description": "An equivalence is faithful.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02C3>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.ess_surj_of_equivalence", "description": "An equivalence is essentially surjective.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02C3>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.congr_left_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.functor_unit_iso_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.congr_right_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.as_equivalence_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.inv_fun_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.of_iso_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.cancel_counit_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.counit", "description": "The counit of an equivalence of categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.inverse_map_inj_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.equiv_of_iso_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.trans", "description": "Equivalence of categories is transitive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.as_equivalence", "description": "Interpret a functor that is an equivalence as an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.fun_inv_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.functor_unit_iso_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.counit_inv_functor_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.unit", "description": "The unit of an equivalence of categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.unit_inv", "description": "The inverse of the unit of an equivalence of categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.trans_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.as_equivalence_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.inverse_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.is_equivalence_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.congr_left_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.counit_app_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.equivalence_mk'_counit_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.adjointify_\u03b7_\u03b5", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.ess_surj_induced_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.as_equivalence_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.of_iso_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.inv_fun_id_assoc", "description": " Composing a functor with both functors of an equivalence yields a naturally isomorphic\nfunctor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.fun_inv_id_assoc", "description": " Composing a functor with both functors of an equivalence yields a naturally isomorphic\nfunctor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.congr_left_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.refl_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.cancel_unit_right_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.inverse_counit_inv_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.of_iso_trans", "description": "Compatibility of `of_iso` with the composition of isomorphisms of functors", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.of_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.is_equivalence_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.int.has_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.trans_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.inv_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.of_equivalence_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.congr_right", "description": "If `C` is equivalent to `D`, then `E \u2964 C` is equivalent to `E \u2964 D`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.as_equivalence_counit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.equiv_of_iso_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.fun_inv_id_assoc_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.equivalence_mk'_unit_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.congr_right_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.inv_fun_id_assoc_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence", "description": " We define an equivalence as a (half)-adjoint equivalence, a pair of functors with\n  a unit and counit which are natural isomorphisms and the triangle law `F\u03b7 \u226b \u03b5F = 1`, or in other\n  words the composite `F \u27f6 FGF \u27f6 F` is the identity.\n\n  In `unit_inverse_comp`, we show that this is actually an adjoint equivalence, i.e., that the\n  composite `G \u27f6 GFG \u27f6 G` is also the identity.\n\n  The triangle equation is written as a family of equalities between morphisms, it is more\n  complicated if we write it as an equality of natural transformations, because then we would have\n  to insert natural transformations like `F \u27f6 F1`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/001J>", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.functor", "description": " We define an equivalence as a (half)-adjoint equivalence, a pair of functors with\n  a unit and counit which are natural isomorphisms and the triangle law `F\u03b7 \u226b \u03b5F = 1`, or in other\n  words the composite `F \u27f6 FGF \u27f6 F` is the identity.\n\n  In `unit_inverse_comp`, we show that this is actually an adjoint equivalence, i.e., that the\n  composite `G \u27f6 GFG \u27f6 G` is also the identity.\n\n  The triangle equation is written as a family of equalities between morphisms, it is more\n  complicated if we write it as an equality of natural transformations, because then we would have\n  to insert natural transformations like `F \u27f6 F1`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/001J>", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.inverse", "description": " We define an equivalence as a (half)-adjoint equivalence, a pair of functors with\n  a unit and counit which are natural isomorphisms and the triangle law `F\u03b7 \u226b \u03b5F = 1`, or in other\n  words the composite `F \u27f6 FGF \u27f6 F` is the identity.\n\n  In `unit_inverse_comp`, we show that this is actually an adjoint equivalence, i.e., that the\n  composite `G \u27f6 GFG \u27f6 G` is also the identity.\n\n  The triangle equation is written as a family of equalities between morphisms, it is more\n  complicated if we write it as an equality of natural transformations, because then we would have\n  to insert natural transformations like `F \u27f6 F1`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/001J>", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.unit_iso", "description": " We define an equivalence as a (half)-adjoint equivalence, a pair of functors with\n  a unit and counit which are natural isomorphisms and the triangle law `F\u03b7 \u226b \u03b5F = 1`, or in other\n  words the composite `F \u27f6 FGF \u27f6 F` is the identity.\n\n  In `unit_inverse_comp`, we show that this is actually an adjoint equivalence, i.e., that the\n  composite `G \u27f6 GFG \u27f6 G` is also the identity.\n\n  The triangle equation is written as a family of equalities between morphisms, it is more\n  complicated if we write it as an equality of natural transformations, because then we would have\n  to insert natural transformations like `F \u27f6 F1`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/001J>", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.counit_iso", "description": " We define an equivalence as a (half)-adjoint equivalence, a pair of functors with\n  a unit and counit which are natural isomorphisms and the triangle law `F\u03b7 \u226b \u03b5F = 1`, or in other\n  words the composite `F \u27f6 FGF \u27f6 F` is the identity.\n\n  In `unit_inverse_comp`, we show that this is actually an adjoint equivalence, i.e., that the\n  composite `G \u27f6 GFG \u27f6 G` is also the identity.\n\n  The triangle equation is written as a family of equalities between morphisms, it is more\n  complicated if we write it as an equality of natural transformations, because then we would have\n  to insert natural transformations like `F \u27f6 F1`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/001J>", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.functor_unit_iso_comp'", "description": " We define an equivalence as a (half)-adjoint equivalence, a pair of functors with\n  a unit and counit which are natural isomorphisms and the triangle law `F\u03b7 \u226b \u03b5F = 1`, or in other\n  words the composite `F \u27f6 FGF \u27f6 F` is the identity.\n\n  In `unit_inverse_comp`, we show that this is actually an adjoint equivalence, i.e., that the\n  composite `G \u27f6 GFG \u27f6 G` is also the identity.\n\n  The triangle equation is written as a family of equalities between morphisms, it is more\n  complicated if we write it as an equality of natural transformations, because then we would have\n  to insert natural transformations like `F \u27f6 F1`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/001J>", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.equivalence_mk'_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.is_equivalence_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.fun_inv_id_assoc_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.refl_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.inv_fun_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.refl_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.fully_faithful_to_ess_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.of_iso_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.congr_left", "description": "If `C` is equivalent to `D`, then `C \u2964 E` is equivalent to `D \u2964 E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.refl", "description": "Equivalence of categories is reflexive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.of_iso_refl", "description": "Compatibility of `of_iso` with identity isomorphisms of functors", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.inv", "description": "The inverse functor of a functor that is an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.mk", "description": "Every equivalence of categories consisting of functors `F` and `G` such that `F \u22d9 G` and\n   `G \u22d9 F` are naturally isomorphic to identity functors can be transformed into a half-adjoint\n   equivalence without changing `F` or `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.functor_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.full_of_equivalence", "description": "An equivalence is full.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02C3>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.symm_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.symm_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.mk", "description": "To see that a functor is an equivalence, it suffices to provide an inverse functor `G` such that\n   `F \u22d9 G` and `G \u22d9 F` are naturally isomorphic to identity functors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.congr_right_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.cancel_unit_right_assoc'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.cancel_unit_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.pow_nat", "description": "Natural number powers of an auto-equivalence.  Use `(^)` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.congr_left_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.pow_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.counit_inv", "description": "The inverse of the counit of an equivalence of categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.cancel_counit_inv_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.induced_functor_of_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.inv_fun_id_assoc_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.symm", "description": "Equivalence of categories is symmetric.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.of_fully_faithfully_ess_surj", "description": "A functor which is full, faithful, and essentially surjective is an equivalence.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02C3>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence", "description": "A functor that is part of a (half) adjoint equivalence", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.inverse", "description": "A functor that is part of a (half) adjoint equivalence", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.unit_iso", "description": "A functor that is part of a (half) adjoint equivalence", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.counit_iso", "description": "A functor that is part of a (half) adjoint equivalence", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.functor_unit_iso_comp'", "description": "A functor that is part of a (half) adjoint equivalence", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.cancel_counit_inv_right_assoc'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.congr_right_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.counit_inv_app_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.equivalence_mk'_counit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.unit_app_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.fun_inv_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.functor_unit_iso_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.trans_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.pow_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.symm_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.pow", "description": "Powers of an auto-equivalence.  Use `(^)` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.refl_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_equivalence.cancel_comp_left", "description": "If `F` and `F \u22d9 G` are equivalence of categories, then `G` is also an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.unit_inv_app_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.unit_inverse_comp", "description": "The other triangle equality. The proof follows the following proof in Globular:\n http://globular.science/1905.001", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.functor_as_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.inverse_as_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.trans_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.cancel_counit_inv_right_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.functor_unit_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.symm_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.cancel_unit_inv_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.of", "description": "In any abelian category with enough projectives,\n`ProjectiveResolution.of Z` constructs a projective resolution of the object `Z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.category_theory.has_projective_resolution", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.category_theory.has_projective_resolutions", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.of_complex_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.of_complex", "description": "Auxiliary definition for `ProjectiveResolution.of`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.of_complex_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.exact_d_f", "description": "When `C` is abelian, `projective.d f` and `f` are exact.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.hom.to_single\u2080_ProjectiveResolution", "description": " If `X` is a chain complex of projective objects and we have a quasi-isomorphism `f : X \u27f6 Y[0]`,\nthen `X` is a projective resolution of `Y.`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.projective_of_preserves_finite_colimits_preadditive_coyoneda_obj", "description": "An object is projective if its preadditive Co-Yoneda functor preserves finite colimits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_finite_colimits_preadditive_coyoneda_obj_of_projective", "description": "The preadditive Co-Yoneda functor on `P` preserves colimits if `P` is projective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cau