en they correspond to the same element in the free group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.monad", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.map_pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.inv_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.step.diamond", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.reduce.min", "description": " The second theorem that characterises the\nfunction `reduce`: the maximal reduction of a word\nonly reduces to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red", "description": "Reflexive-transitive closure of red.step", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.map.id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.decidable_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.lift.unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.map_eq_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.red.step.diamond", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.reduce.eq_of_red", "description": "If a word reduces to another word, then they have\na common maximal reduction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.sum", "description": " If `\u03b1` is a group, then any function from `\u03b1` to `\u03b1`\nextends uniquely to a homomorphism from the\nfree group over `\u03b1` to `\u03b1`. This is the additive\nversion of `prod`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.enum", "description": "A list containing every word that `w\u2081` reduces to.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.step.bnot_rev", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.free_group_unit_equiv_int", "description": "The bijection between the free group on a singleton, and the integers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.step", "description": "Reduction step for the multiplicative free group relation: `w * x * x\u207b\u00b9 * v ~> w * v`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.step.bnot", "description": "Reduction step for the multiplicative free group relation: `w * x * x\u207b\u00b9 * v ~> w * v`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.reduce.red", "description": "The first theorem that characterises the function\n`reduce`: a word reduces to its maximal reduction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.induction_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.norm_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.to_word_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.red.cons_nil_iff_singleton", "description": "If `x` is a letter and `w` is a word such that `x + w` reduces to the empty word,\nthen `w` reduces to `-x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.lift", "description": " If `\u03b2` is a group, then any function from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2`\nextends uniquely to a group homomorphism from\nthe free group over `\u03b1` to `\u03b2`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.reduce.idem", "description": "`reduce` is idempotent, i.e. the maximal reduction\nof the maximal reduction of a word is the maximal\nreduction of the word.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.quot_lift_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.map_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.prod", "description": " If `\u03b1` is a group, then any function from `\u03b1` to `\u03b1`\nextends uniquely to a homomorphism from the\nfree group over `\u03b1` to `\u03b1`. This is the multiplicative\nversion of `free_group.sum`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.red.nil_iff", "description": "The empty word `[]` only reduces to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.red.reduce_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.reduce.not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.free_add_group_congr", "description": "Equivalent types give rise to additively equivalent additive free groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.nil_iff", "description": "The empty word `[]` only reduces to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.reduce.rev", "description": "If words `w\u2081 w\u2082` are such that `w\u2081` reduces to `w\u2082`,\nthen `w\u2082` reduces to the maximal reduction of `w\u2081`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.red.append_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.lift.mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.singleton_iff", "description": "A letter only reduces to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.red.not_step_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.reduce.cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.zero_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.sum.map_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.reduce_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.free_add_group.red.reduce_eq", "description": "**Alias** of `free_add_group.reduce.eq_of_red`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.map", "description": "Any function from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2` extends uniquely to an additive group homomorphism\nfrom the additive free group over `\u03b1` to the additive free group over `\u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.mk_to_word", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.reduce_eq", "description": "**Alias** of `free_group.reduce.eq_of_red`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.sum.of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.to_word_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.exact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.subtype.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.cons_cons_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.inv_of_red_of_ne", "description": " If `x` and `y` are distinct letters and `w\u2081 w\u2082` are words such that `xw\u2081` reduces to `yw\u2082`, then\n`w\u2081` reduces to `x\u207b\u00b9yw\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.red_iff_irreducible", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.inv_rev_bijective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.lift_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.norm_mul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.sum", "description": "If `\u03b1` is an additive group, then any function from `\u03b1` to `\u03b1`\nextends uniquely to an additive homomorphism from the\nadditive free group over `\u03b1` to `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.step.append_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.step_inv_rev_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.neg_rev", "description": "Transform a word representing a free group element into a word representing its\nnegative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.lift.unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.map.id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.red.length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.to_append_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.red.neg_of_red_of_ne", "description": "If `x` and `y` are distinct letters and `w\u2081 w\u2082` are words such that `x + w\u2081` reduces to `y + w\u2082`,\nthen `w\u2081` reduces to `-x + y + w\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.reduce.eq_of_red", "description": " If a word reduces to another word, then they have\na common maximal reduction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.pure_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.neg_rev_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.lift", "description": "If `\u03b2` is an additive group, then any function from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2`\nextends uniquely to an additive group homomorphism from\nthe free additive group over `\u03b1` to `\u03b2`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group", "description": "The free additive group over a type, i.e. the words formed by the elements of the\ntype and their formal inverses, quotient by one step reduction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.lift.aux", "description": "Given `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` with `\u03b2` a group, the canonical map `list (\u03b1 \u00d7 bool) \u2192 \u03b2`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.step.cons_cons_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.norm_inv_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.red.append_append_left_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.free_add_group_congr_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.red.step.cons_bnot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.lift.range_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.equivalence_join_red", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.red.step.to_red", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.is_lawful_monad", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_group.of_injective", "description": "The canonical map from the type to the free group is an injection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_group.red.reduce_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_