: "sub_mul_action.mem_one'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.one_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mul_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.equiv_opposite", "description": " The ring of submodules of the opposite algebra is isomorphic to the opposite ring of\nsubmodules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mul_to_add_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_span_mul_finite_of_mem_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.map_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.smul_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.module_set", "description": "R-submodules of the R-algebra A are a module over `set A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.pow_induction_on_right", "description": " To show a property on elements of `M ^ n` holds, it suffices to show that it holds for scalars,\nis closed under addition, and holds for `x * m` where `m \u2208 M` and it holds for `x`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.pow_induction_on_left", "description": " To show a property on elements of `M ^ n` holds, it suffices to show that it holds for scalars,\nis closed under addition, and holds for `m * x` where `m \u2208 M` and it holds for `x`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.pow_subset_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.one_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.one_le_one_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.algebra_map_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_span_singleton_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mul_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mul_induction_on'", "description": "A dependent version of `mul_induction_on`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.has_one", "description": "`1 : submodule R A` is the submodule R of A.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mul_le_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_mul_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mul_le_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.map_unop_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mul_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mul_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.supr_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.le_div_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.map_unop_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.equiv_opposite_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.map_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.map_hom", "description": "`submonoid.map` as a `monoid_with_zero_hom`, when applied to `alg_hom`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.has_mul", "description": " Multiplication of sub-R-modules of an R-algebra A. The submodule `M * N` is the\nsmallest R-submodule of `A` containing the elements `m * n` for `m \u2208 M` and `n \u2208 N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.comap_op_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mul_one_div_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.comap_op_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mul_mem_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.smul_le_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.pow_induction_on_right'", "description": "Dependent version of `submodule.pow_induction_on_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.map_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_div_iff_forall_mul_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span.ring_hom", "description": " `span` is a semiring homomorphism (recall multiplication is pointwise multiplication of subsets\non either side).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.bot_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.map_unop_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.map_op_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.has_div", "description": " The elements of `I / J` are the `x` such that `x \u2022 J \u2286 I`.\n\nIn fact, we define `x \u2208 I / J` to be `\u2200 y \u2208 J, x * y \u2208 I` (see `mem_div_iff_forall_mul_mem`),\nwhich is equivalent to `x \u2022 J \u2286 I` (see `mem_div_iff_smul_subset`), but nicer to use in proofs.\n\nThis is the general form of the ideal quotient, traditionally written $I : J$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.one_eq_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.le_div_iff_mul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_span_mul_finite_of_mem_span_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.map_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.smul_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.one_eq_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.pow_to_add_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mul_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.le_pow_to_add_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.idem_comm_semiring", "description": "Sub-R-modules of an R-algebra A form a semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_mul_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.comap_unop_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.map_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.one_eq_span_one_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.comap_unop_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.idem_semiring", "description": "Sub-R-modules of an R-algebra form an idempotent semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mul_subset_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.comap_op_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.pow_induction_on_left'", "description": "Dependent version of `submodule.pow_induction_on_left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.has_distrib_pointwise_neg", "description": " `submodule.has_pointwise_neg` distributes over multiplication.\n\nThis is available as an instance in the `pointwise` locale.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.to_sub_mul_action_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mul_mem_mul_rev", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_div_iff_smul_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.sup_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.comap_unop_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.pow_mem_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.pow_eq_span_pow_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.pointwise_mul_semiring_action", "description": " The action on a submodule corresponding to applying the action to every element.\n\nThis is available as an instance in the `pointwise` locale.\n\nThis is a stronger version of `submodule.pointwise_distrib_mul_action`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mul_eq_span_mul_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.map_op_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mul_le_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.le_one_to_add_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mul_induction_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sub_mul_action.algebra_map_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span.ring_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.\u0393_obj_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.forget_to_Top", "description": "The forgetful functor from `Scheme` to `Top`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.comp_val_base_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.comp_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.comp_coe_base_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.forget_to_LocallyRingedSpace.full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.basic_open_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.basic_open_res_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.id_val_base", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.sheaf", "description": "The structure sheaf of a Scheme.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.Spec_map", "description": "The induced map of a ring homomorphism on the ring spectra, as a morphism of schemes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.comp_val_c_app_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.Spec_obj_to_LocallyRingedSpace", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.category_theory.category", "description": "Schemes are a full subcategory of locally ringed spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.comp_coe_base", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.congr_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.forget_to_Top_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme", "description": "We define `Scheme` as a `X : LocallyRingedSpace`,\nalong with a proof that every point has an open neighbourhood `U`\nso that that the restriction of `X` to `U` is isomorphic,\nas a locally ringed space, to `Spec.to_LocallyRingedSpace.obj (op R)`\nfor some `R : CommRing`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.to_LocallyRingedSpace", "description": "We define `Scheme` as a `X : LocallyRingedSpace`,\nalong with a proof that every point has an open neighbourhood `U`\nso that that the restriction of `X` to `U` is isomorphic,\nas a locally ringed space, to `Spec.to_LocallyRingedSpace.obj (op R)`\nfor some `R : CommRing`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.local_affine", "description": "We define `Scheme` as a `X : LocallyRingedSpace`,\nalong with a proof that every point has an open neighbourhood `U`\nso that that the restriction of `X` to `U` is isomorphic,\nas a locally ringed space, to `Spec.to_LocallyRingedSpace.obj (op R)`\nfor some `R : CommRing`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.\u0393_map_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.id_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.basic_open_eq_of_affine", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.\u0393_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.comp_val_base_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.basic_open", "description": "The subset of the underlying space where the given section does not vanish.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.hom", "description": "A morphism between schemes is a morphism between the underlying locally ringed spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.mem_basic_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.Spec_map_2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.has_emptyc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.empty_to_LocallyRingedSpace_to_SheafedSpace_to_PresheafedSpace_presheaf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.Spec_map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.basic_open_eq_of_affine'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.preimage_basic_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.Spec", "description": "The spectrum, as a contravariant functor from commutative rings to schemes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.forget_to_LocallyRingedSpace_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.mem_basic_open_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.\u0393_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.empty", "description": "The empty scheme.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.comp_val_c_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.forget_to_LocallyRingedSpace_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.forget_to_LocallyRingedSpace", "description": "The forgetful functor from `Scheme` to `LocallyRingedSpace`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.hom.app_le", "description": " Given a morphism of schemes `f : X \u27f6 Y`, and open sets `U \u2286 Y`, `V \u2286 f \u207b\u00b9' U`,\nthis is the induced map `\u0393(Y, U) \u27f6 \u0393(X, V)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.\u0393", "description": "The global sections, notated Gamma.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.comp_val_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.Spec_map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.basic_open_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.basic_open_res", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.Spec_obj_2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.is_LocallyRingedSpace_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.forget_to_LocallyRingedSpace_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.basic_open_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.empty_to_LocallyRingedSpace_to_SheafedSpace_to_PresheafedSpace_carrier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.Spec_obj", "description": "The spectrum of a commutative ring, as a scheme.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.inv_val_c_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.app_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.forget_to_Top_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.comp_val_base", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.basic_open_of_is_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.\u0393_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.forget_to_LocallyRingedSpace.faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_strict_initial_objects", "description": "We say `C` has strict initial objects if every initial object is strict, ie given any morphism\n`f : A \u27f6 I` where `I` is initial, then `f` is an isomorphism.\n\nStrictly speaking, this says that *any* initial object must be strict, rather than that strict\ninitial objects exist.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_strict_initial_objects.out", "description": "We say `C` has strict initial objects if every initial object is strict, ie given any morphism\n`f : A \u27f6 I` where `I` is initial, then `f` is an isomorphism.\n\nStrictly speaking, this says that *any* initial object must be strict, rather than that strict\ninitial objects exist.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal.subsingleton_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_strict_terminal_objects_of_terminal_is_strict", "description": " If `C` has an object such that every morphism *from* it is an isomorphism, then `C`\nhas strict terminal objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mul_initial_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial.subsingleton_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.terminal_is_iso_from", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.terminal.subsingleton_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial_mul_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal.strict_hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial_mul_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.terminal.hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal.is_iso_from", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mul_is_initial_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mul_is_initial", "description": "If `I` is initial, then `X \u2a2f I` is isomorphic to it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial_mul_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial.is_iso_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mul_initial_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial_mul", "description": "If `I` is initial, then `I \u2a2f X` is isomorphic to it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial_is_iso_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit_\u03c0_is_iso_of_is_strict_terminal", "description": " If all but one object in a diagram is strict terminal, the the limit is isomorphic to the\nsaid object via `limit.\u03c0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial.strict_hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mul_is_initial_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial.hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial_mul", "description": "The product of `X` with an initial object in a category with strict initial objects is itself\ninitial.\nThis is the generalisation of the fact that `empty \u00d7 X \u2243 empty` for types (or `0 * n = 0`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_strict_initial_objects_of_initial_is_strict", "description": " If `C` has an initial object such that every morphism *to* it is an isomorphism, then `C`\nhas strict initial objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mul_initial", "description": "The product of `X` with an initial object in a category with strict initial objects is itself\ninitial.\nThis is the generalisation of the fact that `X \u00d7 empty \u2243 empty` for types (or `n * 0 = 0`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial_mul_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_strict_terminal_objects", "description": "We say `C` has strict terminal objects if every terminal object is strict, ie given any morphism\n`f : I \u27f6 A` where `I` is terminal, then `f` is an isomorphism.\n\nStrictly speaking, this says that *any* terminal object must be strict, rather than that strict\nterminal objects exist.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_strict_terminal_objects.out", "description": "We say `C` has strict terminal objects if every terminal object is strict, ie given any morphism\n`f : I \u27f6 A` where `I` is terminal, then `f` is an isomorphism.\n\nStrictly speaking, this says that *any* terminal object must be strict, rather than that strict\nterminal objects exist.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial.subsingleton_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial_mono_of_strict_initial_objects", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.find_index", "description": "Get the index of the first element of `s` satisfying `p`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.destruct_flatten", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.exists_of_mem_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.ret", "description": "The monadic `return a` is a singleton list containing `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.append_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.bind", "description": "Monadic bind operator for weak sequences", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.destruct_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.destruct_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.join_ret", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.nil_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.lift_rel_flatten", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.of_mem_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.union", "description": "`union s1 s2` is a weak sequence which interleaves `s1` and `s2` in\n some order (nondeterministically).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.map_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.join_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.filter_map", "description": "Map the elements of `s` over `f`, removing any values that yield `none`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.flatten", "description": "Encode a computation yielding a weak sequence into additional\n `think` constructors in a weak sequence", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.all", "description": "Returns `tt` if every element of `s` satisfies `p`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.join_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.think", "description": "Compute for one tick, without producing any elements", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.indexes_of", "description": "Get the indexes of occurrences of `a` in `s`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.destruct_congr_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.lift_rel_o.imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.append", "description": "Append two weak sequences. As with `seq.append`, this may not use\n the second sequence if the first one takes forever to compute", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.lift_rel_o", "description": "lift a relation to a relation over weak sequences", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.to_list_terminates", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq", "description": "Weak sequences.\n\n While the `seq` structure allows for lists which may not be finite,\n a weak sequence also allows the computation of each element to\n involve an indeterminate amount of computation, including possibly\n an infinite loop. This is represented as a regular `seq` interspersed\n with `none` elements to indicate that computation is ongoing.\n\n This model is appropriate for Haskell style lazy lists, and is closed\n under most interesting computation patterns on infinite lists,\n but conversely it is difficult to extract elements from it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.lift_rel_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.map", "description": "Map a function over a weak sequence", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.coe_stream", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.lift_rel_think_right", 