m into a weak sequence", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.think_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.nth", "description": "Get the nth element of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.map_ret", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.cons_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.dropn_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.update_nth", "description": "Replace the `n`th element of `s` with `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.head_terminates", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.lift_rel_o.swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.of_seq", "description": "Turn a sequence into a weak sequence", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.drop.aux_none", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.seq_destruct_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.split_at", "description": "Split the sequence at position `n` into a finite initial segment\n and the weak sequence tail", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.mem_of_mem_tail", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.lift_rel_dropn_destruct", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.eq_or_mem_iff_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.has_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.destruct_terminates_of_nth_terminates", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.destruct_tail", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.productive_of_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.head_terminates_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.length", "description": "Get the length of `s` (if it is finite and completes in finite time).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.destruct_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.join_join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.rec_on", "description": "Recursion principle for weak sequences, compare with `list.rec_on`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.filter", "description": "Select the elements of `s` that satisfy `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.any", "description": "Returns `tt` if any element of `s` satisfies `p`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.is_empty", "description": "Returns `tt` if `s` is `nil` and `ff` if `s` has an element", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.nth_terminates", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.of_list_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.to_list_of_list", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.lift_rel.equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.compute", "description": "Calculate one step of computation", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.to_list_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.mem_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.map_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.mem_of_mem_dropn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.join_map_ret", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.equiv.equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.destruct_join.aux", "description": "auxilary defintion of `destruct_join` over weak sequences", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.lift_rel_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.equiv.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.equiv", "description": "If two sequences are equivalent, then they have the same values and\n the same computational behavior (i.e. if one loops forever then so does\n the other), although they may differ in the number of `think`s needed to\n arrive at the answer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.not_mem_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.destruct_some_of_destruct_tail_some", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.to_seq", "description": "Given a productive weak sequence, we can collapse all the `think`s to\n produce a sequence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.mem", "description": "membership for weak sequences", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.to_list'_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.destruct_append.aux", "description": "auxilary defintion of `destruct_append` over weak sequences", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.append_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.nth_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.monad", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.nth_tail", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.lift_rel_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.join_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.destruct_think", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.find_indexes", "description": "Get the list of indexes of elements of `s` satisfying `p`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.bind_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.nil", "description": "The empty weak sequence", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.join", "description": "Flatten a sequence of weak sequences. (Note that this allows\n empty sequences, unlike `seq.join`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.flatten_think", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.map_join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.find", "description": "Get the first element of `s` satisfying `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.cons_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.think_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.tail_of_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.lift_rel", "description": "Two weak sequences are `lift_rel R` related if they are either both empty,\n or they are both nonempty and the heads are `R` related and the tails are\n `lift_rel R` related. (This is a coinductive definition.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.head_think", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.map_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.dropn_think", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.to_list'_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.dropn_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.equiv.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.index_of", "description": "Get the index of the first occurrence of `a` in `s`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.mem_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.nth_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.flatten_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.drop", "description": "drop the first `n` elements from `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.head_of_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.is_finite", "description": "A weak sequence is finite if `to_list s` terminates. Equivalently,\n it is a finite number of `think` and `cons` applied to `nil`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.is_finite.out", "description": "A weak sequence is finite if `to_list s` terminates. Equivalently,\n it is a finite number of `think` and `cons` applied to `nil`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.to_list_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.exists_dropn_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.coe_list", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.tail_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.head_terminates_of_head_tail_terminates", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.mem_cons_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.head", "description": "Get the head of a weak sequence. This involves a possibly\n infinite computation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.scanl", "description": "Apply a function to the elements of the sequence to produce a sequence\n of partial results. (There is no `scanr` because this would require\n working from the end of the sequence, which may not exist.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.lift_rel_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.productive_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.map_think", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.seq_destruct_think", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.of_list_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.exists_of_mem_join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.head_terminates_of_nth_terminates", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.join_think", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.lift_rel.swap_lem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.head_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.destruct", "description": "Destruct a weak sequence, to (eventually possibly) produce either\n `none` for `nil` or `some (a, s)` if an element is produced.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.destruct_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.destruct_dropn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.dropn_tail", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.tail", "description": "Get the tail of a weak sequence. This doesn't need a `computation`\n wrapper, unlike `head`, because `flatten` allows us to hide this\n in the construction of the weak sequence itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.productive", "description": "A weak sequence is *productive* if it never stalls forever - there are\nalways a finite number of `think`s between `cons` constructors.\nThe sequence itself is allowed to be infinite though.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.productive.nth_terminates", "description": "A weak sequence is *productive* if it never stalls forever - there are\nalways a finite number of `think`s between `cons` constructors.\nThe sequence itself is allowed to be infinite though.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.mem_think", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.join_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.tail_think", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.exists_of_lift_rel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.lift_rel.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.mem_append_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.bind_ret", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.lift_rel.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.exists_of_mem_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.lift_rel_o.imp_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.bisim_o.imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.lift_rel_join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.lift_rel_think_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.zip_with", "description": "Zip a function over two weak sequences", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.lift_rel_destruct_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.to_list'_think", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.mem_cons_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.zip", "description": "Zip two weak sequences into a single sequence of pairs", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.flatten_ret", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.productive_tail", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.remove_nth", "description": "Remove the `n`th element of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.bind_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.head_terminates_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.wseq.inits", "description": "Get the weak sequence of initial segments of the input sequence", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.fslope", "description": " The formal counterpart of `dslope`, corresponding to the expansion of `(f z - f 0) / z`. If `f`\nhas `p` as a power series, then `dslope f` has `fslope p` as a power series.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.coeff", "description": "The `n`th coefficient of `p` when seen as a power series.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.coeff_fslope", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.order_eq_find'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "const_formal_multilinear_series_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.unshift", "description": " Adding a zeroth term to a formal multilinear series taking values in `E \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] F`. This\ncorresponds to starting from a Taylor series for the derivative of a function, and building a Taylor\nseries for the function itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series", "description": " A formal multilinear series over a field `\ud835\udd5c`, from `E` to `F`, is given by a family of\nmultilinear maps from `E^n` to `F` for all `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.apply_eq_pow_smul_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.ne_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.coeff_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.order_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.comp_formal_multilinear_series", "description": " Composing each term `p\u2099` in a formal multilinear series with a continuous linear map `f` on the\nleft gives a new formal multilinear series `f.comp_formal_multilinear_series p` whose general term\nis `f \u2218 p\u2099`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.shift", "description": " Forgetting the zeroth term in a formal multilinear series, and interpreting the following terms\nas multilinear maps into `E \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] F`. If `p` corresponds to the Taylor series of a function, then\n`p.shift` is the Taylor series of the derivative of the function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.congr", "description": " Convenience congruence lemma stating in a dependent setting that, if the arguments to a formal\nmultilinear series are equal, then the values are also equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "const_formal_multilinear_series", "description": " The formal multilinear series where all terms of positive degree are equal to zero, and the term\nof degree zero is `c`. It is the power series expansion of the constant function equal to `c`\neverywhere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.comp_formal_multilinear_series_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.mk_pi_field_coeff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_continuous_linear_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.remove_zero_coeff_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.apply_eq_zero_of_lt_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_continuous_linear_map", "description": " Composing each term `p\u2099` in a formal multilinear series with `(u, ..., u)` where `u` is a fixed\ncontinuous linear map, gives a new formal multilinear series `p.comp_continuous_linear_map u`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.apply_eq_prod_smul_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.order_eq_zero_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.norm_apply_eq_norm_coef", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.ne_zero_of_order_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.remove_zero", "description": "Killing the zeroth coefficient in a formal multilinear series", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.remove_zero_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.coeff_iterate_fslope", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.apply_order_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.order", "description": "The index of the first non-zero coefficient in `p` (or `0` if all coefficients are zero). This\n is the order of the isolated zero of an analytic function `f` at a point if `p` is the Taylor\n series of `f` at that point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.order_eq_find", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.apply_order_ne_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.restrict_scalars", "description": "Reinterpret a formal `\ud835\udd5c'`-multilinear series as a formal `\ud835\udd5c`-multilinear series.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.remove_zero_coeff_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.comp_formal_multilinear_series_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.order_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.is_colimit_coimage", "description": "If `(f, g)` is exact, then `coimages.coimage.\u03c0 g` is a cokernel of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.mono_iff_kernel_\u03b9_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.epi_iff_cokernel_\u03c0_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.preserves_finite_limits_of_preserves_monos_and_cokernels", "description": "A functor preserving zero morphisms, monos, and cokernels preserves finite limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.exact_iff_exact_coimage_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.category_theory.limits.cokernel.desc.category_theory.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.is_equivalence.exact_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.is_colimit_of_exact_of_epi", "description": "If `X \u27f6 Y \u27f6 Z \u27f6 0` is exact, then the second map is a cokernel of the first.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.exact_iff_exact_image_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.kernel.lift.inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_exact", "description": " A functor preserving finite limits and finite colimits preserves exactness. The converse\nresult is also true, see `functor.preserves_finite_limits_of_map_exact` and\n`functor.preserves_finite_colimits_of_map_exact`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.exact_iff_image_eq_kernel", "description": "In an abelian category, a pair of morphisms `f : X \u27f6 Y`, `g : Y \u27f6 Z` is exact\niff `image_subobject f = kernel_subobject g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.exact_tfae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.preserves_finite_limits_of_map_exact", "description": " A functor which preserves exactness is left exact, i.e. preserves finite limits.\nThis is part of the inverse implication to `functor.map_exact`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.exact_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.tfae_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.exact_epi_comp_iff", "description": "The dual result is true even in non-abelian categories, see\n   `category_theory.exact_comp_mono_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.exact_of_is_cokernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.reflects_exact_sequences_of_preserves_zero_morphisms_of_faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.exact.op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.is_limit_image", "description": "If `(f, g)` is exact, then `abelian.image.\u03b9 f` is a kernel of `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.exact_cokernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.kernel.lift.inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.exact.unop_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.preserves_zero_morphisms_of_map_exact", "description": "A functor which preserves exactness preserves zero morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.cokernel.desc.inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.category_theory.limits.kernel.lift.category_theory.is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.tfae_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.exact.op_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.is_colimit_image", "description": "If `(f, g)` is exact, then `factor_thru_image g` is a cokernel of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.preserves_cokernels_of_map_exact", "description": "A functor which preserves exactness preserves zero cokernels.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.preserves_epimorphisms_of_map_exact", "description": "A functor which preserves exactness preserves epimorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.preserves_kernels_of_map_exact", "description": "A functor which preserves exactness preserves kernels.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.exact_of_is_kernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.exact.unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.preserves_monomorphisms_of_map_exact", "description": "A functor which preserves exactness preserves monomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.is_limit_image'", "description": "If `(f, g)` is exact, then `image.\u03b9 f` is a kernel of `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.cokernel.desc.inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.category_theory.limits.cokernel.desc.category_theory.is_iso", "description": "If `ex : exact f g` and `epi g`, then `cokernel.desc _ _ ex.w` is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.preserves_finite_colimits_of_preserves_epis_and_kernels", "description": "A functor preserving zero morphisms, epis, and kernels preserves finite colimits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.is_limit_of_exact_of_mono", "description": "If `0 \u27f6 X \u27f6 Y \u27f6 Z` is exact, then the first map is a kernel of the second.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.exact_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.preserves_finite_colimits_of_map_exact", "description": " A functor which preserves exactness is right exact, i.e. preserves finite colimits.\nThis is part of the inverse implication to `functor.map_exact`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even_hom.compr\u2082", "description": "Compose an `even_hom` with an `alg_hom` on the output.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even.lift.aux", "description": " The final auxiliary construction for `clifford_algebra.even.lift`. This map is the forwards\ndirection of that equivalence, but not in the fully-bundled form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even.lift.aux_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even.\u03b9_bilin_apply_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even.alg_hom_ext", "description": " Two algebra morphisms from the even subalgebra are equal if they agree on pairs of generators.\n\nSee note [partially-applied ext lemmas].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even_hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even.lift.aux_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even.\u03b9", "description": "The embedding of pairs of vectors into the even subalgebra, as a bilinear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even_hom", "description": "The type of bilinear maps which are accepted by `clifford_algebra.even.lift`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even_hom.bilin", "description": "The type of bilinear maps which are accepted by `clifford_algebra.even.lift`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even_hom.contract", "description": "The type of bilinear maps which are accepted by `clifford_algebra.even.lift`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even_hom.contract_mid", "description": "The type of bilinear maps which are accepted by `clifford_algebra.even.lift`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even_to_submodule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even", "description": "The even submodule `clifford_algebra.even_odd Q 0` is also a subalgebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even.lift.aux_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even_hom.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even.lift_symm_apply_bilin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even_hom.compr\u2082_bilin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even.lift", "description": " Every algebra morphism from the even subalgebra is in one-to-one correspondence with a\nbilinear map that sends duplicate arguments to the quadratic form, and contracts across\nmultiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even_hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even.lift_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even.lift.aux_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even.lift.aux_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_ext_coord_change", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_ext_chart_at_symm''", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.pi", "description": " Given a finite family of `model_with_corners` `I i` on `(E i, H i)`, we define the model with\ncorners `pi I` on `(\u03a0 i, E i, model_pi H)`. See note [Manifold type tags] for explanation about\n`model_pi H`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.map_extend_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_source_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_source_mem_nhds_within'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_source_mem_nhds'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_within_ext_chart_at_target_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.unique_diff_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.prod", "description": " Given two model_with_corners `I` on `(E, H)` and `I'` on `(E', H')`, we define the model with\ncorners `I.prod I'` on `(E \u00d7 E', model_prod H H')`. This appears in particular for the manifold\nstructure on the tangent bundle to a manifold modelled on `(E, H)`: it will be modelled on\n`(E \u00d7 E, H \u00d7 E)`. See note [Manifold type tags] for explanation about `model_prod H H'`\nvs `H \u00d7 H'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.range_eq_univ_prod", "description": "If two model with corners are boundaryless, their product also is", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_preimage_mem_nhds_within'", "description": " Technical lemma ensuring that the preimage under an extended chart of a neighborhood of a point\nin the source is a neighborhood of the preimage, within a set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_coe_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.continuous_within_at_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_ext_chart_at_symm_nhds_within'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.mk_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_ext_chart_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.to_local_equiv_coe_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.map_nhds_within_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.simps.apply", "description": "See Note [custom simps projection]. We need to specify this projection explicitly in this case,\n because it is a composition of multiple projections.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_groupoid_zero_eq", "description": " The groupoid of `0`-times continuously differentiable maps is just the groupoid of all\nlocal homeomorphisms", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_ext_chart_at_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend_coord_change_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "open_embedding.singleton_smooth_manifold_with_corners", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.symm_map_nhds_within_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend_source_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.closed_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at", "description": " The preferred extended chart on a manifold with corners around a point `x`, from a neighborhood\nof `x` to the model vector space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_coord_change_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_model_space_eq_id", "description": " In the case of the manifold structure on a vector space, the extended charts are just the\nidentity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.continuous_at_extend_symm'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_model_space_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.map_nhds_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.image_mem_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.simps.symm_apply", "description": "See Note [custom simps projection]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend_symm_preimage_inter_range_eventually_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.right_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_manifold_with_corners.chart_mem_maximal_atlas", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners", "description": " A structure containing informations on the way a space `H` embeds in a\nmodel vector space `E` over the field `\ud835\udd5c`. This is all what is needed to\ndefine a smooth manifold with model space `H`, and model vector space `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.to_local_equiv", "description": " A structure containing informations on the way a space `H` embeds in a\nmodel vector space `E` over the field `\ud835\udd5c`. This is all what is needed to\ndefine a smooth manifold with model space `H`, and model vector space `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.source_eq", "description": " A structure containing informations on the way a space `H` embeds in a\nmodel vector space `E` over the field `\ud835\udd5c`. This is all what is needed to\ndefine a smooth manifold with model space `H`, and model vector space `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.unique_diff'", "description": " A structure containing informations on the way a space `H` embeds in a\nmodel vector space `E` over the field `\ud835\udd5c`. This is all what is needed to\ndefine a smooth manifold with model space `H`, and model vector space `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.continuous_to_fun", "description": " A structure containing informations on the way a space `H` embeds in a\nmodel vector space `E` over the field `\ud835\udd5c`. This is all what is needed to\ndefine a smooth manifold with model space `H`, and model vector space `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.continuous_inv_fun", "description": " A structure containing informations on the way a space `H` embeds in a\nmodel vector space `E` over the field `\ud835\udd5c`. This is all what is needed to\ndefine a smooth manifold with model space `H`, and model vector space `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_groupoid", "description": " Given a model with corners `(E, H)`, we define the groupoid of `C^n` transformations of `H` as\nthe maps that are `C^n` when read in `E` through `I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_ext_chart_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.continuous_on_extend_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_target_mem_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.target_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_ext_chart_at'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_target_mem_nhds_within'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.range_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_preimage_mem_nhds'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.continuous_within_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend_preimage_mem_nhds_within", "description": " Technical lemma ensuring that the preimage under an extended chart of a neighborhood of a point\nin the source is a neighborhood of the preimage, within a set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.symm_continuous_within_at_comp_right_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_ext_chart_at_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.continuous_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_groupoid_le", "description": " Inclusion of the groupoid of `C^n` local diffeos in the groupoid of `C^m` local diffeos when\n`m \u2264 n`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_manifold_with_corners", "description": " Typeclass defining smooth manifolds with corners with respect to a model with corners, over a\nfield `\ud835\udd5c` and with infinite smoothness to simplify typeclass search and statements later on.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_manifold_with_corners.to_has_groupoid", "description": " Typeclass defining smooth manifolds with corners with respect to a model with corners, over a\nfield `\ud835\udd5c` and with infinite smoothness to simplify typeclass search and statements later on.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_preimage_mem_nhds", "description": " Technical lemma ensuring that the preimage under an extended chart of a neighborhood of a point\nis a neighborhood of the preimage.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_preimage_mem_nhds_within", "description": " Technical lemma ensuring that the preimage under an extended chart of a neighborhood of the\nbase point is a neighborhood of the preimage, within a set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners_self_local_equiv", "description": "In the trivial model with corners, the associated local equiv is the identity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_within_ext_chart_at_target_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_preimage_inter_eq", "description": " Technical lemma to rewrite suitably the preimage of an intersection under an extended chart, to\nbring it into a convenient form to apply derivative lemmas.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_space_smooth", "description": "For any model with corners, the model space is a smooth manifold", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_open_extend_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.maps_to_extend", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend_preimage_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.tangent", "description": " Special case of product model with corners, which is trivial on the second factor. This shows up\nas the model to tangent bundles.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "maps_to_ext_chart_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_ext_chart_at_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_ext_chart_at_symm_nhds_within_range'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.map_extend_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend_coe_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_set_mem_cont_diff_groupoid", "description": "An identity local homeomorphism belongs to the `C^n` groupoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_groupoid_prod", "description": "The product of two smooth local homeomorphisms is smooth.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend_source_mem_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at_ext_coord_change", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.continuous_at_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "symm_trans_mem_cont_diff_groupoid", "description": " The composition of a local homeomorphism from `H` to `M` and its inverse belongs to\nthe `C^n` groupoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_ext_chart_at_preimage'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend", "description": " Given a chart `f` on a manifold with corners, `f.extend I` is the extended chart to the model\nvector space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend_target_subset_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.unique_diff_preimage_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners_self_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend_preimage_inter_eq", "description": " Technical lemma to rewrite suitably the preimage of an intersection under an extended chart, to\nbring it into a convenient form to apply derivative lemmas.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend_symm_continuous_within_at_comp_right_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_ext_chart_at_nhds_within_eq_image'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners_prod_coe_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_ext_chart_at_nhds'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.prod_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend_symm_preimage_inter_range_eventually_eq_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "written_in_ext_chart_at", "description": " Conjugating a function to write it in the preferred charts around `x`.\nThe manifold derivative of `f` will just be the derivative of this conjugated function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_self_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.map_extend_symm_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners_self_boundaryless", "description": "The trivial model with corners has no boundary", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_groupoid.closed_under_restriction", "description": "The `C^n` groupoid is closed under restriction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_ext_chart_at_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend_target_mem_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_to_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_manifold_with_corners_of_cont_diff_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_ext_chart_at_symm'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_open_extend_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.second_countable_topology", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.left_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners_self", "description": "A vector space is a model with corners.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend_coord_change_source_mem_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_manifold_with_corners.prod", "description": "The product of two smooth manifolds with corners is naturally a smooth manifold with corners.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.unique_diff_at_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.image_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.continuous_on_extend", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend_image_source_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.boundaryless", "description": "Property ensuring that the model with corners `I` defines manifolds without boundary.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.boundaryless.range_eq_univ", "description": "Property ensuring that the model with corners `I` defines manifolds without boundary.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.map_extend_nhds_within_eq_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.symm_comp_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.symm_map_nhds_within_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.right_inv_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_ext_chart_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.prod_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend_left_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.continuous_on_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners_prod_to_local_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners_self_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.closed_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.locally_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_ext_chart_at_symm_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.continuous_at_extend_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_ext_chart_at_nhds_within_eq_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.cont_diff_within_at_extend_coord_change'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.smooth_manifold_with_corners", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_ext_chart_at_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.symm", "description": "The inverse to a model with corners, only registered as a local equiv.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.cont_diff_on_extend_coord_change", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.continuous_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_target_subset_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners_prod_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_source_mem_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.cont_diff_within_at_extend_coord_change", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_self_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_manifold_with_corners.compatible_of_mem_maximal_atlas", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners_self_coe_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_ext_chart_at_nhds_within'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.to_local_equiv_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_ext_chart_at_symm_nhds_within_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.left_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.preimage_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_open_extend_preimage'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.singleton_smooth_manifold_with_corners", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_chart_at_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_ext_chart_at_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.map_extend_symm_nhds_within_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.continuous_at_extend", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_manifold_with_corners.mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.nhds_within_extend_target_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.extend_coord_change_source_mem_nhds_within'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_manifold_with_corners.maximal_atlas", "description": " The maximal atlas of `M` for the smooth manifold with corners structure corresponding to the\nmodel with corners `I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.unique_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_manifold_with_corners.subset_maximal_atlas", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "model_with_corners.prod_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.ae_tendsto_average", "description": " *Lebesgue differentiation theorem*: for almost every point `x`, the\naverage of `f` on `a` tends to `f x` as `a` shrinks to `x` along a Vitali family.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.ae_tendsto_div", "description": " If `\u03c1` is absolutely continuous with respect to `\u03bc`, then for almost every `x`,\nthe ratio `\u03c1 a / \u03bc a` converges as `a` shrinks to `x` along a Vitali family for `\u03bc`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.null_of_frequently_le_of_frequently_ge", "description": " A set of points `s` satisfying both `\u03c1 a \u2264 c * \u03bc a` and `\u03c1 a \u2265 d * \u03bc a` at arbitrarily small\nsets in a Vitali family has measure `0` if `c < d`. Indeed, the first inequality should imply\nthat `\u03c1 s \u2264 c * \u03bc s`, and the second one that `\u03c1 s \u2265 d * \u03bc s`, a contradiction if `0 < \u03bc s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.ae_measurable_lim_ratio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.measure_lim_ratio_meas_top", "description": "The points with `v.lim_ratio_meas h\u03c1 x = \u221e` have measure `0` for `\u03bc`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.le_mul_with_density", "description": " As an intermediate step to show that `\u03bc.with_density (v.lim_ratio_meas h\u03c1) = \u03c1`, we show here\nthat `\u03c1 \u2264 t \u03bc.with_density (v.lim_ratio_meas h\u03c1)` for any `t > 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.ae_tendsto_rn_deriv", "description": " Main theorem on differentiation of measures: given a Vitali family `v` for a locally finite\nmeasure `\u03bc`, and another locally finite measure `\u03c1`, then for `\u03bc`-almost every `x` the\nratio `\u03c1 a / \u03bc a` converges, when `a` shrinks to `x` along the Vitali family, towards the\nRadon-Nikodym derivative of `\u03c1` with respect to `\u03bc`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.ae_eventually_measure_pos", "description": " For almost every point `x`, sufficiently small sets in a Vitali family around `x` have positive\nmeasure. (This is a nontrivial result, following from the covering property of Vitali families).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.measure_lim_ratio_meas_zero", "description": "The points with `v.lim_ratio_meas h\u03c1 x = 0` have measure `0` for `\u03c1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.ae_tendsto_lintegral_div'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.measure_le_mul_of_subset_lim_ratio_meas_lt", "description": " If, for all `x` in a set `s`, one has frequently `\u03c1 a / \u03bc a < p`, then `\u03c1 s \u2264 p * \u03bc s`, as\nproved in `measure_le_of_frequently_le`. Since `\u03c1 a / \u03bc a` tends almost everywhere to\n`v.lim_ratio_meas h\u03c1 x`, the same property holds for sets `s` on which `v.lim_ratio_meas h\u03c1 < p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.ae_tendsto_average_norm_sub", "description": " *Lebesgue differentiation theorem*: for almost every point `x`, the\naverage of `\u2016f y - f x\u2016` on `a` tends to `0` as `a` shrinks to `x` along a Vitali family.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.eventually_measure_lt_top", "description": " For every point `x`, sufficiently small sets in a Vitali family around `x` have finite measure.\n(This is a trivial result, following from the fact that the measure is locally finite).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.ae_tendsto_rn_deriv_of_absolutely_continuous", "description": " Weak version of the main theorem on differentiation of measures: given a Vitali family `v`\nfor a locally finite measure `\u03bc`, and another locally finite measure `\u03c1`, then for `\u03bc`-almost\nevery `x` the ratio `\u03c1 a / \u03bc a` converges, when `a` shrinks to `x` along the Vitali family,\ntowards the Radon-Nikodym derivative of `\u03c1` with respect to `\u03bc`.\n\nThis version assumes that `\u03c1` is absolutely continuous with respect to `\u03bc`. The general version\nwithout this superfluous assumption is `vitali_family.ae_tendsto_rn_deriv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.measure_le_of_frequently_le", "description": " If two measures `\u03c1` and `\u03bd` have, at every point of a set `s`, arbitrarily small sets in a\nVitali family satisfying `\u03c1 a \u2264 \u03bd a`, then `\u03c1 s \u2264 \u03bd s` if `\u03c1 \u226a \u03bc`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.ae_tendsto_lim_ratio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.exists_measurable_supersets_lim_ratio", "description": " Given two thresholds `p < q`, the sets `{x | v.lim_ratio \u03c1 x < p}`\nand `{x | q < v.lim_ratio \u03c1 x}` are obviously disjoint. The key to proving that `v.lim_ratio \u03c1` is\nalmost everywhere measurable is to show that these sets have measurable supersets which are also\ndisjoint, up to zero measure. This is the content of this lemma.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.lim_ratio", "description": " The limit along a Vitali family of `\u03c1 a / \u03bc a` where it makes sense, and garbage otherwise.\nDo *not* use this definition: it is only a temporary device to show that this ratio tends almost\neverywhere to the Radon-Nikodym derivative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.ae_tendsto_lintegral_nnnorm_sub_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.lim_ratio_meas_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.ae_eventually_measure_zero_of_singular", "description": " If a measure `\u03c1` is singular with respect to `\u03bc`, then for `\u03bc` almost every `x`, the ratio\n`\u03c1 a / \u03bc a` tends to zero when `a` shrinks to `x` along the Vitali family. This makes sense\nas `\u03bc a` is eventually positive by `ae_eventually_measure_pos`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.with_density_le_mul", "description": " As an intermediate step to show that `\u03bc.with_density (v.lim_ratio_meas h\u03c1) = \u03c1`, we show here\nthat `\u03bc.with_density (v.lim_ratio_meas h\u03c1) \u2264 t^2 \u03c1` for any `t > 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.ae_tendsto_measure_inter_div", "description": " Given an arbitrary set `s`, then `\u03bc (s \u2229 a) / \u03bc a` converges to `1` when `a` shrinks to a\ntypical point of `s` along a Vitali family. This shows that almost every point of `s` is a\nLebesgue density point for `s`. A stronger version for measurable sets is given\nin `ae_tendsto_measure_inter_div_of_measurable_set`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.ae_tendsto_measure_inter_div_of_measurable_set", "description": " Given a measurable set `s`, then `\u03bc (s \u2229 a) / \u03bc a` converges when `a` shrinks to a typical\npoint `x` along a Vitali family. The limit is `1` for `x \u2208 s` and `0` for `x \u2209 s`. This shows that\nalmost every point of `s` is a Lebesgue density point for `s`. A version for non-measurable sets\nholds, but it only gives the first conclusion, see `ae_tendsto_measure_inter_div`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.with_density_lim_ratio_meas_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.ae_tendsto_lintegral_nnnorm_sub_div'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.ae_tendsto_lim_ratio_meas", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.lim_ratio_meas", "description": " A measurable version of `v.lim_ratio \u03c1`. Do *not* use this definition: it is only a temporary\ndevice to show that `v.lim_ratio` is almost everywhere equal to the Radon-Nikodym derivative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.mul_measure_le_of_subset_lt_lim_ratio_meas", "description": " If, for all `x` in a set `s`, one has frequently `q < \u03c1 a / \u03bc a`, then `q * \u03bc s \u2264 \u03c1 s`, as\nproved in `measure_le_of_frequently_le`. Since `\u03c1 a / \u03bc a` tends almost everywhere to\n`v.lim_ratio_meas h\u03c1 x`, the same property holds for sets `s` on which `q < v.lim_ratio_meas h\u03c1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vitali_family.ae_tendsto_lintegral_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.comap_map_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_int_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_singleton_smul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.coord_apply_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_span_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_span_singleton_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.closure_le_to_add_submonoid_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ext_on_range", "description": " If the range of `v : \u03b9 \u2192 M` generates the whole module and linear maps `f`, `g` are equal at\neach `v i`, then they are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.subset_span_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_range_eq_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_Union\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_prod_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.supr_to_add_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.finite_span_is_compact_element", "description": "The span of a finite subset is compact in the lattice of submodules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_monotone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_supr_of_chain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_insert_eq_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_compactly_generated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_singleton_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.sup_to_add_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.sup_to_add_subgroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_smul_eq_of_is_unit", "description": " See `submodule.span_smul_eq` (in `ring_theory.ideal.operations`) for\n`span R (r \u2022 s) = r \u2022 span R s` that holds for arbitrary `r` in a `comm_semiring`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.coord_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_span_singleton_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.span_preimage_le", "description": "**Alias** of `submodule.span_preimage_le`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_inf_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_eq_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.eq_on_span", "description": " If two linear maps are equal on a set `s`, then they are equal on `submodule.span s`.\n\nSee also `linear_map.eq_on_span'` for a version using `set.eq_on`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_span_singleton_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.lt_sup_iff_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.closure_subset_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.subset_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_span_singleton_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.to_span_nonzero_singleton_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_span_pair", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_span_singleton_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_eq_top_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_span_insert'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.supr_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.not_mem_span_of_apply_not_mem_span_image", "description": "`f` is an explicit argument so we can `apply` this theorem and obtain `h` as a new goal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span", "description": "The span of a set `s \u2286 M` is the smallest submodule of M that contains `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_span_le", "description": "**Alias** of `submodule.map_span_le`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.comap_map_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_le_map_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.supr_induction'", "description": "A dependent version of `submodule.supr_induction`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.sup_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.coe_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_zero_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.span_singleton_sup_ker_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.singleton_span_is_compact_element", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_insert_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.coe_scott_continuous", "description": " We can regard `coe_supr_of_chain` as the statement that `coe : (submodule R M) \u2192 set M` is\nScott continuous for the \u03c9-complete partial order induced by the complete lattice structures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_Sup_of_directed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_span_of_tower", "description": " Taking the span by a large ring of the span by the small ring is the same as taking the span\nby just the large ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_modular_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_singleton_eq_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.to_span_nonzero_singleton", "description": " Given a nonzero element `x` of a torsion-free module `M` over a ring `R`, the natural\nisomorphism from `R` to the span of `x` given by $r \\mapsto r \\cdot x$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_coe_eq_restrict_scalars", "description": "A version of `submodule.span_eq` for when the span is by a smaller ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.gi", "description": "`span` forms a Galois insertion with the coercion from submodule to set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.map_span_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.apply_mem_span_image_of_mem_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.map_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_subset_span", "description": "A version of `submodule.span_le_restrict_scalars` with coercions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ker_to_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_le_restrict_scalars", "description": "If `R` is \"smaller\" ring than `S` then the span by `R` is smaller than the span by `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_nat_eq_add_submonoid_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_eq_supr_of_singleton_spans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_singleton_eq_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_induction", "description": " An induction principle for span membership. If `p` holds for 0 and all elements of `s`, and is\npreserved under addition and scalar multiplication, then `p` holds for all elements of the span of\n`s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_span_singleton", "description": "Given an element `x` of a module `M` over `R`, the natural map from\n   `R` to scalar multiples of `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.eq_on_span'", "description": " If two linear maps are equal on a set `s`, then they are equal on `submodule.span s`.\n\nThis version uses `set.eq_on`, and the hidden argument will expand to `h : x \u2208 (span R s : set M)`.\nSee `linear_map.eq_on_span` for a version that takes `h : x \u2208 span R s` as an argument.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_induction'", "description": "A dependent version of `submodule.span_induction`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_int_eq_add_subgroup_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_preimage_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_sup'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.coe_supr_of_directed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.le_span_singleton_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_singleton_eq_top_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.supr_induction", "description": " An induction principle for elements of `\u2a06 i, p i`.\nIf `C` holds for `0` and all elements of `p i` for all `i`, and is preserved under addition,\nthen it holds for all elements of the supremum of `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.coe_supr_of_chain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.supr_eq_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_singleton_group_smul_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.finset_span_is_compact_element", "description": "The span of a finite subset is compact in the lattice of submodules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_singleton_smul_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.map_subtype_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.disjoint_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_nat_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_span_finite_of_mem_span", "description": " For every element in the span of a set, there exists a finite subset of the set\nsuch that the element is contained in the span of the subset.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ext_on", "description": " If `s` generates the whole module and linear maps `f`, `g` are equal on `s`, then they are\nequal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_sup_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.coord", "description": " Given a nonzero element `x` of a torsion-free module `M` over a ring `R`, the natural\nisomorphism from the span of `x` to `R` given by $r \\cdot x \\mapsto r$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_supr_of_directed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_eq_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_le_map_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_smul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod", "description": "The product of two submodules is a submodule.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_span_coe_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_singleton_le_iff_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.span_singleton_eq_range", "description": "The range of `to_span_singleton x` is the span of `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.disjoint_span_singleton'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_attach_bUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.span_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_span", "description": "**Alias** of `submodule.map_span`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.nontrivial_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.submodule_eq_Sup_le_nonzero_spans", "description": "A submodule is equal to the supremum of the spans of the submodule's nonzero elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.regular_act", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.category_theory.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.id_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.regular", "description": "A monoid object as a module over itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.hom", "description": "A morphism of module objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.hom.hom", "description": "A morphism of module objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.hom.act_hom'", "description": "A morphism of module objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.comap_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.comap_map_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.hom.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.regular_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.hom_inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.comap", "description": "A morphism of monoid objects induces a \"restriction\" or \"comap\" functor\nbetween the categories of module objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.forget", "description": "The forgetful functor from module objects to the ambient category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.assoc_flip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.id_hom'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.comp", "description": "Composition of module object morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_", "description": "A module object for a monoid object, all internal to some monoidal category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.X", "description": "A module object for a monoid object, all internal to some monoidal category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.act", "description": "A module object for a monoid object, all internal to some monoidal category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.one_act'", "description": "A module object for a monoid object, all internal to some monoidal category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.assoc'", "description": "A module object for a monoid object, all internal to some monoidal category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.id", "description": "The identity morphism on a module object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.comp_hom'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.comp_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.hom.act_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.one_act_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.hom.act_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.one_act", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.assoc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mod_.comap_obj_act", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic.cardinal_mk_le_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic.aleph_0_le_cardinal_mk_of_char_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic.cardinal_mk_lift_le_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic.cardinal_mk_le_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic.cardinal_mk_of_countble_of_char_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic.infinite_of_char_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic.cardinal_mk_lift_le_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic.cardinal_mk_lift_of_infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic.cardinal_mk_of_infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic.countable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_to_square_block_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_triangular.det_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_triangular_block_diagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_triangular.transpose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_triangular_transpose_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_triangular_diagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_triangular_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_triangular_reindex_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.upper_two_block_triangular", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.two_block_triangular_det", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_to_block", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_triangular.submatrix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_triangular.inv_to_block", "description": " The inverse of an upper-left subblock of a block-triangular matrix `M` is the upper-left\nsubblock of `M\u207b\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_triangular_inv_of_block_triangular", "description": "The inverse of a block-triangular matrix is block-triangular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.two_block_triangular_det'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_triangular.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_triangular.det", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_triangular_block_diagonal'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_triangular.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_triangular.invertible_to_block", "description": "An upper-left subblock of an invertible block-triangular matrix is invertible.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_triangular.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_triangular.to_block_inverse_mul_to_block_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_block_inverse_eq_zero", "description": " A lower-left subblock of the inverse of a block-triangular matrix is zero. This is a first step\ntowards `block_triangular.inv_to_block` below.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_of_upper_triangular", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_triangular.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.equiv_block_det", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_triangular", "description": " Let `b` map rows and columns of a square matrix `M` to blocks indexed by `\u03b1`s. Then\n`block_triangular M n b` says the matrix is block triangular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_of_lower_triangular", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.mk_lt_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.add_equiv_of_quotient_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.symm_comp_of_add_equiv_of_localizations_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mk'_eq_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_order_embedding", "description": "An ordered cancellative monoid injects into its localization by sending `a` to `a / b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.eq_iff_exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.away_to_away_right", "description": " Given `x y : M` and localization maps `F : M \u2192* N, G : M \u2192* P` away from `x` and `x * y`\nrespectively, the homomorphism induced from `N` to `P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.mk_zero_eq_add_monoid_of_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.add_equiv_of_add_equiv_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.sec", "description": " Given a localization map `f : M \u2192* N`, a section function sending `z : N` to some\n`(x, y) : M \u00d7 S` such that `f x * (f y)\u207b\u00b9 = z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.eq_of_eq", "description": " Given a localization map `f : M \u2192* N` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M` and a map of `comm_monoid`s\n`g : M \u2192* P` such that `g(S) \u2286 units P`, `f x = f y \u2192 g x = g y` for all `x y : M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.map_mul_right", "description": " Given localization maps `f : M \u2192* N, k : P \u2192* Q` for submonoids `S, T` respectively, if a\n`comm_monoid` homomorphism `g : M \u2192* P` induces a `f.map hy k : N \u2192* Q`, then for all `z : N`,\nwe have `f.map hy k z * k (g y) = k (g x)` where `x : M, y \u2208 S` are such that\n`z * f y = f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.add_equiv_of_localizations_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.map_map", "description": "If `add_comm_monoid` homs `g : M \u2192+ P, l : P \u2192+ A` induce maps of localizations,\nthe composition of the induced maps equals the map of localizations induced by `l \u2218 g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.add_equiv_of_add_equiv_eq_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.mk_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mk'_spec'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.mk'_eq_of_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.mk'_eq_iff_eq_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.of_add_equiv_of_localizations_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.neg_unique", "description": "Given an add_monoid hom `f : M \u2192+ N` and submonoid `S \u2286 M` such that\n`f(S) \u2286 add_units N`, for all `y \u2208 S`, `- (f y)` is unique.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mk'_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.add_equiv_of_quotient_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.lift_on", "description": "Non-dependent recursion principle for `add_localizations`: given elements `f a b : p`\nfor all `a b`, such that `r S (a, b) (c, d)` implies `f a b = f c d`,\nthen `f` is defined on the whole `localization S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.mk'_add_eq_mk'_of_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_left_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mk'_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.map_comp_map", "description": "If `add_comm_monoid` homs `g : M \u2192+ P, l : P \u2192+ A` induce maps of localizations,\nthe composition of the induced maps equals the map of localizations induced by `l \u2218 g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.away.monoid_of", "description": " Given `x : M`, the natural hom sending `y : M`, `M` a `comm_monoid`, to the equivalence class\nof `(y, 1)` in the localization of `M` at the submonoid generated by `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.to_map", "description": "Short for `to_add_monoid_hom`; used to apply a localization map as a function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.eq_mk'_iff_add_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.sec_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mul_equiv_of_quotient_symm_monoid_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.is_unit_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.lift_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.of_mul_equiv_of_dom_id", "description": "A special case of `f \u2218 id = f`, `f` a localization map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.map_units", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.mk'_self'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mk'_eq_iff_mk'_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.lift_mul_right", "description": " Given a localization map `f : M \u2192* N` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M`, if a `comm_monoid` map\n`g : M \u2192* P` induces a map `f.lift hg : N \u2192* P` then for all `z : N`, we have\n`f.lift hg z * g y = g x`, where `x : M, y \u2208 S` are such that `z * f y = f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.r_iff_exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.one", "description": "The identity element of a localization is defined as `\u27e81, 1\u27e9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mk'_self'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.of_add_equiv_of_dom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_with_zero_map.lift", "description": " Given a localization map `f : M \u2192*\u2080 N` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M` and a map of\n`comm_monoid_with_zero`s `g : M \u2192*\u2080 P` such that `g y` is invertible for all `y : S`, the\nhomomorphism induced from `N` to `P` sending `z : N` to `g x * (g y)\u207b\u00b9`, where `(x, y) : M \u00d7 S`\nare such that `z = f x * (f y)\u207b\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.mk'_sec", "description": "Given a localization map `f : M \u2192+ N` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M`, for all `z : N`\nwe have that if `x : M, y \u2208 S` are such that `z + f y = f x`, then `f x - f y = z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mul_equiv_of_localizations_left_inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.r'", "description": "An alternate form of the congruence relation on `M \u00d7 S`, `M` a `comm_monoid` and\n`S` a submonoid of `M`, whose quotient is the localization of `M` at `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.lift", "description": " Given a localization map `f : M \u2192* N` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M` and a map of `comm_monoid`s\n`g : M \u2192* P` such that `g y` is invertible for all `y : S`, the homomorphism induced from\n`N` to `P` sending `z : N` to `g x * (g y)\u207b\u00b9`, where `(x, y) : M \u00d7 S` are such that\n`z = f x * (f y)\u207b\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.of_mul_equiv_of_dom_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.has_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mul_inv_right", "description": " Given a monoid hom `f : M \u2192* N` and submonoid `S \u2286 M` such that `f(S) \u2286 N\u02e3`, for all\n`w : M, z : N` and `y \u2208 S`, we have `z = w * (f y)\u207b\u00b9 \u2194 z * f y = w`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.lift_on\u2082_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.mk_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.lift_left_inverse", "description": "Given two localization maps `f : M \u2192+ N, k : M \u2192+ P` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M`,\nthe hom from `P` to `N` induced by `f` is left inverse to the hom from `N` to `P`\ninduced by `k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.add_neg", "description": "Given an add_monoid hom `f : M \u2192+ N` and submonoid `S \u2286 M` such that\n`f(S) \u2286 add_units N`, for all `x\u2081 x\u2082 : M` and `y\u2081, y\u2082 \u2208 S`, we have\n`f x\u2081 - f y\u2081 = f x\u2082 - f y\u2082 \u2194 f (x\u2081 + y\u2082) = f (x\u2082 + y\u2081)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mul", "description": "Multiplication in a localization is defined as `\u27e8a, b\u27e9 * \u27e8c, d\u27e9 = \u27e8a * c, b * d\u27e9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.map_add_left", "description": "Given localization maps `f : M \u2192+ N, k : P \u2192+ Q` for submonoids `S, T` respectively,\nif an `add_comm_monoid` homomorphism `g : M \u2192+ P` induces a `f.map hy k : N \u2192+ Q`, then for all\n`z : N`, we have `k (g y) + f.map hy k z = k (g x)` where `x : M, y \u2208 S` are such that\n`z + f y = f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.map", "description": "Given a `add_comm_monoid` homomorphism `g : M \u2192+ P` where for submonoids\n`S \u2286 M, T \u2286 P` we have `g(S) \u2286 T`, the induced add_monoid homomorphism from the localization of `M`\nat `S` to the localization of `P` at `T`: if `f : M \u2192+ N` and `k : P \u2192+ Q` are localization maps\nfor `S` and `T` respectively, we send `z : N` to `k (g x) - k (g y)`, where `(x, y) : M \u00d7 S` are\nsuch that `z = f x - f y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.map_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_le_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization", "description": "The localization of a `comm_monoid` at one of its submonoids (as a quotient type).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.r_iff_exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.lift_left_inverse", "description": " Given two localization maps `f : M \u2192* N, k : M \u2192* P` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M`,\nthe hom from `P` to `N` induced by `f` is left inverse to the hom from `N` to `P`\ninduced by `k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.map_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_eq_monoid_of_mk'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.add_mk'_zero_eq_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.add_equiv_of_quotient_add_monoid_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.of_add_equiv_of_add_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.lift_mk'", "description": " Given a localization map `f : M \u2192* N` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M` and a map of `comm_monoid`s\n`g : M \u2192* P` such that `g y` is invertible for all `y : S`, the homomorphism induced from\n`N` to `P` maps `f x * (f y)\u207b\u00b9` to `g x * (g y)\u207b\u00b9` for all `x : M, y \u2208 S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_eq_monoid_of_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.add_equiv_of_add_equiv_eq_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.lift_injective_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.add_equiv_of_quotient_symm_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.eq_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.mk'_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.lift_on_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.mk_order_embedding", "description": "An ordered cancellative monoid injects into its localization by sending `a` to\n`a - b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.surj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.rec_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.comp_eq_of_eq", "description": " Given `comm_monoid`s `M, P`, localization maps `f : M \u2192* N, k : P \u2192* Q` for submonoids\n`S, T` respectively, and `g : M \u2192* P` such that `g(S) \u2286 T`, `f x = f y` implies\n`k (g x) = k (g y)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.is_add_unit_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.mk_order_embedding_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.add", "description": "Addition in an `add_localization` is defined as `\u27e8a, b\u27e9 + \u27e8c, d\u27e9 = \u27e8a + c, b + d\u27e9`.\n\nShould not be confused with the ring localization counterpart `localization.add`, which maps\n`\u27e8a, b\u27e9 + \u27e8c, d\u27e9` to `\u27e8d * a + b * c, b * d\u27e9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.lift_on", "description": " Non-dependent recursion principle for localizations: given elements `f a b : p`\nfor all `a b`, such that `r S (a, b) (c, d)` implies `f a b = f c d`,\nthen `f` is defined on the whole `localization S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.lift_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.of_add_equiv_of_localizations_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.away_map.lift", "description": " Given `x : A`, a localization map `F : A \u2192+ B` away from `x`, and a map of `add_comm_monoid`s\n`g : A \u2192+ C` such that `g x` is invertible, the homomorphism induced from `B` to `C` sending\n`z : B` to `g y - n \u2022 g x`, where `y : A, n : \u2115` are such that `z = F y - n \u2022 F x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.of_mul_equiv_of_localizations_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.neg_inj", "description": "Given an add_monoid hom `f : M \u2192+ N` and submonoid `S \u2286 M` such that\n`f(S) \u2286 add_units N`, for all `y, z \u2208 S`, we have `- (f y) = - (f z) \u2192 f y = f z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mk'_eq_iff_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.of_mul_equiv_of_mul_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.of_add_equiv_of_localizations_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.mk_eq_mk_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.add_neg_left", "description": "Given an add_monoid hom `f : M \u2192+ N` and submonoid `S \u2286 M` such that\n`f(S) \u2286 add_units N`, for all `w : M, z : N` and `y \u2208 S`, we have `w - f y = z \u2194 w = f y + z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.lift_spec_mul", "description": " Given a localization map `f : M \u2192* N` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M`, if a `comm_monoid` map\n`g : M \u2192* P` induces a map `f.lift hg : N \u2192* P` then for all `z : N, v w : P`, we have\n`f.lift hg z * w = v \u2194 g x * w = g y * v`, where `x : M, y \u2208 S` are such that\n`z * f y = f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.lift_on\u2082_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.add_equiv_of_localizations", "description": "If `f : M \u2192+ N` and `k : M \u2192+ R` are localization maps for a submonoid `S`,\nwe get an isomorphism of `N` and `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.of_mul_equiv_of_mul_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mul_equiv_of_localizations_left_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.of_add_equiv_of_localizations", "description": "If `f : M \u2192+ N` is a localization map for a submonoid `S` and `k : N \u2243+ P` is an\nisomorphism of `add_comm_monoid`s, `k \u2218 f` is a localization map for `M` at `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.decidable_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.lift_on_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.of_mul_equiv_of_localizations_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.smul", "description": "Scalar multiplication in a monoid localization is defined as `c \u2022 \u27e8a, b\u27e9 = \u27e8c \u2022 a, b\u27e9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mk'_mul_eq_mk'_of_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.comp_eq_of_eq", "description": "Given `add_comm_monoid`s `M, P`, localization maps `f : M \u2192+ N, k : P \u2192+ Q` for\nsubmonoids `S, T` respectively, and `g : M \u2192+ P` such that `g(S) \u2286 T`, `f x = f y`\nimplies `k (g x) = k (g y)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.mk'_eq_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.has_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.lift_add_right", "description": "Given a localization map `f : M \u2192+ N` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M`, if\nan `add_comm_monoid` map `g : M \u2192+ P` induces a map `f.lift hg : N \u2192+ P` then for all `z : N`, we\nhave `f.lift hg z + g y = g x`, where `x : M, y \u2208 S` are such that `z + f y = f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mul_equiv_of_quotient_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map", "description": " The type of add_monoid homomorphisms satisfying the characteristic predicate: if `f : M \u2192+ N`\nsatisfies this predicate, then `N` is isomorphic to the localization of `M` at `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.to_add_monoid_hom", "description": " The type of add_monoid homomorphisms satisfying the characteristic predicate: if `f : M \u2192+ N`\nsatisfies this predicate, then `N` is isomorphic to the localization of `M` at `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.map_add_units'", "description": " The type of add_monoid homomorphisms satisfying the characteristic predicate: if `f : M \u2192+ N`\nsatisfies this predicate, then `N` is isomorphic to the localization of `M` at `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.surj'", "description": " The type of add_monoid homomorphisms satisfying the characteristic predicate: if `f : M \u2192+ N`\nsatisfies this predicate, then `N` is isomorphic to the localization of `M` at `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.eq_iff_exists'", "description": " The type of add_monoid homomorphisms satisfying the characteristic predicate: if `f : M \u2192+ N`\nsatisfies this predicate, then `N` is isomorphic to the localization of `M` at `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.rec", "description": " Dependent recursion principle for localizations: given elements `f a b : p (mk a b)`\nfor all `a b`, such that `r S (a, b) (c, d)` implies `f a b = f c d` (with the correct coercions),\nthen `f` is defined on the whole `localization S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mul_equiv_of_mul_equiv_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.away_map.lift_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.of_add_equiv_of_dom_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.of_add_equiv_of_dom_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.surj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.decidable_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.monoid_of", "description": " Natural hom sending `x : M`, `M` a `comm_monoid`, to the equivalence class of\n`(x, 1)` in the localization of `M` at a submonoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.mk'", "description": "Given a localization map `f : M \u2192+ N`, the surjection sending `(x, y) : M \u00d7 S`\nto `f x - f y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mul_equiv_of_localizations_right_inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mul_equiv_of_quotient_symm_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.lift_mk'_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.away", "description": "Given `x : M`, the localization of `M` at the submonoid generated\nby `x`, as a quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.smul_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.map_left_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.away_map", "description": " Given `x : M`, the type of `comm_monoid` homomorphisms `f : M \u2192* N` such that `N`\nis isomorphic to the localization of `M` at the submonoid generated by `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.rec_on_subsingleton\u2082", "description": "Copy of `quotient.rec_on_subsingleton\u2082` for `localization`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.sec_spec'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.r", "description": "The congruence relation on `M \u00d7 S`, `M` an `add_comm_monoid` and `S`\nan `add_submonoid` of `M`, whose quotient is the localization of `M` at `S`, defined as the unique\ncongruence relation on `M \u00d7 S` such that for any other congruence relation `s` on `M \u00d7 S` where\nfor all `y \u2208 S`, `(0, 0) \u223c (y, y)` under `s`, we have that `(x\u2081, y\u2081) \u223c (x\u2082, y\u2082)` by `r` implies\n`(x\u2081, y\u2081) \u223c (x\u2082, y\u2082)` by `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.away.mk_eq_add_monoid_of_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.of_add_equiv_of_dom_comp_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.of_mul_equiv_of_dom_comp_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.of_mul_equiv_of_dom_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.induction_on\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.add_equiv_of_localizations_right_inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mk'_eq_of_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.mk_eq_add_monoid_of_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mk'", "description": " Given a localization map `f : M \u2192* N`, the surjection sending `(x, y) : M \u00d7 S` to\n`f x * (f y)\u207b\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.away_to_away_right", "description": " Given `x y : A` and localization maps `F : A \u2192+ B, G : A \u2192+ C` away from `x` and `x + y`\nrespectively, the homomorphism induced from `B` to `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.lift_on\u2082_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.lift_injective_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.of_add_equiv_of_dom", "description": "Given `comm_monoid`s `M, P` and submonoids `S \u2286 M, T \u2286 P`, if `f : M \u2192* N` is\na localization map for `S` and `k : P \u2243* M` is an isomorphism of `comm_monoid`s such that\n`k(T) = S`, `f \u2218 k` is a localization map for `T`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mul_mk'_one_eq_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mul_equiv_of_quotient_symm_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.comm_monoid_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.one_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.of_mul_equiv_of_dom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.map_spec", "description": "Given localization maps `f : M \u2192+ N, k : P \u2192+ Q` for submonoids `S, T` respectively,\nif an `add_comm_monoid` homomorphism `g : M \u2192+ P` induces a `f.map hy k : N \u2192+ Q`, then for all\n`z : N`, `u : Q`, we have `f.map hy k z = u \u2194 k (g x) = k (g y) + u` where `x : M, y \u2208 S` are such\nthat `z + f y = f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.inv_inj", "description": " Given a monoid hom `f : M \u2192* N` and submonoid `S \u2286 M` such that `f(S) \u2286 N\u02e3`, for all\n`y, z \u2208 S`, we have `(f y)\u207b\u00b9 = (f z)\u207b\u00b9 \u2192 f y = f z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.eq_of_eq", "description": "Given a localization map `f : M \u2192+ N` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M` and a map\nof `add_comm_monoid`s `g : M \u2192+ P` such that `g(S) \u2286 add_units P`, `f x = f y \u2192 g x = g y`\nfor all `x y : M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.away.add_monoid_of", "description": "Given `x : M`, the natural hom sending `y : M`, `M` an `add_comm_monoid`,\nto the equivalence class of `(y, 0)` in the localization of `M` at the submonoid\ngenerated by `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.lift_add_left", "description": "Given a localization map `f : M \u2192+ N` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M`, if\nan `add_comm_monoid` map `g : M \u2192+ P` induces a map `f.lift hg : N \u2192+ P` then for all `z : N`, we\nhave `g y + f.lift hg z = g x`, where `x : M, y \u2208 S` are such that `z + f y = f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.of_add_equiv_of_add_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.map_left_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.lift_mul_left", "description": " Given a localization map `f : M \u2192* N` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M`, if a `comm_monoid` map\n`g : M \u2192* P` induces a map `f.lift hg : N \u2192* P` then for all `z : N`, we have\n`g y * f.lift hg z = g x`, where `x : M, y \u2208 S` are such that `z * f y = f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.add_equiv_of_localizations_left_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.away.inv_self", "description": " Given `x : M`, `inv_self` is `x\u207b\u00b9` in the localization (as a quotient type) of `M` at the\nsubmonoid generated by `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.eq_mk'_iff_mul_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.r_of_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.symm_comp_of_mul_equiv_of_localizations_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.r_eq_r'", "description": " The congruence relation used to localize a `comm_monoid` at a submonoid can be expressed\nequivalently as an infimum (see `localization.r`) or explicitly\n(see `localization.r'`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.mk'_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.rec_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.mk'_eq_of_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.r_eq_r'", "description": "The additive congruence relation used to localize an `add_comm_monoid` at a\nsubmonoid can be expressed equivalently as an infimum (see `add_localization.r`) or\nexplicitly (see `add_localization.r'`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.mk'_add_cancel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.linear_ordered_cancel_add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mk'_mul_cancel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mul_equiv_of_mul_equiv_eq_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.lift", "description": "Given a localization map `f : M \u2192+ N` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M` and a map\nof `add_comm_monoid`s `g : M \u2192+ P` such that `g y` is invertible for all `y : S`, the homomorphism\ninduced from `N` to `P` sending `z : N` to `g x - g y`, where `(x, y) : M \u00d7 S` are such that\n`z = f x - f y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.of_add_equiv_of_localizations_eq_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.map_map", "description": " If `comm_monoid` homs `g : M \u2192* P, l : P \u2192* A` induce maps of localizations, the composition\nof the induced maps equals the map of localizations induced by `l \u2218 g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.map_comp_map", "description": " If `comm_monoid` homs `g : M \u2192* P, l : P \u2192* A` induce maps of localizations, the composition\nof the induced maps equals the map of localizations induced by `l \u2218 g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.has_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.add_equiv_of_add_equiv_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.decidable_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mul_equiv_of_mul_equiv", "description": " Given localization maps `f : M \u2192* N, k : P \u2192* U` for submonoids `S, T` respectively, an\nisomorphism `j : M \u2243* P` such that `j(S) = T` induces an isomorphism of localizations\n`N \u2243* U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.to_map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mk'_eq_iff_eq_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.away_map.lift_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_eq_mk_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mul_equiv_of_localizations_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.away_map.lift", "description": " Given `x : M`, a localization map `F : M \u2192* N` away from `x`, and a map of `comm_monoid`s\n`g : M \u2192* P` such that `g x` is invertible, the homomorphism induced from `N` to `P` sending\n`z : N` to `g y * (g x)\u207b\u207f`, where `y : M, n : \u2115` are such that `z = F y * (F x)\u207b\u207f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.to_map", "description": "Short for `to_monoid_hom`; used to apply a localization map as a function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.lift_surjective_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.mk'_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.of_mul_equiv_of_dom", "description": " Given `comm_monoid`s `M, P` and submonoids `S \u2286 M, T \u2286 P`, if `f : M \u2192* N` is a localization\nmap for `S` and `k : P \u2243* M` is an isomorphism of `comm_monoid`s such that `k(T) = S`, `f \u2218 k`\nis a localization map for `T`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.map_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.map_right_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.away_map", "description": "Given `x : M`, the type of `add_comm_monoid` homomorphisms `f : M \u2192+ N`\nsuch that `N` is isomorphic to the localization of `M` at the submonoid generated by `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.away.mul_equiv_of_quotient", "description": " Given `x : M` and a localization map `f : M \u2192* N` away from `x`, we get an isomorphism between\nthe localization of `M` at the submonoid generated by `x` as a quotient type and `N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.away", "description": "Given `x : M`, the localization of `M` at the submonoid generated by `x`, as a quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.map_add_units", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_with_zero_map.to_monoid_with_zero_hom", "description": "The monoid with zero hom underlying a `localization_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.mk'_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mk'_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.add_neg_right", "description": "Given an add_monoid hom `f : M \u2192+ N` and submonoid `S \u2286 M` such that\n`f(S) \u2286 add_units N`, for all `w : M, z : N` and `y \u2208 S`, we have `z = w - f y \u2194 z + f y = w`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mk'_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.lift_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.lift_mk'_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.sec_zero_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.exists_of_sec_mk'", "description": "Given a localization map `f : M \u2192+ N` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M`, for all `x\u2081 : M`\nand `y\u2081 \u2208 S`, if `x\u2082 : M, y\u2082 \u2208 S` are such that `(f x\u2081 - f y\u2081) + f y\u2082 = f x\u2082`, then there exists\n`c \u2208 S` such that `x\u2081 + y\u2082 + c = x\u2082 + y\u2081 + c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.r'", "description": " An alternate form of the congruence relation on `M \u00d7 S`, `M` a `comm_monoid` and `S` a\nsubmonoid of `M`, whose quotient is the localization of `M` at `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.is_scalar_tower_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_with_zero_map", "description": " The type of homomorphisms between monoids with zero satisfying the characteristic predicate:\nif `f : M \u2192*\u2080 N` satisfies this predicate, then `N` is isomorphic to the localization of `M` at\n`S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_with_zero_map.to_localization_map", "description": " The type of homomorphisms between monoids with zero satisfying the characteristic predicate:\nif `f : M \u2192*\u2080 N` satisfies this predicate, then `N` is isomorphic to the localization of `M` at\n`S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_with_zero_map.map_zero'", "description": " The type of homomorphisms between monoids with zero satisfying the characteristic predicate:\nif `f : M \u2192*\u2080 N` satisfies this predicate, then `N` is isomorphic to the localization of `M` at\n`S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.add_equiv_of_localizations_symm_eq_add_equiv_of_localizations", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.zero_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.sec", "description": "Given a localization map `f : M \u2192+ N`, a section function sending `z : N`\nto some `(x, y) : M \u00d7 S` such that `f x - f y = z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.npow", "description": " Exponentiation in a localization is defined as `\u27e8a, b\u27e9 ^ n = \u27e8a ^ n, b ^ n\u27e9`.\n\nThis is a separate `irreducible` def to ensure the elaborator doesn't waste its time\ntrying to unify some huge recursive definition with itself, but unfolded one step less.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.add_equiv_of_quotient_symm_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.lift_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.induction_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.lift_on_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.lift_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization", "description": "The localization of an `add_comm_monoid` at one\nof its submonoids (as a quotient type).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.smul_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.decidable_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.lift_on\u2082_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.mk'_add_cancel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.add_equiv_of_add_equiv", "description": "Given localization maps `f : M \u2192+ N, k : P \u2192+ U` for submonoids `S, T` respectively,\nan isomorphism `j : M \u2243+ P` such that `j(S) = T` induces an isomorphism of\nlocalizations `N \u2243+ U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.of_add_equiv_of_dom_id", "description": "A special case of `f \u2218 id = f`, `f` a localization map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.of_add_equiv_of_localizations_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.lift_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mk'_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mul_distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.lift_mk'", "description": "Given a localization map `f : M \u2192+ N` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M` and a map\nof `add_comm_monoid`s `g : M \u2192+ P` such that `g y` is invertible for all `y : S`, the homomorphism\ninduced from `N` to `P` maps `f x - f y` to `g x - g y` for all `x : M, y \u2208 S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mk'_eq_of_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.induction_on\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.inv_unique", "description": " Given a monoid hom `f : M \u2192* N` and submonoid `S \u2286 M` such that `f(S) \u2286 N\u02e3`, for all\n`y \u2208 S`, `(f y)\u207b\u00b9` is unique.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.of_mul_equiv_of_localizations_eq_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.zero", "description": " The zero element in a localization is defined as `(0, 1)`.\n\nShould not be confused with `add_localization.zero` which is `(0, 0)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.symm_comp_of_mul_equiv_of_localizations_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mul_equiv_of_localizations_right_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.mk'_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.map_right_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mul_equiv_of_localizations", "description": " If `f : M \u2192* N` and `k : M \u2192* P` are localization maps for a submonoid `S`, we get an\nisomorphism of `N` and `P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.lift_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mul_equiv_of_localizations_symm_eq_mul_equiv_of_localizations", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.lift_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.induction_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mul_inv", "description": " Given a monoid hom `f : M \u2192* N` and submonoid `S \u2286 M` such that\n`f(S) \u2286 N\u02e3`, for all `x\u2081 x\u2082 : M` and `y\u2081, y\u2082 \u2208 S`, we have\n`f x\u2081 * (f y\u2081)\u207b\u00b9 = f x\u2082 * (f y\u2082)\u207b\u00b9 \u2194 f (x\u2081 * y\u2082) = f (x\u2082 * y\u2081)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.add_monoid_of", "description": "Natural homomorphism sending `x : M`, `M` an `add_comm_monoid`, to the equivalence\nclass of `(x, 0)` in the localization of `M` at a submonoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_eq_mk_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.epic_of_localization_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.add_equiv_of_localizations_left_neg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.mk'_eq_iff_mk'_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.lift_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.lift_surjective_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.is_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk", "description": " Given a `comm_monoid` `M` and submonoid `S`, `mk` sends `x : M`, `y \u2208 S` to the equivalence\nclass of `(x, y)` in the localization of `M` at `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mul_equiv_of_mul_equiv_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.mk'_eq_iff_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.lift_on\u2082", "description": "Non-dependent recursion principle for localizations: given elements `f x y : p`\nfor all `x` and `y`, such that `r S x x'` and `r S y y'` implies `f x y = f x' y'`,\nthen `f` is defined on the whole `localization S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.induction_on\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.away.mk_eq_monoid_of_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.nsmul", "description": "Multiplication with a natural in an `add_localization` is defined as `n \u2022 \u27e8a, b\u27e9 = \u27e8n \u2022 a, n \u2022 b\u27e9`.\n\nThis is a separate `irreducible` def to ensure the elaborator doesn't waste its time\ntrying to unify some huge recursive definition with itself, but unfolded one step less.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.map_spec", "description": " Given localization maps `f : M \u2192* N, k : P \u2192* Q` for submonoids `S, T` respectively, if a\n`comm_monoid` homomorphism `g : M \u2192* P` induces a `f.map hy k : N \u2192* Q`, then for all `z : N`,\n`u : Q`, we have `f.map hy k z = u \u2194 k (g x) = k (g y) * u` where `x : M, y \u2208 S` are such that\n`z * f y = f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_one_eq_monoid_of_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mul_mk'_eq_mk'_of_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mk'_mul_cancel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.epic_of_localization_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.exists_of_sec_mk'", "description": " Given a localization map `f : M \u2192* N` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M`, for all `x\u2081 : M` and `y\u2081 \u2208 S`,\nif `x\u2082 : M, y\u2082 \u2208 S` are such that `f x\u2081 * (f y\u2081)\u207b\u00b9 * f y\u2082 = f x\u2082`, then there exists `c \u2208 S`\nsuch that `x\u2081 * y\u2082 * c = x\u2082 * y\u2081 * c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.away_map.lift_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.mk_eq_mk_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.lift_spec", "description": " Given a localization map `f : M \u2192* N` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M`, if a `comm_monoid` map\n`g : M \u2192* P` induces a map `f.lift hg : N \u2192* P` then for all `z : N, v : P`, we have\n`f.lift hg z = v \u2194 g x = g y * v`, where `x : M, y \u2208 S` are such that `z * f y = f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.lift_on\u2082", "description": " Non-dependent recursion principle for localizations: given elements `f x y : p`\nfor all `x` and `y`, such that `r S x x'` and `r S y y'` implies `f x y = f x' y'`,\nthen `f` is defined on the whole `localization S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.lift_on_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mk'_sec", "description": " Given a localization map `f : M \u2192* N` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M`, for all `z : N` we have that if\n`x : M, y \u2208 S` are such that `z * f y = f x`, then `f x * (f y)\u207b\u00b9 = z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.ind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.map_add_right", "description": "Given localization maps `f : M \u2192+ N, k : P \u2192+ Q` for submonoids `S, T` respectively,\nif an `add_comm_monoid` homomorphism `g : M \u2192+ P` induces a `f.map hy k : N \u2192+ Q`, then\nfor all `z : N`, we have `f.map hy k z + k (g y) = k (g x)` where `x : M, y \u2208 S` are such that\n`z + f y = f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.lift_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_order_embedding_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.eq_iff_exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.add_equiv_of_quotient", "description": "Given a localization map `f : M \u2192+ N` for a submonoid `S`, we get an isomorphism\nbetween the localization of `M` at `S` as a quotient type and `N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.lift_of_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mk_lt_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.away.neg_self", "description": "Given `x : M`, `neg_self` is `-x` in the localization (as a quotient type) of `M`\nat the submonoid generated by `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.rec", "description": "Dependent recursion principle for `add_localization`s: given elements `f a b : p (mk a b)`\nfor all `a b`, such that `r S (a, b) (c, d)` implies `f a b = f c d` (with the correct coercions),\nthen `f` is defined on the whole `add_localization S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.symm_comp_of_add_equiv_of_localizations_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mul_equiv_of_localizations_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mul_equiv_of_quotient_monoid_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.away.add_equiv_of_quotient", "description": "Given `x : M` and a localization map `f : M \u2192+ N` away from `x`, we get an\nisomorphism between the localization of `M` at the submonoid generated by `x` as a quotient type\nand `N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.map_mul_left", "description": " Given localization maps `f : M \u2192* N, k : P \u2192* Q` for submonoids `S, T` respectively, if a\n`comm_monoid` homomorphism `g : M \u2192* P` induces a `f.map hy k : N \u2192* Q`, then for all `z : N`,\nwe have `k (g y) * f.map hy k z = k (g x)` where `x : M, y \u2208 S` are such that\n`z * f y = f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.mk_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.add_equiv_of_localizations_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.lift_spec_add", "description": "Given a localization map `f : M \u2192+ N` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M`, if\nan `add_comm_monoid` map `g : M \u2192+ P` induces a map `f.lift hg : N \u2192+ P` then for all\n`z : N, v w : P`, we have `f.lift hg z + w = v \u2194 g x + w = g y + v`, where `x : M, y \u2208 S` are such\nthat `z + f y = f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.lift_spec", "description": "Given a localization map `f : M \u2192+ N` for a submonoid `S \u2286 M`, if\nan `add_comm_monoid` map `g : M \u2192+ P` induces a map `f.lift hg : N \u2192+ P` then for all\n`z : N, v : P`, we have `f.lift hg z = v \u2194 g x = g y + v`, where `x : M, y \u2208 S` are such that\n`z + f y = f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.ordered_cancel_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.mk_le_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.sec_spec'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mul_equiv_of_mul_equiv_eq_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.mk_eq_add_monoid_of_mk'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.of_mul_equiv_of_localizations_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.eq_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.add_equiv_of_quotient_symm_add_monoid_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mul_equiv_of_quotient_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.add_equiv_of_localizations_right_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.ordered_cancel_add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.induction_on\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.zero", "description": "The identity element of an `add_localization` is defined as `\u27e80, 0\u27e9`.\n\nShould not be confused with the ring localization counterpart `localization.zero`,\nwhich is defined as `\u27e80, 1\u27e9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.sec_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.mk_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.mk_left_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.away_map.lift_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.r", "description": " The congruence relation on `M \u00d7 S`, `M` a `comm_monoid` and `S` a submonoid of `M`, whose\nquotient is the localization of `M` at `S`, defined as the unique congruence relation on\n`M \u00d7 S` such that for any other congruence relation `s` on `M \u00d7 S` where for all `y \u2208 S`,\n`(1, 1) \u223c (y, y)` under `s`, we have that `(x\u2081, y\u2081) \u223c (x\u2082, y\u2082)` by `r` implies\n`(x\u2081, y\u2081) \u223c (x\u2082, y\u2082)` by `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map", "description": " The type of monoid homomorphisms satisfying the characteristic predicate: if `f : M \u2192* N`\nsatisfies this predicate, then `N` is isomorphic to the localization of `M` at `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.to_monoid_hom", "description": " The type of monoid homomorphisms satisfying the characteristic predicate: if `f : M \u2192* N`\nsatisfies this predicate, then `N` is isomorphic to the localization of `M` at `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.map_units'", "description": " The type of monoid homomorphisms satisfying the characteristic predicate: if `f : M \u2192* N`\nsatisfies this predicate, then `N` is isomorphic to the localization of `M` at `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.surj'", "description": " The type of monoid homomorphisms satisfying the characteristic predicate: if `f : M \u2192* N`\nsatisfies this predicate, then `N` is isomorphic to the localization of `M` at `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.eq_iff_exists'", "description": " The type of monoid homomorphisms satisfying the characteristic predicate: if `f : M \u2192* N`\nsatisfies this predicate, then `N` is isomorphic to the localization of `M` at `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.away_map.inv_self", "description": "Given `x : M` and a localization map `F : M \u2192* N` away from `x`, `inv_self` is `(F x)\u207b\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.add_equiv_of_quotient_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_localization_map", "description": "Makes a localization map from an `add_comm_monoid` hom satisfying the characteristic\npredicate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.of_mul_equiv_of_localizations", "description": " If `f : M \u2192* N` is a localization map for a submonoid `S` and `k : N \u2243* P` is an isomorphism\nof `comm_monoid`s, `k \u2218 f` is a localization map for `M` at `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.map_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.mk'_spec'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.smul_comm_class_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.lift_on_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.mul_inv_left", "description": " Given a monoid hom `f : M \u2192* N` and submonoid `S \u2286 M` such that `f(S) \u2286 N\u02e3`, for all\n`w : M, z : N` and `y \u2208 S`, we have `w * (f y)\u207b\u00b9 = z \u2194 w = f y * z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mul_equiv_of_quotient_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.has_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.lift_of_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.to_map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.add_mk'_eq_mk'_of_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.rec_on_subsingleton\u2082", "description": "Copy of `quotient.rec_on_subsingleton\u2082` for `add_localization`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.ind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.mul_equiv_of_quotient", "description": " Given a localization map `f : M \u2192* N` for a submonoid `S`, we get an isomorphism between\nthe localization of `M` at `S` as a quotient type and `N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.of_mul_equiv_of_localizations_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.localization_map.away_map.neg_self", "description": "Given `x : A` and a localization map `F : A \u2192+ B` away from `x`, `neg_self` is `- (F x)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.mk", "description": "Given an `add_comm_monoid` `M` and submonoid `S`, `mk` sends `x : M`, `y \u2208 S` to\nthe equivalence class of `(x, y)` in the localization of `M` at `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_localization.r_of_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.linear_ordered_cancel_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.localization_map.map", "description": " Given a `comm_monoid` homomorphism `g : M \u2192* P` where for submonoids `S \u2286 M, T \u2286 P` we have\n`g(S) \u2286 T`, the induced monoid homomorphism from the localization of `M` at `S` to the\nlocalization of `P` at `T`: if `f : M \u2192* N` and `k : P \u2192* Q` are localization maps for `S` and\n`T` respectively, we send `z : N` to `k (g x) * (k (g y))\u207b\u00b9`, where `(x, y) : M \u00d7 S` are such\nthat `z = f x * (f y)\u207b\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.to_localization_map", "description": "Makes a localization map from a `comm_monoid` hom satisfying the characteristic predicate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "neg_of_mul_pos_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_le_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lt_mul_of_le_of_one_lt'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pos_mul_mono_rev.to_pos_mul_reflect_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_pos_reflect_lt.to_mul_pos_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pos_mul_reflect_lt.to_pos_mul_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right.one_lt_mul_of_lt_of_lt", "description": "Assumes right covariance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right.neg_of_mul_neg_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_nonpos_of_nonpos_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pos_mul_reflect_lt.to_pos_mul_mono_rev", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_lt_of_le_of_lt_one'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_le_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right.mul_nonneg", "description": "Assumes right covariance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_lt_mul_of_pos_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_le_iff_le_one_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"n