ription": " If `F` is left adjoint to `G`, then the category of algebras over `F` is equivalent to the\ncategory of coalgebras over `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.endofunctor.algebra.id_eq_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.endofunctor.adjunction.coalgebra.to_algebra_of", "description": " Given an adjunction `F \u22a3 G`, the functor that associates to a coalgebra over `G` an algebra over\n`F` defined via adjunction applied to the structure map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.endofunctor.algebra.initial.right_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.endofunctor.algebra.equiv_of_nat_iso_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.endofunctor.adjunction.coalgebra.hom_equiv_naturality_str_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.endofunctor.coalgebra.comp_eq_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.endofunctor.coalgebra.functor_of_nat_trans_id_hom_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.endofunctor.algebra.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.endofunctor.adjunction.alg_coalg_equiv.counit_iso", "description": " Given an adjunction, assigning to a coalgebra over the right adjoint an algebra over the left\nadjoint and going back is isomorphic to the identity functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.endofunctor.algebra.functor_of_nat_trans_eq_hom_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.endofunctor.coalgebra.forget", "description": "The forgetful functor from the category of coalgebras, forgetting the coalgebraic structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.endofunctor.algebra.functor_of_nat_trans_obj_A", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.endofunctor.algebra.functor_of_nat_trans_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.endofunctor.algebra.forget_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.endofunctor.coalgebra.id_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.endofunctor.algebra.functor_of_nat_trans_id_hom_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.endofunctor.algebra.functor_of_nat_trans_eq_inv_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.endofunctor.coalgebra.iso_mk_inv_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.add_eq_mul_one_add_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.has_neg", "description": "Each element of the group of units of a ring has an additive inverse.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.divp_add_divp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.divp_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.has_distrib_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.divp_sub_divp_same", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.add_divp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.coe_neg_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.divp_sub_divp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.neg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.neg_divp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.divp_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.sub_divp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.sub_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.divp_add_divp_same", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.coe_neg", "description": "Representing an element of a ring's unit group as an element of the ring commutes with\n   mapping this element to its additive inverse.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.inv_rotate_map_hom\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.inv_rotate_obj\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.rotate.category_theory.is_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.rotate_mor\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.inv_rotate_obj\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.rot_comp_inv_rot_hom_app_hom\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.inv_rot_comp_rot_inv_app_hom\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.rotate_obj\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.inv_rotate_map_hom\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.rotate_map_hom\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.rotate", "description": "If you rotate a triangle, you get another triangle.\nGiven a triangle of the form:\n```lean\n      f       g       h\n  X  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Y  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Z  \u2500\u2500\u2500> X\u27e61\u27e7\n```\napplying `rotate` gives a triangle of the form:\n```lean\n      g       h        -f\u27e61\u27e7'\n  Y  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Z  \u2500\u2500\u2500>  X\u27e61\u27e7 \u2500\u2500\u2500> Y\u27e61\u27e7\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.rotate_map_hom\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.inv_rotate_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.rotate_obj\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.inv_rot_comp_rot_hom_app_hom\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_rotation_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.inv_rotate", "description": "Given a triangle of the form:\n```lean\n      f       g       h\n  X  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Y  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Z  \u2500\u2500\u2500> X\u27e61\u27e7\n```\napplying `inv_rotate` gives a triangle that can be thought of as:\n```lean\n        -h\u27e6-1\u27e7'     f       g\n  Z\u27e6-1\u27e7  \u2500\u2500\u2500>  X  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Y  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Z\n```\n(note that this diagram doesn't technically fit the definition of triangle, as `Z\u27e6-1\u27e7\u27e61\u27e7` is\nnot necessarily equal to `Z`, but it is isomorphic, by the `counit_iso` of `shift C`)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_rotation_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_rotation", "description": "Rotating triangles gives an auto-equivalence on the category of triangles in `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.rotate_map_hom\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.rot_comp_inv_rot_inv_app_hom\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.rot_comp_inv_rot_hom_app_hom\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.inv_rotate_mor\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_rotation_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.inv_rot_comp_rot_inv_app_hom\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.rotate_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.inv_rot_comp_rot_inv_app_hom\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.inv_rotate_mor\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.inv_rot_comp_rot_hom_app_hom\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.inv_rot_comp_rot_hom_app_hom\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.inv_rotate_mor\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.inv_rotate_map_hom\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.inv_rotate.category_theory.is_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.inv_rot_comp_rot", "description": " The counit isomorphism of the auto-equivalence of categories `triangle_rotation C` of\n`triangle C` given by the rotation of triangles.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.rot_comp_inv_rot_hom_app_hom\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.inv_rotate_obj\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.rot_comp_inv_rot_inv_app_hom\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.rot_comp_inv_rot", "description": " The unit isomorphism of the auto-equivalence of categories `triangle_rotation C` of\n`triangle C` given by the rotation of triangles.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.rotate_mor\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.rot_comp_inv_rot_inv_app_hom\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.rotate_obj\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.rotate", "description": "Rotating triangles gives an endofunctor on the category of triangles in `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_rotation_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.inv_rotate", "description": "The inverse rotation of triangles gives an endofunctor on the category of triangles in `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.rotate_mor\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_id_set_eq_sUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_eq_Sup_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup'_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_product_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.infi_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.of_dual_sup'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.set_bInter_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.min_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.induction_on_min_value", "description": " Induction principle for `finset`s in any type from which a given function `f` maps to a linearly\nordered type : a predicate is true on all `s : finset \u03b1` provided that:\n\n* it is true on the empty `finset`,\n* for every `s : finset \u03b1` and an element `a` such that for elements of `s` denoted by `x` we have\n  `f a \u2264 f x`, `p s` implies `p (insert a s)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_sup'_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.is_glb_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.exists_mem_eq_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_inf_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup'_mul_le_mul_sup'_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.coe_inf'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup", "description": "Supremum of a finite set: `sup {a, b, c} f = f a \u2294 f b \u2294 f c`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.exists_next_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.set_bUnion_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.min'_eq_inf'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mem_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf'_induction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.min_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.min_le_of_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.lt_sup_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.max_erase_ne_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf'_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf'_sup_inf'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_min'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup'_product_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infi_eq_infi_finset", "description": " Infimum of `s i`, `i : \u03b9`, is equal to the infimum over `t : finset \u03b9` of infima\n`\u2a05 i \u2208 t, s i`. This version assumes `\u03b9` is a `Type*`. See `infi_eq_infi_finset'` for a version\nthat works for `\u03b9 : Sort*`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_attach", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_bUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.min'_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.set_bInter_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_le_diff_of_interleaved", "description": "If finsets `s` and `t` are interleaved, then `finset.card s \u2264 finset.card (t \\ s) + 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.supr_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf'_lt_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_product_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.exists_nat_subset_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.disjoint_sup_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.max'_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.max_mem_image_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup'_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.count_finset_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup'_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf'_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_lt_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup'_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.max_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup'_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_le", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `finset.sup_le_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_attach", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.induction_on_max", "description": " Induction principle for `finset`s in a linearly ordered type: a predicate is true on all\n`s : finset \u03b1` provided that:\n\n* it is true on the empty `finset`,\n* for every `s : finset \u03b1` and an element `a` strictly greater than all elements of `s`, `p s`\n  implies `p (insert a s)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.infi_insert_update", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.is_glb_iff_is_least", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf'_le_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_eq_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.supr_option_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_himp_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.max'", "description": " Given a nonempty finset `s` in a linear order `\u03b1`, then `s.max' h` is its maximum, as an\nelement of `\u03b1`, where `h` is a proof of nonemptiness. Without this assumption, use instead `s.max`,\ntaking values in `with_bot \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.min_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.infi_bUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.min'", "description": " Given a nonempty finset `s` in a linear order `\u03b1`, then `s.min' h` is its minimum, as an\nelement of `\u03b1`, where `h` is a proof of nonemptiness. Without this assumption, use instead `s.min`,\ntaking values in `with_top \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.min'_erase_ne_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_sdiff_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf'_sup_distrib_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.max_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.supr_bUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.lt_inf_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.exists_min_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup'_eq_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.to_dual_sup'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.max'_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_mono_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.max'_eq_sup'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.foldr_sup_eq_sup_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf'_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf'_product_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_closed_of_inf_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.of_dual_min'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_const_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.max'_lt_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.exists_mem_eq_sup'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.supr_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.coe_inf_of_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf'_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.comp_sup'_eq_sup'_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.foldr_inf_eq_inf_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.max", "description": " Let `s` be a finset in a linear order. Then `s.max` is the maximum of `s` if `s` is not empty,\nand `\u22a5` otherwise. It belongs to `with_bot \u03b1`. If you want to get an element of `\u03b1`, see\n`s.max'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_inf'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_eq_Inf_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_mono_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_induction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_eq_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_finset_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_inf", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `finset.le_inf_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.map_finset_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.is_lub_iff_is_greatest", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_singleton''", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_inf_distrib_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.set_bUnion_finset_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup'_product_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.max_of_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.not_mem_of_max_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_finset_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "supr_eq_supr_finset", "description": " Supremum of `s i`, `i : \u03b9`, is equal to the supremum over `t : finset \u03b9` of suprema\n`\u2a06 i \u2208 t, s i`. This version assumes `\u03b9` is a `Type*`. See `supr_eq_supr_finset'` for a version\nthat works for `\u03b9 : Sort*`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.to_dual_max'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.codisjoint_inf_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup'_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup'_inf_distrib_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.induction_on_max_value", "description": " Induction principle for `finset`s in any type from which a given function `f` maps to a linearly\nordered type : a predicate is true on all `s : finset \u03b1` provided that:\n\n* it is true on the empty `finset`,\n* for every `s : finset \u03b1` and an element `a` such that for elements of `s` denoted by `x` we have\n  `f x \u2264 f a`, `p s` implies `p (insert a s)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_max'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.min'_singleton", "description": "`{a}.min' _` is `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.lt_max'_of_mem_erase_max'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.min_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.coe_max'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.set_bUnion_option_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mem_of_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.is_least_min'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.of_dual_inf'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.to_dual_min'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.min_mem_image_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.set_bInter_insert_update", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup'_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf'_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_sup'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.max_eq_sup_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup'_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.comp_inf_eq_inf_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.supr_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf", "description": "Infimum of a finite set: `inf {a, b, c} f = f a \u2293 f b \u2293 f c`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.subset_range_sup_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.comp_inf_eq_inf_comp_of_is_total", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf'", "description": " Given nonempty finset `s` then `s.inf' H f` is the infimum of its image under `f` in (possibly\nunbounded) meet-semilattice `\u03b1`, where `H` is a proof of nonemptiness. If `\u03b1` has a top element you\nmay instead use `finset.inf` which does not require `s` nonempty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "supr_eq_supr_finset'", "description": " Supremum of `s i`, `i : \u03b9`, is equal to the supremum over `t : finset \u03b9` of suprema\n`\u2a06 i \u2208 t, s i`. This version works for `\u03b9 : Sort*`. See `supr_eq_supr_finset` for a version\nthat assumes `\u03b9 : Type*` but has no `plift`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.set_bInter_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_coe", "description": "Computing `inf` in a subtype (closed under `inf`) is the same as computing it in `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.max_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.map_of_dual_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.max_eq_sup_with_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf'_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup'_induction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.codisjoint_inf_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_induction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup'_bUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.comp_sup_eq_sup_comp_of_is_total", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf'_eq_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.supr_finset_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_finset_inf'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.lt_sup'_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_sup_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.max_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf'_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_mul_le_mul_sup_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.not_mem_of_coe_lt_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.to_dual_inf'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_coe", "description": "Computing `sup` in a subtype (closed under `sup`) is the same as computing it in `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.coe_min'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_lt_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mem_of_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.of_dual_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.is_greatest_max'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf'_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.disjoint_sup_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_inf_distrib_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.min_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_le_of_le_directed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_sup'_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.max_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.is_lub_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.lt_min'_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.coe_sup_of_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.of_dual_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.lt_inf'_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_sdiff_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_inf_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.map_to_dual_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.coe_sup'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.set_bUnion_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_id_set_eq_sInter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.set_bInter_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup'", "description": " Given nonempty finset `s` then `s.sup' H f` is the supremum of its image under `f` in (possibly\nunbounded) join-semilattice `\u03b1`, where `H` is a proof of nonemptiness. If `\u03b1` has a bottom element\nyou may instead use `finset.sup` which does not require `s` nonempty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.infi_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.infi_option_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.set_bUnion_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.min_mem_insert_top_image_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_inf'_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_id_eq_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_closed_of_sup_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.min_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.subset_set_bUnion_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_le_of_interleaved", "description": "If finsets `s` and `t` are interleaved, then `finset.card s \u2264 finset.card t + 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.not_mem_of_max_lt_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_sup_distrib_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf'_mul_le_mul_inf'_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.max_mem_insert_bot_image_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_sup_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_le_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.compl_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.set_bUnion_preimage_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.max_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_eq_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset