ve better definitional equalities for `source` and `target`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eq_on_source_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_source''", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.frontier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.target_inter_inv_preimage_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.set.eq_on.restr_eq_on_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.refl_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.of_image_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.subtype_restr", "description": " The restriction of a local homeomorphism `e` to an open subset `s` of the domain type produces a\nlocal homeomorphism whose domain is the subtype `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.prod_to_local_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.maps_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eq_of_local_equiv_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.symm_eq_on_of_inter_eq_of_eq_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.trans_local_homeomorph_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.restr_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.mk_coe_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.inj_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.source_inter_preimage_inv_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.subtype_restr_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.source_preimage_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.subtype_restr_symm_trans_subtype_restr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.image_open_of_open'", "description": "The image of the restriction of an open set to the source is open.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.map_nhds_within_preimage_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.image_open_of_open", "description": "The image of an open set in the source is open.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.map_subtype_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.prod_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.of_continuous_open_restrict", "description": "A `local_equiv` with continuous open forward map and an open source is a `local_homeomorph`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.symm_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "open_embedding.continuous_at_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.refl_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "open_embedding.to_local_homeomorph", "description": " An open embedding of `\u03b1` into `\u03b2`, with `\u03b1` nonempty, defines a local homeomorphism whose source\nis all of `\u03b1`.  The converse is also true; see `local_homeomorph.to_open_embedding`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.to_open_embedding", "description": " A local homeomorphism whose source is all of `\u03b1` defines an open embedding of `\u03b1` into `\u03b2`.  The\nconverse is also true; see `open_embedding.to_local_homeomorph`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.of_continuous_open", "description": "A `local_equiv` with continuous open forward map and an open source is a `local_homeomorph`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.symm_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.replace_equiv_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.restr_source'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.replace_equiv", "description": "Replace `to_local_equiv` field to provide better definitional equalities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eq_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eq_on_source.symm'", "description": "If two local homeomorphisms are equivalent, so are their inverses", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.local_homeomorph_subtype_coe", "description": " The inclusion of an open subset `s` of a space `\u03b1` into `\u03b1` is a local homeomorphism from the\nsubtype `s` to `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.refl", "description": "The identity on the whole space as a local homeomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.restr", "description": " Restricting a local homeomorphism `e` to `e.source \u2229 interior s`. We use the interior to make\nsure that the restriction is well defined whatever the set s, since local homeomorphisms are by\ndefinition defined on open sets. In applications where `s` is open, this coincides with the\nrestriction of local equivalences", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "open_embedding.to_local_homeomorph_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.image_source_inter_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.apply_mem_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.restr_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.prod_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.iff_preimage_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.preimage_open_of_open_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eventually_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_of_set'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eq_on_source.eq_on", "description": "Two equivalent local homeomorphisms have coinciding `to_fun` on the source", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.coe_coe_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.symm_preimage_eq", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `local_homeomorph.is_image.iff_symm_preimage_eq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.left_inv_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.of_symm_preimage_eq'", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `local_homeomorph.is_image.iff_symm_preimage_eq'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.map_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.of_symm_preimage_eq", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `local_homeomorph.is_image.iff_symm_preimage_eq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.subtype_restr_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.prod_eq_prod_of_nonempty'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.bij_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_homeomorph", "description": " Postcompose a local homeomorphism with an homeomorphism.\nWe modify the source and target to have better definitional behavior.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image_source_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_self_symm", "description": " Composition of a local homeomorphism and its inverse is equivalent to the restriction of the\nidentity to the source", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph", "description": "local homeomorphisms, defined on open subsets of the space", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.to_local_equiv", "description": "local homeomorphisms, defined on open subsets of the space", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.open_source", "description": "local homeomorphisms, defined on open subsets of the space", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.open_target", "description": "local homeomorphisms, defined on open subsets of the space", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.continuous_to_fun", "description": "local homeomorphisms, defined on open subsets of the space", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.continuous_inv_fun", "description": "local homeomorphisms, defined on open subsets of the space", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_target''", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.tendsto_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_source'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.restr_source_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.inv_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eventually_right_inverse'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.nhds_within_target_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.symm_image_target_eq_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eventually_right_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eq_on_source.trans'", "description": "Composition of local homeomorphisms respects equivalence", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.of_set_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.of_set", "description": "The identity local equiv on a set `s`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eq_on_source.restr", "description": "Restriction of local homeomorphisms respects equivalence", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.preimage_eq", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `local_homeomorph.is_image.iff_preimage_eq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.of_set_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.of_set_trans'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.to_local_homeomorph_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.inv_image_trans_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.map_nhds_within_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.restr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.restr", "description": "Restrict a `local_homeomorph` to a pair of corresponding open sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.prod_eq_prod_of_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.local_homeomorph_subtype_coe_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.iff_preimage_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_homeomorph_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.prod", "description": "The product of two local homeomorphisms, as a local homeomorphism on the product space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.of_set_trans_of_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_homeomorph_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.interior", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.continuous_on_iff_continuous_on_comp_left", "description": " A function is continuous on a set if and only if its composition with a local homeomorphism\non the left is continuous on the corresponding set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.inv_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.of_preimage_eq", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `local_homeomorph.is_image.iff_preimage_eq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.trans_local_homeomorph", "description": " Precompose a local homeomorphism with an homeomorphism.\nWe modify the source and target to have better definitional behavior.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.preimage_eventually_eq_target_inter_preimage_inter", "description": "This lemma is useful in the manifold library in the case that `e` is a chart. It states that\n locally around `e x` the set `e.symm \u207b\u00b9' s` is the same as the set intersected with the target\n of `e` and some other neighborhood of `f x` (which will be the source of a chart on `\u03b3`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eq_of_eq_on_source_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.restr_eq_of_source_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.symm_to_local_homeomorph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.pi", "description": "The product of a finite family of `local_homeomorph`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans", "description": " Composing two local homeomorphisms, by restricting to the maximal domain where their\ncomposition is well defined.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eventually_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.coe_trans_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eventually_nhds_within'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.symm_apply_mem_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.nhds_within_source_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.homeomorph_of_image_subset_source", "description": "The homeomorphism obtained by restricting a `local_homeomorph` to a subset of the source.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.map_nhds_within_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.source_inter_preimage_target_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.right_inv_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eventually_nhds'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.is_open_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eq_on_source.source_eq", "description": "Two equivalent local homeomorphisms have the same source", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.to_homeomorph_of_source_eq_univ_target_eq_univ_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_to_local_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.symm_maps_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.of_set_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.symm_image_target_inter_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.of_set_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.symm_image_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.ext", "description": " Two local homeomorphisms are equal when they have equal `to_fun`, `inv_fun` and `source`.\nIt is not sufficient to have equal `to_fun` and `source`, as this only determines `inv_fun` on\nthe target. This would only be true for a weaker notion of equality, arguably the right one,\ncalled `eq_on_source`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.inter_eq_of_inter_eq_of_eq_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.coe_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eq_on_source.symm_eq_on_target", "description": "Two equivalent local homeomorphisms have coinciding `inv_fun` on the target", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.to_local_homeomorph_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.restr_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "open_embedding.to_local_homeomorph_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.image_trans_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.symm", "description": "The inverse of a local homeomorphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.simps.apply", "description": "See Note [custom simps projection]. We need to specify this projection explicitly in this case,\n because it is a composition of multiple projections.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.restr_to_local_equiv'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.restr_open_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image_source_target_of_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.image_source_inter_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.continuous_iff_continuous_comp_left", "description": " A function is continuous if and only if its composition with a local homeomorphism\non the left is continuous and its image is contained in the source.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_symm_eq_symm_trans_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.left_inv_on_piecewise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "open_embedding.to_local_homeomorph_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.subtype_restr_symm_eq_on_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.homeomorph_of_image_subset_source_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.prod_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.continuous_at_symm", "description": "A local homeomorphism inverse is continuous at any point of its target", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_equiv_eq_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.left_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.to_local_homeomorph", "description": "A homeomorphism induces a local homeomorphism on the whole space", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.symm_map_nhds_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.symm_to_local_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.refl_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.iff_symm_preimage_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.continuous_on_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.prod_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.right_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.continuous_on_iff_continuous_on_comp_right", "description": " A function is continuous on a set if and only if its composition with a local homeomorphism\non the right is continuous on the corresponding set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.trans_local_homeomorph_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.to_local_homeomorph_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.prod_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.refl_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.image_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.symm_preimage_eq'", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `local_homeomorph.is_image.iff_symm_preimage_eq'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.continuous_within_at_iff_continuous_within_at_comp_right", "description": " Continuity within a set at a point can be read under right composition with a local\nhomeomorphism, if the point is in its target", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_homeomorph_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.symm_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.symm_maps_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.piecewise_to_local_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.of_set_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.continuous_within_at_iff_continuous_within_at_comp_left", "description": " Continuity within a set at a point can be read under left composition with a local\nhomeomorphism if a neighborhood of the initial point is sent to the source of the local\nhomeomorphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.refl_prod_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.refl_local_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.local_homeomorph_subtype_coe_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.surj_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.continuous_at_iff_continuous_at_comp_right", "description": " Continuity at a point can be read under right composition with a local homeomorphism, if the\npoint is in its target", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.symm_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.homeomorph_of_image_subset_source_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.simps.symm_apply", "description": "See Note [custom simps projection]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.piecewise", "description": " Combine two `local_homeomorph`s using `set.piecewise`. The source of the new `local_homeomorph`\nis `s.ite e.source e'.source = e.source \u2229 s \u222a e'.source \\ s`, and similarly for target.  The\nfunction sends `e.source \u2229 s` to `e.target \u2229 t` using `e` and `e'.source \\ s` to `e'.target \\ t`\nusing `e'`, and similarly for the inverse function. To ensure that the maps `to_fun` and `inv_fun`\nare inverse of each other on the new `source` and `target`, the definition assumes that the sets `s`\nand `t` are related both by `e.is_image` and `e'.is_image`. To ensure that the new maps are\ncontinuous on `source`/`target`, it also assumes that `e.source` and `e'.source` meet `frontier s`\non the same set and `e x = e' x` on this intersection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_homeomorph_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_of_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.of_symm_image_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.continuous_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.restr_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.trans_local_homeomorph_eq_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.preimage_frontier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.restr_to_local_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.trans_local_homeomorph_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.iff_symm_preimage_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.preimage_eq'", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `local_homeomorph.is_image.iff_preimage_eq'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.continuous_at", "description": "A local homeomorphism is continuous at any point of its source", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.restr_to_local_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.map_nhds_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.of_set_to_local_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eventually_left_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eventually_ne_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.maps_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_target'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.to_local_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.preimage_interior", "description": " Preimage of interior or interior of preimage coincide for local homeomorphisms, when restricted\nto the source.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.trans_to_local_homeomorph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.to_homeomorph_source_target", "description": "A local homeomrphism defines a homeomorphism between its source and target.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.trans_local_homeomorph_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eventually_left_inverse'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.to_homeomorph_of_source_eq_univ_target_eq_univ_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.to_local_equiv_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.restr_open", "description": " Restricting a local homeomorphism `e` to `e.source \u2229 s` when `s` is open. This is sometimes hard\nto use because of the openness assumption, but it has the advantage that when it can\nbe used then its local_equiv is defeq to local_equiv.restr", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.symm_piecewise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.local_homeomorph_subtype_coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.symm_image_eq_source_inter_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.preimage_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.restr_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.piecewise_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.of_set_univ_eq_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.trans_symm_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.refl_to_local_homeomorph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.preimage_open_of_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.subtype_restr_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.second_countable_topology_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.to_homeomorph_of_source_eq_univ_target_eq_univ", "description": " If a local homeomorphism has source and target equal to univ, then it induces a homeomorphism\nbetween the whole spaces, expressed in this definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image", "description": " We say that `t : set \u03b2` is an image of `s : set \u03b1` under a local homeomorphism `e` if any of the\nfollowing equivalent conditions hold:\n\n* `e '' (e.source \u2229 s) = e.target \u2229 t`;\n* `e.source \u2229 e \u207b\u00b9 t = e.source \u2229 s`;\n* `\u2200 x \u2208 e.source, e x \u2208 t \u2194 x \u2208 s` (this one is used in the definition).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.of_preimage_eq'", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `local_homeomorph.is_image.iff_preimage_eq'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.pi_to_local_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eq_on_source_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.to_local_homeomorph_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.eq_on_source", "description": " `eq_on_source e e'` means that `e` and `e'` have the same source, and coincide there. They\nshould really be considered the same local equiv.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.setoid", "description": "`eq_on_source` is an equivalence relation", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.continuous_at_iff_continuous_at_comp_left", "description": " Continuity at a point can be read under left composition with a local homeomorphism if a\nneighborhood of the initial point is sent to the source of the local homeomorphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.map_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.restr_open_to_local_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.image_eq_target_inter_inv_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_homeomorph.is_image.image_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cofinite_topology.continuous_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t5_space", "description": " A topological space `\u03b1` is a *completely normal Hausdorff space* if each subspace `s : set \u03b1` is\na normal Hausdorff space. Equivalently, `\u03b1` is a `T\u2081` space and for any two sets `s`, `t` such that\n`closure s` is disjoint with `t` and `s` is disjoint with `closure t`, there exist disjoint\nneighbourhoods of `s` and `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t5_space.to_t1_space", "description": " A topological space `\u03b1` is a *completely normal Hausdorff space* if each subspace `s : set \u03b1` is\na normal Hausdorff space. Equivalently, `\u03b1` is a `T\u2081` space and for any two sets `s`, `t` such that\n`closure s` is disjoint with `t` and `s` is disjoint with `closure t`, there exist disjoint\nneighbourhoods of `s` and `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t5_space.completely_normal", "description": " A topological space `\u03b1` is a *completely normal Hausdorff space* if each subspace `s : set \u03b1` is\na normal Hausdorff space. Equivalently, `\u03b1` is a `T\u2081` space and for any two sets `s`, `t` such that\n`closure s` is disjoint with `t` and `s` is disjoint with `closure t`, there exist disjoint\nneighbourhoods of `s` and `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.is_topological_basis.exists_mem_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "embedding.t0_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact_closure_of_subset_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_space_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.left_inverse.closed_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inducing.embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtype.t3_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes_iff_inseparable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.regular_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.t1_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separated_nhds.preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "singleton_mem_nhds_within_of_mem_discrete", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtype.t0_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separated_by_open_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.binary_compact_cover", "description": "If a compact set is covered by two open sets, then we can cover it by two compact subsets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_within_insert_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "compact_t2_tot_disc_iff_tot_sep", "description": "A compact Hausdorff space is totally disconnected if and only if it is totally separated, this\n is also true for locally compact spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.t2_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_singleton_of_finite_mem_nhds", "description": "A point with a finite neighborhood has to be isolated.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_compact_of_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.lim_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "discrete_topology.to_t2_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separated_nhds.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset_disjoint_finset_opens_of_t2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_set_inj_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtype.t1_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.subsingleton.closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.t0_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t2_space.t1_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.t1_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specialization_order", "description": "Specialization forms a partial order on a t0 topological space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bornology.relatively_compact", "description": " In a `t1_space`, relatively compact sets form a bornology. Its cobounded filter is\n`filter.coclosed_compact`. See also `bornology.in_compact` the bornology of sets contained\nin a compact set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.eq_on.closure", "description": " If two continuous maps are equal on `s`, then they are equal on the closure of `s`. See also\n`set.eq_on.of_subset_closure` for a more general version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_on_closure\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_on_closure\u2082'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t1_space_of_injective_of_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.eventually_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Pi.t2_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t0_space_of_injective_of_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_space.of_lift'_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_within_of_mem_discrete", "description": " The neighbourhoods filter of `x` within `s`, under the discrete topology, is equal to\nthe pure `x` filter (which is the principal filter at the singleton `{x}`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t0_space", "description": " A T\u2080 space, also known as a Kolmogorov space, is a topological space such that for every pair\n`x \u2260 y`, there is an open set containing one but not the other. We formulate the definition in terms\nof the `inseparable` relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t0_space.t0", "description": " A T\u2080 space, also known as a Kolmogorov space, is a topological space such that for every pair\n`x \u2260 y`, there is an open set containing one but not the other. We formulate the definition in terms\nof the `inseparable` relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pairwise_disjoint_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_compact_superset_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsingleton_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Lim_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "injective_nhds_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pure_le_nhds_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_iff_ultrafilter'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "disjoint_nhds_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t1_space_tfae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_nhds_unique_of_eventually_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normal_space_of_t3_second_countable", "description": " A T\u2083 topological space with second countable topology is a normal space.\nThis lemma is not an instance to avoid a loop.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.coclosed_compact_le_cofinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "loc_compact_t2_tot_disc_iff_tot_sep", "description": "A locally compact Hausdorff space is totally disconnected\n if and only if it is totally separated.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closed_embedding.normal_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_mem_nhds_is_closed_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_set_of_disjoint_nhds_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.ext_on", "description": "If two continuous functions are equal on a dense set, then they are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "compl_singleton_mem_nhds_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "embedding.t5_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact_is_compact_separated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite.is_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separated_nhds.empty_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at_update_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.t3_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t1_space.t0_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separated_nhds.union_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "connected_space.infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "compact_exists_clopen_in_open", "description": "Every member of an open set in a compact Hausdorff totally disconnected space\n is contained in a clopen set contained in the open set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.Lim_eq_iff_le_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes.eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_of_tendsto_nhds", "description": " If a function to a `t1_space` tends to some limit `b` at some point `a`, then necessarily\n`b = f a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "embedding.t2_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "discrete_of_t1_of_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normal_space", "description": "A T\u2084 space, also known as a normal space (although this condition sometimes\n omits T\u2082), is one in which for every pair of disjoint closed sets `C` and `D`,\n there exist disjoint open sets containing `C` and `D` respectively.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normal_space.to_t1_space", "description": "A T\u2084 space, also known as a normal space (although this condition sometimes\n omits T\u2082), is one in which for every pair of disjoint closed sets `C` and `D`,\n there exist disjoint open sets containing `C` and `D` respectively.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normal_space.normal", "description": "A T\u2084 space, also known as a normal space (although this condition sometimes\n omits T\u2082), is one in which for every pair of disjoint closed sets `C` and `D`,\n there exist disjoint open sets containing `C` and `D` respectively.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separated_nhds.empty_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inducing.injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closed_nhds_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.normal_space", "description": " The `separation_quotient` of a normal space is a T\u2084 space. We don't have separate typeclasses\nfor normal spaces (without T\u2081 assumption) and T\u2084 spaces, so we use the same class for assumption\nand for conclusion.\n\nOne can prove this using a homeomorphism between `\u03b1` and `separation_quotient \u03b1`. We give an\nalternative proof that works without assuming that `\u03b1` is a T\u2081 space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t2_iff_nhds", "description": "A space is T\u2082 iff the neighbourhoods of distinct points generate the bottom filter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.coclosed_compact_eq_cocompact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Lim_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t0_space_iff_inseparable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bornology.relatively_compact_eq_in_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.t3_space", "description": "The `separation_quotient` of a regular space is a T\u2083 space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_basis_nhds_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtype.t2_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "compl_singleton_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t3_space.t2_5_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.finite_compact_cover", "description": "For every finite open cover `U\u1d62` of a compact set, there exists a compact cover `K\u1d62 \u2286 U\u1d62`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_space.of_exists_mem_nhds_is_closed_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "image_closure_of_is_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t5_space.to_normal_space", "description": "A `T\u2085` space is a `T\u2084` space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separated_by_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_diagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.is_closed", "description": "In a `t2_space`, every compact set is closed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t1_space_antitone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t2_iff_is_closed_diagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.eq_on.of_subset_closure", "description": " If `f x = g x` for all `x \u2208 s` and `f`, `g` are continuous on `t`, `s \u2286 t \u2286 closure s`, then\n`f x = g x` for all `x \u2208 t`. See also `set.eq_on.closure`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_update_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bInter_basis_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.regular_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normal_separation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "embedding_iff_inducing", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t1_space_iff_continuous_cofinite_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.is_topological_basis.exists_closure_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_const_nhds_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t0_space.of_open_cover", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normal_space.t3_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtype.regular_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t0_space_iff_exists_is_open_xor_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normal_exists_closure_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_preirreducible_iff_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_inter_eq_singleton_of_mem_discrete", "description": " A point `x` in a discrete subset `s` of a topological space admits a neighbourhood\nthat only meets `s` at `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtype.t5_space", "description": "A subspace of a `T\u2085` space is a `T\u2085` space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_open_with_compact_closure", "description": "In a locally compact T\u2082 space, every point has an open neighborhood with compact closure", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_nhds_disjoint_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "totally_separated_space_of_t1_of_basis_clopen", "description": "A T1 space with a clopen basis is totally separated.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.is_closed_map", "description": "A continuous map from a compact space to a Hausdorff space is a closed map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "disjoint_lift'_closure_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_basis_clopen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minimal_nonempty_closed_eq_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_preirreducible.subsingleton", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `is_preirreducible_iff_subsingleton`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t0_space.of_cover", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_map_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sigma.t2_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t1_space_iff_disjoint_nhds_pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne.nhds_within_compl_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_compl_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "disjoint_nhds_set_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "disjoint_pure_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.is_open_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_le_nhds_set_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infinite_of_mem_nhds", "description": " If the punctured neighborhoods of a point form a nontrivial filter, then any neighborhood is\ninfinite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t2_separation", "description": "Two different points can be separated by open sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_of_nhds_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t2_5_space.t2_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_irreducible_iff_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_subset_nhds_of_is_compact", "description": " If `V : \u03b9 \u2192 set \u03b1` is a decreasing family of compact sets then any neighborhood of\n`\u22c2 i, V i` contains some `V i`. This is a version of `exists_subset_nhd_of_compact'` where we\ndon't need to assume each `V i` closed because it follows from compactness since `\u03b1` is\nassumed to be Hausdorff.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.t3_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bornology.relatively_compact.is_bounded_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_set_of_eventually_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_space", "description": " A topological space is called a *regular space* if for any closed set `s` and `a \u2209 s`, there\nexist disjoint open sets `U \u2287 s` and `V \u220b a`. We formulate this condition in terms of `disjoint`ness\nof filters `\ud835\udcdd\u02e2 s` and `\ud835\udcdd a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_space.regular", "description": " A topological space is called a *regular space* if for any closed set `s` and `a \u2209 s`, there\nexist disjoint open sets `U \u2287 s` and `V \u220b a`. We formulate this condition in terms of `disjoint`ness\nof filters `\ud835\udcdd\u02e2 s` and `\ud835\udcdd a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_space_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_update_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t0_space_iff_not_inseparable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_open_nhds_disjoint_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t1_space", "description": "A T\u2081 space, also known as a Fr\u00e9chet space, is a topological space\n where every singleton set is closed. Equivalently, for every pair\n `x \u2260 y`, there is an open set containing `x` and not `y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t1_space.t1", "description": "A T\u2081 space, also known as a Fr\u00e9chet space, is a topological space\n where every singleton set is closed. Equivalently, for every pair\n `x \u2260 y`, there is an open set containing `x` and not `y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t2_space_iff_disjoint_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_space_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.left_inverse.closed_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "compl_singleton_mem_nhds_set_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable.eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t1_space_iff_disjoint_pure_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t0_space_iff_nhds_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minimal_nonempty_open_eq_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.t0_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.subset_trans", "description": " Let `X` be a topological space and let `s, t \u2286 X` be two subsets.  If there is an inclusion\n`t \u2286 s`, then the topological space structure on `t` induced by `X` is the same as the one\nobtained by the induced topological space structure on `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separated_nhds.disjoint_closure_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_ne_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t3_space", "description": " A T\u2083 space is a T\u2080 space which is a regular space. Any T\u2083 space is a T\u2081 space, a T\u2082 space, and\na T\u2082.\u2085 space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t3_space.to_t0_space", "description": " A T\u2083 space is a T\u2080 space which is a regular space. Any T\u2083 space is a T\u2081 space, a T\u2082 space, and\na T\u2082.\u2085 space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t3_space.to_regular_space", "description": " A T\u2083 space is a T\u2080 space which is a regular space. Any T\u2083 space is a T\u2081 space, a T\u2082 space, and\na T\u2082.\u2085 space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "embedding.t3_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.t2_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t2_space_iff_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separated_nhds", "description": "`separated_nhds` is a predicate on pairs of sub`set`s of a topological space.  It holds if the two\nsub`set`s are contained in disjoint open sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_set_of_inseparable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.diff_singleton", "description": "Removing a non-isolated point from a dense set, one still obtains a dense set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_space_tfae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable_eq_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t1_space_iff_specializes_imp_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_topological_basis_clopen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_nhds_unique'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normal_of_compact_t2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_basis_opens_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "point_disjoint_finset_opens_of_t2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_is_open_xor_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.t5_space", "description": " The `separation_quotient` of a completely normal space is a T\u2085 space. We don't have separate\ntypeclasses for completely normal spaces (without T\u2081 assumption) and T\u2085 spaces, so we use the same\nclass for assumption and for conclusion.\n\nOne can prove this using a homeomorphism between `\u03b1` and `separation_quotient \u03b1`. We give an\nalternative proof that works without assuming that `\u03b1` is a T\u2081 space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t2_space", "description": "A T\u2082 space, also known as a Hausdorff space, is one in which for every\n `x \u2260 y` there exists disjoint open sets around `x` and `y`. This is\n the most widely used of the separation axioms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t2_space.t2", "description": "A T\u2082 space, also known as a Hausdorff space, is one in which for every\n `x \u2260 y` there exists disjoint open sets around `x` and `y`. This is\n the most widely used of the separation axioms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.closed_embedding", "description": "An injective continuous map from a compact space to a Hausdorff space is a closed embedding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separated_nhds.disjoint_closure_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t2_iff_ultrafilter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strict_mono_nhds_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lift'_nhds_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "disjoint_nhds_nhds_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.is_open_mul_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lim_nhds_within_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inducing.regular_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_compact_of_compact_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separated_nhds.comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.lim_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "compact_exhaustion.is_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite.t2_separation", "description": "Points of a finite set can be separated by open sets from each other.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Lim_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_open_superset_and_is_compact_closure", "description": "In a locally compact T\u2082 space, every compact set has an open neighborhood with compact closure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "disjoint_nhds_nhds_iff_not_specializes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_preconnected.infinite_of_nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne.nhds_within_diff_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t2_separation_compact_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.eventually_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separated_nhds_iff_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minimal_nonempty_closed_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_set_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "disjoint_nhds_within_of_mem_discrete", "description": " For point `x` in a discrete subset `s` of a topological space, there is a set `U`\nsuch that\n1. `U` is a punctured neighborhood of `x` (ie. `U \u222a {x}` is a neighbourhood of `x`),\n2. `U` is disjoint from `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_open_between_and_is_compact_closure", "description": "In a locally compact T\u2082 space, given a compact set `K` inside an open set `U`, we can find a\nopen set `V` between these sets with compact closure: `K \u2286 V` and the closure of `V` is inside `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_preirreducible_nontrivial_t2", "description": "There does not exist a nontrivial preirreducible T\u2082 space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "disjoint_nhds_pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_space.of_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t2_space_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_le_nhds_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.exists_closed_singleton", "description": " Given a closed set `S` in a compact T\u2080 space,\nthere is some `x \u2208 S` such that `{x}` is closed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.lim_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.diff_finset", "description": " Removing a finset from a dense set in a space without isolated points, one still\nobtains a dense set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes_eq_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "loc_compact_Haus_tot_disc_of_zero_dim", "description": "A locally compact Hausdorff totally disconnected space has a basis with clopen elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "insert_mem_nhds_within_of_subset_insert", "description": " If `t` is a subset of `s`, except for one point,\nthen `insert x s` is a neighborhood of `x` within `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.is_topological_basis.nhds_basis_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_basis.exists_inter_eq_singleton_of_mem_discrete", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t1_space_iff_exists_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separated_nhds.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minimal_nonempty_open_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_of_tendsto_nhds", "description": " To prove a function to a `t1_space` is continuous at some point `a`, it suffices to prove that\n`f` admits *some* limit at `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_open_singleton_of_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "connected_components.t2", "description": "`connected_components \u03b1` is Hausdorff when `\u03b1` is Hausdorff and compact", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "preconnected_space.trivial_of_discrete", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cofinite_topology.t1_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t0_space_iff_or_not_mem_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t2_separation_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_space.inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_nhds_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_open_singleton_of_open_finite", "description": "Given an open finite set `S` in a T\u2080 space, there is some `x \u2208 S` such that `{x}` is open.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.t0_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_eq_nhds_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.diff_finite", "description": " Removing a finite set from a dense set in a space without isolated points, one still\nobtains a dense set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "disjoint_nested_nhds", "description": " Given two points `x \u2260 y`, we can find neighbourhoods `x \u2208 V\u2081 \u2286 U\u2081` and `y \u2208 V\u2082 \u2286 U\u2082`,\nwith the `V\u2096` closed and the `U\u2096` open, such that the `U\u2096` are disjoint.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separated_nhds.union_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.is_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "embedding.t1_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t2_5_space", "description": "A T\u2082.\u2085 space, also known as a Urysohn space, is a topological space\n where for every pair `x \u2260 y`, there are two open sets, with the intersection of closures\n empty, one containing `x` and the other `y` .", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t2_5_space.t2_5", "description": "A T\u2082.\u2085 space, also known as a Urysohn space, is a topological space\n where for every pair `x \u2260 y`, there are two open sets, with the intersection of closures\n empty, one containing `x` and the other `y` .", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Lim_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_set_of_specializes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_nhds_unique_of_frequently_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lim_nhds_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_space_induced", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes.symm", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `specializes_comm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separated_nhds.disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_basis.nhds_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "connected_component_eq_Inter_clopen", "description": " In a compact t2 space, the connected component of a point equals the intersection of all\nits clopen neighbourhoods.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_map.of_surjective_continuous", "description": "A surjective continuous map from a compact space to a Hausdorff space is a quotient map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.subtype_perm_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.mul_left_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.of_subtype_apply_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.inv_add_left", "description": "", 