", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.blimsup_and_le_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.limsup_eq_infi_supr_of_nat'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.le_Liminf_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.Liminf_eq_supr_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.is_cobounded_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.Limsup", "description": " The `Limsup` of a filter `f` is the infimum of the `a` such that, eventually for `f`,\nholds `x \u2264 a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.is_bounded.is_cobounded_flip", "description": " A filter which is eventually bounded is in particular frequently bounded (in the opposite\ndirection). At least if the filter is not trivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.is_bounded.is_cobounded_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.is_bounded_iff", "description": " `f` is eventually bounded if and only if, there exists an admissible set on which it is\nbounded.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.inf_liminf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.Liminf_le_Liminf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.is_cobounded_le_of_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.bliminf_false", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.liminf_sdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.Inf_hom.le_apply_bliminf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.infi_le_liminf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.not_is_bounded_under_of_tendsto_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.lt_mem_sets_of_Limsup_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.Limsup_le_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.limsup_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.is_bounded_under.bdd_above_range_of_cofinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.mono_b