}, {"name": "direct_sum.sigma_lcurry", "description": "`curry` as a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.to_module_lof", "description": " The map constructed using the universal property gives back the original maps when\nrestricted to each component.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.mk_smul", "description": "Scalar multiplication commutes with direct sums.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.is_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.apply_eq_component", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lid", "description": "The natural linear equivalence between `\u2a01 _ : \u03b9, M` and `M` when `unique \u03b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.smul_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.is_internal.collected_basis", "description": " Given an internal direct sum decomposition of a module `M`, and a basis for each of the\ncomponents of the direct sum, the disjoint union of these bases is a basis for `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.is_internal_submodule_iff_independent_and_supr_eq_top", "description": " `iff` version of `direct_sum.is_internal_submodule_of_independent_of_supr_eq_top`,\n`direct_sum.is_internal.independent`, and `direct_sum.is_internal.supr_eq_top`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lset_to_set", "description": "The inclusion of a subset of the direct summands\ninto a larger subset of the direct summands, as a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.sigma_lcurry_equiv", "description": "`curry_equiv` as a linear equiv.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.sigma_luncurry", "description": "`uncurry` as a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.is_internal.submodule_independent", "description": "If a direct sum of submodules is internal then the submodules are independent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lequiv_congr_left", "description": "Reindexing terms of a direct sum is linear.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.is_internal_submodule_of_independent_of_supr_eq_top", "description": " Note that this is not generally true for `[semiring R]`; see\n`complete_lattice.independent.dfinsupp_lsum_injective` for details.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.coe_linear_map_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.of_smul", "description": "Scalar multiplication commutes with the inclusion of each component into the direct sum.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.coe_to_module_eq_coe_to_add_monoid", "description": " Coproducts in the categories of modules and additive monoids commute with the forgetful functor\nfrom modules to additive monoids.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lequiv_prod_direct_sum", "description": "Linear isomorphism obtained by separating the term of index `none` of a direct sum over\n`option \u03b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.sigma_luncurry_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.linear_equiv_fun_on_fintype_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.component", "description": "The projection map onto one component, as a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.is_internal.submodule_supr_eq_top", "description": "If a direct sum of submodules is internal then the submodules span the module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.component.lof_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.is_internal_submodule_iff_is_compl", "description": " If a collection of submodules has just two indices, `i` and `j`, then\n`direct_sum.is_internal` is equivalent to `is_compl`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.support_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.linear_equiv_fun_on_fintype_lof", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.coe_linear_map", "description": " The canonical embedding from `\u2a01 i, A i` to `M`  where `A` is a collection of `submodule R M`\nindexed by `\u03b9`. This is `direct_sum.coe_add_monoid_hom` as a `linear_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.single_eq_lof", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.to_module", "description": "The linear map constructed using the universal property of the coproduct.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.is_internal.collected_basis_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lmk", "description": "Create the direct sum given a family `M` of `R` modules indexed over `\u03b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.linear_equiv_fun_on_fintype_symm_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.linear_equiv_fun_on_fintype_symm_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.is_internal.add_subgroup_independent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lof_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lequiv_congr_left_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.linear_equiv_fun_on_fintype", "description": " Given `fintype \u03b1`, `linear_equiv_fun_on_fintype R` is the natural `R`-linear equivalence\nbetween `\u2a01 i, M i` and `\u03a0 i, M i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lof_eq_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.is_internal.is_compl", "description": " When indexed by only two distinct elements, `direct_sum.is_internal` implies\nthe two submodules are complementary. Over a `ring R`, this is true as an iff, as\n`direct_sum.is_internal_iff_is_compl`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.is_internal.add_submonoid_independent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.linear_map_ext", "description": " Two `linear_map`s out of a direct sum are equal if they agree on the generators.\n\nSee note [partially-applied ext lemmas].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lequiv_prod_direct_sum_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_weighted_homogeneous.weighted_total_degree", "description": "A non zero weighted homogeneous polynomial of weighted degree `n` has weighted total degree\n `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_weighted_homogeneous.mul", "description": "The product of weighted homogeneous polynomials of weighted degrees `m` and `n` is weighted\n homogeneous of weighted degree `m + n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.weighted_homogeneous_component_eq_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_weighted_homogeneous_C", "description": "Constant polynomials are weighted homogeneous of degree 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.weighted_total_degree'_zero", "description": "The `weighted_total_degree'` of the zero polynomial is `\u22a5`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.le_weighted_total_degree", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.weighted_homogeneous_submodule_eq_finsupp_supported", "description": "The submodule ` weighted_homogeneous_submodule R w m` of homogeneous `mv_polynomial`s of\n degree `n` is equal to the `R`-submodule of all `p : (\u03c3 \u2192\u2080 \u2115) \u2192\u2080 R` such that\n `p.support \u2286 {d | weighted_degree' w d = m}`. While equal, the former has a\n convenient definitional reduction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.weighted_total_degree_coe", "description": "This lemma relates `weighted_total_degree` and `weighted_total_degree'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.weighted_homogeneous_submodule", "description": "The submodule of homogeneous `mv_polynomial`s of degree `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.weighted_homogeneous_submodule_mul", "description": "The submodule generated by products `Pm *Pn` of weighted homogeneous polynomials of degrees `m`\n and `n` is contained in the submodule of weighted homogeneous polynomials of degree `m + n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_weighted_homogeneous_one", "description": "1 is weighted homogeneous of degree 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.weighted_degree'", "description": "The `weighted degree'` of the finitely supported function `s : \u03c3 \u2192\u2080 \u2115` is the sum\n `\u2211(s i)\u2022(w i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_weighted_homogeneous.prod", "description": "A product of weighted homogeneous polynomials is weighted homogeneous, with weighted degree\n equal to the sum of the weighted degrees.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.weighted_homogeneous_component_C_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.weighted_total_degree", "description": "When `M` has a `\u22a5` element, we can define the weighted total degree of a multivariate\n polynomial as a function taking values in `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_weighted_homogeneous_zero", "description": "0 is weighted homogeneous of any degree.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.weighted_total_degree_zero", "description": "The `weighted_total_degree` of the zero polynomial is `\u22a5`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.sum_weighted_homogeneous_component", "description": "Every polynomial is the sum of its weighted homogeneous components.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_weighted_homogeneous_of_total_degree_zero", "description": "A polynomial of weighted_total_degree `\u22a5` is weighted_homogeneous of degree `\u22a5`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_weighted_homogeneous", "description": "A multivariate polynomial `\u03c6` is weighted homogeneous of weighted degree `m` if all monomials\n occuring in `\u03c6` have weighted degree `m`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_weighted_homogeneous.coeff_eq_zero", "description": "The weighted degree of a weighted homogeneous polynomial controls its support.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_weighted_homogeneous.inj_right", "description": "The weighted degree of a nonzero weighted homogeneous polynomial is well-defined.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_weighted_homogeneous_monomial", "description": "Monomials are weighted homogeneous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.weighted_homogeneous_component", "description": "`weighted_homogeneous_component w n \u03c6` is the part of `\u03c6` that is weighted homogeneous of\n weighted degree `n`, with respect to the weights `w`.\n See `sum_weighted_homogeneous_component` for the statement that `\u03c6` is equal to the sum\n of all its weighted homogeneous components.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_weighted_homogeneous.add", "description": "The sum of two weighted homogeneous polynomials of degree `n` is weighted homogeneous of\n weighted degree `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.weighted_homogeneous_component_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_weighted_homogeneous.weighted_homogeneous_submodule.gcomm_monoid", "description": "The weighted homogeneous submodules form a graded monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.coeff_weighted_homogeneous_component", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.weighted_homogeneous_component_finsupp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_weighted_homogeneous.sum", "description": "The sum of weighted homogeneous polynomials of degree `n` is weighted homogeneous of\n weighted degree `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.weighted_homogeneous_component_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.mem_weighted_homogeneous_submodule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_weighted_homogeneous_X", "description": "An indeterminate `i : \u03c3` is weighted homogeneous of degree `w i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.weighted_total_degree'_eq_bot_iff", "description": "The `weighted_total_degree'` of a polynomial `p` is `\u22a5` if and only if `p = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.weighted_homogeneous_component_weighted_homogeneous_polynomial", "description": "The weighted homogeneous components of a weighted homogeneous polynomial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.weighted_total_degree'", "description": "The weighted total degree of a multivariate polynomial, taking values in `with_bot M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.weighted_homogeneous_component_is_weighted_homogeneous", "description": " The `n` weighted homogeneous component of a polynomial is weighted homogeneous of\nweighted degree `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.weighted_homogeneous_component_zero", "description": "If `M` is a `canonically_ordered_add_monoid`, then the `weighted_homogeneous_component`\n of weighted degree `0` of a polynomial is its constant coefficient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "widget_override.filter_local", "description": "Filters a local constant using the given filter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "widget_override.tactic_render", "description": "Renders the current tactic state.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "widget_override.group_local_collection", "description": "Groups consecutive local collections by type", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "widget_override.interactive_expression.view", "description": "Renders a subexpression as a list of html elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "widget_override.interactive_expression.sf.flatten", "description": "Flattens an `sf`, i.e. merges adjacent `of_string` constructors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "widget_override.interactive_expression.sf.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "widget_override.local_collection", "description": "A group of local constants in the context that should be rendered as one line.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "widget_override.local_collection.key", "description": "A group of local constants in the context that should be rendered as one line.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "widget_override.local_collection.locals", "description": "A group of local constants in the context that should be rendered as one line.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "widget_override.local_collection.type", "description": "A group of local constants in the context that should be rendered as one line.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "widget_override.local_collection.value", "description": "A group of local constants in the context that should be rendered as one line.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "widget_override.interactive_expression.sf.elim_part_apps", "description": "Post-process an `sf` object to eliminate tags for partial applications by\npushing the `app_fn` as far into the expression as possible. The effect is\nthat clicking on a sub-expression always includes the full argument list in\nthe popup.\n\nConsider the expression `id id 0`. We push the `app_fn` for the partial\napplication `id id` inwards and eliminate it.  Before:\n```lean\n(tag_expr [app_fn]\n  `(id.{1} (nat -> nat) (id.{1} nat))\n  (tag_expr [app_fn] `(id.{1} (nat -> nat)) \"id\")\n  \"\\n\"\n  (tag_expr [app_arg] `(id.{1} nat) \"id\"))\n\"\\n\"\n(tag_expr [app_arg] `(has_zero.zero.{0} nat nat.has_zero) \"0\")\n```\nAfter:\n```lean\n\"id\"\n\"\\n\"\n(tag_expr [app_fn, app_arg] `(id.{1} nat) \"id\")\n\"\\n\"\n(tag_expr [app_arg] `(has_zero.zero.{0} nat nat.has_zero) \"0\")\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "widget_override.tactic_state_widget", "description": "Component showing the current tactic state.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "widget_override.interactive_expression.sf", "description": "eformat but without any of the formatting stuff like highlighting, groups etc.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "widget_override.interactive_expression.sf.tag_expr", "description": "eformat but without any of the formatting stuff like highlighting, groups etc.", "p": "mathlib"}, {