pty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.mem_pair", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.mem_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.resp.equiv.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.omega", "description": "`omega` is the first infinite von Neumann ordinal", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet", "description": "The type of pre-sets in universe `u`. A pre-set\n is a family of pre-sets indexed by a type in `Type u`.\n The ZFC universe is defined as a quotient of this\n to ensure extensionality.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.mk", "description": "The type of pre-sets in universe `u`. A pre-set\n is a family of pre-sets indexed by a type in `Type u`.\n The ZFC universe is defined as a quotient of this\n to ensure extensionality.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.equiv.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Class.mem_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Class.coe_powerset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.equiv.eq", "description": "Two pre-sets are equivalent iff they have the same members.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.subset", "description": " A pre-set is a subset of another pre-set if every element of the first family is extensionally\nequivalent to some element of the second family.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.embed", "description": "Embedding of one universe in another", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.type", "description": "The underlying type of a pre-set", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.has_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.has_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.pair", "description": "Kuratowski ordered pair", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.nonempty", "description": "A nonempty set is one that contains some element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Class", "description": " The collection of all classes.\n\nWe define `Class` as `set Set`, as this allows us to get many instances automatically. However, in\npractice, we treat it as (the definitionally equal) `Set \u2192 Prop`. This means, the preferred way to\nstate that `x : Set` belongs to `A : Class` is to write `A x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.mem_wf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.omega_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Class.has_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.insert_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.nonempty_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.choice_is_func", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.omega", "description": "The von Neumann ordinal \u03c9", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.image", "description": "The image of a (definable) ZFC set function", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.has_mem.mem.is_asymm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "arity_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.sUnion_lem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.definable.resp", "description": "Turns a definable function into a function that respects equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Class.has_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.resp.equiv.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.equiv.exists_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.prod", "description": "The cartesian product, `{(a, b) | a \u2208 x, b \u2208 y}`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.empty", "description": "The empty ZFC set", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Class.has_emptyc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.mem_sUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.has_well_founded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Class.coe_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.insert", "description": "`insert x y` is the set `{x} \u222a y`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.map_fval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.nonempty_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.resp.f", "description": " The `n`-ary image of a `(n + 1)`-ary function respecting equivalence as a function respecting\nequivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.func_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.mem_asymm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.nonempty_mk_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.is_lawful_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.map", "description": "Graph of a function: `map f x` is the ZFC function which maps `a \u2208 x` to `f a`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.map_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Class.mem_asymm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.sInter", "description": " The intersection operator, the collection of elements in all of the elements of a ZFC set. We\nspecial-case `\u22c2\u2080 \u2205 = \u2205`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.has_subset.subset.is_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.sep", "description": "`{x \u2208 a | p x}` is the set of elements in `a` satisfying `p`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.mem_irrefl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.inter", "description": "The binary intersection operation", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Class.iota_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.hereditarily.mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Class.sUnion_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.type.is_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.sep", "description": "The pre-set separation operation `{x \u2208 a | p x}`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Class.mem_irrefl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Class.sUnion", "description": "The union of a class is the class of all members of ZFC sets in the class", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.sUnion_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.pair_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Class.has_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.set.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Class.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.has_mem.mem.is_asymm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.choice_mem_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.not_mem_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.mem_sep", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.has_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.is_func", "description": " `is_func x y f` is the assertion that `f` is a subset of `x \u00d7 y` which relates to each element\nof `x` a unique element of `y`, so that we can consider `f`as a ZFC function `x \u2192 y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.equiv.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.has_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Class.fval", "description": "Function value", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pSet.resp.equiv", "description": "Function equivalence for functions respecting equivalence. See `pSet.arity.equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Class.coe_sep", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Set.mk", "description": "Turns a pre-set into a ZFC set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Class.coe_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_option", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_sigma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_fiberwise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_sum_type", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_option", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_univ_eq_sum_range", "description": "It is equivalent to sum a function over `fin n` or `finset.range n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.bijective.sum_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_pi_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sum_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_sum_elim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_sum_type", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_univ_pi", "description": "Taking a product over `univ.pi t` is the same as taking the product over `fintype.pi_finset t`.\n `univ.pi t` and `fintype.pi_finset t` are essentially the same `finset`, but differ\n in the type of their element, `univ.pi t` is a `finset (\u03a0 a \u2208 univ, t a)` and\n `fintype.pi_finset t` is a `finset (\u03a0 a, t a)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_fin_eq_prod_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_extend_by_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_bool", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.prod_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_fiberwise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "card_vector", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_fiberwise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.eq_of_subsingleton_of_prod_eq", "description": " If a product of a `finset` of a subsingleton type has a given\nvalue, so do the terms in that product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_univ_pi", "description": "Taking a sum over `univ.pi t` is the same as taking the sum over\n  `fintype.pi_finset t`. `univ.pi t` and `fintype.pi_finset t` are essentially the same `finset`,\n  but differ in the type of their element, `univ.pi t` is a `finset (\u03a0 a \u2208 univ, t a)` and\n  `fintype.pi_finset t` is a `finset (\u03a0 a, t a)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_univ_sum", "description": "The product over `univ` of a sum can be written as a sum over the product of sets,\n `fintype.pi_finset`. `finset.prod_sum` is an alternative statement when the product is not\n over `univ`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_to_finset_eq_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_eq_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_univ_eq_prod_range", "description": "It is equivalent to compute the product of a function over `fin n` or `finset.range n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_pow_mul_eq_add_pow", "description": " Summing `a^s.card * b^(n-s.card)` over all finite subsets `s` of a fintype of cardinality `n`\ngives `(a + b)^n`. The \"good\" proof involves expanding along all coordinates using the fact that\n`x^n` is multilinear, but multilinear maps are only available now over rings, so we give instead\na proof reducing to the usual binomial theorem to have a result over semirings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sum_comp'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_to_finset_eq_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_fiberwise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_bool", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_dite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_attach_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.bijective.prod_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_eq_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_sum_elim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_extend_by_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_fin_eq_sum_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_eq_sum_ones", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.prod_comp'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.eq_of_subsingleton_of_sum_eq", "description": "If a sum of a `finset` of a subsingleton type has a given\nvalue, so do the terms in that sum.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_eq_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_attach_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_eq_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unsigned_sz", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "unsigned", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "unsigned.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "unsigned.to_nat", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "unsigned.of_nat'", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.coe_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.continuous_open_map_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.comp", "description": "Composition of `continuous_open_map`s as a `continuous_open_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.has_coe_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.copy_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.cancel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.cancel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.copy", "description": " Copy of a `continuous_open_map` with a new `continuous_map` equal to the old one. Useful to fix\ndefinitional equalities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map_class", "description": " `continuous_open_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of continuous open maps.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `continuous_open_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map_class.coe", "description": " `continuous_open_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of continuous open maps.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `continuous_open_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map_class.coe_injective'", "description": " `continuous_open_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of continuous open maps.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `continuous_open_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map_class.map_continuous", "description": " `continuous_open_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of continuous open maps.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `continuous_open_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map_class.map_open", "description": " `continuous_open_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of continuous open maps.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `continuous_open_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.coe_copy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map_class.to_continuous_map_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.has_coe_to_fun", "description": " Helper instance for when there's too many metavariables to apply `fun_like.has_coe_to_fun`\ndirectly.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.id", "description": "`id` as a `continuous_open_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map", "description": "The type of continuous open maps from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2`, aka Priestley homomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.to_continuous_map", "description": "The type of continuous open maps from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2`, aka Priestley homomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.map_open'", "description": "The type of continuous open maps from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2`, aka Priestley homomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_open_map.comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.paste_vert_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.inr_iso_pushout_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.of_is_bilimit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.inl_iso_pushout_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.inl_snd'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.map", "description": "**Alias** of `category_theory.functor.map_is_pushout`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.zero_top", "description": "The square with `0 : 0 \u27f6 0` on the top and `\ud835\udfd9 X` on the bottom is a pushout square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.zero_top", "description": "The square with `0 : 0 \u27f6 0` on the top and `\ud835\udfd9 X` on the bottom is a pullback square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.of_is_bilimit'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.cone_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.of_has_binary_product", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.cocone_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.flip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.cocone_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.of_is_product'", "description": "A variant of `of_is_product` that is more useful with `apply`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.of_iso_pullback", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.paste_vert", "description": "Paste two pushout squares \"vertically\" to obtain another pushout square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.cocone", "description": "The (not necessarily limiting) `pushout_cocone f g` implicit in the statement\nthat we have `comm_sq f g h i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.of_has_binary_coproduct'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.paste_horiz", "description": "Paste two pushout squares \"horizontally\" to obtain another pushout square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.paste_vert_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.has_pushout_biprod_fst_biprod_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.cone_op", "description": " The pushout cocone in the opposite category associated to the cone of\na commutative square identifies to the cocone of the flipped commutative square in\nthe opposite category", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.of_map_of_faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.of_has_binary_biproduct", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicartesian_sq.of_has_biproduct\u2081", "description": "```lean\n X \u229e Y --fst--> X\n   |            |\n  snd           0\n   |            |\n   v            v\n   Y -----0---> 0\n```\nis a bicartesian square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.has_pullback_biprod_fst_biprod_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.cocone_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.cone_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicartesian_sq.flip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_is_pushout", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.cocone", "description": "The (colimiting) `pushout_cocone f g` implicit in the statement\nthat we have a `is_pushout f g inl inr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.cone_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.of_horiz_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback", "description": " The proposition that a square\n```lean\n  P --fst--> X\n  |          |\n snd         f\n  |          |\n  v          v\n  Y ---g---> Z\n\n```\nis a pullback square. (Also known as a fibered product or cartesian square.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.to_comm_sq", "description": " The proposition that a square\n```lean\n  P --fst--> X\n  |          |\n snd         f\n  |          |\n  v          v\n  Y ---g---> Z\n\n```\nis a pullback square. (Also known as a fibered product or cartesian square.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.is_limit'", "description": " The proposition that a square\n```lean\n  P --fst--> X\n  |          |\n snd         f\n  |          |\n  v          v\n  Y ---g---> Z\n\n```\nis a pullback square. (Also known as a fibered product or cartesian square.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.cone_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.of_bot", "description": " Given a pullback square assembled from a commuting square on the top and\na pullback square on the bottom, the top square is a pullback square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.paste_horiz", "description": "Paste two pullback squares \"horizontally\" to obtain another pullback square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.pushout_biprod_fst_biprod_snd", "description": "The pushout of `biprod.fst` and `biprod.snd` is the zero object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.iso_pullback_hom_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.inl_snd", "description": "The square\n```lean\n  X --inl--> X \u229e Y\n  |            |\n  0           snd\n  |            |\n  v            v\n  0 ---0-----> Y\n```\nis a pullback square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.of_bot", "description": " Given a pushout square assembled from a pushout square on the top and\na commuting square on the bottom, the bottom square is a pushout square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.iso_pushout", "description": " Any object at the top left of a pullback square is\nisomorphic to the pullback provided by the `has_limit` API.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.of_vert_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicartesian_sq.of_is_pullback_is_pushout", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.paste_horiz_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicartesian_sq.to_is_pullback", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.inr_fst'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.of_right", "description": " Given a pushout square assembled from a pushout square on the left and\na commuting square on the right, the right square is a pushout square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.zero_right", "description": "The square with `0 : 0 \u27f6 0` on the right and `\ud835\udfd9 X` on the left is a pushout square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.inr_fst", "description": "The square\n```lean\n  Y --inr--> X \u229e Y\n  |            |\n  0           fst\n  |            |\n  v            v\n  0 ---0-----> X\n```\nis a pushout square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.map_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.zero_bot", "description": "The square with `0 : 0 \u27f6 0` on the bottom and `\ud835\udfd9 X` on the top is a pushout square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicartesian_sq.to_is_pushout", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.zero_bot", "description": "The square with `0 : 0 \u27f6 0` on the bottom and `\ud835\udfd9 X` on the top is a pullback square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.of_vert_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_is_pullback", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.paste_vert", "description": "Paste two pullback squares \"vertically\" to obtain another pullback square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.of_has_binary_product'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.iso_pullback_hom_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.of_right", "description": " Given a pullback square assembled from a commuting square on the left and\na pullback square on the right, the left square is a pullback square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.cocone_op", "description": " The pullback cone in the opposite category associated to the cocone of\na commutative square identifies to the cone of the flipped commutative square in\nthe opposite category", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.flip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.of_is_coproduct", "description": " If `c` is a colimiting binary coproduct cocone, and we have an initial object,\nthen we have `is_pushout 0 0 c.inl c.inr`\n(where each `0` is the unique morphism from the initial object).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.map", "description": "**Alias** of `category_theory.functor.map_is_pullback`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.of_has_pullback", "description": "The pullback provided by `has_pullback f g` fits into a `is_pullback`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.of_has_pushout", "description": "The pushout provided by `has_pushout f g` fits into a `is_pushout`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.of_is_colimit", "description": "If `c` is a colimiting pushout cocone, then we have a `is_pushout f g c.inl c.inr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.is_limit", "description": "The cone obtained from `is_pullback fst snd f g` is a limit cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.map_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.zero_left", "description": "The square with `0 : 0 \u27f6 0` on the right left `\ud835\udfd9 X` on the right is a pushout square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.iso_pullback_inv_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.of_is_coproduct'", "description": "A variant of `of_is_coproduct` that is more useful with `apply`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.of_horiz_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.of_has_binary_coproduct", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.cone_unop", "description": " The pushout cocone obtained from the pullback cone associated to a\ncommutative square in the opposite category identifies to the cocone associated\nto the flipped square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.iso_pullback_inv_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicartesian_sq.of_is_biproduct\u2082", "description": "```lean\n   0 -----0---> X\n   |            |\n   0           inl\n   |            |\n   v            v\n   Y --inr--> X \u229e Y\n```\nis a bicartesian square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicartesian_sq.of_has_biproduct\u2082", "description": "```lean\n   0 -----0---> X\n   |            |\n   0           inl\n   |            |\n   v            v\n   Y --inr--> X \u229e Y\n```\nis a bicartesian square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.zero_right", "description": "The square with `0 : 0 \u27f6 0` on the right and `\ud835\udfd9 X` on the left is a pullback square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.of_has_biproduct", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout", "description": " The proposition that a square\n```lean\n  Z ---f---> X\n  |          |\n  g         inl\n  |          |\n  v          v\n  Y --inr--> P\n\n```\nis a pushout square. (Also known as a fiber coproduct or cocartesian square.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.to_comm_sq", "description": " The proposition that a square\n```lean\n  Z ---f---> X\n  |          |\n  g         inl\n  |          |\n  v          v\n  Y --inr--> P\n\n```\nis a pushout square. (Also known as a fiber coproduct or cocartesian square.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.is_colimit'", "description": " The proposition that a square\n```lean\n  Z ---f---> X\n  |          |\n  g         inl\n  |          |\n  v          v\n  Y --inr--> P\n\n```\nis a pushout square. (Also known as a fiber coproduct or cocartesian square.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.flip_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicartesian_sq.of_is_biproduct\u2081", "description": "```lean\n X \u229e Y --fst--> X\n   |            |\n  snd           0\n   |            |\n   v            v\n   Y -----0---> 0\n```\nis a bicartesian square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.of_is_bilimit'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.of_iso_pushout", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.pullback_biprod_inl_biprod_inr", "description": "The pullback of `biprod.inl` and `biprod.inr` is the zero object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.cocone_unop", "description": " The pullback cone obtained from the pushout cone associated to a\ncommutative square in the opposite category identifies to the cone associated\nto the flipped square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.inr_fst'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.of_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.inl_snd'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.of_is_limit", "description": "If `c` is a limiting pullback cone, then we have a `is_pullback c.fst c.snd f g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.cone", "description": "The (not necessarily limiting) `pullback_cone h i` implicit in the statement\nthat we have `comm_sq f g h i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.iso_pullback", "description": " Any object at the top left of a pullback square is\nisomorphic to the pullback provided by the `has_limit` API.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.of_is_limit'", "description": "A variant of `of_is_limit` that is more useful with `apply`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.of_is_colimit'", "description": "A variant of `of_is_colimit` that is more useful with `apply`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.flip_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.of_has_biproduct", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.of_has_binary_biproduct", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.zero_left", "description": "The square with `0 : 0 \u27f6 0` on the left and `\ud835\udfd9 X` on the right is a pullback square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.paste_horiz_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.of_map_of_faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.inr_fst", "description": "The square\n```lean\n  Y --inr--> X \u229e Y\n  |            |\n  0           fst\n  |            |\n  v            v\n  0 ---0-----> X\n```\nis a pullback square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.cocone_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicartesian_sq", "description": " A *bicartesian* square is a commutative square\n```lean\n  W ---f---> X\n  |          |\n  g          h\n  |          |\n  v          v\n  Y ---i---> Z\n\n```\nthat is both a pullback square and a pushout square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bicartesian_sq.mk", "description": " A *bicartesian* square is a commutative square\n```lean\n  W ---f---> X\n  |          |\n  g          h\n  |          |\n  v          v\n  Y ---i---> Z\n\n```\nthat is both a pullback square and a pushout square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.cone", "description": "The (limiting) `pullback_cone f g` implicit in the statement\nthat we have a `is_pullback fst snd f g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.of_is_bilimit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.inl_iso_pushout_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.of_is_product", "description": " If `c` is a limiting binary product cone, and we have a terminal object,\nthen we have `is_pullback c.fst c.snd 0 0`\n(where each `0` is the unique morphism to the terminal object).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.of_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.is_limit_fork", "description": " If `f : X \u27f6 Y`, `g g' : Y \u27f6 Z` forms a pullback square, then `f` is the equalizer of\n`g` and `g'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.is_limit_fork", "description": " If `f f' : X \u27f6 Y`, `g : Y \u27f6 Z` forms a pushout square, then `g` is the coequalizer of\n`f` and `f'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.inl_snd", "description": "The square\n```lean\n  X --inl--> X \u229e Y\n  |            |\n  0           snd\n  |            |\n  v            v\n  0 ---0-----> Y\n```\nis a pushout square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pullback.op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.inr_iso_pushout_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_pushout.is_colimit", "description": "The cocone obtained from `is_pushout f g inl inr` is a colimit cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.leibniz_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.has_coe_to_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.leibniz_of_mul_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.map_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.congr_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.restrict_scalars", "description": " If `A` is both an `R`-algebra and an `S`-algebra; `M` is both an `R`-module and an `S`-module,\nthen an `S`-derivation `A \u2192 M` is also an `R`-derivation if it is also `R`-linear.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.coe_mk'_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.has_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.coe_fn_add_monoid_hom", "description": "`coe_fn` as an `add_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.add_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.eq_on_adjoin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.neg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.coe_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.map_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.coe_smul_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.to_linear_map_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.coe_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.coe_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.map_one_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.llcomp", "description": "The composition of a derivation with a linear map as a bilinear map", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.coe_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.coe_add_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.coe_neg_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.ext_of_adjoin_eq_top", "description": " If adjoin of a set is the whole algebra, then any two derivations equal on this set are equal\non the whole algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.leibniz", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.map_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.leibniz_inv_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.coe_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.map_coe_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.coe_fn_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.mk'", "description": " Define `derivation R A M` from a linear map when `M` is cancellative by verifying the Leibniz\nrule.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.has_coe_to_fun", "description": " Helper instance for when there's too many metavariables to apply `fun_like.has_coe_to_fun`\ndirectly.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.coe_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.coe_sub_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.is_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.map_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.coe_to_linear_map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.map_smul_of_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation", "description": " `D : derivation R A M` is an `R`-linear map from `A` to `M` that satisfies the `leibniz`\nequality. We also require that `D 1 = 0`. See `derivation.mk'` for a constructor that deduces this\nassumption from the Leibniz rule when `M` is cancellative.\n\nTODO: update this when bimodules are defined.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.to_linear_map", "description": " `D : derivation R A M` is an `R`-linear map from `A` to `M` that satisfies the `leibniz`\nequality. We also require that `D 1 = 0`. See `derivation.mk'` for a constructor that deduces this\nassumption from the Leibniz rule when `M` is cancellative.\n\nTODO: update this when bimodules are defined.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.map_one_eq_zero'", "description": " `D : derivation R A M` is an `R`-linear map from `A` to `M` that satisfies the `leibniz`\nequality. We also require that `D 1 = 0`. See `derivation.mk'` for a constructor that deduces this\nassumption from the Leibniz rule when `M` is cancellative.\n\nTODO: update this when bimodules are defined.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.leibniz'", "description": " `D : derivation R A M` is an `R`-linear map from `A` to `M` that satisfies the `leibniz`\nequality. We also require that `D 1 = 0`. See `derivation.mk'` for a constructor that deduces this\nassumption from the Leibniz rule when `M` is cancellative.\n\nTODO: update this when bimodules are defined.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.sub_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.coe_zero_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.comp_der", "description": " We can push forward derivations using linear maps, i.e., the composition of a derivation with a\nlinear map is a derivation. Furthermore, this operation is linear on the spaces of derivations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.smul_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.map_coe_int", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.comp_der", "description": "Pushing a derivation foward through a linear equivalence is an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.leibniz_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.llcomp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.add_monoid_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_injective_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.sum_diff_subset_apply_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.univ_pi", "description": "The set `set.pi set.univ s` is equivalent to `\u03a0 a, s a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set_prod_equiv_sigma", "description": "A set `s` in `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2` is equivalent to the sigma-type `\u03a3 x, {y | (x, y) \u2208 s}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_injective", "description": "If `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is an injective function, then domain `\u03b1` is equivalent to the range of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.sum_diff_subset_symm_apply_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.congr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.range_eq_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.subset_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.of_eq_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_preimage_equiv", "description": "A family of equivalences between preimages of points gives an equivalence between domains.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.univ_pi_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_left_inverse_eq_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.sum_compl_apply_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.preimage_pi_equiv_pi_subtype_prod_symm_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.insert_apply_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.union_sum_inter", "description": " If `s` is a set with decidable membership, then the sum of `s \u222a t` and `s \u2229 t` is equivalent\nto `s \u2295 t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.insert", "description": "If `a \u2209 s`, then `insert a s` is equivalent to `s \u2295 punit`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_preimage_equiv_symm_apply_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.sum_compl_symm_apply_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.image_eq_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.union'", "description": " If sets `s` and `t` are separated by a decidable predicate, then `s \u222a t` is equivalent to\n`s \u2295 t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.eq_preimage_iff_image_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.empty", "description": "An empty set is equivalent to the `empty` type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.image_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.image_symm_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.sum_compl_symm_apply_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.symm_preimage_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_left_inverse_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.self_comp_of_injective_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_preimage_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.image_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.image_of_inj_on", "description": "If a function `f` is injective on a set `s`, then `s` is equivalent to `f '' s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.congr", "description": "If `\u03b1` is equivalent to `\u03b2`, then `set \u03b1` is equivalent to `set \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_equiv_eq_preimage_symm", "description": "Alias for `equiv.image_eq_preimage`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.powerset", "description": "The set `\ud835\udcab S := {x | x \u2286 S}` is equivalent to the type `set S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.insert_symm_apply_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.singleton", "description": "A singleton set is equivalent to a `punit` type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_injective_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.congr_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_preimage_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_preimage_equiv", "description": " `sigma_fiber_equiv f` for `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is the natural equivalence between\nthe type of all preimages of points under `f` and the total space `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.image_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.range_splitting_image_equiv_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_left_inverse'_eq_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.image", "description": "If `f` is an injective function, then `s` is equivalent to `f '' s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.range_splitting_image_equiv", "description": "If `s` is a set in `range f`,\nthen its image under `range_splitting f` is in bijection (via `f`) with `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_preimage_equiv_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.insert_apply_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.preimage_eq_iff_eq_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.pempty", "description": "An empty set is equivalent to a `pempty` type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dite_comp_equiv_update", "description": " The composition of an updated function with an equiv on a subset can be expressed as an\nupdated function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.union_symm_apply_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.image", "description": "A set is equivalent to its image under an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.prod_assoc_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.bij_on.equiv", "description": " If a function is a bijection between two sets `s` and `t`, then it induces an\nequivalence between the types `\u21a5s` and `\u21a5t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.image_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.univ_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.symm_image_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.prod", "description": "The set product of two sets is equivalent to the type product of their coercions to types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.univ", "description": "`univ \u03b1` is equivalent to `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_preimage_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.apply_of_injective_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_left_inverse", "description": " If `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` has a left-inverse when `\u03b1` is nonempty, then `\u03b1` is computably equivalent to the\nrange of `f`.\n\nWhile awkward, the `nonempty \u03b1` hypothesis on `f_inv` and `hf` allows this to be used when `\u03b1` is\nempty too. This hypothesis is absent on analogous definitions on stronger `equiv`s like\n`linear_equiv.of_left_inverse` and `ring_equiv.of_left_inverse` as their typeclass assumptions\nare already sufficient to ensure non-emptiness.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.preimage_symm_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.range_splitting_image_equiv_apply_coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.sum_diff_subset_apply_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.sum_compl_symm_apply_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.univ_pi_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.preimage_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.union_symm_apply_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.eq_image_iff_symm_image_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.prod_assoc_symm_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.union_apply_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.image_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.sum_diff_subset_symm_apply_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.image_symm_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set_congr", "description": "The subtypes corresponding to equal sets are equivalent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.union_apply_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.sum_compl_apply_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.mem_image_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_equiv_eq_image_symm", "description": "Alias for `equiv.image_eq_preimage`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.of_eq", "description": " Equal sets are equivalent.\n\nTODO: this is the same as `equiv.set_congr`!", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.image_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.coe_of_injective_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set_forall_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.preimage_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.of_eq_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_left_inverse_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.univ_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sigma_preimage_equiv_symm_apply_snd_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.sum_compl_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.union", "description": "If sets `s` and `t` are disjoint, then `s \u222a t` is equivalent to `s \u2295 t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.sep", "description": "The set `{x \u2208 s | t x}` is equivalent to the set of `x : s` such that `t x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.sum_diff_subset", "description": " `sum_diff_subset s t` is the natural equivalence between\n`s \u2295 (t \\ s)` and `t`, where `s` and `t` are two sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.insert_symm_apply_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.prod_assoc_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.prod_assoc_symm_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set_congr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.sum_compl", "description": "If `s : set \u03b1` is a set with decidable membership, then `s \u2295 s\u1d9c` is equivalent to `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.image_eq_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.subset_image'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.image_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_left_inverse'", "description": " If `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` has a left-inverse, then `\u03b1` is computably equivalent to the range of `f`.\n\nNote that if `\u03b1` is empty, no such `f_inv` exists and so this definition can't be used, unlike\nthe stronger but less convenient `of_left_inverse`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.set.compl", "description": " Given an equivalence `e\u2080` between sets `s : set \u03b1` and `t : set \u03b2`, the set of equivalences\n`e : \u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2` such that `e \u2191x = \u2191(e\u2080 x)` for each `x : s` is equivalent to the set of equivalences\nbetween `s\u1d9c` and `t\u1d9c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.dist_sq_eq_dist_sq_add_dist_sq_iff_angle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": "**Pythagorean theorem**, if-and-only-if angle-at-point form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.sin_angle_add_of_inner_eq_zero", "description": "The sine of an angle in a right-angled triangle as a ratio of sides.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.tan_angle_add_mul_norm_of_inner_eq_zero", "description": " The tangent of an angle in a right-angled triangle multiplied by the adjacent side equals\nthe opposite side.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_lt_pi_div_two_of_angle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": "An angle in a non-degenerate right-angled triangle is less than `\u03c0 / 2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_add_le_pi_div_two_of_inner_eq_zero", "description": "An angle in a right-angled triangle is at most `\u03c0 / 2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.dist_div_tan_angle_of_angle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": " A side of a right-angled triangle divided by the tangent of the opposite angle equals the\nadjacent side.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_add_eq_arcsin_of_inner_eq_zero", "description": "An angle in a right-angled triangle expressed using `arcsin`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.tan_angle_add_of_inner_eq_zero", "description": "The tangent of an angle in a right-angled triangle as a ratio of sides.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.cos_angle_of_angle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": "The cosine of an angle in a right-angled triangle as a ratio of sides.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.norm_div_sin_angle_add_of_inner_eq_zero", "description": " A side of a right-angled triangle divided by the sine of the opposite angle equals the\nhypotenuse.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_sub_pos_of_inner_eq_zero", "description": " An angle in a non-degenerate right-angled triangle is positive, version subtracting\nvectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.norm_sub_sq_eq_norm_sq_add_norm_sq'", "description": "Pythagorean theorem, subtracting vectors, vector angle form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.norm_div_tan_angle_sub_of_inner_eq_zero", "description": " A side of a right-angled triangle divided by the tangent of the opposite angle equals the\nadjacent side, version subtracting vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_sub_eq_arcsin_of_inner_eq_zero", "description": "An angle in a right-angled triangle expressed using `arcsi