ack", "description": "Pull back a term of `meq P S` with respect to a morphism `f : Y \u27f6 X` in `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.sheafification", "description": " The sheafification of a presheaf `P`, as a functor.\n*NOTE:* Additional hypotheses are needed to obtain a proof that this is a sheaf!", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.sheafify_lift", "description": " Given a sheaf `Q` and a morphism `P \u27f6 Q`, construct a morphism from\n`J.sheafifcation P` to `Q`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.to_sheafify_sheafify_lift_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.to_sheafification", "description": " The canonical map from `P` to its sheafification, as a natural transformation.\n*Note:* We only show this is a sheaf under additional hypotheses on `D`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.to_sheafify", "description": "The canonical map from `P` to its sheafification.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sheafification_adjunction", "description": "The sheafification functor is left adjoint to the forgetful functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.sheafification_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.sheafify_map_sheafify_lift_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.plus.sep", "description": "`P\u207a` is always separated.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.sheafify_lift_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.meq.equiv", "description": "The equivalence between the type associated to `multiequalizer (S.index P)` and `meq P S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.plus.is_sheaf_of_sep", "description": "If `P` is separated, then `P\u207a` is a sheaf.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.plus.inj_of_sep", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sheafification_iso", "description": "A sheaf `P` is isomorphic to its own sheafification.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.plus.exists_rep", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.sheafify_map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.to_sheafify_sheafify_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.meq.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.sheafify", "description": " The sheafification of a presheaf `P`.\n*NOTE:* Additional hypotheses are needed to obtain a proof that this is a sheaf!", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.plus.to_plus_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.meq.refine_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.meq.mk", "description": "Make a term of `meq P S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.to_sheafify_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presheaf_to_Sheaf", "description": "The sheafification functor, as a functor taking values in `Sheaf`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.sheafification_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.plus.res_mk_eq_mk_pullback", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.plus.is_sheaf_plus_plus", "description": "`P\u207a\u207a` is always a sheaf.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.sheafify_map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presheaf_to_Sheaf_preserves_zero_morphisms", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.rotation_rotation", "description": "Rotating twice is equivalent to rotating by the sum of the angles.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.rotation_aux", "description": "Auxiliary construction to build a rotation by the oriented angle `\u03b8`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_rotation_self_left", "description": "The rotation of a vector by `\u03b8` has an angle of `-\u03b8` from that vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.rotation_trans", "description": "Rotating twice is equivalent to rotating by the sum of the angles.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.rotation", "description": "A rotation by the oriented angle `\u03b8`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_eq_iff_eq_pos_smul_rotation_or_eq_zero", "description": " The angle between two vectors is `\u03b8` if and only if they are nonzero and the second vector\nis the first rotated by `\u03b8` and scaled by a positive real, or `\u03b8` and at least one of the\nvectors are zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.kahler_rotation_right", "description": "Rotating the second of two vectors by `\u03b8` scales their Kahler form by `cos \u03b8 + sin \u03b8 * I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_rotation_left", "description": "Rotating the first vector by `\u03b8` subtracts `\u03b8` from the angle between two vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.rotation_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_smul_rotation_pi_div_two_left", "description": " The inner product between a multiple of a `\u03c0 / 2` rotation of a vector and that vector is\nzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.rotation_pi_apply", "description": "Rotation by \u03c0 is negation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_eq_iff_eq_norm_div_norm_smul_rotation_of_ne_zero", "description": " The angle between two nonzero vectors is `\u03b8` if and only if the second vector is the first\nrotated by `\u03b8` and scaled by the ratio of the norms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.rotation_pi_div_two", "description": "Rotation by \u03c0 / 2 is the \"right-angle-rotation\" map `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.rotation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_smul_rotation_pi_div_two_right", "description": " The inner product between a vector and a multiple of a `\u03c0 / 2` rotation of that vector is\nzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.rotation_eq_self_iff", "description": "A rotation of a vector equals that vector if and only if the vector or the angle is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_rotation_right", "description": "Rotating the second vector by `\u03b8` adds `\u03b8` to the angle between two vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_rotation_self_right", "description": "A vector has an angle of `\u03b8` from the rotation of that vector by `\u03b8`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_eq_iff_eq_norm_div_norm_smul_rotation_or_eq_zero", "description": " The angle between two vectors is `\u03b8` if and only if they are nonzero and the second vector\nis the first rotated by `\u03b8` and scaled by the ratio of the norms, or `\u03b8` and at least one of the\nvectors are zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.neg_rotation_pi_div_two", "description": "Negating a rotation by \u03c0 / 2 is equivalent to rotation by -\u03c0 / 2.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.exists_linear_isometry_equiv_eq_of_det_pos", "description": "Any linear isometric equivalence in `V` with positive determinant is `rotation`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_rotation_pi_div_two_right_smul", "description": " The inner product between a multiple of a vector and a `\u03c0 / 2` rotation of that vector is\nzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_rotation_pi_div_two_left", "description": "The inner product between a `\u03c0 / 2` rotation of a vector and that vector is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.rotation_oangle_eq_iff_norm_eq", "description": " Rotating a vector by the angle to another vector gives the second vector if and only if the\nnorms are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.eq_rotation_self_iff_angle_eq_zero", "description": "A nonzero vector equals a rotation of that vector if and only if the angle is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.kahler_rotation_left'", "description": "Rotating the first of two vectors by `\u03b8` scales their Kahler form by `cos (-\u03b8) + sin (-\u03b8) * I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_rotation_oangle_right", "description": " Rotating the first vector by the angle between the two vectors and swapping the vectors\nresults an an angle of 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_smul_rotation_pi_div_two_smul_left", "description": " The inner product between a multiple of a `\u03c0 / 2` rotation of a vector and a multiple of\nthat vector is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.rotation_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.rotation_aux_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_smul_rotation_pi_div_two_smul_right", "description": " The inner product between a multiple of a vector and a multiple of a `\u03c0 / 2` rotation of\nthat vector is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.neg_rotation_neg_pi_div_two", "description": "Negating a rotation by -\u03c0 / 2 is equivalent to rotation by \u03c0 / 2.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.rotation_eq_self_iff_angle_eq_zero", "description": "A rotation of a nonzero vector equals that vector if and only if the angle is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.rotation_neg_orientation_eq_neg", "description": "Negating the orientation negates the angle in `rotation`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.neg_rotation", "description": "Negating a rotation is equivalent to rotation by \u03c0 plus the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_rotation_pi_div_two_left_smul", "description": " The inner product between a `\u03c0 / 2` rotation of a vector and a multiple of that vector is\nzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.linear_equiv_det_rotation", "description": "The determinant of `rotation` (as a linear equiv) is equal to `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.rotation_zero", "description": "Rotation by 0 is the identity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.rotation_eq_matrix_to_lin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_eq_iff_eq_pos_smul_rotation_of_ne_zero", "description": " The angle between two nonzero vectors is `\u03b8` if and only if the second vector is the first\nrotated by `\u03b8` and scaled by a positive real.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_rotation", "description": "Rotating both vectors by the same angle does not change the angle between those vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.rotation_pi", "description": "Rotation by \u03c0 is negation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_rotation_pi_div_two_right", "description": "The inner product between a vector and a `\u03c0 / 2` rotation of that vector is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.kahler_rotation_left", "description": "Rotating the first of two vectors by `\u03b8` scales their Kahler form by `cos \u03b8 - sin \u03b8 * I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_rotation_oangle_left", "description": "Rotating the first vector by the angle between the two vectors results an an angle of 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.rotation_symm", "description": "The inverse of `rotation` is rotation by the negation of the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.rotation_map_complex", "description": " Rotation in an oriented real inner product space of dimension 2 can be evaluated in terms of a\ncomplex-number representation of the space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.eq_rotation_self_iff", "description": "A vector equals a rotation of that vector if and only if the vector or the angle is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.rotation_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.det_rotation", "description": "The determinant of `rotation` (as a linear map) is equal to `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_eq_zero_iff_eq_zero_or_eq_smul_rotation_pi_div_two", "description": " The inner product between two vectors is zero if and only if the first vector is zero or\nthe second is a multiple of a `\u03c0 / 2` rotation of that vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_sup_union_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_inf_union_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_inf_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_sup_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_sup_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_inf_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_inf_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_truncated_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_inf_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_inf_sups", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.map_truncated_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_inf_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.map_truncated_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_inf_sups_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_inf_union_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_sup_union_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_sup_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_sup_infs_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.compl_truncated_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_sup", "description": "The infimum of the elements of `s` less than `a` if there are some, otherwise `\u22a4`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_inf_union_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.compl_truncated_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_inf", "description": "The infimum of the elements of `s` less than `a` if there are some, otherwise `\u22a5`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_sup_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_sup_infs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.truncated_sup_union_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_truncated_sup_union_add_card_truncated_sup_infs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.fst_iso_of_right_embedding_range_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_snd", "description": "The second projection from the pullback.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_fst_image_snd_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.fst_embedding_of_right_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_iso_prod_subtype_inv_snd_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_iso_prod_subtype_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_iso_prod_subtype_inv_fst_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_cone_is_limit", "description": "The constructed cone is a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.snd_embedding_of_left_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_iso_prod_subtype_inv_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.colimit_topology", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.snd_iso_of_left_embedding_range_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.colimit_is_open_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_iso_prod_subtype_hom_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.open_embedding_of_pullback_open_embeddings", "description": "If `X \u27f6 S`, `Y \u27f6 S` are open embeddings, then so is `X \u00d7\u209b Y \u27f6 S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_iso_prod_subtype", "description": "The pullback of two maps can be identified as a subspace of `X \u00d7 Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.range_pullback_to_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_iso_prod_subtype_inv_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.embedding_pullback_to_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_iso_prod_subtype_hom_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_map_open_embedding_of_open_embeddings", "description": "If there is a diagram where the morphisms `W \u27f6 Y` and `X \u27f6 Z` are open embeddings, and `S \u27f6 T`\nis mono, then the induced morphism `W \u00d7\u209b X \u27f6 Y \u00d7\u209c Z` is also an open embedding.\n  W  \u27f6  Y\n    \u2198      \u2198\n      S  \u27f6  T\n    \u2197       \u2197\n  X  \u27f6  Z", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_fst_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.embedding_of_pullback_embeddings", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.coequalizer_is_open_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.inducing_pullback_to_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.fst_open_embedding_of_right_open_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.coinduced_of_is_colimit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_map_embedding_of_embeddings", "description": "If there is a diagram where the morphisms `W \u27f6 Y` and `X \u27f6 Z` are embeddings,\nthen the induced morphism `W \u00d7\u209b X \u27f6 Y \u00d7\u209c Z` is also an embedding.\n\n  W  \u27f6  Y\n    \u2198      \u2198\n      S  \u27f6  T\n    \u2197      \u2197\n  X  \u27f6  Z", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_snd_image_fst_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_topology", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.snd_open_embedding_of_left_open_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_iso_prod_subtype_inv_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_fst", "description": "The first projection from the pullback.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_iso_prod_subtype_inv_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_snd_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.range_pullback_map", "description": "If the map `S \u27f6 T` is mono, then there is a description of the image of `W \u00d7\u209b X \u27f6 Y \u00d7\u209c Z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pullback_cone", "description": "The explicit pullback cone of `X, Y` given by `{ p : X \u00d7 Y // f p.1 = g p.2 }`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.star_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_rat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_semigroup_of_comm", "description": "Any commutative monoid admits the trivial `*`-structure.\n\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ring", "description": "A `*`-ring `R` is a (semi)ring with an involutive `star` operation which is additive\nwhich makes `R` with its multiplicative structure into a `*`-semigroup\n(i.e. `star (r * s) = star s * star r`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ring.to_star_semigroup", "description": "A `*`-ring `R` is a (semi)ring with an involutive `star` operation which is additive\nwhich makes `R` with its multiplicative structure into a `*`-semigroup\n(i.e. `star (r * s) = star s * star r`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ring.star_add", "description": "A `*`-ring `R` is a (semi)ring with an involutive `star` operation which is additive\nwhich makes `R` with its multiplicative structure into a `*`-semigroup\n(i.e. `star (r * s) = star s * star r`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ring_aut_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute_star_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_involutive_star", "description": "Typeclass for a star operation with is involutive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_involutive_star.to_has_star", "description": "Typeclass for a star operation with is involutive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_involutive_star.star_involutive", "description": "Typeclass for a star operation with is involutive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_div'", "description": "When multiplication is commutative, `star` preserves division.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semiconj_by.star_star_star", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `semiconj_by_star_star_star`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_hom_class", "description": "`star_hom_class F R S` states that `F` is a type of `star`-preserving maps from `R` to `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_hom_class.coe", "description": "`star_hom_class F R S` states that `F` is a type of `star`-preserving maps from `R` to `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_hom_class.coe_injective'", "description": "`star_hom_class F R S` states that `F` is a type of `star`-preserving maps from `R` to `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_hom_class.map_star", "description": "`star_hom_class F R S` states that `F` is a type of `star`-preserving maps from `R` to `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.star_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_mul_aut_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_div", "description": "When multiplication is commutative, `star` preserves division.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_inv'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_star", "description": "Notation typeclass (with no default notation!) for an algebraic structure with a star operation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_star.star", "description": "Notation typeclass (with no default notation!) for an algebraic structure with a star operation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ring_end_apply", "description": "This is not a simp lemma, since we usually want simp to keep `star_ring_end` bundled.\nFor example, for complex conjugation, we don't want simp to turn `conj x`\ninto the bare function `star x` automatically since most lemmas are about `conj x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.has_involutive_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_mul_equiv", "description": "`star` as an `mul_equiv` from `R` to `R\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_inv_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_semigroup.to_opposite_star_module", "description": " A commutative star monoid is a star module over its opposite via\n`monoid.to_opposite_mul_action`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_hom_class.to_fun_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.has_involutive_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_eq_iff_star_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ring_aut", "description": "`star` as a ring automorphism, for commutative `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.has_star", "description": "The opposite type carries the same star operation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "invertible.star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_bit1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_add_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ring_end_self_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_trivial_star", "description": "Typeclass for a trivial star operation. This is mostly meant for `\u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_trivial_star.star_trivial", "description": "Typeclass for a trivial star operation. This is mostly meant for `\u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_inv_pair.star_ring_end.ring_hom_inv_pair", "description": " Instance needed to define star-linear maps over a commutative star ring\n(ex: conjugate-linear maps when R = \u2102).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.star_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_id_of_comm", "description": "Note that since `star_semigroup_of_comm` is reducible, `simp` can already prove this.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.unop_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ring_of_comm", "description": "Any commutative semiring admits the trivial `*`-structure.\n\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_add_equiv", "description": "`star` as an `add_equiv`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semiconj_by_star_star_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.star", "description": "`star` as an equivalence when it is involutive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.coe_star_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_mul_aut", "description": "`star` as a `mul_aut` for commutative `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_semigroup.to_star_module", "description": "A commutative star monoid is a star module over itself via `monoid.to_mul_action`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.op_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_mul'", "description": "In a commutative ring, make `simp` prefer leaving the order unchanged.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_mul_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.star_star", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `commute_star_star`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ring_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_mul_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_star_of_eq_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_zpow\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_bit0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_mem_class", "description": "`star_mem_class S G` states `S` is a type of subsets `s \u2286 G` closed under star.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_mem_class.star_mem", "description": "`star_mem_class S G` states `S` is a type of subsets `s \u2286 G` closed under star.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_star_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.star_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_module", "description": "A star module `A` over a star ring `R` is a module which is a star add monoid,\nand the two star structures are compatible in the sense\n`star (r \u2022 a) = star r \u2022 star a`.\n\nNote that it is up to the user of this typeclass to enforce\n`[semiring R] [star_ring R] [add_comm_monoid A] [star_add_monoid A] [module R A]`, and that\nthe statement only requires `[has_star R] [has_star A] [has_smul R A]`.\n\nIf used as `[comm_ring R] [star_ring R] [semiring A] [star_ring A] [algebra R A]`, this represents a\nstar algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_module.star_smul", "description": "A star module `A` over a star ring `R` is a module which is a star add monoid,\nand the two star structures are compatible in the sense\n`star (r \u2022 a) = star r \u2022 star a`.\n\nNote that it is up to the user of this typeclass to enforce\n`[semiring R] [star_ring R] [add_comm_monoid A] [star_add_monoid A] [module R A]`, and that\nthe statement only requires `[has_star R] [has_star A] [has_smul R A]`.\n\nIf used as `[comm_ring R] [star_ring R] [semiring A] [star_ring A] [algebra R A]`, this represents a\nstar algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_mem_class.has_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.conj_conj", "description": "**Alias** of `star_ring_end_self_apply`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ring.to_star_add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.star_add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.coe_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ring_end", "description": " `star` as a ring endomorphism, for commutative `R`. This is used to denote complex\nconjugation, and is available under the notation `conj` in the locale `complex_conjugate`.\n\nNote that this is the preferred form (over `star_ring_aut`, available under the same hypotheses)\nbecause the notation `E \u2192\u2097\u22c6[R] F` for an `R`-conjugate-linear map (short for\n`E \u2192\u209b\u2097[star_ring_end R] F`) does not pretty-print if there is a coercion involved, as would be the\ncase for `(\u2191star_ring_aut : R \u2192* R)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute_star_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_star_iff_eq_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_semigroup", "description": "A `*`-semigroup is a semigroup `R` with an involutive operations `star`\nso `star (r * s) = star s * star r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_semigroup.to_has_involutive_star", "description": "A `*`-semigroup is a semigroup `R` with an involutive operations `star`\nso `star (r * s) = star s * star r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_semigroup.star_mul", "description": "A `*`-semigroup is a semigroup `R` with an involutive operations `star`\nso `star (r * s) = star s * star r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.inverse_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_add_monoid", "description": "A `*`-additive monoid `R` is an additive monoid with an involutive `star` operation which\npreserves addition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_add_monoid.to_has_involutive_star", "description": "A `*`-additive monoid `R` is an additive monoid with an involutive `star` operation which\npreserves addition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_add_monoid.star_add", "description": "A `*`-additive monoid `R` is an additive monoid with an involutive `star` operation which\npreserves addition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ring_equiv", "description": "`star` as an `ring_equiv` from `R` to `R\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.star_module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_R_or_C.conj_conj", "description": "**Alias** of `star_ring_end_self_apply`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.star_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic.coe_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_seq.norm_values_discrete", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic.has_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic.char_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_seq.norm_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic.coe_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_seq.lift_index_left_left", "description": "An auxiliary lemma for manipulating sequence indices.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_seq.norm_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_seq.norm_eq_of_add_equiv_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_seq.valuation", "description": " The `p`-adic valuation on `\u211a` lifts to `padi