 {"name": "padic_val_nat.prime_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_int.one", "description": "`padic_val_int p 1` is `0` for any `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_nat_primes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_int.of_ne_one_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_int_dvd_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_int_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_nat.one", "description": "`padic_val_nat p 1` is `0` for any `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_nat_def'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_nat.zero", "description": "`padic_val_nat p 0` is `0` for any `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_nat.self", "description": "If `p \u2260 0` and `p \u2260 1`, then `padic_val_rat p p` is `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_nat.div_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_rat.sum_pos_of_pos", "description": " A finite sum of rationals with positive `p`-adic valuation has positive `p`-adic valuation\n(if the sum is non-zero).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_int.self", "description": "If `p \u2260 0` and `p \u2260 1`, then `padic_val_int p p` is `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_rat.pow", "description": "A rewrite lemma for `padic_val_rat p (q^k)` with condition `q \u2260 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dvd_iff_padic_val_nat_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_nat.div", "description": "Dividing out by a prime factor reduces the `padic_val_nat` by `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_nat_dvd_iff_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_rat.of_int_multiplicity", "description": "The `p`-adic value of an integer `z \u2260 0` is the multiplicity of `p` in `z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_rat.le_padic_val_rat_add_of_le", "description": " Sufficient conditions to show that the `p`-adic valuation of `q` is less than or equal to the\n`p`-adic valuation of `q + r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_rat.of_nat", "description": "The `p`-adic value of an integer `z \u2260 0` is its `p`-adic value as a rational.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_nat_def", "description": " A simplification of `padic_val_nat` when one input is prime, by analogy with\n`padic_val_rat_def`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_nat_dvd_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_nat.div'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_nat.mul", "description": "A rewrite lemma for `padic_val_nat p (a * b)` with conditions `a \u2260 0`, `b \u2260 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_int.zero", "description": "`padic_val_int p 0` is `0` for any `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_int.of_nat", "description": "The `p`-adic value of a natural is its `p`-adic value as an integer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_nat_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_int.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_rat.multiplicity_sub_multiplicity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_nat.pow", "description": "A version of `padic_val_rat.pow` for `padic_val_nat`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dvd_of_one_le_padic_val_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_rat.neg", "description": "`padic_val_rat p q` is symmetric in `q`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_nat.eq_zero_of_not_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "range_pow_padic_val_nat_subset_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "range_pow_padic_val_nat_subset_divisors'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_le_padic_val_nat_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_nat.eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_rat.div", "description": "A rewrite lemma for `padic_val_rat p (q / r)` with conditions `q \u2260 0`, `r \u2260 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_int_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_rat.defn", "description": "A rewrite lemma for `padic_val_rat p q` when `q` is expressed in terms of `rat.mk`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_rat_of_nat", "description": "`padic_val_rat` coincides with `padic_val_nat`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_nat.div_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_rat.finite_int_prime_iff", "description": "The multiplicity of `p : \u2115` in `a : \u2124` is finite exactly when `a \u2260 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_rat.zero", "description": "`padic_val_rat p 0` is `0` for any `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_rat.one", "description": "`padic_val_rat p 1` is `0` for any `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_nat", "description": " For `p \u2260 1`, the `p`-adic valuation of a natural `n \u2260 0` is the largest natural number `k` such\nthat `p^k` divides `z`. If `n = 0` or `p = 1`, then `padic_val_nat p q` defaults to `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_rat", "description": " `padic_val_rat` defines the valuation of a rational `q` to be the valuation of `q.num` minus the\nvaluation of `q.denom`. If `q = 0` or `p = 1`, then `padic_val_rat p q` defaults to `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_rat.self", "description": "If `p \u2260 0` and `p \u2260 1`, then `padic_val_rat p p` is `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_rat.padic_val_rat_le_padic_val_rat_iff", "description": " A condition for `padic_val_rat p (n\u2081 / d\u2081) \u2264 padic_val_rat p (n\u2082 / d\u2082)`, in terms of\ndivisibility by `p^n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_rat.mul", "description": "A rewrite lemma for `padic_val_rat p (q * r)` with conditions `q \u2260 0`, `r \u2260 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_rat.of_int", "description": "The `p`-adic value of an integer `z \u2260 0` is its `p`-adic_value as a rational.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_int_mul_eq_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_val_rat.min_le_padic_val_rat_add", "description": "The minimum of the valuations of `q` and `r` is at most the valuation of `q + r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.fgModule_coevaluation_apply_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.category_theory.monoidal_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.category_theory.monoidal_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.to_fgModule_iso", "description": "Converts a `linear_equiv` to an isomorphism in the category `fgModule R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.of", "description": "Lift an unbundled finitely generated module to `fgModule R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.to_fgModule_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.fgModule_dual", "description": "The dual module is the dual in the rigid monoidal category `fgModule K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.category_theory.monoidal_linear", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.concrete_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.exact_pairing", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.forget\u2082_monoidal_linear", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.forget\u2082_monoidal", "description": "The forgetful functor `fgModule R \u2964 Module R` as a monoidal functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.category_theory.symmetric_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.forget\u2082_monoidal_additive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.forget\u2082_monoidal_faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.category_theory.monoidal_preadditive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.category_theory.linear", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.iso.conj_eq_conj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.fgModule_coevaluation", "description": "The coevaluation map is defined in `linear_algebra.coevaluation`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule", "description": "Define `fgModule` as the subtype of `Module.{u} R` of finitely generated modules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.fgModule_evaluation", "description": "The evaluation morphism is given by the contraction map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.category_theory.forget\u2082.category_theory.full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.preadditive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.iso_to_linear_equiv", "description": " Converts and isomorphism in the category `fgModule R` to a `linear_equiv` between the underlying\nmodules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.obj.module.finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.large_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.Module.category_theory.has_forget\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.monoidal_predicate_module_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.right_dual", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.right_rigid_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.fgModule_evaluation_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.ihom_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.quiver.hom.module.finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.to_fgModule_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fgModule.closed_predicate_module_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.to_karoubi_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.coe_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.coe_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.quiver.hom.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.to_karoubi", "description": " The obvious fully faithful functor `to_karoubi` sends an object `X : C` to the obvious\nformal direct factor of `X` given by `\ud835\udfd9 X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.decomp_id_p", "description": "The split epi which appears in the factorisation `decomp_id P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.quiver.hom.add_comm_group_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.decomp_id_i", "description": "The split mono which appears in the factorisation `decomp_id P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.p_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.to_karoubi_is_equivalence", "description": "If `C` is idempotent complete, the functor `to_karoubi : C \u2964 karoubi C` is an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.idem_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.comp_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.quiver.hom.add_comm_group_zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.quiver.hom.add_comm_group_zero_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.decomp_id_i_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.category_theory.is_idempotent_complete", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.coe", "description": " It is possible to coerce an object of `C` into an object of `karoubi C`.\nSee also the functor `to_karoubi`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.p_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.comp_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.to_karoubi_equivalence_functor_additive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.decomp_id_p_to_karoubi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.comp_p_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.hom.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.decomp_id_p_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.decomp_id_p_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.decomp_id_i_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.to_karoubi_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.sum_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.hom_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.inclusion_hom", "description": "The map sending `f : P \u27f6 Q` to `f.f : P.X \u27f6 Q.X` is additive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.quiver.hom.add_comm_group_add_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.eq_to_hom_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.id_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.decomp_id_i_to_karoubi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.comp_proof", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.to_karoubi.category_theory.functor.additive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi", "description": " In a preadditive category `C`, when an object `X` decomposes as `X \u2245 P \u2a3f Q`, one may\nconsider `P` as a direct factor of `X` and up to unique isomorphism, it is determined by the\nobvious idempotent `X \u27f6 P \u27f6 X` which is the projection onto `P` with kernel `Q`. More generally,\none may define a formal direct factor of an object `X : C` : it consists of an idempotent\n`p : X \u27f6 X` which is thought as the \"formal image\" of `p`. The type `karoubi C` shall be the\ntype of the objects of the karoubi enveloppe of `C`. It makes sense for any category `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.X", "description": " In a preadditive category `C`, when an object `X` decomposes as `X \u2245 P \u2a3f Q`, one may\nconsider `P` as a direct factor of `X` and up to unique isomorphism, it is determined by the\nobvious idempotent `X \u27f6 P \u27f6 X` which is the projection onto `P` with kernel `Q`. More generally,\none may define a formal direct factor of an object `X : C` : it consists of an idempotent\n`p : X \u27f6 X` which is thought as the \"formal image\" of `p`. The type `karoubi C` shall be the\ntype of the objects of the karoubi enveloppe of `C`. It makes sense for any category `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.p", "description": " In a preadditive category `C`, when an object `X` decomposes as `X \u2245 P \u2a3f Q`, one may\nconsider `P` as a direct factor of `X` and up to unique isomorphism, it is determined by the\nobvious idempotent `X \u27f6 P \u27f6 X` which is the projection onto `P` with kernel `Q`. More generally,\none may define a formal direct factor of an object `X : C` : it consists of an idempotent\n`p : X \u27f6 X` which is thought as the \"formal image\" of `p`. The type `karoubi C` shall be the\ntype of the objects of the karoubi enveloppe of `C`. It makes sense for any category `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.idem", "description": " In a preadditive category `C`, when an object `X` decomposes as `X \u2245 P \u2a3f Q`, one may\nconsider `P` as a direct factor of `X` and up to unique isomorphism, it is determined by the\nobvious idempotent `X \u27f6 P \u27f6 X` which is the projection onto `P` with kernel `Q`. More generally,\none may define a formal direct factor of an object `X : C` : it consists of an idempotent\n`p : X \u27f6 X` which is thought as the \"formal image\" of `p`. The type `karoubi C` shall be the\ntype of the objects of the karoubi enveloppe of `C`. It makes sense for any category `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.to_karoubi_obj_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.decomp_id", "description": " The formal direct factor of `P.X` given by the idempotent `P.p` in the category `C`\nis actually a direct factor in the category `karoubi C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.category_theory.category", "description": "The category structure on the karoubi envelope of a category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.quiver.hom.add_comm_group_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.hom", "description": " A morphism `P \u27f6 Q` in the category `karoubi C` is a morphism in the underlying category\n`C` which satisfies a relation, which in the preadditive case, expresses that it induces a\nmap between the corresponding \"formal direct factors\" and that it vanishes on the complement\nformal direct factor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.hom.f", "description": " A morphism `P \u27f6 Q` in the category `karoubi C` is a morphism in the underlying category\n`C` which satisfies a relation, which in the preadditive case, expresses that it induces a\nmap between the corresponding \"formal direct factors\" and that it vanishes on the complement\nformal direct factor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.hom.comm", "description": " A morphism `P \u27f6 Q` in the category `karoubi C` is a morphism in the underlying category\n`C` which satisfies a relation, which in the preadditive case, expresses that it induces a\nmap between the corresponding \"formal direct factors\" and that it vanishes on the complement\nformal direct factor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.inclusion_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.decomp_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.zsmul_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.to_karoubi.category_theory.faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.category_theory.preadditive", "description": "The category `karoubi C` is preadditive if `C` is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.quiver.hom.add_comm_group_neg_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.to_karoubi_equivalence", "description": "The equivalence `C \u2245 karoubi C` when `C` is idempotent complete.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.p_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.to_karoubi.category_theory.full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.to_karoubi.category_theory.ess_surj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.bot_lt_ker_of_det_eq_zero", "description": "If the determinant of a map vanishes, then the map is not injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_aux_def", "description": " Unfold lemma for `det_aux`.\n\nSee also `det_aux_def'` which allows you to vary the basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_to_matrix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.det_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_aux_def'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.det_reindex'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.det_reindex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.det_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.range_lt_top_of_det_eq_zero", "description": "If the determinant of a map vanishes, then the map is not onto.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.of_is_unit_det_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.det_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.is_unit_det", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.det_is_unit_smul", "description": "The determinant of a basis constructed by `is_unit_smul` is the product of the given units.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_to_lin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_cases", "description": "To show `P f.det` it suffices to consider `P (to_matrix _ _ f).det` and `P 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_basis_ne_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coe_det", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.det_conj", "description": "Conjugating a linear equiv by a linear equiv does not change its determinant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.det_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_conj", "description": "Conjugating a linear map by a linear equiv does not change its determinant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_aux_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.associated_det_of_eq_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.coe_inv_det", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.det_mul_det_symm", "description": "The determinants of a `linear_equiv` and its inverse multiply to 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.of_is_unit_det_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_eq_det_to_matrix_of_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_aux_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.det_units_smul_self", "description": "The determinant of a basis constructed by `units_smul` is the product of the given units.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.det", "description": "On a `linear_equiv`, the domain of `linear_map.det` can be promoted to `R\u02e3`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.of_is_unit_det", "description": "Builds a linear equivalence from a linear map whose determinant in some bases is a unit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_eq_one_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.det_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_smul", "description": "Multiplying a map by a scalar `c` multiplies its determinant by `c ^ dim M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.det_ne_zero", "description": "`basis.det` is not the zero map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.det_smul_mk_coord_eq_det_update", "description": " If we fix a background basis `e`, then for any other basis `v`, we can characterise the\ncoordinates provided by `v` in terms of determinants relative to `e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.det_coe_symm", "description": "The determinant of `f.symm` is the inverse of that of `f` when `f` is a linear equiv.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_basis_iff_det", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.basis_fun_det", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.det_is_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.is_unit_det'", "description": "Specialization of `linear_equiv.is_unit_det`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_aux", "description": " The determinant of an endomorphism given a basis.\n\nSee `linear_map.det` for a version that populates the basis non-computably.\n\nAlthough the `trunc (basis \u03b9 A M)` parameter makes it slightly more convenient to switch bases,\nthere is no good way to generalize over universe parameters, so we can't fully state in `det_aux`'s\ntype that it does not depend on the choice of basis. Instead you can use the `det_aux_def'` lemma,\nor avoid mentioning a basis at all using `linear_map.det`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.equiv_of_det_ne_zero", "description": " Builds a linear equivalence from a linear map on a finite-dimensional vector space whose\ndeterminant is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_to_matrix'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_to_lin'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.is_unit_det", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.associated_det_comp_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det", "description": " The determinant of an endomorphism independent of basis.\n\nIf there is no finite basis on `M`, the result is `1` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.finite_dimensional_of_det_ne_one", "description": "If a linear map has determinant different from `1`, then the space is finite-dimensional.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_comm'", "description": " If there exists a two-sided inverse `M'` for `M` (indexed differently),\nthen `det (N \u2b1d M) = det (M \u2b1d N)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.index_equiv_of_inv", "description": " If `M` and `M'` are each other's inverse matrices, they are square matrices up to\nequivalence of types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.det_units_smul", "description": " If a basis is multiplied columnwise by scalars `w : \u03b9 \u2192 R\u02e3`, then the determinant with respect\nto this basis is multiplied by the product of the inverse of these scalars.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.det_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.det_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.eq_smul_basis_det", "description": " Any alternating map to `R` where `\u03b9` has the cardinality of a basis equals the determinant\nmap with respect to that basis, multiplied by the value of that alternating map on that basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.det_comp_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.det_symm_mul_det", "description": "The determinants of a `linear_equiv` and its inverse multiply to 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_eq_one_of_finrank_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_zero", "description": " In a finite-dimensional vector space, the zero map has determinant `1` in dimension `0`,\nand `0` otherwise. We give a formula that also works in infinite dimension, where we define\nthe determinant to be `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_of_pi_lequiv_pi", "description": "If `R^m` and `R^n` are linearly equivalent, then `m` and `n` are also equivalent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_conj_of_mul_eq_one", "description": " If `M'` is a two-sided inverse for `M` (indexed differently), `det (M \u2b1d N \u2b1d M') = det N`.\n\nSee `matrix.det_conj` and `matrix.det_conj'` for the case when `M' = M\u207b\u00b9` or vice versa.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.coe_det", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_basis_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_to_matrix_eq_det_to_matrix", "description": "The determinant of `linear_map.to_matrix` does not depend on the choice of basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.coe_of_is_unit_det", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.det_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_unit_det", "description": "If a linear map is invertible, so is its determinant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.det_map'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.det", "description": " The determinant of a family of vectors with respect to some basis, as an alternating\nmultilinear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.det_reindex_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.generate_sets", "description": "`generate_sets g s`: `s` is in the filter closure of `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.generate_sets.basic", "description": "`generate_sets g s`: `s` is in the filter closure of `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.generate_sets.univ", "description": "`generate_sets g s`: `s` is in the filter closure of `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.generate_sets.superset", "description": "`generate_sets g s`: `s` is in the filter closure of `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.generate_sets.inter", "description": "`generate_sets g s`: `s` is in the filter closure of `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.principal_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.supr_sets_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.join", "description": "The join of a filter of filters is defined by the relation `s \u2208 join f \u2194 {t | s \u2208 t} \u2208 f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.mem_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.inter_mem_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.sup_join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.inf_principal_eq_bot_iff_com