_of_inj_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_inf_principal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_mem_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_eq_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_true", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.not_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.infi_ne_bot_of_directed'", "description": " If `f : \u03b9 \u2192 filter \u03b1` is directed, `\u03b9` is not empty, and `\u2200 i, f i \u2260 \u22a5`, then `infi f \u2260 \u22a5`.\nSee also `infi_ne_bot_of_directed` for a version assuming `nonempty \u03b1` instead of `nonempty \u03b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_eq.inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.inter_eventually_eq_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.comap_fst_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.sInter_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.inter_mem_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_le.mul_le_mul'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_eq_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.principal_eq_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.comap_ne_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.comap", "description": " The inverse map of a filter. A set `s` belongs to `filter.comap m f` if either of the following\nequivalent conditions hold.\n\n1. There exists a set `t \u2208 f` such that `m \u207b\u00b9' t \u2286 s`. This is used as a definition.\n2. The set `{y | \u2200 x, m x = y \u2192 x \u2208 s}` belongs to `f`, see `filter.mem_comap'`.\n3. The set `(m '' s\u1d9c)\u1d9c` belongs to `f`, see `filter.mem_comap_iff_compl` and\n`filter.compl_mem_comap`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.maps_to.tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_eq.filter_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.distrib_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.frequently.and_eventually", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.comap_ne_bot_iff_compl_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_functor_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_functor", "description": "Implementation of `sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_equalizer_products.diagram", "description": "The equalizer diagram for the sheaf condition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_equalizer_products.left_res", "description": "The morphism `\u03a0 F.obj (U i) \u27f6 \u03a0 F.obj (U i) \u2293 (U j)` whose components\nare given by the restriction maps from `U i` to `U i \u2293 U j`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_unit_iso_app", "description": "Implementation of `sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_unit_iso_app_inv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_counit_iso_inv_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.is_sheaf_equalizer_products", "description": "The sheaf condition for a `F : presheaf C X` requires that the morphism\n`F.obj U \u27f6 \u220f F.obj (U i)` (where `U` is some open set which is the union of the `U i`)\nis the equalizer of the two morphisms\n`\u220f F.obj (U i) \u27f6 \u220f F.obj (U i) \u2293 (U j)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_equalizer_products.fork.iso_of_iso", "description": "If `F G : presheaf C X` are isomorphic presheaves,\nthen the `fork F U`, the canonical cone of the sheaf condition diagram for `F`,\nis isomorphic to `fork F G` postcomposed with the corresponding isomorphism between\nsheaf condition diagrams.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_equalizer_products.fork_\u03c0_app_walking_parallel_pair_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_counit_iso_2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_equalizer_products.diagram.iso_of_iso", "description": "Isomorphic presheaves have isomorphic sheaf condition diagrams.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_functor_2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_equalizer_products.w_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_equalizer_products.res_\u03c0_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_equalizer_products.fork_\u03c0_app_walking_parallel_pair_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_inverse_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.is_sheaf_iff_is_sheaf_equalizer_products", "description": "The sheaf condition in terms of an equalizer diagram is equivalent\nto the default sheaf condition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_equalizer_products.pi_inters", "description": "The product of the sections of a presheaf over the pairwise intersections of\na family of open sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_equalizer_products.pi_opens.iso_of_iso", "description": "Isomorphic presheaves have isomorphic `pi_opens` for any cover `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_inverse", "description": "Implementation of `sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_equalizer_products.pi_opens", "description": "The product of the sections of a presheaf over a family of open sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_functor_obj_2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.is_limit_sheaf_condition_fork_of_is_limit_map_cone", "description": "If `F.map_cone (cone U)` is a limit cone,\nthen `sheaf_condition_equalizer_products.fork` is an equalizer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_counit_iso", "description": "Implementation of `sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_unit_iso_inv_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_equalizer_products.fork_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv", "description": "Cones over `diagram U \u22d9 F` are the same as a cones over the usual sheaf condition equalizer diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_equalizer_products.res_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_inverse_obj_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_equalizer_products.fork", "description": "The restriction map `F.obj U \u27f6 \u03a0 F.obj (U i)` gives a cone over the equalizer diagram\nfor the sheaf condition. The sheaf condition asserts this cone is a limit cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_unit_iso_app_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_equalizer_products.res", "description": "The morphism `F.obj U \u27f6 \u03a0 F.obj (U i)` whose components\nare given by the restriction maps from `U j` to `U i \u2293 U j`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_unit_iso_2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_equalizer_products.fork_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.is_limit_map_cone_of_is_limit_sheaf_condition_fork", "description": "If `sheaf_condition_equalizer_products.fork` is an equalizer,\nthen `F.map_cone (cone U)` is a limit cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_unit_iso_hom_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_counit_iso_hom_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_inverse_map_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_equalizer_products.right_res", "description": "The morphism `\u03a0 F.obj (U i) \u27f6 \u03a0 F.obj (U i) \u2293 (U j)` whose components\nare given by the restriction maps from `U j` to `U i \u2293 U j`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_inverse_2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_functor_obj_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_pairwise_intersections.cone_equiv_inverse_obj_2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition_equalizer_product