in that number.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.add_nat", "description": "`add_nat m i` adds `m` to `i`, generalizes `fin.succ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.succ_above_lt_iff", "description": " Embedding `i : fin n` into `fin (n + 1)` using a pivot `p` that is greater\nresults in a value that is less than `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.exists_succ_above_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.has_zero_of_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.forall_fin_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin_zero_elim", "description": "Elimination principle for the empty set `fin 0`, dependent version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.succ_lt_succ_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.coe_nat_eq_last", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.coe_of_injective_cast_succ_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.nat_add", "description": "`nat_add n i` adds `n` to `i` \"on the left\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.succ_rec", "description": " Define `C n i` by induction on `i : fin n` interpreted as `(0 : fin (n - i)).succ.succ\u2026`.\nThis function has two arguments: `H0 n` defines `0`-th element `C (n+1) 0` of an `(n+1)`-tuple,\nand `Hs n i` defines `(i+1)`-st element of `(n+1)`-tuple based on `n`, `i`, and `i`-th element\nof `n`-tuple.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.strict_anti_iff_succ_lt", "description": " A function `f` on `fin (n + 1)` is strictly antitone if and only if `f (i + 1) < f i`\nfor all `i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.cast_le", "description": "`cast_le h i` embeds `i` into a larger `fin` type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.succ_succ_above_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.coe_one'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.cast_succ_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.cast_eq_cast", "description": " While in many cases `fin.cast` is better than `equiv.cast`/`cast`, sometimes we want to