", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prime_spectrum.closed_embedding_comap_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prime_spectrum.zero_locus_singleton_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prime_spectrum.compact_space", "description": "The prime spectrum of a commutative ring is a compact topological space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.constant_coeff_witt_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.add_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_zsmul_vars", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_add", "description": "The polynomials used for defining the addition of the ring of Witt vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.has_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.nsmul_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.v2_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_neg_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.add_coeff_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_pow_vars", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.constant_coeff_witt_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.has_nat_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_neg_vars", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_sub_vars", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.coeff_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_one_pos_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_nsmul", "description": "The polynomials used for defining repeated addition of the ring of Witt vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.zsmul_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.one_coeff_eq_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.mul_coeff_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_mul", "description": "The polynomials used for defining the multiplication of the ring of Witt vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.mul_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.constant_coeff_witt_zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_nsmul_vars", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.constant_coeff_witt_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_mul_vars", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.eval", "description": "Let `\u03c6` be a family of polynomials, indexed by natural numbers, whose variables come from the\ndisjoint union of `k` copies of `\u2115`, and let `x\u1d62` be a Witt vector for `0 \u2264 i < k`.\n\n`eval \u03c6 x` evaluates `\u03c6` mapping the variable `X_(i, n)` to the `n`th coefficient of `x\u1d62`.\n\nInstantiating `\u03c6` with certain polynomials defined in `structure_polynomial.lean` establishes the\nring operations on `\ud835\udd4e R`. For example, `witt_vector.witt_add` is such a `\u03c6` with `k = 2`;\nevaluating this at `(x\u2080, x\u2081)` gives us the sum of two Witt vectors `x\u2080 + x\u2081`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.neg_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.constant_coeff_witt_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_pow", "description": "The polynomials used for defining repeated addition of the ring of Witt vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.has_int_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_add_vars", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_mul_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.one_coeff_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_zero", "description": "The polynomials used for defining the element `0` of the ring of Witt vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.constant_coeff_witt_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_sub", "description": "The polynomials used for describing the subtraction of the ring of Witt vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_add_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.has_nat_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.is_lawful_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_one", "description": "The polynomials used for defining the element `1` of the ring of Witt vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.has_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.zero_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_sub_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_one_zero_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_zero_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector", "description": " `witt_vector p R` is the ring of `p`-typical Witt vectors over the commutative ring `R`,\nwhere `p` is a prime number.\n\nIf `p` is invertible in `R`, this ring is isomorphic to `\u2115 \u2192 R` (the product of `\u2115` copies of `R`).\nIf `R` is a ring of characteristic `p`, then `witt_vector p R` is a ring of characteristic `0`.\nThe canonical example is `witt_vector p (zmod p)`,\nwhich is isomorphic to the `p`-adic integers `\u2124_[p]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.coeff", "description": " `witt_vector p R` is the ring of `p`-typical Witt vectors over the commutative ring `R`,\nwhere `p` is a prime number.\n\nIf `p` is invertible in `R`, this ring is isomorphic to `\u2115 \u2192 R` (the product of `\u2115` copies of `R`).\nIf `R` is a ring of characteristic `p`, then `witt_vector p R` is a ring of characteristic `0`.\nThe canonical example is `witt_vector p (zmod p)`,\nwhich is isomorphic to the `p`-adic integers `\u2124_[p]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_zsmul", "description": "The polynomials used for defining repeated addition of the ring of Witt vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.has_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.peval", "description": " An auxiliary definition used in `witt_vector.eval`.\nEvaluates a polynomial whose variables come from the disjoint union of `k` copies of `\u2115`,\nwith a curried evaluation `x`.\nThis can be defined more generally but we use only a specific instance here.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.sub_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.pow_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_neg", "description": "The polynomials used for defining the negation of the ring of Witt vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.tprod", "description": " Construct a product of `n` elements of the module within the tensor algebra.\n\nSee also `pi_tensor_product.tprod`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_algebra.to_tensor", "description": " The canonical image of the `free_algebra` in the `tensor_algebra`, which maps\n`free_algebra.\u03b9 R x` to `tensor_algebra.\u03b9 R x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.\u03b9_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.algebra_map_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.lift_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.\u03b9_range_disjoint_one", "description": "The generators of the tensor algebra are disjoint from its scalars.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.\u03b9_eq_algebra_map_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.algebra_map_eq_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.induction", "description": " If `C` holds for the `algebra_map` of `r : R` into `tensor_algebra R M`, the `\u03b9` of `x : M`,\nand is preserved under addition and muliplication, then it holds for all of `tensor_algebra R M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_algebra.to_tensor_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra", "description": "The tensor algebra of the module `M` over the commutative semiring `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.\u03b9_left_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.algebra_map_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.to_triv_sq_zero_ext", "description": " The canonical map from `tensor_algebra R M` into `triv_sq_zero_ext R M` that sends\n`tensor_algebra.\u03b9` to `triv_sq_zero_ext.inr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.hom_ext", "description": "See note [partially-applied ext lemmas].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.\u03b9_ne_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.lift_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.tprod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.\u03b9_comp_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.lift", "description": "Given a linear map `f : M \u2192 A` where `A` is an `R`-algebra, `lift R f` is the unique lift\nof `f` to a morphism of `R`-algebras `tensor_algebra R M \u2192 A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.\u03b9_inv", "description": " The left-inverse of `\u03b9`.\n\nAs an implementation detail, we implement this using `triv_sq_zero_ext` which has a suitable\nalgebra structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.rel", "description": "An inductively defined relation on `pre R M` used to force the initial algebra structure on\nthe associated quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.rel.add", "description": "An inductively defined relation on `pre R M` used to force the initial algebra structure on\nthe associated quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.rel.smul", "description": "An inductively defined relation on `pre R M` used to force the initial algebra structure on\nthe associated quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.to_triv_sq_zero_ext_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.\u03b9_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.algebra_map_left_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.algebra_map_inv", "description": "The left-inverse of `algebra_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.lift_comp_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.\u03b9", "description": "The canonical linear map `M \u2192\u2097[R] tensor_algebra R M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.ring_quot_mk_alg_hom_free_algebra_\u03b9_eq_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.lift_\u03b9_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.lf.is_irrefl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.zero_lf_le", "description": "The definition of `0 \u29cf x` on pre-games, in terms of `0 \u2264`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.equiv.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathli