r `of_lists`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.sub_self_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.zero_add_equiv", "description": "`0 + x` is equivalent to `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.lf_mk_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.le_of_forall_lf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.zero_le_neg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.move_right", "description": "The new game after Right makes an allowed move.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.sub_congr_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.equiv.is_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.move_left_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.relabelling.add_congr", "description": " If `w` has the same moves as `x` and `y` has the same moves as `z`,\nthen `w + y` has the same moves as `x + z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.neg_lf_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.sub_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.fuzzy_congr_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.equiv_rfl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.add_move_right_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.has_involutive_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.is_empty_zero_left_moves", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.zero_le_add_left_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.left_moves", "description": "The indexing type for allowable moves by Left.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.subsequent", "description": " `subsequent x y` says that `x` can be obtained by playing some nonempty sequence of moves from\n`y`. It is the transitive closure of `is_option`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.right_response_spec", "description": " Show that the response for right provided by `right_response` preserves the right-player-wins\ncondition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.relabelling.refl", "description": "The identity relabelling.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.subsequent.mk_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.relabelling.ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.has_le", "description": " The less or equal relation on pre-games.\n\nIf `0 \u2264 x`, then Left can win `x` as the second player.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.move_right_neg_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.equiv.ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.relabelling.le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.fuzzy_congr_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.equiv.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.relabel_move_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.equiv.not_fuzzy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.fuzzy.is_irrefl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame", "description": "The type of pre-games, before we have quotiented\n by equivalence (`pgame.setoid`). In ZFC, a combinatorial game is constructed from\n two sets of combinatorial games that have been constructed at an earlier\n stage. To do this in type theory, we say that a pre-game is built\n inductively from two families of pre-games indexed over any type\n in Type u. The resulting type `pgame.{u}` lives in `Type (u+1)`,\n reflecting that it is a proper class in ZFC.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mk", "description": "The type of pre-games, before we have quotiented\n by equivalence (`pgame.setoid`). In ZFC, a combinatorial game is constructed from\n two sets of combinatorial games that have been constructed at an earlier\n stage. To do this in type theory, we say that a pre-game is built\n inductively from two families of pre-games indexed over any type\n in Type u. The resulting type `pgame.{u}` lives in `Type (u+1)`,\n reflecting that it is a proper class in ZFC.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.star_left_moves", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mk_add_move_left_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.is_option.mk_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.zero_le_add_right_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.not_fuzzy_of_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.add_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.add_move_right_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.left_response", "description": " Given a game won by the left player when they play second, provide a response to any move by\nright.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.fuzzy", "description": " The fuzzy, confused, or incomparable relation on pre-games.\n\nIf `x \u2016 0`, then the first player can always win `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mk_lf_mk", "description": "Definition of `x \u29cf y` on pre-games built using the constructor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.lf_of_lt_of_lf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.of_lists_move_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.neg", "description": "The negation of `{L | R}` is `{-R | -L}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.relabelling.mk'_left_moves_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.add_lf_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.right_moves_add_cases", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.lf_zero", "description": "The definition of `x \u29cf 0` on pre-games, in terms of `\u29cf 0` two moves later.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.relabelling.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.equiv_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mk_add_move_left_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.relabelling.neg_congr", "description": "If `x` has the same moves as `y`, then `-x` has the sames moves as `-y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.is_option_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, 