s a `finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.is_subgraph", "description": " The relation that one `simple_graph` is a subgraph of another.\nNote that this should be spelled `\u2264`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.simple_graph_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart", "description": " A `dart` is an oriented edge, implemented as an ordered pair of adjacent vertices.\nThis terminology comes from combinatorial maps, and they are also known as \"half-edges\"\nor \"bonds.\"", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart.to_prod", "description": " A `dart` is an oriented edge, implemented as an ordered pair of adjacent vertices.\nThis terminology comes from combinatorial maps, and they are also known as \"half-edges\"\nor \"bonds.\"", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart.is_adj", "description": " A `dart` is an oriented edge, implemented as an ordered pair of adjacent vertices.\nThis terminology comes from combinatorial maps, and they are also known as \"half-edges\"\nor \"bonds.\"", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.embedding.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.common_neighbors_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.induce_spanning_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_set_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.iso.complete_graph", "description": "Equivalences of types induce isomorphisms of complete graphs on those types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.adj.ne'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.map_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.mem_common_neighbors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.iso.to_embedding_complete_graph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.simple_graph_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.compl_eq_delete_edges", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.incidence_finset_eq_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_set_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.embedding.map_edge_set_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart_of_neighbor_set", "description": " For a given vertex `v`, this is the bijective map from the neighbor set at `v`\nto the darts `d` with `d.fst = v`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.embedding.spanning_coe", "description": "Graphs on a set of vertices embed in their `spanning_coe`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.embedding.coe_to_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.embedding.map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart.symm_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.embedding", "description": "A graph embedding is an embedding `f` such that for vertices `v w : V`,\n`G.adj f(v) f(w) \u2194 G.adj v w `. Its image is an induced subgraph of G'.\n\nThe notation `G \u21aag G'` represents the type of graph embeddings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_finset_strict_mono", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `simple_graph.edge_finset_ssubset_edge_finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_set_eq_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.compl_neighbor_set_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.bot_adj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.iso.to_embedding", "description": "An isomorphism of graphs gives rise to an embedding of graphs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.inf.adj_decidable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.has_inf", "description": "The infimum of two graphs `x \u2293 y` has edges where both `x` and `y` have edges.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "empty_graph", "description": "The graph with no edges on a given vertex type `V`. `mathlib` prefers the notation `\u22a5`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_set", "description": "The edges of G consist of the unordered pairs of vertices related by\n`G.adj`.\n\nThe way `edge_set` is defined is such that `mem_edge_set` is proved by `refl`.\n(That is, `\u27e6(v, w)\u27e7 \u2208 G.edge_set` is definitionally equal to `G.adj v w`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.degree_lt_card_verts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.has_sdiff", "description": "The difference of two graphs `x \\ y` has the edges of `x` with the edges of `y` removed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.fintype_edge_set_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.degree_pos_iff_exists_adj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart_edge_eq_mk_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.from_edge_set_edge_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.comap_map_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart_edge_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.irrefl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.map_le_iff_le_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart.edge_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.embedding.map_neighbor_set_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.is_regular_of_degree.top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.inhabited_default", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.neighbor_finset_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.hom", "description": "A graph homomorphism is a map on vertex sets that respects adjacency relations.\n\nThe notation `G \u2192g G'` represents the type of graph homomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.card_incidence_finset_eq_degree", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.embedding.map_mem_edge_set_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_finset_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.from_edge_set_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.from_edge_set_sdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.neighbor_finset_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.from_edge_set_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.from_edge_set_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.has_compl", "description": "We define `G\u1d9c` to be the `simple_graph V` such that no two adjacent vertices in `G`\nare adjacent in the complement, and every nonadjacent pair of vertices is adjacent\n(still ensuring that vertices are not adjacent to themselves).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.hom.comp", "description": "Composition of graph homomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.incidence_set_equiv_neighbor_set_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.nonempty_dart_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.delete_edges_adj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.decidable_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.incidence_set_inter_incidence_set_of_not_adj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.sdiff_adj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.embedding.comp", "description": "Composition of graph embeddings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart.symm_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.neighbor_set_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.embedding.comap", "description": " Given an injective function, there is an embedding from the comapped graph into the original\ngraph.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.complete_graph_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.embedding.to_hom", "description": "An embedding of graphs gives rise to a homomorphism of graphs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.incidence_set_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.compl_adj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.adj.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.embedding.complete_graph", "description": "Embeddings of types induce embeddings of complete graphs on those types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.map_monotone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.hom.map_dart_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_set_mono", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `simple_graph.edge_set_subset_edge_set`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.simple_graph_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.Inf_adj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.adj_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.common_neighbors", "description": "The set of common neighbors between two vertices `v` and `w` in a graph `G` is the\nintersection of the neighbor sets of `v` and `w`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.mem_edge_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.iso.map_edge_set_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.support", "description": "`G.support` is the set of vertices that form edges in `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.iso.comp", "description": "Composition of graph isomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.iso.map_adj_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.simple_graph", "description": "Equivalent types have equivalent simple graphs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.iso.map_neighbor_set_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.iso.comap_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.induce_hom_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_set_sdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_finset_delete_edges", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.delete_edges_eq_sdiff_from_edge_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.hom.map_spanning_subgraphs_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph", "description": "A simple graph is an irreflexive symmetric relation `adj` on a vertex type `V`.\nThe relation describes which pairs of vertices are adjacent.\nThere is exactly one edge for every pair of adjacent vertices;\nsee `simple_graph.edge_set` for the corresponding edge set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.adj", "description": "A simple graph is an irreflexive symmetric relation `adj` on a vertex type `V`.\nThe relation describes which pairs of vertices are adjacent.\nThere is exactly one edge for every pair of adjacent vertices;\nsee `simple_graph.edge_set` for the corresponding edge set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.symm", "description": "A simple graph is an irreflexive symmetric relation `adj` on a vertex type `V`.\nThe relation describes which pairs of vertices are adjacent.\nThere is exactly one edge for every pair of adjacent vertices;\nsee `simple_graph.edge_set` for the corresponding edge set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.loopless", "description": "A simple graph is an irreflexive symmetric relation `adj` on a vertex type `V`.\nThe relation describes which pairs of vertices are adjacent.\nThere is exactly one edge for every pair of adjacent vertices;\nsee `simple_graph.edge_set` for the corresponding edge set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.hom.map_neighbor_set_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.delete_far.le_card_sub_card", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `simple_graph.delete_far_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.hom.map_mem_edge_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.mem_incidence_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.comap_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.neighbor_set.mem_decidable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.delete_edges_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.left_inverse_comap_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.iso.map_neighbor_set", "description": "A graph isomorphism induces an equivalence of neighbor sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.card_common_neighbors_le_degree_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart.edge", "description": "The edge associated to the dart.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.supr_adj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.top.adj_decidable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_other_incident_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.card_common_neighbors_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.degree", "description": "`G.degree v` is the number of vertices adjacent to `v`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.comap_adj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.iso.comap_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.is_regular_of_degree.compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.hom.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.card_incidence_set_eq_degree", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.delete_far_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.hom.map_edge_set", "description": " The map between edge sets induced by a homomorphism.\nThe underlying map on edges is given by `sym2.map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.iso.map_edge_set", "description": "An isomorphism of graphs induces an equivalence of edge sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.Sup_adj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.bot_degree", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.delete_far", "description": " A graph is `r`-*delete-far* from a property `p` if we must delete at least `r` edges from it to\nget a graph with the property `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.hom.of_le", "description": "The graph homomorphism from a smaller graph to a bigger one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.adj_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.card_common_neighbors_lt_card_verts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.has_Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.hom.map_edge_set_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.delete_edges", "description": " Given a set of vertex pairs, remove all of the corresponding edges from the\ngraph's edge set, if present.\n\nSee also: `simple_graph.subgraph.delete_edges`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_finset_mono", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `simple_graph.edge_finset_subset_edge_finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.sup_adj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.comap_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.hom.finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.not_mem_neighbor_set_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.inf_adj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.bot.adj_decidable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.embedding.refl", "description": "The identity embedding from a graph to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart.to_prod_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.complete_boolean_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.max_degree", "description": "The maximum degree of all vertices (and `0` if there are no vertices).\nThe key properties of this are given in `exists_maximal_degree_vertex`, `degree_le_max_degree`\nand `max_degree_le_of_forall_degree_le`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.common_neighbors_top_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.neighbor_finset_eq_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.neighbor_finset_disjoint_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.common_neighbors_subset_neighbor_set_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.not_is_diag_of_mem_edge_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.embedding.comap_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.from_edge_set_adj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.induce_hom_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.delete_edges_empty_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.neighbor_set_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart.snd", "description": "The second vertex for the dart.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.iso.map_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.incidence_set_equiv_neighbor_set", "description": "There is an equivalence between the set of edges incident to a given\nvertex and the set of vertices adjacent to the vertex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.exists_minimal_degree_vertex", "description": "There exists a vertex of minimal degree. Note the assumption of being nonempty is necessary, as\nthe lemma implies there exists a vertex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.not_mem_common_neighbors_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.spanning_coe_induce_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.iso.map_edge_set_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_finset_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.hom.id", "description": "The identity homomorphism from a graph to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.embedding.induce", "description": " Induced graphs embed in the original graph.\n\nNote that if `G.induce s = \u22a4` (i.e., if `s` is a clique) then this gives the embedding of a\ncomplete graph.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart.symm", "description": "The dart with reversed orientation from a given dart.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart_of_neighbor_set_to_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.hom.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.disjoint_edge_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_set_delete_edges", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.map_adj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart.symm_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.coe_induce_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_bipartite_graph", "description": "Two vertices are adjacent in the complete bipartite graph on two vertex types\nif and only if they are not from the same side.\nBipartite graphs in general may be regarded as being subgraphs of one of these.\n\nTODO also introduce complete multi-partite graphs, where the vertex type is a sigma type of an\nindexed family of vertex types", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.hom.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.is_subgraph_eq_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.card_neighbor_set_eq_degree", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.not_is_diag_of_mem_edge_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.map", "description": " Given an injective function, there is an covariant induced map on graphs by pushing forward\nthe adjacency relation.\n\nThis is injective (see `simple_graph.map_injective`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.delete_edges_eq_inter_edge_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.hom.comap", "description": " There is a homomorphism to a graph from a comapped graph.\nWhen the function is injective, this is an embedding (see `simple_graph.embedding.comap`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.iso.map_neighbor_set_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.map_comap_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.is_regular_of_degree", "description": "A locally finite simple graph is regular of degree `d` if every vertex has degree `d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.comap_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart.fst", "description": "The first vertex for the dart.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.embedding.map_edge_set", "description": "A graph embedding induces an embedding of edge sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.degree_le_max_degree", "description": "The maximum degree in the graph is at least the degree of any particular vertex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.card_common_neighbors_le_degree_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_set_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.hom.map_neighbor_set", "description": "The map between neighbor sets induced by a homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.iso", "description": "A graph isomorphism is an bijective map on vertex sets that respects adjacency relations.\n\nThe notation `G \u2243g G'` represents the type of graph isomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.common_neighbors_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.delete_edges_delete_edges", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.complete_graph_degree", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.comap", "description": " Given a function, there is a contravariant induced map on graphs by pulling back the\nadjacency relation.\nThis is one of the ways of creating induced graphs. See `simple_graph.induce` for a wrapper.\n\nThis is surjective when `f` is injective (see `simple_graph.comap_surjective`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.spanning_coe", "description": " Given a graph on a set of vertices, we can make it be a `simple_graph V` by\nadding in the remaining vertices without adding in any additional edges.\nThis is a wrapper around `simple_graph.map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_set_strict_mono", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `simple_graph.edge_set_ssubset_edge_set`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.neighbor_set", "description": "`G.neighbor_set v` is the set of vertices adjacent to `v` in `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.comap_monotone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_set_univ_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart.symm_involutive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.iso.map_mem_edge_set_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.comap_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_set.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.iso.map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.sdiff_eq_delete_edges", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.iso.apply_mem_neighbor_set_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_finset_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_set_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.induce_hom", "description": "The restriction of a morphism of graphs to induced subgraphs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.from_rel", "description": "Construct the simple graph induced by the given relation. It\nsymmetrizes the relation and makes it irreflexive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_finset_ssubset_edge_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.iso.symm", "description": "The inverse of a graph isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.adj.card_common_neighbors_lt_degree", "description": "If the condition `G.adj v w` fails, then `card_common_neighbors_le_degree` is\nthe best we can do in general.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart_edge_eq_mk_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_bipartite_graph_adj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_set_subset_edge_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart.edge_comp_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.delete_edges_le_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.disjoint_from_edge_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.distrib_lattice", "description": "For graphs `G`, `H`, `G \u2264 H` iff `\u2200 a b, G.adj a b \u2192 H.adj a b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.symm_simple_graph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_mem_incidence_set_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.min_degree", "description": "The minimum degree of all vertices (and `0` if there are no vertices).\nThe key properties of this are given in `exists_minimal_degree_vertex`, `min_degree_le_degree`\nand `le_min_degree_of_forall_le_degree`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.delete_far.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart.edge_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.has_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.neighbor_finset", "description": "`G.neighbors v` is the `finset` version of `G.adj v` in case `G` is\nlocally finite at `v`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.neg_modeq_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq.add_iff_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq_iff_eq_mod_zmultiples", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq.sub", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `add_comm_group.modeq.sub_iff_left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq.add_right_cancel", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `add_comm_group.modeq.add_iff_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.nsmul_modeq_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.add_zsmul_modeq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.self_modeq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq.zsmul_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq.of_zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq.sub_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq.sub_right_cancel'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq_iff_int_modeq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add