 {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq", "description": " `a \u2261 b [PMOD p]` means that `b` is congruent to `a` modulo `p`.\n\nEquivalently (as shown in `algebra.order.to_interval_mod`), `b` does not lie in the open interval\n`(a, a + p)` modulo `p`, or `to_Ico_mod hp a` disagrees with `to_Ioc_mod hp a` at `b`, or\n`to_Ico_div hp a` disagrees with `to_Ioc_div hp a` at `b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq.sub_iff_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.of_nat_cast", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `add_comm_group.nat_cast_modeq_nat_cast`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq.sub_right_cancel", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `add_comm_group.modeq.sub_iff_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq.int_cast", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `add_comm_group.int_cast_modeq_int_cast`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.add_modeq_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.add_modeq_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq_sub_iff_add_modeq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq.add_iff_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq_sub_iff_add_modeq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq_rfl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.sub_modeq_iff_modeq_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq.nat_cast", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `add_comm_group.nat_cast_modeq_nat_cast`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq.of_neg", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `add_comm_group.neg_modeq_neg`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.modeq.nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.sub_modeq_iff_modeq_add'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_