s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "well_founded_gt.apply", "description": "All values are accessible under the well-founded `>`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "well_founded_gt.induction", "description": "Inducts on a well-founded `>` relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.continuous_of_dominated_interval", "description": "Continuity of interval integral with respect to a parameter.\n Given `F : X \u2192 \u211d \u2192 E`, assume each `F x` is ae-measurable on `[a, b]`,\n and assume it is bounded by a function integrable on `[a, b]` independent of `x`.\n If `(\u03bb x, F x t)` is continuous for almost every `t` in `[a, b]`\n then the same holds for `(\u03bb x, \u222b t in a..b, F x t \u2202\u03bc) s x\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.continuous_on_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.continuous_within_at_primitive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.ae_strongly_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.norm_integral_le_integral_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.inv_smul_integral_comp_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_add_adjacent_intervals", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_comp_add_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_comp_mul_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_interval_sub_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_eq_integral_of_support_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_interval_sub_interval_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.interval_integral_pos_of_pos_on", "description": " If `f : \u211d \u2192 \u211d` is integrable on `(a, b]` for real numbers `a < b`, and positive on the interior\nof the interval, then its integral over `a..b` is strictly positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_comp_sub_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_indicator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.eventually_interval_integrable_ae", "description": " Let `l'` be a measurably generated filter; let `l` be a of filter such that each `s \u2208 l'`\neventually includes `Ioc u v` as both `u` and `v` tend to `l`. Let `\u03bc` be a measure finite at `l'`.\n\nSuppose that `f : \u211d \u2192 E` has a finite limit at `l' \u2293 \u03bc.ae`. Then `f` is interval integrable on\n`u..v` provided that both `u` and `v` tend to `l`.\n\nTypeclass instances allow Lean to find `l'` based on `l` but not vice versa, so\n`apply tendsto.eventually_interval_integrable_ae` will generate goals `filter \u211d` and\n`tendsto_Ixx_class Ioc ?m_1 l'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.inv_smul_integral_comp_div_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.interval_integrable", "description": "If a function is integrable with respect to a given measure `\u03bc` then it is interval integrable\n with respect to `\u03bc` on `uIcc a b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_nonneg_of_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.iff_comp_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_comp_div_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.smul_integral_comp_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_add_adjacent_intervals_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.trans_iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.has_sum_interval_integral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.mono_set_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_mono_ae_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.interval_integrable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_comp_sub_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.continuous_on_primitive_interval'", "description": "Note: this assumes that `f` is `interval_integrable`, in contrast to some other lemmas here.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_non_ae_strongly_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.interval_integrable", "description": " A continuous function on `\u211d` is `interval_integrable` with respect to any locally finite measure\n`\u03bd` on \u211d.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.tsum_interval_integral_eq_of_summable_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral", "description": " The interval integral `\u222b x in a..b, f x \u2202\u03bc` is defined\nas `\u222b x in Ioc a b, f x \u2202\u03bc - \u222b x in Ioc b a, f x \u2202\u03bc`. If `a \u2264 b`, then it equals\n`\u222b x in Ioc a b, f x \u2202\u03bc`, otherwise it equals `-\u222b x in Ioc b a, f x \u2202\u03bc`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_comp_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.inv_smul_integral_comp_div_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.mono_fun'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_mono_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone_on.interval_integrable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.continuous_primitive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_smul_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.abs_integral_mono_interval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.comp_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_comp_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.comp_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_const'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.mono_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.trans_iterate_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.abs_integral_eq_abs_integral_uIoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable_iff_integrable_Ioc_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.ae_strongly_measurable'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.eventually_interval_integrable", "description": " Let `l'` be a measurably generated filter; let `l` be a of filter such that each `s \u2208 l'`\neventually includes `Ioc u v` as both `u` and `v` tend to `l`. Let `\u03bc` be a measure finite at `l'`.\n\nSuppose that `f : \u211d \u2192 E` has a finite limit at `l`. Then `f` is interval integrable on `u..v`\nprovided that both `u` and `v` tend to `l`.\n\nTypeclass instances allow Lean to find `l'` based on `l` but not vice versa, so\n`apply tendsto.eventually_interval_integrable_ae` will generate goals `filter \u211d` and\n`tendsto_Ixx_class Ioc ?m_1 l'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.sum_integral_adjacent_intervals_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_of_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.interval_integral_comp_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_const_of_cdf", "description": "If `\u03bc` is a finite measure then `\u222b x in a..b, c \u2202\u03bc = (\u03bc (Iic b) - \u03bc (Iic a)) \u2022 c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable", "description": " A function `f` is called *interval integrable* with respect to a measure `\u03bc` on an unordered\ninterval `a..b` if it is integrable on both intervals `(a, b]` and `(b, a]`. One of these\nintervals is always empty, so this property is equivalent to `f` being integrable on\n`(min a b, max a b]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_Iic_sub_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.norm_interval_integral_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.norm_integral_min_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_comp_div_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.interval_integral_eq_integral_uIoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_same", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.comp_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.mono_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_eq_zero_iff_of_nonneg_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.const_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.div_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_mul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_zero_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_nonneg_of_ae_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.has_sum_interval_integral_comp_add_int", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.norm_integral_le_of_norm_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.interval_integrable_of_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.smul_integral_comp_mul_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.interval_integrable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_lt_integral_of_ae_le_of_measure_set_of_lt_ne_zero", "description": " If `f` and `g` are two functions that are interval integrable on `a..b`, `a \u2264 b`,\n`f x \u2264 g x` for a.e. `x \u2208 set.Ioc a b`, and `f x < g x` on a subset of `set.Ioc a b`\nof nonzero measure, then `\u222b x in a..b, f x \u2202\u03bc < \u222b x in a..b, g x \u2202\u03bc`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_smul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_nonneg_of_forall", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.interval_integral_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.comp_sub_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.norm_integral_le_of_norm_le_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.inv_smul_integral_comp_sub_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.mul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_congr_ae'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.interval_integrable_of_integral_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_interval_sub_interval_comm'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_comp_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_comp_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_pos_iff_support_of_nonneg_ae'", "description": " If `f` is nonnegative and integrable on the unordered interval `set.uIoc a b`, then its\nintegral over `a..b` is positive if and only if `a < b` and the measure of\n`function.support f \u2229 set.Ioc a b` is positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.continuous_on_primitive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.mul_continuous_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_lt_integral_of_continuous_on_of_le_of_exists_lt", "description": " If `f` and `g` are continuous on `[a, b]`, `a < b`, `f x \u2264 g x` on this interval, and\n`f c < g c` at some point `c \u2208 [a, b]`, then `\u222b x in a..b, f x < \u222b x in a..b, g x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.has_sum_integral_of_dominated_convergence", "description": "Lebesgue dominated convergence theorem for series.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone_on.interval_integrable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.norm_integral_le_abs_integral_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.norm_integral_eq_norm_integral_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_comp_sub_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_comp_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.continuous_on_primitive_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.smul_integral_comp_mul_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_cases", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.interval_integrable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.smul_integral_comp_add_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.tendsto_integral_filter_of_dominated_convergence", "description": "Lebesgue dominated convergence theorem for filters with a countable basis", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.sum_integral_adjacent_intervals", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.interval_integral_pos_of_pos", "description": " If `f : \u211d \u2192 \u211d` is strictly positive everywhere, and integrable on `(a, b]` for real numbers\n`a < b`, then its integral over `a..b` is strictly positive. (See `interval_integral_pos_of_pos_on`\nfor a version only assuming positivity of `f` on `(a, b)` rather than everywhere.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_pos_iff_support_of_nonneg_ae", "description": " If `f` is nonnegative a.e.-everywhere and it is integrable on the unordered interval\n`set.uIoc a b`, then its integral over `a..b` is positive if and only if `a < b` and the\nmeasure of `function.support f \u2229 set.Ioc a b` is positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.continuous_primitive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable_iff_integrable_Icc_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_comp_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_comp_add_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.interval_integrable_norm_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_of_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_const_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_comp_sub_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.comp_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.mono_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.smul_integral_comp_sub_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable_iff", "description": "A function is interval integrable with respect to a given measure `\u03bc` on `a..b` if and\n only if it is integrable on `uIoc a b` with respect to `\u03bc`. This is an equivalent\n definition of `interval_integrable`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_mono_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.def", "description": "If a function is interval integrable with respect to a given measure `\u03bc` on `a..b` then\n it is integrable on `uIoc a b` with respect to `\u03bc`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.continuous_within_at_of_dominated_interval", "description": "Continuity of interval integral with respect to a parameter, at a point within a set.\n Given `F : X \u2192 \u211d \u2192 E`, assume `F x` is ae-measurable on `[a, b]` for `x` in a\n neighborhood of `x\u2080`\u00a0within `s` and at `x\u2080`, and assume it is bounded by a function integrable\n on `[a, b]` independent of `x` in a neighborhood of `x\u2080`\u00a0within `s`. If `(\u03bb x, F x t)`\n is continuous at `x\u2080` within `s` for almost every `t` in `[a, b]`\n then the same holds for `(\u03bb x, \u222b t in a..b, F x t \u2202\u03bc) s x\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.smul_integral_comp_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.mono_set'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.abs_integral_le_integral_abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_interval_add_interval_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_non_ae_strongly_measurable_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.norm_integral_le_integral_norm_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_congr_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.abs_interval_integral_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.continuous_at_of_dominated_interval", "description": "Continuity of interval integral with respect to a parameter at a point.\n Given `F : X \u2192 \u211d \u2192 E`, assume `F x` is ae-measurable on `[a, b]` for `x` in a\n neighborhood of `x\u2080`, and assume it is bounded by a function integrable on\n `[a, b]` independent of `x` in a neighborhood of `x\u2080`. If `(\u03bb x, F x t)`\n is continuous at `x\u2080` for almost every `t` in `[a, b]`\n then the same holds for `(\u03bb x, \u222b t in a..b, F x t \u2202\u03bc) s x\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.continuous_on_primitive_interval_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable.comp_sub_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable_const_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.continuous_on_primitive_interval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_undef", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_comp_mul_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_mono_interval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.inv_smul_integral_comp_add_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone.interval_integrable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.has_sum_interval_integral_of_summable_norm", "description": " Interval integrals commute with countable sums, when the supremum norms are summable (a\nspecial case of the dominated convergence theorem).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_eq_zero_iff_of_le_of_nonneg_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.norm_integral_le_of_norm_le_const_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integral.integral_congr", "description": "If two functions are equal in the relevant interval, their interval integrals are also equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.from_structured_arrow_map_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.equiv_costructured_arrow_functor_map_right_down_down", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.from_structured_arrow", "description": "Construct a cocone on `F` from an object of the category `(F \u2193 \u0394)`. This is part of an\n   equivalence, see `cocone.equiv_structured_arrow`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.equiv_structured_arrow", "description": "The category of cocones on `F` is just the comma category `(F \u2193 \u0394)`, where `\u0394` is the constant\n   functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.of_reflects_cone_terminal", "description": "If `G : cone F \u2964 cone F'` reflects terminal objects, it reflects limit cones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.equiv_structured_arrow_counit_iso_inv_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.equiv_structured_arrow_unit_iso_hom_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.equiv_costructured_arrow_counit_iso_inv_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.from_costructured_arrow_obj_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.equiv_structured_arrow_inverse_obj_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.equiv_costructured_arrow_functor_obj_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.equiv_costructured_arrow_counit_iso_hom_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal.from_eq_lift_cone_morphism", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.to_structured_arrow_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.equiv_structured_arrow_functor_map_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.of_reflects_cocone_initial", "description": "If `G : cocone F \u2964 cocone F'` reflects initial objects, it reflects colimit cocones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.equiv_structured_arrow_functor_map_left_down_down", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial.to_eq_desc_cocone_morphism", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.from_costructured_arrow_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.equiv_costructured_arrow_unit_iso_hom_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.equiv_costructured_arrow_functor_obj