, {"name": "quotient_add_group.automorphize_smul_left", "description": "Automorphization of a function into an `R`-`module` distributes, that is, commutes with the `R`\n -scalar multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_even_add_odd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.summable_of_eq_zero_or_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_subtype_iff_of_support_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.update'", "description": " Version of `has_sum.update` for `add_comm_monoid` rather than `add_comm_group`.\nRather than showing that `f.update` has a specific sum in terms of `has_sum`,\nit gives a relationship between the sums of `f` and `f.update` given that both exist.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_comm'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.prod_fiberwise", "description": " If a series `f` on `\u03b2 \u00d7 \u03b3` has sum `a` and for each `b` the restriction of `f` to `{b} \u00d7 \u03b3`\nhas sum `g b`, then the series `g` has sum `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_add_group.automorphize", "description": "Given a subgroup `\u0393` of an additive group `G`, and a function `f : G \u2192 M`, we\n  automorphize `f` to a function `G \u29f8 \u0393 \u2192 M` by summing over `\u0393` orbits,\n  `g \u21a6 \u2211' (\u03b3 : \u0393), f(\u03b3 \u2022 g)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum", "description": "`\u2211' i, f i` is the sum of `f` it exists, or 0 otherwise", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_subtype_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_ite_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_zero", "description": "Constant zero function has sum `0`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_nat_add_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.add_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.has_sum_iff_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite.summable_compl_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_dite_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.map_iff_of_equiv", "description": "A special case of `summable.map_iff_of_left_inverse` for convenience", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_const_smul'", "description": "Infinite sums commute with scalar multiplication. Version for scalars living in a `group`, but\n not requiring any summability hypothesis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.automorphize_smul_left", "description": "Automorphization of a function into an `R`-`module` distributes, that is, commutes with the \n `R`-scalar multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.sigma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cauchy_seq_finset_iff_vanishing", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_pi_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.has_sum_iff_tendsto_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_nat_add_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum", "description": " Infinite sum on a topological monoid\n\nThe `at_top` filter on `finset \u03b2` is the limit of all finite sets towards the entire type. So we sum\nup bigger and bigger sets. This sum operation is invariant under reordering. In particular,\nthe function `\u2115 \u2192 \u211d` sending `n` to `(-1)^n / (n+1)` does not have a\nsum for this definition, but a series which is absolutely convergent will have the correct sum.\n\nThis is based on Mario Carneiro's\n[infinite sum `df-tsms` in Metamath](http://us.metamath.org/mpeuni/df-tsms.html).\n\nFor the definition or many statements, `\u03b1` does not need to be a topological monoid. We only add\nthis assumption later, for the lemmas where it is relevant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum_add_tsum_nat_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.has_sum_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_star_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.map_iff_of_left_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.comp_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.update", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.compl_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_sigma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.summable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.prod_factor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_eq_tsum_of_ne_zero_bij", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.add_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.has_sum_iff_of_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.sigma_of_has_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_subtype_iff_indicator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.tsum_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_add_of_has_sum_ite", "description": " Version of `has_sum_ite_sub_has_sum` for `add_comm_monoid` rather than `add_comm_group`.\nRather than showing that the `ite` expression has a specific sum in terms of `has_sum`,\nit gives a relationship between the sums of `f` and `ite (n = b) 0 (f n)` given that both exist.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.of_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.sigma_factor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_iff_has_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.summable_iff_of_has_sum_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_neg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_iff_vanishing", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_iff_of_summable_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.tsum_subtype'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.tsum_eq_tsum_of_has_sum_iff_has_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.has_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum_eq_tsum_indicator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_Union_decode\u2082", "description": "`tsum_supr_decode\u2082` specialized to the complete lattice of sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_ite_sub_has_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.has_sum_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.summable_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.update", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.tsum_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.summable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.even_add_odd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_eq_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.summable_compl_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.tendsto_sum_nat", "description": "If `f : \u2115 \u2192 \u03b1` has sum `a`, then the partial sums `\u2211_{i=0}^{n-1} f i` converge to `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.pos_add_zero_add_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_eq_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.has_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.tendsto_at_top_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.summable_iff_of_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.nonneg_add_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_ite_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.sigma'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_subtype_add_tsum_subtype_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.tsum_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_sum_nat_add", "description": " For `f : \u2115 \u2192 \u03b1`, then `\u2211' k, f (k + i)` tends to zero. This does not require a summability\nassumption on `f`, as otherwise all sums are zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_action.automorphize", "description": "Given an additive group `\u03b1` acting on a type `\u03b2`, and a function `f : \u03b2 \u2192 M`,\n  we automorphize `f` to a function `\u03b2 \u29f8 \u03b1 \u2192 M` by summing over `\u03b1` orbits,\n  `b \u21a6 \u2211' (a : \u03b1), f(a \u2022 b)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_iff_has_sum_of_ne_zero_bij", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.has_sum_of_sum_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action.automorphize_smul_left", "description": "Automorphization of a function into an `R`-`module` distributes, that is, commutes with the \n `R`-scalar multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.summable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.sigma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable", "description": "`summable f` means that `f` has some (infinite) sum. Use `tsum` to get the value.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_union_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.indicator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_sup_add", "description": "If a function is countably sub-additive then it is binary sub-additive", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_eq_zero_of_not_summable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_nat_add_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_bool", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_eq_tsum_of_has_sum_iff_has_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.summable_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_supr_tsum", "description": "If a function is countably sub-additive then it is sub-additive on countable types", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_pi_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.has_sum_compl_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.sum_nat_of_sum_int", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.tsum_eq_tsum_of_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_congr_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action.automorphize", "description": "Given a group `\u03b1` acting on a type `\u03b2`, and a function `f : \u03b2 \u2192 M`, we \"automorphize\" `f` to a\n function `\u03b2 \u29f8 \u03b1 \u2192 M` by summing over `\u03b1` orbits, `b \u21a6 \u2211' (a : \u03b1), f(a \u2022 b)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_subtype_and_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_finset_bUnion_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.summable_compl_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.add_is_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.has_sum_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.has_sum_iff_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum_add_tsum_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_sum_of_ne_finset_zero", "description": "If a function `f` vanishes outside of a finite set `s`, then it `has_sum` `\u2211 b in s, f b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_supr_decode\u2082", "description": "You can compute a sum over an encodably type by summing over the natural numbers and\n taking a supremum. This is useful for outer measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_subtype_eq_of_support_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_action.automorphize_smul_left", "description": "Automorphization of a function into an `R`-`module` distributes, that is, commutes with the \n `R`-scalar multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.vanishing", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_supr_sum", "description": "If a function is countably sub-additive then it is sub-additive on finite sets", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_eq_add_tsum_ite'", "description": " Version of `tsum_eq_add_tsum_ite` for `add_comm_monoid` rather than `add_comm_group`.\nRequires a different convergence assumption involving `function.update`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.tendsto_cofinite_zero", "description": " Series divergence test: if `f` is a convergent series, then `f x` tends to zero along\n`cofinite`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_add_tsum_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_const_smul''", "description": "Infinite sums commute with scalar multiplication. Version for scalars living in a\n `division_ring`; no summability hypothesis. This could be made to work for a\n `[group_with_zero \u03b3]` if there was such a thing as `distrib_mul_action_with_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.int_rec", "description": " If `f\u2080, f\u2081, f\u2082, ...` and `g\u2080, g\u2081, g\u2082, ...` are both convergent then so is the `\u2124`-indexed\nsequence: `..., g\u2082, g\u2081, g\u2080, f\u2080, f\u2081, f\u2082, ...`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum_add_tsum_subtype_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_group.automorphize", "description": "Given a subgroup `\u0393` of a group `G`, and a function `f : G \u2192 M`, we \"automorphize\" `f` to a\n function `G \u29f8 \u0393 \u2192 M` by summing over `\u0393` orbits, `g \u21a6 \u2211' (\u03b3 : \u0393), f(\u03b3 \u2022 g)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.compl_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_sum_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_const_smul", "description": "Infinite sums commute with scalar multiplication. Version for scalars living in a `monoid`, but\n requiring a summability hypothesis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_star_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_upper_central_series_step", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lower_central_series_eq_bot_iff_nilpotency_class_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_nilpotent_of_product_of_sylow_group", "description": "If a finite group is the direct product of its Sylow groups, it is nilpotent", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "descending_central_series_ge_lower", "description": "Any descending central series for a group is bounded below by the lower central series.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lower_central_series_pi_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "upper_central_series.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derived_le_lower_central", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lower_central_series.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_nilpotent_prod", "description": "Products of nilpotent groups are nilpotent", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilpotency_class_pi", "description": "The nilpotency class of an n-ary product is the sup of the nilpotency classes of the factors", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilpotent_iff_lower_central_series", "description": "A group is nilpotent if and only if its lower central series eventually reaches\n the trivial subgroup.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_ascending_central_series", "description": "A sequence of subgroups of `G` is an ascending central series if `H 0` is trivial and\n `\u2045H (n + 1), G\u2046 \u2286 H n` for all `n`. Note that we do not require that `H n = G` for some `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group.nilpotency_class", "description": " The nilpotency class of a nilpotent group is the smallest natural `n` such that\nthe `n`'th term of the upper central series is `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lower_central_series_map_subtype_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "upper_central_series_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_quotient_center_nilpotent", "description": "If the quotient by `center G` is nilpotent, then so is G.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_p_group.is_nilpotent", "description": "A p-group is nilpotent", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "upper_central_series_eq_top_iff_nilpotency_class_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "upper_central_series_is_ascending_central_series", "description": "The upper central series of a group is an ascending central series.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilpotency_class_eq_quotient_center_plus_one", "description": "The nilpotency class of a non-trivial group is one more than its quotient by the center", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_nilpotent_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilpotent_of_surjective", "description": "The range of a surjective homomorphism from a nilpotent group is nilpotent", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_group.is_nilpotent", "description": "Abelian groups are nilpotent", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "upper_central_series", "description": "`upper_central_series G n` is the `n`th term in the upper central series of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_nilpotent_pi_of_bounded_class", "description": "products of nilpotent groups are nilpotent if their nipotency class is bounded", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilpotency_class_le_of_surjective", "description": " The nilpotency class of the range of a surejctive homomorphism from a\nnilpotent group is less or equal the nilpotency class of the domain", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilpotency_class_quotient_center", "description": "Quotienting the `center G` reduces the nilpotency class by 1", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_nilpotent_of_ker_le_center", "description": " The preimage of a nilpotent group is nilpotent if the kernel of the homomorphism is contained\nin the center", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_descending_central_series", "description": "A sequence of subgroups of `G` is a descending central series if `H 0` is `G` and\n `\u2045H n, G\u2046 \u2286 H (n + 1)` for all `n`. Note that we do not requre that `H n = {1}` for some `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilpotent_center_quotient_ind", "description": " A custom induction principle for nilpotent groups. The base case is a trivial group\n(`subsingleton G`), and in the induction step, one can assume the hypothesis for\nthe group quotiented by its center.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "upper_central_series_step.subgroup.normal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lower_central_series_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilpotency_class_zero_iff_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "least_descending_central_series_length_eq_nilpotency_class", "description": " The nilpotency class of a nilpotent `G` is equal to the smallest `n` for which the descending\ncentral series reaches `\u22a5` in its `n`'th term.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "upper_central_series_step_eq_comap_center", "description": " The proof that `upper_central_series_step H` is the preimage of the centre of `G/H` under\nthe canonical surjection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_upper_central_series_succ_iff", "description": " The `n+1`st term of the upper central series `H i` has underlying set equal to the `x` such\nthat `\u2045x,G\u2046 \u2286 H n`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_lower_central_series_succ_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lower_central_series_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_nilpotent_pi", "description": "n-ary products of nilpotent groups are nilpotent", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_ascending_rev_series_of_is_descending", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lower_central_series_succ_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.is_nilpotent", "description": "A subgroup of a nilpotent group is nilpotent", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "least_ascending_central_series_length_eq_nilpotency_class", "description": " The nilpotency class of a nilpotent `G` is equal to the smallest `n` for which an ascending\ncentral series reaches `G` in its `n`'th term.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "upper_central_series_aux", "description": " An auxiliary type-theoretic definition defining both the upper central series of\na group, and a proof that it is normal, all in one go.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "upper_central_series_nilpotency_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lower_central_series_is_descending_central_series", "description": "The lower central series of a group is a descending central series.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lower_central_series_nilpotency_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "upper_central_series_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_group.nilpotency_class_le_one", "description": "Abelian groups have nilpotency class at most one", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilpotent_iff_finite_ascending_central_series", "description": "A group `G` is nilpotent iff there exists an ascending central series which reaches `G` in\n finitely many steps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_nilpotent.to_is_solvable", "description": "A nilpotent subgroup is solvable", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_decending_rev_series_of_is_ascending", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilpotent_quotient_of_nilpotent", "description": "A quotient of a nilpotent group is nilpotent", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilpotent_iff_finite_descending_central_series", "description": "A group `G` is nilpotent iff there exists a descending central series which reaches the\n trivial group in a finite time.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lower_central_series_pi_of_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lower_central_series", "description": "The lower central series of a group `G` is a sequence `H n` of subgroups of `G`, defined\n by `H 0` is all of `G` and for `n\u22651`, `H (n + 1) = \u2045H n, G\u2046`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilpotency_class_prod", "description": "The nilpotency class of a product is the max of the nilpotency classes of the factors", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_nilpotent_of_finite_tfae", "description": " A finite group is nilpotent iff the normalizer condition holds, and iff all maximal groups are\nnormal and iff all sylow groups are normal and iff the group is the direct product of its sylow\ngroups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normalizer_condition_of_is_nilpotent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilpotency_class_le_of_ker_le_center", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.nilpotency_class_le", "description": "A the nilpotency class of a subgroup is less or equal the the nilpotency class of the group", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilpotency_class_quotient_le", "description": "The nilpotency class of a quotient of `G` is less or equal the nilpotency class of `G`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lower_central_series_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group.is_nilpotent", "description": "A group `G` is nilpotent if its upper central series is eventually `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group.is_nilpotent.nilpotent", "description": "A group `G` is nilpotent if its upper central series is eventually `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lower_central_series_length_eq_nilpotency_class", "description": "The nilpotency class of a nilpotent `G` is equal to the length of the lower central series.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lower_central_series_antitone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "upper_central_series_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "upper_central_series_step", "description": " If `H` is a normal subgroup of `G`, then the set `{x : G | \u2200 y : G, x*y*x\u207b\u00b9*y\u207b\u00b9 \u2208 H}`\nis a subgroup of `G` (because it is the preimage in `G` of the centre of the\nquotient group `G/H`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_group_of_nilpotency_class", "description": "Groups with nilpotency class at most one are abelian", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilpotent_of_mul_equiv", "description": "Nilpotency respects isomorphisms", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ascending_central_series_le_upper", "description": "Any ascending central series for a group is bounded above by the upper central series.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lower_central_series_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "upper_central_series.subgroup.normal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lower_central_series.subgroup.normal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comap_upper_central_series_quotient_center", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.discrete_topology", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.discrete_topology", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_map_of_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.fst'", "description": "Precomposing `f` with `prod.fst` is continuous", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sigma.topological_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_pi_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.snd''", "description": "Precomposing `f` with `prod.snd` is continuous at `x : \u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_subtype_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_nhds_square", "description": "Given a neighborhood `s` of `(x, x)`, then `(x, x)` has a square open neighborhood\n that is a subset of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map_to_dual", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_to_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_uncurry_of_discrete_topology", "description": " If a function `f x y` is such that `y \u21a6 f x y` is continuous for all `x`, and `x` lives in a\ndiscrete space, then `f` is 