ation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.submonoid", "description": "The submonoid of `M \u00d7 M` defined by a congruence relation on a monoid `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.add_submonoid", "description": "The `add_submonoid` of `M \u00d7 M` defined by an additive congruence\nrelation on an `add_monoid` `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.ker_lift_mk", "description": "The diagram described by the universal property for quotients of monoids, when the congruence\n   relation is the kernel of the homomorphism, commutes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.Sup_eq_con_gen", "description": "The supremum of a set of congruence relations `S` equals the smallest congruence relation\n   containing the binary relation 'there exists `c \u2208 S` such that `x` is related to `y` by\n   `c`'.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.hrec_on\u2082_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.map", "description": "Given congruence relations `c, d` on a monoid such that `d` contains `c`, `d`'s quotient\n   map induces a homomorphism from the quotient by `c` to the quotient by `d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.quotient_quotient_equiv_quotient", "description": "The third isomorphism theorem for monoids.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.comap_quotient_equiv", "description": "The second isomorphism theorem for `add_monoid`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse", "description": "The first isomorphism theorem for `add_monoid`s in the case of a homomorphism\nwith right inverse.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.rel_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.add_comm_monoid", "description": "The quotient of an `add_comm_monoid` by an additive congruence\nrelation is an `add_comm_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.has_mem", "description": "Given a type `M` with a multiplication, a congruence relation `c` on `M`, and elements of `M`\n   `x, y`, `(x, y) \u2208 M \u00d7 M` iff `x` is related to `y` by `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.comap_eq", "description": "Given a monoid homomorphism `f : N \u2192 M` and a congruence relation `c` on `M`, the congruence\n   relation induced on `N` by `f` equals the kernel of `c`'s quotient homomorphism composed with\n   `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.nsmul", "description": "Additive congruence relations preserve natural scaling.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.ker_lift_injective", "description": "A monoid homomorphism `f` induces an injective homomorphism on the quotient by `f`'s kernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.pow", "description": "Multiplicative congruence relations preserve natural powers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.comap", "description": "Given types with multiplications `M, N` and a congruence relation `c` on `N`, a\n   multiplication-preserving map `f : M \u2192 N` induces a congruence relation on `f`'s domain\n   defined by '`x \u2248 y` iff `f(x)` is related to `f(y)` by `c`.'", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.coe_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.complete_lattice", "description": "The complete lattice of congruence relations on a given type with a multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.coe_one", "description": "The 1 of the quotient of a monoid by a congruence relation is the equivalence class of the\n   monoid's 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.rel_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.prod", "description": "Given types with multiplications `M, N`, the product of two congruence relations `c` on `M` and\n   `d` on `N`: `(x\u2081, x\u2082), (y\u2081, y\u2082) \u2208 M \u00d7 N` are related by `c.prod d` iff `x\u2081` is related to `y\u2081`\n   by `c` and `x\u2082` is related to `y\u2082` by `d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.to_setoid_inj", "description": "The map sending a congruence relation to its underlying equivalence relation is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.ker_lift", "description": "The homomorphism induced on the quotient of an `add_monoid` by the kernel\nof an `add_monoid` homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "A coercion from an additive congruence relation to its underlying binary relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.congr", "description": "Makes an additive isomorphism of quotients by two additive congruence relations,\ngiven that the relations are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.add_semigroup", "description": "The quotient of an `add_semigroup` by an additive congruence relation is\nan `add_semigroup`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.gi", "description": "There is a Galois insertion of congruence relations on a type with a multiplication `M` into\n   binary relations on `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.ker", "description": "The kernel of a monoid homomorphism as a congruence relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.lift_on", "description": "The function on the quotient by a congruence relation `c` induced by a function that is\n   constant on `c`'s equivalence classes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.rel_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.neg", "description": "Additive congruence relations preserve negation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.map", "description": "Given additive congruence relations `c, d` on an `add_monoid` such that `d`\ncontains `c`, `d`'s quotient map induces a homomorphism from the quotient by `c` to the quotient\nby `d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.rel_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.ext_iff", "description": "Iff version of extensionality rule for additive congruence relations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.monoid", "description": "The quotient of a monoid by a congruence relation is a monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.induction_on_add_units", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.ker_eq_lift_of_injective", "description": "Given a monoid homomorphism `f` from `M` to `P`, the kernel of `f` is the unique congruence\n   relation on `M` whose induced map from the quotient of `M` to `P` is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.quot_mk_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.ker_rel", "description": "The definition of the congruence relation defined by a monoid homomorphism's kernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.lift_on_coe", "description": "Definition of the function on the quotient by a congruence relation `c` induced by a function\n   that is constant on `c`'s equivalence classes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.mem_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.lift", "description": "The homomorphism on the quotient of a monoid by a congruence relation `c` induced by a\n   homomorphism constant on `c`'s equivalence classes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.quotient.has_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.add_con_gen_of_add_con", "description": "Additive congruence relations equal the smallest\nadditive congruence relation in which they are contained.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.quotient_quotient_equiv_quotient", "description": "The third isomorphism theorem for `add_monoid`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.has_mul", "description": "The multiplication induced on the quotient by a congruence relation on a type with a\n   multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.quotient.has_zsmul", "description": "The integer scaling induced on the quotient by a congruence relation on a type with a\n   subtraction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.le_def", "description": "Definition of `\u2264` for congruence relations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.lift_funext", "description": "Homomorphisms on the quotient of an `add_monoid` by an additive congruence relation\nare equal if they are equal on elements that are coercions from the `add_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.map_gen", "description": "Given a function `f`, the smallest additive congruence relation containing the\nbinary relation on `f`'s image defined by '`x \u2248 y` iff the elements of `f\u207b\u00b9(x)` are related to the\nelements of `f\u207b\u00b9(y)` by an additive congruence relation `c`.'", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.has_Inf", "description": "The infimum of a set of additive congruence relations on a given type with\nan addition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.symm", "description": "Additive congruence relations are symmetric.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.mul_distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.quotient.decidable_eq", "description": "The quotient by a decidable congruence relation has decidable equality.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.comap", "description": "Given types with additions `M, N` and an additive congruence relation `c` on `N`,\nan addition-preserving map `f : M \u2192 N` induces an additive congruence relation on `f`'s domain\ndefined by '`x \u2248 y` iff `f(x)` is related to `f(y)` by `c`.'", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.Sup_def", "description": "The supremum of a set of additive congruence relations is the same as the smallest\nadditive congruence relation containing the supremum of the set's image under the map to the\nunderlying binary relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.sup_eq_add_con_gen", "description": "The supremum of additive congruence relations `c, d` equals the\nsmallest additive congruence relation containing the binary relation '`x` is related to `y`\nby `c` or `d`'.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.has_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.coe_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.Inf_def", "description": "The infimum of a set of additive congruence relations is the same as the infimum\nof the set's image under the map to the underlying binary relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.lift_apply_mk'", "description": "Given a homomorphism `f` from the quotient of an `add_monoid` by an additive\ncongruence relation, `f` equals the homomorphism on the quotient induced by `f` composed with the\nnatural map from the `add_monoid` to the quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.lift", "description": "The homomorphism on the quotient of an `add_monoid` by an additive congruence\nrelation `c` induced by a homomorphism constant on `c`'s equivalence classes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.lift_range", "description": "Given an additive congruence relation `c` on an `add_monoid` and a homomorphism `f`\nconstant on `c`'s equivalence classes, `f` has the same image as the homomorphism that `f` induces\non the quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.has_le", "description": "For congruence relations `c, d` on a type `M` with a multiplication, `c \u2264 d` iff `\u2200 x y \u2208 M`,\n   `x` is related to `y` by `d` if `x` is related to `y` by `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.gi", "description": "There is a Galois insertion of additive congruence relations on a type with\nan addition `M` into binary relations on `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.mk'_surjective", "description": "The natural homomorphism from a monoid to its quotient by a congruence relation is\n   surjective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.quotient.inhabited", "description": "There exists an element of the quotient of an `add_monoid` by a congruence relation\n(namely 0).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.ext", "description": "Extensionality rule for congruence relations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.con_gen_le", "description": "The smallest congruence relation containing a binary relation `r` is contained in any\n   congruence relation containing `r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.pi", "description": "The product of an indexed collection of congruence relations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.quotient.has_coe_t", "description": " Coercion from a type with a multiplication to its quotient by a congruence relation.\n\nSee Note [use has_coe_t].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.hrec_on\u2082", "description": "A version of `quotient.hrec_on\u2082'` for quotients by `add_con`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.mul_one_class", "description": "The quotient of a monoid by a congruence relation is a monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con", "description": "A congruence relation on a type with an addition is an equivalence relation which\n   preserves addition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.to_setoid", "description": "A congruence relation on a type with an addition is an equivalence relation which\n   preserves addition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.add'", "description": "A congruence relation on a type with an addition is an equivalence relation which\n   preserves addition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.ker_lift_range_eq", "description": "Given an `add_monoid` homomorphism `f`, the induced homomorphism\non the quotient by `f`'s kernel has the same image as `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.semigroup", "description": "The quotient of a semigroup by a congruence relation is a semigroup.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.comap_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.add_con_gen_eq", "description": "The inductively defined smallest additive congruence relation\ncontaining a binary relation `r` equals the infimum of the set of additive congruence relations\ncontaining `r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.con_gen_of_con", "description": "Congruence relations equal the smallest congruence relation in which they are contained.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.lift_on_units", "description": " In order to define a function `(con.quotient c)\u02e3 \u2192 \u03b1` on the units of `con.quotient c`,\nwhere `c : con M` is a multiplicative congruence on a monoid, it suffices to define a function `f`\nthat takes elements `x y : M` with proofs of `c (x * y) 1` and `c (y * x) 1`, and returns an element\nof `\u03b1` provided that `f x y _ _ = f x' y' _ _` whenever `c x x'` and `c y y'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.sup_def", "description": "The supremum of two congruence relations equals the smallest congruence relation containing\n   the supremum of the underlying binary operations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.sup_def", "description": "The supremum of two additive congruence relations equals the smallest additive\ncongruence relation containing the supremum of the underlying binary operations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con_gen.rel", "description": "The inductively defined smallest additive congruence relation containing a given binary\n   relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con_gen.rel.of", "description": "The inductively defined smallest additive congruence relation containing a given binary\n   relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con_gen.rel.refl", "description": "The inductively defined smallest additive congruence relation containing a given binary\n   relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con_gen.rel.symm", "description": "The inductively defined smallest additive congruence relation containing a given binary\n   relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con_gen.rel.trans", "description": "The inductively defined smallest additive congruence relation containing a given binary\n   relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con_gen.rel.add", "description": "The inductively defined smallest additive congruence relation containing a given binary\n   relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.quotient", "description": "Defining the quotient by an additive congruence relation of a type with\nan addition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.lift_on\u2082", "description": "The binary function on the quotient by a congruence relation `c`\ninduced by a binary function that is constant on `c`'s equivalence classes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.inv", "description": "Multiplicative congruence relations preserve inversion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.lift_unique", "description": "The uniqueness part of the universal property for quotients of `add_monoid`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.has_Inf", "description": "The infimum of a set of congruence relations on a given type with a multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.sub", "description": "Additive congruence relations preserve subtraction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con_gen", "description": "The inductively defined smallest multiplicative congruence relation containing a given binary\n   relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.add_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.add_con_gen_mono", "description": "Given binary relations `r, s` with `r` contained in `s`, the\nsmallest additive congruence relation containing `s` contains the smallest additive congruence\nrelation containing `r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.lift_coe", "description": "The diagram describing the universal property for quotients of monoids commutes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.add_ker", "description": "The kernel of an addition-preserving function as an additive congruence relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.ext", "description": "Extensionality rule for additive congruence relations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.lift_comp_mk'", "description": "The diagram describing the universal property for quotients of monoids commutes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.quotient_ker_equiv_of_surjective", "description": "The first isomorphism theorem for `add_monoid`s in the case of a surjective\nhomomorphism.\n\nFor a `computable` version, see `add_con.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.ext'_iff", "description": "Two congruence relations are equal iff their underlying binary relations are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.lift_unique", "description": "The uniqueness part of the universal property for quotients of monoids.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.has_neg", "description": "The negation induced on the quotient by an additive congruence relation on a type\nwith an negation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.hrec_on\u2082_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.mrange_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.to_add_submonoid_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.lift_on", "description": "The function on the quotient by a congruence relation `c`\ninduced by a function that is constant on `c`'s equivalence classes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.con_gen_eq", "description": "The inductively defined smallest congruence relation containing a binary relation `r` equals\n   the infimum of the set of congruence relations containing `r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.has_zpow", "description": "The integer power induced on the quotient by a congruence relation on a type with a\n   division.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.Inf_def", "description": "The infimum of a set of congruence relations is the same as the infimum of the set's image\n   under the map to the underlying binary relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.map_of_surjective", "description": "Given a surjective multiplicative-preserving function `f` whose kernel is contained in a\n   congruence relation `c`, the congruence relation on `f`'s codomain defined by '`x \u2248 y` iff the\n   elements of `f\u207b\u00b9(x)` are related to the elements of `f\u207b\u00b9(y)` by `c`.'", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.coe_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con", "description": "A congruence relation on a type with a multiplication is an equivalence relation which\n   preserves multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.to_setoid", "description": "A congruence relation on a type with a multiplication is an equivalence relation which\n   preserves multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.mul'", "description": "A congruence relation on a type with a multiplication is an equivalence relation which\n   preserves multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.induction_on_units", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.map_of_surjective_eq_map_gen", "description": "A specialization of 'the smallest additive congruence relation containing\nan additive congruence relation `c` equals `c`'.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.quotient_ker_equiv_of_surjective", "description": " The first isomorphism theorem for monoids in the case of a surjective homomorphism.\n\nFor a `computable` version, see `con.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.quotient.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.has_sub", "description": "The subtraction induced on the quotient by an additive congruence relation on a type\nwith a subtraction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.add_con_gen_le", "description": "The smallest additive congruence relation containing a binary\nrelation `r` is contained in any additive congruence relation containing `r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.comm_monoid", "description": "The quotient of a `comm_monoid` by a congruence relation is a `comm_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.to_submonoid_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.add_con_gen_idem", "description": "The map sending a binary relation to the smallest additive\ncongruence relation in which it is contained is idempotent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.mk'", "description": "The natural homomorphism from a monoid to its quotient by a congruence relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.lift_on\u2082", "description": "The binary function on the quotient by a congruence relation `c` induced by a binary function\n   that is constant on `c`'s equivalence classes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.sup_eq_con_gen", "description": "The supremum of congruence relations `c, d` equals the smallest congruence relation containing\n   the binary relation '`x` is related to `y` by `c` or `d`'.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.induction_on", "description": "The inductive principle used to prove propositions about\nthe elements of a quotient by an additive congruence relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.to_submonoid", "description": "Coercion from a congruence relation `c` on a monoid `M` to the submonoid of `M \u00d7 M` whose\n   elements are `(x, y)` such that `x` is related to `y` by `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.map_apply", "description": "Given additive congruence relations `c, d` on an `add_monoid` such that `d`\ncontains `c`, the definition of the homomorphism from the quotient by `c` to the quotient by `d`\ninduced by `d`'s quotient map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.nat.has_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.quot_mk_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.mul_ker", "description": "The kernel of a multiplication-preserving function as a congruence relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.ker_lift_range_eq", "description": "Given a monoid homomorphism `f`, the induced homomorphism on the quotient by `f`'s kernel has\n   the same image as `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.eq", "description": "Two elements are related by a congruence relation `c` iff they are represented by the same\n   element of the quotient by `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.lift_on_add_units", "description": " In order to define a function `(con.quotient c)\u02e3 \u2192 \u03b1` on the units of `con.quotient c`,\nwhere `c : con M` is a multiplicative congruence on a monoid, it suffices to define a function `f`\nthat takes elements `x y : M` with proofs of `c (x * y) 1` and `c (y * x) 1`, and returns an element\nof `\u03b1` provided that `f x y _ _ = f x' y' _ _` whenever `c x x'` and `c y y'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.Sup_eq_add_con_gen", "description": "The supremum of a set of additive congruence relations `S` equals\nthe smallest additive congruence relation containing the binary relation 'there exists `c \u2208 S`\nsuch that `x` is related to `y` by `c`'.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.add_group", "description": "The quotient of an `add_group` by an additive congruence relation is\nan `add_group`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.ext'", "description": "The map sending a congruence relation to its underlying binary relation is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.lift_coe", "description": "The diagram describing the universal property for quotients of `add_monoid`s\ncommutes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.induction_on", "description": "The inductive principle used to prove propositions about the elements of a quotient by a\n   congruence relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.mem_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.coe_zero", "description": "The 0 of the quotient of an `add_monoid` by an additive congruence relation\nis the equivalence class of the `add_monoid`'s 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con_gen.rel", "description": "The inductively defined smallest multiplicative congruence relation containing a given binary\n   relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con_gen.rel.of", "description": "The inductively defined smallest multiplicative congruence relation containing a given binary\n   relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con_gen.rel.refl", "description": "The inductively defined smallest multiplicative congruence relation containing a given binary\n   relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con_gen.rel.symm", "description": "The inductively defined smallest multiplicative congruence relation containing a given binary\n   relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con_gen.rel.trans", "description": "The inductively defined smallest multiplicative congruence relation containing a given binary\n   relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con_gen.rel.mul", "description": "The inductively defined smallest multiplicative congruence relation containing a given binary\n   relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.map_gen", "description": "Given a function `f`, the smallest congruence relation containing the binary relation on `f`'s\n   image defined by '`x \u2248 y` iff the elements of `f\u207b\u00b9(x)` are related to the elements of `f\u207b\u00b9(y)`\n   by a congruence relation `c`.'", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.has_inv", "description": "The inversion induced on the quotient by a congruence relation on a type with a\n   inversion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.lift_on_coe", "description": "Definition of the function on the quotient by an additive congruence\nrelation `c` induced by a function that is constant on `c`'s equivalence classes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.mul", "description": "Multiplicative congruence relations preserve multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.quotient_ker_equiv_range", "description": "The first isomorphism theorem for `add_monoid`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.comap_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.inf_def", "description": "The infimum of two congruence relations equals the infimum of the underlying binary\n   operations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.ker_lift_mk", "description": "The diagram described by the universal property for quotients\nof `add_monoid`s, when the additive congruence relation is the kernel of the homomorphism,\ncommutes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.lift_on_units_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.congr", "description": "Makes an isomorphism of quotients by two congruence relations, given that the relations are\n   equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.mul_ker_mk_eq", "description": "The kernel of the quotient map induced by a congruence relation `c` equals `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.lift_funext", "description": "Homomorphisms on the quotient of a monoid by a congruence relation are equal if they\n   are equal on elements that are coercions from the monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.map_apply", "description": "Given congruence relations `c, d` on a monoid such that `d` contains `c`, the definition of\n   the homomorphism from the quotient by `c` to the quotient by `d` induced by `d`'s quotient\n   map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "A coercion from a congruence relation to its underlying binary relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.quotient.inhabited", "description": "There exists an element of the quotient of a monoid by a congruence relation (namely 1).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.has_le", "description": "For additive congruence relations `c, d` on a type `M` with an addition, `c \u2264 d` iff\n`\u2200 x y \u2208 M`, `x` is related to `y` by `d` if `x` is related to `y` by `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.has_div", "description": "The division induced on the quotient by a congruence relation on a type with a\n   division.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.comap_quotient_equiv", "description": "The second isomorphism theorem for monoids.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.inf_iff_and", "description": "Definition of the infimum of two congruence relations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.correspondence", "description": "Given a congruence relation `c` on a type `M` with a multiplication, the order-preserving\n   bijection between the set of congruence relations containing `c` and the congruence relations\n   on the quotient of `M` by `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.quotient_ker_equiv_range", "description": "The first isomorphism theorem for monoids.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.add_ker_mk_eq", "description": "The kernel of the quotient map induced by an additive congruence relation\n`c` equals `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.to_setoid_inj", "description": "The map sending an additive congruence relation to its underlying equivalence\nrelation is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.add_zero_class", "description": "The quotient of an `add_monoid` by an additive congruence relation is\nan `add_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.Inf_to_setoid", "description": "The infimum of a set of additive congruence relations is the same as the infimum of\nthe set's image under the map to the underlying equivalence relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.add", "description": "Additive congruence relations preserve addition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.inf_iff_and", "description": "Definition of the infimum of two additive congruence relations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.prod", "description": "Given types with additions `M, N`, the product of two congruence relations\n`c` on `M` and `d` on `N`: `(x\u2081, x\u2082), (y\u2081, y\u2082) \u2208 M \u00d7 N` are related by `c.prod d` iff `x\u2081`\nis related to `y\u2081` by `c` and `x\u2082` is related to `y\u2082` by `d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.mk'_ker", "description": "The kernel of the natural homomorphism from a monoid to its quotient by a congruence\n   relation `c` equals `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.ext'", "description": "The map sending an additive congruence relation to its underlying binary relation\nis injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.map_of_surjective", "description": "Given a surjective addition-preserving function `f` whose kernel is contained in\nan additive congruence relation `c`, the additive congruence relation on `f`'s codomain defined\nby '`x \u2248 y` iff the elements of `f\u207b\u00b9(x)` are related to the elements of `f\u207b\u00b9(y)` by `c`.'", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.induction_on\u2082", "description": "A version of `con.induction_on` for predicates which take two arguments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.trans", "description": "Additive congruence relations are transitive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.coe_mul", "description": "The coercion to the quotient of a congruence relation commutes with multiplication (by\n   definition).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.le_def", "description": "Definition of `\u2264` for additive congruence relations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.map_of_surjective_eq_map_gen", "description": "A specialization of 'the smallest congruence relation containing a congruence relation `c`\n   equals `c`'.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.of_submonoid", "description": "The congruence relation on a monoid `M` from a submonoid of `M \u00d7 M` for which membership\n   is an equivalence relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.ext'_iff", "description": "Two additive congruence relations are equal iff their underlying binary relations\nare equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.Sup_def", "description": "The supremum of a set of congruence relations is the same as the smallest congruence relation\n   containing the supremum of the set's image under the map to the underlying binary relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.inf_def", "description": "The infimum of two additive congruence relations equals the infimum of the\nunderlying binary operations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.zpow", "description": "Multiplicative congruence relations preserve integer powers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.pi", "description": "The product of an indexed collection of additive congruence relations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.quotient.has_coe_t", "description": "Coercion from a type with an addition to its quotient by an additive congruence\nrelation", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.lift_mk'", "description": "The diagram describing the universal property for quotients of `add_monoid`s\ncommutes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.add_comm_semigroup", "description": "The quotient of an `add_comm_semigroup` by an additive congruence relation is\nan `add_semigroup`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.has_add", "description": "The addition induced on the quotient by an additive congruence relation on a type\nwith an addition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.ker_apply_eq_preimage", "description": "The elements related to `x \u2208 M`, `M` an `add_monoid`, by the kernel of\nan `add_monoid` homomorphism are those in the preimage of `f(x)` under `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.quotient", "description": "Defining the quotient by a congruence relation of a type with a multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.ext_iff", "description": "Iff version of extensionality rule for congruence relations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.lift_surjective_of_surjective", "description": "Surjective monoid homomorphisms constant on a congruence relation `c`'s equivalence classes\n   induce a surjective homomorphism on `c`'s quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.has_mem", "description": "Given a type `M` with an addition, `x, y \u2208 M`, and an additive congruence relation\n`c` on `M`, `(x, y) \u2208 M \u00d7 M` iff `x` is related to `y` by `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.lift_mk'", "description": "The diagram describing the universal property for quotients of monoids commutes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.lift_surjective_of_surjective", "description": "Surjective `add_monoid` homomorphisms constant on an additive congruence\nrelation `c`'s equivalence classes induce a surjective homomorphism on `c`'s quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.mk'", "description": "The natural homomorphism from an `add_monoid` to its quotient by an additive\ncongruence relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.eq", "description": "Two elements are related by an additive congruence relation `c` iff they\nare represented by the same element of the quotient by `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.lift_comp_mk'", "description": "The diagram describing the universal property for quotients of `add_monoid`s\ncommutes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.quotient.decidable_eq", "description": "The quotient by a decidable additive congruence relation has decidable equality.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.complete_lattice", "description": "The complete lattice of additive congruence relations on a given type with\nan addition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.ker_rel", "description": "The definition of the additive congruence relation defined by an `add_monoid`\nhomomorphism's kernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.Inf_to_setoid", "description": "The infimum of a set of congruence relations is the same as the infimum of the set's image\n   under the map to the underlying equivalence relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.symm", "description": "Congruence relations are symmetric.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.lift_on_add_units_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.lift_range", "description": "Given a congruence relation `c` on a monoid and a homomorphism `f` constant on `c`'s\n   equivalence classes, `f` has the same image as the homomorphism that `f` induces on the\n   quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.comm_semigroup", "description": "The quotient of a commutative semigroup by a congruence relation is a semigroup.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.mk'_surjective", "description": "The natural homomorphism from an `add_monoid` to its quotient by a congruence\nrelation is surjective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.comap_eq", "description": "Given an `add_monoid` homomorphism `f : N \u2192 M` and an additive congruence relation\n`c` on `M`, the additive congruence relation induced on `N` by `f` equals the kernel of `c`'s\nquotient homomorphism composed with `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.refl", "description": "Congruence relations are reflexive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.add_monoid", "description": "The quotient of an `add_monoid` by an additive congruence relation is\nan `add_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.quotient.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.ker_apply_eq_preimage", "description": "The elements related to `x \u2208 M`, `M` a monoid, by the kernel of a monoid homomorphism are\n   those in the preimage of `f(x)` under `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.ker", "description": "The kernel of an `add_monoid` homomorphism as an additive congruence relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.mrange_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.quotient_ker_equiv_of_right_inverse", "description": "The first isomorphism theorem for monoids in the case of a homomorphism with right inverse.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.ker_eq_lift_of_injective", "description": "Given an `add_monoid` homomorphism `f` from `M` to `P`, the kernel of `f`\nis the unique additive congruence relation on `M` whose induced map from the quotient of `M`\nto `P` is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.coe_add", "description": "The coercion to the quotient of an additive congruence relation commutes with\naddition (by definition).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.induction_on\u2082", "description": "A version of `add_con.induction_on` for predicates which take\ntwo arguments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.refl", "description": "Additive congruence relations are reflexive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.correspondence", "description": "Given an additive congruence relation `c` on a type `M` with an addition,\nthe order-preserving bijection between the set of additive congruence relations containing `c` and\nthe additive congruence relations on the quotient of `M` by `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.of_add_submonoid", "description": "The additive congruence relation on an `add_monoid` `M` from\nan `add_submonoid` of `M \u00d7 M` for which membership is an equivalence relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.coe_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.ker_lift", "description": "The homomorphism induced on the quotient of a monoid by the kernel of a monoid homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.con_gen_mono", "description": "Given binary relations `r, s` with `r` contained in `s`, the smallest congruence relation\n   containing `s` contains the smallest congruence relation containing `r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.div", "description": "Multiplicative congruence relations preserve division.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.hrec_on\u2082", "description": "A version of `quotient.hrec_on\u2082'` for quotients by `con`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.group", "description": "The quotient of a group by a congruence relation is a group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.mk'_ker", "description": "The kernel of the natural homomorphism from an `add_monoid` to its quotient by\nan additive congruence relation `c` equals `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.con_gen_idem", "description": "The map sending a binary relation to the smallest congruence relation in which it is\n   contained is idempotent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.zsmul", "description": "Additive congruence relations preserve integer scaling.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.to_add_submonoid", "description": "Coercion from a congruence relation `c` on an `add_monoid` `M`\nto the `add_submonoid` of `M \u00d7 M` whose elements are `(x, y)` such that `x`\nis related to `y` by `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.trans", "description": "Congruence relations are transitive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "con.lift_apply_mk'", "description": "Given a homomorphism `f` from the quotient of a monoid by a congruence relation, `f` equals the\n   homomorphism on the quotient induced by `f` composed with the natural map from the monoid to\n   the quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_con.ker_lift_injective", "description": "An `add_monoid` homomorphism `f` induces an injective homomorphism on the quotient\nby `f`'s kernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_at.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_on.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_on.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_on.inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_at.inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_within_at.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lie_add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_at.div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_on.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_within_at.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_within_at.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth.div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_at.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_at.div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff.inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_on.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_add_group", "description": " A Lie (additive) group is a group and a smooth manifold at the same time in which\nthe