ption": "Seminormed ring structure on the product of finitely many seminormed rings,\n using the sup norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nnnorm_prod_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.densely_normed_field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_inv_inv\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semi_normed_ring.induced", "description": " A non-unital ring homomorphism from an `ring` to a `semi_normed_ring` induces a\n`semi_normed_ring` structure on the domain.\n\nSee note [reducible non-instances]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_semi_normed_ring.to_seminormed_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semi_normed_ring.to_non_unital_semi_normed_ring", "description": "A seminormed ring is a non-unital seminormed ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "densely_normed_field.to_nontrivially_normed_field", "description": " A densely normed field is always a nontrivially normed field.\nSee note [lower instance priority].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.norm_prod_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_pow_le", "description": "If `\u03b1` is a seminormed ring with `\u20161\u2016 = 1`, then `\u2016a ^ n\u2016 \u2264 \u2016a\u2016 ^ n`. See also `norm_pow_le'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.norm_cast_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_mul_left_cobounded", "description": " Multiplication on the left by a nonzero element of a normed division ring tends to infinity at\ninfinity. TODO: use `bornology.cobounded` instead of `filter.comap has_norm.norm filter.at_top`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_field.punctured_nhds_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnnorm_pow_le'", "description": " If `\u03b1` is a seminormed ring, then `\u2016a ^ n\u2016\u208a \u2264 \u2016a\u2016\u208a ^ n` for `n > 0`.\nSee also `nnnorm_pow_le`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.normed_comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.to_nnreal_mul_nnnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnreal.nnnorm_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.normed_comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semi_normed_ring", "description": " A seminormed ring is a ring endowed with a seminorm which satisfies the inequality\n`\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semi_normed_ring.to_has_norm", "description": " A seminormed ring is a ring endowed with a seminorm which satisfies the inequality\n`\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semi_normed_ring.to_ring", "description": " A seminormed ring is a ring endowed with a seminorm which satisfies the inequality\n`\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semi_normed_ring.to_pseudo_metric_space", "description": " A seminormed ring is a ring endowed with a seminorm which satisfies the inequality\n`\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semi_normed_ring.dist_eq", "description": " A seminormed ring is a ring endowed with a seminorm which satisfies the inequality\n`\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semi_normed_ring.norm_mul", "description": " A seminormed ring is a ring endowed with a seminorm which satisfies the inequality\n`\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnnorm_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnnorm_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ulift.normed_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_ring.induced", "description": " An injective non-unital ring homomorphism from an `ring` to a `normed_ring` induces a\n`normed_ring` structure on the domain.\n\nSee note [reducible non-instances]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_comm_group.tendsto_at_top'", "description": "A variant of `normed_add_comm_group.tendsto_at_top` that\nuses `\u2203 N, \u2200 n > N, ...` rather than `\u2203 N, \u2200 n \u2265 N, ...`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring_class.to_semi_normed_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nnnorm_prod_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_mul_right_cobounded", "description": " Multiplication on the right by a nonzero element of a normed division ring tends to infinity at\ninfinity. TODO: use `bornology.cobounded` instead of `filter.comap has_norm.norm filter.at_top`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_semi_normed_ring", "description": " A non-unital seminormed ring is a not-necessarily-unital ring\nendowed with a seminorm which satisfies the inequality `\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_semi_normed_ring.to_has_norm", "description": " A non-unital seminormed ring is a not-necessarily-unital ring\nendowed with a seminorm which satisfies the inequality `\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_semi_normed_ring.to_non_unital_ring", "description": " A non-unital seminormed ring is a not-necessarily-unital ring\nendowed with a seminorm which satisfies the inequality `\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_semi_normed_ring.to_pseudo_metric_space", "description": " A non-unital seminormed ring is a not-necessarily-unital ring\nendowed with a seminorm which satisfies the inequality `\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_semi_normed_ring.dist_eq", "description": " A non-unital seminormed ring is a not-necessarily-unital ring\nendowed with a seminorm which satisfies the inequality `\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_semi_normed_ring.norm_mul", "description": " A non-unital seminormed ring is a not-necessarily-unital ring\nendowed with a seminorm which satisfies the inequality `\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_normed_ring", "description": " A non-unital normed ring is a not-necessarily-unital ring\nendowed with a norm which satisfies the inequality `\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_normed_ring.to_has_norm", "description": " A non-unital normed ring is a not-necessarily-unital ring\nendowed with a norm which satisfies the inequality `\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_normed_ring.to_non_unital_ring", "description": " A non-unital normed ring is a not-necessarily-unital ring\nendowed with a norm which satisfies the inequality `\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_normed_ring.to_metric_space", "description": " A non-unital normed ring is a not-necessarily-unital ring\nendowed with a norm which satisfies the inequality `\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_normed_ring.dist_eq", "description": " A non-unital normed ring is a not-necessarily-unital ring\nendowed with a norm which satisfies the inequality `\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_normed_ring.norm_mul", "description": " A non-unital normed ring is a not-necessarily-unital ring\nendowed with a norm which satisfies the inequality `\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_ring.to_semi_normed_ring", "description": "A normed ring is a seminormed ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring_class.to_normed_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.non_unital_normed_ring", "description": " Non-unital normed ring structure on the product of two non-unital normed rings,\nusing the sup norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nndist_inv_inv\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_isometric", "description": " This class states that a ring homomorphism is isometric. This is a sufficient assumption\nfor a continuous semilinear map to be bounded and this is the main use for this typeclass.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_isometric.is_iso", "description": " This class states that a ring homomorphism is isometric. This is a sufficient assumption\nfor a continuous semilinear map to be bounded and this is the main use for this typeclass.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.non_unital_normed_ring", "description": " Normed ring structure on the product of finitely many non-unital normed rings, using the sup\nnorm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_one_class.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.semi_normed_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnnorm_pow_le", "description": " If `\u03b1` is a seminormed ring with `\u20161\u2016\u208a = 1`, then `\u2016a ^ n\u2016\u208a \u2264 \u2016a\u2016\u208a ^ n`.\nSee also `nnnorm_pow_le'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.non_unital_semi_normed_ring", "description": "Non-unital seminormed ring structure on the product of two non-unital seminormed rings,\n using the sup norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.nnnorm_prod_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.norm_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_field.nhds_within_is_unit_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_field.exists_lt_norm_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_isometric.ids", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.nnnorm_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.semi_normed_ring", "description": "Seminormed ring structure on the product of two seminormed rings,\n using the sup norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nontrivially_normed_field", "description": " A nontrivially normed field is a normed field in which there is an element of norm different\nfrom `0` and `1`. This makes it possible to bring any element arbitrarily close to `0` by\nmultiplication by the powers of any element, and thus to relate algebra and topology.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nontrivially_normed_field.to_normed_field", "description": " A nontrivially normed field is a normed field in which there is an element of norm different\nfrom `0` and `1`. This makes it possible to bring any element arbitrarily close to `0` by\nmultiplication by the powers of any element, and thus to relate algebra and topology.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nontrivially_normed_field.non_trivial", "description": " A nontrivially normed field is a normed field in which there is an element of norm different\nfrom `0` and `1`. This makes it possible to bring any element arbitrarily close to `0` by\nmultiplication by the powers of any element, and thus to relate algebra and topology.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_one_of_pow_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.norm_one_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnnorm_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.non_unital_semi_normed_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_normed_ring.to_normed_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.nnnorm_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_ring", "description": "A normed ring is a ring endowed with a norm which satisfies the inequality `\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_ring.to_has_norm", "description": "A normed ring is a ring endowed with a norm which satisfies the inequality `\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_ring.to_ring", "description": "A normed ring is a ring endowed with a norm which satisfies the inequality `\u2016x y\u2016 \u2264 \u2016x\u2016 \u2016y\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"na