lib"}, {"name": "multiset.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.map_filter'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.disjoint_of_le_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.card_eq_three", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.erase_cons_tail", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.map_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.has_ordered_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.disjoint_of_subset_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.mem_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.mem_cons_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.eq_zero_of_forall_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.filter_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.filter_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.zero_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.sub_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.map", "description": "`map f s` is the lift of the list `map` operation. The multiplicity\n of `b` in `map f s` is the number of `a \u2208 s` (counting multiplicity)\n such that `f a = b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.erase_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.card_le_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.subset.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.disjoint_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.count_erase_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.eq_of_mem_replicate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.pair_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.count_singleton_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.forall_mem_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.disjoint", "description": "`disjoint s t` means that `s` and `t` have no elements in common.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.card_erase_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.count_map_eq_count", "description": " `multiset.map f` preserves `count` if `f` is injective on the set of elements contained in\nthe multiset", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.map_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.rec_on_0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.countp_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.rel_map_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.countp_cons_of_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.attach", "description": "\"Attach\" a proof that `a \u2208 s` to each element `a` in `s` to produce\n a multiset on `{x // x \u2208 s}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.map_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.coe_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.to_list_eq_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.strong_downward_induction", "description": " Suppose that, given that `p t` can be defined on all supersets of `s` of cardinality less than\n`n`, one knows how to define `p s`. Then one can inductively define `p s` for all multisets `s` of\ncardinality less than `n`, starting from multisets of card `n` and iterating. This\ncan be used either to define data, or to prove properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.sub", "description": "`s - t` is the multiset such that `count a (s - t) = count a s - count a t` for all `a`\n (note that it is truncated subtraction, so it is `0` if `count a t \u2265 count a s`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.foldr_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.le_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.card_erase_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.card_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, 