_form.to_quadratic_form_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_form.polar_smul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_form.has_smul", "description": " `quadratic_form R M` inherits the scalar action from any algebra over `R`.\n\nWhen `R` is commutative, this provides an `R`-action via `algebra.id`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.nondegenerate_of_anisotropic", "description": "A bilinear form is nondegenerate if the quadratic form it is associated with is anisotropic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_form.is_symm_to_matrix'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_form.add_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_form.sq", "description": "`sq` is the quadratic form mapping the vector `x : R\u2081` to `x * x`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_form.fun_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_form.map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_quadratic_form'", "description": "`M.to_quadratic_form` is the map `\u03bb x, col x \u2b1d M \u2b1d row x` as a quadratic form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_form.polar_zero_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_form.basis_repr_eq_of_is_Ortho", "description": "On an orthogonal basis, the basis representation of `Q` is just a sum of squares.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_form.polar_smul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_form.nondegenerate_of_anisotropic", "description": "The associated bilinear form of an anisotropic quadratic form is nondegenerate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_form.exists_quadratic_form_ne_zero", "description": " There exists a non-null vector with respect to any quadratic form `Q` whose associated\nbilinear form is non-zero, i.e. there exists `x` such that `Q x \u2260 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_form.polar_add_left_iff", "description": "Auxiliary lemma to express bili