t_reverse", "description": " The `list` of a vector after a `reverse`, retrieved by `to_list` is equal\nto the `list.reverse` after retrieving a vector's `to_list`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.remove_nth_insert_nth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.replicate", "description": "A vector with `n` elements `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.tail_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.m_of_fn", "description": " Monadic analog of `vector.of_fn`.\nGiven a monadic function on `fin n`, return a `vector \u03b1 n` inside the monad.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.nth_cons_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.to_list_singleton", "description": " The list that makes up a `vector` made up of a single element,\nretrieved via `to_list`, is equal to the list of that single element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.sum_update_nth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.of_fn_nth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.remove_nth_insert_nth'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.to_list_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.scanl_cons", "description": "The recursive step of `scanl` splits a vector `x ::\u1d65 v : vector \u03b1 (n + 1)`\ninto the provided starting value `b : \u03b2` and the recursed `scanl`\n`f b x : \u03b2` as the starting value.\n\nThis lemma is the `cons` version of `scanl_nth`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.eq_cons_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.id_traverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.nth_update_nth_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.nth_of_fn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.to_list_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.nth_cons_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.update_nth", "description": "`update_nth v n a` replaces the `n`th element of `v` with `a`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.prod_update_nth'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.scanl", "description": "Construct a `vector \u03b2 (n + 1)` from a `vector \u03b1 n` by scanning `f : \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2`\nfrom the \"left\", that is, from 0 to `fin.last n`, using `b : \u03b2` as the starting value.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.mmap_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.not_empty_to_list", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.nth_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.traverse", "description": "Apply an applicative function to each component of a vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.head_of_fn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.last_def", "description": "The last element of a `vector`, given that the vector is at least one element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.vector_equiv_fin", "description": "The natural equivalence between length-`n` vectors and functions from `fin n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.mmap", "description": " Apply a monadic function to each component of a vector,\nreturning a vector inside the monad.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.nth_cons_nil", "description": " Accessing the `nth` element of a vector made up\nof one element `x : \u03b1` is `x` itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.flip.traversable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.scanl_nth", "description": "For an index `i : fin n`, the `nth` element of `scanl` of a\nvector `v : vector \u03b1 n` at `i.succ`, is equal to the application\nfunction `f : \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` of the `i.cast_succ` element of\n`scanl f b v` and `nth v i`.\n\nThis lemma is the `nth` version of `scanl_cons`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.singleton_tail", "description": "The `tail` of a vector made up of one element is `nil`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.reverse_nth_zero", "description": "The `last` element of a vector is the `head` of the `reverse` vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.reverse", "description": "Reverse a vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.tail_nil", "description": "The `tail` of a `nil` vector is `nil`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.mmap_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.traverse_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.to_list_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.nth_tail", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.map_id", "description": "Mapping under `id` does not change a vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.traverse_eq_map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.induction_on", "description": " Define `C v` by induction on `v : vector \u03b1 n`.\n\nThis function has two arguments: `h_nil` handles the base case on `C nil`,\nand `h_cons` defines the inductive step using `\u2200 x : \u03b1, C w \u2192 C (x ::\u1d65 w)`.\n\nThis can be used as `induction v using vector.induction_on`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.nth_replicate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.exists_eq_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.scanl_head", "description": "The first element of `scanl` of a vector `v : vector \u03b1 n`,\nretrieved via `head`, is the starting value `b : \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "centroid_hom.has_npow_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "centroid_hom.coe_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "centroid_hom.add_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "centroid_hom.nsmul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "centroid_hom.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "centroid_hom.ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "centroid_hom.to_End_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "centroid_hom.coe_copy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {