s a type of ordered monoid homomorphisms.\n\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `order_add_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_add_monoid_hom_class.map_zero", "description": " `order_add_monoid_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of ordered monoid homomorphisms.\n\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `order_add_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_add_monoid_hom_class.monotone", "description": " `order_add_monoid_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of ordered monoid homomorphisms.\n\nYou should also extend this typeclass when you extend `order_add_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_monoid_hom.to_order_hom_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_add_monoid_hom.comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_add_monoid_hom.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_monoid_with_zero_hom.id", "description": "The identity map as an ordered monoid with zero homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_monoid_hom.comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_monoid_hom.one_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_add_monoid_hom.add_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_add_monoid_hom.id", "description": "The identity map as an ordered additive monoid homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_add_monoid_hom.mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_monoid_hom.has_coe_to_fun", "description": " Helper instance for when there's too many metavariables to apply `fun_like.has_coe_to_fun`\ndirectly.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_monoid_hom.id", "description": "The identity map as an ordered monoid homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_add_monoid_hom.coe_order_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_monoid_hom.comp", "description": "Composition of `order_monoid_hom`s as an `order_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_monoid_hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_add_monoid_hom.coe_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_add_monoid_hom", "description": " `\u03b1 \u2192+o \u03b2` is the type of monotone functions `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` that preserve the `ordered_add_comm_monoid`\nstructure.\n\n`order_add_monoid_hom` is also used for ordered group homomorphisms.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : \u03b1 \u2192+o \u03b2)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [order_add_monoid_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `order_add_monoid_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_add_monoid_hom.to_add_monoid_hom", "description": " `\u03b1 \u2192+o \u03b2` is the type of monotone functions `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` that preserve the `ordered_add_comm_monoid`\nstructure.\n\n`order_add_monoid_hom` is also used for ordered group homomorphisms.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : \u03b1 \u2192+o \u03b2)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [order_add_monoid_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `order_add_monoid_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_add_monoid_hom.monotone'", "description": " `\u03b1 \u2192+o \u03b2` is the type of monotone functions `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` that preserve the `ordered_add_comm_monoid`\nstructure.\n\n`order_add_monoid_hom` is also used for ordered group homomorphisms.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : \u03b1 \u2192+o \u03b2)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [order_add_monoid_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `order_add_monoid_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_monoid_with_zero_hom.coe_order_monoid_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_monoid_hom.to_order_hom", "description": "Reinterpret an ordered monoid homomorphism as an order homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_monoid_with_zero_hom.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_add_monoid_hom.to_add_monoid_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_monoid_with_zero_hom.comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_monoid_hom.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_add_monoid_hom.to_add_monoid_hom_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_monoid_hom.order_monoid_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone_iff_map_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_monoid_hom_class.to_order_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_monoid_with_zero_hom.coe_comp_order_monoid_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.exists_ne_map_eq_of_infinite", "description": "The pigeonhole principle for infinitely many pigeons in finitely many pigeonholes. If there are\ninfinitely many pigeons in finitely many pigeonholes, then there are at least two pigeons in the\nsame pigeonhole.\n\nSee also: `fintype.exists_ne_map_eq_of_card_lt`, `finite.exists_infinite_fiber`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_quotient_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.injective_iff_surjective_of_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_fin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.injective_iff_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_punit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_lt_iff_ne_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_eq_iff_eq_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_pempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.equiv_of_fintype_self_embedding_to_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.univ_map_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.nodup.length_le_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infinite.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_fin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set_fintype_card_le_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infinite.of_not_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_lt_univ_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.exists_infinite_fiber", "description": "The strong pigeonhole principle for infinitely many pigeons in\nfinitely many pigeonholes.  If there are infinitely many pigeons in\nfinitely many pigeonholes, then there is a pigeonhole with infinitely\nmany pigeons.\n\nSee also: `finite.exists_ne_map_eq_of_infinite`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.one_lt_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_subtype_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_lex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_eq_zero_equiv_equiv_empty", "description": "A `fintype` with cardinality zero is equivalent to `empty`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.equiv_fin_of_card_eq", "description": " If the cardinality of `\u03b1` is `n`, there is noncomputably a bijection between `\u03b1` and `fin n`.\n\nSee `fintype.trunc_equiv_fin_of_card_eq` for the computable definition,\nand `fintype.trunc_equiv_fin` and `fintype.equiv_fin` for the bijection `\u03b1 \u2243 fin (card \u03b1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.well_founded_of_trans_of_irrefl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_left_inverse_of_card_le", "description": "Construct an equivalence from functions that are inverse to each other.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_pos_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_surjective_finite_infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_left", "description": " Given that `\u03b1 \u2295 \u03b2` is a fintype, `\u03b1` is also a fintype. This is non-computable as it uses\nthat `sum.inl` is an injection, but there's no clear inverse if `\u03b1` is empty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_order_dual", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infinite.exists_not_mem_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_ulift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_Prop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.exists_ne_map_eq_of_card_lt", "description": "The pigeonhole principle for finitely many pigeons and pigeonholes.\nThis is the `fintype` version of `finset.exists_ne_map_eq_of_card_lt_of_maps_to`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.right_inverse.left_inverse_of_card_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_bool", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infinite.of_surjective_from_set", "description": "If `s : set \u03b1` is a proper subset of `\u03b1` and `f : s \u2192 \u03b1` is surjective, then `\u03b1` is infinite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_le_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_subtype_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_of_finset'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_injective_infinite_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.one_lt_card_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.finite.to_well_founded_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.exists_ne_of_one_lt_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_left_inverse_of_card_le_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_subtype_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.nonempty_iff_card_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_of_bijective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_empty_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.exists_of_card_le_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.nonempty_of_card_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infinite.of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.bijective_iff_injective_and_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_left_inverse_of_card_le_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infinite.exists_superset_card_eq", "description": " See `infinite.exists_subset_card_eq` for a version that provides an arbitrary\n`s : finset \u03b1` for any cardinality.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_of_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.is_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.trunc_fin_bijection", "description": " There is (computably) a bijection between `fin (card \u03b1)` and `\u03b1`.\n\nSince it is not unique and depends on which permutation\nof the universe list is used, the bijection is wrapped in `trunc` to\npreserve computability.\n\nSee `fintype.trunc_equiv_fin` for a version that gives an equivalence\ngiven `[decidable_eq \u03b1]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_right", "description": " Given that `\u03b1 \u2295 \u03b2` is a fintype, `\u03b2` is also a fintype. This is non-computable as it uses\nthat `sum.inr` is an injection, but there's no clear inverse if `\u03b2` is empty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.trunc_equiv_fin_of_card_eq", "description": " If the cardinality of `\u03b1` is `n`, there is computably a bijection between `\u03b1` and `fin n`.\n\nSee `fintype.equiv_fin_of_card_eq` for the noncomputable definition,\nand `fintype.trunc_equiv_fin` and `fintype.equiv_fin` for the bijection `\u03b1 \u2243 fin (card \u03b1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.surjective_of_fintype", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `finite.injective_iff_surjective_of_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.trunc_equiv_of_card_eq", "description": " Two `fintype`s with the same cardinality are (computably) in bijection.\n\nSee `fintype.equiv_of_card_eq` for the noncomputable version,\nand `fintype.trunc_equiv_fin_of_card_eq` and `fintype.equiv_fin_of_card_eq` for\nthe specialization to `fin`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_eq_one_iff_nonempty_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.surjective_iff_bijective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.trunc_equiv_fin", "description": " There is (computably) an equivalence between `\u03b1` and `fin (card \u03b1)`.\n\nSince it is not unique and depends on which permutation\nof the universe list is used, the equivalence is wrapped in `trunc` to\npreserve computability.\n\nSee `fintype.equiv_fin` for the noncomputable version,\nand `fintype.trunc_equiv_fin_of_card_eq` and `fintype.equiv_fin_of_card_eq`\nfor an equiv `\u03b1 \u2243 fin n` given `fintype.card \u03b1 = n`.\n\nSee `fintype.trunc_fin_bijection` for a version without `[decidable_eq \u03b1]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.bijective_iff_surjective_and_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.injective_of_fintype", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `finite.injective_iff_surjective_of_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.of_equiv_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_iff_nonempty_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_congr'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_subtype_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_le_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.linear_order.is_well_order_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infinite.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_subtype_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.equiv_fin", "description": "Noncomputable equivalence between a finset `s` coerced to a type and `fin s.card`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonempty_fintype", "description": "See also `nonempty_encodable`, `nonempty_denumerable`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_eq_one_of_forall_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.of_finite", "description": " Noncomputably get a `fintype` instance from a `finite` instance. This is not an\ninstance because we want `fintype` instances to be useful for computations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set_fintype_card_eq_univ_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.equiv_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.equiv_fin_of_card_eq", "description": " Noncomputable equivalence between a finset `s` as a fintype and `fin n`, when there is a\nproof that `s.card = n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.induction_subsingleton_or_nontrivial", "description": " A custom induction principle for fintypes. The base case is a subsingleton type,\nand the induction step is for non-trivial types, and one can assume the hypothesis for\nsmaller types (via `fintype.card`).\n\nThe major premise is `fintype \u03b1`, so to use this with the `induction` tactic you have to give a name\nto that instance and use that name.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.infinite_of_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.exists_minimal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infinite.nat_embedding", "description": "Embedding of `\u2115` into an infinite type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.linear_order.is_well_order_gt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.cast_eq_cast'", "description": "A reversed version of `fin.cast_eq_cast` that is easier to rewrite with.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype_of_not_infinite", "description": "A non-infinite type is a fintype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.exists_maximal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.infinite_of_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.is_empty_of_card_lt", "description": " If `\u2016\u03b2\u2016 < \u2016\u03b1\u2016` there are no embeddings `\u03b1 \u21aa \u03b2`.\nThis is a formulation of the pigeonhole principle.\n\nNote this cannot be an instance as it needs `h`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_compl_lt_iff_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infinite.exists_subset_card_eq", "description": " See `infinite.exists_superset_card_eq` for a version that, for a `s : finset \u03b1`,\nprovides a superset `t : finset \u03b1`, `s \u2286 t` such that `t.card` is fixed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.two_lt_card_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.of_fintype", "description": " For efficiency reasons, we want `finite` instances to have higher\npriority than ones coming from `fintype` instances.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_compl_eq_card_compl", "description": "If two subtypes of a fintype have equal cardinality, so do their complements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.exists_pair_of_one_lt_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_le_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.one_lt_card_iff_nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_eq_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.trunc_of_card_le", "description": "A constructive embedding of a fintype `\u03b1` in another fintype `\u03b2` when `card \u03b1 \u2264 card \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.equiv_of_fintype_self_embedding", "description": "An embedding from a `fintype` to itself can be promoted to an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infinite.of_injective_to_set", "description": "If `s : set \u03b1` is a proper subset of `\u03b1` and `f : \u03b1 \u2192 s` is injective, then `\u03b1` is infinite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.subtype_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.false", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin_injective", "description": " `fin` as a map from `\u2115` to `Type` is injective. Note that since this is a statement about\nequality of types, using it should be avoided if possible.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.infinite_of_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.infinite_of_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_right_inverse_of_card_le", "description": "Construct an equivalence from functions that are inverse to each other.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_right_inverse_of_card_le_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infinite.of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.equiv_of_card_eq", "description": " Two `fintype`s with the same cardinality are (noncomputably) in bijection.\n\nSee `fintype.trunc_equiv_of_card_eq` for the computable version,\nand `fintype.trunc_equiv_fin_of_card_eq` and `fintype.equiv_fin_of_card_eq` for\nthe specialization to `fin`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_lt_of_surjective_not_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_of_is_empty", "description": " Note: this lemma is specifically about `fintype.of_is_empty`. For a statement about\narbitrary `fintype` instances, use `fintype.card_eq_zero_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_quotient_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_le_of_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_finset_card", "description": "Extension for the `positivity` tactic: `finset.card s` is positive if `s` is nonempty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_lt_of_injective_not_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.of_right_inverse_of_card_le_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_le_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.bijective_of_finite", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `finite.injective_iff_bijective`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infinite.set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.bijective_of_finite", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `finite.surjective_iff_bijective`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.injective_iff_bijective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.eq_univ_of_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "univ_eq_singleton_of_card_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "card_finset_fin_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_le_one_iff_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_range_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_compl_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_lt_of_injective_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.exists_univ_list", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trunc_of_card_pos", "description": "A `fintype` with positive cardinality constructively contains an element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_univ_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_plift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.finite.to_well_founded_gt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.equiv_fin", "description": " There is (noncomputably) an equivalence between `\u03b1` and `fin (card \u03b1)`.\n\nSee `fintype.trunc_equiv_fin` for the computable version,\nand `fintype.trunc_equiv_fin_of_card_eq` and `fintype.equiv_fin_of_card_eq`\nfor an equiv `\u03b1 \u2243 fin n` given `fintype.card \u03b1 = n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.equiv_of_card_eq", "description": " Noncomputable equivalence between two finsets `s` and `t` as fintypes when there is a proof\nthat `s.card = t.card`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_of_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.left_inverse.right_inverse_of_card_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype_of_finset_card_le", "description": "If every finset in a type has bounded cardinality, that type is finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card", "description": "`card \u03b1` is the number of elements in `\u03b1`, defined when `\u03b1` is a fintype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_of_subsingleton", "description": " Note: this lemma is specifically about `fintype.of_subsingleton`. For a statement about\narbitrary `fintype` instances, use either `fintype.card_le_one_iff_subsingleton` or\n`fintype.card_unique`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_subtype_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype_or_infinite", "description": "Any type is (classically) either a `fintype`, or `infinite`.\n\nOne can obtain the relevant typeclasses via `cases fintype_or_infinite \u03b1; resetI`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.singleton_vsub_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.add_torsor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vsub_sub_vsub_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.snd_vsub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_of_vsub_eq_zero", "description": "If subtracting two points produces 0, they are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.point_reflection_involutive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vsub_eq_sub", "description": " Simplify subtraction for a torsor for an `add_group G` over\nitself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vadd_vsub_vadd_cancel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_torsor.subsingleton_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.coe_vadd_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vadd_vsub_vadd_cancel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.coe_const_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.point_reflection_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.point_reflection_fixed_iff_of_injective_bit0", "description": " `x` is the only fixed point of `point_reflection x`. This lemma requires\n`x + x = y + y \u2194 x = y`. There is no typeclass to use here, so we add it as an explicit argument.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.point_reflection_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.mk_vadd_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.mk_vsub_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vadd_right_injective", "description": " Adding a group element to the point `p` is an injective\nfunction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_torsor", "description": " An `add_torsor G P` gives a structure to the nonempty type `P`,\nacted on by an `add_group G` with a transitive and free action given\nby the `+\u1d65` operation and a corresponding subtraction given by the\n`-\u1d65` operation. In the case of a vector space, it is an affine\nspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_torsor.to_add_action", "description": " An `add_torsor G P` gives a structure to the nonempty type `P`,\nacted on by an `add_group G` with a transitive and free action given\nby the `+\u1d65` operation and a corresponding subtraction given by the\n`-\u1d65` operation. In the case of a vector space, it is an affine\nspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_torsor.to_has_vsub", "description": " An `add_torsor G P` gives a structure to the nonempty type `P`,\nacted on by an `add_group G` with a transitive and free action given\nby the `+\u1d65` operation and a corresponding subtraction given by the\n`-\u1d65` operation. In the case of a vector space, it is an affine\nspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_torsor.nonempty", "description": " An `add_torsor G P` gives a structure to the nonempty type `P`,\nacted on by an `add_group G` with a transitive and free action given\nby the `+\u1d65` operation and a corresponding subtraction given by the\n`-\u1d65` operation. In the case of a vector space, it is an affine\nspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_torsor.vsub_vadd'", "description": " An `add_torsor G P` gives a structure to the nonempty type `P`,\nacted on by an `add_group G` with a transitive and free action given\nby the `+\u1d65` operation and a corresponding subtraction given by the\n`-\u1d65` operation. In the case of a vector space, it is an affine\nspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_torsor.vadd_vsub'", "description": " An `add_torsor G P` gives a structure to the nonempty type `P`,\nacted on by an `add_group G` with a transitive and free action given\nby the `+\u1d65` operation and a corresponding subtraction given by the\n`-\u1d65` operation. In the case of a vector space, it is an affine\nspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vsub_vadd_eq_vsub_sub", "description": " Subtracting the result of adding a group element produces the same result\nas subtracting the points and subtracting that group element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.const_vadd_hom", "description": "`equiv.const_vadd` as a homomorphism from `multiplicative G` to `equiv.perm P`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.point_reflection_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.fst_vsub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vadd_right_cancel_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vadd_vsub_eq_sub_vsub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vsub_left_injective", "description": "Subtracting the point `p` is an injective function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.point_reflection", "description": "Point reflection in `x` as a permutation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.const_vsub", "description": "`p' \u21a6 p -\u1d65 p'` as an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vadd_vsub", "description": " Adding a group element then subtracting the original point\nproduces that group element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vadd_eq_vadd_iff_sub_eq_vsub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vsub_add_vsub_cancel", "description": "Cancellation adding the results of two subtractions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "neg_vsub_eq_vsub_rev", "description": " Subtracting two points in the reverse order produces the negation\nof subtracting them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vsub_right_injective", "description": " Subtracting a point from the point `p` is an injective\nfunction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vsub_right_cancel", "description": " If subtracting two points from the same point produces equal\nresults, those points are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vadd_eq_vadd_iff_neg_add_eq_vsub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.const_vadd", "description": "The permutation given by `p \u21a6 v +\u1d65 p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vadd_vsub_assoc", "description": " Adding a group element to a point, then subtracting another point,\nproduces the same result as subtracting the points then adding the\ngroup element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.coe_vadd_const_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vsub_sub_vsub_cancel_right", "description": "Cancellation subtracting the results of two subtractions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vsub_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.vadd_const", "description": "`v \u21a6 v +\u1d65 p` as an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vadd_right_cancel", "description": " If the same point added to two group elements produces equal\nresults, those group elements are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vsub_left_cancel_iff", "description": " The same point subtracted from two points produces equal results\nif and only if those points are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.snd_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vsub_left_cancel", "description": " If the same point subtracted from two points produces equal\nresults, those points are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.const_vadd_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.add_torsor", "description": "A product of `add_torsor`s is an `add_torsor`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.injective_point_reflection_left_of_injective_bit0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_vadd_iff_vsub_eq", "description": " Convert between an equality with adding a group element to a point\nand an equality of a subtraction of two points with a group\nelement.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.const_vadd_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vsub_sub_vsub_cancel_left", "description": "Cancellation subtracting the results of two subtractions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vsub_eq_zero_iff_eq", "description": " Subtracting two points produces 0 if and only if they are\nequal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.coe_const_vsub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vsub_right_cancel_iff", "description": " Subtracting two points from the same point produces equal results\nif and only if those points are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_is_add_torsor", "description": "An `add_group G` is a torsor for itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vsub_self", "description": "Subtracting a point from itself produces 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vsub_vadd_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vsub_vadd", "description": " Adding the result of subtracting from another point produces that\npoint.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.coe_const_vsub_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.fst_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.to_span_singleton_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.add_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_semilinear_equiv_class", "description": " `continuous_semilinear_equiv_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled continuous\n`\u03c3`-semilinear equivs `M \u2192 M\u2082`.  See also `continuous_linear_equiv_class F R M M\u2082` for the case\nwhere `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.  A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring\nhomomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S` is semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y`\nand `f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_semilinear_equiv_class.coe", "description": " `continuous_semilinear_equiv_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled continuous\n`\u03c3`-semilinear equivs `M \u2192 M\u2082`.  See also `continuous_linear_equiv_class F R M M\u2082` for the case\nwhere `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.  A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring\nhomomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S` is semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y`\nand `f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_semilinear_equiv_class.inv", "description": " `continuous_semilinear_equiv_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled continuous\n`\u03c3`-semilinear equivs `M \u2192 M\u2082`.  See also `continuous_linear_equiv_class F R M M\u2082` for the case\nwhere `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.  A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring\nhomomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S` is semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y`\nand `f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_semilinear_equiv_class.left_inv", "description": " `continuous_semilinear_equiv_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled continuous\n`\u03c3`-semilinear equivs `M \u2192 M\u2082`.  See also `continuous_linear_equiv_class F R M M\u2082` for the case\nwhere `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.  A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring\nhomomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S` is semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y`\nand `f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_semilinear_equiv_class.right_inv", "description": " `continuous_semilinear_equiv_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled continuous\n`\u03c3`-semilinear equivs `M \u2192 M\u2082`.  See also `continuous_linear_equiv_class F R M M\u2082` for the case\nwhere `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.  A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring\nhomomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S` is semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y`\nand `f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_semilinear_equiv_class.coe_injective'", "description": " `continuous_semilinear_equiv_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled continuous\n`\u03c3`-semilinear equivs `M \u2192 M\u2082`.  See also `continuous_linear_equiv_class F R M M\u2082` for the case\nwhere `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.  A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring\nhomomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S` is semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y`\nand `f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_semilinear_equiv_class.map_add", "description": " `continuous_semilinear_equiv_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled continuous\n`\u03c3`-semilinear equivs `M \u2192 M\u2082`.  See also `continuous_linear_equiv_class F R M M\u2082` for the case\nwhere `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.  A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring\nhomomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S` is semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y`\nand `f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_semilinear_equiv_class.map_smul\u209b\u2097", "description": " `continuous_semilinear_equiv_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled continuous\n`\u03c3`-semilinear equivs `M \u2192 M\u2082`.  See also `continuous_linear_equiv_class F R M M\u2082` for the case\nwhere `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.  A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring\nhomomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S` is semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y`\nand `f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_semilinear_equiv_class.map_continuous", "description": " `continuous_semilinear_equiv_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled continuous\n`\u03c3`-semilinear equivs `M \u2192 M\u2082`.  See also `continuous_linear_equiv_class F R M M\u2082` for the case\nwhere `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.  A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring\nhomomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S` is semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y`\nand `f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_semilinear_equiv_class.inv_continuous", "description": " `continuous_semilinear_equiv_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled continuous\n`\u03c3`-semilinear equivs `M \u2192 M\u2082`.  See also `continuous_linear_equiv_class F R M M\u2082` for the case\nwhere `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.  A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring\nhomomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S` is semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y`\nand `f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_range.topological_closure_map_submodule", "description": " Under a dense continuous linear map, a submodule whose `topological_closure` is `\u22a4` is sent to\nanother such submodule.  That is, the image of a dense set under a map with dense range is dense.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.prod_equiv", "description": "`continuous_linear_map.prod` as an `equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.coe_fun_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.fst_comp_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.map_nhds_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.comp_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.apply_has_faithful_smul", "description": "`continuous_linear_map.apply_module` is faithful.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.pi", "description": " `pi` construction for continuous linear functions. From a family of continuous linear functions\nit produces a continuous linear function into a family of topological modules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.fin_two_arrow_to_linear_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.coe_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.continuous_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map_of_tendsto", "description": "Construct a bundled linear map from a pointwise limit of linear maps", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coprod_inl_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coprod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.eq_top_of_nonempty_interior'", "description": " If `M` is a topological module over `R` and `0` is a limit of invertible elements of `R`, then\n`\u22a4` is the only submodule of `M` with a nonempty interior.\nThis is the case, e.g., if `R` is a nontrivially normed field.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.to_span_singleton", "description": " Given an element `x` of a topological space `M` over a semiring `R`, the natural continuous\nlinear map from `R` to `M` by taking multiples of `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.arrow_congr_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.closed_complemented_ker_of_right_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.coe_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.mul_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.inl_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"na