lib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.prod", "description": "Product of two continuous linear equivalences. The map comes from `equiv.prod_congr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.self_comp_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.pi_fin_two_to_linear_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.symm_trans_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.inverse_equiv", "description": "By definition, if `f` is invertible then `inverse f = f.symm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.map_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.closed_complemented_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.coe_subtypeL'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.map_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.simps.apply", "description": "See Note [custom simps projection]. We need to specify this projection explicitly in this case,\n because it is a composition of multiple projections.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.symm", "description": "The inverse of a continuous linear equivalence as a continuous linear equivalence", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.to_linear_map_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_lm\u209b\u2097", "description": "The coercion from `M \u2192SL[\u03c3] M\u2082` to `M \u2192\u209b\u2097[\u03c3] M\u2082`, as a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.to_fun", "description": "Coerce continuous linear maps to functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.smul_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.map_smul_of_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.ring_inverse_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.uniform_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.restrict_scalars", "description": " If `A` is an `R`-algebra, then a continuous `A`-linear map can be interpreted as a continuous\n`R`-linear map. We assume `linear_map.compatible_smul M M\u2082 R A` to match assumptions of\n`linear_map.map_smul_of_tower`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.simps.apply", "description": "See Note [custom simps projection]. We need to specify this projection explicitly in this case,\n because it is a composition of multiple projections.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.equiv_of_inverse_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.fun_unique", "description": "If `\u03b9` has a unique element, then `\u03b9 \u2192 M` is continuously linear equivalent to `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.units_equiv_aut", "description": "Continuous linear equivalences `R \u2243L[R] R` are enumerated by `R\u02e3`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_proj_ker_of_right_inverse_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.smul_right\u2097", "description": " Given `c : E \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] \ud835\udd5c`, `c.smul_right\u2097` is the linear map from `F` to `E \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] F`\nsending `f` to `\u03bb e, c e \u2022 f`. See also `continuous_linear_map.smul_rightL`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.ext_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.prod_ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.linear_map.has_coe", "description": "Coerce continuous linear maps to linear maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_smul_right\u2097", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.is_open_map_of_ne_zero", "description": "A nonzero continuous linear functional is open.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.restrict_scalars_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.neg_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.image_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.one_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_fn_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.prod\u2097", "description": "`continuous_linear_map.prod` as a `linear_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_prod_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_semilinear_map_class", "description": " `continuous_semilinear_map_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled continuous\n`\u03c3`-semilinear maps `M \u2192 M\u2082`.  See also `continuous_linear_map_class F R M M\u2082` for the case where\n`\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.  A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring\nhomomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S` is semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y`\nand `f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_semilinear_map_class.coe", "description": " `continuous_semilinear_map_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled continuous\n`\u03c3`-semilinear maps `M \u2192 M\u2082`.  See also `continuous_linear_map_class F R M M\u2082` for the case where\n`\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.  A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring\nhomomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S` is semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y`\nand `f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_semilinear_map_class.coe_injective'", "description": " `continuous_semilinear_map_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled continuous\n`\u03c3`-semilinear maps `M \u2192 M\u2082`.  See also `continuous_linear_map_class F R M M\u2082` for the case where\n`\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.  A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring\nhomomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S` is semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y`\nand `f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_semilinear_map_class.map_add", "description": " `continuous_semilinear_map_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled continuous\n`\u03c3`-semilinear maps `M \u2192 M\u2082`.  See also `continuous_linear_map_class F R M M\u2082` for the case where\n`\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.  A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring\nhomomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S` is semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y`\nand `f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_semilinear_map_class.map_smul\u209b\u2097", "description": " `continuous_semilinear_map_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled continuous\n`\u03c3`-semilinear maps `M \u2192 M\u2082`.  See also `continuous_linear_map_class F R M M\u2082` for the case where\n`\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.  A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring\nhomomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S` is semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y`\nand `f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_semilinear_map_class.map_continuous", "description": " `continuous_semilinear_map_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled continuous\n`\u03c3`-semilinear maps `M \u2192 M\u2082`.  See also `continuous_linear_map_class F R M M\u2082` for the case where\n`\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.  A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring\nhomomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S` is semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y`\nand `f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.coe_to_homeomorph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.map_smul\u209b\u2097", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.is_closed_ker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.fin_two_arrow_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_neg'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.coe_symm_comp_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.skew_prod_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map_of_mem_closure_range_coe_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map", "description": " Continuous linear maps between modules. We only put the type classes that are necessary for the\ndefinition, although in applications `M` and `M\u2082` will be topological modules over the topological\nring `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.to_linear_map", "description": " Continuous linear maps between modules. We only put the type classes that are necessary for the\ndefinition, although in applications `M` and `M\u2082` will be topological modules over the topological\nring `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.cont", "description": " Continuous linear maps between modules. We only put the type classes that are necessary for the\ndefinition, although in applications `M` and `M\u2082` will be topological modules over the topological\nring `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.complete_space_ker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.le_topological_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.snd_equiv_of_right_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.coe_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.bijective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.pi_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_closed_range_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.mul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.inr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.equiv_of_right_inverse_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.sub_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.ext_on", "description": " If the submodule generated by a set `s` is dense in the ambient module, then two continuous\nlinear maps equal on `s` are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_pi'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.map_smul\u209b\u2097", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.has_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.is_closed_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.eq_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.equiv_of_right_inverse", "description": " A pair of continuous linear maps such that `f\u2081 \u2218 f\u2082 = id` generates a continuous\nlinear equivalence `e` between `M` and `M\u2082 \u00d7 f\u2081.ker` such that `(e x).2 = x` for `x \u2208 f\u2081.ker`,\n`(e x).1 = f\u2081 x`, and `(e (f\u2082 y)).2 = 0`. The map is given by `e x = (f\u2081 x, x - f\u2082 (f\u2081 x))`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map_class", "description": " `continuous_linear_map_class F R M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled continuous\n`R`-linear maps `M \u2192 M\u2082`.  This is an abbreviation for\n`continuous_semilinear_map_class F (ring_hom.id R) M M\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.ring_inverse_eq_map_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.preimage_symm_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.proj_ker_of_right_inverse_comp_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_sub'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.pi_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.ext\u2081", "description": "An extensionality lemma for `R \u2243L[R] M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.coe_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.topological_closure_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.closed_complemented", "description": "A submodule `p` is called *complemented* if there exists a continuous projection `M \u2192\u2097[R] p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.symm_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.subtypeL", "description": "`submodule.subtype` as a `continuous_linear_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.simps.symm_apply", "description": "See Note [custom simps projection]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_eq_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.has_continuous_smul_quotient", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.uniform_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.smul_right", "description": " The linear map `\u03bb x, c x \u2022 f`.  Associates to a scalar-valued linear map and an element of\n`M\u2082` the `M\u2082`-valued linear map obtained by multiplying the two (a.k.a. tensoring by `M\u2082`).\nSee also `continuous_linear_map.smul_right\u2097` and `continuous_linear_map.smul_rightL`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.symm_preimage_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_semilinear_map_class.to_semilinear_map_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.smul_right_one_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.is_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.trans_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.units_equiv_aut_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.is_complete_ker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.smul_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.skew_prod", "description": "Equivalence given by a block lower diagonal matrix. `e` and `e'` are diagonal square blocks,\n and `f` is a rectangular block below the diagonal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.has_continuous_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.proj_ker_of_right_inverse", "description": " Given a right inverse `f\u2082 : M\u2082 \u2192L[R] M` to `f\u2081 : M \u2192L[R] M\u2082`,\n`proj_ker_of_right_inverse f\u2081 f\u2082 h` is the projection `M \u2192L[R] f\u2081.ker` along `f\u2082.range`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.coe_subtypeL", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.default_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.closed_complemented.has_closed_complement", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.comp_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.zero_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.smul_right_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_prod_map'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.smul_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_smul.of_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map_of_mem_closure_range_coe", "description": " Constructs a bundled linear map from a function and a proof that this function belongs to the\nclosure of the set of linear maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.fin_two_arrow_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.ulift", "description": "The continuous linear equivalence between `ulift M\u2081` and `M\u2081`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.monoid_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.pi_fin_two_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_set_of_map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.topological_closure", "description": " The (topological-space) closure of a submodule of a topological `R`-module `M` is itself\na submodule.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.closure_smul_self_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.inverse_non_equiv", "description": "By definition, if `f` is not invertible then `inverse f = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.preimage_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.symm_comp_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dense_iff_topological_closure_eq_top", "description": "A subspace is dense iff its topological closure is the entire space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.prod_map", "description": "`prod.map` of two continuous linear maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.to_linear_map_ring_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.to_homeomorph", "description": "A continuous linear equivalence induces a homeomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.apply_smul_comm_class'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_coprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.pi_fin_two", "description": "Continuous linear equivalence between dependent functions `\u03a0 i : fin 2, M i` and `M 0 \u00d7 M 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.topological_add_group_quotient", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.refl_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.closure_smul_self_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.sum_