s_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.smul_right_one_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_closed_or_dense_of_is_coatom", "description": " A maximal proper subspace of a topological module (i.e a `submodule` satisfying `is_coatom`)\nis either closed or dense.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_semilinear_equiv_class.continuous_semilinear_map_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_cod_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "Coerce continuous linear equivs to maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.closed_complemented_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.has_zero", "description": "The continuous map that is constantly zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.to_continuous_linear_map", "description": "A continuous linear equivalence induces a continuous linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_open_map_mkq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_snd'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_fst'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.arrow_congr_equiv", "description": " A pair of continuous (semi)linear equivalences generates an equivalence between the spaces of\ncontinuous linear maps. See also `continuous_linear_equiv.arrow_congr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv", "description": " Continuous linear equivalences between modules. We only put the type classes that are necessary\nfor the definition, although in applications `M` and `M\u2082` will be topological modules over the\ntopological semiring `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.to_linear_equiv", "description": " Continuous linear equivalences between modules. We only put the type classes that are necessary\nfor the definition, although in applications `M` and `M\u2082` will be topological modules over the\ntopological semiring `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.continuous_to_fun", "description": " Continuous linear equivalences between modules. We only put the type classes that are necessary\nfor the definition, although in applications `M` and `M\u2082` will be topological modules over the\ntopological semiring `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.continuous_inv_fun", "description": " Continuous linear equivalences between modules. We only put the type classes that are necessary\nfor the definition, although in applications `M` and `M\u2082` will be topological modules over the\ntopological semiring `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.simps.coe", "description": "See Note [custom simps projection].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.fin_two_arrow", "description": "Continuous linear equivalence between vectors in `M\u00b2 = fin 2 \u2192 M` and `M \u00d7 M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.proj_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.inverse", "description": " Introduce a function `inverse` from `M \u2192L[R] M\u2082` to `M\u2082 \u2192L[R] M`, which sends `f` to `f.symm` if\n`f` is a continuous linear equivalence and to `0` otherwise.  This definition is somewhat ad hoc,\nbut one needs a fully (rather than partially) defined inverse function for some purposes, including\nfor calculus.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.unique_of_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.ker_prod_ker_le_ker_coprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.copy", "description": " Copy of a `continuous_linear_map` with a new `to_fun` equal to the old one. Useful to fix\ndefinitional equalities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.submodule_topological_closure_eq", "description": "The topological closure of a closed submodule `s` is equal to `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.restrict_scalars_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.to_span_singleton_smul'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.symm_apply_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map_of_tendsto_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.to_span_singleton_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.add_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.fst_prod_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.coe_to_linear_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.symm_map_nhds_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.snd", "description": "`prod.snd` as a `continuous_linear_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.range_prod_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.topological_closure.complete_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.comp", "description": "Composition of bounded linear maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_id'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.prod_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.proj_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.ker_cod_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.refl", "description": "The identity map as a continuous linear equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.prod_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_restrict_scalars\u2097", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.image_eq_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.arrow_congr_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.inr", "description": "The right injection into a product is a continuous linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.cod_restrict", "description": "Restrict codomain of a continuous linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.units_equiv_aut_apply_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.snd_comp_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.comp_continuous_on_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_lm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.proj_ker_of_right_inverse_apply_idem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.image_symm_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.closed_complemented.is_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.trans_to_linear_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.unique_of_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.inl", "description": "The left injection into a product is a continuous linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.of_unit", "description": "An invertible continuous linear map `f` determines a continuous equivalence from `M` to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.infi_ker_proj_equiv", "description": " If `I` and `J` are complementary index sets, the product of the kernels of the `J`th projections\nof `\u03c6` is linearly equivalent to the product over `I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.to_ring_inverse", "description": " The function `continuous_linear_equiv.inverse` can be written in terms of `ring.inverse` for the\nring of self-maps of the domain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.sub_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.fst", "description": "`prod.fst` as a `continuous_linear_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.pi_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.prod_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.copy_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.punctured_nhds_ne_bot", "description": " Let `R` be a topological ring such that zero is not an isolated point (e.g., a nontrivially\nnormed field, see `normed_field.punctured_nhds_ne_bot`). Let `M` be a nontrivial module over `R`\nsuch that `c \u2022 x = 0` implies `c = 0 \u2228 x = 0`. Then `M` has no isolated points. We formulate this\nusing `ne_bot (\ud835\udcdd[\u2260] x)`.\n\nThis lemma is not an instance because Lean would need to find `[has_continuous_smul ?m_1 M]` with\nunknown `?m_1`. We register this as an instance for `R = \u211d` in `real.punctured_nhds_module_ne_bot`.\nOne can also use `haveI := module.punctured_nhds_ne_bot R M` in a proof.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.uniform_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.restrict_scalars_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_smul'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.to_unit", "description": "A continuous equivalence from `M` to itself determines an invertible continuous linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.smul_right_one_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_cod_restrict_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.coe_comp_coe_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.automorphism_group", "description": "The continuous linear equivalences from `M` to itself form a group under composition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.continuous_on_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.units_equiv", "description": " The units of the algebra of continuous `R`-linear endomorphisms of `M` is multiplicatively\nequivalent to the type of continuous linear equivalences between `M` and itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_restrict_scalars'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.fst_equiv_of_right_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.map_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.topological_closure_minimal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {