"subalgebra.subsingleton_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.coe_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.gi", "description": "Galois insertion between `adjoin` and `coe`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.to_comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.module'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.range_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.algebra'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.to_linear_ordered_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.is_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.subring_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.range_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.top_equiv", "description": " The top subalgebra is isomorphic to the algebra.\n\nThis is the algebra version of `submodule.top_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.to_submodule", "description": "The forgetful map from `subalgebra` to `submodule` as an `order_embedding`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.coe_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.copy_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.coe_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.coe_to_subring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.coe_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.coe_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.inf_to_submodule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.inclusion_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.to_subring_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.to_subsemiring_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.centralizer_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.prod", "description": "The product of two subalgebras is a subalgebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.supr_lift_inclusion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.mem_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_equiv.of_injective", "description": "Restrict an injective algebra homomorphism to an algebra isomorphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.bot_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.adjoin", "description": "The minimal subalgebra that includes `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.map", "description": "Transport a subalgebra via an algebra homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra_of_subsemiring", "description": "A subsemiring is a `\u2115`-subalgebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.fintype_range", "description": " The range of a morphism of algebras is a fintype, if the domain is a fintype.\n\nNote that this instance can cause a diamond with `subtype.fintype` if `B` is also a fintype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.zsmul_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.to_submodule_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.coe_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.center_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.to_submodule_equiv", "description": " Linear equivalence between `S : submodule R A` and `S`. Though these types are equal,\nwe define it as a `linear_equiv` to avoid type equalities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.sub_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.to_ordered_comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.sum_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.list_prod_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.to_linear_ordered_comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.coe_to_subsemiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.to_comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.mem_centralizer_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.has_faithful_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.prod_inf_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.comap", "description": "Preimage of a subalgebra under an algebra homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.coe_nat_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.coe_to_submodule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.coe_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_equiv.of_left_inverse", "description": " Restrict an algebra homomorphism with a left inverse to an algebra isomorphism to its range.\n\nThis is a computable alternative to `alg_equiv.of_injective`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_to_subalgebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.smul_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.inclusion", "description": " The map `S \u2192 T` when `S` is a subalgebra contained in the subalgebra `T`.\n\nThis is the subalgebra version of `submodule.of_le`, or `subring.inclusion`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.center", "description": " The center of an algebra is the set of elements which commute with every element. They form a\nsubalgebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.eq_on_horizontal_strip", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in a strip `U = {z : \u2102 | a < im z < b}`.\nLet `f g : \u2102 \u2192 E` be functions such that\n\n* `f` and `g` are differentiable on `U` and are continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` and `\u2016g z\u2016` are bounded from above by `A * exp(B * exp(c * |re z|))` on `U` for some\n  `c < \u03c0 / (b - a)`;\n* `f z = g z` on the boundary of `U`.\n\nThen `f` is equal to `g` on the closed strip `{z : \u2102 | a \u2264 im z \u2264 b}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.quadrant_III", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in the third quadrant. Let `f : \u2102 \u2192 E` be a function such that\n\n* `f` is differentiable in the open third quadrant and is continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by `A * exp (B * (abs z) ^ c)` on the open third quadrant\n  for some `c < 2`;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by a constant `C` on the boundary of the third quadrant.\n\nThen `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by the same constant on the closed third quadrant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.eq_zero_on_horizontal_strip", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in a strip `U = {z : \u2102 | a < im z < b}`.\nLet `f : \u2102 \u2192 E` be a function such that\n\n* `f` is differentiable on `U` and is continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by `A * exp(B * exp(c * |re z|))` on `U` for some `c < \u03c0 / (b - a)`;\n* `f z = 0` on the boundary of `U`.\n\nThen `f` is equal to zero on the closed strip `{z : \u2102 | a \u2264 im z \u2264 b}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.right_half_plane_of_bounded_on_real", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in the right half-plane. Let `f : \u2102 \u2192 E` be a function such that\n\n* `f` is differentiable in the open right half-plane and is continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by `A * exp(B * (abs z) ^ c)` on the open right half-plane\n  for some `c < 2`;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by a constant `C` on the imaginary axis;\n* `\u2016f x\u2016` is bounded from above by a constant for large real values of `x`.\n\nThen `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by `C` on the closed right half-plane.\nSee also `phragmen_lindelof.right_half_plane_of_tendsto_zero_on_real` for a weaker version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.eq_on_vertical_strip", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in a strip `U = {z : \u2102 | a < re z < b}`.\nLet `f g : \u2102 \u2192 E` be functions such that\n\n* `f` and `g` are differentiable on `U` and are continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` and `\u2016g z\u2016` are bounded from above by `A * exp(B * exp(c * |im z|))` on `U` for some\n  `c < \u03c0 / (b - a)`;\n* `f z = g z` on the boundary of `U`.\n\nThen `f` is equal to `g` on the closed strip `{z : \u2102 | a \u2264 re z \u2264 b}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.eq_on_right_half_plane_of_superexponential_decay", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in the right half-plane. Let `f g : \u2102 \u2192 E` be functions such\nthat\n\n* `f` and `g` are differentiable in the open right half-plane and are continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` and `\u2016g z\u2016` are bounded from above by `A * exp(B * (abs z) ^ c)` on the open right\n  half-plane for some `c < 2`;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` and `\u2016g z\u2016` are bounded from above by constants on the imaginary axis;\n* `f x - g x`, `x : \u211d`, tends to zero superexponentially fast as `x \u2192 \u221e`:\n  for any natural `n`, `exp (n * x) * \u2016f x - g x\u2016` tends to zero as `x \u2192 \u221e`.\n\nThen `f` is equal to `g` on the closed right half-plane.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.eq_zero_on_quadrant_I", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in the first quadrant. Let `f : \u2102 \u2192 E` be a function such that\n\n* `f` is differentiable in the open first quadrant and is continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by `A * exp(B * (abs z) ^ c)` on the open first quadrant\n  for some `A`, `B`, and `c < 2`;\n* `f` is equal to zero on the boundary of the first quadrant.\n\nThen `f` is equal to zero on the closed first quadrant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.vertical_strip", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in a strip `U = {z : \u2102 | a < re z < b}`.\nLet `f : \u2102 \u2192 E` be a function such that\n\n* `f` is differentiable on `U` and is continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by `A * exp(B * exp(c * |im z|))` on `U` for some `c < \u03c0 / (b - a)`;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by a constant `C` on the boundary of `U`.\n\nThen `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded by the same constant on the closed strip\n`{z : \u2102 | a \u2264 re z \u2264 b}`. Moreover, it suffices to verify the second assumption\nonly for sufficiently large values of `|im z|`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.eq_zero_on_right_half_plane_of_superexponential_decay", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in the right half-plane. Let `f : \u2102 \u2192 E` be a function such that\n\n* `f` is differentiable in the open right half-plane and is continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by `A * exp(B * (abs z) ^ c)` on the open right half-plane\n  for some `c < 2`;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by a constant on the imaginary axis;\n* `f x`, `x : \u211d`, tends to zero superexponentially fast as `x \u2192 \u221e`:\n  for any natural `n`, `exp (n * x) * \u2016f x\u2016` tends to zero as `x \u2192 \u221e`.\n\nThen `f` is equal to zero on the closed right half-plane.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.eq_zero_on_quadrant_III", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in the third quadrant. Let `f : \u2102 \u2192 E` be a function such that\n\n* `f` is differentiable in the open third quadrant and is continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by `A * exp(B * (abs z) ^ c)` on the open third quadrant\n  for some `A`, `B`, and `c < 2`;\n* `f` is equal to zero on the boundary of the third quadrant.\n\nThen `f` is equal to zero on the closed third quadrant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.eq_zero_on_quadrant_IV", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in the fourth quadrant. Let `f : \u2102 \u2192 E` be a function such that\n\n* `f` is differentiable in the open fourth quadrant and is continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by `A * exp(B * (abs z) ^ c)` on the open fourth quadrant\n  for some `A`, `B`, and `c < 2`;\n* `f` is equal to zero on the boundary of the fourth quadrant.\n\nThen `f` is equal to zero on the closed fourth quadrant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.eq_on_quadrant_I", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in the first quadrant. Let `f g : \u2102 \u2192 E` be functions such that\n\n* `f` and `g` are differentiable in the open first quadrant and are continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` and `\u2016g z\u2016` are bounded from above by `A * exp(B * (abs z) ^ c)` on the open first\n  quadrant for some `A`, `B`, and `c < 2`;\n* `f` is equal to `g` on the boundary of the first quadrant.\n\nThen `f` is equal to `g` on the closed first quadrant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.quadrant_I", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in the first quadrant. Let `f : \u2102 \u2192 E` be a function such that\n\n* `f` is differentiable in the open first quadrant and is continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by `A * exp(B * (abs z) ^ c)` on the open first quadrant\n  for some `c < 2`;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by a constant `C` on the boundary of the first quadrant.\n\nThen `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by the same constant on the closed first quadrant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.eq_on_quadrant_IV", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in the fourth quadrant. Let `f g : \u2102 \u2192 E` be functions such that\n\n* `f` and `g` are differentiable in the open fourth quadrant and are continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` and `\u2016g z\u2016` are bounded from above by `A * exp(B * (abs z) ^ c)` on the open fourth\n  quadrant for some `A`, `B`, and `c < 2`;\n* `f` is equal to `g` on the boundary of the fourth quadrant.\n\nThen `f` is equal to `g` on the closed fourth quadrant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.quadrant_IV", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in the fourth quadrant. Let `f : \u2102 \u2192 E` be a function such that\n\n* `f` is differentiable in the open fourth quadrant and is continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by `A * exp(B * (abs z) ^ c)` on the open fourth quadrant\n  for some `c < 2`;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by a constant `C` on the boundary of the fourth quadrant.\n\nThen `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by the same constant on the closed fourth quadrant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.horizontal_strip", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in a strip `U = {z : \u2102 | a < im z < b}`.\nLet `f : \u2102 \u2192 E` be a function such that\n\n* `f` is differentiable on `U` and is continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by `A * exp(B * exp(c * |re z|))` on `U` for some `c < \u03c0 / (b - a)`;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by a constant `C` on the boundary of `U`.\n\nThen `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded by the same constant on the closed strip\n`{z : \u2102 | a \u2264 im z \u2264 b}`. Moreover, it suffices to verify the second assumption\nonly for sufficiently large values of `|re z|`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.is_O_sub_exp_rpow", "description": " An auxiliary lemma that combines two \u201cexponential of a power\u201d estimates into a similar estimate\non the difference of the functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.quadrant_II", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in the second quadrant. Let `f : \u2102 \u2192 E` be a function such that\n\n* `f` is differentiable in the open second quadrant and is continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by `A * exp(B * (abs z) ^ c)` on the open second quadrant\n  for some `c < 2`;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by a constant `C` on the boundary of the second quadrant.\n\nThen `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by the same constant on the closed second quadrant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.eq_zero_on_quadrant_II", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in the second quadrant. Let `f : \u2102 \u2192 E` be a function such that\n\n* `f` is differentiable in the open second quadrant and is continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by `A * exp(B * (abs z) ^ c)` on the open second quadrant\n  for some `A`, `B`, and `c < 2`;\n* `f` is equal to zero on the boundary of the second quadrant.\n\nThen `f` is equal to zero on the closed second quadrant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.eq_zero_on_vertical_strip", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in a strip `U = {z : \u2102 | a < re z < b}`.\nLet `f : \u2102 \u2192 E` be a function such that\n\n* `f` is differentiable on `U` and is continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by `A * exp(B * exp(c * |im z|))` on `U` for some `c < \u03c0 / (b - a)`;\n* `f z = 0` on the boundary of `U`.\n\nThen `f` is equal to zero on the closed strip `{z : \u2102 | a \u2264 re z \u2264 b}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.eq_on_quadrant_II", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in the second quadrant. Let `f g : \u2102 \u2192 E` be functions such that\n\n* `f` and `g` are differentiable in the open second quadrant and are continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` and `\u2016g z\u2016` are bounded from above by `A * exp(B * (abs z) ^ c)` on the open second\n  quadrant for some `A`, `B`, and `c < 2`;\n* `f` is equal to `g` on the boundary of the second quadrant.\n\nThen `f` is equal to `g` on the closed second quadrant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.eq_on_quadrant_III", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in the third quadrant. Let `f g : \u2102 \u2192 E` be functions such that\n\n* `f` and `g` are differentiable in the open third quadrant and are continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` and `\u2016g z\u2016` are bounded from above by `A * exp(B * (abs z) ^ c)` on the open third\n  quadrant for some `A`, `B`, and `c < 2`;\n* `f` is equal to `g` on the boundary of the third quadrant.\n\nThen `f` is equal to `g` on the closed third quadrant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.right_half_plane_of_tendsto_zero_on_real", "description": " **Phragmen-Lindel\u00f6f principle** in the right half-plane. Let `f : \u2102 \u2192 E` be a function such that\n\n* `f` is differentiable in the open right half-plane and is continuous on its closure;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by `A * exp(B * (abs z) ^ c)` on the open right half-plane\n  for some `c < 2`;\n* `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by a constant `C` on the imaginary axis;\n* `f x \u2192 0` as `x : \u211d` tends to infinity.\n\nThen `\u2016f z\u2016` is bounded from above by the same constant on the closed right half-plane.\nSee also `phragmen_lindelof.right_half_plane_of_bounded_on_real` for a stronger version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "phragmen_lindelof.is_O_sub_exp_exp", "description": " An auxiliary lemma that combines two double exponential estimates into a similar estimate\non the difference of the functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum_hom_units", "description": " In an integral domain, a sum indexed by a homomorphism from a finite group is zero,\nunless the homomorphism is trivial, in which case the sum is equal to the cardinality of the group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.field_of_domain", "description": " Every finite commutative domain is a field.\n\nTODO: Prove Wedderburn's little theorem, which shows a finite domain is automatically commutative,\ndropping one assumption from this theorem.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "card_nth_roots_subgroup_units", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.group_with_zero_of_cancel", "description": "Every finite nontrivial cancel_monoid_with_zero is a group_with_zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_right_bijective_of_finite\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_left_bijective_of_finite\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup_units_cyclic", "description": "A finite subgroup of the units of an integral domain is cyclic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_eq_pow_of_mul_eq_pow_of_coprime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.exists_eq_pow_of_mul_eq_pow_of_coprime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum_hom_units_eq_zero", "description": "In an integral domain, a sum indexed by a nontrivial homomorphism from a finite group is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.is_field_of_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.division_ring_of_is_domain", "description": " Every finite domain is a division ring.\n\nTODO: Prove Wedderburn's little theorem,\nwhich shows a finite domain is in fact commutative, hence a field.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.is_cyclic", "description": " The unit group of a finite integral domain is cyclic.\n\nTo support `\u2124\u02e3` and other infinite monoids with finite groups of units, this requires only\n`finite R\u02e3` rather than deducing it from `finite R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.div_eq_quo_add_rem_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "card_fiber_eq_of_mem_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclic_of_subgroup_is_domain", "description": "A finite subgroup of the unit group of an integral domain is cyclic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.lt_zpow_succ_log_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.log_of_left_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.clog_of_right_le_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.lt_zpow_iff_log_lt", "description": "`zpow b` and `int.log b` (almost) form a Galois connection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.log_of_right_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.clog_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.log_zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.zpow_log_gi", "description": "Over suitable subtypes, `zpow` and `int.log` form a galois coinsertion", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.clog_one_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.log_mono_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.le_zpow_iff_clog_le", "description": "`int.clog b` and `zpow b` (almost) form a Galois connection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.neg_log_inv_eq_clog", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.zpow_lt_iff_lt_clog", "description": "`int.clog b` and `zpow b` (almost) form a Galois connection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.log_of_one_le_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.clog_mono_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.neg_clog_inv_eq_log", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.log", "description": "The greatest power of `b` such that `b ^ log b r \u2264 r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.clog_zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.clog_zero_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.clog_of_left_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.self_le_zpow_clog", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.zpow_log_le_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.log_zero_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.clog", "description": "The least power of `b` such that `r \u2264 b ^ log b r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.log_one_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.clog_of_one_le_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.zpow_pred_clog_lt_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.clog_zpow_gi", "description": "Over suitable subtypes, `int.clog` and `zpow` form a galois insertion", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.clog_of_right_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.log_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.log_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.log_of_right_le_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.zpow_le_iff_le_log", "description": "`zpow b` and `int.log b` (almost) form a Galois connection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.clog_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of.semilattice_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of_max_adjoin.extend_ideal_to_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of_max_adjoin.snd", "description": "If `x \u2208 M \u2294 \u27e8y\u27e9`, then `x = m + r \u2022 y`, `snd` pick an arbitrary such `r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.injective_iff_injective_object", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.injective", "description": "**Baer's criterion** for injective module : a Baer module is an injective module, i.e. if every\nlinear map from an ideal can be extended, then the module is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of.max", "description": "The maximal element of every nonempty chain of `extension_of i f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of_max_is_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of_max_adjoin.extension_to_fun", "description": "We can finally define a linear map `M \u2294 \u27e8y\u27e9 \u27f6 Q` by `x + r \u2022 y \u21a6 f x + \u03c6 r`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of_max_adjoin.extend_ideal_to_wd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of_max_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of_max_adjoin", "description": "The linear map `M \u2294 \u27e8y\u27e9 \u27f6 Q` by `x + r \u2022 y \u21a6 f x + \u03c6 r` is an extension of `f`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.chain_linear_pmap_of_chain_extension_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of_max_adjoin.extension_to_fun_wd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of_max_adjoin.extend_ideal_to_is_extension", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of_max_adjoin.extend_ideal_to", "description": " Since we assumed `Q` being Baer, the linear map `x \u21a6 f' (x \u2022 y) : I \u27f6 Q` extends to `R \u27f6 Q`,\ncall this extended map `\u03c6`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of_max_adjoin.fst", "description": "If `x \u2208 M \u2294 \u27e8y\u27e9`, then `x = m + r \u2022 y`, `fst` pick an arbitrary such `m`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.injective", "description": "An `R`-module `Q` is injective if and only if every injective `R`-linear map descends to a linear\nmap to `Q`, i.e. in the following diagram, if `f` is injective then there is an `R`-linear map\n`h : Y \u27f6 Q` such that `g = h \u2218 f`\n  ```lean\n  X --- f ---> Y\n  |\n  | g\n  v\n  Q\n  ```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.injective.out", "description": "An `R`-module `Q` is injective if and only if every injective `R`-linear map descends to a linear\nmap to `Q`, i.e. in the following diagram, if `f` is injective then there is an `R`-linear map\n`h : Y \u27f6 Q` such that `g = h \u2218 f`\n  ```lean\n  X --- f ---> Y\n  |\n  | g\n  v\n  Q\n  ```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.injective_module_of_injective_object", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of_max_adjoin.extend_ideal_to_wd'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of_max_adjoin.ideal_to", "description": "A linear map `I \u27f6 Q` by `x \u21a6 f' (x \u2022 y)` where `f'` is the maximal extension", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of_max_adjoin.ideal", "description": "the ideal `I = {r | r \u2022 y \u2208 N}`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of_max_adjoin.eqn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of", "description": " If we view `M` as a submodule of `N` via the injective linear map `i : M \u21aa N`, then a submodule\nbetween `M` and `N` is a submodule `N'` of `N`. To prove Baer's criterion, we need to consider\npairs of `(N', f')` such that `M \u2264 N' \u2264 N` and `f'` extends `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of.to_linear_pmap", "description": " If we view `M` as a submodule of `N` via the injective linear map `i : M \u21aa N`, then a submodule\nbetween `M` and `N` is a submodule `N'` of `N`. To prove Baer's criterion, we need to consider\npairs of `(N', f')` such that `M \u2264 N' \u2264 N` and `f'` extends `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of.le", "description": " If we view `M` as a submodule of `N` via the injective linear map `i : M \u21aa N`, then a submodule\nbetween `M` and `N` is a submodule `N'` of `N`. To prove Baer's criterion, we need to consider\npairs of `(N', f')` such that `M \u2264 N' \u2264 N` and `f'` extends `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of.is_extension", "description": " If we view `M` as a submodule of `N` via the injective linear map `i : M \u21aa N`, then a submodule\nbetween `M` and `N` is a submodule `N'` of `N`. To prove Baer's criterion, we need to consider\npairs of `(N', f')` such that `M \u2264 N' \u2264 N` and `f'` extends `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of.has_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of_max", "description": " Since every nonempty chain has a maximal element, by Zorn's lemma, there is a maximal\n`extension_of i f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer", "description": "An `R`-module `Q` satisfies Baer's criterion if any `R`-linear map from an `ideal R` extends to\nan `R`-linear map `R \u27f6 Q`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of.le_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.injective_object_of_injective_module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.Baer.extension_of_max_to_submodule_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.\u03b9_colimit_limit_to_limit_colimit_\u03c0", "description": "Since `colimit_limit_to_limit_colimit` is a morphism from a colimit to a limit,\nthis lemma characterises it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit_limit_to_limit_colimit_cone", "description": "The map `colimit_limit_to_limit_colimit` realized as a map of cones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.\u03b9_colimit_limit_to_limit_colimit_\u03c0_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.\u03b9_colimit_limit_to_limit_colimit_\u03c0_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.map_id_right_eq_curry_swap_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit_limit_to_limit_colimit_cone_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit_limit_to_limit_colimit", "description": "The universal morphism\n$\\colim_k \\lim_j F(j,k) \u2192 \\lim_j \\colim_k F(j, k)$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.map_id_left_eq_curry_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.commute.minimal_period_of_comp_dvd_lcm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.minimal_period_snd_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.nodup_periodic_orbit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt_zero", "description": "Any point is a periodic point of period `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_mem_periodic_orbit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.Union_pnat_pts_of_period", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.minimal_period_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_prod_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.minimal_period_apply_iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.apply_iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.minimal_period_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.minimal_period_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.minimal_period_pos_of_mem_periodic_pts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.eq_iff_lt_minimal_period_of_iterate_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.minimal_period_pos_iff_mem_periodic_pts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.mem_periodic_orbit_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.bij_on_pts_of_period", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic_orbit_eq_nil_of_not_periodic_pt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.eq_of_lt_minimal_period_of_iterate_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_action.nsmul_vadd_mod_minimal_period", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.iterate_mod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.minimal_period_eq_zero_iff_nmem_periodic_pts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.minimal_period_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic_pts", "description": "The set of periodic points of a map `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt_minimal_period", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic_orbit_chain'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.commute.minimal_period_of_comp_eq_mul_of_coprime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_fixed_pt_prod_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.minimal_period_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt_prod_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_id", "description": "For the identity map, all points are periodic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.semiconj.maps_to_periodic_pts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.decidable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt", "description": " A point `x` is a periodic point of `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1` of period `n` if `f^[n] x = x`.\nNote that we do not require `0 < n` in this definition. Many theorems about periodic points\nneed this assumption.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.right_of_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic_orbit_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.self_mem_periodic_orbit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.mem_periodic_pts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic_orbit_eq_nil_iff_not_periodic_pt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.minimal_period_iterate_eq_div_gcd'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.eq_of_apply_eq", "description": " If `f` sends two periodic points `x` and `y` of positive periods to the same point,\nthen `x = y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.bUnion_pts_of_period", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.minimal_period", "description": " Minimal period of a point `x` under an endomorphism `f`. If `x` is not a periodic point of `f`,\nthen `minimal_period f x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic_orbit_chain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.bij_on_periodic_pts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_action.zsmul_vadd_eq_iff_minimal_period_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt_iff_minimal_period_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_mod_minimal_period_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action.zpow_smul_eq_iff_minimal_period_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.is_fixed_pt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_fixed_pt.is_periodic_pt", "description": "A fixed point of `f` is a periodic point of `f` of any prescribed period.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.minimal_period_prod_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_minimal_period", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_action.nsmul_vadd_eq_iff_minimal_period_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.gcd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.mk_mem_periodic_pts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.eq_of_apply_eq_same", "description": " If `f` sends two periodic points `x` and `y` of the same positive period to the same point,\nthen `x = y`. For a similar statement about points of different periods see `eq_of_apply_eq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.le_of_lt_minimal_period_of_iterate_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.semiconj.maps_to_pts_of_period", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic_orbit_apply_iterate_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.left_of_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.pts_of_period", "description": "The set of periodic points of a given (possibly non-minimal) period.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic_orbit_apply_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.comp_lcm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.mem_pts_of_period", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.minimal_period_fst_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action.pow_smul_eq_iff_minimal_period_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_action.zsmul_vadd_mod_minimal_period", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.mul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.eq_zero_of_lt_minimal_period", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.minimal_period_eq_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action.zpow_smul_mod_minimal_period", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_add_minimal_period_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.left_of_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.minimal_period_eq_prime_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt_of_mem_periodic_pts_of_is_periodic_pt_iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic_orbit", "description": " The orbit of a periodic point `x` of `f` is the cycle `[x, f x, f (f x), ...]`. Its length is\nthe minimal period of `x`.\n\nIf `x` is not a periodic point, then this is the empty (aka nil) cycle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action.pow_smul_mod_minimal_period", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.const_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.directed_pts_of_period_pnat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.minimal_period_eq_zero_of_nmem_periodic_pts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic_orbit_def", "description": "The definition of a periodic orbit, in terms of `list.map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic_orbit_eq_cycle_map", "description": "The definition of a periodic orbit, in terms of `cycle.map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.minimal_period_eq_minimal_period_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_periodic_pt.trans_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.is_fixed_point_iff_minimal_period_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.commute.minimal_period_of_comp_dvd_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.minimal_period_iterate_eq_div_gcd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.not_is_periodic_pt_of_pos_of_lt_minimal_period", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddGroup.of_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.to_AddCommGroup_iso_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Group.group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.to_Group_iso", "description": "Build an isomorphism in the category `Group` from a `mul_equiv` between `group`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.to_CommGroup_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CommGroup.of_hom", "description": "Typecheck a `monoid_hom` as a morphism in `CommGroup`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddGroup.of_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.comm_group