os_num.distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "num.add_of_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "num.mod_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "num.lt_to_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pos_num.lt_iff_cmp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pos_num.of_to_nat'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "num.zneg_to_znum_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "num.cast_to_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "num.pred_to_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "num.add_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pos_num.cast_sub'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.of_snum", "description": "Cast a `snum` to the corresponding integer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "znum.zneg_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pos_num.cast_to_znum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "znum.cast_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "num.of_nat_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "snum.has_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "num.size_to_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pos_num.comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pos_num.one_sub'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pos_num.cast_to_num", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.tautology", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.symm_eq", "description": "Given hypotheses `a` and `b`, build a proof that `a` is equivalent to `b`,\napplying congruence and recursing into arguments if `a` and `b`\nare applications of function symbols.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.root", "description": "Retrieve the root of the hypothesis `e` from the proof forest.\nIf `e` has not been internalized, add it to the proof forest.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.tactic.tautology", "description": "This tactic (with shorthand `tauto`) breaks down assumptions of the form\n`_ \u2227 _`, `_ \u2228 _`, `_ \u2194 _` and `\u2203 _, _`\nand splits a goal of the form `_ \u2227 _`, `_ \u2194 _` or `\u2203 _, _` until it can be discharged\nusing `reflexivity` or `solve_by_elim`. This is a finishing tactic: it\neither closes the goal or raises an error.\n\nThe variants `tautology!` and `tauto!` use the law of excluded middle.\n\nFor instance, one can write:\n```lean\nexample (p q r : Prop) [decidable p] [decidable r] : p \u2228 (q \u2227 r) \u2194 (p \u2228 q) \u2227 (r \u2228 p \u2228 r) := by tauto\n```\nand the decidability assumptions can be dropped if `tauto!` is used\ninstead of `tauto`.\n\n`tauto {closer := tac}` will use `tac` on any subgoals created by `tauto`\nthat it is unable to solve before failing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.assumption_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.tauto_state", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.contradiction_with", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_symm_proof", "description": "If there exists a symmetry lemma that can be applied to the hypothesis `e`,\nstore it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.tauto_cfg", "description": "Configuration options for `tauto`.\nIf `classical` is `tt`, runs `classical` before the rest of `tauto`.\n`closer` is run on any remaining subgoals left by `tauto_core; basic_tauto_tacs`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.tauto_cfg.classical", "description": "Configuration options for `tauto`.\nIf `classical` is `tt`, runs `classical` before the rest of `tauto`.\n`closer` is run on any remaining subgoals left by `tauto_core; basic_tauto_tacs`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.tauto_cfg.closer", "description": "Configuration options for `tauto`.\nIf `classical` is `tt`, runs `classical` before the rest of `tauto`.\n`closer` is run on any remaining subgoals left by `tauto_core; basic_tauto_tacs`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.distrib_not", "description": "find all assumptions of the shape `\u00ac (p \u2227 q)` or `\u00ac (p \u2228 q)` and\nreplace them using de Morgan's law.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_edge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.tauto", "description": "`tauto` breaks down assumptions of the form `_ \u2227 _`, `_ \u2228 _`, `_ \u2194 _` and `\u2203 _, _`\nand splits a goal of the form `_ \u2227 _`, `_ \u2194 _` or `\u2203 _, _` until it can be discharged\nusing `reflexivity` or `solve_by_elim`.\nThis is a finishing tactic: it either closes the goal or raises an error.\nThe variant `tauto!` uses the law of excluded middle.\n\n`tauto {closer := tac}` will use `tac` on any subgoals created by `tauto`\nthat it is unable to solve before failing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.assumption_with", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.modify_ref", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.tautology", "description": "`tautology` breaks down assumptions of the form `_ \u2227 _`, `_ \u2228 _`, `_ \u2194 _` and `\u2203 _, _`\nand splits a goal of the form `_ \u2227 _`, `_ \u2194 _` or `\u2203 _, _` until it can be discharged\nusing `reflexivity` or `solve_by_elim`.\nThis is a finishing tactic: it either closes the goal or raises an error.\nThe variant `tautology!` uses the law of excluded middle.\n\n`tautology {closer := tac}` will use `tac` on any subgoals created by `tautology`\nthat it is unable to solve before failing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.contradiction_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.find_eq_type", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.P_infty_idem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.Q_infty_idem_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.P_infty_f_comp_Q_infty_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.Q_infty_comp_P_infty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.P_infty_comp_Q_infty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.map_P_infty_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.P_infty_f_idem_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.P_infty_add_Q_infty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.Q_infty_f_comp_P_infty_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.P_infty_f_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.Q_infty_f_comp_P_infty_f_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.nat_trans_P_infty", "description": " `P_infty` induces a natural transformation, i.e. an endomorphism of\nthe functor `alternating_face_map_complex C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.karoubi_P_infty_f", "description": " Given an object `Y : karoubi (simplicial_object C)`, this lemma\ncomputes `P_infty` for the associated object in `simplicial_object (karoubi C)`\nin terms of `P_infty` for `Y.X : simplicial_object C` and `Y.p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.Q_infty_comp_P_infty_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.nat_trans_P_infty_f", "description": "The natural transformation in each degree that is induced by `nat_trans_P_infty`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.P_infty_f_naturality_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.Q_is_eventually_constant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.P_infty", "description": "The endomorphism `P_infty : K[X] \u27f6 K[X]` obtained from the `P q` by passing to the limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.P_infty_f_idem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"na