"description": "Construct a bundled `SemiNormedGroup\u2081` from the underlying type and typeclass.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "SemiNormedGroup.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "SemiNormedGroup.of_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "SemiNormedGroup\u2081.mk_iso", "description": "Promote an isomorphism in `SemiNormedGroup` to an isomorphism in `SemiNormedGroup\u2081`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "SemiNormedGroup\u2081.coe_comp'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "SemiNormedGroup.is_zero_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "SemiNormedGroup.seminormed_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "SemiNormedGroup.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "SemiNormedGroup\u2081.has_zero_object", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "SemiNormedGroup.of", "description": "Construct a bundled `SemiNormedGroup` from the underlying type and typeclass.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "SemiNormedGroup\u2081.mk_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "SemiNormedGroup.has_zero_object", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "SemiNormedGroup\u2081.iso_isometry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "SemiNormedGroup.zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "SemiNormedGroup\u2081.of_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "SemiNormedGroup.large_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "SemiNormedGroup\u2081.is_zero_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.one_lt_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_eq_zero_of_embedding", "description": "NB: `nat.card` is defined to be `0` for infinite types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_le_one_iff_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_subtype_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.equiv_fin_of_card_eq", "description": "Similar to `finite.equiv_fin` but with control over the term used for the cardinality.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_le_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_eq_zero_of_injective", "description": "NB: `nat.card` is defined to be `0` for infinite types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_le_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.one_lt_card_iff_nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.cast_card_eq_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part_enat.card_eq_coe_nat_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_le_of_embedding'", "description": "If `f` is an embedding, then `nat.card \u03b1 \u2264 nat.card \u03b2`. We must also assume\n `nat.card \u03b2 = 0 \u2192 nat.card \u03b1 = 0` since `nat.card` is defined to be `0` for infinite types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_subtype_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_range_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.card_union_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_eq_zero_of_surjective", "description": "NB: `nat.card` is defined to be `0` for infinite types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_le_of_injective'", "description": "If `f` is injective, then `nat.card \u03b1 \u2264 nat.card \u03b2`. We must also assume\n `nat.card \u03b2 = 0 \u2192 nat.card \u03b1 = 0` since `nat.card` is defined to be `0` for infinite types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_option", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.equiv_fin", "description": "There is (noncomputably) an equivalence between a finite type `\u03b1` and `fin (nat.card \u03b1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_le_of_surjective'", "description": "If `f` is surjective, then `nat.card \u03b2 \u2264 nat.card \u03b1`. We must also assume\n `nat.card \u03b1 = 0 \u2192 nat.card \u03b2 = 0` since `nat.card` is defined to be `0` for infinite types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_image_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_le_of_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.card_pos_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.var", "description": "A single variable `n` is represented by a sum with coefficient `1` and monomial `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.one", "description": "The unit monomial `one` is represented by the empty rb map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.to_comp_fold", "description": "`to_comp_fold red e_map exprs monom_map` folds `to_comp` over `exprs`,\nupdating `e_map` and `monom_map` as it goes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.monom.lt", "description": "Compare monomials by first comparing their keys and then their powers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.sum.one", "description": "`1` is represented as the singleton sum of the monomial `monom.one` with coefficient 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.sum", "description": "Linear combinations of monomials are represented by mapping monomials to coefficients.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.sum.mul", "description": "`sum.mul s1 s2` distributes the multiplication of two sums.`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.sum_of_monom", "description": "`sum_of_monom m` lifts `m` to a sum with coefficient `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.sum.scale_by_monom", "description": "`sum.scale_by_monom s m` multiplies every monomial in `s` by `m`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.monom.has_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.linear_form_of_atom", "description": "`linear_form_of_atom red map e` is the atomic case for `linear_form_of_expr`.\nIf `e` appears with index `k` in `map`, it returns the singleton sum `var k`.\nOtherwise it updates `map`, adding `e` with index `n`, and returns the singleton sum `var n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.monom", "description": "Variables (represented by natural numbers) map to their power.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.linear_forms_and_max_var", "description": "`linear_forms_and_vars red pfs` is the main interface for computing the linear forms of a list\nof expressions. Given a list `pfs` of proofs of comparisons, it produces a list `c` of `comps` of\nthe same length, such that `c[i]` represents the linear form of the type of `pfs[i]`.\n\nIt also returns the largest variable index that appears in comparisons in `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.monom.one", "description": "`1` is represented by the empty monomial, the product of no variables.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.to_comp", "description": "`to_comp red e e_map monom_map` converts an expression of the form `t < 0`, `t \u2264 0`, or `t = 0`\ninto a `comp` object.\n\n`e_map` maps atomic expressions to indices; `monom_map` maps monomials to indices.\nBoth of these are updated during processing and returned.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.linear_form_of_expr", "description": "`linear_form_of_expr red map e` computes the linear form of `e`.\n\n`map` is a lookup map from atomic expressions to variable numbers.\nIf a new atomic expression is encountered, it is added to the map with a new number.\nIt matches atomic expressions up to reducibility given by `red`.\n\nBecause it matches up to definitional equality, this function must be in the `tactic` monad,\nand forces some functions that call it into `tactic` as well.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.sum.pow", "description": "The `n`th power of `s : sum` is the `n`-fold product of `s`, with `s.pow 0 = sum.one`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.sum_to_lf", "description": "`sum_to_lf s map` eliminates the monomial level of the `sum` `s`.\n\n`map` is a lookup map from monomials to variable numbers.\nThe output `rb_map \u2115 \u2124` has the same structure as `sum`,\nbut each monomial key is replaced with its index according to `map`.\nIf any new monomials are encountered, they are assigned variable numbers and `map` is updated.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.scalar", "description": "A scalar `z` is represented by a `sum` with coefficient `z` and monomial `one`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_lawful_monad_cont", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_lawful_monad_cont.to_is_lawful_monad", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_lawful_monad_cont.call_cc_bind_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_lawful_monad_cont.call_cc_bind_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_lawful_monad_cont.call_cc_dummy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "reader_t.call_cc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "state_t.goto_mk_label", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_t.run_with_cont_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option_t.call_cc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "reader_t.is_lawful_monad_cont", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "except_t.monad_cont", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "except_t.goto_mk_label", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_t.equiv", "description": " reduce the equivalence between two continuation passing monads to the equivalence between\ntheir underlying monad", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_t.monad_except", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option_t.monad_cont", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_t.with_cont_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monad_cont.label", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monad_cont.label.apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_t.has_monad_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option_t.goto_mk_label", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option_t.is_lawful_monad_cont", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "except_t.is_lawful_monad_cont", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_t.monad_cont", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "writer_t.monad_cont", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_t.monad_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_t.run_cont_t_map_cont_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_t.monad_run", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "writer_t.call_cc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "except_t.mk_label", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_t.is_lawful_monad_cont", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "state_t.monad_cont", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_t.run", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "writer_t.mk_label", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "reader_t.goto_mk_label", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "reader_t.monad_cont", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "state_t.mk_label", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "state_t.is_lawful_monad_cont", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option_t.mk_label", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_t.is_lawful_monad", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "reader_t.mk_label", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_t.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monad_cont.goto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "state_t.call_cc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "writer_t.goto_mk_label", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_t.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "except_t.call_cc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_t.monad_lift_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"},