", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint", "description": " A set is `pairwise_disjoint` under `f`, if the images of any distinct two elements under `f`\nare disjoint.\n\n`s.pairwise disjoint` is (definitionally) the same as `s.pairwise_disjoint id`. We prefer the latter\nin order to allow dot notation on `set.pairwise_disjoint`, even though the former unfolds more\nnicely.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pairwise_disjoint_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "symmetric.pairwise_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_iff_of_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_union_of_symmetric", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise.insert_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint.eq_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint.elim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.nonempty.pairwise_iff_exists_forall", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint_fiber", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint.image_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint.prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_insert_of_symmetric", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint_image_left_iff", "description": " The partial images of a binary function `f` whose partial evaluations are injective are pairwise\ndisjoint iff `f` is injective .", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint.mono_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise.mono'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint.elim_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pairwise_on_bool", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint.insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_insert_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_pair", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise.insert_of_symmetric_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_eq_iff_exists_eq", "description": " A function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b9` with nonempty codomain takes pairwise equal values on a set `s` if and\nonly if for some `z` in the codomain, `f` takes value `z` on all `x \u2208 s`. See also\n`set.nonempty.pairwise_eq_iff_exists_eq` for a version that assumes `set.nonempty s` instead of\n`[nonempty \u03b9]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_insert_of_symmetric_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_pair_of_symmetric", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pairwise_disjoint_fiber", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pairwise.set_of_subtype", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `pairwise_subtype_iff_pairwise_set`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint_range_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pairwise_subtype_iff_pairwise_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pairwise_disjoint_on_bool", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise.of_refl", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `set.pairwise_iff_of_refl`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint_image_right_iff", "description": " The partial images of a binary function `f` whose partial evaluations are injective are pairwise\ndisjoint iff `f` is injective .", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint.elim'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise.subsingleton", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `set.pairwise_bot_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint_insert_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.inj_on.pairwise_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_iff_exists_forall", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise.insert_of_symmetric", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.subsingleton.pairwise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint.range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pairwise_disjoint.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.nonempty.pairwise_eq_iff_exists_eq", "description": " For a nonempty set `s`, a function `f` takes pairwise equal values on `s` if and only if\nfor some `z` in the codomain, `f` takes value `z` on all `x \u2208 s`. See also\n`set.pairwise_eq_iff_exists_eq` for a version that assumes `[nonempty \u03b9]` instead of\n`set.nonempty s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint.subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.direct_limit.of.zero_exact_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.direct_limit.of.zero_exact", "description": " A component that corresponds to zero in the direct limit is already zero in some\nbigger module in the directed system.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.direct_limit.lift_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.direct_limit.exists_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.direct_limit.exists_of", "description": " Every element of the direct limit corresponds to some element in\nsome component of the directed system.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.direct_limit.lift_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.direct_limit.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.direct_limit.of.zero_exact", "description": " A component that corresponds to zero in the direct limit is already zero in some\nbigger module in the directed system.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.direct_limit.lift_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.direct_limit.of.zero_exact_aux2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.direct_limit.lift_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.direct_limit.lift", "description": " The universal property of the direct limit: maps from the components to another abelian group\nthat respect the directed system structure (i.e. make some diagram commute) give rise\nto a unique map out of the direct limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.direct_limit.of_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.direct_limit", "description": "The direct limit of a directed system is the abelian groups glued together along the maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.direct_limit.lift_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.direct_limit.of_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.direct_limit.ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.direct_limit.induction_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.direct_limit.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.direct_limit.to_module_totalize_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.direct_limit.totalize_of_not_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.direct_limit.lift", "description": " The universal property of the direct limit: maps from the components to another ring\nthat respect the directed system structure (i.e. make some diagram commute) give rise\nto a unique map out of the direct limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.direct_limit.induction_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.direct_limit.totalize", "description": " `totalize G f i j` is a linear map from `G i` to `G j`, for *every* `i` and `j`.\nIf `i \u2264 j`, then it is the map `f i j` that comes with the directed system `G`,\nand otherwise it is the zero map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.direct_limit.induction_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.direct_limit.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.direct_limit.polynomial.exists_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.direct_limit.of.zero_exact", "description": " A component that corresponds to zero in the direct limit is already zero in some\nbigger module in the directed system.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.direct_limit.lift_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.directed_system.map_map", "description": " A copy of `directed_system.map_map` specialized to linear maps, as otherwise the\n`\u03bb i j h, f i j h` can confuse the simplifier.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.direct_limit.directed_system", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "directed_system", "description": "A directed system is a functor from a category (directed poset) to another category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "directed_system.map_self", "description": "A directed system is a functor from a category (directed poset) to another category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "directed_system.map_map", "description": "A directed system is a functor from a category (directed poset) to another category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.direct_limit", "description": "The direct limit of a directed system is the modules glued together along the maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.direct_limit.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.direct_limit.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.direct_limit.inv_mul_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.direct_limit.of_injective", "description": " If the maps in the directed system are injective, then the canonical maps\nfrom the components to the direct limits are injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.direct_limit.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.direct_limit.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.direct_limit.totalize_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.direct_limit", "description": "The direct limit of a directed system is the rings glued together along the maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.direct_limit.of", "description": "The canonical map from a component to the direct limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.direct_limit.lift", "description": " The universal property of the direct limit: maps from the components to another module\nthat respect the directed system structure (i.e. make some diagram commute) give rise\nto a unique map out of the direct limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.direct_limit.of_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.direct_limit.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.direct_limit.of", "description": "The canonical map from a component to the direct limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.direct_limit.of", "description": "The canonical map from a component to the direct limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.directed_system.map_self", "description": " A copy of `directed_system.map_self` specialized to linear maps, as otherwise the\n`\u03bb i j h, f i j h` can confuse the simplifier.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.direct_limit.mul_inv_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, 