localization.construction.relations.id", "description": "The relations by which we take the quotient in order to get the localized category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.relations.comp", "description": "The relations by which we take the quotient in order to get the localized category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.relations.Winv\u2081", "description": "The relations by which we take the quotient in order to get the localized category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.relations.Winv\u2082", "description": "The relations by which we take the quotient in order to get the localized category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.morphism_property.Q_inverts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.whiskering_left_equivalence.unit_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.loc_quiver", "description": " If `W : morphism_property C`, `loc_quiver W` is a quiver with the same objects\nas `C`, and whose morphisms are those in `C` and placeholders for formal\ninverses of the morphisms in `W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.loc_quiver.obj", "description": " If `W : morphism_property C`, `loc_quiver W` is a quiver with the same objects\nas `C`, and whose morphisms are those in `C` and placeholders for formal\ninverses of the morphisms in `W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.whiskering_left_equivalence.unit_iso", "description": "The unit isomorphism of the equivalence of categories `whiskering_left_equivalence W D`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.morphism_property_is_top", "description": " A `morphism_property` in `W.localization` is satisfied by all\nmorphisms in the localized category if it contains the image of the\nmorphisms in the original category, the inverses of the morphisms\nin `W` and if it is stable under composition", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.whiskering_left_equivalence.counit_iso", "description": "The counit isomorphism of the equivalence of categories `whiskering_left_equivalence W D`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.lift_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.lift_to_path_category_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.nat_trans_extension_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.nat_trans_extension_hcomp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.obj_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.morphism_property.localization", "description": " The localized category obtained by formally inverting the morphisms\nin `W : morphism_property C`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.lift_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.whiskering_left_equivalence.inverse_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.morphism_property.localization.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.whiskering_left_equivalence.functor", "description": " The functor `(W.localization \u2964 D) \u2964 (W.functors_inverting D)` induced by the\ncomposition with `W.Q : C \u2964 W.localization`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.obj_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.uniq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.whiskering_left_equivalence.inverse_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.fac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.Winv", "description": "The formal inverse in `W.localization` of a morphism `w` in `W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.nat_trans_extension.app_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.nat_trans_extension.app", "description": " If `F\u2081` and `F\u2082` are functors `W.localization \u2964 D` and if we have\n`\u03c4 : W.Q \u22d9 F\u2081 \u27f6 W.Q \u22d9 F\u2082`, we shall define a natural transformation `F\u2081 \u27f6 F\u2082`.\nThis is the `app` field of this natural transformation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.obj_equiv", "description": " The canonical bijection between objects in a category and its\nlocalization with respect to a morphism_property `W`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.whiskering_left_equivalence.inverse", "description": " The function `(W.functors_inverting D) \u2964 (W.localization \u2964 D)` induced by\n`construction.lift`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.Wiso", "description": "The isomorphism in `W.localization` associated to a morphism `w` in W", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.whiskering_left_equivalence.functor_obj_obj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.whiskering_left_equivalence.functor_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.whiskering_left_equivalence", "description": " The equivalence of categories `(W.localization \u2964 D) \u224c (W.functors_inverting D)`\ninduced by the composition with `W.Q : C \u2964 W.localization`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.\u03c8\u2081", "description": "T