: "measure_theory.integrable_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.congr'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_add_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_const_mul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.lipschitz_with.integrable_comp_iff_of_antilipschitz", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_finite_measure_with_density_of_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_eq_fun.integrable", "description": " A class of almost everywhere equal functions is `integrable` if its function representative\nis integrable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.has_finite_integral.congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.mul_const'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.bdd_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.adjoin_gen_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.is_integral_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.nat_degree_minpoly", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.lift_equiv'_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.dim_le_nat_degree_of_root", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.minpoly_gen_monic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.lift_equiv'_symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.lift_equiv_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.equiv_of_root", "description": " `pb.equiv_of_root pb' h\u2081 h\u2082` is an equivalence of algebras with the same power basis,\nwhere \"the same\" means that `pb` is a root of `pb'`s minimal polynomial and vice versa.\n\nSee also `power_basis.equiv_of_minpoly` which takes the hypothesis that the\nminimal polynomials are identical.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.constr_pow_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.equiv_of_root_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_pow", "description": " Useful lemma to show `x` generates a power basis:\nthe powers of `x` less than the degree of `x`'s minimal polynomial are linearly independent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.mem_span_pow'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.nat_degree_minpoly_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.map_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.minpoly_gen", "description": "`pb.minpoly_gen` is the minimal polynomial for `pb.gen`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.dim_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.lift_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.constr_pow_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.lift_equiv", "description": " `pb.lift_equiv` states that roots of the minimal polynomial of `pb.gen` correspond to\nmaps sending `pb.gen` to that root.\n\nThis is the bundled equiv version of `power_basis.lift`.\nIf the codomain of the `alg_hom`s is an integral domain, then the roots form a multiset,\nsee `lift_equiv'` for the corresponding statement.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.dim_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.map_dim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.adjoin_eq_top_of_gen_mem_adjoin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.dim_le_degree_of_root", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.degree_minpoly_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis", "description": " `pb : power_basis R S` states that `1, pb.gen, ..., pb.gen ^ (pb.dim - 1)`\nis a basis for the `R`-algebra `S` (viewed as `R`-module).\n\nThis is a structure, not a class, since the same algebra can have many power bases.\nFor the common case where `S` is defined by adjoining an integral element to `R`,\nthe canonical power basis is given by `{algebra,intermediate_field}.adjoin.power_basis`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.gen", "description": " `pb : power_basis R S` states that `1, pb.gen, ..., pb.gen ^ (pb.dim - 1)`\nis a basis for the `R`-algebra `S` (viewed as `R`-module).\n\nThis is a structure, not a class, since the same algebra can have many power bases.\nFor the common case where `S` is defined by adjoining an integral element to `R`,\nthe canonical power basis is given by `{algebra,intermediate_field}.adjoin.power_basis`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.dim", "description": " `pb : power_basis R S` states that `1, pb.gen, ..., pb.gen ^ (pb.dim - 1)`\nis a basis for the `R`-algebra `S` (viewed as `R`-module).\n\nThis is a structure, not a class, since the same algebra can have many power bases.\nFor the common case where `S` is defined by adjoining an integral element to `R`,\nthe canonical power basis is given by `{algebra,intermediate_field}.adjoin.power_basis`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.basis", "description": " `pb : power_basis R S` states that `1, pb.gen, ..., pb.gen ^ (pb.dim - 1)`\nis a basis for the `R`-algebra `S` (viewed as `R`-module).\n\nThis is a structure, not a class, since the same algebra can have many power bases.\nFor the common case where `S` is defined by adjoining an integral element to `R`,\nthe canonical power basis is given by `{algebra,intermediate_field}.adjoin.power_basis`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.basis_eq_pow", "description": " `pb : power_basis R S` states that `1, pb.gen, ..., pb.gen ^ (pb.dim - 1)`\nis a basis for the `R`-algebra `S` (viewed as `R`-module).\n\nThis is a structure, not a class, since the same algebra can have many power bases.\nFor the common case where `S` is defined by adjoining an integral element to `R`,\nthe canonical power basis is given by `{algebra,intermediate_field}.adjoin.power_basis`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.equiv_of_minpoly_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.equiv_of_minpoly", "description": " `pb.equiv_of_minpoly pb' h` is an equivalence of algebras with the same power basis,\nwhere \"the same\" means that they have identical minimal polynomials.\n\nSee also `power_basis.equiv_of_root` which takes the hypothesis that each generator is a root of the\nother basis' minimal polynomial; `power_basis.equiv_root` is more general if `A` is not a field.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.alg_hom.fintype", "description": " There are finitely many algebra homomorphisms `S \u2192\u2090[A] B` if `S` is of the form `A[x]`\nand `B` is an integral domain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.minpoly_gen_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.equiv_of_minpoly_aeval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.degree_minpoly", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.mem_span_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.constr_pow_aeval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.exists_eq_aeval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.lift", "description": " `pb.lift y hy` is the algebra map sending `pb.gen` to `y`,\nwhere `hy` states the higher powers of `y` are the same as the higher powers of `pb.gen`.\n\nSee `power_basis.lift_equiv` for a bundled equiv sending `\u27e8y, hy\u27e9` to the algebra map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.left_mul_matrix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.minpoly_gen_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.aeval_minpoly_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.equiv_of_minpoly_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.exists_eq_aeval'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.lift_equiv'", "description": " `pb.lift_equiv'` states that elements of the root set of the minimal\npolynomial of `pb.gen` correspond to maps sending `pb.gen` to that root.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.equiv_of_root_aeval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.equiv_of_root_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.lift_aeval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.map", "description": "`power_basis.map pb (e : S \u2243\u2090[R] S')` is the power basis for `S'` generated by `e pb.gen`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.map_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.finrank", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.alg_hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.coe_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.constr_pow_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_integral.mem_span_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.equiv_of_minpoly_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.equiv_of_root_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.lift_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.equiv_of_root_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.equiv_of_minpoly_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.finite_dimensional", "description": "Cannot be an instance because `power_basis` cannot be a class.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_iso.eq_inv_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso.cancel_iso_inv_right_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_iso.of_is_iso_comp_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_iso.comp_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso.hom_inv_id_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.hom_comp_eq_id", "d