me": "circle_deg1_lift.le_iterate_of_add_int_le_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translate_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translation_number_lt_of_forall_lt_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.le_iterate_pos_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.tendsto_translation_number_of_dist_bounded_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.tendsto_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translation_number_translate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.dist_map_map_zero_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.le_map_map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.mul_floor_map_zero_le_floor_iterate_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.floor_map_map_zero_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.transnum_aux_seq_dist_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.coe_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.strict_mono_iff_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.map_nat_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.commute_nat_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.exists_eq_add_translation_number", "description": " If `f` is a continuous monotone map `\u211d \u2192 \u211d`, `f (x + 1) = f x + 1`, then there exists `x`\nsuch that `f x = x + \u03c4 f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.coe_to_order_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.is_unit_iff_bijective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.le_floor_map_map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.commute_sub_int", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translation_number_mul_of_commute", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translation_number_of_map_pow_eq_add_int", "description": " If `f^n x - x`, `n > 0`, is an integer number `m` for some point `x`, then\n`\u03c4 f = m / n`. On the circle this means that a map with a periodic orbit has\na rational rotation number.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.map_le_of_map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.map_int_of_map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translation_number_eq_of_dist_bounded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.coe_to_order_iso_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.lt_map_of_nat_lt_translation_number", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translation_number_eq_of_semiconj_by", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.lt_iterate_pos_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.coe_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.le_translation_number_of_add_int_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.semiconj_of_is_unit_of_translation_number_eq", "description": " If two lifts of circle homeomorphisms have the same translation number, then they are\nsemiconjugate by a `circle_deg1_lift`. This version uses assumptions `is_unit f\u2081` and `is_unit f\u2082`\nto assume that `f\u2081` and `f\u2082` are homeomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translate_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.map_lt_add_translation_number_add_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translation_number_le_of_le_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift", "description": "A lift of a monotone degree one map `S\u00b9 \u2192 S\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.to_fun", "description": "A lift of a monotone degree one map `S\u00b9 \u2192 S\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.monotone'", "description": "A lift of a monotone degree one map `S\u00b9 \u2192 S\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.map_add_one'", "description": "A lift of a monotone degree one map `S\u00b9 \u2192 S\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.forall_map_sub_of_Icc", "description": " If a predicate depends only on `f x - x` and holds for all `0 \u2264 x \u2264 1`,\nthen it holds for all `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translate", "description": " The map `y \u21a6 x + y` as a `circle_deg1_lift`. More precisely, we define a homomorphism from\n`multiplicative \u211d` to `circle_deg1_lift\u02e3`, so the translation by `x` is\n`translation (multiplicative.of_add x)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.map_add_int", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.commute_int_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translation_number_eq_of_tendsto\u2080'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.iterate_pos_lt_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.tendsto_translation_number_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.coe_to_order_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.map_add_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.commute_add_int", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translation_number_eq_of_tendsto_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.iterate_eq_of_map_eq_add_int", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.map_fract_sub_fract_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translation_number_of_eq_add_int", "description": " If `f x - x` is an integer number `m` for some point `x`, then `\u03c4 f = m`.\nOn the circle this means that a map with a fixed point has rotation number zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.semiconj_by_iff_semiconj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translation_number_eq_of_tendsto\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.iterate_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translation_number", "description": " The translation number of a `circle_deg1_lift`, $\u03c4(f)=\\lim_{n\u2192\u221e}\\frac{f^n(x)-x}{n}$. We use\nan auxiliary sequence `\\frac{f^{2^n}(0)}{2^n}` to define `\u03c4(f)` because some proofs are simpler\nthis way.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.tendsto_translation_number", "description": " For any `x : \u211d` the sequence $\\frac{f^n(x)-x}{n}$ tends to the translation number of `f`.\nIn particular, this limit does not depend on `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.units_semiconj_of_translation_number_eq", "description": " If two lifts of circle homeomorphisms have the same translation number, then they are\nsemiconjugate by a `circle_deg1_lift`. This version uses arguments `f\u2081 f\u2082 : circle_deg1_lift\u02e3`\nto assume that `f\u2081` and `f\u2082` are homeomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translation_number_conj_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translation_number_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.dist_map_zero_lt_of_semiconj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.semiconj_of_group_action_of_forall_translation_number_eq", "description": " Consider two actions `f\u2081 f\u2082 : G \u2192* circle_deg1_lift` of a group on the real line by lifts of\norientation preserving circle homeomorphisms. Suppose that for each `g : G` the homeomorphisms\n`f\u2081 g` and `f\u2082 g` have equal rotation numbers. Then there exists `F : circle_deg1_lift`  such that\n`F * f\u2081 g = f\u2082 g * F` for all `g : G`.\n\nThis is a version of Proposition 5.4 from [\u00c9tienne Ghys, Groupes d'homeomorphismes du cercle et\ncohomologie bornee][ghys87:groupes].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translation_number_zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.units_has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.commute_iff_commute", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.map_lt_add_floor_translation_number_add_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.transnum_aux_seq", "description": "An auxiliary sequence used to define the translation number.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.ceil_map_map_zero_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.map_one_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translation_number_units_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.pow_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.translation_number_le_of_le_add_int", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_deg1_lift.tendsto_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fraction_ring.mk'_num_denom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fraction_ring.num_mul_denom_eq_num_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fraction_ring.is_integer_of_is_unit_denom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fraction_ring.num_denom_reduced", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fraction_ring.exists_reduced_fraction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fraction_ring.is_unit_denom_of_num_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fraction_ring.eq_zero_of_num_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fraction_ring.num", "description": "`f.num x` is the numerator of `x : f.codomain` as a reduced fraction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fraction_ring.num_mul_denom_eq_num_iff_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fraction_ring.denom", "description": "`f.num x` is the denominator of `x : f.codomain` as a reduced fraction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fraction_ring.num_mul_denom_eq_num_mul_denom_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.exists_right_transversal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.smul_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.vadd_apply_eq_vadd_apply_neg_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.mem_left_transversals.to_equiv", "description": "A left transversal is in bijection with left cosets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.mem_right_transversals.add_neg_to_fun_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.mem_left_transversals_iff_exists_unique_quotient_mk'_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.mem_right_transversals.to_equiv", "description": "A right transversal is in bijection with right cosets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.mem_left_transversals.to_fun", "description": "A left transversal can be viewed as a function mapping each element of the group\n to the chosen representative from that left coset.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.mem_right_transversals.to_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.transfer_transversal", "description": "The transfer transversal. Contains elements of the