ription": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_bot.mul_pos_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_top.semigroup_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_bot.ordered_comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_bot.semigroup_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_bot.pos_mul_reflect_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_top.mul_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_bot.pos_mul_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_top.mul_zero_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_top.untop'_zero_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_top.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.self_eq_neg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.range_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.has_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type", "description": "The type of signs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.zero", "description": "The type of signs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.neg", "description": "The type of signs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.pos", "description": "The type of signs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.one_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.pos_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.neg_eq_self_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_signed_sum'", "description": "We can decompose a sum of absolute value less than `n` into a sum of at most `n` signs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.le.decidable_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_eq_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.coe_neg_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.nonneg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_nonneg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.nonpos_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.has_distrib_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_signed_sum", "description": "We can decompose a sum of absolute value `n` into a sum of `n` signs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right.sign_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_hom", "description": " `sign` as a `monoid_with_zero_hom` for a nontrivial ordered semiring. Note that linearity\nis required; consider \u2102 with the order `z \u2264 w` iff they have the same imaginary part and\n`z - w \u2264 0` in the reals; then `1 + i` and `1 - i` are incomparable to zero, and thus we have:\n`0 * 0 = sign (1 + i) * sign (1 - i) \u2260 sign 2 = 1`. (`complex.ordered_comm_ring`)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.linear_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.lt_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.cast_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.fin3_equiv", "description": "`sign_type` is equivalent to `fin 3`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.not_lt_neg_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.not_one_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_eq_neg_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.sign_eq_sign", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.cast_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_nonpos_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.le", "description": "The less-than relation on signs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.le.of_neg", "description": "The less-than relation on signs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.le.zero", "description": "The less-than relation on signs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.le.of_pos", "description": "The less-than relation on signs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.neg_eq_neg_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.cast_hom", "description": "`sign_type.cast` as a `mul_with_zero_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.neg_one_lt_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.comm_group_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.neg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.nonneg_iff_ne_neg_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.zero_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.neg_one_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left.sign_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.nonpos_iff_ne_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.le_neg_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.neg_one_lt_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.cast", "description": " Turn a `sign_type` into zero, one, or minus one. This is a coercion instance, but note it is\nonly a `has_coe_t` instance: see note [use has_coe_t].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign", "description": "The sign of an element is 1 if it's positive, -1 if negative, 0 otherwise.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.bounded_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.has_coe_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_type.pos_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.field", "description": " The quotient by a maximal ideal is a field. This is a `def` rather than `instance`, since users\nwill have computable inverses (and `qsmul`, `rat_cast`) in some applications.\n\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.map_pi", "description": "If `f : R^n \u2192 R^m` is an `R`-linear map and `I \u2286 R` is an ideal, then the image of `I^n` is\n   contained in `I^m`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient_inf_equiv_quotient_prod_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.exists_sub_one_mem_and_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient_inf_equiv_quotient_prod", "description": "**Chinese remainder theorem**, specialized to two ideals.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.has_quotient", "description": " The quotient `R/I` of a ring `R` by an ideal `I`.\n\nThe ideal quotient of `I` is defined to equal the quotient of `I` as an `R`-submodule of `R`.\nThis definition is marked `reducible` so that typeclass instances can be shared between\n`ideal.quotient I` and `submodule.quotient I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.fst_comp_quotient_inf_equiv_quotient_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.ring_con", "description": "On `ideal`s, `submodule.quotient_rel` is a ring congruence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.quotient_ring_saturate", "description": " If `I` is an ideal of a commutative ring `R`, if `q : R \u2192 R/I` is the quotient map, and if\n`s \u2286 R` is a subset, then `q\u207b\u00b9(q(s)) = \u22c3\u1d62(i + s)`, the union running over all `i \u2208 I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.pi_quot_equiv", "description": "`R^n/I^n` is isomorphic to `(R/I)^n` as an `R/I`-module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quot_equiv_of_eq", "description": " Quotienting by equal ideals gives equivalent rings.\n\nSee also `submodule.quot_equiv_of_eq` and `ideal.quotient_equiv_alg_of_eq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.no_zero_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.is_domain_iff_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.zero_ne_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.zero_eq_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.exists_sub_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.lift_surjective_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.mk.ring_hom_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.ring_hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient_inf_to_pi_quotient", "description": "The homomorphism from `R/(\u22c2 i, f i)` to `\u220f i, (R / f i)` featured in the Chinese\n Remainder Theorem. It is bijective if the ideals `f i` are comaximal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.lift_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.maximal_of_is_field", "description": "If the quotient by an ideal is a field, then the ideal is maximal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.module_pi", "description": "`R^n/I^n` is a `R/I`-module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.smul_comm_class'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.mk_eq_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.mk_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient_inf_to_pi_quotient_bijective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.lift", "description": " Given a ring homomorphism `f : R \u2192+* S` sending all elements of an ideal to zero,\nlift it to the quotient by this ideal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.smul_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.mk", "description": "The ring homomorphism from a ring `R` to a quotient ring `R/I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.maximal_ideal_iff_is_field_quotient", "description": "The quotient of a ring by an ideal is a field iff the ideal is maximal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.subsingleton_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.factor", "description": " The ring homomorphism from the quotient by a smaller ideal to the quotient by a larger ideal.\n\nThis is the `ideal.quotient` version of `quot.factor`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.factor_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.snd_comp_quotient_inf_equiv_quotient_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient_inf_equiv_quotient_prod_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.exists_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient_inf_ring_equiv_pi_quotient", "description": "Chinese Remainder Theorem. Eisenbud Ex.2.6. Similar to Atiyah-Macdonald 1.10 and Stacks 00DT", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quot_equiv_of_eq_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.is_scalar_tower_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.has_quotient.quotient.unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.factor_comp_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quot_equiv_of_eq_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.is_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.group_with_zero", "description": " The quotient by a maximal ideal is a group with zero. This is a `def` rather than `instance`,\nsince users will have computable inverses in some applications.\n\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.bdd_below_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.l_binfi_u", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Inf_image2_eq_Sup_Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.monotone_intro", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.l_inf_u", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.lift_bounded_order", "description": "Lift the top, bottom, suprema, and infima along a Galois coinsertion", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.l_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.to_galois_connection", "description": "Makes a Galois connection from an order-preserving bijection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.u_bsupr_l", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.bdd_above_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.u_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.lift_semilattice_sup", "description": "Lift the suprema along a Galois coinsertion", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.l_bsupr_u", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.l_infi_of_ul_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.is_least_l", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.left_inverse_l_u", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.l_comm_of_u_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.l_supr_u", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.l_le_l_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Sup_image2_eq_Sup_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.dual", "description": " Make a `galois_coinsertion` between `\u03b1\u1d52\u1d48` and `\u03b2\u1d52\u1d48` from a `galois_insertion` between `\u03b1` and\n`\u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.l_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.lift_semilattice_sup", "description": "Lift the suprema along a Galois insertion", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.u_infi\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.l_binfi_of_ul_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.u_sup_l", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.lt_iff_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.l_u_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion", "description": " A Galois coinsertion is a Galois connection where `u \u2218 l = id`. It also contains a constructive\nchoice function, to give better definitional equalities when lifting order structures. Dual to\n`galois_insertion`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.choice", "description": " A Galois coinsertion is a Galois connection where `u \u2218 l = id`. It also contains a constructive\nchoice function, to give better definitional equalities when lifting order structures. Dual to\n`galois_insertion`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.gc", "description": " A Galois coinsertion is a Galois connection where `u \u2218 l = id`. It also contains a constructive\nchoice function, to give better definitional equalities when lifting order structures. Dual to\n`galois_insertion`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.u_l_le", "description": " A Galois coinsertion is a Galois connection where `u \u2218 l = id`. It also contains a constructive\nchoice function, to give better definitional equalities when lifting order structures. Dual to\n`galois_insertion`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.choice_eq", "description": " A Galois coinsertion is a Galois connection where `u \u2218 l = id`. It also contains a constructive\nchoice function, to give better definitional equalities when lifting order structures. Dual to\n`galois_insertion`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.le_u_l", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.dual", "description": " Make a `galois_insertion` between `\u03b1\u1d52\u1d48` and `\u03b2\u1d52\u1d48` from a `galois_coinsertion` between `\u03b1` and\n`\u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.le_u_l_trans", "description": " If `(l, u)` is a Galois connection, then the relation `x \u2264 u (l y)` is a transitive relation.\nIf `l` is a closure operator (`submodule.span`, `subgroup.closure`, ...) and `u` is the coercion to\n`set`, this reads as \"if `U` is in the closure of `V` and `V` is in the closure of `W` then `U` is\nin the closure of `W`\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.monotone_intro", "description": "A constructor for a Galois coinsertion with the trivial `choice` function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.l_Inf_u_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.lift_order_bot", "description": "Lift the bottom along a Galois connection", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.l_infi_u", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.l_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.is_lub_u", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.lift_semilattice_inf", "description": "Lift the infima along a Galois coinsertion", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.strict_mono_u", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.u_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.le_iff_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.lift_complete_lattice", "description": "Lift all suprema and infima along a Galois insertion", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.is_lub_of_u_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.is_glb_of_l_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.strict_mono_l", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.l_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.u_Inf_l_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.monotone_u", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.is_glb_u_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.u_supr_l", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.l_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.l_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.is_lub_l_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.lift_lattice", "description": "Lift the suprema and infima along a Galois coinsertion", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.bdd_above_l_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.to_galois_insertion", "description": "Makes a Galois insertion from an order-preserving bijection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.u_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.u_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.is_greatest_u", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.l_u_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.l_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.u_l_left_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.lift_bounded_order", "description": "Lift the top, bottom, suprema, and infima along a Galois insertion", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.bdd_below_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.u_l_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.of_dual", "description": " Make a `galois_coinsertion` between `\u03b1` and `\u03b2` from a `galois_insertion` between `\u03b1\u1d52\u1d48` and\n`\u03b2\u1d52\u1d48`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.exists_eq_u", "description": "If there exists a `b` such that `a = u a`, then `b = l a` is one such element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Inf_image2_eq_Sup_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.bdd_below_u_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Sup_image2_eq_Sup_Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.l_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.u_l_u_eq_u'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.upper_bounds_l_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.u_l_u_eq_u", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.lower_bounds_u_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.is_lub_of_l_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.is_glb_of_u_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.u_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.lift_order_top", "description": "Lift the top along a Galois insertion", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.lift_order_top", "description": "Lift the top along a Galois connection", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.to_galois_coinsertion", "description": "Makes a Galois coinsertion from an order-preserving bijection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.le_u", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.lift_order_bot", "description": "Lift the bot along a Galois coinsertion", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Sup_image2_eq_Inf_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.u_comm_of_l_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.u_Sup_l_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.u_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.dfun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection", "description": "A Galois connection is a pair of functions `l` and `u` satisfying\n `l a \u2264 b \u2194 a \u2264 u b`. They are special cases of adjoint functors in category theory,\n   but do not depend on the category theory library in mathlib.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.l_sup_u", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Sup_image2_eq_Inf_Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.u_supr_of_lu_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Inf_image2_eq_Inf_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.u_infi_l", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.to_galois_coinsertion", "description": "Make a `galois_coinsertion l u` from a `galois_connection l u` such that `\u2200 b, b \u2264 l (u b)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.u_inf_l", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.l_comm_iff_u_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.l_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.l_u_l_eq_l'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.dual", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.u_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_bot.gi_unbot'_bot", "description": " If `\u03b1` is a partial order with bottom element (e.g., `\u2115`, `\u211d\u22650`), then `with_bot.unbot' \u22a5` and\ncoercion form a Galois insertion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.monotone_l", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.to_galois_insertion", "description": "Make a `galois_insertion l u` from a `galois_connection l u` such that `\u2200 b, b \u2264 l (u b)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.u_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.l_u_le_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.l_Sup_u_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.lift_lattice", "description": "Lift the suprema and infima along a Galois insertion", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.compose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.bdd_above_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.galois_connection_mul_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.monotone_intro", "description": "A constructor for a Galois insertion with the trivial `choice` function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.lift_complete_lattice", "description": "Lift all suprema and infima along a Galois coinsertion", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion", "description": " A Galois insertion is a Galois connection where `l \u2218 u = id`. It also contains a constructive\nchoice function, to give better definitional equalities when lifting order structures. Dual\nto `galois_coinsertion`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.choice", "description": " A Galois insertion is a Galois connection where `l \u2218 u = id`. It also contains a constructive\nchoice function, to give better definitional equalities when lifting order structures. Dual\nto `galois_coinsertion`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.gc", "description": " A Galois insertion is a Galois connection where `l \u2218 u = id`. It also contains a constructive\nchoice function, to give better definitional equalities when lifting order structures. Dual\nto `galois_coinsertion`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.le_l_u", "description": " A Galois insertion is a Galois connection where `l \u2218 u = id`. It also contains a constructive\nchoice function, to give better definitional equalities when lifting order structures. Dual\nto `galois_coinsertion`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.choice_eq", "description": " A Galois insertion is a Galois connection where `l \u2218 u = id`. It also contains a constructive\nchoice function, to give better definitional equalities when lifting order structures. Dual\nto `galois_coinsertion`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.l_u_l_eq_l", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.lift_semilattice_inf", "description": "Lift the infima along a Galois insertion", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.of_dual", "description": " Make a `galois_insertion` between `\u03b1` and `\u03b2` from a `galois_coinsertion` between `\u03b1\u1d52\u1d48` and\n`\u03b2\u1d52\u1d48`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.l_supr\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.exists_eq_l", "description": "If there exists an `a` such that `b = l a`, then `a = u b` is one such element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.l_Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_coinsertion.u_bsupr_of_lu_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.u_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Inf_image2_eq_Inf_Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_insertion.u_le_u_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.is_glb_l", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dual_number.snd_mul", "description": "A version of `triv_sq_zero_ext.snd_mul` with `*` instead of `\u2022`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dual_number.eps", "description": "The unit element $\u03b5$ that squares to zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dual_number.lift_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dual_number.inr_eq_smul_eps", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dual_number.alg_hom_ext", "description": "For two algebra morphisms out of `R[\u03b5]` to agree, it suffices for them to agree on `\u03b5`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dual_number.lift", "description": " A universal property of the dual numbers, providing a unique `R[\u03b5] \u2192\u2090[R] A` for every element\nof `A` which squares to `0`.\n\nThis isomorphism is named to match the very similar `complex.lift`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dual_number.snd_eps", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dual_number.lift_apply_eps", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dual_number.lift_eps", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dual_number", "description": "The type of dual numbers, numbers of the form $a + b\u03b5$ where $\u03b5^2 = 0$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dual_number.lift_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dual_number.fst_eps", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dual_number.eps_mul_eps", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.zero_ne_one_of_proper", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_maximal.exists_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_pair_add_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.unit_mul_mem_iff_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.exists_not_is_unit_of_not_is_field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.eq_bot_of_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_mem_nonunits_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal", "description": " A (left) ideal in a semiring `R` is an additive submonoid `s` such that\n`a * b \u2208 s` whenever `b \u2208 s`. If `R` is a ring, then `s` is an additive subgroup.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.pow_mem_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_singleton_lt_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.eq_top_iff_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_prime.mem_or_mem_of_mul_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonunits", "description": "The set of non-invertible elements of a monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_sup_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.add_mem_iff_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.maximal_of_no_maximal", "description": "If P is not properly contained in any maximal ideal then it is not properly contained\n in any proper ideal", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.Inf_is_prime_of_is_chain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_pair_add_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_singleton_ne_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_span_singleton_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.ne_top_iff_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.pow_multiset_sum_mem_span_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.eq_top_of_is_unit_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_pow_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_maximal.coprime_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mul_mem_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.ne_bot_of_is_maximal_of_not_is_field", "description": "When a ring is not a field, the maximal ideals are nontrivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_sup_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_singleton_eq_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_not_mem_nonunits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mul_unit_mem_iff_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_prime", "description": "An ideal `P` of a ring `R` is prime if `P \u2260 R` and `xy \u2208 P \u2192 x \u2208 P \u2228 y \u2208 P`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_prime.ne_top'", "description": "An ideal `P` of a ring `R` is prime if `P \u2260 R` and `xy \u2208 P \u2192 x \u2208 P \u2228 y \u2208 P`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_prime.mem_or_mem'", "description": "An ideal `P` of a ring `R` is prime if `P \u2260 R` and `xy \u2208 P \u2192 x \u2208 P \u2228 y \u2208 P`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.eq_top_of_unit_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_maximal_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_supr_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.is_field_iff_is_simple_order_ideal", "description": " Also see `ideal.is_simple_order` for the forward direction as an instance when `R` is a\ndivision (semi)ring. \n\nThis result actually holds for all division semirings, but we lack the predicate to state it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_span_insert'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_prime.ne_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.add_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_pair_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_maximal.eq_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_maximal", "description": "An ideal is maximal if it is maximal in the collection of proper ideals.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_maximal.out", "description": "An ideal is maximal if it is maximal in the collection of proper ideals.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.bot_is_maximal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_span_pair", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_maximal.is_prime'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_singleton_mul_right_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.exists_maximal", "description": "Krull's theorem: a nontrivial ring has a maximal ideal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.add_mem_iff_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.submodule_span_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.sum_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.eq_bot_or_top", "description": "All ideals in a division (semi)ring are trivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "coe_subset_nonunits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.sub_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mul_mem_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_singleton_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_coatomic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span", "description": "The ideal generated by a subset of a ring", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.neg_mem_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.of_rel", "description": "The ideal generated by an arbitrary binary relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_mem_nonunits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_singleton_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.bot_lt_of_maximal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.zero_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.not_is_field_iff_exists_ideal_bot_lt_and_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_span_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_singleton_mul_left_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_singleton_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_prime.pow_mem_iff_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_span_singleton_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_maximal.is_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.not_is_prime_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mul_sub_mul_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_span_singleton'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.sum_pow_mem_span_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_prime_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_eq_top_iff_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_singleton_le_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.pi", "description": "`I^n` as an ideal of `R^n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_nonunits_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_simple_order", "description": " Ideals of a `division_semiring` are a simple order. Thanks to the way abbreviations work,\nthis automatically gives a `is_simple_module K` instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.factors_decreasing", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_prime.mem_of_pow_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.not_is_field_iff_exists_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_maximal_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_singleton_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.subset_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_prime.mem_or_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.bot_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.exists_le_maximal", "description": "**Krull's theorem**: if `I` is an ideal that is not the whole ring, then it is included in some\n   maximal ideal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_prime.mul_mem_iff_mem_or_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_max_ideal_of_mem_nonunits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_maximal.ne_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_Sup_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_singleton_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_singleton_le_iff_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_mem_nonunits_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_succ_eq_comp_right", "description": " Writing explicitly the `n+1`-th derivative as the composition of a currying linear equiv,\nand the `n`-th derivative of the derivative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.continuous_on_fderiv_of_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_within_inter'", "description": " The iterated differential within a set `s` at a point `x` is not modified if one intersects\n`s` with a neighborhood of `x` within `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_all_iff_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff.continuous_fderiv_apply", "description": " If a function is at least `C^1`, its bundled derivative (mapping `(x, v)` to `Df(x) v`) is\ncontinuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff.differentiable", "description": "If a function is `C^n` with `n \u2265 1`, then it is differentiable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.cont_diff_on'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.congr_of_eventually_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_within_one_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_zero_eq_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_at.cont_diff_within_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_succ_of_fderiv_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_within_zero_eq_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on.has_fderiv_within_at", "description": " If a function has a Taylor series at order at least `1`, then the term of order `1` of this\nseries is a derivative of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_iterated_fderiv_fderiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to.cont_diff", "description": "If `f` has a Taylor series up to `n`, then it is `C^n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff.differentiable_iterated_fderiv", "description": "If `f` is `C^n` then its `m`-times iterated derivative is differentiable for `m < n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_eq.iterated_fderiv_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.congr_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.differentiable_on", "description": "If a function is `C^n` on a set with `n \u2265 1`, then it is differentiable there.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.continuous_within_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to.has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on_succ_iff_left", "description": " `p` is a Taylor series of `f` up to `n+1` if and only if `p` is a Taylor series up to `n`, and\n`p (n + 1)` is a derivative of `p n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff.of_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.cont_diff_within_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff.continuous_iterated_fderiv", "description": "If `f` is `C^n` then its `m`-times iterated derivative is continuous for `m \u2264 n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on_top_iff'", "description": " In the case that `n = \u221e` we don't need the continuity assumption in\n`has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.continuous_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff", "description": " A function is continuously differentiable up to `n` if it admits derivatives up to\norder `n`, which are continuous. Contrary to the case of definitions in domains (where derivatives\nmight not be unique) we do not need to localize the definition in space or time.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_succ_apply_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff.cont_diff_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_at.congr_of_eventually_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_iff_continuous_on_differentiable_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.one_of_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff.of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on", "description": " A function is continuously differentiable up to `n` on `s` if, for any point `x` in `s`, it\nadmits continuous derivatives up to order `n` on a neighborhood of `x` in `s`.\n\nFor `n = \u221e`, we only require that this holds up to any finite order (where the neighborhood may\ndepend on the finite order we consider).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_of_differentiable_iterated_fderiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to.continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_at.eventually", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_iterated_fderiv_within_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_top_iff_fderiv", "description": " A function is `C^\u221e` if and only if it is differentiable,\nand its derivative (formulated in terms of `fderiv`) is `C^\u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.congr_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_at_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_at", "description": " A function is continuously differentiable up to `n` at a point `x` if, for any integer `k \u2264 n`,\nthere is a neighborhood of `x` where `f` admits derivatives up to order `n`, which are continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_succ_iff_fderiv", "description": " A function is `C^(n + 1)` if and only if it is differentiable,\nand its derivative (formulated in terms of `fderiv`) is `C^n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.of_insert", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `cont_diff_within_at_insert`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ftaylor_series_within_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff.continuous_fderiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at_congr_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_iterated_fderiv_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.cont_diff_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to.differentiable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_one_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on.congr", "description": " If two functions coincide on a set `s`, then a Taylor series for the first one is as well a\nTaylor series for the second one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on.of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to.zero_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on.has_fderiv_at", "description": " If a function has a Taylor series at order at least `1` on a neighborhood of `x`, then the term\nof order `1` of this series is a derivative of `f` at `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_succ_iff_right", "description": " `p` is a Taylor series of `f` up to `n+1` if and only if `p.shift` is a Taylor series up to `n`\nfor `p 1`, which is a derivative of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.differentiable_on_iterated_fderiv_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to", "description": " `has_ftaylor_series_up_to n f p` registers the fact that `p 0 = f` and `p (m+1)` is a\nderivative of `p m` for `m < n`, and is continuous for `m \u2264 n`. This is a predicate analogous to\n`has_fderiv_at` but for higher order derivatives.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to.zero_eq", "description": " `has_ftaylor_series_up_to n f p` registers the fact that `p 0 = f` and `p (m+1)` is a\nderivative of `p m` for `m < n`, and is continuous for `m \u2264 n`. This is a predicate analogous to\n`has_fderiv_at` but for higher order derivatives.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to.fderiv", "description": " `has_ftaylor_series_up_to n f p` registers the fact that `p 0 = f` and `p (m+1)` is a\nderivative of `p m` for `m < n`, and is continuous for `m \u2264 n`. This is a predicate analogous to\n`has_fderiv_at` but for higher order derivatives.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to.cont", "description": " `has_ftaylor_series_up_to n f p` registers the fact that `p 0 = f` and `p (m+1)` is a\nderivative of `p m` for `m < n`, and is continuous for `m \u2264 n`. This is a predicate analogous to\n`has_fderiv_at` but for higher order derivatives.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at_succ_iff_has_fderiv_within_at", "description": "A function is `C^(n + 1)` on a domain iff locally, it has a derivative which is `C^n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_iff_ftaylor_series", "description": " When a function is `C^n` in a set `s` of unique differentiability, it admits\n`ftaylor_series_within \ud835\udd5c f s` as a Taylor series up to order `n` in `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_at.continuous_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff.cont_diff_within_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fderiv_iterated_fderiv", "description": " Writing explicitly the derivative of the `n`-th derivative as the composition of a currying\nlinear equiv, and the `n + 1`-th derivative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff.one_of_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff.continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_at_succ_iff_has_fderiv_at", "description": "A function is `C^(n + 1)` at a point iff locally, it has a derivative which is `C^n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.differentiable_within_at_iterated_fderiv_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_with_zero_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.continuous_on_fderiv_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff.cont_diff_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_of_continuous_on_differentiable_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.insert'", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `cont_diff_within_at_insert`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to.of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.fderiv_of_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.congr_of_eventually_eq_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.of_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at", "description": " A function is continuously differentiable up to order `n` within a set `s` at a point `x` if\nit admits continuous derivatives up to order `n` in a neighborhood of `x` in `s \u222a {x}`.\nFor `n = \u221e`, we only require that this holds up to any finite order (where the neighborhood may\ndepend on the finite order we consider).\n\nFor instance, a real function which is `C^m` on `(-1/m, 1/m)` for each natural `m`, but not\nbetter, is `C^\u221e` at `0` within `univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_top_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on", "description": " `has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on n f p s` registers the fact that `p 0 = f` and `p (m+1)` is a\nderivative of `p m` for `m < n`, and is continuous for `m \u2264 n`. This is a predicate analogous to\n`has_fderiv_within_at` but for higher order derivatives.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on.zero_eq", "description": " `has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on n f p s` registers the fact that `p 0 = f` and `p (m+1)` is a\nderivative of `p m` for `m < n`, and is continuous for `m \u2264 n`. This is a predicate analogous to\n`has_fderiv_within_at` but for higher order derivatives.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on.fderiv_within", "description": " `has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on n f p s` registers the fact that `p 0 = f` and `p (m+1)` is a\nderivative of `p m` for `m < n`, and is continuous for `m \u2264 n`. This is a predicate analogous to\n`has_fderiv_within_at` but for higher order derivatives.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on.cont", "description": " `has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on n f p s` registers the fact that `p 0 = f` and `p (m+1)` is a\nderivative of `p m` for `m < n`, and is continuous for `m \u2264 n`. This is a predicate analogous to\n`has_fderiv_within_at` but for higher order derivatives.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.congr'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.congr_of_eventually_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_within", "description": "The `n`-th derivative of a function along a set, defined inductively by saying that the `n+1`-th\nderivative of `f` is the derivative of the `n`-th derivative of `f` along this set, together with\nan uncurrying step to see it as a multilinear map in `n+1` variables..", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on.zero_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ftaylor_series_within", "description": "Formal Taylor series associated to a function within a set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.fderiv_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.continuous_on_iterated_fderiv_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on.differentiable_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_within_of_is_open", "description": " In an open set, the iterated derivative within this set coincides with the global iterated\nderivative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.eventually", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to.has_fderiv_at", "description": " If a function has a Taylor series at order at least `1`, then the term of order `1` of this\nseries is a derivative of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on.cont_diff_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at_inter'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_within_succ_eq_comp_left", "description": " Writing explicitly the `n+1`-th derivative as the composition of a currying linear equiv,\nand the derivative of the `n`-th derivative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_within_congr", "description": " If two functions coincide on a set `s`, then their iterated differentials within this set\ncoincide. See also `filter.eventually_eq.iterated_fderiv_within_eq` and\n`filter.eventually_eq.iterated_fderiv_within`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_succ_iff_has_fderiv_within_at", "description": "A function is `C^(n + 1)` on a domain iff locally, it has a derivative which is `C^n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_top_iff'", "description": " In the case that `n = \u221e` we don't need the continuity assumption in\n`has_ftaylor_series_up_to`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv", "description": "The `n`-th derivative of a function, as a multilinear map, defined inductively.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_iff_forall_nat_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.differentiable_within_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_within_succ_apply_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on.eventually_has_fderiv_at", "description": " If a function has a Taylor series at order at least `1` on a neighborhood of `x`, then\nin a neighborhood of `x`, the term of order `1` of this series is a derivative of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_within_succ_apply_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_succ_iff_has_fderiv", "description": "A function is `C^(n+1)` iff it has a `C^n` derivative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_within_eventually_congr_set'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_of_locally_cont_diff_on", "description": "If a function is `C^n` around each point in a set, then it is `C^n` on the set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.mono_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_top_iff_fderiv_of_open", "description": " A function is `C^\u221e` on an open domain if and only if it is differentiable there, and its\nderivative (expressed with `fderiv`) is `C^\u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_within_eventually_congr_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at_succ_iff_has_fderiv_within_at'", "description": "A version of `cont_diff_within_at_succ_iff_has_fderiv_within_at` where all derivatives\n are taken within the same set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_succ_eq_comp_left", "description": " Writing explicitly the `n+1`-th derivative as the composition of a currying linear equiv,\nand the derivative of the `n`-th derivative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_at_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_within_inter_open", "description": " The iterated differential within a set `s` at a point `x` is not modified if one intersects\n`s` with an open set containing `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_of_differentiable_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_iff_continuous_differentiable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_at.differentiable_at", "description": "If a function is `C^n` with `n \u2265 1` at a point, then it is differentiable there.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_fderiv_iterated_fderiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_top_iff_fderiv_within", "description": " A function is `C^\u221e` on a domain with unique derivatives if and only if it is differentiable\nthere, and its derivative (expressed with `fderiv_within`) is `C^\u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_eq.iterated_fderiv_within'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.differentiable_within_at'", "description": " If a function is `C^n` within a set at a point, with `n \u2265 1`, then it is differentiable\nwithin this set at this point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_all_iff_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.cont_diff_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_iff_forall_nat_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_at.of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_within_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_compact_support.iterated_fderiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ftaylor_series", "description": "Formal Taylor series associated to a function within a set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_eq.cont_diff_within_at_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_succ_iff_has_fderiv_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_within_inter", "description": " The iterated differential within a set `s` at a point `x` is not modified if one intersects\n`s` with a neighborhood of `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_iterated_fderiv_within_fderiv_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.eq_on.iterated_fderiv_within", "description": " If two functions coincide on a set `s`, then their iterated differentials within this set\ncoincide. See also `filter.eventually_eq.iterated_fderiv_within_eq` and\n`filter.eventually_eq.iterated_fderiv_within`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at_iff_forall_nat_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on_top_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on.differentiable_at", "description": " If a function has a Taylor series at order at least `1` on a neighborhood of `x`, then\nit is differentiable at `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_succ_apply_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on_succ_iff_right", "description": " `p` is a Taylor series of `f` up to `n+1` if and only if `p.shift` is a Taylor series up to `n`\nfor `p 1`, which is a derivative of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_succ_iff_fderiv_within", "description": " A function is `C^(n + 1)` on a domain with unique derivatives if and only if it is\ndifferentiable there, and its derivative (expressed with `fderiv_within`) is `C^n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_within_succ_eq_comp_right", "description": " Writing explicitly the `n+1`-th derivative as the composition of a currying linear equiv,\nand the `n`-th derivative of the derivative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_within_congr_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on.continuous_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_succ_iff_fderiv_of_open", "description": " A function is `C^(n + 1)` on an open domain if and only if it is\ndifferentiable there, and its derivative (expressed with `fderiv`) is `C^n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_eq.iterated_fderiv_within_eq", "description": " If two functions coincide in a neighborhood of `x` within a set `s` and at `x`, then their\niterated differentials within this set at `x` coincide.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_one_iff_fderiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_iff_cont_diff_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.ftaylor_series_within", "description": " When a function is `C^n` in a set `s` of unique differentiability, it admits\n`ftaylor_series_within \ud835\udd5c f s` as a Taylor series up to order `n` in `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on_univ_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_fderiv_within_iterated_fderiv_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_ftaylor_series_up_to_on.eq_ftaylor_series_of_unique_diff_on", "description": " On a set with unique differentiability, any choice of iterated differential has to coincide\nwith the one we have chosen in `iterated_fderiv_within \ud835\udd5c m f s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_within_zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.cocone_morphism", "description": "The monoid homomorphism from a given monoid in the diagram to the colimit monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.desc_morphism", "description": "The monoid homomorphism from the colimit monoid to the cone point of any other cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.has_colimits_Mon", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.colimit_is_colimit", "description": "Evidence that the proposed colimit is the colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.monoid_colimit_type", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.quot_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.colimit", "description": "The bundled monoid giving the colimit of a diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.desc_fun_lift", "description": "The function from the free monoid on the diagram to the cone point of any other cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.colimit_type", "description": "The underlying type of the colimit of a diagram in `Mon`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.cocone_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.relation", "description": "The relation on `prequotient` saying when two expressions are equal\nbecause of the monoid laws, or\nbecause one element is mapped to another by a morphism in the diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.relation.refl", "description": "The relation on `prequotient` saying when two expressions are equal\nbecause of the monoid laws, or\nbecause one element is mapped to another by a morphism in the diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.relation.symm", "description": "The relation on `prequotient` saying when two expressions are equal\nbecause of the monoid laws, or\nbecause one element is mapped to another by a morphism in the diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.relation.trans", "description": "The relation on `prequotient` saying when two expressions are equal\nbecause of the monoid laws, or\nbecause one element is mapped to another by a morphism in the diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.relation.map", "description": "The relation on `prequotient` saying when two expressions are equal\nbecause of the monoid laws, or\nbecause one element is mapped to another by a morphism in the diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.relation.mul", "description": "The relation on `prequotient` saying when two expressions are equal\nbecause of the monoid laws, or\nbecause one element is mapped to another by a morphism in the diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.relation.one", "description": "The relation on `prequotient` saying when two expressions are equal\nbecause of the monoid laws, or\nbecause one element is mapped to another by a morphism in the diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.relation.mul_1", "description": "The relation on `prequotient` saying when two expressions are equal\nbecause of the monoid laws, or\nbecause one element is mapped to another by a morphism in the diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.relation.mul_2", "description": "The relation on `prequotient` saying when two expressions are equal\nbecause of the monoid laws, or\nbecause one element is mapped to another by a morphism in the diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.relation.mul_assoc", "description": "The relation on `prequotient` saying when two expressions are equal\nbecause of the monoid laws, or\nbecause one element is mapped to another by a morphism in the diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.relation.one_mul", "description": "The relation on `prequotient` saying when two expressions are equal\nbecause of the monoid laws, or\nbecause one element is mapped to another by a morphism in the diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.relation.mul_one", "description": "The relation on `prequotient` saying when two expressions are equal\nbecause of the monoid laws, or\nbecause one element is mapped to another by a morphism in the diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.desc_fun", "description": "The function from the colimit monoid to the cone point of any other cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.quot_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.colimit_cocone", "description": "The cocone over the proposed colimit monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.cocone_naturality_components", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.prequotient.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.colimit_type.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.colimit_setoid", "description": "The setoid corresponding to monoid expressions modulo monoid relations and identifications.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.prequotient", "description": "An inductive type representing all monoid expressions (without relations)\non a collection of types indexed by the objects of `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.prequotient.of", "description": "An inductive type representing all monoid expressions (without relations)\non a collection of types indexed by the objects of `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.prequotient.one", "description": "An inductive type representing all monoid expressions (without relations)\non a collection of types indexed by the objects of `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.prequotient.mul", "description": "An inductive type representing all monoid expressions (without relations)\non a collection of types indexed by the objects of `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.colimits.cocone_fun", "description": "The function from a given monoid in the diagram to the colimit monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.whiskering_right\u2082", "description": "A version of `category_theory.whiskering_right` for bifunctors, obtained by uncurrying,\napplying `whiskering_right` and currying back", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.whiskering_right\u2082_map_app_app_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.curry_obj_obj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.curry_map_app_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.curry", "description": "The currying functor, taking a functor `(C \u00d7 D) \u2964 E` and producing a functor `C \u2964 (D \u2964 E)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.currying_inverse_map_app_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.curry_obj_obj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.whiskering_right\u2082_obj_map_app_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.currying_inverse_obj_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.uncurry_obj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.uncurry_obj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.flip_iso_curry_swap_uncurry_inv_app_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.whiskering_right\u2082_obj_obj_obj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.currying_counit_iso_hom_app_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.currying_unit_iso_hom_app_app_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.currying_functor_obj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.currying", "description": "The equivalence of functor categories given by currying/uncurrying.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.currying_inverse_obj_obj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.uncurry_obj_flip", "description": " The uncurrying of `F.flip` is isomorphic to\nswapping the factors followed by the uncurrying of `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.uncurry_obj_flip_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.flip_iso_curry_swap_uncurry_hom_app_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.uncurry", "description": "The uncurrying functor, taking a functor `C \u2964 (D \u2964 E)` and producing a functor `(C \u00d7 D) \u2964 E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.curry_obj", "description": "The object level part of the currying functor. (See `curry` for the functorial version.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.uncurry_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.uncurry_obj_flip_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.currying_functor_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.currying_inverse_obj_obj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.currying_unit_iso_inv_app_app_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.flip_iso_curry_swap_uncurry", "description": "`F.flip` is isomorphic to uncurrying `F`, swapping the variables, and currying.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.curry_obj_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.currying_functor_obj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.whiskering_right\u2082_obj_obj_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.currying_counit_iso_inv_app_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.whiskering_right\u2082_obj_obj_obj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_le_of_lipschitz", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.extend_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.clm_comp_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.Sup_unit_ball_eq_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.mul_left_right_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.prod\u2097\u1d62", "description": "`continuous_linear_map.prod` as a `linear_isometry_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_deriv\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.is_O_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.lsmul", "description": "Scalar multiplication as a continuous bilinear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.is_O_with_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.mk_continuous_norm_le", "description": " If a continuous linear map is constructed from a linear map via the constructor `mk_continuous`,\nthen its norm is bounded by the bound given to the constructor if it is nonnegative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.bound_of_shell", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_restrict_scalarsL'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.le_op_nnnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.norm_compL_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_nnnorm_le_bound'", "description": "If one controls the norm of every `A x`, `\u2016x\u2016\u208a \u2260 0`, then one controls the norm of `A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.exists_lt_apply_of_lt_op_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_mul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.is_compact_image_coe_of_bounded_of_closed_image", "description": " Let `s` be a bounded set in the space of continuous (semi)linear maps `E \u2192SL[\u03c3] F` taking values\nin a proper space. If `s` interpreted as a set in the space of maps `E \u2192 F` with topology of\npointwise convergence is closed, then it is compact.\n\nTODO: reformulate this in terms of a type synonym with the right topology.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm", "description": "The operator norm of a continuous linear map is the inf of all its bounds.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.flip\u2097\u1d62'_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.le_of_op_norm_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.bound", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.compSL", "description": "Composition of continuous semilinear maps as a continuous semibilinear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.tmp_topological_add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_mul_left_right_apply_apply_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.flip\u2097\u1d62", "description": " Flip the order of arguments of a continuous bilinear map.\nThis is a version bundled as a `linear_isometry_equiv`.\nFor an unbundled version see `continuous_linear_map.flip`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.antilipschitz_of_embedding", "description": " If a continuous linear map is a topology embedding, then it is expands the distances\nby a positive factor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.to_semi_normed_ring", "description": "Continuous linear maps form a seminormed ring with respect to the operator norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.le_op_norm\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.mul_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.coord_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.is_weak_closed_closed_ball", "description": " A closed ball is closed in the weak-* topology. We don't have a name for `E \u2192SL[\u03c3] F` with\nweak-* topology in `mathlib`, so we use an equivalent condition (see `is_closed_induced_iff'`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.tmp_uniform_space_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.is_closed_image_coe_closed_ball", "description": " The set of functions `f : E \u2192 F` that represent continuous linear maps `f : E \u2192SL[\u03c3\u2081\u2082] F`\nat distance `\u2264 r` from `f\u2080 : E \u2192SL[\u03c3\u2081\u2082] F` is closed in the topology of pointwise convergence.\nThis is one of the key steps in the proof of the **Banach-Alaoglu** theorem.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.compL_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.exists_mul_lt_of_lt_op_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_mul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.is_O_sub_rev", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.norm_subtypeL", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.is_compact_image_coe_closed_ball", "description": " **Banach-Alaoglu** theorem. The set of functions `f : E \u2192 F` that represent continuous linear\nmaps `f : E \u2192SL[\u03c3\u2081\u2082] F` at distance `\u2264 r` from `f\u2080 : E \u2192SL[\u03c3\u2081\u2082] F` is compact in the topology of\npointwise convergence. Other versions of this theorem can be found in\n`analysis.normed_space.weak_dual`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.flip", "description": " Flip the order of arguments of a continuous bilinear map.\nFor a version bundled as `linear_isometry_equiv`, see\n`continuous_linear_map.flipL`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.dist_le_op_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_le_of_shell", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_le_of_shell'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.tendsto_of_tendsto_pointwise_of_cauchy_seq", "description": " If a Cauchy sequence of continuous linear map converges to a continuous linear map pointwise,\nthen it converges to the same map in norm. This lemma is used to prove that the space of continuous\nlinear maps is complete provided that the codomain is a complete space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.flip_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.restrict_scalarsL", "description": "`continuous_linear_map.restrict_scalars` as a `continuous_linear_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_le_of_unit_norm", "description": " For a continuous real linear map `f`, if one controls the norm of every `f x`, `\u2016x\u2016 = 1`, then\none controls the norm of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.to_normed_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.mk_continuous\u2082", "description": " Create a bilinear map (represented as a map `E \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] F \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] G`) from the corresponding linear\nmap and a bound on the norm of the image. The linear map can be constructed using\n`linear_map.mk\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.to_span_singleton_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.prod_map_equivL", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_mul_left_right_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.bounds_bdd_below", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.of_tendsto_of_bounded_range", "description": " Let `f : E \u2192 F` be a map, let `g : \u03b1 \u2192 E \u2192SL[\u03c3\u2081\u2082] F` be a family of continuous (semi)linear maps\nthat takes values in a bounded set and converges to `f` pointwise along a nontrivial filter. Then\n`f` is a continuous (semi)linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.is_O_comp_rev", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.unit_le_op_norm", "description": "The image of the unit ball under a continuous linear map is bounded.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.mul\u2097\u1d62", "description": " Multiplication in a normed algebra as a linear isometry to the space of\ncontinuous linear maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_map_class.bound_of_shell_semi_normed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_eq_of_bounds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.is_compact_image_coe_of_bounded_of_weak_closed", "description": " If a set `s` of semilinear functions is bounded and is closed in the weak-* topology, then its\nimage under coercion to functions `E \u2192 F` is a compact set. We don't have a name for `E \u2192SL[\u03c3] F`\nwith weak-* topology in `mathlib`, so we use an equivalent condition (see `is_closed_induced_iff'`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_restrict_scalars_isometry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.is_closed_image_coe_of_bounded_of_weak_closed", "description": " If a set `s` of semilinear functions is bounded and is closed in the weak-* topology, then its\nimage under coercion to functions `E \u2192 F` is a closed set. We don't have a name for `E \u2192SL[\u03c3] F`\nwith weak-* topology in `mathlib`, so we use an equivalent condition (see `is_closed_induced_iff'`).\n\nTODO: reformulate this in terms of a type synonym with the right topology.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.tmp_topological_space", "description": " The `topological_space` structure on `E \u2192SL[\u03c3\u2081\u2082] F` coming from\n`continuous_linear_map.tmp_seminormed_add_comm_group`.\nSee Note [forgetful inheritance]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.to_seminormed_add_comm_group", "description": "Continuous linear maps themselves form a seminormed space with respect to\n   the operator norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.exists_lt_apply_of_lt_op_nnnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.norm_to_continuous_linear_map_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_extend_le", "description": " If a dense embedding `e : E \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] G` expands the norm by a constant factor `N\u207b\u00b9`, then the\nnorm of the extension of `f` along `e` is bounded by `N * \u2016f\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.homothety_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.extend", "description": " Extension of a continuous linear map `f : E \u2192SL[\u03c3\u2081\u2082] F`, with `E` a normed space and `F` a\ncomplete normed space, along a uniform and dense embedding `e : E \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] F\u2097`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.of_mem_closure_image_coe_bounded", "description": " Construct a bundled continuous (semi)linear map from a map `f : E \u2192 F` and a proof of the fact\nthat it belongs to the closure of the image of a bounded set `s : set (E \u2192SL[\u03c3\u2081\u2082] F)` under coercion\nto function. Coercion to function of the result is definitionally equal to `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.extend_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_lsmul_le", "description": "The norm of `lsmul` is at most 1 in any semi-normed group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.lipschitz", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.of_mem_closure_image_coe_bounded_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.tmp_uniform_space", "description": " The `uniform_space` structure on `E \u2192SL[\u03c3\u2081\u2082] F` coming from\n`continuous_linear_map.tmp_seminormed_add_comm_group`.\nSee Note [forgetful inheritance]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.mk_continuous_norm_le'", "description": " If a continuous linear map is constructed from a linear map via the constructor `mk_continuous`,\nthen its norm is bounded by the bound or zero if bound is negative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.nndist_le_op_nnnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.extend_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.tmp_seminormed_add_comm_group", "description": " Continuous linear maps themselves form a seminormed space with respect to\nthe operator norm. This is only a temporary definition because we want to replace the topology\nwith `continuous_linear_map.topological_space` to avoid diamond issues.\nSee Note [forgetful inheritance]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_zero_iff", "description": "An operator is zero iff its norm vanishes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.apply_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.le_op_norm_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.norm_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.precompR", "description": "Apply `L(x,-)` pointwise to bilinear maps, as a continuous bilinear map", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.bilinear_comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.to_pseudo_metric_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.apply'", "description": " The continuous semilinear map obtained by applying a continuous semilinear map at a given\nvector.\n\nThis is the continuous version of `linear_map.apply\u2097`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.coe_to_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.has_op_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_lsmul", "description": " The norm of `lsmul` equals 1 in any nontrivial normed group.\n\nThis is `continuous_linear_map.op_norm_lsmul_le` as an equality.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.precompL", "description": "Apply `L(-,y)` pointwise to bilinear maps, as a continuous bilinear map", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_mul_left_right_apply_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.flip_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.mul", "description": "Multiplication in a non-unital normed algebra as a continuous bilinear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.norm_compSL_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.mk_continuous\u2082_norm_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.is_O_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.mk_continuous\u2082_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.smul_rightL", "description": " `continuous_linear_map.smul_right` as a continuous trilinear map:\n`smul_rightL (c : E \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] \ud835\udd5c) (f : F) (x : E) = c x \u2022 f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.antilipschitz", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.bound_of_ball_bound", "description": "`linear_map.bound_of_ball_bound'` is a version of this lemma over a field satisfying `is_R_or_C`\nthat produces a concrete bound.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.tmp_pseudo_metric_space", "description": " The `pseudo_metric_space` structure on `E \u2192SL[\u03c3\u2081\u2082] F` coming from\n`continuous_linear_map.tmp_seminormed_add_comm_group`.\nSee Note [forgetful inheritance]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_nnnorm_le_bound", "description": "If one controls the norm of every `A x`, then one controls the norm of `A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.to_normed_algebra", "description": " For a normed space `E`, continuous linear endomorphisms form a normed algebra with\nrespect to the operator norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.compL", "description": "Composition of continuous linear maps as a continuous bilinear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.norm_smul_rightL", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_restrict_scalarsL", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.flip_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.norm_one_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.lipschitz_apply", "description": "Evaluation of a continuous linear map `f` at a point is Lipschitz continuous in `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_le_bound\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_nnnorm_le_of_lipschitz", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_le_of_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.flip_flip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.norm_id", "description": "If a normed space is non-trivial, then the norm of the identity equals `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.norm_restrict_scalars", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.deriv\u2082", "description": " Derivative of a continuous bilinear map `f : E \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] F \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] G` interpreted as a map `E \u00d7 F \u2192 G`\nat point `p : E \u00d7 F` evaluated at `q : E \u00d7 F`, as a continuous bilinear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.Sup_closed_unit_ball_eq_nnnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.apply", "description": " The continuous semilinear map obtained by applying a continuous semilinear map at a given\nvector.\n\nThis is the continuous version of `linear_map.apply\u2097`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.prod_mapL_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.norm_to_continuous_linear_map_comp", "description": " Postcomposition of a continuous linear map with a linear isometry preserves\nthe operator norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_mul_apply_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.precompR_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.subsingleton_or_norm_symm_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.is_O_with_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.norm_id_le", "description": " The norm of the identity is at most `1`. It is in fact `1`, except when the space is trivial\nwhere it is `0`. It means that one can not do better than an inequality in general.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_le_bound", "description": "If one controls the norm of every `A x`, then one controls the norm of `A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.is_O_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.nnnorm_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.prod_mapL", "description": "`continuous_linear_map.prod_map` as a continuous linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.is_O_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.flip\u2097\u1d62_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.norm_smul_rightL_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.compSL_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.prod_mapL", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_image_of_norm_zero", "description": "If `\u2016x\u2016 = 0` and `f` is continuous then `\u2016f x\u2016 = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_coercive", "description": "A bounded bilinear form `B` in a real normed space is *coercive*\nif there is some positive constant C such that `C * \u2016u\u2016 * \u2016u\u2016 \u2264 B u u`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_comp_le", "description": "The operator norm is submultiplicative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.to_normed_ring", "description": "Continuous linear maps form a normed ring with respect to the operator norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_zero", "description": "The norm of the `0` operator is `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.complete_space", "description": " If the target space is complete, the space of continuous linear maps with its norm is also\ncomplete. This works also if the source space is seminormed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_mul\u2097\u1d62", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_flip\u2097\u1d62", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.norm_precompL_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.norm_symm_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.Sup_unit_ball_eq_nnnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_nnnorm_eq_of_bounds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.ratio_le_op_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.restrict_scalars_isometry_to_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.prod_map_equivL", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_comp_linear_isometry_equiv", "description": "Precomposition with a linear isometry preserves the operator norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.is_O_with_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.nnnorm_symm_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.tmp_closed_ball_div_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_flip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.prod_mapL", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.nnnorm_smul_right_apply", "description": " The non-negative norm of the tensor product of a scalar linear map and of an element of a normed\nspace is the product of the non-negative norms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.Sup_closed_unit_ball_eq_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.bilinear_comp", "description": "Compose a bilinear map `E \u2192SL[\u03c3\u2081\u2083] F \u2192SL[\u03c3\u2082\u2083] G` with two linear maps\n`E' \u2192SL[\u03c3\u2081'] E` and `F' \u2192SL[\u03c3\u2082'] F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.flip\u2097\u1d62'", "description": " Flip the order of arguments of a continuous bilinear map.\nThis is a version bundled as a `linear_isometry_equiv`.\nFor an unbundled version see `continuous_linear_map.flip`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.lipschitz", "description": "continuous linear maps are Lipschitz continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.restrict_scalars_isometry", "description": "`continuous_linear_map.restrict_scalars` as a `linear_isometry`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.mk_continuous\u2082_norm_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.map_add_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.antilipschitz_of_comap_nhds_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.norm_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_lsmul_apply_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.lsmul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.is_compact_closure_image_coe_of_bounded", "description": " Let `s` be a bounded set in the space of continuous (semi)linear maps `E \u2192SL[\u03c3] F` taking values\nin a proper space. Then `s` interpreted as a set in the space of maps `E \u2192 F` with topology of\npointwise convergence is precompact: its closure is a compact set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_smul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.one_le_norm_mul_norm_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_add_le", "description": "The operator norm satisfies the triangle inequality.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.of_tendsto_of_bounded_range_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_le_of_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_nnnorm_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.norm_to_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.coe_flip\u2097\u1d62'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.norm_subtypeL_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.is_O_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.norm_id_of_nontrivial_seminorm", "description": " If there is an element with norm different from `0`, then the norm of the identity equals `1`.\n(Since we are working with seminorms supposing that the space is non-trivial is not enough.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.subsingleton_or_nnnorm_symm_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.tmp_topology_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.le_op_norm", "description": "The fundamental property of the operator norm: `\u2016f x\u2016 \u2264 \u2016f\u2016 * \u2016x\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_le_bound'", "description": "If one controls the norm of every `A x`, `\u2016x\u2016 \u2260 0`, then one controls the norm of `A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.bounds_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_nnnorm_le_of_unit_nnnorm", "description": " For a continuous real linear map `f`, if one controls the norm of every `f x`, `\u2016x\u2016\u208a = 1`, then\none controls the norm of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.to_normed_add_comm_group", "description": "Continuous linear maps themselves form a normed space with respect to\n   the operator norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.norm_precompR_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.const_clm_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.to_span_singleton", "description": "Given a unit-length element `x` of a normed space `E` over a field `\ud835\udd5c`, the natural linear\n   isometry map from `\ud835\udd5c` to `E` by taking multiples of `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_norm_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.exists_mul_lt_apply_of_lt_op_nnnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.mul_left_right", "description": " Simultaneous left- and right-multiplication in a non-unital normed algebra, considered as a\ncontinuous trilinear map. This is akin to its non-continuous version `linear_map.mul_left_right`,\nbut there is a minor difference: `linear_map.mul_left_right` is uncurried.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.norm_smul_right_apply", "description": " The norm of the tensor product of a scalar linear map and of an element of a normed space\nis the product of the norms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.norm_to_continuous_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.op_nnnorm_comp_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_map_class.bound_of_continuous", "description": " A continuous linear map between seminormed spaces is bounded when the field is nontrivially\nnormed. The continuity ensures boundedness on a ball of some radius `\u03b5`. The nontriviality of the\nnorm is then used to rescale any element into an element of norm in `[\u03b5/C, \u03b5]`, whose image has a\ncontrolled norm. The norm control for the original element follows by rescaling.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_quotient.quotient.finite_dimensional", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associated_norm_prod_smith", "description": " For a nonzero element `f` in an algebra `S` over a principal ideal domain `R` that is finite and\nfree as an `R`-module, the norm of `f` relative to `R` is associated to the product of the Smith\ncoefficients of the ideal generated by `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finrank_quotient_span_eq_nat_degree_norm", "description": " For a nonzero element `f` in a `F[X]`-module `S`, the dimension of $S/\\langle f \\rangle$ as an\n`F`-vector space is the degree of the norm of `f` relative to `F[X]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.scale_roots_common_denom_mem_lifts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_integral_closure.is_fraction_ring_of_algebraic", "description": " If the field `L` is an algebraic extension of the integral domain `A`,\nthe integral closure `C` of `A` in `L` has fraction field `L`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integral_closure.is_fraction_ring_of_algebraic", "description": " If the field `L` is an algebraic extension of the integral domain `A`,\nthe integral closure of `A` in `L` has fraction field `L`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.integer_normalization_aeval_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.coeff_integer_normalization", "description": " `coeff_integer_normalization p` gives the coefficients of the polynomial\n`integer_normalization p`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_integral_localization", "description": " If `R \u2192 S` is an integral extension, `M` is a submonoid of `R`,\n`R\u2098` is the localization of `R` at `M`,\nand `S\u2098` is the localization of `S` at the image of `M` under the extension map,\nthen the induced map `R\u2098 \u2192 S\u2098` is also an integral extension", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fraction_ring.is_algebraic_iff'", "description": "`S` is algebraic over `R` iff a fraction ring of `S` is algebraic over `R`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fraction_ring.ideal_span_singleton_map_subset", "description": " If the `S`-multiples of `a` are contained in some `R`-span, then `Frac(S)`-multiples of `a`\nare contained in the equivalent `Frac(R)`-span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_integral_closure.is_fraction_ring_of_finite_extension", "description": " If the field `L` is a finite extension of the fraction field of the integral domain `A`,\nthe integral closure `C` of `A` in `L` has fraction field `L`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fraction_ring.integer_normalization_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.integer_normalization_eval\u2082_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.integer_normalization_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.is_integral_elem_localization_at_leading_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.integer_normalization_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.integer_normalization", "description": " `integer_normalization g` normalizes `g` to have integer coefficients\nby clearing the denominators", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.integer_normalization_map_to_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fraction_ring.comap_is_algebraic_iff", "description": "A ring is algebraic over the ring `A` iff it is algebraic over the field of fractions of `A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.coeff_integer_normalization_mem_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_integral_localization_at_leading_coeff", "description": " Given a particular witness to an element being algebraic over an algebra `R \u2192 S`,\nWe can localize to a submonoid containing the leading coefficient to make it integral.\nExplicitly, the map between the localizations will be an integral ring morphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_integral_localization'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integral_closure.is_fraction_ring_of_finite_extension", "description": " If the field `L` is a finite extension of the fraction field of the integral domain `A`,\nthe integral closure of `A` in `L` has fraction field `L`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.coeff_integer_normalization_of_not_mem_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_integral.exists_multiple_integral_of_is_localization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fraction_ring.is_algebraic_iff", "description": " An element of a ring is algebraic over the ring `A` iff it is algebraic\nover the field of fractions of `A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.join_map_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.join_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measurable_of_measurable_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.join_map_dirac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.bind_zero_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measurable_lintegral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.join_dirac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.bind_zero_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.lintegral_join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measurable_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.bind_zero_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measurable_join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measurable_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.bind_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.bind_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.has_measurable_add\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.bind_dirac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measurable_dirac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.dirac_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.join_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.join", "description": " Monadic join on `measure` in the category of measurable spaces and measurable\nfunctions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measurable_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.join_eq_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measurable_space", "description": "Measurability structure on `measure`: Measures are measurable w.r.t. all projections", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.bind", "description": " Monadic bind on `measure`, only works in the category of measurable spaces and measurable\nfunctions. When the function `f` is not measurable the result is not well defined.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.join_map_join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measurable_bind'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.lintegral_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.binary_product_limit_cone_cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.has_limit.product_limit_cone_is_limit_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.binary_product_limit_cone_cone_\u03c0_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.binary_product_limit_cone_cone_\u03c0_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.biprod_iso_prod_inv_comp_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.biproduct_iso_pi_inv_comp_\u03c0_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lequiv_prod_of_right_split_exact", "description": "The isomorphism `A \u00d7 B \u2243\u2097[R] M` coming from a right split exact sequence `0 \u27f6 A \u27f6 M \u27f6 B \u27f6 0`\nof modules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.biproduct_iso_pi_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.biprod_iso_prod_inv_comp_snd_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.biproduct_iso_pi", "description": "We verify that the biproduct we've just defined is isomorphic to the `Module R` structure\non the dependent function type", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.biprod_iso_prod_inv_comp_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.biprod_iso_prod", "description": "We verify that the biproduct in `Module R` is isomorphic to\nthe cartesian product of the underlying types:", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.has_limit.lift", "description": "The map from an arbitrary cone over a indexed family of abelian groups\nto the cartesian product of those groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lequiv_prod_of_left_split_exact", "description": "The isomorphism `A \u00d7 B \u2243\u2097[R] M` coming from a left split exact sequence `0 \u27f6 A \u27f6 M \u27f6 B \u27f6 0`\nof modules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.binary_product_limit_cone_is_limit_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.category_theory.limits.has_finite_biproducts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.biprod_iso_prod_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.has_limit.lift_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.biprod_iso_prod_inv_comp_fst_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.binary_product_limit_cone", "description": "Construct limit data for a binary product in `Module R`, using `Module.of R (M \u00d7 N)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.has_limit.product_limit_cone_cone_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.has_limit.product_limit_cone", "description": "Construct limit data for a product in `Module R`, using `Module.of R (\u03a0 j, F.obj j)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.biproduct_iso_pi_inv_comp_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.category_theory.limits.has_binary_biproducts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.has_limit.product_limit_cone_cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.stalk_map_to_stalk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.SheafedSpace_obj_to_PresheafedSpace_presheaf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.LocallyRingedSpace_obj", "description": "The spectrum of a commutative ring, as a `LocallyRingedSpace`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.SheafedSpace_obj", "description": "The spectrum of a commutative ring, as a `SheafedSpace`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_pushforward_stalk_alg_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec_map_localization_is_iso", "description": "The stalk map of `Spec M\u207b\u00b9R \u27f6 Spec R` is an iso for each `p : Spec M\u207b\u00b9R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.is_localized_module_to_pushforward_stalk_alg_hom_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.to_Spec_\u0393_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.basic_open_hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.SheafedSpace_map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec_\u0393_identity_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.SheafedSpace_obj_to_PresheafedSpace_carrier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.is_localized_module_to_pushforward_stalk_alg_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.to_LocallyRingedSpace_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_pushforward_stalk", "description": "For an algebra `f : R \u2192+* S`, this is the ring homomorphism `S \u2192+* (f\u2217 \ud835\udcaa\u209b)\u209a` for a `p : Spec R`.\nThis is shown to be the localization at `p` in `is_localized_module_to_pushforward_stalk_alg_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.to_pushforward_stalk_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.Top_map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.to_PresheafedSpace_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.LocallyRingedSpace_map_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.to_Top_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.LocallyRingedSpace_map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.to_PresheafedSpace_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.structure_sheaf.algebra_map_pushforward_stalk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.to_PresheafedSpace_obj_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.to_Top", "description": "The spectrum, as a contravariant functor from commutative rings to topological spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.to_PresheafedSpace", "description": "Spec, as a contravariant functor from commutative rings to presheafed spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.to_SheafedSpace_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.LocallyRingedSpace_map_comp", "description": "", "p": "