": "dfinsupp.equiv_prod_dfinsupp_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.zip_with", "description": " Let `f i` be a binary operation `\u03b2\u2081 i \u2192 \u03b2\u2082 i \u2192 \u03b2 i` such that `f i 0 0 = 0`.\nThen `zip_with f hf` is a binary operation `\u03a0\u2080 i, \u03b2\u2081 i \u2192 \u03a0\u2080 i, \u03b2\u2082 i \u2192 \u03a0\u2080 i, \u03b2 i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.support_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.neg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.sigma_curry_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.comp_lift_add_hom", "description": "The `dfinsupp` version of `finsupp.comp_lift_add_hom`,", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.infinite_of_right", "description": "See `dfinsupp.infinite_of_exists_right` for the case that only one `\u03c0 \u03b9` is infinite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.single_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.comap_domain_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.filter_ne_eq_erase'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.filter_linear_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.add_closure_Union_range_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.prod_neg_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.dfinsupp_prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp_sum_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.single_eq_single_iff", "description": "Like `finsupp.single_eq_single_iff`, but with a `heq` due to dependent types", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.support_update_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.filter_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.map_range", "description": " The composition of `f : \u03b2\u2081 \u2192 \u03b2\u2082` and `g : \u03a0\u2080 i, \u03b2\u2081 i` is\n  `map_range f hf