81` with `[category.{v\u2081} J]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.cocone_morphism", "description": "The cocone morphism from the arbitrary choice of colimit cocone to any cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limit.iso_of_equivalence_inv_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.pre_pre", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.iso_limit_cone_hom_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.post_\u03c0_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimit_equivalence_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.is_limit_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimit.iso_of_nat_iso_\u03b9_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.hom_iso", "description": "The isomorphism (in `Type`) between\nmorphisms from a specified object `W` to the limit object,\nand cones with cone point `W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limit.iso_of_nat_iso_inv_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimit.iso_of_nat_iso", "description": "The colimits of `F : J \u2964 C` and `G : J \u2964 C` are isomorphic,\nif the functors are naturally isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.w", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limit_of_iso", "description": "If a functor `F` has a limit, so does any naturally isomorphic functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.pre_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimit.iso_of_equivalence", "description": "The colimits of `F : J \u2964 C` and `G : K \u2964 C` are isomorphic,\nif there is an equivalence `e : J \u224c K` making the triangle commute up to natural isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.w_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.const_lim_adj", "description": "The constant functor and limit functor are adjoint to each other", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimit.iso_of_nat_iso_\u03b9_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limit_of_equivalence_comp", "description": "If a `E \u22d9 F` has a limit, and `E` is an equivalence, we can construct a limit of `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.cone_morphism_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limit.lift_iso_of_nat_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.lim_yoneda", "description": "The isomorphism between\nmorphisms from `W` to the cone point of the limit cone for `F`\nand cones over `F` with cone point `W`\nis natural in `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.iso_limit_cone_inv_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.hom_iso'", "description": "The isomorphism (in `Type`) between\nmorphisms from the colimit object to a specified object `W`,\nand an explicit componentwise description of cocones with cone point `W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.cocone_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limit.iso_of_nat_iso_hom_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.pre", "description": "The canonical morphism from the limit of `F` to the limit of `E \u22d9 F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limit.of_cones_iso", "description": " If a functor `G` has the same collection of cones as a functor `F`\nwhich has a limit, then `G` also has a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.cone_morphism", "description": "The cone morphism from any cone to the arbitrary choice of limit cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.\u03c0", "description": "The projection from the limit object to a value of the functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimit.mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.desc", "description": "The morphism from the colimit object to the cone point of any other cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.comp_cocone_point_unique_up_to_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.pre_pre", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit_equiv_is_colimit_op", "description": "`t : cone F` is a limit cone if and only is `t.op : cocone F.op` is a colimit cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimit.iso_of_nat_iso_\u03b9_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.post", "description": "The canonical morphism from `G` applied to the colimit of `F \u22d9 G`\nto `G` applied to the colimit of `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.id_pre", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.is_colimit_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limit.iso_of_nat_iso_hom_\u03c0_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimit.iso_of_nat_iso_hom_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimit.iso_of_nat_iso_inv_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.exists_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limit_equivalence_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimits_of_shape_of_equivalence", "description": "We can transport colimits of shape `J` along an equivalence `J \u224c J'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.map_post", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colim_map", "description": "Functoriality of colimits.\n\nUsually this morphism should be accessed through `colim.map`,\nbut may be needed separately when you have specified colimits for the source and target functors,\nbut not necessarily for all functors of shape `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.lift_cone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimit.iso_of_nat_iso_inv_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.\u03b9_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimits_of_shape", "description": "`C` has colimits of shape `J` if there exists a colimit for every functor `F : J \u2964 C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimits_of_shape.has_colimit", "description": "`C` has colimits of shape `J` if there exists a colimit for every functor `F : J \u2964 C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.iso_colimit_cocone_\u03b9_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimits.has_colimits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limits_of_shape_of_has_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.lim", "description": "`limit F` is functorial in `F`, when `C` has all limits of shape `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limits", "description": "`C` has all (small) limits if it has limits of every shape that is as big as its hom-sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colim.category_theory.is_left_adjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"na