F.op` is a colimit cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimit_of_iso", "description": "If `F` has a colimit, so does any naturally isomorphic functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.lim_map_\u03c0_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.lim_map_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limits_of_shape", "description": "`C` has limits of shape `J` if there exists a limit for every functor `F : J \u2964 C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limits_of_shape.has_limit", "description": "`C` has limits of shape `J` if there exists a limit for every functor `F : J \u2964 C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.lift_pre", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limit.lift_iso_of_nat_iso_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_smallest_colimits_of_has_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.unop", "description": "If `t : cocone F.op` is a colimit cocone, then `t.unop : cone F.` is a limit cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_smallest_limits_of_has_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.cocone", "description": "An arbitrary choice of colimit cocone of a functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.pre_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.hom_iso", "description": "The isomorphism (in `Type`) between\nmorphisms from the colimit object to a specified object `W`,\nand cocones with cone point `W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.comp_cocone_point_unique_up_to_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimit_of_has_colimits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.map_pre", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.\u03b9_cocone_morphism", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.\u03b9_desc", "description": "We have lots of lemmas describing how to simplify `colimit.\u03b9 F j \u226b _`,\nand combined with `colimit.ext` we rely on these lemmas for many calculations.\n\nHowever, since `category.assoc` is a `@[simp]` lemma, often expressions are\nright associated, and it's hard to apply these lemmas about `colimit.\u03b9`.\n\nWe thus use `reassoc` to define additional `@[simp]` lemmas, with an arbitrary extra morphism.\n(see `tactic/reassoc_axiom.lean`)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.post_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.iso_limit_cone_hom_\u03c0_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colim_coyoneda", "description": "The isomorphism between\nmorphisms from the cone point of the colimit cocone for `F` to `W`\nand cocones over `F` with cone point `W`\nis natural in `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.lim_map_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.lift_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.pre_map'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.desc_cocone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimit.iso_of_nat_iso_hom_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit", "description": "An arbitrary choice of limit object of a functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.pre_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colim_map_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.map_post", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.cone_point_unique_up_to_iso_inv_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.\u03b9", "description": "The coprojection from a value of the functor to the colimit object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit_cone", "description": "`limit_cone F` contains a cone over `F` together with the information that it is a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit_cone.cone", "description": "`limit_cone F` contains a cone over `F` together with the information that it is a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit_cone.is_limit", "description": "`limit_cone F` contains a cone over `F` together with the information that it is a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit_cocone", "description": "`colimit_cocone F` contains a cocone over `F` together with the information that it is a\n   colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit_cocone.cocone", "description": "`colimit_cocone F` contains a cocone over `F` together with the information that it is a\n   colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit_cocone.is_colimit", "description": "`colimit_cocone F` contains a cocone over `F` together with the information that it is a\n   colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.\u03b9_pre", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.\u03b9_post", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.cone_point_unique_up_to_iso_inv_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limit.iso_of_nat_iso", "description": "The limits of `F : J \u2964 C` and `G : J \u2964 C` are isomorphic,\nif the functors are naturally isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.desc_extend", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.get_limit_cone", "description": "Use the axiom of choice to extract explicit `limit_cone F` from `has_limit F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.pre_post", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimit_of_equivalence_comp", "description": "If a `E \u22d9 F` has a colimit, and `E` is an equivalence, we can construct a colimit of `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.iso_colimit_cocone", "description": "Given any other colimit cocone for `F`, the chosen `colimit F` is isomorphic to the cocone point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.lim_map_eq_lim_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.iso_colimit_cocone_\u03b9_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.cone", "description": "An arbitrary choice of limit cone for a functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimits_of_size_shrink", "description": "`has_colimits_of_size_shrink.{v u} C` tries to obtain `has_colimits_of_size.{v u} C`\nfrom some other `has_colimits_of_size C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.pre_post", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.exists_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimit.of_cocones_iso", "description": " If a functor `G` has the same collection of cocones as a functor `F`\nwhich has a colimit, then `G` also has a colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.\u03b9_colim_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limit", "description": "`has_limit F` represents the mere existence of a limit for `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limit.exists_limit", "description": "`has_limit F` represents the mere existence of a limit for `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.iso_colimit_cocone_\u03b9_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimits", "description": "`C` has all (small) colimits if it has colimits of every shape that is as big as its hom-sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limit.iso_of_nat_iso_inv_\u03c0_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.get_colimit_cocone", "description": "Use the axiom of choice to extract explicit `colimit_cocone F` from `has_colimit F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.w_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.post_post", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.cocone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.\u03b9_pre_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colim_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.iso_colimit_cocone_\u03b9_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.lift_post", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.pre_eq", "description": "-\nIf we have particular limit cones available for `E \u22d9 F` and for `F`,\nwe obtain a formula for `limit.pre F E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.hom_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.cone_morphism_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colim_const_adj", "description": "The colimit functor and constant functor are adjoint to each other", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.unop", "description": "If `t : cone F.op` is a limit cone, then `t.unop : cocone F` is a colimit cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.comp_cocone_point_unique_up_to_iso_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimits_of_size", "description": "`C` has all colimits of size `v\u2081 u\u2081` (`has_colimits_of_size.{v\u2081 u\u2081} C`)\nif it has colimits of every shape `J : Type u\u2081` with `[category.{v\u2081} J]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimits_of_size.has_colimits_of_shape", "description": "`C` has all colimits of size `v\u2081 u\u2081` (`has_colimits_of_size.{v\u2081 u\u2081} C`)\nif it has colimits of every shape `J : Type u\u2081` with `[category.{v\u2081} J]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limits_of_size_shrink", "description": "`has_limits_of_size_shrink.{v u} C` tries to obtain `has_limits_of_size.{v u} C`\nfrom some other `has_limits_of_size C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimit", "description": "`has_colimit F` represents the mere existence of a colimit for `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimit.exists_colimit", "description": "`has_colimit F` represents the mere existence of a colimit for `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.lim_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.pre", "description": "The canonical morphism from the colimit of `E \u22d9 F` to the colimit of `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.lift_\u03c0_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit.pre_eq", "description": "-\nIf we have particular colimit cocones available for `E \u22d9 F` and for `F`,\nwe obtain a formula for `colimit.pre F E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimit.iso_of_nat_iso_\u03b9_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit.hom_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.op", "description": "If