 "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_within_sub_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_const_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.bernoulli_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.pure_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.filter_apply_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.to_measure_of_fintype_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.of_finset_apply_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.support_normalize", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.of_finset", "description": "Given a finset `s` and a function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u211d\u22650\u221e` with sum `1` on `s`,\n such that `f a = 0` for `a \u2209 s`, we get a `pmf`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.of_fintype_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.map", "description": "The functorial action of a function on a `pmf`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.filter_apply_ne_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.support_of_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.mem_support_seq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.support_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.monad_seq_eq_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.to_outer_measure_of_finset_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.normalize_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.mem_support_normalize_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.to_measure_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.of_finset_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.bernoulli", "description": "A `pmf` which assigns probability `p` to `tt` and `1 - p` to `ff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.to_outer_measure_of_fintype_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.support_of_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.filter", "description": "Create new `pmf` by filtering on a set with non-zero measure and normalizing", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.seq_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.mem_support_bernoulli_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.support_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.is_lawful_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.bind_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.filter_apply_eq_zero_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.bind_pure_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.filter_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.map_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.support_bernoulli", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.is_lawful_monad", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.to_outer_measure_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.monad_map_eq_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.of_fintype", "description": "Given a finite type `\u03b1` and a function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u211d\u22650\u221e` with sum 1, we get a `pmf`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.support_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.mem_support_of_fintype_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.map_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.mem_support_map_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.to_measure_of_finset_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.mem_support_filter_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.normalize", "description": "Given a `f` with non-zero and non-infinite sum, get a `pmf` by normalizing `f` by its `tsum`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.seq", "description": "The monadic sequencing operation for `pmf`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.mem_support_of_finset_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.iso_mk_inv_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.forget_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.map_comp", "description": "Mapping by the composite morphism `f \u226b g` is the same as mapping by `f` then by `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.over_morphism.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.map_obj_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.hom_mk", "description": "To give a morphism in the over category, it suffices to give an arrow fitting in a commutative\n   triangle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.forget_faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.map_map_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.forget", "description": "The forgetful functor mapping an arrow to its domain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.iterated_slice_backward_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.map_map_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.forget_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.forget_reflects_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.iterated_slice_equiv", "description": "Given f : Y \u27f6 X, we have an equivalence between (T/X)/f and T/Y", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.post", "description": "A functor `F : T \u2964 D` induces a functor `under X \u2964 under (F.obj X)` in the obvious way.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.map_obj_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.hom_mk_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.iterated_slice_backward_forget_forget", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.hom_mk_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.forget_cocone_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.post_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.w", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.forget_faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.iso_mk_hom_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.epi_of_epi_right", "description": "If `k.right` is a epimorphism, then `k` is a epimorphism. In other words, `under.forget X` reflects\nepimorphisms.\nThe converse of `category_theory.under.epi_right_of_epi`.\n\nThis lemma is not an instance, to avoid loops in type class inference.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.iterated_slice_equiv_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.mono_of_mono_left", "description": "If `k.left` is a monomorphism, then `k` is a monomorphism. In other words, `over.forget X` reflects\nmonomorphisms.\nThe converse of `category_theory.over.mono_left_of_mono`.\n\nThis lemma is not an instance, to avoid loops in type class inference.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.map_comp", "description": "Mapping by the composite morphism `f \u226b g` is the same as mapping by `f` then by `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.forget_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.comp_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.coe_from_hom", "description": "We can set up a coercion from arrows with codomain `X` to `over X`. This most likely should not\n   be a global instance, but it is sometimes useful.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.w_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.comp_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.map_id", "description": "Mapping by the identity morphism is just the identity functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.iterated_slice_equiv_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.mono_left_of_mono", "description": "If `k` is a monomorphism, then `k.left` is a monomorphism. In other words, `over.forget X` preserves\nmonomorphisms.\nThe converse of `category_theory.over.mono_of_mono_left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.iterated_slice_forward_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.forget", "description": "The forgetful functor mapping an arrow to its domain.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/001G>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.epi_right_of_epi", "description": "If `k` is a epimorphism, then `k.right` is a epimorphism. In other words, `under.forget X` preserves\nepimorphisms.\nThe converse of `category_theory.under.epi_of_epi_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.map_obj_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.iterated_slice_forward", "description": "Given f : Y \u27f6 X, this is the obvious functor from (T/X)/f to T/Y", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.iterated_slice_backward_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.hom_mk_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.w_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.post_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.under_morphism.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.coe_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.forget_cone_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.hom_mk_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.mk_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.id_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.forget_cone", "description": "The natural cone over the forgetful functor `under X \u2964 T` with cone point `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.iso_mk", "description": "Construct an isomorphism in the over category given isomorphisms of the objects whose forward\ndirection gives a commutative triangle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.forget_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.post_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.mk_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.forget_cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.epi_of_epi_left", "description": "If `k.left` is an epimorphism, then `k` is an epimorphism. In other words, `over.forget X` reflects\nepimorphisms.\nThe converse does not hold without additional assumptions on the underlying category, see\n`category_theory.over.epi_left_of_epi`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.iterated_slice_backward", "description": "Given f : Y \u27f6 X, this is the obvious functor from T/Y to (T/X)/f", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under", "description": "The under category has as objects arrows with domain `X` and as morphisms commutative\n   triangles.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.map", "description": "A morphism `X \u27f6 Y` induces a functor `under Y \u2964 under X` in the obvious way.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.mk_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.post", "description": "A functor `F : T \u2964 D` induces a functor `over X \u2964 over (F.obj X)` in the obvious way.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.mono_of_mono_right", "description": "If `k.right` is a monomorphism, then `k` is a monomorphism. In other words, `under.forget X`\nreflects epimorphisms.\nThe converse does not hold without additional assumptions on the underlying category, see\n`category_theory.under.mono_right_of_mono`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.iso_mk_hom_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.iso_mk_hom_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.under_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.over_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.mk_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.map_obj_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.mk", "description": "To give an object in the over category, it suffices to give a morphism with codomain `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.iterated_slice_equiv_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.forget_reflects_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.mk", "description": "To give an object in the under category, it suffices to give an arrow with domain `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.hom_mk", "description": "To give a morphism in the under category, it suffices to give a morphism fitting in a\n   commutative triangle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.iterated_slice_forward_forget", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.map_id", "description": "Mapping by the identity morphism is just the identity functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.iso_mk_inv_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.iso_mk_inv_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.iterated_slice_equiv_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over", "description": "The over category has as objects arrows in `T` with codomain `X` and as morphisms commutative\ntriangles.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/001G>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.map", "description": "A morphism `f : X \u27f6 Y` induces a functor `over X \u2964 over Y` in the obvious way.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/001G>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.iso_mk", "description": "Construct an isomorphism in the over category given isomorphisms of the objects whose forward\ndirection gives a commutative triangle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.forget_cocone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.forget_cocone", "description": "The natural cocone over the forgetful functor `over X \u2964 T` with cocone point `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.post_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.iterated_slice_forward_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.id_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.w", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.eq_pow_of_pow_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_equiv.restrict_roots_of_unity_coe_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.zmod_equiv_zpowers_symm_apply_zpow'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.pow", "description": " If there is a `n`-th primitive root of unity in `R` and `b` divides `n`,\nthen there is a `b`-th primitive root of unity in `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.nth_roots_one_eq_bUnion_primitive_roots", "description": " `nth_roots n` as a `finset` is equal to the union of `primitive_roots i R` for `i \u2223 n`\nif there is a primitive root of unity in `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "roots_of_unity_le_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.zmod_equiv_zpowers_apply_coe_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.zpow_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root_of_mem_primitive_roots", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "roots_of_unity.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.nth_roots_nodup", "description": " The multiset `nth_roots \u2191n (1 : R)` has no repeated elements\nif there is a primitive root of unity in `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.map_iff_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.coe_aut_to_pow_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.zpowers_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_roots_of_unity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "roots_of_unity.coe_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.neg_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_equiv.restrict_roots_of_unity", "description": "Restrict a ring isomorphism to the nth roots of unity", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.card_primitive_roots", "description": "If an integral domain has a primitive `k`-th root of unity, then it has `\u03c6 k` of them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.coe_units_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.eq_order_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "primitive_roots", "description": " `primitive_roots k R` is the finset of primitive `k`-th roots of unity\nin the integral domain `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.iff_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "roots_of_unity.coe_mk_of_pow_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_primitive_roots", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.zpow_of_gcd_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.mem_nth_roots_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.map_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.coe_inv_to_roots_of_unity_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "roots_of_unity_equiv_nth_roots", "description": " Equivalence between the `k`-th roots of unity in `R` and the `k`-th roots of `1`.\n\nThis is implemented as equivalence of subtypes,\nbecause `roots_of_unity` is a subgroup of the group of units,\nwhereas `nth_roots` is a multiset.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "primitive_roots_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.inv_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.pow_iff_coprime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.pow_eq_one_iff_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "roots_of_unity.is_cyclic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_roots_of_unity_coe_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "roots_of_unity.coe_mk_of_pow_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "roots_of_unity", "description": "`roots_of_unity k M` is the subgroup of elements `m : M\u02e3` that satisfy `m ^ k = 1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.pow_of_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_roots_of_unity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.pow_sub_one_eq", "description": "If `1 < k`, then `\u03b6 ^ k.pred = -(\u2211 i in range k.pred, \u03b6 ^ i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_roots_of_unity", "description": "Restrict a ring homomorphism to the nth roots of unity", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_roots_of_unity_iff_mem_nth_roots", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.coe_to_roots_of_unity_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.aut_to_pow", "description": "The `monoid_hom` that takes an automorphism to the power of \u03bc that \u03bc gets mapped to under it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.pow_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "card_roots_of_unity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "roots_of_unity_equiv_nth_roots_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.not_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "roots_of_unity_equiv_nth_roots_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.eq_pow_of_mem_roots_of_unity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.zmod_equiv_zpowers_apply_coe_int", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.order_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.pow_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.to_roots_of_unity", "description": "Turn a primitive root \u03bc into a member of the `roots_of_unity` subgroup.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.of_map_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.is_primitive_root_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "roots_of_unity.coe_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.aut_to_pow_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.zmod_equiv_zpowers_symm_apply_zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.one_right_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.eq_neg_one_of_two_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root", "description": " An element `\u03b6` is a primitive `k`-th root of unity if `\u03b6 ^ k = 1`,\nand if `l` satisfies `\u03b6 ^ l = 1` then `k \u2223 l`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.pow_eq_one", "description": " An element `\u03b6` is a primitive `k`-th root of unity if `\u03b6 ^ k = 1`,\nand if `l` satisfies `\u03b6 ^ l = 1` then `k \u2223 l`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.dvd_of_pow_eq_one", "description": " An element `\u03b6` is a primitive `k`-th root of unity if `\u03b6 ^ k = 1`,\nand if `l` satisfies `\u03b6 ^ l = 1` then `k \u2223 l`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.pow_of_coprime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.zmod_equiv_zpowers_symm_apply_pow'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "roots_of_unity.mk_of_pow_eq", "description": " Make an element of `roots_of_unity` from a member of the base ring, and a proof that it has\na positive power equal to one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.is_primitive_root_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_equiv.restrict_roots_of_unity_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.zmod_equiv_zpowers_symm_apply_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.ne_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.disjoint", "description": "The sets `primitive_roots k R` are pairwise disjoint.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_roots_of_unity_prime_pow_mul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.card_roots_of_unity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.card_nth_roots_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.card_nth_roots", "description": " The cardinality of the multiset `nth_roots \u2191n (1 : R)` is `n`\nif there is a primitive root of unity in `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.pow_ne_one_of_pos_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.is_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.ne_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.geom_sum_eq_zero", "description": "If `1 < k` then `(\u2211 i in range k, \u03b6 ^ i) = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.primitive_roots_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.zmod_equiv_zpowers", "description": " The (additive) monoid equivalence between `zmod k`\nand the powers of a primitive root of unity `\u03b6`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.mem_roots_of_unity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_roots_of_unity'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.mk_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.zpow_eq_one_iff_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.card_roots_of_unity'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_root_of_unity_eq_pow_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.nth_roots_one_eq_bUnion_primitive_roots'", "description": " `nth_roots n` as a `finset` is equal to the union of `primitive_roots i R` for `i \u2223 n`\nif there is a primitive root of unity in `R`.\nThis holds for any `nat`, not just `pnat`, see `nth_roots_one_eq_bUnion_primitive_roots`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.coe_submonoid_class_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Union_accumulate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.bUnion_accumulate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.subset_accumulate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.mem_accumulate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.accumulate", "description": "`accumulate s` is the union of `s y` for `y \u2264 x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.accumulate_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.monotone_accumulate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.pi_lt_3141593", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.pi_lower_bound_start", "description": " From an upper bound on `sqrt_two_add_series 0 n = 2 cos (\u03c0 / 2 ^ (n+1))` of the form\n`sqrt_two_add_series 0 n \u2264 2 - (a / 2 ^ (n + 1)) ^ 2)`, one can deduce the lower bound `a < \u03c0`\nthanks to basic trigonometric inequalities as expressed in `pi_gt_sqrt_two_add_series`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.sqrt_two_add_series_step_down", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.pi_lower_bound", "description": " Create a proof of `a < \u03c0` for a fixed rational number `a`, given a witness, which is a\nsequence of rational numbers `sqrt 2 < r 1 < r 2 < ... < r n < 2` satisfying the property that\n`sqrt (2 + r i) \u2264 r(i+1)`, where `r 0 = 0` and `sqrt (2 - r n) \u2265 a/2^(n+1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.pi_gt_3141592", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.pi_gt_31415", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.pi_lt_315", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.pi_upper_bound_start", "description": " From a lower bound on `sqrt_two_add_series 0 n = 2 cos (\u03c0 / 2 ^ (n+1))` of the form\n`2 - ((a - 1 / 4 ^ n) / 2 ^ (n + 1)) ^ 2 \u2264 sqrt_two_add_series 0 n`, one can deduce the upper bound\n`\u03c0 < a` thanks to basic trigonometric formulas as expressed in `pi_lt_sqrt_two_add_series`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.pi_gt_three", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.pi_gt_sqrt_two_add_series", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.pi_lt_sqrt_two_add_series", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.pi_lt_31416", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.sqrt_two_add_series_step_up", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.pi_upper_bound", "description": " Create a proof of `\u03c0 < a` for a fixed rational number `a`, given a witness, which is a\nsequence of rational numbers `sqrt 2 < r 1 < r 2 < ... < r n < 2` satisfying the property that\n`sqrt (2 + r i) \u2265 r(i+1)`, where `r 0 = 0` and `sqrt (2 - r n) \u2265 (a - 1/4^n) / 2^(n+1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.pi_gt_314", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.simplicial_object.\u03b4_comp_\u03c3_succ_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cosimplicial_object.augmented.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cosimplicial_object.truncated.category_theory.limits.has_limits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.simplicial_object.augment_hom_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.simplicial_object.truncated.whiskering_obj_obj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cosimplicial_object.truncated.whiskering", "description": "Functor composition induces a functor on truncated cosimplicial objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.simplicial_object.category_theory.limits.has_colimits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cosimplicial_object.augmented.point_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cosimplicial_object.augmented.left_op_right_op_iso_hom_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cosimplicial_simplicial_equiv_inverse_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_the