linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.map_smul'", "description": "A linear equivalence is an invertible linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.inv_fun", "description": "A linear equivalence is an invertible linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.left_inv", "description": "A linear equivalence is an invertible linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.right_inv", "description": "A linear equivalence is an invertible linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.automorphism_group.to_linear_map_monoid_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.smul_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.to_add_equiv_to_int_linear_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.trans_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.eq_comp_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.map_smul\u209b\u2097", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.coe_of_involutive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.to_int_linear_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_equiv_class", "description": " `semilinear_equiv_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear equivs\n`M \u2192 M\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_equiv_class F R M M\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_equiv_class.coe", "description": " `semilinear_equiv_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear equivs\n`M \u2192 M\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_equiv_class F R M M\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_equiv_class.inv", "description": " `semilinear_equiv_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear equivs\n`M \u2192 M\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_equiv_class F R M M\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_equiv_class.left_inv", "description": " `semilinear_equiv_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear equivs\n`M \u2192 M\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_equiv_class F R M M\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_equiv_class.right_inv", "description": " `semilinear_equiv_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear equivs\n`M \u2192 M\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_equiv_class F R M M\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_equiv_class.coe_injective'", "description": " `semilinear_equiv_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear equivs\n`M \u2192 M\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_equiv_class F R M M\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_equiv_class.map_add", "description": " `semilinear_equiv_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear equivs\n`M \u2192 M\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_equiv_class F R M M\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_equiv_class.map_smul\u209b\u2097", "description": " `semilinear_equiv_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear equivs\n`M \u2192 M\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_equiv_class F R M M\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.refl", "description": "The identity map is a linear equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.trans_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.image_eq_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.of_subsingleton_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.restrict_scalars_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.map_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.semilinear_equiv_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.coe_to_linear_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.coe_to_nat_linear_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "distrib_mul_action.to_module_aut", "description": " Each element of the group defines a module automorphism.\n\nThis is a stronger version of `distrib_mul_action.to_add_aut`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.of_subsingleton_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "distrib_mul_action.to_module_aut_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.coe_symm_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.eq_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.symm_trans_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.apply_distrib_mul_action", "description": " The tautological action by `M \u2243\u2097[R] M` on `M`.\n\nThis generalizes `function.End.apply_mul_action`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.to_nat_linear_equiv_to_add_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.coe_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.restrict_scalars", "description": " If `M` and `M\u2082` are both `R`-semimodules and `S`-semimodules and `R`-semimodule structures\nare defined by an action of `R` on `S` (formally, we have two scalar towers), then any `S`-linear\nequivalence from `M` to `M\u2082` is also an `R`-linear equivalence.\n\nSee also `linear_map.restrict_scalars`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.restrict_scalars_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.image_symm_eq_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "distrib_mul_action.to_linear_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linea