{"name": "linear_equiv.of_involutive", "description": "An involutive linear map is a linear equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.to_linear_map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.comp_hom.to_linear_equiv", "description": "`g : R \u2243+* S` is `R`-linear when the module structure on `S` is `module.comp_hom S g` .", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.to_int_linear_equiv_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.refl_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.trans", "description": "Linear equivalences are transitive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.apply_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.comp_hom.to_linear_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.inv_fun_eq_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.to_linear_equiv", "description": "An additive equivalence whose underlying function preserves `smul` is a linear equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.map_ne_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.comp_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_equiv.to_semilinear_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.frequently_high_scores", "description": "If `u` is a sequence which is unbounded above,\nthen it `frequently` reaches a value strictly greater than all previous values.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_of_add_bdd_below_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_diagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_add_at_top_eq_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.prod_at_bot_at_bot_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.at_top_div_const", "description": " If a function tends to infinity along a filter, then this function divided by a positive\nconstant also tends to infinity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.at_top_mul_neg_const", "description": " If a function tends to infinity along a filter, then this function multiplied by a negative\nconstant (on the right) tends to negative infinity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_finset_preimage_at_top_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.frequently_at_bot'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.neg_const_mul_at_bot", "description": " If a function tends to negative infinity along a filter, then this function multiplied by\na negative constant (on the left) tends to positive infinity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.eventually_ne_at_top'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_antitone_basis.eventually_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.tendsto_at_bot_at_bot", "description": "**Alias** of `filter.tendsto_at_bot_at_bot_of_monotone`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_at_top_prod_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_of_add_const_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.eventually_ne_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_le_mul_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_const_mul_at_bot_iff_neg", "description": " If `f` tends to infinity along a nontrivial filter `l`, then `\u03bb x, r * f x` tends to negative\ninfinity if and only if `r < 0. `", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_at_top_finset_prod_le_of_prod_eq", "description": " Let `f` and `g` be two maps to the same commutative monoid. This lemma gives a sufficient\ncondition for comparison of the filter `at_top.map (\u03bb s, \u220f b in s, f b)` with\n`at_top.map (\u03bb s, \u220f b in s, g b)`. This is useful to compare the set of limit points of\n`\u03a0 b in s, f b` as `s \u2192 at_top` with the similar set for `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ici_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_finset_image_at_top_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_comp_coe_Iio_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_mul_const_at_bot_iff", "description": " The function `\u03bb x, f x * r` tends to negative infinity along a nontrivial filter if and only if\n`r > 0` and `f` tends to negative infinity or `r < 0` and `f` tends to infinity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_bit0_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.unbounded_of_tendsto_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.eventually_gt_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_of_add_bdd_above_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.tendsto_at_top_finset", "description": "**Alias** of `filter.tendsto_at_top_finset_of_monotone`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_of_add_bdd_above_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_of_add_const_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.extraction_forall_of_frequently", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.exists_lt_of_tendsto_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.prod_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strict_mono.tendsto_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.strict_mono_subseq_of_tendsto_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.disjoint_at_bot_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_finset_of_monotone", "description": " If `f` is a monotone sequence of `finset`s and each `x` belongs to one of `f n`, then\n`tendsto f at_top at_top`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ioi_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_neg_at_top_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.Ici_mem_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_neg_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.disjoint_at_bot_principal_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.eventually_lt_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_neg_at_top_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.mem_at_top_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.disjoint_at_top_principal_Iio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_at_top_of_monotone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.map_at_top_finset_sum_eq", "description": " Let `g : \u03b3 \u2192 \u03b2` be an injective function and `f : \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b1` be a function from the codomain of `g`\nto an additive commutative monoid. Suppose that `f x = 0` outside of the range of `g`. Then the\nfilters `at_top.map (\u03bb s, \u2211 i in s, f (g i))` and `at_top.map (\u03bb s, \u2211 i in s, f i)` coincide.\n\nThis lemma is used to prove the equality `\u2211' x, f (g x) = \u2211' y, f y` under\nthe same assumptions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.prod_at_top_at_top_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.const_mul_at_bot", "description": " If a function tends to negative infinity along a filter, then this function multiplied by\na positive constant (on the left) also tends to negative infinity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_bit0_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_antitone_basis.comp_strict_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_const_mul_at_bot_iff", "description": " The function `\u03bb x, r * f x` tends to negative infinity along a nontrivial filter if and only if\n`r > 0` and `f` tends to negative infinity or `r < 0` and `f` tends to infinity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_bit1_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_mul_const_at_bot_of_pos", "description": " If `r` is a positive constant, then `\u03bb x, f x * r` tends to negative infinity along a filter if\nand only if `f` tends to negative infinity along the same filter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_mul_const_at_top_iff_pos", "description": " If `f` tends to infinity along a nontrivial filter `l`, then `\u03bb x, f x * r` tends to infinity\nif and only if `0 < r. `", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_mono'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.comap_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_of_add_bdd_above_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.at_top_basis_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_add_left_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.unbounded_of_tendsto_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.exists_seq_forall_of_frequently", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_coe_at_top_of_Ici_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.exists_le_of_tendsto_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_add_const_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.Iio_mem_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_of_add_bdd_above_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_const_mul_at_top_iff", "description": " The function `\u03bb x, r * f x` tends to infinity along a nontrivial filter if and only if `r > 0`\nand `f` tends to infinity or `r < 0` and `f` tends to negative infinity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.extraction_forall_of_eventually'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.at_bot.is_countably_generated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.at_top_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_add_nonneg_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.nonneg_of_eventually_pow_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_principal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.at_bot_mul_neg_const", "description": " If a function tends to negative infinity along a filter, then this function multiplied by\na negative constant (on the right) tends to positive infinity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.neg_const_mul_at_top", "description": " If a function tends to infinity along a filter, then this function multiplied by a negative\nconstant (on the left) tends to negative infinity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_add_nonneg_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.subseq_forall_of_frequently", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.prod_map_prod_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.order_top.at_top_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_add_nonpos_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.const_mul_at_top", "description": " If a function tends to infinity along a filter, then this function multiplied by a positive\nconstant (on the left) also tends to infinity. For a version working in `\u2115` or `\u2124`, use\n`filter.tendsto.const_mul_at_top'` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually.exists_forall_of_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_coe_Iic_at_bot", "description": " The `at_bot` filter for an open interval `Iic a` comes from the `at_bot` filter in the ambient\norder.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_add_left_of_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.at_bot_Iio_eq", "description": " The `at_bot` filter for an open interval `Iio a` comes from the `at_bot` filter in the ambient\norder.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_const_mul_pow_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_comp_coe_Ici_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_gt_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.extraction_forall_of_eventually", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_iff_forall_eventually_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.at_top_of_mul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_antitone_basis.comp_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.at_bot_mul_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.zero_pow_eventually_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_at_bot_prod_self'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_abs_at_bot_at_top", "description": "$\\lim_{x\\to-\\infty}|x|=+\\infty$", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_iff_seq_tendsto", "description": " An abstract version of continuity of sequentially continuous functions on metric spaces:\nif a filter `k` is countably generated then `tendsto f k l` iff for every sequence `u`\nconverging to `k`, `f \u2218 u` tends to `l`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_add_right_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.tendsto_at_top_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_div_at_top_eq_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_