p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.disjoint_at_top_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_at_top_curry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_mul_const_at_bot_iff_pos", "description": " If `f` tends to negative infinity along a nontrivial filter `l`, then `\u03bb x, f x * r` tends to\nnegative infinity if and only if `0 < r. `", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.frequently.forall_exists_of_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_at_bot_eq_of_gc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.subseq_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_pow_at_top_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_of_add_const_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.at_top_mul_const", "description": " If a function tends to infinity along a filter, then this function multiplied by a positive\nconstant (on the right) also tends to infinity. For a version working in `\u2115` or `\u2124`, use\n`filter.tendsto.at_top_mul_const'` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.exists_le_of_tendsto_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_of_add_bdd_below_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_coe_Ioi_at_top", "description": "The image of the filter `at_top` on `Ioi a` under the coercion equals `at_top`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_add_const_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.eventually_ne_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_mul_const_at_bot_of_neg", "description": " If `r` is a negative constant, then `\u03bb x, f x * r` tends to negative infinity along a filter if\nand only if `f` tends to infinity along the same filter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.disjoint_at_top_principal_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.extraction_of_eventually_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_of_add_const_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.prod_map_at_top_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.nsmul_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_antitone_basis.subbasis_with_rel", "description": " Given an antitone basis `s : \u2115 \u2192 set \u03b1` of a filter, extract an antitone subbasis `s \u2218 \u03c6`,\n`\u03c6 : \u2115 \u2192 \u2115`, such that `m < n` implies `r (\u03c6 m) (\u03c6 n)`. This lemma can be used to extract an\nantitone basis with basis sets decreasing \"sufficiently fast\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.not_tendsto_const_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_of_monotone_of_filter", "description": " If a monotone function `u : \u03b9 \u2192 \u03b1` tends to `at_top` along *some* non-trivial filter `l`, then\nit tends to `at_top` along `at_top`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.subsingleton.at_bot_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_lt_mul_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.disjoint_pure_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_const_mul_at_top_of_pos", "description": " If `r` is a positive constant, then `\u03bb x, r * f x` tends to infinity along a filter if and only\nif `f` tends to infinity along the same filter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_neg_at_bot_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_add_const_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.comap_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.nsmul_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.map_at_top_finset_prod_eq", "description": " Let `g : \u03b3 \u2192 \u03b2` be an injective function and `f : \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b1` be a function from the codomain of `g`\nto a commutative monoid. Suppose that `f x = 1` outside of the range of `g`. Then the filters\n`at_top.map (\u03bb s, \u220f i in s, f (g i))` and `at_top.map (\u03bb s, \u220f i in s, f i)` coincide.\n\nThe additive version of this lemma is used to prove the equality `\u2211' x, f (g x) = \u2211' y, f y` under\nthe same assumptions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_add_right_of_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_const_mul_at_bot_iff_pos", "description": " If `f` tends to negative infinity along a nontrivial filter `l`, then `\u03bb x, r * f x` tends to\nnegative infinity if and only if `0 < r. `", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.tendsto_at_bot_at_bot_iff", "description": "**Alias** of `filter.tendsto_at_bot_at_bot_iff_of_monotone`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.not_tendsto_pow_at_top_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_add_nonpos_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.at_top_mul_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_add_at_top_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_at_top_of_monotone'", "description": " If `u` is a monotone function with linear ordered codomain and the range of `u` is not bounded\nabove, then `tendsto u at_top at_top`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.prod_map_prod_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.at_top", "description": "`at_top` is the filter representing the limit `\u2192 \u221e` on an ordered set.\n It is generated by the collection of up-sets `{b | a \u2264 b}`.\n (The preorder need not have a top element for this to be well defined,\n and indeed is trivial when a top element exists.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_diagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_sub_at_top_eq_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.comap_abs_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.frequently_low_scores", "description": "If `u` is a sequence which is unbounded below,\nthen it `frequently` reaches a value strictly smaller than all previous values.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.comap_neg_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.extraction_of_frequently_at_top'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_of_add_bdd_below_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.high_scores", "description": "If `u` is a sequence which is unbounded above,\nthen after any point, it reaches a value strictly greater than all previous values.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_embedding", "description": "A function `f` goes to `-\u221e` independent of an order-preserving embedding `e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_neg_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_of_monotone_of_subseq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.at_top_Ici_eq", "description": " The `at_top` filter for an open interval `Ici a` comes from the `at_top` filter in the ambient\norder.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_of_add_bdd_below_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.not_tendsto_const_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_at_top_eq_of_gc", "description": " A function `f` maps upwards closed sets (at_top sets) to upwards closed sets when it is a\nGalois insertion. The Galois \"insertion\" and \"connection\" is weakened to only require it to be an\ninsertion and a connetion above `b'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.at_top_basis'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_at_top_prod_self'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.comap_embedding_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.at_bot", "description": "`at_bot` is the filter representing the limit `\u2192 -\u221e` on an ordered set.\n It is generated by the collection of down-sets `{b | b \u2264 a}`.\n (The preorder need not have a bottom element for this to be well defined,\n and indeed is trivial when a bottom element exists.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_const_mul_at_top_iff_neg", "description": " If `f` tends to negative infinity along a nontrivial filter `l`, then `\u03bb x, r * f x` tends to\ninfinity if and only if `r < 0. `", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_at_bot_prod_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_abs_at_top_at_top", "description": "$\\lim_{x\\to+\\infty}|x|=+\\infty$", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_lt_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_at_bot_iff_of_monotone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.at_bot_Iic_eq", "description": " The `at_bot` filter for an open interval `Iic a` comes from the `at_bot` filter in the ambient\norder.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.Ioi_mem_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_ne_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.map_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_mono'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_antitone_basis.tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_mul_const_at_top_iff_neg", "description": " If `f` tends to negative infinity along a nontrivial filter `l`, then `\u03bb x, f x * r` tends to\ninfinity if and only if `r < 0. `", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.comap_neg_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.at_top_finset_eq_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually.exists_forall_of_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.low_scores", "description": "If `u` is a sequence which is unbounded below,\nthen after any point, it reaches a value strictly smaller than all previous values.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.at_top_mul_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_of_subseq_tendsto", "description": "A sequence converges if every subsequence has a convergent subsequence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.tendsto_at_top_at_top", "description": "**Alias** of `filter.tendsto_at_top_at_top_of_monotone`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.map_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.exists_lt_of_tendsto_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_at_bot_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.mem_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_comp_coe_Ioi_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.at_bot_countable_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_add_nonpos_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.disjoint_at_bot_principal_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.eventually_ge_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.unbounded_of_tendsto_at_top'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_const_mul_pow_at_top_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_of_monotone_of_subseq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_at_top_iff_of_monotone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.frequently_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.tendsto_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_const_mul_at_top_of_neg", "description": " If `r` is a negative constant, then `\u03bb x, r * f x` tends to infinity along a filter if and only\nif `f` tends to negative infinity along the same filter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.not_tendsto_iff_exists_frequently_nmem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_const_mul_at_top_iff_pos", "description": " If `f` tends to infinity along a nontrivial filter `l`, then `\u03bb x, r * f x` tends to infinity\nif and only if `0 < r. `", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_sub_at_top_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_mul_self_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.frequently_at_top'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.at_top_Ioi_eq", "description": " The `at_top` filter for an open interval `Ioi a` comes from the `at_top` filter in the ambient\norder.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_at_top", "description": "A function `f` grows to `+\u221e` independent of an order-preserving embedding `e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.unbounded_of_tendsto_at_bot'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_add_right_of_ge'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.prod_map_at_bot_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_mul_const_at_bot_iff_neg", "description": " If `f` tends to infinity along a nontrivial filter `l`, then `\u03bb x, f x * r` tends to negative\ninfinity if and only if `r < 0. `", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.subseq_tendsto_of_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.tendsto_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_const_mul_at_bot_of_pos", "description": " If `r` is a positive constant, then `\u03bb x, r * f x` tends to negative infinity along a filter if\nand only if `f` tends to negative infinity along the same filter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_mul_const_at_top_iff", "description": " The function `\u03bb x, f x * r` tends to infinity along a nontrivial filter if and only if `r > 0`\nand `f` tends to infinity or `r < 0` and `f` tends to negative infinity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.at_bot_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.frequently_iff_seq_frequently", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_mul_const_at_top_of_pos", "description": " If `r` is a positive constant, then `\u03bb x, f x * r` tends to infinity along a filter if and only\nif `f` tends to infinity along the same filter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.comap_embedding_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_add_const_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.at_top_countable_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.prod_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_add_right_of_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_of_monotone_of_filter", "description": " If a monotone function `u : \u03b9 \u2192 \u03b1` tends to `at_bot` along *some* non-trivial filter `l`, then\nit tends to `at_bot` along `at_bot`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_add_nonneg_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_coe_Iio_at_bot", "description": " The `at_bot` filter for an open interval `Iio a` comes from the `at_bot` filter in the ambient\norder.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_add_left_of_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_ge_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.at_bot_mul_const", "description": " If a function tends to negative infinity along a filter, then this function multiplied by\na positive constant (on the right) also tends to negative infinity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.frequently_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_le_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_principal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_pow_at_top", "description": " The monomial function `x^n` tends to `+\u221e` at `+\u221e` for any positive natural `n`.\nA version for positive real powers exists as `tendsto_rpow_at_top`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_neg_const_mul_pow_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.at_top.is_countably_generated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_iff_seq_eventually", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_bot_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Iio_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_comp_coe_Iic_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.extraction_of_frequently_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_at_top_add_nonneg_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Iic_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.eventually_le_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lie_algebra_of_ideals", "description": "See `direct_sum.lie_ring_of_ideals` comment.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lie_algebra_of_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lie_module_component", "description": "The projection map onto one component, as a morphism of Lie modules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.to_lie_algebra_to_linear_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lie_algebra_component", "description": "The projection map onto one component, as a morphism of Lie algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lie_module_bracket_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lie_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lie_module_of", "description": "The inclusion of each component into a direct sum as a morphism of Lie modules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lie_of_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lie_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.bracket_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lie_algebra_component_to_linear_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lie_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lie_ring_of_ideals", "description": " The fact that this instance is necessary seems to be a bug in typeclass inference. See\n[this Zulip thread](https://leanprover.zulipchat.com/#narrow/stream/113488-general/topic/\nTypeclass.20resolution.20under.20binders/near/245151099).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lie_module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lie_ring_module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lie_algebra_of_to_linear_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lie_algebra_of", "description": "The inclusion of each component into the direct sum as morphism of Lie algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.to_lie_algebra", "description": " Given a family of Lie algebras `L i`, together with a family of morphisms of Lie algebras\n`f i : L i \u2192\u2097\u2045R\u2046 L'` into a fixed Lie algebra `L'`, we have a natural linear map:\n`(\u2a01 i, L i) \u2192\u2097[R] L'`. If in addition `\u2045f i x, f j y\u2046 = 0` for any `x \u2208 L i` and `y \u2208 L j` (`i \u2260 j`)\nthen this map is a morphism of Lie algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lie_algebra_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lie_of_of_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.to_lie_algebra_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.lie_algebra_component_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.comap_cobounded_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.edist_le_mul_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.to_restrict", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `lipschitz_on_with_iff_restrict`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.weaken", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.bounded.right_of_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.min_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.prod_mk_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.subtype_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.of_le_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.to_locally_bounded_map", "description": "A Lipschitz continuous map is a locally bounded map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.le_add_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_of_locally_lipschitz", "description": "If a function is locally Lipschitz around a point, then it is continuous at this point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.ediam_image_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.le_add_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.dist_le_mul", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `lipschitz_on_with_iff_dist_le_mul`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with_iff_dist_le_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.of_le_add_mul", "description": " For functions to `\u211d`, it suffices to prove `f x \u2264 f y + K * dist x y`; this version\nassumes `0\u2264K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.maps_to_emetric_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.of_dist_le_mul", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `lipschitz_with_iff_dist_le_mul`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.lipschitz_on_with", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.maps_to_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.of_le_add_mul'", "description": " For functions to `\u211d`, it suffices to prove `f x \u2264 f y + K * dist x y`; this version\ndoesn't assume `0\u2264K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.bounded_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "maps_to.lipschitz_on_with_iff_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with_iff_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.coe_to_locally_bounded_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.iff_le_add_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.of_le_add_mul", "description": " For functions to `\u211d`, it suffices to prove `f x \u2264 f y + K * dist x y`; this version\nassumes `0\u2264K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.mul_edist_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.subtype_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.proj_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.mk_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.const_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.edist_lt_of_edist_lt_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.dist_lt_mul_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with", "description": " A function `f` is Lipschitz continuous with constant `K \u2265 0` if for all `x, y`\nwe have `dist (f x) (f y) \u2264 K * dist x y`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.bounded.left_of_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.dist_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.of_edist_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_prod_of_continuous_on_lipschitz_on", "description": " Consider a function `f : \u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b3`. Suppose that it is continuous on each \u201cvertical fiber\u201d\n`{a} \u00d7 t`, `a \u2208 s`, and is Lipschitz continuous on each \u201chorizontal fiber\u201d `s \u00d7 {b}`, `b \u2208 t`\nwith the same Lipschitz constant `K`. Then it is continuous on `s \u00d7 t`.\n\nThe actual statement uses (Lipschitz) continuity of `\u03bb y, f (a, y)` and `\u03bb x, f (x, b)` instead\nof continuity of `f` on subsets of the product space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.bounded_image2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.nndist_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.extend_real", "description": " A function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u211d` which is `K`-Lipschitz on a subset `s` admits a `K`-Lipschitz extension\nto the whole space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.edist_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.prod_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.of_dist_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.dist_le_mul_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.list_prod", "description": " The product of a list of Lipschitz continuous endomorphisms is a Lipschitz continuous\nendomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.diam_image_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.of_dist_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.mk_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.extend_pi", "description": " A function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 (\u03b9 \u2192 \u211d)` which is `K`-Lipschitz on a subset `s` admits a `K`-Lipschitz\nextension to the whole space.\nTODO: state the same result (with the same proof) for the space `\u2113^\u221e (\u03b9, \u211d)` over a possibly\ninfinite type `\u03b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.const_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.edist_iterate_succ_le_geometric", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with_iff_dist_le_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.uniform_continuous_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.iff_le_add_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.edist_le_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.ediam_image2_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.of_le_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.edist_lt_of_edist_lt_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.edist_lt_mul_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.uncurry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.of_dist_le_mul", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `lipschitz_on_with_iff_dist_le_mul`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.max_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.to_restrict_maps_to", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `maps_to.lipschitz_on_with_iff_restrict`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.dist_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.prod_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.dist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.dist_iterate_succ_le_geometric", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with", "description": " A function `f` is Lipschitz continuous with constant `K \u2265 0` on `s` if for all `x, y` in `s`\nwe have `dist (f x) (f y) \u2264 K * dist x y`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.dist_le_mul", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `lipschitz_with_iff_dist_le_mul`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.of_le_add_mul'", "description": " For functions to `\u211d`, it suffices to prove `f x \u2264 f y + K * dist x y`; this version\ndoesn't assume `0\u2264K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.bounded_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.comp_lipschitz_on_with", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_prod_of_continuous_lipschitz", "description": " Consider a function `f : \u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b3`. Suppose that it is continuous on each \u201cvertical section\u201d\n`{a} \u00d7 univ`, `a : \u03b1`, and is Lipschitz continuous on each \u201chorizontal section\u201d\n`univ \u00d7 {b}`, `b : \u03b2` with the same Lipschitz constant `K`. Then it is continuous.\n\nThe actual statement uses (Lipschitz) continuity of `\u03bb y, f (a, y)` and `\u03bb x, f (x, b)` instead\nof continuity of `f` on subsets of the product space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.bounded_prod_of_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.prod_mk_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.maps_to_emetric_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.continuous_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.uniform_continuous", "description": "A Lipschitz function is uniformly continuous", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.subtype_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.maps_to_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.continuous", "description": "A Lipschitz function is continuous", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.source_affine_locally_is_local", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme_restrict_basic_open_of_localization_preserves", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.source_affine_locally_of_source_open_cover_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.affine_locally_respects_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.property_is_local.is_local_affine_locally", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.property_is_local.affine_locally_of_is_open_immersion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.property_is_local.source_affine_locally_of_source_open_cover", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.property_is_local.open_cover_tfae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.source_affine_locally_respects_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.property_is_local.source_affine_locally_comp_of_is_open_immersion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.affine_locally", "description": " For `P` a property of ring homomorphisms, `affine_locally P` holds for `f : X \u27f6 Y` if for each\naffine open `U = Spec A \u2286 Y` and `V = Spec B \u2286 f \u207b\u00b9' U`, the ring hom `A \u27f6 B` satisfies `P`.\nAlso see `affine_locally_iff_affine_opens_le`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.affine_locally_iff_affine_opens_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.respects_iso.of_restrict_morphism_restrict_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.property_is_local.affine_locally_of_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.property_is_local.is_local_source_affine_locally", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.property_is_local.source_affine_open_cover_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.property_is_local.source_open_cover_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.source_affine_locally", "description": " For `P` a property of ring homomorphisms, `source_affine_locally P` holds for `f : X \u27f6 Y`\nwhenever `P` holds for the restriction of `f` on every affine open subset of `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.property_is_local.affine_open_cover_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_open_immersion_comp_of_source_affine_locally", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.respects_iso.basic_open_iff_localization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.property_is_local.affine_open_cover_tfae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.respects_iso.basic_open_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.property_is_local.affine_locally_stable_under_composition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.stable_under_base_change.\u0393_pullback_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "num_derangements_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derangements.decidable_pred", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "card_derangements_fin_eq_num_derangements", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "card_derangements_eq_num_derangements", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "num_derangements_add_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "num_derangements_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "num_derangements_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derangements.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "card_derangements_invariant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "card_derangements_fin_add_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "num_derangements", "description": "The number of derangements of an `n`-element set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "num_derangements_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.map_glue_data_V", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.diagram", "description": "(Implementation) The diagram to take colimit of.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.t_inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.\u03b9_glued_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.diagram_iso", "description": "The diagram of the image of a `glue_data` under a functor `F` is naturally isomorphic to the\noriginal diagram of the `glue_data` via `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.V_pullback_cone_is_limit_of_map", "description": " If `F` preserves the gluing, and reflects the pullback of `U i \u27f6 glued` and `U j \u27f6 glued`,\nthen `F` reflects the fact that `V_pullback_cone` is a pullback.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.diagram_snd_from", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.map_glue_data", "description": "A functor that preserves the pullbacks of `f i j` and `f i k` can map a family of glue data.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.types_\u03b9_jointly_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.glue_condition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.\u03b9_glued_iso_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.diagram_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.map_glue_data_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.glued", "description": "The glued object given a family of gluing data.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.\u03b9_glued_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.t'_iij", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.map_glue_data_t'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.diagram_iso_inv_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.\u03b9", "description": "The map `D.U i \u27f6 D.glued` for each `i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.t'_comp_eq_pullback_symmetry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.t_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.t_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.diagram_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.diagram_iso_inv_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.map_glue_data_U", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.V_pullback_cone", "description": " The pullback cone spanned by `V i j \u27f6 U i` and `V i j \u27f6 U j`.\nThis will often be a pullback diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.\u03b9_glued_iso_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data", "description": "A gluing datum consists of\n1. An index type `J`\n2. An object `U i` for each `i : J`.\n3. An object `V i j` for each `i j : J`.\n4. A monomorphism `f i j : V i j \u27f6 U i` for each `i j : J`.\n5. A transition map `t i j : V i j \u27f6 V j i` for each `i j : J`.\nsuch that\n6. `f i i` is an isomorphism.\n7. `t i i` is the identity.\n8. The pullback for `f i j` and `f i k` exists.\n9. `V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V i j \u27f6 V j i` factors through `V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i \u27f6 V j i` via some\n    `t' : V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i`.\n10. `t' i j k \u226b t' j k i \u226b t' k i j = \ud835\udfd9 _`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.J", "description": "A gluing datum consists of\n1. An index type `J`\n2. An object `U i` for each `i : J`.\n3. An object `V i j` for each `i j : J`.\n4. A monomorphism `f i j : V i j \u27f6 U i` for each `i j : J`.\n5. A transition map `t i j : V i j \u27f6 V j i` for each `i j : J`.\nsuch that\n6. `f i i` is an isomorphism.\n7. `t i i` is the identity.\n8. The pullback for `f i j` and `f i k` exists.\n9. `V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V i j \u27f6 V j i` factors through `V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i \u27f6 V j i` via some\n    `t' : V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i`.\n10. `t' i j k \u226b t' j k i \u226b t' k i j = \ud835\udfd9 _`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.U", "description": "A gluing datum consists of\n1. An index type `J`\n2. An object `U i` for each `i : J`.\n3. An object `V i j` for each `i j : J`.\n4. A monomorphism `f i j : V i j \u27f6 U i` for each `i j : J`.\n5. A transition map `t i j : V i j \u27f6 V j i` for each `i j : J`.\nsuch that\n6. `f i i` is an isomorphism.\n7. `t i i` is the identity.\n8. The pullback for `f i j` and `f i k` exists.\n9. `V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V i j \u27f6 V j i` factors through `V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i \u27f6 V j i` via some\n    `t' : V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i`.\n10. `t' i j k \u226b t' j k i \u226b t' k i j = \ud835\udfd9 _`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.V", "description": "A gluing datum consists of\n1. An index type `J`\n2. An object `U i` for each `i : J`.\n3. An object `V i j` for each `i j : J`.\n4. A monomorphism `f i j : V i j \u27f6 U i` for each `i j : J`.\n5. A transition map `t i j : V i j \u27f6 V j i` for each `i j : J`.\nsuch that\n6. `f i i` is an isomorphism.\n7. `t i i` is the identity.\n8. The pullback for `f i j` and `f i k` exists.\n9. `V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V i j \u27f6 V j i` factors through `V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i \u27f6 V j i` via some\n    `t' : V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i`.\n10. `t' i j k \u226b t' j k i \u226b t' k i j = \ud835\udfd9 _`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.f", "description": "A gluing datum consists of\n1. An index type `J`\n2. An object `U i` for each `i : J`.\n3. An object `V i j` for each `i j : J`.\n4. A monomorphism `f i j : V i j \u27f6 U i` for each `i j : J`.\n5. A transition map `t i j : V i j \u27f6 V j i` for each `i j : J`.\nsuch that\n6. `f i i` is an isomorphism.\n7. `t i i` is the identity.\n8. The pullback for `f i j` and `f i k` exists.\n9. `V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V i j \u27f6 V j i` factors through `V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i \u27f6 V j i` via some\n    `t' : V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i`.\n10. `t' i j k \u226b t' j k i \u226b t' k i j = \ud835\udfd9 _`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.f_mono", "description": "A gluing datum consists of\n1. An index type `J`\n2. An object `U i` for each `i : J`.\n3. An object `V i j` for each `i j : J`.\n4. A monomorphism `f i j : V i j \u27f6 U i` for each `i j : J`.\n5. A transition map `t i j : V i j \u27f6 V j i` for each `i j : J`.\nsuch that\n6. `f i i` is an isomorphism.\n7. `t i i` is the identity.\n8. The pullback for `f i j` and `f i k` exists.\n9. `V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V i j \u27f6 V j i` factors through `V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i \u27f6 V j i` via some\n    `t' : V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i`.\n10. `t' i j k \u226b t' j k i \u226b t' k i j = \ud835\udfd9 _`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.f_has_pullback", "description": "A gluing datum consists of\n1. An index type `J`\n2. An object `U i` for each `i : J`.\n3. An object `V i j` for each `i j : J`.\n4. A monomorphism `f i j : V i j \u27f6 U i` for each `i j : J`.\n5. A transition map `t i j : V i j \u27f6 V j i` for each `i j : J`.\nsuch that\n6. `f i i` is an isomorphism.\n7. `t i i` is the identity.\n8. The pullback for `f i j` and `f i k` exists.\n9. `V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V i j \u27f6 V j i` factors through `V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i \u27f6 V j i` via some\n    `t' : V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i`.\n10. `t' i j k \u226b t' j k i \u226b t' k i j = \ud835\udfd9 _`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.f_id", "description": "A gluing datum consists of\n1. An index type `J`\n2. An object `U i` for each `i : J`.\n3. An object `V i j` for each `i j : J`.\n4. A monomorphism `f i j : V i j \u27f6 U i` for each `i j : J`.\n5. A transition map `t i j : V i j \u27f6 V j i` for each `i j : J`.\nsuch that\n6. `f i i` is an isomorphism.\n7. `t i i` is the identity.\n8. The pullback for `f i j` and `f i k` exists.\n9. `V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V i j \u27f6 V j i` factors through `V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i \u27f6 V j i` via some\n    `t' : V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i`.\n10. `t' i j k \u226b t' j k i \u226b t' k i j = \ud835\udfd9 _`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.t", "description": "A gluing datum consists of\n1. An index type `J`\n2. An object `U i` for each `i : J`.\n3. An object `V i j` for each `i j : J`.\n4. A monomorphism `f i j : V i j \u27f6 U i` for each `i j : J`.\n5. A transition map `t i j : V i j \u27f6 V j i` for each `i j : J`.\nsuch that\n6. `f i i` is an isomorphism.\n7. `t i i` is the identity.\n8. The pullback for `f i j` and `f i k` exists.\n9. `V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V i j \u27f6 V j i` factors through `V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i \u27f6 V j i` via some\n    `t' : V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i`.\n10. `t' i j k \u226b t' j k i \u226b t' k i j = \ud835\udfd9 _`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.t_id", "description": "A gluing datum consists of\n1. An index type `J`\n2. An object `U i` for each `i : J`.\n3. An object `V i j` for each `i j : J`.\n4. A monomorphism `f i j : V i j \u27f6 U i` for each `i j : J`.\n5. A transition map `t i j : V i j \u27f6 V j i` for each `i j : J`.\nsuch that\n6. `f i i` is an isomorphism.\n7. `t i i` is the identity.\n8. The pullback for `f i j` and `f i k` exists.\n9. `V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V i j \u27f6 V j i` factors through `V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i \u27f6 V j i` via some\n    `t' : V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i`.\n10. `t' i j k \u226b t' j k i \u226b t' k i j = \ud835\udfd9 _`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.t'", "description": "A gluing datum consists of\n1. An index type `J`\n2. An object `U i` for each `i : J`.\n3. An object `V i j` for each `i j : J`.\n4. A monomorphism `f i j : V i j \u27f6 U i` for each `i j : J`.\n5. A transition map `t i j : V i j \u27f6 V j i` for each `i j : J`.\nsuch that\n6. `f i i` is an isomorphism.\n7. `t i i` is the identity.\n8. The pullback for `f i j` and `f i k` exists.\n9. `V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V i j \u27f6 V j i` factors through `V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i \u27f6 V j i` via some\n    `t' : V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i`.\n10. `t' i j k \u226b t' j k i \u226b t' k i j = \ud835\udfd9 _`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.t_fac", "description": "A gluing datum consists of\n1. An index type `J`\n2. An object `U i` for each `i : J`.\n3. An object `V i j` for each `i j : J`.\n4. A monomorphism `f i j : V i j \u27f6 U i` for each `i j : J`.\n5. A transition map `t i j : V i j \u27f6 V j i` for each `i j : J`.\nsuch that\n6. `f i i` is an isomorphism.\n7. `t i i` is the identity.\n8. The pullback for `f i j` and `f i k` exists.\n9. `V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V i j \u27f6 V j i` factors through `V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i \u27f6 V j i` via some\n    `t' : V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i`.\n10. `t' i j k \u226b t' j k i \u226b t' k i j = \ud835\udfd9 _`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.cocycle", "description": "A gluing datum consists of\n1. An index type `J`\n2. An object `U i` for each `i : J`.\n3. An object `V i j` for each `i j : J`.\n4. A monomorphism `f i j : V i j \u27f6 U i` for each `i j : J`.\n5. A transition map `t i j : V i j \u27f6 V j i` for each `i j : J`.\nsuch that\n6. `f i i` is an isomorphism.\n7. `t i i` is the identity.\n8. The pullback for `f i j` and `f i k` exists.\n9. `V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V i j \u27f6 V j i` factors through `V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i \u27f6 V j i` via some\n    `t' : V i j \u00d7[U i] V i k \u27f6 V j k \u00d7[U j] V j i`.\n10. `t' i j k \u226b t' j k i \u226b t' k i j = \ud835\udfd9 _`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.diagram_L", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.t'_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.diagram_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.glued_iso", "description": "If `F` preserves the gluing, we obtain an iso between the glued objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.diagram_iso_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.t'_iji", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.t'_jii", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.map_glue_data_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.diagram_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.\u03c0", "description": "The projection `\u2210 D.U \u27f6 D.glued` given by the colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.category_theory.functor.map.category_theory.limits.has_pullback", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.sigma_opens", "description": "(Implementation) The disjoint union of `U i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.diagram_iso_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.map_glue_data_J", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.types_\u03c0_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.t'_comp_eq_pullback_symmetry_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.t_fac_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.glue_condition_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.has_colimit_map_glue_data_diagram", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.\u03b9_jointly_surjective", "description": " If there is a forgetful functor into `Type` that preserves enough (co)limits, then `D.\u03b9` will\nbe jointly surjective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.diagram_R", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.diagram_iso_hom_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.t'_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.has_colimit_multispan_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.\u03c0_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.diagram_iso_hom_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.diagram_fst_from", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.t_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.glue_data.cocycle_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.lift_cover_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.has_coe_to_fun", "description": " Helper instance for when there's too many metavariables to apply `fun_like.has_coe_to_fun`\ndirectly.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.symm_comp_to_continuous_map", "description": "Left inverse to a continuous map from a homeomorphism, mirroring `equiv.symm_comp_self`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.to_continuous_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.lift_cover", "description": " A family `\u03c6 i` of continuous maps `C(S i, \u03b2)`, where the domains `S i` contain a neighbourhood\nof each point in `\u03b1` and the functions `\u03c6 i` agree pairwise on intersections, can be glued to\nconstruct a continuous map in `C(\u03b1, \u03b2)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.const", "description": "The constant map as a continuous map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous", "description": "Deprecated. Use `map_continuous` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.comp_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.equiv_fn_of_discrete", "description": "The continuous functions from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2` are the same as the plain functions when `\u03b1` is discrete.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.coe_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.congr_arg", "description": "Deprecated. Use `fun_like.congr_arg` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.congr_fun", "description": "Deprecated. Use `fun_like.congr_fun` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.comp", "description": "The composition of continuous maps, as a continuous map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.const_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.lift_cover'", "description": " A family `F s` of continuous maps `C(s, \u03b2)`, where (1) the domains `s` are taken from a set `A`\nof sets in `\u03b1` which contain a neighbourhood of each point in `\u03b1` and (2) the functions `F s` agree\npairwise on intersections, can be glued to construct a continuous map in `C(\u03b1, \u03b2)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.copy_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.prod_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.cancel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_continuous_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map_class.to_fun_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.restrict_apply_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.equiv_fn_of_discrete_symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.lift_cover_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.pi", "description": "Abbreviation for product of continuous maps, which is continuous", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.restrict", "description": "The restriction of a continuous function `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` to a subset `s` of `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.prod_map", "description": "Given two continuous maps `f` and `g`, this is the continuous map `(x, y) \u21a6 (f x, g y)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous_at", "description": "Deprecated. Use `map_continuous_at` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.pi_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.to_continuous_map_as_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_copy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.const_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.cancel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.coe_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.restrict_preimage_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.equiv_fn_of_discrete_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.to_continuous_map", "description": "The forward direction of a homeomorphism, as a bundled continuous map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.to_continuous_map_comp_symm", "description": "Right inverse to a continuous map from a homeomorphism, mirroring `equiv.self_comp_symm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.restrict_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.prod_mk", "description": "Given two continuous maps `f` and `g`, this is the continuous map `x \u21a6 (f x, g x)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous_map_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.continuous_map.has_coe", "description": "`homeomorph.to_continuous_map` as a coercion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map_class", "description": " `continuous_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of continuous maps.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `continuous_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map_class.coe", "description": " `continuous_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of continuous maps.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `continuous_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map_class.coe_injective'", "description": " `continuous_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of continuous maps.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `continuous_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map_class.map_continuous", "description": " `continuous_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of continuous maps.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `continuous_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.id", "description": "The identity as a continuous map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.has_coe_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.lift_cover_coe'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.lift_cover_restrict'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_continuous_within_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.map_specializes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map", "description": " The type of continuous maps from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2`.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : C(\u03b1, \u03b2))`,\nyou should parametrize over `{F : Type*} [continuous_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `continuous_map_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.to_fun", "description": " The type of continuous maps from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2`.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : C(\u03b1, \u03b2))`,\nyou should parametrize over `{F : Type*} [continuous_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `continuous_map_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous_to_fun", "description": " The type of continuous maps from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2`.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : C(\u03b1, \u03b2))`,\nyou should parametrize over `{F : Type*} [continuous_map_class F \u03b1 \u03b2] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `continuous_map_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.prod_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous_set_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.copy", "description": " Copy of a `continuous_map` with a new `to_fun` equal to the old one. Useful to fix definitional\nequalities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.restrict_preimage", "description": "The restriction of a continuous map to the preimage of a set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.right_adjoint_uniq_hom_app_counit_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.nat_iso_of_right_adjoint_nat_iso", "description": "Given two adjunctions, if the right adjoints are naturally isomorphic, then so are the left\nadjoints.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.unit_right_adjoint_uniq_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.op_adjoint_op_of_adjoint_counit_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.right_adjoint_uniq", "description": "If `G` and `G'` are both right adjoint to `F`, then they are naturally isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.adjoint_of_unop_adjoint_unop", "description": "If `G.unop` is adjoint to `F.unop` then `F` is adjoint to `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.unit_left_adjoint_uniq_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.left_adjoint_uniq_hom_app_counit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.right_adjoint_uniq_trans_app_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.hom_equiv_left_adjoint_uniq_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.adjoint_op_of_adjoint_unop", "description": "If `G` is adjoint to `F.unop` then `F` is adjoint to `G.op`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.left_adjoint_uniq_hom_counit_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.left_adjoint_uniq_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.left_adjoint_uniq_trans_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.op_adjoint_of_unop_adjoint", "description": "If `G.unop` is adjoint to `F` then `F.op` is adjoint to `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.right_adjoint_uniq_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.left_adjoint_uniq", "description": "If `F` and `F'` are both left adjoint to `G`, then they are naturally isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.left_adjoint_uniq_hom_counit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.unit_right_adjoint_uniq_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.right_adjoint_uniq_trans_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.left_adjoint_uniq_hom_app_counit_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.adjoint_of_op_adjoint_op_counit_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.nat_iso_of_left_adjoint_nat_iso", "description": "Given two adjunctions, if the left adjoints are naturally isomorphic, then so are the right\nadjoints.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.left_adjoint_uniq_trans_app_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.left_adjoint_uniq_trans_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.adjoint_of_op_adjoint_op", "description": "If `G.op` is adjoint to `F.op` then `F` is adjoint to `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.right_adjoint_uniq_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.right_adjoint_uniq_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.right_adjoint_uniq_hom_counit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.unit_right_adjoint_uniq_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.right_adjoint_uniq_trans_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.unit_left_adjoint_uniq_hom_app_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.left_adjoint_uniq_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.hom_equiv_symm_right_adjoint_uniq_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.right_adjoint_uniq_hom_counit_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.unop_adjoint_of_op_adjoint", "description": "If `G.op` is adjoint to `F` then `F.unop` is adjoint to `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.adjoint_of_op_adjoint_op_unit_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.unit_left_adjoint_uniq_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.unit_right_adjoint_uniq_hom_app_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.left_adjoint_uniq_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.right_adjoint_uniq_hom_app_counit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.op_adjoint_op_of_adjoint", "description": "If `G` is adjoint to `F` then `F.op` is adjoint to `G.op`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.left_adjoints_coyoneda_equiv", "description": "If `F` and `F'` are both adjoint to `G`, there is a natural isomorphism\n`F.op \u22d9 coyoneda \u2245 F'.op \u22d9 coyoneda`.\nWe use this in combination with `fully_faithful_cancel_right` to show left adjoints are unique.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.unop_adjoint_unop_of_adjoint", "description": "If `G` is adjoint to `F` then `F.unop` is adjoint to `G.unop`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.adjoint_unop_of_adjoint_op", "description": "If `G` is adjoint to `F.op` then `F` is adjoint to `G.unop`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.unit_left_adjoint_uniq_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.op_adjoint_op_of_adjoint_unit_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.bounded_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.lex.densely_ordered", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.order_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.has_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.to_lex_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.lt_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.no_max_order_of_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.partial_order", "description": "Dictionary / lexicographic partial_order for pairs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.order_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.no_min_order_of_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.has_le", "description": "Dictionary / lexicographic ordering on pairs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.preorder", "description": "Dictionary / lexicographic preorder for pairs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.no_min_order_of_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.no_max_order_of_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.to_lex_strict_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.linear_order", "description": "Dictionary / lexicographic linear_order for pairs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.lex.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.lex.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.matrix_block_diag'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_update_column", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.has_continuous_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_diagonal_tsum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_block_diag'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.matrix_diagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_submatrix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_matrix_diag", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_block_diagonal'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.matrix_diag", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_dot_product", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.topological_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.block_diagonal'_tsum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_update_row", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_block_diag", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.topological_add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.diagonal_tsum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_vec_mul_vec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.topological_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_cramer", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.has_continuous_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.matrix_block_diagonal'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_col", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.conj_transpose_tsum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_matrix_inv", "description": " When `ring.inverse` is continuous at the determinant (such as in a `normed_ring`, or a\n`topological_field`), so is `matrix.has_inv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.matrix_block_diagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_reindex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.matrix_block_diag'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.has_continuous_const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_matrix", "description": " To show a function into matrices is continuous it suffices to show the coefficients of the\nresulting matrix are continuous", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.matrix_diagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.matrix_conj_transpose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_mul_vec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_matrix_block_diagonal'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_block_diagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_matrix_transpose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.matrix_block_diagonal'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.matrix_block_diag", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.has_continuous_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.has_continuous_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.matrix_block_diag", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_trace", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.has_continuous_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_matrix_conj_transpose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.matrix_transpose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.topological_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_conj_transpose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_matrix_block_diagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_adjugate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_mul", "description": "For square matrices the usual `continuous_mul` can be used.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_vec_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_matrix_diagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_row", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.matrix_diag", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_from_blocks", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.matrix_transpose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_diag", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_det", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_elem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.transpose_tsum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.t2_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_diagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.matrix_conj_transpose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.matrix_transpose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.matrix_block_diagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_cluster_pt_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_eq_self_union_frontier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_eventually_eq_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_eq.eq_of_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_nhds_lim", "description": " If `g` tends to some `\ud835\udcdd a` along `f`, then it tends to `\ud835\udcdd (lim f g)`. We formulate\nthis lemma with a `[nonempty \u03b1]` argument of `lim` derived from `h` to make it useful for types\nwithout a `[nonempty \u03b1]` instance. Because of the built-in proof irrelevance, Lean will unify\nthis instance with any other instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_at_top_of_eventually_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Lim'", "description": "If `f` is a filter satisfying `ne_bot f`, then `Lim' f` is a limit of the filter, if it exists.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_singleton_iff_punctured_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.closure_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.inter_open_nonempty", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `dense_iff_inter_open`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.le_lift'_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_nonempty_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_frontier", "description": "The frontier of a set is closed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open", "description": "`is_open s` means that `s` is open in the ambient topological space on `\u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.frontier_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_range_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.lift'_closure_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_mem_of_not_mem_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_basis.lift'_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.mem_of_frequently_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_le_of_le", "description": " To show a filter is above the neighborhood filter at `a`, it suffices to show that it is above\nthe principal filter of some open set `s` containing `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.is_closed_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_iff_cluster_pt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_iff_closure_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_iff_inter_open", "description": "A set is dense if and only if it has a nonempty intersection with each nonempty open set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_iff_frequently", "description": " A set `s` is closed iff for every point `x`, if there is a point `y` close to `x` that belongs\nto `s` then `x` is in `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_range", "description": "`f : \u03b9 \u2192 \u03b2` has dense range if its range (image) is a dense subset of \u03b2.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_range.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frontier_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_eq_iff_is_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_subset_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "library_note.comp_of_eq lemmas", "description": "Lean's elaborator has trouble elaborating applications of lemmas that state that the composition of\ntwo functions satisfy some property at a point, like `continuous_at.comp` / `cont_diff_at.comp` and\n`cont_mdiff_within_at.comp`. The reason is that a lemma like this looks like\n`continuous_at g (f x) \u2192 continuous_at f x \u2192 continuous_at (g \u2218 f) x`.\nSince Lean's elaborator elaborates the arguments from left-to-right, when you write `hg.comp hf`,\nthe elaborator will try to figure out *both* `f` and `g` from the type of `hg`. It tries to figure\nout `f` just from the point where `g` is continuous. For example, if `hg : continuous_at g (a, x)`\nthen the elaborator will assign `f` to the function `prod.mk a`, since in that case `f x = (a, x)`.\nThis is undesirable in most cases where `f` is not a variable. There are some ways to work around\nthis, for example by giving `f` explicitly, or to force Lean to elaborate `hf` before elaborating\n`hg`, but this is annoying.\nAnother better solution is to reformulate composition lemmas to have the following shape\n`continuous_at g y \u2192 continuous_at f x \u2192 f x = y \u2192 continuous_at (g \u2218 f) x`.\nThis is even useful if the proof of `f x = y` is `rfl`.\nThe reason that this works better is because the type of `hg` doesn't mention `f`.\nOnly after elaborating the two `continuous_at` arguments, Lean will try to unify `f x` with `y`,\nwhich is often easy after having chosen the correct functions for `f` and `g`.\nHere is an example that shows the difference:\n```lean\nexample {x\u2080 : \u03b1} (f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2) (hf : continuous_at (function.uncurry f) (x\u2080, x\u2080)) :\n  continuous_at (\u03bb x => f x x) x\u2080 :=\n-- hf.comp x (continuous_at_id.prod continuous_at_id) -- type mismatch\n-- hf.comp_of_eq (continuous_at_id.prod continuous_at_id) rfl -- works\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.exists_mem_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.sdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "all_mem_nhds_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_eq_iff_is_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "library_note.continuity lemma statement", "description": "The library contains many lemmas stating that functions/operations are continuous. There are many\nways to formulate the continuity of operations. Some are more convenient than others.\nNote: for the most part this note also applies to other properties\n(`measurable`, `differentiable`, `continuous_on`, ...).\n\n### The traditional way\nAs an example, let's look at addition `(+) : M \u2192 M \u2192 M`. We can state that this is continuous\nin different definitionally equal ways (omitting some typing information)\n* `continuous (\u03bb p, p.1 + p.2)`;\n* `continuous (function.uncurry (+))`;\n* `continuous \u21bf(+)`. (`\u21bf` is notation for recursively uncurrying a function)\n\nHowever, lemmas with this conclusion are not nice to use in practice because\n1. They confuse the elaborator. The following two examples fail, because of limitations in the\n  elaboration process.\n  ```lean\n  variables {M : Type*} [has_add M] [topological_space M] [has_continuous_add M]\n  example : continuous (\u03bb x : M, x + x) :=\n  continuous_add.comp _\n\n  example : continuous (\u03bb x : M, x + x) :=\n  continuous_add.comp (continuous_id.prod_mk continuous_id)\n  ```\n  The second is a valid proof, which is accepted if you write it as\n  `continuous_add.comp (continuous_id.prod_mk continuous_id : _)`\n\n2. If the operation has more than 2 arguments, they are impractical to use, because in your\n  application the arguments in the domain might be in a different order or associated differently.\n\n### The convenient way\nA much more convenient way to write continuity lemmas is like `continuous.add`:\n```lean\ncontinuous.add {f g : X \u2192 M} (hf : continuous f) (hg : continuous g) : continuous (\u03bb x, f x + g x)\n```\nThe conclusion can be `continuous (f + g)`, which is definitionally equal.\nThis has the following advantages\n* It supports projection notation, so is shorter to write.\n* `continuous.add _ _` is recognized correctly by the elaborator and gives useful new goals.\n* It works generally, since the domain is a variable.\n\nAs an example for an unary operation, we have `continuous.neg`.\n```lean\ncontinuous.neg {f : \u03b1 \u2192 G} (hf : continuous f) : continuous (\u03bb x, -f x)\n```\nFor unary functions, the elaborator is not confused when applying the traditional lemma\n(like `continuous_neg`), but it's still convenient to have the short version available (compare\n`hf.neg.neg.neg` with `continuous_neg.comp $ continuous_neg.comp $ continuous_neg.comp hf`).\n\nAs a harder example, consider an operation of the following type:\n```lean\ndef strans {x : F} (\u03b3 \u03b3' : path x x) (t\u2080 : I) : path x x\n```\nThe precise definition is not important, only its type.\nThe correct continuity principle for this operation is something like this:\n```lean\n{f : X \u2192 F} {\u03b3 \u03b3' : \u2200 x, path (f x) (f x)} {t\u2080 s : X \u2192 I}\n  (h\u03b3 : continuous \u21bf\u03b3) (h\u03b3' : continuous \u21bf\u03b3')\n  (ht : continuous t\u2080) (hs : continuous s) :\n  continuous (\u03bb x, strans (\u03b3 x) (\u03b3' x) (t x) (s x))\n```\nNote that *all* arguments of `strans` are indexed over `X`, even the basepoint `x`, and the last\nargument `s` that arises since `path x x` has a coercion to `I \u2192 F`. The paths `\u03b3` and `\u03b3'` (which\nare unary functions from `I`) become binary functions in the continuity lemma.\n\n### Summary\n* Make sure that your continuity lemmas are stated in the most general way, and in a convenient\n  form. That means that:\n  - The conclusion has a variable `X` as domain (not something like `Y \u00d7 Z`);\n  - Wherever possible, all point arguments `c : Y` are replaced by functions `c : X \u2192 Y`;\n  - All `n`-ary function arguments are replaced by `n+1`-ary functions\n    (`f : Y \u2192 Z` becomes `f : X \u2192 Y \u2192 Z`);\n  - All (relevant) arguments have continuity assumptions, and perhaps there are additional\n    assumptions needed to make the operation continuous;\n  - The function in the conclusion is fully applied.\n* These remarks are mostly about the format of the *conclusion* of a continuity lemma.\n  In assumptions it's fine to state that a function with more than 1 argument is continuous using\n  `\u21bf` or `function.uncurry`.\n\n### Functions with discontinuities\n\nIn some cases, you want to work with discontinuous functions, and in certain expressions they are\nstill continuous. For example, consider the fractional part of a number, `fract : \u211d \u2192 \u211d`.\nIn this case, you want to add conditions to when a function involving `fract` is continuous, so you\nget something like this: (assumption `hf` could be weakened, but the important thing is the shape\nof the conclusion)\n```lean\nlemma continuous_on.comp_fract {X Y : Type*} [topological_space X] [topological_space Y]\n  {f : X \u2192 \u211d \u2192 Y} {g : X \u2192 \u211d} (hf : continuous \u21bff) (hg : continuous g) (h : \u2200 s, f s 0 = f s 1) :\n  continuous (\u03bb x, f x (fract (g x)))\n```\nWith `continuous_at` you can be even more precise about what to prove in case of discontinuities,\nsee e.g. `continuous_at.comp_div_cases`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.frequently.mem_of_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_eq_nhds'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_closure_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_closure_iff_ultrafilter", "description": "`x` belongs to the closure of `s` if and only if some ultrafilter\n supported on `s` converges to `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.open_subset_closure_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "acc_pt.mono", "description": " If `x` is an accumulation point of `F` and `F \u2264 G`, then\n`x` is an accumulation point of `D.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "self_diff_frontier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_sInter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense", "description": "A set is dense in a topological space if every point belongs to its closure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "acc_pt_iff_frequently", "description": " `x` is an accumulation point of a set `C` iff\nthere are points near `x` in `C` and different from `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "all_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_iff_continuous_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually.self_of_nhds", "description": "If a predicate is true in a neighborhood of `a`, then it is true for `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_iff_is_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Lim", "description": "If `f` is a filter, then `Lim f` is a limit of the filter, if it exists.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.mem_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.Lim", "description": "If `F` is an ultrafilter, then `filter.ultrafilter.Lim F` is a limit of the filter, if it exists.\nNote that dot notation `F.Lim` can be used for `F : ultrafilter \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_singleton", "description": "If `x` is not an isolated point of a topological space, then the interior of `{x}` is empty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.frontier_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_compl_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "acc_iff_cluster", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_eq_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_within", "description": " The \"neighborhood within\" filter. Elements of `\ud835\udcdd[s] a` are sets containing the\nintersection of `s` and a neighborhood of `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_closure_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_basis_opens'", "description": " The open neighborhoods of `a` are a basis for the neighborhood filter. See `nhds_basis_opens`\nfor a variant using open sets around `a` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds", "description": " A set is called a neighborhood of `a` if it contains an open set around `a`. The set of all\nneighborhoods of `a` forms a filter, the neighborhood filter at `a`, is here defined as the\ninfimum over the principal filters of all open sets containing `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure", "description": "The closure of `s` is the smallest closed set containing `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_compl_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_subset_preimage_closure_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_cluster_pt_of_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_of_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_def'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.interior_union_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frontier_closure_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.of_closed", "description": " A constructor for topologies by specifying the closed sets,\nand showing that they satisfy the appropriate conditions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cluster_pt.of_le_nhds'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.compl_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_nhds_iff", "description": " A predicate is true in a neighborhood of `a` iff it is true for all the points in an open set\ncontaining `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually.eventually_nhds", "description": " If a predicate is true in a neighbourhood of `a`, then for `y` sufficiently close\nto `a` this predicate is true in a neighbourhood of `y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.of_closure", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `dense_closure`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_eventually_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_eq_interior_union_frontier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_closure_iff_comap_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.nonempty.of_closure", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `closure_nonempty_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_bUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_eventually_le_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cluster_pt", "description": " A point `x` is a cluster point of a filter `F` if `\ud835\udcdd x \u2293 F \u2260 \u22a5`. Also known as\nan accumulation point or a limit point, but beware that terminology varies. This\nis *not* the same as asking `\ud835\udcdd[\u2260] x \u2293 F \u2260 \u22a5`. See `mem_closure_iff_cluster_pt` in particular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_inter_subset_inter_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_iff_ultrafilter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed", "description": "A set is closed if its complement is open", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.is_open_compl", "description": "A set is closed if its complement is open", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.frequently.mem_closure", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `mem_closure_iff_frequently`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cluster_pt.of_nhds_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_closure_iff_cluster_pt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_basis_closeds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_iff_ultrafilter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_iff_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frontier_compl", "description": "The complement of a set has the same frontier as the original set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_closure_of_frequently_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_interior", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.interior_union_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_of_closure_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_bInter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.cluster_pt_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_eq_cluster_pts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space", "description": "A topology on `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.is_open", "description": "A topology on `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.is_open_univ", "description": "A topology on `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.is_open_inter", "description": "A topology on `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.is_open_sUnion", "description": "A topology on `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_eq_zero_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_basis_opens", "description": " The open sets containing `a` are a basis for the neighborhood filter. See `nhds_basis_opens'`\nfor a variant using open neighborhoods instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_closure_iff_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.closure_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_interior_iff_is_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_nhds_Lim", "description": " If a filter `f` is majorated by some `\ud835\udcdd a`, then it is majorated by `\ud835\udcdd (Lim f)`. We formulate\nthis lemma with a `[nonempty \u03b1]` argument of `Lim` derived from `h` to make it useful for types\nwithout a `[nonempty \u03b1]` instance. Because of the built-in proof irrelevance, Lean will unify\nthis instance with any other instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_open_set_nhds'", "description": " If `U` is a neighborhood of each point of a set `s` then it is a neighborhood of s:\nit contains an open set containing `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at", "description": " A function between topological spaces is continuous at a point `x\u2080`\nif `f x` tends to `f x\u2080` when `x` tends to `x\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_bUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_maximal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.interior_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "image_closure_subset_closure_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.maps_to.closure", "description": "If a continuous map `f` maps `s` to `t`, then it maps `closure s` to `closure t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_basis.cluster_pt_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_basis.lift'_closure_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.inter_of_open_left", "description": "The intersection of an open dense set with a dense set is a dense set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_range.closure_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_bind_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_closure_of_mem_closure_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_union_is_closed_of_interior_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lim", "description": " If `f` is a filter in `\u03b2` and `g : \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b1` is a function, then `lim f` is a limit of `g` at `f`,\nif it exists.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_range.subset_closure_image_preimage_of_is_open", "description": " If `f` has dense range and `s` is an open set in the codomain of `f`, then the image of the\npreimage of `s` under `f` is dense in `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_range.mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_range.nonempty_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "acc_pt_iff_nhds", "description": " `x` is an accumulation point of a set `C` iff every neighborhood\nof `x` contains a point of `C` other than `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_inter_open_nonempty_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frontier_eq_closure_inter_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_iff_ultrafilter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "compl_frontier_eq_union_interior", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_range.exists_mem_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_iff_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cluster_pt.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cluster_pt.of_inf_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous", "description": "A function between topological spaces is continuous if the preimage\n of every open set is open. Registered as a structure to make sure it is not unfolded by Lean.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.is_open_preimage", "description": "A function between topological spaces is continuous if the preimage\n of every open set is open. Registered as a structure to make sure it is not unfolded by Lean.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cluster_pt.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_range.comp", "description": " Composition of a continuous map with dense range and a function with dense range has dense\nrange.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.range_subset_closure_image_dense", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_range_iff_closure_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_Inter\u2082_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cluster_pt_principal_iff_frequently", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_closure_iff_nhds_within_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_closure_iff_nhds_basis'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.interior_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_eq.continuous_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "acc_pt", "description": "A point `x` is an accumulation point of a filter `F` if `\ud835\udcdd[\u2260] x \u2293 F \u2260 \u22a5`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_set_of_cluster_pt", "description": " The set of cluster points of a filter is closed. In particular, the set of limit points\nof a sequence is closed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.dense_range_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.maps_to.closure_left", "description": "If a continuous map `f` maps `s` to a closed set `t`, then it maps `closure s` to `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_diff_frontier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_closure", "description": "The closure of a set `s` is dense if and only if `s` is dense.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_range.dense_of_maps_to", "description": " If a continuous map with dense range maps a dense set to a subset of `t`, then `t` is a dense\nset.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frontier_eq_inter_compl_interior", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_is_open_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_eq_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "diff_subset_closure_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frequently_frequently_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.mem_nhds_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frontier_inter_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_interior_iff_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_closure_iff_frequently", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.frontier_preimage_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.closure_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_diff_interior", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.preimage_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_at_bot_of_eventually_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "disjoint.closure_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pure_le_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.dense_range", "description": "A surjective map has dense range.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.subset_interior_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_closure_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_closure_iff_nhds_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_compl_singleton_iff_not_open", "description": "Complement to a singleton is dense if and only if the singleton is not an open set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.tendsto'", "description": " A version of `continuous.tendsto` that allows one to specify a simpler form of the limit.\nE.g., one can write `continuous_exp.tendsto' 0 1 exp_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_fold", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_minimal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.inter_of_open_right", "description": "The intersection of a dense set with an open dense set is a dense set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_sInter_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_iff_forall_mem_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.frontier_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_le.eventually_le_nhds", "description": " If `f x \u2264 g x` in a neighbourhood of `a`, then for `y` sufficiently close to `a` we have\n`f x \u2264 g x` in a neighbourhood of `y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.sdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_nhds_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.continuous_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_inf_principal_nhds_iff_of_forall_eq", "description": " Suppose that `f` sends the complement to `s` to a single point `a`, and `l` is some filter.\nThen `f` tends to `a` along `l` restricted to `s` if and only if it tends to `a` along `l`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_cluster_pt", "description": " A point `x` is a cluster point of a sequence `u` along a filter `F` if it is a cluster point\nof `map u F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_range.dense_image", "description": "The image of a dense set under a continuous map with dense range is a dense set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_set_of_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior", "description": "The interior of a set `s` is the largest open subset of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_closure_iff_nhds_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_eq_empty_iff_dense_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cluster_pt.of_le_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_Inter_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "disjoint.frontier_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_nhds_iff", "description": "A filter lies below the neighborhood filter at `a` iff it contains every open set around `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frontier_union_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_bInter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_top.tendsto_at_top_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_at_top_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_iff_eventually", "description": "A set `s` is open iff for every point `x` in `s` and every `y` close to `x`, `y` is in `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.inter_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.interior_Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_open_set_nhds", "description": " If `U` is a neighborhood of each point of a set `s` then it is a neighborhood of `s`:\nit contains an open set containing `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cluster_pt_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.closure_subset_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.closure_bUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "disjoint.frontier_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frontier", "description": "The frontier of a set is the set of points between the closure and interior.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.nonempty_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_set_of_eventually_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frontier_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_sInter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_pure_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frontier_interior_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_subset_iff_is_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cluster_pt_principal_iff", "description": " `x` is a cluster point of a set `s` if every neighbourhood of `x` meets `s` on a nonempty\nset. See also `mem_closure_iff_cluster_pt`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_frontier", "description": "The frontier of a closed set has no interior point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_interior", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.mem_iff_closure_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_eq.eventually_eq_nhds", "description": " If two functions are equal in a neighbourhood of `a`, then for `y` sufficiently close\nto `a` these functions are equal in a neighbourhood of `y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_interior_iff_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.closure", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `dense_closure`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_bInter_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_const_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_sUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_interior_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frontier_subset_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_singleton_iff_nhds_eq_pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_compl_singleton", "description": " If `x` is not an isolated point of a topological space, then the closure of `{x}\u1d9c` is the whole\nspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_interior", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_compl_singleton", "description": " If `x` is not an isolated point of a topological space, then `{x}\u1d9c` is dense in the whole\nspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cluster_pt.ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.closure_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_of_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "preimage_interior_subset_interior_preimage", "description": "See also `interior_preimage_subset_preimage_interior`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_eq_compl_interior_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.closure_preimage_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.comp_of_eq", "description": "See note [comp_of_eq lemmas]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.eventually_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cluster_pt.of_inf_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_empty_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_iff_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_closure_iff_nhds'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.inter_nhds_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "disjoint.closure_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "acc_principal_iff_cluster", "description": "`x` is an accumulation point of a set `C` iff it is a cluster point of `C \u2216 {x}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.and", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.inter_frontier_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_range.some", "description": "Given a function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` with dense range and `b : \u03b2`, returns some `a : \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.nonempty.closure", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `closure_nonempty_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_mem_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.tsnd", "description": "traverse on the second functor argument", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.comp_tsnd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.tfst_comp_tfst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.id_tsnd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.tfst", "description": "traverse on the first functor argument", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.tsnd_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.id_tfst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.tsnd_comp_tfst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.tsnd_tfst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.tsnd_eq_snd_id'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.tfst_eq_fst_id'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.comp_tfst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.tsnd_comp_tsnd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.tsnd_eq_snd_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.tfst_comp_tsnd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.tfst_tsnd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.tfst_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.tfst_eq_fst_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.assoc_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.swap_binary_fan", "description": "If a cone `t` over `P Q` is a limit cone, then `t.swap` is a limit cone over `Q P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.assoc", "description": "Given binary fans `sXY` over `X Y`, and `sYZ` over `Y Z`, and `s` over `sXY.X Z`,\nif `sYZ` is a limit cone we can construct a binary fan over `X sYZ.X`.\n\nThis is an ingredient of building the associator for a cartesian category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.right_unitor", "description": "Construct a right unitor from specified limit cones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.assoc_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.left_unitor_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.left_unitor_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_chosen_finite_products.tensor_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_chosen_finite_products.left_unitor_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.swap_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_chosen_finite_products.triangle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_chosen_finite_products.monoidal_of_chosen_finite_products_synonym.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.associator", "description": "Given two pairs of limit cones corresponding to the parenthesisations of `X \u00d7 Y \u00d7 Z`,\nwe obtain an isomorphism between the cone points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.assoc_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.assoc_inv_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_binary_product.swap", "description": "Construct `has_binary_product Q P` from `has_binary_product P Q`.\nThis can't be an instance, as it would cause a loop in typeclass search.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.assoc_inv", "description": "Given binary fans `sXY` over `X Y`, and `sYZ` over `Y Z`, and `s` over `X sYZ.X`,\nif `sYZ` is a limit cone we can construct a binary fan over `sXY.X Z`.\n\nThis is an ingredient of building the associator for a cartesian category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_chosen_finite_products.right_unitor_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_chosen_finite_products.monoidal_of_chosen_finite_products_synonym", "description": "A type synonym for `C` carrying a monoidal category structure corresponding to\na fixed choice of limit data for the empty functor, and for `pair X Y` for every `X Y : C`.\n\nThis is an implementation detail for `symmetric_of_chosen_finite_products`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.assoc_inv_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.assoc", "description": "If all the binary fans involved a limit cones, `binary_fan.assoc` produces another limit cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.associator_of_limit_cone", "description": "Given a fixed family of limit data for every pair `X Y`, we obtain an associator.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_chosen_finite_products.monoidal_of_chosen_finite_products_synonym.category_theory.monoidal_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_chosen_finite_products.associator_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_chosen_finite_products.tensor_obj", "description": "Implementation of the tensor product for `monoidal_of_chosen_finite_products`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_chosen_finite_products.pentagon", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.swap", "description": "Swap the two sides of a `binary_fan`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.left_unitor", "description": "Construct a left unitor from specified limit cones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.swap_binary_fan_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.braiding", "description": "Given a limit cone over `X` and `Y`, and another limit cone over `Y` and `X`, we can construct\nan isomorphism between the cone points. Relative to some fixed choice of limits cones for every\npair, these isomorphisms constitute a braiding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.swap_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_chosen_finite_products.tensor_hom", "description": "Implementation of the tensor product of morphisms for `monoidal_of_chosen_finite_products`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.right_unitor_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_chosen_finite_products", "description": "A category with a terminal object and binary products has a natural monoidal structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.right_unitor_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_chosen_finite_products.tensor_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.univ_disj_sum_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infinite_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_subtype_or_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype_of_fintype_ne", "description": "If the subtype of all-but-one elements is a `fintype` then the type itself is a `fintype`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.maps_to.exists_equiv_extend_of_card_eq", "description": " Any injection from a set `s` in a fintype `\u03b1` to a finset `t` of the same cardinality as `\u03b1`\ncan be extended to a bijection between `\u03b1` and `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_subtype_or", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "image_subtype_ne_univ_eq_image_erase", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.exists_equiv_extend_of_card_eq", "description": " Any injection from a finset `s` in a fintype `\u03b1` to a finset `t` of the same cardinality as `\u03b1`\ncan be extended to a bijection between `\u03b1` and `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "image_subtype_univ_ssubset_image_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.set_lintegral_cond_kernel_eq_measure_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.lintegral_cond_kernel_real_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.cond_kernel_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.const_eq_comp_prod_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_kernel_real_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_kernel_real.is_markov_kernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ae_cond_kernel_real_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.set_lintegral_cond_kernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measure_eq_comp_prod", "description": " **Disintegration** of finite product measures on `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03a9`, where `\u03a9` is Polish Borel. Such a\nmeasure can be written as the composition-product of the constant kernel with value `\u03c1.fst`\n(marginal measure over `\u03b1`) and a Markov kernel from `\u03b1` to `\u03a9`. We call that Markov kernel\n`probability_theory.cond_kernel \u03c1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.const_eq_comp_prod", "description": " **Disintegration** of constant kernels. A constant kernel on a product space `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03a9`, where `\u03a9`\nis Polish Borel, can be written as the composition-product of the constant kernel with value `\u03c1.fst`\n(marginal measure over `\u03b1`) and a Markov kernel from `\u03b1` to `\u03a9`. We call that Markov kernel\n`probability_theory.cond_kernel \u03c1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measure_theory.measure.cond_kernel.is_markov_kernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.lintegral_cond_kernel_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.integral_cond_kernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.exists_cond_kernel", "description": "Existence of a conditional kernel. Use the definition `cond_kernel` to get that kernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.set_integral_cond_kernel_univ_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measure_eq_comp_prod_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.set_lintegral_cond_kernel_real_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.ae_integrable_cond_kernel_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.integral_cond_kernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_kernel_real", "description": " Conditional measure on the second space of the product given the value on the first, as a\nkernel. Use the more general `cond_kernel`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.set_integral_cond_kernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.set_lintegral_cond_kernel_univ_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.cond_kernel", "description": " Conditional kernel of a measure on a product space: a Markov kernel such that\n`\u03c1 = ((kernel.const unit \u03c1.fst) \u2297\u2096 (kernel.prod_mk_left unit \u03c1.cond_kernel)) ()`\n(see `probability_theory.measure_eq_comp_prod`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.lintegral_cond_kernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.set_integral_cond_kernel_univ_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.lintegral_cond_kernel_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.set_lintegral_cond_kernel_univ_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.set_lintegral_cond_kernel_real_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.integral_cond_kernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.lintegral_cond_kernel_real_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.integral_norm_cond_kernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.set_lintegral_cond_kernel_real_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {