inimal grades.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_min_order.covby_grade", "description": "A `\ud835\udd46`-graded order where minimal elements have minimal grades.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_min_order.is_min_grade", "description": "A `\ud835\udd46`-graded order where minimal elements have minimal grades.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_min_order.lift_left", "description": "Lifts a graded order along a strictly monotone function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_le_grade_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_max_order", "description": "A `\ud835\udd46`-graded order where maximal elements have maximal grades.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_max_order.grade", "description": "A `\ud835\udd46`-graded order where maximal elements have maximal grades.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_max_order.grade_strict_mono", "description": "A `\ud835\udd46`-graded order where maximal elements have maximal grades.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_max_order.covby_grade", "description": "A `\ud835\udd46`-graded order where maximal elements have maximal grades.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_max_order.is_max_grade", "description": "A `\ud835\udd46`-graded order where maximal elements have maximal grades.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_order", "description": " An `\ud835\udd46`-graded order is an order `\u03b1` equipped with a strictly monotone function `grade \ud835\udd46 : \u03b1 \u2192 \ud835\udd46`\nwhich preserves order covering (`covby`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_order.grade", "description": " An `\ud835\udd46`-graded order is an order `\u03b1` equipped with a strictly monotone function `grade \ud835\udd46 : \u03b1 \u2192 \ud835\udd46`\nwhich preserves order covering (`covby`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_order.grade_strict_mono", "description": " An `\ud835\udd46`-graded order is an order `\u03b1` equipped with a strictly monotone function `grade \ud835\udd46 : \u03b1 \u2192 \ud835\udd46`\nwhich preserves order covering (`covby`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_order.covby_grade", "description": " An `\ud835\udd46`-graded order is an order `\u03b1` equipped with a strictly monotone function `grade \ud835\udd46 : \u03b1 \u2192 \ud835\udd46`\nwhich preserves order covering (`covby`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_bounded_order.lift_left", "description": "Lifts a graded order along a strictly monotone function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covby_iff_lt_covby_grade", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_covby_grade_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_min_order.fin_to_nat", "description": " A `fin n`-graded order is also `\u2115`-graded. We do not mark this an instance because `n` is not\ninferrable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_min_order.lift_right", "description": "Lifts a graded order along a strictly monotone function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_bounded_order.to_grade_min_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_min_order.to_grade_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_lt_grade_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_ne_grade_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade", "description": " The grade of an element in a graded order. Morally, this is the number of elements you need to\ngo down by to get to `\u22a5`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_bounded_order.lift_right", "description": "Lifts a graded order along a strictly monotone function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.grade_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_to_dual", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_max_grade_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_order.fin_to_nat", "description": " A `fin n`-graded order is also `\u2115`-graded. We do not mark this an instance because `n` is not\ninferrable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "grade_bounded_order.to_grade_max_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_min_grade_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.eq_mlocus_same", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.dense_induction", "description": "If `s` is a dense set in an additive monoid `M`,\n`add_submonoid.closure s = \u22a4`, then in order to prove that some predicate `p` holds for all `x : M`\nit suffices to verify `p x` for `x \u2208 s`, verify `p 0`, and verify that `p x` and `p y` imply\n`p (x + y)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid_class", "description": " `add_submonoid_class S M` says `S` is a type of subsets `s \u2264 M` that contain `0`\nand are closed under `(+)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid_class.to_add_mem_class", "description": " `add_submonoid_class S M` says `S` is a type of subsets `s \u2264 M` that contain `0`\nand are closed under `(+)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid_class.to_zero_mem_class", "description": " `add_submonoid_class S M` says `S` is a type of subsets `s \u2264 M` that contain `0`\nand are closed under `(+)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.eq_on_mclosure", "description": "If two monoid homomorphisms are equal on a set, then they are equal on its submonoid closure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.simps.coe", "description": "See Note [custom simps projection]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.coe_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.closure_eq", "description": "Closure of a submonoid `S` equals `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.has_top", "description": "The submonoid `M` of the monoid `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.closure", "description": "The `submonoid` generated by a set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.eq_on_mclosure", "description": "If two monoid homomorphisms are equal on a set, then they are equal on its submonoid\nclosure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.copy_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.has_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.closure_induction", "description": " An induction principle for closure membership. If `p` holds for `1` and all elements of `s`, and\nis preserved under multiplication, then `p` holds for all elements of the closure of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.of_mclosure_eq_top_right", "description": "/-- Let `s` be a subset of an additive monoid `M` such that the closure of `s` is\nthe whole monoid. Then `add_monoid_hom.of_mclosure_eq_top_right` defines an additive monoid\nhomomorphism from `M` asking for a proof of `f (x + y) = f x + f y` only for `y \u2208 s`. -/", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_unit.add_submonoid", "description": "The additive submonoid consisting of the additive units of an additive monoid", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.supr_eq_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.ext", "description": "Two `add_submonoid`s are equal if they have the same elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.mk_le_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.coe_set_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.coe_of_mclosure_eq_top_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.simps.coe", "description": "See Note [custom simps projection]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.mem_carrier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.closure_induction\u2082", "description": "An induction principle for additive closure membership for\npredicates with two arguments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.has_inf", "description": "The inf of two `add_submonoid`s is their intersection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.mem_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.closure_mono", "description": "Additive submonoid closure of a set is monotone in its argument: if `s \u2286 t`,\nthen `closure s \u2264 closure t`", "p": "mathlib"},