ffine schemes", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_basis_basic_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.iso_Spec", "description": "The canonical isomorphism `X \u2245 Spec \u0393(X)` for an affine scheme.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_affine_open.image_is_open_immersion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.map_prime_spectrum_basic_open_of_affine", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.obj.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.AffineScheme.Spec.faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_affine_open.from_Spec_prime_ideal_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_localization_of_eq_basic_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.quasi_compact_of_affine", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_affine_open.prime_ideal_of", "description": "The prime ideal of `\ud835\udcaa\u2093(U)` corresponding to a point `x : U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.basic_open_sections_to_affine.category_theory.is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.AffineScheme.forget_to_Scheme", "description": "The forgetful functor `AffineScheme \u2964 Scheme`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_affine_open.is_localization_stalk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_affine_open.is_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_affine_open.is_open_immersion_from_Spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Scheme.affine_cover_is_affine", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_affine_open.from_Spec_image_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_affine_open.opens_map_from_Spec_basic_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.basic_open_sections_to_affine", "description": " The canonical map `\u0393(\ud835\udcaa\u2093, D(f)) \u27f6 \u0393(Spec \ud835\udcaa\u2093(U), D(Spec_\u0393_identity.inv f))`\nThis is an isomorphism, as witnessed by an `is_iso` instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.AffineScheme.forget_to_Scheme_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.AffineScheme.Spec", "description": "The `Spec` functor into the category of affine schemes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.AffineScheme.of_hom", "description": "Type check a morphism of schemes as a morphism in `AffineScheme`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.AffineScheme.category_theory.limits.has_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.inv_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.smul_comm_class_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_units.add_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.has_faithful_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_units.has_faithful_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.mul_action'", "description": " If an action `G` associates and commutes with multiplication on `M`, then it lifts to an\naction on `M\u02e3`. Notably, this provides `mul_action M\u02e3 N\u02e3` under suitable\nconditions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.smul_inv", "description": "Note that this lemma exists more generally as the global `smul_inv`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.mul_distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_units.vadd_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.distrib_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_units.has_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.mul_distrib_mul_action'", "description": "A stronger form of `units.mul_action'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.smul_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.is_scalar_tower'", "description": "Transfer `is_scalar_tower G H M` to `is_scalar_tower G H M\u02e3`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.smul_comm_class_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.smul_zero_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.coe_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.is_scalar_tower'_left", "description": "Transfer `is_scalar_tower G M \u03b1` to `is_scalar_tower G M\u02e3 \u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.smul_comm_class'", "description": "Transfer `smul_comm_class G H M` to `smul_comm_class G H M\u02e3`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.smul_is_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strict_mono_vec_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone.vec_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lift_fun_vec_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone_vec_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strict_mono.vec_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strict_anti_vec_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strict_anti.vec_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.vec_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone_vec_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.discrete.braided_functor", "description": "A multiplicative morphism between commutative monoids gives a braided functor between\nthe corresponding discrete braided monoidal categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_braided_functor.mk_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name