 and `Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.pullback_limit_cone_is_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.coequalizer_colimit", "description": "Show that the quotient by the relation generated by `f(x) ~ g(x)`\nis a coequalizer for the pair `(f, g)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_functor", "description": "The functor which sends `X, Y` to the product type `X \u00d7 Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_cone_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.product_iso", "description": "The categorical product in `Type u` is the type theoretic product `\u03a0 j, F j`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.terminal_limit_cone", "description": "The category of types has `punit` as a terminal object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.pi_lift_\u03c0_apply", "description": "A restatement of `types.lift_\u03c0_apply` that uses `pi.\u03c0` and `pi.lift`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.pullback_cone", "description": "The explicit pullback cone on `pullback_obj f g`.\nThis is bundled with the `is_limit` data as `pullback_limit_cone f g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_limit_cone", "description": "The category of types has `X \u00d7 Y`, the usual cartesian product,\nas the binary product of `X` and `Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_coproduct_colimit", "description": "The sum type `X \u2295 Y` is a binary coproduct for `X` and `Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.product_iso_hom_comp_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.equalizer_limit", "description": "Show that the subtype `{x : Y // g x = h x}` is an equalizer for the pair `(g,h)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_coproduct_iso_inl_comp_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.equalizer_iso_inv_comp_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_iso_prod", "description": "The product functor given by the instance `has_binary_products (Type u)` is isomorphic to the\nexplicit binary product functor given by the product type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.pullback_limit_cone_cone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.equalizer_iso_hom_comp_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_functor_obj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.equalizer_iso", "description": "The categorical equalizer in `Type u` is `{x : Y // g x = h x}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_iso_hom_comp_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.coequalizer_iso_quot_comp_inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.coproduct_iso_\u03b9_comp_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.product_iso_inv_comp_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.pullback_obj", "description": "The usual explicit pullback in the category of types, as a subtype of the product.\nThe full `limit_cone` data is bundled as `pullback_limit_cone f g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_coproduct_iso_inr_comp_inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.is_coprod_of_mono", "description": "Any monomorphism in `Type` is an coproduct injection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_functor_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_cone_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.initial_iso", "description": "The initial object in `Type u` is `pempty`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.pullback_cone_iso_pullback", "description": "The pullback cone given by the instance `has_pullbacks (Type u)` is isomorphic to the\nexplicit pullback cone given by `pullback_limit_cone`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.coequalizer_rel", "description": "(Implementation) The relation to be quotiented to obtain the coequalizer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.coequalizer_rel.rel", "description": "(Implementation) The relation to be quotiented to obtain the coequalizer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.initial_colimit_cocone", "description": "The category of types has `pempty` as an initial object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_iso_hom_comp_fst_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.pullback_iso_pullback_inv_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_iso_inv_comp_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_coproduct_cocone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_coproduct_iso_inr_comp_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.coproduct_iso", "description": "The categorical coproduct in `Type u` is the type theoretic coproduct `\u03a3 j, F j`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_coproduct_iso_inr_comp_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_iso_hom_comp_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.coproduct_colimit_cocone", "description": "The category of types has `\u03a3 j, f j` as the coproduct of a type family `f : J \u2192 Type`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.type_equalizer_of_unique", "description": "Show the given fork in `Type u` is an equalizer given that any element in the \"difference kernel\"\ncomes from `X`.\nThe converse of `unique_of_type_equalizer`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.coequalizer_iso_quot_comp_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.pi_map_\u03c0_apply", "description": "A restatement of `types.map_\u03c0_apply` that uses `pi.\u03c0` and `pi.map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.equalizer_iso_hom_comp_subtype_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.product_limit_cone", "description": "The category of types has `\u03a0 j, f j` as the product of a type family `f : J \u2192 Type`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.product_iso_hom_comp_eval_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_functor_obj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_limit", "description": "The product type `X \u00d7 Y` is a binary product for `X` and `Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_coproduct_colimit_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.coproduct_iso_mk_comp_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.pullback_iso_pullback_hom_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_iso_inv_comp_fst_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_coproduct_iso_inr_comp_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_iso_hom_comp_snd_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_limit_cone_cone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.coequalizer_preimage_image_eq_of_preimage_eq", "description": " If `\u03c0 : Y \u27f6 Z` is an equalizer for `(f, g)`, and `U \u2286 Y` such that `f \u207b\u00b9' U = g \u207b\u00b9' U`,\nthen `\u03c0 \u207b\u00b9' (\u03c0 '' U) = U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.coequalizer_iso", "description": "The categorical coequalizer in `Type u` is the quotient by `f g ~ g x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_limit_cone_is_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.terminal_iso", "description": "The terminal object in `Type u` is `punit`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_coproduct_colimit_cocone", "description": "The category of types has `X \u2295 Y`,\nas the binary coproduct of `X` and `Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.is_initial_punit", "description": "The initial object in `Type u` is `pempty`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.unique_of_type_equalizer", "description": "The converse of `type_equalizer_of_unique`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_iso_inv_comp_snd_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_coproduct_cocone", "description": "The sum type `X \u2295 Y` forms a cocone for the binary coproduct of `X` and `Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.pullback_iso_pullback_hom_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.is_terminal_punit", "description": "The terminal object in `Type u` is `punit`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_coproduct_iso", "description": "The categorical binary coproduct in `Type u` is the sum `X \u2295 Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_coproduct_iso_inl_comp_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_iso", "description": "The categorical binary product in `Type u` is cartesian product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.pullback_iso_pullback_inv_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.equalizer_iso_inv_comp_\u03b9_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_coproduct_iso_inl_comp_inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_cofan_is_colimit_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.product_iso_inv_comp_\u03c0_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.pullback_iso_pullback", "description": "The pullback given by the instance `has_pullbacks (Type u)` is isomorphic to the\nexplicit pullback object given by `pullback_limit_obj`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_product_iso_inv_comp_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.type_equalizer_iff_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.types.binary_coproduct_cocone_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "acc.of_downward_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "transitive.comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen.trans_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.flip_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "reflexive.comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen.head_induction_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen.cases_head", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen_iff_eq_or_trans_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen.is_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_refl.reflexive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flip_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen_idem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen.swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_gen.is_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.join_of_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.comp", "description": "The composition of two relations, yielding a new relation.  The result\nrelates a term of `\u03b1` and a term of `\u03b3` if there is an intermediate\nterm of `\u03b2` related to both.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.equivalence_join_refl_trans_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.comp_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen.lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "reflexive.ne_imp_iff", "description": " If a reflexive relation `r : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1 \u2192 Prop` holds over `x y : \u03b1`,\nthen it holds whether or not `x \u2260 y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.map_id_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen.closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen.tail'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen.cases_head_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "reflexive.rel_of_ne_imp", "description": " To show a reflexive relation `r : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1 \u2192 Prop` holds over `x y : \u03b1`,\nit suffices to show it holds when `x \u2260 y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.reflexive_refl_trans_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equivalence.comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equivalence.eqv_gen_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen.head", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen.head_induction_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.fibration", "description": "A function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is a fibration between the relation `r\u03b1` and `r\u03b2` if for all\n `a : \u03b1` and `b : \u03b2`, whenever `b : \u03b2` and `f a` are related by `r\u03b2`, `b` is the image\n of some `a' : \u03b1` under `f`, and `a'` and `a` are related by `r\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eqv_gen.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.map.decidable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.map", "description": "The map of a relation `r` through a pair of functions pushes the\nrelation to the codomains of the functions.  The resulting relation is\ndefined by having pairs of terms related if they have preimages\nrelated by `r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.eq_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen.head", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen.cases_tail", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "symmetric.comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_gen.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen.is_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.comp_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen_of_transitive_reflexive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_gen", "description": "`refl_gen r`: reflexive closure of `r`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_gen.refl", "description": "`refl_gen r`: reflexive closure of `r`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_gen.single", "description": "`refl_gen r`: reflexive closure of `r`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "acc_trans_gen_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.join_of_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen", "description": "`trans_gen r`: transitive closure of `r`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen.single", "description": "`trans_gen r`: transitive closure of `r`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen.tail", "description": "`trans_gen r`: transitive closure of `r`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "acc.of_fibration", "description": "If `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is a fibration between relations `r\u03b1` and `r\u03b2`, and `a : \u03b1` is\n accessible under `r\u03b1`, then `f a` is accessible under `r\u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.church_rosser", "description": "A sufficient condition for the Church-Rosser property.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen_of_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.join", "description": "The join of a relation on a single type is a new relation for which\npairs of terms are related if there is a third term they are both\nrelated to.  For example, if `r` is a relation representing rewrites\nin a term rewriting system, then *confluence* is the property that if\n`a` rewrites to both `b` and `c`, then `join r` relates `b` and `c`\n(see `relation.church_rosser`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen.to_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "swap_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.iff_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen.head'_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.map_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen", "description": "`refl_trans_gen r`: reflexive transitive closure of `r`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen.refl", "description": "`refl_trans_gen r`: reflexive transitive closure of `r`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen.tail", "description": "`refl_trans_gen r`: reflexive transitive closure of `r`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen_idem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_gen.to_refl_trans_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen.head'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen.total_of_right_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen.lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen.trans_induction_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_gen_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "well_founded.trans_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen.trans_induction_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.reflexive_join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.transitive_join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.transitive_refl_trans_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen.symmetric", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen.lift'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen.lift'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equivalence.eqv_gen_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen.tail'_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "symmetric.iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.transitive_trans_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen.swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "reflexive_ne_imp_iff", "description": " If a reflexive relation `r : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1 \u2192 Prop` holds over `x y : \u03b1`,\nthen it holds whether or not `x \u2260 y`. Unlike `reflexive.ne_imp_iff`, this uses `[is_refl \u03b1 r]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen.is_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.equivalence_join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen.trans_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.symmetric_join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "acc.trans_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.trans_gen_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen.cases_tail_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen.single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "symmetric.flip_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "symmetric.swap_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "relation.refl_trans_gen_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod_comparison_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod_comparison_nat_iso_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.map_inr_inv_coprod_comparison", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.symmetry_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod_comparison_nat_trans_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod_comparison_inv_natural", "description": "If the coproduct comparison morphism is an iso, its inverse is natural.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inv_prod_comparison_map_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_id_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.functor_obj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.pentagon", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.\u03c0_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.lift_fst_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_comp_inl_inr_codiag", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.fst", "description": "The first projection of a binary fan.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.\u03c0_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.is_limit_iff_is_iso_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.left_unitor", "description": "The left unitor isomorphism for binary products with the terminal object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.symmetry'_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diag", "description": "diagonal arrow of the binary product in the category `fam I`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.mk_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod", "description": "If we have a coproduct of `X` and `Y`, we can access it using `coprod X Y ` or\n   `X \u2a3f Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.functor_obj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_pair.equiv_bool", "description": "An equivalence from `walking_pair` to `bool`, sometimes useful when reindexing limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.right_unitor_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.map_inl_inv_coprod_comparison", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.desc'", "description": "If the coproduct of `X` and `Y` exists, then every pair of morphisms `f : X \u27f6 W` and\n   `g : Y \u27f6 W` induces a morphism `l : X \u2a3f Y \u27f6 W` satisfying `coprod.inl \u226b l = f` and\n   `coprod.inr \u226b l = g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_cofan.is_colimit_iff_is_iso_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pair_function_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.map_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.map_pair_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod_comparison_natural_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.coprod_obj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.left_unitor_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod_comparison_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.mk_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.associator", "description": "The associator isomorphism for binary products.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod_comparison_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod_is_prod", "description": "The binary fan constructed from the projection maps is a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.diag_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.map_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inv_prod_comparison_map_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_cofan.is_colimit_comp_right_iso", "description": "If `Y' \u2245 Y`, then `X \u2a3f Y` also is the coproduct of `X` and `Y'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_cofan.is_colimit.mk", "description": "A convenient way to show that a binary cofan is a colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.inl_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.map_pair_iso_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod_comparison_nat_trans", "description": "The coproduct comparison morphism from `FA \u2a3f F-` to `F(A \u2a3f -)`, whose components are given by\n`coprod_comparison`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.mk_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.inr_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod_comparison_nat_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.associator_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_binary_coproduct", "description": "An abbreviation for `has_colimit (pair X Y)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.lift_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.right_unitor", "description": "The right unitor isomorphism for binary coproducts with the initial object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.diag_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.inl_map_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.map_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_cofan.mk_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod_comparison_natural_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.left_unitor_hom_naturality_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod_comparison_inr_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.map_inr_inv_coprod_comparison_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.iso_binary_cofan_mk", "description": "Every `binary_fan` is isomorphic to an application of `binary_fan.mk`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_cofan.inr", "description": "The second inclusion of a binary cofan.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.comp_diag", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_pair.swap", "description": "The equivalence swapping left and right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.is_limit_comp_left_iso", "description": "If `X' \u2245 X`, then `X \u00d7 Y` also is the product of `X'` and `Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.snd", "description": "The second projection of a binary fan.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.map_pair_iso", "description": " The natural isomorphism between two functors out of the walking pair, specified by its\ncomponents.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.braiding", "description": "The braiding isomorphism which swaps a binary product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.pentagon", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.right_unitor_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_pair.equiv_bool_apply_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.is_limit_comp_right_iso", "description": "If `Y' \u2245 Y`, then `X x Y` also is the product of `X` and `Y'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inv_prod_comparison_map_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.coprod_obj", "description": "Auxiliary definition for `over.coprod`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.map_comp_id_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.right_unitor_hom_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.left_unitor_inv_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod_comparison_nat_iso", "description": "The natural isomorphism `FA \u2a3f F- \u2245 F(A \u2a3f -)`, provided each `coprod_comparison F A B` is an\nisomorphism (as `B` changes).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pair_obj_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod_comparison_inl_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.inr", "description": "The inclusion map from the second component of the coproduct.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.map_pair_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_comp_inl_inr_codiag_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.diag_map_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod_right_unitor_inv_naturality_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.mono_lift_of_mono_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod_comparison_natural", "description": "Naturality of the prod_comparison morphism in both arguments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.pentagon_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod_comparison_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod_comparison_natural", "description": "Naturality of the coprod_comparison morphism in both arguments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_cofan.is_colimit_comp_left_iso", "description": "If `X' \u2245 X`, then `X \u2a3f Y` also is the coproduct of `X'` and `Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_coprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.diag_map_fst_snd_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.symmetry", "description": "The braiding isomorphism is symmetric.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.symmetry'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map", "description": "If the coproducts `W \u2a3f X` and `Y \u2a3f Z` exist, then every pair of morphisms `f : W \u27f6 Y` and\n   `g : W \u27f6 Z` induces a morphism `coprod.map f g : W \u2a3f X \u27f6 Y \u2a3f Z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.map_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.left_unitor_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.fst", "description": "The projection map to the first component of the product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.mono_lift_of_mono_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.braiding_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod_comparison_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.associator_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod_comparison_nat_trans", "description": "The product comparison morphism from `F(A \u2a2f -)` to `FA \u2a2f F-`, whose components are given by\n`prod_comparison`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.map_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diag.category_theory.is_split_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.lift", "description": "If the product of `X` and `Y` exists, then every pair of morphisms `f : W \u27f6 X` and `g : W \u27f6 Y`\n   induces a morphism `prod.lift f g : W \u27f6 X \u2a2f Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_codiag", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.braiding_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.codiag", "description": "codiagonal arrow of the binary coproduct", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_cofan.is_colimit_mk", "description": "This is a more convenient formulation to show that a `binary_cofan` constructed using\n`binary_cofan.mk` is a colimit cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.is_limit.hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.map_inl_inv_coprod_comparison_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod_comparison", "description": "The product comparison morphism.\n\nIn `category_theory/limits/preserves` we show this is always an iso iff F preserves binary products.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.lift_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_cofan.is_colimit_iff_is_iso_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_cofan.is_colimit_flip", "description": "Binary coproducts are symmetric.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_cofan.is_colimit.desc'", "description": "If `s` is a colimit binary cofan over `X` and `Y`,, then every pair of morphisms `f : X \u27f6 W` and\n   `g : Y \u27f6 W` induces a morphism `l : s.X \u27f6 W` satisfying `s.inl \u226b l = f` and `s.inr \u226b l = g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.inl_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.inr_map_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inv_prod_comparison_map_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.diag_map_fst_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_pair.equiv_bool_symm_apply_ff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.braiding_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod_comparison_nat_iso_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.lift'", "description": "If the product of `X` and `Y` exists, then every pair of morphisms `f : W \u27f6 X` and `g : W \u27f6 Y`\n   induces a morphism `l : W \u27f6 X \u2a2f Y` satisfying `l \u226b prod.fst = f` and `l \u226b prod.snd = g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.map_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagram_iso_pair", "description": "Every functor out of the walking pair is naturally isomorphic (actually, equal) to a `pair`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.associator_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod_comparison_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_cofan.\u03b9_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_cofan.\u03b9_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.coprod", "description": "A category with binary coproducts has a functorial `sup` operation on over categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_pair.swap_symm_apply_tt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.comp_lift_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.right_unitor", "description": "The right unitor isomorphism for binary products with the terminal object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod_right_unitor_inv_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.lift_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.symmetry'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.braiding_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_binary_coproducts", "description": "`has_binary_coproducts` represents a choice of coproduct for every pair of objects.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04AP>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_comp_id_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pair_function_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_pair.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.map_id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod_comparison_inv_natural_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.associator_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagram_iso_pair_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.braiding", "description": "The braiding isomorphism which swaps a binary coproduct.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.functor_left_comp", "description": "The product functor can be decomposed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.functor", "description": "The binary coproduct functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.lift_fst_comp_snd_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.left_unitor_inv_naturality_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.map_pair", "description": " The natural transformation between two functors out of the\n walking pair, specified by its\ncomponents.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.functor_obj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_binary_products", "description": "`has_binary_products` represents a choice of product for every pair of objects.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/001T>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.lift_map_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan", "description": "A binary fan is just a cone on a diagram indexing a product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.lift_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_pair.swap_symm_apply_ff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.associator_naturality_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_inl_inr_codiag", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.coprod_obj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.diag_map_fst_snd_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.symmetry'_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.inl_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_pair.swap_apply_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.functor_obj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.desc_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.desc_comp_inl_comp_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.functor_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_pair", "description": "The type of objects for the diagram indexing a binary (co)product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_pair.left", "description": "The type of objects for the diagram indexing a binary (co)product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_pair.right", "description": "The type of objects for the diagram indexing a binary (co)product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_pair.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.mk", "description": "A binary fan with vertex `P` consists of the two projections `\u03c0\u2081 : P \u27f6 X` and `\u03c0\u2082 : P \u27f6 Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.diag_map_fst_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod_is_coprod", "description": "The binary cofan constructed from the coprojection maps is a colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_binary_products_of_has_limit_pair", "description": "If `C` has all limits of diagrams `pair X Y`, then it has all binary products", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.braid_natural_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_iso", "description": "If the coproducts `W \u2a3f X` and `Y \u2a3f Z` exist, then every pair of isomorphisms `f : W \u2245 Y` and\n   `g : W \u2245 Z` induces a isomorphism `coprod.map_iso f g : W \u2a3f X \u2245 Y \u2a3f Z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_map_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pair_function", "description": "The function on the walking pair, sending the two points to `X` and `Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.functor", "description": "The binary product functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pair_comp", "description": "The natural isomorphism between `pair X Y \u22d9 F` and `pair (F.obj X) (F.obj Y)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.inr_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.desc", "description": "If the coproduct of `X` and `Y` exists, then every pair of morphisms `f : X \u27f6 W` and\n   `g : Y \u27f6 W` induces a morphism `coprod.desc f g : X \u2a3f Y \u27f6 W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.epi_desc_of_epi_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_pair.swap_apply_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.left_unitor_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.functor_left_comp", "description": "The coproduct functor can be decomposed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.map_id_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagram_iso_pair_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.map_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod_comparison_nat_iso", "description": "The natural isomorphism `F(A \u2a2f -) \u2245 FA \u2a2f F-`, provided each `prod_comparison F A B` is an\nisomorphism (as `B` changes).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.comp_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.lift_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.snd", "description": "The projecton map to the second component of the product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_cofan.mk_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.associator_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.map_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.is_limit_flip", "description": "Binary products are symmetric.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod_comparison_nat_trans_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.right_unitor_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.map_iso", "description": "If the products `W \u2a2f X` and `Y \u2a2f Z` exist, then every pair of isomorphisms `f : W \u2245 Y` and\n   `g : X \u2245 Z` induces an isomorphism `prod.map_iso f g : W \u2a2f X \u2245 Y \u2a2f Z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_cofan.inl", "description": "The first inclusion of a binary cofan.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod_comparison_nat_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.associator", "description": "The associator isomorphism for binary coproducts.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_cofan.is_colimit.desc'_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.coprod_obj_2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.is_limit_mk", "description": "This is a more convenient formulation to show that a `binary_fan` constructed using\n`binary_fan.mk` is a limit cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_binary_coproducts_of_has_colimit_pair", "description": "If `C` has all colimits of diagrams `pair X Y`, then it has all binary coproducts", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.is_limit_iff_is_iso_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.is_limit.lift'", "description": "If `s` is a limit binary fan over `X` and `Y`, then every pair of morphisms `f : W \u27f6 X` and\n   `g : W \u27f6 Y` induces a morphism `l : W \u27f6 s.X` satisfying `l \u226b s.fst = f` and `l \u226b s.snd = g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.right_unitor_hom_naturality_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pair", "description": "The diagram on the walking pair, sending the two points to `X` and `Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_swap_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.functor_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_pair.equiv_bool_apply_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.left_unitor_hom_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_cofan", "description": "A binary cofan is just a cocone on a diagram indexing a coproduct.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.map_swap_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_cofan.mk", "description": "A binary cofan with vertex `P` consists of the two inclusions `\u03b9\u2081 : X \u27f6 P` and `\u03b9\u2082 : Y \u27f6 P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.coprod_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_id_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.map", "description": "If the products `W \u2a2f X` and `Y \u2a2f Z` exist, then every pair of morphisms `f : W \u27f6 Y` and\n   `g : X \u27f6 Z` induces a morphism `prod.map f g : W \u2a2f X \u27f6 Y \u2a2f Z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.map_pair_iso_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.inr_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.inl", "description": "The inclusion map from the first component of the coproduct.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.triangle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pair_obj_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod", "description": "If we have a product of `X` and `Y`, we can access it using `prod X Y` or\n   `X \u2a2f Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.left_unitor", "description": "The left unitor isomorphism for binary coproducts with the initial object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_binary_product", "description": "An abbreviation for `has_limit (pair X Y)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_cofan.is_colimit.hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.epi_desc_of_epi_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod_comparison_inv_natural", "description": "If the product comparison morphism is an iso, its inverse is natural.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_inl_inr_codiag_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.map_codiag_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.associator_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.desc_inl_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.braid_natural", "description": "The braiding isomorphism can be passed through a map by swapping the order.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.is_limit.lift'_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.map_comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod_comparison", "description": "The coproduct comparison morphism.\n\nIn `category_theory/limits/preserves` we show\nthis is always an iso iff F preserves binary coproducts.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.walking_pair.equiv_bool_symm_apply_tt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.map_map_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.right_unitor_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.symmetry", "description": "The braiding isomorphism is symmetric.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod_comparison_inv_natural_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.iso_binary_fan_mk", "description": "Every `binary_fan` is isomorphic to an application of `binary_fan.mk`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.map_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_cofan.mk_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.binary_fan.is_limit.mk", "description": "A convenient way to show that a binary fan is a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.triangle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.left_unitor_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.prod.map_id_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coprod.desc_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_eq_of_equiv_fin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_eq_fintype_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.finite_of_card_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part_enat.card_image_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part_enat.card_eq_top_of_infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_zmod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_eq_two_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_plift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.to_part_enat_le_coe_nat_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part_enat.card_eq_coe_fintype_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.coe_nat_lt_coe_iff_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_eq_of_bijective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part_enat.card_ulift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_ulift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part_enat.card_le_one_iff_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.to_part_enat_eq_coe_nat_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part_enat.card", "description": "`part_enat.card \u03b1` is the cardinality of `\u03b1` as an extended natural number.\n If `\u03b1` is infinite, `part_enat.card \u03b1 = \u22a4`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_eq_two_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part_enat.is_finite_of_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part_enat.card_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part_enat.card_eq_zero_iff_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.coe_nat_eq_to_part_enat_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part_enat.one_lt_card_iff_nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part_enat.card_image_of_inj_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.equiv_fin_of_card_pos", "description": " If the cardinality is positive, that means it is a finite type, so there is\nan equivalence between `\u03b1` and `fin (nat.card \u03b1)`. See also `finite.equiv_fin`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_eq_zero_of_infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card", "description": "`nat.card \u03b1` is the cardinality of `\u03b1` as a natural number.\n If `\u03b1` is infinite, `nat.card \u03b1 = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_of_is_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part_enat.card_plift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_eq_one_iff_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.lt_coe_nat_iff_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.coe_nat_le_to_part_enat_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_chain_complex_equivalence_functor_obj_X_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.counit_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.homological_complex.p_comm_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_chain_complex_equivalence_inverse_obj_X_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_cochain_complex_equivalence_counit_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_chain_complex_equivalence_inverse_obj_p_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_cochain_complex_equivalence_functor_obj_X_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_chain_complex_equivalence_functor_obj_X_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.homological_complex.category_theory.is_idempotent_complete", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_cochain_complex_equivalence_inverse_map_f_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_chain_complex_equivalence_inverse_map_f_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_chain_complex_equivalence_functor_obj_d_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_cochain_complex_equivalence", "description": "The equivalence `karoubi (cochain_complex C \u03b1) \u224c cochain_complex (karoubi C) \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_cochain_complex_equivalence_inverse_obj_X_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.functor.obj_d_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.homological_complex.p_idem_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_cochain_complex_equivalence_functor_map_f_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.inverse.map", "description": " The functor `homological_complex (karoubi C) c \u2964 karoubi (homological_complex C c)`,\non morphisms", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.inverse.obj_p_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.functor.map_f_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.homological_complex.comp_p_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.unit_iso_inv_app_f_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_cochain_complex_equivalence_inverse_obj_p_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.homological_complex.p_comm_f_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence", "description": "The equivalence `karoubi (homological_complex C c) \u224c homological_complex (karoubi C) c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_chain_complex_equivalence_functor_map_f_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.counit_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_chain_complex_equivalence", "description": "The equivalence `karoubi (chain_complex C \u03b1) \u224c chain_complex (karoubi C) \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.inverse.obj_X_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.inverse_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.functor", "description": "The functor `karoubi (homological_complex C c) \u2964 homological_complex (karoubi C) c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.counit_iso", "description": " The counit isomorphism of the equivalence\n`karoubi (homological_complex C c) \u224c homological_complex (karoubi C) c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_chain_complex_equivalence_counit_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.inverse.obj", "description": " The functor `homological_complex (karoubi C) c \u2964 karoubi (homological_complex C c)`,\non objects", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.inverse.obj_X_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.inverse_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.homological_complex.comp_p_d_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_cochain_complex_equivalence_inverse_obj_X_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.homological_complex.p_comp_d_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.unit_iso", "description": " The unit isomorphism of the equivalence\n`karoubi (homological_complex C c) \u224c homological_complex (karoubi C) c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_chain_complex_equivalence_unit_iso_hom_app_f_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_cochain_complex_equivalence_functor_obj_d_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.functor.map", "description": " The functor `karoubi (homological_complex C c) \u2964 homological_complex (karoubi C) c`,\non morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_chain_complex_equivalence_inverse_obj_X_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.homological_complex.p_comp_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_chain_complex_equivalence_counit_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_cochain_complex_equivalence_unit_iso_inv_app_f_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_cochain_complex_equivalence_unit_iso_hom_app_f_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.functor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.inverse.map_f_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.functor.obj_X_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.functor.obj", "description": " The functor `karoubi (homological_complex C c) \u2964 homological_complex (karoubi C) c`,\non objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_chain_complex_equivalence_unit_iso_inv_app_f_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.unit_iso_hom_app_f_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi.homological_complex.p_idem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.inverse", "description": "The functor `homological_complex (karoubi C) c \u2964 karoubi (homological_complex C c)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_cochain_complex_equivalence_functor_obj_X_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_cochain_complex_equivalence_counit_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_homological_complex_equivalence.functor.obj_X_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_dedekind_domain.ramification_idx_eq_normalized_factors_count", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient_to_quotient_range_pow_quot_succ", "description": "`S \u29f8 P` embeds into the quotient by `P^(i+1) \u29f8 P^e` as a subspace of `P^i \u29f8 P^e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.factors.finite_dimensional_quotient_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.ramification_idx", "description": " The ramification index of `P` over `p` is the largest exponent `n` such that\n`p` is contained in `P^n`.\n\nIn particular, if `p` is not contained in `P^n`, then the ramification index is 0.\n\nIf there is no largest such `n` (e.g. because `p = \u22a5`), then `ramification_idx` is\ndefined to be 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.factors.finrank_pow_ramification_idx", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.le_comap_of_ramification_idx_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient_to_quotient_range_pow_quot_succ_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.factors.finite_dimensional_quotient", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.factors.fact_ramification_idx_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.algebra_quotient_pow_ramification_idx", "description": " `R / p` has a canonical map to `S / (P ^ e)`, where `e` is the ramification index\nof `P` over `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.le_pow_of_le_ramification_idx", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.ramification_idx_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.factors.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_dedekind_domain.ramification_idx_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.rank_pow_quot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.ramification_idx_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.finrank_quotient_map", "description": " If `p` is a maximal ideal of `R`, and `S` is the integral closure of `R` in `L`,\nthen the dimension `[S/pS : R/p]` is equal to `[Frac(S) : Frac(R)]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient_to_quotient_range_pow_quot_succ_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.ramification_idx_of_not_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.factors.is_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.factors.ramification_idx_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.inertia_deg_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient_to_quotient_range_pow_quot_succ_aux", "description": " `S \u29f8 P` embeds into the quotient by `P^(i+1) \u29f8 P^e` as a subspace of `P^i \u29f8 P^e`.\nSee `quotient_to_quotient_range_pow_quot_succ` for this as a linear map,\nand `quotient_range_pow_quot_succ_inclusion_equiv` for this as a linear equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.algebra_map_quotient_of_ramification_idx_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.algebra_quotient_of_ramification_idx_ne_zero", "description": " If `P` lies over `p`, then `R / p` has a canonical map to `S / P`.\n\nThis can't be an instance since the map `f : R \u2192 S` is generally not inferrable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.ramification_idx_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient_to_quotient_range_pow_quot_succ_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.factors.inertia_deg_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.finrank_quotient_map.linear_independent_of_nontrivial", "description": " Let `V` be a vector space over `K = Frac(R)`, `S / R` a ring extension\nand `V'` a module over `S`. If `b`, in the intersection `V''` of `V` and `V'`,\nis linear independent over `S` in `V'`, then it is linear independent over `R` in `V`.\n\nThe statement we prove is actually slightly more general:\n * it suffices that the inclusion `algebra_map R S : R \u2192 S` is nontrivial\n * the function `f' : V'' \u2192 V'` doesn't need to be injective", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.rank_pow_quot_aux", "description": " Since the inclusion `(P^(i + 1) / P^e) \u2282 (P^i / P^e)` has a kernel isomorphic to `P / S`,\n`[P^i / P^e : R / p] = [P^(i+1) / P^e : R / p] + [P / S : R / p]`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.le_comap_pow_ramification_idx", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.finrank_prime_pow_ramification_idx", "description": " If `p` is a maximal ideal of `R`, `S` extends `R` and `P^e` lies over `p`,\nthen the dimension `[S/(P^e) : R/p]`, as a natural number, is equal to `e * [S/P : R/p]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.ramification_idx_eq_find", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.finrank_quotient_map.span_eq_top", "description": " If `b` mod `p` spans `S/p` as `R/p`-space, then `b` itself spans `Frac(S)` as `K`-space.\n\nHere,\n * `p` is an ideal of `R` such that `R / p` is nontrivial\n * `K` is a field that has an embedding of `R` (in particular we can take `K = Frac(R)`)\n * `L` is a field extension of `K`\n * `S` is the integral closure of `R` in `L`\n\nMore precisely, we avoid quotients in this statement and instead require that `b \u222a pS` spans `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient_range_pow_quot_succ_inclusion_equiv", "description": " Quotienting `P^i / P^e` by its subspace `P^(i+1) \u29f8 P^e` is\n`R \u29f8 p`-linearly isomorphic to `S \u29f8 P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.inertia_deg", "description": " The inertia degree of `P : ideal S` lying over `p : ideal R` is the degree of the\nextension `(S / P) : (R / p)`.\n\nWe do not assume `P` lies over `p` in the definition; we return `0` instead.\n\nSee `inertia_deg_algebra_map` for the common case where `f = algebra_map R S`\nand there is an algebra structure `R / p \u2192 S / P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.rank_prime_pow_ramification_idx", "description": " If `p` is a maximal ideal of `R`, `S` extends `R` and `P^e` lies over `p`,\nthen the dimension `[S/(P^e) : R/p]` is equal to `e * [S/P : R/p]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient_to_quotient_range_pow_quot_succ_aux_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.factors.pi_quotient_equiv_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.inertia_deg_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.factors.pi_quotient_equiv", "description": " **Chinese remainder theorem** for a ring of integers: if the prime ideal `p : ideal R`\nfactors in `S` as `\u220f i, P i ^ e i`, then `S \u29f8 I` factors as `\u03a0 i, R \u29f8 (P i ^ e i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.factors.ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.pow_quot_succ_inclusion", "description": "The inclusion `(P^(i + 1) / P^e) \u2282 (P^i / P^e)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.le_pow_ramification_idx", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.algebra_map_quotient_pow_ramification_idx", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.factors.pi_quotient_linear_equiv", "description": " **Chinese remainder theorem** for a ring of integers: if the prime ideal `p : ideal R`\nfactors in `S` as `\u220f i, P i ^ e i`,\nthen `S \u29f8 I` factors `R \u29f8 I`-linearly as `\u03a0 i, R \u29f8 (P i ^ e i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.sum_ramification_inertia", "description": " The **fundamental identity** of ramification index `e` and inertia degree `f`:\nfor `P` ranging over the primes lying over `p`, `\u2211 P, e P * f P = [Frac(S) : Frac(R)]`;\nhere `S` is a finite `R`-module (and thus `Frac(S) : Frac(R)` is a finite extension) and `p`\nis maximal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.pow_quot_succ_inclusion_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.ramification_idx_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_dedekind_domain.ramification_idx_eq_factors_count", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.ramification_idx_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.pow_quot_succ_inclusion_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.factors.pi_quotient_equiv_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.tmul_mul_tmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.comm_tmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.basis_aux_map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.product_map_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra.module", "description": " If `M` is a representation of two different `R`-algebras `A` and `B` whose actions commute,\nthen it is a representation the `R`-algebra `A \u2297[R] B`.\n\nAn important example arises from a semiring `S`; allowing `S` to act on itself via left and right\nmultiplication, the roles of `R`, `A`, `B`, `M` are played by `\u2115`, `S`, `S\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`, `S`. This example\nis important because a submodule of `S` as a `module` over `S \u2297[\u2115] S\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56` is a two-sided ideal.\n\nNB: This is not an instance because in the case `B = A` and `M = A \u2297[R] A` we would have a diamond\nof `smul` actions. Furthermore, this would not be a mere definitional diamond but a true\nmathematical diamond in which `A \u2297[R] A` had two distinct scalar actions on itself: one from its\nmultiplication, and one from this would-be instance. Arguably we could live with this but in any\ncase the real fix is to address the ambiguity in notation, probably along the lines outlined here:\nhttps://leanprover.zulipchat.com/#narrow/stream/144837-PR-reviews/topic/.234773.20base.20change/near/240929258", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.alg_hom_of_linear_map_tensor_product_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra_tensor_module.restrict_scalars_curry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.congr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.include_left_comp_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.base_change_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.comm", "description": "The tensor product of R-algebras is commutative, up to algebra isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra.module_aux", "description": " An auxiliary definition, used for constructing the `module (A \u2297[R] B) M` in\n`tensor_product.algebra.module` below.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra_tensor_module.uncurry", "description": " Heterobasic version of `tensor_product.uncurry`:\n\nLinearly constructing a linear map `M \u2297[R] N \u2192[A] P` given a bilinear map `M \u2192[A] N \u2192[R] P`\nwith the property that its composition with the canonical bilinear map `M \u2192[A] N \u2192[R] M \u2297[R] N` is\nthe given bilinear map `M \u2192[A] N \u2192[R] P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.base_change_tmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.map", "description": "The tensor product of a pair of algebra morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.base_change_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.smul_comm_class_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.basis_aux", "description": " Given a `k`-algebra `R` and a `k`-basis of `M,` this is a `k`-linear isomorphism\n`R \u2297[k] M \u2243 (\u03b9 \u2192\u2080 R)` (which is in fact `R`-linear).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.product_left_alg_hom", "description": " If `A`, `B` are `R`-algebras, `A'` is an `A`-algebra, then the product map of `f : A' \u2192\u2090[A] S`\nand `g : B \u2192\u2090[R] S` is an `A`-algebra homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra.module_aux_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.lmul'_apply_tmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.rid_tmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.one_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.mul_assoc'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.basis_aux_tmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.lmul'_comp_include_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.alg_equiv_of_linear_equiv_triple_tensor_product_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.product_left_alg_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.assoc_aux_2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.base_change", "description": "`base_change A f` for `f : M \u2192\u2097[R] N` is the `A`-linear map `A \u2297[R] M \u2192\u2097[A] A \u2297[R] N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.alg_equiv_of_linear_equiv_tensor_product_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.lmul'_comp_include_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.adjoin_tmul_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra_tensor_module.smul_eq_lsmul_rtensor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.right_algebra", "description": " `S \u2297[R] T` has a `T`-algebra structure. This is not a global instance or else the action of\n`S` on `S \u2297[R] S` would be ambiguous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.assoc_tmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.is_scalar_tower_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.map_tmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.map_comp_include_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.tensor_product.ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.lmul'_to_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.mul_aux_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.left_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.product_map_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra_tensor_module.curry_injective", "description": " Just as `tensor_product.ext` is marked `ext` instead of `tensor_product.ext'`, this is\na better `ext` lemma than `tensor_product.algebra_tensor_module.ext` below.\n\nSee note [partially-applied ext lemmas].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.base_change_hom", "description": "`base_change` as a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.base_change_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.algebra_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.tmul_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.mul", "description": "(Implementation detail)\nThe multiplication map on `A \u2297[R] B`,\nas an `R`-bilinear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra_tensor_module.lift", "description": " Heterobasic version of `tensor_product.lift`:\n\nConstructing a linear map `M \u2297[R] N \u2192[A] P` given a bilinear map `M \u2192[A] N \u2192[R] P` with the\nproperty that its composition with the canonical bilinear map `M \u2192[A] N \u2192[R] M \u2297[R] N` is\nthe given bilinear map `M \u2192[A] N \u2192[R] P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.base_change_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.finite_dimensional_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.map_comp_include_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.basis", "description": "Given a `k`-algebra `R`, this is the `R`-basis of `R \u2297[k] M` induced by a `k`-basis of `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.base_change_eq_ltensor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.lid", "description": "The base ring is a left identity for the tensor product of algebra, up to algebra isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.right_is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.product_map", "description": "If `S` is commutative, for a pair of morphisms `f : A \u2192\u2090[R] S`, `g : B \u2192\u2090[R] S`,\nWe obtain a map `A \u2297[R] B \u2192\u2090[R] S` that commutes with `f`, `g` via `a \u2297 b \u21a6 f(a) * g(b)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.mul_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.mul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.basis_repr_tmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra.smul_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.alg_equiv_of_linear_equiv_triple_tensor_product", "description": "Build an algebra equivalence from a linear equivalence out of a triple tensor product,\nand evidence of multiplicativity on pure tensors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.include_right_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End_tensor_End_alg_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.product_map_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra_tensor_module.uncurry_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.mul_aux", "description": "(Implementation detail)\nThe multiplication map on `A \u2297[R] B`,\nfor a fixed pure tensor in the first argument,\nas an `R`-linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.congr_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.assoc", "description": "The associator for tensor product of R-algebras, as an algebra isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.include_left", "description": "The `R`-algebra morphism `A \u2192\u2090[R] A \u2297[R] B` sending `a` to `a \u2297\u209c 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra_tensor_module.curry", "description": " Heterobasic version of `tensor_product.curry`:\n\nGiven a linear map `M \u2297[R] N \u2192[A] P`, compose it with the canonical\nbilinear map `M \u2192[A] N \u2192[R] M \u2297[R] N` to form a bilinear map `M \u2192[A] N \u2192[R] P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra_tensor_module.mk_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.map_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra_tensor_module.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End_tensor_End_alg_hom", "description": " The algebra homomorphism from `End M \u2297 End N` to `End (M \u2297 N)` sending `f \u2297\u209c g` to\nthe `tensor_product.map f g`, the tensor product of the two maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.tensor_product.algebra", "description": "The tensor product of two `R`-algebras is an `R`-algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.base_change_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra_tensor_module.curry_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra_tensor_module.lift_tmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.assoc_aux_1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.include_left_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra_tensor_module.lcurry_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.tensor_product.semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.product_map_left_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.product_map_apply_tmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra_tensor_module.lift_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.mul_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.tensor_product.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.lmul'", "description": "`linear_map.mul'` is an alg_hom on commutative rings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.basis_repr_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra_tensor_module.lift.equiv", "description": " Heterobasic version of `tensor_product.lift.equiv`:\n\nA linear equivalence constructing a linear map `M \u2297[R] N \u2192[A] P` given a\nbilinear map `M \u2192[A] N \u2192[R] P` with the property that its composition with the\ncanonical bilinear map `M \u2192[A] N \u2192[R] M \u2297[R] N` is the given bilinear map `M \u2192[A] N \u2192[R] P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.rid", "description": "The base ring is a right identity for the tensor product of algebra, up to algebra isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.include_left_ring_hom", "description": "The ring morphism `A \u2192+* A \u2297[R] B` sending `a` to `a \u2297\u209c 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.product_map_right_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra_tensor_module.assoc", "description": " Heterobasic version of `tensor_product.assoc`:\n\nLinear equivalence between `(M \u2297[A] N) \u2297[R] P` and `M \u2297[A] (N \u2297[R] P)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.alg_hom_of_linear_map_tensor_product", "description": "Build an algebra morphism from a linear map out of a tensor product,\nand evidence of multiplicativity on pure tensors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.one_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.include_right", "description": "The algebra morphism `B \u2192\u2090[R] A \u2297[R] B` sending `b` to `1 \u2297\u209c b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.include_left_ring_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.congr", "description": "Construct an isomorphism between tensor products of R-algebras\nfrom isomorphisms between the tensor factors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.alg_equiv_of_linear_equiv_tensor_product", "description": "Build an algebra equivalence from a linear equivalence out of a tensor product,\nand evidence of multiplicativity on pure tensors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.lid_tmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.tensor_product.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra_tensor_module.lcurry", "description": " Heterobasic version of `tensor_product.lcurry`:\n\nGiven a linear map `M \u2297[R] N \u2192[A] P`, compose it with the canonical\nbilinear map `M \u2192[A] N \u2192[R] M \u2297[R] N` to form a bilinear map `M \u2192[A] N \u2192[R] P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.base_change_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.algebra_tensor_module.mk", "description": " Heterobasic version of `tensor_product.mk`:\n\nThe canonical bilinear map `M \u2192[A] N \u2192[R] M \u2297[R] N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.tensor_product.tensor_product.add_monoid_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Twop.swap", "description": "Swaps the pointed elements of a two-pointed type. `two_pointing.swap` as a functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Pointed_to_Twop_fst", "description": "The functor from `Pointed` to `Twop` which adds a second point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Pointed_to_Twop_snd_comp_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Twop.swap_equiv_inverse_map_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Twop", "description": "The category of two-pointed types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Twop.X", "description": "The category of two-pointed types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Twop.to_two_pointing", "description": "The category of two-pointed types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Twop.to_Bipointed", "description": " Turns a two-pointed type into a bipointed type, by forgetting that the pointed elements are\ndistinct.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Twop.swap_equiv", "description": "The equivalence between `Twop` and itself induced by `prod.swap` both ways.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Twop.swap_equiv_functor_obj_to_two_pointing_to_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Twop.swap_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Twop.large_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Twop.has_coe_to_sort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Pointed_to_Twop_fst_comp_forget_to_Bipointed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Twop.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Twop_swap_comp_forget_to_Bipointed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Twop.swap_obj_to_two_pointing", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Pointed_to_Twop_fst_forget_comp_Bipointed_to_Pointed_fst_adjunction", "description": "Adding a second point is left adjoint to forgetting the second point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Pointed_to_Twop_snd_comp_forget_to_Bipointed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Twop.swap_equiv_counit_iso_hom_app_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Pointed_to_Twop_snd_map_to_fun", "des