": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_isometry_class.ediam_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_equiv.diam_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_equiv.map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_equiv.to_continuous_linear_equiv_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.comp_continuous_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_equiv.congr_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.to_continuous_linear_map_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.is_complete_image_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.map_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_isometry_class.ediam_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_equiv.preimage_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_equiv.injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_isometry_class.isometry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.ediam_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_equiv.coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_equiv.dist_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_equiv.symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_equiv.preimage_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.equiv_range_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_equiv.coe_of_linear_isometry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.to_linear_map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_equiv.map_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_equiv.coe_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_isometry_equiv_class", "description": " `semilinear_isometry_equiv_class F \u03c3 E E\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear\nisometric equivs `E \u2192 E\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_isometry_equiv_class F R E E\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_isometry_equiv_class.coe", "description": " `semilinear_isometry_equiv_class F \u03c3 E E\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear\nisometric equivs `E \u2192 E\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_isometry_equiv_class F R E E\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_isometry_equiv_class.inv", "description": " `semilinear_isometry_equiv_class F \u03c3 E E\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear\nisometric equivs `E \u2192 E\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_isometry_equiv_class F R E E\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_isometry_equiv_class.left_inv", "description": " `semilinear_isometry_equiv_class F \u03c3 E E\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear\nisometric equivs `E \u2192 E\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_isometry_equiv_class F R E E\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_isometry_equiv_class.right_inv", "description": " `semilinear_isometry_equiv_class F \u03c3 E E\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear\nisometric equivs `E \u2192 E\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_isometry_equiv_class F R E E\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_isometry_equiv_class.coe_injective'", "description": " `semilinear_isometry_equiv_class F \u03c3 E E\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear\nisometric equivs `E \u2192 E\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_isometry_equiv_class F R E E\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_isometry_equiv_class.map_add", "description": " `semilinear_isometry_equiv_class F \u03c3 E E\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear\nisometric equivs `E \u2192 E\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_isometry_equiv_class F R E E\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_isometry_equiv_class.map_smul\u209b\u2097", "description": " `semilinear_isometry_equiv_class F \u03c3 E E\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear\nisometric equivs `E \u2192 E\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_isometry_equiv_class F R E E\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_isometry_equiv_class.norm_map", "description": " `semilinear_isometry_equiv_class F \u03c3 E E\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear\nisometric equivs `E \u2192 E\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_isometry_equiv_class F R E E\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_equiv.surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_equiv.comp_continuous_on_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.map_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.norm_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_equiv.coe_to_linear_isometry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_equiv.continuous_linear_map.has_coe_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.is_complete_map_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_equiv.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_equiv.map_smul\u