ial object `X` consists of the datum of a sequence\nof objects `N`, a sequence of morphisms `\u03b9 : N n \u27f6 X _[n]` such that\nfor all `\u0394 : simplex_categoryh\u1d52\u1d56`, the canonical map `splitting.map X \u03b9 \u0394`\nis an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.map_is_iso'", "description": " A splitting of a simplicial object `X` consists of the datum of a sequence\nof objects `N`, a sequence of morphisms `\u03b9 : N n \u27f6 X _[n]` such that\nfor all `\u0394 : simplex_categoryh\u1d52\u1d56`, the canonical map `splitting.map X \u03b9 \u0394`\nis an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.index_set", "description": "The index set which appears in the definition of split simplicial objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.summand", "description": " Given a sequences of objects `N : \u2115 \u2192 C` in a category `C`, this is\na family of objects indexed by the elements `A : splitting.index_set \u0394`.\nThe `\u0394`-simplices of a split simplicial objects shall identify to the\ncoproduct of objects in such a family.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.map", "description": " The canonical morphism `coprod N \u0394 \u27f6 X.obj \u0394` attached to a sequence\nof objects `N` and a sequence of morphisms `N n \u27f6 X _[n]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.\u03b9_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.congr_F", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.index_set.eq_id_iff_len_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.\u03b9_summand_epi_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.congr_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.forget_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.index_set.pull", "description": "When `A : index_set \u0394` and `\u03b8 : \u0394 \u2192 \u0394'` is a morphism in `simplex_category\u1d52\u1d56`,\nan element in `index_set \u0394'` can be defined by using the epi-mono factorisation\nof `\u03b8.unop \u226b A.e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.id_F", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.index_set.mk", "description": "The element in `splitting.index_set \u0394` attached to an epimorphism `f : \u0394 \u27f6 \u0394'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.\u03c6", "description": " As it is stated in `splitting.hom_ext`, a morphism `f : X \u27f6 Y` from a split\nsimplicial object to any simplicial object is determined by its restrictions\n`s.\u03c6 f n : s.N n \u27f6 Y _[n]` to the distinguished summands in each degree `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.\u03b9_summand_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.index_set.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.index_set.id", "description": " The distinguished element in `splitting.index_set \u0394` which corresponds to the\nidentity of `\u0394`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.desc", "description": " The map `X.obj \u0394 \u27f6 Z` obtained by providing a family of morphisms on all the\nterms of decomposition given by a splitting `s : splitting X`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.\u03b9_coprod", "description": "The inclusion of a summand in the coproduct.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.iso", "description": "The isomorphism on simplices given by the axiom `splitting.map_is_iso'`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split", "description": " The category `simplicial_object.split C` is the category of simplicial objects\nin `C` equipped with a splitting, and morphisms are morphisms of simplicial objects\nwhich are compatible with the splittings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.X", "description": " The category `simplicial_object.split C` is the category of simplicial objects\nin `C` equipped with a splitting, and morphisms are morphisms of simplicial objects\nwhich are compatible with the splittings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.s", "description": " The category `simplicial_object.split C` is the category of simplicial objects\nin `C` equipped with a splitting, and morphisms are morphisms of simplicial objects\nwhich are compatible with the splittings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.\u03b9_summand_epi_naturality_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.\u03b9_summand_naturality_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.index_set.fac_pull", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.forget", "description": " The functor `simplicial_object.split C \u2964 simplicial_object C` which forgets\nthe splitting.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.mk'_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.nat_trans_\u03b9_summand", "description": " The inclusion of each summand in the coproduct decomposition of simplices\nin split simplicial objects is a natural transformation of functors\n`simplicial_object.split C \u2964 C`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.\u03b9_summand_naturality_symm_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.hom.comm_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.category_theory.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.hom_ext'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.eval_N_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.index_set.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.index_set.e", "description": "The epimorphism in `simplex_category` associated to `A : splitting.index_set \u0394`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.index_set.eq_id", "description": " The condition that an element `splitting.index_set \u0394` is the distinguished\nelement `splitting.index_set.id \u0394`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.index_set.e.category_theory.epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.nat_trans_\u03b9_summand_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.\u03b9_summand_comp_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.id_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.of_iso_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.index_set.fac_pull_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.\u03b9_summand", "description": " Via the isomorphism `s.iso \u0394`, this is the inclusion of a summand\nin the direct sum decomposition given by the splitting `s : splitting X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.index_set.mk_snd_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.index_set.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.index_set.epi_comp_snd_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.coprod", "description": "The coproduct of the family `summand N \u0394`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.hom", "description": " Morphisms in `simplicial_object.split C` are morphisms of simplicial objects that\nare compatible with the splittings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.hom.F", "description": " Morphisms in `simplicial_object.split C` are morphisms of simplicial objects that\nare compatible with the splittings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.hom.f", "description": " Morphisms in `simplicial_object.split C` are morphisms of simplicial objects that\nare compatible with the splittings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.hom.comm'", "description": " Morphisms in `simplicial_object.split C` are morphisms of simplicial objects that\nare compatible with the splittings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.index_set.ext'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.forget_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.comp_F", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.mk'", "description": " The object in `simplicial_object.split C` attached to a splitting `s : splitting X`\nof a simplicial object `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.hom.comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.\u03b9_summand_comp_app_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.splitting.index_set.eq_id_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.split.eval_N", "description": " The functor `simplicial_object.split C \u2964 C` which sends a simplicial object equipped\nwith a splitting to its nondegenerate `n`-simplices.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvqpf.fix.ind_rec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvqpf.W_setoid", "description": "Define the fixed point as the quotient of trees under the equivalence relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvqpf.Wequiv_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvqpf.fix.drec", "description": "Dependent recursor for `fix F`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvqpf.Wrepr_equiv", "description": 