n `\u2115` and `hp : \u2203 (n : \u2115), p n` is a proof that\nthere exists some natural number satisfying `p`, then `nat.find hp` is the\nsmallest natural number satisfying `p`. Note that `nat.find` is protected,\nmeaning that you can't just write `find`, even if the `nat` namespace is open.\n\nThe API for `nat.find` is:\n\n* `nat.find_spec` is the proof that `nat.find hp` satisfies `p`.\n* `nat.find_min` is the proof that if `m < nat.find hp` then `m` does not satisfy `p`.\n* `nat.find_min'` is the proof that if `m` does satisfy `p` then `nat.find hp \u2264 m`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.dvd_mod_iff", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.dvd_sub", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.dvd_add", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.add_le_add_iff_right", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.lt_succ_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.eq_one_of_dvd_one", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.iterate", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.case_strong_induction_on", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.le.intro", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.sub_self_add", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.discriminate", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.mul_lt_mul_of_pos_left", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.sub_one_sub_lt", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.mul_le_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.add_lt_add_right", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.le_add_right", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.dvd_of_mul_dvd_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.zero_min", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.succ_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.mul_mod_left", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.add_div_right", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.mul_lt_mul_of_pos_right", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"n