iverse as `M`) into which the indexing family injects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent.maximal", "description": "A linearly independent family is maximal if there is no strictly larger linearly independent family.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_monoid_hom", "description": "Dedekind's linear independence of characters", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_empty_type", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.linear_independent_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent.of_comp", "description": " If the image of a family of vectors under a linear map is linearly independent, then so is\nthe original family.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent", "description": "`linear_independent R v` states the family of vectors `v` is linearly independent over `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent.ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_Union_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent.subset_span_extend", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent.coe_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_fin_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_iff_not_smul_mem_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_subtype_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent.subset_extend", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent.to_subtype_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_iff''", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_in