ame": "category_theory.limits.image.eq_to_iso", "description": "An equation between morphisms gives an isomorphism between the images.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.of_iso_comp_m", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.ext", "description": " The morphism `m` in a factorisation `f = e \u226b m` through a monomorphism is uniquely\ndetermined.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.factor_thru_image_pre_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.lift_fac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_image_map.transport", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.comp_iso_inv_comp_image_\u03b9_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.map", "description": "The map on images induced by a commutative square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.iso_ext_hom_m", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_image_map_of_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.iso_ext", "description": " Two factorisations through monomorphisms satisfying the universal property\nmust factor through isomorphic objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.as_factor_thru_image", "description": "Rewrite in terms of the `factor_thru_image` interface.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_factorisation.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.lift_fac_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.fac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.eq_fac", "description": "As long as the category has equalizers,\nthe image inclusion maps commute with `image.eq_to_iso`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.e_iso_ext_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_map.map_\u03b9_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.strong_epi_factor_thru_image_of_strong_epi_mono_factorisation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.epi_image_of_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.strong_epi_mono_factorisation", "description": "A strong epi-mono factorisation is a decomposition `f = e \u226b m` with `e` a strong epimorphism\n   and `m` a monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.strong_epi_mono_factorisation.to_mono_factorisation", "description": "A strong epi-mono factorisation is a decomposition `f = e \u226b m` with `e` a strong epimorphism\n   and `m` a monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.strong_epi_mono_factorisation.e_strong_epi", "description": "A strong epi-mono factorisation is a decomposition `f = e \u226b m` with `e` a strong epimorphism\n   and `m` a monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.pre_comp_comp", "description": "The two step comparison map\n  `image (f \u226b (g \u226b h)) \u27f6 image (g \u226b h) \u27f6 image h`\nagrees with the one step comparison map\n  `image (f \u226b (g \u226b h)) \u2245 image ((f \u226b g) \u226b h) \u27f6 image h`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_map_comp", "description": "Image maps for composable commutative squares induce an image map in the composite square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.\u03b9.category_theory.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.comp_iso_hom_comp_image_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_image_map", "description": "`has_image_map sq` means that there is an `image_map` for the square `sq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_image_map.has_image_map", "description": "`has_image_map sq` means that there is an `image_map` for the square `sq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.im", "description": "The functor from the arrow category of `C` to `C` itself that maps a morphism to its image\n   and a commutative square to the induced morphism on images.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.of_iso_comp", "description": " A mono factorisation of `g \u226b f`, where `g` is an isomorphism,\ngives a mono factorisation of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_map", "description": "An image map is a morphism `image f \u2192 image g` fitting into a commutative square and satisfying\n   the obvious commutativity conditions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_map.map", "description": "An image map is a morphism `image f \u2192 image g` fitting into a commutative square and satisfying\n   the obvious commutativity conditions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_map.map_\u03b9'", "description": "An image map is a morphism `image f \u2192 image g` fitting into a commutative square and satisfying\n   the obvious commutativity conditions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.pre_comp_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_image_iso_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_image.mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.epi_of_epi_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.factor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.comp_mono", "description": "Any mono factorisation of `f` gives a mono factorisation of `f \u226b g` when `g` is a mono.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.comp_mono_e", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_image_map.mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.pre_comp", "description": "The comparison map `image (f \u226b g) \u27f6 image g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.of_comp_iso_e", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_map.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.comp_iso_hom_comp_image_\u03b9_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.eq_to_hom", "description": "An equation between morphisms gives a comparison map between the images\n(which momentarily we prove is an iso).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_image", "description": "`has_image f` means that there exists an image factorisation of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_image.exists_image", "description": "`has_image f` means that there exists an image factorisation of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_mono_iso_source_inv_\u03b9_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.lift_fac_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_image_comp_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.self_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.map_hom_mk'_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.iso_strong_epi_mono_hom_comp_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.of_comp_iso", "description": " A mono factorisation of `f \u226b g`, where `g` is an isomorphism,\ngives a mono factorisation of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.map_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.comp_iso_inv_comp_image_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_strong_epi_images_of_has_pullbacks_of_has_equalizers", "description": "If a category has images, equalizers and pullbacks, then images are automatically strong epi\n   images.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_has_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_factorisation.of_arrow_iso_is_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.lift_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.factor_thru_image", "description": "The map from the source to the image of a morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.iso_comp_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.comp_iso", "description": "Postcomposing by an isomorphism induces an isomorphism on the image.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.lift", "description": " Any other factorisation of the morphism `f` through a monomorphism receives a map from the\nimage.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.strong_epi_mono_factorisation.to_mono_is_image", "description": "A mono factorisation coming from a strong epi-mono factorisation always has the universal\n   property of the image.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.category_theory.category_struct.comp.has_image", "description": "If `has_image g`, then `has_image (f \u226b g)` when `f` is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.fac_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.of_arrow_iso_e", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.iso_comp_m", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.iso_comp", "description": "Any mono factorisation of `f` gives a mono factorisation of `g \u226b f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.of_arrow_iso_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.lift_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.factor_thru_image.category_theory.epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_map.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.strong_epi_of_strong_epi_mono_factorisation", "description": "If there is a single strong epi-mono factorisation of `f`, then every image factorisation is a\n   strong epi-mono factorisation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.comp_mono_m", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.iso_strong_epi_mono", "description": "If `C` has strong epi mono factorisations, then the image is unique up to isomorphism, in that if\n`f` factors as a strong epi followed by a mono, this factorisation is essentially the image\nfactorisation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.lift_\u03b9_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_map.factor_map_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.is_image", "description": " The witness of the universal property for the chosen factorisation of `f` through\na monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.of_iso_comp_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.iso_ext_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.e_iso_ext_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_image_maps_of_has_strong_epi_images", "description": "A category with strong epi images has image maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_map.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.strong_epi_mono_factorisation_inhabited", "description": "Satisfying the inhabited linter", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.fac_lift_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.fac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.fac_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_images_of_has_strong_epi_mono_factorisations", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_factorisation.of_arrow_iso", "description": " If `f` and `g` are isomorphic arrows, then an image factorisation of `f`\ngives an image factorisation of `g`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_factorisation", "description": "Data exhibiting that a morphism `f` has an image.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_factorisation.F", "description": "Data exhibiting that a morphism `f` has an image.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_factorisation.is_image", "description": "Data exhibiting that a morphism `f` has an image.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_image_maps", "description": "If a category `has_image_maps`, then all commutative squares induce morphisms on images.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_image_maps.has_image_map", "description": "If a category `has_image_maps`, then all commutative squares induce morphisms on images.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.of_iso_comp_e", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inhabited_image_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image", "description": "Data exhibiting that a given factorisation through a mono is initial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.lift", "description": "Data exhibiting that a given factorisation through a mono is initial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.lift_fac'", "description": "Data exhibiting that a given factorisation through a mono is initial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.pre_comp_epi_of_epi", "description": "`image.pre_comp f g` is an epimorphism when `f` is an epimorphism\n(we need `C` to have equalizers to prove this).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_mono_iso_source_inv_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_factorisation.of_arrow_iso_F", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.is_iso_precomp_iso", "description": "`image.pre_comp f g` is an isomorphism when `f` is an isomorphism\n(we need `C` to have equalizers to prove this).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.of_arrow_iso", "description": " If `f` and `g` are isomorphic arrows, then a mono factorisation of `f`\ngives a mono factorisation of `g`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_mono_iso_source_hom_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.iso_comp_e", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.fac_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_map_id", "description": "The identity `image f \u27f6 image f` fits into the commutative square represented by the identity\n   morphism `\ud835\udfd9 f` in the arrow category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.eq_to_hom.category_theory.is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.lift_fac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.im_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.pre_comp_mono", "description": "`image.pre_comp f g` is a monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.has_strong_epi_mono_factorisations_imp_of_is_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation", "description": "A factorisation of a morphism `f = e \u226b m`, with `m` monic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.I", "description": "A factorisation of a morphism `f = e \u226b m`, with `m` monic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.m", "description": "A factorisation of a morphism `f = e \u226b m`, with `m` monic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.m_mono", "description": "A factorisation of a morphism `f = e \u226b m`, with `m` monic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.e", "description": "A factorisation of a morphism `f = e \u226b m`, with `m` monic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.fac'", "description": "A factorisation of a morphism `f = e \u226b m`, with `m` monic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.fac_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_mono_iso_source_hom_self_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.self", "description": "The trivial factorisation of a monomorphism satisfies the universal property.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_image_map.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.pre_comp_\u03b9_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_images", "description": "`has_images` asserts that every morphism has an image.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_images.has_image", "description": "`has_images` asserts that every morphism has an image.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.of_arrow_iso", "description": " If `f` and `g` are isomorphic arrows, then a mono factorisation of `f` that is an image\ngives a mono factorisation of `g` that is an image", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image", "description": "The categorical image of a morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_image.uniq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.of_comp_iso_m", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.self", "description": "The obvious factorisation of a monomorphism through itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.\u03b9", "description": "The inclusion of the image of a morphism into the target.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_map.map_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.fac_lift_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.of_arrow_iso_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_map.factor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.im_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.hom.has_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.mono_factorisation", "description": "Some factorisation of `f` through a monomorphism (selected with choice).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_strong_epi_images_of_has_strong_epi_mono_factorisations", "description": "If we constructed our images from strong epi-mono factorisations, then these images are\n   strong epi images.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.iso_strong_epi_mono_inv_comp_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.of_comp_iso_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation.of_arrow_iso_m", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.iso_ext_inv_m", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_map.transport", "description": "To give an image map for a commutative square with `f` at the top and `g` at the bottom, it\n   suffices to give a map between any mono factorisation of `f` and any image factorisation of\n   `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_image.iso_ext_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_strong_epi_mono_factorisations", "description": "A category has strong epi-mono factorisations if every morphism admits a strong epi-mono\n   factorisation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_strong_epi_mono_factorisations.has_fac", "description": "A category has strong epi-mono factorisations if every morphism admits a strong epi-mono\n   factorisation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_strong_epi_mono_factorisations.mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay_iff_superpolynomial_decay_abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay.mul_param", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay.congr'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay.mul_param_zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay.param_inv_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay_mul_param_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay.param_zpow_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay_const_mul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay_iff_abs_tendsto_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay_iff_superpolynomial_decay_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay.polynomial_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay.trans_abs_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay.trans_eventually_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay_mul_const_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay", "description": "`f` has superpolynomial decay in parameter `k` along filter `l` if\n `k ^ n * f` tends to zero at `l` for all naturals `n`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay_iff_norm_tendsto_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay.param_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay_iff_is_o", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay.const_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay_iff_abs_is_bounded_under", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay_param_pow_mul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay_iff_is_O", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay_mul_param_pow_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay.mul_polynomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay_param_mul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay.mul_param_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay_iff_zpow_tendsto_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay.param_pow_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay.trans_eventually_abs_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay.congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay.mul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.superpolynomial_decay.inv_param_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.rename_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.map_rename", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.exists_finset_rename\u2082", "description": "`exists_finset_rename` for two polyonomials at once: for any two polynomials `p\u2081`, `p\u2082` in a\n polynomial semiring `R[\u03c3]` of possibly infinitely many variables, `exists_finset_rename\u2082` yields\n a finite subset `s` of `\u03c3` such that both `p\u2081` and `p\u2082` are contained in the polynomial semiring\n `R[s]` of finitely many variables.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.rename_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.eval\u2082_rename_prodmk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.rename_prodmk_eval\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.rename_equiv_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.aeval_rename", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.rename_monomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.kill_compl_comp_rename", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.eval\u2082_rename", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.rename_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.eval\u2082_hom_rename", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.exists_fin_rename", "description": "Every polynomial is a polynomial in finitely many variables.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.rename_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.eval_rename_prodmk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.coeff_rename_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.rename_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.exists_finset_rename", "description": "Every polynomial is a polynomial in finitely many variables.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.rename_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.constant_coeff_rename", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.kill_compl", "description": "Given a function between sets of variables `f : \u03c3 \u2192 \u03c4` that is injective with proof `hf`,\n `kill_compl hf` is the `alg_hom` from `R[\u03c4]` to `R[\u03c3]` that is left inverse to\n `rename f : R[\u03c3] \u2192 R[\u03c4]` and sends the variables in the complement of the range of `f` to `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.eval\u2082_cast_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.rename_eval\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.rename", "description": "Rename all the variables in a multivariable polynomial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.kill_compl_rename_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.rename_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.rename_equiv_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.coeff_rename_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.support_rename_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.rename_rename", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.coeff_rename_map_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.rename_equiv", "description": "`mv_polynomial.rename e` is an equivalence when `e` is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_colimits_of_monad_preserves", "description": "For `D : J \u2964 algebra T`, `D \u22d9 forget T` has a colimit, then `D` has a colimit provided colimits\nof shape `J` are preserved by `T`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_colimits.lifted_cocone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.has_limit_of_reflective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.left_adjoint_preserves_terminal_of_reflective", "description": "The reflector always preserves terminal objects. Note this in general doesn't apply to any other\nlimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monadic_creates_limits", "description": "Any monadic functor creates limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_limits.lifted_cone_is_limit_lift_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_limits.\u03b3", "description": "(Impl) The natural transformation used to define the new cone", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_limits.lifted_cone", "description": "(Impl) Construct the lifted cone in `algebra T` which will be limiting.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_limits.lifted_cone_\u03c0_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.has_colimits_of_reflective", "description": "If `C` has colimits then any reflective subcategory has colimits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_limits.new_cone", "description": "(Impl) This new cone is used to construct the algebra structure", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_limits.lifted_cone_is_limit", "description": "(Impl) Prove that the lifted cone is limiting.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_colimits.lifted_cocone_\u03b9_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_limits.cone_point", "description": "The algebra structure which will be the apex of the new limit cone for `D`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.has_limits_of_shape_of_reflective", "description": "If `C` has limits of shape `J` then any reflective subcategory has limits of shape `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_limits.\u03b3_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_limits.lifted_cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_limits.cone_point_a", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_colimits.new_cocone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_limits.new_cone_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_colimits.cocone_point", "description": "(Impl)\nConstruct the colimiting algebra from the map `\u03bb : TL \u27f6 L` given by `lambda`. We are required to\nshow it satisfies the two algebra laws, which follow from the algebra laws for the image of `D` and\nour `commuting` lemma.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comp_comparison_has_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_colimit", "description": "The forgetful functor from the Eilenberg-Moore category for a monad creates any colimit\nwhich the monad itself preserves.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_colimits.\u03b3_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_colimits.cocone_point_A", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.has_colimits_of_shape_of_reflective", "description": "If `C` has colimits of shape `J` then any reflective subcategory has colimits of shape `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monadic_creates_colimits_of_preserves_colimits", "description": "A monadic functor creates colimits if it preserves colimits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_limits", "description": "The forgetful functor from the Eilenberg-Moore category creates limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_colimits.lifted_cocone_is_colimit", "description": "(Impl) Prove that the lifted cocone is colimiting.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_colimits.lifted_cocone_is_colimit_desc_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_colimits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.has_limits_of_reflective", "description": "If `C` has limits then any reflective subcategory has limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_colimits.new_cocone_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comp_comparison_forget_has_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_colimits.new_cocone", "description": "(Impl)\nA cocone for the diagram `(D \u22d9 forget T) \u22d9 T` found by composing the natural transformation `\u03b3`\nwith the colimiting cocone for `D \u22d9 forget T`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_colimits.lambda", "description": "(Impl)\nDefine the map `\u03bb : TL \u27f6 L`, which will serve as the structure of the coalgebra on `L`, and\nwe will show is the colimiting object. We use the cocone constructed by `c` and the fact that\n`T` preserves colimits to produce this morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monadic_creates_colimit_of_preserves_colimit", "description": "The forgetful functor from the Eilenberg-Moore category for a monad creates any colimit\nwhich the monad itself preserves.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.has_limit_of_comp_forget_has_limit", "description": "`D \u22d9 forget T` has a limit, then `D` has a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_limits.cone_point_A", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_colimits.cocone_point_a", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monadic_creates_colimits_of_shape_of_preserves_colimits_of_shape", "description": "A monadic functor creates any colimits of shapes it preserves.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_colimits.lifted_cocone", "description": "(Impl) Construct the lifted cocone in `algebra T` which will be colimiting.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_colimits.commuting", "description": "(Impl) The key property defining the map `\u03bb : TL \u27f6 L`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget_creates_colimits.\u03b3", "description": "(Impl)\nThe natural transformation given by the algebra structure maps, used to construct a cocone `c` with\napex `colimit (D \u22d9 forget T)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.has_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.pair_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.order_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.seq_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.lintegral_eq_of_subset'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.map_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.lintegral_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.extend_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.map_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.mem_image_of_mem_range_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.lintegral_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.const_mul_lintegral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.has_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.has_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.piecewise_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.coe_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.range_const_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.pair", "description": " Combine two simple functions `f : \u03b1 \u2192\u209b \u03b2` and `g : \u03b1 \u2192\u209b \u03b2`\ninto `\u03bb a, (f a, g a)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.fin_meas_supp.lintegral_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.support_indicator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.sum_range_measure_preimage_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.simple_func_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.has_int_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.sup_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.neg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.restrict_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.lintegral_congr", "description": "If two simple functions are equal a.e., then their `lintegral`s are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.coe_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.order_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.range_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.add_eq_map\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.coe_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.comp", "description": "Composition of a `simple_fun` and a measurable function is a `simple_func`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.map_preimage_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.restrict_lintegral_eq_lintegral_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.sup_eq_map\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.zero_lintegral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.const_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.apply_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.bounded_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.fin_meas_supp.map\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.coe_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.map_lintegral", "description": "Calculate the integral of `(g \u2218 f)`, where `g : \u03b2 \u2192 \u211d\u22650\u221e` and `f : \u03b1 \u2192\u209b \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.mem_restrict_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.range_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.map_coe_ennreal_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func", "description": " A function `f` from a measurable space to any type is called *simple*,\nif every preimage `f \u207b\u00b9' {x}` is measurable, and the range is finite. This structure bundles\na function with these properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.to_fun", "description": " A function `f` from a measurable space to any type is called *simple*,\nif every preimage `f \u207b\u00b9' {x}` is measurable, and the range is finite. This structure bundles\na function with these properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.measurable_set_fiber'", "description": " A function `f` from a measurable space to any type is called *simple*,\nif every preimage `f \u207b\u00b9' {x}` is measurable, and the range is finite. This structure bundles\na function with these properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.finite_range'", "description": " A function `f` from a measurable space to any type is called *simple*,\nif every preimage `f \u207b\u00b9' {x}` is measurable, and the range is finite. This structure bundles\na function with these properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.range", "description": "Range of a simple function `\u03b1 \u2192\u209b \u03b2` as a `finset \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.div_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.const_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.preorder", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.const_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.forall_range_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.fin_meas_supp.of_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.coe_zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.seq", "description": " If `f` is a simple function taking values in `\u03b2 \u2192 \u03b3` and `g` is another simple function\nwith the same domain and codomain `\u03b2`, then `f.seq g = f a (g a)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.coe_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.coe_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.measurable_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.lintegral", "description": "Integral of a simple function whose codomain is `\u211d\u22650\u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.lintegral_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.piecewise_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.sum_measure_preimage_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.coe_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.support_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.approx", "description": " Fix a sequence `i : \u2115 \u2192 \u03b2`. Given a function `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2`, its `n`-th approximation\nby simple functions is defined so that in case `\u03b2 = \u211d\u22650\u221e` it sends each `a` to the supremum\nof the set `{i k | k \u2264 n \u2227 i k \u2264 f a}`, see `approx_apply` and `supr_approx_apply` for details.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable.ennreal_induction", "description": " To prove something for an arbitrary measurable function into `\u211d\u22650\u221e`, it suffices to show\nthat the property holds for (multiples of) characteristic functions and is closed under addition\nand supremum of increasing sequences of functions.\n\nIt is possible to make the hypotheses in the induction steps a bit stronger, and such conditions\ncan be added once we need them (for example in `h_add` it is only necessary to consider the sum of\na simple function with a multiple of a characteristic function and that the intersection\nof their images is a subset of `{0}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.monotone_approx", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.exists_range_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.eapprox", "description": "Approximate a function `\u03b1 \u2192 \u211d\u22650\u221e` by a sequence of simple functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.piecewise", "description": "If-then-else as a `simple_func`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.fin_meas_supp.pair", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.le_sup_lintegral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.supr_approx_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.finite_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.smul_eq_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.add_lintegral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.fin_meas_supp.iff_lintegral_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.const_lintegral_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.coe_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.has_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.coe_piecewise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.eapprox_diff", "description": " Approximate a function `\u03b1 \u2192 \u211d\u22650\u221e` by a series of simple functions taking their values\nin `\u211d\u22650`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.map", "description": "Given a function `g : \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b3` and a simple function `f : \u03b1 \u2192\u209b \u03b2`, `f.map g` return the simple\n   function `g \u2218 f : \u03b1 \u2192\u209b \u03b3`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.lintegral_map'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.bind_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.restrict_const_lintegral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.coe_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.mem_range_of_measure_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.const_mul_eq_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.pair_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.semilattice_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.fin_meas_supp.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.restrict", "description": " Restrict a simple function `f : \u03b1 \u2192\u209b \u03b2` to a set `s`. If `s` is measurable,\nthen `f.restrict s a = if a \u2208 s then f a else 0`, otherwise `f.restrict s = const \u03b1 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.zpow_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.has_nat_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.restrict_lintegral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.eapprox_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.ae_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.restrict_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.lintegral_eq_of_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.restrict_of_not_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.fin_meas_supp.meas_preimage_singleton_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.coe_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.lintegral_eq_of_measure_preimage", "description": "`simple_func.lintegral` depends only on the measures of `f \u207b\u00b9' {y}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.coe_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.fin_meas_supp", "description": " A `simple_func` has finite measure support if it is equal to `0` outside of a set of finite\nmeasure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.lintegral_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.extend_comp_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.approx_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.range_indicator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.sub_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.induction", "description": " To prove something for an arbitrary simple function, it suffices to show\nthat the property holds for (multiples of) characteristic functions and is closed under\naddition (of functions with disjoint support).\n\nIt is possible to make the hypotheses in `h_add` a bit stronger, and such conditions can be added\nonce we need them (for example it is only necessary to consider the case where `g` is a multiple\nof a characteristic function, and that this multiple doesn't appear in the image of `f`)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.range_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.monotone_eapprox", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.approx_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.mem_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.measurable_set_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.extend", "description": " Extend a `simple_func` along a measurable embedding: `f\u2081.extend g hg f\u2082` is the function\n`F : \u03b2 \u2192\u209b \u03b3` such that `F \u2218 g = f\u2081` and `F y = f\u2082 y` whenever `y \u2209 range g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.simple_func_bot'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.restrict_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.finset_sup_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.coe_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.fin_meas_supp.of_lintegral_ne_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.fin_meas_supp_iff_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.of_is_empty", "description": "Simple function defined on the empty type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.pow_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.semilattice_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.piecewise_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.fin_meas_supp.map_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.preimage_eq_empty_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.add_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.sum_eapprox_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.supr_eapprox_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.lintegral_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.bind_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"na