on": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "elemental_star_algebra.star_self_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "elemental_star_algebra.comm_semiring", "description": "The `elemental_star_algebra` generated by a normal element is commutative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "elemental_star_algebra.closed_embedding_coe", "description": "The coercion from an elemental algebra to the full algebra as a `closed_embedding`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "elemental_star_algebra.le_of_is_closed_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_alg_hom.ext_topological_closure", "description": " Continuous `star_alg_hom`s from the the topological closure of a `star_subalgebra` whose\ncompositions with the `star_subalgebra.inclusion` map agree are, in fact, equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.topological_closure", "description": "The closure of a star subalgebra in a topological star algebra as a star subalgebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.comm_semiring_topological_closure", "description": " If a star subalgebra of a topological star algebra is commutative, then so is its topological\nclosure. See note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.has_continuous_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_alg_hom_class.ext_topological_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.closed_embedding_inclusion", "description": "The `star_subalgebra.inclusion` of a closed star subalgebra is a `closed_embedding`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "elemental_star_algebra.is_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.topological_closure_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.topological_closure_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.le_topological_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "elemental_star_algebra.complete_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.topological_closure_minimal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.topological_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.comm_ring_topological_closure", "description": " If a star subalgebra of a topological star algebra is commutative, then so is its topological\nclosure. See note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "elemental_star_algebra", "description": "The topological closure of the subalgebra generated by a single element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "elemental_star_algebra.comm_ring", "description": "The `elemental_star_algebra` generated by a normal element is commutative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "elemental_star_algebra.self_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.is_closed_topological_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.category_theory.forget.category_theory.is_right_adjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Free.ext", "description": "Two `R`-linear functors out of the `R`-linear completion are isomorphic iff their\ncompositions with the embedding functor are isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.free.\u03b5", "description": "(Implementation detail) The unitor for `free R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Free.single_comp_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Free.lift_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Free.lift", "description": "A functor to an `R`-linear category lifts to a functor from its `R`-linear completion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.free.obj.category_theory.lax_monoidal_\u03b5", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Free.lift_linear", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Free.category_theory.linear", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.free.\u03bc", "description": "(Implementation detail) The tensorator for `free R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.free.obj.category_theory.lax_monoidal_\u03bc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.free.\u03b5_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.free.left_unitality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.monoidal_free", "description": "The free functor `Type u \u2964 Module R`, as a monoidal functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Free.lift_unique", "description": "`Free.lift` is unique amongst `R`-linear functors `Free R C \u2964 D`\nwhich compose with `embedding \u2124 C` to give the original functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.free.\u03bc_natural", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Free.lift_additive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.free", "description": "The free functor `Type u \u2964 Module R` sending a type `X` to the\nfree `R`-module with generators `x : X`, implemented as the type `X \u2192\u2080 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Free.embedding", "description": "A category embeds into its `R`-linear completion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Free.lift_map_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.free.right_unitality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.free.associativity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Free.embedding_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Free.category_theory.preadditive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.free_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Free", "description": "`Free R C` is a type synonym for `C`, which, given `[comm_ring R]` and `[category C]`,\nwe will equip with a category structure where the morphisms are formal `R`-linear combinations\nof the morphisms in `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.adj", "description": "The free-forgetful adjunction for R-modules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Free.of", "description": "Consider an object of `C` as an object of the `R`-linear completion.\n\nIt may be preferable to use `(Free.embedding R C).obj X` instead;\nthis functor can also be used to lift morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Free.lift_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.free.category_theory.lax_monoidal.\u03b5.category_theory.is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.free_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.free.obj.category_theory.lax_monoidal", "description": "The free R-module functor is lax monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Free.embedding_lift_iso", "description": "The embedding into the `R`-linear completion, followed by the lift,\nis isomorphic to the original functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Free.embedding_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.category_Free", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.comp_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.comp_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.equiv_polynomial", "description": "`polynomial_module R S` is isomorphic to `S[X]` as an `R` module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.map_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.is_scalar_tower'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.eval", "description": "Evaulate a polynomial `p : polynomial_module R M` at `r : R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.monomial_smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.smul_single_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.eval_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.single_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.lsingle_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.monomial_smul_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.eval_map'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.single", "description": " The monomial `m * x ^ i`. This is defeq to `finsupp.single_add_hom`, and is redefined here\nso that it has the desired type signature.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.eval_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.single_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.comp_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.map", "description": "The image of a polynomial under a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.eval_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.eval_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module", "description": "The `R[X]`-module `M[X]` for an `R`-module `M`.\nThis is isomorphic (as an `R`-module) to `M[X]` when `M` is a ring.\n\nWe require all the module instances `module S (polynomial_module R M)` to factor through `R` except\n`module R[X] (polynomial_module R M)`.\nIn this constraint, we have the following instances for example :\n- `R` acts on `polynomial_module R R[X]`\n- `R[X]` acts on `polynomial_module R R[X]` as `R[Y]` acting on `R[X][Y]`\n- `R` acts on `polynomial_module R[X] R[X]`\n- `R[X]` acts on `polynomial_module R[X] R[X]` as `R[X]` acting on `R[X][Y]`\n- `R[X][X]` acts on `polynomial_module R[X] R[X]` as `R[X][Y]` acting on itself\n\nThis is also the reason why `R` is included in the alias, or else there will be two different\ninstances of `module R[X] (polynomial_module R[X])`.\n\nSee https://leanprover.zulipchat.com/#narrow/stream/144837-PR-reviews/topic/.2315065.20polynomial.20modules\nfor the full discussion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.comp", "description": "`comp p q` is the composition of `p : R[X]` and `q : M[X]` as `q(p(x))`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.polynomial_module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.induction_linear", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.module", "description": "This is required to have the `is_scalar_tower S R M` instance to avoid diamonds.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.equiv_polynomial_self", "description": "`polynomial_module R R` is isomorphic to `R[X]` as an `R[X]` module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.lsingle", "description": "`polynomial_module.single` as a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial_module.eval_lsingle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.ord_proj_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.eq_iff_prime_padic_val_nat_eq", "description": "Two positive naturals are equal if their prime padic valuations are equal", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_lt", "description": "A crude upper bound on `n.factorization p`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_le_factorization_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prime.factorization", "description": "The only prime factor of prime `p` is `p` itself, with multiplicity `1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factor_iff_mem_factorization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_eq_zero_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.ord_proj_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.eq_factorization_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prime.factorization_pow", "description": "For prime `p` the only prime factor of `p^k` is `p` with multiplicity `k`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Icc_factorization_eq_pow_dvd", "description": " The set of positive powers of prime `p` that divide `n` is exactly the set of\npositive natural numbers up to `n.factorization p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.rec_on_prime_coprime", "description": " Given `P 0`, `P (p ^ n)` for all prime powers, and a way to extend `P a` and `P b` to\n`P (a * b)` when `a, b` are positive coprime, we can define `P` for all natural numbers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.ord_compl_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.ord_compl_dvd_ord_compl_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_eq_zero_of_non_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prod_factorization_eq_prod_factors", "description": " If a product over `n.factorization` doesn't use the multiplicities of the prime factors\nthen it's equal to the corresponding product over `n.factors.to_finset`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_multiples", "description": "Exactly `n / p` naturals in `[1, n]` are multiples of `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prime.dvd_iff_one_le_factorization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.set_of_pow_dvd_eq_Icc_factorization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.ord_proj_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.exists_eq_pow_mul_and_not_dvd", "description": " If `n` is a nonzero natural number and `p \u2260 1`, then there are natural numbers `e`\nand `n'` such that `n'` is not divisible by `p` and `n = p^e * n'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_le_factorization_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.eq_pow_of_factorization_eq_single", "description": "If the factorization of `n` contains just one number `p` then `n` is a power of `p`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_gcd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_eq_zero_iff_remainder", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_mul_apply_of_coprime", "description": "For coprime `a` and `b`, the power of `p` in `a * b` is the sum of the powers in `a` and `b`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prime.factorization_self", "description": "The multiplicity of prime `p` in `p` is `1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_eq_factors_multiset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_eq_card_pow_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_mul_support_of_coprime", "description": "For coprime `a` and `b` the prime factorization `a * b` is the union of those of `a` and `b`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prod_prime_factors_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prime_of_mem_factorization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prod_pow_prime_padic_val_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_mul", "description": "For nonzero `a` and `b`, the power of `p` in `a * b` is the sum of the powers in `a` and `b`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.dvd_ord_proj_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prime.pow_dvd_iff_le_factorization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.dvd_of_factorization_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_mul_of_coprime", "description": "For coprime `a` and `b`, the power of `p` in `a * b` is the sum of the powers in `a` and `b`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.ord_compl_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prime.factorization_pos_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.multiplicative_factorization", "description": " For any multiplicative function `f` with `f 1 = 1` and any `n \u2260 0`,\nwe can evaluate `f n` by evaluating `f` at `p ^ k` over the factorization of `n`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_eq_zero_of_remainder", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.rec_on_prime_pow", "description": " Given `P 0, P 1` and a way to extend `P a` to `P (p ^ n * a)` for prime `p` not dividing `a`,\nwe can define `P` for all natural numbers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.coprime_ord_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.le_of_mem_factorization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.ord_proj_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_ord_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.ord_compl_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_equiv_inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_eq_zero_of_not_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.ord_proj_of_not_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factors_count_eq", "description": " We can write both `n.factorization p` and `n.factors.count p` to represent the power\nof `p` in the factorization of `n`: we declare the former to be the simp-normal form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prod_pow_factorization_eq_self", "description": " Any finsupp `f : \u2115 \u2192\u2080 \u2115` whose support is in the primes is equal to the factorization of\nthe product `\u220f (a : \u2115) in f.support, a ^ f a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.rec_on_mul", "description": " Given `P 0`, `P 1`, `P p` for all primes, and a way to extend `P a` and `P b` to\n`P (a * b)`, we can define `P` for all natural numbers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Ico_filter_pow_dvd_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_prod", "description": " For any `p : \u2115` and any function `g : \u03b1 \u2192 \u2115` that's non-zero on `S : finset \u03b1`,\nthe power of `p` in `S.prod g` equals the sum over `x \u2208 S` of the powers of `p` in `g x`.\nGeneralises `factorization_mul`, which is the special case where `S.card = 2` and `g = id`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_prod_pow_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.ord_compl_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.dvd_iff_prime_pow_dvd_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_disjoint_of_coprime", "description": "The prime factorizations of coprime `a` and `b` are disjoint", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization", "description": "`n.factorization` is the finitely supported function `\u2115 \u2192\u2080 \u2115`\nmapping each prime factor of `n` to its multiplicity in `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_equiv", "description": "The equiv between `\u2115+` and `\u2115 \u2192\u2080 \u2115` with support in the primes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_pow", "description": "For any `p`, the power of `p` in `n^k` is `k` times the power in `n`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.support_factorization", "description": "The support of `n.factorization` is exactly `n.factors.to_finset`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.rec_on_pos_prime_pos_coprime", "description": " Given `P 0`, `P 1`, and `P (p ^ n)` for positive prime powers, and a way to extend `P a` and\n`P b` to `P (a * b)` when `a, b` are positive coprime, we can define `P` for all natural numbers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_lcm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.dvd_ord_compl_of_dvd_not_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_eq_zero_iff'", "description": "The only numbers with empty prime factorization are `0` and `1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.sum_factors_gcd_add_sum_factors_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.multiplicity_eq_factorization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_le_iff_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pos_of_mem_factorization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.ord_proj_dvd_ord_proj_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.ord_compl_of_not_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.ord_proj_mul_ord_compl_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.exists_factorization_lt_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prod_factors_gcd_mul_prod_factors_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.dvd_of_mem_factorization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.multiplicative_factorization'", "description": " For any multiplicative function `f` with `f 1 = 1` and `f 0 = 1`,\nwe can evaluate `f n` by evaluating `f` at `p ^ k` over the factorization of `n`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_mul_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.ord_proj_dvd_ord_proj_iff_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.not_dvd_ord_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prime.eq_of_factorization_pos", "description": "The only prime factor of prime `p` is `p` itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Ioc_filter_dvd_card_eq_div", "description": "Exactly `n / p` naturals in `(0, n]` are multiples of `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_one_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.eq_of_factorization_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_prime_le_iff_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.ord_compl_dvd_ord_compl_iff_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prime.pow_dvd_iff_dvd_ord_proj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.dvd_iff_div_factorization_eq_tsub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_eq_of_coprime_right", "description": " If `p` is a prime factor of `b` then the power of `p` in `b` is the same that in `a * b`,\nfor any `a` coprime to `b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_succ_factorization_not_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_le_of_le_pow", "description": "An upper bound on `n.factorization p`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_inj", "description": "Every nonzero natural number has a unique prime factorization", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_eq_of_coprime_left", "description": " If `p` is a prime factor of `a` then the power of `p` in `a` is the same that in `a * b`,\nfor any `b` coprime to `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.factorization_zero_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_inv_pair.symm", "description": "Swap the direction of a `ring_hom_inv_pair`. This is not an instance as it would loop, and better\ninstances are often available and may often be preferrable to using this one. Indeed, this\ndeclaration is not currently used in mathlib.\n\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_inv_pair.triples", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_comp_triple.right_ids", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_surjective.ids", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.is_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_inv_pair.comp_apply_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_inv_pair.triples\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_inv_pair.of_ring_equiv", "description": "Construct a `ring_hom_inv_pair` from both directions of a ring equiv.\n\nThis is not an instance, as for equivalences that are involutions, a better instance\nwould be `ring_hom_inv_pair e e`. Indeed, this declaration is not currently used in mathlib.\n\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_inv_pair", "description": " Class that expresses the fact that two ring homomorphisms are inverses of each other. This is\nused to handle `symm` for semilinear equivalences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_inv_pair.comp_eq", "description": " Class that expresses the fact that two ring homomorphisms are inverses of each other. This is\nused to handle `symm` for semilinear equivalences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_inv_pair.comp_eq\u2082", "description": " Class that expresses the fact that two ring homomorphisms are inverses of each other. This is\nused to handle `symm` for semilinear equivalences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_comp_triple", "description": " Class that expresses the fact that three ring homomorphisms form a composition triple. This is\nused to handle composition of semilinear maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_comp_triple.comp_eq", "description": " Class that expresses the fact that three ring homomorphisms form a composition triple. This is\nused to handle composition of semilinear maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_comp_triple.ids", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_inv_pair.ids", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_surjective.inv_pair", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_inv_pair.comp_apply_eq\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_surjective.comp", "description": "This cannot be an instance as there is no way to infer `\u03c3\u2081\u2082` and `\u03c3\u2082\u2083`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_surjective", "description": " Class expressing the fact that a `ring_hom` is surjective. This is needed in the context\nof semilinear maps, where some lemmas require this.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_surjective.is_surjective", "description": " Class expressing the fact that a `ring_hom` is surjective. This is needed in the context\nof semilinear maps, where some lemmas require this.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom_comp_triple.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.neg", "description": "When the `add_group` is commutative, `equiv.neg` is an `add_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.add_right_bijective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.div_left_eq_inv_trans_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sub_left", "description": "A version of `equiv.add_left a (-b)` that is defeq to `a - b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.mul_left", "description": "Left multiplication by a unit of a monoid is a permutation of the underlying type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.map_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.mul_right_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.neg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.mul_left_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group.mul_left_bijective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.add_left", "description": "Left addition in an `add_group` is a permutation of the underlying type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.add_right_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_units.add_left_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_units", "description": "A group is isomorphic to its group of units.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_add_units", "description": "An additive group is isomorphic to its group of additive units", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.div_right_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.coe_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.map_equiv", "description": " A multiplicative equivalence of monoids defines a multiplicative equivalence\nof their groups of units.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.div_left_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.mul_righ