"linear_map.coe_proj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.fun_unique_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.vec_empty", "description": "The linear map defeq to `matrix.vec_empty`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.pi_option_equiv_prod", "description": "This is `equiv.pi_option_equiv_prod` as a `linear_equiv`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.fin_two_arrow", "description": "Linear equivalence between vectors in `M\u00b2 = fin 2 \u2192 M` and `M \u00d7 M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.sum_arrow_lequiv_prod_arrow_apply_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.proj_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.diag", "description": "`diag i j` is the identity map if `i = j`. Otherwise it is the constant 0 map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.vec_empty\u2082_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.comp_left_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.vec_cons_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.infi_ker_proj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.pi_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.pi_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.fun_unique", "description": "If `\u03b9` has a unique element, then `\u03b9 \u2192 M` is linearly equivalent to `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.pi_fin_two_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.Pi_congr_left'", "description": " Transport dependent functions through an equivalence of the base space.\n\nThis is `equiv.Pi_congr_left'` as a `linear_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.comp_left", "description": " Linear map between the function spaces `I \u2192 M\u2082` and `I \u2192 M\u2083`, induced by a linear map `f`\nbetween `M\u2082` and `M\u2083`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.vec_cons\u2082_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.infi_ker_proj_equiv", "description": " If `I` and `J` are disjoint index sets, the product of the kernels of the `J`th projections of\n`\u03c6` is linearly equivalent to the product over `I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.pi_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.pi", "description": " `pi` construction for linear functions. From a family of linear functions it produces a linear\nfunction into a family of modules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.binfi_comap_proj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.extend_by_zero.linear_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.single", "description": "The `linear_map` version of `add_monoid_hom.single` and `pi.single`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.lsum_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.vec_cons", "description": " A linear map into `fin n.succ \u2192 M\u2083` can be built out of a map into `M\u2083` and a map into\n`fin n \u2192 M\u2083`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.proj", "description": " The projections from a family of modules are linear maps.\n\nNote:  known here as `linear_map.proj`, this construction is in other categories called `eval`, for\nexample `pi.eval_monoid_hom`, `pi.eval_ring_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.pi_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.Pi_congr_left'_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.Pi_congr_right", "description": " Combine a family of linear equivalences into a linear equivalence of `pi`-types.\n\nThis is `equiv.Pi_congr_right` as a `linear_equiv`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.pi_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.sum_arrow_lequiv_prod_arrow", "description": "`equiv.sum_arrow_equiv_prod_arrow` as a linear equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.lsum", "description": " The linear equivalence between linear functions on a finite product of modules and\nfamilies of functions on these modules. See note [bundled maps over different rings].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.vec_empty_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.Pi_congr_left'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.pi_ring_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.pi_ext'", "description": " This is used as the ext lemma instead of `linear_map.pi_ext` for reasons explained in\nnote [partially-applied ext lemmas].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.vec_cons\u2082", "description": " A bilinear map into `fin n.succ \u2192 M\u2083` can be built out of a map into `M\u2083` and a map into\n`fin n \u2192 M\u2083`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.Pi_congr_right_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.pi_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.sum_arrow_lequiv_prod_arrow_symm_apply_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.vec_empty\u2082", "description": "The empty bilinear map defeq to `matrix.vec_empty`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.update_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.pi_ring", "description": " Linear equivalence between linear functions `R\u207f \u2192 M` and `M\u207f`. The spaces `R\u207f` and `M\u207f`\nare represented as `\u03b9 \u2192 R` and `\u03b9 \u2192 M`, respectively, where `\u03b9` is a finite type.\n\nThis as an `S`-linear equivalence, under the assumption that `S` acts on `M` commuting with `R`.\nWhen `R` is commutative, we can take this to be the usual action with `S = R`.\nOtherwise, `S = \u2115` shows that the equivalence is additive.\nSee note [bundled maps over different rings].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.pi_fin_two", "description": "Linear equivalence between dependent functions `\u03a0 i : fin 2, M i` and `M 0 \u00d7 M 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.sum_arrow_lequiv_prod_arrow_symm_apply_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.pi_ext'_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.apply_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.Pi_congr_right_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.fin_two_arrow_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.infi_comap_proj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.pi", "description": " A version of `set.pi` for submodules. Given an index set `I` and a family of submodules\n`p : \u03a0 i, submodule R (\u03c6 i)`, `pi I s` is the submodule of dependent functions `f : \u03a0 i, \u03c6 i`\nsuch that `f i` belongs to `p a` whenever `i \u2208 I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.supr_map_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.pi_ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.fun_unique_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.le_comap_single_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.lsum_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.pi_fin_two_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.pi_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coe_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ker_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.Pi_congr_right_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.lsum_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.pi_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.fin_two_arrow_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.coe_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.Pi_congr_left", "description": " Transporting dependent functions through an equi