ilter extending the inf of a comapped ultrafilter and a principal ultrafilter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.comap_inf_principal_ne_bot_of_image_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.comap", "description": " The pullback of an ultrafilter along an injection whose range is large with respect to the given\nultrafilter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.inf_ne_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.le_of_inf_ne_bot'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.nonempty_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.hyperfilter", "description": "The ultrafilter extending the cofinite filter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.frequently.eventually", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `ultrafilter.frequently_iff_eventually`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.exists_ultrafilter_le", "description": "**Alias** of `ultrafilter.exists_le`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.coe_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.lt_pure_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.Iic_pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.of_compl_not_mem_iff", "description": " If `s\u1d9c \u2209 f \u2194 s \u2208 f`, then `f` is an ultrafilter. The other implication is given by\n`ultrafilter.compl_not_mem_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.supr_ultrafilter_le_eq", "description": "A filter equals the intersection of all the ultrafilters which contain it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_dom_congr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_coprod.summand", "description": "summand used in `alternating_map.dom_coprod`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_dom_congr", "description": " Transfer the arguments to a map along an equivalence between argument indices.\n\nThis is the alternating version of `multilinear_map.dom_dom_congr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coe_comp_alternating_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_dom_congr_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_vec_cons_smul", "description": "A version of `multilinear_map.cons_smul` for `alternating_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.coe_multilinear_map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.const_of_is_empty", "description": "The constant map is alternating when `\u03b9` is empty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.to_multilinear_map_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_lcongr_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.pi_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.coe_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.is_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_dom_lcongr", "description": "`alternating_map.dom_dom_congr` as a linear equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.mod_sum_congr.swap_smul_involutive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_linear_dependent", "description": "If the arguments are linearly dependent then the result is `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.coe_fn_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_dom_congr_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.coe_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_add_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_eq_zero_of_not_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.of_subsingleton_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.coe_smul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_coprod'", "description": " A more bundled version of `alternating_map.dom_coprod` that maps\n`((\u03b9\u2081 \u2192 N) \u2192 N\u2081) \u2297 ((\u03b9\u2082 \u2192 N) \u2192 N\u2082)` to `(\u03b9\u2081 \u2295 \u03b9\u2082 \u2192 N) \u2192 N\u2081 \u2297 N\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_perm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_lcongr", "description": "Construct a linear equivalence between maps from a linear equivalence between domains.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.curry_left_same", "description": "Currying with the same element twice gives the zero map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_update_update", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multilinear_map.alternatization", "description": " Produce an `alternating_map` out of a `multilinear_map`, by summing over all argument\npermutations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.comp_linear_map_assoc", "description": " Composing an alternating map twice with the same linear map in each argument is\nthe same as composing with their composition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multilinear_map.alternatization_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.add_comp_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_dom_congr_eq_iff", "description": "The results of applying `dom_dom_congr` to two maps are equal if and only if those maps are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.comp_linear_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multilinear_map.alternatization_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_update_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multilinear_map.dom_coprod_alternization_eq", "description": " Taking the `multilinear_map.alternatization` of the `multilinear_map.dom_coprod` of two\n`alternating_map`s gives a scaled version of the `alternating_map.coprod` of those maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.const_of_is_empty_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.smul_right_eq_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_coprod", "description": " Like `multilinear_map.dom_coprod`, but ensures the result is also alternating.\n\nNote that this is usually defined (for instance, as used in Proposition 22.24 in [Gallier2011Notes])\nover integer indices `\u03b9a = fin n` and `\u03b9b = fin m`, as\n$$\n(f \\wedge g)(u_1, \\ldots, u_{m+n}) =\n  \\sum_{\\operatorname{shuffle}(m, n)} \\operatorname{sign}(\\sigma)\n    f(u_{\\sigma(1)}, \\ldots, u_{\\sigma(m)}) g(u_{\\sigma(m+1)}, \\ldots, u_{\\sigma(m+n)}),\n$$\nwhere $\\operatorname{shuffle}(m, n)$ consists of all permutations of $[1, m+n]$ such that\n$\\sigma(1) < \\cdots < \\sigma(m)$ and $\\sigma(m+1) < \\cdots < \\sigma(m+n)$.\n\nHere, we generalize this by replacing:\n* the product in the sum with a tensor product\n* the filtering of $[1, m+n]$ to shuffles with an isomorphic quotient\n* the additions in the subscripts of $\\sigma$ with an index of type `sum`\n\nThe specialized version can be obtained by combining this definition with `fin_sum_fin_equiv` and\n`linear_map.mul'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_coord_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_eq_zero_of_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.curry_left", "description": " Given an alternating map `f` in `n+1` variables, split the first variable to obtain\na linear map into alternating maps in `n` variables, given by `x \u21a6 (m \u21a6 f (matrix.vec_cons x m))`.\nIt can be thought of as a map $Hom(\\bigwedge^{n+1} M, N) \\to Hom(M, Hom(\\bigwedge^n M, N))$.\n\nThis is `multilinear_map.curry_left` for `alternating_map`. See also\n`alternating_map.curry_left_linear_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_coprod'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.pi", "description": " Combine a family of alternating maps with the same domain and codomains `N i` into an\nalternating map taking values in the space of functions `\u03a0 i, N i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.smul_right_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.curry_left_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.to_multilinear_map", "description": "The multilinear map associated to an alternating map", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map", "description": "An alternating map is a multilinear map that vanishes when two of its arguments are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.to_fun", "description": "An alternating map is a multilinear map that vanishes when two of its arguments are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_add'", "description": "An alternating map is a multilinear map that vanishes when two of its arguments are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_smul'", "description": "An alternating map is a multilinear map that vanishes when two of its arguments are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_eq_zero_of_eq'", "description": "An alternating map is a multilinear map that vanishes when two of its arguments are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_update_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.curry_left_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.coe_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.prod", "description": "The cartesian product of two alternating maps, as a multilinear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.curry_left_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_coprod.summand_add_swap_smul_eq_zero", "description": "Swapping elements in `\u03c3` with equal values in `v` results in an addition that cancels", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.fun_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.neg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.const_linear_equiv_of_is_empty_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_dom_congr_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_dom_congr_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.curry_left_linear_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.coe_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.coe_multilinear_map_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.coe_comp_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.congr_arg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.comp_linear_equiv_eq_zero_iff", "description": " Composing an alternating map with the same linear equiv on each argument gives the zero map\nif and only if the alternating map is the zero map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_lcongr_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_dom_congr_perm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.module", "description": " The space of multilinear maps over an algebra over `R` is a module over `R`, for the pointwise\naddition and scalar multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.coe_alternatization", "description": " Alternatizing a multilinear map that is already alternating results in a scale factor of `n!`,\nwhere `n` is the number of inputs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_dom_lcongr_to_add_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_lcongr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.curry_left_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_congr_perm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_dom_congr_equiv", "description": " `alternating_map.dom_dom_congr` as an equivalence.\n\nThis is declared separately because it does not work with dot notation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multilinear_map.alternatization_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.comp_linear_map_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.add_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multilinear_map.dom_coprod_alternization_coe", "description": "A helper lemma for `multilinear_map.dom_coprod_alternization`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.coe_dom_dom_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.sub_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.has_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.coe_multilinear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.coe_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.comp_alternating_map", "description": "Composing a alternating map with a linear map on the left gives again an alternating map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.subtype_comp_alternating_map_cod_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.coe_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_dom_congr_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.comp_linear_map_id", "description": "Composing an alternating map with the identity linear map in each argument.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.coe_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_dom_lcongr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.curry_left_linear_map", "description": " `alternating_map.curry_left` as a `linear_map`. This is a separate definition as dot notation\ndoes not work for this version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_dom_lcongr_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.coe_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.smul_right", "description": " Given an alternating `R`-multilinear map `f` taking values in `R`, `f.smul_right z` is the map\nsending `m` to `f m \u2022 z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multilinear_map.dom_coprod_alternization", "description": " Computing the `multilinear_map.alternatization` of the `multilinear_map.dom_coprod` is the same\nas computing the `alternating_map.dom_coprod` of the `multilinear_map.alternatization`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.zero_comp_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_vec_cons_add", "description": "A version of `multilinear_map.cons_add` for `alternating_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_coprod.summand_eq_zero_of_smul_invariant", "description": " Swapping elements in `\u03c3` with equal values in `v` result in zero if the swap has no effect\non the quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_swap_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.comp_linear_map_injective", "description": "Composing with a surjective linear map is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.multilinear_map.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.curry_left_comp_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.congr_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_lcongr_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.of_subsingleton", "description": "The evaluation map from `\u03b9 \u2192 M` to `M` at a given `i` is alternating when `\u03b9` is subsingleton.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_dom_congr_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_dom_congr_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_dom_congr_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_coprod.summand_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.curry_left_comp_alternating_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.comp_linear_map", "description": " Composing a alternating map with the same linear map on each argument gives again an\nalternating map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.comp_alternating_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_dom_lcongr_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.const_linear_equiv_of_is_empty", "description": " The space of constant maps is equivalent to the space of maps that are alternating with respect\nto an empty family.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.ext_alternating", "description": " Two alternating maps indexed by a `fintype` are equal if they are equal when all arguments\nare distinct basis vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.mod_sum_congr", "description": "Elements which are considered equivalent if they differ only by swaps within \u03b1 or \u03b2", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.cod_restrict_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.const_linear_equiv_of_is_empty_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_coprod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.cod_restrict", "description": "Restrict the codomain of an alternating map to a submodule.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.comp_linear_map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.comp_alternating_map_cod_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.map_update_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.no_zero_smul_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.dom_coprod_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.comp_multilinear_map_alternatization", "description": "Composition with a linear map before and after alternatization are equivalent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antivary.sum_smul_eq_sum_comp_perm_smul_iff", "description": " **Equality case of the Rearrangement Inequality**: Pointwise scalar multiplication of `f` and\n`g`, which antivary together, is unchanged by a permutation if and only if `f \u2218 \u03c3` and `g` antivary\ntogether. Stated by permuting the entries of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antivary_on.sum_mul_lt_sum_comp_perm_mul_iff", "description": " **Strict inequality case of the Rearrangement Inequality**: Pointwise multiplication of\n`f` and `g`, which antivary together, is strictly decreased by a permutation if and only if\n`f \u2218 \u03c3` and `g` do not antivary together. Stated by permuting the entries of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antivary.sum_smul_lt_sum_comp_perm_smul_iff", "description": " **Strict inequality case of the Rearrangement Inequality**: Pointwise scalar multiplication of\n`f` and `g`, which antivary together, is strictly decreased by a permutation if and only if\n`f \u2218 \u03c3` and `g` do not antivary together. Stated by permuting the entries of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antivary.sum_smul_le_sum_smul_comp_perm", "description": " **Rearrangement Inequality**: Pointwise scalar multiplication of `f` and `g` is minimized when\n`f` and `g` antivary together. Stated by permuting the entries of `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monovary_on.sum_smul_comp_perm_lt_sum_smul_iff", "description": " **Strict inequality case of Rearrangement Inequality**: Pointwise scalar multiplication of\n`f` and `g`, which monovary together, is strictly decreased by a permutation if and only if\n`f` and `g \u2218 \u03c3` do not monovary together. Stated by permuting the entries of `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monovary_on.sum_smul_comp_perm_le_sum_smul", "description": " **Rearrangement Inequality**: Pointwise scalar multiplication of `f` and `g` is maximized when\n`f` and `g` monovary together. Stated by permuting the entries of `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antivary.sum_smul_lt_sum_smul_comp_perm_iff", "description": " **Strict inequality case of the Rearrangement Inequality**: Pointwise scalar multiplication of\n`f` and `g`, which anti