" `fractional_ideal.mul` is the product of two fractional ideals,\nused to define the `has_mul` instance.\n\nThis is only an auxiliary definition: the preferred way of writing `I.mul J` is `I * J`.\n\nElaborated terms involving `fractional_ideal` tend to grow quite large,\nso by making definitions irreducible, we hope to avoid deep unfolds.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.is_fractional", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.coe_to_submodule_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.eq_one_div_of_mul_eq_one_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.coe_ideal_hom", "description": "`coe_ideal_hom (S : submonoid R) P` is `coe : ideal R \u2192 fractional_ideal S P` as a ring hom", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.coe_ideal_fg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.coe_ideal_inj'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.is_noetherian", "description": "Every fractional ideal of a noetherian integral domain is noetherian.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.map_symm_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.span_singleton_mul_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fractional.pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.span_singleton_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.mul_le_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.div_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.div_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.mem_map", "de