ms is associative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.coe_monoid_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.has_coe_monoid_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.to_add_monoid_hom", "description": " Reinterpret a ring homomorphism `f : \u03b1 \u2192+* \u03b2` as an additive monoid homomorphism `\u03b1 \u2192+ \u03b2`.\nThe `simp`-normal form is `(f : \u03b1 \u2192+ \u03b2)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.coe_monoid_hom_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.ring_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.coe_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom", "description": " Bundled non-unital semiring homomorphisms `\u03b1 \u2192\u2099+* \u03b2`; use this for bundled non-unital ring\nhomomorphisms too.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : \u03b1 \u2192\u2099+* \u03b2)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [non_unital_ring_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `non_unital_ring_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.to_fun", "description": " Bundled non-unital semiring homomorphisms `\u03b1 \u2192\u2099+* \u03b2`; use this for bundled non-unital ring\nhomomorphisms too.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : \u03b1 \u2192\u2099+* \u03b2)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [non_unital_ring_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `non_unital_ring_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.map_mul'", "description": " Bundled non-unital semiring homomorphisms `\u03b1 \u2192\u2099+* \u03b2`; use this for bundled non-unital ring\nhomomorphisms too.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : \u03b1 \u2192\u2099+* \u03b2)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [non_unital_ring_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `non_unital_ring_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.map_zero'", "description": " Bundled non-unital semiring homomorphisms `\u03b1 \u2192\u2099+* \u03b2`; use this for bundled non-unital ring\nhomomorphisms too.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : \u03b1 \u2192\u2099+* \u03b2)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [non_unital_ring_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `non_unital_ring_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.map_add'", "description": " Bundled non-unital semiring homomorphisms `\u03b1 \u2192\u2099+* \u03b2`; use this for bundled non-unital ring\nhomomorphisms too.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : \u03b1 \u2192\u2099+* \u03b2)`,\nyou should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [non_unital_ring_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `non_unital_ring_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.cancel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.comp", "description": "Composition of non-unital ring homomorphisms is a non-unital ring homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.cancel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.coe_mul_hom_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.coe_add_monoid_hom_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.map_bit1", "description": "Ring homomorphisms preserve `bit1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.map_sub", "description": "Ring homomorphisms preserve subtraction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.id_comp", "descriptio