ends from both `monoid_hom` and `monoid_with_zero_hom` in order to put the fields in a\nsensible order, even though `monoid_with_zero_hom` already extends `monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.map_mul'", "description": " Bundled semiring homomorphisms; use this for bundled ring homomorphisms too.\n\nThis extends from both `monoid_hom` and `monoid_with_zero_hom` in order to put the fields in a\nsensible order, even though `monoid_with_zero_hom` already extends `monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.map_zero'", "description": " Bundled semiring homomorphisms; use this for bundled ring homomorphisms too.\n\nThis extends from both `monoid_hom` and `monoid_with_zero_hom` in order to put the fields in a\nsensible order, even though `monoid_with_zero_hom` already extends `monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.map_add'", "description": " Bundled semiring homomorphisms; use this for bundled ring homomorphisms too.\n\nThis extends from both `monoid_hom` and `monoid_with_zero_hom` in order to put the fields in a\nsensible order, even though `monoid_with_zero_hom` already extends `monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.to_mul_hom", "description": " Reinterpret a non-unital ring homomorphism `f : \u03b1 \u2192\u2099+* \u03b2` as a semigroup\nhomomorphism `\u03b1 \u2192\u2099* \u03b2`. The `simp`-normal form is `(f : \u03b1 \u2192\u2099* \u03b2)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.map_bit0", "description": "Ring homomorphisms preserve `bit0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.coe_monoid_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.map_ite_zero_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.codomain_trivial_iff_range_eq_singleton_zero", "description": "`f : \u03b1 \u2192+* \u03b2` has a trivial codomain iff its range is `{0}`.", "p": "mathlib"