"ball_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "singleton_mul_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.closed_ball_zero_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "singleton_add_ball_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closed_ball_zero_sub_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "singleton_mul_ball_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "neg_thickening", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.add_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ball_add_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ball_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_for.valid_glue", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes_bot_equiv_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.sieve.equalizer_sheaf_condition", "description": "`P` is a sheaf for `S`, iff the fork given by `w` is an equalizer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes_bot_equiv_unit_iso_inv_app_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_for.extend", "description": "If `P` is a sheaf for the sieve `S` on `X`, a natural transformation from `S` (viewed as a functor)\nto `P` can be (uniquely) extended to all of `yoneda.obj X`.\n\n      f\n   S  \u2192  P\n   \u2193  \u2197\n   yX", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes_bot_equiv_unit_iso_hom_app_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_for.functor_inclusion_comp_extend", "description": "Show that the extension of `f : S.functor \u27f6 P` to all of `yoneda.obj X` is in fact an extension, ie\nthat the triangle below commutes, provided `P` is a sheaf for `S`\n\n      f\n   S  \u2192  P\n   \u2193  \u2197\n   yX", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.sieve.w", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.presieve.compatible_iff", "description": "The family of elements given by `x : first_obj P S` is compatible iff `first_map` and `second_map`\nmap it to the same point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.first_obj_eq_family", "description": "Show that `first_obj` is isomorphic to `family_of_elements`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_for_iff_yoneda_sheaf_condition", "description": "The yoneda version of the sheaf condition is equivalent to the sheaf condition.\n\nC2.1.4 of [Elephant].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.compatible_equiv_generate_sieve_compatible_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes_bot_equiv_inverse_obj_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.sieve.first_map", "description": "The map `p` of Equations (3,4) [MM92].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_for.is_separated_for", "description": "If `P` is a sheaf for `R`, it is separated for `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.compatible.functor_pullback", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.sieve_compatible", "description": "If the arrow set for a family of elements is actually a sieve (i.e. it is downward closed) then the\nconsistency condition can be simplified.\nThis is an equivalent condition, see `compatible_iff_sieve_compatible`.\n\nThis is the notion of \"matching\" given for families on sieves given in [MM92], Chapter III,\nSection 4, Equation 1, and nlab: https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/matching+family.\nSee also the discussion before Lemma C2.1.4 of [Elephant].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.compatible_iff_sieve_compatible", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.compatible_equiv_generate_sieve_compatible_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.presieve.second_map", "description": "The map `pr\u2081*` of <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00VL>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.functor_pullback", "description": "Given a family of elements of a sieve `S` on `F(X)`, we can realize it as a family of elements of\n`S.functor_pullback F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes_bot_equiv", "description": "The category of sheaves on the bottom (trivial) grothendieck topology is equivalent to the category\nof presheaves.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.pullback_compatible_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.first_obj_eq_family_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_for.is_amalgamation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.restrict", "description": "A family of elements for a presheaf on the presieve `R\u2082` can be restricted to a smaller presieve\n`R\u2081`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.restrict_inj", "description": "Two compatible families on the sieve generated by a presieve `R` are equal if and only if they are\nequal when restricted to `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.presieve.second_obj.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.pullback", "description": "Given a family of elements of a sieve `S` on `X`, and a map `Y \u27f6 X`, we can obtain a\nfamily of elements of `S.pullback f` by taking the same elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.is_amalgamation.comp_presheaf_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.comp_presheaf_map", "description": "Given a morphism of presheaves `f : P \u27f6 Q`, we can take a family of elements valued in `P` to a\nfamily of elements valued in `Q` by composing with `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_separated_of_is_sheaf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.compatible_equiv_generate_sieve_compatible", "description": "Compatible families of elements for a presheaf of types `P` and a presieve `R`\n   are in 1-1 correspondence with compatible families for the same presheaf and\n   the sieve generated by `R`, through extension and restriction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.extend_agrees", "description": "The extension of a family agrees with the original family.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes_to_presheaf.full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.sieve.second_map", "description": "The map `a` of Equations (3,4) [MM92].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_of_yoneda", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.presieve.w", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_separated_for.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.sieve.second_obj", "description": "The rightmost object of the fork diagram of Equation (3) [MM92], which contains the data used\nto check a family is compatible.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements", "description": "A family of elements for a presheaf `P` given a collection of arrows `R` with fixed codomain `X`\nconsists of an element of `P Y` for every `f : Y \u27f6 X` in `R`.\nA presheaf is a sheaf (resp, separated) if every *compatible* family of elements has exactly one\n(resp, at most one) amalgamation.\n\nThis data is referred to as a `family` in [MM92], Chapter III, Section 4. It is also a concrete\nversion of the elements of the middle object in https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00VM which is\nmore useful for direct calculations. It is also used implicitly in Definition C2.1.2 in [Elephant].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_for.unique_extend", "description": "The extension of `f` to `yoneda.obj X` is unique.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.restrict_extend", "description": "The restriction of an extension is the original.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_separated_for.is_sheaf_for", "description": "If `P` is separated for `R` and every family has an amalgamation, then `P` is a sheaf for `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes.category_theory.category_comp_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_separated_for_iff_generate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes_bot_equiv_inverse_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.compatible.restrict", "description": "The restriction of a compatible family is compatible.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes.hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.functor_pushforward", "description": "Given a family of elements of a sieve `S` on `X` whose values factors through `F`, we can\nrealize it as a family of elements of `S.functor_pushforward F`. Since the preimage is obtained by\nchoice, this is not well-defined generally.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_amalgamation_sieve_extend", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.pullback_compatible", "description": "If the category `C` has pullbacks, this is an alternative condition for a family of elements to be\ncompatible: For any `f : Y \u27f6 X` and `g : Z \u27f6 X` in the presieve `R`, the restriction of the\ngiven elements for `f` and `g` to the pullback agree.\nThis is equivalent to being compatible (provided `C` has pullbacks), shown in\n`pullback_compatible_iff`.\n\nThis is the definition for a \"matching\" family given in [MM92], Chapter III, Section 4,\nEquation (5). Viewing the type `family_of_elements` as the middle object of the fork in\nhttps://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00VM, this condition expresses that `pr\u2080* (x) = pr\u2081* (x)`,\nusing the notation defined there.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.comp_presheaf_map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.comp_of_compatible", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf", "description": "A presheaf is a sheaf for a topology if it is a sheaf for every sieve in the topology.\n\nIf the given topology is given by a pretopology, `is_sheaf_for_pretopology` shows it suffices to\ncheck the sheaf condition at presieves in the pretopology.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.presieve.sheaf_condition", "description": "`P` is a sheaf for `R`, iff the fork given by `w` is an equalizer.\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00VM>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.compatible", "description": "A family of elements for the arrow set `R` is *compatible* if for any `f\u2081 : Y\u2081 \u27f6 X` and\n`f\u2082 : Y\u2082 \u27f6 X` in `R`, and any `g\u2081 : Z \u27f6 Y\u2081` and `g\u2082 : Z \u27f6 Y\u2082`, if the square `g\u2081 \u226b f\u2081 = g\u2082 \u226b f\u2082`\ncommutes then the elements of `P Z` obtained by restricting the element of `P Y\u2081` along `g\u2081` and\nrestricting the element of `P Y\u2082` along `g\u2082` are the same.\n\nIn special cases, this condition can be simplified, see `pullback_compatible_iff` and\n`compatible_iff_sieve_compatible`.\n\nThis is referred to as a \"compatible family\" in Definition C2.1.2 of [Elephant], and on nlab:\nhttps://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/sheaf#GeneralDefinitionInComponents", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_separated_for", "description": "A presheaf is separated for a presieve if there is at most one amalgamation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_pretopology", "description": "For a topology generated by a basis, it suffices to check the sheaf condition on the basis\npresieves only.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.presieve.second_obj", "description": "The rightmost object of the fork diagram of https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00VM, which\ncontains the data used to check a family of elements for a presieve is compatible.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.comp_prersheaf_map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_for_iff_generate", "description": "C2.1.3 in [Elephant]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_bot", "description": "Any presheaf is a sheaf for the bottom (trivial) grothendieck topology.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes.category_theory.category_id_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes_bot_equiv_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.compatible.pullback", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_for_subsieve", "description": "If `P` is a sheaf for every pullback of the sieve `S`, then `P` is a sheaf for any presieve which\ncontains `S`.\nThis is closely related to [Elephant] C2.1.6.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes.hom.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes_to_presheaf_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_for_top_sieve", "description": "Every presheaf is a sheaf for the maximal sieve.\n\n[Elephant] C2.1.5(ii)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.sieve.second_obj.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_for.amalgamate", "description": "Get the amalgamation of the given compatible family, provided we have a sheaf.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_separated_for_and_exists_is_amalgamation_iff_sheaf_for", "description": "`P` is a sheaf for `R` iff it is separated for `R` and there exists an amalgamation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes_to_presheaf", "description": "The inclusion functor from sheaves to presheaves.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.first_obj.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_for.hom_ext", "description": "If `P` is a sheaf for the sieve `S` on `X`, then if two natural transformations from `yoneda.obj X`\nto `P` agree when restricted to the subfunctor given by `S`, they are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_for_iso", "description": "If `P` is a sheaf for `S`, and it is iso to `P'`, then `P'` is a sheaf for `S`. This shows that\n\"being a sheaf for a presieve\" is a mathematical or hygenic property.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.sieve_extend", "description": "Extend a family of elements to the sieve generated by an arrow set.\nThis is the construction described as \"easy\" in Lemma C2.1.3 of [Elephant].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.extension_iff_amalgamation", "description": "(Implementation). A lemma useful to prove `yoneda_condition_iff_sheaf_condition`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.sieve.compatible_iff", "description": "The family of elements given by `x : first_obj P S` is compatible iff `first_map` and `second_map`\nmap it to the same point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes_to_presheaf_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_for_subsieve_aux", "description": "If a presieve `R` on `X` has a subsieve `S` such that:\n\n* `P` is a sheaf for `S`.\n* For every `f` in `R`, `P` is separated for the pullback of `S` along `f`,\n\nthen `P` is a sheaf for `R`.\n\nThis is closely related to [Elephant] C2.1.6(i).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.first_obj", "description": "The middle object of the fork diagram given in Equation (3) of [MM92], as well as the fork diagram\nof <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00VM>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.is_amalgamation", "description": "The given element `t` of `P.obj (op X)` is an *amalgamation* for the family of elements `x` if every\nrestriction `P.map f.op t = x_f` for every arrow `f` in the presieve `R`.\n\nThis is the definition given in  https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/sheaf#GeneralDefinitionInComponents,\nand https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/matching+family, as well as [MM92], Chapter III, Section 4,\nequation (2).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes", "description": "The category of sheaves on a grothendieck topology.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes.val", "description": "The category of sheaves on a grothendieck topology.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes.cond", "description": "The category of sheaves on a grothendieck topology.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.fork_map", "description": "The left morphism of the fork diagram given in Equation (3) of [MM92], as well as the fork diagram\nof <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00VM>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_for_singleton_iso", "description": "Every presheaf is a sheaf for the family {\ud835\udfd9 X}.\n\n[Elephant] C2.1.5(i)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf.is_sheaf_for", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.extend_restrict", "description": "Given a family of elements `x` for the sieve `S` generated by a presieve `R`, if `x` is restricted\nto `R` and then extended back up to `S`, the resulting extension equals `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.nat_trans_equiv_compatible_family", "description": "(Implementation). This is a (primarily internal) equivalence between natural transformations\nand compatible families.\n\nCf the discussion after Lemma 7.47.10 in <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00YW>. See also\nthe proof of C2.1.4 of [Elephant], and the discussion in [MM92], Chapter III, Section 4.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.presieve.first_map", "description": "The map `pr\u2080*` of <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00VL>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_separated_for_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.compatible.sieve_extend", "description": "The extension of a compatible family to the generated sieve is compatible.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_compatible_of_exists_amalgamation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_for", "description": "We define `P` to be a sheaf for the presieve `R` if every compatible family has a unique\namalgamation.\n\nThis is the definition of a sheaf for the given presieve given in C2.1.2 of [Elephant], and\nhttps://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/sheaf#GeneralDefinitionInComponents.\nUsing `compatible_iff_sieve_compatible`,\nthis is equivalent to the definition of a sheaf in [MM92], Chapter III, Section 4.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer.first_obj_eq_family_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_iso", "description": "The property of being a sheaf is preserved by isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes.category_theory.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.yoneda_sheaf_condition", "description": "This is an equivalent condition to be a sheaf, which is useful for the abstraction to local\noperators on elementary toposes. However this definition is defined only for sieves, not presieves.\nThe equivalence between this and `is_sheaf_for` is given in `yoneda_condition_iff_sheaf_condition`.\nThis version is also useful to establish that being a sheaf is preserved under isomorphism of\npresheaves.\n\nSee the discussion before Equation (3) of [MM92], Chapter III, Section 4. See also C2.1.4 of\n[Elephant]. This is also a direct reformulation of <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z8>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes_to_presheaf.faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_for.functor_inclusion_comp_extend_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes.hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.compatible.comp_presheaf_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_amalgamation_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.family_of_elements.compatible.to_sieve_compatible", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes.hom", "description": "Morphisms between sheaves of types are just morphisms between the underlying presheaves.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.SheafOfTypes.hom.val", "description": "Morphisms between sheaves of types are just morphisms between the underlying presheaves.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_sheaf_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.is_separated", "description": "A presheaf is separated for a topology if it is separated for every sieve in the topology.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.CommMon_functor_category_equivalence.functor_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.Mon_functor_category_equivalence.inverse_obj_mul_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.CommMon_functor_category_equivalence", "description": "When `D` is a braided monoidal category,\ncommutative monoid objects in `C \u2964 D` are the same thing\nas functors from `C` into the commutative monoid objects of `D`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.Mon_functor_category_equivalence.functor", "description": "Functor translating a monoid object in a functor category\nto a functor into the category of monoid objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.Mon_functor_category_equivalence_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.CommMon_functor_category_equivalence.inverse_obj_to_Mon_", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.Mon_functor_category_equivalence.functor_map_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.CommMon_functor_category_equivalence.unit_iso_inv_app_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.Mon_functor_category_equivalence.counit_iso_inv_app_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.CommMon_functor_category_equivalence.counit_iso", "description": "The counit for the equivalence `CommMon_ (C \u2964 D) \u224c C \u2964 CommMon_ D`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.Mon_functor_category_equivalence.inverse", "description": "Functor translating a functor into the category of monoid objects\nto a monoid object in the functor category", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.Mon_functor_category_equivalence.unit_iso_hom_app_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.Mon_functor_category_equivalence.unit_iso", "description": "The unit for the equivalence `Mon_ (C \u2964 D) \u224c C \u2964 Mon_ D`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.Mon_functor_category_equivalence.inverse_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.CommMon_functor_category_equivalence_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.CommMon_functor_category_equivalence.counit_iso_inv_app_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.CommMon_functor_category_equivalence.inverse", "description": "Functor translating a functor into the category of commutative monoid objects\nto a commutative monoid object in the functor category", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.CommMon_functor_category_equivalence_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.Mon_functor_category_equivalence.unit_iso_inv_app_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.Mon_functor_category_equivalence", "description": "When `D` is a monoidal category,\nmonoid objects in `C \u2964 D` are the same thing\nas functors from `C` into the monoid objects of `D`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.CommMon_functor_category_equivalence.inverse_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.Mon_functor_category_equivalence.functor_obj_obj_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.Mon_functor_category_equivalence.counit_iso", "description": "The counit for the equivalence `Mon_ (C \u2964 D) \u224c C \u2964 Mon_ D`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.Mon_functor_category_equivalence.functor_obj_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal.CommMon_functor_category_equivalence.functor_obj_map", "