ption": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_key", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.find_one_difference", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_selection.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.get_operator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_head_candidates", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.compare", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.monotonicity.check_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.side", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_cfg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_cfg.unify", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.same_operator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.get_monotonicity_lemmas", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_cfg.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.match_imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_selection", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_selection.left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_selection.right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_selection.both", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.last_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_selection.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.monotonicity.check", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_selection.has_reflect", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.derived_series_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.derived_series_of_ideal", "description": " A generalisation of the derived series of a Lie algebra, whose zeroth term is a specified ideal.\n\nIt can be more convenient to work with this generalisation when considering the derived series of\nan ideal since it provides a type-theoretic expression of the fact that the terms of the ideal's\nderived series are also ideals of the enclosing algebra.\n\nSee also `lie_ideal.derived_series_eq_derived_series_of_ideal_comap` and\n`lie_ideal.derived_series_eq_derived_series_of_ideal_map` below.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.abelian_of_solvable_ideal_eq_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.derived_length_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.derived_series_of_ideal_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.derived_series_of_ideal_add_le_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.derived_series_of_bot_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.solvable_iff_equiv_solvable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.derived_series_of_ideal_antitone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.derived_series_of_derived_length_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.radical_is_solvable", "description": "The radical of a Noetherian Lie algebra is solvable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.is_solvable_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.abelian_iff_derived_one_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.of_abelian_is_solvable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.derived_series_add_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.derived_series_of_ideal_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.lie_algebra_is_solvable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.derived_length_eq_derived_length_of_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.derived_series_eq_derived_series_of_ideal_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.derived_series_of_ideal_le_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.derived_series_map_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.is_solvable", "description": "A Lie algebra is solvable if its derived series reaches 0 (in a finite number of steps).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.is_solvable.solvable", "description": "A Lie algebra is solvable if its derived series reaches 0 (in a finite number of steps).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.center_le_radical", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.le_solvable_ideal_solvable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.lie_ideal.solvable_iff_le_radical", "description": "The `\u2192` direction of this lemma is actually true without the `is_noetherian` assumption.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.derived_series", "description": "The derived series of Lie ideals of a Lie algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.derived_series_map_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_hom.is_solvable_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.derived_series_of_ideal_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.abelian_iff_derived_succ_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.derived_series_eq_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.is_solvable_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.derived_abelian_of_ideal", "description": " Given a solvable Lie ideal `I` with derived series `I = D\u2080 \u2265 D\u2081 \u2265 \u22ef \u2265 D\u2096 = \u22a5`, this is the\n`k-1`th term in the derived series (and is therefore an Abelian ideal contained in `I`).\n\nFor a non-solvable ideal, this is the zero ideal, `\u22a5`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.lie_algebra_is_solvable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.radical", "description": "The (solvable) radical of Lie algebra is the `Sup` of all solvable ideals.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.abelian_derived_abelian_of_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.derived_series_of_ideal_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.derived_series_of_ideal_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.derived_series_of_ideal_succ_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.derived_length_of_ideal", "description": " Given a solvable Lie ideal `I` with derived series `I = D\u2080 \u2265 D\u2081 \u2265 \u22ef \u2265 D\u2096 = \u22a5`, this is the\nnatural number `k` (the number of inclusions).\n\nFor a non-solvable ideal, the value is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.derived_series_eq_derived_series_of_ideal_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.derived_length", "description": " The derived length of a Lie algebra is the derived length of its 'top' Lie ideal.\n\nSee also `lie_algebra.derived_length_eq_derived_length_of_ideal`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.reflects_mono_of_reflects_limit", "description": "If `F` reflects pullbacks, then it reflects monomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.reflects_epimorphisms_of_reflects_colimits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.reflects_monomorphisms_of_reflects_limits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.reflects_epi_of_reflects_colimit", "description": "If `F` reflects pushouts, then it reflects epimorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_mono_of_preserves_limit", "description": "If `F` preserves pullbacks, then it preserves monomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_monomorphisms_of_preserves_limits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_epimorphisms_of_preserves_colimits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_epi_of_preserves_colimit", "description": "If `F` preserves pushouts, then it preserves epimorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_coannihilator", "description": " The `dual_annihilator` of a submodule of the dual space pulled back along the evaluation map\n`module.dual.eval`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_copairing_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.eval_apply_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ker_dual_map_eq_dual_annihilator_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_prod_dual_equiv_dual_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.finrank_add_finrank_dual_coannihilator_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.comap_eval_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_quot_equiv_dual_annihilator_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_copairing_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_annihilator_dual_coannihilator_dual_annihilator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_restrict_ker_eq_dual_annihilator", "description": " That $\\operatorname{ker}(\\iota^* : V^* \\to W^*) = \\operatorname{ann}(W)$.\nThis is the definition of the dual annihilator of the submodule $W$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.to_dual_to_dual", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.to_dual_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.module.dual.finite_dimensional", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.supr_dual_annihilator_le_infi", "description": "See also `subspace.dual_annihilator_infi_eq` for vector subspaces when `\u03b9` is finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.dual_pairing_nondegenerate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.dual_lift_of_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual.eval_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_restrict", "description": "The `dual_restrict` of a submodule `W` of `M` is the linear map from the\n dual of `M` to the dual of `W` such that the domain of each linear map is\n restricted to `W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_bases.lc", "description": " linear combinations of elements of `e`.\nThis is a convenient abbreviation for `finsupp.total _ M R e l`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.dual_distrib_equiv_of_basis", "description": "A linear equivalence between `dual M \u2297 dual N` and `dual (M \u2297 N)` given bases for `M` and `N`.\nIt sends `f \u2297 g` to the composition of `tensor_product.map f g` with the natural\nisomorphism `R \u2297 R \u2243 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.dual_map", "description": " Given a linear map `f : M\u2081 \u2192\u2097[R] M\u2082`, `f.dual_map` is the linear map between the dual of\n`M\u2082` and `M\u2081` such that it maps the functional `\u03c6` to `\u03c6 \u2218 f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.dual_lift", "description": " Given a subspace `W` of `V` and an element of its dual `\u03c6`, `dual_lift W \u03c6` is\nan arbitrary extension of `\u03c6` to an element of the dual of `V`.\nThat is, `dual_lift W \u03c6` sends `w \u2208 W` to `\u03c6 x` and `x` in a chosen complement of `W` to `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.dual_map_injective_of_surjective", "description": "If a linear map is surjective, then its dual is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual.transpose_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.range_dual_map_eq_dual_annihilator_ker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_coannihilator_anti", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_bases.basis", "description": "`(h : dual_bases e \u03b5).basis` shows the family of vectors `e` forms a basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_prod_dual_equiv_dual_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.dual_lift_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.dual_map_comp_dual_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual.transpose", "description": " The transposition of linear maps, as a linear map from `M \u2192\u2097[R] M'` to\n`dual R M' \u2192\u2097[R] dual R M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.dual_lift_right_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.dual_restrict_left_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_restrict_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.dual_distrib_inv_of_basis", "description": "An inverse to `dual_tensor_dual_map` given bases.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.dual_map_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.to_dual_ker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.dual_basis_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coe_to_dual_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.map_eval_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_bases.coeffs_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.le_dual_annihilator_iff_le_dual_coannihilator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_dual_annihilator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.dual_map_bijective_iff", "description": "`f.dual_map` is bijective if and only if `f` is", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_annihilator_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.dual_pairing_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.finrank_range_dual_map_eq_finrank_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_annihilator_anti", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_coannihilator_sup_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.dual_distrib_equiv_of_basis_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.le_dual_coannihilator_dual_annihilator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.dual_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.dual_map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.to_dual_flip_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.eval_equiv", "description": "A module with a basis is linearly equivalent to the dual of its dual space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.map_eval_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "use_finite_instance", "description": "Try using `set.to_finite` to dispatch a `set.finite` goal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.dual_annihilator_dual_annihilator_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.dual_map", "description": "The `linear_equiv` version of `linear_map.dual_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.dual_distrib", "description": "The canonical linear map from `dual M \u2297 dual N` to `dual (M \u2297 N)`,\nsending `f \u2297 g` to the composition of `tensor_product.map f g` with\nthe natural isomorphism `R \u2297 R \u2243 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.range_dual_map_eq_dual_annihilator_ker_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_pairing_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_annihilator_sup_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.dual_rank_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.dual_restrict_comp_dual_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_pairing_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.dual_annihilator_infi_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_pairing", "description": "The canonical pairing of a vector space and its algebraic dual.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.to_dual_total_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_quot_equiv_dual_annihilator", "description": " Equivalence $(M/W)^* \\approx \\operatorname{ann}(W)$. That is, there is a one-to-one\ncorrespondence between the dual of `M \u29f8 W` and those elements of the dual of `M` that\nvanish on `W`.\n\nThe inverse of this is `submodule.dual_copairing`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.to_dual", "description": " The linear map from a vector space equipped with basis to its dual vector space,\ntaking basis elements to corresponding dual basis elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_coannihilator_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_dual_coannihilator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_annihilator", "description": "The `dual_annihilator` of a submodule `W` is the set of linear maps `\u03c6` such\n that `\u03c6 w = 0` for all `w \u2208 W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.eval_equiv_to_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.dual_basis_equiv_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.dual_distrib_equiv_of_basis_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_coannihilator_dual_annihilator_dual_coannihilator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.forall_dual_apply_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_bases", "description": "`e` and `\u03b5` have characteristic properties of a basis and its dual", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_bases.eval", "description": "`e` and `\u03b5` have characteristic properties of a basis and its dual", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_bases.total", "description": "`e` and `\u03b5` have characteristic properties of a basis and its dual", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_bases.finite", "description": "`e` and `\u03b5` have characteristic properties of a basis and its dual", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_product.dual_distrib_equiv", "description": "A linear equivalence between `dual M \u2297 dual N` and `dual (M \u2297 N)` when `M` and `N` are finite free\nmodules. It sends `f \u2297 g` to the composition of `tensor_product.map f g` with the natural\nisomorphism `R \u2297 R \u2243 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_bases.dual_lc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.eval_ker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.eval_equiv_to_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.quot_annihilator_equiv", "description": "The quotient by the `dual_annihilator` of a subspace is isomorphic to the\n dual of that subspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.map_eval_equiv", "description": "The isomorphism `module.eval_equiv` induces an order isomorphism on subspaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_bases.lc_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_restrict_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.range_dual_map_mkq_eq", "description": "That $\\operatorname{im}(q^* : (V/W)^* \\to V^*) = \\operatorname{ann}(W)$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.dual_annihilator_gci", "description": "`submodule.dual_annihilator` and `submodule.dual_coannihilator` form a Galois coinsertion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.dual_quot_distrib", "description": " For finite-dimensional vector spaces, one can distribute duals over quotients by identifying\n`W.dual_lift.range` with `W`. Note that this depends on a choice of splitting of `V\u2081`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_bases.coeffs_lc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_bases.coe_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.is_compl_dual_annihilator", "description": " For vector spaces, dual annihilators carry direct sum decompositions\nto direct sum decompositions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_quot_equiv_dual_annihilator_symm_apply_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_annihilator_gc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.eval_equiv", "description": "A vector space is linearly equivalent to the dual of its dual space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.dual_basis_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_bases.lc_coeffs", "description": "For any m : M n, \\sum_{p \u2208 Q n} (\u03b5 p m) \u2022 e p = m", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.dual_finrank_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_bases.basis_repr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.total_coord", "description": "`simp` normal form version of `total_dual_basis`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_annihilator_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_bases.basis_repr_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.to_dual_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.dual_coannihilator_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.dual_annihilator_inf_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.to_dual_eq_equiv_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.dual_equiv_dual_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.dual_copairing_nondegenerate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.sum_dual_apply_smul_coord", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.dual_map_injective_iff", "description": "`f.dual_map` is injective if and only if `f` is surjective", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.range_dual_map_le_dual_annihilator_ker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.to_dual_equiv", "description": "A vector space is linearly equivalent to its dual space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual", "description": "The dual space of an R-module M is the R-module of linear maps `M \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_pairing", "description": " Given a submodule, restrict to the pairing on `W` by\nsimultaneously corestricting to `module.dual R M \u29f8 W.dual_annihilator`.\nThis is `submodule.dual_restrict` factored through the quotient by its kernel (which\nis `W.dual_annihilator` by definition).\n\nSee `subspace.dual_pairing_nondegenerate`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.dual_basis_apply_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dual_copairing", "description": " Given a submodule, corestrict to the pairing on `M \u29f8 W` by\nsimultaneously restricting to `W.dual_annihilator`.\n\nSee `subspace.dual_copairing_nondegenerate`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.to_dual_apply_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.dual_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_prod_dual_equiv_dual", "description": "Taking duals distributes over products.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.dual_pairing_nondegenerate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.to_dual_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_bases.mem_of_mem_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.range_dual_map_eq_dual_annihilator_ker_of_subtype_range_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.map_eval_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.to_dual_eq_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.finrank_dual_coannihilator_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.to_dual_total_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_bases.coe_dual_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.dual_prod_dual_equiv_dual_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subspace.quot_annihilator_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.erange_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.dual_free", "description": "", "p