ory.martingale_of_set_integral_eq_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.supermartingale", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale.sub_martingale", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.supermartingale.strongly_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale.set_integral_le", "description": "The converse of this lemma is `measure_theory.submartingale_of_set_integral_le`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.submartingale", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.supermartingale.condexp_ae_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.integrable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale", "description": " A family of functions `f : \u03b9 \u2192 \u03a9 \u2192 E` is a martingale with respect to a filtration `\u2131` if `f`\nis adapted with respect to `\u2131` and for all `i \u2264 j`, `\u03bc[f j | \u2131 i] =\u1d50[\u03bc] f i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.supermartingale_of_set_integral_succ_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale.ae_le_condexp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale", "description": " A family of integrable functions `f : \u03b9 \u2192 \u03a9 \u2192 E` is a submartingale with respect to a\nfiltration `\u2131` if `f` is adapted with respect to `\u2131` and for all `i \u2264 j`,\n`f i \u2264\u1d50[\u03bc] \u03bc[f j | \u2131.le i]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale.integrable_stopped_value", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale_condexp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale.adapted", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale.sub_supermartingale", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale.pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.strongly_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale_of_set_integral_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.supermartingale.sub_martingale", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale_const_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale.sum_mul_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale.sum_mul_sub'", "description": " Given a discrete submartingale `f` and a predictable process `\u03be` (i.e. `\u03be (n + 1)` is adapted)\nthe process defined by `\u03bb n, \u2211 k in finset.range n, \u03be (k + 1) * (f (k + 1) - f k)` is also a\nsubmartingale.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale.strongly_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale.add_martingale", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.supermartingale.set_integral_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.supermartingale", "description": " A family of integrable functions `f : \u03b9 \u2192 \u03a9 \u2192 E` is a supermartingale with respect to a\nfiltration `\u2131` if `f` is adapted with respect to `\u2131` and for all `i \u2264 j`,\n`\u03bc[f j | \u2131.le i] \u2264\u1d50[\u03bc] f i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale_of_condexp_sub_eq_zero_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.adapted", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.condexp_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.supermartingale.integrable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.supermartingale.le_zero_of_predictable", "description": "A predictable supermartingale is a.e. less equal than its initial state.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.supermartingale_of_condexp_sub_nonneg_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lean.parser.sep_by", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.run_with_input", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.run", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser_state.cur_pos", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.many", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.reflectable.to_parser", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.reflectable.optional", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.list_include_var_names", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.of_tactic", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.with_input", "description": "Temporarily replace input of the parser state, run `p`, and return remaining input.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser_state.options", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.skip_info", "description": "Do not report info from content parsed by `p`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.val", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.set_goal_info_pos", "description": "Set goal info position of content parsed by `p` to current position. Nested calls take precedence.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.reflectable", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.reflectable.full", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.set_env", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser_result", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.small_nat", "description": "Make sure the next token is a small nat, consume it, and produce it", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.tk", "description": "Check that the next token is `tk` and consume it. `tk` must be a registered token.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.add_local", "description": "a variable to local scope", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.pop_local_scope", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.ident", "description": "Make sure the next token is an identifier, consume it, and\n   produce the quoted name `t, where t is the identifier.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.omit_var", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.reflectable.has_reflect", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.list_available_include_vars", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.command_like", "description": "Parse a top-level command.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.reflectable.cast", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.reflectable.expr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser_state.env", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.include_var", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.alternative", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.pexpr", "description": " Parse an unelaborated expression using the given right-binding power.\nWhen `pat := tt`, the expression is parsed as a pattern, i.e. local\nconstants are not checked.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.itactic", "description": "Parse an interactive tactic block: `begin` .. `end`", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser_state", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.parser_orelse", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.add_local_level", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.push_local_scope", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.reflect", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.cur_pos", "description": "Return the current parser position without consuming any input.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.get_env", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.itactic_reflected", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "lean.parser.with_local_scope", "description": "Run the parser in a local declaration scope.\n\nLocal declarations added via `add_local` do not propagate outside of this scope.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "finsupp.to_multiset_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_id_lt_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.prod_to_multiset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.to_multiset_sum_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.to_finsupp", "description": " Given a multiset `s`, `s.to_finsupp` returns the finitely supported function on `\u2115` given by\nthe multiplicities of the elements of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.to_multiset_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.to_multiset_to_finsupp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.to_finsupp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.to_finsupp_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.to_finsupp_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.to_finsupp_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.card_to_multiset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lt_wf", "description": "The order on `\u03b9 \u2192\u2080 \u2115` is well-founded.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.order_iso_multiset", "description": "`finsupp.to_multiset` as an order isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.to_multiset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.to_finsupp_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.to_multiset_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.mem_to_multiset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.to_finsupp_strict_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.to_multiset", "description": " Given `f : \u03b1 \u2192\u2080 \u2115`, `f.to_multiset` is the multiset with multiplicities given by the values of\n`f` on the elements of `\u03b1`. We define this function as an `add_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.to_finsupp_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.to_finsupp_to_multiset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.to_multiset_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.coe_order_iso_multiset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.to_multiset_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.to_multiset_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.coe_order_iso_multiset_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.to_multiset_strict_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.to_finset_to_multiset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.count_to_multiset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.mono", "description": "If a number is Liouville with exponent `p`, then it is Liouville with any smaller exponent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.add_int_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.nat_sub_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.nat_add_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.sub_rat_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.rat_sub_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.mul_nat_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.rat_add_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.int_mul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.add_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.add_int", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.add_nat_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.neg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.nat_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.sub_int_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.int_add_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.sub_nat_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with_one", "description": "For `p = 1` (hence, for any `p \u2264 1`), the condition `liouville_with p x` is trivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.rat_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.mul_int_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.nat_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.int_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.nat_mul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.int_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville.liouville_with", "description": "A Liouville number is a Liouville number with any real exponent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.mul_rat_iff", "description": " The product `x * r`, `r : \u211a`, `r \u2260 0`, is a Liouville number with exponent `p` if and only if\n`x` satisfies the same condition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.sub_int", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.add_rat_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with", "description": " We say that a real number `x` is a Liouville number with exponent `p : \u211d` if there exists a real\nnumber `C` such that for infinitely many denominators `n` there exists a numerator `m` such that\n`x \u2260 m / n` and `|x - m / n| < C / n ^ p`.\n\nA number is a Liouville number in the sense of `liouville` if it is `liouville_with` any real\nexponent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.exists_pos", "description": " The constant `C` provided by the definition of `liouville_with` can be made positive.\nWe also add `1 \u2264 n` to the list of assumptions about the denominator. While it is equivalent to\nthe original statement, the case `n = 0` breaks many arguments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.mul_rat", "description": "The product of a Liouville number and a nonzero rational number is again a Liouville number.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.mul_int", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.rat_mul_iff", "description": " The product `r * x`, `r : \u211a`, `r \u2260 0`, is a Liouville number with exponent `p` if and only if\n`x` satisfies the same condition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.mul_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.int_sub_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.ne_cast_int", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.sub_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.rat_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.add_rat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.irrational", "description": "A number satisfying the Liouville condition with exponent `p > 1` is an irrational number.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "forall_liouville_with_iff", "description": " A number satisfies the Liouville condition with any exponent if and only if it is a Liouville\nnumber.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.rat_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.sub_rat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.frequently_lt_rpow_neg", "description": " If `x` satisfies Liouville condition with exponent `p` and `q < p`, then `x`\nsatisfies Liouville condition with exponent `q` and constant `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.int_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville_with.nat_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville.frequently_exists_num", "description": " If `x` is a Liouville number, then for any `n`, for infinitely many denominators `b` there\nexists a numerator `a` such that `x \u2260 a / b` and `|x - a / b| < 1 / b ^ n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.creates_limit_full_subcategory_inclusion", "description": "If a `J`-shaped diagram in `full_subcategory P` has a limit in `C` whose cone point lives in the\n   full subcategory, then this defines a limit in the full subcategory.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.closed_under_limits_of_shape", "description": "We say that a property is closed under limits of shape `J` if whenever all objects in a\n   `J`-shaped diagram have the property, any limit of this diagram also has the property.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.creates_colimit_full_subcategory_inclusion_of_closed", "description": "If `P` is closed under colimits of shape `J`, then the inclusion creates such colimits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limit_of_closed_under_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.closed_under_colimits_of_shape", "description": "We say that a property is closed under colimits of shape `J` if whenever all objects in a\n   `J`-shaped diagram have the property, any colimit of this diagram also has the property.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.creates_colimits_of_shape_full_subcategory_inclusion", "description": "If `P` is closed under colimits of shape `J`, then the inclusion creates such colimits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.creates_limit_full_subcategory_inclusion'", "description": "If a `J`-shaped diagram in `full_subcategory P` has a limit cone in `C` whose cone point lives\n   in the full subcategory, then this defines a limit in the full subcategory.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.creates_colimit_full_subcategory_inclusion", "description": "If a `J`-shaped diagram in `full_subcategory P` has a colimit in `C` whose cocone point lives in\n   the full subcategory, then this defines a colimit in the full subcategory.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limits_of_shape_of_closed_under_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimit_of_closed_under_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.closed_under_colimits_of_shape.colimit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.closed_under_limits_of_shape.limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.creates_limits_of_shape_full_subcategory_inclusion", "description": "If `P` is closed under limits of shape `J`, then the inclusion creates such limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.creates_colimit_full_subcategory_inclusion'", "description": "If a `J`-shaped diagram in `full_subcategory P` has a colimit cocone in `C` whose cocone point\n   lives in the full subcategory, then this defines a colimit in the full subcategory.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimits_of_shape_of_closed_under_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.creates_limit_full_subcategory_inclusion_of_closed", "description": "If `P` is closed under limits of shape `J`, then the inclusion creates such limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_add_const_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_div_const_uIcc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_mul_const_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_mul_right_Icc'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_mul_left_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_const_sub_Iio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_neg_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_sub_const_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_const_mul_Ici_of_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_neg_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_mul_const_Ioi_of_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_neg_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_neg_uIcc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_const_add_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_const_sub_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_const_mul_Ioo_of_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_mul_const_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_add_const_uIcc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.abs_sub_le_of_uIcc_subset_uIcc", "description": " If `[c, d]` is a subinterval of `[a, b]`, then the distance between `c` and `d` is less than or\nequal to that of `a` and `b`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_const_sub_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_const_sub_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_const_mul_Ioi_of_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_const_mul_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_const_add_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_const_mul_uIcc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_const_sub_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_mul_right_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_sub_const_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.inv_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_mul_const_Ioc", "description": "