eft", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interactive.loc.has_reflect", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "has_sizeof_derive_handler", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "prod.has_reflect", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "bool.has_reflect", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "sum.has_reflect", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "derive_handler", "description": "A handler that may or may not be able to implement the typeclass `cls` for `decl`.\n   It should return `tt` if it was able to derive `cls` and `ff` if it does not know\n   how to derive `cls`, in which case lower-priority handlers will be tried next.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "derive_handler_attr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "instance_derive_handler", "description": "Given a tactic `tac` that can solve an application of `cls` in the right context,\n   `instance_derive_handler` uses it to build an instance declaration of `cls n`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "option.has_reflect", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "has_reflect_derive_handler", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "pos.has_reflect", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "derive_attr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.zeta_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.norm_of_cyclotomic_irreducible", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.prime_ne_two_pow_norm_zeta_sub_one", "description": " If `irreducible (cyclotomic (p ^ (k + 1)) K)` (in particular for `K = \u211a`) and `p` is an odd\nprime, then the norm of `zeta (p ^ (k + 1)) K L - 1` is `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.zeta", "description": " If `B` is a `n`-th cyclotomic extension of `A`, then `zeta n A B` is a primitive root of\nunity in `B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.two_pow_norm_zeta_sub_one", "description": " If `irreducible (cyclotomic (2 ^ k) K)` (in particular for `K = \u211a`) and `k` is at least `2`,\nthen the norm of `zeta (2 ^ k) K L - 1` is `2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.sub_one_power_basis_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.is_prime_pow_norm_zeta_sub_one", "description": " If `is_prime_pow (n : \u2115)`, `n \u2260 2` and `irreducible (cyclotomic n K)` (in particular for\n`K = \u211a`), then the norm of `zeta n K L - 1` is `(n : \u2115).min_fac`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.norm_zeta_eq_one", "description": " If `irreducible (cyclotomic n K)` (in particular for `K = \u211a`), the norm of `zeta n K L` is `1`\nif `n` is odd.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.norm_eq_neg_one_pow", "description": "This mathematically trivial result is complementary to `norm_eq_one` below.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.embeddings_equiv_primitive_roots", "description": "The equivalence between `L \u2192\u2090[K] C` and `primitive_roots n C` given by a primitive root `\u03b6`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.prime_ne_two_pow_norm_zeta_pow_sub_one", "description": " If `irreducible (cyclotomic (p ^ (k + 1)) K)` (in particular for `K = \u211a`) and `p` is a prime,\nthen the norm of `(zeta (p ^ (k + 1)) K L) ^ (p ^ s) - 1` is `p ^ (p ^ s)`\nif `p ^ (k - s + 1) \u2260 2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.aeval_zeta", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.sub_one_norm_prime_ne_two", "description": " If `irreducible (cyclotomic (p ^ (k + 1)) K)` (in particular for `K = \u211a`) and `p` is an odd\nprime, then the norm of `\u03b6 - 1` is `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.pow_sub_one_norm_prime_pow_ne_two", "description": " If `irreducible (cyclotomic (p ^ (k + 1)) K)` (in particular for `K = \u211a`) and `p` is a prime,\nthen the norm of `\u03b6 ^ (p ^ s) - 1` is `p ^ (p ^ s)` if `p ^ (k - s + 1) \u2260 2`. See the next lemmas\nfor similar results.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.sub_one_norm_is_prime_pow", "description": " If `is_prime_pow (n : \u2115)`, `n \u2260 2` and `irreducible (cyclotomic n K)` (in particular for\n`K = \u211a`), then the norm of `\u03b6 - 1` is `(n : \u2115).min_fac`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.sub_one_norm_prime", "description": " If `irreducible (cyclotomic p K)` (in particular for `K = \u211a`) and `p` is an odd prime,\nthen the norm of `\u03b6 - 1` is `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.sub_one_norm_two", "description": " If `irreducible (cyclotomic (2 ^ k) K)` (in particular for `K = \u211a`) and `k` is at least `2`,\nthen the norm of `\u03b6 - 1` is `2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.pow_sub_one_norm_prime_ne_two", "description": " If `irreducible (cyclotomic (p ^ (k + 1)) K)` (in particular for `K = \u211a`) and `p` is a prime,\nthen the norm of `\u03b6 ^ (p ^ s) - 1` is `p ^ (p ^ s)` if `p \u2260 2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.power_basis_dim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.minpoly_sub_one_eq_cyclotomic_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.sub_one_power_basis", "description": "The `power_basis` given by `\u03b7 - 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.norm_eq_one", "description": " If `irreducible (cyclotomic n K)` (in particular for `K = \u211a`), the norm of a primitive root is\n`1` if `n \u2260 2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.pow_sub_one_norm_two", "description": " If `irreducible (cyclotomic (2 ^ (k + 1)) K)` (in particular for `K = \u211a`), then the norm of\n`\u03b6 ^ (2 ^ k) - 1` is `(-2) ^ (2 ^ k)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.power_basis", "description": "The `power_basis` given by a primitive root `\u03b7`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.sub_one_power_basis_dim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.power_basis_gen_mem_adjoin_zeta_sub_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.finrank", "description": " If `irreducible (cyclotomic n K)` (in particular for `K = \u211a`), then the `finrank` of a\ncyclotomic extension is `n.totient`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.norm_eq_one_of_linearly_ordered", "description": "If `K` is linearly ordered, the norm of a primitive root is `1` if `n` is odd.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.zeta_spec", "description": "`zeta n A B` is a primitive `n`-th root of unity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.power_basis_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.pow_sub_one_norm_prime_pow_of_ne_zero", "description": " If `irreducible (cyclotomic (p ^ (k + 1)) K)` (in particular for `K = \u211a`) and `p` is a prime,\nthen the norm of `\u03b6 ^ (p ^ s) - 1` is `p ^ (p ^ s)` if `k \u2260 0` and `s \u2264 k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.zeta_is_root", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.sub_one_norm_eq_eval_cyclotomic", "description": " If `irreducible (cyclotomic n K)` (in particular for `K = \u211a`), then the norm of\n`\u03b6 - 1` is `eval 1 (cyclotomic n \u2124)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.prime_ne_two_norm_zeta_sub_one", "description": " If `irreducible (cyclotomic p K)` (in particular for `K = \u211a`) and `p` is an odd prime,\nthen the norm of `zeta p K L - 1` is `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.embeddings_equiv_primitive_roots_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_chaar_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.regular_of_is_add_left_invariant", "description": "To show that an invariant \u03c3-finite measure is regular it is sufficient to show that\nit is finite on some compact set with non-empty interior.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_prehaar_sup_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_measure_unique", "description": "The additive Haar measure is unique up to scaling. More precisely: every \u03c3-finite\nleft invariant measure is a scalar multiple of the additive Haar measure. This is slightly weaker\nthan assuming that `\u03bc` is an additive Haar measure (in particular we don't require `\u03bc \u2260 0`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.div_mem_nhds_one_of_haar_pos", "description": "**Steinhaus Theorem** In any locally compact group `G` with a haar measure `\u03bc`, for any\n measurable set `E` of positive measure, the set `E / E` is a neighbourhood of `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.is_left_invariant_add_chaar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.is_add_left_invariant_add_haar_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.prehaar_le_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_index_union_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_measure_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.is_left_invariant_prehaar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.le_add_index_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_haar_content_self", "description": "The variant of `add_chaar_self` for `add_haar_content`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.prehaar_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_chaar_sup_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_index_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_index_union_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_index_elim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_index_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.is_add_haar_measure_add_haar_measure", "description": "The additive Haar measure is an additive Haar measure, i.e., it is invariant and\ngives  finite mass to compact sets and positive mass to nonempty open sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar_measure_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_haar_product", "description": "additive version of `measure_theory.measure.haar.haar_product`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.haar_product", "description": "`haar_product K\u2080` is the product of intervals `[0, (K : K\u2080)]`, for all compact sets `K`.\n For all `U`, we can show that `prehaar K\u2080 U \u2208 haar_product K\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar_measure", "description": "The Haar measure on the locally compact group `G`, scaled so that `haar_measure K\u2080 K\u2080 = 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.index", "description": "The index or Haar covering number or ratio of `K` w.r.t. `V`, denoted `(K : V)`:\n it is the smallest number of (left) translates of `V` that is necessary to cover `K`.\n It is defined to be 0 if no finite number of translates cover `K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.is_haar_measure.is_inv_invariant", "description": "Any Haar measure is invariant under inversion in an abelian group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_prehaar_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.regular_haar_measure", "description": "The Haar measure is regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.is_add_haar_measure_eq_smul_is_add_haar_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.le_index_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.chaar", "description": "This is the \"limit\" of `prehaar K\u2080 U K` as `U` becomes a smaller and smaller open\n neighborhood of `(1 : G)`. More precisely, it is defined to be an arbitrary element\n in the intersection of all the sets `cl_prehaar K\u2080 V` in `haar_product K\u2080`.\n This is roughly equal to the Haar measure on compact sets,\n but it can differ slightly. We do know that\n `haar_measure K\u2080 (interior K) \u2264 chaar K\u2080 K \u2264 haar_measure K\u2080 K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.mem_prehaar_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.is_left_invariant_add_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.chaar_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.prehaar_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sub_mem_nhds_zero_of_add_haar_pos", "description": "**Steinhaus Theorem** In any locally compact group `G` with a haar measure `\u03bc`,\n  for any measurable set `E` of positive measure, the set `E - E` is a neighbourhood of `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.haar_content_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.index_union_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.prehaar_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.regular_add_haar_measure", "description": "The additive Haar measure is regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_chaar_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.index_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_haar_content_outer_measure_self_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_prehaar_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.regular_of_is_haar_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_index", "description": "additive version of `measure_theory.measure.haar.index`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.chaar_mem_cl_prehaar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.is_left_invariant_chaar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.chaar_sup_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.index_defined", "description": "If `K` is compact and `V` has nonempty interior, then the index `(K : V)` is well-defined,\n there is a finite set `t` satisfying the desired properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sigma_finite_haar_measure", "description": "The Haar measure is sigma-finite in a second countable group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.is_haar_measure_haar_measure", "description": " The Haar measure is a Haar measure, i.e., it is invariant and gives finite mass to compact\nsets and positive mass to nonempty open sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.nonempty_Inter_cl_add_prehaar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.haar_content", "description": "The function `chaar` interpreted in `\u211d\u22650`, as a content", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_chaar_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_preserving_zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.prehaar_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar", "description": "`add_haar` is some choice of a Haar measure, on a locally compact\nadditive group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_preserving.zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_preserving_zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_prehaar", "description": "additive version of `measure_theory.measure.haar.prehaar`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_prehaar_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.is_left_invariant_add_haar_content", "description": "The variant of `is_left_invariant_add_chaar` for `add_haar_content`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.mul_left_index_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.prehaar_mem_haar_product", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.chaar_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar", "description": "`haar` is some choice of a Haar measure, on a locally compact group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.chaar_mem_haar_product", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.is_left_invariant_add_prehaar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_chaar_mem_cl_add_prehaar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_prehaar_mem_add_haar_product", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar_measure_unique", "description": "The Haar measure is unique up to scaling. More precisely: every \u03c3-finite left invariant measure\n is a scalar multiple of the Haar measure.\n This is slightly weaker than assuming that `\u03bc` is a Haar measure (in particular we don't require\n `\u03bc \u2260 0`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_chaar_mem_add_haar_product", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_haar_content", "description": "additive version of `measure_theory.measure.haar.haar_content`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.is_mul_left_invariant_haar_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.haar_content_outer_measure_self_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_left_add_index_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.is_haar_measure_eq_smul_is_haar_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.chaar_sup_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.nonempty_Inter_cl_prehaar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.index_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_haar_content_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sigma_finite_add_haar_measure", "description": "The additive Haar measure is sigma-finite in a second countable group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.haar_content_self", "description": "The variant of `chaar_self` for `haar_content`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.prehaar_sup_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.index_union_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_prehaar_sup_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.prehaar", "description": "`prehaar K\u2080 U K` is a weighted version of the index, defined as `(K : U)/(K\u2080 : U)`.\n In the applications `K\u2080` is compact with non-empty interior, `U` is open containing `1`,\n and `K` is any compact set.\n The argument `K` is a (bundled) compact set, so that we can consider `prehaar K\u2080 U` as an\n element of `haar_product` (below).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar_measure_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.index_elim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_index_defined", "description": "If `K` is compact and `V` has nonempty interior, then the index\n`(K : V)` is well-defined, there is a finite set `t` satisfying the desired properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.chaar_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.mem_add_prehaar_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_prehaar_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.regular_of_is_mul_left_invariant", "description": "To show that an invariant \u03c3-finite measure is regular it is sufficient to show that it is finite\n on some compact set with non-empty interior.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.chaar_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.prehaar_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_chaar_sup_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.prehaar_sup_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.is_add_haar_measure.is_neg_invariant", "description": "Any additive Haar measure is invariant under negation in an abelian group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_prehaar_le_add_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_chaar_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.index_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.cl_add_prehaar", "description": "additive version of `measure_theory.measure.haar.cl_prehaar`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_chaar", "description": "additive version of `measure_theory.measure.haar.chaar`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_measure", "description": "The Haar measure on the locally compact additive group `G`,\nscaled so that `add_haar_measure K\u2080 K\u2080 = 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.is_left_invariant_haar_content", "description": "The variant of `is_left_invariant_chaar` for `haar_content`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.cl_prehaar", "description": "The closure of the collection of elements of the form `prehaar K\u2080 U`,\n for `U` open neighbourhoods of `1`, contained in `V`. The closure is taken in the space\n `compacts G \u2192 \u211d`, with the topology of pointwise convergence.\n We show that the intersection of all these sets is nonempty, and the Haar measure\n on compact sets is defined to be an element in the closure of this intersection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_preserving.zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.is_left_invariant_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.regular_of_is_add_haar_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_measure_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_prehaar_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.haar.add_index_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computation.parallel_promises", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computation.map_parallel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computation.terminates_parallel.aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computation.parallel", "description": "Parallel computation of an infinite stream of computations,\n taking the first result", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computation.parallel_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computation.parallel_congr_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computation.parallel_rec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computation.parallel_congr_lem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computation.exists_of_mem_parallel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computation.parallel.aux1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computation.mem_parallel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computation.terminates_parallel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computation.parallel_congr_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computation.parallel.aux2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.can_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.add_one_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat", "description": "Extended natural numbers `\u2115\u221e = with_top \u2115`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.to_nat_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.to_nat", "description": "Conversion of `\u2115\u221e` to `\u2115` sending `\u221e` to `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.le_of_lt_add_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.has_well_founded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.order_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.coe_to_nat_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.to_nat_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.has_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.has_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.to_nat_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.coe_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.succ_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.order_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.canonically_linear_ordered_add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.add_comm_monoid_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.one_le_iff_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.well_founded_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.linear_ordered_add_comm_monoid_with_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.to_nat_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.canonically_ordered_comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.char_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.has_ordered_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.succ_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.linear_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.has_lt.lt.is_well_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.to_nat_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.coe_to_nat_le_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.add_one_le_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.nat_induction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.coe_to_nat", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `enat.coe_to_nat_eq_self`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.coe_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.has_coe_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.one_le_iff_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "enat.has_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.fst_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.functions_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.functions_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.functions_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.functions_ext'", "description": "This is used as the ext lemma instead of `add_monoid_hom.functions_ext` for reasons explained in\nnote [partially-applied ext lemmas].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.list_sum_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_fn", "description": "An 'unapplied' analogue of `finset.sum_apply`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.fst_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.univ_sum_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.functions_ext'", "description": " This is used as the ext lemma instead of `monoid_hom.functions_ext` for reasons explained in\nnote [partially-applied ext lemmas].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod_mk_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.multiset_sum_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.univ_prod_mul_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.snd_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.sum_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_fn", "description": "An 'unapplied' analogue of `finset.prod_apply`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.multiset_prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.list_prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod_mk_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.snd_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_sum", "description": "Sum of a `s : multiset \u03b1` with `[add_monoid \u03b1]`, given a proof that `+` commutes\non all elements `x \u2208 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_prod_mul_distrib_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_sum_eq_card_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_sum_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_sum_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_sum", "description": "Sum of a `s : finset \u03b1` mapped with `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` with `[add_monoid \u03b2]`,\ngiven a proof that `+` commutes on all elements `f x` for `x \u2208 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_prod", "description": " Product of a `s : finset \u03b1` mapped with `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` with `[monoid \u03b2]`,\ngiven a proof that `*` commutes on all elements `f x` for `x \u2208 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_foldr_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_sum_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_prod_map_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_prod_eq_pow_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_sum_cons'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_sum_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_fold_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_sum_add_commute", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_sum_add_distrib", "description": "The non-commutative version of `finset.sum_add_distrib`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_prod_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_prod_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_sum_add_commute", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_sum_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_sum_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_foldr_eq_foldr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_prod_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_prod_mul_distrib", "description": "The non-commutative version of `finset.prod_mul_distrib`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_prod_commute", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_prod", "description": " Product of a `s : multiset \u03b1` with `[monoid \u03b1]`, given a proof that `*` commutes\non all elements `x \u2208 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_sum_insert_of_not_mem'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_sum_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_sum_add_distrib_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_prod_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_prod_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_fold_eq_fold", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_prod_mul_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_sum_eq_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_sum_union_of_disjoint", "description": "The non-commutative version of `finset.sum_union`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_prod_eq_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_foldr_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_foldr_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_sum_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_prod_insert_of_not_mem'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_prod_cons'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_sum_eq_card_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_prod_eq_pow_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_sum_map_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_prod_union_of_disjoint", "description": "The non-commutative version of `finset.prod_union`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_fold_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_sum_insert_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_prod_eq_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.pi_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_prod_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_prod_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_prod_insert_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_prod_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_sum_eq_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_prod_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_prod_commute", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.pi_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_sum_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_foldr", "description": " Fold of a `s : multiset \u03b1` with `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b2`, given a proof that `left_commutative f`\non all elements `x \u2208 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_sum_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_fold", "description": " Fold of a `s : multiset \u03b1` with an associative `op : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1`, given a proofs that `op`\nis commutative on all elements `x \u2208 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.noncomm_fold_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_sum_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.noncomm_prod_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like", "description": " The class `equiv_like E \u03b1 \u03b2` expresses that terms of type `E` have an\ninjective coercion to bijections between `\u03b1` and `\u03b2`.\n\nThis typeclass is used in the definition of the homomorphism typeclasses,\nsuch as `zero_equiv_class`, `mul_equiv_class`, `monoid_equiv_class`, ....", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.coe", "description": " The class `equiv_like E \u03b1 \u03b2` expresses that terms of type `E` have an\ninjective coercion to bijections between `\u03b1` and `\u03b2`.\n\nThis typeclass is used in the definition of the homomorphism typeclasses,\nsuch as `zero_equiv_class`, `mul_equiv_class`, `monoid_equiv_class`, ....", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.inv", "description": " The class `equiv_like E \u03b1 \u03b2` expresses that terms of type `E` have an\ninjective coercion to bijections between `\u03b1` and `\u03b2`.\n\nThis typeclass is used in the definition of the homomorphism typeclasses,\nsuch as `zero_equiv_class`, `mul_equiv_class`, `monoid_equiv_class`, ....", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.left_inv", "description": " The class `equiv_like E \u03b1 \u03b2` expresses that terms of type `E` have an\ninjective coercion to bijections between `\u03b1` and `\u03b2`.\n\nThis typeclass is used in the definition of the homomorphism typeclasses,\nsuch as `zero_equiv_class`, `mul_equiv_class`, `monoid_equiv_class`, ....", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.right_inv", "description": " The class `equiv_like E \u03b1 \u03b2` expresses that terms of type `E` have an\ninjective coercion to bijections between `\u03b1` and `\u03b2`.\n\nThis typeclass is used in the definition of the homomorphism typeclasses,\nsuch as `zero_equiv_class`, `mul_equiv_class`, `monoid_equiv_class`, ....", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.coe_injective'", "description": " The class `equiv_like E \u03b1 \u03b2` expresses that terms of type `E` have an\ninjective coercion to bijections between `\u03b1` and `\u03b2`.\n\nThis typeclass is used in the definition of the homomorphism typeclasses,\nsuch as `zero_equiv_class`, `mul_equiv_class`, `monoid_equiv_class`, ....", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.to_embedding_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.apply_eq_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.inv_apply_apply", "description": " This lemma is only supposed to be used in the generic context, when working with instances\nof classes extending `equiv_like`.\nFor concrete isomorphism types such as `equiv`, you should use `equiv.symm_apply_apply`\nor its equivalent.\n\nTODO: define a generic form of `equiv.symm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.apply_inv_apply", "description": " This lemma is only supposed to be used in the generic context, when working with instances\nof classes extending `equiv_like`.\nFor concrete isomorphism types such as `equiv`, you should use `equiv.apply_symm_apply`\nor its equivalent.\n\nTODO: define a generic form of `equiv.symm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.surjective_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.bijective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.inv_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.comp_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.bijective_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.comp_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.subsingleton_dom", "description": "This is not an instance to avoid slowing down every single `subsingleton` typeclass search.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.injective_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_like.comp_bijective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.pi", "description": " Given a finset `s` of `\u03b1` and for all `a : \u03b1` a finset `t a` of `\u03b4 a`, then one can define the\nfinset `s.pi t` of all functions defined on elements of `s` taking values in `t a` for `a \u2208 s`.\nNote that the elements of `s.pi t` are only partially defined, on `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.pi.cons_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mem_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.pi.cons_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.pi_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.pi.cons_same", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.pi.empty", "description": " The empty dependent product function, defined on the empty set. The assumption `a \u2208 \u2205` is never\nsatisfied.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.pi.cons", "description": " Given a function `f` defined on a finset `s`, define a new function on the finset `s \u222a {a}`,\nequal to `f` on `s` and sending `a` to a given value `b`. This function is denoted\n`s.pi.cons a b f`. If `a` already belongs to `s`, the new function takes the value `b` at `a`\nanyway.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.pi_const_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.pi_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.pi_disjoint_of_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.pi_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.pi_singletons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.pi_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computability.left_inverse_section_inclusion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computability.decode_bool", "description": "A decoding function from `list bool` to bool.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computability.unary_decode_encode_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computability.inhabited_encoding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computability.\u0393'.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computability.encoding", "description": "An encoding of a type in a certain alphabet, together with a decoding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computability.encoding.\u0393", "description": "An encoding of a type in a certain alphabet, together with a decoding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computability.encoding.encode", "description": "An encoding of a type in a certain alphabet, together with a decoding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computability.encoding.decode", "description": "An encoding of a type in a certain alphabet, together with a decoding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computab