 proposition", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.or", "description": "bitwise or", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.bits_to_nat", "description": "Given a `list` of `bool`s, return the `nat` they represent as a list of binary digits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.not", "description": "bitwise not", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.to_nat", "description": "Return the natural number encoded by the input bitvector", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.fill_shr", "description": " `fill_shr x i fill` is the bitvector obtained by right-shifting `x` `i` times and then\npadding with `fill : bool`. If `x.length < i` then this will return the constant `fill`\nbitvector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.ule", "description": "unsigned less-than-or-equal-to proposition", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.append", "description": "`bitvec` specific version of `vector.append`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.to_int", "description": "Return the integer encoded by the input bitvector", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.sle", "description": "signed less-than-or-equal-to proposition", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.sgt", "description": "signed greater-than proposition", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.ugt", "description": "unsigned greater-than proposition", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.sge", "description": "signed greater-than-or-equal-to proposition", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.mul", "description": "The product of two bitvectors", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.ushr", "description": "unsigned shift right", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.sshr", "description": "signed shift right", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.sub", "description": "The difference of two bitvectors", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.adc", "description": "Add with carry (no overflow)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.bits_to_nat_to_list", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.ugt.decidable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.sbb", "description": "Subtract with borrow", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.has_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.of_int", "description": "Create a bitvector in the two's complement representation from an `int`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.of_nat", "description": "Create a bitvector from a `nat`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.to_nat_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.uge", "description": "unsigned greater-than-or-equal-to proposition", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.neg", "description": "`neg x` is the two's complement of `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.zero", "description": "Create a zero bitvector", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.shl", "description": " `shl x i` is the bitvector obtained by left-shifting `x` `i` times and padding with `ff`.\nIf `x.length < i` then this will return the all-`ff`s bitvector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.to_nat_of_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.xor3", "description": "`xor3 x y c` is `((x XOR y) XOR c)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.sborrow", "description": "`sborrow x y` returns `tt` iff `x < y` as two's complement integers", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.bits_to_nat_to_bool", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitvec.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.inf_eq_map_pullback", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.factors_left_of_inf_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.bot_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.semilattice_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.bot_coe_iso_zero", "description": "The object underlying `\u22a5 : subobject B` is (up to isomorphism) the zero object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.pullback_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.Sup", "description": " When `[well_powered C] [has_images C] [has_coproducts C]`,\n`subobject A` has arbitrary supremums.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.map_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.inf_map", "description": "`\u2293` commutes with map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.bounded_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.top_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.Inf", "description": "When `[well_powered C]` and `[has_wide_pullbacks C]`, `subobject A` has arbitrary infimums.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.underlying_iso_inv_top_arrow_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.small_coproduct_desc", "description": "The univesal morphism out of the coproduct of a set of subobjects,\nafter using `[well_powered C]` to reindex by a small type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.bot_eq_initial_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.complete_semilattice_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.le_Inf_cone_\u03c0_app_none", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.inf", "description": "The functorial infimum on `mono_over A` descends to an infimum on `subobject A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.is_iso_arrow_iff_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.top_le_pullback_self", "description": " There is a morphism from `\u22a4 : mono_over A` to the pullback of a monomorphism along itself;\nas the category is thin this is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.factors_right_of_inf_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.map_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.le_inf", "description": "A morphism version of the `le_inf` axiom.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.sup_le", "description": "A morphism version of `sup_le`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.inf_arrow_factors_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.finset_inf_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.le_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.has_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.sup_factors_of_factors_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.mk_eq_top_of_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.top_eq_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.sup", "description": " When `[has_images C] [has_binary_coproducts C]`, `mono_over A` has a `sup` construction,\nwhich is functorial in both arguments,\nand which on `subobject A` will induce a `semilattice_sup`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.pullback_self", "description": "The pullback of a monomorphism along itself is isomorphic to the top object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.bot_le", "description": "The (unique) morphism from `\u22a5 : mono_over X` to any other `f : mono_over X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.bot_factors_iff_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.underlying_iso_inv_top_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.le_Inf_cone", "description": "Auxiliary construction of a cone for `le_Inf`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.underlying_iso_top_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.sup", "description": "The functorial supremum on `mono_over A` descends to an supremum on `subobject A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.inf_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.functor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.subobject_order_iso", "description": "The subobject lattice of a subobject `Y` is order isomorphic to the interval `set.Iic Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.semilattice_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.Inf_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.wide_pullback", "description": "The limit of `wide_cospan s`. (This will be the supremum of the set of subobjects.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.bot_coe_iso_initial", "description": "The object underlying `\u22a5 : subobject B` is (up to isomorphism) the initial object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.finset_inf_arrow_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.is_iso_top_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.le_top", "description": "The morphism to the top object in `mono_over X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.le_Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.inf_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.wide_pullback_\u03b9", "description": "The inclusion map from `wide_pullback s` to `A`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.wide_cospan", "description": "The \"wide cospan\" diagram, with a small indexing type, constructed from a set of subobjects.\n(This is just the diagram of all the subobjects pasted together, but using `well_powered C`\nto make the diagram small.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.complete_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.wide_pullback_\u03b9_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.complete_semilattice_Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.functor", "description": "Sending `X : C` to `subobject X` is a contravariant functor `C\u1d52\u1d56 \u2964 Type`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.nontrivial_of_not_is_zero", "description": "A nonzero object has nontrivial subobject lattice.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.bot_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.is_iso_iff_mk_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.bot_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.le_sup_right", "description": "A morphism version of `le_sup_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.bot_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.order_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.pullback_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.finset_sup_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.sup_factors_of_factors_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.inf_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.top_arrow_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.wide_cospan_map_term", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.le_sup_left", "description": "A morphism version of `le_sup_left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.top_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.prod_eq_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.le_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.mk_eq_bot_iff_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.map_bot", "description": "`map f` sends `\u22a5 : mono_over X` to `\u22a5 : mono_over Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.inf_arrow_factors_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.pullback_top", "description": " The pullback of the top object in `mono_over Y`\nis (isomorphic to) the top object in `mono_over X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.inf_le_right", "description": "A morphism from the \"infimum\" of two objects in `mono_over A` to the second object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.symm_apply_mem_iff_mem_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.order_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.bot_arrow_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.bot_coe_iso_zero", "description": "The object underlying `\u22a5 : subobject B` is (up to isomorphism) the zero object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.map_top", "description": "`map f` sends `\u22a4 : mono_over X` to `\u27e8X, f\u27e9 : mono_over Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.inf_le_left", "description": "A morphism from the \"infimum\" of two objects in `mono_over A` to the first object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.Sup_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.inf_pullback", "description": "`\u2293` commutes with pullback.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.has_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.inf_le_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.eq_top_of_is_iso_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.inf_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.top_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.inf_eq_map_pullback'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.subobject.inf_le_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_over.inf", "description": "When `[has_pullbacks C]`, `mono_over A` has \"intersections\", functorial in both arguments.\n\nAs `mono_over A` is only a preorder, this doesn't satisfy the axioms of `semilattice_inf`,\nbut we reuse all the names from `semilattice_inf` because they will be used to construct\n`semilattice_inf (subobject A)` shortly.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.exists_mul_vec_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.range_to_lin_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.nondegenerate.det_ne_zero", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `matrix.nondegenerate_iff_det_ne_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.nondegenerate_iff_det_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_linear_equiv'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.nondegenerate.of_det_ne_zero", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `matrix.nondegenerate_iff_det_ne_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_linear_equiv'_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_linear_equiv'", "description": " An invertible matrix yields a linear equivalence from the free module to itself.\n\nSee `matrix.to_linear_equiv` for the same map on arbitrary modules.",