"measure_theory.measure.tprod_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.volume_preserving_pi_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.sigma_finite_tprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.pi_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_countably_spanning.pi", "description": "Boxes of countably spanning sets are countably spanning.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pi.is_inv_invariant_volume", "description": " We intentionally restrict this only to the nondependent function space, since type-class\ninference cannot find an instance for `\u03b9 \u2192 \u211d` when this is stated for dependent function spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system.pi", "description": "Boxes formed by \u03c0-systems form a \u03c0-system.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pi_premeasure_pi_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_pi", "description": "Boxes form a \u03c0-system.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_pi_equiv_pi_subtype_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.tprod", "description": "A product of measures in `tprod \u03b1 l`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.univ_pi_Ioo_ae_eq_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.pi.is_inv_invariant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pi.is_add_left_invariant_volume", "description": "We intentionally restrict this only to the nondependent function space, since\ntype-class inference cannot find an instance for `\u03b9 \u2192 \u211d` when this is stated for dependent function\nspaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.pi.measure_theory.has_no_atoms", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.pi", "description": "`measure.pi \u03bc` is the finite product of the measures `{\u03bc i | i : \u03b9}`.\n It is