le_same", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.coe_to_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.inner_product_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.dist_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis", "description": " An orthonormal basis on E is an identification of `E` with its dimensional-matching\n`euclidean_space \ud835\udd5c \u03b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.repr", "description": " An orthonormal basis on E is an identification of `E` with its dimensional-matching\n`euclidean_space \ud835\udd5c \u03b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.equiv_to_linear_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_Lp.equiv_symm_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.dist_single_same", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finrank_euclidean_space_fin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.nnnorm_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.is_internal.sigma_orthonormal_basis_index_equiv", "description": " Exhibit a bijection between `fin n` and the index set of a certain basis of an `n`-dimensional\ninner product space `E`.  This should not be accessed directly, but only via the subsequent API.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.proj\u2097", "description": "The projection on the `i`-th coordinate of `euclidean_space \ud835\udd5c \u03b9`, as a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.to_basis_to_orthonormal_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.extend", "description": " Let `S` be a subspace of a finite-dimensional complex inner product space `V`.  A linear\nisometry mapping `S` into `V` can be extended to a full isometry of `V`.\n\nTODO:  The case when `S` is a finite-dimensional subspace of an infinite-dimensional `V`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.to_matrix_orthonormal_basis_mem_unitary", "description": "The change-of-basis matrix between two orthonormal bases `a`, `b` is a unitary matrix.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "`b i` is the `i`th basis vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.repr_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.single", "description": " The vector given in euclidean space by being `1 : \ud835\udd5c` at coordinate `i : \u03b9` and `0 : \ud835\udd5c` at\nall other coordinates.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space", "description": " The standard real/complex Euclidean space, functions on a finite type. For an `n`-dimensional\nspace use `euclidean_space \ud835\udd5c (fin n)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coe_to_orthonormal_basis_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.nnnorm_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.proj_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.is_internal.collected_orthonormal_basis", "description": " Given an internal direct sum decomposition of a module `M`, and an orthonormal basis for each\nof the components of the direct sum, the disjoint union of these orthonormal bases is an\northonormal basis for `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.coe_to_basis_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.finite_dimensional", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.single_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_Lp.inner_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coe_to_orthonormal_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.map", "description": "Mapping an orthonormal basis along a `linear_isometry_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.norm_