ormal.exists_orthonormal_basis_extension_of_card_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.to_basis", "description": "The `basis \u03b9 \ud835\udd5c E` underlying the `orthonormal_basis`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.orthonormal_basis_one_I_repr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.coe_orthonormal_basis_one_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.sum_inner_mul_inner", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.edist_single_same", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.sum_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_euclidean_lin", "description": "`matrix.to_lin'` adapted for `euclidean_space \ud835\udd5c _`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.is_internal.subordinate_orthonormal_basis_index", "description": " An `n`-dimensional `inner_product_space` equipped with a decomposition as an internal direct\nsum has an orthonormal basis indexed by `fin n` and subordinate to that direct sum. This function\nprovides the mapping by which it is subordinate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.is_internal.subordinate_orthonormal_basis", "description": " An `n`-dimensional `inner_product_space` equipped with a decomposition as an internal direct\nsum has an orthonormal basis indexed by `fin n` and subordinate to that direct sum.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.is_internal.collected_orthonormal_basis_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.sum_repr_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coe_to_orthonormal_basis_repr_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.inner_single_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "std_orthonormal_basis", "description": "A finite-dimensional `inner_product_space` has an orthonormal basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.inner_eq_star_dot_product", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.from_orthogonal_span_singleton", "description": " Given a natural number `n` one less than the `finrank` of a finite-dimensional inner product\nspace, there exists an isometry from the orthogonal complement of a nonzero singleton to\n`euclidean_space \ud835\udd5c (fin n)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.coe_of_orthogonal_eq_bot_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.equiv_to_linear_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.det_to_matrix_orthonormal_basis_real", "description": "The determinant of the change-of-basis matrix between two orthonormal bases `a`, `b` is \u00b11.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.inner_pi_Lp_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.pi_Lp_equiv_to_euclidean_lin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.span", "description": "Any finite subset of a orthonormal family is an `orthonormal_basis` for its span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.to_matrix_orthonormal_basis_mem_orthogonal", "description": "The change-of-basis matrix between two orthonormal bases `a`, `b` is an orthogonal matrix.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.inner_single_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.coe_reindex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.reindex", "description": "`b.reindex (e : \u03b9 \u2243 \u03b9')` is an `orthonormal_basis` indexed by `\u03b9'`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.repr_reindex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.norm_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.det_to_matrix_orthonormal_basis", "description": " The determinant of the change-of-basis matrix between two orthonormal bases `a`, `b` has\nunit length.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.orthonormal_basis_one_I", "description": "`![1, I]` is an orthonormal basis for `\u2102` considered as a real inner product space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.to_basis_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.span_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_space.proj", "description": " The projection on the `i`-th coordinate of `euclidean_space \ud835\udd5c \u03b9`,\nas a continuous linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.to_orthonormal_basis", "description": "A basis that is orthonormal is an orthonormal basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_char_neg_two", "description": "The value of the quadratic character at `-2`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_char_two", "description": "The value of the quadratic character at `2`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_char_card_card", "description": " The relation between the values of the quadratic character of one field `F` at the\ncardinality of another field `F'` and of the quadratic character of `F'` at the cardinality\nof `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_field.is_square_two_iff", "description": "`2` is a square in `F` iff `#F` is not congruent to `3` or `5` mod `8`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_char_odd_prime", "description": "The value of the quadratic character at an odd prime `p` different from `ring_char F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_field.is_square_neg_two_iff", "description": "`-2` is a square in `F` iff `#F` is not congruent to `5` or `7` mod `8`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_field.is_square_odd_prime_iff", "description": " An odd prime `p` is a square in `F` iff the quadratic character of `zmod p` does not\ntake the value `-1` on `\u03c7\u2084(#F) * #F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.add_omega_opow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.principal_mul_omega", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}