"description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_div_pow_anti", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_div_lt_one_div_of_neg", "description": "For the single implications with fewer assumptions, see `one_div_lt_one_div_of_lt` and\n `lt_of_one_div_lt_one_div`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_mul_lt_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "div_neg_of_neg_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_glb.mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "div_neg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_of_forall_sub_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_div_lt_of_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "half_le_self", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `half_le_self_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_mul_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "div_two_lt_of_pos", "description": "**Alias** of `half_lt_self`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_glb.mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "div_lt_div_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_lt_one_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_div_le_one_div_of_neg", "description": "For the single implications with fewer assumptions, see `one_div_lt_one_div_of_neg_of_lt` and\n `lt_of_one_div_lt_one_div`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_sub_div_two_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_lt", "description": " In a linear ordered field, for positive `a` and `b` we have `a\u207b\u00b9 < b \u2194 b\u207b\u00b9 < a`.\nSee also `inv_lt_of_inv_lt` for a one-sided implication with one fewer assumption.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_sub_mul_div_mul_neg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "half_lt_self_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_div_le_neg_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "div_lt_div_of_mul_sub_mul_div_neg", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `mul_sub_mul_div_mul_neg_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lt_inv_of_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_pow_anti", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "div_le_of_nonneg_of_le_mul", "description": "One direction of `div_le_iff` where `b` is allowed to be `0` (but `c` must be nonnegative)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zpow_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.mod_div_aux", "description": "We define `m % k` and `m / k` in the same way as for `\u2115`\n except that when `m = n * k` we take `m % k = k` and\n `m / k = n - 1`.  This ensures that `m % k` is always positive\n and `m = (m % k) + k * (m / k)` in all cases.  Later we\n define a function `div_exact` which gives the usual `m / k`\n in the case where `k` divides `m`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.to_pnat'_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.has_well_founded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.one_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat", "description": "`\u2115+` is the type of positive natural numbers. It is defined as a subtype,\n and the VM representation of `\u2115+` is the same as `\u2115` because the proof\n is not stored.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.can_lift_pnat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.mod_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.mk_le_mk", "description": "We now define a long list of structures on \u2115+ induced by\nsimilar structures on \u2115. Most of these behave in a completely\nobvious way, but there are a few things to be said about\nsubtraction, division and powers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.nat_pred_eq_pred", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.mk_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.coe_eq_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "coe_pnat_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.coe_le_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.nat_pred", "description": "Predecessor of a `\u2115+`, as a `\u2115`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.one_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.to_pnat", "description": "Convert a natural number to a positive natural number. The\n positivity assumption is inferred by `dec_trivial`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.to_pnat'", "description": "Convert a natural number to a pnat. `n+1` is mapped to itself,\n and `0` becomes `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.succ_pnat_nat_pred", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.not_lt_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.div_exact", "description": "If `h : k | m`, then `k * (div_exact m k) = m`. Note that this is not equal to `m / k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne_zero.pnat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.coe_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.mod", "description": "We define `m % k` in the same way as for `\u2115`\n except that when `m = n * k` we take `m % k = k` This ensures that `m % k` is always positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.coe_lt_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.mk_lt_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.mod_div", "description": "`mod_div m k = (m % k, m / k)`.\n We define `m % k` and `m / k` in the same way as for `\u2115`\n except that when `m = n * k` we take `m % k = k` and\n `m / k = n - 1`.  This ensures that `m % k` is always positive\n and `m = (m % k) + k * (m / k)` in all cases.  Later we\n define a function `div_exact` which gives the usual `m / k`\n in the case where `k` divides `m`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.coe_to_pnat'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.div_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.nat_pred_succ_pnat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.linear_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.has_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.succ_pnat", "description": "Write a successor as an element of `\u2115+`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.div", "description": "We define `m / k` in the same way as for `\u2115` except that when `m = n * k` we take\n `m / k = n - 1`. This ensures that `m = (m % k) + k * (m / k)` in all cases. Later we\n define a function `div_exact` which gives the usual `m / k` in the case where `k` divides `m`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.can_lift_pnat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.succ_pnat_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.to_pnat'_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.strong_induction_on", "description": "Strong induction on `\u2115+`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.integral_clm", "description": "The Bochner integral over simple functions in L1 space as a continuous linear map over \u211d.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.integral_clm", "description": "The Bochner integral in L1 space as a continuous linear map over \u211d.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_simple_func_larger_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.tendsto_set_integral_nhds_zero", "description": " If `f` is integrable, then `\u222b x in s, f x \u2202\u03bc` is absolutely continuous in `s`: it tends\nto zero as `\u03bc s` tends to zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.snorm_one_le_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.coe_to_larger_space_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.integral_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.has_sum_integral_of_dominated_convergence", "description": "Lebesgue dominated convergence theorem for series.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.tendsto_integral_of_dominated_convergence", "description": "Lebesgue dominated convergence theorem provides sufficient conditions under which almost\n everywhere convergence of a sequence of functions implies the convergence of their integrals.\n We could weaken the condition `bound_integrable` to require `has_finite_integral bound \u03bc` instead\n (i.e. not requiring that `bound` is measurable), but in all applications proving integrability\n is easier.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.continuous_of_dominated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.integral_eq_norm_pos_part_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.has_sum_integral_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.weighted_smul_union'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.integral_eq_set_to_L1s", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_non_ae_strongly_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.has_finite_integral.tendsto_set_integral_nhds_zero", "description": " If `f` has finite integral, then `\u222b x in s, f x \u2202\u03bc` is absolutely continuous in `s`: it tends\nto zero as `\u03bc s` tends to zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.norm_integral_le_lintegral_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.continuous_on_of_dominated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_eq_integral_pos_part_sub_integral_neg_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving.integral_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.integral", "description": "The Bochner integral over simple functions in L1 space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.integral_eq_sum_of_subset", "description": "The Bochner integral is equal to a sum over any set that includes `f.range` (except `0`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.pos_part_sub_neg_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_nonpos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_le_trim_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.weighted_smul_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.neg_part", "description": "Negative part of a simple function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.norm_integral_le_integral_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.norm_integral_le_of_norm_le_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.lintegral_coe_eq_integral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.integral_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.weighted_smul_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_trim_simple_func", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_mono_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.integral_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.weighted_smul", "description": " Given a set `s`, return the continuous linear map `\u03bb x, (\u03bc s).to_real \u2022 x`. The extension of\nthat set function through `set_to_L1` gives the Bochner integral of L1 functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.continuous_integral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.integral_eq_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_neg'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.pos_part_map_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.integral_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.integral_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_eq_lintegral_pos_part_sub_lintegral_neg_part", "description": "The Bochner integral of a real-valued function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u211d` is the difference between the\n integral of the positive part of `f` and the integral of the negative part of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_dirac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.integral_eq_sum_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.norm_Integral_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.integral_clm'", "description": "The Bochner integral in L1 space as a continuous linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.weighted_smul_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.weighted_smul_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_eq_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.integral_eq_norm_pos_part_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral", "description": "The Bochner integral", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.integral_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.pos_part_to_simple_func", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.tendsto_integral_approx_on_of_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.integral_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_of_integral_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.weighted_smul_null", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.norm_set_to_simple_func_le_integral_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.continuous_within_at_of_dominated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_add'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.weighted_smul_smul_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_sum_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_finset_sum_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.snorm_one_le_of_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.mem_\u2112p.snorm_eq_integral_rpow_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.mul_meas_ge_le_integral_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.integral_piecewise_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.integral_eq_lintegral'", "description": "`simple_func.integral` and `simple_func.lintegral` agree when the integrand has type\n   `\u03b1 \u2192\u209b \u211d\u22650\u221e`. But since `\u211d\u22650\u221e` is not a `normed_space`, we need some form of coercion.\n   See `integral_eq_lintegral` for a simpler version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_mul_le_Lp_mul_Lq_of_nonneg", "description": " H\u00f6lder's inequality for functions `\u03b1 \u2192 \u211d`. The integral of the product of two nonnegative\nfunctions is bounded by the product of their `\u2112p` and `\u2112q` seminorms when `p` and `q` are conjugate\nexponents.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_pos_iff_support_of_nonneg_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_pos_iff_support_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.pos_part", "description": "Positive part of a simple function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.integral_L1_eq_integral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.lintegral_coe_le_coe_iff_integral_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.tendsto_integral_approx_on_of_measurable_of_range_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.norm_integral_le_of_norm_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.of_real_integral_eq_lintegral_of_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.integral_eq_lintegral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_map_of_strongly_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_mul_norm_le_Lp_mul_Lq", "description": " H\u00f6lder's inequality for the integral of a product of norms. The integral of the product of two\nnorms of functions is bounded by the product of their `\u2112p` and `\u2112q` seminorms when `p` and `q` are\nconjugate exponents.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.neg_part_map_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.integral_eq_integral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_coe_le_of_lintegral_coe_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.coe_pos_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.continuous_integral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_congr_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.norm_weighted_smul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_dirac'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.to_larger_space", "description": "Simple function seen as simple function of a larger `measurable_space`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_eq_trim_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.dominated_fin_meas_additive_weighted_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_eq_set_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_trim_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_add_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_trim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_sub'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_to_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.norm_Integral_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_undef", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_nonneg_of_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.norm_of_fun_eq_integral_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.integral_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.integral_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_le_trim_of_strongly_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.integral_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.integral_add_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.neg_part_to_simple_func", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_eq_zero_iff_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_nonpos_of_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_dirac'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.norm_eq_integral_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closed_embedding.integral_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_mono_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.continuous_at_of_dominated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.integral_eq_integral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.norm_integral_le_integral_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_smul_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_zero_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.weighted_smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_eq_lintegral_of_nonneg_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.weighted_smul_zero_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_eq_zero_iff_of_nonneg_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.integral_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.integral", "description": "The Bochner integral in L1 space", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.map_integral", "description": "Calculate the integral of `g \u2218 f : \u03b1 \u2192\u209b F`, where `f` is an integrable function from `\u03b1` to `E`\n   and `g` is a function from `E` to `F`. We require `g 0 = 0` so that `g \u2218 f` is integrable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_embedding.integral_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ennnorm_integral_le_lintegral_ennnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.integral_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.tendsto_integral_filter_of_dominated_convergence", "description": "Lebesgue dominated convergence theorem for filters with a countable basis", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_dirac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.norm_integral_le_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_eq_trim_of_strongly_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.integral_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.integral_eq_set_to_L1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_norm_eq_lintegral_nnnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.of_real_integral_norm_eq_lintegral_nnnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.integral_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_mono_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.norm_integral_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.norm_eq_integral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.weighted_smul_add_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.nndist_integral_add_measure_le_lintegral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_tsum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.integral_clm'", "description": "The Bochner integral over simple functions in L1 space as a continuous linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.weighted_smul_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.integral_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.pos_part", "description": "Positive part of a simple function in L1 space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.tendsto_integral_of_L1", "description": "If `F i \u2192 f` in `L1`, then `\u222b x, F i x \u2202\u03bc \u2192 \u222b x, f x \u2202\u03bc`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.coe_neg_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.integral_of_fun_eq_integral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.integral", "description": " Bochner integral of simple functions whose codomain is a real `normed_space`.\nThis is equal to `\u2211 x in f.range, (\u03bc (f \u207b\u00b9' {x})).to_real \u2022 x` (see `integral_eq`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_eq_zero_of_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.integral_eq_integral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.L1.simple_func.neg_part", "description": "Negative part of a simple function in L1 space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_map_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.integral_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.integral_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.simple_func.integral_eq_lintegral", "description": "`simple_func.bintegral` and `simple_func.integral` agree when the integrand has type\n   `\u03b1 \u2192\u209b \u211d\u22650\u221e`. But since `\u211d\u22650\u221e` is not a `normed_space`, we need some form of coercion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.hom_equiv_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.has_coe_to_sort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.ihom_obj_\u03c1_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.left_regular_hom_equiv", "description": " Given a `k`-linear `G`-representation `A`, there is a `k`-linear isomorphism between\nrepresentation morphisms `Hom(k[G], A)` and `A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.ihom", "description": " Given a `k`-linear `G`-representation `(A, \u03c1\u2081)`, this is the 'internal Hom' functor sending\n`(B, \u03c1\u2082)` to the representation `Hom\u2096(A, B)` that maps `g : G` and `f : A \u2192\u2097[k] B` to\n`(\u03c1\u2082 g) \u2218\u2097 f \u2218\u2097 (\u03c1\u2081 g\u207b\u00b9)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.of_Module_monoid_algebra_obj_\u03c1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.left_regular", "description": "The `k`-linear `G`-representation on `k[G]`, induced by left multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.linearization_of_mul_action_iso", "description": " The linearization of a type `H` with a `G`-action is definitionally isomorphic to the\n`k`-linear `G`-representation on `k[H]` induced by the `G`-action on `H`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.diagonal", "description": "The `k`-linear `G`-representation on `k[G\u207f]`, induced by left multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.\u03c1_self_inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.\u03c1", "description": "Specialize the existing `Action.\u03c1`, changing the type to `representation k G V`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.category_theory.monoidal_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.left_regular_hom_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.has_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.preadditive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.counit_iso", "description": "Auxilliary definition for `equivalence_Module_monoid_algebra`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.left_regular_hom", "description": " Given an element `x : A`, there is a natural morphism of representations `k[G] \u27f6 A` sending\n`g \u21a6 A.\u03c1(g)(x).`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.linearization_\u03b5_inv_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.to_Module_monoid_algebra_map", "description": "Auxilliary definition for `to_Module_monoid_algebra`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.hom_equiv", "description": " Given a `k`-linear `G`-representation `A`, this is the Hom-set bijection in the adjunction\n`A \u2297 - \u22a3 ihom(A, -)`. It sends `f : A \u2297 B \u27f6 C` to a `Rep k G` morphism defined by currying the\n`k`-linear map underlying `f`, giving a map `A \u2192\u2097[k] B \u2192\u2097[k] C`, then flipping the arguments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.ihom_ev_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.to_Module_monoid_algebra", "description": "Functorially convert a representation of `G` into a module over `monoid_algebra k G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.ihom_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "representation.Rep_of_tprod_iso_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.of_\u03c1_apply", "description": " Allows us to apply lemmas about the underlying `\u03c1`, which would take an element `g : G` rather\nthan `g : Mon.of G` as an argument.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "representation.Rep_of_tprod_iso_inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.monoidal_closed.linear_hom_equiv", "description": " There is a `k`-linear isomorphism between the sets of representation morphisms`Hom(A \u2297 B, C)`\nand `Hom(B, Hom\u2096(A, C))`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.linearization_\u03b5_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.abelian", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.large_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.of_\u03c1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.monoidal_category.braiding_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.category_theory.linear", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.linearization_trivial_iso_inv_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.ihom_obj_\u03c1_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.monoidal_closed.linear_hom_equiv_comm_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.of_mul_action", "description": " Given a `G`-action on `H`, this is `k[H]` bundled with the natural representation\n`G \u2192* End(k[H])` as a term of type `Rep k G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.has_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.equivalence_Module_monoid_algebra", "description": "The categorical equivalence `Rep k G \u224c Module (monoid_algebra k G)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.left_regular_hom_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.Action_\u03c1_eq_\u03c1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.linearization_\u03bc_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.counit_iso_add_equiv", "description": "Auxilliary definition for `equivalence_Module_monoid_algebra`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.of", "description": "Lift an unbundled representation to `Rep`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.\u03c1_inv_self_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.linearization_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.to_Module_monoid_algebra_map_aux", "description": "Auxilliary lemma for `to_Module_monoid_algebra`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.left_regular_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.linearization_obj_\u03c1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.monoidal_closed.linear_hom_equiv_symm_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.monoidal_category.braiding_inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep", "description": "The category of `k`-linear representations of a monoid `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.coe_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.concrete_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.linearization_\u03bc_inv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.monoidal_closed.linear_hom_equiv_comm", "description": " There is a `k`-linear isomorphism between the sets of representation morphisms`Hom(A \u2297 B, C)`\nand `Hom(A, Hom\u2096(B, C))`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.hom_equiv_apply_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.trivial", "description": "The trivial `k`-linear `G`-representation on a `k`-module `V.`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.monoidal_closed.linear_hom_equiv_comm_symm_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.monoidal_closed.linear_hom_equiv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.hom_equiv_symm_apply_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.ihom_coev_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.unit_iso", "description": "Auxilliary definition for `equivalence_Module_monoid_algebra`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.of_Module_monoid_algebra", "description": "Functorially convert a module over `monoid_algebra k G` into a representation of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.linearization_map_hom_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.unit_iso_add_equiv", "description": "Auxilliary definition for `equivalence_Module_monoid_algebra`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.of_Module_monoid_algebra_obj_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.trivial_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.linearization", "description": " The monoidal functor sending a type `H` with a `G`-action to the induced `k`-linear\n`G`-representation on `k[H].`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.left_regular_hom_equiv_symm_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.linearization_map_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.left_regular_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.ihom_map_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.hom_comm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "representation.Rep_of_tprod_iso", "description": "Tautological isomorphism to help Lean in typechecking.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.unit_iso_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.linearization_trivial_iso", "description": " The linearization of a type `X` on which `G` acts trivially is the trivial `G`-representation\non `k[X]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Rep.linearization_trivial_iso_hom_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.has_strict_fderiv_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.tendsto_implicit_function", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.implicit_function", "description": "Implicit function `g` defined by `f (g z y) = z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.mem_implicit_to_local_homeomorph_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.eq_implicit_function_of_complemented", "description": " Any point in some neighborhood of `a` can be represented as `implicit_function`\nof some point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.mem_implicit_to_local_homeomorph_of_complemented_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.implicit_function_of_complemented_apply_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.implicit_to_local_homeomorph_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data", "description": " Data for the general version of the implicit function theorem. It holds two functions\n`f : E \u2192 F` and `g : E \u2192 G` (named `left_fun` and `right_fun`) and a point `a` (named `pt`)\nsuch that\n\n* both functions are strictly differentiable at `a`;\n* the derivatives are surjective;\n* the kernels of the derivatives are complementary subspaces of `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.left_fun", "description": " Data for the general version of the implicit function theorem. It holds two functions\n`f : E \u2192 F` and `g : E \u2192 G` (named `left_fun` and `right_fun`) and a point `a` (named `pt`)\nsuch that\n\n* both functions are strictly differentiable at `a`;\n* the derivatives are surjective;\n* the kernels of the derivatives are complementary subspaces of `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.left_deriv", "description": " Data for the general version of the implicit function theorem. It holds two functions\n`f : E \u2192 F` and `g : E \u2192 G` (named `left_fun` and `right_fun`) and a point `a` (named `pt`)\nsuch that\n\n* both functions are strictly differentiable at `a`;\n* the derivatives are surjective;\n* the kernels of the derivatives are complementary subspaces of `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.right_fun", "description": " Data for the general version of the implicit function theorem. It holds two functions\n`f : E \u2192 F` and `g : E \u2192 G` (named `left_fun` and `right_fun`) and a point `a` (named `pt`)\nsuch that\n\n* both functions are strictly differentiable at `a`;\n* the derivatives are surjective;\n* the kernels of the derivatives are complementary subspaces of `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.right_deriv", "description": " Data for the general version of the implicit function theorem. It holds two functions\n`f : E \u2192 F` and `g : E \u2192 G` (named `left_fun` and `right_fun`) and a point `a` (named `pt`)\nsuch that\n\n* both functions are strictly differentiable at `a`;\n* the derivatives are surjective;\n* the kernels of the derivatives are complementary subspaces of `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.pt", "description": " Data for the general version of the implicit function theorem. It holds two functions\n`f : E \u2192 F` and `g : E \u2192 G` (named `left_fun` and `right_fun`) and a point `a` (named `pt`)\nsuch that\n\n* both functions are strictly differentiable at `a`;\n* the derivatives are surjective;\n* the kernels of the derivatives are complementary subspaces of `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.left_has_deriv", "description": " Data for the general version of the implicit function theorem. It holds two functions\n`f : E \u2192 F` and `g : E \u2192 G` (named `left_fun` and `right_fun`) and a point `a` (named `pt`)\nsuch that\n\n* both functions are strictly differentiable at `a`;\n* the derivatives are surjective;\n* the kernels of the derivatives are complementary subspaces of `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.right_has_deriv", "description": " Data for the general version of the implicit function theorem. It holds two functions\n`f : E \u2192 F` and `g : E \u2192 G` (named `left_fun` and `right_fun`) and a point `a` (named `pt`)\nsuch that\n\n* both functions are strictly differentiable at `a`;\n* the derivatives are surjective;\n* the kernels of the derivatives are complementary subspaces of `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.left_range", "description": " Data for the general version of the implicit function theorem. It holds two functions\n`f : E \u2192 F` and `g : E \u2192 G` (named `left_fun` and `right_fun`) and a point `a` (named `pt`)\nsuch that\n\n* both functions are strictly differentiable at `a`;\n* the derivatives are surjective;\n* the kernels of the derivatives are complementary subspaces of `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.right_range", "description": " Data for the general version of the implicit function theorem. It holds two functions\n`f : E \u2192 F` and `g : E \u2192 G` (named `left_fun` and `right_fun`) and a point `a` (named `pt`)\nsuch that\n\n* both functions are strictly differentiable at `a`;\n* the derivatives are surjective;\n* the kernels of the derivatives are complementary subspaces of `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.is_compl_ker", "description": " Data for the general version of the implicit function theorem. It holds two functions\n`f : E \u2192 F` and `g : E \u2192 G` (named `left_fun` and `right_fun`) and a point `a` (named `pt`)\nsuch that\n\n* both functions are strictly differentiable at `a`;\n* the derivatives are surjective;\n* the kernels of the derivatives are complementary subspaces of `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.map_implicit_function_of_complemented_eq", "description": "`implicit_function_of_complemented` sends `(z, y)` to a point in `f \u207b\u00b9' z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.prod_fun", "description": "The function given by `x \u21a6 (left_fun x, right_fun x)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.implicit_to_local_homeomorph_of_complemented_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.implicit_to_local_homeomorph_of_complemented", "description": " A local homeomorphism between `E` and `F \u00d7 f'.ker` sending level surfaces of `f`\nto vertical subspaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.to_implicit_function", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.eq_implicit_function", "description": " Any point in some neighborhood of `a` can be represented as `implicit_function`\nof some point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.implicit_to_local_homeomorph_of_complemented_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.implicit_to_local_homeomorph_of_complemented_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.implicit_function", "description": " Implicit function theorem. If `f : E \u2192 F` and `g : E \u2192 G` are two maps strictly differentiable\nat `a`, their derivatives `f'`, `g'` are surjective, and the kernels of these derivatives are\ncomplementary subspaces of `E`, then `implicit_function_of_is_compl_ker` is the unique (germ of a)\nmap `\u03c6 : F \u2192 G \u2192 E` such that `f (\u03c6 y z) = y` and `g (\u03c6 y z) = z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.left_map_implicit_function", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.implicit_to_local_homeomorph_apply_ker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.right_map_implicit_function", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.implicit_function", "description": "**Alias** of `has_strict_fderiv_at.tendsto_implicit_function`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.map_pt_mem_to_local_homeomorph_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.prod_fun_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.implicit_function_apply_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.implicit_function_data_of_complemented", "description": " Data used to apply the generic implicit function theorem to the case of a strictly\ndifferentiable map such that its derivative is surjective and has a complemented kernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.implicit_to_local_homeomorph_of_complemented_apply_ker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.to_local_homeomorph", "description": " Implicit function theorem. If `f : E \u2192 F` and `g : E \u2192 G` are two maps strictly differentiable\nat `a`, their derivatives `f'`, `g'` are surjective, and the kernels of these derivatives are\ncomplementary subspaces of `E`, then `x \u21a6 (f x, g x)` defines a local homeomorphism between\n`E` and `F \u00d7 G`. In particular, `{x | f x = f a}` is locally homeomorphic to `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.to_local_homeomorph_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.to_local_homeomorph_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.to_implicit_function_of_complemented", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.implicit_to_local_homeomorph", "description": " Given a map `f : E \u2192 F` to a finite dimensional space with a surjective derivative `f'`,\nreturns a local homeomorphism between `E` and `F \u00d7 ker f'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.implicit_function_has_strict_fderiv_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.implicit_to_local_homeomorph_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.prod_map_implicit_function", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.mem_implicit_to_local_homeomorph_of_complemented_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.implicit_function_of_complemented", "description": "Implicit function `g` defined by `f (g z y) = z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.map_implicit_function_eq", "description": "`implicit_function` sends `(z, y)` to a point in `f \u207b\u00b9' z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.mem_implicit_to_local_homeomorph_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.pt_mem_to_local_homeomorph_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.map_nhds_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "implicit_function_data.implicit_function_apply_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvqpf.prj.map", "description": "`map` on functor `prj i`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvqpf.prj.mvqpf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvqpf.prj.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvqpf.prj.mvfunctor", "description": "", "p": "