3b1 \u2192 \u03b1` is said to be ergodic with respect to a measure `\u03bc` if it is measure\npreserving and pre-ergodic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quasi_ergodic", "description": " A map `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1` is said to be quasi ergodic with respect to a measure `\u03bc` if it is quasi\nmeasure preserving and pre-ergodic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quasi_ergodic.to_quasi_measure_preserving", "description": " A map `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1` is said to be quasi ergodic with respect to a measure `\u03bc` if it is quasi\nmeasure preserving and pre-ergodic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quasi_ergodic.to_pre_ergodic", "description": " A map `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1` is said to be quasi ergodic with respect to a measure `\u03bc` if it is quasi\nmeasure preserving and pre-ergodic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pre_ergodic.measure_self_or_compl_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray_or_ne_zero_and_same_ray_neg_iff_not_linear_independent", "description": " Two vectors are in the same ray, or they are nonzero and the first is in the same ray as the\nnegation of the second, if and only if they are not linearly independent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray", "description": "A ray (equivalence class of nonzero vectors with common positive multiples) in a module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray_neg_smul_right_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.pos_smul_left", "description": "A positive multiple of a vector is in the same ray as one it is in the same ray as.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.zero_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.of_neg", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `same_ray_neg_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray_neg_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray_smul_right_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_pos_right_iff_same_ray_and_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray_nonneg_smul_left", "description": "A nonnegative multiple of a vector is in the same ray as that vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.some_vector_ne_zero", "description": "`some_vector` is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ray_vector", "description": " Nonzero vectors, as used to define rays. This type depends on an unused argument `R` so that\n`ray_vector.setoid` can be an instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.nonneg_smul_right", "description": "A vector is in the same ray as a nonnegative multiple of one it is in the same ray as.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray_smul_left_iff_of_ne", "description": " A multiple of a nonzero vector is in the same ray as that vector if and only if that multiple\nis positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray_pos_smul_right", "description": "A vector is in the same ray as a positive multiple of itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ray_vector.mul_action", "description": " Any invertible action preserves the non-zeroness of ray vectors. This is primarily of interest\nwhen `G = R\u02e3`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.map_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.of_subsingleton'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.zero_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ray_vector.setoid", "description": "The setoid of the `same_ray` relation for the subtype of nonzero vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.exists_eq_smul_add", "description": " If vectors `v\u2081` and `v\u2082` are on the same ray, then for some nonnegative `a b`, `a + b = 1`, we\nhave `v\u2081 = a \u2022 (v\u2081 + v\u2082)` and `v\u2082 = b \u2022 (v\u2081 + v\u2082)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.exists_pos_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units_smul_eq_self_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.has_involutive_neg", "description": "Negating a ray twice produces the original ray.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.some_vector_ray", "description": "The ray of `some_vector`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_zero_of_same_ray_neg_smul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray_of_mem_orbit", "description": "`same_ray` follows from membership of `mul_action.orbit` for the `units.pos_subgroup`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_nonneg_right_iff_same_ray", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.units_smul_of_neg", "description": "Scaling by a negative unit is negation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.exists_pos", "description": " If `x` and `y` are nonzero vectors on the same ray, then there exist positive numbers `r\u2081 r\u2082`\nsuch that `r\u2081 \u2022 x = r\u2082 \u2022 y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ray_vector.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.map_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.trans", "description": " `same_ray` is transitive unless the vector in the middle is zero and both other vectors are\nnonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.exists_nonneg_right", "description": " If a vector `v\u2081` is on the same ray as a nonzero vector `v\u2082`, then it is equal to `c \u2022 v\u2082` for\nsome nonnegative `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.ne_neg_self", "description": "A ray does not equal its own negation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units_smul_eq_neg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_pos_left_iff_same_ray", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.some_ray_vector_ray", "description": "The ray of `some_ray_vector`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray_neg_iff", "description": "`same_ray.neg` as an `iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.neg_units_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.pos_smul_right", "description": "A vector is in the same ray as a positive multiple of one it is in the same ray as.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.units_smul_of_pos", "description": "Scaling by a positive unit is a no-op.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.refl", "description": "`same_ray` is reflexive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray_nonneg_smul_right", "description": "A vector is in the same ray as a nonnegative multiple of itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray_or_same_ray_neg_iff_not_linear_independent", "description": " Two vectors are in the same ray, or the first is in the same ray as the negation of the\nsecond, if and only if they are not linearly independent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.add_left", "description": "If `x` and `y` are on the same ray as `z`, then so is `x + y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray", "description": " Two vectors are in the same ray if either one of them is zero or some positive multiples of them\nare equal (in the typical case over a field, this means one of them is a nonnegative multiple of\nthe other).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.linear_equiv_smul_eq_map", "description": "The action via `linear_equiv.apply_distrib_mul_action` corresponds to `module.ray.map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.add_right", "description": "If `y` and `z` are on the same ray as `x`, then so is `y + z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.map", "description": "An equivalence between modules implies an equivalence between rays.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.has_neg", "description": "Negating a ray.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ray_eq_iff", "description": " The rays given by two nonzero vectors are equal if and only if those vectors\nsatisfy `same_ray`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.same_ray_map_iff", "description": " The images of two vectors under an injective linear map are on the same ray if and only if the\noriginal vectors are on the same ray.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ray_vector.equiv_neg_iff", "description": "If two nonzero vectors are equivalent, so are their negations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.some_vector", "description": "An arbitrary nonzero vector giving a ray.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.some_ray_vector", "description": "An arbitrary `ray_vector` giving a ray.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.exists_pos_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray_pos_smul_left", "description": "A positive multiple of a vector is in the same ray as that vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray_smul_left_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray_neg_smul_right_iff_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray_smul_right_iff_of_ne", "description": " A nonzero vector is in the same ray as a multiple of itself if and only if that multiple\nis positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ray_vector.coe_neg", "description": "Negating a nonzero vector commutes with coercion to the underlying module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray_neg_smul_left_iff_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_pos_right_iff_same_ray", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.rfl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_pos_left_iff_same_ray_and_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "neg_ray_of_ne_zero", "description": "The ray given by the negation of a nonzero vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray_map_iff", "description": " The images of two vectors under a linear equivalence are on the same ray if and only if the\noriginal vectors are on the same ray.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.ind", "description": "An induction principle for `module.ray`, used as `induction x using module.ray.ind`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.symm", "description": "`same_ray` is symmetric.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smul_ray_of_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.nonneg_smul_left", "description": "A nonnegative multiple of a vector is in the same ray as one it is in the same ray as.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ray_pos_smul", "description": "The ray given by a positive multiple of a nonzero vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units_inv_smul", "description": "Scaling by an inverse unit is the same as scaling by itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.mul_action", "description": " Any invertible action preserves the non-zeroness of rays. This is primarily of interest when\n`G = R\u02e3`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ray_vector.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ray_vector.has_involutive_neg", "description": "Negating a nonzero vector twice produces the original vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ray_vector.has_neg", "description": "Negating a nonzero vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_zero_of_same_ray_self_neg", "description": "If a vector is in the same ray as its negation, that vector is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ray_vector.map_linear_equiv", "description": "An equivalence between modules implies an equivalence between ray vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ray_of_ne_zero", "description": "The ray given by a nonzero vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.exists_nonneg_left", "description": " If a vector `v\u2082` is on the same ray as a nonzero vector `v\u2081`, then it is equal to `c \u2022 v\u2081` for\nsome nonnegative `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_nonneg_left_iff_same_ray", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.ray.map_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.smul", "description": " If two vectors are on the same ray then both scaled by the same action are also on the same\nray.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_iff_same_ray", "description": "Equivalence of nonzero vectors, in terms of same_ray.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "same_ray.exists_eq_smul", "description