partrec.code.encode_lt_prec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.const_prim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.rfind_prim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.eval_curry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.encode_code", "description": "An encoding of a `nat.partrec.code` as a \u2115.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.const", "description": "Returns a code for the constant function outputting a particular natural.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.fixed_point", "description": "Roger's fixed-point theorem: Any total, computable `f` has a fixed point: That is, under the\ninterpretation given by `nat.partrec.code.eval`, there is a code `c` such that `c` and `f c` have\nthe same evaluation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.denumerable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.evaln_prim", "description": "The `nat.partrec.code.evaln` function is primitive recursive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.encode_lt_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.rfind'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.encode_lt_pair", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.fixed_point\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.curry", "description": "Given a code `c` taking a pair as input, returns a code using `n` as the first argument to `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.encode_lt_rfind'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.evaln", "description": "A modified evaluation for the code which returns an `option \u2115` instead of a `part \u2115`. To avoid\nundecidability, `evaln` takes a parameter `k` and fails if it encounters a number \u2265 k in the course\nof its execution. Other than this, the semantics are the same as in `nat.partrec.code.eval`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.eval_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.rec_prim'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.of_nat_code", "description": "A decoder for `nat.partrec.code.encode_code`, taking any \u2115 to the `nat.partrec.code` it represents.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.of_nat_code_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.eval_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code", "description": "Code for partial recursive functions from \u2115 to \u2115.\nSee `nat.partrec.code.eval` for the interpretation of these constructors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.zero", "description": "Code for partial recursive functions from \u2115 to \u2115.\nSee `nat.partrec.code.eval` for the interpretation of these constructors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.succ", "description": "Code for partial recursive functions from \u2115 to \u2115.\nSee `nat.partrec.code.eval` for the interpretation of these constructors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.left", "description": "Code for partial recursive functions from \u2115 to \u2115.\nSee `nat.partrec.code.eval` for the interpretation of these constructors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.right", "description": "Code for partial recursive functions from \u2115 to \u2115.\nSee `nat.partrec.code.eval` for the interpretation of these constructors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.pair", "description": "Code for partial recursive functions from \u2115 to \u2115.\nSee `nat.partrec.code.eval` for the interpretation of these constructors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.comp", "description": "Code for partial recursive functions from \u2115 to \u2115.\nSee `nat.partrec.code.eval` for the interpretation of these constructors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.prec", "description": "Code for partial recursive functions from \u2115 to \u2115.\nSee `nat.partrec.code.eval` for the interpretation of these constructors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.rfind'", "description": "Code for partial recursive functions from \u2115 to \u2115.\nSee `nat.partrec.code.eval` for the interpretation of these constructors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.has_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.eval_prec_zero", "description": "Helper lemma for the evaluation of `prec` in the base case.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.const_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.pair_prim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.encode_code_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.evaln_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.evaln_complete", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.eval_eq_rfind_opt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.evaln_bound", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.comp_prim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.eval", "description": "The interpretation of a `nat.partrec.code` as a partial function.\n* `nat.partrec.code.zero`: The constant zero function.\n* `nat.partrec.code.succ`: The successor function.\n* `nat.partrec.code.left`: Left unpairing of a pair of \u2115 (encoded by `nat.mkpair`)\n* `nat.partrec.code.right`: Right unpairing of a pair of \u2115 (encoded by `nat.mkpair`)\n* `nat.partrec.code.pair`: Pairs the outputs of argument codes using `nat.mkpair`.\n* `nat.partrec.code.comp`: Composition of two argument codes.\n* `nat.partrec.code.prec`: Primitive recursion. Given an argument of the form `nat.mkpair a n`:\n  * If `n = 0`, returns `eval cf a`.\n  * If `n = succ k`, returns `eval cg (mkpair a (mkpair k (eval (prec cf cg) (mkpair a k))))`\n* `nat.partrec.code.rfind'`: Minimization. For `f` an argument of the form `nat.mkpair a m`,\n  `rfind' f m` returns the least `a` such that `f a m = 0`, if one exists and `f b m` terminates\n  for `b < a`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.evaln_sound", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.id", "description": "A code for the identity function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.exists_code", "description": "A function is partial recursive if and only if there is a code implementing it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.eval_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.smn", "description": "The $S_n^m$ theorem: There is a computable function, namely `nat.partrec.code.curry`, that takes a\nprogram and a \u2115 `n`, and returns a new program using `n` as the first argument.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.code.eval_prec_succ", "description": "Helper lemma for the evaluation of `prec` in the recursive case.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inf_Sup_eq_supr_inf_sup_finset", "description": "This property is equivalent to `\u03b1` being upper continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.is_compact_element.exists_finset_of_le_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.compactly_generated_of_well_founded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.is_sup_closed_compact.well_founded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.finset_sup_compact_of_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "directed_on.disjoint_Sup_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.well_founded_iff_is_Sup_finite_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.well_founded.finite_of_independent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_iff_compact_le_imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.is_Sup_finite_compact_iff_all_elements_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Sup_compact_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.is_Sup_finite_compact", "description": " A compactness property for a complete lattice is that any subset has a finite subset with the\nsame `Sup`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compactly_generated", "description": " A complete lattice is said to be compactly generated if any\nelement is the `Sup` of compact elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compactly_generated.exists_Sup_eq", "description": " A complete lattice is said to be compactly generated if any\nelement is the `Sup` of compact elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_set_independent_of_Sup_atoms_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "directed.inf_supr_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.well_founded.finite_of_set_independent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.set_independent_iff_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.coatomic_of_top_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.is_compact_element_iff_le_of_directed_Sup_le", "description": " An element `k` is compact if and only if any directed set with `Sup` above\n`k` already got above `k` at some point in the set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "directed.supr_inf_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_atomic_of_complemented_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.set_independent_Union_of_directed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.is_compact_element_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.is_compact_element.directed_Sup_lt_of_lt", "description": " A compact element `k` has the property that any directed set lying strictly below `k` has\nits Sup strictly below `k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.is_Sup_finite_compact.is_sup_closed_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complemented_lattice_of_Sup_atoms_eq_top", "description": "See [Theorem 6.6][calugareanu].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.is_sup_closed_compact_iff_well_founded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complemented_lattice_iff_is_atomistic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "directed_on.inf_Sup_eq", "description": "This property is sometimes referred to as `\u03b1` being upper continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.well_founded_characterisations", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.is_compact_element", "description": " An element `k` of a complete lattice is said to be compact if any set with `Sup`\nabove `k` has a finite subset with `Sup` above `k`.  Such an element is also called\n\"finite\" or \"S-compact\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.is_Sup_finite_compact_iff_is_sup_closed_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.is_Sup_finite_compact.well_founded", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `complete_lattice.well_founded_iff_is_Sup_finite_compact`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_atomistic_of_complemented_lattice", "description": "See [Lemma 5.1][calugareanu].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "directed_on.disjoint_Sup_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.independent_sUnion_of_directed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.is_sup_closed_compact", "description": " A compactness property for a complete lattice is that any `sup`-closed non-empty subset\ncontains its `Sup`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_set_independent_is_compl_Sup_atoms", "description": " In an atomic lattice, every element `b` has a complement of the form `Sup s`, where each element\nof `s` is an atom. See also `complemented_lattice_of_Sup_atoms_eq_top`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Sup_compact_le_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "directed.directed_on_range", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `directed_on_range`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "directed_on.Sup_inf_eq", "description": "This property is sometimes referred to as `\u03b1` being upper continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complemented_lattice_of_is_atomistic", "description": "See [Theorem 6.6][calugareanu].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.well_founded.is_Sup_finite_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "directed.disjoint_supr_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "directed.disjoint_supr_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.Iic_coatomic_of_compact_element", "description": " A compact element `k` has the property that any `b < k` lies below a \"maximal element below\n`k`\", which is to say `[\u22a5, k]` is coatomic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "well_founded.is_sup_closed_compact", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `complete_lattice.is_sup_closed_compact_iff_well_founded`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.is_sup_closed_compact.is_Sup_finite_compact", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `complete_lattice.is_Sup_finite_compact_iff_is_sup_closed_compact`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.neg_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.char_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "injective_pow_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pth_root", "description": "`p`-th root of an element in a `perfect_ring` as a `ring_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frobenius_pth_root", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_inverse_pth_root_frobenius", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.map_pth_root", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.mk_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frobenius_equiv", "description": "Frobenius automorphism of a perfect ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.one_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.mk_mul_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.of", "description": "Embedding of `K` into `perfect_closure K p`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute_frobenius_pth_root", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.eq_pth_root", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.lift", "description": " Given a field `K` of characteristic `p` and a perfect ring `L` of the same characteristic,\nany homomorphism `K \u2192+* L` can be lifted to `perfect_closure K p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.map_pth_root", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.mk_zero_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.frobenius_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.r_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pth_root_pow_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.map_iterate_pth_root", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.lift_on", "description": "Lift a function `\u2115 \u00d7 K \u2192 L` to a function on `perfect_closure K p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.induction_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.r", "description": "`perfect_closure K p` is the quotient by this relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.r.intro", "description": "`perfect_closure K p` is the quotient by this relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.map_iterate_pth_root", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "coe_frobenius_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.nat_cast_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.has_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_pth_root_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_ring.of_surjective", "description": "A reduced ring with prime characteristic and surjective frobenius map is perfect.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.perfect_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pth_root_pow_p'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_inverse_pth_root_frobenius", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pth_root_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure", "description": "The perfect closure is the smallest extension that makes frobenius surjective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pth_root_frobenius", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.lift_on_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_ring", "description": "A perfect ring is a ring of characteristic p that has p-th root.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_ring.pth_root'", "description": "A perfect ring is a ring of characteristic p that has p-th root.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_ring.frobenius_pth_root'", "description": "A perfect ring is a ring of characteristic p that has p-th root.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_ring.pth_root_frobenius'", "description": "A perfect ring is a ring of characteristic p that has p-th root.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.mk_add_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.mk", "description": "Constructor for `perfect_closure`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.zero_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "coe_frobenius_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.quot_mk_eq_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.of_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.r.sound", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect_closure.eq_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.bisim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.path_dest_right", "description": "Implementation of destructor for M-type of `P`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.dest", "description": "Destructor for M-types", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.dest_corec'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.dest_corec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.dest_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.corec_contents", "description": "Using corecursion, construct the contents of an M-type", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.path", "description": "A path from the root of a tree to one of its node", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.path.root", "description": "A path from the root of a tree to one of its node", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.path.child", "description": "A path from the root of a tree to one of its node", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.path_dest_left", "description": "Implementation of destructor for M-type of `P`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.cast_lastB", "description": "Proof of type equality as a function", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.dest'", "description": "Destructor for M-type of `P`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.map_dest", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.Mp", "description": " Polynomial functor of the M-type of `P`. `A` is a data-less\npossibly infinite tree whereas, for a given `a : A`, `B a` is a valid\npath in tree `a` so that `Wp.obj \u03b1` is made of a tree and a function\nfrom its valid paths to the values it contains", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.dest'_eq_dest'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.mk", "description": "Constructor for M-types", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.bisim'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.inhabited_M", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.corec_shape", "description": " construct through corecursion the shape of an M-type\nwithout its contents", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.cast_dropB", "description": "Proof of type equality as an arrow", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.dest_eq_dest'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.bisim\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.bisim_lemma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.corec", "description": "Corecursor for M-type of `P`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M", "description": "`n`-ary M-type for `P`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.path.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.mvfunctor_M", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mvpfunctor.M.corec'", "description": "Corecursor for M-type of `P`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_div", "description": " Extension for the `positivity` tactic: division is nonnegative if both numerator and denominator\nare nonnegative, and strictly positive if both numerator and denominator are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_pow", "description": " Extension for the `positivity` tactic: raising a number `a` to a natural/integer power `n` is\npositive if `n = 0` (since `a ^ 0 = 1`) or if `0 < a`, and is nonnegative if `n` is even (squares\nare nonnegative) or if `0 \u2264 a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_min", "description": " Extension for the `positivity` tactic: the `min` of two numbers is nonnegative if both are\nnonnegative, and strictly positive if both are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_mul", "description": " Extension for the `positivity` tactic: multiplication is nonnegative/positive/nonzero if both\nmultiplicands are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.orelse", "description": " Given two tactics whose result is `strictness`, report a `strictness`:\n- if at least one gives `positive`, report `positive` and one of the expressions giving a proof of\n  positivity\n- if one reports `nonnegative` and the other reports `nonzero`, report `positive`\n- else if at least one reports `nonnegative`, report `nonnegative` and one of the\n  expressions giving a proof of nonnegativity\n- else if at least one reports `nonzero`, report `nonzero` and one of the expressions giving a proof\n  of nonzeroness\n- if both fail, fail", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.compare_hyp", "description": " Third base case of the `positivity` tactic.  Prove an expression `e` is\npositive/nonnegative/nonzero by finding a hypothesis of the form `a < e`, `a \u2264 e` or `a = e` in\nwhich `a` can be proved positive/nonnegative/nonzero by `norm_num`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.norm_num.positivity", "description": " First base case of the `positivity` tactic.  We try `norm_num` to prove directly that an\nexpression `e` is positive, nonnegative or non-zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.attr", "description": " Attribute allowing a user to tag a tactic as an extension for `tactic.interactive.positivity`.\nThe main (recursive) step of this tactic is to try successively all the extensions tagged with this\nattribute on the expression at hand, and also to try the two \"base case\" tactics\n`tactic.norm_num.positivity`, `tactic.positivity.compare_hyp` on the expression at hand.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.strictness.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_nat_abs", "description": " Extension for the `positivity` tactic: `int.nat_abs` is positive when its input is.\n\nSince the output type of `int.nat_abs` is `\u2115`, the nonnegative case is handled by the default\n`positivity` tactic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_inv", "description": " Extension for the `positivity` tactic: an inverse of a positive number is positive, an inverse\nof a nonnegative number is nonnegative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_max", "description": " Extension for the `positivity` tactic: the `max` of two numbers is nonnegative if at least one\nis nonnegative, strictly positive if at least one is positive, and nonzero if both are nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_canon_pow", "description": " Extension for the `positivity` tactic: raising a positive number in a canonically ordered\nsemiring gives a positive number.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abs_pos_of_ne_zero", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `abs_pos`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.strictness.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.core", "description": " Look for a proof of positivity/nonnegativity of an expression `e`; if found, return the proof\ntogether with a `strictness` stating whether the proof found was for strict positivity\n(`positive p`), nonnegativity (`nonnegative p`), or nonzeroness (`nonzero p`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.tactic.positivity", "description": " Tactic solving goals of the form `0 \u2264 x`, `0 < x` and `x \u2260 0`.  The tactic works recursively\naccording to the syntax of the expression `x`, if the atoms composing the expression all have\nnumeric lower bounds which can be proved positive/nonnegative/nonzero by `norm_num`.  This tactic\neither closes the goal or fails.\n\nExamples:\n```lean\nexample {a : \u2124} (ha : 3 < a) : 0 \u2264 a ^ 3 + a := by positivity\n\nexample {a : \u2124} (ha : 1 < a) : 0 < |(3:\u2124) + a| := by positivity\n\nexample {b : \u2124} : 0 \u2264 max (-3) (b ^ 2) := by positivity\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.compare_hyp_ne", "description": " Calls `norm_num` on `a` to prove nonzeroness of `e` assuming `b` is defeq to `e` and\n`p\u2082 : b \u2260 a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_abs", "description": " Extension for the `positivity` tactic: an absolute value is nonnegative, and is strictly\npositive if its input is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.compare_hyp_le", "description": " Calls `norm_num` on `a` to prove positivity/nonnegativity of `e` assuming `b` is defeq to `e`\nand `p\u2082 : a \u2264 b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.compare_hyp_eq", "description": " Calls `norm_num` on `a` to prove positivity/nonnegativity/nonzeroness of `e` assuming `b` is\ndefeq to `e` and `p\u2082 : a = b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.order_rel", "description": " Inductive type recording whether the goal `positivity` is called on is nonnegativity, positivity\nor different from `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.order_rel.le", "description": " Inductive type recording whether the goal `positivity` is called on is nonnegativity, positivity\nor different from `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.order_rel.lt", "description": " Inductive type recording whether the goal `positivity` is called on is nonnegativity, positivity\nor different from `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.order_rel.ne", "description": " Inductive type recording whether the goal `positivity` is called on is nonnegativity, positivity\nor different from `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.order_rel.ne'", "description": " Inductive type recording whether the goal `positivity` is called on is nonnegativity, positivity\nor different from `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.strictness.has_to_string", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_canon", "description": " Second base case of the `positivity` tactic: Any element of a canonically ordered additive\nmonoid is nonnegative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.order_rel.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.compare_hyp_lt", "description": " Calls `norm_num` on `a` to prove positivity/nonnegativity of `e` assuming `b` is defeq to `e`\nand `p\u2082 : a < b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_asc_factorial", "description": "Extension for the `positivity` tactic: `nat.asc_factorial` is always positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_add", "description": " Extension for the `positivity` tactic: addition is nonnegative if both summands are nonnegative,\nand strictly positive if at least one summand is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_factorial", "description": "Extension for the `positivity` tactic: `nat.factorial` is always positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.positivity_fail", "description": " This tactic fails with a message saying that `positivity` couldn't prove anything about `e`\nif we only know that `a` and `b` are positive/nonnegative/nonzero (according to `pa` and `pb`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_coe", "description": "Extension for the `positivity` tactic: casts from `\u2115`, `\u2124`, `\u211a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.order_rel.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_map", "description": "Extension for the `positivity` tactic: nonnegative maps take nonnegative values.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_ite", "description": " Extension for the `positivity` tactic: the `if then else` of two numbers is\npositive/nonnegative/nonzero if both are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.positivity", "description": " Tactic solving goals of the form `0 \u2264 x`, `0 < x` and `x \u2260 0`.  The tactic works recursively\naccording to the syntax of the expression `x`, if the atoms composing the expression all have\nnumeric lower bounds which can be proved positive/nonnegative/nonzero by `norm_num`.  This tactic\neither closes the goal or fails.\n\nExamples:\n```lean\nexample {a : \u2124} (ha : 3 < a) : 0 \u2264 a ^ 3 + a := by positivity\n\nexample {a : \u2124} (ha : 1 < a) : 0 < |(3:\u2124) + a| := by positivity\n\nexample {b : \u2124} : 0 \u2264 max (-3) (b ^ 2) := by positivity\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_succ", "description": "Extension for the `positivity` tactic: `nat.succ` is always positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.strictness", "description": " Inductive type recording either `positive` and an expression (typically a proof of a fact\n`0 < x`) or `nonnegative` and an expression (typically a proof of a fact `0 \u2264 x`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.strictness.positive", "description": " Inductive type recording either `positive` and an expression (typically a proof of a fact\n`0 < x`) or `nonnegative` and an expression (typically a proof of a fact `0 \u2264 x`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.strictness.nonnegative", "description": " Inductive type recording either `positive` and an expression (typically a proof of a fact\n`0 < x`) or `nonnegative` and an expression (typically a proof of a fact `0 \u2264 x`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity.strictness.nonzero", "description": " Inductive type recording either `positive` and an expression (typically a proof of a fact\n`0 < x`) or `nonnegative` and an expression (typically a proof of a fact `0 \u2264 x`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.id_cover_lifting", "description": "The identity functor on a site is cover-lifting.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sites.pullback_copullback_adjunction_unit_app_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Ran_is_sheaf_of_cover_lifting.glued_section", "description": "The section obtained by passing `glued_limit_cone` into `category_theory.limits.limit.lift`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Ran_is_sheaf_of_cover_lifting.glued_limit_cone", "description": "The limit cone in order to glue the sections obtained via `get_section`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Ran_is_sheaf_of_cover_lifting.get_section_is_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Ran_is_sheaf_of_cover_lifting.glued_section_is_unique", "description": "Verify that the amalgamation is indeed unique.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Ran_is_sheaf_of_cover_lifting.glued_limit_cone_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Ran_is_sheaf_of_cover_lifting.category_theory.limits.has_limits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Ran_is_sheaf_of_cover_lifting.glued_section_is_amalgamation", "description": "Verify that the `glued_section` is an amalgamation of `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sites.pullback_copullback_adjunction_counit_app_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Ran_is_sheaf_of_cover_lifting.helper", "description": "A helper lemma for the following two lemmas. Basically stating that if the section `y : X \u27f6 \ud835\udca2(V)`\ncoincides with `x` on `G(V')` for all `G(V') \u2286 V \u2208 S`, then `X \u27f6 \ud835\udca2(V) \u27f6 \u2131(W)` is indeed the\nsection obtained in `get_sections`. That said, this is littered with some more categorical jargon\nin order to be applied in the following lemmas easier.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Ran_is_sheaf_of_cover_lifting.get_section_commute", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Ran_is_sheaf_of_cover_lifting.get_section", "description": "Given a `G(Y) \u2286 U`, we can find a unique section `X \u27f6 \u2131(Y)` that agrees with `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Ran_is_sheaf_of_cover_lifting", "description": "If `G` is cover_lifting, then `Ran G.op` pushes sheaves to sheaves.\n\nThis result is basically https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00XK,\nbut without the condition that `C` or `D` has pullbacks.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_lifting", "description": "A functor `G : (C, J) \u2964 (D, K)` between sites is called to have the cover-lifting property\nif for all covering sieves `R` in `D`, `R.pullback G` is a covering sieve in `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_lifting.cover_lift", "description": "A functor `G : (C, J) \u2964 (D, K)` between sites is called to have the cover-lifting property\nif for all covering sieves `R` in `D`, `R.pullback G` is a covering sieve in `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sites.copullback", "description": "A cover-lifting functor induces a morphism of sites in the same direction as the functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Ran_is_sheaf_of_cover_lifting.get_section_is_amalgamation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Ran_is_sheaf_of_cover_lifting.pulledback_family", "description": "The family of morphisms `X \u27f6 \ud835\udca2(G(Y')) \u27f6 \u2131(Y')` defined on `{ Y' \u2286 Y : G(Y') \u2286 U \u2208 S}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Ran_is_sheaf_of_cover_lifting.pulledback_family_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sites.pullback_copullback_adjunction", "description": "Given a functor between sites that is cover-preserving, cover-lifting, and compatible-preserving,\nthe pullback and copullback along `G` are adjoint to each other", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comp_cover_lifting", "description": "The composition of two cover-lifting functors are cover-lifting", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.guard", "description": "`guard p a` returns `some a` if `p a` holds, otherwise `none`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.decidable_eq_none", "description": "`o = none` is decidable even if the wrapped type does not have decidable equality.\n\nThis is not an instance because it is not definitionally equal to `option.decidable_eq`.\nTry to use `o.is_none` or `o.is_some` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.lift_or_get_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.lift_or_get_idem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.melim", "description": "A monadic analogue of `option.elim`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.maybe", "description": " If you maybe have a monadic computation in a `[monad m]` which produces a term of type `\u03b1`, then\nthere is a naturally associated way to always perform a computation in `m` which maybe produces a\nresult.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.some_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.elim", "description": "An elimination principle for `option`. It is a nondependent version of `option.rec`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.filter", "description": "`filter p o` returns `some a` if `o` is `some a` and `p a` holds, otherwise `none`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.lift_or_get_is_left_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.pbind", "description": "Partial bind. If for some `x : option \u03b1`, `f : \u03a0 (a : \u03b1), a \u2208 x \u2192 option \u03b2` is a\n partial function defined on `a : \u03b1` giving an `option \u03b2`, where `some a = x`,\n then `pbind x f h` is essentially the same as `bind x f`\n but is defined only when all `x = some a`, using the proof to apply `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.has_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.decidable_exists_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.is_none_iff_eq_none", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.mget_or_else", "description": "A monadic analogue of `option.get_or_else`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.lift_or_get", "description": " Two arguments failsafe function. Returns `f a b` if the inputs are `some a` and `some b`, and\n\"does nothing\" otherwise.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.iget", "description": "Inhabited `get` function. Returns `a` if the input is `some a`, otherwise returns `default`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.mem_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.join", "description": "Flatten an `option` of `option`, a specialization of `mjoin`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.mem_some_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.mem_to_list", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.rel", "description": " Lifts a relation `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 Prop` to a relation `option \u03b1 \u2192 option \u03b2 \u2192 Prop` by just adding\n`none ~ none`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.rel.some", "description": " Lifts a relation `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 Prop` to a relation `option \u03b1 \u2192 option \u03b2 \u2192 Prop` by just adding\n`none ~ none`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.rel.none", "description": " Lifts a relation `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 Prop` to a relation `option \u03b1 \u2192 option \u03b2 \u2192 Prop` by just adding\n`none ~ none`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.pmap", "description": " Partial map. If `f : \u03a0 a, p a \u2192 \u03b2` is a partial function defined on `a : \u03b1` satisfying `p`,\nthen `pmap f x h` is essentially the same as `map f x` but is defined only when all members of `x`\nsatisfy `p`, using the proof to apply `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.lift_or_get_is_right_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.traverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.mem_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.mmap", "description": "Map a monadic function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 m \u03b2` over an `o : option \u03b1`, maybe producing a result.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.to_list", "description": " Cast of `option` to `list `. Returns `[a]` if the input is `some a`, and `[]` if it is\n`none`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.lift_or_get_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.iget_some", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.decidable_forall_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "denumerable.list_of_nat_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "denumerable.raise'_finset", "description": "Makes `raise' l n` into a finset. Elements are distinct thanks to `raise'_sorted`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.countable", "description": "If `\u03b1` is countable, then so is `finset \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.encode_list_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.countable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.encode_list", "description": "Explicit encoding function for `list \u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.mem_sorted_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.trunc_encodable", "description": " A finite type is encodable. Because the encoding is not unique, we wrap it in `trunc` to\npreserve computability.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.list_equiv_self_of_equiv_nat", "description": "If `\u03b1` is equivalent to `\u2115`, then `list \u03b1` is equivalent to `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "denumerable.raise'_sorted", "description": "`raise' l n` is a strictly increasing sequence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "denumerable.lower", "description": " Outputs the list of differences of the input list, that is\n`lower [a\u2081, a\u2082, ...] n = [a\u2081 - n, a\u2082 - a\u2081, ...]`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "denumerable.raise_lower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "denumerable.finset", "description": " If `\u03b1` is denumerable, then so is `finset \u03b1`. Warning: this is *not* the same encoding as used\nin `finset.encodable`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "denumerable.raise", "description": " Outputs the list of partial sums of the input list, that is\n`raise [a\u2081, a\u2082, ...] n = [n + a\u2081, n + a\u2081 + a\u2082, ...]`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.countable", "description": "If `\u03b1` is countable, then so is `vector \u03b1 n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.countable", "description": "If `\u03b1` is countable, then so is `multiset \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "denumerable.lower_raise'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.encodable", "description": " If `\u03b1` is encodable, then so is `list \u03b1`. This uses the `mkpair` and `unpair` functions from\n`data.nat.pairing`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.encodable_of_list", "description": "A listable type with decidable equality is encodable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.fin_arrow", "description": "If `\u03b1` is encodable, then so is `fin n \u2192 \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "denumerable.raise'", "description": " Outputs the list of partial sums plus one of the input list, that is\n`raise [a\u2081, a\u2082, a\u2083, ...] n = [n + a\u2081, n + a\u2081 + a\u2082 + 1, n + a\u2081 + a\u2082 + a\u2083 + 2, ...]`. Adding one each\ntime ensures the elements are distinct.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.fin_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.encode_list_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.encodable", "description": "If `\u03b1` is encodable, then so is `multiset \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.fintype_arrow_of_encodable", "description": "If `\u03b1` and `\u03b2` are encodable and `\u03b1` is a fintype, then `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is encodable as well.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.decode_list_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "denumerable.lower'", "description": " Outputs the list of differences minus one of the input list, that is\n`lower' [a\u2081, a\u2082, a\u2083, ...] n = [a\u2081 - n, a\u2082 - a\u2081 - 1, a\u2083 - a\u2082 - 1, ...]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.length_le_encode", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "denumerable.raise_lower'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "denumerable.raise_sorted", "description": "`raise l n` is an non-decreasing sequence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.sorted_univ_nodup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.list_unit_equiv", "description": "The type lists on unit is canonically equivalent to the natural numbers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.to_encodable", "description": " A noncomputable way to arbitrarily choose an ordering on a finite type.\nIt is not made into a global instance, since it involves an arbitrary choice.\nThis can be locally made into an instance with `local attribute [instance] fintype.to_encodable`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "denumerable.denumerable_list", "description": "If `\u03b1` is denumerable, then so is `list \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.fintype_pi", "description": " When `\u03b1` is finite and all `\u03c0 a` are encodable, `\u03a0 a, \u03c0 a` is encodable too. Because the\nencoding is not unique, we wrap it in `trunc` to preserve computability.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.decode_list", "description": "Explicit decoding function for `list \u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "denumerable.multiset", "description": " If `\u03b1` is denumerable, then so is `multiset \u03b1`. Warning: this is *not* the same encoding as used\nin `multiset.encodable`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "denumerable.list_of_nat_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.decode_multiset", "description": "Explicit decoding function for `multiset \u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "denumerable.raise'_chain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "denumerable.lower_raise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.sorted_univ_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.fintype_arrow", "description": " When `\u03b1` is finite and `\u03b2` is encodable, `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is encodable too. Because the encoding is not\nunique, we wrap it in `trunc` to preserve computability.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.encodable", "description": "If `\u03b1` is encodable, then so is `finset \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "denumerable.denumerable_list_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.sorted_univ", "description": "The elements of a `fintype` as a sorted list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.list_nat_equiv_nat", "description": "`list \u2115` is equivalent to `\u2115`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "denumerable.raise_chain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.length_sorted_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector.encodable", "description": "If `\u03b1` is encodable, then so is `vector \u03b1 n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.decode_list_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.fintype_equiv_fin", "description": "An encodable `fintype` is equivalent to the same size `fin`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "encodable.encode_multiset", "description": "Explicit encoding function for `multiset \u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_seminorm_class.to_mul_le_add_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "library_note.out-param inheritance", "description": "Diamond inheritance cannot depend on `out_param`s in the following circumstances:\n * there are three classes `top`, `middle`, `bottom`\n * all of these classes have a parameter `(\u03b1 : out_param _)`\n * all of these classes have an instance parameter `[root \u03b1]` that depends on this `out_param`\n * the `root` class has two child classes: `left` and `right`, these are siblings in the hierarchy\n * the instance `bottom.to_middle` takes a `[left \u03b1]` parameter\n * the instance `middle.to_top` takes a `[right \u03b1]` parameter\n * there is a `leaf` class that inherits from both `left` and `right`.\nIn that case, given instances `bottom \u03b1` and `leaf \u03b1`, Lean cannot synthesize a `top \u03b1` instance,\neven though the hypotheses of the instances `bottom.to_middle` and `middle.to_top` are satisfied.\n\nThere are two workarounds:\n* You could replace the bundled inheritance implemented by the instance `middle.to_top` with\n  unbundled inheritance implemented by adding a `[top \u03b1]` parameter to the `middle` class. This is\n  the preferred option since it is also more compatible with Lean 4, at the cost of being more work\n  to implement and more verbose to use.\n* You could weaken the `bottom.to_middle` instance by making it depend on a subclass of\n  `middle.to_top`'s parameter, in this example replacing `[left \u03b1]` with `[leaf \u03b1]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonarchimedean_hom_class", "description": "`nonarchimedean_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of non-archimedean morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonarchimedean_hom_class.coe", "description": "`nonarchimedean_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of non-archimedean morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonarchimedean_hom_class.coe_injective'", "description": "`nonarchimedean_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of non-archimedean morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonarchimedean_hom_class.map_add_le_max", "description": "`nonarchimedean_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of non-archimedean morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_norm_class.to_add_group_norm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_norm_class.to_add_group_seminorm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_div_le_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_map_add_map_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_ne_zero_iff_ne_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_seminorm_class.to_nonneg_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonarchimedean_hom_class.to_fun_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_seminorm_class", "description": " `add_group_seminorm_class F \u03b1` states that `F` is a type of `\u03b2`-valued seminorms on the additive\ngroup `\u03b1`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `add_group_seminorm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_seminorm_class.coe", "description": " `add_group_seminorm_class F \u03b1` states that `F` is a type of `\u03b2`-valued seminorms on the additive\ngroup `\u03b1`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `add_group_seminorm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_seminorm_class.coe_injective'", "description": " `add_group_seminorm_class F \u03b1` states that `F` is a type of `\u03b2`-valued seminorms on the additive\ngroup `\u03b1`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `add_group_seminorm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_seminorm_class.map_add_le_add", "description": " `add_group_seminorm_class F \u03b1` states that `F` is a type of `\u03b2`-valued seminorms on the additive\ngroup `\u03b1`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `add_group_seminorm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_seminorm_class.map_zero", "description": " `add_group_seminorm_class F \u03b1` states that `F` is a type of `\u03b2`-valued seminorms on the additive\ngroup `\u03b1`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `add_group_seminorm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_seminorm_class.map_neg_eq_map", "description": " `add_group_seminorm_class F \u03b1` states that `F` is a type of `\u03b2`-valued seminorms on the additive\ngroup `\u03b1`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `add_group_seminorm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_map_add_map_sub'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submultiplicative_hom_class.to_fun_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_pos_of_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg_hom_class", "description": "`nonneg_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of nonnegative morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg_hom_class.coe", "description": "`nonneg_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of nonnegative morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg_hom_class.coe_injective'", "description": "`nonneg_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of nonnegative morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg_hom_class.map_nonneg", "description": "`nonneg_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of nonnegative morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm_class.to_nonneg_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_map_div_add_map_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_norm_class.to_mul_ring_seminorm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subadditive_hom_class.to_fun_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submultiplicative_hom_class", "description": "`submultiplicative_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of submultiplicative morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submultiplicative_hom_class.coe", "description": "`submultiplicative_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of submultiplicative morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submultiplicative_hom_class.coe_injective'", "description": "`submultiplicative_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of submultiplicative morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submultiplicative_hom_class.map_mul_le_mul", "description": "`submultiplicative_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of submultiplicative morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_eq_zero_iff_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm_class.to_add_group_seminorm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_sub_rev", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm_class", "description": " `mul_ring_seminorm_class F \u03b1` states that `F` is a type of `\u03b2`-valued multiplicative seminorms\non the ring `\u03b1`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `mul_ring_seminorm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm_class.coe", "description": " `mul_ring_seminorm_class F \u03b1` states that `F` is a type of `\u03b2`-valued multiplicative seminorms\non the ring `\u03b1`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `mul_ring_seminorm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm_class.coe_injective'", "description": " `mul_ring_seminorm_class F \u03b1` states that `F` is a type of `\u03b2`-valued multiplicative seminorms\non the ring `\u03b1`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `mul_ring_seminorm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm_class.map_add_le_add", "description": " `mul_ring_seminorm_class F \u03b1` states that `F` is a type of `\u03b2`-valued multiplicative seminorms\non the ring `\u03b1`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `mul_ring_seminorm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm_class.map_zero", "description": " `mul_ring_seminorm_class F \u03b1` states that `F` is a type of `\u03b2`-valued multiplicative seminorms\non the ring `\u03b1`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `mul_ring_seminorm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm_class.map_neg_eq_map", "description": " `mul_ring_seminorm_class F \u03b1` states that `F` is a type of `\u03b2`-valued multiplicative seminorms\non the ring `\u03b1`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `mul_ring_seminorm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm_class.map_mul", "description": " `mul_ring_seminorm_class F \u03b1` states that `F` is a type of `\u03b2`-valued multiplicative seminorms\non the ring `\u03b1`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `mul_ring_seminorm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm_class.map_one", "description": " `mul_ring_seminorm_class F \u03b1` states that `F` is a type of `\u03b2`-valued multiplicative seminorms\non the ring `\u03b1`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `mul_ring_seminorm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_norm_class.to_ring_seminorm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_ne_zero_iff_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subadditive_hom_class", "description": "`subadditive_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of subadditive morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subadditive_hom_class.coe", "description": "`subadditive_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of subadditive morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subadditive_hom_class.coe_injective'", "description": "`subadditive_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of subadditive morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subadditive_hom_class.map_add_le_add", "description": "`subadditive_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of subadditive morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_le_add_hom_class", "description": "`mul_le_add_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of subadditive morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_le_add_hom_class.coe", "description": "`mul_le_add_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of subadditive morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_le_add_hom_class.coe_injective'", "description": "`mul_le_add_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of subadditive morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_le_add_hom_class.map_mul_le_add", "description": "`mul_le_add_hom_class F \u03b1 \u03b2` states that `F` is a type of subadditive morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_norm_class.to_add_group_norm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg_hom_class.to_fun_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_norm_class", "description":