n`X` given by multiplication of a constant element of the group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_sub_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.mul_left_to_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.inv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_isometric_vadd.opposite_of_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.const_vadd_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.const_smul_to_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.preimage_mul_left_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.neg_to_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ediam_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.div_left_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nndist_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.add_right_to_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_smul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.div_right_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.preimage_mul_right_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.has_isometric_vadd''", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.div_left_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.linear_proj_add_linear_proj_of_is_compl_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_equiv_of_is_compl", "description": " If `q` is a complement of `p`, then `p \u00d7 q` is isomorphic to `E`. It is the unique\nlinear map `f : E \u2192 p` such that `f x = x` for `x \u2208 p` and `f x = 0` for `x \u2208 q`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.exists_unique_add_of_is_compl_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.linear_proj_of_is_compl_of_proj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient_equiv_of_is_compl_apply_mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_proj.cod_restrict", "description": "Restriction of the codomain of a projection of onto a subspace `p` to `p` instead of the whole\nspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient_equiv_of_is_compl", "description": "If `q` is a complement of `p`, then `M/p \u2243 q`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.of_is_compl_left_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.of_is_compl_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.of_is_compl", "description": " Given linear maps `\u03c6` and `\u03c8` from complement submodules, `of_is_compl` is\nthe induced linear map over the entire module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_proj.eq_conj_prod_map'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.equiv_prod_of_surjective_of_is_compl", "description": " If `f : E \u2192\u2097[R] F` and `g : E \u2192\u2097[R] G` are two surjective linear maps and\ntheir kernels are complement of each other, then `x \u21a6 (f x, g x)` defines\na linear equivalence `E \u2243\u2097[R] F \u00d7 G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_proj_iff_idempotent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient_equiv_of_is_compl_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.of_is_compl_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_proj.is_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.coe_prod_equiv_of_is_compl'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.linear_proj_of_is_compl", "description": "Projection to a submodule along its complement.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.coe_prod_equiv_of_is_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.of_is_compl_prod", "description": "The linear map from `(p \u2192\u2097[R\u2081] F) \u00d7 (q \u2192\u2097[R\u2081] F)` to `E \u2192\u2097[R\u2081] F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.of_is_compl_prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_compl_equiv_proj", "description": " Equivalence between submodules `q` such that `is_compl p q` and linear maps `f : E \u2192\u2097[R] p`\nsuch that `\u2200 x : p, f x = x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_equiv_of_is_compl_symm_apply_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_comm_trans_prod_equiv_of_is_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_proj.cod_restrict_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.exists_unique_add_of_is_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coe_equiv_prod_of_surjective_of_is_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.linear_proj_of_is_compl_apply_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.linear_proj_of_is_compl_apply_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.coe_is_compl_equiv_proj_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.equiv_prod_of_surjective_of_is_compl_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_equiv_of_is_compl_symm_apply_fst_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.linear_proj_of_is_compl_idempotent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_proj", "description": "A linear endomorphism of a module `E` is a projection onto a submodule `p` if it sends every element\nof `E` to `p` and fixes every element of `p`.\nThe definition allow more generally any `fun_like` type and not just linear maps, so that it can be\nused for example with `continuous_linear_map` or `matrix`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_proj.map_mem", "description": "A linear endomorphism of a module `E` is a projection onto a submodule `p` if it sends every element\nof `E` to `p` and fixes every element of `p`.\nThe definition allow more generally any `fun_like` type and not just linear maps, so that it can be\nused for example with `continuous_linear_map` or `matrix`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_proj.map_id", "description": "A linear endomorphism of a module `E` is a projection onto a submodule `p` if it sends every element\nof `E` to `p` and fixes every element of `p`.\nThe definition allow more generally any `fun_like` type and not just linear maps, so that it can be\nused for example with `continuous_linear_map` or `matrix`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_equiv_of_is_compl_symm_apply_snd_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.of_is_compl_prod_equiv", "description": "The natural linear equivalence between `(p \u2192\u2097[R\u2081] F) \u00d7 (q \u2192\u2097[R\u2081] F)` and `E \u2192\u2097[R\u2081] F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_equiv_of_is_compl_symm_apply_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.range_eq_of_proj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.linear_proj_of_is_compl_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ker_id_sub_eq_of_proj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_proj.cod_restrict_apply_cod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.of_is_compl_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_proj.eq_conj_prod_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.coe_is_compl_equiv_proj_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mk_quotient_equiv_of_is_compl_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.of_is_compl_right_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.of_is_compl_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.linear_proj_of_is_compl_ker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.of_is_compl_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_proj.cod_restrict_ker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.linear_proj_of_is_compl_apply_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_compl_of_proj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.linear_proj_of_is_compl_apply_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.linear_proj_of_is_compl_comp_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopic.proj_pi", "description": "Lemmas showing projection is the inverse of pi", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.pi_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.prod", "description": "The product of homotopies `F` and `G`,\n where `F` takes `f\u2080` to `f\u2081`  and `G` takes `g\u2080` to `g\u2081`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopic.proj_left", "description": "Abbreviation for projection onto the left coordinate of a path class", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopic.prod_homotopy", "description": "The product of homotopies h\u2081 and h\u2082.\n   This is `homotopy_rel.prod` specialized for path homotopies.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopic.comp_pi_eq_pi_comp", "description": "Composition and products commute.\n This is `path.trans_pi_eq_pi_trans` descended to path homotopy classes", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopic.proj_right_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopic.pi_proj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopic.prod_proj_left_proj_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopic.proj", "description": "Abbreviation for projection onto the ith coordinate", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopic.pi", "description": "The product of a family of path homotopy classes", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.pi_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopic.prod_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopic.pi_homotopy", "description": "The product of a family of path homotopies. This is just a specialization of `homotopy_rel`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopic.pi_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.pi", "description": "The relative product homotopy of `homotopies` between functions `f` and `g`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.prod_to_homotopy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopic.proj_right", "description": "Abbreviation for projection onto the right coordinate of a path class", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopic.prod", "description": "The product of path classes q\u2081 and q\u2082. This is `path.prod` descended to the quotient", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.pi", "description": "The product homotopy of `homotopies` between functions `f` and `g`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.prod", "description": "The relative product of homotopies `F` and `G`,\n where `F` takes `f\u2080` to `f\u2081`  and `G` takes `g\u2080` to `g\u2081`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopic.proj_left_prod", "description": "Lemmas showing projection is the inverse of product", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.pi_to_homotopy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopic.comp_prod_eq_prod_comp", "description": "Products commute with path composition.\n   This is `trans_prod_eq_prod_trans` descended to the quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.triangle.orthocenter_eq_smul_vsub_vadd_circumcenter", "description": " The position of the orthocenter in relation to the circumcenter\nand centroid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.finrank_direction_altitude", "description": "An altitude is one-dimensional (i.e., a line).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.altitude_def", "description": "The definition of an altitude.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.triangle.orthocenter_replace_orthocenter_eq_point", "description": " Suppose we are given a triangle `t\u2081`, and replace one of its\nvertices by its orthocenter, yielding triangle `t\u2082` (with vertices not\nnecessarily listed in the same order).  Then the orthocenter of `t\u2082`\nis the vertex of `t\u2081` that was replaced.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.mem_altitude", "description": "A vertex lies in the corresponding altitude.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.monge_plane", "description": " A Monge plane of an (n+2)-simplex is the (n+1)-dimensional affine\nsubspace of the subspace spanned by the simplex that passes through\nthe centroid of an n-dimensional face and is orthogonal to the\nopposite edge (in 2 dimensions, this is the same as an altitude).\nThis definition is only intended to be used when `i\u2081 \u2260 i\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.affine_span_of_orthocentric_system", "description": " Any three points in an orthocentric system span the same subspace\nas the whole orthocentric system.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.exists_of_range_subset_orthocentric_system", "description": " This is an auxiliary lemma giving information about the relation\nof two triangles in an orthocentric system; it abstracts some\nreasoning, with no geometric content, that is common to some other\nlemmas.  Suppose the orthocentric system is generated by triangle `t`,\nand we are given three points `p` in the orthocentric system.  Then\neither we can find indices `i\u2081`, `i\u2082` and `i\u2083` for `p` such that `p\ni\u2081` is the orthocenter of `t` and `p i\u2082` and `p i\u2083` are points `j\u2082`\nand `j\u2083` of `t`, or `p` has the same points as `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.triangle.altitude_eq_monge_plane", "description": " In the case of a triangle, altitudes are the same thing as Monge\nplanes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.eq_monge_point_of_forall_mem_monge_plane", "description": " The Monge point is the only point in all the Monge planes from any\none vertex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.monge_point_mem_monge_plane", "description": "The Monge point lies in the Monge planes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.triangle.eq_orthocenter_of_forall_mem_altitude", "description": " The orthocenter is the only point lying in any two of the\naltitudes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.triangle.altitude_replace_orthocenter_eq_affine_span", "description": " Suppose we are given a triangle `t\u2081`, and replace one of its\nvertices by its orthocenter, yielding triangle `t\u2082` (with vertices not\nnecessarily listed in the same order).  Then an altitude of `t\u2082` from\na vertex that was not replaced is the corresponding side of `t\u2081`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.orthocentric_system.affine_independent", "description": "Any three points in an orthocentric system are affinely independent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.triangle.dist_orthocenter_reflection_circumcenter", "description": " The distance from the orthocenter to the reflection of the\ncircumcenter in a side equals the circumradius.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.monge_point_eq_affine_combination_of_points_with_circumcenter", "description": " The Monge point of an (n+2)-simplex, in terms of\n`points_with_circumcenter`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.monge_point_mem_affine_span", "description": "The Monge point lies in the affine span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.orthocentric_system.eq_insert_orthocenter", "description": " Given any triangle in an orthocentric system, the fourth point is\nits orthocenter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.direction_altitude", "description": "The direction of an altitude.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.triangle.orthocenter_mem_altitude", "description": "The orthocenter lies in the altitudes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.sum_monge_point_weights_with_circumcenter", "description": "`monge_point_weights_with_circumcenter` sums to 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.triangle.orthocenter_eq_monge_point", "description": "The orthocenter equals the Monge point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.altitude", "description": " An altitude of a simplex is the line that passes through a vertex\nand is orthogonal to the opposite face.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.triangle.orthocenter_eq_of_range_eq", "description": "Two triangles with the same points have the same orthocenter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.triangle.dist_orthocenter_reflection_circumcenter_finset", "description": " The distance from the orthocenter to the reflection of the\ncircumcenter in a side equals the circumradius, variant using a\n`finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.monge_point_vsub_face_centroid_eq_weighted_vsub_of_points_with_circumcenter", "description": " The Monge point of an (n+2)-simplex, minus the centroid of an\nn-dimensional face, in terms of `points_with_circumcenter`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.sum_monge_point_vsub_face_centroid_weights_with_circumcenter", "description": "`monge_point_vsub_face_centroid_weights_with_circumcenter` sums to 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.orthocentric_system.exists_circumradius_eq", "description": "All triangles in an orthocentric system have the same circumradius.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.monge_plane_comm", "description": " The Monge plane associated with vertices `i\u2081` and `i\u2082` equals that\nassociated with `i\u2082` and `i\u2081`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.vector_span_is_ortho_altitude_direction", "description": " The vector span of the opposite face lies in the direction\northogonal to an altitude.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.exists_dist_eq_circumradius_of_subset_insert_orthocenter", "description": " For any three points in an orthocentric system generated by\ntriangle `t`, there is a point in the subspace spanned by the triangle\nfrom which the distance of all those three points equals the circumradius.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.monge_point_eq_smul_vsub_vadd_circumcenter", "description": " The position of the Monge point in relation to the circumcenter\nand centroid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.monge_plane_def", "description": "The definition of a Monge plane.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.inner_monge_point_vsub_face_centroid_vsub", "description": " The Monge point of an (n+2)-simplex, minus the centroid of an\nn-dimensional face, is orthogonal to the difference of the two\nvertices not in that face.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.affine_span_pair_eq_altitude_iff", "description": " A line through a vertex is the altitude through that vertex if and\nonly if it is orthogonal to the opposite face.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.monge_point_weights_with_circumcenter", "description": " The weights for the Monge point of an (n+2)-simplex, in terms of\n`points_with_circumcenter`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.finite_dimensional_direction_altitude", "description": "An altitude is finite-dimensional.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.triangle.orthocenter_mem_affine_span", "description": "The orthocenter lies in the affine span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.triangle.affine_span_orthocenter_point_le_altitude", "description": " The affine span of the orthocenter and a vertex is contained in\nthe altitude.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.monge_point_vsub_face_centroid_weights_with_circumcenter_eq_sub", "description": " `monge_point_vsub_face_centroid_weights_with_circumcenter` is the\nresult of subtracting `centroid_weights_with_circumcenter` from\n`monge_point_weights_with_circumcenter`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.monge_point_eq_of_range_eq", "description": "Two simplices with the same points have the same Monge point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.orthocentric_system", "description": " Four points form an orthocentric system if they consist of the\nvertices of a triangle and its orthocenter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.monge_point", "description": " The Monge point of a simplex (in 2 or more dimensions) is a\ngeneralization of the orthocenter of a triangle.  It is defined to be\nthe intersection of the Monge planes, where a Monge plane is the\n(n-1)-dimensional affine subspace of the subspace spanned by the\nsimplex that passes through the centroid of an (n-2)-dimensional face\nand is orthogonal to the opposite edge (in 2 dimensions, this is the\nsame as an altitude).  The circumcenter O, centroid G and Monge point\nM are collinear in that order on the Euler line, with OG : GM = (n-1)\n: 2.  Here, we use that ratio to define the Monge point (so resulting\nin a point that equals the centroid in 0 or 1 dimensions), and then\nshow in subsequent lemmas that the point so defined lies in the Monge\nplanes and is their unique point of intersection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.triangle.orthocenter", "description": " The orthocenter of a triangle is the intersection of its\naltitudes.  It is defined here as the 2-dimensional case of the\nMonge point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.monge_point_vsub_face_centroid_weights_with_circumcenter", "description": " The weights for the Monge point of an (n+2)-simplex, minus the\ncentroid of an n-dimensional face, in terms of\n`points_with_circumcenter`.  This definition is only valid when `i\u2081 \u2260 i\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.direction_monge_plane", "description": "The direction of a Monge plane.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd_dual_comp_forget_to_Lat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd.iso.mk_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd.dual_equiv_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd.dual_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd.dual_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd.has_coe_to_sort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd", "description": "The category of linear orders.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd.dual", "description": "`order_dual` as a functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd.coe_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd.large_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd.linear_order.to_partial_order.category_theory.bundled_hom.parent_projection", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd.iso.mk_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd.has_forget_to_Lat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd.of", "description": "Construct a bundled `LinOrd` from the underlying type and typeclass.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd.dual_equiv", "description": "The equivalence between `LinOrd` and itself induced by `order_dual` both ways.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd.linear_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd.dual_equiv_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd.concrete_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "LinOrd.iso.mk", "description": "Constructs an equivalence between linear orders from an order isomorphism between them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ioo_at_top_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ixx_class_principal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ioo_pure_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ioc_at_bot_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ioo_Iio_Iio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ioc_uIcc_uIcc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ico_Iio_Iio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.uIcc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ioo_Ioi_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ioc_Iio_Iio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Icc_at_bot_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ico_Ici_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Icc_at_top_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ioc_at_top_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ico_pure_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Icc_Icc_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ico_at_bot_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_uIcc_of_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.ord_connected.tendsto_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Icc_uIcc_uIcc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ioc_pure_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ixx_class_of_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_basis.tendsto_Ixx_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ioc_Icc_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ico_Ioi_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ioo_Ici_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ioc_Ioi_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ioo_Iic_Iio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ico_at_top_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ico_Iic_Iio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ixx_class", "description": " A pair of filters `l\u2081`, `l\u2082` has `tendsto_Ixx_class Ixx` property if `Ixx a b` tends to\n`l\u2082.small_sets` as `a` and `b` tend to `l\u2081`. In all instances `Ixx` is one of `Icc`, `Ico`, `Ioc`,\nor `Ioo`. The instances provide the best `l\u2082` for a given `l\u2081`. In many cases `l\u2081 = l\u2082` but\nsometimes we can drop an endpoint from an interval: e.g., we prove `tendsto_Ixx_class Ico (\ud835\udcdf $ Iic\na) (\ud835\udcdf $ Iio a)`, i.e., if `u\u2081 n` and `u\u2082 n` belong eventually to `Iic a`, then the interval `Ico (u\u2081\nn) (u\u2082 n)` is eventually included in `Iio a`.\n\nWe mark `l\u2082` as an `out_param` so that Lean can automatically find an appropriate `l\u2082` based on\n`Ixx` and `l\u2081`. This way, e.g., `tendsto.Ico h\u2081 h\u2082` works without specifying explicitly `l\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ixx_class.tendsto_Ixx", "description": " A pair of filters `l\u2081`, `l\u2082` has `tendsto_Ixx_class Ixx` property if `Ixx a b` tends to\n`l\u2082.small_sets` as `a` and `b` tend to `l\u2081`. In all instances `Ixx` is one of `Icc`, `Ico`, `Ioc`,\nor `Ioo`. The instances provide the best `l\u2082` for a given `l\u2081`. In many cases `l\u2081 = l\u2082` but\nsometimes we can drop an endpoint from an interval: e.g., we prove `tendsto_Ixx_class Ico (\ud835\udcdf $ Iic\na) (\ud835\udcdf $ Iio a)`, i.e., if `u\u2081 n` and `u\u2082 n` belong eventually to `Iic a`, then the interval `Ico (u\u2081\nn) (u\u2082 n)` is eventually included in `Iio a`.\n\nWe mark `l\u2082` as an `out_param` so that Lean can automatically find an appropriate `l\u2082` based on\n`Ixx` and `l\u2081`. This way, e.g., `tendsto.Ico h\u2081 h\u2082` works without specifying explicitly `l\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ioc_Iic_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ioo_at_bot_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Icc_pure_pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ioc_Ici_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_Ixx_class_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.is_quotient_quotient", "description": "`S.normed_mk` satisfies `is_quotient`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.norm_mk_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bdd_below_image_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.lift_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "image_norm_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.normed_comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_mk_zero", "description": "The quotient norm of `0` is `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.lift_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.lift_norm_noninc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_zero_eq_zero", "description": " If `(m : M)` has norm equal to `0` in `M \u29f8 S` for a closed subgroup `S` of `M`, then\n`m \u2208 S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_nhd_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_norm_eq_zero_iff", "description": " The norm of the image of `m : M` in the quotient by `S` is zero if and only if `m` belongs\nto the closure of `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.quotient_norm_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.norm_trivial_quotient_mk", "description": "The operator norm of the projection is `0` if the subspace is dense.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.norm_mk_lt", "description": " For any `x : M \u29f8 S` and any `0 < \u03b5`, there is `m : M` such that `submodule.quotient.mk m = x`\nand `\u2016m\u2016 < \u2016x\u2016 + \u03b5`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.ker_normed_mk", "description": "The kernel of `S.normed_mk` is `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_mk_lt", "description": " For any `x : M \u29f8 S` and any `0 < \u03b5`, there is `m : M` such that `mk' S m = x`\nand `\u2016m\u2016 < \u2016x\u2016 + \u03b5`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.is_quotient.norm_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.normed_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.is_quotient.norm_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.norm_normed_mk_le", "description": "The operator norm of the projection is at most `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_norm_mk_eq", "description": "The norm of the image under the natural morphism to the quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_mk_lt'", "description": "For any `m : M` and any `0 < \u03b5`, there is `s \u2208 S` such that `\u2016m + s\u2016 < \u2016mk' S m\u2016 + \u03b5`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.normed_add_comm_group_quotient", "description": "The quotient in the category of normed groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.normed_mk", "description": "The morphism from a seminormed group to the quotient by a subgroup.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_norm_mk_le", "description": "The norm of the projection is smaller or equal to the norm of the original element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_on_quotient", "description": "The definition of the norm on the quotient by an additive subgroup.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.normed_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.norm_mk_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.seminormed_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.semi_normed_comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_norm_sub_rev", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.is_quotient", "description": " `is_quotient f`, for `f : M \u27f6 N` means that `N` is isomorphic to the quotient of `M`\nby the kernel of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.is_quotient.surjective", "description": " `is_quotient f`, for `f : M \u27f6 N` means that `N` is isomorphic to the quotient of `M`\nby the kernel of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.is_quotient.norm", "description": " `is_quotient f`, for `f : M \u27f6 N` means that `N` is isomorphic to the quotient of `M`\nby the kernel of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_mk_nonneg", "description": "The quotient norm is nonnegative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.normed_mk.apply", "description": "`S.normed_mk` agrees with `quotient_add_group.mk' S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.lift_norm_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_norm_add_le", "description": "The quotient norm satisfies the triangle inequality.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_norm_neg", "description": "The norm on the quotient satisfies `\u2016-x\u2016 = \u2016x\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.normed_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.surjective_normed_mk", "description": "`S.normed_mk` is surjective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.lift", "description": " Given  `f : normed_add_group_hom M N` such that `f s = 0` for all `s \u2208 S`, where,\n`S : add_subgroup M` is closed, the induced morphism `normed_add_group_hom (M \u29f8 S) N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_norm_nonneg", "description": "The quotient norm is nonnegative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.norm_normed_mk", "description": "The operator norm of the projection is `1` if the subspace is not dense.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.complete_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.seminormed_add_comm_group_quotient", "descriptio