ween `log (1-x)` and its Taylor series at `0`,\nwhere the main point of the bound is that it tends to `0`. The goal is to deduce the series\nexpansion of the logarithm, in `has_sum_pow_div_log_of_abs_lt_1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_within_at.log", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.log", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_at.log", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fderiv_within.log", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.continuous_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.exists_FP_of_large", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.exists_idempotent_ultrafilter_le_FP", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FP_drop_subset_FP", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.exists_FS_of_large", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FS.add", "description": "If `m` and `m'` are finite sums in `M`, then so is `m + m'`, provided that `m'`\nis obtained from a subsequence of `M` starting sufficiently late.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.eventually_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FS_partition_regular", "description": "The strong form of **Hindman's theorem**: in any finite cover of\nan FS-set, one the parts contains an FS-set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.eventually_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FP.finset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FP.mul_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.exists_idempotent_ultrafilter_le_FS", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FS.singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.has_mul", "description": "Multiplication of ultrafilters given by `\u2200\u1da0 m in U*V, p m \u2194 \u2200\u1da0 m in U, \u2200\u1da0 m' in V, p (m*m')`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FP_partition_regular", "description": " The strong form of **Hindman's theorem**: in any finite cover of an FP-set, one the parts\ncontains an FP-set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.has_add", "description": "Addition of ultrafilters given by\n`\u2200\u1da0 m in U+V, p m \u2194 \u2200\u1da0 m in U, \u2200\u1da0 m' in V, p (m+m')`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.exists_FS_of_finite_cover", "description": "The weak form of **Hindman's theorem**: in any finite cover\nof a nonempty additive semigroup, one of the parts contains an FS-set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FS.add_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.semigroup", "description": "Semigroup structure on `ultrafilter M` induced by a semigroup structure on `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.add_semigroup", "description": "Additive semigroup structure on `ultrafilter M` induced by an additive semigroup\nstructure on `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FS", "description": " `FS a` is the set of finite sums in `a`, i.e. `m \u2208 FS a` if `m` is the sum of a nonempty\nsubsequence of `a`. We give a direct inductive definition instead of talking about subsequences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FS.head", "description": " `FS a` is the set of finite sums in `a`, i.e. `m \u2208 FS a` if `m` is the sum of a nonempty\nsubsequence of `a`. We give a direct inductive definition instead of talking about subsequences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FS.tail", "description": " `FS a` is the set of finite sums in `a`, i.e. `m \u2208 FS a` if `m` is the sum of a nonempty\nsubsequence of `a`. We give a direct inductive definition instead of talking about subsequences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FS.cons", "description": " `FS a` is the set of finite sums in `a`, i.e. `m \u2208 FS a` if `m` is the sum of a nonempty\nsubsequence of `a`. We give a direct inductive definition instead of talking about subsequences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.exists_FP_of_finite_cover", "description": " The weak form of **Hindman's theorem**: in any finite cover of a nonempty semigroup, one of the\nparts contains an FP-set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FP.mul", "description": " If `m` and `m'` are finite products in `M`, then so is `m * m'`, provided that `m'` is obtained\nfrom a subsequence of `M` starting sufficiently late.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ultrafilter.continuous_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FP", "description": " `FP a` is the set of finite products in `a`, i.e. `m \u2208 FP a` if `m` is the product of a nonempty\nsubsequence of `a`. We give a direct inductive definition instead of talking about subsequences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FP.head", "description": " `FP a` is the set of finite products in `a`, i.e. `m \u2208 FP a` if `m` is the product of a nonempty\nsubsequence of `a`. We give a direct inductive definition instead of talking about subsequences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FP.tail", "description": " `FP a` is the set of finite products in `a`, i.e. `m \u2208 FP a` if `m` is the product of a nonempty\nsubsequence of `a`. We give a direct inductive definition instead of talking about subsequences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FP.cons", "description": " `FP a` is the set of finite products in `a`, i.e. `m \u2208 FP a` if `m` is the product of a nonempty\nsubsequence of `a`. We give a direct inductive definition instead of talking about subsequences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FP.singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FS_iter_tail_sub_FS", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hindman.FS.finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.to_ess_image_comp_essential_image_inclusion_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.to_ess_image_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.to_ess_image", "description": "Given a functor `F : C \u2964 D`, we have an (essentially surjective) functor from `C` to the essential\nimage of `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.ess_image.get_iso", "description": "Extract the isomorphism between `F.obj h.witness` and `Y` itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.faithful.to_ess_image", "description": "The induced functor of a faithful functor is faithful", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.ess_image_eq_of_nat_iso", "description": "Isomorphic functors have equal essential images.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.obj_mem_ess_image", "description": "An object in the image is in the essential image.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.ess_image_inclusion.full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.ess_image_inclusion", "description": "The essential image as a subcategory has a fully faithful inclusion into the target category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.ess_image.of_nat_iso", "description": "If `Y` is in the essential image of `F` then it is in the essential image of `F'` as long as\n`F \u2245 F'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.to_ess_image_obj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.obj_preimage", "description": "Given an essentially surjective functor, we can find a preimage for every object `Y` in the\n   codomain. Applying the functor to this preimage will yield an object isomorphic to `Y`, see\n   `obj_obj_preimage_iso`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.ess_image_inclusion.faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.to_ess_image_comp_essential_image_inclusion_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.ess_image_inclusion_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.to_ess_image.ess_surj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.ess_image_subcategory.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.ess_image.of_iso", "description": "Being in the essential image is a \"hygenic\" property: it is preserved under isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.obj_obj_preimage_iso", "description": "Applying an essentially surjective functor to a preimage of `Y` yields an object that is\n   isomorphic to `Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.ess_image", "description": "The essential image of a functor `F` consists of those objects in the target category which are\nisomorphic to an object in the image of the function `F.obj`. In other words, this is the closure\nunder isomorphism of the function `F.obj`.\nThis is the \"non-evil\" way of describing the image of a functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.ess_image_inclusion_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.to_ess_image_comp_essential_image_inclusion", "description": "The functor `F` factorises through its essential image, where the first functor is essentially\nsurjective and the second is fully faithful.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ess_surj", "description": "A functor `F : C \u2964 D` is essentially surjective if every object of `D` is in the essential image\nof `F`. In other words, for every `Y : D`, there is some `X : C` with `F.obj X \u2245 Y`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/001C>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ess_surj.mem_ess_image", "description": "A functor `F : C \u2964 D` is essentially surjective if every object of `D` is in the essential image\nof `F`. In other words, for every `Y : D`, there is some `X : C` with `F.obj X \u2245 Y`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/001C>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.ess_image.witness", "description": "Get the witnessing object that `Y` is in the subcategory given by `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.full.to_ess_image", "description": "The induced functor of a full functor is full", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.ess_image_subcategory", "description": "The essential image of a functor, interpreted of a full subcategory of the target category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.coe_forget_to_Lat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.iso.mk", "description": " Constructs an equivalence between bounded lattices from an order isomorphism\nbetween them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.category_theory.large_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Lat_to_BddLat_comp_dual_iso_dual_comp_Lat_to_BddLat_inv_app_to_lattice_hom_to_sup_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.has_forget_to_SemilatSup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Lat_to_BddLat_comp_dual_iso_dual_comp_Lat_to_BddLat", "description": "`Lat_to_BddLat` and `order_dual` commute.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Lat_to_BddLat_comp_dual_iso_dual_comp_Lat_to_BddLat_hom_app_to_lattice_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.of", "description": "Construct a bundled `BddLat` from `lattice` + `bounded_order`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.iso.mk_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.iso.mk_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.coe_forget_to_SemilatSup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.forget_SemilatSup_PartOrd_eq_forget_BddOrd_PartOrd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.has_forget_to_SemilatInf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat_dual_comp_forget_to_SemilatInf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.forget_SemilatInf_PartOrd_eq_forget_BddOrd_PartOrd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Lat_to_BddLat", "description": "The functor that adds a bottom and a top element to a lattice. This is the free functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.dual_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat", "description": "The category of bounded lattices with bounded lattice morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.to_Lat", "description": "The category of bounded lattices with bounded lattice morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.is_bounded_order", "description": "The category of bounded lattices with bounded lattice morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.dual_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Lat_to_BddLat_forget_adjunction", "description": " `Lat_to_BddLat` is left adjoint to the forgetful functor, meaning it is the free\nfunctor from `Lat` to `BddLat`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.dual_equiv", "description": "The equivalence between `BddLat` and itself induced by `order_dual` both ways.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.has_coe_to_sort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat_dual_comp_forget_to_BddOrd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.dual", "description": "`order_dual` as a functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.coe_forget_to_SemilatInf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.dual_equiv_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.coe_forget_to_BddOrd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.coe_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.dual_equiv_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.has_forget_to_Lat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.forget_Lat_PartOrd_eq_forget_BddOrd_PartOrd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat_dual_comp_forget_to_Lat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.has_forget_to_BddOrd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat_dual_comp_forget_to_SemilatSup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "BddLat.categ