"", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry.nndist_eq", "description": "An isometry preserves non-negative distances.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.image_emetric_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.comp_continuous_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry.right_inv", "description": "The right inverse of an isometry is an isometry.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_subsingleton", "description": "Any map on a subsingleton is an isometry", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry.preimage_emetric_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry.preimage_set_of_dist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.nndist_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry", "description": " An isometry (also known as isometric embedding) is a map preserving the edistance\nbetween pseudoemetric spaces, or equivalently the distance between pseudometric space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.image_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.refl", "description": "The identity isometry of a space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry.comp_continuous_on_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.image_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.coe_to_homeomorph_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry.maps_to_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry.maps_to_emetric_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.self_comp_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.to_homeomorph_to_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "embedding.to_isometry", "description": " An embedding from a topological space to a metric space is an isometry with respect to the\ninduced metric space structure on the source space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry.edist_eq", "description": "An isometry preserves edistances.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.comp_continuous_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry.isometry_equiv_on_range", "description": " An isometry induces an isometric isomorphism between the source space and the\nrange of the isometry.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.preimage_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry.lipschitz", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.fun_unique", "description": "`equiv.fun_unique` as an `isometry_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.coe_eq_to_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.image_sphere", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.fun_unique_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry.closed_embedding", "description": "An isometry from a complete emetric space is a closed embedding", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.mk'", "description": " Alternative constructor for isometric bijections,\ntaking as input an isometry, and a right inverse.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.fun_unique_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.preimage_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry.ediam_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.symm", "description": "The inverse of an isometric isomorphism, as an isometric isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry.preimage_emetric_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_iff_dist_eq", "description": "On pseudometric spaces, a map is an isometry if and only if it preserves distances.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry.preimage_sphere", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry_equiv.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "isometry.diam_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"n