ward direction of `filter.eventually_small_sets_forall`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.comap_small_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.monotone_small_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.small_sets_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.small_sets_eq_generate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.small_sets_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.frequently_small_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_small_sets_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_small_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_small_sets_eventually", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_antitone_basis.tendsto_small_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.small_sets_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.small_sets_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.small_sets", "description": "The filter `l.small_sets` is the largest filter containing all powersets of members of `l`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.small_sets_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_basis_small_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.of_small_sets", "description": " Generalized **squeeze theorem** (also known as **sandwich theorem**). If `s : \u03b1 \u2192 set \u03b2` is a\nfamily of sets that tends to `filter.small_sets lb` along `la` and `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is a function such\nthat `f x \u2208 s x` eventually along `la`, then `f` tends to `lb` along `la`.\n\nIf `s x` is the closed interval `[g x, h x]` for some functions `g`, `h` that tend to the same limit\n`\ud835\udcdd y`, then we obtain the standard squeeze theorem, see\n`tendsto_of_tendsto_of_tendsto_of_le_of_le'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually.small_sets", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `filter.eventually_small_sets_forall`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.small_sets_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.frequently_small_sets_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.small_sets_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_basis.small_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_small_sets_forall", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_dimensional.finrank_mul_finrank'", "description": " Tower law: if `A` is a `K`-module and `K` is an extension of `F` then\n$\\operatorname{rank}_F(A) = \\operatorname{rank}_F(K) * \\operatorname{rank}_K(A)$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_dimensional.left", "description": " In a tower of field extensions `L / K / F`, if `L / F` is finite, so is `K / F`.\n\n(In fact, it suffices that `L` is a nontrivial ring.)\n\nNote this cannot be an instance as Lean cannot infer `L`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_dimensional.finrank_mul_finrank", "description": " Tower law: if `A` is a `K`-vector space and `K` is a field extension of `F` then\n`dim_F(A) = dim_F(K) * dim_K(A)`.\n\nThis is `finite_dimensional.finrank_mul_finrank'` with one fewer finiteness assumption.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.finite_dimensional''", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_dimensional.subalgebra.is_simple_order_of_finrank_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_dimensional.right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_mul_rank", "description": " Tower law: if `A` is a `K`-module and `K` is an extension of `F` then\n$\\operatorname{rank}_F(A) = \\operatorname{rank}_F(K) * \\operatorname{rank}_K(A)$.\n\nThis is a simpler version of `lift_rank_mul_lift_rank` with `K` and `A` in the same universe.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lift_rank_mul_lift_rank", "description": " Tower law: if `A` is a `K`-module and `K` is an extension of `F` then\n$\\operatorname{rank}_F(A) = \\opera