: "Restrict the codomain of an initial segment", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.init", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.lt_equiv", "description": "Composition of a principal segment with an order isomorphism, as a principal segment", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.antisymm_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.trans", "description": "Composition of functions shows that `\u227ci` is transitive", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.rel_embedding.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.cod_restrict_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.trans_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.subsingleton_of_trichotomous_of_irrefl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.equiv_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.refl", "description": "The identity function shows that `\u227ci` is reflexive", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.trans_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.of_element_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.rel_embedding.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.equiv_lt", "description": "Composition of an order isomorphism with a principal segment, as a principal segment", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.of_is_empty", "description": "Principal segment from an empty type into a type with a minimal element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_embedding.collapse_F", "description": " Given an order embedding into a well order, collapse the order embedding by filling the\ngaps, to obtain an initial segment. Here, we construct the collapsed order embedding pointwise,\nbut the proof of the fact that it is an initial segment will be given in `collapse`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.subsingleton", "description": "Given a well order `s`, there is a most one principal segment embedding of `r` into `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.coe_fn_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.down", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.acc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.trans", "description": "Composition of two principal segments as a principal segment", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.antisymm", "description": " If we have order embeddings between `\u03b1` and `\u03b2` whose images are initial segments, and `\u03b2`\nis a well-order then `\u03b1` and `\u03b2` are order-isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.subrel_iso", "description": "For any principal segment `r \u227ai s`, there is a `subrel` of `s` order isomorphic to `r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.top_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.of_is_empty_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.irrefl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_embedding.collapse_F.not_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.apply_subrel_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.of_element_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.le_lt_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.coe_coe_fn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.of_iso", "description": "An order isomorphism is an initial segment", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.of_is_empty", "description": "Initial segment from an empty type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.le_add", "description": "Initial segment embedding of an order `r` into the disjoint union of `r` and `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg", "description": " If `r` is a relation on `\u03b1` and `s` in a relation on `\u03b2`, then `f : r \u227ai s` is an order\nembedding whose range is an open interval `(-\u221e, top)` for some element `top` of `\u03b2`. Such order\nembeddings are called principal segments", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.to_rel_embedding", "description": " If `r` is a relation on `\u03b1` and `s` in a relation on `\u03b2`, then `f : r \u227ai s` is an order\nembedding whose range is an open interval `(-\u221e, top)` for some element `top` of `\u03b2`. Such order\nembeddings are called principal segments", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.top", "description": " If `r` is a relation on `\u03b1` and `s` in a relation on `\u03b2`, then `f : r \u227ai s` is an order\nembedding whose range is an open interval `(-\u221e, top)` for some element `top` of `\u03b2`. Such order\nembeddings are called principal segments", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.down'", "description": " If `r` is a relation on `\u03b1` and `s` in a relation on `\u03b2`, then `f : r \u227ai s` is an order\nembedding whose range is an open interval `(-\u221e, top)` for some element `top` of `\u03b2`. Such order\nembeddings are called principal segments", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.antisymm_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.le_lt", "description": "Composition of an initial segment taking values in a well order and a principal segment.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.coe_fn_to_rel_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.subrel_iso_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.trans_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.acc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.antisymm.aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.lt_or_eq", "description": " To an initial segment taking values in a well order, one can associate either a principal\nsegment (if the range is not everything, hence one can take as top the minimum of the complement\nof the range) or an order isomorphism (if the range is everything).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.subrel_iso_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_embedding.collapse_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.has_coe_initial_seg", "description": "A principal segment is in particular an initial segment.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.coe_fn_to_rel_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_embedding.collapse_F.lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.init", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.init_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.cod_restrict_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_seg.cod_restrict", "description": "Restrict the codomain of a principal segment", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.init_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg", "description": " If `r` is a relation on `\u03b1` and `s` in a relation on `\u03b2`, then `f : r \u227ci s` is an order\nembedding whose range is an initial segment. That is, whenever `b < f a` in `\u03b2` then `b` is in the\nrange of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.to_rel_embedding", "description": " If `r` is a relation on `\u03b1` and `s` in a relation on `\u03b2`, then `f : r \u227ci s` is an order\nembedding whose range is an initial segment. That is, whenever `b < f a` in `\u03b2` then `b` is in the\nrange of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.init'", "description": " If `r` is a relation on `\u03b1` and `s` in a relation on `\u03b2`, then `f : r \u227ci s` is an order\nembedding whose range is an initial segment. That is, whenever `b < f a` in `\u03b2` then `b` is in the\nrange of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "initial_seg.map_rel_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"nam