"pi.mul_single_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.coe_fn_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.left_cancel_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.eval_monoid_hom", "description": " Evaluation of functions into an indexed collection of monoids at a point is a monoid\nhomomorphism.\nThis is `function.eval i` as a `monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.single_mul_left_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.const_add_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.right_cancel_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.eval_add_hom", "description": "Evaluation of functions into an indexed collection of additive semigroups at a\npoint is an additive semigroup homomorphism.\nThis is `function.eval i` as an `add_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.coe_fn", "description": "Coercion of an `add_monoid_hom` into a function is itself a `add_monoid_hom`.\n\nSee also `add_monoid_hom.eval`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.comp_left", "description": " Monoid homomorphism between the function spaces `I \u2192 \u03b1` and `I \u2192 \u03b2`, induced by a monoid\nhomomorphism `f` between `\u03b1` and `\u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.eval_monoid_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.add_zero_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.coe_fn_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.piecewise_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.single_add_single_eq_single_add_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.update_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.single_commute", "description": "The injection into an additive pi group at different indices commutes.\n\nFor injections of commuting elements at the same index, see `add_commute.map`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.mul_zero_one_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.add_comm_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.single_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.subtraction_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.single_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.circumsphere_radius", "description": "The radius of the circumsphere is the circumradius.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent.exists_unique_dist_eq", "description": " Given a finite nonempty affinely independent family of points,\nthere is a unique (circumcenter, circumradius) pair for those points\nin the affine subspace they span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.circumcenter", "description": "The circumcenter of a simplex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.circumcenter_eq_of_cospherical", "description": " Two n-simplices among cospherical points in n-space have the same\ncircumcenter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.circumcenter_eq_point", "description": "The circumcenter of a 0-simplex equals its unique point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.circumcenter_reindex", "description": "Reindexing a simplex along an `equiv` of index types does not change the circumcenter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.circumsphere_reindex", "description": "Reindexing a simplex along an `equiv` of index types does not change the circumsphere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.circumradius_eq_of_cospherical", "description": " Two n-simplices among cospherical points in n-space have the same\ncircumradius.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.orthogonal_projection_vadd_smul_vsub_orthogonal_projection", "description": " Adding a vector to a point in the given subspace, then taking the\northogonal projection, produces the original point if the vector is a\nmultiple of the result of subtracting a point's orthogonal projection\nfrom that point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.circumradius_eq_of_cospherical_subset", "description": " Two n-simplices among cospherical points in an n-dimensional\nsubspace have the same circumradius.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.points_with_circumcenter", "description": "The vertices of a simplex plus its circumcenter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.circumsphere_center", "description": "The center of the circumsphere is the circumcenter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.reflection_circumcenter_weights_with_circumcenter", "description": " The weights for the reflection of the circumcenter in an edge of a\nsimplex.  This definition is only valid with `i\u2081 \u2260 i\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.circumsphere", "description": "The circumsphere of a simplex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.exists_circumradius_eq_of_cospherical", "description": " All n-simplices among cospherical points in n-space have the same\ncircumradius.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.centroid_weights_with_circumcenter", "description": " The weights for the centroid of some vertices of a simplex, in\nterms of `points_with_circumcenter`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.sum_point_weights_with_circumcenter", "description": "`point_weights_with_circumcenter` sums to 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.exists_unique_dist_eq_of_insert", "description": " The induction step for the existence and uniqueness of the\ncircumcenter.  Given a nonempty set of points in a nonempty affine\nsubspace whose direction is complete, such that there is a unique\n(circumcenter, circumradius) pair for those points in that subspace,\nand a point `p` not in that subspace, there is a unique (circumcenter,\ncircumradius) pair for the set with `p` added, in the span of the\nsubspace with `p` added.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.circumcenter_eq_centroid", "description": "The circumcenter of a 1-simplex equals its centroid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.sum_points_with_circumcenter", "description": "The sum of a function over `points_with_circumcenter_index`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.dist_set_eq_iff_dist_orthogonal_projection_eq", "description": " `p` is equidistant from a set of points in `s` if and only if its\n`orthogonal_projection` is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.sum_reflection_circumcenter_weights_with_circumcenter", "description": "`reflection_circumcenter_weights_with_circumcenter` sums to 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.exists_circumradius_eq_of_cospherical_subset", "description": " All n-simplices among cospherical points in an n-dimensional\nsubspace have the same circumradius.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.orthogonal_projection_eq_circumcenter_of_exists_dist_eq", "description": " If there exists a distance that a point has from all vertices of a\nsimplex, the orthogonal projection of that point onto the subspace\nspanned by that simplex is its circumcenter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.coe_orthogonal_projection_vadd_smul_vsub_orthogonal_projection", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.points_with_circumcenter_index_inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.eq_circumradius_of_dist_eq", "description": " Given a point in the affine span from which all the points are\nequidistant, that distance is the circumradius.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.eq_circumcenter_of_dist_eq", "description": " Given a point in the affine span from which all the points are\nequidistant, that point is the circumcenter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.circumradius_pos", "description": " The circumradius of a simplex with at least two points is\npositive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.point_weights_with_circumcenter", "description": " The weights for a single vertex of a simplex, in terms of\n`points_with_circumcenter`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.orthogonal_projection_circumcenter", "description": " The orthogonal projection of the circumcenter onto a face is the\ncircumcenter of that face.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.circumradius", "description": "The circumradius of a simplex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.point_index_embedding", "description": "`point_index` as an embedding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.exists_circumcenter_eq_of_cospherical_subset", "description": " All n-simplices among cospherical points in an n-dimensional\nsubspace have the same circumcenter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.dist_circumcenter_eq_circumradius", "description": " All points have distance from the circumcenter equal to the\ncircumradius.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.circumcenter_mem_affine_span", "description": "The circumcenter lies in the affine span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.circumsphere_eq_of_cospherical", "description": " Two n-simplices among cospherical points in n-space have the same\ncircumsphere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.sum_circumcenter_weights_with_circumcenter", "description": "`circumcenter_weights_with_circumcenter` sums to 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.point_eq_affine_combination_of_points_with_circumcenter", "description": "A single vertex, in terms of `points_with_circumcenter`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.eq_or_eq_reflection_of_dist_eq", "description": " Suppose all distances from `p\u2081` and `p\u2082` to the points of a\nsimplex are equal, and that `p\u2081` and `p\u2082` lie in the affine span of\n`p` with the vertices of that simplex.  Then `p\u2081` and `p\u2082` are equal\nor reflections of each other in the affine span of the vertices of the\nsimplex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.cospherical_iff_exists_mem_of_finite_dimensional", "description": " Given a nonempty affine subspace, whose direction is\nfinite-dimensional, that contains a set of points, those points are\ncospherical if and only if they are equidistant from some point in\nthat subspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.circumcenter_eq_affine_combination_of_points_with_circumcenter", "description": " The circumcenter of a simplex, in terms of\n`points_with_circumcenter`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.dist_circumcenter_eq_circumradius'", "description": " All points have distance to the circumcenter equal to the\ncircumradius.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.circumcenter_weights_with_circumcenter", "description": " The weights for the circumcenter of a simplex, in terms of\n`points_with_circumcenter`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.mem_circumsphere", "description": "All points lie in the circumsphere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.circumcenter_eq_of_range_eq", "description": "Two simplices with the same points have the same circumcenter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.exists_dist_eq_iff_exists_dist_orthogonal_projection_eq", "description": " There exists `r` such that `p` has distance `r` from all the\npoints of a set of points in `s` if and only if there exists (possibly\ndifferent) `r` such that its `orthogonal_projection` has that distance\nfrom all the points in that set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.points_with_circumcenter_index.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.dist_eq_iff_dist_orthogonal_projection_eq", "description": " `p` is equidistant from two points in `s` if and only if its\n`orthogonal_projection` is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.circumcenter_eq_of_cospherical_subset", "description": " Two n-simplices among cospherical points in an n-dimensional\nsubspace have the same circumcenter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.exists_circumsphere_eq_of_cospherical_subset", "description": " All n-simplices among cospherical points in an n-dimensional\nsubspace have the same circumsphere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.sum_centroid_weights_with_circumcenter", "description": " `centroid_weights_with_circumcenter` sums to 1, if the `finset` is\nnonempty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.reflection_circumcenter_eq_affine_combination_of_points_with_circumcenter", "description": " The reflection of the circumcenter of a simplex in an edge, in\nterms of `points_with_circumcenter`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.orthogonal_projection_eq_circumcenter_of_dist_eq", "description": " If a point has the same distance from all vertices of a simplex,\nthe orthogonal projection of that point onto the subspace spanned by\nthat simplex is its circumcenter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.exists_circumsphere_eq_of_cospherical", "description": " All n-simplices among cospherical points in n-space have the same\ncircumsphere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.circumsphere_unique_dist_eq", "description": "The property satisfied by the circumsphere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.dist_circumcenter_sq_eq_sq_sub_circumradius", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.exists_circumcenter_eq_of_cospherical", "description": " All n-simplices among cospherical points in n-space have the same\ncircumcenter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.circumsphere_eq_of_cospherical_subset", "description": " Two n-simplices among cospherical points in an n-dimensional\nsubspace have the same circumsphere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.circumradius_reindex", "description": "Reindexing a simplex along an `equiv` of index types does not change the circumradius.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.points_with_circumcenter_eq_circumcenter", "description": " `points_with_circumcenter`, applied to `circumcenter_index`, equals the\ncircumcenter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.circumradius_nonneg", "description": "The circumradius is non-negative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.points_with_circumcenter_index", "description": " An index type for the vertices of a simplex plus its circumcenter.\nThis is for use in calculations where it is convenient to work with\naffine combinations of vertices together with the circumcenter.  (An\nequivalent form sometimes used in the literature is placing the\ncircumcenter at the origin and working with vectors for the vertices.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.points_with_circumcenter_index.point_index", "description": " An index type for the vertices of a simplex plus its circumcenter.\nThis is for use in calculations where it is convenient to work with\naffine combinations of vertices together with the circumcenter.  (An\nequivalent form sometimes used in the literature is placing the\ncircumcenter at the origin and working with vectors for the vertices.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.points_with_circumcenter_index.circumcenter_index", "description": " An index type for the vertices of a simplex plus its circumcenter.\nThis is for use in calculations where it is convenient to work with\naffine combinations of vertices together with the circumcenter.  (An\nequivalent form sometimes used in the literature is placing the\ncircumcenter at the origin and working with vectors for the vertices.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.orthogonal_projection_span", "description": "The orthogonal projection of a point `p` onto the hyperplane spanned by the simplex's points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.dist_sq_eq_dist_orthogonal_projection_sq_add_dist_orthogonal_projection_sq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.points_with_circumcenter_point", "description": " `points_with_circumcenter`, applied to a `point_index` value,\nequals `points` applied to that value.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.centroid_eq_affine_combination_of_points_with_circumcenter", "description": " The centroid of some vertices of a simplex, in terms of\n`points_with_circumcenter`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.cospherical_iff_exists_mem_of_complete", "description": " Given a nonempty affine subspace, whose direction is complete,\nthat contains a set of points, those points are cospherical if and\nonly if they are equidistant from some point in that subspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sigma_lift_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mem_sigma_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sigma_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sigma_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sigma_lift", "description": "Lifts maps `\u03b1 i \u2192 \u03b2 i \u2192 finset (\u03b3 i)` to a map `\u03a3 i, \u03b1 i \u2192 \u03a3 i, \u03b2 i \u2192 finset (\u03a3 i, \u03b3 i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sigma_eq_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.disj_Union_map_sigma_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sigma_lift_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_sigma_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mk_mem_sigma_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.inf_sigma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sigma_eq_bUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_sigma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mem_sigma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.not_mem_sigma_lift_of_ne_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.coe_sigma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.pairwise_disjoint_map_sigma_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sigma", "description": "`s.sigma t` is the finset of dependent pairs `\u27e8i, a\u27e9` such that `i \u2208 s` and `a \u2208 t i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sigma_lift_eq_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.not_mem_sigma_lift_of_ne_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field.normal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field_aux.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field_aux.of_mv_polynomial", "description": " The natural map from `mv_polynomial (f.root_set (splitting_field_aux f.nat_degree f))`\nto `splitting_field_aux f.nat_degree f` sendind a variable to the corresponding root.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.is_splitting_field.polynomial.splitting_field.no_zero_smul_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.is_splitting_field.alg_equiv", "description": "Any splitting field is isomorphic to `splitting_field f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.fact_irreducible_factor", "description": "See note [fact non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field_aux.of_mv_polynomial_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.is_splitting_field.splitting_field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.is_splitting_field.polynomial.splitting_field.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.factor_dvd_of_degree_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field_aux.algebra''", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field.adjoin_root_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field_aux", "description": " Auxiliary construction to a splitting field of a polynomial, which removes\n`n` (arbitrarily-chosen) factors. It is the type constructed in `splitting_field_aux_aux`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.remove_factor", "description": "Divide a polynomial f by X - C r where r is a root of f in a bigger field extension.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field.char_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field_aux.adjoin_root_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field_aux.algebra'''", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field_aux.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field_aux.algebra'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_remove_factor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field_aux.field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.factor_dvd_of_nat_degree_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field_aux_aux", "description": " Auxiliary construction to a splitting field of a polynomial, which removes\n`n` (arbitrarily-chosen) factors.\n\nIt constructs the type, proves that is a field and algebra over the base field.\n\nUses recursion on the degree.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_remove_factor'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.X_sub_C_mul_remove_factor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field.splits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field.alg_equiv_splitting_field_aux", "description": " The algebra equivalence with `splitting_field_aux`,\nwhich we will use to construct the field structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field.algebra'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.factor_dvd_of_not_is_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field_aux.succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field_aux.alg_equiv_quotient_mv_polynomial", "description": " The algebra isomorphism between the quotient of\n`mv_polynomial (f.root_set (splitting_field_aux f.nat_degree f)) K` by the kernel of\n`of_mv_polynomial f` and `splitting_field_aux f.nat_degree f`. It is used to transport all the\nalgebraic structures from the latter to `f.splitting_field`, that is defined as the former.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field.lift", "description": "Embeds the splitting field into any other field that splits the polynomial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field.field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field_aux.splits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field", "description": "A splitting field of a polynomial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field_aux.polynomial.is_splitting_field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field_aux.scalar_tower'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field_aux.algebra_map_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.factor", "description": "Non-computably choose an irreducible factor from a polynomial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.is_splitting_field.polynomial.splitting_field.finite_dimensional", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.irreducible_factor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.splitting_field.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.gen.monad", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.gen.has_orelse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.gen.freq_aux", "description": "`freq_aux xs i _` takes a weighted list of generator and a number meant to select one of the\ngenerators.\n\nIf we consider `freq_aux [(1, gena), (3, genb), (5, genc)] 4 _`, we choose a generator by splitting\nthe interval 1-9 into 1-1, 2-4, 5-9 so that the width of each interval corresponds to one of the\nnumber in the list of generators. Then, we check which interval 4 falls into: it selects `genb`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.gen.resize", "description": "Apply a function to the size parameter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.gen.list_of", "description": " Create a list of examples using `cmd`. The size is controlled\nby the size parameter of `gen`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.gen.choose", "description": "Lift `random.random_r` to the `gen` monad.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.gen.vector_of", "description": "Create `n` examples using `cmd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.io.run_gen", "description": " Execute a `gen` inside the `io` monad using `i` as the example\nsize and with a fresh random number generator.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.gen.elements", "description": "Given a list of example generators, choose one to create an example.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.gen.choose_any", "description": "Lift `random.random` to the `gen` monad.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.gen.choose_nat", "description": "Generate a `nat` example between `x` and `y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.gen", "description": " Monad to generate random examples to test properties with.\nIt has a `nat` parameter so that the caller can decide on the\nsize of the examples.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.gen.is_lawful_monad", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.gen.choose_nat'", "description": "Generate a `nat` example between `x` and `y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.gen.freq", "description": "`freq [(1, gena), (3, genb), (5, genc)] _` will choose one of `gena`, `genb`, `genc` with\nprobabilities proportional to the number accompanying them. In this example, the sum of\nthose numbers is 9, `gena` will be chosen with probability ~1/9, `genb` with ~3/9 (i.e. 1/3)\nand `genc` with probability 5/9.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.gen.sized", "description": " Get access to the size parameter of the `gen` monad. For\nreasons of universe polymorphism, it is specified in\ncontinuation passing style.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.gen.one_of", "description": "Given a list of example generators, choose one to create an example.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.gen.permutation_of", "description": "Generate a random permutation of a given list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slim_check.gen.uliftable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.change_origin", "description": "Changing the origin of a formal multilinear series `p`, so that\n`p.sum (x+y) = (p.change_origin x).sum y` when this makes sense.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.le_radius_of_summable_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.radius_eq_top_of_summable_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.radius_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.const_formal_multilinear_series_radius", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.change_origin_eval", "description": "Summing the series `p.change_origin x` at a point `y` gives back `p (x + y)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.eq_formal_multilinear_series", "description": "One-dimensional formal multilinear series representing the same function are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at", "description": " Given a function `f : E \u2192 F` and a formal multilinear series `p`, we say that `f` has `p` as\na power series around `x` if `f (x + y) = \u2211' p\u2099 y\u207f` for all `y` in a neighborhood of `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.uniform_geometric_approx'", "description": " If a function admits a power series expansion, then it is exponentially close to the partial\nsums of this power series on strict subdisks of the disk of convergence.\n\nThis version provides an upper estimate that decreases both in `\u2016y\u2016` and `n`. See also\n`has_fpower_series_on_ball.uniform_geometric_approx` for a weaker version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.eventually_has_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.summable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.has_fpower_series_on_ball_change_origin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.comp_has_fpower_series_on_ball", "description": " If a function `f` has a power series `p` on a ball and `g` is linear, then `g \u2218 f` has the\npower series `g \u2218 p` on the same ball.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.change_origin_index_equiv_apply_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.analytic_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.r_eq_top_of_exists", "description": " If a function `f : \ud835\udd5c \u2192 E` has power series representation `p` on a ball of some radius and for\neach positive radius it has some power series representation, then `p` converges to `f` on the whole\n`\ud835\udd5c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.le_radius_of_is_O", "description": "If `\u2016p\u2099\u2016 r\u207f = O(1)`, as `n \u2192 \u221e`, then the radius of `p` is at least `r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.eventually_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.le_radius_of_bound_nnreal", "description": "If `\u2016p\u2099\u2016 r\u207f` is bounded in `n`, then the radius of `p` is at least `r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.exchange_radius", "description": " If a function `f : \ud835\udd5c \u2192 E` has two power series representations at `x`, then the given radii in\nwhich convergence is guaranteed may be interchanged. This can be useful when the formal multilinear\nseries in one representation has a particularly nice form, but the other has a larger radius.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.radius_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.summable_norm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.continuous_on", "description": "The sum of a converging power series is continuous in its disk of convergence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.eventually_has_sum_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.tendsto_locally_uniformly_on", "description": " If a function admits a power series expansion at `x`, then it is the locally uniform limit of\nthe partial sums of this power series on the disk of convergence, i.e., `f (x + y)`\nis the locally uniform limit of `p.partial_sum n y` there.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.nnnorm_change_origin_series_term_apply_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.le_radius_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.coeff_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.summable_norm_mul_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.norm_mul_pow_le_of_lt_radius", "description": "For `r` strictly smaller than the radius of `p`, then `\u2016p\u2099\u2016 r\u207f` is bounded.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "analytic_on.continuous_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.le_mul_pow_of_radius_pos", "description": "If the radius of `p` is positive, then `\u2016p\u2099\u2016` grows at most geometrically.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.change_origin_index_equiv_symm_apply_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.le_radius_of_bound", "description": "If `\u2016p\u2099\u2016 r\u207f` is bounded in `n`, then the radius of `p` is at least `r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.coeff_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.nnnorm_mul_pow_le_of_lt_radius", "description": "For `r` strictly smaller than the radius of `p`, then `\u2016p\u2099\u2016 r\u207f` is bounded.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.not_summable_norm_of_radius_lt_nnnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.partial_sum", "description": " Given a formal multilinear series `p` and a vector `x`, then `p.partial_sum n x` is the sum\n`\u03a3 p\u2096 x\u1d4f` for `k \u2208 {0,..., n-1}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.is_O_image_sub_norm_mul_norm_sub", "description": " If `f` has formal power series `\u2211 n, p\u2099` at `x`, then\n`f y - f z - p 1 (\u03bb _, y - z) = O(\u2016(y, z) - (x, x)\u2016 * \u2016y - z\u2016)` as `(y, z) \u2192 (x, x)`.\nIn particular, `f` is strictly differentiable at `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.uniform_geometric_approx", "description": " If a function admits a power series expansion, then it is exponentially close to the partial\nsums of this power series on strict subdisks of the disk of convergence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.is_O_image_sub_image_sub_deriv_principal", "description": " If `f` has formal power series `\u2211 n, p\u2099` on a ball of radius `r`, then for `y, z` in any smaller\nball, the norm of the difference `f y - f z - p 1 (\u03bb _, y - z)` is bounded above by\n`C * (max \u2016y - x\u2016 \u2016z - x\u2016) * \u2016y - z\u2016`. This lemma formulates this property using `is_O` and\n`filter.principal` on `E \u00d7 E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.radius_le_radius_continuous_linear_map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.min_radius_le_radius_add", "description": "The radius of the sum of two formal series is at least the minimum of their two radii.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.eventually_has_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "analytic_at.continuous_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.change_origin", "description": " If a function admits a power series expansion `p` on a ball `B (x, r)`, then it also admits a\npower series on any subball of this ball (even with a different center), given by `p.change_origin`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.tendsto_locally_uniformly_on'", "description": " If a function admits a power series expansion at `x`, then it is the locally uniform limit of\nthe  partial sums of this power series on the disk of convergence, i.e., `f y`\nis the locally uniform limit of `p.partial_sum n (y - x)` there.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.is_O_sub_partial_sum_pow", "description": "Taylor formula for an analytic function, `is_O` version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "analytic_at_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.partial_sum_continuous", "description": "The partial sums of a formal multilinear series are continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "analytic_on.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball", "description": " Given a function `f : E \u2192 F` and a formal multilinear series `p`, we say that `f` has `p` as\na power series on the ball of radius `r > 0` around `x` if `f (x + y) = \u2211' p\u2099 y\u207f` for all `\u2016y\u2016 < r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.r_le", "description": " Given a function `f : E \u2192 F` and a formal multilinear series `p`, we say that `f` has `p` as\na power series on the ball of radius `r > 0` around `x` if `f (x + y) = \u2211' p\u2099 y\u207f` for all `\u2016y\u2016 < r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.r_pos", "description": " Given a function `f : E \u2192 F` and a formal multilinear series `p`, we say that `f` has `p` as\na power series on the ball of radius `r > 0` around `x` if `f (x + y) = \u2211' p\u2099 y\u207f` for all `\u2016y\u2016 < r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.has_sum", "description": " Given a function `f : E \u2192 F` and a formal multilinear series `p`, we say that `f` has `p` as\na power series on the ball of radius `r > 0` around `x` if `f (x + y) = \u2211' p\u2099 y\u207f` for all `\u2016y\u2016 < r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.eventually_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.tendsto_uniformly_on", "description": " If a function admits a power series expansion at `x`, then it is the uniform limit of the\npartial sums of this power series on strict subdisks of the disk of convergence, i.e., `f (x + y)`\nis the uniform limit of `p.partial_sum n y` there.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.radius_eq_top_of_eventually_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.has_fpower_series_on_ball", "description": " In a complete space, the sum of a converging power series `p` admits `p` as a power series.\nThis is not totally obvious as we need to check the convergence of the series.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "analytic_at.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.norm_le_div_pow_of_pos_of_lt_radius", "description": "For `r` strictly smaller than the radius of `p`, then `\u2016p\u2099\u2016 r\u207f` is bounded.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.radius_eq_top_of_forall_image_add_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.comp_sub", "description": " If a function `f` has a power series `p` around `x`, then the function `z \u21a6 f (z - y)` has the\nsame power series around `x + y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.radius_eq_top_iff_summable_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.comp_analytic_on", "description": " If a function `f` is analytic on a set `s` and `g` is linear, then `g \u2218 f` is analytic\non `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.change_origin_series_summable_aux\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.is_o_of_lt_radius", "description": " For `r` strictly smaller than the radius of `p`, then `\u2016p\u2099\u2016 r\u207f` tends to zero exponentially:\nfor some `0 < a < 1`, `\u2016p n\u2016 r\u207f = o(a\u207f)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.tendsto_uniformly_on'", "description": " If a function admits a power series expansion at `x`, then it is the uniform limit of the\npartial sums of this power series on strict subdisks of the disk of convergence, i.e., `f y`\nis the uniform limit of `p.partial_sum n (y - x)` there.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.nnnorm_change_origin_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.has_sum_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "analytic_at.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_analytic_at", "description": " For any function `f` from a normed vector space to a Banach space, the set of points `x` such\nthat `f` is analytic at `x` is open.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.change_origin_index_equiv", "description": " An auxiliary equivalence useful in the proofs about\n`formal_multilinear_series.change_origin_series`: the set of triples `(k, l, s)`, where `s` is a\n`finset (fin (k + l))` of cardinality `l` is equivalent to the set of pairs `(n, s)`, where `s` is a\n`finset (fin n)`.\n\nThe forward map sends `(k, l, s)` to `(k + l, s)` and the inverse map sends `(n, s)` to\n`(n - finset.card s, finset.card s, s)`. The actual definition is less readable because of problems\nwith non-definitional equalities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.summable_nnnorm_mul_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.continuous_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.change_origin_index_equiv_apply_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.change_origin_series_summable_aux\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "analytic_on_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.eq_zero_of_eventually", "description": "A one-dimensional formal multilinear series representing a locally zero function is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.radius_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.eventually_has_sum_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.change_origin_index_equiv_symm_apply_snd_snd_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.image_sub_sub_deriv_le", "description": " If `f` has formal power series `\u2211 n, p\u2099` on a ball of radius `r`, then for `y, z` in any smaller\nball, the norm of the difference `f y - f z - p 1 (\u03bb _, y - z)` is bounded above by\n`C * (max \u2016y - x\u2016 \u2016z - x\u2016) * \u2016y - z\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.nnnorm_change_origin_series_apply_le_tsum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "analytic_on.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.analytic_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.analytic_at_of_mem", "description": " If a function admits a power series expansion `p` on an open ball `B (x, r)`, then\nit is analytic at every point of this ball.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at_iff", "description": " A function `f : \ud835\udd5c \u2192 E` has `p` as power series expansion at a point `z\u2080` iff it is the sum of\n`p` in a neighborhood of `z\u2080`. This makes some proofs easier by hiding the fact that\n`has_fpower_series_at` depends on `p.radius`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.continuous_on", "description": "If a function admits a power series expansion on a disk, then it is continuous there.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.has_fpower_series_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.change_origin_index_equiv_symm_apply_snd_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.norm_mul_pow_le_mul_pow_of_lt_radius", "description": " For `r` strictly smaller than the radius of `p`, then `\u2016p\u2099\u2016 r\u207f` tends to zero exponentially:\nfor some `0 < a < 1` and `C > 0`,  `\u2016p n\u2016 * r ^ n \u2264 C * a ^ n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.change_origin_radius", "description": " The radius of convergence of `p.change_origin x` is at least `p.radius - \u2016x\u2016`. In other words,\n`p.change_origin x` is well defined on the largest ball contained in the original ball of\nconvergence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.norm_change_origin_series_term", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "analytic_at", "description": " Given a function `f : E \u2192 F`, we say that `f` is analytic at `x` if it admits a convergent power\nseries expansion around `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.eq_zero", "description": "A one-dimensional formal multilinear series representing the zero function is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.eventually", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.radius", "description": " The radius of a formal multilinear series is the largest `r` such that the sum `\u03a3 \u2016p\u2099\u2016 \u2016y\u2016\u207f`\nconverges for all `\u2016y\u2016 < r`. This implies that `\u03a3 p\u2099 y\u207f` converges for all `\u2016y\u2016 < r`, but these\ndefinitions are *not* equivalent in general.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "analytic_on.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.le_radius_of_summable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.le_radius_of_summable_nnnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.le_change_origin_series_radius", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.is_o_one_of_lt_radius", "description": "For `r` strictly smaller than the radius of `p`, then `\u2016p\u2099\u2016 r\u207f = o(1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.change_origin_series_summable_aux\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.lt_radius_of_is_O", "description": "If `r \u2260 0` and `\u2016p\u2099\u2016 r\u207f = O(a\u207f)` for some `-1 < a < 1`, then `r < p.radius`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.nnnorm_change_origin_series_le_tsum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "analytic_at.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.change_origin_series_term", "description": " A term of `formal_multilinear_series.change_origin_series`.\n\nGiven a formal multilinear series `p` and a point `x` in its ball of convergence,\n`p.change_origin x` is a formal multilinear series such that\n`p.sum (x+y) = (p.change_origin x).sum y` when this makes sense. Each term of `p.change_origin x`\nis itself an analytic function of `x` given by the series `p.change_origin_series`. Each term in\n`change_origin_series` is the sum of `change_origin_series_term`'s over all `s` of cardinality `l`.\nThe definition is such that\n`p.change_origin_series_term k l s hs (\u03bb _, x) (\u03bb _, y) = p (k + l) (s.piecewise (\u03bb _, x) (\u03bb _, y))`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.nnnorm_change_origin_series_term", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.is_O.continuous_multilinear_map_apply_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.apply_eq_zero", "description": " If a formal multilinear series `p` represents the zero function at `x : E`, then the\nterms `p n (\u03bb i, y)` appearing the in sum are zero for any `n : \u2115`, `y : E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.change_origin_series_term_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.eq_formal_multilinear_series_of_eventually", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.radius_eq_top_of_forall_nnreal_is_O", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.sum", "description": " Given a formal multilinear series `p` and a vector `x`, then `p.sum x` is the sum `\u03a3 p\u2099 x\u207f`. A\npriori, it only behaves well when `\u2016x\u2016 < p.radius`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.le_radius_of_eventually_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.has_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.change_origin_series", "description": " The power series for `f.change_origin k`.\n\nGiven a formal multilinear series `p` and a point `x` in its ball of convergence,\n`p.change_origin x` is a formal multilinear series such that\n`p.sum (x+y) = (p.change_origin x).sum y` when this makes sense. Its `k`-th term is the sum of\nthe series `p.change_origin_series k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "analytic_on", "description": " Given a function `f : E \u2192 F`, we say that `f` is analytic on a set `s` if it is analytic around\nevery point of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_ball.analytic_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.tendsto_const_mul_rpow_nhds_zero_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.continuous_at_const_rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.nnrpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.continuous_at_cpow_of_re_pos", "description": " See also `continuous_at_cpow` for a version that assumes `p.1 \u2260 0` but makes no\nassumptions about `p.2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.continuous_at_const_rpow'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at.cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnreal.eventually_pow_one_div_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.ennrpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_const_cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnreal.continuous_rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.continuous_at_rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.continuous_rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.rpow_eq_nhds_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_cpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.continuous_at_rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cpow_eq_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.rpow_eq_nhds_of_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.continuous_at_cpow_zero_of_re_pos", "description": "See also `continuous_at_cpow` and `complex.continuous_at_cpow_of_re_pos`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.continuous_at_rpow_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_cpow_eq_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.continuous_of_real_cpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnreal.continuous_at_rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.const_cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.continuous_at_cpow_const_of_re_pos", "description": " See also `continuous_at_cpow_const` for a version that assumes `z \u2260 0` but makes no\nassumptions about `w`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cpow_eq_nhds'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.cpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.const_cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.continuous_at_of_real_cpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.continuous_at_of_real_cpow", "description": "Continuity of `(x, y) \u21a6 x ^ y` as a function on `\u211d \u00d7 \u2102`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.const_cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at.const_cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_cpow", "description": " The function `z ^ w` is continuous in `(z, w)` provided that `z` does not belong to the interval\n`(-\u221e, 0]` on the real line. See also `complex.continuous_at_cpow_zero_of_re_pos` for a version that\nworks for `z = 0` but assumes `0 < re w`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.const_cpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_const_cpow'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.continuous_at_rpow_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.eventually_pow_one_div_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at.rpow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnreal.continuous_at_rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.zero_of_source_iso_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.zero_iso_terminal_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.id_zero_equiv_iso_zero_apply_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.of_mono_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_of_source_target_iso_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.id_zero_equiv_iso_zero_apply_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.iff_is_split_epi_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_zero_self_equiv", "description": "A zero morphism `0 : X \u27f6 X` is an isomorphism if and only if\nthe identity on `X` is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_morphisms.comp_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation_zero_m", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.zero_of_comp_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.zero_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.iff_is_split_mono_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.iso_zero_of_mono_eq_zero", "description": "If a monomorphism out of `X` is zero, then `X \u2245 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.nonzero_image_of_nonzero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.zero_of_source_iso_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.zero_iso_initial_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.zero_iso_terminal_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object_of_has_initial_object", "description": "If there are zero morphisms, any initial object is a zero object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.zero_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.id_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_morphisms_punit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.comp_factor_thru_image_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_zero_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_morphisms.zero_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.of_epi_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.id_zero_equiv_iso_zero", "description": "An object `X` has `\ud835\udfd9 X = 0` if and only if it is isomorphic to the zero object.\n\nBecause `X \u2245 0` contains data (even if a subsingleton), we express this `\u2194` as an `\u2243`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.zero_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_split_epi_prod_snd", "description": "In the presence of zero morphisms, projections into a product are (split) epimorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation_zero_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.iff_id_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.of_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_zero_equiv", "description": "A zero morphism `0 : X \u27f6 Y` is an isomorphism if and only if\nthe identities on both `X` and `Y` are zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_\u03b9_comp_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.zero_of_epi_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_morphisms.ext", "description": "If you're tempted to use this lemma \"in the wild\", you should probably\ncarefully consider whether you've made a mistake in allowing two\ninstances of `has_zero_morphisms` to exist at all.\n\nSee, particularly, the note on `zero_morphisms_of_zero_object` below.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_morphisms.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.zero_of_target_iso_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_zero'", "description": "The image of a morphism which is equal to zero is the zero object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.iso_zero_of_mono_zero", "description": "If `0 : X \u27f6 Y` is an monomorphism, then `X \u2245 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.iso_zero_of_mono_zero_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_zero", "description": "The image of a zero morphism is the zero object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_morphisms_opposite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.iso_of_is_isomorphic_zero", "description": " If an object `X` is isomorphic to 0, there's no need to use choice to construct\nan explicit isomorphism: the zero morphism suffices.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation_zero", "description": "The zero morphism has a `mono_factorisation` through the zero object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_split_mono_coprod_inl", "description": "In the presence of zero morphisms, coprojections into a coproduct are (split) monomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_morphisms", "description": " A category \"has zero morphisms\" if there is a designated \"zero morphism\" in each morphism space,\nand compositions of zero morphisms with anything give the zero morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_morphisms.has_zero", "description": " A category \"has zero morphisms\" if there is a designated \"zero morphism\" in each morphism space,\nand compositions of zero morphisms with anything give the zero morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_morphisms.comp_zero'", "description": " A category \"has zero morphisms\" if there is a designated \"zero morphism\" in each morphism space,\nand compositions of zero morphisms with anything give the zero morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_morphisms.zero_comp'", "description": " A category \"has zero morphisms\" if there is a designated \"zero morphism\" in each morphism space,\nand compositions of zero morphisms with anything give the zero morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.zero_iso_is_initial_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_split_epi_prod_fst", "description": "In the presence of zero morphisms, projections into a product are (split) epimorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.zero_morphisms_of_zero_object", "description": "A category with a zero object has zero morphisms.\n\n   It is rarely a good idea to use this. Many categories that have a zero object have zero\n   morphisms for some other reason, for example from additivity. Library code that uses\n   `zero_morphisms_of_zero_object` will then be incompatible with these categories because\n   the `has_zero_morphisms` instances will not be definitionally equal. For this reason library\n   code should generally ask for an instance of `has_zero_morphisms` separately, even if it already\n   asks for an instance of `has_zero_objects`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object_of_has_terminal_object", "description": "If there are zero morphisms, any terminal object is a zero object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.iso_zero_of_epi_zero_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.of_mono_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_zero_equiv_iso_zero", "description": "A zero morphism `0 : X \u27f6 Y` is an isomorphism if and only if\n`X` and `Y` are isomorphic to the zero object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.comp_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.epi_of_target_iso_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_of_source_iso_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.\u03b9_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.zero_iso_is_initial_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.eq_zero_of_tgt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_zero_self_equiv_iso_zero", "description": "A zero morphism `0 : X \u27f6 X` is an isomorphism if and only if\n`X` is isomorphic to the zero object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_split_mono_coprod_inr", "description": "In the presence of zero morphisms, coprojections into a coproduct are (split) monomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_factorisation_zero", "description": "The factorisation through the zero object is an image factorisation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_factorisation_zero_e", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.iso_zero_of_mono_zero_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_split_epi_pi_\u03c0", "description": "In the presence of zero morphisms, projections into a product are (split) epimorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_split_mono_sigma_\u03b9", "description": "In the presence of zero morphisms, coprojections into a coproduct are (split) monomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image.\u03b9_zero'", "description": "If we know `f = 0`,\nit requires a little work to conclude `image.\u03b9 f = 0`,\nbecause `f = g` only implies `image f \u2245 image g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.zero_iso_is_terminal_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.zero_iso_initial_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.zero_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.iso_zero_of_epi_eq_zero", "description": "If an epimorphism in to `Y` is zero, then `Y \u2245 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.iso_zero_of_epi_zero_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.zero_of_from_zero", "description": "An arrow starting at the zero object is zero", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.has_zero_morphisms", "description": "A category with a zero object has zero morphisms.\n\n   It is rarely a good idea to use this. Many categories that have a zero object have zero\n   morphisms for some other reason, for example from additivity. Library code that uses\n   `zero_morphisms_of_zero_object` will then be incompatible with these categories because\n   the `has_zero_morphisms` instances will not be definitionally equal. For this reason library\n   code should generally ask for an instance of `has_zero_morphisms` separately, even if it already\n   asks for an instance of `has_zero_objects`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.of_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.zero_of_to_zero", "description": "An arrow ending in the zero object is zero", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.of_epi_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.category_theory.functor.has_zero_object", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_zero.eq_zero_of_src", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.eq_zero_of_image_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_object.zero_iso_is_terminal_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.zero_of_target_iso_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_image_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.iso_zero_of_epi_zero", "description": "If `0 : X \u27f6 Y` is an epimorphism, then `Y \u2245 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_zero_morphisms_pempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_zero_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.category_theory.functor.has_zero_morphisms", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normalized_factors_equiv_span_normalized_factors_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain_inv.dimension_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.le_of_pow_le_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.le_self_mul_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.exists_not_mem_one_of_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal_factors_equiv_of_quot_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.is_principal_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.le_mul_of_no_prime_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.span_singleton_inv_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "irreducible_pow_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normalized_factors_equiv_of_quot_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.sup_mul_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.dimension_le_one.prime_le_prime_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.height_one_spectrum.infi_localization_eq_bot", "description": " A Dedekind domain is equal to the intersection of its localizations at all its height one\nnon-zero prime ideals viewed as subalgebras of its field of fractions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal_factors_equiv_of_quot_equiv_is_dvd_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.invertible_of_principal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.normalized_gcd_monoid", "description": " Ideals in a Dedekind domain have gcd and lcm operators that (trivially) are compatible with\nthe normalization operator.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.pow_lt_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.mul_left_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.exist_integer_multiples_not_mem", "description": " Strengthening of `is_localization.exist_integer_multiples`:\nLet `J \u2260 \u22a4` be an ideal in a Dedekind domain `A`, and `f \u2260 0` a finite collection\nof elements of `K = Frac(A)`, then we can multiply the elements of `f` by some `a : K`\nto find a collection of elements of `A` that is not completely contained in `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.prime_iff_is_prime", "description": " In a Dedekind domain, the (nonzero) prime elements of the monoid with zero `ideal A`\nare exactly the prime ideals.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.coe_ideal_le_self_mul_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_prime_iff_bot_or_prime", "description": " In a Dedekind domain, the the prime ideals are the zero ideal together with the prime elements\nof the monoid with zero `ideal A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal_factors_fun_of_quot_hom", "description": "The map from ideals of `R` dividing `I` to the ideals of `A` dividing `J` induced by\n a homomorphism `f : R/I \u2192+* A/J`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.span_singleton_div_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.exists_mem_pow_not_mem_pow_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.inv_nonzero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.span_singleton_div_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal_factors_fun_of_quot_hom_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain_inv.inv_mul_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.span_singleton_mul_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.height_one_spectrum.equiv_maximal_spectrum", "description": "An equivalence between the height one and maximal spectra for rings of Krull dimension 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.has_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.height_one_spectrum.prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.dvd_not_unit_iff_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.unique_factorization_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.mem_inv_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.lcm_eq_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal_factors_equiv_of_quot_equiv_mem_normalized_factors_of_mem_normalized_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.inv_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicity_normalized_factors_equiv_span_normalized_factors_symm_eq_multiplicity", "description": "The bijection `normalized_factors_equiv_span_normalized_factors.symm` between the set of prime\n   factors of the ideal `\u27e8r\u27e9` and the set of prime factors of `r` preserves multiplicities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_prime_of_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "span_singleton_dvd_span_singleton_iff_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.coe_ideal_span_singleton_div_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.wf_dvd_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.quotient_equiv_pi_of_finset_prod_eq", "description": " **Chinese remainder theorem** for a Dedekind domain: if the ideal `I` factors as\n`\u220f i in s, P i ^ e i`, then `R \u29f8 I` factors as `\u03a0 (i : s), R \u29f8 (P i ^ e i)`.\n\nThis is a version of `is_dedekind_domain.quotient_equiv_pi_of_prod_eq` where we restrict\nthe product to a finite subset `s` of a potentially infinite indexing type `\u03b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.dvd_iff_le", "description": "For ideals in a Dedekind domain, to divide is to contain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normalized_factors_equiv_of_quot_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normalized_factors_equiv_of_quot_equiv_multiplicity_eq_multiplicity", "description": "The map `normalized_factors_equiv_of_quot_equiv` preserves multiplicities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.one_mem_inv_coe_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.pow_succ_lt_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.inf_eq_mul_of_coprime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normalized_factors_equiv_span_normalized_factors", "description": "The bijection between the (normalized) prime factors of `r` and the (normalized) prime factors\n   of `span {r}`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal_factors_equiv_of_quot_equiv", "description": "The bijection between ideals of `R` dividing `I` and the ideals of `A` dividing `J` induced by\n an isomorphism `f : R/I \u2245 A/J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_prime.mul_mem_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.inf_prime_pow_eq_prod", "description": " The intersection of distinct prime powers in a Dedekind domain is the product of these\nprime powers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain_inv.mul_inv_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.coe_ideal_mul_inv", "description": " Nonzero integral ideals in a Dedekind domain are invertible.\n\nWe will use this to show that nonzero fractional ideals are invertible,\nand finally conclude that fractional ideals in a Dedekind domain form a group with zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.mul_inv_cancel_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.inv_one_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.coe_ideal_span_singleton_inv_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_multiset_prod_cons_le_and_prod_not_le", "description": " Specialization of `exists_prime_spectrum_prod_le_and_ne_bot_of_domain` to Dedekind domains:\nLet `I : ideal A` be a nonzero ideal, where `A` is a Dedekind domain that is not a field.\nThen `exists_prime_spectrum_prod_le_and_ne_bot_of_domain` states we can find a product of prime\nideals that is contained within `I`. This lemma extends that result by making the product minimal:\nlet `M` be a maximal ideal that contains `I`, then the product including `M` is contained within `I`\nand the product excluding `M` is not contained within `I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normalized_factors_equiv_of_quot_equiv", "description": "The bijection between the sets of normalized factors of I and J induced by a ring\n   isomorphism `f : R/I \u2245 A/J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.coprime_of_no_prime_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "count_le_of_ideal_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.semifield", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.quotient_equiv_pi_factors_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "irreducible_pow_sup_of_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal_factors_fun_of_quot_hom_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal_factors_equiv_of_quot_equiv_symm_apply_coe_carrier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal_factors_equiv_of_quot_equiv_apply_coe_carrier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.height_one_spectrum.associates_irreducible", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.mul_inv_cancel", "description": " Nonzero fractional ideals in a Dedekind domain are units.\n\nThis is also available as `_root_.mul_inv_cancel`, using the\n`comm_group_with_zero` instance defined below.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.mul_generator_self_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.exists_representative_mod_finset", "description": " Corollary of the Chinese remainder theorem: given elements `x i : R / P i ^ e i`,\nwe can choose a representative `y : R` such that `y \u2261 x i (mod P i ^ e i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.pow_le_prime_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain_inv", "description": "A Dedekind domain is an integral domain such that every fractional ideal has an inverse.\n\nThis is equivalent to `is_dedekind_domain`.\nIn particular we provide a `fractional_ideal.comm_group_with_zero` instance,\nassuming `is_dedekind_domain A`, which implies `is_dedekind_domain_inv`. For **integral** ideals,\n`is_dedekind_domain`(`_inv`) implies only `ideal.cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.map_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient_mul_equiv_quotient_prod", "description": "**Chinese remainder theorem**, specialized to two ideals.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain_inv.is_noetherian_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.prod_le_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.mul_left_strict_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.div_eq_mul_inv", "description": "This is also available as `_root_.div_eq_mul_inv`, using the\n`comm_group_with_zero` instance defined below.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain_inv.integrally_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.normalization_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "singleton_span_mem_normalized_factors_of_mem_normalized_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sup_eq_prod_inf_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero", "description": " Fractional ideals have cancellative multiplication in a Dedekind domain.\n\nAlthough this instance is a direct consequence of the instance\n`fractional_ideal.comm_group_with_zero`, we define this instance to provide\na computable alternative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.span_singleton_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.invertible_iff_generator_nonzero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.mul_right_strict_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.exists_forall_sub_mem_ideal", "description": " Corollary of the Chinese remainder theorem: given elements `x i : R`,\nwe can choose a representative `y : R` such that `y - x i \u2208 P i ^ e i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicity_eq_multiplicity_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain_inv_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.gcd_eq_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicity_normalized_factors_equiv_span_normalized_factors_eq_multiplicity", "description": "The bijection `normalized_factors_equiv_span_normalized_factors` between the set of prime\n   factors of `r` and the set of prime factors of the ideal `\u27e8r\u27e9` preserves multiplicities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.adjoin_integral_eq_one_of_is_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.dvd_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.height_one_spectrum.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.eq_prime_pow_of_succ_lt_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.coe_inv_of_nonzero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "irreducible_pow_sup_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.height_one_spectrum", "description": " The height one prime spectrum of a Dedekind domain `R` is the type of nonzero prime ideals of\n`R`. Note that this equals the maximal spectrum if `R` has Krull dimension 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.height_one_spectrum.as_ideal", "description": " The height one prime spectrum of a Dedekind domain `R` is the type of nonzero prime ideals of\n`R`. Note that this equals the maximal spectrum if `R` has Krull dimension 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.height_one_spectrum.is_prime", "description": " The height one prime spectrum of a Dedekind domain `R` is the type of nonzero prime ideals of\n`R`. Note that this equals the maximal spectrum if `R` has Krull dimension 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.height_one_spectrum.ne_bot", "description": " The height one prime spectrum of a Dedekind domain `R` is the type of nonzero prime ideals of\n`R`. Note that this equals the maximal spectrum if `R` has Krull dimension 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.mul_inv_cancel_of_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.prime_of_is_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain_inv.is_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.coe_ideal_span_singleton_mul_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.strict_anti_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal_factors_fun_of_quot_hom_coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normalized_factors_equiv_span_normalized_factors_apply_coe_carrier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.right_inverse_eq", "description": "`I\u207b\u00b9` is the inverse of `I` if `I` has an inverse.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain_inv.is_dedekind_domain", "description": " Showing one side of the equivalence between the definitions\n`is_dedekind_domain_inv` and `is_dedekind_domain` of Dedekind domains.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.inv_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.height_one_spectrum.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.inv_anti_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.quotient_equiv_pi_factors", "description": " **Chinese remainder theorem** for a Dedekind domain: `R \u29f8 I` factors as `\u03a0 i, R \u29f8 (P i ^ e i)`,\nwhere `P i` ranges over the prime factors of `I` and `e i` over the multiplicities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain_iff_is_dedekind_domain_inv", "description": " `is_dedekind_domain` and `is_dedekind_domain_inv` are equivalent ways\nto express that an integral domain is a Dedekind domain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod_normalized_factors_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.count_normalized_factors_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.mul_inv_cancel_iff_is_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.mul_right_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.le_singleton_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.height_one_spectrum.is_maximal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.quotient_equiv_pi_of_prod_eq", "description": " **Chinese remainder theorem** for a Dedekind domain: if the ideal `I` factors as\n`\u220f i, P i ^ e i`, then `R \u29f8 I` factors as `\u03a0 i, R \u29f8 (P i ^ e i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.height_one_spectrum.irreducible", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_bounded_smul.of_norm_smul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nndist_smul\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_smul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnnorm_smul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_smul\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nndist_smul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_smul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnnorm_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_semi_normed_ring.to_has_bounded_op_smul", "description": "Right multiplication is bounded.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_semi_normed_ring.to_has_bounded_smul", "description": "Left multiplication is bounded.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_smul\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_smul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.span_single_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lapply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lmap_domain_disjoint_ker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_eq_fintype_total", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_equiv_map_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lmap_domain_total", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.supported_Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_total", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lhom_ext", "description": "Two `R`-linear maps from `finsupp X M` which agree on each `single x y` agree everywhere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.linear_equiv", "description": "`finsupp.map_range` as a `linear_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.apply_total", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sigma_finsupp_lequiv_pi_finsupp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.supr_lsingle_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.restrict_dom_comp_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.restrict_dom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.dom_lcongr_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_finsupp_lequiv_prod_finsupp", "description": " The linear equivalence between `(\u03b1 \u2295 \u03b2) \u2192\u2080 M` and `(\u03b1 \u2192\u2080 M) \u00d7 (\u03b2 \u2192\u2080 M)`.\n\nThis is the `linear_equiv` version of `finsupp.sum_finsupp_equiv_prod_finsupp`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.llift_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sigma_finsupp_lequiv_pi_finsupp_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.subsingleton_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.mem_span_range_iff_exists_finsupp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.linear_equiv_to_add_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.congr", "description": "An equivalence of sets induces a linear equivalence of `finsupp`s supported on those sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lcoe_fun_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.total_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.supported_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_finsupp_lequiv_prod_finsupp_symm_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lsum", "description": " Lift a family of linear maps `M \u2192\u2097[R] N` indexed by `x : \u03b1` to a linear map from `\u03b1 \u2192\u2080 M` to\n`N` using `finsupp.sum`. This is an upgraded version of `finsupp.lift_add_hom`.\n\nSee note [bundled maps over different rings] for why separate `R` and `S` semirings are used.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.total_apply_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lmap_domain_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total", "description": "Interprets (l : \u03b1 \u2192\u2080 R) as linear combination of the elements in the family (v : \u03b1 \u2192 M) and\n   evaluates this linear combination.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.supported_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_map_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.linear_equiv_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_finsupp_total", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lcongr_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_comp_lmap_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.linear_map", "description": "`finsupp.map_range` as a `linear_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_on", "description": " `finsupp.total_on M v s` interprets `p : \u03b1 \u2192\u2080 R` as a linear combination of a\nsubset of the vectors in `v`, mapping it to the span of those vectors.\n\nThe subset is indicated by a set `s : set \u03b1` of indices.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.linear_map_to_add_monoid_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.single_mem_supported", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_apply_of_mem_supported", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.finsupp_prod_lequiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lhom_ext'", "description": " Two `R`-linear maps from `finsupp X M` which agree on each `single x y` agree everywhere.\n\nWe formulate this fact using equality of linear maps `\u03c6.comp (lsingle a)` and `\u03c8.comp (lsingle a)`\nso that the `ext` tactic can apply a type-specific extensionality lemma to prove equality of these\nmaps. E.g., if `M = R`, then it suffices to verify `\u03c6 (single a 1) = \u03c8 (single a 1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_comap_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.supported_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.linear_equiv_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.mem_supported", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.subsingleton_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.exists_finset_of_mem_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.supported_equiv_finsupp", "description": " Interpret `finsupp.restrict_support_equiv` as a linear equivalence between\n`supported M R s` and `s \u2192\u2080 M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.range_total", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.ker_lsingle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.supported_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.splitting_of_fun_on_fintype_surjective_splits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.left_inverse_splitting_of_fun_on_fintype_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lcoe_fun", "description": " Forget that a function is finitely supported.\n\nThis is the linear version of `finsupp.to_fun`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.supported_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_option", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.mem_span_image_iff_total", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.splitting_of_finsupp_surjective_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "span.finsupp_total_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.mem_supported'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lapply", "description": "Interpret `\u03bb (f : \u03b1 \u2192\u2080 M), f a` as a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.disjoint_lsingle_lsingle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.linear_map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lmap_domain_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_eq_fintype_total_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.dom_lcongr_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lsum_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.span_image_eq_map_total", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_on_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.dom_lcongr", "description": " An equivalence of domains induces a linear equivalence of finitely supported functions.\n\nThis is `finsupp.dom_congr` as a `linear_equiv`.\nSee also `linear_map.fun_congr_left` for the case of arbitrary functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.snd_sum_finsupp_lequiv_prod_finsupp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.supported_eq_span_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.coe_lsum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "span.repr", "description": "Pick some representation of `x : span R w` as a linear combination in `w`,\nusing the axiom of choice.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.splitting_of_fun_on_fintype_surjective_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.finsupp_prod_lequiv", "description": " The linear equivalence between `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2 \u2192\u2080 M` and `\u03b1 \u2192\u2080 \u03b2 \u2192\u2080 M`.\n\nThis is the `linear_equiv` version of `finsupp.finsupp_prod_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.linear_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.dom_lcongr_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lcongr", "description": " An equivalence of domain and a linear equivalence of codomain induce a linear equivalence of the\ncorresponding finitely supported functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.linear_map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.range_total", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lsum_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_emb_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.subsingleton_equiv", "description": "If `subsingleton R`, then `M \u2243\u2097[R] \u03b9 \u2192\u2080 R` for any type `\u03b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.splitting_of_finsupp_surjective_splits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_fin_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_on_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lift", "description": "A slight rearrangement from `lsum` gives us\nthe bijection underlying the free-forgetful adjunction for R-modules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.total", "description": " `fintype.total R S v f` is the linear combination of vectors in `v` with weights in `f`.\nThis variant of `finsupp.total` is defined on fintype indexed vectors.\n\nThis map is linear in `v` if `R` is commutative, and always linear in `f`.\nSee note [bundled maps over different rings] for why separate `R` and `S` semirings are used.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.splitting_of_finsupp_surjective", "description": "A surjective linear map to finitely supported functions has a splitting.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.mem_supported_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.linear_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_id_surjective", "description": " Any module is a quotient of a free module. This is stated as surjectivity of\n`finsupp.total M M R id : (M \u2192\u2080 R) \u2192\u2097[R] M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.finsupp_sum_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.left_inverse_splitting_of_finsupp_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_span_set", "description": " An element `m \u2208 M` is contained in the `R`-submodule spanned by a set `s \u2286 M`, if and only if\n`m` can be written as a finite `R`-linear combination of elements of `s`.\nThe implementation uses `finsupp.sum`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.splitting_of_fun_on_fintype_surjective", "description": "A surjective linear map to functions on a finite type has a splitting.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lcomap_domain", "description": " Given `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` and a proof `hf` that `f` is injective, `lcomap_domain f hf` is the linear map\nsending  `l : \u03b2 \u2192\u2080 M` to the finitely supported function from `\u03b1` to `M` given by composing\n`l` with `f`.\n\nThis is the linear version of `finsupp.comap_domain`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.disjoint_supported_supported", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lsum_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lsingle_range_le_ker_lapply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.dom_lcongr_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lsubtype_domain", "description": "Interpret `finsupp.subtype_domain s` as a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lsingle", "description": "Interpret `finsupp.single a` as a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.infi_ker_lapply_le_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.disjoint_supported_supported_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.range_restrict_dom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lmap_domain", "description": "Interpret `finsupp.map_domain` as a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.dom_lcongr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lcongr_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lsubtype_domain_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_finsupp_lequiv_prod_finsupp_symm_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_supr_iff_exists_finset", "description": "`submodule.exists_finset_of_mem_supr` as an `iff`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.linear_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_finsupp_lequiv_prod_finsupp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "top_le_span_range_iff_forall_exists_fun", "description": "A family `v : \u03b1 \u2192 V` is generating `V` iff every element `(x : V)`\ncan be written as sum `\u2211 c\u1d62 \u2022 v\u1d62 = x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_span_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lmap_domain_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.restrict_dom", "description": "Interpret `finsupp.filter s` as a linear map from `\u03b1 \u2192\u2080 M` to `supported M R s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun", "description": "An element `x` lies in the span of `v` iff it can be written as sum `\u2211 c\u1d62 \u2022 v\u1d62 = x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.supported_comap_lmap_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lsingle_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.supported_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.linear_equiv_to_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.llift_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lcongr_symm_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.finsupp_prod_lequiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.span_eq_range_total", "description": "A version of `finsupp.range_total` which is useful for going in the other direction", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lift_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.mem_span_iff_total", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.fst_sum_finsupp_lequiv_prod_finsupp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lmap_domain_supported", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.supported", "description": "`finsupp.supported M R s` is the `R`-submodule of all `p : \u03b1 \u2192\u2080 M` such that `p.support \u2286 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lift_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_finsupp_lequiv_prod_finsupp_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.total_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.lcongr_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.llift", "description": " Given compatible `S` and `R`-module structures on `M` and a type `X`, the set of functions\n`X \u2192 M` is `S`-linearly equivalent to the `R`-linear maps from the free `R`-module\non `X` to `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sigma_finsupp_lequiv_pi_finsupp", "description": " On a `fintype \u03b7`, `finsupp.split` is a linear equivalence between\n`(\u03a3 (j : \u03b7), \u03b9s j) \u2192\u2080 M` and `\u03a0 j, (\u03b9s j \u2192\u2080 M)`.\n\nThis is the `linear_equiv` version of `finsupp.sigma_finsupp_add_equiv_pi_finsupp`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.ultraproduct.fun_map_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.ultraproduct.term_realize_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.ultraproduct.realize_formula_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.ultraproduct.sentence_realize", "description": "\u0141o\u015b's Theorem : A sentence is true in an ultraproduct if and only if the set of structures it is\n true in is in the ultrafilter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.ultraproduct.Structure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.ultraproduct.setoid_prestructure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.ultraproduct.product.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.ultraproduct.bounded_formula_realize_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin2.remap_left", "description": "`remap_left f k : fin2 (m + k) \u2192 fin2 (n + k)` applies the function\n `f : fin2 m \u2192 fin2 n` to inputs less than `m`, and leaves the right part\n on the right (that is, `remap_left f k (m + i) = n + i`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin2.is_lt.zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin2.insert_perm", "description": "`insert_perm a` is a permutation of `fin2 n` with the following properties:\n * `insert_perm a i = i+1` if `i < a`\n * `insert_perm a a = 0`\n * `insert_perm a i = i` if `i > a`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin2.cases'", "description": " Define a dependent function on `fin2 (succ n)` by giving its value at\nzero (`H1`) and by giving a dependent function on the rest (`H2`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin2.add", "description": "`i + k : fin2 (n + k)` when `i : fin2 n` and `k : \u2115`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin2.is_lt", "description": "This is a simple type class inference prover for proof obligations\n of the form `m < n` where `m n : \u2115`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin2.is_lt.h", "description": "This is a simple type class inference prover for proof obligations\n of the form `m < n` where `m n : \u2115`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin2.left", "description": "`left k` is the embedding `fin2 n \u2192 fin2 (k + n)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin2.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin2.opt_of_nat", "description": "Converts a natural into a `fin2` if it is in range", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin2.is_lt.succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin2.of_nat'", "description": " Use type class inference to infer the boundedness proof, so that we can directly convert a\n`nat` into a `fin2 n`. This supports notation like `&1 : fin 3`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin2.to_nat", "description": "Converts a `fin2` into a natural.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin2.elim0", "description": "Ex falso. The dependent eliminator for the empty `fin2 0` type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin2", "description": "An alternate definition of `fin n` defined as an inductive type instead of a subtype of `\u2115`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin2.fz", "description": "An alternate definition of `fin n` defined as an inductive type instead of a subtype of `\u2115`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin2.fs", "description": "An alternate definition of `fin n` defined as an inductive type instead of a subtype of `\u2115`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.map_le_map_iff_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.embedding.subtype_comp_cod_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.lift_card_closure_le_card_term", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.coe_closure_eq_range_term_realize", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.comap_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.comap_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.closure_induction'", "description": "A dependent version of `substructure.closure_induction`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.coe_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.coe_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.mem_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.embedding.dom_restrict_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.subtype", "description": "The natural embedding of an `L.substructure` of `M` into `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.gci_map_comap", "description": "`map f` and `comap f` form a `galois_coinsertion` when `f` is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"nam