= g x`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.mem_map_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.embedding.cod_restrict_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.comap_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.closure_mono", "description": " Substructure closure of a set is monotone in its argument: if `s \u2286 t`,\nthen `closure L s \u2264 closure L t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.closure", "description": "The `L.substructure` generated by a set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.comap_infi_map_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.map_inf_comap_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.map_comap_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.hom.range_le_iff_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.hom.cod_restrict_to_fun_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.hom.subtype_comp_cod_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.embedding.comp_cod_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.closed_under.Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.hom.dom_restrict_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.comap_map_eq_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.mem_carrier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.mem_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.hom.mem_range_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.comap", "description": "The preimage of a substructure along a homomorphism is a substructure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.apply_coe_mem_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.map_le_of_le_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.le_comap_of_map_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.map_strict_mono_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.hom.map_le_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.map_le_iff_le_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.hom.range_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.closed_under", "description": "Indicates that a set in a given structure is a closed under a function symbol.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.coe_with_constants", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.hom.cod_restrict", "description": " A first-order hom `f : M \u2192 N` whose values lie in a substructure `p \u2286 N` can be restricted to a\nhom `M \u2192 p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.map_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.countable.substructure_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.map_comap_eq_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.hom.range_eq_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.embedding.equiv_range", "description": "The equivalence between the domain and the range of an embedding `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.has_top", "description": "The substructure `M` of the structure `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.mem_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.hom.dom_restrict", "description": "The restriction of a first-order hom to a substructure `s \u2286 M` gives a hom `s \u2192 N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.coe_inclusion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.mem_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.map_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.hom.range", "description": " The range of a first-order hom `f : M \u2192 N` is a submodule of `N`.\nSee Note [range copy pattern].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.embedding.substructure_equiv_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.range_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.mem_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.closed_under.inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.hom.eq_of_eq_on_dense", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.coe_substructure_reduct", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.realize_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.constants_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.gc_map_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.closure_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.ext", "description": "Two substructures are equal if they have the same elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.substructure_reduct", "description": "Reduces the language of a substructure along a language hom.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.coe_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.copy", "description": "Copy a substructure replacing `carrier` with a set that is equal to it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.map_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.closure_eq_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.closure_le", "description": "A substructure `S` includes `closure L s` if and only if it includes `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.map_injective_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.hom.range_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.closure_induction", "description": " An induction principle for closure membership. If `p` holds for all elements of `s`, and\nis preserved under function symbols, then `p` holds for all elements of the closure of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.comap_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.hom.mem_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.mem_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.subset_closure_with_constants", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.closed_under_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.hom.comp_cod_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.closure_eq", "description": "Closure of a substructure `S` equals `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.mem_substructure_reduct", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.dense_induction", "description": " If `s` is a dense set in a structure `M`, `substructure.closure L s = \u22a4`, then in order to prove\nthat some predicate `p` holds for all `x : M` it suffices to verify `p x` for `x \u2208 s`, and verify\nthat `p` is preserved under function symbols.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.small_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.coe_copy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.mem_closure_iff_exists_term", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.mem_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.has_inf", "description": "The inf of two substructures is their intersection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.map_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.inclusion", "description": "The embedding associated to an inclusion of substructures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.mem_with_constants", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.equiv.to_hom_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.coe_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.comap_surjective_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.closure_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.simps.coe", "description": "See Note [custom simps projection]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.copy_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.complete_lattice", "description": "Substructures of a structure form a complete lattice.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.gi", "description": "`closure` forms a Galois insertion with the coercion to set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.closure_with_constants_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.comap_le_comap_iff_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.hom.eq_on_closure", "description": "If two `L.hom`s are equal on a set, then they are equal on its substructure closure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.hom.range_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.map", "description": "The image of a substructure along a homomorphism is a substructure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.closure_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.small_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.map_supr_comap_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.map_sup_comap_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.coe_top_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.embedding.substructure_equiv_map", "description": "The equivalence between a substructure `s` and its image `s.map f.to_hom`, where `f` is an\n embedding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.set_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.comap_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.not_mem_of_not_mem_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.closed_under.inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.comap_inf_map_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure", "description": "A substructure of a structure `M` is a set closed under application of function symbols.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.carrier", "description": "A substructure of a structure `M` is a set closed under application of function symbols.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.fun_mem", "description": "A substructure of a structure `M` is a set closed under application of function symbols.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.embedding.equiv_range_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.comap_map_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.comap_strict_mono_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.embedding.dom_restrict", "description": "The restriction of a first-order embedding to a substructure `s \u2286 M` gives an embedding `s \u2192 N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.embedding.cod_restrict", "description": " A first-order embedding `f : M \u2192 N` whose values lie in a substructure `p \u2286 N` can be restricted\nto an embedding `M \u2192 p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.monotone_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.closure_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.map_infi_comap_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.subset_closure", "description": "The substructure generated by a set includes the set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.comap_sup_map_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.monotone_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.coe_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.with_constants", "description": "Turns any substructure containing a constant set `A` into a `L[[A]]`-substructure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.induced_Structure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cross_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cross_product", "description": "The cross product of two vectors in $R^3$ for $R$ a commutative ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cross_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cross.lie_ring", "description": "The three-dimensional vectors together with the operations + and \u00d7\u2083 form a Lie ring.\n   Note we do not make this an instance as a conflicting one already exists\n   via `lie_ring.of_associative_ring`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "triple_product_permutation", "description": "Cyclic permutations preserve the triple product. See also `triple_product_eq_det`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dot_self_cross", "description": "The cross product of two vectors is perpendicular to the first vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cross_dot_cross", "description": "The scalar quadruple product identity, related to the Binet-Cauchy identity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "jacobi_cross", "description": "Jacobi identity: For a cross product of three vectors,\n   their sum over the three even permutations is equal to the zero vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "triple_product_eq_det", "description": "The triple product of `u`, `v`, and `w` is equal to the determinant of the matrix\n   with those vectors as its rows.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dot_cross_self", "description": "The cross product of two vectors is perpendicular to the second vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cross_cross", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cross_anticomm'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "leibniz_cross", "description": "The cross product satisfies the Leibniz lie property.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cross_anticomm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "neg_cross", "description": "**Alias** of `cross_anticomm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_succ_eq_succ_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_le_fib_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_bit1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.prove_fib_aux", "description": "`prove_fib_aux ic n` returns `(ic', a, b, \u22a2 is_fib_aux n a b)`, where `n` is a numeral.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.gcd_fib_add_mul_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.is_fib_aux", "description": "Auxiliary definition for `prove_fib` plugin.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.eval_fib", "description": " A `norm_num` plugin for `fib n` when `n` is a numeral.\nUses the binary representation of `n` like `nat.fast_fib`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.is_fib_aux_bit1_done", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fast_fib_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib", "description": "Implementation of the fibonacci sequence satisfying\n`fib 0 = 0, fib 1 = 1, fib (n + 2) = fib n + fib (n + 1)`.\n\n*Note:* We use a stream iterator for better performance when compared to the naive recursive\nimplementation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fast_fib", "description": " Computes `nat.fib n` using the binary representation of `n`.\nProved to be equal to `nat.fib` in `nat.fast_fib_eq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_two_mul_add_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.is_fib_aux_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_succ_eq_sum_choose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fast_fib_aux_bit_tt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.prove_fib", "description": " A `norm_num` plugin for `fib n` when `n` is a numeral.\nUses the binary representation of `n` like `nat.fast_fib`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_coprime_fib_succ", "description": "Subsequent Fibonacci numbers are coprime,\n see https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Consecutive_Fibonacci_Numbers_are_Coprime", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.le_fib_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_add_two", "description": "Shows that `fib` indeed satisfies the Fibonacci recurrence `F\u2099\u208a\u2082 = F\u2099 + F\u2099\u208a\u2081.`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_add", "description": "See https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Fibonacci_Number_in_terms_of_Smaller_Fibonacci_Numbers", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_bit0_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_two_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.gcd_fib_add_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_add_two_sub_fib_add_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_lt_fib_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_bit0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fast_fib_aux", "description": " Computes `(nat.fib n, nat.fib (n + 1))` using the binary representation of `n`.\nSupports `nat.fast_fib`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.is_fib_aux_bit1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fast_fib_aux_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.is_fib_aux_bit0_done", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_bit1_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fast_fib_aux_bit_ff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_gcd", "description": "`fib n` is a strong divisibility sequence,\n see https://proofwiki.org/wiki/GCD_of_Fibonacci_Numbers", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.fib_add_two_strict_mono", "description": "`fib (n + 2)` is strictly monotone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.is_fib_aux_bit0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.ac_refine", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.find_rule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mk_fun_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.tactic.mono", "description": "- `mono` applies a monotonicity rule.\n- `mono*` applies monotonicity rules repetitively.\n- `mono with x \u2264 y` or `mono with [0 \u2264 x,0 \u2264 y]` creates an assertion for the listed\n  propositions. Those help to select the right monotonicity rule.\n- `mono left` or `mono right` is useful when proving strict orderings:\n   for `x + y < w + z` could be broken down into either\n    - left:  `x \u2264 w` and `y < z` or\n    - right: `x < w` and `y \u2264 z`\n- `mono using [rule1,rule2]` calls `simp [rule1,rule2]` before applying mono.\n- The general syntax is\n  `mono '*'? ('with' hyp | 'with' [hyp1,hyp2])? ('using' [hyp1,hyp2])? mono_cfg?`\n\nTo use it, first import `tactic.monotonicity`.\n\nHere is an example of mono:\n\n```lean\nexample (x y z k : \u2124)\n  (h : 3 \u2264 (4 : \u2124))\n  (h' : z \u2264 y) :\n  (k + 3 + x) - y \u2264 (k + 4 + x) - z :=\nbegin\n  mono, -- unfold `(-)`, apply add_le_add\n  { -- \u22a2 k + 3 + x \u2264 k + 4 + x\n    mono, -- apply add_le_add, refl\n    -- \u22a2 k + 3 \u2264 k + 4\n    mono },\n  { -- \u22a2 -y \u2264 -z\n    mono /- apply neg_le_neg -/ }\nend\n```\n\nMore succinctly, we can prove the same goal as:\n\n```lean\nexample (x y z k : \u2124)\n  (h : 3 \u2264 (4 : \u2124))\n  (h' : z \u2264 y) :\n  (k + 3 + x) - y \u2264 (k + 4 + x) - z :=\nby mono*\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_function.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.fold_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.find_lemma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.hide_meta_vars'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.side_conditions", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.assert_or_rule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.pi_head", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.parse_ac_mono_function'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.delete_expr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.ac_mono_ctx'.traversable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.unify_with_instance", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.match_assoc", "description": "`(prefix,left,right,suffix) \u2190 match_assoc unif l r` finds the\nlongest prefix and suffix common to `l` and `r` and\nreturns them along with the differences", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.check_ac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.match_prefix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.as_goal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.has_to_tactic_format_mono_law", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mk_pattern", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.ac_mono_ctx'.traverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono", "description": "- `mono` applies a monotonicity rule.\n- `mono*` applies monotonicity rules repetitively.\n- `mono with x \u2264 y` or `mono with [0 \u2264 x,0 \u2264 y]` creates an assertion for the listed\n  propositions. Those help to select the right monotonicity rule.\n- `mono left` or `mono right` is useful when proving strict orderings:\n   for `x + y < w + z` could be broken down into either\n    - left:  `x \u2264 w` and `y < z` or\n    - right: `x < w` and `y \u2264 z`\n- `mono using [rule1,rule2]` calls `simp [rule1,rule2]` before applying mono.\n- The general syntax is\n  `mono '*'? ('with' hyp | 'with' [hyp1,hyp2])? ('using' [hyp1,hyp2])? mono_cfg?`\n\nTo use it, first import `tactic.monotonicity`.\n\nHere is an example of mono:\n\n```lean\nexample (x y z k : \u2124)\n  (h : 3 \u2264 (4 : \u2124))\n  (h' : z \u2264 y) :\n  (k + 3 + x) - y \u2264 (k + 4 + x) - z :=\nbegin\n  mono, -- unfold `(-)`, apply add_le_add\n  { -- \u22a2 k + 3 + x \u2264 k + 4 + x\n    mono, -- apply add_le_add, refl\n    -- \u22a2 k + 3 \u2264 k + 4\n    mono },\n  { -- \u22a2 -y \u2264 -z\n    mono /- apply neg_le_neg -/ }\nend\n```\n\nMore succinctly, we can prove the same goal as:\n\n```lean\nexample (x y z k : \u2124)\n  (h : 3 \u2264 (4 : \u2124))\n  (h' : z \u2264 y) :\n  (k + 3 + x) - y \u2264 (k + 4 + x) - z :=\nby mono*\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.parse_assoc_chain'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.parse_assoc_chain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mk_congr_args", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.parse_ac_mono_function", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.match_ac'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.ac_mono_ctx_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.rep_arity.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.match_rule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.bin_op_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.ac_mono", "description": "`ac_mono` reduces the `f x \u2291 f y`, for some relation `\u2291` and a\nmonotonic function `f` to `x \u227a y`.\n\n`ac_mono*` unwraps monotonic functions until it can't.\n\n`ac_mono^k`, for some literal number `k` applies monotonicity `k`\ntimes.\n\n`ac_mono := h`, with `h` a hypothesis, unwraps monotonic functions and\nuses `h` to solve the remaining goal. Can be combined with `*` or `^k`:\n`ac_mono* := h`\n\n`ac_mono : p` asserts `p` and uses it to discharge the goal result\nunwrapping a series of monotonic functions. Can be combined with * or\n^k: `ac_mono* : p`\n\nIn the case where `f` is an associative or commutative operator,\n`ac_mono` will consider any possible permutation of its arguments and\nuse the one the minimizes the difference between the left-hand side\nand the right-hand side.\n\nTo use it, first import `tactic.monotonicity`.\n\n`ac_mono` can be used as follows:\n\n```lean\nexample (x y z k m n : \u2115)\n  (h\u2080 : z \u2265 0)\n  (h\u2081 : x \u2264 y) :\n  (m + x + n) * z + k \u2264 z * (y + n + m) + k :=\nbegin\n  ac_mono,\n  -- \u22a2 (m + x + n) * z \u2264 z * (y + n + m)\n  ac_mono,\n  -- \u22a2 m + x + n \u2264 y + n + m\n  ac_mono,\nend\n```\n\nAs with `mono*`, `ac_mono*` solves the goal in one go and so does\n`ac_mono* := h\u2081`. The latter syntax becomes especially interesting in the\nfollowing example:\n\n```lean\nexample (x y z k m n : \u2115)\n  (h\u2080 : z \u2265 0)\n  (h\u2081 : m + x + n \u2264 y + n + m) :\n  (m + x + n) * z + k \u2264 z * (y + n + m) + k :=\nby ac_mono* := h\u2081.\n```\n\nBy giving `ac_mono` the assumption `h\u2081`, we are asking `ac_refl` to\nstop earlier than it would normally would.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_function.to_tactic_format", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.rep_arity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.rep_arity.one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.rep_arity.exactly", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.rep_arity.many", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.bin_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_law.to_tactic_format", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.tactic.ac_mono", "description": "`ac_mono` reduces the `f x \u2291 f y`, for some relation `\u2291` and a\nmonotonic function `f` to `x \u227a y`.\n\n`ac_mono*` unwraps monotonic functions until it can't.\n\n`ac_mono^k`, for some literal number `k` applies monotonicity `k`\ntimes.\n\n`ac_mono := h`, with `h` a hypothesis, unwraps monotonic functions and\nuses `h` to solve the remaining goal. Can be combined with `*` or `^k`:\n`ac_mono* := h`\n\n`ac_mono : p` asserts `p` and uses it to discharge the goal result\nunwrapping a series of monotonic functions. Can be combined with * or\n^k: `ac_mono* : p`\n\nIn the case where `f` is an associative or commutative operator,\n`ac_mono` will consider any possible permutation of its arguments and\nuse the one the minimizes the difference between the left-hand side\nand the right-hand side.\n\nTo use it, first import `tactic.monotonicity`.\n\n`ac_mono` can be used as follows:\n\n```lean\nexample (x y z k m n : \u2115)\n  (h\u2080 : z \u2265 0)\n  (h\u2081 : x \u2264 y) :\n  (m + x + n) * z + k \u2264 z * (y + n + m) + k :=\nbegin\n  ac_mono,\n  -- \u22a2 (m + x + n) * z \u2264 z * (y + n + m)\n  ac_mono,\n  -- \u22a2 m + x + n \u2264 y + n + m\n  ac_mono,\nend\n```\n\nAs with `mono*`, `ac_mono*` solves the goal in one go and so does\n`ac_mono* := h\u2081`. The latter syntax becomes especially interesting in the\nfollowing example:\n\n```lean\nexample (x y z k m n : \u2115)\n  (h\u2080 : z \u2265 0)\n  (h\u2081 : m + x + n \u2264 y + n + m) :\n  (m + x + n) * z + k \u2264 z * (y + n + m) + k :=\nby ac_mono* := h\u2081.\n```\n\nBy giving `ac_mono` the assumption `h\u2081`, we are asking `ac_refl` to\nstop earlier than it would normally would.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.apply_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.repeat_until", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.list.minimum_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.solve_mvar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mk_congr_law", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.match_chaining_rules", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.has_to_tactic_format_mono_function", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.match_ac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_law", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_law.assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_law.congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_law.other", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.ac_mono_ctx.to_tactic_format", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.same_function_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.repeat_until_or_at_most", "description": "(repeat_until_or_at_most n t u): repeat tactic `t` at most n times or until u succeeds", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.best_match", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.ac_mono_ctx'.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.repeat_or_not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.ac_monotonicity_goal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.ac_mono_ctx", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.ac_mono_ctx'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.ac_mono_ctx'.to_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.ac_mono_ctx'.function", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.ac_mono_ctx'.left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.ac_mono_ctx'.right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.ac_mono_ctx'.rel_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.ac_mono_aux", "description": "transforms a goal of the form `f x \u227c f y` into `x \u2264 y` using lemmas\nmarked as `monotonic`.\n\nSpecial care is taken when `f` is the repeated application of an\nassociative operator and if the operator is commutative", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.one_line", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mk_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.ac_mono_ctx'.functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.arity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_function", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_function.non_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_function.assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mono_function.assoc_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.fold_assoc1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.has_to_tactic_format_mono_ctx", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.bin_op_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.same_function", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.rep_arity.has_reflect", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.find_if_cond_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.split_ifs", "description": " Splits all if-then-else-expressions into multiple goals.\n\nGiven a goal of the form `g (if p then x else y)`, `split_ifs` will produce\ntwo goals: `p \u22a2 g x` and `\u00acp \u22a2 g y`.\n\nIf there are multiple ite-expressions, then `split_ifs` will split them all,\nstarting with a top-most one whose condition does not contain another\nite-expression.\n\n`split_ifs at *` splits all ite-expressions in all hypotheses as well as the goal.\n\n`split_ifs with h\u2081 h\u2082 h\u2083` overrides the default names for the hypotheses.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.find_if_cond", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.split_ifs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.tactic.split_ifs", "description": " Splits all if-then-else-expressions into multiple goals.\n\nGiven a goal of the form `g (if p then x else y)`, `split_ifs` will produce\ntwo goals: `p \u22a2 g x` and `\u00acp \u22a2 g y`.\n\nIf there are multiple ite-expressions, then `split_ifs` will split them all,\nstarting with a top-most one whose condition does not contain another\nite-expression.\n\n`split_ifs at *` splits all ite-expressions in all hypotheses as well as the goal.\n\n`split_ifs with h\u2081 h\u2082 h\u2083` overrides the default names for the hypotheses.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.split_if1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.reduce_ifs_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "except_t.lift", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except.error", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except.ok", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except_t.return", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except.monad", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except.bind", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except_t.bind_cont", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except_t.monad_map", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except.to_option", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "monad_except.orelse", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "monad_except", "description": "An implementation of [MonadError](https://hackage.haskell.org/package/mtl-2.2.2/docs/Control-Monad-Except.html#t:MonadError)", "p": "core"}, {"name": "monad_except.throw", "description": "An implementation of [MonadError](https://hackage.haskell.org/package/mtl-2.2.2/docs/Control-Monad-Except.html#t:MonadError)", "p": "core"}, {"name": "monad_except.catch", "description": "An implementation of [MonadError](https://hackage.haskell.org/package/mtl-2.2.2/docs/Control-Monad-Except.html#t:MonadError)", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except_t.monad_run", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except_t.adapt", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except_t.monad_except", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "monad_except.orelse'", "description": "Alternative orelse operator that allows to select which exception should be used.\n   The default is to use the first exception since the standard `orelse` uses the second.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except.map", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except_t.monad_functor", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except.to_bool", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except_t.bind", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except_t.monad", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "monad_except_adapter", "description": "Adapt a monad stack, changing its top-most error type.\n\n   Note: This class can be seen as a simplification of the more \"principled\" definition\n   ```lean\n   class monad_except_functor (\u03b5 \u03b5' : out_param (Type u)) (n n' : Type u \u2192 Type u) :=\n   (map {\u03b1 : Type u} : (\u2200 {m : Type u \u2192 Type u} [monad m], except_t \u03b5 m \u03b1 \u2192 except_t \u03b5' m \u03b1) \u2192 n \u03b1 \u2192 n' \u03b1)\n   ```", "p": "core"}, {"name": "monad_except_adapter.adapt_except", "description": "Adapt a monad stack, changing its top-most error type.\n\n   Note: This class can be seen as a simplification of the more \"principled\" definition\n   ```lean\n   class monad_except_functor (\u03b5 \u03b5' : out_param (Type u)) (n n' : Type u \u2192 Type u) :=\n   (map {\u03b1 : Type u} : (\u2200 {m : Type u \u2192 Type u} [monad m], except_t \u03b5 m \u03b1 \u2192 except_t \u03b5' m \u03b1) \u2192 n \u03b1 \u2192 n' \u03b1)\n   ```", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except_t", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except_t.run", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except.return", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "monad_except_adapter_trans", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except_t.catch", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except.map_error", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except_t.monad_except_adapter", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "except_t.has_monad_lift", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "complex.exp_two_pi_mul_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cos_eq_one_iff_of_lt_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cos_nat_mul_two_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.sq_cos_pi_div_six", "description": " The square of the cosine of `\u03c0 / 6` is `3 / 4` (this is sometimes more convenient than the\nresult for cosine itself).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.sin_sub_pi_div_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.pi_le_four", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.tan_add_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.sin_pi_div_six", "description": "The sine of `\u03c0 / 6` is `1 / 2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.tan_int_mul_pi_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cos_le_cos_of_nonneg_of_le_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.continuous_on_cos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cos_two_pi_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.cos_two_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cos_int_mul_two_pi_sub_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.sin_add_int_mul_two_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.continuous_sin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.tendsto_cos_pi_div_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnreal.pi", "description": "`\u03c0` considered as a nonnegative real.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.range_sin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.cos_sub_pi_div_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.sin_sub_pi_div_two", "description": ""