: "wcovby.le_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wcovby_iff_Ioo_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covby_iff_lt_and_eq_or_eq", "description": "An `iff` version of `covby.eq_or_eq` and `covby_of_eq_or_eq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covby.is_irrefl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covby_iff_Ioo_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.wcovby_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antisymm_rel.trans_wcovby", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wcovby_of_le_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wcovby.Ioc_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covby.unique_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_covby_of_lt_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wcovby.le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_lt.lt.exists_lt_lt", "description": "**Alias** of `exists_lt_lt_of_not_covby`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antisymm_rel.trans_covby", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covby.ge_of_gt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "densely_ordered_iff_forall_not_covby", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wcovby.Ico_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.mk_wcovby_mk_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wcovby_iff_le_and_eq_or_eq", "description": "An `iff` version of `wcovby.eq_or_eq` and `wcovby_of_eq_or_eq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wcovby_of_eq_or_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vm_decl.to_name", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_core.ret", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_decl.olean", "description": "Return .olean file where the given VM declaration was imported from.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj.fields", "description": "For constructor vm_obj's, it returns the data stored in the object.\n  For closure vm_obj's, it returns the local arguments captured by the closure.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.stack_obj", "description": "Return the vm_obj stored at the given position on the execution stack.\n  It fails if position >= vm.stack_size", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj.to_level", "description": "For level vm_obj's, it returns the universe level wrapped by the vm_obj.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj.fn_idx", "description": "For closure vm_obj's, it returns the internal function index.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.pp_expr", "description": "Pretty print the given expression.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.pc", "description": "Return the program counter.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.get_override", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_decl_kind", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_decl_kind.bytecode", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_decl_kind.builtin", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_decl_kind.cfun", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.pp_stack_obj", "description": "Pretty print the vm_obj at the given position on the execution stack.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.call_stack_fn", "description": "Return the function name at the given stack frame.\n  Action fails if position >= vm.call_stack_size.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj_kind.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_decl", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.bp", "description": "Return the base stack pointer for the frame on top of the call stack.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.get_attribute", "description": "Return the list of declarations tagged with the given attribute.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.eof", "description": "Return tt if end of the input stream has been reached.\n  For example, this can happen if the user presses Ctrl-D", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj.to_nat", "description": "For simple and mpz vm_obj's", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_core.map", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_decl.arity", "description": "Number of arguments needed to execute the given VM declaration.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.call_stack_var_range", "description": "Return the range [start, end) for the given stack frame.\n  Action fails if position >= vm.call_stack_size.\n  The values start and end correspond to positions at the execution stack.\n  We have that 0 <= start < end <= vm.stack_size", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_decl.idx", "description": "Internal function index associated with the given VM declaration.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj.to_declaration", "description": "For declaration vm_obj's, it returns the declaration wrapped by the vm_obj.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.call_stack_size", "description": "Number of frames on the call stack.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_decl.override_idx", "description": "If the given declaration is overridden by another declaration using the vm_override attribute, then this returns the overriding declaration.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.stack_obj_info", "description": "Return (name, type) for the object at the given position on the execution stack.\n  It fails if position >= vm.stack_size.\n  The name is anonymous if vm_obj is a transient value created by the compiler.\n  Type information is only recorded if the type is a closed term at compilation time.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj.to_format", "description": "For format vm_obj's, it returns the format object wrapped by the vm_obj.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj.to_name", "description": "For name vm_obj's, it returns the name wrapped by the vm_obj.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.get_line", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.curr_fn", "description": "Return the name of the function on top of the call stack.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.put_str", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.trace", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.get_options", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_decl.pos", "description": "Return source position if available", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.get_decl", "description": "Returns the vm declaration associated with the given name. Remark: does _not_ return the vm_override if present.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.stack_size", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_core.monad", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_core.bind", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj_kind", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj_kind.simple", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj_kind.constructor", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj_kind.closure", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj_kind.native_closure", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj_kind.mpz", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj_kind.name", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj_kind.level", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj_kind.expr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj_kind.declaration", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj_kind.environment", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj_kind.tactic_state", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj_kind.format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj_kind.options", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj_kind.other", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj.kind", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.get_env", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_local_info", "description": "Information for local variables and arguments on the VM stack.\n  Remark: type is only available if it is a closed term at compilation time.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_local_info.id", "description": "Information for local variables and arguments on the VM stack.\n  Remark: type is only available if it is a closed term at compilation time.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_local_info.type", "description": "Information for local variables and arguments on the VM stack.\n  Remark: type is only available if it is a closed term at compilation time.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_monitor", "description": "A Lean VM monitor. Monitors are registered using the [vm_monitor] attribute.\n\n   If option 'debugger' is true, then the VM will initialize the vm_monitor state using the\n   'init' field, and will invoke the function 'step' before each instruction is invoked.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_monitor.init", "description": "A Lean VM monitor. Monitors are registered using the [vm_monitor] attribute.\n\n   If option 'debugger' is true, then the VM will initialize the vm_monitor state using the\n   'init' field, and will invoke the function 'step' before each instruction is invoked.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_monitor.step", "description": "A Lean VM monitor. Monitors are registered using the [vm_monitor] attribute.\n\n   If option 'debugger' is true, then the VM will initialize the vm_monitor state using the\n   'init' field, and will invoke the function 'step' before each instruction is invoked.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_core", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_decl.args_info", "description": "Return names .olean file where the given VM declaration was imported from.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj.cidx", "description": "For simple and constructor vm_obj's, it returns the constructor tag/index.\n  Return 0 otherwise.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.decl_of_idx", "description": "Returns the vm declaration associated with the given index. Remark: does _not_ return the vm_override if present.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_decl.kind", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj.to_environment", "description": "For environment vm_obj's, it returns the environment wrapped by the vm_obj.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj.to_expr", "description": "For expr vm_obj's, it returns the expression wrapped by the vm_obj.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm.obj_to_string", "description": "Convert the given vm_obj into a string", "p": "core"}, {"name": "vm_obj.to_tactic_state", "description": "For tactic_state vm_obj's, it returns the tactic_state object wrapped by the vm_obj.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "option.map_map\u2082_antidistrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map_map\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_map_left_anticomm", "description": "Symmetric statement to `option.map_map\u2082_antidistrib_left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_left_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_none_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_def", "description": " `option.map\u2082` in terms of monadic operations. Note that this can't be taken as the definition\nbecause of the lack of universe polymorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_map_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_coe_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_right_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map_map\u2082_antidistrib_right", "description": "Symmetric statement to `option.map_map\u2082_right_anticomm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_curry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map_map\u2082_right_comm", "description": "Symmetric statement to `option.map_map\u2082_distrib_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map_map\u2082_distrib_left", "description": "Symmetric statement to `option.map\u2082_map_left_comm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map_map\u2082_right_anticomm", "description": "Symmetric statement to `option.map_map\u2082_antidistrib_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map_map\u2082_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map_map\u2082_distrib_right", "description": "Symmetric statement to `option.map_map\u2082_right_comm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_none_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map_map\u2082_antidistrib_left", "description": "Symmetric statement to `option.map\u2082_map_left_anticomm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_map_left_comm", "description": "Symmetric statement to `option.map_map\u2082_distrib_left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_some_some", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_right_identity", "description": " If `b` is a right identity for a binary operation `f`, then `some b` is a right identity for\n`option.map\u2082 f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_coe_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.mem_map\u2082_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_eq_none_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map_uncurry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082", "description": " The image of a binary function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b3` as a function `option \u03b1 \u2192 option \u03b2 \u2192 option \u03b3`.\nMathematically this should be thought of as the image of the corresponding function `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b3`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_left_identity", "description": " If `a` is a left identity for a binary operation `f`, then `some a` is a left identity for\n`option.map\u2082 f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_map_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.map\u2082_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sieve.cover_by_image", "description": "For a functor `G : C \u2964 D`, and an object `U : D`, `sieve.cover_by_image G U` is the sieve of `U`\nconsisting of those arrows that factor through images of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.sheaf_iso", "description": "Given an natural isomorphism `G \u22d9 \u2131 \u2245 G \u22d9 \u2131'` between presheaves of arbitrary category,\nwhere `G` is full and cover-dense, and `\u2131', \u2131` are sheaves,\nwe may obtain a natural isomorphism between presheaves.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.types.presheaf_iso_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.sheaf_iso_inv_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.presheaf_iso", "description": "Given an natural isomorphism `G \u22d9 \u2131 \u2245 G \u22d9 \u2131'` between presheaves of arbitrary category,\nwhere `G` is full and cover-dense, and `\u2131', \u2131` are sheaves,\nwe may obtain a natural isomorphism between presheaves.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.sheaf_coyoneda_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.hom_over_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.types.presheaf_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.Sheaf_equiv_of_cover_preserving_cover_lifting_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.types.app_hom_valid_glue", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.types.presheaf_iso_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.restrict_hom_equiv_hom", "description": "A full and cover-dense functor `G` induces an equivalence between morphisms into a sheaf and\nmorphisms over the restrictions via `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.iso_over", "description": "(Implementation). Given an iso between the pullbacks of two sheaves, we can whisker it with\n`coyoneda` to obtain an iso between the pullbacks of the sheaves of maps from `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.types.app_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.sheaf_hom_restrict_eq", "description": "The constructed `sheaf_hom \u03b1` is equal to `\u03b1` when restricted onto `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.sheaf_iso_hom_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.Sheaf_equiv_of_cover_preserving_cover_lifting_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.cover_by_image_structure", "description": "An auxiliary structure that witnesses the fact that `f` factors through an image object of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.cover_by_image_structure.obj", "description": "An auxiliary structure that witnesses the fact that `f` factors through an image object of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.cover_by_image_structure.lift", "description": "An auxiliary structure that witnesses the fact that `f` factors through an image object of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.cover_by_image_structure.map", "description": "An auxiliary structure that witnesses the fact that `f` factors through an image object of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.cover_by_image_structure.fac'", "description": "An auxiliary structure that witnesses the fact that `f` factors through an image object of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.iso_over_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.types.sheaf_iso", "description": "Given an natural isomorphism `G \u22d9 \u2131 \u2245 G \u22d9 \u2131'` between presheaves of types, where `G` is full and\ncover-dense, and `\u2131, \u2131'` are sheaves, we may obtain a natural isomorphism between sheaves.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.types.sheaf_iso_inv_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.iso_over_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.types.app_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.sheaf_eq_amalgamation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.cover_by_image", "description": "For a functor `G : C \u2964 D`, and an object `U : D`, `presieve.cover_by_image G U` is the presieve\nof `U` consisting of those arrows that factor through images of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense", "description": "A functor `G : (C, J) \u2964 (D, K)` is called `cover_dense` if for each object in `D`,\n  there exists a covering sieve in `D` that factors through images of `G`.\n\nThis definition can be found in https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/dense+sub-site Definition 2.2.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.is_cover", "description": "A functor `G : (C, J) \u2964 (D, K)` is called `cover_dense` if for each object in `D`,\n  there exists a covering sieve in `D` that factors through images of `G`.\n\nThis definition can be found in https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/dense+sub-site Definition 2.2.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.types.app_hom", "description": "(Implementation). The morphism `\u2131(X) \u27f6 \u2131'(X)` given by gluing the `pushforward_family`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.types.presheaf_iso", "description": "Given an natural isomorphism `G \u22d9 \u2131 \u2245 G \u22d9 \u2131'` between presheaves of types, where `G` is full and\ncover-dense, and `\u2131, \u2131'` are sheaves, we may obtain a natural isomorphism between presheaves.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.in_cover_by_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.types.pushforward_family_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.sheaf_yoneda_hom", "description": "(Implementation). `sheaf_coyoneda_hom` but the order of the arguments of the functor are swapped.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.sheaf_hom", "description": "Given an natural transformation `G \u22d9 \u2131 \u27f6 G \u22d9 \u2131'` between presheaves of arbitrary category,\nwhere `G` is full and cover-dense, and `\u2131'` is a sheaf, we may obtain a natural transformation\nbetween presheaves.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.types.app_iso", "description": "(Implementation). The maps given in `app_iso` is inverse to each other and gives a `\u2131(X) \u2245 \u2131'(X)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.cover_by_image_structure.fac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.presheaf_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.types.pushforward_family", "description": "(Implementation). Given a section of `\u2131` on `X`, we can obtain a family of elements valued in `\u2131'`\nthat is defined on a cover generated by the images of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.types.sheaf_iso_hom_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.hom_over", "description": "(Implementation). Given an hom between the pullbacks of two sheaves, we can whisker it with\n`coyoneda` to obtain an hom between the pullbacks of the sheaves of maps from `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.types.pushforward_family_compatible", "description": "(Implementation). The `pushforward_family` defined is compatible.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.compatible_preserving", "description": "A fully faithful cover-dense functor preserves compatible families.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.sheaf_hom_eq", "description": "If the pullback map is obtained via whiskering,\nthen the result `sheaf_hom (whisker_left G.op \u03b1)` is equal to `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.functor_pullback_pushforward_covering", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.types.app_hom_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.iso_of_restrict_iso", "description": "Given a full and cover-dense functor `G` and a natural transformation of sheaves `\u03b1 : \u2131 \u27f6 \u2131'`,\nif the pullback of `\u03b1` along `G` is iso, then `\u03b1` is also iso.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.sheaf_coyoneda_hom", "description": "(Implementation). The sheaf map given in `types.sheaf_hom` is natural in terms of `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.sites.pullback.full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.presheaf_iso_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.types.presheaf_hom", "description": "Given an natural transformation `G \u22d9 \u2131 \u27f6 G \u22d9 \u2131'` between presheaves of types, where `G` is full\nand cover-dense, and `\u2131'` is a sheaf, we may obtain a natural transformation between sheaves.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.Sheaf_equiv_of_cover_preserving_cover_lifting", "description": "Given a functor between small sites that is cover-dense, cover-preserving, and cover-lifting,\nit induces an equivalence of category of sheaves valued in a complete category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cover_dense.sites.pullback.faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presieve.cover_by_image_structure.fac_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_ring_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.finite.of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_def", "description": "An R-module is Noetherian iff all its submodules are finitely-generated.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_ring_iff_ideal_fg", "description": "A ring is Noetherian if and only if all its ideals are finitely-generated.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian.bijective_of_surjective_endomorphism", "description": "Any surjective endomorphism of a Noetherian module is bijective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian.injective_of_surjective_endomorphism", "description": "Any surjective endomorphism of a Noetherian module is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.is_noetherian", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_ring.is_nilpotent_nilradical", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_of_submodule_of_noetherian", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_iff_fg_well_founded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fg_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_of_fg_of_noetherian", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_of_linear_independent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_ring_of_ring_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_pi'", "description": " A version of `is_noetherian_pi` for non-dependent functions. We need this instance because\nsometimes Lean fails to apply the dependent version in non-dependent settings (e.g., it fails to\nprove that `\u03b9 \u2192 \u211d` is finite dimensional over `\u211d`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian.equiv_punit_of_prod_injective", "description": "If `M \u2295 N` embeds into `M`, for `M` noetherian over `R`, then `N` is trivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.is_noetherian.finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_iff_well_founded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fg_of_ker_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian", "description": "`is_noetherian R M` is the proposition that `M` is a Noetherian `R`-module,\nimplemented as the predicate that all `R`-submodules of `M` are finitely generated.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian.noetherian", "description": "`is_noetherian R M` is the proposition that `M` is a Noetherian `R`-module,\nimplemented as the predicate that all `R`-submodules of `M` are finitely generated.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set_has_maximal_iff_noetherian", "description": "A module is Noetherian iff every nonempty set of submodules has a maximal submodule among them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone_stabilizes_iff_noetherian", "description": "A module is Noetherian iff every increasing chain of submodules stabilizes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_ring", "description": "A (semi)ring is Noetherian if it is Noetherian as a module over itself,\ni.e. all its ideals are finitely generated.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian.exists_endomorphism_iterate_ker_inf_range_eq_bot", "description": "For any endomorphism of a Noetherian module, there is some nontrivial iterate\nwith disjoint kernel and range.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_ring_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_of_ker_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_span_of_finite", "description": " In a module over a noetherian ring, the submodule generated by finitely many vectors is\nnoetherian.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_of_subsingleton", "description": "Modules over the trivial ring are Noetherian.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian.disjoint_partial_sups_eventually_bot", "description": "A sequence `f` of submodules of a noetherian module,\nwith `f (n+1)` disjoint from the supremum of `f 0`, ..., `f n`,\nis eventually zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian.induction", "description": "If `\u2200 I > J, P I` implies `P J`, then `P` holds for all submodules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_ring_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_of_linear_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_top_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_of_range_eq_ker", "description": "If the first and final modules in a short exact sequence are noetherian,\n then the middle module is also noetherian.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_of_fg_of_noetherian'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_of_tower", "description": " If `M / S / R` is a scalar tower, and `M / R` is Noetherian, then `M / S` is\nalso noetherian.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_submodule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "well_founded_submodule_gt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_submodule'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_submodule_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_submodule_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_of_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derive_fintype.finset_in.mk", "description": " To construct the finset, we use an injective map from the type `\u0393`, which will be the\nsigma over all constructor arguments. We use sigma instances and existing fintype instances\nto prove that `\u0393` is a fintype, and construct the function `f` that maps `\u27e8a, b, c, ...\u27e9`\nto `C_n a b c ...` where `C_n` is the nth constructor, and `mem` asserts\n`enum (C_n a b c ...) = n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derive_fintype.mk_fintype", "description": "Construct a fintype instance from a completed `finset_above`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.derive_fintype.mk_sigma_elim_eq", "description": " Prove the goal `a |- enum (f a) = n`, where `f` is the function constructed in `mk_sigma_elim`,\nand `enum` is a function that reduces to `n` on the constructor `C_n`. Here we just have to case on\n`a` `m` times, and then `reflexivity` finishes the proof.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.derive_fintype.mk_sigma_elim_inj", "description": " Prove the goal `a, b |- f a = f b \u2192 g a = g b` where `f` is the function we constructed in\n`mk_sigma_elim`, and `g` is some other term that gets built up and eventually closed by\nreflexivity. Here `a` and `b` have sigma types so the proof approach is to case on `a` and `b`\nuntil the goal reduces to `C_n a1 ... am = C_n b1 ... bm \u2192 \u27e8a1, ..., am\u27e9 = \u27e8b1, ..., bm\u27e9`, at which\npoint cases on the equality reduces the problem to reflexivity.\n\nThe arguments are the number `m` returned from `mk_sigma_elim`, and the hypotheses `a,b` that we\nneed to case on.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.derive_fintype.mk_finset", "description": " Prove the goal `|- finset_above T enum k`, where `T` is the inductive type and `enum` is the\ndiscriminant function. The arguments are `args`, the parameters to the inductive type (and all\nconstructors), `k`, the index of the current variant, and `cs`, the list of constructor names.\nThis uses `finset_above.cons` for basic variants and `finset_above.union` for variants with\narguments, using the auxiliary functions `mk_sigma`, `mk_sigma_elim`, `mk_sigma_elim_inj`,\n`mk_sigma_elim_eq` to close subgoals.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.fintype_instance", "description": "Tries to derive a `fintype` instance for inductives and structures.\n\nFor example:\n```lean\n@[derive fintype]\ninductive foo (n m : \u2115)\n| zero : foo\n| one : bool \u2192 foo\n| two : fin n \u2192 fin m \u2192 foo\n```\nHere, `@[derive fintype]` adds the instance `foo.fintype`. The underlying finset\ndefinitionally unfolds to a list that enumerates the elements of the inductive in\nlexicographic order.\n\nIf the structure/inductive has a type parameter `\u03b1`, then the generated instance will have an\nargument `fintype \u03b1`, even if it is not used.  (This is due to the implementation using\n`instance_derive_handler`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.mk_fintype_instance", "description": " Proves `|- fintype T` where `T` is a non-recursive inductive type with no indices,\nwhere all arguments to all constructors are fintypes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derive_fintype.finset_in", "description": " This is a finset covering a nontrivial variant (with one or more constructor arguments).\nThe property `P` here is `\u03bb a, enum a = n` where `n` is the discriminant for the current\nvariant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.derive_fintype.mk_sigma_mem", "description": "Prove the goal `|- \u03a3' (a:A) (b: B a) (c:C a b), unit` given a list of terms `a, b, c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.derive_fintype.mk_sigma", "description": " Construct the term `\u03a3' (a:A) (b:B a) (c:C a b), unit` from\n`\u03a0 (a:A) (b:B a), C a b \u2192 T` (the type of a constructor).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derive_fintype.finset_above.mem_cons_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derive_fintype.finset_above.mem_union_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derive_fintype.finset_above.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derive_fintype.finset_above.union", "description": " For nontrivial variants, we split the constructor list into a `finset_in` component for the\ncurrent constructor and a `finset_above` for the rest.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derive_fintype.finset_above.nil", "description": "The base case is when we run out of variants; we just put an empty finset at the end.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derive_fintype.finset_above.mem_cons_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derive_fintype.finset_above", "description": " A step in the construction of `finset.univ` for a finite inductive type.\nWe will set `enum` to the discriminant of the inductive type, so a `finset_above`\nrepresents a finset that enumerates all elements in a tail of the constructor list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derive_fintype.finset_in.mem_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.derive_fintype.mk_sigma_elim", "description": " Prove the goal `(\u03a3' (a:A) (b:B a) (c:C a b), unit) \u2192 T`\n(this is the function `f` in `finset_in.mk`) using recursive `psigma.elim`,\nfinishing with the constructor. The two arguments are the type of the constructor,\nand the constructor term itself; as we recurse we add arguments\nto the constructor application and destructure the pi type of the constructor. We return the number\nof `psigma.elim` applications constructed, which is the number of constructor arguments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derive_fintype.finset_above.cons", "description": "This is the case for a simple variant (no arguments) in an inductive type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.derive_fintype.mk_finset_total", "description": " This function is called to prove `a : T |- a \u2208 S.1` where `S` is the `finset_above` constructed\nby `mk_finset`, after the initial cases on `a : T`, producing a list of subgoals. For each case,\nwe have to navigate past all the variants that don't apply (which is what the `tac` input tactic\ndoes), and then call either `finset_above.mem_cons_self` for trivial variants or\n`finset_above.mem_union_left` and `finset_in.mem_mk` for nontrivial variants. Either way the proof\nis quite simple.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derive_fintype.finset_above.mem_union_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.has_int_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.hom.f_add_monoid_hom", "description": "The `i`-th component of a chain map, as an additive map from chain maps to morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.sub_f_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.map_homological_complex_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.single_map_homological_complex_hom_app_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_homological_complex_id_iso_hom_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans.map_homological_complex", "description": "A natural transformation between functors induces a natural transformation\nbetween those functors applied to homological complexes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.map_homological_complex_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_homological_complex_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.quiver.hom.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_iso.map_homological_complex", "description": "A natural isomorphism between functors induces a natural isomorphism\nbetween those functors applied to homological complexes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_homological_complex_reflects_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cochain_complex.single\u2080_map_homological_complex_hom_app_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.homology_additive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_homological_complex_id_iso_inv_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.category_theory.preadditive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cochain_complex.single\u2080_map_homological_complex_hom_app_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_homological_complex", "description": "An additive functor induces a functor between homological complexes.\nThis is sometimes called the \"prolongation\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.single_map_homological_complex_inv_app_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_iso.map_homological_complex_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cochain_complex.single\u2080_map_homological_complex", "description": "Turning an object into a cochain complex supported at zero then applying a functor is\nthe same as applying the functor then forming the cochain complex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.boundaries_additive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans.map_homological_complex_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.eval_additive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.quiver.hom.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.single\u2080_map_homological_complex_inv_app_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cochain_complex.single\u2080_map_homological_complex_inv_app_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.neg_f_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans.map_homological_complex_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.hom.f_add_monoid_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.map_homological_complex_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.nsmul_f_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.has_nat_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.add_f_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.map_homological_complex", "description": "An equivalence of categories induces an equivalences between the respective categories\nof homological complex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_homological_complex_id_iso", "description": " The functor on homological complexes induced by the identity functor is\nisomorphic to the identity functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.quiver.hom.has_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans.map_homological_complex_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_homological_complex_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.zero_f_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.quiver.hom.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.single_map_homological_complex", "description": "Turning an object into a complex supported at `j` then applying a functor is\nthe same as applying the functor then forming the complex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.single_map_homological_complex_hom_app_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_homogical_complex_additive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.single\u2080_map_homological_complex_inv_app_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.map_homological_complex_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans.map_homological_complex_naturality_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.map_chain_complex_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.cycles_additive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_homological_complex_obj_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.single\u2080_map_homological_complex", "description": "Turning an object into a chain complex supported at zero then applying a functor is\nthe same as applying the functor then forming the complex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_iso.map_homological_complex_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.zsmul_f_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.single\u2080_map_homological_complex_hom_app_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.single_map_homological_complex_inv_app_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans.map_homological_complex_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.quiver.hom.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.single\u2080_map_homological_complex_hom_app_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cochain_complex.single\u2080_map_homological_complex_inv_app_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient.fin_choice_aux", "description": " An auxiliary function for `quotient.fin_choice`.  Given a\ncollection of setoids indexed by a type `\u03b9`, a (finite) list `l` of\nindices, and a function that for each `i \u2208 l` gives a term of the\ncorresponding quotient type, then there is a corresponding term in the\nquotient of the product of the setoids indexed by `l`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient.fin_choice_aux_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient.fin_choice_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient.fin_choice", "description": " Given a collection of setoids indexed by a fintype `\u03b9` and a\nfunction that for each `i : \u03b9` gives a term of the corresponding\nquotient type, then there is corresponding term in the quotient of the\nproduct of the setoids.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.has_mod", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.mod", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.mod_core", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.div", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.div_core", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "nat.has_div", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_restrict_of_ae_imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_Ioi_comp_mul_right_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.integral_eq_of_tendsto_of_nonneg_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.bUnion_Iic_ae_cover", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.comp_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Ioo_of_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.ae_tendsto_indicator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_Iic_of_interval_integral_norm_bounded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Ioo_of_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.integrable_of_lintegral_nnnorm_tendsto'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Ico_of_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_Ioi_of_interval_integral_norm_bounded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_Ioi_of_has_deriv_at_of_tendsto", "description": " **Fundamental theorem of calculus-2**, on semi-infinite intervals `(a, +\u221e)`.\nWhen a function has a limit at infinity `m`, and its derivative is integrable, then the\nintegral of the derivative on `(a, +\u221e)` is `m - f a`. Version assuming differentiability\non `(a, +\u221e)` and continuity on `[a, +\u221e)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_Ioi_deriv_of_nonpos", "description": " When a function has a limit at infinity, and its derivative is nonpositive, then the derivative\nis automatically integrable on `(a, +\u221e)`. Version assuming differentiability\non `(a, +\u221e)` and continuity on `[a, +\u221e)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Ioc_of_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Ico_of_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.integrable_of_integral_norm_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Ico_of_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Ioc_of_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover", "description": "A sequence `\u03c6` of subsets of `\u03b1` is a `ae_cover` w.r.t. a measure `\u03bc` and a filter `l`\n   if almost every point (w.r.t. `\u03bc`) of `\u03b1` eventually belongs to `\u03c6 n` (w.r.t. `l`), and if\n   each `\u03c6 n` is measurable.\n   This definition is a technical way to avoid duplicating a lot of proofs.\n   It should be thought of as a sufficient condition for being able to interpret\n   `\u222b x, f x \u2202\u03bc` (if it exists) as the limit of `\u222b x in \u03c6 n, f x \u2202\u03bc` as `n` tends to `l`.\n\n   See for example `measure_theory.ae_cover.lintegral_tendsto_of_countably_generated`,\n   `measure_theory.ae_cover.integrable_of_integral_norm_tendsto` and\n   `measure_theory.ae_cover.integral_tendsto_of_countably_generated`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.ae_eventually_mem", "description": "A sequence `\u03c6` of subsets of `\u03b1` is a `ae_cover` w.r.t. a measure `\u03bc` and a filter `l`\n   if almost every point (w.r.t. `\u03bc`) of `\u03b1` eventually belongs to `\u03c6 n` (w.r.t. `l`), and if\n   each `\u03c6 n` is measurable.\n   This definition is a technical way to avoid duplicating a lot of proofs.\n   It should be thought of as a sufficient condition for being able to interpret\n   `\u222b x, f x \u2202\u03bc` (if it exists) as the limit of `\u222b x in \u03c6 n, f x \u2202\u03bc` as `n` tends to `l`.\n\n   See for example `measure_theory.ae_cover.lintegral_tendsto_of_countably_generated`,\n   `measure_theory.ae_cover.integrable_of_integral_norm_tendsto` and\n   `measure_theory.ae_cover.integral_tendsto_of_countably_generated`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.measurable", "description": "A sequence `\u03c6` of subsets of `\u03b1` is a `ae_cover` w.r.t. a measure `\u03bc` and a filter `l`\n   if almost every point (w.r.t. `\u03bc`) of `\u03b1` eventually belongs to `\u03c6 n` (w.r.t. `l`), and if\n   each `\u03c6 n` is measurable.\n   This definition is a technical way to avoid duplicating a lot of proofs.\n   It should be thought of as a sufficient condition for being able to interpret\n   `\u222b x, f x \u2202\u03bc` (if it exists) as the limit of `\u222b x in \u03c6 n, f x \u2202\u03bc` as `n` tends to `l`.\n\n   See for example `measure_theory.ae_cover.lintegral_tendsto_of_countably_generated`,\n   `measure_theory.ae_cover.integrable_of_integral_norm_tendsto` and\n   `measure_theory.ae_cover.integral_tendsto_of_countably_generated`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_Ioi_deriv_of_nonpos'", "description": " When a function has a limit at infinity, and its derivative is nonpositive, then the derivative\nis automatically integrable on `(a, +\u221e)`. Version assuming differentiability\non `[a, +\u221e)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_Ioi_deriv_of_nonneg", "description": " When a function has a limit at infinity, and its derivative is nonnegative, then the derivative\nis automatically integrable on `(a, +\u221e)`. Version assuming differentiability\non `(a, +\u221e)` and continuity on `[a, +\u221e)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_comp_smul_deriv_Ioi", "description": " Change-of-variables formula for `Ioi` integrals of vector-valued functions, proved by taking\nlimits from the result for finite intervals.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_comp_mul_deriv_Ioi", "description": "Change-of-variables formula for `Ioi` integrals of scalar-valued functions", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.integrable_of_lintegral_nnnorm_bounded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_Ioi_of_has_deriv_at_of_nonneg'", "description": " When a function has a limit at infinity `l`, and its derivative is nonnegative, then the\nintegral of the derivative on `(a, +\u221e)` is `l - g a` (and the derivative is integrable, see\n`integrable_on_Ioi_deriv_of_nonneg'`). Version assuming differentiability on `[a, +\u221e)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_Ioc_of_interval_integral_norm_bounded_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_Ioc_of_interval_integral_norm_bounded_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Ioc_of_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_Ioi_of_has_deriv_at_of_nonneg", "description": " When a function has a limit at infinity `l`, and its derivative is nonnegative, then the\nintegral of the derivative on `(a, +\u221e)` is `l - g a` (and the derivative is integrable, see\n`integrable_on_Ioi_deriv_of_nonneg`). Version assuming differentiability on `(a, +\u221e)` and\ncontinuity on `[a, +\u221e)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.bInter_Ici_ae_cover", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_Ioi_comp_rpow_iff'", "description": " The substitution `y = x ^ p` in integrals over `Ioi 0` preserves integrability (version\nwithout `|p|` factor)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_Ioi_of_has_deriv_at_of_tendsto'", "description": " **Fundamental theorem of calculus-2**, on semi-infinite intervals `(a, +\u221e)`.\nWhen a function has a limit at infinity `m`, and its derivative is integrable, then the\nintegral of the derivative on `(a, +\u221e)` is `m - f a`. Version assuming differentiability\non `[a, +\u221e)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.ae_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_Ioi_deriv_of_nonneg'", "description": " When a function has a limit at infinity, and its derivative is nonnegative, then the derivative\nis automatically integrable on `(a, +\u221e)`. Version assuming differentiability\non `[a, +\u221e)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_Ioi_comp_mul_left_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.lintegral_tendsto_of_countably_generated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Ico_of_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_Ioi_of_interval_integral_norm_tendsto", "description": " If `f` is integrable on intervals `Ioc a (b i)`,\nwhere `b i` tends to \u221e, and\n`\u222b x in a .. b i, \u2016f x\u2016 \u2202\u03bc` converges to `I : \u211d` along a filter `l`,\nthen `f` is integrable on the interval (a, \u221e)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_Iic_of_interval_integral_norm_tendsto", "description": " If `f` is integrable on intervals `Ioc (a i) b`,\nwhere `a i` tends to -\u221e, and\n`\u222b x in a i .. b, \u2016f x\u2016 \u2202\u03bc` converges to `I : \u211d` along a filter `l`,\nthen `f` is integrable on the interval (-\u221e, b)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Iio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.integrable_of_lintegral_nnnorm_bounded'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Icc_of_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.interval_integral_tendsto_integral_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_comp_mul_left_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Ioc_of_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_comp_mul_right_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Ioo_of_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_Ioi_comp_rpow_iff", "description": "The substitution `y = x ^ p` in integrals over `Ioi 0` preserves integrability.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Icc_of_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_Ioi_of_has_deriv_at_of_nonpos", "description": " When a function has a limit at infinity `l`, and its derivative is nonpositive, then the\nintegral of the derivative on `(a, +\u221e)` is `l - g a` (and the derivative is integrable, see\n`integrable_on_Ioi_deriv_of_nonneg`). Version assuming differentiability on `(a, +\u221e)` and\ncontinuity on `[a, +\u221e)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_of_interval_integral_norm_bounded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.interval_integral_tendsto_integral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Icc_of_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_comp_rpow_Ioi", "description": "Substitution `y = x ^ p` in integrals over `Ioi 0`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.interval_integral_tendsto_integral_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_comp_rpow_Ioi_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Icc_of_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Ioo_of_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.supr_lintegral_eq_of_countably_generated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_Ioi_of_has_deriv_at_of_nonpos'", "description": " When a function has a limit at infinity `l`, and its derivative is nonpositive, then the\nintegral of the derivative on `(a, +\u221e)` is `l - g a` (and the derivative is integrable, see\n`integrable_on_Ioi_deriv_of_nonneg'`). Version assuming differentiability on `[a, +\u221e)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.integral_eq_of_tendsto", "description": "Slight reformulation of\n   `measure_theory.ae_cover.integral_tendsto_of_countably_generated`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.integrable_of_integral_tendsto_of_nonneg_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.lintegral_eq_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.integrable_of_lintegral_nnnorm_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.integral_tendsto_of_countably_generated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_of_interval_integral_norm_tendsto", "description": " If `f` is integrable on intervals `Ioc (a i) (b i)`,\nwhere `a i` tends to -\u221e and `b i` tends to \u221e, and\n`\u222b x in a i .. b i, \u2016f x\u2016 \u2202\u03bc` converges to `I : \u211d` along a filter `l`,\nthen `f` is integrable on the interval (-\u221e, \u221e)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.inter_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.ae_strongly_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.integrable_of_integral_bounded_of_nonneg_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_Ioc_of_interval_integral_norm_bounded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.lintegral_tendsto_of_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_cover.integrable_of_integral_norm_bounded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "PartOrd.iso.mk_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "PartOrd.dual", "description": "`order_dual` as a functor.", "