ders. `\u27e8i, a\u27e9 < \u27e8j, b\u27e9` iff `i = j` and `a < b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sigma.lex.le_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sigma.le", "description": "Disjoint sum of orders. `\u27e8i, a\u27e9 \u2264 \u27e8j, b\u27e9` iff `i = j` and `a \u2264 b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sigma.le.fiber", "description": "Disjoint sum of orders. `\u27e8i, a\u27e9 \u2264 \u27e8j, b\u27e9` iff `i = j` and `a \u2264 b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sigma.lex.densely_ordered", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sigma.lex.lt_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sigma.preorder", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sigma.has_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sigma.lex.has_le", "description": "The lexicographical `\u2264` on a sigma type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sigma.lex.preorder", "description": "The lexicographical preorder on a sigma type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sigma.lex.has_lt", "description": "The lexicographical `<` on a sigma type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sigma.lex.order_top", "description": "The lexicographical linear order on a sigma type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sigma.lex.bounded_order", "description": "The lexicographical linear order on a sigma type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite_iff_small_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.comp_inj_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.continuous_on_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.eventually_small_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.nhds_within_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.exists_forall_eventually_eq_prod", "description": " Let `f : \u2115 \u2192 \u03a0 a, \u03b2 a` be a sequence of (dependent) functions on a topological space. Suppose\nthat the family of sets `s n = {x | f (n + 1) x \u2260 f n x}` is locally finite. Then there exists a\nfunction `F : \u03a0 a, \u03b2 a` such that for any `x`, we have `f n x = F x` on the product of an infinite\ninterval `[N, +\u221e)` and a neighbourhood of `x`.\n\nWe formulate the conclusion in terms of the product of filter `filter.at_top` and `\ud835\udcdd x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.locally_finite_comp_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.comp_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.Inter_compl_mem_nhds", "description": " If `f : \u03b2 \u2192 set \u03b1` is a locally finite family of closed sets, then for any `x : \u03b1`, the\nintersection of the complements to `f i`, `x \u2209 f i`, is a neighbourhood of `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.point_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.exists_mem_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.option_elim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.sum_elim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite_option", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.continuous'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.preimage_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.continuous_on_Union'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.closure_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.is_closed_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.exists_forall_eventually_at_top_eventually_eq'", "description": " Let `f : \u2115 \u2192 \u03a0 a, \u03b2 a` be a sequence of (dependent) functions on a topological space. Suppose\nthat the family of sets `s n = {x | f (n + 1) x \u2260 f n x}` is locally finite. Then there exists a\nfunction `F : \u03a0 a, \u03b2 a` such that for any `x`, for sufficiently large values of `n`, we have\n`f n y = F y` in a neighbourhood of `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite_of_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite.exists_forall_eventually_at_top_eventually_eq", "description": " Let `f : \u2115 \u2192 \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` be a sequence of functions on a topological space. Suppose\nthat the family of sets `s n = {x | f (n + 1) x \u2260 f n x}` is locally finite. Then there exists a\nfunction `F :  \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` such that for any `x`, for sufficiently large values of `n`, we have\n`f n =\u1da0[\ud835\udcdd x] F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "locally_finite", "description": " A family of sets in `set X` is locally finite if at every point `x : X`,\nthere is a neighborhood of `x` which meets only finitely many sets in the family.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.neg_succ_of_nat_coe'", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "int.add_comm", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "int.of_nat_mul_of_nat", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "int.neg_add", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "int.sub_nat_nat_of_le", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "int.nat_abs_of_nat", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "int.coe_nat_add_out", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "int.has_add", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "int.neg_of_nat", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "int.repr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "int.mod", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "int.add_assoc", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "int.has_div", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "int.nat_abs_mul_self", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "int.nat_abs_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "int.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "int.has_sub", "description": "", "p