eory.limits.mono_coprod", "description": "This condition expresses that inclusion morphisms into coproducts are monomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_coprod.binary_cofan_inl", "description": "This condition expresses that inclusion morphisms into coproducts are monomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_coprod.mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_coprod.binary_cofan_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_coprod.category_theory.limits.coprod.inl.category_theory.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mono_coprod.mono_coprod_type", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_unique_add_zsmul_mem_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_unique_sub_zsmul_mem_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_nat_gt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "archimedean_iff_nat_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_of_forall_lt_rat_imp_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "archimedean_iff_rat_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_int_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_mem_Ioc_zpow", "description": " Every positive `x` is between two successive integer powers of\nanother `y` greater than one. This is the same as `exists_mem_Ico_zpow`,\nbut with \u2264 and < the other way around.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_rat_btwn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rat.archimedean", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "archimedean", "description": " An ordered additive commutative monoid is called `archimedean` if for any two elements `x`, `y`\nsuch that `0 < y` there exists a natural number `n` such that `x \u2264 n \u2022 y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "archimedean.arch", "description": " An ordered additive commutative monoid is called `archimedean` if for any two elements `x`, `y`\nsuch that `0 < y` there exists a natural number `n` such that `x \u2264 n \u2022 y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "archimedean_iff_int_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_unique_zsmul_near_of_pos", "description": " An archimedean decidable linearly ordered `add_comm_group` has a version of the floor: for\n`a > 0`, any `g` in the group lies between some two consecutive multiples of `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_unique_sub_zsmul_mem_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.archimedean", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "archimedean_iff_int_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_pow_lt_of_lt_one", "description": "For any `y < 1` and any positive `x`, there exists `n : \u2115` with `y ^ n < x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "floor_ring.archimedean", "description": "A linear ordered field that is a floor ring is archimedean.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_rat_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_of_forall_lt_rat_iff_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pow_unbounded_of_one_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_unique_add_zsmul_mem_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.archimedean", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_unique_zsmul_near_of_pos'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_one_pow_unbounded_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_of_forall_rat_lt_imp_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_of_forall_rat_lt_iff_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_pos_rat_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_mem_Ico_zpow", "description": " Every positive `x` is between two successive integer powers of\nanother `y` greater than one. This is the same as `exists_mem_Ioc_zpow`,\nbut with \u2264 and < the other way around.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_rat_near", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_nat_pow_near_of_lt_one", "description": " Given `x` and `y` between `0` and `1`, `x` is between two successive powers of `y`.\nThis is the same as `exists_nat_pow_near`, but for elements between `0` and `1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "archimedean_iff_nat_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.archimedean", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_floor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_rat_gt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_nat_pow_near", "description": " Every x greater than or equal to 1 is between two successive\nnatural-number powers of every y greater than one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_int_gt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_nat_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_nat_one_div_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "archimedean.floor_ring", "description": " A linear ordered archimedean ring is a floor ring. This is not an `instance` because in some\ncases we have a computable `floor` function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "archimedean_iff_rat_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computation.run", "description": "`run c` is an unsound meta function that runs `c` to completion, possibly\n resulting in an infinite loop in the VM.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computation.is_lawful_monad", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computation.run_for", "description": "`run_for c n` evaluates `c` for `n` steps and returns the result, or `none`\n if it did not terminate after `n` steps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computation.corec", "description": "`corec f b` is the corecursor for `computation \u03b1` as a coinductive type.\n If `f b = inl a` then `corec f b = return a`, and if `f b = inl b'` then\n `corec f b = think (corec f b')`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computation.empty", "description": "`empty \u03b1` is the computation that never returns, an infinite sequence of\n `think`s.", "p": "mathlib"}