": "measure_theory.null_measurable_space.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.exists_subordinate_pairwise_disjoint", "description": " If `s\u1d62` is a countable family of (null) measurable pairwise `\u03bc`-a.e. disjoint sets, then there\nexists a subordinate family `t\u1d62 \u2286 s\u1d62` of measurable pairwise disjoint sets such that\n`t\u1d62 =\u1d50[\u03bc] s\u1d62`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable.congr_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.null_measurable_set.compl_to_measurable_compl_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ico.coe_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.comm_monoid_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ico.mk_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ico.nonneg", "description": "like `coe_nonneg`, but with the inequality in `Ico (0:\u03b1) 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioc.coe_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioc.coe_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioo.one_sub_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.le_one", "description": "like `coe_le_one`, but with the inequality in `Icc (0:\u03b1) 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.mem_iff_one_sub_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ico.comm_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioc.coe_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ico.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.coe_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioo.mem_iff_one_sub_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.mul_le_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioc.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioc.comm_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioc.semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ico.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioc.cancel_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.one_sub_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioo.semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioc.mk_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.mul_le_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioo.lt_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ico.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioo.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.monoid_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.coe_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioc.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ico.semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.has_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioo.comm_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioc.coe_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.coe_ne_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.mk_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioc.has_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioc.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.mk_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ico.coe_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.cancel_monoid_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.one_sub_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.coe_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ico.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioo.one_minus_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioc.coe_ne_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.coe_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioo.one_minus_lt_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.nonneg", "description": "like `coe_nonneg`, but with the inequality in `Icc (0:\u03b1) 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.coe_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioc.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.coe_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioo.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.one_sub_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioc.monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioc.le_one", "description": "like `coe_le_one`, but with the inequality in `Ioc (0:\u03b1) 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ico.coe_lt_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioc.cancel_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioo.pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ico.coe_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ioc.comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.copy_attribute'", "description": "`copy_attribute' attr_name src tgt p d_name` copy (user) attribute `attr_name` from\n  `src` to `tgt` if it is defined for `src`; unlike `copy_attribute` the primed version also copies\n  the parameter of the user attribute, in the user attribute case. Make it persistent if `p` is\n  `tt`; if `p` is `none`, the copied attribute is made persistent iff it is persistent on `src`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.additive_test", "description": "`additive_test f replace_all ignore e` tests whether the expression `e` contains no constant\n`nm` that is not applied to any arguments, and such that `f nm = none`.\nThis is used in `@[to_additive]` for deciding which subexpressions to transform: we only transform\nconstants if `additive_test` applied to their first argument returns `tt`.\nThis means we will replace expression applied to e.g. `\u03b1` or `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2`, but not when applied to\ne.g. `\u2115` or `\u211d \u00d7 \u03b1`.\n`f` is the dictionary of declarations that are in the `to_additive` dictionary.\nWe ignore all arguments specified in the `name_map` `ignore`.\nIf `replace_all` is `tt` the test always return `tt`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.additive_test_aux", "description": " Auxilliary function for `additive_test`. The bool argument *only* matters when applied\nto exactly a constant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.transform_decl_with_prefix_fun", "description": "Make a new copy of a declaration,\nreplacing fragments of the names of identifiers in the type and the body using the function `f`.\nThis is used to implement `@[to_additive]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.transform_decl_with_prefix_fun_aux", "description": " transform the declaration `src` and all declarations `pre._proof_i` occurring in `src`\nusing the dictionary `f`.\n`replace_all`, `trace`, `ignore` and `reorder` are configuration options.\n`pre` is the declaration that got the `@[to_additive]` attribute and `tgt_pre` is the target of this\ndeclaration.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.transform_decl_with_prefix_dict", "description": "Make a new copy of a declaration, replacing fragments of the names of identifiers in the type and\nthe body using the dictionary `dict`.\nThis is used to implement `@[to_additive]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.tidy.ext1_wrapper", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.tidy_hole_cmd", "description": " Invoking the hole command `tidy` (\"Use `tidy` to complete the goal\") runs the tactic of\nthe same name, replacing the hole with the tactic script `tidy` produces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.tidy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.hole_command.tidy", "description": " Invoking the hole command `tidy` (\"Use `tidy` to complete the goal\") runs the tactic of\nthe same name, replacing the hole with the tactic script `tidy` produces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.tidy.default_tactics", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.tidy.cfg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.tidy.cfg.trace_result", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.tidy.cfg.trace_result_prefix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.tidy.cfg.tactics", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.attribute.tidy", "description": " Tag interactive tactics (locally) with `[tidy]` to add them to the list of default tactics\ncalled by `tidy`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.tidy.tidy_attribute", "description": " Tag interactive tactics (locally) with `[tidy]` to add them to the list of default tactics\ncalled by `tidy`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.tidy.core", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.tactic.tidy", "description": " Use a variety of conservative tactics to solve goals.\n\n`tidy?` reports back the tactic script it found. As an example\n```lean\nexample : \u2200 x : unit, x = unit.star :=\nbegin\n  tidy? -- Prints the trace message: \"Try this: intros x, exact dec_trivial\"\nend\n```\n\nThe default list of tactics is stored in `tactic.tidy.default_tidy_tactics`.\nThis list can be overridden using `tidy { tactics := ... }`.\n(The list must be a `list` of `tactic string`, so that `tidy?`\ncan report a usable tactic script.)\n\nTactics can also be added to the list by tagging them (locally) with the\n`[tidy]` attribute.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.tidy.run_tactics", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.tidy", "description": " Use a variety of conservative tactics to solve goals.\n\n`tidy?` reports back the tactic script it found. As an example\n```lean\nexample : \u2200 x : unit, x = unit.star :=\nbegin\n  tidy? -- Prints the trace message: \"Try this: intros x, exact dec_trivial\"\nend\n```\n\nThe default list of tactics is stored in `tactic.tidy.default_tidy_tactics`.\nThis list can be overridden using `tidy { tactics := ... }`.\n(The list must be a `list` of `tactic string`, so that `tidy?`\ncan report a usable tactic script.)\n\nTactics can also be added to the list by tagging them (locally) with the\n`[tidy]` attribute.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.tsum_inner_mul_inner", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_hilbert_sum.mk", "description": " If `V : \u03a0 i, G i \u2192\u2097\u1d62[\ud835\udd5c] E` is an orthogonal family such that the supremum of the ranges of\n`V i` is dense, then `(E, V)` is a Hilbert sum of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.orthonormal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal.linear_isometry_equiv_symm_apply_single_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.coe_to_hilbert_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_hilbert_sum.mk_internal", "description": "This is `orthogonal_family.is_hilbert_sum` in the case of actual inclusions from subspaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "`b i` is the `i`th basis vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal.exists_hilbert_basis_extension", "description": "A Hilbert space admits a Hilbert basis extending a given orthonormal subset.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthogonal_family.linear_isometry", "description": " A mutually orthogonal family of subspaces of `E` induce a linear isometry from `lp 2` of the\nsubspaces into `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.repr_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.coe_of_orthogonal_eq_bot_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_hilbert_sum.linear_isometry_equiv_symm_apply_single", "description": " In the canonical isometric isomorphism between a Hilbert sum `E` of `G : \u03b9 \u2192 Type*` and\n`lp G 2`, an \"elementary basis vector\" in `lp G 2` supported at `i : \u03b9` is the image of the\nassociated element in `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_hilbert_sum.linear_isometry_equiv_apply_dfinsupp_sum_single", "description": " In the canonical isometric isomorphism between a Hilbert sum `E` of `G : \u03b9 \u2192 Type*` and\n`lp G 2`, a finitely-supported vector in `lp G 2` is the image of the associated finite sum of\nelements of `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthogonal_family.linear_isometry_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lp.inner_single_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.summable_inner_mul_inner", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lp.has_sum_inner", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.has_sum_repr_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthogonal_family.linear_isometry_apply_dfinsupp_sum_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthogonal_family.has_sum_linear_isometry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.has_sum_inner_mul_inner", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.to_orthonormal_basis", "description": "A finite Hilbert basis is an orthonormal basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.has_sum_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lp.inner_eq_tsum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_hilbert_basis", "description": "A Hilbert space admits a Hilbert basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_hilbert_sum_orthogonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.repr_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_basis.to_hilbert_basis", "description": "An orthonormal basis is an Hilbert basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.finite_spans_dense", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lp.inner_product_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_hilbert_sum.has_sum_linear_isometry_equiv_symm", "description": " In the canonical isometric isomorphism between a Hilbert sum `E` of `G` and `lp G 2`,\na vector `w : lp G 2` is the image of the infinite sum of the associated elements in `E`, and this\nsum indeed converges.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_hilbert_sum.linear_isometry_equiv_symm_apply_dfinsupp_sum_single", "description": " In the canonical isometric isomorphism between a Hilbert sum `E` of `G : \u03b9 \u2192 Type*` and\n`lp G 2`, a finitely-supported vector in `lp G 2` is the image of the associated finite sum of\nelements of `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lp.inner_single_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis", "description": " A Hilbert basis on `\u03b9` for an inner product space `E` is an identification of `E` with the `lp`\nspace `\u2113\u00b2(\u03b9, \ud835\udd5c)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.repr", "description": " A Hilbert basis on `\u03b9` for an inner product space `E` is an identification of `E` with the `lp`\nspace `\u2113\u00b2(\u03b9, \ud835\udd5c)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthogonal_family.range_linear_isometry", "description": " The canonical linear isometry from the `lp 2` of a mutually orthogonal family of subspaces of\n`E` into E, has range the closure of the span of the subspaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthogonal_family.summable_of_lp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_hilbert_sum", "description": " Given a family of Hilbert spaces `G : \u03b9 \u2192 Type*`, a Hilbert sum of `G` consists of a Hilbert\nspace `E` and an orthogonal family `V : \u03a0 i, G i \u2192\u2097\u1d62[\ud835\udd5c] E` such that the induced isometry\n`\u03a6 : lp G 2 \u2192 E` is surjective.\n\nKeeping in mind that `lp G 2` is \"the\" external Hilbert sum of `G : \u03b9 \u2192 Type*`, this is analogous\nto `direct_sum.is_internal`, except that we don't express it in terms of actual submodules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_hilbert_sum.orthogonal_family", "description": " Given a family of Hilbert spaces `G : \u03b9 \u2192 Type*`, a Hilbert sum of `G` consists of a Hilbert\nspace `E` and an orthogonal family `V : \u03a0 i, G i \u2192\u2097\u1d62[\ud835\udd5c] E` such that the induced isometry\n`\u03a6 : lp G 2 \u2192 E` is surjective.\n\nKeeping in mind that `lp G 2` is \"the\" external Hilbert sum of `G : \u03b9 \u2192 Type*`, this is analogous\nto `direct_sum.is_internal`, except that we don't express it in terms of actual submodules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_hilbert_sum.surjective_isometry", "description": " Given a family of Hilbert spaces `G : \u03b9 \u2192 Type*`, a Hilbert sum of `G` consists of a Hilbert\nspace `E` and an orthogonal family `V : \u03a0 i, G i \u2192\u2097\u1d62[\ud835\udd5c] E` such that the induced isometry\n`\u03a6 : lp G 2 \u2192 E` is surjective.\n\nKeeping in mind that `lp G 2` is \"the\" external Hilbert sum of `G : \u03b9 \u2192 Type*`, this is analogous\nto `direct_sum.is_internal`, except that we don't express it in terms of actual submodules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.repr_symm_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.coe_to_orthonormal_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_hilbert_sum.linear_isometry_equiv_symm_apply", "description": " In the canonical isometric isomorphism between a Hilbert sum `E` of `G` and `lp G 2`,\na vector `w : lp G 2` is the image of the infinite sum of the associated elements in `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.mk", "description": "An orthonormal family of vectors whose span is dense in the whole module is a Hilbert basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lp.summable_inner", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.mk_of_orthogonal_eq_bot", "description": " An orthonormal family of vectors whose span has trivial orthogonal complement is a Hilbert\nbasis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.has_sum_orthogonal_projection", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_hilbert_sum.linear_isometry_equiv", "description": " *A* Hilbert sum `(E, V)` of `G` is canonically isomorphic to *the* Hilbert sum of `G`,\ni.e `lp G 2`.\n\nNote that this goes in the opposite direction from `orthogonal_family.linear_isometry`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hilbert_basis.dense_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal.is_hilbert_sum", "description": " Given a total orthonormal family `v : \u03b9 \u2192 E`, `E` is a Hilbert sum of `\u03bb i : \u03b9, \ud835\udd5c` relative to\nthe family of linear isometries `\u03bb i, \u03bb k, k \u2022 v i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthogonal_family.linear_isometry_apply_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_iso.equiv_of_comp_fully_faithful", "description": " Horizontal composition with a fully faithful functor induces a bijection on\nnatural isomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.fully_faithful_cancel_right", "description": "Given a natural isomorphism between `F \u22d9 H` and `G \u22d9 H` for a fully faithful functor `H`, we\ncan 'cancel' it to give a natural iso between `F` and `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.preimage_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.preimage_iso", "description": "If `F : C \u2964 D` is fully faithful, every isomorphism `F.obj X \u2245 F.obj Y` has a preimage.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.faithful.id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_iso.equiv_of_comp_fully_faithful_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso_equiv_of_fully_faithful", "description": "If `F` is fully faithful, we have an equivalence of iso-sets `X \u2245 Y` and `F X \u2245 F Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.fully_faithful_cancel_right_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equiv_of_fully_faithful", "description": "If `F` is fully faithful, we have an equivalence of hom-sets `X \u27f6 Y` and `F X \u27f6 F Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_iso_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.faithful.of_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.preimage_iso_map_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.full.of_iso", "description": "If `F` is full, and naturally isomorphic to some `F'`, then `F'` is also full.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equiv_of_fully_faithful_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.faithful", "description": "A functor `F : C \u2964 D` is faithful if for each `X Y : C`, `F.map` is injective.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/001C>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.faithful.map_injective'", "description": "A functor `F : C \u2964 D` is faithful if for each `X Y : C`, `F.map` is injective.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/001C>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.full_of_exists", "description": "Deduce that `F` is full from the existence of preimages, using choice.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.faithful.div_faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.preimage", "description": "The specified preimage of a morphism under a full functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_iso_of_comp_fully_faithful", "description": " We can construct a natural isomorphism between functors by constructing a natural isomorphism\nbetween those functors composed with a fully faithful functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.faithful.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preimage_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_iso_of_comp_fully_faithful_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans_of_comp_fully_faithful_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.full", "description": "A functor `F : C \u2964 D` is full if for each `X Y : C`, `F.map` is surjective.\nIn fact, we use a constructive definition, so the `full F` typeclass contains data,\nspecifying a particular preimage of each `f : F.obj X \u27f6 F.obj Y`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/001C>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.full.preimage", "description": "A functor `F : C \u2964 D` is full if for each `X Y : C`, `F.map` is surjective.\nIn fact, we use a constructive definition, so the `full F` typeclass contains data,\nspecifying a particular preimage of each `f : F.obj X \u27f6 F.obj Y`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/001C>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.full.witness'", "description": "A functor `F : C \u2964 D` is full if for each `X Y : C`, `F.map` is surjective.\nIn fact, we use a constructive definition, so the `full F` typeclass contains data,\nspecifying a particular preimage of each `f : F.obj X \u27f6 F.obj Y`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/001C>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_iso_of_fully_faithful", "description": "If the image of a morphism under a fully faithful functor in an isomorphism,\nthen the original morphisms is also an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equiv_of_fully_faithful_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso.faithful_of_comp", "description": "**Alias** of `category_theory.faithful.of_comp_iso`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso_equiv_of_fully_faithful_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso_equiv_of_fully_faithful_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_iso_of_comp_fully_faithful_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_iso_of_comp_fully_faithful_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.faithful.of_comp_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.faithful.of_comp_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.full_of_surjective", "description": "Deduce that `F` is full from surjectivity of `F.map`, using choice.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans.equiv_of_comp_fully_faithful", "description": " Horizontal composition with a fully faithful functor induces a bijection on\nnatural transformations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_iso_of_comp_fully_faithful_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preimage_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.full.id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.full.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_iso.equiv_of_comp_fully_faithful_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans.equiv_of_comp_fully_faithful_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.faithful.map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans_of_comp_fully_faithful", "description": " We can construct a natural transformation between functors by constructing a\nnatural transformation between those functors composed with a fully faithful functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq.faithful_of_comp", "description": "**Alias** of `category_theory.faithful.of_c