map_basic_open", "description": "`r` is a unit as a section on the basic open defined by `r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.\u0393_Spec.adjunction", "description": "The adjunction `\u0393 \u22a3 Spec` from `CommRing\u1d52\u1d56` to `Scheme`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.to_\u0393_Spec_continuous", "description": "`to_\u0393_Spec_fun` is continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.\u0393_Spec_left_triangle", "description": "`to_Spec_\u0393 _` is an isomorphism so these are mutually two-sided inverses.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.\u0393_Spec.adjunction_counit_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.identity_to_\u0393_Spec", "description": "The unit as a natural transformation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.\u0393_Spec.LocallyRingedSpace_adjunction", "description": "The adjunction `\u0393 \u22a3 Spec` from `CommRing\u1d52\u1d56` to `LocallyRingedSpace`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.to_\u0393_Spec", "description": "The canonical morphism from `X` to the spectrum of its global sections.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.\u0393_Spec.right_triangle", "description": "`Spec_\u0393_identity` is iso so these are mutually two-sided inverses.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.to_\u0393_Spec_preim_basic_open_eq", "description": " The preimage of a basic open in `Spec \u0393(X)` under the unit is the basic\nopen in `X` defined by the same element (they are equal as sets).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.to_\u0393_Spec_base", "description": " The canonical (bundled) continuous map from the underlying topological\nspace of `X` to the prime spectrum of its global sections.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.not_mem_prime_iff_unit_in_stalk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Spec.to_LocallyRingedSpace.category_theory.faithful", "description": "Spec is a faithful functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.\u0393_Spec.adjunction_unit_app_app_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.comp_ring_hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.LocallyRingedSpace.to_\u0393_Spec_map_basic_open_eq", "description": "The preimage is the basic open in `X` defined by the same element `r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_topology.to_add_group_topology.order_embedding", "description": "The order embedding from ring topologies on `a` to additive group topologies on `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "absolute_value.comp", "description": " Construct an absolute value on a semiring `T` from an absolute value on a semiring `R`\nand an injective ring homomorphism `f : T \u2192+* R`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_topology.complete_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.topological_closure_minimal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_ring", "description": " A topological ring is a ring `R` where addition, multiplication and negation are continuous.\n\nIf `R` is a (unital) ring, then continuity of negation can be derived from continuity of\nmultiplication as it is multiplication with `-1`. (See\n`topological_semiring.has_continuous_neg_of_mul` and\n`topological_semiring.to_topological_add_group`)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_ring.to_topological_semiring", "description": " A topological ring is a ring `R` where addition, multiplication and negation are continuous.\n\nIf `R` is a (unital) ring, then continuity of negation can be derived from continuity of\nmultiplication as it is multiplication with `-1`. (See\n`topological_semiring.has_continuous_neg_of_mul` and\n`topological_semiring.to_topological_add_group`)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_ring.to_has_continuous_neg", "description": " A topological ring is a ring `R` where addition, multiplication and negation are continuous.\n\nIf `R` is a (unital) ring, then continuity of negation can be derived from continuity of\nmultiplication as it is multiplication with `-1`. (See\n`topological_semiring.has_continuous_neg_of_mul` and\n`topological_semiring.to_topological_add_group`)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_topology.coinduced", "description": "  Given `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` and a topology on `\u03b1`, the coinduced ring topology on `\u03b2` is the finest\ntopology such that `f` is continuous and `\u03b2` is a topological ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_topology.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.has_continuous_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.topological_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.topological_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.has_continuous_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_semiring.has_continuous_neg_of_mul", "description": " If `R` is a ring with a continuous multiplication, then negation is continuous as well since it\nis just multiplication with `-1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_topology.complete_semilattice_Inf", "description": " Ring topologies on `\u03b1` form a complete lattice, with `\u22a5` the discrete topology and `\u22a4` the\nindiscrete topology.\n\nThe infimum of a collection of ring topologies is the topology generated by all their open sets\n(which is a ring topology).\n\nThe supremum of two ring topologies `s` and `t` is the infimum of the family of all ring topologies\ncontained in the intersection of `s` and `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.topological_ring", "description": "The product topology on the cartesian product of two topological rings\n makes the product into a topological ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.topological_closure", "description": " The (topological-space) closure of a subring of a topological ring is\nitself a subring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.topological_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.has_continuous_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.topological_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_right_continuous", "description": "In a topological semiring, the right-multiplication `add_monoid_hom` is continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "discrete_topology.topological_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.le_topological_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.topological_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_topology", "description": " A ring topology on a ring `\u03b1` is a topology for which addition, negation and multiplication\nare continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_topology.to_topological_space", "description": " A ring topology on a ring `\u03b1` is a topology for which addition, negation and multiplication\nare continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_topology.to_topological_ring", "description": " A ring topology on a ring `\u03b1` is a topology for which addition, negation and multiplication\nare continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.topological_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.topological_closure", "description": " The (topological-space) closure of a subsemiring of a topological semiring is\nitself a subsemiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_topology.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.is_closed_topological_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_topology.partial_order", "description": "The ordering on ring topologies on the ring `\u03b1`.\n `t \u2264 s` if every set open in `s` is also open in `t` (`t` is finer than `s`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_ring.to_topological_add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_topology.ext'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.is_closed_topological_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.topological_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_semiring", "description": " a topological semiring is a semiring `R` where addition and multiplication are continuous.\nWe allow for non-unital and non-associative semirings as well.\n\nThe `topological_semiring` class should *only* be instantiated in the presence of a\n`non_unital_non_assoc_semiring` instance; if there is an instance of `non_unital_non_assoc_ring`,\nthen `topological_ring` should be used. Note: in the presence of `non_assoc_ring`, these classes are\nmathematically equivalent (see `topological_semiring.has_continuous_neg_of_mul` or\n`topological_semiring.to_topological_ring`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_semiring.to_has_continuous_add", "description": " a topological semiring is a semiring `R` where addition and multiplication are continuous.\nWe allow for non-unital and non-associative semirings as well.\n\nThe `topological_semiring` class should *only* be instantiated in the presence of a\n`non_unital_non_assoc_semiring` instance; if there is an instance of `non_unital_non_assoc_ring`,\nthen `topological_ring` should be used. Note: in the presence of `non_assoc_ring`, these classes are\nmathematically equivalent (see `topological_semiring.has_continuous_neg_of_mul` or\n`topological_semiring.to_topological_ring`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_semiring.to_has_continuous_mul", "description": " a topological semiring is a semiring `R` where addition and multiplication are continuous.\nWe allow for non-unital and non-associative semirings as well.\n\nThe `topological_semiring` class should *only* be instantiated in the presence of a\n`non_unital_non_assoc_semiring` instance; if there is an instance of `non_unital_non_assoc_ring`,\nthen `topological_ring` should be used. Note: in the presence of `non_assoc_ring`, these classes are\nmathematically equivalent (see `topological_semiring.has_continuous_neg_of_mul` or\n`topological_semiring.to_topological_ring`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_ring.of_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_topology.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "discrete_topology.topological_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_ring.of_add_group_of_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_semiring.to_topological_ring", "description": " If `R` is a ring which is a topological semiring, then it is automatically a topological\nring. This exists so that one can place a topological ring structure on `R` without explicitly\nproving `continuous_neg`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.comm_ring_topological_closure", "description": "If a subring of a topological ring is commutative, then so is its topological closure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_left_continuous", "description": "In a topological semiring, the left-multiplication `add_monoid_hom` is continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_topology.coinduced_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.comm_semiring_topological_closure", "description": " If a subsemiring of a topological semiring is commutative, then so is its\ntopological closure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.topological_semiring", "description": "The product topology on the cartesian product of two topological semirings\n makes the product into a topological semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_topology.to_add_group_topology", "description": "The forgetful functor from ring topologies on `a` to additive group topologies on `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.topological_closure_minimal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemiring.topological_closure_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.le_topological_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.topological_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.has_coe_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.has_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one", "description": "Add an extra element `1` to a type", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.has_coe_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.coe_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.rec_zero_coe", "description": "Recursor for `with_zero` using the preferred forms `0` and `\u2191a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.nat.has_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.inv_one_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.rec_one_coe", "description": "Recursor for `with_one` using the preferred forms `1` and `\u2191a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.has_involutive_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.add_zero_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.one_ne_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.ne_one_iff_exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.unzero_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.coe_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.mul_zero_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.can_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.unzero", "description": "Deconstruct a `x : with_zero \u03b1` to the underlying value in `\u03b1`, given a proof that `x \u2260 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.group_with_zero", "description": "if `G` is a group then `with_zero G` is a group with zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.with_zero.has_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.cases_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.unone_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.int.has_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.coe_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero", "description": "Add an extra element `0` to a type", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.coe_ne_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.div_inv_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.division_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.coe_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.mul_one_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.zero_ne_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.coe_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.inv_one_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.mul_zero_one_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.has_involutive_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.monad", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.comm_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.has_involutive_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.has_inv", "description": "Given an inverse operation on `\u03b1` there is an inverse operation\n on `with_zero \u03b1` sending `0` to `0`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.ne_zero_iff_exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.comm_group_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.division_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.cases_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.div_inv_one_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.neg_zero_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.can_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.semigroup_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.coe_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.inv_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.some_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.coe_zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.unone", "description": "Deconstruct a `x : with_one \u03b1` to the underlying value in `\u03b1`, given a proof that `x \u2260 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.some_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.coe_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.coe_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.monad", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.coe_unzero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.comm_monoid_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.has_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.has_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.add_monoid_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.no_zero_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.monoid_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.coe_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.has_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_one.coe_unone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.mem_iff_eq_smul_ann_ideal_generator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.ann_ideal_generator_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.ann_ideal_generator_aeval_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.ann_ideal", "description": " `ann_ideal R a` is the *annihilating ideal* of all `p : R[X]` such that `p(a) = 0`.\n\nThe informal notation `p(a)` stand for `polynomial.aeval a p`.\nAgain informally, the annihilating ideal of `a` is\n`{ p \u2208 R[X] | p(a) = 0 }`. This is an ideal in `R[X]`.\nThe formal definition uses the kernel of the aeval map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.monic_ann_ideal_generator", "description": "The generator we chose for the annihilating ideal is monic when the ideal is non-zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.mem_ann_ideal_iff_aeval_eq_zero", "description": "It is useful to refer to ideal membership sometimes\nand the annihilation condition other times.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.degree_ann_ideal_generator_le_of_mem", "description": "The generator of the annihilating ideal has minimal degree among\nthe non-zero members of the annihilating ideal", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.span_singleton_ann_ideal_generator", "description": "`ann_ideal_generator \ud835\udd5c a` is indeed a generator.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.mem_iff_ann_ideal_generator_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.ann_ideal_generator_mem", "description": "The annihilating ideal generator is a member of the annihilating ideal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.ann_ideal_generator_eq_minpoly", "description": "The generator of the annihilating ideal is the minimal polynomial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.monic_generator_eq_minpoly", "description": "If a monic generates the annihilating ideal, it must match our choice\nof the annihilating ideal generator.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.ann_ideal_generator", "description": " `ann_ideal_generator \ud835\udd5c a` is the monic generator of `ann_ideal \ud835\udd5c a`\nif one exists, otherwise `0`.\n\nSince `\ud835\udd5c[X]` is a principal ideal domain there is a polynomial `g` such that\n `span \ud835\udd5c {g} = ann_ideal a`. This picks some generator.\n We prefer the monic generator of the ideal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.measure", "description": " The measure associated to a Stieltjes function, giving mass `f b - f a` to the\ninterval `(a, b]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function", "description": "Bundled monotone right-continuous real functions, used to construct Stieltjes measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.to_fun", "description": "Bundled monotone right-continuous real functions, used to construct Stieltjes measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.mono'", "description": "Bundled monotone right-continuous real functions, used to construct Stieltjes measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.right_continuous'", "description": "Bundled monotone right-continuous real functions, used to construct Stieltjes measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.measure_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_seq_antitone_tendsto_at_top_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.tendsto_measure_Iic_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.measure_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.length", "description": " Length of an interval. This is the largest monotone function which correctly measures all\nintervals.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.stieltjes_function_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.outer_trim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.tendsto_measure_Ico_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.measure_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.infi_Ioi_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.outer", "description": "The Stieltjes outer measure associated to a Stieltjes function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.length_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.measure_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.measure_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.measure_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.countable_left_lim_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.tendsto_measure_Ici_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.measure_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.measure_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infi_Ioi_eq_infi_rat_gt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.length_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_lim_eq_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.tendsto_measure_Ioc_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.outer_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "supr_eq_supr_subseq_of_antitone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_lim_eq_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.measure.measure_theory.is_locally_finite_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.stieltjes_function", "description": " If a function `f : \u211d \u2192 \u211d` is monotone, then the function mapping `x` to the right limit of `f`\nat `x` is a Stieltjes function, i.e., it is monotone and right-continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.id_left_lim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.length_subadditive_Icc_Ioo", "description": " If a compact interval `[a, b]` is covered by a union of open interval `(c i, d i)`, then\n`f b - f a \u2264 \u2211 f (d i) - f (c i)`. This is an auxiliary technical statement to prove the same\nstatement for half-open intervals, the point of the current statement being that one can use\ncompactness to reduce it to a finite sum, and argue by induction on the size of the covering set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.outer_le_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_seq_monotone_tendsto_at_top_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.infi_rat_gt_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.borel_le_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.right_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.id", "description": "The identity of `\u211d` as a Stieltjes function, used to construct Lebesgue measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_function.measurable_set_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stieltjes_functi