"description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map.add_comm_group", "description": "The set of affine maps to a vector space is an additive commutative group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map.homothety_affine", "description": "`homothety` as an affine map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map.to_const_prod_linear_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "`to_fun` is the same as the result of coercing to a function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map.id", "description": "Identity map as an affine map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map.const", "description": "Constant function as an `affine_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map.pi_line_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map", "description": " An `affine_map k P1 P2` (notation: `P1 \u2192\u1d43[k] P2`) is a map from `P1` to `P2` that\ninduces a corresponding linear map from `V1` to `V2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map.to_fun", "description": " An `affine_map k P1 P2` (notation: `P1 \u2192\u1d43[k] P2`) is a map from `P1` to `P2` that\ninduces a corresponding linear map from `V1` to `V2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map.linear", "description": " An `affine_map k P1 P2` (notation: `P1 \u2192\u1d43[k] P2`) is a map from `P1` to `P2` that\ninduces a corresponding linear map from `V1` to `V2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map.map_vadd'", "description": " An `affine_map k P1 P2` (notation: `P1 \u2192\u1d43[k] P2`) is a map from `P1` to `P2` that\ninduces a corresponding linear map from `V1` to `V2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map.neg_linear", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map.snd_line_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map.coe_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.const.mk'", "description": " `const.mk'` is `const.mk` but specialized to map `\u03b1` to\n`const \u03b1 punit`, where `punit` is the terminal object in `Type*`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.map_comp_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.supp", "description": " If we consider `x : F \u03b1` to, in some sense, contain values of type `\u03b1`, then\n`supp x` is the set of values of type `\u03b1` that `x` contains.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.has_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.applicative", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.const", "description": " `const \u03b1` is the constant functor, mapping every type to `\u03b1`. When\n`\u03b1` has a monoid structure, `const \u03b1` has an `applicative` instance.\n(If `\u03b1` has an additive monoid structure, see `functor.add_const`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.liftp", "description": " If we consider `x : F \u03b1` to, in some sense, contain values of type `\u03b1`,\npredicate `liftp p x` holds iff every value contained by `x` satisfies `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.const.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.comp_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.const.is_lawful_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.run_pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.map_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.add_const.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.map", "description": "The map operation for the composition `comp F G` of functors `F` and `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.add_const.functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.functor_id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.functor_comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.add_const.is_lawful_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp", "description": "`functor.comp` is a wrapper around `function.comp` for types.\n   It prevents Lean's type class resolution mechanism from trying\n   a `functor (comp F id)` when `functor F` would do.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.const.mk", "description": " `const.mk` is the canonical map `\u03b1 \u2192 const \u03b1 \u03b2` (the identity), and\nit can be used as a pattern to extract this value.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.seq", "description": "The `<*>` operation for the composition of applicative functors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.run", "description": "Extract a term of `F (G \u03b1)` from a term of `comp F G \u03b1`, which is the same type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.add_const.mk", "description": " `add_const.mk` is the canonical map `\u03b1 \u2192 add_const \u03b1 \u03b2`, which is the identity,\nwhere `add_const \u03b1 \u03b2 = const \u03b1 \u03b2`. It can be used as a pattern to extract this value.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "id.mk", "description": " Introduce the `id` functor. Incidentally, this is `pure` for\n`id` as a `monad` and as an `applicative` functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.is_lawful_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.add_const", "description": " `add_const \u03b1` is a synonym for constant functor `const \u03b1`, mapping\nevery type to `\u03b1`. When `\u03b1` has a additive monoid structure,\n`add_const \u03b1` has an `applicative` instance. (If `\u03b1` has a\nmultiplicative monoid structure, see `functor.const`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.run_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.has_pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.const.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.of_mem_supp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.liftr", "description": " If we consider `x : F \u03b1` to, in some sense, contain values of type `\u03b1`, then\n`liftr r x y` relates `x` and `y` iff (1) `x` and `y` have the same shape and\n(2) we can pair values `a` from `x` and `b` from `y` so that `r a b` holds.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.const.functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.const.run", "description": "Extract the element of `\u03b1` from the `const` functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.add_const.run", "description": "Extract the element of `\u03b1` from the constant functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.mk", "description": " Construct a term of `comp F G \u03b1` from a term of `F (G \u03b1)`, which is the same type.\nCan be used as a pattern to extract a term of `F (G \u03b1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.id_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.run_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.const.map", "description": "The map operation of the `const \u03b3` functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.coe_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.add_monoid_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.comm_monoid_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.mk_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.coe_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.coe_add_monoid_hom", "description": "Coercion `{x : \u03b1 // 0 \u2264 x} \u2192 \u03b1` as a `add_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.mk_add_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.linear_ordered_add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.to_nonneg_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.nsmul_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.coe_to_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.conditionally_complete_linear_order_bot", "description": " If `Sup \u2205 \u2264 a` then `{x : \u03b1 // a \u2264 x}` is a `conditionally_complete_linear_order_bot`.\n\nThis instance uses data fields from `subtype.linear_order` to help type-class inference.\nThe `set.Ici` data fields are definitionally equal, but that requires unfolding semireducible\ndefinitions, so type-class inference won't see this.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.monoid_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.coe_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.has_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.semilattice_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.linear_ordered_cancel_add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.nsmul_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.ordered_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.to_nonneg_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.order_bot", "description": " This instance uses data fields from `subtype.partial_order` to help type-class inference.\nThe `set.Ici` data fields are definitionally equal, but that requires unfolding semireducible\ndefinitions, so type-class inference won't see this.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.mk_sub_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.canonically_ordered_comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.distrib_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.linear_ordered_comm_monoid_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.to_nonneg_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.semilattice_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.no_max_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.coe_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.strict_ordered_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.to_nonneg_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.conditionally_complete_linear_order", "description": "If `Sup \u2205 \u2264 a` then `{x : \u03b1 // a \u2264 x}` is a `conditionally_complete_linear_order`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.to_nonneg", "description": "The function `a \u21a6 max a 0` of type `\u03b1 \u2192 {x : \u03b1 // 0 \u2264 x}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.linear_ordered_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.has_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.has_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.ordered_comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.densely_ordered", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.coe_ring_hom", "description": "Coercion `{x : \u03b1 // 0 \u2264 x} \u2192 \u03b1` as a `ring_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.ordered_cancel_add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.mk_mul_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.strict_ordered_comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.mk_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.ordered_add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.mk_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.mk_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.canonically_ordered_add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.has_ordered_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.canonically_linear_ordered_add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.bot_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonneg.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.idem_of_id_sub_idem", "description": " In a preadditive category, when `p : X \u27f6 X` is idempotent,\nthen `\ud835\udfd9 X - p` is also idempotent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.is_idempotent_complete_iff_opposite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.opposite.category_theory.is_idempotent_complete", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.split_imp_of_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.is_idempotent_complete_iff_idempotents_have_kernels", "description": "A preadditive category is pseudoabelian iff all idempotent endomorphisms have a kernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.is_idempotent_complete_of_is_idempotent_complete_opposite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_idempotent_complete", "description": " A category is idempotent complete iff all idempotent endomorphisms `p`\nsplit as a composition `p = e \u226b i` with `i \u226b e = \ud835\udfd9 _`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_idempotent_complete.idempotents_split", "description": " A category is idempotent complete iff all idempotent endomorphisms `p`\nsplit as a composition `p = e \u226b i` with `i \u226b e = \ud835\udfd9 _`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.is_idempotent_complete_of_abelian", "description": "An abelian category is idempotent complete.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.is_idempotent_complete_iff_of_equivalence", "description": "If `C` and `D` are equivalent categories, that `C` is idempotent complete iff `D` is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.split_iff_of_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.equivalence.is_idempotent_complete", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.is_idempotent_complete_iff_has_equalizer_of_id_and_idempotent", "description": " A category is idempotent complete iff for all idempotent endomorphisms,\nthe equalizer of the identity and this idempotent exists.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "widget.mouse_event_kind", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.mouse_event_kind.on_click", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.mouse_event_kind.on_mouse_enter", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.mouse_event_kind.on_mouse_leave", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.save_widget", "description": "Same as `tactic.save_info_thunk` except saves a widget to be displayed by a compatible infoviewer.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.as_element", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.select_item", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.select_item.result", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.select_item.key", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.select_item.view", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.className", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.with_attr", "description": "If the html is not an of_element it will wrap it in a div.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.on_click", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.cn", "description": "Alias for className.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.key", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.effects", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.with_attrs", "description": "If the html is not an of_element it will wrap it in a div.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.trace_widget_at", "description": "Outputs a widget trace position at the given position.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.with_cn", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.effect", "description": " An effect is some change that the widget makes outside of its own state.\nUsually, giving instructions to the editor to perform some task.\n- `insert_text_relative` will insert at a line relative to the position of the widget.\n- `insert_text_absolute` will insert text at the precise position given.\n- `reveal_position` will move the editor to view the given position.\n- `highlight_position` will add a text highlight to the given position.\n- `clear_highlighting` will remove all highlights created with `highlight_position`.\n- `copy_text` will copy the given text to the clipboard.\n- `custom` can be used to pass custom effects to the client without having to recompile Lean.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.effect.insert_text_absolute", "description": " An effect is some change that the widget makes outside of its own state.\nUsually, giving instructions to the editor to perform some task.\n- `insert_text_relative` will insert at a line relative to the position of the widget.\n- `insert_text_absolute` will insert text at the precise position given.\n- `reveal_position` will move the editor to view the given position.\n- `highlight_position` will add a text highlight to the given position.\n- `clear_highlighting` will remove all highlights created with `highlight_position`.\n- `copy_text` will copy the given text to the clipboard.\n- `custom` can be used to pass custom effects to the client without having to recompile Lean.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.effect.insert_text_relative", "description": " An effect is some change that the widget makes outside of its own state.\nUsually, giving instructions to the editor to perform some task.\n- `insert_text_relative` will insert at a line relative to the position of the widget.\n- `insert_text_absolute` will insert text at the precise position given.\n- `reveal_position` will move the editor to view the given position.\n- `highlight_position` will add a text highlight to the given position.\n- `clear_highlighting` will remove all highlights created with `highlight_position`.\n- `copy_text` will copy the given text to the clipboard.\n- `custom` can be used to pass custom effects to the client without having to recompile Lean.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.effect.reveal_position", "description": " An effect is some change that the widget makes outside of its own state.\nUsually, giving instructions to the editor to perform some task.\n- `insert_text_relative` will insert at a line relative to the position of the widget.\n- `insert_text_absolute` will insert text at the precise position given.\n- `reveal_position` will move the editor to view the given position.\n- `highlight_position` will add a text highlight to the given position.\n- `clear_highlighting` will remove all highlights created with `highlight_position`.\n- `copy_text` will copy the given text to the clipboard.\n- `custom` can be used to pass custom effects to the client without having to recompile Lean.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.effect.highlight_position", "description": " An effect is some change that the widget makes outside of its own state.\nUsually, giving instructions to the editor to perform some task.\n- `insert_text_relative` will insert at a line relative to the position of the widget.\n- `insert_text_absolute` will insert text at the precise position given.\n- `reveal_position` will move the editor to view the given position.\n- `highlight_position` will add a text highlight to the given position.\n- `clear_highlighting` will remove all highlights created with `highlight_position`.\n- `copy_text` will copy the given text to the clipboard.\n- `custom` can be used to pass custom effects to the client without having to recompile Lean.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.effect.clear_highlighting", "description": " An effect is some change that the widget makes outside of its own state.\nUsually, giving instructions to the editor to perform some task.\n- `insert_text_relative` will insert at a line relative to the position of the widget.\n- `insert_text_absolute` will insert text at the precise position given.\n- `reveal_position` will move the editor to view the given position.\n- `highlight_position` will add a text highlight to the given position.\n- `clear_highlighting` will remove all highlights created with `highlight_position`.\n- `copy_text` will copy the given text to the clipboard.\n- `custom` can be used to pass custom effects to the client without having to recompile Lean.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.effect.copy_text", "description": " An effect is some change that the widget makes outside of its own state.\nUsually, giving instructions to the editor to perform some task.\n- `insert_text_relative` will insert at a line relative to the position of the widget.\n- `insert_text_absolute` will insert text at the precise position given.\n- `reveal_position` will move the editor to view the given position.\n- `highlight_position` will add a text highlight to the given position.\n- `clear_highlighting` will remove all highlights created with `highlight_position`.\n- `copy_text` will copy the given text to the clipboard.\n- `custom` can be used to pass custom effects to the client without having to recompile Lean.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.effect.custom", "description": " An effect is some change that the widget makes outside of its own state.\nUsually, giving instructions to the editor to perform some task.\n- `insert_text_relative` will insert at a line relative to the position of the widget.\n- `insert_text_absolute` will insert text at the precise position given.\n- `reveal_position` will move the editor to view the given position.\n- `highlight_position` will add a text highlight to the given position.\n- `clear_highlighting` will remove all highlights created with `highlight_position`.\n- `copy_text` will copy the given text to the clipboard.\n- `custom` can be used to pass custom effects to the client without having to recompile Lean.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.select", "description": "Choose from a dropdown selection list.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.on_mouse_enter", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.trace_widget", "description": "Outputs a widget trace position at the current default trace position.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.effect.insert_text", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.textbox", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.on_mouse_leave", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.h", "description": "Alias for `html.element`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.with_key", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.with_style", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.button", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.coe_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.has_zero_zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.sum_partition_boxes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.map_split_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.sum_boxes_congr", "description": " If `f` is a box additive function on subboxes of `I` and `\u03c0\u2081`, `\u03c0\u2082` are two prepartitions of\n`I` that cover the same part of `I`, then `\u2211 J in \u03c0\u2081.boxes, f J = \u2211 J in \u03c0\u2082.boxes, f J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.to_smul", "description": " If `f` is a box-additive map, then so is the map sending `I` to the scalar multiplication\nby `f I` as a continuous linear map from `E` to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.map", "description": " If `g : M \u2192 N` is an additive map and `f` is a box additive map, then `g \u2218 f` is a box additive\nmap.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.upper_sub_lower_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.restrict_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.upper_sub_lower", "description": " Given a box `I\u2080` in `\u211d\u207f\u207a\u00b9`, `f x : box (fin n) \u2192 G` is a family of functions indexed by a real\n`x` and for `x \u2208 [I\u2080.lower i, I\u2080.upper i]`, `f x` is box-additive on subboxes of the `i`-th face of\n`I\u2080`, then `\u03bb J, f (J.upper i) (J.face i) - f (J.lower i) (J.face i)` is box-additive on subboxes of\n`I\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.of_map_split_add", "description": " If `f : box \u03b9 \u2192 M` is box additive on partitions of the form `split I i x`, then it is box\nadditive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.coe_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.restrict", "description": " If `f` is box-additive on subboxes of `I\u2080`, then it is box-additive on subboxes of any\n`I \u2264 I\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map", "description": " A function on `box \u03b9` is called box additive if for every box `J` and a partition `\u03c0` of `J`\nwe have `f J = \u2211 Ji in \u03c0.boxes, f Ji`. A function is called box additive on subboxes of `I : box \u03b9`\nif the same property holds for `J \u2264 I`. We formalize these two notions in the same definition\nusing `I : with_bot (box \u03b9)`: the value `I = \u22a4` corresponds to functions box additive on the whole\nspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.to_fun", "description": " A function on `box \u03b9` is called box additive if for every box `J` and a partition `\u03c0` of `J`\nwe have `f J = \u2211 Ji in \u03c0.boxes, f Ji`. A function is called box additive on subboxes of `I : box \u03b9`\nif the same property holds for `J \u2264 I`. We formalize these two notions in the same definition\nusing `I : with_bot (box \u03b9)`: the value `I = \u22a4` corresponds to functions box additive on the whole\nspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.sum_partition_boxes'", "description": " A function on `box \u03b9` is called box additive if for every box `J` and a partition `\u03c0` of `J`\nwe have `f J = \u2211 Ji in \u03c0.boxes, f Ji`. A function is called box additive on subboxes of `I : box \u03b9`\nif the same property holds for `J \u2264 I`. We formalize these two notions in the same definition\nusing `I : with_bot (box \u03b9)`: the value `I = \u22a4` corresponds to functions box additive on the whole\nspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.to_smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box_additive_map.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "open_embedding_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "open_embedding.of_comp_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map.nhds_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map.to_quotient_map", "description": "A continuous surjective open map is a quotient map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "open_embedding.open_iff_image_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inducing.nhds_set_eq_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.left_inverse.embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inducing.closure_eq_preimage_closure_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map.id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "open_embedding_of_embedding_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closed_embedding.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inducing.continuous_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "embedding.discrete_topology", "description": " The topology induced under an inclusion `f : X \u2192 Y` from the discrete topological space `Y`\nis the discrete topology on `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "embedding_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_map.id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closed_embedding_of_continuous_injective_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_map.is_open_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "embedding", "description": "A function between topological spaces is an embedding if it is injective,\n and for all `s : set \u03b1`, `s` is open iff it is the preimage of an open set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "embedding.to_inducing", "description": "A function between topological spaces is an embedding if it is injective,\n and for all `s : set \u03b1`, `s` is open iff it is the preimage of an open set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "embedding.inj", "description": "A function between topological spaces is an embedding if it is injective,\n and for all `s : set \u03b1`, `s` is open iff it is the preimage of an open set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closed_embedding", "description": "A closed embedding is an embedding with clo