isomorphic, then `F.map_cone c` being a limit implies\n`G.map_cone c` is also a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.of_iso_limit", "description": "Transport evidence that a cone is a limit cone across an isomorphism of cones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.of_nat_iso", "description": "If `F.cocones` is corepresentable, then the cocone corresponding to the identity morphism on\nthe representing object is a colimit cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.comp_cocone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.iso_unique_cone_morphism", "description": "A cone is a limit cone exactly if\nthere is a unique cone morphism from any other cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.of_nat_iso", "description": "If `F.cones` is representable, then the cone corresponding to the identity morphism on\nthe representing object is a limit cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.of_nat_iso.colimit_cocone", "description": " If `F.cocones` is corepresented by `X`, the cocone corresponding to the identity morphism on `X`\nwill be a colimit cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.uniq_cone_morphism", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.of_point_iso", "description": "If the canonical morphism to a cocone point from a colimiting cocone point is an iso, then the\nfirst cocone was colimiting also.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.desc_cocone_morphism", "description": "The universal morphism from a colimit cocone to any other cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.desc_cocone_morphism_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.cocone_points_iso_of_nat_iso", "description": "The cocone points of two colimit cocones for naturally isomorphic functors\nare themselves isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.lift_comp_cone_point_unique_up_to_iso_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.\u03b9_map_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.cocone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.uniq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.hom_iso'", "description": "Another, more explicit, formulation of the universal property of a colimit cocone.\nSee also `hom_iso`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.cocone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_hom_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.cocone_point_unique_up_to_iso_inv_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.of_cocone_equiv", "description": "Given two functors which have equivalent categories of cocones,\nwe can transport a colimiting cocone across the equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.uniq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.unique_up_to_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.comp_cocone_point_unique_up_to_iso_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.unique_up_to_iso", "description": "Limit cones on `F` are unique up to isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.of_nat_iso.cone_of_hom_fac", "description": " If `F.cones` is represented by `X`, the cone corresponding to a morphism `f : Y \u27f6 X` is\nthe limit cone extended by `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.unique_up_to_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.hom_iso", "description": "The universal property of a colimit cocone: a map `X \u27f6 W` is the same as\n a cocone on `F` with vertex `W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.cocone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_hom_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.whisker_equivalence", "description": "If `s : cocone F` is a colimit cocone, so is `s` whiskered by an equivalence `e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.cocone_point_unique_up_to_iso_hom_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.cone_points_iso_of_nat_iso", "description": "The cone points of two limit cones for naturally isomorphic functors\nare themselves isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.unique_up_to_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.lift_comp_cone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.of_nat_iso.hom_of_cone", "description": "If `F.cones` is represented by `X`, each cone `s` gives a morphism `s.X \u27f6 X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.\u03b9_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.of_nat_iso.cone_of_hom_of_cone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.fac_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.mk_cone_morphism_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.cocone_points_iso_of_equivalence_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.hom_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.cone_points_iso_of_equivalence_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.of_nat_iso.cone_of_hom", "description": " If `F.cones` is represented by `X`, each morphism `f : Y \u27f6 X` gives a cone with cone point\n`Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.hom_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.postcompose_hom_equiv", "description": "A cone postcomposed with a natural isomorphism is a limit cone if and only if the original cone is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.whisker_equivalence_equiv", "description": "Given an equivalence of diagrams `e`, `s` is a colimit cocone iff `s.whisker e.functor` is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.hom_is_iso", "description": "Any cone morphism between limit cones is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.of_whisker_equivalence", "description": "If `s : cocone F` whiskered by an equivalence `e` is a colimit cocone, so is `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.nat_iso", "description": "The limit of `F` represents the functor taking `W` to\n the set of cones on `F` with vertex `W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.lift_cone_morphism", "description": "The universal morphism from any other cone to a limit cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.lift_comp_cone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.of_point_iso", "description": "If the canonical morphism from a cone point to a limiting cone point is an iso, then the\nfirst cone was limiting also.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.of_exists_unique", "description": "Noncomputably make a colimit cocone from the existence of unique factorizations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.cone_point_unique_up_to_iso_hom_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.equiv_iso_colimit_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.comp_cocone_point_unique_up_to_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.cocone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.of_nat_iso.cocone_fac", "description": " If `F.cocones` is corepresented by `X`, any cocone is the extension of the colimit cocone by the\ncorresponding morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.unique_up_to_iso", "description": "Colimit cocones on `F` are unique up to isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.equiv_of_nat_iso_of_iso", "description": "Constructing an equivalence `is_colimit c \u2243 is_colimit d` from a natural isomorphism\nbetween the underlying functors, and then an isomorphism between `c` transported along this and `d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.exists_unique", "description": "Restating the definition of a limit cone in terms of the \u2203! operator.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.nat_iso", "description": "The colimit of `F` represents the functor taking `W` to\n the set of cocones on `F` with vertex `W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit", "description": "A cone `t` on `F` is a limit cone if each cone on `F` admits a unique\ncone morphism to `t`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/002E>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.lift", "description": "A cone `t` on `F` is a limit cone if each cone on `F` admits a unique\ncone morphism to `t`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/002E>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.fac'", "description": "A cone `t` on `F` is a limit cone if each cone on `F` admits a unique\ncone morphism to `t`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/002E>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.uniq'", "description": "A cone `t` on `F` is a limit cone if each cone on `F` admits a unique\ncone morphism to `t`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/002E>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.of_iso_limit_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.of_iso_colimit_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.map", "description": " Given a natural transformation `\u03b1 : F \u27f6 G`, we give a morphism from the cocone point\nof a colimit cocone over `F` to the cocone point of any cocone over `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.lift_comp_cone_point_unique_up_to_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.cocone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_inv_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.fac_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.uniq_cocone_morphism", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.of_nat_iso.cocone_of_hom_of_cocone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.of_cone_equiv_apply_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.of_left_adjoint", "description": "Given a left adjoint functor between categories of cocones,\nthe image of a colimit cocone is a colimit cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.cone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_inv_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.of_iso_colimit", "description": "Transport evidence that a cocone is a colimit cocone across an isomorphism of cocones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.lift_comp_cone_point_unique_up_to_iso_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.cone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_hom_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.of_cocone_equiv_symm_apply_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.lift_comp_cone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.cone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_inv_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.iso_unique_cocone_morphism", "description": "A cocone is a colimit cocone exactly if\nthere is a unique cocone morphism from any other cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.comp_cocone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.of_exists_unique", "description": "Noncomputably make a colimit cocone from the existence of unique factorizations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.lift_comp_cone_point_unique_up_to_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.of_right_adjoint", "description": "Given a right adjoint functor between categories of cones,\nthe image of a limit cone is a limit cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.exists_unique", "description": "Restating the definition of a colimit cocone in terms of the \u2203! operator.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.fac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.comp_cocone_point_unique_up_to_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.cone_point_unique_up_to_iso", "description": "Limits of `F` are unique up to isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.comp_cocone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.cone_point_unique_up_to_iso_hom_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.hom_ext", "description": "Two morphisms into a limit are equal if their compositions with\n each cone morphism are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.precompose_inv_equiv", "description": "A cocone precomposed with the inverse of a natural isomorphism is a colimit cocone\nif and only if the original cocone is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.cocone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_inv_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.cone_point_unique_up_to_iso_inv_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.lift_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.cone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.map", "description": " Given a natural transformation `\u03b1 : F \u27f6 G`, we give a morphism from the cone point\nof any cone over `F` to the cone point of a limit cone over `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.of_faithful", "description": "If G : C \u2192 D is a faithful functor which sends t to a limit cone,\n then it suffices to check that the induced maps for the image of t\n can be lifted to maps of C.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.mk_cocone_morphism", "description": "Alternative constructor for `is_colimit`,\nproviding a morphism of cocones rather than a morphism between the cocone points\nand separately the factorisation condition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.of_nat_iso.cocone_of_hom", "description": " If `F.cocones` is corepresented by `X`, each morphism `f : X \u27f6 Y` gives a cocone with cone\npoint `Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.lift_comp_cone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.cocone_point_unique_up_to_iso_inv_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.unique_up_to_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.of_cone_equiv_symm_apply_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.hom_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.equiv_of_nat_iso_of_iso", "description": "Constructing an equivalence `is_limit c \u2243 is_limit d` from a natural isomorphism\nbetween the underlying functors, and then an isomorphism between `c` transported along this and `d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.of_cocone_equiv_apply_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.of_nat_iso.hom_of_cocone_of_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.of_nat_iso.hom_of_cone_of_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.cone_points_iso_of_equivalence_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.fac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.hom_is_iso", "description": "Any cocone morphism between colimit cocones is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.hom_ext", "description": "Two morphisms out of a colimit are equal if their compositions with\n each cocone morphism are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.map_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.mk_cone_morphism", "description": "Alternative constructor for `is_limit`,\nproviding a morphism of cones rather than a morphism between the cone points\nand separately the factorisation condition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.postcompose_inv_equiv", "description": "A cone postcomposed with the inverse of a natural isomorphism is a limit cone if and only if\nthe original cone is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.equiv_iso_limit_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.cone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_hom_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.mk_cocone_morphism_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.map_\u03c0_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.lift_cone_morphism_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.of_cone_equiv", "description": "Given two functors which have equivalent categories of cones, we can transport a limiting cone\nacross the equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.whisker_equivalence", "description": "If `s : cone F` is a limit cone, so is `s` whiskered by an equivalence `e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.desc_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.equiv_iso_limit", "description": "Isomorphism of cones preserves whether or not they are limiting cones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.of_nat_iso.cone_fac", "description": " If `F.cones` is represented by `X`, any cone is the extension of the limit cone by the\ncorresponding morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.cone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.cone_points_iso_of_equivalence", "description": "We can prove two cone points `(s : cone F).X` and `(t.cone G).X` are isomorphic if\n* both cones are limit cones\n* their indexing categories are equivalent via some `e : J \u224c K`,\n* the triangle of functors commutes up to a natural isomorphism: `e.functor \u22d9 G \u2245 F`.\n\nThis is the most general form of uniqueness of cone points,\nallowing relabelling of both the indexing category (up to equivalence)\nand the functor (up to natural isomorphism).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.equiv_iso_colimit", "description": "Isomorphism of cocones preserves whether or not they are colimiting cocones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.cocone_points_iso_of_equivalence_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.cocone_point_unique_up_to_iso", "description": "Colimits of `F` are unique up to isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.equiv_iso_limit_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.map_cocone_equiv", "description": "If `F` and `G` are naturally isomorphic, then `F.map_cone c` being a colimit implies\n`G.map_cone c` is also a colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.comp_cocone_points_iso_of_nat_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.cocone_points_iso_of_equivalence", "description": "We can prove two cocone points `(s : cocone F).X` and `(t.cocone G).X` are isomorphic if\n* both cocones are colimit cocones\n* their indexing categories are equivalent via some `e : J \u224c K`,\n* the triangle of functors commutes up to a natural isomorphism: `e.functor \u22d9 G \u2245 F`.\n\nThis is the most general form of uniqueness of cocone points,\nallowing relabelling of both the indexing category (up to equivalence)\nand the functor (up to natural isomorphism).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit", "description": "A cocone `t` on `F` is a colimit cocone if each cocone on `F` admits a unique\ncocone morphism from `t`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/002F>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.desc", "description": "A cocone `t` on `F` is a colimit cocone if each cocone on `F` admits a unique\ncocone morphism from `t`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/002F>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.fac'", "description": "A cocone `t` on `F` is a colimit cocone if each cocone on `F` admits a unique\ncocone morphism from `t`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/002F>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.uniq'", "description": "A cocone `t` on `F` is a colimit cocone if each cocone on `F` admits a unique\ncocone morphism from `t`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/002F>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.of_nat_iso.cocone_of_hom_fac", "description": " If `F.cocones` is corepresented by `X`, the cocone corresponding to a morphism `f : Y \u27f6 X` is\nthe colimit cocone extended by `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.of_nat_iso.hom_of_cocone", "description": "If `F.cocones` is corepresented by `X`, each cocone `s` gives a morphism `X \u27f6 s.X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.hom_iso", "description": "The universal property of a limit cone: a map `W \u27f6 X` is the same as\n a cone on `F` with vertex `W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.of_whisker_equivalence", "description": "If `s : cone F` whiskered by an equivalence `e` is a limit cone, so is `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.precompose_hom_equiv", "description": "A cocone precomposed with a natural isomorphism is a colimit cocone\nif and only if the original cocone is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.hom_iso'", "description": "Another, more explicit, formulation of the universal property of a limit cone.\nSee also `hom_iso`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.comp_cocone_point_unique_up_to_iso_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.whisker_equivalence_equiv", "description": "Given an equivalence of diagrams `e`, `s` is a limit cone iff `s.whisker e.functor` is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.equiv_iso_colimit_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.of_faithful", "description": "If G : C \u2192 D is a faithful functor which sends t to a colimit cocone,\n then it suffices to check that the induced maps for the image of t\n can be lifted to maps of C.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.hom_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit.cocone_point_unique_up_to_iso_hom_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit.of_nat_iso.limit_cone", "description": " If `F.cones` is represented by `X`, the cone corresponding to the identity morphism on `X`\nwill be a limit cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coe_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ker_prod_ker_le_ker_coprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.graph", "description": "Graph of a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.snd_map_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coprod_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.sup_range_inl_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.fst_eq_coprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.snd_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.tailing", "description": "Give an injective map `f : M \u00d7 N \u2192\u2097[R] M` we can find a sequence of submodules\nall isomorphic to `N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.coe_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.fst", "description": "The first projection of a product is a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ker_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.fst_map_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod", "description": "The prod of two linear maps is a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.le_prod_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_comap_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_map_alg_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.snd_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coe_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coprod_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.prod_prod_prod_comm_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.tunnel'", "description": "Auxiliary definition for `tunnel`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.prod_prod_prod_comm_to_add_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.fst_equiv_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.tailing_linear_equiv", "description": "Each `tailing f i n` is a copy of `N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_map_ring_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.inr_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.map_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.prod", "description": "Product of linear equivalences; the maps come from `equiv.prod_congr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.inl_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.tailings", "description": "The supremum of all the copies of `N` found inside the tunnel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.fst_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.tailings_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.tailings_disjoint_tunnel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ker_coprod_of_disjoint_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.tailing_disjoint_tunnel_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.tunnel_aux_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coprod_map_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coe_prod_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.mem_graph_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.snd_equiv_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_equiv", "description": " Taking the product of two maps with the same domain is equivalent to taking the product of\ntheir codomains.\n\nSee note [bundled maps over different rings] for why separate `R` and `S` semirings are used.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.fst_equiv", "description": "`M` as a submodule of `M \u00d7 N` is isomorphic to `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.fst_sup_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coprod_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_eq_sup_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.fst_inf_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.snd", "description": "`N` as a submodule of `M \u00d7 N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coprod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.pair_fst_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.inl_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.comap_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.fst_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.range_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.range_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_map_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.range_prod_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.tailing_sup_tunnel_succ_le_tunnel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.disjoint_inl_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_eq_inf_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_eq_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.snd_equiv", "description": "`N` as a submodule of `M \u00d7 N` is isomorphic to `N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coprod_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.snd_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_map_alg_hom", "description": "`linear_map.prod_map` as an `algebra_hom`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coprod_comp_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.prod_comm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.snd_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.fst", "description": "`M` as a submodule of `M \u00d7 N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.tailings_disjoint_tailing", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.skew_prod", "description": "Equivalence given by a block lower diagonal matrix. `e\u2081` and `e\u2082` are diagonal square blocks,\n and `f` is a rectangular block below the diagonal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ker_prod_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.snd_map_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_map_comap_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_map", "description": "`prod.map` of two linear maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.tailings_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.span_inl_union_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.comap_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_map_linear", "description": "`linear_map.prod_map` as a `linear_map`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.range_coprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_map_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.inr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.range_prod_eq", "description": " If the union of the kernels `ker f` and `ker g` spans the domain, then the range of\n`prod f g` is equal to the product of `range f` and `range g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.fst_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.inr_map_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.tunnel_aux", "description": " An auxiliary construction for `tunnel`.\nThe composition of `f`, followed by the isomorphism back to `K`,\nfollowed by the inclusion of this submodule back into `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.graph_eq_range_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_eq_top_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.inl_map_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.tunnel", "description": "Give an injective map `f : M \u00d7 N \u2192\u2097[R] M` we can find a nested sequence of submodules\nall isomorphic to `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coe_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.prod_prod_prod_comm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_compl_range_inl_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.range_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.graph_eq_ker_coprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.prod_prod_prod_comm", "description": "Four-way commutativity of `prod`. The name matches `mul_mul_mul_comm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ker_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_map_linear_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.inl", "description": "The left injection into a product is a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_map_ring_hom", "description": "`linear_map.prod_map` as a `ring_hom`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.sup_eq_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.skew_prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.fst_map_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.prod_comm", "description": "Product of modules is commutative up to linear isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_comap_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.inr", "description": "The right injection into a product is a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_ext", "description": "Split equality of linear maps from a product into linear maps over each component, to allow `ext`\nto apply lemmas specific to `M \u2192\u2097 M\u2083` and `M\u2082 \u2192\u2097 M\u2083`.\n\nSee note [partially-applied ext lemmas].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.tailing_le_tunnel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.fst_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.range_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.inl_eq_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.prod_map_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.snd_eq_coprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.ker_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coprod", "description": "The coprod function `\u03bb x : M \u00d7 M\u2082, f x.1 + g x.2` is a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.comp_coprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.skew_prod_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.inr_eq_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coprod_inl_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.map_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.prod_map_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coprod_equiv", "description": " Taking the product of two maps with the same codomain is equivalent to taking the product of\ntheir domains.\n\nSee note [bundled maps over different rings] for why separate `R` and `S` semirings are used.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.ker_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ker_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.prod_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_coprod_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.comap_prod_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.snd", "description": "The second projection of a product is a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.closed", "description": "An object `X` is (right) closed if `(X \u2297 -)` is a left adjoint.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.closed.is_adj", "description": "An object `X` is (right) closed if `(X \u2297 -)` is a left adjoint.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.uncurry_id_eq_ev", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.id_tensor_pre_app_comp_ev", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.uncurry_natural_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.curry_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.curry_natural_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed", "description": "A monoidal category `C` is (right) monoidal closed if every object is (right) closed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.closed'", "description": "A monoidal category `C` is (right) monoidal closed if every object is (right) closed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ihom.coev_naturality_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ihom.ev", "description": "The evaluation natural transformation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.pre", "description": "Pre-compose an internal hom with an external hom.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.curry_id_eq_coev", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ihom.coev_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.unit_closed", "description": "The unit object is always closed.\nThis isn't an instance because most of the time we'll prove closedness for all objects at once,\nrather than just for this one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.eq_curry_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.curry_uncurry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.of_equiv_curry_def", "description": " Suppose we have a monoidal equivalence `F : C \u224c D`, with `D` monoidal closed. We can pull the\nmonoidal closed instance back along the equivalence. For `X, Y, Z : C`, this lemma describes the\nresulting currying map `Hom(X \u2297 Y, Z) \u2192 Hom(Y, (X \u27f6[C] Z))`. (`X \u27f6[C] Z` is defined to be\n`F\u207b\u00b9(F(X) \u27f6[D] F(Z))`, so currying in `C` is given by essentially conjugating currying in\n`D` by `F.`)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.curry_natural_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.internal_hom_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.uncurry_pre", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.curry_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.of_equiv", "description": "Transport the property of being monoidal closed across a monoidal equivalence of categories", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.curry_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ihom", "description": "This is the internal hom `A \u27f6[C] -`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.hom_equiv_apply_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.internal_hom_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.uncurry_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ihom.adjunction", "description": "The adjunction between `A \u2297 -` and `A \u27f9 -`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.uncurry_natural_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.curry", "description": "Currying in a monoidal closed category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.coev_app_comp_pre_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.uncurry_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.id_tensor_pre_app_comp_ev_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.uncurry_natural_left_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.uncurry_curry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.curry_natural_right_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ihom.ev_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.of_equiv_uncurry_def", "description": " Suppose we have a monoidal equivalence `F : C \u224c D`, with `D` monoidal closed. We can pull the\nmonoidal closed instance back along the equivalence. For `X, Y, Z : C`, this lemma describes the\nresulting uncurrying map `Hom(Y, (X \u27f6[C] Z)) \u2192 Hom(X \u2297 Y \u27f6 Z)`. (`X \u27f6[C] Z` is\ndefined to be `F\u207b\u00b9(F(X) \u27f6[D] F(Z))`, so uncurrying in `C` is given by essentially conjugating\nuncurrying in `D` by `F.`)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ihom.ihom_adjunction_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.internal_hom", "description": "The internal hom functor given by the monoidal closed structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.tensor_left.limits.preserves_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ihom.ev_coev", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.tensor_closed", "description": "If `X` and `Y` are closed then `X \u2297 Y` is.\nThis isn't an instance because it's not usually how we want to construct internal homs,\nwe'll usually prove all objects are closed uniformly.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.uncurry_natural_right_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.coev_app_comp_pre_app_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.pre_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ihom.ev_coev_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.curry_natural_left_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ihom.coev_ev_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ihom.ev_naturality_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.pre_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.uncurry", "description": "Uncurrying in a monoidal closed category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ihom.coev", "description": "The coevaluation natural transformation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.pre_comm_ihom_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_closed.hom_equiv_symm_apply_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ihom.coev_ev", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ihom.ihom_adjunction_counit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.map_term_rel_map_term_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.constants_vars_equiv_left_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.relabel_id_eq_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.on_sentence", "description": "Maps a sentence's symbols along a language map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_qf_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.to_prenex_imp", "description": "An auxiliary operation to `first_order.language.bounded_formula.to_prenex`.\n If `\u03c6` and `\u03c8` are in prenex normal form, then `\u03c6.to_prenex_imp \u03c8`\n is a prenex normal form for `\u03c6.imp \u03c8`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.not_all_is_qf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.on_Theory", "description": "Maps a theory's symbols along a language map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.relabel_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.inhabited_of_constant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_prenex.lift_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lequiv.on_bounded_formula_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.formula.equiv_sentence_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_atomic.relabel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_atomic", "description": "An atomic formula is either equality or a relation symbol applied to terms.\n Note that `\u22a5` and `\u22a4` are not considered atomic in this convention.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_atomic.equal", "description": "An atomic formula is either equality or a relation symbol applied to terms.\n Note that `\u22a5` and `\u22a4` are not considered atomic in this convention.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_atomic.rel", "description": "An atomic formula is either equality or a relation symbol applied to terms.\n Note that `\u22a5` and `\u22a4` are not considered atomic in this convention.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_atomic.is_prenex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.relabel_falsum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.subst", "description": "Substitutes the variables in a given formula with terms.