an combinations of atomic formulas.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_qf.falsum", "description": " A quantifier-free formula is a formula defined without quantifiers. These are all equivalent\nto boolean combinations of atomic formulas.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_qf.of_is_atomic", "description": " A quantifier-free formula is a formula defined without quantifiers. These are all equivalent\nto boolean combinations of atomic formulas.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_qf.imp", "description": " A quantifier-free formula is a formula defined without quantifiers. These are all equivalent\nto boolean combinations of atomic formulas.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lequiv.on_bounded_formula_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_atomic.lift_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lequiv.on_formula_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.relabel_relabel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.not", "description": "The negation of a bounded formula is also a bounded formula.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.formula.relabel", "description": "Relabels a formula's variables along a particular function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.relabel_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.sum_elim_comp_relabel_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lequiv.on_sentence_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.relabel_imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.relabel_aux", "description": "A function to help relabel the variables in bounded formulas.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.cast_le_cast_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_qf.lift_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_atomic.cast_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.bd_equal", "description": "The equality of two terms as a bounded formula.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.map_term_rel_equiv", "description": " An equivalence of bounded formulas given by an equivalence of terms and an equivalence of\nrelations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_qf.to_prenex_imp_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.relations.total", "description": "The sentence indicating that a basic relation symbol is total.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_prenex_to_prenex_imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.to_prenex", "description": "For any bounded formula `\u03c6`, `\u03c6.to_prenex` is a semantically-equivalent formula in prenex normal\n form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.on_bounded_formula", "description": "Maps a bounded formula's symbols along a language map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.constants_vars_equiv", "description": "A bijection between terms with constants and terms with extra variables.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.relations.formula\u2082", "description": "Applies a binary relation to two terms as a formula.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.sentence", "description": "A sentence is a formula with no free variables.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.comp_on_bounded_formula", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.formula.not", "description": "The negation of a formula.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_prenex.relabel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lequiv.on_sentence", "description": "Maps a sentence's symbols along a language equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.monotone_distinct_constants_theory", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.not_ex_is_atomic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.relations.bounded_formula\u2081", "description": "Applies a unary relation to a term as a bounded formula.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_prenex", "description": "Indicates that a bounded formula is in prenex normal form - that is, it consists of quantifiers\n applied to a quantifier-free formula.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_prenex.of_is_qf", "description": "Indicates that a bounded formula is in prenex normal form - that is, it consists of quantifiers\n applied to a quantifier-free formula.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_prenex.all", "description": "Indicates that a bounded formula is in prenex normal form - that is, it consists of quantifiers\n applied to a quantifier-free formula.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_prenex.ex", "description": "Indicates that a bounded formula is in prenex normal form - that is, it consists of quantifiers\n applied to a quantifier-free formula.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lequiv.on_term", "description": "Maps a term's symbols along a language equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.not_ex_is_qf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.relations.reflexive", "description": "The sentence indicating that a basic relation symbol is reflexive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.exs", "description": "Places existential quantifiers on all extra variables of a bounded formula.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.to_formula", "description": "Turns the extra variables of a bounded formula into free variables.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.functions.apply\u2082", "description": "Applies a binary function to two terms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.directed_distinct_constants_theory", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lequiv.on_bounded_formula", "description": "Maps a bounded formula's symbols along a language equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.relabel_equiv", "description": "Relabels a term's variables along a bijection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.constants_vars_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.var_finset", "description": "The `finset` of variables used in a given term.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.restrict_var", "description": "Restricts a term to use only a set of the given variables.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.relations.bounded_formula\u2082", "description": "Applies a binary relation to two terms as a bounded formula.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.has_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.relations.symmetric", "description": "The sentence indicating that a basic relation symbol is symmetric.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.relations.formula", "description": "Applies a relation to terms as a bounded formula.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lequiv.on_formula", "description": "Maps a formula's symbols along a language equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.relabel_comp_relabel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.relations.bounded_formula", "description": "Applies a relation to terms as a bounded formula.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.iff", "description": "The biimplication between two bounded formulas.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.inhabited_of_var", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.is_qf.relabel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.on_term", "description": "Maps a term's symbols along a language map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.id_on_term", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Theory", "description": "A theory is a set of sentences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.constants_vars_equiv", "description": "A bijection sending formulas with constants to formulas with extra variables.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.restrict_var_left", "description": "Restricts a term to use only a set of the given variables on the left side of a sum.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.id_on_bounded_formula", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.not_all_is_atomic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.functions.apply\u2081", "description": "Applies a unary function to a term.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.lift_at", "description": "Raises all of the `fin`-indexed variables of a term greater than or equal to `m` by `n'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.map_term_rel", "description": "Maps bounded formulas along a map of terms and a map of relations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.formula.is_atomic_graph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.to_prenex_is_prenex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.re