`.\nThe default for `div` is such that `a / b = a * b\u207b\u00b9` holds by definition.\n\nAdding `div` as a field rather than defining `a / b := a * b\u207b\u00b9` allows us to\navoid certain classes of unification failures, for example:\nLet `foo X` be a type with a `\u2200 X, has_div (foo X)` instance but no\n`\u2200 X, has_inv (foo X)`, e.g. when `foo X` is a `euclidean_domain`. Suppose we\nalso have an instance `\u2200 X [cromulent X], group_with_zero (foo X)`. Then the\n`(/)` coming from `group_with_zero_has_div` cannot be definitionally equal to\nthe `(/)` coming from `foo.has_div`.\n\nIn the same way, adding a `zpow` field makes it possible to avoid definitional failures\nin diamonds. See the definition of `monoid` and Note [forgetful inheritance] for more\nexplanations on this.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "div_inv_monoid.zpow_neg'", "description": " A `div_inv_monoid` is a `monoid` with operations `/` and `\u207b\u00b9` satisfying\n`div_eq_mul_inv : \u2200 a b, a / b = a * b\u207b\u00b9`.\n\nThis deduplicates the name `div_eq_mul_inv`.\nThe default for `div` is such that `a / b = a * b\u207b\u00b9` holds by definition.\n\nAdding `div` as a field rather than defining `a / b := a * b\u207b\u00b9` allows us to\navoid certain classes of unification failures, for example:\nLet `foo X` be a type with a `\u2200 X, has_div (foo X)` instance but no\n`\u2200 X, has_inv (foo X)`, e.g. when `foo X` is a `euclidean_domain`. Suppose we\nalso have an instance `\u2200 X [cromulent X], group_with_zero (foo X)`. Then the\n`(/)` coming from `group_with_zero_has_div` cannot be definitionally equal to\nthe `(/)` coming from `foo.has_div`.\n\nIn the same way, adding a `zpow` field makes it possible to avoid definitional failures\nin diamonds. See the definition of `monoid` and Note [forgetful inheritance] for more\nexplanations on this.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.to_add_zero_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.to_sub_neg_add_monoid_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_right_cancel_semigroup", "description": " An `add_right_cancel_semigroup` is an additive semigroup such that\n`a + b = c + b` implies `a = c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_right_cancel_semigroup.add", "description": " An `add_right_cancel_semigroup` is an additive semigroup such that\n`a + b = c + b` implies `a = c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_right_cancel_semigroup.add_assoc", "description": " An `add_right_cancel_semigroup` is an additive semigroup such that\n`a + b = c + b` implies `a = c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_right_cancel_semigroup.add_right_cancel", "description": " An `add_right_cancel_semigroup` is an additive semigroup such that\n`a + b = c + b` implies `a = c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_neg_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_inv_cancel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_right_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_cancel_monoid", "description": "A monoid in which multiplication is right-cancellative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_cancel_monoid.mul", "description": "A monoid in which multiplication is right-cancellative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_cancel_monoid.mul_assoc", "description": "A monoid in which multiplication is right-cancellative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_cancel_monoid.mul_right_cancel", "description": "A monoid in which multiplication is right-cancellative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_cancel_monoid.one", "description": "A monoid in which multiplication is right-cancellative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_cancel_monoid.one_mul", "description": "A monoid in which multiplication is right-cancellative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_cancel_monoid.mul_one", "description": "A monoid in which multiplication is right-cancellative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_cancel_monoid.npow", "description": "A monoid in which multiplication is right-cancellative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_cancel_monoid.npow_zero'", "description": "A monoid in which multiplication is right-cancellative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_cancel_monoid.npow_succ'", "description": "A monoid in which multiplication is right-cancellative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_left_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_comm_monoid.to_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group", "description": " An `add_group` is an `add_monoid` with a unary `-` satisfying `-a + a = 0`.\n\nThere is also a binary operation `-` such that `a - b = a + -b`,\nwith a default so that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.add", "description": " An `add_group` is an `add_monoid` with a unary `-` satisfying `-a + a = 0`.\n\nThere is also a binary operation `-` such that `a - b = a + -b`,\nwith a default so that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.add_assoc", "description": " An `add_group` is an `add_monoid` with a unary `-` satisfying `-a + a = 0`.\n\nThere is also a binary operation `-` such that `a - b = a + -b`,\nwith a default so that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.zero", "description": " An `add_group` is an `add_monoid` with a unary `-` satisfying `-a + a = 0`.\n\nThere is also a binary operation `-` such that `a - b = a + -b`,\nwith a default so that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.zero_add", "description": " An `add_group` is an `add_monoid` with a unary `-` satisfying `-a + a = 0`.\n\nThere is also a binary operation `-` such that `a - b = a + -b`,\nwith a default so that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.add_zero", "description": " An `add_group` is an `add_monoid` with a unary `-` satisfying `-a + a = 0`.\n\nThere is also a binary operation `-` such that `a - b = a + -b`,\nwith a default so that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.nsmul", "description": " An `add_group` is an `add_monoid` with a unary `-` satisfying `-a + a = 0`.\n\nThere is also a binary operation `-` such that `a - b = a + -b`,\nwith a default so that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.nsmul_zero'", "description": " An `add_group` is an `add_monoid` with a unary `-` satisfying `-a + a = 0`.\n\nThere is also a binary operation `-` such that `a - b = a + -b`,\nwith a default so that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.nsmul_succ'", "description": " An `add_group` is an `add_monoid` with a unary `-` satisfying `-a + a = 0`.\n\nThere is also a binary operation `-` such that `a - b = a + -b`,\nwith a default so that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.neg", "description": " An `add_group` is an `add_monoid` with a unary `-` satisfying `-a + a = 0`.\n\nThere is also a binary operation `-` such that `a - b = a + -b`,\nwith a default so that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.sub", "description": " An `add_group` is an `add_monoid` with a unary `-` satisfying `-a + a = 0`.\n\nThere is also a binary operation `-` such that `a - b = a + -b`,\nwith a default so that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.sub_eq_add_neg", "description": " An `add_group` is an `add_monoid` with a unary `-` satisfying `-a + a = 0`.\n\nThere is also a binary operation `-` such that `a - b = a + -b`,\nwith a default so that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.zsmul", "description": " An `add_group` is an `add_monoid` with a unary `-` satisfying `-a + a = 0`.\n\nThere is also a binary operation `-` such that `a - b = a + -b`,\nwith a default so that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.zsmul_zero'", "description": " An `add_group` is an `add_monoid` with a unary `-` satisfying `-a + a = 0`.\n\nThere is also a binary operation `-` such that `a - b = a + -b`,\nwith a default so that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.zsmul_succ'", "description": " An `add_group` is an `add_monoid` with a unary `-` satisfying `-a + a = 0`.\n\nThere is also a binary operation `-` such that `a - b = a + -b`,\nwith a default so that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.zsmul_neg'", "description": " An `add_group` is an `add_monoid` with a unary `-` satisfying `-a + a = 0`.\n\nThere is also a binary operation `-` such that `a - b = a + -b`,\nwith a default so that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.add_left_neg", "description": " An `add_group` is an `add_monoid` with a unary `-` satisfying `-a + a = 0`.\n\nThere is also a binary operation `-` such that `a - b = a + -b`,\nwith a default so that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_semigroup.is_right_cancel_add.to_is_cancel_add", "description": "Any `add_comm_semigroup G`\nthat satisfies `is_right_cancel_add G` also satisfies `is_cancel_add G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_right_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sub_neg_zero_monoid.to_sub_neg_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.to_add_group_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_one_class", "description": " Typeclass for expressing that a type `M` with multiplication and a one satisfies\n`1 * a = a` and `a * 1 = a` for all `a : M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_one_class.one", "description": " Typeclass for expressing that a type `M` with multiplication and a one satisfies\n`1 * a = a` and `a * 1 = a` for all `a : M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_one_class.mul", "description": " Typeclass for expressing that a type `M` with multiplication and a one satisfies\n`1 * a = a` and `a * 1 = a` for all `a : M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_one_class.one_mul", "description": " Typeclass for expressing that a type `M` with multiplication and a one satisfies\n`1 * a = a` and `a * 1 = a` for all `a : M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_one_class.mul_one", "description": " Typeclass for expressing that a type `M` with multiplication and a one satisfies\n`1 * a = a` and `a * 1 = a` for all `a : M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_inv_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_right_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_semigroup.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_comm_monoid.to_cancel_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_monoid", "description": "A commutative monoid is a monoid with commutative `(*)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_monoid.mul", "description": "A commutative monoid is a monoid with commutative `(*)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_monoid.mul_assoc", "description": "A commutative monoid is a monoid with commutative `(*)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_monoid.one", "description": "A commutative monoid is a monoid with commutative `(*)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_monoid.one_mul", "description": "A commutative monoid is a monoid with commutative `(*)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_monoid.mul_one", "description": "A commutative monoid is a monoid with commutative `(*)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_monoid.npow", "description": "A commutative monoid is a monoid with commutative `(*)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_monoid.npow_zero'", "description": "A commutative monoid is a monoid with commutative `(*)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_monoid.npow_succ'", "description": "A commutative monoid is a monoid with commutative `(*)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_monoid.mul_comm", "description": "A commutative monoid is a monoid with com