rations\nsatisfying `sub_eq_add_neg : \u2200 a b, a - b = a + -b`.\n\nThe default for `sub` is such that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.\n\nAdding `sub` as a field rather than defining `a - b := a + -b` allows us to\navoid certain classes of unification failures, for example:\nLet `foo X` be a type with a `\u2200 X, has_sub (foo X)` instance but no\n`\u2200 X, has_neg (foo X)`. Suppose we also have an instance\n`\u2200 X [cromulent X], add_group (foo X)`. Then the `(-)` coming from\n`add_group.has_sub` cannot be definitionally equal to the `(-)` coming from\n`foo.has_sub`.\n\nIn the same way, adding a `zsmul` field makes it possible to avoid definitional failures\nin diamonds. See the definition of `add_monoid` and Note [forgetful inheritance] for more\nexplanations on this.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_monoid.to_right_cancel_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_one_class.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "succ_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_left_cancel_semigroup.to_is_left_cancel_add", "description": "Any `add_left_cancel_semigroup` satisfies `is_left_cancel_add`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "div_inv_one_monoid.to_div_inv_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_cancel_monoid.to_add_right_cancel_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cancel_add", "description": "A mixin for cancellative addition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cancel_add.add_left_cancel", "description": "A mixin for cancellative addition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cancel_add.add_right_cancel", "description": "A mixin for cancellative addition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_semigroup.is_right_cancel_add.to_is_left_cancel_add", "description": "Any\n`add_comm_semigroup G` that satisfies `is_right_cancel_add G` also satisfies\n`is_right_cancel_add G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_left_cancel_semigroup.to_add_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cancel_add.to_is_right_cancel_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group.to_cancel_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_one_class.to_has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid.add", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid.add_assoc", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid.zero", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid.zero_add", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid.add_zero", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid.nsmul", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid.nsmul_zero'", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid.nsmul_succ'", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid.neg", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid.sub", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid.sub_eq_add_neg", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid.zsmul", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid.zsmul_zero'", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid.zsmul_succ'", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid.zsmul_neg'", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid.neg_neg", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid.neg_add_rev", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid.neg_eq_of_add", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtraction_comm_monoid.add_comm", "description": "Commutative `subtraction_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_semigroup.is_left_cancel_mul.to_is_cancel_mul", "description": " Any `comm_semigroup G` that satisfies `is_left_cancel_mul G` also satisfies\n`is_cancel_mul G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.to_add_monoid", "description": "Abbreviation for `@sub_neg_monoid.to_add_monoid _ (@add_group.to_sub_neg_monoid _ _)`.\n\nUseful because it corresponds to the fact that `AddGroup` is a subcategory of `AddMon`.\nNot an instance since it duplicates\n`@sub_neg_monoid.to_add_monoid _ (@add_group.to_sub_neg_monoid _ _)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_cancel_semigroup.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group.to_monoid", "description": " Abbreviation for `@div_inv_monoid.to_monoid _ (@group.to_div_inv_monoid _ _)`.\n\nUseful because it corresponds to the fact that `Grp` is a subcategory of `Mon`.\nNot an instance since it duplicates `@div_inv_monoid.to_monoid _ (@group.to_div_inv_monoid _ _)`.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_cancel_comm_monoid.to_add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_monoid", "description": " A `division_monoid` is a `div_inv_monoid` with involutive inversion and such that\n`(a * b)\u207b\u00b9 = b\u207b\u00b9 * a\u207b\u00b9` and `a * b = 1 \u2192 a\u207b\u00b9 = b`.\n\nThis is the immediate common ancestor of `group` and `group_with_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_monoid.mul", "description": " A `division_monoid` is a `div_inv_monoid` with involutive inversion and such that\n`(a * b)\u207b\u00b9 = b\u207b\u00b9 * a\u207b\u00b9` and `a * b = 1 \u2192 a\u207b\u00b9 = b`.\n\nThis is the immediate common ancestor of `group` and `group_with_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_monoid.mul_assoc", "description": " A `division_monoid` is a `div_inv_monoid` with involutive inversion and such that\n`(a * b)\u207b\u00b9 = b\u207b\u00b9 * a\u207b\u00b9` and `a * b = 1 \u2192 a\u207b\u00b9 = b`.\n\nThis is the immediate common ancestor of `group` and `group_with_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_monoid.one", "description": " A `division_monoid` is a `div_inv_monoid` with involutive inversion and such that\n`(a * b)\u207b\u00b9 = b\u207b\u00b9 * a\u207b\u00b9` and `a * b = 1 \u2192 a\u207b\u00b9 = b`.\n\nThis is the immediate common ancestor of `group` and `group_with_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_monoid.one_mul", "description": " A `division_monoid` is a `div_inv_monoid` with involutive inversion and such that\n`(a * b)\u207b\u00b9 = b\u207b\u00b9 * a\u207b\u00b9` and `a * b = 1 \u2192 a\u207b\u00b9 = b`.\n\nThis is the immediate common ancestor of `group` and `group_with_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_monoid.mul_one", "description": " A `division_monoid` is a `div_inv_monoid` with involutive inversion and such that\n`(a * b)\u207b\u00b9 = b\u207b\u00b9 * a\u207b\u00b9` and `a * b = 1 \u2192 a\u207b\u00b9 = b`.\n\nThis is the immediate common ancestor of `group` and `group_with_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_monoid.npow", "description": " A `division_monoid` is a `div_inv_monoid` with involutive inversion and such that\n`(a * b)\u207b\u00b9 = b\u207b\u00b9 * a\u207b\u00b9` and `a * b = 1 \u2192 a\u207b\u00b9 = b`.\n\nThis is the immediate common ancestor of `group` and `group_with_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_monoid.npow_zero'", "description": " A `division_monoid` is a `div_inv_monoid` with involutive inversion and such that\n`(a * b)\u207b\u00b9 = b\u207b\u00b9 * a\u207b\u00b9` and `a * b = 1 \u2192 a\u207b\u00b9 = b`.\n\nThis is the immediate common ancestor of `group` and `group_with_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_monoid.npow_succ'", "description": " A `division_monoid` is a `div_inv_monoid` with involutive inversion and such that\n`(a * b)\u207b\u00b9 = b\u207b\u00b9 * a\u207b\u00b9` and `a * b = 1 \u2192 a\u207b\u00b9 = b`.\n\nThis is the immediate common ancestor of `group` and `group_with_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_monoid.inv", "description": " A `division_monoid` is a `div_inv_monoid` with involutive inversion and such that\n`(a * b)\u207b\u00b9 = b\u207b\u00b9 * a\u207b\u00b9` and `a * b = 1 \u2192 a\u207b\u00b9 = b`.\n\nThis is the immediate common ancestor of `group` and `group_with_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_monoid.div", "description": " A `division_monoid` is a `div_inv_monoid` with involutive inversion and such that\n`(a * b)\u207b\u00b9 = b\u207b\u00b9 * a\u207b\u00b9` and `a * b = 1 \u2192 a\u207b\u00b9 = b`.\n\nThis is the immediate common ancestor of `group` and `group_with_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_monoid.div_eq_mul_inv", "description": " A `division_monoid` is a `div_inv_monoid` with involutive inversion and such that\n`(a * b)\u207b\u00b9 = b\u207b\u00b9 * a\u207b\u00b9` and `a * b = 1 \u2192 a\u207b\u00b9 = b`.\n\nThis is the immediate common ancestor of `group` and `group_with_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_monoid.zpow", "description": " A `division_monoid` is a `div_inv_monoid` with involutive inversion and such that\n`(a * b)\u207b\u00b9 = b\u207b\u00b9 * a\u207b\u00b9` and `a * b = 1 \u2192 a\u207b\u00b9 = b`.\n\nThis is the immediate common ancestor of `group` and `group_with_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_monoid.zpow_zero'", "description": " A `division_monoid` is a `div_inv_monoid` with involutive inversion and such that\n`(a * b)\u207b\u00b9 = b\u207b\u00b9 * a\u207b\u00b9` and `a * b = 1 \u