h has better definitional behavior.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_semigroup", "description": "A commutative semigroup is a type with an associative commutative `(*)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_semigroup.mul", "description": "A commutative semigroup is a type with an associative commutative `(*)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_semigroup.mul_assoc", "description": "A commutative semigroup is a type with an associative commutative `(*)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_semigroup.mul_comm", "description": "A commutative semigroup is a type with an associative commutative `(*)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_right_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_ne_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_cancel_monoid", "description": " An additive monoid in which addition is cancellative on both sides.\nMain examples are `\u2115` and groups. This is the right typeclass for many sum lemmas, as having a zero\nis useful to define the sum over the empty set, so `add_right_cancel_semigroup` is not enough.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_cancel_monoid.add", "description": " An additive monoid in which addition is cancellative on both sides.\nMain examples are `\u2115` and groups. This is the right typeclass for many sum lemmas, as having a zero\nis useful to define the sum over the empty set, so `add_right_cancel_semigroup` is not enough.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_cancel_monoid.add_assoc", "description": " An additive monoid in which addition is cancellative on both sides.\nMain examples are `\u2115` and groups. This is the right typeclass for many sum lemmas, as having a zero\nis useful to define the sum over the empty set, so `add_right_cancel_semigroup` is not enough.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_cancel_monoid.add_left_cancel", "description": " An additive monoid in which addition is cancellative on both sides.\nMain examples are `\u2115` and groups. This is the right typeclass for many sum lemmas, as having a zero\nis useful to define the sum over the empty set, so `add_right_cancel_semigroup` is not enough.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_cancel_monoid.zero", "description": " An additive monoid in which addition is cancellative on both sides.\nMain examples are `\u2115` and groups. This is the right typeclass for many sum lemmas, as having a zero\nis useful to define the sum over the empty set, so `add_right_cancel_semigroup` is not enough.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_cancel_monoid.zero_add", "description": " An additive monoid in which addition is cancellative on both sides.\nMain examples are `\u2115` and groups. This is the right typeclass for many sum lemmas, as having a zero\nis useful to define the sum over the empty set, so `add_right_cancel_semigroup` is not enough.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_cancel_monoid.add_zero", "description": " An additive monoid in which addition is cancellative on both sides.\nMain examples are `\u2115` and groups. This is the right typeclass for many sum lemmas, as having a zero\nis useful to define the sum over the empty set, so `add_right_cancel_semigroup` is not enough.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_cancel_monoid.nsmul", "description": " An additive monoid in which addition is cancellative on both sides.\nMain examples are `\u2115` and groups. This is the right typeclass for many sum lemmas, as having a zero\nis useful to define the sum over the empty set, so `add_right_cancel_semigroup` is not enough.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_cancel_monoid.nsmul_zero'", "description": " An additive monoid in which addition is cancellative on both sides.\nMain examples are `\u2115` and groups. This is the right typeclass for many sum lemmas, as having a zero\nis useful to define the sum over the empty set, so `add_right_cancel_semigroup` is not enough.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_cancel_monoid.nsmul_succ'", "description": " An additive monoid in which addition is cancellative on both sides.\nMain examples are `\u2115` and groups. This is the right typeclass for many sum lemmas, as having a zero\nis useful to define the sum over the empty set, so `add_right_cancel_semigroup` is not enough.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_cancel_monoid.add_right_cancel", "description": " An additive monoid in which addition is cancellative on both sides.\nMain examples are `\u2115` and groups. This is the right typeclass for many sum lemmas, as having a zero\nis useful to define the sum over the empty set, so `add_right_cancel_semigroup` is not enough.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nsmul_rec", "description": " The fundamental scalar multiplication in an additive monoid. `nsmul_rec n a = a+a+...+a` n\ntimes. Use instead `n \u2022 a`, which has better definitional behavior.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_monoid.to_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_one_class.to_has_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_involutive_inv.to_has_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_semigroup", "description": "A commutative additive semigroup is a type with an associative commutative `(+)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_semigroup.add", "description": "A commutative additive semigroup is a type with an associative commutative `(+)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_semigroup.add_assoc", "description": "A commutative additive semigroup is a type with an associative commutative `(+)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_semigroup.add_comm", "description": "A commutative additive semigroup is a type with an associative commutative `(+)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_one_class.to_has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "div_eq_mul_inv", "description": " Dividing by an element is the same as multiplying by its inverse.\n\nThis is a duplicate of `div_inv_monoid.div_eq_mul_inv` ensuring that the types unfold better.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_vsub", "description": "Type class for the `-\u1d65` notation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name"