`set.fintype_insert` instance requires decidable equality, but when `a \u2208 s`\nis decidable for this particular `a` we can still get a `fintype` instance by using\n`set.fintype_insert_of_not_mem` or `set.fintype_insert_of_mem`.\n\nThis instance pre-dates `set.fintype_insert`, and it is less efficient.\nWhen `decidable_mem_of_fintype` is made a local instance, then this instance would\noverride `set.fintype_insert` if not for the fact that its priority has been\nadjusted. See Note [lower instance priority].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite.mem_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite.card_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite.bUnion'", "description": "Dependent version of `finite.bUnion`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.exists_lower_bound_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.card_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite.coe_sort_to_finset", "description": "Note that this is an equality of types not holding definitionally. Use wisely.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.set.finite_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.infinite_of_not_bdd_below", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finite", "description": "Constructor for `set.finite` using a `finite` instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.set.finite_image2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.set.finite_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.fintype_pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.exists_min_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite.inter_of_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite.bdd_above_bUnion", "description": "A finite union of sets which are all bounded above is still bounded above.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite_range_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.nat.fintype_Iio", "description": " This is not an instance 