rs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.oangle_left_eq_arcsin_of_oangle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": "An angle in a right-angled triangle expressed using `arcsin`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.tan_oangle_sub_right_of_oangle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": " The tangent of an angle in a right-angled triangle as a ratio of sides, version subtracting\nvectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.dist_div_sin_oangle_left_of_oangle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": " A side of a right-angled triangle divided by the sine of the opposite angle equals the\nhypotenuse.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.tan_oangle_add_left_mul_norm_of_oangle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": " The tangent of an angle in a right-angled triangle multiplied by the adjacent side equals\nthe opposite side.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_add_left_eq_arcsin_of_oangle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": "An angle in a right-angled triangle expressed using `arcsin`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.cos_oangle_add_left_mul_norm_of_oangle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": " The cosine of an angle in a right-angled triangle multiplied by the hypotenuse equals the\nadjacent side.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.tan_oangle_left_mul_dist_of_oangle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": " The tangent of an angle in a right-angled triangle multiplied by the adjacent side equals\nthe opposite side.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.norm_div_sin_oangle_sub_right_of_oangle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": " A side of a right-angled triangle divided by the sine of the opposite angle equals the\nhypotenuse, version subtracting vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.tan_oangle_right_mul_dist_of_oangle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": " The tangent of an angle in a right-angled triangle multiplied by the adjacent side equals\nthe opposite side.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.tan_oangle_add_right_mul_norm_of_oangle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": " The tangent of an angle in a right-angled triangle multiplied by the adjacent side equals\nthe opposite side.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_add_left_eq_arctan_of_oangle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": "An angle in a right-angled triangle expressed using `arctan`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.tan_oangle_right_of_oangle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": "The tangent of an angle in a right-angled triangle as a ratio of sides.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp_lequiv_direct_sum_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp_lequiv_direct_sum", "description": " The finitely supported functions `\u03b9 \u2192\u2080 M` are in linear equivalence with the direct sum of\ncopies of M indexed by \u03b9.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp_lequiv_direct_sum_symm_lof", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.smul_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.module", "description": "When `M` is a module over a ring `S`, and `S` is an algebra over `R`, then `M` inherits a\nmodule structure over `R`.\n\nThe preferred way of setting this up is `[module R M] [module S M] [is_scalar_tower R S M]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.lsmul", "description": "The `R`-algebra homomorphism from the original coefficient algebra `S` to endomorphisms\nof `restrict_scalars R S M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.op_module", "description": "When `M` is a right-module over a ring `S`, and `S` is an algebra over `R`, then `M` inherits a\nright-module structure over `R`.\nThe preferred way of setting this up is\n`[module R\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 M] [module S\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 M] [is_scalar_tower R\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 S\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 M]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.ring_equiv", "description": "Tautological ring isomorphism `restrict_scalars R S A \u2243+* A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.add_equiv_symm_map_smul_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.is_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.add_equiv_symm_map_algebra_map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.is_scalar_tower", "description": "This instance is only relevant when `restrict_scalars.module_orig` is available as an instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.ring_equiv_map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.algebra", "description": "`R \u27f6 S` induces `S-Alg \u2964 R-Alg`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.module_orig", "description": "We temporarily install an action of the original ring on `restrict_sclars R S M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.ring_equiv_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.add_equiv", "description": "`restrict_scalars.add_equiv` is the additive equivalence with the original module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.lsmul_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars", "description": " If we put an `R`-algebra structure on a semiring `S`, we get a natural equivalence from the\ncategory of `S`-modules to the category of representations of the algebra `S` (over `R`). The type\nsynonym `restrict_scalars` is essentially this equivalence.\n\nWarning: use this type synonym judiciously! Consider an example where we want to construct an\n`R`-linear map from `M` to `S`, given:\n```lean\nvariables (R S M : Type*)\nvariables [comm_semiring R] [semiring S] [algebra R S] [add_comm_monoid M] [module S M]\n```\nWith the assumptions above we can't directly state our map as we have no `module R M` structure, but\n`restrict_scalars` permits it to be written as:\n```lean\n-- an `R`-module structure on `M` is provided by `restrict_scalars` which is compatible\nexample : restrict_scalars R S M \u2192\u2097[R] S := sorry\n```\nHowever, it is usually better just to add this extra structure as an argument:\n```lean\n-- an `R`-module structure on `M` and proof of its compatibility is provided by the user\nexample [module R M] [is_scalar_tower R S M] : M \u2192\u2097[R] S := sorry\n```\nThe advantage of the second approach is that it defers the duty of providing the missing typeclasses\n`[module R M] [is_scalar_tower R S M]`. If some concrete `M` naturally carries these (as is often\nthe case) then we have avoided `restrict_scalars` entirely. If not, we can pass\n`restrict_scalars R S M` later on instead of `M`.\n\nNote that this means we almost always want to state definitions and lemmas in the language of\n`is_scalar_tower` rather than `restrict_scalars`.\n\nAn example of when one might want to use `restrict_scalars` would be if one has a vector space\nover a field of characteristic zero and wishes to make use of the `\u211a`-algebra structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.add_equiv_map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.sign_coe_nat_of_nonzero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.mod_add_div'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.neg_nat_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.mod_add_div_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.of_nat_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.neg_of_nat_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.mod_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.nat_abs_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.neg_succ_not_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.nat_abs_sub_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.div_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.to_nat_sub_to_nat_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.neg_succ_sub_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.to_nat_neg_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.to_nat_coe_nat_add_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.add_comm_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.div_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.mul_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.succ", "description": "Immediate successor of an integer: `succ n = n + 1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.nat_abs_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.nat_abs_sign", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.zero_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.sign_neg_succ_of_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.neg_succ_mul_coe_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.div_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.sign_coe_add_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.neg_add_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.succ_neg_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.le_to_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.div_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.nat_abs_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.pred_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.div_add_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.to_nat_add_to_nat_neg_eq_nat_abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.neg_