ription": "The `\ud835\udfd9_ V`-shaped generalized element giving the identity in a `V`-enriched category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.e_comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.e_id_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.forget_enrichment_id'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor.map_id_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_nat_trans.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_nat_trans.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_nat_trans", "description": "The type of `A`-graded natural transformations between `V`-functors `F` and `G`.\nThis is the type of morphisms in `V` from `A` to the `V`-object of natural transformations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_nat_trans.app", "description": "The type of `A`-graded natural transformations between `V`-functors `F` and `G`.\nThis is the type of morphisms in `V` from `A` to the `V`-object of natural transformations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_nat_trans.naturality", "description": "The type of `A`-graded natural transformations between `V`-functors `F` and `G`.\nThis is the type of morphisms in `V` from `A` to the `V`-object of natural transformations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor_Type_equiv_functor_apply_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_category_Type_equiv_category", "description": "We verify that an enriched category in `Type u` is just the same thing as an honest category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_category", "description": "A `V`-category is a category enriched in a monoidal category `V`.\n\nNote that we do not assume that `V` is a concrete category,\nso there may not be an \"honest\" underlying category at all!", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_category.hom", "description": "A `V`-category is a category enriched in a monoidal category `V`.\n\nNote that we do not assume that `V` is a concrete category,\nso there may not be an \"honest\" underlying category at all!", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_category.id", "description": "A `V`-category is a category enriched in a monoidal category `V`.\n\nNote that we do not assume that `V` is a concrete category,\nso there may not be an \"honest\" underlying category at all!", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_category.comp", "description": "A `V`-category is a category enriched in a monoidal category `V`.\n\nNote that we do not assume that `V` is a concrete category,\nso there may not be an \"honest\" underlying category at all!", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_category.id_comp", "description": "A `V`-category is a category enriched in a monoidal category `V`.\n\nNote that we do not assume that `V` is a concrete category,\nso there may not be an \"honest\" underlying category at all!", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_category.comp_id", "description": "A `V`-category is a category enriched in a monoidal category `V`.\n\nNote that we do not assume that `V` is a concrete category,\nso there may not be an \"honest\" underlying category at all!", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_category.assoc", "description": "A `V`-category is a category enriched in a monoidal category `V`.\n\nNote that we do not assume that `V` is a concrete category,\nso there may not be an \"honest\" underlying category at all!", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor.id", "description": "The identity enriched functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor.comp", "description": "Composition of enriched functors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor_Type_equiv_functor_apply_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.forget_enrichment_id", "description": "The identity in the \"underlying\" category of an enriched category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_nat_trans_yoneda_Type_iso_yoneda_nat_trans", "description": "We verify that the presheaf representing natural transformations\nbetween `Type v`-enriched functors is actually represented by\nthe usual type of natural transformations!", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.forget_enrichment.hom_to_hom_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor.comp_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.forget_enrichment.of_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor_Type_equiv_functor_symm_apply_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.e_comp", "description": "The composition `V`-morphism for a `V`-enriched category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.transport_enrichment.enriched_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_category_Type_of_category", "description": "Construct a `Type v`-enriched category from an honest category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor.map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.category_forget_enrichment", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor_Type_equiv_functor", "description": "We verify that an enriched functor between `Type v` enriched categories\nis just the same thing as an honest functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor.comp_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.forget_enrichment.hom_to", "description": "Typecheck a morphism in `forget_enrichment W C` as a `(\ud835\udfd9_ W)`-shaped `W`-morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.forget_enrichment.to", "description": "Typecheck an object of `forget_enrichment W C` as an object of `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor.map_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_nat_trans_yoneda_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.forget_enrichment_comp", "description": "Composition in the \"underlying\" category of an enriched category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor.forget", "description": "An enriched functor induces an honest functor of the underlying categories,\nby mapping the `(\ud835\udfd9_ W)`-shaped morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor_Type_equiv_functor_symm_apply_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_nat_trans_yoneda_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor", "description": "A `V`-functor `F` between `V`-enriched categories\nhas a `V`-morphism from `X \u27f6[V] Y` to `F.obj X \u27f6[V] F.obj Y`,\nsatisfying the usual axioms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor.obj", "description": "A `V`-functor `F` between `V`-enriched categories\nhas a `V`-morphism from `X \u27f6[V] Y` to `F.obj X \u27f6[V] F.obj Y`,\nsatisfying the usual axioms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor.map", "description": "A `V`-functor `F` between `V`-enriched categories\nhas a `V`-morphism from `X \u27f6[V] Y` to `F.obj X \u27f6[V] F.obj Y`,\nsatisfying the usual axioms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor.map_id'", "description": "A `V`-functor `F` between `V`-enriched categories\nhas a `V`-morphism from `X \u27f6[V] Y` to `F.obj X \u27f6[V] F.obj Y`,\nsatisfying the usual axioms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor.map_comp'", "description": "A `V`-functor `F` between `V`-enriched categories\nhas a `V`-morphism from `X \u27f6[V] Y` to `F.obj X \u27f6[V] F.obj Y`,\nsatisfying the usual axioms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.e_comp_id_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.e_assoc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.forget_enrichment", "description": " A type synonym for `C`, which should come equipped with a `V`-enriched category structure.\nIn a moment we will equip this with the (honest) category structure\nso that `X \u27f6 Y` is `(\ud835\udfd9_ W) \u27f6 (X \u27f6[W] Y)`.\n\nWe obtain this category by\ntransporting the enrichment in `V` along the lax monoidal functor `coyoneda_tensor_unit`,\nthen using the equivalence of `Type`-enriched categories with honest categories.\n\nThis is sometimes called the \"underlying\" category of an enriched category,\nalthough some care is needed as the functor `coyoneda_tensor_unit`,\nwhich always exists, does not necessarily coincide with\n\"the forgetful functor\" from `V` to `Type`, if such exists.\nWhen `V` is any of `Type`, `Top`, `AddCommGroup`, or `Module R`,\n`coyoneda_tensor_unit` is just the usual forgetful functor, however.\nFor `V = Algebra R`, the usual forgetful functor is coyoneda of `R[X]`, not of `R`.\n(Perhaps we should have a typeclass for this situation: `concrete_monoidal`?)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_nat_trans_yoneda", "description": "A presheaf isomorphic to the Yoneda embedding of\nthe `V`-object of natural transformations from `F` to `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.category_of_enriched_category_Type", "description": "Construct an honest category from a `Type v`-enriched category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor.id_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.forget_enrichment.of", "description": "Typecheck an object of `C` as an object of `forget_enrichment W C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.e_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.enriched_functor.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.transport_enrichment", "description": "A type synonym for `C`, which should come equipped with a `V`-enriched category structure.\nIn a moment we will equip this with the `W`-enriched category structure\nobtained by applying the functor `F : lax_monoidal_functor V W` to each hom object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum.norm_le_of_bounded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_of_subseq_of_summable", "description": " If a function `f` is summable in norm, and along some sequence of finsets exhausting the space\nits sum is converging to a limit `a`, then this holds along all finsets, i.e., `f` is summable\nwith sum `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_of_norm_bounded_eventually", "description": " Variant of the direct comparison test for series:  if the norm of `f` is eventually bounded by a\nreal function `g` which is summable, then `f` is summable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cauchy_seq_finset_iff_vanishing_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_of_summable_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_tsum_le_tsum_norm", "description": " If `\u2211' i, \u2016f i\u2016` is summable, then `\u2016\u2211' i, f i\u2016 \u2264 (\u2211' i, \u2016f i\u2016)`. Note that we do not assume\nthat `\u2211' i, f i` is summable, and it might not be the case if `\u03b1` is not a complete space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_iff_tendsto_nat_of_summable_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_of_nnnorm_bounded", "description": " Quantitative result associated to the direct comparison test for series: If `\u2211' i, g i` is\nsummable, and for all `i`, `\u2016f i\u2016\u208a \u2264 g i`, then `\u2016\u2211' i, f i\u2016\u208a \u2264 \u2211' i, g i`. Note that we\ndo not assume that `\u2211' i, f i` is summable, and it might not be the case if `\u03b1` is not a complete\nspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cauchy_seq_finset_of_summable_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_of_summable_nnnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_iff_vanishing_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnnorm_tsum_le", "description": " If `\u2211' i, \u2016f i\u2016\u208a` is summable, then `\u2016\u2211' i, f i\u2016\u208a \u2264 \u2211' i, \u2016f i\u2016\u208a`. Note that\nwe do not assume that `\u2211' i, f i` is summable, and it might not be the case if `\u03b1` is not a complete\nspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_of_nnnorm_bounded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cauchy_seq_finset_of_norm_bounded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cauchy_seq_range_of_norm_bounded", "description": " A version of the **direct comparison test** for conditionally convergent series.\nSee `cauchy_seq_finset_of_norm_bounded` for the same statement about absolutely convergent ones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_of_norm_bounded", "description": " The direct comparison test for series:  if the norm of `f` is bounded by a real function `g`\nwhich is summable, then `f` is summable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_of_norm_bounded", "description": " Quantitative result associated to the direct comparison test for series:  If `\u2211' i, g i` is\nsummable, and for all `i`, `\u2016f i\u2016 \u2264 g i`, then `\u2016\u2211' i, f i\u2016 \u2264 \u2211' i, g i`. Note that we do not\nassume that `\u2211' i, f i` is summable, and it might not be the case if `\u03b1` is not a complete space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cauchy_seq_finset_of_norm_bounded_eventually", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.get_subsingleton_info", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "param_info.to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "subsingleton_info.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fun_info.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "param_info", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "param_info.is_implicit", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "param_info.is_inst_implicit", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "param_info.is_prop", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "param_info.has_fwd_deps", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "param_info.is_dec_inst", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "param_info.back_deps", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "subsingleton_info_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.fold_explicit_args", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.get_spec_subsingleton_info", "description": "`get_spec_subsingleton_info t` return subsingleton parameter\n  information for the function application t of the form\n     `f a_1 ... a_n`.\n\n   This tactic is more precise than `get_subsingleton_info f` and `get_subsingleton_info_n f n`\n\n   Example: given `f : Pi (\u03b1 : Type), \u03b1 -> \u03b1`, `get_spec_subsingleton_info` for\n\n   `f unit b`\n\n   returns a fun_info with two param_info\n   1) specialized = tt\n   2) is_subsingleton = tt\n\n   The second argument is marked as subsingleton only because the resulting information\n   is taking into account the first argument.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "subsingleton_info", "description": "specialized is true if the result of fun_info has been specifialized\nusing this argument.\nFor example, consider the function\n\n           f : Pi (\u03b1 : Type), \u03b1 -> \u03b1\n\nNow, suppse we request get_specialize fun_info for the application\n\n       f unit a\n\nfun_info_manager returns two param_info objects:\n1) specialized = true\n2) is_subsingleton = true\n\nNote that, in general, the second argument of f is not a subsingleton,\nbut it is in this particular case/specialization.\n\n\\remark This bit is only set if it is a dependent parameter.\n\n Moreover, we only set is_specialized IF another parameter\n becomes a subsingleton", "p": "core"}, {"name": "subsingleton_info.specialized", "description": "specialized is true if the result of fun_info has been specifialized\nusing this argument.\nFor example, consider the function\n\n           f : Pi (\u03b1 : Type), \u03b1 -> \u03b1\n\nNow, suppse we request get_specialize fun_info for the application\n\n       f unit a\n\nfun_info_manager returns two param_info objects:\n1) specialized = true\n2) is_subsingleton = true\n\nNote that, in general, the second argument of f is not a subsingleton,\nbut it is in this particular case/specialization.\n\n\\remark This bit is only set if it is a dependent parameter.\n\n Moreover, we only set is_specialized IF another parameter\n becomes a subsingleton", "p": "core"}, {"name": "subsingleton_info.is_subsingleton", "description": "specialized is true if the result of fun_info has been specifialized\nusing this argument.\nFor example, consider the function\n\n           f : Pi (\u03b1 : Type), \u03b1 -> \u03b1\n\nNow, suppse we request get_specialize fun_info for the application\n\n       f unit a\n\nfun_info_manager returns two param_info objects:\n1) specialized = true\n2) is_subsingleton = true\n\nNote that, in general, the second argument of f is not a subsingleton,\nbut it is in this particular case/specialization.\n\n\\remark This bit is only set if it is a dependent parameter.\n\n Moreover, we only set is_specialized IF another parameter\n becomes a subsingleton", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fun_info_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.fold_explicit_args_aux", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fun_info", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fun_info.params", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fun_info.result_deps", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.get_fun_info", "description": "If nargs is not none, then return information assuming the function has only nargs arguments.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "param_info.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.get_spec_prefix_size", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "exists_associated_mem_of_dvd_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prime.exists_mem_finset_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.prod_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prime.exists_mem_multiset_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.finset_prod_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prime.exists_mem_multiset_map_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_primes_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.rel_associated_iff_map_eq_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.prod_le_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.prod_primes_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.exists_mem_multiset_le_of_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.prod_ne_zero_of_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prime.dvd_finset_prod_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prime.dvd_finsupp_prod_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.prod_eq_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.cyclic_permutations_eq_singleton_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.mem_cyclic_permutations_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated_singleton_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated.mem_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.mem_rotate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_eq_rotate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate'_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate'_cons_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated_concat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated_reverse_comm_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.nth_le_rotate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated_singleton_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated_iff_mem_map_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.cyclic_permutations_of_ne_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.map_rotate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_eq_self_iff_eq_replicate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_eq_rotate'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated_cyclic_permutations_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated_nil_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_perm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.cyclic_permutations_eq_nil_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated_iff_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_replicate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.head'_rotate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate'_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_length_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated.perm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.singleton_eq_rotate_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated.forall", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_rotate_eq_one_of_prod_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate'_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.length_cyclic_permutations_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated.cyclic_permutations", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.length_rotate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_eq_nil_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated.nodup_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.cyclic_permutations_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_rotate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.cyclic_permutations", "description": " List of all cyclic permutations of `l`.\nThe `cyclic_permutations` of a nonempty list `l` will always contain `list.length l` elements.\nThis implies that under certain conditions, there are duplicates in `list.cyclic_permutations l`.\nThe `n`th entry is equal to `l.rotate n`, proven in `list.nth_le_cyclic_permutations`.\nThe proof that every cyclic permutant of `l` is in the list is `list.mem_cyclic_permutations_iff`.\n\n     cyclic_permutations [1, 2, 3, 2, 4] =\n       [[1, 2, 3, 2, 4], [2, 3, 2, 4, 1], [3, 2, 4, 1, 2],\n        [2, 4, 1, 2, 3], [4, 1, 2, 3, 2]]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate'_length_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.nil_eq_rotate_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate'_rotate'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.nth_rotate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_cons_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.setoid.r.decidable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated.eqv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.nodup.cyclic_permutations", "description": "If a `l : list \u03b1` is `nodup l`, then all of its cyclic permutants are distinct.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.nth_le_cyclic_permutations", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated_reverse_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.length_mem_cyclic_permutations", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_eq_singleton_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.cyclic_permutations_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.reverse_rotate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_reverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_one_eq_self_iff_eq_replicate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate'_eq_drop_append_take", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_eq_drop_append_take_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.zip_with_rotate_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_append_length_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated_nil_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.nodup_rotate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.cyclic_permutations_rotate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.nodup.rotate_eq_self_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated", "description": "`is_rotated l\u2081 l\u2082` or `l\u2081 ~r l\u2082` asserts that `l\u2081` and `l\u2082` are cyclic permutations\n of each other. This is defined by claiming that `\u2203 n, l.rotate n = l'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_eq_drop_append_take", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.nth_le_rotate_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated_decidable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.mem_cyclic_permutations_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate'_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rotate_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.nodup.rotate_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated.setoid", "description": "The relation `list.is_rotated l l'` forms a `setoid` of cycles.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated.reverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.length_cyclic_permutations_of_ne_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.zip_with_rotate_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.is_rotated.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.length_rotate'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.nth_le_rotate'", "description": "A variant of `nth_le_rotate` useful for rewrites.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.cone_maps", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_hom.is_cofiltered", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered_of_directed_ge_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.coeq\u2083", "description": "`coeq\u2083 f g h`, for morphisms `f g h : j\u2081 \u27f6 j\u2082`, is an arbitrary choice of object\nwhich admits a morphism `coeq\u2083_hom f g h : j\u2082 \u27f6 coeq\u2083 f g h` such that\n`coeq\u2083_condition\u2081`, `coeq\u2083_condition\u2082` and `coeq\u2083_condition\u2083` are satisfied.\nIts existence is ensured by `is_filtered`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.cocone_nonempty", "description": "If we have `is_filtered C`, then for any functor `F : J \u2964 C` with `fin_category J`,\nthere exists a cocone over `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered_or_empty_of_directed_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.inf_to_commutes", "description": "The triangles consisting of a morphism in `H` and the maps from `inf O H` commute.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.inf_to", "description": "The morphisms from `inf O H`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.cone_objs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered_op_of_is_filtered", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered_or_empty", "description": "A category `is_filtered_or_empty` if\n1. for every pair of objects there exists another object \"to the right\", and\n2. for every pair of parallel morphisms there exists a morphism to the right so the compositions\n   are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered_or_empty.cocone_objs", "description": "A category `is_filtered_or_empty` if\n1. for every pair of objects there exists another object \"to the right\", and\n2. for every pair of parallel morphisms there exists a morphism to the right so the compositions\n   are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered_or_empty.cocone_maps", "description": "A category `is_filtered_or_empty` if\n1. for every pair of objects there exists another object \"to the right\", and\n2. for every pair of parallel morphisms there exists a morphism to the right so the compositions\n   are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.coeq\u2083_hom", "description": "`coeq\u2083_hom f g h`, for morphisms `f g h : j\u2081 \u27f6 j\u2082`, is an arbitrary choice of morphism\n`j\u2082 \u27f6 coeq\u2083 f g h` such that `coeq\u2083_condition\u2081`, `coeq\u2083_condition\u2082` and `coeq\u2083_condition\u2083`\nare satisfied. Its existence is ensured by `is_filtered`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.right_to_max", "description": "`right_to_max j j'` is an arbitrary choice of morphism from `j'` to `max j j'`,\nwhose existence is ensured by `is_filtered`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.as_small.is_filtered", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift.is_filtered", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.coeq\u2083_condition\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered", "description": "A category `is_cofiltered` if\n1. for every pair of objects there exists another object \"to the left\",\n2. for every pair of parallel morphisms there exists a morphism to the left so the compositions\n   are equal, and\n3. there exists some object.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04AZ>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.to_is_cofiltered_or_empty", "description": "A category `is_cofiltered` if\n1. for every pair of objects there exists another object \"to the left\",\n2. for every pair of parallel morphisms there exists a morphism to the left so the compositions\n   are equal, and\n3. there exists some object.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04AZ>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.nonempty", "description": "A category `is_cofiltered` if\n1. for every pair of objects there exists another object \"to the left\",\n2. for every pair of parallel morphisms there exists a morphism to the left so the compositions\n   are equal, and\n3. there exists some object.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04AZ>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.second_to_max\u2083", "description": "`second_to_max\u2083 j\u2081 j\u2082 j\u2083` is an arbitrary choice of morphism from `j\u2082` to `max\u2083 j\u2081 j\u2082 j\u2083`,\nwhose existence is ensured by `is_filtered`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.sup_objs_exists", "description": "Any finite collection of objects in a filtered category has an object \"to the right\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.span", "description": "For every span `j \u27f5 i \u27f6 j'`, there\n  exists a cocone `j \u27f6 k \u27f5 j'` such that the square commutes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.to_sup_commutes", "description": "The triangles of consisting of a morphism in `H` and the maps to `sup O H` commute.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.cone", "description": "An arbitrary choice of cone over `F : J \u2964 C`, for `fin_category J` and `is_cofiltered C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.cone_nonempty", "description": "If we have `is_cofiltered C`, then for any functor `F : J \u2964 C` with `fin_category J`,\nthere exists a cone over `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.max", "description": "`max j j'` is an arbitrary choice of object to the right of both `j` and `j'`,\nwhose existence is ensured by `is_filtered`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift.is_cofiltered", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.inf_exists", "description": "Given any `finset` of objects `{X, ...}` and\nindexed collection of `finset`s of morphisms `{f, ...}` in `C`,\nthere exists an object `S`, with a morphism `T X : S \u27f6 X` from each `X`,\nsuch that the triangles commute: `T X \u226b f = T Y`, for `f : X \u27f6 Y` in the `finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered_or_empty_of_directed_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.of_right_adjoint", "description": "If `C` is filtered, and we have a functor `R : C \u2964 D` with a left adjoint, then `D` is filtered.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered_of_semilattice_sup_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.min", "description": "`min j j'` is an arbitrary choice of object to the left of both `j` and `j'`,\nwhose existence is ensured by `is_cofiltered`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.of_equivalence", "description": "Being filtered is preserved by equivalence of categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.of_left_adjoint", "description": "If `C` is cofiltered, and we have a functor `L : C \u2964 D` with a right adjoint,\nthen `D` is cofiltered.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.coeq_condition", "description": "`coeq_condition f f'`, for morphisms `f f' : j \u27f6 j'`, is the proof that\n`f \u226b coeq_hom f f' = f' \u226b coeq_hom f f'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.coeq\u2083_condition\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.eq_condition_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.sup", "description": "An arbitrary choice of object \"to the right\"\nof a finite collection of objects `O` and morphisms `H`,\nmaking all the triangles commute.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.of_is_left_adjoint", "description": "If `C` is cofiltered, and we have a left adjoint functor `L : C \u2964 D`, then `D` is cofiltered.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.of_is_right_adjoint", "description": "If `C` is filtered, and we have a right adjoint functor `R : C \u2964 D`, then `D` is filtered.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.sup_exists", "description": "Given any `finset` of objects `{X, ...}` and\nindexed collection of `finset`s of morphisms `{f, ...}` in `C`,\nthere exists an object `S`, with a morphism `T X : X \u27f6 S` from each `X`,\nsuch that the triangles commute: `f \u226b T Y = T X`, for `f : X \u27f6 Y` in the `finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered_op_of_is_cofiltered", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.discrete.is_cofiltered", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.eq", "description": "`eq f f'`, for morphisms `f f' : j \u27f6 j'`, is an arbitrary choice of object\nwhich admits a morphism `eq_hom f f' : eq f f' \u27f6 j` such that\n`eq_condition : eq_hom f f' \u226b f = eq_hom f f' \u226b f'`.\nIts existence is ensured by `is_cofiltered`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.bowtie", "description": "Given a \"bowtie\" of morphisms\n```lean\n j\u2081   j\u2082\n |\\  /|\n | \\/ |\n | /\\ |\n |/  \\\u2223\n vv  vv\n k\u2081  k\u2082\n```\nin a filtered category, we can construct an object `s` and two morphisms from `k\u2081` and `k\u2082` to `s`,\nmaking the resulting squares commute.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.eq_condition", "description": "`eq_condition f f'`, for morphisms `f f' : j \u27f6 j'`, is the proof that\n`eq_hom f f' \u226b f = eq_hom f f' \u226b f'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.discrete.is_filtered", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.coeq", "description": "`coeq f f'`, for morphisms `f f' : j \u27f6 j'`, is an arbitrary choice of object\nwhich admits a morphism `coeq_hom f f' : j' \u27f6 coeq f f'` such that\n`coeq_condition : f \u226b coeq_hom f f' = f' \u226b coeq_hom f f'`.\nIts existence is ensured by `is_filtered`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.coeq_condition_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.coeq_hom", "description": "`coeq_hom f f'`, for morphisms `f f' : j \u27f6 j'`, is an arbitrary choice of morphism\n`coeq_hom f f' : j' \u27f6 coeq f f'` such that\n`coeq_condition : f \u226b coeq_hom f f' = f' \u226b coeq_hom f f'`.\nIts existence is ensured by `is_filtered`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.inf", "description": "An arbitrary choice of object \"to the left\"\nof a finite collection of objects `O` and morphisms `H`,\nmaking all the triangles commute.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.cospan", "description": "For every cospan `j \u27f6 i \u27f5 j'`,\nthere exists a cone `j \u27f5 k \u27f6 j'` such that the square commutes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.cocone", "description": "An arbitrary choice of cocone over `F : J \u2964 C`, for `fin_category J` and `is_filtered C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.third_to_max\u2083", "description": "`third_to_max\u2083 j\u2081 j\u2082 j\u2083` is an arbitrary choice of morphism from `j\u2083` to `max\u2083 j\u2081 j\u2082 j\u2083`,\nwhose existence is ensured by `is_filtered`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered_or_empty_of_semilattice_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered", "description": "A category `is_filtered` if\n1. for every pair of objects there exists another object \"to the right\",\n2. for every pair of parallel morphisms there exists a morphism to the right so the compositions\n   are equal, and\n3. there exists some object.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/002V>. (They also define a diagram being filtered.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.to_is_filtered_or_empty", "description": "A category `is_filtered` if\n1. for every pair of objects there exists another object \"to the right\",\n2. for every pair of parallel morphisms there exists a morphism to the right so the compositions\n   are equal, and\n3. there exists some object.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/002V>. (They also define a diagram being filtered.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.nonempty", "description": "A category `is_filtered` if\n1. for every pair of objects there exists another object \"to the right\",\n2. for every pair of parallel morphisms there exists a morphism to the right so the compositions\n   are equal, and\n3. there exists some object.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/002V>. (They also define a diagram being filtered.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered_or_empty", "description": "A category `is_cofiltered_or_empty` if\n1. for every pair of objects there exists another object \"to the left\", and\n2. for every pair of parallel morphisms there exists a morphism to the left so the compositions\n   are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered_or_empty.cone_objs", "description": "A category `is_cofiltered_or_empty` if\n1. for every pair of objects there exists another object \"to the left\", and\n2. for every pair of parallel morphisms there exists a morphism to the left so the compositions\n   are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered_or_empty.cone_maps", "description": "A category `is_cofiltered_or_empty` if\n1. for every pair of objects there exists another object \"to the left\", and\n2. for every pair of parallel morphisms there exists a morphism to the left so the compositions\n   are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered_of_directed_le_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.of_equivalence", "description": "Being cofiltered is preserved by equivalence of categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_hom.is_filtered", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.coeq\u2083_condition\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered_of_semilattice_inf_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.cocone_objs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.to_sup", "description": "The morphisms to `sup O H`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.min_to_right", "description": "`min_to_right j j'` is an arbitrary choice of morphism from `min j j'` to `j'`,\nwhose existence is ensured by `is_cofiltered`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.max\u2083", "description": "`max\u2083 j\u2081 j\u2082 j\u2083` is an arbitrary choice of object to the right of `j\u2081`, `j\u2082` and `j\u2083`,\nwhose existence is ensured by `is_filtered`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.ranges_directed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.tulip", "description": "Given a \"tulip\" of morphisms\n```lean\n j\u2081    j\u2082    j\u2083\n |\\   / \\   / |\n | \\ /   \\ /  |\n |  vv    vv  |\n \\  k\u2081    k\u2082 /\n  \\         /\n   \\       /\n    \\     /\n     \\   /\n      v v\n       l\n```\nin a filtered category, we can construct an object `s` and three morphisms from `k\u2081`, `k\u2082` and `l`\nto `s`, making the resulting squares commute.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.min_to_left", "description": "`min_to_left j j'` is an arbitrary choice of morphism from `min j j'` to `j`,\nwhose existence is ensured by `is_cofiltered`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.as_small.is_cofiltered", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.cocone_maps", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.left_to_max", "description": "`left_to_max j j'` is an arbitrary choice of morphism from `j` to `max j j'`,\nwhose existence is ensured by `is_filtered`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_filtered.first_to_max\u2083", "description": "`first_to_max\u2083 j\u2081 j\u2082 j\u2083` is an arbitrary choice of morphism from `j\u2081` to `max\u2083 j\u2081 j\u2082 j\u2083`,\nwhose existence is ensured by `is_filtered`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered_or_empty_of_semilattice_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.inf_objs_exists", "description": "Any finite collection of objects in a cofiltered category has an object \"to the left\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_cofiltered.eq_hom", "description": "`eq_hom f f'`, for morphisms `f f' : j \u27f6 j'`, is an arbitrary choice of morphism\n`eq_hom f f' : eq f f' \u27f6 j` such that\n`eq_condition : eq_hom f f' \u226b f = eq_hom f f' \u226b f'`.\nIts existence is ensured by `is_cofiltered`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.biprod_iso_prod_inv_comp_fst_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.category_theory.limits.has_finite_biproducts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.biproduct_iso_pi_inv_comp_\u03c0_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.biprod_iso_prod_inv_comp_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.biprod_iso_prod", "description": "We verify that the biproduct in AddCommGroup is isomorphic to\nthe cartesian product of the underlying types:", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.biproduct_iso_pi_inv_comp_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.binary_product_limit_cone_cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.has_limit.product_limit_cone", "description": "Construct limit data for a product in `AddCommGroup`, using `AddCommGroup.of (\u03a0 j, F.obj j)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.biproduct_iso_pi_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.has_limit.product_limit_cone_cone_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.has_limit.lift_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.has_limit.product_limit_cone_cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.biprod_iso_prod_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.category_theory.limits.has_binary_biproducts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.binary_product_limit_cone_cone_\u03c0_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.biproduct_iso_pi", "description": "We verify that the biproduct we've just defined is isomorphic to the AddCommGroup structure\non the dependent function type", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.binary_product_limit_cone_cone_\u03c0_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.binary_product_limit_cone", "description": "Construct limit data for a binary product in `AddCommGroup`, using `AddCommGroup.of (G \u00d7 H)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.binary_product_limit_cone_is_limit_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.biprod_iso_prod_inv_comp_snd_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.biprod_iso_prod_inv_comp_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.has_limit.product_limit_cone_is_limit_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.has_limit.lift", "description": "The map from an arbitrary cone over a indexed family of abelian groups\nto the cartesian product of those groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology_op", "description": " Given `f, g` with `f \u226b g = 0`, the homology of `g.op, f.op` is the opposite of the homology of\n`f, g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop_counit_iso", "description": "Auxilliary definition for `unop_equivalence`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op_inverse_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op_symm", "description": "Sends a complex `X` with objects in `V` to the corresponding complex with objects in `V\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op_inverse", "description": "Auxilliary definition for `op_equivalence`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop_functor", "description": "Auxilliary definition for `unop_equivalence`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op_symm_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op_functor_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop_equivalence_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop_symm", "description": "Sends a complex `X` with objects in `V\u1d52\u1d56` to the corresponding complex with objects in `V`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.homology_unop", "description": " Given a complex `C` of objects in `V\u1d52\u1d56`, the `i`th homology of its 'opposite' complex (with\nobjects in `V`) is the opposite of the `i`th homology of `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op_equivalence_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop", "description": "Sends a complex `X` with objects in `V\u1d52\u1d56` to the corresponding complex with objects in `V`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop_inverse_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop_equivalence", "description": " Given a category of complexes with objects in `V\u1d52\u1d56`, there is a natural equivalence between its\nopposite category and a category of complexes with objects in `V`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop_unit_iso", "description": "Auxilliary definition for `unop_equivalence`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "image_to_kernel_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.homology_unop_def", "description": "Auxilliary tautological definition for `homology_unop`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "image_to_kernel_unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op_unit_iso", "description": "Auxilliary definition for `op_equivalence`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op_equivalence_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op_functor", "description": "Auxilliary definition for `op_equivalence`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop_equivalence_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop_inverse_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology_unop", "description": " Given morphisms `f, g` in `V\u1d52\u1d56` with `f \u226b g = 0`, the homology of `g.unop, f.unop` is the\nopposite of the homology of `f, g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop_functor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op_equivalence", "description": " Given a category of complexes with objects in `V`, there is a natural equivalence between its\nopposite category and a category of complexes with objects in `V\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop_inverse", "description": "Auxilliary definition for `unop_equivalence`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op_counit_iso", "description": "Auxilliary definition for `op_equivalence`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop_symm_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop_functor_additive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop_functor_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.homology_op", "description": " Given a complex `C` of objects in `V`, the `i`th homology of its 'opposite' complex (with\nobjects in `V\u1d52\u1d56`) is the opposite of the `i`th homology of `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op_equivalence_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op_symm_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop_symm_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop_equivalence_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op_functor_additive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op_inverse_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op_functor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op_equivalence_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.unop_equivalence_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.op", "description": "Sends a complex `X` with objects in `V` to the corresponding complex with objects in `V\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.homology_op_def", "description": "Auxilliary tautological definition for `homology_op`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.right_adjoint_preserves_limits", "description": "A right adjoint preserves limits.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0038>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.is_equivalence_creates_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.cones_iso", "description": "When `F \u22a3 G`,\nthe functor associating to each `X` the cones over `K` with cone point `F.op.obj X`\nis naturally isomorphic to\nthe functor associating to each `X` the cones over `K \u22d9 G` with cone point `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.functoriality_counit", "description": "The counit for the adjunction for `cocones.functoriality K F : cocone K \u2964 cocone (K \u22d9 F)`.\n\nAuxiliary definition for `functoriality_is_left_adjoint`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.is_equivalence_reflects_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.functoriality_is_left_adjoint", "description": "The functor `cocones.functoriality K F : cocone K \u2964 cocone (K \u22d9 F)` is a left adjoint.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.functoriality_unit'_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.functoriality_counit'", "description": "The counit for the adjunction for`cones.functoriality K G : cone K \u2964 cone (K \u22d9 G)`.\n\nAuxiliary definition for `functoriality_is_right_adjoint`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.functoriality_counit_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.functoriality_left_adjoint", "description": "The left adjoint of `cones.functoriality K G : cone K \u2964 cone (K \u22d9 G)`.\n\nAuxiliary definition for `functoriality_is_right_adjoint`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.cocones_iso_component_hom", "description": "auxiliary construction for `cocones_iso`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.functoriality_is_right_adjoint", "description": "The functor `cones.functoriality K G : cone K \u2964 cone (K \u22d9 G)` is a right adjoint.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.has_limit_of_comp_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.cocones_iso", "description": "When `F \u22a3 G`,\nthe functor associating to each `Y` the cocones over `K \u22d9 F` with cone point `Y`\nis naturally isomorphic to\nthe functor associating to each `Y` the cocones over `K` with cone point `G.obj Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.has_colimit_comp_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.functoriality_unit", "description": "The unit for the adjunction for `cocones.functoriality K F : cocone K \u2964 cocone (K \u22d9 F)`.\n\nAuxiliary definition for `functoriality_is_left_adjoint`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.functoriality_right_adjoint", "description": "The right adjoint of `cocones.functoriality K F : cocone K \u2964 cocone (K \u22d9 F)`.\n\nAuxiliary definition for `functoriality_is_left_adjoint`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.has_limit_comp_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.cocones_iso_component_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.has_limits_of_shape_of_equivalence", "description": "Transport a `has_limits_of_shape` instance across an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.cones_iso_component_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.has_colimit_of_comp_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.has_limits_of_equivalence", "description": "Transport a `has_limits` instance across an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.cones_iso_component_hom", "description": "auxiliary construction for `cones_iso`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.cocones_iso_component_inv", "description": "auxiliary construction for `cocones_iso`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.cocones_iso_component_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.functoriality_unit'", "description": "The unit for the adjunction for`cones.functoriality K G : cone K \u2964 cone (K \u22d9 G)`.\n\nAuxiliary definition for `functoriality_is_right_adjoint`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.functoriality_counit'_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.cones_iso_component_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.left_adjoint_preserves_colimits", "description": "A left adjoint preserves colimits.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0038>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.has_colimits_of_equivalence", "description": "Transport a `has_colimits` instance across an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.cones_iso_component_inv", "description": "auxiliary construction for `cones_iso`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.functoriality_unit_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.is_equivalence_reflects_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.is_equivalence_creates_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.is_equivalence_preserves_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.is_equivalence_preserves_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.has_colimits_of_shape_of_equivalence", "description": "Transport a `has_colimits_of_shape` instance across an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_sub_ordered", "description": "`\u220f i, (f i - g i) = (\u220f i, f i) - \u2211 i, g i * (\u220f j < i, f j - g j) * (\u220f j > i, f j)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_range_cast_nat_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_mul_boole", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_pow_eq_pow_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mul_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_sum", "description": "The product over a sum can be written as a sum over the product of sets, `finset.pi`.\n `finset.prod_univ_sum` is an alternative statement when the product is over `univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_add_ordered", "description": "`\u220f i, (f i + g i) = (\u220f i, f i) + \u2211 i, g i * (\u220f j < i, f j + g j) * (\u220f j > i, f j)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_powerset", "description": "A sum over `powerset s` is equal to the double sum over sets of subsets of `s` with\n`card s = k`, for `k = 1, ..., card s`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_boole_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_powerset", "description": " A product over `powerset s` is equal to the double product over sets of subsets of `s` with\n`card s = k`, for `k = 1, ..., card s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_add", "description": "The product of `f a + g a` over all of `s` is the sum\n over the powerset of `s` of the product of `f` over a subset `t` times\n the product of `g` over the complement of `t`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_one_sub_ordered", "description": " `\u220f i, (1 - f i) = 1 - \u2211 i, f i * (\u220f j < i, 1 - f j)`. This formula is useful in construction of\na partition of unity from a collection of \u201cbump\u201d functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_powerset_insert", "description": "A sum over all subsets of `s \u222a {x}` is obtained by summing the sum over all subsets\nof `s`, and over all subsets of `s` to which one adds `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.dvd_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_pow_mul_eq_add_pow", "description": "  Summing `a^s.card * b^(n-s.card)` over all finite subsets `s` of a `finset`\ngives `(a + b)^s.card`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_range_succ_mul_sum_range_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_mul_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_powerset_insert", "description": " A product over all subsets of `s \u222a {x}` is obtained by multiplying the product over all subsets\nof `s`, and over all subsets of `s` to which one adds `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.associator_Bimod.inv_aux", "description": " An auxiliary morphism for the definition of the underlying morphism of the inverse component of\nthe associator isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.regular_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.whisker_right_comp_Bimod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.right_assoc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.tensor_hom", "description": "Tensor product of two morphisms of bimodule objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.regular", "description": "A monoid object as a bimodule over itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.whisker_right_id_Bimod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.tensor_Bimod.X", "description": "The underlying object of the tensor product of two bimodules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.iso_of_iso", "description": "Construct an isomorphism of bimodules by giving an isomorphism between the underlying objects\nand checking compatibility with left and right actions only in the forward direction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.iso_of_iso_inv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.hom.left_act_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.tensor_Bimod", "description": "Tensor product of two bimodule objects as a bimodule object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.middle_assoc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.iso_of_iso_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.hom.right_act_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.comp_whisker_left_Bimod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.whisker_left_comp_Bimod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.left_unitor_Bimod.hom_right_act_hom'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.associator_Bimod.hom_right_act_hom'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.left_unitor_Bimod.hom_left_act_hom'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.tensor_Bimod.act_left", "description": "Left action for the tensor product of two bimodules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.left_unitor_Bimod", "description": "The left unitor as a bimodule isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.tensor_Bimod.right_assoc'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.regular_act_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.right_unitor_Bimod", "description": "The right unitor as a bimodule isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.associator_Bimod.hom_aux", "description": " An auxiliary morphism for the definition of the underlying morphism of the forward component of\nthe associator isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Bimod.id_ho