": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.add_comm_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.positive", "description": "The positive cone is the convex cone formed by the set of nonnegative elements in an ordered\nmodule.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "riesz_extension.exists_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.has_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.flat.pointed", "description": "A flat cone is always pointed (contains `0`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_extension_of_le_sublinear", "description": " **Hahn-Banach theorem**: if `N : E \u2192 \u211d` is a sublinear map, `f` is a linear map\ndefined on a subspace of `E`, and `f x \u2264 N x` for all `x` in the domain of `f`,\nthen `f` can be extended to the whole space to a linear map `g` such that `g x \u2264 N x`\nfor all `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.mem_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.salient", "description": "A convex cone is salient if it doesn't include `x` and `-x` for any nonzero `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.has_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.pointed.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.coe_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.map_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.add_zero_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.salient_positive", "description": "The positive cone of an ordered module is always salient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.coe_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.to_ordered_smul", "description": "Constructs an ordered module given an `ordered_add_comm_group`, a cone, and a proof that\nthe order relation is the one defined by the cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.pointed", "description": "A convex cone is pointed if it includes `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.salient.anti", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_hull_to_cone_is_least", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.to_preorder", "description": "A pointed convex cone defines a preorder.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.to_convex_cone_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.mem_to_cone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.pointed_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.comap_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.mem_to_cone'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.blunt", "description": "A convex cone is blunt if it doesn't include `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.mem_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.map", "description": "The image of a convex cone under a `\ud835\udd5c`-linear map is a convex cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_hull_to_cone_eq_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.flat", "description": "A convex cone is flat if it contains some nonzero vector `x` and its opposite `-x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.mem_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.mem_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.blunt.salient", "description": "A blunt cone (one not containing `0`) is always salient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.has_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.to_cone_is_least", "description": "`hs.to_cone s` is the least cone that includes `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.pointed_positive", "description": "The positive cone of an ordered module is always pointed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "riesz_extension.step", "description": " Induction step in M. Riesz extension theorem. Given a convex cone `s` in a vector space `E`,\na partially defined linear map `f : f.domain \u2192 \u211d`, assume that `f` is nonnegative on `f.domain \u2229 p`\nand `p + s = E`. If `f` is not defined on the whole `E`, then we can extend it to a larger\nsubmodule without breaking the non-negativity condition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.blunt_iff_not_pointed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.comap", "description": "The preimage of a convex cone under a `\ud835\udd5c`-linear map is a convex cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.mem_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.set_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.flat.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.strictly_positive", "description": " The cone of strictly positive elements.\n\nNote that this naming diverges from the mathlib convention of `pos` and `nonneg` due to \"positive\ncone\" (`convex_cone.positive`) being established terminology for the non-negative elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.comap_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.coe_positive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.to_convex_cone_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.mem_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.to_cone", "description": "The set of vectors proportional to those in a convex set forms a convex cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "riesz_extension", "description": " M. **Riesz extension theorem**: given a convex cone `s` in a vector space `E`, a submodule `p`,\nand a linear `f : p \u2192 \u211d`, assume that `f` is nonnegative on `p \u2229 s` and `p + s = E`. Then\nthere exists a globally defined linear function `g : E \u2192 \u211d` that agrees with `f` on `p`,\nand is nonnegative on `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.blunt_strictly_positive", "description": "The strictly positive cone of an ordered module is always blunt.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.positive_le_strictly_positive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone", "description": " A convex cone is a subset `s` of a `\ud835\udd5c`-module such that `a \u2022 x + b \u2022 y \u2208 s` whenever `a, b > 0`\nand `x, y \u2208 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.carrier", "description": " A convex cone is a subset `s` of a `\ud835\udd5c`-module such that `a \u2022 x + b \u2022 y \u2208 s` whenever `a, b > 0`\nand `x, y \u2208 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.smul_mem'", "description": " A convex cone is a subset `s` of a `\ud835\udd5c`-module such that `a \u2022 x + b \u2022 y \u2208 s` whenever `a, b > 0`\nand `x, y \u2208 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.add_mem'", "description": " A convex cone is a subset `s` of a `\ud835\udd5c`-module such that `a \u2022 x + b \u2022 y \u2208 s` whenever `a, b > 0`\nand `x, y \u2208 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.smul_mem_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.subset_to_cone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.coe_strictly_positive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.coe_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.to_ordered_add_comm_group", "description": "A pointed and salient cone defines an `ordered_add_comm_group`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.complete_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.pointed_to_convex_cone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.coe_to_convex_cone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.ordered_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.to_mul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.canonically_linear_ordered_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.canonically_ordered_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.canonically_linear_ordered_add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.to_mul_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.ordered_cancel_add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.has_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.of_add_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.linear_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.ordered_cancel_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.has_exists_mul_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.of_mul_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.linear_ordered_add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.has_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.of_mul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.has_exists_add_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.order_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.to_add_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.bounded_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.canonically_ordered_add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.linear_ordered_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.of_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.bounded_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.order_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.to_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.order_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.preorder", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.order_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.has_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.linear_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.has_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.preorder", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.ordered_add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.eventually_split_many_inf_eq_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.split_many_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box.split_upper_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.restrict_split", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.Union_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box.split_lower", "description": " Given a box `I` and `x \u2208 (I.lower i, I.upper i)`, the hyperplane `{y : \u03b9 \u2192 \u211d | y i = x}` splits\n`I` into two boxes. `box_integral.box.split_lower I i x` is the box `I \u2229 {y | y i \u2264 x}`\n(if it is nonempty). As usual, we represent a box that may be empty as\n`with_bot (box_integral.box \u03b9)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.is_partition_split_many", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box.coe_split_upper", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.mem_split_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box.split_lower_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.Union_split_many", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box.split_upper", "description": " Given a box `I` and `x \u2208 (I.lower i, I.upper i)`, the hyperplane `{y : \u03b9 \u2192 \u211d | y i = x}` splits\n`I` into two boxes. `box_integral.box.split_upper I i x` is the box `I \u2229 {y | x < y i}`\n(if it is nonempty). As usual, we represent a box that may be empty as\n`with_bot (box_integral.box \u03b9)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.not_disjoint_imp_le_of_subset_of_mem_split_many", "description": " Let `s : finset (\u03b9 \u00d7 \u211d)` be a set of hyperplanes `{x : \u03b9 \u2192 \u211d | x i = r}` in `\u03b9 \u2192 \u211d` encoded as\npairs `(i, r)`. Suppose that this set contains all faces of a box `J`. The hyperplanes of `s` split\na box `I` into subboxes. Let `Js` be one of them. If `J` and `Js` have nonempty intersection, then\n`Js` is a subbox of `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.inf_split", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box.coe_split_lower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box.split_lower_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box.split_upper_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.Union_split", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.eventually_not_disjoint_imp_le_of_mem_split_many", "description": " Let `s` be a finite set of boxes in `\u211d\u207f = \u03b9 \u2192 \u211d`. Then there exists a finite set `t\u2080` of\nhyperplanes (namely, the set of all hyperfaces of boxes in `s`) such that for any `t \u2287 t\u2080`\nand any box `I` in `\u211d\u207f` the following holds. The hyperplanes from `t` split `I` into subboxes.\nLet `J'` be one of them, and let `J` be one of the boxes in `s`. If these boxes have a nonempty\nintersection, then `J' \u2264 J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box.split_upper_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box.split_lower_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.coe_eq_of_mem_split_of_lt_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.split_many", "description": " Split a box along many hyperplanes `{y | y i = x}`; each hyperplane is given by the pair\n`(i x)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.split_many_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box.split_lower_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.split_many_le_split", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.is_partition_split", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box.disjoint_split_lower_split_upper", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.mem_split_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.exists_Union_eq_diff", "description": " For every prepartition `\u03c0` of `I` there exists a prepartition that covers exactly\n`I \\ \u03c0.Union`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box.split_upper_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.coe_eq_of_mem_split_of_mem_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.is_partition.exists_split_many_le", "description": " If `\u03c0` is a partition of `I`, then there exists a finite set `s` of hyperplanes such that\n`split_many I s \u2264 \u03c0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.box.split_lower_ne_split_upper", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.split_of_not_mem_Ioo", "description": "If `x \u2209 (I.lower i, I.upper i)`, then the hyperplane `{y | y i = x}` does not split `I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.sum_split_boxes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.is_partition.compl_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.exists_split_many_inf_eq_filter_of_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.inf_split_many", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.compl", "description": " If `\u03c0` is a prepartition of `I`, then `\u03c0.compl` is a prepartition of `I`\nsuch that `\u03c0.compl.Union = I \\ \u03c0.Union`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.compl_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.compl_congr", "description": " Since the definition of `box_integral.prepartition.compl` uses `Exists.some`,\nthe result depends only on `\u03c0.Union`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.split", "description": " The partition of `I : box \u03b9` into the boxes `I \u2229 {y | y \u2264 x i}` and `I \u2229 {y | x i < y}`.\nOne of these boxes can be empty, then this partition is just the single-box partition `\u22a4`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.proj_Iic_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.proj_Icc_eq_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Ici_extend_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Icc_extend_of_right_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.range_proj_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.proj_Iic_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.proj_Ici_surj_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strict_mono.strict_mono_on_Iic_extend", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strict_mono.strict_mono_on_Ici_extend", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.proj_Iic_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Iic_extend_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.proj_Ici_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.proj_Iic", "description": "Projection of `\u03b1` to the closed interval `]-\u221e, b]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.range_proj_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.proj_Icc_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.coe_proj_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name