ul\u2082_of_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_div_const'", "description": "A version of `measurable_div_const` that assumes `has_measurable_mul` instead of\n `has_measurable_div`. This can be nice to avoid unnecessary type-class assumptions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_measurable.mul'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable.pow_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.measurable_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_measurable_div_of_mul_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.ae_measurable_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_measurable_div", "description": " We say that a type `has_measurable_div` if `((/) c)` and `(/ c)` are measurable functions.\nFor a typeclass assuming measurability of `uncurry (/)` see `has_measurable_div\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_measurable_div.measurable_const_div", "description": " We say that a type `has_measurable_div` if `((/) c)` and `(/ c)` are measurable functions.\nFor a typeclass assuming measurability of `uncurry (/)` see `has_measurable_div\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_measurable_div.measurable_div_const", "description": " We say that a type `has_measurable_div` if `((/) c)` and `(/ c)` are measurable functions.\nFor a typeclass assuming measurability of `uncurry (/)` see `has_measurable_div\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_measurable.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_measurable.const_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.measurable_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_measurable_vadd_of_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_measurable_sub", "description": " We say that a type `has_measurable_sub` if `(\u03bb x, c - x)` and `(\u03bb x, x - c)` are measurable\nfunctions. For a typeclass assuming measurability of `uncurry (-)` see `has_measurable_sub\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ha