"", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_top.add_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_bot.zero_le_one_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_bot.add_lt_add_iff_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_top.coe_bit0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_bot.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_top.add_le_add_iff_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_top.contravariant_class_swap_add_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_hom.with_bot_map", "description": "A version of `with_bot.map` for `zero_hom`s", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.complete_copy_id_homeo", "description": " The identity between the type synonym `complete_copy s` (with its modified metric) and the\noriginal subtype `s` is a homeomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.aux_copy", "description": " A sequence of type synonyms of a given type `\u03b1`, useful in the proof of\n`exists_polish_space_forall_le` to endow each copy with a different topology.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.has_dist_complete_copy", "description": " A distance on a subset `s` of a metric space, designed to make it complete if `s` is open.\nIt is given by `dist' x y = dist x y + |1 / dist x s\u1d9c - 1 / dist y s\u1d9c|`, where the second term\nblows up close to the boundary to ensure that Cauchy sequences for `dist'` remain well\ninside `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.pi_countable", "description": "A countable product of Polish spaces is Polish.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.is_clopenable.compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "upgrade_polish_space", "description": " This definition endows a Polish space with a complete metric. Use it as:\n`letI := upgrade_polish_space \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space_of_complete_second_countable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.dist_complete_copy_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.sigma", "description": "A countable disjoint union of Polish spaces is Polish.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closed_embedding.polish_space", "description": "Given a closed embedding into a Polish space, the source space is also Polish.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space", "description": " A Polish space is a topological space with second countable topology, that can be endowed\nwith a metric for which it is complete.\nWe register an instance from complete second countable metric space to polish space, and not the\nother way around as this is the most common use case.\n\nTo endow a Polish space with a complete metric space structure, do `letI := upgrade_polish_space \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.second_countable", "description": " A Polish space is a topological space with second countable topology, that can be endowed\nwith a metric for which it is complete.\nWe register an instance from complete second countable metric space to polish space, and not the\nother way around as this is the most common use case.\n\nTo endow a Polish space with a complete metric space structure, do `letI := upgrade_polish_space \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.complete", "description": " A Polish space is a topological space with second countable topology, that can be endowed\nwith a metric for which it is complete.\nWe register an instance from complete second countable metric space to polish space, and not the\nother way around as this is the most common use case.\n\nTo endow a Polish space with a complete metric space structure, do `letI := upgrade_polish_space \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.is_clopenable", "description": " Given a closed set `s` in a Polish space, one can construct a finer Polish topology for\nwhich `s` is both open and closed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.polish_space", "description": "A closed subset of a Polish space is also Polish.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.complete_copy_metric_space", "description": " A metric space structure on a subset `s` of a metric space, designed to make it complete\nif `s` is open. It is given by `dist' x y = dist x y + |1 / dist x s\u1d9c - 1 / dist y s\u1d9c|`, where the\nsecond term blows up close to the boundary to ensure that Cauchy sequences for `dist'` remain well\ninside `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.complete_copy", "description": " A type synonym for a subset `s` of a metric space, on which we will construct another metric\nfor which it will be complete.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.exists_polish_space_forall_le", "description": " Given a Polish space, and countably many finer Polish topologies, there exists another Polish\ntopology which is finer than all of them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.polish_space_induced", "description": "Pulling back a Polish topology under an equiv gives again a Polish topology.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.complete_space_complete_copy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.dist_le_dist_complete_copy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space_metric", "description": "Construct on a Polish space a metric (compatible with the topology) which is complete.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.nat_fun", "description": "Without this instance, `polish_space (\u2115 \u2192 \u2115)` is not found by typeclass inference.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "upgraded_polish_space", "description": " A convenience class, for a Polish space endowed with a complete metric. No instance of this\nclass should be registered: It should be used as `letI := upgrade_polish_space \u03b1` to endow a Polish\nspace with a complete metric.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "upgraded_polish_space.to_metric_space", "description": " A convenience class, for a Polish space endowed with a complete metric. No instance of this\nclass should be registered: It should be used as `letI := upgrade_polish_space \u03b1` to endow a Polish\nspace with a complete metric.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "upgraded_polish_space.to_second_countable_topology", "description": " A convenience class, for a Polish space endowed with a complete metric. No instance of this\nclass should be registered: It should be used as `letI := upgrade_polish_space \u03b1` to endow a Polish\nspace with a complete metric.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "upgraded_polish_space.to_complete_space", "description": " A convenience class, for a Polish space endowed with a complete metric. No instance of this\nclass should be registered: It should be used as `letI := upgrade_polish_space \u03b1` to endow a Polish\nspace with a complete metric.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.is_clopenable", "description": " A set in a topological space is clopenable if there exists a finer Polish topology for which\nthis set is open and closed. It turns out that this notion is equivalent to being Borel-measurable,\nbut this is nontrivial (see `is_clopenable_iff_measurable_set`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.is_clopenable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.exists_nat_nat_continuous_surjective", "description": "Any nonempty Polish space is the continuous image of the fundamental space `\u2115 \u2192 \u2115`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.t2_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.is_clopenable.Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.polish_space", "description": "An open subset of a Polish space is also Polish.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polish_space.sum", "description": "The disjoint union of two Polish spaces is Polish.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_polish_space_metric", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.bounded_lt_inter_not_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.unbounded_le_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.unbounded_ge_univ", "descr