scription": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_deriv_within_at_arcsin_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.differentiable_on_arcsin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.deriv_arccos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.differentiable_at_arcsin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cont_diff_at_arcsin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_deriv_within_at_arcsin_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.differentiable_within_at_arccos_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.differentiable_within_at_arcsin_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_deriv_at_arcsin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cont_diff_at_arccos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.differentiable_within_at_arcsin_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_strict_deriv_at_arcsin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.deriv_arcsin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cont_diff_at_arcsin_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.differentiable_within_at_arccos_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.cont_diff_on_arccos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_deriv_within_at_arccos_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_deriv_within_at_arccos_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.c_mk", "description": " Helper when we need some `c.rel i j` (i.e. `complex_shape.down \u2115`),\ne.g. `c_mk n (n+1) rfl`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.h\u03c3'_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.h\u03c3'_naturality", "description": "The maps `h\u03c3' q n m hnm` are natural on the simplicial object", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.homotopy_H\u03c3_to_zero", "description": "`H\u03c3` is null homotopic", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.h\u03c3'_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.c", "description": " As we are using chain complexes indexed by `\u2115`, we shall need the relation\n`c` such `c m n` if and only if `n+1=m`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.map_h\u03c3'", "description": "The maps `h\u03c3' q n m hnm` are compatible with the application of additive functors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.map_H\u03c3", "description": "The null homotopic maps `H\u03c3` are compatible with the application of additive functors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.H\u03c3", "description": "The null homotopic map $(h\u03c3 q) \u2218 d + d \u2218 (h\u03c3 q)$", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.nat_trans_H\u03c3", "description": "For each q, `H\u03c3 q` is a natural transformation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.h\u03c3'", "description": "We can turn `h\u03c3` into a datum that can be passed to `null_homotopic_map'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.cs_down_0_not_rel_left", "description": "This lemma is meant to be used with `null_homotopic_map'_f_of_not_rel_left`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.H\u03c3_eq_zero", "description": "In degree `0`, the null homotopic map `H\u03c3` is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.h\u03c3'_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.h\u03c3", "description": " The sequence of maps which gives the null homotopic maps `H\u03c3` that shall be in\nthe inductive construction of the projections `P q : K[X] \u27f6 K[X]`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod_Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_cdf'", "description": " Conditional cdf of the measure given the value on `\u03b1`, as a plain function. This is an auxiliary\ndefinition used to define `cond_cdf`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.set_lintegral_pre_cdf_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measurable_measure_cond_cdf", "description": "The function `a \u21a6 (cond_cdf \u03c1 a).measure` is measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.Iic_snd_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_cdf", "description": "Conditional cdf of the measure given the value on `\u03b1`, as a Stieltjes function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.tendsto_cond_cdf_at_bot", "description": "The conditional cdf tends to 0 at -\u221e for all `a : \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lintegral_infi_directed_of_measurable", "description": "Monotone convergence for an infimum over a directed family and indexed by a countable type", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.tendsto_pre_cdf_at_bot_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "directed.sequence_anti", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.monotone_cond_cdf_rat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measure_cond_cdf_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_cdf_eq_cond_cdf_rat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measurable_cond_cdf_rat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.tendsto_Iic_snd_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.tendsto_cond_cdf_rat_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_cdf_set", "description": " A measurable set of elements of `\u03b1` such that `\u03c1` has a conditional cdf at all\n`a \u2208 cond_cdf_set`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measure_cond_cdf_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_cdf_rat_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.tendsto_pre_cdf_at_top_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_cdf_le_one", "description": "The conditional cdf is lower or equal to 1 for all `a : \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.has_cond_cdf", "description": " A product measure on `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u211d` is said to have a conditional cdf at `a : \u03b1` if `pre_cdf` is\nmonotone with limit 0 at -\u221e and 1 at +\u221e, and is right continuous.\nThis property holds almost everywhere (see `has_cond_cdf_ae`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.has_cond_cdf.mono", "description": " A product measure on `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u211d` is said to have a conditional cdf at `a : \u03b1` if `pre_cdf` is\nmonotone with limit 0 at -\u221e and 1 at +\u221e, and is right continuous.\nThis property holds almost everywhere (see `has_cond_cdf_ae`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.has_cond_cdf.le_one", "description": " A product measure on `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u211d` is said to have a conditional cdf at `a : \u03b1` if `pre_cdf` is\nmonotone with limit 0 at -\u221e and 1 at +\u221e, and is right continuous.\nThis property holds almost everywhere (see `has_cond_cdf_ae`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.has_cond_cdf.tendsto_at_top_one", "description": " A product measure on `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u211d` is said to have a conditional cdf at `a : \u03b1` if `pre_cdf` is\nmonotone with limit 0 at -\u221e and 1 at +\u221e, and is right continuous.\nThis property holds almost everywhere (see `has_cond_cdf_ae`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.has_cond_cdf.tendsto_at_bot_zero", "description": " A product measure on `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u211d` is said to have a conditional cdf at `a : \u03b1` if `pre_cdf` is\nmonotone with limit 0 at -\u221e and 1 at +\u221e, and is right continuous.\nThis property holds almost everywhere (see `has_cond_cdf_ae`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.has_cond_cdf.infi_rat_gt_eq", "description": " A product measure on `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u211d` is said to have a conditional cdf at `a : \u03b1` if `pre_cdf` is\nmonotone with limit 0 at -\u221e and 1 at +\u221e, and is right continuous.\nThis property holds almost everywhere (see `has_cond_cdf_ae`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.set_lintegral_infi_gt_pre_cdf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.continuous_within_at_cond_cdf'_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.Inter_Iic_rat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.mem_cond_cdf_set_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.integral_cond_cdf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.pre_cdf_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.tendsto_Iic_snd_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.of_real_cond_cdf_rat_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.Iic_snd_le_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.tendsto_lintegral_pre_cdf_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measurable_pre_cdf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measurable_cond_cdf", "description": "The conditional cdf is a measurable function of `a : \u03b1` for all `x : \u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.strongly_measurable_cond_cdf", "description": "The conditional cdf is a strongly measurable function of `a : \u03b1` for all `x : \u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_cdf_rat_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_cdf_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.set_lintegral_cond_cdf_rat", "description": "Auxiliary lemma for `set_lintegral_cond_cdf`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.infi_Iic_snd_gt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measurable_set_cond_cdf_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.has_cond_cdf_of_mem_cond_cdf_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.monotone_cond_cdf'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "directed.sequence_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.pre_cdf", "description": " `pre_cdf` is the Radon-Nikodym derivative of `\u03c1.Iic_snd` with respect to `\u03c1.fst` at each\n`r : \u211a`. This function `\u211a \u2192 \u03b1 \u2192 \u211d\u22650\u221e` is such that for almost all `a : \u03b1`, the function `\u211a \u2192 \u211d\u22650\u221e`\nsatisfies the properties of a cdf (monotone with limit 0 at -\u221e and 1 at +\u221e, right-continuous).\n\nWe define this function on `\u211a` and not `\u211d` because `\u211a` is countable, which allows us to prove\nproperties of the form `\u2200\u1d50 a \u2202\u03c1.fst, \u2200 q, P (pre_cdf q a)`, instead of the weaker\n`\u2200 q, \u2200\u1d50 a \u2202\u03c1.fst, P (pre_cdf q a)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_cdf_rat", "description": " Conditional cdf of the measure given the value on `\u03b1`, restricted to the rationals.\nIt is defined to be `pre_cdf` if `a \u2208 cond_cdf_set`, and a default cdf-like function\notherwise. This is an auxiliary definition used to define `cond_cdf`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.with_density_pre_cdf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_cdf_rat_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measure.measure_theory.is_probability_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_of_antitone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.has_cond_cdf_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.tendsto_cond_cdf_rat_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.Iic_snd_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.Iic_snd_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_cdf'_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.Union_Iic_rat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.of_real_cond_cdf_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_cdf_rat_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.tendsto_cond_cdf_at_top", "description": "The conditional cdf tends to 1 at +\u221e for all `a : \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.inf_gt_cond_cdf_rat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "at_bot_le_nhds_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.set_lintegral_cond_cdf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.Iic_snd", "description": "Measure on `\u03b1` such that for a measurable set `s`, `\u03c1.Iic_snd r s = \u03c1 (s \u00d7\u02e2 Iic r)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_cdf_rat_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_cdf'_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "at_top_le_nhds_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.bdd_below_range_cond_cdf_rat_gt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_cdf'_eq_cond_cdf_rat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.set_integral_cond_cdf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.Iic_snd_ac_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.monotone_pre_cdf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.tendsto_lintegral_pre_cdf_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.lintegral_cond_cdf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.of_real_cinfi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.is_finite_measure.Iic_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_cdf_nonneg", "description": "The conditional cdf is non-negative for all `a : \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.inf_gt_pre_cdf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.integrable_cond_cdf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.lt_fold_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_op_rel_iff_or", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_disj_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_min_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_fold_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_union_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_max_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_image_idem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold", "description": "`fold op b f s` folds the commutative associative operation `op` over the\n `f`-image of `s`, i.e. `fold (+) b f {1,2,3} = f 1 + f 2 + f 3 + b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_op_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_min_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_op_rel_iff_and", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_insert_idem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_union_empty_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_max_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.lt_fold_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_max_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_disj_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.le_fold_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_ite'", "description": " A stronger version of `finset.fold_ite`, but relies on\nan explicit proof of idempotency on the seed element, rather\nthan relying on typeclass idempotency over the whole type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_sup_bot_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.fold_ite", "description": " A weaker version of `finset.fold_ite'`,\nrelying on typeclass idempotency over the whole type,\ninstead of solely on the seed element.\nHowever, this is easier to use because it does not generate side goals.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imo1962_q1.case_3_digit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q1.without_digits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q1.case_0_digit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q1.case_2_digit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q1.case_more_digits", "description": "`linarith` fails on numbers this large, so this lemma spells out some of the arithmetic\nthat normally would be automated.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q1.helper_5_digit", "description": "Putting this inline causes a deep recursion error, so we separate it out.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q1.case_1_digit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q1.no_smaller_solutions", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q1.case_5_digit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q1.problem_predicate'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q1.satisfied_by_153846", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q1.problem_predicate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q1.case_4_digit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "Module.forget\u2082_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.as_hom_left", "description": "Reinterpreting a linear map in the category of `R`-modules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.to_Module_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.comp_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.has_coe_to_sort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.of_self_iso", "description": " Forgetting to the underlying type and then building the bundled object returns the original\nmodule.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso.to_linear_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.forget\u2082_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.forget\u2082_AddCommGroup_additive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.to_Module_iso'_left_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.to_Module_iso'_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.Module_concrete_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso.to_linear_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.of", "description": "The object in the category of R-modules associated to an R-module", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.is_zero_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv_iso_Module_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.to_Module_iso'_right_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.of_self_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.of_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.coe_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.iso.hom_congr_eq_arrow_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.to_Module_iso'_left", "description": "Build an isomorphism in the category `Module R` from a `linear_equiv` between `module`s.\n\nThis version is better than `linear_equiv_to_Module_iso` when applicable, because Lean can't see\n`Module.of R M` is defeq to `M` when `M : Module R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.to_Module_iso'_right_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.as_hom_right", "description": "Reinterpreting a linear map in the category of `R`-modules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.of_self_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.category_theory.linear", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv_iso_Module_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.forget\u2082_obj_Module_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.of_hom", "description": "Typecheck a `linear_map` as a morphism in `Module R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.to_Module_iso'", "description": "Build an isomorphism in the category `Module R` from a `linear_equiv` between `module`s.\n\nThis version is better than `linear_equiv_to_Module_iso` when applicable, because Lean can't see\n`Module.of R M` is defeq to `M` when `M : Module R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.category_theory.limits.has_zero_object", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.to_Module_iso", "description": "Build an isomorphism in the category `Module R` from a `linear_equiv` between `module`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.to_Module_iso'_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.as_hom", "description": "Reinterpreting a linear map in the category of `R`-modules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.of_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.category_theory.preadditive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.has_forget_to_AddCommGroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.to_Module_iso'_left_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.to_Module_iso'_right", "description": "Build an isomorphism in the category `Module R` from a `linear_equiv` between `module`s.\n\nThis version is better than `linear_equiv_to_Module_iso` when applicable, because Lean can't see\n`Module.of R M` is defeq to `M` when `M : Module R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module", "description": " The category of R-modules and their morphisms.\n\n Note that in the case of `R = \u2124`, we can not\nimpose here that the `\u2124`-multiplication field from the module structure is defeq to the one coming\nfrom the `is_add_comm_group` structure (contrary to what we do for all module structures in\nmathlib), which creates some difficulties down the road.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.carrier", "description": " The category of R-modules and their morphisms.\n\n Note that in the case of `R = \u2124`, we can not\nimpose here that the `\u2124`-multiplication field from the module structure is defeq to the one coming\nfrom the `is_add_comm_group` structure (contrary to what we do for all module structures in\nmathlib), which creates some difficulties down the road.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.is_add_comm_group", "description": " The category of R-modules and their morphisms.\n\n Note that in the case of `R = \u2124`, we can not\nimpose here that the `\u2124`-multiplication field from the module structure is defeq to the one coming\nfrom the `is_add_comm_group` structure (contrary to what we do for all module structures in\nmathlib), which creates some difficulties down the road.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.is_module", "description": " The category of R-modules and their morphisms.\n\n Note that in the case of `R = \u2124`, we can not\nimpose here that the `\u2124`-multiplication field from the module structure is defeq to the one coming\nfrom the `is_add_comm_group` structure (contrary to what we do for all module structures in\nmathlib), which creates some difficulties down the road.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.to_Module_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.iso.conj_eq_conj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso.to_linear_equiv", "description": "Build a `linear_equiv` from an isomorphism in the category `Module R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv_iso_Module_iso", "description": " linear equivalences between `module`s are the same as (isomorphic to) isomorphisms\nin `Module`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.linear_map_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.Module_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_abs_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable.abs", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `summable_abs_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_ne_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_has_sum_of_le_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_strict_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_le_of_sum_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_lt_tsum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_tsum'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_of_is_lub_of_nonneg", "description