or that distributes across multiplication.\n\nThis is useful for dealing with submonoids of a ring that contain `-1` without having to duplicate\nlemmas.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_distrib_neg.neg_neg", "description": " Typeclass for a negation operator that distributes across multiplication.\n\nThis is useful for dealing with submonoids of a ring that contain `-1` without having to duplicate\nlemmas.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_distrib_neg.neg_mul", "description": " Typeclass for a negation operator that distributes across multiplication.\n\nThis is useful for dealing with submonoids of a ring that contain `-1` without having to duplicate\nlemmas.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_distrib_neg.mul_neg", "description": " Typeclass for a negation operator that distributes across multiplication.\n\nThis is useful for dealing with submonoids of a ring that contain `-1` without having to duplicate\nlemmas.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_semiring.to_semigroup_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_semiring.to_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_semiring.to_non_unital_non_assoc_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_non_assoc_ring.to_has_distrib_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_comm_ring.to_non_unital_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_domain", "description": "A domain is a nontrivial semiring such multiplication by a non zero element is cancellative,\n on both sides. In other words, a nontrivial semiring `R` satisfying\n `\u2200 {a b c : R}, a \u2260 0 \u2192 a * b = a * c \u2192 b = c` and\n `\u2200 {a b c : R}, b \u2260 0 \u2192 a * b = c * b \u2192 a = c`.\n\n This is implemented as a mixin for `semiring \u03b1`.\n To obtain an integral domain use `[comm_ring \u03b1] [is_domain \u03b1]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_domain.mul_left_cancel_of_ne_zero", "description": "A domain is a nontrivial semiring such multiplication by a non zero element is cancellative,\n on both sides. In other words, a nontrivial semiring `R` satisfying\n `\u2200 {a b c : R}, a \u2260 0 \u2192 a * b = a * c \u2192 b = c` and\n `\u2200 {a b c : R}, b \u2260 0 \u2192 a * b = c * b \u2192 a = c`.\n\n This is implemented as a mixin for `semiring \u03b1`.\n To obtain an integral domain use `[comm_ring \u03b1] [is_domain \u03b1]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_domain.mul_right_cancel_of_ne_zero", "description": "A domain is a nontrivial semiring such multiplication by a non zero element is cancellative,\n on both sides. In other words, a nontrivial semiring `R` satisfying\n `\u2200 {a b c : R}, a \u2260 0 \u2192 a * b = a * c \u2192 b = c` and\n `\u2200 {a b c : R}, b \u2260 0 \u2192 a * b = c * b \u2192 a = c`.\n\n This is implemented as a mixin for `semiring \u03b1`.\n To obtain an integral domain use `[comm_ring \u03b1] [is_domain \u03b1]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_domain.exists_pair_ne", "description": "A domain is a nontrivial semiring such multiplication by a non zero element is cancellative,\n on both sides. In other words, a nontrivial semiring `R` satisfying\n `\u2200 {a b c : R}, a \u2260 0 \u2192 a * b = a * c \u2192 b = c` and\n `\u2200 {a b c : R}, b \u2260 0 \u2192 a * b = c * b \u2192 a = c`.\n\n This is implemented as a mixin for `semiring \u03b1`.\n To obtain an integral domain use `[comm_ring \u03b1] [is_domain \u03b1]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "distrib.to_has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_assoc_ring.to_non_unital_non_assoc_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "distrib_three_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_distrib_class", "description": "A typeclass stating that multiplication is left distributive over addition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_distrib_class.left_distrib", "description": "A typec