roup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_non_assoc_semiring.to_add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_non_assoc_semiring", "description": "A not-necessarily-unital, not-necessarily-associative semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_non_assoc_semiring.add", "description": "A not-necessarily-unital, not-necessarily-associative semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_non_assoc_semiring.add_assoc", "description": "A not-necessarily-unital, not-necessarily-associative semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_non_assoc_semiring.zero", "description": "A not-necessarily-unital, not-necessarily-associative semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_non_assoc_semiring.zero_add", "description": "A not-necessarily-unital, not-necessarily-associative semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_non_assoc_semiring.add_zero", "description": "A not-necessarily-unital, not-necessarily-associative semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_non_assoc_semiring.nsmul", "description": "A not-necessarily-unital, not-necessarily-associative semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_non_assoc_semiring.nsmul_zero'", "description": "A not-necessarily-unital, not-necessarily-associative semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_non_assoc_semiring.nsmul_succ'", "description": "A not-necessarily-unital, not-necessarily-associative semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_non_assoc_semiring.add_comm", "description": "A not-necessarily-unital, not-necessarily-associative semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_non_assoc_semiring.mul", "description": "A not-necessarily-unital, not-necessarily-associative semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_non_assoc_semiring.left_distrib", "description": "A not-necessarily-unital, not-necessarily-associative semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_non_assoc_semiring.right_distrib", "description": "A not-necessarily-unital, not-necessarily-associative semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_non_assoc_semiring.zero_mul", "description": "A not-necessarily-unital, not-necessarily-associative semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_non_assoc_semiring.mul_zero", "description": "A not-necessarily-unital, not-necessarily-associative semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_add", "description": "**Alias** of `left_distrib`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_bot_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_fun.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_sets_of_indep_sets_of_le_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_sets", "description": " Two sets of sets `s\u2081, s\u2082` are independent with respect to a measure `\u03bc` if for any sets\n`t\u2081 \u2208 p\u2081, t\u2082 \u2208 s\u2082`, then `\u03bc (t\u2081 \u2229 t\u2082) = \u03bc (t\u2081) * \u03bc (t\u2082)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_fun.indep_fun_finset_sum_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_sets_singleton_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep", "description": " A family of measurable space structures (i.e. of \u03c3-algebras) is independent with respect to a\nmeasure `\u03bc` (typically defined on a finer \u03c3-algebra) if the family of sets of measurable sets they\ndefine is independent. `m : \u03b9 \u2192 measurable_space \u03a9` is independent with respect to measure `\u03bc` if\nfor any finite set of indices `s = {i_1, ..., i_n}`, for any sets\n`f i_1 \u2208 m i_1, ..., f i_n \u2208 m i_n`, then `\u03bc (\u22c2 i in s, f i) = \u220f i in s, \u03bc (f i) `.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_set_iff_measure_inter_eq_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_fun_iff_measure_inter_preimage_eq_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_set_empty_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_sets", "description": " A family of sets of sets `\u03c0 : \u03b9 \u2192 set (set \u03a9)` is independent with respect to a measure `\u03bc` if\nfor any finite set of indices `s = {i_1, ..., i_n}`, for any sets\n`f i_1 \u2208 \u03c0 i_1, ..., f i_n \u2208 \u03c0 i_n`, then `\u03bc (\u22c2 i in s, f i) = \u220f i in s, \u03bc (f i) `.\nIt will be used for families of pi_systems.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_of_indep_of_le_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_set_iff_Indep_sets_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_supr_of_antitone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_sets.indep_set_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_fun.indep_fun_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_supr_of_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_set", "description": " A family of sets is independent if the family of measurable space structures they generate is\nindependent. For a set `s`, the generated measurable space has measurable sets `\u2205, s, s\u1d9c, univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_set_iff_measure_Inter_eq_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_of_indep_of_le_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_fun.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_set.indep_generate_from_le_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_fun.indep_fun_prod_range_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_set.indep_generate_from_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_fun", "description": " A family of functions defined on the same space `\u03a9` and taking values in possibly different\nspaces, each with a measurable space structure, is independent if the family of measurable space\nstructures they generate on `\u03a9` is independent. For a function `g` with codomain having measurable\nspace structure `m`, the generated measurable space structure is `measurable_space.comap g m`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_sets.pi_Union_Inter_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_bot_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_fun.indep_fun_sum_range_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_fun.indep_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_set", "description": " Two sets are independent if the two measurable space structures they generate are independent.\nFor a set `s`, the generated measurable space structure has measurable sets `\u2205, s, s\u1d9c, univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_fun", "description": " Two functions are independent if the two measurable space structures they generate are\nindependent. For a function `f` with codomain having measurable space structure `m`, the generated\nmeasurable space structure is `measurable_space.comap f m`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_fun_iff_indep_set_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_fun.indep_fun_finset_prod_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_set.indep_generate_from_of_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep.Indep_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_sets.indep'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_set.Indep_fun_indicator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_iff_forall_indep_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_sets.Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep.indep_set_of_measurable_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_fun.indep_fun_finset", "description": " If `f` is a family of mutually independent random variables (`Indep_fun m f \u03bc`) and `S, T` are\ntwo disjoint finite index sets, then the tuple formed by `f i` for `i \u2208 S` is independent of the\ntuple `(f i)_i` for `i \u2208 T`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_fun.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_sets.meas_Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_sets.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_fun.ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep.indep_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep.indep", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_supr_of_monotone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_set.indep_generate_from_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_sets.indep", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_set_empty_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_sets.inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_sets.bInter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_sets_pi_Union_Inter_of_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_sets.bUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_sets.Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_sets.Indep_set_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_sets_singleton_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_sets.Indep", "description": "The measurable space structures generated by independent pi-systems are independent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_fun_iff_measure_inter_preimage_eq_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_set.Indep_comap_mem", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `probability_theory.Indep_comap_mem_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_supr_of_directed_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_sets_of_indep_sets_of_le_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep", "description": " Two measurable space structures (or \u03c3-algebras) `m\u2081, m\u2082` are independent with respect to a\nmeasure `\u03bc` (defined on a third \u03c3-algebra) if for any sets `t\u2081 \u2208 m\u2081, t\u2082 \u2208 m\u2082`,\n`\u03bc (t\u2081 \u2229 t\u2082) = \u03bc (t\u2081) * \u03bc (t\u2082)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_set_iff_indep_sets_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_sets.indep_sets", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_fun.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_sets.union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_comap_mem_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_sets.union_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dioph.ne_dioph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dioph.dioph_fn_vec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "poly", "description": "The type of multivariate integer polynomials", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "poly.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "poly.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dioph.const_dioph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dioph.inject_dummies_lem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "poly.neg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dioph.modeq_dioph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dioph.proj_dioph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "poly.ext", "description": "Extensionality for `poly \u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "poly.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "poly.coe_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "poly.is_poly", "description": "The underlying function of a `poly` is a polynomial", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "poly.sumsq", "description": "The sum of squares of a list of polynomials. This is relevant for\n Diophantine equations, because it means that a list of equations\n can be encoded as a single equation: `x = 0 \u2227 y = 0 \u2227 z = 0` is\n equivalent to `x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dioph.dioph_pfun_vec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dioph.dom_dioph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dioph.reindex_dioph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dioph.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "poly.const_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dioph.eq_dioph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dioph.union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dioph.mod_dioph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "poly.map", "description": "Map the index set of variables, replacing `x_i` with `x_(f i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "poly.fun_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dioph.pow_dioph", "description": "A version of **Matiyasevic's theorem**", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dioph.ex_dioph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "poly.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name