d `b` if `a` and `b` both\ncover `a \u2293 b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_lower_modular_lattice.to_is_weak_lower_modular_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sup_lt_sup_of_lt_of_inf_le_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_modular_lattice_iff_inf_sup_inf_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covby_sup_of_inf_covby_of_inf_covby_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.is_upper_modular_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inf_covby_of_covby_sup_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inf_strict_mono_on_Icc_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inf_Icc_order_iso_Icc_sup", "description": "The diamond isomorphism between the intervals `[a \u2293 b, a]` and `[b, a \u2294 b]`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compl.Iic_order_iso_Ici", "description": "The diamond isomorphism between the intervals `set.Iic a` and `set.Ici b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covby.inf_of_sup_right", "description": "**Alias** of `inf_covby_of_covby_sup_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covby.sup_of_inf_left", "description": "**Alias** of `covby_sup_of_inf_covby_left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inf_Ioo_order_iso_Ioo_sup", "description": "The diamond isomorphism between the intervals `]a \u2293 b, a[` and `}b, a \u2294 b[`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inf_Icc_order_iso_Icc_sup_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sup_strict_mono_on_Icc_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.lift", "description": "A morphism in `C` lifts to a chain map between projective resolutions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.homotopy_equiv", "description": "Any two projective resolutions are homotopy equivalent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.lift_id_homotopy", "description": "The lift of the identity morphism is homotopic to the identity chain map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.\u03c0_f_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.lift_homotopy_zero_succ", "description": "An auxiliary definition for `lift_homotopy_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.homotopy_equiv_inv_\u03c0_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.complex_d_succ_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.projective_resolutions", "description": "Taking projective resolutions is functorial,\nif considered with target the homotopy category\n(`\u2115`-indexed chain complexes and chain maps up to homotopy).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution", "description": "A `ProjectiveResolution Z` consists of a bundled `\u2115`-indexed chain complex of projective objects,\nalong with a quasi-isomorphism to the complex consisting of just `Z` supported in degree `0`.\n\n(We don't actually ask here that the chain map is a quasi-iso, just exactness everywhere:\nthat `\u03c0` is a quasi-iso is a lemma when the category is abelian.\nShould we just ask for it here?)\n\nExcept in situations where you want to provide a particular projective resolution\n(for example to compute a derived functor),\nyou will not typically need to use this bundled object, and will instead use\n* `projective_resolution Z`: the `\u2115`-indexed chain complex\n  (equipped with `projective` and `exact` instances)\n* `projective_resolution.\u03c0 Z`: the chain map from `projective_resolution Z` to\n  `(single C _ 0).obj Z` (all the components are equipped with `epi` instances,\n  and when the category is `abelian` we will show `\u03c0` is a quasi-iso).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.complex", "description": "A `ProjectiveResolution Z` consists of a bundled `\u2115`-indexed chain complex of projective objects,\nalong with a quasi-isomorphism to the complex consisting of just `Z` supported in degree `0`.\n\n(We don't actually ask here that the chain map is a quasi-iso, just exactness everywhere:\nthat `\u03c0` is a quasi-iso is a lemma when the category is abelian.\nShould we just ask for it here?)\n\nExcept in situations where you want to provide a particular projective resolution\n(for example to compute a derived functor),\nyou will not typically need to use this bundled object, and will instead use\n* `projective_resolution Z`: the `\u2115`-indexed chain complex\n  (equipped with `projective` and `exact` instances)\n* `projective_resolution.\u03c0 Z`: the chain map from `projective_resolution Z` to\n  `(single C _ 0).obj Z` (all the components are equipped with `epi` instances,\n  and when the category is `abelian` we will show `\u03c0` is a quasi-iso).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.\u03c0", "description": "A `ProjectiveResolution Z` consists of a bundled `\u2115`-indexed chain complex of projective objects,\nalong with a quasi-isomorphism to the complex consisting of just `Z` supported in degree `0`.\n\n(We don't actually ask here that the chain map is a quasi-iso, just exactness everywhere:\nthat `\u03c0` is a quasi-iso is a lemma when the category is abelian.\nShould we just ask for it here?)\n\nExcept in situations where you want to provide a particular projective resolution\n(for example to compute a derived functor),\nyou will not typically need to use this bundled object, and will instead use\n* `projective_resolution Z`: the `\u2115`-indexed chain complex\n  (equipped with `projective` and `exact` instances)\n* `projective_resolution.\u03c0 Z`: the chain map from `projective_resolution Z` to\n  `(single C _ 0).obj Z` (all the components are equipped with `epi` instances,\n  and when the category is `abelian` we will show `\u03c0` is a quasi-iso).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.projective", "description": "A `ProjectiveResolution Z` consists of a bundled `\u2115`-indexed chain complex of projective objects,\nalong with a quasi-isomorphism to the complex consisting of just `Z` supported in degree `0`.\n\n(We don't actually ask here that the chain map is a quasi-iso, just exactness everywhere:\nthat `\u03c0` is a quasi-iso is a lemma when the category is abelian.\nShould we just ask for it here?)\n\nExcept in situations where you want to provide a particular projective resolution\n(for example to compute a derived functor),\nyou will not typically need to use this bundled object, and will instead use\n* `projective_resolution Z`: the `\u2115`-indexed chain complex\n  (equipped with `projective` and `exact` instances)\n* `projective_resolution.\u03c0 Z`: the chain map from `projective_resolution Z` to\n  `(single C _ 0).obj Z` (all the components are equipped with `epi` instances,\n  and when the category is `abelian` we will show `\u03c0` is a quasi-iso).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.exact\u2080", "description": "A `ProjectiveResolution Z` consists of a bundled `\u2115`-indexed chain complex of projective objects,\nalong with a quasi-isomorphism to the complex consisting of just `Z` supported in degree `0`.\n\n(We don't actually ask here that the chain map is a quasi-iso, just exactness everywhere:\nthat `\u03c0` is a quasi-iso is a lemma when the category is abelian.\nShould we just ask for it here?)\n\nExcept in situations where you want to provide a particular projective resolution\n(for example to compute a derived functor),\nyou will not typically need to use this bundled object, and will instead use\n* `projective_resolution Z`: the `\u2115`-indexed chain complex\n  (equipped with `projective` and `exact` instances)\n* `projective_resolution.\u03c0 Z`: the chain map from `projective_resolution Z` to\n  `(single C _ 0).obj Z` (all the components are equipped with `epi` instances,\n  and when the category is `abelian` we will show `\u03c0` is a quasi-iso).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.exact", "description": "A `ProjectiveResolution Z` consists of a bundled `\u2115`-indexed chain complex of projective objects,\nalong with a quasi-isomorphism to the complex consisting of just `Z` supported in degree `0`.\n\n(We don't actually ask here that the chain map is a quasi-iso, just exactness everywhere:\nthat `\u03c0` is a quasi-iso is a lemma when the category is abelian.\nShould we just ask for it here?)\n\nExcept in situations where you want to provide a particular projective resolution\n(for example to compute a derived functor),\nyou will not typically need to use this bundled object, and will instead use\n* `projective_resolution Z`: the `\u2115`-indexed chain complex\n  (equipped with `projective` and `exact` instances)\n* `projective_resolution.\u03c0 Z`: the chain map from `projective_resolution Z` to\n  `(single C _ 0).obj Z` (all the components are equipped with `epi` instances,\n  and when the category is `abelian` we will show `\u03c0` is a quasi-iso).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.epi", "description": "A `ProjectiveResolution Z` consists of a bundled `\u2115`-indexed chain complex of projective objects,\nalong with a quasi-isomorphism to the complex consisting of just `Z` supported in degree `0`.\n\n(We don't actually ask here that the chain map is a quasi-iso, just exactness everywhere:\nthat `\u03c0` is a quasi-iso is a lemma when the category is abelian.\nShould we just ask for it here?)\n\nExcept in situations where you want to provide a particular projective resolution\n(for example to compute a derived functor),\nyou will not typically need to use this bundled object, and will instead use\n* `projective_resolution Z`: the `\u2115`-indexed chain complex\n  (equipped with `projective` and `exact` instances)\n* `projective_resolution.\u03c0 Z`: the chain map from `projective_resolution Z` to\n  `(single C _ 0).obj Z` (all the components are equipped with `epi` instances,\n  and when the category is `abelian` we will show `\u03c0` is a quasi-iso).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.lift_f_one_zero_comm", "description": "Auxiliary lemma for `lift`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.lift_commutes", "description": "The resolution maps intertwine the lift of a morphism and that morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.lift_commutes_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.has_projective_resolutions", "description": "You will rarely use this typeclass directly: it is implied by the combination\n`[enough_projectives C]` and `[abelian C]`.\nBy itself it's enough to set up the basic theory of derived functors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.has_projective_resolutions.out", "description": "You will rarely use this typeclass directly: it is implied by the combination\n`[enough_projectives C]` and `[abelian C]`.\nBy itself it's enough to set up the basic theory of derived functors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.lift_homotopy_zero_one", "description": "An auxiliary definition for `lift_homotopy_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.self", "description": "A projective object admits a trivial projective resolution: itself in degree 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.lift_homotopy_zero_zero", "description": "An auxiliary definition for `lift_homotopy_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.lift_f_succ", "description": "Auxiliary construction for `lift`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.complex_d_comp_\u03c0_f_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ProjectiveResolution.lift_homotopy_zero", "description": "Any lift of the zero morphism is homotopic to zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {