ence between sesquilinear forms and `n \u00d7 m` matrices", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.nondegenerate_to_matrix\u2082'_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_matrix'_to_linear_map\u209b\u2097\u2082'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_skew_adjoint", "description": " The condition for a square matrix `A` to be skew-adjoint with respect to the square matrix\n`J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_linear_map\u209b\u2097\u2082'_to_matrix'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_matrix\u2082_aux", "description": " The linear map from sesquilinear forms to `matrix n m R` given an `n`-indexed basis for `M\u2081`\nand an `m`-indexed basis for `M\u2082`.\n\nThis is an auxiliary definition for the equivalence `matrix.to_linear_map\u209b\u2097\u2082'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_linear_map\u209b\u2097\u2082'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_matrix\u2082'_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_self_adjoint_matrices_submodule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_linear_map\u2082_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_matrix\u2082_aux_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_matrix\u2082", "description": " `linear_map.to_matrix\u2082 b\u2081 b\u2082` is the equivalence between `R`-bilinear forms on `M` and\n`n`-by-`n` matrices with entries in `R`, if `b` is an `R`-basis for `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_linear_map\u2082'_to_matrix'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_linear_map\u2082_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_linear_map\u2082_compl\u2081\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char.val_of_nat_eq_of_is_valid", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "char.of_nat_eq_of_not_is_valid", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "char.val_of_nat_eq_of_not_is_valid", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "char.of_nat_ne_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_of_is_pushout_fst_of_normal", "description": "The first leg of a pushout cocone is a normal epimorphism if the left component is too.\n\nSee also `pushout.fst_of_epi` for the basic epimorphism version, and\n`normal_of_is_pushout_snd_of_normal` for the flipped version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_of_is_pullback_fst_of_normal", "description": "The first leg of a pullback cone is a normal monomorphism if the left component is too.\n\nSee also `pullback.fst_of_mono` for the basic monomorphism version, and\n`normal_of_is_pullback_snd_of_normal` for the flipped version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_mono.regular_mono", "description": "Every normal monomorphism is a regular monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_mono.lift'", "description": "If `f` is a normal mono, then any map `k : W \u27f6 Y` such that `k \u226b normal_mono.g = 0` induces\n   a morphism `l : W \u27f6 X` such that `l \u226b f = k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_of_is_pushout_snd_of_normal", "description": "The second leg of a pushout cocone is a normal epimorphism if the right component is too.\n\nSee also `pushout.snd_of_epi` for the basic epimorphism version, and\n`normal_of_is_pushout_fst_of_normal` for the flipped version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_epi_of_epi", "description": "In a category in which every epimorphism is normal, we can express every epimorphism as\n   a kernel. This is not an instance because it would create an instance loop.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_mono_of_normal_epi_unop", "description": "A normal epi becomes a normal mono in the opposite category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_epi", "description": "A normal epimorphism is a morphism which is the cokernel of some morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_epi.W", "description": "A normal epimorphism is a morphism which is the cokernel of some morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_epi.g", "description": "A normal epimorphism is a morphism which is the cokernel of some morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_epi.w", "description": "A normal epimorphism is a morphism which is the cokernel of some morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_epi.is_colimit", "description": "A normal epimorphism is a morphism which is the cokernel of some morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_mono_category_of_normal_mono_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_mono_category", "description": "A normal mono category is a category in which every monomorphism is normal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_mono_category.normal_mono_of_mono", "description": "A normal mono category is a category in which every monomorphism is normal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_epi.regular_epi", "description": "Every normal epimorphism is a regular epimorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_epi_category_of_normal_epi_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence_reflects_normal_epi", "description": "If `F` is an equivalence and `F.map f` is a normal epi, then `f` is a normal epi.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence_reflects_normal_mono", "description": "If `F` is an equivalence and `F.map f` is a normal mono, then `f` is a normal mono.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_mono", "description": "A normal monomorphism is a morphism which is the kernel of some morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_mono.Z", "description": "A normal monomorphism is a morphism which is the kernel of some morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_mono.g", "description": "A normal monomorphism is a morphism which is the kernel of some morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_mono.w", "description": "A normal monomorphism is a morphism which is the kernel of some morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_mono.is_limit", "description": "A normal monomorphism is a morphism which is the kernel of some morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_mono_of_mono", "description": "In a category in which every monomorphism is normal, we can express every monomorphism as\n   a kernel. This is not an instance because it would create an instance loop.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_epi_category", "description": "A normal epi category is a category in which every epimorphism is normal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_epi_category.normal_epi_of_epi", "description": "A normal epi category is a category in which every epimorphism is normal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_epi_of_normal_mono_unop", "description": "A normal mono becomes a normal epi in the opposite category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_of_is_pullback_snd_of_normal", "description": "The second leg of a pullback cone is a normal monomorphism if the right component is too.\n\nSee also `pullback.snd_of_mono` for the basic monomorphism version, and\n`normal_of_is_pullback_fst_of_normal` for the flipped version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.normal_epi.desc'", "description": "If `f` is a normal epi, then every morphism `k : X \u27f6 W` satisfying `normal_epi.g \u226b k = 0`\n   induces `l : Y \u27f6 W` such that `f \u226b l = k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Union_smul_eq_set_of_exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.vadd_set_sdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.Inter_vadd_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.mul_action", "description": " A multiplic