map_left_comm", "description": "Symmetric statement to `filter.map_map\u2082_distrib_left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_map\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_distrib_le_left", "description": "The other direction does not hold because of the `f`-`f` cross terms on the RHS.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_map\u2082_right_comm", "description": "Symmetric statement to `filter.map_map\u2082_distrib_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.ne_bot.map\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_sup_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_map\u2082_distrib_left", "description": "Symmetric statement to `filter.map\u2082_map_left_comm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_map\u2082_antidistrib_left", "description": "Symmetric statement to `filter.map\u2082_map_left_anticomm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2083", "description": " The image of a ternary function `m : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b3 \u2192 \u03b4` as a function\n`filter \u03b1 \u2192 filter \u03b2 \u2192 filter \u03b3 \u2192 filter \u03b4`. Mathematically this should be thought of as the image\nof the corresponding function `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2 \u00d7 \u03b3 \u2192 \u03b4`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_bot_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_bot_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_distrib_le_right", "description": "The other direction does not hold because of the `h`-`h` cross terms on the RHS.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_mono_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_map\u2082_distrib_right", "description": "Symmetric statement to `filter.map_map\u2082_right_comm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_map\u2082_right_anticomm", "description": "Symmetric statement to `filter.map_map\u2082_antidistrib_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_eq_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.ne_bot.of_map\u2082_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_inf_subset_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_mono_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_left_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.ne_bot.of_map\u2082_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_map\u2082_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_prod_eq_map\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_right_identity", "description": " If `b` is a right identity for `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b1`, then `pure b` is a right identity for\n`filter.map\u2082 f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_mk_eq_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_map\u2082_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_map_left_anticomm", "description": "Symmetric statement to `filter.map_map\u2082_antidistrib_left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_right_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_left_identity", "description": " If `a` is a left identity for `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b2`, then `pure a` is a left identity for\n`filter.map\u2082 f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_pure_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_map\u2082_antidistrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_map\u2082_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_map\u2082_antidistrib_right", "description": "Symmetric statement to `filter.map_map\u2082_right_anticomm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map\u2082_pure_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {