", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.range_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.to_subalgebra_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.star_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.coe_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.star_closure_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.subtype_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_alg_hom.ext_adjoin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.star_adjoin_comm", "description": "The star operation on `subalgebra` commutes with `algebra.adjoin`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.mem_sup_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.adjoin_induction", "description": " If some predicate holds for all `x \u2208 (s : set A)` and this predicate is closed under the\n`algebra_map`, addition, multiplication and star operations, then it holds for `a \u2208 adjoin R s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.coe_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.map_le_iff_le_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.to_subalgebra_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.adjoin_induction'", "description": "The difference with `star_subalgebra.adjoin_induction` is that this acts on the subtype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.subsemiring_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.centralizer_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.mul_mem_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.range_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.mem_sup_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.coe_copy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_subalgebra.map_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle.smooth_manifold_with_corners", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.sphere.charted_space", "description": " The unit sphere in an `n + 1`-dimensional inner product space `E` is a charted space\nmodelled on the Euclidean space of dimension `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereo_to_fun_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_coe_sphere", "description": "The inclusion map (i.e., `coe`) from the sphere in `E` to `E` is smooth.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_stereo_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereographic_neg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereographic_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereographic_apply_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_stereo_inv_fun_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereo_to_fun", "description": " Stereographic projection, forward direction. This is a map from an inner product space `E` to\nthe orthogonal complement of an element `v` of `E`. It is smooth away from the affine hyperplane\nthrough `v` parallel to the orthogonal complement.  It restricts on the sphere to the stereographic\nprojection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereo_inv_fun_ne_north_pole", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereo_inv_fun_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "range_mfderiv_coe_sphere", "description": " Consider the differential of the inclusion of the sphere in `E` at the point `v` as a continuous\nlinear map from `tangent_space (\ud835\udce1 n) v` to `E`.  The range of this map is the orthogonal complement\nof `v` in `E`.\n\nNote that there is an abuse here of the defeq between `E` and the tangent space to `E` at `(v:E`).\nIn general this defeq is not canonical, but in this case (the tangent space of a vector space) it is\ncanonical.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mfderiv_coe_sphere_injective", "description": " Consider the differential of the inclusion of the sphere in `E` at the point `v` as a continuous\nlinear map from `tangent_space (\ud835\udce1 n) v` to `E`.  This map is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereographic'", "description": " Variant of the stereographic projection, for the sphere in an `n + 1`-dimensional inner product\nspace `E`.  This version has codomain the Euclidean space of dimension `n`, and is obtained by\ncomposing the original sterographic projection (`stereographic`) with an arbitrary linear isometry\nfrom `(\u211d \u2219 v)\u15ee` to the Euclidean space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereographic_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereo_right_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereo_inv_fun_aux_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.sphere.smooth_manifold_with_corners", "description": " The unit sphere in an `n + 1`-dimensional inner product space `E` is a smooth manifold,\nmodelled on the Euclidean space of dimension `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_stereo_inv_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at_stereo_inv_fun_aux_comp_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereographic'_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle.lie_group", "description": "The unit circle in `\u2102` is a Lie group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereo_left_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereographic'_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereographic_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereo_inv_fun", "description": " Stereographic projection, reverse direction.  This is a map from the orthogonal complement of a\nunit vector `v` in an inner product space `E` to the unit sphere in `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sphere_ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle.charted_space", "description": " The unit circle in `\u2102` is a charted space modelled on `euclidean_space \u211d (fin 1)`.  This\nfollows by definition from the corresponding result for `metric.sphere`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereo_inv_fun_aux_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_stereo_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_exp_map_circle", "description": "The map `\u03bb t, exp (t * I)` from `\u211d` to the unit circle in `\u2102` is smooth.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereographic", "description": " Stereographic projection from the unit sphere in `E`, centred at a unit vector `v` in `E`; this\nis the version as a local homeomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_neg_sphere", "description": "The antipodal map is smooth.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff.cod_restrict_sphere", "description": " If a `cont_mdiff` function `f : M \u2192 E`, where `M` is some manifold, takes values in the\nsphere, then it restricts to a `cont_mdiff` function from `M` to the sphere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereo_inv_fun_aux", "description": " Auxiliary function for the construction of the reverse direction of the stereographic\nprojection.  This is a map from the orthogonal complement of a unit vector `v` in an inner product\nspace `E` to `E`; we will later prove that it takes values in the unit sphere.\n\nFor most purposes, use `stereo_inv_fun`, not `stereo_inv_fun_aux`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stereographic'_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at_stereo_inv_fun_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_vsub_midpoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_vsub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_sub_midpoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_self_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_add_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_zero_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_unique", "description": "`midpoint` does not depend on the ring `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_equiv.point_reflection_midpoint_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint", "description": "`midpoint x y` is the midpoint of the segment `[x, y]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.of_map_midpoint", "description": "A map `f : E \u2192 F` sending zero to zero and midpoints to midpoints is an `add_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map.map_midpoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_vsub_midpoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_eq_right_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_vsub_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vsub_midpoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.coe_of_map_midpoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_eq_smul_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_equiv.point_reflection_midpoint_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_sub_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_eq_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_vadd_midpoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_sub_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_add_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_sub_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_vsub_midpoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_eq_midpoint_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_eq_left_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_eq_midpoint_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_vsub_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_eq_midpoint_iff_vsub_eq_vsub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "midpoint_neg_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_equiv.map_midpoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_sub_midpoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_units_int", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_units", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units_int.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units_int.univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.covariant_class_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.contravariant_class_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.contravariant_class_swap_add_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.subtype.semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.subtype.add_left_cancel_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.subtype.ordered_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.subtype.add_right_cancel_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.subtype.distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.contravariant_class_add_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.subtype.add_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.covariant_class_add_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.subtype.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.subtype.linear_ordered_cancel_comm_monoid", "description": " If `R` is a nontrivial linear ordered commutative semiring, then `{x : R // 0 < x}` is a linear\nordered cancellative commutative monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.coe_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.subtype.add_comm_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.nat.has_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.subtype.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.covariant_class_swap_add_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.subtype.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.coe_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.subtype.monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.contravariant_class_swap_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.subset_span_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.span_eq_Inf", "description": " The span of a set of points in a projective space is equal to the infimum of the collection of\nsubspaces which contain the set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.subspace_inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.has_inf", "description": "The infimum of two subspaces exists.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace", "description": " A subspace of a projective space is a structure consisting of a set of points such that:\nIf two nonzero vectors determine points which are in the set, and the sum of the two vectors is\nnonzero, then the point determined by the sum is also in the set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.carrier", "description": " A subspace of a projective space is a structure consisting of a set of points such that:\nIf two nonzero vectors determine points which are in the set, and the sum of the two vectors is\nnonzero, then the point determined by the sum is also in the set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.mem_add'", "description": " A subspace of a projective space is a structure consisting of a set of points such that:\nIf two nonzero vectors determine points which are in the set, and the sum of the two vectors is\nnonzero, then the point determined by the sum is also in the set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.gi", "description": " The span of a set of points is a Galois insertion between sets of points of a projective space\nand subspaces of the projective space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.projectivization.set_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.complete_lattice", "description": "The subspaces of a projective space form a complete lattice.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.span", "description": "The span of a set of points in projective space is a subspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.span_univ", "description": "The span of the entire projective space is the top of the lattice of subspaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.mem_carrier_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.mem_span", "description": " A point in a projective space is contained in the span of a set of points if and only if the\npoint is contained in all subspaces of the projective space which contain the set of points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.span_Union", "description": " The supremum of a collection of subspaces is equal to the span of the union of the\ncollection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.monotone_span", "description": " If a set of points is a subset of another set of points, then its span will be contained in the\nspan of that set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.has_Inf", "description": "Infimums of arbitrary collections of subspaces exist.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.mem_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.subset_span", "description": "The span of a set of points contains the set of points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.span_coe", "description": "The span of a subspace is the subspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.sup_span", "description": " The supremum of a subspace and the span of a set of points is equal to the span of the union of\nthe subspace and the set of points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.span_carrier", "description": " The span of a set of points in a projective space is defined inductively to be the set of points\nwhich contains the original set, and contains all points determined by the (nonzero) sum of two\nnonzero vectors, each of which determine points in the span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.span_carrier.of", "description": " The span of a set of points in a projective space is defined inductively to be the set of points\nwhich contains the original set, and contains all points determined by the (nonzero) sum of two\nnonzero vectors, each of which determine points in the span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.span_carrier.mem_add", "description": " The span of a set of points in a projective space is defined inductively to be the set of points\nwhich contains the original set, and contains all points determined by the (nonzero) sum of two\nnonzero vectors, each of which determine points in the span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.span_le_subspace_iff", "description": " The span of a set of points is contained in a subspace if and only if the set of points is\ncontained in the subspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.span_union", "description": "The supremum of two subspaces is equal to the span of their union.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.span_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.span_eq_span_iff", "description": " The spans of two sets of points in a projective space are equal if and only if each set of\npoints is contained in the span of the other set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.span_eq_of_le", "description": " If a set of points in projective space is contained in a subspace, and that subspace is\ncontained in the span of the set of points, then the span of the set of points is equal to\nthe subspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projectivization.subspace.span_empty", "description": "The span of the empty set is the bottom of the lattice of subspaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.fixed_point_is_fixed_pt", "description": "The point provided by `contracting_with.fixed_point` is actually a fixed point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.apriori_edist_iterate_efixed_point_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.dist_inequality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.efixed_point_is_fixed_pt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.to_lipschitz_with", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.exists_fixed_point'", "description": "Banach fixed-point theorem for maps contracting on a complete subset.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.fixed_point_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.aposteriori_dist_iterate_fixed_point_le", "description": "Aposteriori estimates on the convergence of iterates to the fixed point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.fixed_point_lipschitz_in_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.edist_le_of_fixed_point", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.dist_le_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.apriori_edist_iterate_efixed_point_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with", "description": "A map is said to be `contracting_with K`, if `K < 1` and `f` is `lipschitz_with K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.exists_fixed_point", "description": " Banach fixed-point theorem, contraction mapping theorem, `emetric_space` version.\nA contracting map on a complete metric space has a fixed point.\nWe include more conclusions in this theorem to avoid proving them again later.\n\nThe main API for this theorem are the functions `efixed_point` and `fixed_point`,\nand lemmas about these functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.one_sub_K_pos'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.apriori_dist_iterate_fixed_point_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.efixed_point_eq_of_edist_lt_top'", "description": " If a globally contracting map `f` has two complete forward-invariant sets `s`, `t`,\nand `x \u2208 s` is at a finite distance from `y \u2208 t`, then the `efixed_point'` constructed by `x`\nis the same as the `efixed_point'` constructed by `y`.\n\nThis lemma takes additional arguments stating that `f` contracts on `s` and `t` because this way\nit can be used to prove the desired equality with non-trivial proofs of these facts.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.edist_efixed_point_lt_top'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.is_fixed_pt_fixed_point_iterate", "description": " If a map `f` has a contracting iterate `f^[n]`, then the fixed point of `f^[n]` is also a fixed\npoint of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.dist_le_of_fixed_point", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.one_sub_K_ne_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.dist_fixed_point_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.edist_efixed_point_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.efixed_point_mem'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.efixed_point_is_fixed_pt'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.tendsto_iterate_fixed_point", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.edist_efixed_point_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.dist_fixed_point_fixed_point_of_dist_le'", "description": " Let `f` be a contracting map with constant `K`; let `g` be another map uniformly\n`C`-close to `f`. If `x` and `y` are their fixed points, then `dist x y \u2264 C / (1 - K)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.edist_inequality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.efixed_point", "description": " Let `x` be a point of a complete emetric space. Suppose that `f` is a contracting map,\nand `edist x (f x) \u2260 \u221e`. Then `efixed_point` is the unique fixed point of `f`\nin `emetric.ball x \u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.restrict", "description": " If a map `f` is `contracting_with K`, and `s` is a forward-invariant set, then\nrestriction of `f` to `s` is `contracting_with K` as well.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.fixed_point", "description": "The unique fixed point of a contracting map in a nonempty complete metric space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.edist_efixed_point_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.efixed_point_eq_of_edist_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.tendsto_iterate_efixed_point", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.one_sub_K_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.tendsto_iterate_efixed_point'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.efixed_point'", "description": " Let `s` be a complete forward-invariant set of a self-map `f`. If `f` contracts on `s`\nand `x \u2208 s` satisfies `edist x (f x) \u2260 \u221e`, then `efixed_point'` is the unique fixed point\nof the restriction of `f` to `s \u2229 emetric.ball x \u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.fixed_point_unique'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.one_sub_K_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contracting_with.eq_or_edist_eq_top_of_fixed_points", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.curry_apply_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.uncurry_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.cases", "description": "Any morphism in the action groupoid is given by some pair.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.\u03c0", "description": "The projection from the action category to the monoid, mapping a morphism to its\n label.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.back", "description": "The canonical map `action_category M X \u2192 X`. It is given by `\u03bb x, x.snd`, but\n has a more explicit type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.curry", "description": "Given `G` acting on `X`, a functor from the corresponding action groupoid to a group `H`\n   can be curried to a group homomorphism `G \u2192* (X \u2192 H) \u22ca G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_as_functor", "description": "A multiplicative action M \u21bb X viewed as a functor mapping the single object of M to X\n and an element `m : M` to the map `X \u2192 X` given by multiplication by `m`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.coe_back", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.curry_apply_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.\u03c0_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.back_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.\u03c0_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.hom_of_pair", "description": "A target vertex `t` and a scalar `g` determine a morphism in the action groupoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.hom_of_pair.val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.hom_as_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_as_functor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.stabilizer_iso_End", "description": "The stabilizer of a point is isomorphic to the endomorphism monoid at the\n corresponding point. In fact they are definitionally equivalent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.has_coe_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.id_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.uncurry", "description": "Given `G` acting on `X`, a group homomorphism `\u03c6 : G \u2192* (X \u2192 H) \u22ca G` can be uncurried to\n   a functor from the action groupoid to `H`, provided that `\u03c6 g = (_, g)` for all `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.stabilizer_iso_End_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.End_mul_equiv_subgroup", "description": "Any subgroup of `G` is a vertex group in its action groupoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.comp_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category", "description": "A multiplicative action M \u21bb X induces a category strucure on X, where a morphism\nfrom x to y is a scalar taking x to y. Due to implementation details, the object type\nof this category is not equal to X, but is in bijection with X.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.uncurry_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.category_theory.groupoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.obj_equiv", "description": "An object of the action category given by M \u21bb X corresponds to an element of X.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.stabilizer_iso_End_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_as_functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.action_category.category_theory.is_connected", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.traversable_derive_handler'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.functor_derive_handler'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.traversable_derive_handler", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.lawful_functor_derive_handler'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.nested_map", "description": "similar to `nested_traverse` but for `functor`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.higher_order_derive_handler", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.guard_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.lawful_traversable_derive_handler", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mk_mapp_aux'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mk_traverse", "description": "derive the `traverse` definition of a `traversable` instance", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.derive_lawful_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.map_field", "description": "similar to `traverse_field` but for `functor`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.derive_traverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.derive_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.lawful_functor_derive_handler", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mk_map", "description": "derive the `map` definition of a `functor`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.with_prefix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.lawful_traversable_derive_handler'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.functor_derive_handler", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.derive_traverse_equations", "description": "derive the equations for a specific `traverse` definition", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mk_one_instance", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.simp_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.get_equations_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.derive_lawful_traversable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.nested_traverse", "description": " ``nested_traverse f \u03b1 (list (array n (list \u03b1)))`` synthesizes the expression\n`traverse (traverse (traverse f))`. `nested_traverse` assumes that `\u03b1` appears in\n`(list (array n (list \u03b1)))`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.traverse_field", "description": "For a sum type `inductive foo (\u03b1 : Type) | foo1 : list \u03b1 \u2192 \u2115 \u2192 foo | ...`\n``traverse_field `foo appl_inst f `\u03b1 `(x : list \u03b1)`` synthesizes\n`traverse f x` as part of traversing `foo1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.traverse_constructor", "description": "For a sum type `inductive foo (\u03b1 : Type) | foo1 : list \u03b1 \u2192 \u2115 \u2192 foo | ...`\n``traverse_constructor `foo1 `foo appl_inst f `\u03b1 `\u03b2 [`(x : list \u03b1), `(y : \u2115)]``\nsynthesizes `foo1 <$> traverse f x <*> pure y.`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.traversable_law_starter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.derive_map_equations", "description": "derive the equations for a specific `map` definition", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.mk_mapp'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.map_constructor", "description": "similar to `traverse_constructor` but for `functor`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_precomplete.bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Hausdorffification.induction_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Hausdorffification.lift_eq", "description": "Uniqueness of lift.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "adic_completion.range_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "adic_completion.eval_comp_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "adic_completion.of_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Hausdorffification", "description": "The Hausdorffification of a module with respect to an ideal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Hausdorffification.lift_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_adic_complete.of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_precomplete", "description": "A module `M` is precomplete with respect to an ideal `I` if every Cauchy sequence converges.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_precomplete.prec'", "description": "A module `M` is precomplete with respect to an ideal `I` if every Cauchy sequence converges.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Hausdorff.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Hausdorff.bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Hausdorffification.lift_comp_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_precomplete.top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "adic_completion.is_Hausdorff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_adic_complete.le_jacobson_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Hausdorffification.lift", "description": " universal property of Hausdorffification: any linear map to a Hausdorff module extends to a\nunique map from the Hausdorffification.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Hausdorff_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_adic_complete", "description": "A module `M` is `I`-adically complete if it is Hausdorff and precomplete.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_adic_complete.to_is_Hausdorff", "description": "A module `M` is `I`-adically complete if it is Hausdorff and precomplete.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_adic_complete.to_is_precomplete", "description": "A module `M` is `I`-adically complete if it is Hausdorff and precomplete.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "adic_completion.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "adic_completion.coe_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_precomplete.of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_precomplete.prec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "adic_completion.of", "description": "The canonical linear map to the completion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_precomplete_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_adic_complete.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "adic_completion", "description": " The completion of a module with respect to an ideal. This is not necessarily Hausdorff.\nIn fact, this is only complete if the ideal is finitely generated.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Hausdorff.haus", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "adic_completion.eval_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Hausdorff.infi_pow_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "adic_completion.eval_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Hausdorffification.of", "description": "The canonical linear map to the Hausdorffification.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_adic_complete.bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Hausdorff", "description": "A module `M` is Hausdorff with respect to an ideal `I` if `\u22c2 I^n M = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Hausdorff.haus'", "description": "A module `M` is Hausdorff with respect to an ideal `I` if `\u22c2 I^n M = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Hausdorffification.is_Hausdorff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "adic_completion.eval", "description": "Linearly evaluating a sequence in the completion at a given input.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Hausdorff.of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.canonize", "description": "Return a term (which is in canonical form by definition)\n   that is equivalent to the input preterm", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.preterm.val_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.preterm.add_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.preterm.val_var", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.preterm.induce", "description": "Helper tactic for proof by induction over preterms", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.preterm.has_reflect", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.preterm.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.preterm.sub_free", "description": "Preterm is free of subtractions", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.preterm.val_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.preterm.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.exprterm", "description": " The shadow syntax for arithmetic terms. All constants are reified to `cst`\n(e.g., `5` is reified to `cst 5`) and all other atomic terms are reified to\n`exp` (e.g., `5 * (list.length l)` is reified to `exp 5 \\`(list.length l)`).\n`exp` accepts a coefficient of type `nat` as its first argument because\nmultiplication by constant is allowed by the omega test.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.exprterm.cst", "description": " The shadow syntax for arithmetic terms. All constants are reified to `cst`\n(e.g., `5` is reified to `cst 5`) and all other atomic terms are reified to\n`exp` (e.g., `5 * (list.length l)` is reified to `exp 5 \\`(list.length l)`).\n`exp` accepts a coefficient of type `nat` as its first argument because\nmultiplication by constant is allowed by the omega test.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.exprterm.exp", "description": " The shadow syntax for arithmetic terms. All constants are reified to `cst`\n(e.g., `5` is reified to `cst 5`) and all other atomic terms are reified to\n`exp` (e.g., `5 * (list.length l)` is reified to `exp 5 \\`(list.length l)`).\n`exp` accepts a coefficient of type `nat` as its first argument because\nmultiplication by constant is allowed by the omega test.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.exprterm.add", "description": " The shadow syntax for arithmetic terms. All constants are reified to `cst`\n(e.g., `5` is reified to `cst 5`) and all other atomic terms are reified to\n`exp` (e.g., `5 * (list.length l)` is reified to `exp 5 \\`(list.length l)`).\n`exp` accepts a coefficient of type `nat` as its first argument because\nmultiplication by constant is allowed by the omega test.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.exprterm.sub", "description": " The shadow syntax for arithmetic terms. All constants are reified to `cst`\n(e.g., `5` is reified to `cst 5`) and all other atomic terms are reified to\n`exp` (e.g., `5 * (list.length l)` is reified to `exp 5 \\`(list.length l)`).\n`exp` accepts a coefficient of type `nat` as its first argument because\nmultiplication by constant is allowed by the omega test.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.preterm.val", "description": "Preterm evaluation", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.preterm.val_constant", "description": " If variable assignments `v` and `w` agree on all variables that occur\nin term `t`, the value of `t` under `v` and `w` are identical.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.val_canonize", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.preterm.val_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.preterm.repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.preterm.fresh_index", "description": "Fresh de Brujin index not used by any variable in argument", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.preterm", "description": " Similar to `exprterm`, except that all exprs are now replaced with\nde Brujin indices of type `nat`. This is akin to generalizing over\nthe terms represented by the said exprs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.preterm.cst", "description": " Similar to `exprterm`, except that all exprs are now replaced with\nde Brujin indices of type `nat`. This is akin to generalizing over\nthe terms represented by the said exprs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.preterm.var", "description": " Similar to `exprterm`, except that all exprs are now replaced with\nde Brujin indices of type `nat`. This is akin to generalizing over\nthe terms represented by the said exprs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.preterm.add", "description": " Similar to `exprterm`, except that all exprs are now replaced with\nde Brujin indices of type `nat`. This is akin to generalizing over\nthe terms represented by the said exprs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.nat.preterm.sub", "description": " Similar to `exprterm`, except that all exprs are now replaced with\nde Brujin indices of type `nat`. This is akin to generalizing over\nthe terms represented by the said exprs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.squeeze_simp", "description": "`squeeze_simp`, `squeeze_simpa` and `squeeze_dsimp` perform the same\ntask with the difference that `squeeze_simp` relates to `simp` while\n`squeeze_simpa` relates to `simpa` and `squeeze_dsimp` relates to\n`dsimp`. The following applies to `squeeze_simp`, `squeeze_simpa` and\n`squeeze_dsimp`.\n\n`squeeze_simp` behaves like `simp` (including all its arguments)\nand prints a `simp only` invocation to skip the search through the\n`simp` lemma list.\n\nFor instance, the following is easily solved with `simp`:\n\n```lean\nexample : 0 + 1 = 1 + 0 := by simp\n```\n\nTo guide the proof search and speed it up, we may replace `simp`\nwith `squeeze_simp`:\n\n```lean\nexample : 0 + 1 = 1 + 0 := by squeeze_simp\n-- prints:\n-- Try this: simp only [add_zero, eq_self_iff_true, zero_add]\n```\n\n`squeeze_simp` suggests a replacement which we can use instead of\n`squeeze_simp`.\n\n```lean\nexample : 0 + 1 = 1 + 0 := by simp only [add_zero, eq_self_iff_true, zero_add]\n```\n\n`squeeze_simp only` prints nothing as it already skips the `simp` list.\n\nThis tactic is useful for speeding up the compilation of a complete file.\nSteps:\n\n   1. search and replace ` simp` with ` squeeze_simp` (the space helps avoid the\n      replacement of `simp` in `@[simp]`) throughout the file.\n   2. Starting at the beginning of the file, go to each printout in turn, copy\n      the suggestion in place of `squeeze_simp`.\n   3. after all the suggestions were applied, search and replace `squeeze_simp` with\n      `simp` to remove the occurrences of `squeeze_simp` that did not produce a suggestion.\n\nKnown limitation(s):\n  * in cases where `squeeze_simp` is used after a `;` (e.g. `cases x; squeeze_simp`),\n    `squeeze_simp` will produce as many suggestions as the number of goals it is applied to.\n    It is likely that none of the suggestion is a good replacement but they can all be\n    combined by concatenating their list of lemmas. `squeeze_scope` can be used to\n    combine the suggestions: `by squeeze_scope { cases x; squeeze_simp }`\n  * sometimes, `simp` lemmas are also `_refl_lemma` and they can be used without appearing in the\n    resulting proof. `squeeze_simp` won't know to try that lemma unless it is called as\n    `squeeze_simp?`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.squeeze_loc_attr_carrier", "description": "dummy declaration used as target of `squeeze_loc` attribute", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.squeeze_dsimp", "description": " `squeeze_dsimp` behaves like `dsimp` (including all its arguments)\nand prints a `dsimp only` invocation to skip the search through the\n`simp` lemma list. See the doc string of `squeeze_simp` for examples.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.parse_config", "description": "translate a `pexpr` into a `simp` configuration", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.prepend_root_if_needed", "description": " If the `name` is (likely) to be overloaded, then prepend a `_root_` on it. The `expr` of an\noverloaded name is constructed using `expr.macro`; this is how we guess whether it's overloaded.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.filter_simp_set", "description": "`filter_simp_set g call_simp user_args simp_args` returns `args'` such that, when calling\n`call_simp tt /- only -/ args'` on the goal `g` (`g` is a meta var) we end up in the same\nstate as if we had called `call_simp ff (user_args ++ simp_args)` and removing any one\nelement of `args'` changes the resulting proof.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.same_result", "description": " `same_result proof tac` runs tactic `tac` and checks if the proof\nproduced by `tac` is equivalent to `proof`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.simp_arg_type.has_to_string", "description": "Turn a `simp_arg_type` into a string.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.simp_arg_type.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.squeeze_simpa", "description": "see `squeeze_simp`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.squeeze_scope", "description": " combinator meant to aggregate the suggestions issued by multiple calls\nof `squeeze_simp` (due, for instance, to `;`).\n\nCan be used as:\n\n```lean\nexample {\u03b1 \u03b2} (xs ys : list \u03b1) (f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2) :\n  (xs ++ ys.tail).map f = xs.map f \u2227 (xs.tail.map f).length = xs.length :=\nbegin\n  have : xs = ys, admit,\n  squeeze_scope\n  { split; squeeze_simp,\n    -- `squeeze_simp` is run twice, the first one requires\n    -- `list.map_append` and the second one\n    -- `[list.length_map, list.length_tail]`\n    -- prints only one message and combine the suggestions:\n    -- > Try this: simp only [list.length_map, list.length_tail, list.map_append]\n    squeeze_simp [this]\n    -- `squeeze_simp` is run only once\n    -- prints:\n    -- > Try this: simp only [this] },\nend\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.mk_suggestion", "description": " Emit a suggestion to the user. If inside a `squeeze_scope` block,\nthe suggestions emitted through `mk_suggestion` will be aggregated so that\nevery tactic that makes a suggestion can consider multiple execution of the\nsame invocation.\nIf `at_pos` is true, make the suggestion at `p` instead of the current position.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.render_simp_arg_list", "description": " Format a list of arguments for use with `simp` and friends. This omits the\nlist entirely if it is empty.\n\nPatch: `pp` was changed to `to_string` because it was getting rid of prefixes\nthat would be necessary for some disambiguations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.name.to_simp_args", "description": "make a `simp_arg_type` that references the name given as an argument", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pos.move_left", "description": "shift `pos` `n` columns to the left", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.tactic.squeeze_simp / squeeze_simpa / squeeze_dsimp / squeeze_scope", "description": "`squeeze_simp`, `squeeze_simpa` and `squeeze_dsimp` perform the same\ntask with the difference that `squeeze_simp` relates to `simp` while\n`squeeze_simpa` relates to `simpa` and `squeeze_dsimp` relates to\n`dsimp`. The following applies to `squeeze_simp`, `squeeze_simpa` and\n`squeeze_dsimp`.\n\n`squeeze_simp` behaves like `simp` (including all its arguments)\nand prints a `simp only` invocation to skip the search through the\n`simp` lemma list.\n\nFor instance, the following is easily solved with `simp`:\n\n```lean\nexample : 0 + 1 = 1 + 0 := by simp\n```\n\nTo guide the proof search and speed it up, we may replace `simp`\nwith `squeeze_simp`:\n\n```lean\nexample : 0 + 1 = 1 + 0 := by squeeze_simp\n-- prints:\n-- Try this: simp only [add_zero, eq_self_iff_true, zero_add]\n```\n\n`squeeze_simp` suggests a replacement which we can use instead of\n`squeeze_simp`.\n\n```lean\nexample : 0 + 1 = 1 + 0 := by simp only [add_zero, eq_self_iff_true, zero_add]\n```\n\n`squeeze_simp only` prints nothing as it already skips the `simp` list.\n\nThis tactic is useful for speeding up the compilation of a complete file.\nSteps:\n\n   1. search and replace ` simp` with ` squeeze_simp` (the space helps avoid the\n      replacement of `simp` in `@[simp]`) throughout the file.\n   2. Starting at the beginning of the file, go to each printout in turn, copy\n      the suggestion in place of `squeeze_simp`.\n   3. after all the suggestions were applied, search and replace `squeeze_simp` with\n      `simp` to remove the occurrences of `squeeze_simp` that did not produce a suggestion.\n\nKnown limitation(s):\n  * in cases where `squeeze_simp` is used after a `;` (e.g. `cases x; squeeze_simp`),\n    `squeeze_simp` will produce as many suggestions as the number of goals it is applied to.\n    It is likely that none of the suggestion is a good replacement but they can all be\n    combined by concatenating their list of lemmas. `squeeze_scope` can be used to\n    combine the suggestions: `by squeeze_scope { cases x; squeeze_simp }`\n  * sometimes, `simp` lemmas are also `_refl_lemma` and they can be used without appearing in the\n    resulting proof. `squeeze_simp` won't know to try that lemma unless it is called as\n    `squeeze_simp?`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "loc.to_string", "description": "pretty print a `loc`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.squeeze_simp_core", "description": " tactic combinator to create a `simp`-like tactic that minimizes its\nargument list.\n\n * `slow`: adds all rfl-lemmas from the environment to the initial list (this is a slower but more\n           accurate strategy)\n * `no_dflt`: did the user use the `only` keyword?\n * `args`:    list of `simp` arguments\n * `tac`:     how to invoke the underlying `simp` tactic", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.struct.to_tactic_format", "description": "pretty print structure instance", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.parse_dsimp_config", "description": "translate a `pexpr` into a `dsimp` configuration", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.struct_inst", "description": "parse structure instance of the shape `{ field1 := value1, .. , field2 := value2 }`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subsemigroup.srange_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemigroup.comap_equiv_eq_map_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemigroup.prod", "description": " Given `subsemigroup`s `s`, `t` of semigroups `M`, `N` respectively, `s \u00d7 t` as a subsemigroup\nof `M \u00d7 N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_mem_class.subtype", "description": "The natural semigroup hom from a subsemigroup of semigroup `M` to `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemigroup.eq_top_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.of_left_inverse_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subsemigroup.to_subsemigroup_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_mem_class.subtype", "description": "The natural semigroup hom from an `add_subsemigroup` of `add_semigroup` `M` to `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemigroup.mem_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subsemigroup.map_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsemigroup.map_injective_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.of_left_inverse", "description": "An additive semigroup homomorphism `f : M \u2192+ N` with a left-inverse `g : N \u2192 M` def