 has a zero object, kernels, cokernels, binary\n   products and coproducts, and every monomorphism and every epimorphism is normal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.to_normal_epi_category", "description": "We call a category `non_preadditive_abelian` if it has a zero object, kernels, cokernels, binary\n   products and coproducts, and every monomorphism and every epimorphism is normal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.has_zero_object", "description": "We call a category `non_preadditive_abelian` if it has a zero object, kernels, cokernels, binary\n   products and coproducts, and every monomorphism and every epimorphism is normal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.has_kernels", "description": "We call a category `non_preadditive_abelian` if it has a zero object, kernels, cokernels, binary\n   products and coproducts, and every monomorphism and every epimorphism is normal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.has_cokernels", "description": "We call a category `non_preadditive_abelian` if it has a zero object, kernels, cokernels, binary\n   products and coproducts, and every monomorphism and every epimorphism is normal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.has_finite_products", "description": "We call a category `non_preadditive_abelian` if it has a zero object, kernels, cokernels, binary\n   products and coproducts, and every monomorphism and every epimorphism is normal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.has_finite_coproducts", "description": "We call a category `non_preadditive_abelian` if it has a zero object, kernels, cokernels, binary\n   products and coproducts, and every monomorphism and every epimorphism is normal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.neg_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.lift_map_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.sub_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.add_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.lift_\u03c3", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.lift_\u03c3_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.comp_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.has_sub", "description": "Subtraction of morphisms in a `non_preadditive_abelian` category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.add_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.neg_add_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.epi_is_cokernel_of_kernel", "description": "In a `non_preadditive_abelian` category, an epi is the cokernel of its kernel. More precisely:\n   If `f` is an epimorphism and `s` is some limit kernel cone on `f`, then `f` is a cokernel\n   of `fork.\u03b9 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.sub_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.neg_sub'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.is_iso_factor_thru_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.mono_\u0394", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.sub_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.mono_is_kernel_of_cokernel", "description": "In a `non_preadditive_abelian` category, a mono is the kernel of its cokernel. More precisely:\n   If `f` is a monomorphism and `s` is some colimit cokernel cocone on `f`, then `f` is a kernel\n   of `cofork.\u03c0 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.has_add", "description": "Addition of morphisms in a `non_preadditive_abelian` category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.add_neg_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.\u03c3", "description": "The composite `A \u2a2f A \u27f6 cokernel (diag A) \u27f6 A` given by the natural projection into the cokernel\n   followed by the inverse of `r`. In the category of modules, using the normal kernels and\n   cokernels, this map is equal to the map `(a, b) \u21a6 a - b`, hence the name `\u03c3` for\n   \"subtraction\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.add_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.neg_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.is_colimit_\u03c3", "description": "\u03c3 is a cokernel of \u0394 X.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.add_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.comp_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.add_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.sub_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.r", "description": "The composite `A \u27f6 A \u2a2f A \u27f6 cokernel (\u0394 A)`, where the first map is `(\ud835\udfd9 A, 0)` and the second map\n   is the canonical projection into the cokernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.category_theory.abelian.factor_thru_coimage.category_theory.mono", "description": "The canonical morphism `i : coimage f \u27f6 Q` is a monomorphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.add_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.diag_\u03c3", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.sub_sub_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.is_iso_factor_thru_coimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.diag_\u03c3_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.epi_r", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.neg_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.category_theory.abelian.factor_thru_image.category_theory.epi", "description": "The map `p : P \u27f6 image f` is an epimorphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.non_preadditive_abelian.has_neg", "description": "Negation of morphisms in a `non_preadditive_abelian` category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.reindex_linear_equiv_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.reindex_linear_equiv_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.reindex_linear_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.reindex_linear_equiv", "description": " The natural map that reindexes a matrix's rows and columns with equivalent types,\n`matrix.reindex`, is a linear equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.reindex_alg_equiv_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.reindex_linear_equiv_comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.mul_reindex_linear_equiv_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.reindex_linear_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.reindex_alg_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_reindex_alg_equiv", "description": " Reindexing both indices along the same equivalence preserves