f `division_ring K` includes maps `rat_cast : \u211a \u2192 K` and `qsmul : \u211a \u2192 K \u2192 K`.\nIf the division ring has positive characteristic p, we define `rat_cast (1 / p) = 1 / 0 = 0`\nfor consistency with our division by zero convention.\nThe fields `rat_cast` and `qsmul` are needed to implement the\n`algebra_rat [division_ring K] : algebra \u211a K` instance, since we need to control the specific\ndefinitions for some special cases of `K` (in particular `K = \u211a` itself).\nSee also Note [forgetful inheritance].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniq_inv_of_is_field", "description": " For each field, and for each nonzero element of said field, there is a unique inverse.\nSince `is_field` doesn't remember the data of an `inv` function and as such,\na lemma that there is a unique inverse could be useful.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_field.to_semifield", "description": "Transferring from `is_field` to `semifield`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.to_comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rat.smul_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rat.cast_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semifield.to_comm_group_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.to_division_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_ring.to_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_is_field_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semifield.to_division_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rat.cast_coe", "description": "Construct the canonical injection from `\u211a` into an arbitrary\n division ring. If the field has positive characteristic `p`,\n we define `1 / p = 1 / 0 = 0` for consistency with our\n division by zero convention.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field", "description": " A `field` is a `comm_ring` with multiplicative inverses for nonzero elements.\n\nAn instance of `field K` includes maps `of_rat : \u211a \u2192 K` and `qsmul : \u211a \u2192 K \u2192 K`.\nIf the field has positive characteristic p, we define `of_rat (1 / p) = 1 / 0 = 0`\nfor consistency with our division by zero convention.\nThe fields `of_rat` and `qsmul are needed to implement the\n`algebra_rat [division_ring K] : algebra \u211a K` instance, since we need to control the specific\ndefinitions for some special cases of `K` (in particular `K = \u211a` itself).\nSee also Note [forgetful inheritance].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.add", "description": " A `field` is a `comm_ring` with multiplicative inverses for nonzero elements.\n\nAn instance of `field K` includes maps `of_rat : \u211a \u2192 K` and `qsmul : \u211a \u2192 K \u2192 K`.\nIf the field has positive characteristic p, we define `of_rat (1 / p) = 1 / 0 = 0`\nfor consistency with our division by zero convention.\nThe fields `of_rat` and `qsmul are needed to implement the\n`algebra_rat [division_ring K] : algebra \u211a K` instance, since we need to control the specific\ndefinitions for some special cases of `K` (in particular `K = \u211a` itself).\nSee also Note [forgetful inheritance].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.add_assoc", "description": " A `field` is a `comm_ring` with multiplicative inverses for nonzero elements.\n\nAn instance of `field K` includes maps `of_rat : \u211a \u2192 K` and `qsmul : \u211a \u2192 K \u2192 K`.\nIf the field has positive characteristic p, we define `of_rat (1 / p) = 1 / 0 = 0`\nfor consistency with our division by zero convention.\nThe fields `of_rat` and `qsmul are needed to implement the\n`algebra_rat [division_ring K] : algebra \u211a K` instance, since we need to control the specific\ndefinitions for some special cases of `K` (in particular `K = \u211a` itself).\nSee also Note [forgetful inheritance].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.zero", "description": " A `field` is a `comm_ring` with multiplicative inverses for nonzero elements.\n\nAn instance of `field K` includes maps `of_rat : \u211a \u2192 K` and `qsmul : \u