comm_ring` with multiplicative inverses for nonzero elements.\n\nAn instance of `field K` includes maps `of_rat : \u211a \u2192 K` and `qsmul : \u211a \u2192 K \u2192 K`.\nIf the field has positive characteristic p, we define `of_rat (1 / p) = 1 / 0 = 0`\nfor consistency with our division by zero convention.\nThe fields `of_rat` and `qsmul are needed to implement the\n`algebra_rat [division_ring K] : algebra \u211a K` instance, since we need to control the specific\ndefinitions for some special cases of `K` (in particular `K = \u211a` itself).\nSee also Note [forgetful inheritance].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.rat_cast_mk", "description": " A `field` is a `comm_ring` with multiplicative inverses for nonzero elements.\n\nAn instance of `field K` includes maps `of_rat : \u211a \u2192 K` and `qsmul : \u211a \u2192 K \u2192 K`.\nIf the field has positive characteristic p, we define `of_rat (1 / p) = 1 / 0 = 0`\nfor consistency with our division by zero convention.\nThe fields `of_rat` and `qsmul are needed to implement the\n`algebra_rat [division_ring K] : algebra \u211a K` instance, since we need to control the specific\ndefinitions for some special cases of `K` (in particular `K = \u211a` itself).\nSee also Note [forgetful inheritance].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.qsmul", "description": " A `field` is a `comm_ring` with multiplicative inverses for nonzero elements.\n\nAn instance of `field K` includes maps `of_rat : \u211a \u2192 K` and `qsmul : \u211a \u2192 K \u2192 K`.\nIf the field has positive characteristic p, we define `of_rat (1 / p) = 1 / 0 = 0`\nfor consistency with our division by zero convention.\nThe fields `of_rat` and `qsmul are needed to implement the\n`algebra_rat [division_ring K] : algebra \u211a K` instance, since we need to control the specific\ndefinitions for some special cases of `K` (in particular `K = \u211a` itself).\nSee also Note [forgetful inheritance].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.qsmul_eq_mul'", "description": " A `field` is a `comm_ring` with multiplicative inverses for nonzero elements.\n\nAn instance of `field K` includes maps `of_rat : \u211a \u2192 K` and `qsmul : \u211a \u2192 K \u2192 K`.\nIf the field has positive characteristic p, we define `of_rat (1 / p) = 1 / 0 = 0`\nfor consistency with our division by zero convention.\nThe fields `of_rat` and `qsmul are needed to implement the\n`algebra_rat [division_ring K] : algebra \u211a K` instance, since we need to control the specific\ndefinitions for some special cases of `K` (in particular `K = \u211a` itself).\nSee also Note [forgetful inheritance].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rat.cast_rec", "description": " The default definition of the coercion `(\u2191(a : \u211a) : K)` for a division ring `K`\nis defined as `(a / b : K) = (a : K) * (b : K)\u207b\u00b9`.\nUse `coe` instead of `rat.cast_rec` for better definitional behaviour.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_ring.to_division_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.to_semifield", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_field.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_semiring.to_group_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qsmul_rec", "description": " The default definition of the scalar multiplication `(a : \u211a) \u2022 (x : K)` for a division ring `K`\nis given by `a \u2022 x = (\u2191 a) * x`.\nUse `(a : \u211a) \u2022 (x : K)` instead of `qsmul_rec` for better definitional behaviour.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_ring.to_has_rat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semifield", "description": "A `semifield` is a `comm_semiring` with multiplicative inverses for nonzero elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semifield.add", "description": "A `semifield` is a `comm_semiring` with multiplicative inverses for nonzero elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semifield.add_assoc", "description": "A `semifield` is a `comm_semiring` with multiplicative inverses for nonzer