ib"}, {"name": "le_implies_le_of_le_of_le", "description": "monotonicity of `\u2264` with respect to `\u2192`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.partial_order", "description": "The pointwise partial order on a product.\n   (The lexicographic ordering is defined in order/lexicographic.lean, and the instances are\n   available via the type synonym `\u03b1 \u00d7\u2097 \u03b2 = \u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_iff_not_lt_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_rec'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne.lt_of_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.mk_le_mk_iff_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtype.linear_order", "description": " A subtype of a linear order is a linear order. We explicitly give the proofs of decidable\nequality and decidable order in order to ensure the decidability instances are all definitionally\nequal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_le.le.eq_of_not_gt", "description": "**Alias** of `eq_of_ge_of_not_gt`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "as_linear_order.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "punit.linear_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lt_of_eq_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.le_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_order.lift'", "description": " Transfer a `linear_order` on `\u03b2` to a `linear_order` on `\u03b1` using an injective\nfunction `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2`. This version autogenerates `min` and `max` fields. See `linear_order.lift`\nfor a version that takes `[has_sup \u03b1]` and `[has_inf \u03b1]`, then uses them as `max` and `min`.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strong_lt.lt", "description": "**Alias** of `lt_of_strong_lt`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_le.le.not_lt", "description": "**Alias** of `not_lt_of_le`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq.trans_le", "description": "**Alias** of `le_of_eq_of_le`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"nam