ul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sub_right_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.pow_mul_m_le_card_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.hundred_div_\u03b5_pow_five_le_m", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.initial_bound", "description": " Auxiliary function for Szemer\u00e9di's regularity lemma. The size of the partition by which we start\nblowing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.mul_sq_le_sum_sq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.step_bound_pos_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.hundred_lt_pow_initial_bound_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.bound_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.card_aux\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.le_initial_bound", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.step_bound_pos", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `szemeredi_regularity.step_bound_pos_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.le_step_bound", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.step_bound_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.card_aux\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.initial_bound_le_bound", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.initial_bound_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.coe_m_add_one_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.add_div_le_sum_sq_div_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.eps_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.seven_le_initial_bound", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_szemeredi_regularity", "description": " Local extension for the `positivity` tactic: A few facts that are needed many times for the\nproof of Szemer\u00e9di's regularity lemma.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.m_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.bound", "description": " An explicit bound on the size of the equipartition whose existence is given by Szemer\u00e9di's\nregularity lemma.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.eps_pow_five_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_szemeredi_regularity_bound", "description": " Extension for the `positivity` tactic: `szemeredi_regularity.initial_bound` and\n`szemeredi_regularity.bound` are always positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.step_bound", "description": " Auxiliary function for Szemer\u00e9di's regularity lemma. Blowing up a partition of size `n` during\nthe induction results in a partition of size at most `step_bound n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.one_le_m_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.hundred_le_m", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.le_bound", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.a_add_one_le_four_pow_parts_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_arrow_comp_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_comp_iso_inv_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_order_hom", "description": "Taking kernels is an order-reversing map from the quotient objects of `X` to the subobjects of\n   `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_iso_comp_kernel_map_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_comp_iso_hom_arrow_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_arrow_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_arrow'_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_comp_mono_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.factor_thru_kernel_subobject", "description": "A factorisation of `h : W \u27f6 X` through `kernel_subobject f`, assuming `h \u226b f = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_zero_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_map_arrow_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_iso", "description": " The underlying object of `image_subobject f` is (up to isomorphism!)\nthe same as the chosen object `image f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_factors_comp_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.factor_thru_kernel_subobject_comp_kernel_subobject_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject", "description": "The kernel of a morphism `f : X \u27f6 Y` as a `subobject X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_arrow'_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_arrow_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_map_arrow_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer_subobject_arrow'_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.factor_thru_image_subobject", "description": "A factorisation of `f : X \u27f6 Y` through `image_subobject f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.factor_thru_image_subobject_comp_self_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer_subobject_arrow_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_iso_comp", "description": "Precomposing by an isomorphism does not change the image subobject.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer_subobject_arrow_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_arrow'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_iso_comp_kernel_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.factor_thru_image_subobject_comp_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_arrow_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.factor_thru_kernel_subobject_comp_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_arrow_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer_subobject_factors_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer_subobject", "description": "The equalizer of morphisms `f g : X \u27f6 Y` as a `subobject X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_order_hom_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_comp_le_epi_of_epi", "description": "The morphism `image_subobject (h \u226b f) \u27f6 image_subobject f`\nis an epimorphism when `h` is an epimorphism.\nIn general this does not imply that `image_subobject (h \u226b f) = image_subobject f`,\nalthough it will when the ambient category is abelian.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_map_comp_image_subobject_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_factors_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_comp_mono", "description": "Postcomposing by an monomorphism does not change the kernel subobject.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_arrow_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer_subobject_arrow'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_map_comp_kernel_subobject_iso_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cokernel_order_hom", "description": "Taking cokernels is an order-reversing map from the subobjects of `X` to the quotient objects\n   of `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject", "description": "The image of a morphism `f g : X \u27f6 Y` as a `subobject Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer_subobject_arrow_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_arrow_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_comp_iso_inv_arrow_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_map_comp_kernel_subobject_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_arrow'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer_subobject_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_comp_le", "description": "The kernel of `f` is always a smaller subobject than the kernel of `f \u226b h`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_iso_comp_hom_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_comp_le", "description": "The image of `h \u226b f` is always a smaller subobject than the image of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_arrow_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_map_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer_subobject_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.le_kernel_subobject", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_map_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_arrow_comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_iso_comp_image_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_map", "description": " Given a commutative square between morphisms `f` and `g`,\nwe have a morphism in the category from `image_subobject f` to `image_subobject g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cokernel_order_hom_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.equalizer_subobject_iso", "description": " The underlying object of `equalizer_subobject f g` is (up to isomorphism!)\nthe same as the chosen object `equalizer f g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_iso_comp", "description": "The isomorphism between the kernel of `f \u226b g` and the kernel of `g`,\nwhen `f` is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_comp_iso", "description": "Postcomposing by an isomorphism gives an isomorphism between image subobjects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_map_arrow_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_comp_iso_hom_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_kernel_subobject_zero_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.factor_thru_image_subobject.category_theory.epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_iso", "description": " The underlying object of `kernel_subobject f` is (up to isomorphism!)\nthe same as the chosen object `kernel f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_iso_comp_inv_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_arrow_comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_le_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.image_subobject_arrow'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_map", "description": "A commuting square induces a morphism between the kernel subobjects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_subobject_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.completion.has_dist", "description": " The distance on the completion is obtained by extending the distance on the original space,\nby uniform continuity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.completion.uniformity_dist'", "description": " Reformulate `completion.mem_uniformity_dist` in terms that are suitable for the definition\nof the metric space structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.completion.uniformity_dist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.completion.coe_isometry", "description": "The embedding of a metric space in its completion is an isometry.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.completion.dist_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.completion.continuous_dist", "description": "The new distance is continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.completion.mem_uniformity_dist", "description": " Elements of the uniformity (defined generally for completions) can be characterized in terms\nof the distance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.completion.dist_triangle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.completion.metric_space", "description": "Metric space structure on the completion of a pseudo_metric space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.completion.uniform_continuous_dist", "description": "The new distance is uniformly continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.completion.dist_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.completion.dist_eq", "description": "The new distance is an extension of the original distance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.completion.edist_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.completion.eq_of_dist_eq_zero", "description": "If two points are at distance 0, then they coincide.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.has_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.eq_pow_count_factors_of_dvd_pow", "description": " The only divisors of prime powers are prime powers. See `eq_pow_find_of_dvd_irreducible_pow`\nfor an explicit expression as a p-power (without using `count`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.count_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.prod_le_prod_iff_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.factors_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.dvd_of_mem_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.count_factors_eq_find_of_dvd_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wf_dvd_monoid.not_unit_iff_exists_factors_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.dvd_not_unit_iff_normalized_factors_lt_normalized_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factor_set_mem", "description": " `factor_set_mem p s` is the predicate that the irreducible `p` is a member of\n`s : factor_set \u03b1`.\n\nIf `p` is not irreducible, `p` is not a member of any `factor_set`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.dvd_of_dvd_mul_right_of_no_prime_factors", "description": " Euclid's lemma: if `a \u2223 b * c` and `a` and `b` have no common prime factors, `a \u2223 c`.\nCompare `is_coprime.dvd_of_dvd_mul_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wf_dvd_monoid.exists_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.exists_mem_normalized_factors_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.count_of_coprime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.induction_on_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.bcount", "description": "`bcount p s` is the multiplicity of `p` in the factor_set `s` (with bundled `p`)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factor_set", "description": " `factor_set \u03b1` representation elements of unique factorization domain as multisets.\n`multiset \u03b1` produced by `normalized_factors` are only unique up to associated elements, while the\nmultisets in `factor_set \u03b1` are unique by equality and restricted to irreducible elements. This\ngives us a representation of each element as a unique multisets (or the added \u22a4 for 0), which has a\ncomplete lattice struture. Infimum is the greatest common divisor and supremum is the least common\nmultiple.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.sup_mul_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.normalized_factors_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factor_set.has_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.dvd_iff_normalized_factors_le_normalized_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "factorization_mul", "description": "For nonzero `a` and `b`, the power of `p` in `a * b` is the sum of the powers in `a` and `b`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.ufm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.mem_factors'_iff_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.induction_on_coprime", "description": " If `P` holds for `0`, units and powers of primes,\nand `P x \u2227 P y` for coprime `x, y` implies `P (x * y)`,\nthen `P` holds on all `a : \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.count_normalized_factors_eq'", "description": " The number of times an irreducible factor `p` appears in `normalized_factors x` is defined by\nthe number of times it divides `x`. This is a slightly more general version of\n`unique_factorization_monoid.count_normalized_factors_eq` that allows `p = 0`.\n\nSee also `multiplicity_eq_count_normalized_factors` if `n` is given by `multiplicity p x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.to_gcd_monoid", "description": "`to_gcd_monoid` constructs a GCD monoid out of a unique factorization domain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.prod_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.pow_right_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "factorization_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.normalized_factors_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "irreducible_iff_prime_of_exists_unique_irreducible_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.pow_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.irreducible_of_normalized_factor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.le_multiplicity_iff_replicate_le_normalized_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.multiplicative_prime_power", "description": " If `f` maps `p ^ i` to `(f p) ^ i` for primes `p`, and `f`\nis multiplicative on coprime elements, then `f` is multiplicative on all products of primes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.normalized_factors_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wf_dvd_monoid.exists_irreducible_factor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.unique'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.iff_exists_prime_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wf_dvd_monoid.wf_dvd_monoid_associates", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.exists_mem_factors_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.coprime_iff_inf_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factors_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factor_set.sup_add_inf_eq_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.count_le_count_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.exists_reduced_factors", "description": " If `a \u2260 0, b` are elements of a unique factorization domain, then dividing\nout their common factor `c'` gives `a'` and `b'` with no factors in common.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.normalized_factors_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prime_factors_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.count_mul_of_coprime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.prod_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.of_exists_prime_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.quot_out", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.normalized_factors_prod_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.prime_of_normalized_factor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.factors", "description": "Noncomputably determines the multiset of prime factors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.reducible_not_mem_factor_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.is_pow_of_dvd_count", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.normalize_normalized_factor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.has_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.factors_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.unique_factorization_monoid_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.normalized_factors", "description": "Noncomputably determines the multiset of prime factors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.count_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factors_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.mem_normalized_factors_eq_of_associated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.bfactor_set_mem", "description": "membership in a factor_set (bundled version)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.count_ne_zero_iff_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wf_dvd_monoid.iff_well_founded_associates", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.normalized_factors_of_irreducible_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.factors_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid", "description": " unique factorization monoids.\n\nThese are defined as `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero`s with well-founded strict divisibility\nrelations, but this is equivalent to more familiar definitions:\n\nEach element (except zero) is uniquely represented as a multiset of irreducible factors.\nUniqueness is only up to associated elements.\n\nEach element (except zero) is non-uniquely represented as a multiset\nof prime factors.\n\nTo define a UFD using the definition in terms of multisets\nof irreducible factors, use the definition `of_exists_unique_irreducible_factors`\n\nTo define a UFD using the definition in terms of multisets\nof prime factors, use the definition `of_exists_prime_factors`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.to_wf_dvd_monoid", "description": " unique factorization monoids.\n\nThese are defined as `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero`s with well-founded strict divisibility\nrelations, but this is equivalent to more familiar definitions:\n\nEach element (except zero) is uniquely represented as a multiset of irreducible factors.\nUniqueness is only up to associated elements.\n\nEach element (except zero) is non-uniquely represented as a multiset\nof prime factors.\n\nTo define a UFD using the definition in terms of multisets\nof irreducible factors, use the definition `of_exists_unique_irreducible_factors`\n\nTo define a UFD using the definition in terms of multisets\nof prime factors, use the definition `of_exists_prime_factors`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.irreducible_iff_prime", "description": " unique factorization monoids.\n\nThese are defined as `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero`s with well-founded strict divisibility\nrelations, but this is equivalent to more familiar definitions:\n\nEach element (except zero) is uniquely represented as a multiset of irreducible factors.\nUniqueness is only up to associated elements.\n\nEach element (except zero) is non-uniquely represented as a multiset\nof prime factors.\n\nTo define a UFD using the definition in terms of multisets\nof irreducible factors, use the definition `of_exists_unique_irreducible_factors`\n\nTo define a UFD using the definition in terms of multisets\nof prime factors, use the definition `of_exists_prime_factors`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "factorization_eq_count", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.dvd_count_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factors_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.normalization_monoid.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.dvd_of_mem_factors'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.fintype_subtype_dvd", "description": " If `y` is a nonzero element of a unique factorization monoid with finitely\nmany units (e.g. `\u2124`, `ideal (ring_of_integers K)`), it has finitely many divisors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.pow_eq_pow_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.map_subtype_coe_factors'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.unique_factorization_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.eq_of_eq_counts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "irreducible_iff_prime_of_exists_prime_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.count_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.ne_zero_of_mem_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.dvd_of_mem_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factor_set.coe_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "irreducible.normalized_factors_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.normalized_factors_irreducible", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.count_le_count_of_factors_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.count_eq_zero_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.exists_prime_dvd_of_not_inf_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factors'_cong", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.eq_of_prod_eq_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.normalized_factors_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.normalization_monoid", "description": "Noncomputably defines a `normalization_monoid` structure on a `unique_factorization_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.mem_factors_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.exists_prime_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factors_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.dvd_of_mem_normalized_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "factorization_pow", "description": "For any `p`, the power of `p` in `x^n` is `n` times the power in `x`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.max_power_factor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wf_dvd_monoid.of_well_founded_associates", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.exists_reduced_factors'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.count_some", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.eq_pow_of_mul_eq_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wf_dvd_monoid.well_founded_associates", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prime_factors_irreducible", "description": "If an irreducible has a prime factorization,\n then it is an associate of one of its prime factors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.prod_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "factorization", "description": "This returns the multiset of irreducible factors as a `finsupp`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wf_dvd_monoid.of_wf_dvd_monoid_associates", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factors_eq_none_iff_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.multiplicity_eq_count_normalized_factors", "description": " The multiplicity of an irreducible factor of a nonzero element is exactly the number of times\nthe normalized factor occurs in the `normalized_factors`.\n\nSee also `count_normalized_factors_eq` which expands the definition of `multiplicity`\nto produce a specification for `count (normalized_factors _) _`..", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.count_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factor_set_mem_eq_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.to_normalized_gcd_monoid", "description": "`to_normalized_gcd_monoid` constructs a GCD monoid out of a normalization on a\n unique factorization domain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.factors_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factors_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.mem_factor_set_some", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.exists_mem_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_ring.wf_dvd_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.prod_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.multiplicative_of_coprime", "description": " If `f` maps `p ^ i` to `(f p) ^ i` for primes `p`, and `f`\nis multiplicative on coprime elements, then `f` is multiplicative everywhere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.le_of_count_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wf_dvd_monoid", "description": " Well-foundedness of the strict version of |, which is equivalent to the descending chain\ncondition on divisibility and to the ascending chain condition on\nprincipal ideals in an integral domain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wf_dvd_monoid.well_founded_dvd_not_unit", "description": " Well-foundedness of the strict version of |, which is equivalent to the descending chain\ncondition on divisibility and to the ascending chain condition on\nprincipal ideals in an integral domain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.factors_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.eq_factors_of_eq_counts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.prime_pow_dvd_iff_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.eq_of_factors_eq_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.no_factors_of_no_prime_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factor_set.prod_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wf_dvd_monoid.induction_on_irreducible", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.prime_pow_coprime_prod_of_coprime_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factors_0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factors_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.irreducible_of_factor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.eq_pow_find_of_dvd_irreducible_pow", "description": "The only divisors of prime powers are prime powers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.factors_eq_normalized_factors", "description": " An arbitrary choice of factors of `x : M` is exactly the (unique) normalized set of factors,\nif `M` has a trivial group of units.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.count_normalized_factors_eq", "description": " The number of times an irreducible factor `p` appears in `normalized_factors x` is defined by\nthe number of times it divides `x`.\n\nSee also `multiplicity_eq_count_normalized_factors` if `n` is given by `multiplicity p x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.count_mul_of_coprime'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.factors_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.count_reducible", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "factorization_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ufm_of_gcd_of_wf_dvd_monoid", "description": "Can't be an instance because it would cause a loop `ufm \u2192 wf_dvd_monoid \u2192 ufm \u2192 ...`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.dvd_count_of_dvd_count_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.exists_associated_prime_pow_of_unique_normalized_factor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factors_eq_some_iff_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factors_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wf_dvd_monoid.of_exists_prime_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.mem_factors'_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.count", "description": " `count p s` is the multiplicity of the irreducible `p` in the factor_set `s`.\n\nIf `p` is not irreducible, `count p s` is defined to be `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factors", "description": "This returns the multiset of irreducible factors of an associate as a `factor_set`,\n a multiset of irreducible associates `with_top`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.normalized_factors_eq_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.mem_factors_iff_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "support_factorization", "description": "The support of `factorization n` is exactly the finset of normalized factors", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.of_exists_unique_irreducible_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factors'", "description": "This returns the multiset of irreducible factors as a `factor_set`,\n a multiset of irreducible associates `with_top`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.exists_mem_normalized_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.factors_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.prod_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factor_set.prod", "description": "Evaluates the product of a `factor_set` to be the product of the corresponding multiset,\n or `0` if there is none.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.zero_not_mem_normalized_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.mem_factor_set_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.prime_of_factor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.induction_on_prime_power", "description": " If `P` holds for units and powers of primes,\nand `P x \u2227 P y` for coprime `x, y` implies `P (x * y)`,\nthen `P` holds on a product of powers of distinct primes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.normalized_factors_prod_of_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factor_set.unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factors_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.associated_iff_normalized_factors_eq_normalized_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associated_of_factorization_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.normalized_factors_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.factors_prime_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_factorization_monoid.dvd_of_dvd_mul_left_of_no_prime_factors", "description": " Euclid's lemma: if `a \u2223 b * c` and `a` and `c` have no common prime factors, `a \u2223 b`.\nCompare `is_coprime.dvd_of_dvd_mul_left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associates.prod_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_form.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_form.neg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cusp_form.zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cusp_form.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cusp_form.coe_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_form.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_form.has_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cusp_form_class.to_slash_invariant_form_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cusp_form.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_form_class.modular_form", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_form_to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cusp_form.smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_form_class.to_slash_invariant_form_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_form_class", "description": "`modular_form_class F \u0393 k` says that `F` is a type of bundled functions that extend\n`slash_invariant_form_class` by requiring that the functions be holomorphic and bounded\nat infinity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_form_class.coe", "description": "`modular_form_class F \u0393 k` says that `F` is a type of bundled functions that extend\n`slash_invariant_form_class` by requiring that the functions be holomorphic and bounded\nat infinity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_form_class.coe_injective'", "description": "`modular_form_class F \u0393 k` says that `F` is a type of bundled functions that extend\n`slash_invariant_form_class` by requiring that the functions be holomorphic and bounded\nat infinity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_form_class.slash_action_eq", "description": "`modular_form_class F \u0393 k` says that `F` is a type of bundled functions that extend\n`slash_invariant_form_class` by requiring that the functions be holomorphic and bounded\nat infinity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_form_class.holo", "description": "`mo