name": "guard_false", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.map_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "seq_eq_bind_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.from_zeta_aut", "description": "Maps `\u03bc` to the `alg_equiv` that sends `is_cyclotomic_extension.zeta` to `\u03bc`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.from_zeta_aut_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.aut_equiv_pow_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.aut_to_pow_injective", "description": " `is_primitive_root.aut_to_pow` is injective in the case that it's considered over a cyclotomic\nfield extension.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.aut_equiv_pow_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gal_cyclotomic_equiv_units_zmod", "description": " `is_cyclotomic_extension.aut_equiv_pow` repackaged in terms of `gal`.\nAsserts that the Galois group of `cyclotomic n K` is equivalent to `(zmod n)\u02e3`\nif `cyclotomic n K` is irreducible in the base field.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gal_X_pow_equiv_units_zmod", "description": " `is_cyclotomic_extension.aut_equiv_pow` repackaged in terms of `gal`.\nAsserts that the Galois group of `X ^ n - 1` is equivalent to `(zmod n)\u02e3`\nif `cyclotomic n K` is irreducible in the base field.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.aut.comm_group", "description": "Cyclotomic extensions are abelian.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.aut_equiv_pow", "description": "The `mul_equiv` that takes an automorphism `f` to the element `k : (zmod n)\u02e3` such that\n `f \u03bc = \u03bc ^ k` for any root of unity `\u03bc`. A  strengthening of `is_primitive_root.aut_to_pow`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_perm_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.trunc_swap_factors", "description": "This computably represents the fact that any permutation can be represented as the product of\n a list of transpositions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_aux_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.perm_maps_to_inl_iff_maps_to_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_aux3_mul_and_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.support_pow_coprime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.eq_sign_of_surjective_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.mem_sum_congr_hom_range_of_perm_maps_to_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_swap'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.perm_inv_maps_to_iff_maps_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_aux", "description": "`sign_aux \u03c3` is the sign of a permutation on `fin n`, defined as the parity of the number of\n pairs `(x\u2081, x\u2082)` such that `x\u2082 < x\u2081` but `\u03c3 x\u2081 \u2264 \u03c3 x\u2082`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.closure_is_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_trans_trans_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_bij_aux", "description": "`sign_bij_aux f \u27e8a, b\u27e9` returns the pair consisting of `f a` and `f b` in decreasing order.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_subtype_perm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.subtype_perm_of_fintype", "description": "If the permutation `f` maps `{x // p x}` into itself, then this returns the permutation\n on `{x // p x}` induced by `f`. Note that the `h` hypothesis is weaker than for\n `equiv.perm.subtype_perm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.perm_inv_on_of_perm_on_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.is_swap.sign_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.swap_factors_aux", "description": "Given a list `l : list \u03b1` and a permutation `f : perm \u03b1` such that the nonfixed points of `f`\n are in `l`, recursively factors `f` as a product of transpositions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_prod_congr_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.swap_factors", "description": " `swap_factors` represents a permutation as a product of a list of transpositions.\nThe representation is non unique and depends on the linear order structure.\nFor types without linear order `trunc_swap_factors` can be used.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.disjoint.extend_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_bij_aux_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.fin_pairs_lt", "description": "set of all pairs (\u27e8a, b\u27e9 : \u03a3 a : fin n, fin n) such that b < a", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_prod_list_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign", "description": " `sign` of a permutation returns the signature or parity of a permutation, `1` for even\npermutations, `-1` for odd permutations. It is the unique surjective group homomorphism from\n`perm \u03b1` to the group with two elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.is_conj_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.swap_induction_on", "description": " An induction principle for permutations. If `P` holds for the identity permutation, and\nis preserved under composition with a non-trivial swap, then `P` holds for all permutations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_of_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_bij", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_aux_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_bij_aux_surj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.perm_inv_maps_to_of_maps_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_aux_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_bij_aux_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.mem_fin_pairs_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_aux_eq_sign_aux2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_extend_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_subtype_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.prod_prod_extend_right", "description": " If we apply `prod_extend_right a (\u03c3 a)` for all `a : \u03b1` in turn,\nwe get `prod_congr_right \u03c3`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_sum_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.disjoint.order_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_prod_extend_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_aux3", "description": "When the multiset `s : multiset \u03b1` contains all nonfixed points of the permutation `f : perm \u03b1`,\n `sign_aux2 f _` recursively calculates the sign of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_aux2", "description": "When the list `l : list \u03b1` contains all nonfixed points of the permutation `f : perm \u03b1`,\n `sign_aux2 l f` recursively calculates the sign of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.r.decidable_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_symm_trans_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.sign_eq_sign_of_equiv", "description"