 Ordinals will be defined as a quotient\nof this type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Well_order.\u03b1", "description": " Bundled structure registering a well order on a type. Ordinals will be defined as a quotient\nof this type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Well_order.r", "description": " Bundled structure registering a well order on a type. Ordinals will be defined as a quotient\nof this type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Well_order.wo", "description": " Bundled structure registering a well order on a type. Ordinals will be defined as a quotient\nof this type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.out_nonempty_iff_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.induction", "description": " Reformulation of well founded induction on ordinals as a lemma that works with the\n`induction` tactic, as in `induction i using ordinal.induction with i IH`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.card_typein_out_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.unique_out_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.enum_iso", "description": "A well order `r` is order isomorphic to the set of ordinals smaller than `type r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.lt_univ'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.one_out_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_well_order.subtype_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.enum_iso_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.univ", "description": "The cardinal `univ` is the cardinality of ordinal `univ`, or\n equivalently the cardinal of `ordinal.{u}`, or `cardinal.{u}`,\n as an element of `cardinal.{v}` (when `u < v`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.ord_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.univ_umax", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.lift_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.add_covariant_class_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.nat_le_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "embedding_to_cardinal", "description": "An embedding of any type to the set of cardinals.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.type_lift_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.univ_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.enum", "description": "`enum r o h` is the `o`-th element of `\u03b1` ordered by `r`.\n That is, `enum` maps an initial segment of the ordinals, those\n less than the order type of `r`, to the elements of `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.lt_one_iff_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.enum_iso_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.card_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.typein_one_out", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.enum_type", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.enum_zero_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.lift_umax'", "description": "`lift.{(max v u) u}` equals `lift.{v u}`. Using `set_option pp.universes true` will make it much\n   easier to understand what's happening when using this lemma.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.lift.initial_seg_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.lift_omega", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.out_empty_iff_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "well_ordering_rel", "description": " Any type can be endowed with a well order, obtained by pulling back the well order over\ncardinals by some embedding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.succ_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.le_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.card_typein_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.initial_seg_out", "description": " Given two ordinals `\u03b1 \u2264 \u03b2`, then `initial_seg_out \u03b1 \u03b2` is the initial segment embedding\nof `\u03b1` to `\u03b2`, as map from a model type for `\u03b1` to a model type for `\u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.succ_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.one_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.card_type", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.add_one_eq_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.typein_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.lift.principal_seg_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.type_eq_one_iff_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.small_iff_lift_mk_lt_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.enum_iso_out_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.enum_iso_out_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.ord_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.conditionally_complete_linear_order_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.ord_eq_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.card_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.univ", "description": "`univ.{u v}` is the order type of the ordinals of `Type u` as a member\n of `ordinal.{v}` (when `u < v`). It is an inaccessible cardinal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.le_enum_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.gci_ord_card", "description": "Galois coinsertion between `cardinal.ord` and `ordinal.card`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.rel_iso_enum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.is_empty_out_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.rel_iso_enum'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.ord.order_embedding_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.type_fin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.ord_le_type", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.zero_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.typein_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.card_typein", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.enum_iso_out", "description": "The order isomorphism between ordinals less than `o` and `o.out.\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.bot_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.add_swap_covariant_class_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.enum_typein", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.type_lt_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.has_add", "description": "`o\u2081 + o\u2082` is the order on the disjoint union of `o\u2081` and `o\u2082` obtained by declaring that\n every element of `o\u2081` is smaller than every element of `o\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.card_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.lift.initial_seg", "description": "Initial segment version of the lift operation on ordinals, embedding `ordinal.{u}` in\n `ordinal.{v}` as an initial segment when `u \u2264 v`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.ord_le_ord", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.type_eq_one_of_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.lift.principal_seg_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.typein_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.pos_iff_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_embedding.ordinal_type_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.ord_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.lift_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.lift_down'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.lift_lt_univ'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.add_monoid_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordinal.ty