}, {"name": "add_opposite.semifield", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.op_rat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.semifield", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.has_rat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.unop_rat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.unop_rat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.has_rat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.division_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.op_rat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.division_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.division_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.division_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.add_quot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.lift_mk_ring_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot", "description": "The quotient of a ring by an arbitrary relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.to_quot", "description": "The quotient of a ring by an arbitrary relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.ideal_quotient_to_ring_quot_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.lift_alg_hom", "description": "Any `S`-algebra homomorphism `f : A \u2192\u2090[S] B` which respects a relation `s : A \u2192 A \u2192 Prop`\nfactors uniquely through a morphism `ring_quot s \u2192\u2090[S]  B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.smul_quot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.ring_quot_ext'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.eq_lift_comp_mk_ring_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.mk_alg_hom_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.has_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.ring_quot_equiv_ideal_quotient", "description": "The ring equivalence between `ring_quot r` and `(ideal.of_rel r).quotient`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.ring_con", "description": "`eqv_gen (ring_quot.rel r)` is a ring congruence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.rel.star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.eqv_gen_rel_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.mk_alg_hom", "description": "The quotient map from an `S`-algebra to its quotient, as a homomorphism of `S`-algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_con.coe_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.rel.sub_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.ideal_quotient_to_ring_quot", "description": "The universal ring homomorphism from `B \u29f8 ideal.of_rel r` to `ring_quot r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.mul_quot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.pow_quot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.zero_quot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.rel", "description": "Given an arbitrary relation `r` on a ring, we strengthen it to a relation `rel r`,\nsuch that the equivalence relation generated by `rel r` has `x ~ y` if and only if\n`x - y` is in the ideal generated by elements `a - b` such that `r a b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.rel.of", "description": "Given an arbitrary relation `r` on a ring, we strengthen it to a relation `rel r`,\nsuch that the equivalence relation generated by `rel r` has `x ~ y` if and only if\n`x - y` is in the ideal generated by elements `a - b` such that `r a b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.rel.add_left", "description": "Given an arbitrary relation `r` on a ring, we strengthen it to a relation `rel r`,\nsuch that the equivalence relation generated by `rel r` has `x ~ y` if and only if\n`x - y` is in the ideal generated by elements `a - b` such that `r a b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.rel.mul_left", "description": "Given an arbitrary relation `r` on a ring, we strengthen it to a relation `rel r`,\nsuch that the equivalence relation generated by `rel r` has `x ~ y` if and only if\n`x - y` is in the ideal generated by elements `a - b` such that `r a b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.rel.mul_right", "description": "Given an arbitrary relation `r` on a ring, we strengthen it to a relation `rel r`,\nsuch that the equivalence relation generated by `rel r` has `x ~ y` if and only if\n`x - y` is in the ideal generated by elements `a - b` such that `r a b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.star_ring", "description": "Transfer a star_ring instance through a quotient, if the quotient is invariant to `star`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.mk_alg_hom_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.ring_quot_to_ideal_quotient_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.eq_lift_alg_hom_comp_mk_alg_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.lift_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.star'_quot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.mk_ring_hom_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.mk_ring_hom_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.rel.sub_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.nat.has_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.mk_alg_hom_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.lift_alg_hom_mk_alg_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.ring_quot_to_ideal_quotient", "description": "The universal ring homomorphism from `ring_quot r` to `B \u29f8 ideal.of_rel r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.mk_ring_hom", "description": "The quotient map from a ring to its quotient, as a homomorphism of rings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.rel.add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.rel.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.one_quot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.ring_quot_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.rel.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.lift_alg_hom_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_con.quotient.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.neg_quot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.lift", "description": "Any ring homomorphism `f : R \u2192+* T` which respects a relation `r : R \u2192 R \u2192 Prop`\nfactors uniquely through a morphism `ring_quot r \u2192+* T`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_quot.sub_quot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "self_zpow_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "self_zpow_of_nonpos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.away.away_map.lift_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.away_lift", "description": "Given a map `f : R \u2192+* S` and an element `r : R`, such that `f r` is invertible,\n we may construct a map `R\u1d63 \u2192+* S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.away.lift", "description": " Given `x : R`, a localization map `F : R \u2192+* S` away from `x`, and a map of `comm_semiring`s\n`g : R \u2192+* P` such that `g x` is invertible, the homomorphism induced from `S` to `P` sending\n`z : S` to `g y * (g x)\u207b\u207f`, where `y : R, n : \u2115` are such that `z = F y * (F x)\u207b\u207f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "self_zpow_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "self_zpow_mul_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.away.mul_inv_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "self_zpow", "description": "`self_zpow x (m : \u2124)` is `x ^ m` as an element of the localization away from `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "self_zpow_of_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "self_zpow_sub_cast_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.away.away_map.lift_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.away.map", "description": "Given a map `f : R \u2192+* S` and an element `r : R`, we may construct a map `R\u1d63 \u2192+* S\u1d63`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.at_unit", "description": "The localization away from a unit is isomorphic to the ring", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.away_map", "description": "Given a map `f : R \u2192+* S` and an element `r : R`, we may construct a map `R\u1d63 \u2192+* S\u1d63`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.away_of_is_unit_of_bijective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "self_zpow_neg_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.away.away_to_away_right", "description": " Given `x y : R` and localizations `S`, `P` away from `x` and `x * y`\nrespectively, the homomorphism induced from `S` to `P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.at_units", "description": "The localization at a module of units is isomorphic to the ring", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_reduced_fraction'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.at_one", "description": "The localization at one is isomorphic to the ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "self_zpow_neg_coe_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.away", "description": " Given `x : R`, the typeclass `is_localization.away x S` states that `S` is\nisomorphic to the localization of `R` at the submonoid generated by `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "self_zpow_coe_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "self_zpow_pow_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.away.inv_self", "description": "Given `x : R` and a localization map `F : R \u2192+* S` away from `x`, `inv_self` is `(F x)\u207b\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "self_zpow_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_subalgebra.to_endomorphism_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ring.of_associative_ring", "description": "An associative ring gives rise to a Lie ring by taking the bracket to be the ring commutator.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.to_endomorphism_comp_subtype_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.ad_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.coe_to_lie_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.to_lie_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.lie_conj_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.to_lie_hom_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ring.of_associative_ring_bracket", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.to_lie_hom", "description": " The map `of_associative_algebra` associating a Lie algebra to an associative algebra is\nfunctorial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.to_endomorphism", "description": " A Lie module yields a Lie algebra morphism into the linear endomorphisms of the module.\n\nSee also `lie_module.to_module_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_equiv.to_lie_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.lie_hom.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_equiv.to_lie_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.ad", "description": "The adjoint action of a Lie algebra on itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ring.lie_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.lie_conj", "description": "A linear equivalence of two modules induces a Lie algebra equivalence of their endomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_equiv.to_lie_equiv", "description": "An equivalence of associative algebras is an equivalence of associated Lie algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.lie_module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.coe_map_to_endomorphism_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.of_associative_module", "description": " A representation of an associative algebra `A` is also a representation of `A`, regarded as a\nLie algebra via the ring commutator.\n\nSee the comment at `lie_ring_module.of_associative_module` for why the possibility `M = A` means\nthis cannot be a global instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.to_lie_hom_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ring_module.of_associative_module", "description": " We can regard a module over an associative ring `A` as a Lie ring module over `A` with Lie\nbracket equal to its ring commutator.\n\nNote that this cannot be a global instance because it would create a diamond when `M = A`,\nspecifically we can build two mathematically-different `has_bracket A A`s:\n 1. `@ring.has_bracket A _` which says `\u2045a, b\u2046 = a * b - b * a`\n 2. `(@lie_ring_module.of_associative_module A _ A _ _).to_has_bracket` which says `\u2045a, b\u2046 = a \u2022 b`\n    (and thus `\u2045a, b\u2046 = a * b`)\n\nSee note [reducible non-instances]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.to_endomorphism_to_linear_map_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.lie_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.lie_ring_module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_subalgebra.ad_comp_incl_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.to_endomorphism_restrict_eq_to_endomorphism", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.to_endomorphism_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute_iff_lie_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.to_lie_hom_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_subalgebra.to_endomorphism_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_subalgebra_of_subalgebra", "description": "A subalgebra of an associative algebra is a Lie subalgebra of the associated Lie algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.to_endomorphism_module_End", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.to_lie_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.ad_eq_lmul_left_sub_lmul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.has_bracket", "description": " The bracket operation for rings is the ring commutator, which captures the extent to which a\nring is commutative. It is identically zero exactly when the ring is commutative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.lie_conj_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.lie_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.of_associative_algebra", "description": " An associative algebra gives rise to a Lie algebra by taking the bracket to be the ring\ncommutator.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_eq_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line", "description": " The type of combinatorial lines. A line `l : line \u03b1 \u03b9` in the hypercube `\u03b9 \u2192 \u03b1` defines a\nfunction `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b9 \u2192 \u03b1` from `\u03b1` to the hypercube, such that for each coordinate `i : \u03b9`, the function\n`\u03bb x, l x i` is either `id` or constant. We require lines to be nontrivial in the sense that\n`\u03bb x, l x i` is `id` for at least one `i`.\n\nFormally, a line is represented by the function `l.idx_fun : \u03b9 \u2192 option \u03b1` which says whether\n`\u03bb x, l x i` is `id` (corresponding to `l.idx_fun i = none`) or constantly `y` (corresponding to\n`l.idx_fun i = some y`).\n\nWhen `\u03b1` has size `1` there can be many elements of `line \u03b1 \u03b9` defining the same function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.idx_fun", "description": " The type of combinatorial lines. A line `l : line \u03b1 \u03b9` in the hypercube `\u03b9 \u2192 \u03b1` defines a\nfunction `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b9 \u2192 \u03b1` from `\u03b1` to the hypercube, such that for each coordinate `i : \u03b9`, the function\n`\u03bb x, l x i` is either `id` or constant. We require lines to be nontrivial in the sense that\n`\u03bb x, l x i` is `id` for at least one `i`.\n\nFormally, a line is represented by the function `l.idx_fun : \u03b9 \u2192 option \u03b1` which says whether\n`\u03bb x, l x i` is `id` (corresponding to `l.idx_fun i = none`) or constantly `y` (corresponding to\n`l.idx_fun i = some y`).\n\nWhen `\u03b1` has size `1` there can be many elements of `line \u03b1 \u03b9` defining the same function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.proper", "description": " The type of combinatorial lines. A line `l : line \u03b1 \u03b9` in the hypercube `\u03b9 \u2192 \u03b1` defines a\nfunction `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b9 \u2192 \u03b1` from `\u03b1` to the hypercube, such that for each coordinate `i : \u03b9`, the function\n`\u03bb x, l x i` is either `id` or constant. We require lines to be nontrivial in the sense that\n`\u03bb x, l x i` is `id` for at least one `i`.\n\nFormally, a line is represented by the function `l.idx_fun : \u03b9 \u2192 option \u03b1` which says whether\n`\u03bb x, l x i` is `id` (corresponding to `l.idx_fun i = none`) or constantly `y` (corresponding to\n`l.idx_fun i = some y`).\n\nWhen `\u03b1` has size `1` there can be many elements of `line \u03b1 \u03b9` defining the same function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.exists_mono_homothetic_copy", "description": " A generalization of Van der Waerden's theorem: if `M` is a finitely colored commutative\nmonoid, and `S` is a finite subset, then there exists a monochromatic homothetic copy of `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.horizontal_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.horizontal", "description": "A line in `\u03b9 \u2192 \u03b1` and a point in `\u03b9' \u2192 \u03b1` determine a line in `\u03b9 \u2295 \u03b9' \u2192 \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.almost_mono.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.prod", "description": "One line in `\u03b9 \u2192 \u03b1` and one in `\u03b9' \u2192 \u03b1` together determine a line in `\u03b9 \u2295 \u03b9' \u2192 \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.apply_none", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.map", "description": " A function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1'` determines a function `line \u03b1 \u03b9 \u2192 line \u03b1' \u03b9`. For a coordinate `i`,\n`l.map f` is the identity at `i` if `l` is, and constantly `f y` if `l` is constantly `y` at `i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.color_focused", "description": " The type of collections of lines such that\n- each line is only one color except possibly at its endpoint\n- the lines all have the same endpoint\n- the colors of the lines are distinct.\nUsed in the proof `exists_mono_in_high_dimension`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.color_focused.lines", "description": " The type of collections of lines such that\n- each line is only one color except possibly at its endpoint\n- the lines all have the same endpoint\n- the colors of the lines are distinct.\nUsed in the proof `exists_mono_in_high_dimension`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.color_focused.focus", "description": " The type of collections of lines such that\n- each line is only one color except possibly at its endpoint\n- the lines all have the same endpoint\n- the colors of the lines are distinct.\nUsed in the proof `exists_mono_in_high_dimension`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.color_focused.is_focused", "description": " The type of collections of lines such that\n- each line is only one color except possibly at its endpoint\n- the lines all have the same endpoint\n- the colors of the lines are distinct.\nUsed in the proof `exists_mono_in_high_dimension`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.color_focused.distinct_colors", "description": " The type of collections of lines such that\n- each line is only one color except possibly at its endpoint\n- the lines all have the same endpoint\n- the colors of the lines are distinct.\nUsed in the proof `exists_mono_in_high_dimension`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.diagonal", "description": "The diagonal line. It is the identity at every coordinate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.vertical", "description": "A point in `\u03b9 \u2192 \u03b1` and a line in `\u03b9' \u2192 \u03b1` determine a line in `\u03b9 \u2295 \u03b9' \u2192 \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.color_focused.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.apply_of_ne_none", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.is_mono", "description": "A line is monochromatic if all its points are the same color.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.exists_mono_in_high_dimension", "description": " The Hales-Jewett theorem: for any finite types `\u03b1` and `\u03ba`, there exists a finite type `\u03b9` such\nthat whenever the hypercube `\u03b9 \u2192 \u03b1` is `\u03ba`-colored, there is a monochromatic combinatorial line.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.vertical_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.diagonal_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.almost_mono", "description": "The type of lines that are only one color except possibly at their endpoints.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.almost_mono.line", "description": "The type of lines that are only one color except possibly at their endpoints.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.almost_mono.color", "description": "The type of lines that are only one color except possibly at their endpoints.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "combinatorics.line.almost_mono.has_color", "description": "The type of lines that are only one color except possibly at their endpoints.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_singleton_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_union_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_hull_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_mono_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_convex_join_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_Union_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_mono_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_right_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_assoc_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_hull_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join", "description": " The join of two sets is the union of the segments joining them. This can be interpreted as the\ntopological join, but within the original space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_convex_join_convex_join_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.convex_join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_subset_convex_hull", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_left_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_empty_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_segment_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_singletons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_segments", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_convex_join_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_singleton_segment", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.convex_hull_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_singleton_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "segment_subset_convex_join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_empty_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_Union_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_convex_join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_union_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_join_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080'_map_F", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.map_on_summand\u2080_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080_obj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.map_epi_on_summand_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.map", "description": "The functor `\u0393\u2080 : chain_complex C \u2115 \u2964 simplicial_object C`, on morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.termwise.map_mono_\u03b4\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2082_map_f_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.map_mono_on_summand_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2082", "description": " The extension of `\u0393\u2080 : chain_complex C \u2115 \u2964 simplicial_object C`\non the idempotent completions. It shall be an equivalence of categories\nfor any additive category `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2082_obj_p_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.P_infty_on_\u0393\u2080_splitting_summand_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.higher_faces_vanish.on_\u0393\u2080_summand_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080'_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.map_on_summand\u2080'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.map_mono_on_summand_id_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.is_\u03b4\u2080.iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.obj\u2082", "description": " The functor `\u0393\u2080` sends a chain complex `K` to the simplicial object which\nsends `\u0394` to the direct sum of the objects `summand K \u0394 A` for all `A : splitting.index_set \u0394`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.splitting_iso_hom_eq_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.is_\u03b4\u2080.eq_\u03b4\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080_obj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.termwise.map_mono_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.termwise.map_mono_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.termwise.map_mono_naturality_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.splitting_map_eq_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.is_\u03b4\u2080", "description": " `is_\u03b4\u2080 i` is a simple condition used to check whether a monomorphism `i` in\n`simplex_category` identifies to the coface map `\u03b4 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.map_epi_on_summand_id_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.splitting", "description": "By construction, the simplicial `\u0393\u2080.obj K` is equipped with a splitting.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.map_on_summand\u2080'_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.termwise.map_mono", "description": " A monomorphism `i : \u0394' \u27f6 \u0394` induces a morphism `K.X \u0394.len \u27f6 K.X \u0394'.len` which\nis the identity if `\u0394 = \u0394'`, the differential on the complex `K` if `i = \u03b4 0`, and\nzero otherwise.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.termwise.map_mono_\u03b4\u2080'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.map", "description": " The simplicial morphism on the simplicial object `\u0393\u2080.obj K` induced by\na morphism `\u0394' \u2192 \u0394` in `simplex_category` is defined on each summand\nassociated to an `A : \u0393_index_set \u0394` in terms of the epi-mono factorisation\nof `\u03b8 \u226b A.e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.termwise.map_mono_comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.summand", "description": " In the definition of `(\u0393\u2080.obj K).obj \u0394` as a direct sum indexed by `A : splitting.index_set \u0394`,\nthe summand `summand K \u0394 A` is `K.X A.1.len`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2082_obj_X_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.termwise.map_mono_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.P_infty_on_\u0393\u2080_splitting_summand_eq_self_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.map_on_summand'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj", "description": "The functor `\u0393\u2080 : chain_complex C \u2115 \u2964 simplicial_object C`, on objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2082_obj_X_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.termwise.map_mono_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.map_on_summand\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.map_on_summand", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080'", "description": " The functor `\u0393\u2080' : chain_complex C \u2115 \u2964 simplicial_object.split C`\nthat induces `\u0393\u2080 : chain_complex C \u2115 \u2964 simplicial_object C`, which\nshall be the inverse functor of the Dold-Kan equivalence for\nabelian or pseudo-abelian categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.map_on_summand_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080", "description": " The functor `\u0393\u2080 : chain_complex C \u2115 \u2964 simplicial_object C`, which is\nthe inverse functor of the Dold-Kan equivalence when `C` is an abelian\ncategory, or more generally a pseudoabelian category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080.obj.map_on_summand'_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.\u0393\u2080'_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.functor", "description": " The function `equiv.map` transfers the functoriality of `t` to\n`t'` using the equivalences `eqv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.traversable", "description": " The function `equiv.traverse` transfers a traversable functor\ninstance across the equivalences `eqv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.traverse_eq_map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.comp_traverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.is_lawful_traversable", "description": " The fact that `t` is a lawful traversable functor carries over the\nequivalences to `t'`, with the traversable functor structure given by\n`equiv.traversable`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.map", "description": " Given a functor `t`, a function `t' : Type u \u2192 Type u`, and\nequivalences `t \u03b1 \u2243 t' \u03b1` for all `\u03b1`, then every function `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` can\nbe mapped to a function `t' \u03b1 \u2192 t' \u03b2` functorially (see\n`equiv.functor`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.is_lawful_functor'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.is_lawful_traversable'", "description": " If the `traversable t'` instance has the properties that `map`,\n`map_const`, and `traverse` are equal to the ones that come from\ncarrying the traversable functor structure from `t` over the\nequivalences, then the fact that `t` is a lawful traversable functor\ncarries over as well.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.comp_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.id_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.id_traverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.traverse", "description": " Like `equiv.map`, a function `t' : Type u \u2192 Type u` can be given\nthe structure of a traversable functor using a traversable functor\n`t'` and equivalences `t \u03b1 \u2243 t' \u03b1` for all \u03b1.  See `equiv.traversable`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.is_lawful_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.add_mod_add_of_le_add_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.odd_mod_four_iff", "description": "A natural number is odd iff it has residue `1` or `3` mod `4`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.of_mul_left", "description": " Cancel left multiplication in the modulus.\n\nFor cancelling left multiplication on both sides of the `\u2261`, see `nat.modeq.mul_left_cancel'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.odd_of_mod_four_eq_three", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.cancel_right_div_gcd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq_iff_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.add_right_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.div_mod_eq_mod_mul_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.cancel_right_div_gcd'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.odd_of_mod_four_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.of_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.add_div_eq_of_le_mod_add_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_dvd.dvd.modeq_zero_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq_iff_dvd'", "description": "A variant of `modeq_iff_dvd` with `nat` divisibility", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.cancel_left_div_gcd", "description": "To cancel a common factor `c` from a `modeq` we must divide the modulus `m` by `gcd m c`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.mod_mul_right_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq_of_dvd", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `nat.modeq_iff_dvd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.add_left_cancel'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.mul_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.eq_of_abs_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.chinese_remainder_lt_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.le_mod_add_mod_of_dvd_add_of_not_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.le_of_lt_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.chinese_remainder", "description": "The natural number less than `n*m` congruent to `a` mod `n` and `b` mod `m`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.dvd", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `nat.modeq_iff_dvd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.add_mod_of_add_mod_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.mul_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.mul_right_cancel_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq", "description": "Modular equality. `n.modeq a b`, or `a \u2261 b [MOD n]`, means that `a - b` is a multiple of `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_dvd.dvd.zero_modeq_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq_and_modeq_iff_modeq_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.add_div_of_dvd_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.mul_right_cancel'", "description": " Cancel right multiplication on both sides of the `\u2261` and in the modulus.\n\nFor cancelling right multiplication in the modulus, see `nat.modeq.of_mul_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.add_modeq_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.add_div_of_dvd_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.add_left_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.eq_of_lt_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.gcd_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.chinese_remainder'", "description": "The natural number less than `lcm n m` congruent to `a` mod `n` and `b` mod `m`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.rfl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.add_modeq_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.odd_mul_odd_div_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.cancel_left_div_gcd'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq.add_right_cancel'", "descri