e_eq_right", "description": "The angle \u2220ABB at a point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_eq_zero_iff_ne_and_wbtw", "description": " The angle between three points is zero if and only if one of the first and third points is\nweakly between the other two, and not equal to the second.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sin_eq_one_iff_angle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": "The sine of the angle between three points is 1 if and only if the angle is \u03c0 / 2.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_right_midpoint_eq_pi_div_two_of_dist_eq", "description": " If M is the midpoint of the segment AB and C is the same distance from A as it is from B\nthen \u2220CMB = \u03c0 / 2.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sin_ne_zero_of_not_collinear", "description": "If three points are not collinear, the sine of the angle between them is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle", "description": " The undirected angle at `p2` between the line segments to `p1` and\n`p3`. If either of those points equals `p2`, this is \u03c0/2. Use\n`open_locale euclidean_geometry` to access the `\u2220 p1 p2 p3`\nnotation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_subspace.angle_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_ne_pi_of_not_collinear", "description": "If three points are not collinear, the angle between them is not \u03c0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sbtw.angle\u2082\u2081\u2083_eq_zero", "description": " If the second of three points is strictly between the other two, the angle at the first point\nis zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_neg", "description": "Angles in a vector space are invariant to inversion", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sbtw.angle\u2083\u2081\u2082_eq_zero", "description": " If the second of three points is strictly between the other two, the angle at the first point\n(reversed) is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_eq_zero_of_angle_eq_pi_left", "description": "If the angle \u2220ABC at a point is \u03c0, the angle \u2220BAC is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_pos_of_not_collinear", "description": "If three points are not collinear, the angle between them is positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_const_vsub", "description": "Angles are translation invariant", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.left_dist_ne_zero_of_angle_eq_pi", "description": "If \u2220ABC = \u03c0 then dist A B \u2260 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_eq_angle_of_angle_eq_pi", "description": "If \u2220BCD = \u03c0, then \u2220ABC = \u2220ABD.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sin_eq_zero_iff_angle_eq_zero_or_angle_eq_pi", "description": "The sine of the angle between three points is 0 if and only if the angle is 0 or \u03c0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.collinear_of_angle_eq_zero", "description": "If the angle between three points is 0, they are collinear.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wbtw.angle\u2082\u2081\u2083_eq_zero_of_ne", "description": " If the second of three points is weakly between the other two, and not equal to the first,\nthe angle at the first point is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wbtw.angle\u2082\u2083\u2081_eq_zero_of_ne", "description": " If the second of three points is weakly between the other two, and not equal to the third,\nthe angle at the third point is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.cos_eq_zero_iff_angle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": "The cosine of the angle between three points is 0 if and only if the angle is \u03c0 / 2.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wbtw.angle\u2083\u2081\u2082_eq_zero_of_ne", "description": " If the second of three points is weakly between the other two, and not equal to the first,\nthe angle at the first point (reversed) is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.cos_eq_one_iff_angle_eq_zero", "description": "The cosine of the angle between three points is 1 if and only if the angle is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.collinear_of_angle_eq_pi", "description": "If the angle between three points is \u03c0, they are collinear.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sbtw.angle\u2083\u2082\u2081_eq_pi", "description": " If the second of three points is strictly between the other two, the angle at that point\n(reversed) is \u03c0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_lt_pi_of_not_collinear", "description": "If three points are not collinear, the angle between them is less than \u03c0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.cos_eq_neg_one_iff_angle_eq_pi", "description": "The cosine of the angle between three points is -1 if and only if the angle is \u03c0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.collinear_of_sin_eq_zero", "description": "If the sine of the angle between three points is 0, they are collinear.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.continuous_at_angle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.dist_eq_add_dist_of_angle_eq_pi", "description": "If \u2220ABC = \u03c0, then (dist A C) = (dist A B) + (dist B C).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_sub_const", "description": "Angles in a vector space are translation invariant", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_vadd_const", "description": "Angles are translation invariant", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.collinear_iff_eq_or_eq_or_angle_eq_zero_or_angle_eq_pi", "description": " Three points are collinear if and only if the first or third point equals the second or the\nangle between them is 0 or \u03c0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_le_pi", "description": "The angle at a point is at most \u03c0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_eq_angle_of_angle_eq_pi_of_angle_eq_pi", "description": " Vertical Angles Theorem: angles opposite each other, formed by two intersecting straight\nlines, are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_eq_pi_iff_sbtw", "description": " The angle between three points is \u03c0 if and only if the second point is strictly between the\nother two.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_eq_zero_of_angle_eq_pi_right", "description": "If the angle \u2220ABC at a point is \u03c0, the angle \u2220BCA is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_eq_left", "description": "The angle \u2220AAB at a point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_isometry.angle_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "wbtw.angle\u2081\u2083\u2082_eq_zero_of_ne", "description": " If the second of three points is weakly between the other two, and not equal to the third,\nthe angle at the third point (reversed) is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_eq_of_ne", "description": "The angle \u2220ABA at a point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_midpoint_eq_pi", "description": "If M is the midpoint of the segment AB, then \u2220AMB = \u03c0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_eq_zero_iff_eq_and_ne_or_sbtw", "description": " The angle between three points is zero if and only if one of the first and third points is\nstrictly between the other two, or those two points are equal but not equal to the second.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.dist_eq_abs_sub_dist_iff_angle_eq_zero", "description": "If A \u2260 B and C \u2260 B then \u2220ABC = 0 if and only if (dist A C) = abs ((dist A B) - (dist B C)).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sbtw.angle\u2082\u2083\u2081_eq_zero", "description": " If the second of three points is strictly between the other two, the angle at the third point\nis zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_add_angle_eq_pi_of_angle_eq_pi", "description": "If \u2220BCD = \u03c0, then \u2220ACB + \u2220ACD = \u03c0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_nonneg", "description": "The angle at a point is nonnegative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_const_add", "description": "Angles in a vector space are translation invariant", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_add_const", "description": "Angles in a vector space are translation invariant", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sbtw.angle\u2081\u2082\u2083_eq_pi", "description": " If the second of three points is strictly between the other two, the angle at that point\nis \u03c0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.dist_eq_abs_sub_dist_of_angle_eq_zero", "description": "If \u2220ABC = 0, then (dist A C) = abs ((dist A B) - (dist B C)).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.angle_const_vadd", "description": "Angles are translation invariant", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.ordered_cancel_add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.ordered_cancel_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.has_exists_add_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.canonically_ordered_monoid", "description": "The product of a family of canonically ordered monoids is a canonically ordered monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.one_le_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.const_nonneg_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.const_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.ordered_comm_monoid", "description": "The product of a family of ordered commutative monoids is an ordered commutative monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.ordered_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.const_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.const_nonpos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.ordered_comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.const_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.const_le_one_of_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.ordered_add_comm_monoid", "description": "The product of a family of ordered additive commutative monoids is\n  an ordered additive commutative monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.one_le_const_of_one_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.has_exists_mul_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.ordered_comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.one_lt_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.const_lt_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.canonically_ordered_add_monoid", "description": "The product of a family of canonically ordered additive monoids is\n  a canonically ordered additive monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.ordered_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_const", "description": " Extension for the `positivity` tactic: `function.const` is positive/nonnegative/nonzero if its\ninput is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.ordered_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.ordered_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.const_nonpos_of_nonpos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.const_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.univ", "description": "The set that contains all elements of a type.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "set.has_sep", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "set", "description": "A set of elements of type `\u03b1`; implemented as a predicate `\u03b1 \u2192 Prop`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "set.has_emptyc", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "set.has_mem", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "set.is_lawful_singleton", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "set_of", "description": "The set `{x | p x}` of elements satisfying the predicate `p`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "set.mem_set_of_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "set.has_insert", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "set.has_singleton", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "class_group.norm_bound", "description": " If `b` is an `R`-basis of `S` of cardinality `n`, then `norm_bound abv b` is an integer\nsuch that for every `R`-integral element `a : S` with coordinates `\u2264 y`,\nwe have algebra.norm a \u2264 norm_bound abv b * y ^ n`. (See also `norm_le` and `norm_lt`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.norm_bound_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.cardM", "description": " If we have a large enough set of elements in `R^\u03b9`, then there will be a pair\nwhose remainders are close together. We'll show that all sets of cardinality\nat least `cardM bS adm` elements satisfy this condition.\n\nThe value of `cardM` is not at all optimal: for specific choices of `R`,\nthe minimum cardinality can be exponentially smaller.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.exists_min", "description": "A nonzero ideal has an element of minimal norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.norm_le", "description": " If the `R`-integral element `a : S` has coordinates `\u2264 y` with respect to some basis `b`,\nits norm is less than `norm_bound abv b * y ^ dim S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.distinct_elems", "description": "In the following results, we need a large set of distinct elements of `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.norm_lt", "description": " If the `R`-integral element `a : S` has coordinates `< y` with respect to some basis `b`,\nits norm is strictly less than `norm_bound abv b * y ^ dim S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.mk_M_mem_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.finset_approx.zero_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.exists_mem_finset_approx'", "description": "We can approximate `a / b : L` with `q / r`, where `r` has finitely many options for `L`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.finset_approx", "description": " `finset_approx` is a finite set such that each fractional ideal in the integral closure\ncontains an element close to `finset_approx`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.ne_bot_of_prod_finset_approx_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.exists_mk0_eq_mk0", "description": " Each class in the class group contains an ideal `J`\nsuch that `M := \u03a0 m \u2208 finset_approx` is in `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.mem_finset_approx", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.fintype_of_admissible_of_finite", "description": " The main theorem: the class group of an integral closure `S` of `R` in a\nfinite extension `L` of `K = Frac(R)` is finite if there is an admissible\nabsolute value.\n\nSee also `class_group.fintype_of_admissible_of_algebraic` where `L` is an\nalgebraic extension of `R`, that includes some extra assumptions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.exists_mem_finset_approx", "description": "We can approximate `a / b : L` with `q / r`, where `r` has finitely many options for `L`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.prod_finset_approx_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.mk_M_mem", "description": " `class_group.mk_M_mem` is a specialization of `class_group.mk0` to (the finite set of)\nideals that contain `M := \u220f m in finset_approx L f abs, m`.\nBy showing this function is surjective, we prove that the class group is finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.fintype_of_admissible_of_algebraic", "description": " The main theorem: the class group of an integral closure `S` of `R` in an\nalgebraic extension `L` is finite if there is an admissible absolute value.\n\nSee also `class_group.fintype_of_admissible_of_finite` where `L` is a finite\nextension of `K = Frac(R)`, supplying most of the required assumptions automatically.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.neg_mul_relabelling", "description": "`-x * y` and `-(x * y)` have the same moves.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.quot_zero_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mk_mul_move_left_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.is_empty_zero_mul_right_moves", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mul_one_relabelling", "description": "`x * 1` has the same moves as `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mul_comm_equiv", "description": "`x * y` is equivalent to `y * x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mul_move_right_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv'", "description": " The inverse of a positive surreal number `x = {L | R}` is\ngiven by `x\u207b\u00b9 = {0,\n  (1 + (R - x) * x\u207b\u00b9L) * R, (1 + (L - x) * x\u207b\u00b9R) * L |\n  (1 + (L - x) * x\u207b\u00b9L) * L, (1 + (R - x) * x\u207b\u00b9R) * R}`.\nBecause the two halves `x\u207b\u00b9L, x\u207b\u00b9R` of `x\u207b\u00b9` are used in their own\ndefinition, the sets and elements are inductively generated.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.lf_iff_game_lf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv_ty.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "game.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.zero_mul_relabelling", "description": "`0 * x` has exactly the same moves as `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mk_mul_move_left_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.one_mul_relabelling", "description": "`1 * x` has the same moves as `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv_one", "description": "`1\u207b\u00b9` has exactly the same moves as `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.quot_left_distrib_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "game.add_comm_group_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "game.covariant_class_swap_add_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.quot_one_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.left_moves_mul_cases", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.lt_iff_game_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.right_distrib_equiv", "description": "`(x + y) * z` is equivalent to `x * z + y * z.`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mul_assoc_equiv", "description": "`x * y * z` is equivalent to `x * (y * z).`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.quot_eq_of_mk_quot_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "game.covariant_class_add_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mul_zero_relabelling", "description": "`x * 0` has exactly the same moves as `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "game.covariant_class_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.is_empty_mul_zero_right_moves", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "game.add_lf_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "game.add_lf_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.to_right_moves_mul", "description": " Turns a left and a right move for `x` and `y` into a right move for `x * y` and vice versa.\n\nEven though these types are the same (not definitionally so), this is the preferred way to convert\nbetween them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mul_one_equiv", "description": "`x * 1` is equivalent to `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mul_zero_equiv", "description": "`x * 0` is equivalent to `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mul_comm_relabelling", "description": "`x * y` and `y * x` have the same moves.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.fuzzy_iff_game_fuzzy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.neg_mk_mul_move_left_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.right_moves_mul_cases", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "game.bdd_below_of_small", "description": "A small set `s` of games is bounded below.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.left_moves_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.is_empty_mul_zero_left_moves", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.to_left_moves_mul", "description": " Turns two left or right moves for `x` and `y` into a left move for `x * y` and vice versa.\n\nEven though these types are the same (not definitionally so), this is the preferred way to convert\nbetween them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv'_zero", "description": "`inv' 0` has exactly the same moves as `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "game.bdd_above_of_small", "description": "A small set `s` of games is bounded above.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mul_move_left_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.quot_mul_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mk_mul_move_right_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.has_mul", "description": " The product of `x = {xL | xR}` and `y = {yL | yR}` is\n`{xL*y + x*yL - xL*yL, xR*y + x*yR - xR*yR | xL*y + x*yR - xL*yR, x*yL + xR*y - xR*yL }`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.neg_mk_mul_move_right_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.setoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.has_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "game.fuzzy", "description": " The fuzzy, confused, or incomparable relation on games.\n\nIf `x \u2016 0`, then the first player can always win `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "game.not_le", "description": "On `game`, simp-normal inequalities should use as few negations as possible.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv_eq_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.quot_mul_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "game.lf", "description": " The less or fuzzy relation on games.\n\nIf `0 \u29cf x` (less or fuzzy with), then Left can win `x` as the first player.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mul_move_right_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.neg_mk_mul_move_left_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.quot_mul_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv_eq_of_lf_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.is_empty_zero_mul_left_moves", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.quot_mul_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.quot_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.quot_mul_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "game.partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.zero_lf_inv'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv'_zero_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "game.covariant_class_swap_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv_val_is_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.quot_right_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mk_mul_move_right_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv_one_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.quot_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv_ty", "description": " Because the two halves of the definition of `inv` produce more elements\non each side, we have to define the two families inductively.\nThis is the indexing set for the function, and `inv_val` is the function part.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv_ty.zero", "description": " Because the two halves of the definition of `inv` produce more elements\non each side, we have to define the two families inductively.\nThis is the indexing set for the function, and `inv_val` is the function part.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv_ty.left\u2081", "description": " Because the two halves of the definition of `inv` produce more elements\non each side, we have to define the two families inductively.\nThis is the indexing set for the function, and `inv_val` is the function part.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv_ty.left\u2082", "description": " Because the two halves of the definition of `inv` produce more elements\non each side, we have to define the two families inductively.\nThis is the indexing set for the function, and `inv_val` is the function part.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv_ty.right\u2081", "description": " Because the two halves of the definition of `inv` produce more elements\non each side, we have to define the two families inductively.\nThis is the indexing set for the function, and `inv_val` is the function part.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv_ty.right\u2082", "description": " Because the two halves of the definition of `inv` produce more elements\non each side, we have to define the two families inductively.\nThis is the indexing set for the function, and `inv_val` is the function part.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.quot_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv'_one", "description": "`inv' 1` has exactly the same moves as `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mul_move_left_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.left_distrib_equiv", "description": "`x * (y + z)` is equivalent to `x * y + x * z.`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.right_moves_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "game", "description": "The type of combinatorial games. In ZFC, a combinatorial game is constructed from\n two sets of combinatorial games that have been constructed at an earlier\n stage. To do this in type theory, we say that a combinatorial pre-game is built\n inductively from two families of combinatorial games indexed over any type\n in Type u. The resulting type `pgame.{u}` lives in `Type (u+1)`,\n reflecting that it is a proper class in ZFC.\n A combinatorial game is then constructed by quotienting by the equivalence\n `x \u2248 y \u2194 x \u2264 y \u2227 y \u2264 x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.unique_inv_ty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.quot_right_distrib_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.quot_left_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.neg_mk_mul_move_right_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.zero_mul_equiv", "description": "`0 * x` is equivalent to `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "game.not_lf", "description": "On `game`, simp-normal inequalities should use as few negations as possible.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv_ty.is_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.mul_neg_relabelling", "description": "`x * -y` and `-(x * y)` have the same moves.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.has_inv", "description": "The inverse of a pre-game in terms of the inverse on positive pre-games.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.quot_neg_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv_eq_of_equiv_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv_val", "description": " Because the two halves of the definition of `inv` produce more elements\nof each side, we have to define the two families inductively.\nThis is the function part, defined by recursion on `inv_ty`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.inv'_one_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.le_iff_game_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "game.ordered_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "game.lf.is_trichotomous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.one_mul_equiv", "description": "`1 * x` is equivalent to `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.equiv_iff_game_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.map_domain_alg_hom", "description": " If `f : G \u2192 H` is an additive homomorphism between two additive monoids, then\n`finsupp.map_domain f` is an algebra homomorphism between their add monoid algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.lift_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.induction_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.map_domain_alg_hom", "description": " If `f : G \u2192 H` is a multiplicative homomorphism between two monoids, then\n`finsupp.map_domain f` is an algebra homomorphism between their monoid algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.smul_comm_class_self", "description": " Note that if `k` is a `comm_semiring` then we have `smul_comm_class k k k` and so we can take\n`R = k` in the below. In other words, if the coefficients are commutative amongst themselves, they\nalso commute with the algebra multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.group_smul.linear_map", "description": "When `V` is a `k[G]`-module, multiplication by a group element `g` is a `k`-linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.single_eq_algebra_map_mul_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra", "description": "The monoid algebra over a semiring `k` generated by the monoid `G`.\nIt is the type of finite formal `k`-linear combinations of terms of `G`,\nendowed with the convolution product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.prod_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.alg_hom_ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.op_ring_equiv", "description": " The opposite of an `add_monoid_algebra R I` is ring equivalent to\nthe `add_monoid_algebra R\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 I` over the opposite ring, taking elements to their opposite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.non_unital_non_assoc_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.non_unital_alg_hom_ext", "description": " A non_unital `k`-algebra homomorphism from `monoid_algebra k G` is uniquely defined by its\nvalues on the functions `single a 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.non_assoc_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.mul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.single_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.ring_hom_ext'", "description": " If two ring homomorphisms from `monoid_algebra k G` are equal on all `single a 1`\nand `single 1 b`, then they are equal.\n\nSee note [partially-applied ext lemmas].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.map_domain_ring_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.smul_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.lift_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.map_domain_mul", "description": "Like `finsupp.map_domain_add`, but for the convolutive multiplication we define in this file", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.equivariant_of_linear_of_comm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.op_ring_equiv_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.single_hom", "description": "`finsupp.single` as a `monoid_hom` from the product type into the additive monoid algebra.\n\nNote the order of the elements of the product are reversed compared to the arguments of\n`finsupp.single`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.map_domain_ring_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.lift_nc_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.map_domain_non_unital_alg_hom", "description": " If `f : G \u2192 H` is a homomorphism between two magmas, then\n`finsupp.map_domain f` is a non-unital algebra homomorphism between their magma algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.single_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.map_domain_one", "description": "Like `finsupp.map_domain_zero`, but for the `1` we define in this file", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.single_zero_ring_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.lift_nc_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.has_one", "description": "The unit of the multiplication is `single 1 1`, i.e. the function\n that is `1` at `1` and zero elsewhere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.lift_magma", "description": " The functor `G \u21a6 add_monoid_algebra k G`, from the category of magmas to the category of\nnon-unital, non-associative algebras over `k` is adjoint to the forgetful functor in the other\ndirection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.to_multiplicative_alg_equiv", "description": " The algebra equivalence between `add_monoid_algebra` and `monoid_algebra` in terms of\n`multiplicative`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.op_ring_equiv_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.alg_hom_ext'", "description": "See note [partially-applied ext lemmas].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.smul_comm_class_symm_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.lift_magma_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.non_assoc_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.mul_apply_antidiagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.mul_single_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.coe_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.op_ring_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.lift_nc_alg_hom", "description": "`lift_nc_ring_hom` as a `alg_hom`, for when `f` is an `alg_hom`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.single_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.single_one_ring_hom", "description": "`finsupp.single 1` as a `ring_hom`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.prod_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.one_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.mul_single_apply_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.single_zero_alg_hom", "description": "`finsupp.single 0` as a `alg_hom`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.algebra", "description": "The instance `algebra k (monoid_algebra A G)` whenever we have `algebra k A`.\n\nIn particular this provides the instance `algebra k (monoid_algebra k G)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.lift_nc", "description": " A non-commutative version of `monoid_algebra.lift`: given a additive homomorphism `f : k \u2192+ R`\nand a homomorphism `g : G \u2192 R`, returns the additive homomorphism from\n`monoid_algebra k G` such that `lift_nc f g (single a b) = f b * g a`. If `f` is a ring homomorphism\nand the range of either `f` or `g` is in center of `R`, then the result is a ring homomorphism.  If\n`R` is a `k`-algebra and `f = algebra_map k R`, then the result is an algebra homomorphism called\n`monoid_algebra.lift`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.has_mul", "description": "The product of `f g : add_monoid_algebra k G` is the finitely supported function\n whose value at `a` is the sum of `f x * g y` over all pairs `x, y`\n such that `x + y = a`. (Think of the product of multivariate\n polynomials where `\u03b1` is the additive monoid of monomial exponents.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.op_ring_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.non_unital_alg_hom_ext'", "description": "See note [partially-applied ext lemmas].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.map_domain_one", "description": "Like `finsupp.map_domain_zero`, but for the `1` we define in this file", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.single_mul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.lift_nc_alg_hom", "description": "`lift_nc_ring_hom` as a `alg_hom`, for when `f` is an `alg_hom`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.mul_single_apply_of_not_exists_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.lift_nc_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.single_mul_apply_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.has_faithful_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.nat_cast_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.has_faithful_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.mul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.of'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.has_one", "description": "The unit of the multiplication is `single 1 1`, i.e. the function\n that is `1` at `0` and zero elsewhere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.non_unital_non_assoc_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.mul_apply_left", "description": "", "p": "m