e": "list.chain'.cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'_iff_pairwise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'_reverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain.imp'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain.sublist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'.iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'.imp_head", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain_iff_forall\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain_map_of_chain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'.tail", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise.chain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'.cons'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain_of_chain_pmap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain.rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rel_of_chain_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'_pair", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain_of_chain_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'_is_infix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain.imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain_split", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain.induction_head", "description": "Given a chain from `a` to `b`, and a predicate true at `b`, if `r x y \u2192 p y \u2192 p x` then\nthe predicate is true at `a`.\nThat is, we can propagate the predicate all the way up the chain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'.rel_head", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'.suffix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.relation_refl_trans_gen_of_exists_chain", "description": "If there is an `r`-chain starting from `a` and ending at `b`, then `a` and `b` are related by the\nreflexive transitive closure of `r`. The converse of `exists_chain_of_relation_refl_trans_gen`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'.append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'.right_of_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'_split", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'.append_overlap", "description": "If `l\u2081 l\u2082` and `l\u2083` are lists and `l\u2081 ++ l\u2082` and `l\u2082 ++ l\u2083` both satisfy\n `chain' R`, then so does `l\u2081 ++ l\u2082 ++ l\u2083` provided `l\u2082 \u2260 []`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain_iff_pairwise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain.pairwise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain_pmap_of_chain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'.imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain.iff_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'.left_of_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.exists_chain_of_relation_refl_trans_gen", "description": "If `a` and `b` are related by the reflexive transitive closure of `r`, then there is a `r`-chain\nstarting from `a` and ending on `b`.\nThe converse of `relation_refl_trans_gen_of_exists_chain`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'_cons'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'_append_cons_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'.rel_head'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'.prefix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain_of_chain_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'.take", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain_append_cons_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise.chain'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain_append_singleton_iff_forall\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain_iff_nth_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'_of_chain'_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain.induction", "description": "Given a chain from `a` to `b`, and a predicate true at `b`, if `r x y \u2192 p y \u2192 p x` then\nthe predicate is true everywhere in the chain and at `a`.\nThat is, we can propagate the predicate up the chain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain.iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'.infix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'_map_of_chain'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'.iff_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'.sublist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'.drop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.chain'_iff_nth_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.prove_jacobi_sym_odd", "description": " This evaluates `r := jacobi_sym_nat a b` recursively using quadratic reciprocity\nand produces a proof term for the equality, assuming that `a < b` and `b` is odd.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.zero_left_even", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.qr\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.zero_left_odd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.one_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.qr\u2081'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.even_odd\u2085", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.norm_num.eval_jacobi_sym", "description": "This is the `norm_num` plug-in that evaluates Jacobi and Legendre symbols.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.one_left_odd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym.mod_left", "description": "The value depends only on the residue class of `a` mod `b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.mod_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.even_odd\u2087", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.prove_jacobi_sym", "description": " This evaluates `r := jacobi_sym a b` and produces a proof term for the equality.\nThis is done by reducing to `r := jacobi_sym_nat (a % b) b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.prove_jacobi_sym_nat", "description": " This evaluates `r := jacobi_sym_nat a b` and produces a proof term for the equality\nby removing powers of `2` from `b` and then calling `prove_jacobi_sym_odd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.even_even", "description": "The symbol vanishes when both entries are even (and `b \u2260 0`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.zero_right", "description": "Base cases: `b = 0`, `b = 1`, `a = 0`, `a = 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.even_odd\u2081", "description": " If `a` is even and `b` is odd, then we can remove a factor `2` from `a`,\nbut we may have to change the sign, depending on `b % 8`.\nWe give one version for each of the four odd residue classes mod `8`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.qr\u2081'_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.qr\u2083_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.one_left_even", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.qr\u2081_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.double_even", "description": "If `a` is divisible by `4` and `b` is odd, then we can remove the factor `4` from `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.even_odd\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.legendre_sym.to_jacobi_sym", "description": "Turn a Legendre symbol into a Jacobi symbol.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat", "description": "The Jacobi symbol restricted to natural numbers in both arguments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.qr\u2081", "description": "Use quadratic reciproity to reduce to smaller `b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.jacobi_sym_nat.odd_even", "description": "When `a` is odd and `b` is even, we can replace `b` by `b / 2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.norm_add_eq_add_norm_iff_angle_eq_zero", "description": " The norm of the sum of two non-zero vectors equals the sum of their norms\nif and only the angle between the two vectors is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle", "description": " The undirected angle between two vectors. If either vector is 0,\nthis is \u03c0/2. See `orientation.oangle` for the corresponding oriented angle\ndefinition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.angle_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_smul_right_of_pos", "description": "The angle between a vector and a positive multiple of a vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.sin_eq_zero_iff_angle_eq_zero_or_angle_eq_pi", "description": "The sine of the angle between two vectors is 0 if and only if the angle is 0 or \u03c0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_le_pi", "description": "The angle between two vectors is at most \u03c0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.norm_sub_eq_add_norm_iff_angle_eq_pi", "description": " The norm of the difference of two non-zero vectors equals the sum of their norms\nif and only the angle between the two vectors is \u03c0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_add_angle_eq_pi_of_angle_eq_pi", "description": " If the angle between two vectors is \u03c0, the angles between those\nvectors and a third vector add to \u03c0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_smul_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.sin_eq_one_iff_angle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": "The sine of the angle between two vectors is 1 if and only if the angle is \u03c0 / 2.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.cos_angle_mul_norm_mul_norm", "description": " The cosine of the angle between two vectors, multiplied by the\nproduct of their norms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.inner_eq_zero_iff_angle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": " Two vectors have inner product 0 if and only if the angle between\nthem is \u03c0/2.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_smul_right_of_neg", "description": "The angle between a vector and a negative multiple of a vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.angle_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_neg_right", "description": "The angle between a vector and the negation of another vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_self_neg_of_nonzero", "description": "The angle between a nonzero vector and its negation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_self", "description": "The angle between a nonzero vector and itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.cos_eq_one_iff_angle_eq_zero", "description": "The cosine of the angle between two vectors is 1 if and only if the angle is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.norm_sub_eq_abs_sub_norm_of_angle_eq_zero", "description": " If the angle between two vectors is 0, the norm of their difference equals\nthe absolute value of the difference of their norms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.sin_angle_mul_norm_mul_norm", "description": " The sine of the angle between two vectors, multiplied by the\nproduct of their norms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.inner_eq_mul_norm_of_angle_eq_zero", "description": "If the angle between two vectors is 0, the inner product equals the product of the norms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_smul_left_of_neg", "description": "The angle between a negative multiple of a vector and a vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.cos_eq_zero_iff_angle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": "The cosine of the angle between two vectors is 0 if and only if the angle is \u03c0 / 2.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_eq_zero_iff", "description": " The angle between two vectors is zero if and only if they are\nnonzero and one is a positive multiple of the other.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.cos_eq_neg_one_iff_angle_eq_pi", "description": "The cosine of the angle between two vectors is -1 if and only if the angle is \u03c0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_smul_left_of_pos", "description": "The angle between a positive multiple of a vector and a vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_comm", "description": "The angle between two vectors does not depend on their order.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_neg_neg", "description": "The angle between the negation of two vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.inner_eq_mul_norm_iff_angle_eq_zero", "description": " The inner product of two non-zero vectors equals the product of their norms\nif and only if the angle between the two vectors is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_neg_self_of_nonzero", "description": " The angle between the negation of a nonzero vector and that\nvector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.norm_add_eq_norm_sub_iff_angle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": " The norm of the sum of two vectors equals the norm of their difference if and only if\nthe angle between them is \u03c0/2.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.norm_add_eq_add_norm_of_angle_eq_zero", "description": " If the angle between two vectors is 0, the norm of their sum equals\nthe sum of their norms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_zero_right", "description": "The angle between a vector and the zero vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.continuous_at_angle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_neg_left", "description": "The angle between the negation of a vector and another vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.cos_angle", "description": "The cosine of the angle between two vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_zero_left", "description": "The angle between the zero vector and a vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.norm_sub_eq_add_norm_of_angle_eq_pi", "description": " If the angle between two vectors is \u03c0, the norm of their difference equals\nthe sum of their norms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_eq_pi_iff", "description": " The angle between two vectors is \u03c0 if and only if they are nonzero\nand one is a negative multiple of the other.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.angle_nonneg", "description": "The angle between two vectors is nonnegative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.norm_sub_eq_abs_sub_norm_iff_angle_eq_zero", "description": " The norm of the difference of two non-zero vectors equals the absolute value\nof the difference of their norms if and only the angle between the two vectors is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.inner_eq_neg_mul_norm_iff_angle_eq_pi", "description": " The inner product of two non-zero vectors equals the negative product of their norms\nif and only if the angle between the two vectors is \u03c0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inner_product_geometry.inner_eq_neg_mul_norm_of_angle_eq_pi", "description": " If the angle between two vectors is \u03c0, the inner product equals the negative product\nof the norms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_one_div_nat_pow_mul_cos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.bernoulli_three_eval_one_quarter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bernoulli_fun", "description": "The function `x \u21a6 B\u2096(x) : \u211d \u2192 \u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integral_bernoulli_fun_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bernoulli_fun_eval_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_one_div_nat_pow_mul_fourier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antideriv_bernoulli_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bernoulli_fun_endpoints_eq_of_ne_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_zeta_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_zeta_four", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_one_div_nat_pow_mul_sin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bernoulli_fun_eval_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "periodized_bernoulli.continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bernoulli_zero_fourier_coeff", "description": "The Fourier coefficients of `B\u2080(x) = 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bernoulli_fourier_coeff_zero", "description": "The `0`-th Fourier coefficient of `B\u2096(x)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bernoulli_fourier_coeff_recurrence", "description": "Recurrence relation (in `k`) for the `n`-th Fourier coefficient of `B\u2096`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at_bernoulli_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bernoulli_fourier_coeff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "periodized_bernoulli", "description": "The Bernoulli polynomial, extended from `[0, 1)` to the unit circle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_bernoulli_fourier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bernoulli_fourier_coeff", "description": "The `n`-th Fourier coefficient of the `k`-th Bernoulli function on the interval `[0, 1]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_L_function_mod_four_eval_three", "description": "Explicit formula for `L(\u03c7, 3)`, where `\u03c7` is the unique nontrivial Dirichlet character modulo 4.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_zeta_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_coeff_bernoulli_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_one_div_pow_mul_fourier_mul_bernoulli_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.id_\u03b4", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad_hom.app_\u03b4_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.coe_comonad", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.right_counit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad_hom.app_\u03bc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.left_counit_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad_to_functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad_hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.left_unit_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.\u03b4", "description": "The comultiplication for the comonad `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad_to_functor.reflects_isomorphisms", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.simps.\u03bc", "description": "A custom simps projection for the multiplication of a monad, in simp normal form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad_to_functor.faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad_hom.app_\u03b5", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad_iso.mk_inv_to_nat_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad_hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad_hom.app_\u03b7", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad", "description": "The data of a monad on C consists of an endofunctor T together with natural transformations\n\u03b7 : \ud835\udfed C \u27f6 T and \u03bc : T \u22d9 T \u27f6 T satisfying three equations:\n- T \u03bc_X \u226b \u03bc_X = \u03bc_(TX) \u226b \u03bc_X (associativity)\n- \u03b7_(TX) \u226b \u03bc_X = 1_X (left unit)\n- T\u03b7_X \u226b \u03bc_X = 1_X (right unit)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.to_functor", "description": "The data of a monad on C consists of an endofunctor T together with natural transformations\n\u03b7 : \ud835\udfed C \u27f6 T and \u03bc : T \u22d9 T \u27f6 T satisfying three equations:\n- T \u03bc_X \u226b \u03bc_X = \u03bc_(TX) \u226b \u03bc_X (associativity)\n- \u03b7_(TX) \u226b \u03bc_X = 1_X (left unit)\n- T\u03b7_X \u226b \u03bc_X = 1_X (right unit)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.\u03b7'", "description": "The data of a monad on C consists of an endofunctor T together with natural transformations\n\u03b7 : \ud835\udfed C \u27f6 T and \u03bc : T \u22d9 T \u27f6 T satisfying three equations:\n- T \u03bc_X \u226b \u03bc_X = \u03bc_(TX) \u226b \u03bc_X (associativity)\n- \u03b7_(TX) \u226b \u03bc_X = 1_X (left unit)\n- T\u03b7_X \u226b \u03bc_X = 1_X (right unit)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.\u03bc'", "description": "The data of a monad on C consists of an endofunctor T together with natural transformations\n\u03b7 : \ud835\udfed C \u27f6 T and \u03bc : T \u22d9 T \u27f6 T satisfying three equations:\n- T \u03bc_X \u226b \u03bc_X = \u03bc_(TX) \u226b \u03bc_X (associativity)\n- \u03b7_(TX) \u226b \u03bc_X = 1_X (left unit)\n- T\u03b7_X \u226b \u03bc_X = 1_X (right unit)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.assoc'", "description": "The data of a monad on C consists of an endofunctor T together with natural transformations\n\u03b7 : \ud835\udfed C \u27f6 T and \u03bc : T \u22d9 T \u27f6 T satisfying three equations:\n- T \u03bc_X \u226b \u03bc_X = \u03bc_(TX) \u226b \u03bc_X (associativity)\n- \u03b7_(TX) \u226b \u03bc_X = 1_X (left unit)\n- T\u03b7_X \u226b \u03bc_X = 1_X (right unit)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.left_unit'", "description": "The data of a monad on C consists of an endofunctor T together with natural transformations\n\u03b7 : \ud835\udfed C \u27f6 T and \u03bc : T \u22d9 T \u27f6 T satisfying three equations:\n- T \u03bc_X \u226b \u03bc_X = \u03bc_(TX) \u226b \u03bc_X (associativity)\n- \u03b7_(TX) \u226b \u03bc_X = 1_X (left unit)\n- T\u03b7_X \u226b \u03bc_X = 1_X (right unit)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.right_unit'", "description": "The data of a monad on C consists of an endofunctor T together with natural transformations\n\u03b7 : \ud835\udfed C \u27f6 T and \u03bc : T \u22d9 T \u27f6 T satisfying three equations:\n- T \u03bc_X \u226b \u03bc_X = \u03bc_(TX) \u226b \u03bc_X (associativity)\n- \u03b7_(TX) \u226b \u03bc_X = 1_X (left unit)\n- T\u03b7_X \u226b \u03bc_X = 1_X (right unit)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.left_counit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.coassoc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad_iso.mk", "description": " Construct a comonad isomorphism from a natural isomorphism of functors where the forward\ndirection is a comonad morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad_hom.comp_to_nat_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.right_unit_assoc", "descriptio