rojection for the functor part of a comonad, as a coercion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.simps.coe", "description": "A custom simps projection for the functor part of a monad, as a coercion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.id", "description": "The identity comonad.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad_to_functor.faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.coassoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad_iso.to_nat_iso", "description": "An isomorphism of monads gives a natural isomorphism of the underlying functors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad_hom.id_to_nat_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.right_counit_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad_hom.app_\u03b4", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad_to_functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad_iso.to_nat_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad_to_functor_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.simps.\u03b7", "description": "A custom simps projection for the unit of a monad, in simp normal form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad_hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad_hom.app_\u03b7_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad_iso.to_nat_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad_hom", "description": "A morphism of comonads is a natural transformation compatible with \u03b5 and \u03b4.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad_hom.to_nat_trans", "description": "A morphism of comonads is a natural transformation compatible with \u03b5 and \u03b4.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad_hom.app_\u03b5'", "description": "A morphism of comonads is a natural transformation compatible with \u03b5 and \u03b4.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad_hom.app_\u03b4'", "description": "A morphism of comonads is a natural transformation compatible with \u03b5 and \u03b4.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad", "description": "The data of a comonad on C consists of an endofunctor G together with natural transformations\n\u03b5 : G \u27f6 \ud835\udfed C and \u03b4 : G \u27f6 G \u22d9 G satisfying three equations:\n- \u03b4_X \u226b G \u03b4_X = \u03b4_X \u226b \u03b4_(GX) (coassociativity)\n- \u03b4_X \u226b \u03b5_(GX) = 1_X (left counit)\n- \u03b4_X \u226b G \u03b5_X = 1_X (right counit)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.to_functor", "description": "The data of a comonad on C consists of an endofunctor G together with natural transformations\n\u03b5 : G \u27f6 \ud835\udfed C and \u03b4 : G \u27f6 G \u22d9 G satisfying three equations:\n- \u03b4_X \u226b G \u03b4_X = \u03b4_X \u226b \u03b4_(GX) (coassociativity)\n- \u03b4_X \u226b \u03b5_(GX) = 1_X (left counit)\n- \u03b4_X \u226b G \u03b5_X = 1_X (right counit)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.\u03b5'", "description": "The data of a comonad on C consists of an endofunctor G together with natural transformations\n\u03b5 : G \u27f6 \ud835\udfed C and \u03b4 : G \u27f6 G \u22d9 G satisfying three equations:\n- \u03b4_X \u226b G \u03b4_X = \u03b4_X \u226b \u03b4_(GX) (coassociativity)\n- \u03b4_X \u226b \u03b5_(GX) = 1_X (left counit)\n- \u03b4_X \u226b G \u03b5_X = 1_X (right counit)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.\u03b4'", "description": "The data of a comonad on C consists of an endofunctor G together with natural transformations\n\u03b5 : G \u27f6 \ud835\udfed C and \u03b4 : G \u27f6 G \u22d9 G satisfying three equations:\n- \u03b4_X \u226b G \u03b4_X = \u03b4_X \u226b \u03b4_(GX) (coassociativity)\n- \u03b4_X \u226b \u03b5_(GX) = 1_X (left counit)\n- \u03b4_X \u226b G \u03b5_X = 1_X (right counit)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.coassoc'", "description": "The data of a comonad on C consists of an endofunctor G together with natural transformations\n\u03b5 : G \u27f6 \ud835\udfed C and \u03b4 : G \u27f6 G \u22d9 G satisfying three equations:\n- \u03b4_X \u226b G \u03b4_X = \u03b4_X \u226b \u03b4_(GX) (coassociativity)\n- \u03b4_X \u226b \u03b5_(GX) = 1_X (left counit)\n- \u03b4_X \u226b G \u03b5_X = 1_X (right counit)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.left_counit'", "description": "The data of a comonad on C consists of an endofunctor G together with natural transformations\n\u03b5 : G \u27f6 \ud835\udfed C and \u03b4 : G \u27f6 G \u22d9 G satisfying three equations:\n- \u03b4_X \u226b G \u03b4_X = \u03b4_X \u226b \u03b4_(GX) (coassociativity)\n- \u03b4_X \u226b \u03b5_(GX) = 1_X (left counit)\n- \u03b4_X \u226b G \u03b5_X = 1_X (right counit)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.right_counit'", "description": "The data of a comonad on C consists of an endofunctor G together with natural transformations\n\u03b5 : G \u27f6 \ud835\udfed C and \u03b4 : G \u27f6 G \u22d9 G satisfying three equations:\n- \u03b4_X \u226b G \u03b4_X = \u03b4_X \u226b \u03b4_(GX) (coassociativity)\n- \u03b4_X \u226b \u03b5_(GX) = 1_X (left counit)\n- \u03b4_X \u226b G \u03b5_X = 1_X (right counit)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad_iso.mk", "description": " Construct a monad isomorphism from a natural isomorphism of functors where the forward\ndirection is a monad morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad_to_functor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad_to_functor_map_iso_monad_iso_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.left_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad_iso.to_nat_iso", "description": "An isomorphism of comonads gives a natural isomorphism of the underlying functors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.assoc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at_integral_of_dominated_loc_of_lip'", "description": " Differentiation under integral of `x \u21a6 \u222b F x a` at a given point `x\u2080`, assuming `F x\u2080` is\nintegrable, `\u2016F x a - F x\u2080 a\u2016 \u2264 bound a * \u2016x - x\u2080\u2016` for `x` in a ball around `x\u2080` for ae `a` with\nintegrable Lipschitz bound `bound` (with a ball radius independent of `a`), and `F x` is\nae-measurable for `x` in the same ball. See `has_fderiv_at_integral_of_dominated_loc_of_lip` for a\nslightly less general but usually more useful version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at_integral_of_dominated_loc_of_deriv_le", "description": " Derivative under integral of `x \u21a6 \u222b F x a` at a given point `x\u2080 : \u211d`, assuming\n`F x\u2080` is integrable, `x \u21a6 F x a` is differentiable on an interval around `x\u2080` for ae `a`\n(with interval radius independent of `a`) with derivative uniformly bounded by an integrable\nfunction, and `F x` is ae-measurable for `x` in a possibly smaller neighborhood of `x\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at_integral_of_dominated_loc_of_lip", "description": " Derivative under integral of `x \u21a6 \u222b F x a` at a given point `x\u2080 : \ud835\udd5c`, `\ud835\udd5c = \u211d` or `\ud835\udd5c = \u2102`,\nassuming `F x\u2080` is integrable, `x \u21a6 F x a` is locally Lipschitz on a ball around `x\u2080` for ae `a`\n(with ball radius independent of `a`) with integrable Lipschitz bound, and `F x` is\nae-measurable for `x` in a possibly smaller neighborhood of `x\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at_integral_of_dominated_loc_of_lip", "description": " Differentiation under integral of `x \u21a6 \u222b F x a` at a given point `x\u2080`, assuming\n`F x\u2080` is integrable, `x \u21a6 F x a` is locally Lipschitz on a ball around `x\u2080` for ae `a`\n(with a ball radius independent of `a`) with integrable Lipschitz bound, and `F x` is ae-measurable\nfor `x` in a possibly smaller neighborhood of `x\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at_integral_of_dominated_of_fderiv_le", "description": " Differentiation under integral of `x \u21a6 \u222b F x a` at a given point `x\u2080`, assuming\n`F x\u2080` is integrable, `x \u21a6 F x a` is differentiable on a ball around `x\u2080` for ae `a` with\nderivative norm uniformly bounded by an integrable function (the ball radius is independent of `a`),\nand `F x` is ae-measurable for `x` in a possibly smaller neighborhood of `x\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.arcsin_eq_arctan", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.arctan_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.coe_tan_local_homeomorph_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.arctan", "description": " Inverse of the `tan` function, returns values in the range `-\u03c0 / 2 < arctan x` and\n`arctan x < \u03c0 / 2`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.arctan_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.tan_add'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.continuous_arctan", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.image_tan_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.arctan_lt_pi_div_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.tan_two_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.continuous_at_arctan", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.arctan_eq_of_tan_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.tan_local_homeomorph", "description": "`real.tan` as a `local_homeomorph` between `(-(\u03c0 / 2), \u03c0 / 2)` and the whole line.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.continuous_tan", "descri