escription": "An open immersion of PresheafedSpaces is an open embedding `f : X \u27f6 U \u2286 Y` of the underlying\nspaces, such that the sheaf map `Y(V) \u27f6 f _* X(V)` is an iso for each `V \u2286 U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.PresheafedSpace.is_open_immersion.pullback_cone_of_left_lift_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.PresheafedSpace.is_open_immersion.inv_app", "description": "For an open immersion `f : X \u27f6 Y` and an open set `U \u2286 X`, we have the map `X(U) \u27f6 Y(U)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.PresheafedSpace.is_open_immersion.open_functor", "description": "The functor `opens X \u2964 opens Y` associated with an open immersion `f : X \u27f6 Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.array_equiv_fin", "description": "The natural equivalence between length-`n` arrays and functions from `fin n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "array.encodable", "description": "If `\u03b1` is encodable, then so is `array n \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "array.traversable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.vector_equiv_array", "description": "The natural equivalence between length-`n` vectors and length-`n` arrays.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "array.countable", "description": "If `\u03b1` is countable, then so is `array n \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.d_array_equiv_fin", "description": " The natural equivalence between length-`n` heterogeneous arrays\nand dependent functions from `fin n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "array.is_lawful_traversable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.\u03c7\u2084", "description": " Define the nontrivial quadratic character on `zmod 4`, `\u03c7\u2084`.\nIt corresponds to the extension `\u211a(\u221a-1)/\u211a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.is_quadratic_\u03c7\u2088'", "description": "`\u03c7\u2088'` takes values in `{0, 1, -1}`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "neg_one_pow_div_two_of_three_mod_four", "descripti