, "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.unop", "description": "The 'unopposite' of an iso `\u03b1\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u2243* \u03b2\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`. Inverse to `mul_equiv.op`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_units.op_equiv", "description": "The additive units of the additive opposites are equivalent to the additive opposites\nof the additive units.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.right_cancel_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.inv'_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.left_cancel_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.op_symm_apply_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.op", "description": "An additive monoid homomorphism `M \u2192+ N` can equivalently be viewed as an\nadditive monoid homomorphism `M\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56 \u2192+ N\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56`. This is the action of the (fully faithful)\n`\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56`-functor on morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.sub_neg_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.to_opposite_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.has_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.semiconj_by_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.from_opposite", "description": "An additive monoid homomorphism `f : M \u2192+ N` such that `f x` additively commutes\nwith `f y` for all `x`, `y` defines an additive monoid homomorphism from `M\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.op", "description": " A monoid homomorphism `M \u2192* N` can equivalently be viewed as a monoid homomorphism\n`M\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u2192* N\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`. This is the action of the (fully faithful) `\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`-functor on morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.neg'", "description": "Negation on an additive group is an `add_equiv` to the opposite group. When `G`\nis commutative, there is `add_equiv.inv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.add_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.mul_one_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semiconj_by.unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.mul_unop", "description": " The 'unopposite' of an additive monoid hom `\u03b1\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u2192+ \u03b2\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`. Inverse to\n`add_monoid_hom.mul_op`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.neg'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.add_comm_group_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.inv'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.op_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.op_equiv", "description": "The units of the opposites are equivalent to the opposites of the units.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.op_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.commute_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.op_symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.right_cancel_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.coe_op_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.left_cancel_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.from_opposite_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.op_symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.subtraction_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.left_cancel_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.op_mul_equiv_to_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.op", "description": "An additive semigroup homomorphism `add_hom M N` can equivalently be viewed as an\nadditive semigroup homomorphism `add_hom M\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56 N\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56`. This is the action of the (fully faithful)\n`\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56`-functor on morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.to_opposite", "description": "An additive semigroup homomorphism `f : add_hom M N` such that `f x` additively\ncommutes with `f y` for all `x, y` defines an additive semigroup homomorphism to `S\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.from_opposite_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.op_symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.unop_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.unop_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.add_comm_group_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.op_symm_apply_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_semiconj_by.op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.op", "description": "A iso `\u03b1 \u2243+ \u03b2` can equivalently be viewed as an iso `\u03b1\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56 \u2243+ \u03b2\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.mul_op_symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.unop", "description": "The 'unopposite' of an iso `\u03b1\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56 \u2243+ \u03b2\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56`. Inverse to `add_equiv.op`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.unop_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.mul_op", "description": " An additive semigroup homomorphism `add_hom M N` can equivalently be viewed as an additive\nhomomorphism `add_hom M\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 N\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`. This is the action of the (fully faithful) `\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`-functor on\nmorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.op_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.inv'", "description": " Inversion on a group is a `mul_equiv` to the opposite group. When `G` is commutative, there is\n`mul_equiv.inv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.add_monoid_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.has_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.op_mul_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.op_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.op_apply_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.mul_unop", "description": "The 'unopposite' of an iso `\u03b1\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u2243+ \u03b2\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`. Inverse to `add_equiv.mul_op`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.op_symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.cancel_add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.op", "description": " A semigroup homomorphism `M \u2192\u2099* N` can equivalently be viewed as a semigroup homomorphism\n`M\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u2192\u2099* N\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`. This is the action of the (fully faithful) `\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`-functor on morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.op_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.left_cancel_add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.mul_one_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.unop", "description": "The 'unopposite' of an additive monoid homomorphism `M\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56 \u2192+ N\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56`. Inverse to\n`add_monoid_hom.op`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.op_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.op_symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.op", "description": "A iso `\u03b1 \u2243* \u03b2` can equivalently be viewed as an iso `\u03b1\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u2243* \u03b2\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.has_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.mul_op_symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.from_opposite_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.op_add_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.add_zero_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.to_opposite_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.from_opposite", "description": " A semigroup homomorphism `f : M \u2192\u2099* N` such that `f x` commutes with `f y` for all `x, y`\ndefines a semigroup homomorphism from `M\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.unop_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.op_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit_unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_semiconj_by.unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.cancel_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.from_opposite", "description": " A monoid homomorphism `f : M \u2192* N` such that `f x` commutes with `f y` for all `x, y` defines\na monoid homomorphism from `M\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.op_add_equiv", "description": "The function `mul_opposite.op` is an additive equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.commute_unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.op_mul_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.cancel_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.from_opposite_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_opposite", "description": "An additive monoid homomorphism `f : M \u2192+ N` such that `f x` additively commutes\nwith `f y` for all `x, y` defines an additive monoid homomorphism to `S\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.comm_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.mul_op_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.op_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.op_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.semiconj_by_unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.unop", "description": "The 'unopposite' of a semigroup homomorphism `M\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u2192\u2099* N\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`. Inverse to `mul_hom.op`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_hom.unop", "description": "The 'unopposite' of an additive semigroup homomorphism `M\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56 \u2192\u2099+ N\u1d43\u1d52\u1d56`. Inverse\nto `add_hom.op`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.op_apply_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.mul_op_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.op_mul_equiv", "description": "The function `add_opposite.op` is a multiplicative equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.semiconj_by_unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.add_group_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.right_cancel_add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.cancel_add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.add_right_cancel_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.commute.unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.mul_op_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.right_cancel_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.add_comm_monoid_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.unop", "description": "The 'unopposite' of a monoid homomorphism `M\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u2192* N\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`. Inverse to `monoid_hom.op`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.sub_neg_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.division_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.op_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.op_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.div_inv_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.division_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.op_add_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.commute_unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_hom.to_opposite", "description": " A semigroup homomorphism `f : M \u2192\u2099* N` such that `f x` commutes with `f y` for all `x, y`\ndefines a semigroup homomorphism to `N\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.unop_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.mul_op_ext", "description": " This ext lemma change equalities on `\u03b1\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u2192+ \u03b2` to equalities on `\u03b1 \u2192+ \u03b2`.\nThis is useful because there are often ext lemmas for specific `\u03b1`s that will apply\nto an equality of `\u03b1 \u2192+ \u03b2` such as `finsupp.add_hom_ext'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposi