ous path connecting two points `x` and `y` in a topological space", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.to_continuous_map", "description": "Continuous path connecting two points `x` and `y` in a topological space", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.source'", "description": "Continuous path connecting two points `x` and `y` in a topological space", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.target'", "description": "Continuous path connecting two points `x` and `y` in a topological space", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.truncate", "description": "`\u03b3.truncate t\u2080 t\u2081` is the path which follows the path `\u03b3` on the\n time interval `[t\u2080, t\u2081]` and stays still otherwise.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "joined.some_path", "description": "When two points are joined, choose some path from `x` to `y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "joined.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_path_connected_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "joined_in.source_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.trans_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path_connected_space.exists_path_through_family'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.symm", "description": "The reverse of a path from `x` to `y`, as a path from `y` to `x`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.map_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "joined_in.mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path_component_subset_component", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.extend", "description": "A continuous map extending a path to `\u211d`, constant before `0` and after `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.extend_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.truncate_zero_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "loc_path_connected_of_is_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.truncate_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, 