.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.path_extend", "description": "See Note [continuity lemma statement].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_path_connected.union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_path_connected.preimage_coe", "description": " If a set `W` is path-connected, then it is also path-connected when seen as a set in a smaller\nambient type `U` (when `U` contains `W`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "joined.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_path_component_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.truncate_of_le", "description": "`\u03b3.truncate_of_le t\u2080 t\u2081 h`, where `h : t\u2080 \u2264 t\u2081` is `\u03b3.truncate t\u2080 t\u2081`\n casted as a path from `\u03b3.extend t\u2080` to `\u03b3.extend t\u2081`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "joined.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_path_component_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.continuous_uncurry_extend_of_continuous_family", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "joined_in.joined", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path_connected_subset_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "joined_in.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.trans_continuous_family", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.pi", "description": " Given a family of paths, one in each X\u1d62, we take their pointwise product to get a path in\n\u03a0 i, X\u1d62.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_path_connected.image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.extend_of_one_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.map_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "joined_in.joined_subtype", "description": "If `x` and `y` are joined in the set `F`, then they are joined in the subtype `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.is_connected_iff_is_path_connected", "description": "", "p": "mathli