ription": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.path_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.refl", "description": "The constant path from a point to itself", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.has_uncurry_path", "description": "Any function `\u03c6 : \u03a0 (a : \u03b1), path (x a) (y a)` can be seen as a function `\u03b1 \u00d7 I \u2192 X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_path_connected.exists_path_through_family'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.extend_of_le_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.reparam", "description": "Given a path `\u03b3` and a function `f : I \u2192 I` where `f 0 = 0` and `f 1 = 1`, `\u03b3.reparam f` is the\npath defined by `\u03b3 \u2218 f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path_component_in_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.trans_prod_eq_prod_trans", "description": "Path composition commutes with products", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_path_connected.subset_path_component", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.map_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.continuous_map.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path_component", "description": "The path component of `x` is the set of points that can be joined to `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.of_line_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "joined_in.target_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "loc_path_connected_space", "description": " A topological space is locally path connected, at every point, path connected\nneighborhoods form a neighborhood basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "loc_path_connected_space.path_connected_basis", "description": " A topological space is locally path connected, at every point, path connected\nneighborhoods form a neighborhood basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.of_line", "description": "The path obtained from a map defined on `\u211d` by restriction to the unit interval.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_path_connected_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "loc_path_connected_of_bases", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.continuous_uncurry_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.continuous_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.add_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path_component_in", "description": "The path component of `x` in `F` is the set of points that can be joined to `x` in `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.continuous_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.truncate_zero_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.cast_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.refl_trans_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_path_connected.exists_path_through_family", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.pi_coe_fn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.refl_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.reparam_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path_connected_space.exists_path_through_family", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "joined_in", "description": " The relation \"being joined by a path in `F`\". Not quite an equivalence relation since it's not\nreflexive for points that do not belong to `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path_connected_space_iff_zeroth_homotopy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "joined_in.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.cast", "description": "Casting a path from `x` to `y` to a path from `x'` to `y'` when `x' = x` and `y' = y`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.truncate_one_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path_connected_space_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.trans_pi_eq_pi_trans", "description": "Path composition commutes with products", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "joined_in.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.truncate_continuous_family", "description": "For a path `\u03b3`, `\u03b3.truncate` gives a \"continuous family of paths\", by which we\n mean the uncurried function which maps `(t\u2080, t\u2081, s)` to `\u03b3.truncate t\u2080 t\u2081 s` is continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_finsupp_equiv_prod_finsupp_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_elim_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.uncurry", "description": " Given a finitely supported function `f` from `\u03b1` to the type of\nfinitely supported functions from `\u03b2` to `M`,\n`uncurry f` is the \"uncurried\" finitely supported function from `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2` to `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_subtype_domain_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.add_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.has_repr", "description": " Stringify a `finsupp` as a sequence of `finsupp.single` terms.\n\nNote this is `meta` as it has to choose some order for the terms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.comap_domain_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_smul_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.mem_support_multiset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_finsupp_add_equiv_prod_finsupp_symm_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_elim_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.single_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_smul_index_add_monoid_hom", "description": "A version of `finsupp.sum_smul_index'` for bundled additive maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.filter_apply_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.equiv_congr_left", "description": " Given `f : \u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2`, the finitely supported function spaces are also in bijection:\n`(\u03b1 \u2192\u2080 M) \u2243 (\u03b2 \u2192\u2080 M)`.\n\nThis is the finitely-supported version of `equiv.Pi_congr_left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.equiv_map_domain_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.image_fst_graph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.single_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.zero_not_mem_frange", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.subtype_domain_finsupp_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.graph_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.add_equiv", "description": "`finsupp.map_range.add_monoid_hom` as an equiv.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.is_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.some", "description": "Restrict a finitely supported function on `option \u03b1` to a finitely supported function on `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.split_comp", "description": " Given `l`, a finitely supported function from the sigma type `\u03a3 i, \u03b1s i` to `\u03b2` and\nan `\u03b9`-indexed family `g` of functions from `(\u03b1s i \u2192\u2080 \u03b2)` to `\u03b3`, `split_comp` defines a\nfinitely supported function from the index type `\u03b9` to `\u03b3` given by composing `g i` with\n`split l i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.subtype_domain_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.subtype_domain_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rat.cast_finsupp_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.erase_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_embedding", "description": "When `f` is an embedding we have an embedding `(\u03b1 \u2192\u2080 \u2115)  \u21aa (\u03b2 \u2192\u2080 \u2115)` given by `map_domain`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.equiv_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.add_monoid_hom_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.comap_domain_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.subtype_domain_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.emb_domain_eq_map_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.filter_pos_add_filter_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.comap_domain.add_monoid_hom", "description": "`finsupp.comap_domain` is an `add_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.add_monoid_hom", "description": "Composition with a fixed additive homomorphism is itself an additive homomorphism on functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.graph", "description": " The graph of a finitely supported function over its support, i.e. the finset of input and output\npairs with non-zero outputs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.distrib_mul_action_hom.single", "description": " `finsupp.single` as a `distrib_mul_action_hom`.\n\nSee also `finsupp.lsingle` for the version as a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.graph_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.no_zero_smul_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.finsupp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.some_single_none", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_elim", "description": "`finsupp.sum_elim f g` maps `inl x` to `f x` and `inr y` to `g y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.support_smul_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.comap_domain_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.comap_distrib_mul_action", "description": "`finsupp.comap_has_smul` is distributive", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_map_range", "description": "When `g` preserves addition, `map_range` and `map_domain` commute.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.equiv_congr_left_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.comap_smul_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.filter", "description": "`filter p f` is the finitely supported function that is `f a` if `p a` is true and 0 otherwise.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.unique_of_right", "description": "The `finsupp` version of `pi.unique`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_notin_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_finsupp_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.some_single_some", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.add_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_finsupp_add_equiv_prod_finsupp_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.some_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range_multiset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.apply_eq_of_mem_graph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.filter_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.equiv_map_domain_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.support_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_option_index_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.equiv_map_domain_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.prod_map_domain_index_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.zero_hom_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_inj_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.graph_eq_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_finsupp_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_filter_add_sum_filter_not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.comap_domain_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain.add_monoid_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.equiv_map_domain_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.comap_smul_apply", "description": "When `G` is a group, `finsupp.comap_has_smul` acts by precomposition with the action of `g\u207b\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.coe_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.comap_domain", "description": " Given `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2`, `l : \u03b2 \u2192\u2080 M` and a proof `hf` that `f` is injective on\nthe preimage of `l.support`, `comap_domain f l hf` is the finitely supported function\nfrom `\u03b1` to `M` given by composing `l` with `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.curry", "description": " Given a finitely supported function `f` from a product type `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2` to `\u03b3`,\n`curry f` is the \"curried\" finitely supported function from `\u03b1` to the type of\nfinitely supported functions from `\u03b2` to `\u03b3`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.filter_eq_indicator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.add_equiv_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.comap_domain_add_of_injective", "description": "A version of `finsupp.comap_domain_add` that's easier to use.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.comap_domain_smul_of_injective", "description": "A version of `finsupp.comap_domain_smul` that's easier to use.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.equiv_map_domain_eq_map_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_embedding_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain.add_monoid_hom_comp_map_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_map_domain_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.filter_add_hom", "description": "`finsupp.filter` as an `add_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_finsupp_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_elim_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.filter_single_of_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.equiv_map_domain_trans'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.equiv", "description": "`finsupp.map_range` as an equiv.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sigma_finsupp_equiv_pi_finsupp", "description": " On a `fintype \u03b7`, `finsupp.split` is an equivalence between `(\u03a3 (j : \u03b7), \u03b9s j) \u2192\u2080 \u03b1`\nand `\u03a0 j, (\u03b9s j \u2192\u2080 \u03b1)`.\n\nThis is the `finsupp` version of `equiv.Pi_curry`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.smul_single_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.subtype_domain_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_support_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.filter_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.add_monoid_hom_to_zero_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.dom_congr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_finsupp_add_equiv_prod_finsupp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.prod_option_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_map_domain_index_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.finsupp_prod_equiv", "description": " `finsupp_prod_equiv` defines the `equiv` between `((\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2) \u2192\u2080 M)` and `(\u03b1 \u2192\u2080 (\u03b2 \u2192\u2080 M))` given by\ncurrying and uncurrying.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.coe_sum_elim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.filter_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sigma_finsupp_add_equiv_pi_finsupp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.mk_mem_graph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.support_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.smul_single'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.equiv_map_domain_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.snd_sum_finsupp_equiv_prod_finsupp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain.add_monoid_hom", "description": "`finsupp.map_domain` is an `add_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.fst_sum_finsupp_add_equiv_prod_finsupp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_map_domain_index_add_monoid_hom", "description": "A version of `sum_map_domain_index` that takes a bundled `add_monoid_hom`,\nrather than separate linearity hypotheses.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.equiv_map_domain", "description": " Given `f : \u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2`, we can map `l : \u03b1 \u2192\u2080 M` to  `equiv_map_domain f l : \u03b2 \u2192\u2080 M` (computably)\nby mapping the support forwards and the function backwards.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.comap_smul_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.comap_domain.add_monoid_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.mem_split_support_iff_nonzero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.frange", "description": "`frange f` is the image of `f` on the support of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.equiv_map_domain_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.dom_congr_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.subtype_domain_add_monoid_hom", "description": "`subtype_domain` but as an `add_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.some_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.restrict_support_equiv", "description": " Given an `add_comm_monoid M` and `s : set \u03b1`, `restrict_support_equiv s M` is the `equiv`\nbetween the subtype of finitely supported functions with support contained in `s` and\nthe type of finitely supported functions from `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_smul_index'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sigma_finsupp_add_equiv_pi_finsupp", "description": " On a `fintype \u03b7`, `finsupp.split` is an additive equivalence between\n`(\u03a3 (j : \u03b7), \u03b9s j) \u2192\u2080 \u03b1` and `\u03a0 j, (\u03b9s j \u2192\u2080 \u03b1)`.\n\nThis is the `add_equiv` version of `finsupp.sigma_finsupp_equiv_pi_finsupp`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rat.cast_finsupp_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.prod_filter_mul_prod_filter_not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_sub_sum_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.subtype_domain_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.filter_single_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_curry_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.split", "description": " Given `l`, a finitely supported function from the sigma type `\u03a3 (i : \u03b9), \u03b1s i` to `M` and\nan index element `i : \u03b9`, `split l i` is the `i`th component of `l`,\na finitely supported function from `as i` to `M`.\n\nThis is the `finsupp` version of `sigma.curry`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.equiv_congr_left_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.filter_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_option_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.unique_of_left", "description": "The `finsupp` version of `pi.unique_of_is_empty`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain.add_monoid_hom_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_comap_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_finsupp_add_equiv_prod_finsupp_symm_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.subtype_domain", "description": "`subtype_domain p f` is the restriction of the finitely supported function `f` to subtype `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.smul_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.filter_curry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_finsupp_equiv_prod_finsupp_symm_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.graph_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.subtype_domain_eq_zero_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.fst_sum_finsupp_equiv_prod_finsupp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.subtype_domain_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.distrib_mul_action_hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.smul_zero_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.filter_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.zero_hom_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.zero_hom", "description": " Composition with a fixed zero-preserving homomorphism is itself an zero-preserving homomorphism\non functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.dom_congr_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sigma_finsupp_equiv_pi_finsupp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.smul_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_comap_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.not_mem_graph_snd_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.zero_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.add_equiv_to_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sigma_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_finsupp_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.dom_congr_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.mem_graph_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.filter_apply_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.mem_frange", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.mk_mem_graph_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.erase_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.mem_support_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_finsupp_equiv_prod_finsupp_symm_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.filter_eq_self_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.split_support", "description": " Given `l`, a finitely supported function from the sigma type `\u03a3 (i : \u03b9), \u03b1s i` to `\u03b2`,\n`split_support l` is the finset of indices in `\u03b9` that appear in the support of `l`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain", "description": "Given `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` and `v : \u03b1 \u2192\u2080 M`, `map_domain f v : \u03b2 \u2192\u2080 M`\n is the finitely supported function whose value at `a : \u03b2` is the sum\n of `v x` over all `x` such that `f x = a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.comap_domain_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.support_curry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.prod_subtype_domain_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.add_monoid_hom_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.add_equiv_to_add_monoid_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.filter_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.some_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.comap_mul_action", "description": "`finsupp.comap_has_smul` is multiplicative", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.distrib_mul_action_hom_ext'", "description": "See note [partially-applied ext lemmas].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.split_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.has_faithful_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sigma_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.distrib_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.prod_filter_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.support_subtype_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.add_monoid_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.filter_eq_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_finsupp_equiv_prod_finsupp", "description": " The equivalence between `(\u03b1 \u2295 \u03b2) \u2192\u2080 \u03b3` and `(\u03b1 \u2192\u2080 \u03b3) \u00d7 (\u03b2 \u2192\u2080 \u03b3)`.\n\nThis is the `finsupp` version of `equiv.sum_arrow_equiv_prod_arrow`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_finsupp_equiv_prod_finsupp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.dom_congr", "description": " Given `add_comm_monoid M` and `e : \u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2`, `dom_congr e` is the corresponding `equiv` between\n`\u03b1 \u2192\u2080 M` and `\u03b2 \u2192\u2080 M`.\n\nThis is `finsupp.equiv_congr_left` as an `add_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.filter_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.filter_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.add_equiv_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.comap_has_smul", "description": " Scalar multiplication acting on the domain.\n\nThis is not an instance as it would conflict with the action on the range.\nSee the `instance_diamonds` test for examples of such conflicts.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.prod_map_domain_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_range.equiv_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_filter_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain.add_monoid_hom_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.curry_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.comap_domain_zero", "description": "Note the `hif` argument is needed for this to work in `rw`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.snd_sum_finsupp_add_equiv_prod_finsupp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.prod_div_prod_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.frange_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_update_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.eq_zero_of_comap_domain_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.subtype_domain_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.map_domain_support_of_inj_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.equiv_map_domain_refl'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_finsupp_add_equiv_prod_finsupp", "description": " The additive equivalence between `(\u03b1 \u2295 \u03b2) \u2192\u2080 M` and `(\u03b1 \u2192\u2080 M) \u00d7 (\u03b2 \u2192\u2080 M)`.\n\nThis is the `finsupp` version of `equiv.sum_arrow_equiv_prod_arrow`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.single_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.int.has_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.coe_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.coe_zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.subtype.linear_ordered_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "positive.subtype.has_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.left_comparison", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonadic_left_adjoint", "description": "A left adjoint functor `L : C \u2964 D` is *comonadic* if the comparison functor `comonad.comparison L`\nfrom `C` to the category of Eilenberg-Moore algebras for the adjunction is an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonadic_left_adjoint.to_is_left_adjoint", "description": "A left adjoint functor `L : C \u2964 D` is *comonadic* if the comparison functor `comonad.comparison L`\nfrom `C` to the category of Eilenberg-Moore algebras for the adjunction is an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonadic_left_adjoint.eqv", "description": "A left adjoint functor `L : C \u2964 D` is *comonadic* if the comparison functor `comonad.comparison L`\nfrom `C` to the category of Eilenberg-Moore algebras for the adjunction is an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.comparison_forget_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.comparison_forget_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.to_comonad_\u03b5", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.comparison_obj_a", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.reflective.app.category_theory.is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.reflective.comparison_ess_surj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.comparison_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.to_comonad", "description": "For a pair of functors `L : C \u2964 D`, `R : D \u2964 C`, an adjunction `h : L \u22a3 R` induces a comonad on\nthe category `D`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monadic_of_reflective", "description": "Any reflective inclusion has a monadic right adjoint.\n   cf Prop 5.3.3 of [Riehl][riehl2017]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monadic_right_adjoint", "description": "A right adjoint functor `R : D \u2964 C` is *monadic* if the comparison functor `monad.comparison R`\nfrom `D` to the category of Eilenberg-Moore algebras for the adjunction is an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monadic_right_adjoint.to_is_right_adjoint", "description": "A right adjoint functor `R : D \u2964 C` is *monadic* if the comparison functor `monad.comparison R`\nfrom `D` to the category of Eilenberg-Moore algebras for the adjunction is an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monadic_right_adjoint.eqv", "description": "A right adjoint functor `R : D \u2964 C` is *monadic* if the comparison functor `monad.comparison R`\nfrom `D` to the category of Eilenberg-Moore algebras for the adjunction is an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.to_monad_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.to_comonad_\u03b4", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.comparison.faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.comparison.ess_surj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.comparison_forget_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.adj_to_comonad_iso", "description": "The comonad induced by the Eilenberg-Moore adjunction is the original comonad.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.adj_to_comonad_iso_inv_to_nat_trans_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.comparison", "description": "Gven any adjunction `L \u22a3 R`, there is a comparison functor `category_theory.monad.comparison R`\nsending objects `Y : D` to Eilenberg-Moore algebras for `L \u22d9 R` with underlying object `R.obj X`.\n\nWe later show that this is full when `R` is full, faithful when `R` is faithful,\nand essentially surjective when `R` is reflective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.forget.comonadic_left_adjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.to_monad_\u03b7", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.adj_to_comonad_iso_hom_to_nat_trans_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.adj_to_monad_iso", "description": "The monad induced by the Eilenberg-Moore adjunction is the original monad.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.comparison.full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.comparison_forget", "description": "The underlying object of `(comonad.comparison L).obj X` is just `L.obj X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.comparison_obj_A", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.comparison_obj_a", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.adj_to_monad_iso_hom_to_nat_trans_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.comparison_faithful_of_faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.to_monad", "description": "For a pair of functors `L : C \u2964 D`, `R : D \u2964 C`, an adjunction `h : L \u22a3 R` induces a monad on\nthe category `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.left_comparison", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03bc_iso_of_reflective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.adj_to_monad_iso_inv_to_nat_trans_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.comparison_forget", "description": "The underlying object of `(monad.comparison R).obj X` is just `R.obj X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.comparison", "description": "Gven any adjunction `L \u22a3 R`, there is a comparison functor `category_theory.comonad.comparison L`\nsending objects `X : C` to Eilenberg-Moore coalgebras for `L \u22d9 R` with underlying object\n`L.obj X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.forget.monadic_right_adjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.comparison_obj_A", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.to_monad_\u03bc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.comparison.full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.comparison.ess_surj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.to_comonad_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.reflective.comparison_full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.comparison_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comonad.comparison_forget_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.arrow.has_colimit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.has_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.arrow.has_limits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.creates_colimits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.creates_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.has_colimits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.cocone_of_preserves", "description": "If `L` preserves the appropriate colimit, then given a colimit cocone for `F \u22d9 fst L R : J \u2964 L` and\na cocone for `F \u22d9 snd L R : J \u2964 R` we can build a cocone for `F` which will turn out to be a\ncolimit cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.has_limits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.arrow.has_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.cone_of_preserves", "description": "If `R` preserves the appropriate limit, then given a cone for `F \u22d9 fst L R : J \u2964 L` and a\nlimit cone for `F \u22d9 snd L R : J \u2964 R` we can build a cone for `F` which will turn out to be a limit\ncone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.arrow.has_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.has_colimit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.colimit_auxiliary_cocone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.cocone_of_preserves_is_colimit", "description": " Provided that `L` preserves the appropriate colimit, then the cocone in `cocone_of_preserves` is\na colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.limit_auxiliary_cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.mono_right_of_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.colimit_auxiliary_cocone", "description": " (Implementation). An auxiliary cocone which is useful in order to construct colimits\nin the comma category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.has_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.has_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.cone_of_preserves_X_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.cone_of_preserves_\u03c0_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.cone_of_preserves_is_limit", "description": " Provided that `R` preserves the appropriate limit, then the cone in `cone_of_preserves` is a\nlimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.creates_limits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.cocone_of_preserves_X_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.arrow.has_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.has_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.mono_iff_mono_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.creates_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.creates_colimit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.epi_iff_epi_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.has_colimits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.cone_of_preserves_X_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.limit_auxiliary_cone", "description": " (Implementation). An auxiliary cone which is useful in order to construct limits\nin the comma category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.cocone_of_preserves_\u03b9_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.cocone_of_preserves_X_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.creates_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.cocone_of_preserves_X_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.has_colimit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.cone_of_preserves_\u03c0_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.arrow.has_colimits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.cone_of_preserves_X_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.has_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.has_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.colimit_auxiliary_cocone_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.limit_auxiliary_cone_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.cocone_of_preserves_\u03b9_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.epi_left_of_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.has_limits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.open_segment_interior_closure_subset_interior", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.add_smul_mem_interior'", "description": "If `x \u2208 closure s` and `x + y \u2208 interior s`, then `x + t y \u2208 interior s` for `t \u2208 (0, 1]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "segment_subset_closure_open_segment", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.interior", "description": "In a topological vector space, the interior of a convex set is convex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.combo_interior_self_mem_interior", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_std_simplex", "description": "`std_simplex \u211d \u03b9` is closed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.combo_self_interior_mem_interior", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.is_connected", "description": "A nonempty convex set is connected.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.add_smul_mem_interior", "description": "If `x \u2208 s` and `x + y \u2208 interior s`, then `x + t y \u2208 interior s` for `t \u2208 (0, 1]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.combo_closure_interior_subset_interior", "description": " If `s` is a convex set, then `a \u2022 closure s + b \u2022 interior s \u2286 interior s` for all `0 \u2264 a`,\n`0 < b`, `a + b = 1`. See also `convex.combo_self_interior_subset_interior` for a weaker version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.convex_iff_is_preconnected", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_add_group.path_connected", "description": "Every topological vector space over \u211d is path connected.\n\nNot an instance, because it creates enormous TC subproblems (turn on `pp.all`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.strict_convex'", "description": " A convex set `s` is strictly convex provided that for any two distinct points of\n`s \\ interior s`, the line passing through these points has nonempty intersection with\n`interior s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact_std_simplex", "description": "`std_simplex \u211d \u03b9` is compact.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.add_smul_sub_mem_interior", "description": "If `x \u2208 s` and `y \u2208 interior s`, then the segment `(x, y]` is included in `interior s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "std_simplex_subset_closed_ball", "description": "Every vector in `std_simplex \ud835\udd5c \u03b9` has `max`-norm at most `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.closure_subset_interior_image_homothety_of_one_lt", "description": " If we dilate a convex set about a point in its interior by a scale `t > 1`, the interior of\nthe result includes the closure of the original set.\n\nTODO Generalise this from convex sets to sets that are balanced / star-shaped about `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.subset_interior_image_homothety_of_one_lt", "description": " If we dilate a convex set about a point in its interior by a scale `t > 1`, the interior of\nthe result includes the closure of the original set.\n\nTODO Generalise this from convex sets to sets that are balanced / star-shaped about `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.open_segment_interior_self_subset_interior", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.combo_self_interior_subset_interior", "description": " If `s` is a convex set, then `a \u2022 s + b \u2022 interior s \u2286 interior s` for all `0 \u2264 a`, `0 < b`,\n`a + b = 1`. See also `convex.combo_closure_interior_subset_interior` for a stronger version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.open_segment_self_interior_subset_interior", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.combo_interior_self_subset_interior", "description": " If `s` is a convex set, then `a \u2022 interior s + b \u2022 s \u2286 interior s` for all `0 < a`, `0 \u2264 b`,\n`a + b = 1`. See also `convex.combo_interior_closure_subset_interior` for a stronger version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite.is_closed_convex_hull", "description": "Convex hull of a finite set is closed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.combo_interior_closure_subset_interior", "description": " If `s` is a convex set, then `a \u2022 interior s + b \u2022 closure s \u2286 interior s` for all `0 < a`,\n`0 \u2264 b`, `a + b = 1`. See also `convex.combo_interior_self_subset_interior` for a weaker version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.is_path_connected", "description": "A nonempty convex set is path connected.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.add_smul_sub_mem_interior'", "description": "If `x \u2208 closure s` and `y \u2208 interior s`, then the segment `(x, y]` is included in `interior s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite.compact_convex_hull", "description": "Convex hull of a finite set is compact.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.closure", "description": "In a topological vector space, the closure of a convex set is convex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.combo_closure_interior_mem_interior", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.combo_interior_closure_mem_interior", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_std_simplex", "description": "`std_simplex \u211d \u03b9` is bounded.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.open_segment_closure_interior_subset_interior", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_preconnected.convex", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `real.convex_iff_is_preconnected`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.is_preconnected", "description": "A convex set is preconnected.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.strict_convex", "description": " A convex set `s` is strictly convex provided that for any two distinct points `x`, `y` of\n`s \\ interior s`, the segment with endpoints `x`, `y` has nonempty intersection with\n`interior s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.closure_subset_image_homothety_interior_of_one_lt", "description": " If we dilate the interior of a convex set about a point in its interior by a scale `t > 1`,\nthe result includes the closure of the original set.\n\nTODO Generalise this from convex sets to sets that are balanced / star-shaped about `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_open_segment", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.range_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_preimage_eq_inter_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_eta", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.nonempty.preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.exists_subset_range_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.compl_compl_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.range_inclusion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.range.nonempty", "descrip