 "description": "If one controls the norm of every `A x`, then one controls the norm of `A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "schwartz_map.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "Helper instance for when there's too many metavariables to apply `fun_like.has_coe_to_fun`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "schwartz_map.to_bounded_continuous_function_clm", "description": " The inclusion map from Schwartz functions to bounded continuous functions as a continuous linear\nmap.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "schwartz_map.seminorm_le_bound", "description": "If one controls the seminorm for every `x`, then one controls the seminorm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "schwartz_map.comp_clm", "description": " Composition with a function on the right is a continuous linear map on Schwartz space\nprovided that the function is temperate and growths polynomially near infinity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "schwartz_map.smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "schwartz_map.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "schwartz_map.decay_add_le_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "schwartz_map.norm_le_seminorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "schwartz_map.decay", "description": "All derivatives of a Schwartz function are rapidly decaying.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "schwartz_map.pderiv_clm", "description": " The partial derivative (or directional derivative) in the direction `m : E` as a\ncontinuous linear map on Schwartz space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "schwartz_map.decay_smul_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "schwartz_map.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "schwartz_map.norm_pow_mul_le_seminorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "schwartz_map.seminorm_le_bound'", "description": " If one controls the seminorm for every `x`, then one controls the seminorm.\n\nVariant for functions `\ud835\udce2(\u211d, F)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "schwartz_map.seminorm_aux_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mat