escription": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `is_top_of_dual_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_min.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_top.of_dual", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `is_bot_of_dual_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_max.to_dual", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `is_min_to_dual_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_min_iff_forall_not_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_min.eq_of_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_max", "description": " `a` is a maximal element of `\u03b1` if no element is strictly greater than it. We spell it without\n`<` to avoid having to convert between `\u2264` and `<`. Instead, `is_max_iff_forall_not_lt` does the\nconversion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bot_to_dual_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_top.to_dual", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `is_bot_to_dual_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.no_min_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_is_max_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_is_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_max_of_dual_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "no_min_order.to_no_bot_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "no_bot_order_iff_no_min_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_min", "description": " `a` is a minimal element of `\u03b1` if no element is strictly less than it. We spell it without `<`\nto avoid having to convert between `\u2264` and `<`. Instead, `is_min_iff_forall_not_lt` does the\nconversion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_max_to_dual_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_is_min_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_is_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "no_bot_order", "description": "Order without bottom elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "no_bot_order.exists_not_ge", "description": "Order without bottom elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_max.snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "no_top_order_iff_no_max_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_min.not_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "no_max_order.to_no_top_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_is_max_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "no_top_order.to_no_max_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.no_top_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_is_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsingleton.is_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bot", "description": " `a : \u03b1` is a bottom element of `\u03b1` if it is less than or equal to any other element of `\u03b1`.\nThis predicate is roughly an unbundled version of `order_bot`, except that a preorder may have\nseveral bottom elements. When `\u03b1` is linear, this is useful to make a case disjunction on\n`no_min_order \u03b1` within a proof.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsingleton.is_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.is_min_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_min.to_dual", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `is_max_to_dual_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "no_max_order_of_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_top_of_dual_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_min.prod_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bot.snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "no_max_order", "description": "Order without maximal elements. Sometimes called cofinal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "no_max_order.exists_gt", "description": "Order without maximal elements. Sometimes called cofinal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_top.snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_lt.lt.not_is_min", "description": "**Alias** of `not_is_min_of_lt`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsingleton.is_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.short_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.lt_decidable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.subsingleton_short", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.lf_decidable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.move_left_short'", "description": "Extracting the `short` instance for a move by Left.\nThis would be a dangerous instance potentially introducing new metavariables\nin typeclass search, so we only make it an instance locally.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.le_lf_decidable", "description": "Auxiliary construction of decidability instances.\nWe build `decidable (x \u2264 y)` and `decidable (x \u29cf y)` in a simultaneous induction.\nInstances for the two projections separately are provided below.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.fintype_right_moves", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.list_short", "description": "Evidence that every `pgame` in a list is `short`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.list_short.nil", "description": "Evidence that every `pgame` in a list is `short`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.list_short.cons", "description": "Evidence that every `pgame` in a list is `short`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.short_0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.short.mk'", "description": "A synonym for `short.mk` that specifies the pgame in an implicit argument.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.move_left_short", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.short_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.list_short_nth_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.short.of_is_empty", "description": "This leads to infinite loops if made into an instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.fintype_left", "description": "Extracting the `fintype` instance for the indexing type for Left's moves in a short game.\nThis is an unindexed typeclass, so it can't be made a global instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.short_birthday", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.short_1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.le_decidable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.short", "description": "A short game is a game with a finite set of moves at every turn.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.short.mk", "description": "A short game is a game with a finite set of moves at every turn.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.move_right_short'", "description": "Extracting the `short` instance for a move by Right.\nThis would be a dangerous instance potentially introducing new metavariables\nin typeclass search, so we only make it an instance locally.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.short_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.short_bit0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.short_of_lists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.fintype_right", "description": "Extracting the `fintype` instance for the indexing type for Right's moves in a short game.\nThis is an unindexed typeclass, so it can't be made a global instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.short_bit1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.fintype_left_moves", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.move_right_short", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.short_of_relabelling", "description": "If `x` is a short game, and `y` is a relabelling of `x`, then `y` is also short.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.equiv_decidable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cc_state.mk_using_hs_core", "description": "Create a congruence closure state object using the hypotheses in the current goal.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.cc_dbg_core", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.mk_using_hs", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.cc_core", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.roots", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.mt", "description": " \"Modification Time\". The field m_mt is used to implement the mod-time optimization introduce by the Simplify theorem prover.\nThe basic idea is to introduce a counter gmt that records the number of heuristic instantiation that have\noccurred in the current branch. It is incremented after each round of heuristic instantiation.\nThe field m_mt records the last time any proper descendant of of thie entry was involved in a merge.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.proof_for", "description": "`proof_for cc e` constructs a proof for e if it is equivalent to true in cc_state", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.add", "description": " Add the given proof term as a new rule.\nThe proof term p must be an `eq _ _`, `heq _ _`, `iff _ _`, or a negation of these.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.cc", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.refutation_for", "description": "`refutation_for cc e` constructs a proof for `not e` if it is equivalent to false in cc_state", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.pp_eqc", "description": "Pretty print the entry associated with the given expression.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.is_cg_root", "description": "Check if `e` is the root of the congruence class.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.eqc_size", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.eqc_of", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.eqc_of_core", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.root", "description": "Get the root representative of the given expression.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state", "description": " Congruence closure state.\nThis may be considered to be a set of expressions and an equivalence class over this set.\nThe equivalence class is generated by the equational rules that are added to the cc_state and congruence,\nthat is, if `a = b` then `f(a) = f(b)` and so on.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.mk_core", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.ac_refl", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.cc_dbg", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.roots_core", "description": " Returns the root expression for each equivalence class in the graph.\nIf the bool argument is set to true then it only returns roots of non-singleton classes.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.gmt", "description": " \"Global Modification Time\". gmt is a number stored on the cc_state,\nit is compared with the modification time of a cc_entry in e-matching. See `cc_state.mt`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.mk", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.inconsistent", "description": "Returns true if the cc_state is inconsistent. For example if it had both `a = b` and `a \u2260 b` in it.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.in_singlenton_eqc", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.mfold_eqc", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.pp_core", "description": " Pretty print the entire cc graph.\nIf the bool argument is set to true then singleton equivalence classes will be omitted.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.fold_eqc_core", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.inc_gmt", "description": "Increment the Global Modification time.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.has_to_tactic_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.is_not_eqv", "description": "Check whether two expressions are not in the same equivalence class.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.next", "description": " Get the next element in the equivalence class.\nNote that if the given expr e is not in the graph then it will just return e.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.proof_for_false", "description": "If the given state is inconsistent, return a proof for false. Otherwise fail.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.internalize", "description": "Add the given expression to the graph.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_config", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_config.ignore_instances", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_config.ac", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_config.ho_fns", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_config.em", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.is_eqv", "description": "Check whether two expressions are in the same equivalence class.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.eqv_proof", "description": "Returns a proof term that the given terms are equivalent in the given cc_state", "p": "core"}, {"name": "cc_state.fold_eqc", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "composition.boundary_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.mem_range_embedding_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.index", "description": "`c.index j` is the index of the block in the composition `c` containing `j`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.embedding_comp_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set", "description": " Combinatorial viewpoint on a composition of `n`, by seeing it as non-empty blocks of\nconsecutive integers in `{0, ..., n-1}`. We register every block by its left end-point, yielding\na finset containing `0`. As this does not make sense for `n = 0`, we add `n` to this finset, and\nget a finset of `{0, ..., n}` containing `0` and `n`. This is the data in the structure\n`composition_as_set n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.boundaries", "description": " Combinatorial viewpoint on a composition of `n`, by seeing it as non-empty blocks of\nconsecutive integers in `{0, ..., n-1}`. We register every block by its left end-point, yielding\na finset containing `0`. As this does not make sense for `n = 0`, we add `n` to this finset, and\nget a finset of `{0, ..., n}` containing `0` and `n`. This is the data in the structure\n`composition_as_set n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.zero_mem", "description": " Combinatorial viewpoint on a composition of `n`, by seeing it as non-empty blocks of\nconsecutive integers in `{0, ..., n-1}`. We register every block by its left end-point, yielding\na finset containing `0`. As this does not make sense for `n = 0`, we add `n` to this finset, and\nget a finset of `{0, ..., n}` containing `0` and `n`. This is the data in the structure\n`composition_as_set n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.last_mem", "description": " Combinatorial viewpoint on a composition of `n`, by seeing it as non-empty blocks of\nconsecutive integers in `{0, ..., n-1}`. We register every block by its left end-point, yielding\na finset containing `0`. As this does not make sense for `n = 0`, we add `n` to this finset, and\nget a finset of `{0, ..., n}` containing `0` and `n`. This is the data in the structure\n`composition_as_set n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.to_composition_blocks", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_equiv", "description": "Equivalence between `composition n` and `composition_as_set n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.mem_boundaries_iff_exists_blocks_sum_take_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.blocks_fin_equiv", "description": " Equivalence between the disjoint union of the blocks (each of them seen as\n`fin (c.blocks_fun i)`) with `fin n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.ones", "description": "The composition made of blocks all of size `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.card_boundaries_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.one_le_blocks", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set_equiv", "description": " Bijection between compositions of `n` and subsets of `{0, ..., n-2}`, defined by\nconsidering the restriction of the subset to `{1, ..., n-1}` and shifting to the left by one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.size_up_to", "description": "The sum of the sizes of the blocks in a composition up to `i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.ne_ones_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.boundary", "description": " The `i`-th boundary of a composition, i.e., the leftmost point of the `i`-th block. We include\na virtual point at the right of the last block, to make for a nice equiv with\n`composition_as_set n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.length", "description": "The length of a composition, i.e., the number of blocks in the composition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.embedding", "description": " Embedding the `i`-th block of a composition (identified with `fin (c.blocks_fun i)`) into\n`fin n` at the relevant position.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.coe_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.size_up_to_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.single_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.blocks_fun", "description": "Size of the `i`-th block in a `composition_as_set`, seen as a function on `fin c.length`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.mem_range_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.index_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.ones_blocks_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.sum_blocks_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.lt_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.order_emb_of_fin_boundaries", "description": " The canonical increasing bijection between `fin (c.length + 1)` and `c.boundaries` is\nexactly `c.boundary`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.disjoint_range", "description": "The embeddings of different blocks of a composition are disjoint.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.mem_range_embedding_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.card_boundaries_eq_succ_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.sigma_eq_iff_blocks_eq", "description": " Two compositions (possibly of different integers) coincide if and only if they have the\nsame sequence of blocks.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.size_up_to_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.inv_embedding_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.index_exists", "description": "`index_exists` asserts there is some `i` with `j < c.size_up_to (i+1)`.\nIn the next definition `index` we use `nat.find` to produce the minimal such index.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.to_composition_as_set_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.to_composition_as_set_boundaries", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.boundary_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.ne_single_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.nth_le_split_wrt_composition_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.length_split_wrt_composition", "description": " When one splits a list along a composition `c`, the number of sublists thus created is\n`c.length`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.blocks_fun_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.card_boundaries_eq_succ_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.inv_embedding", "description": " Mapping an element `j` of `fin n` to the element in the block containing it, identified with\n`fin (c.blocks_fun (c.index j))` through the canonical increasing bijection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.lt_length'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.single_blocks", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.size_up_to_index_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.one_le_blocks'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.single_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.join_split_wrt_composition", "description": " If one splits a list along a composition, and then joins the sublists, one gets back the\noriginal list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.blocks_fun", "description": " The blocks of a composition, seen as a function on `fin c.length`. When composing analytic\nfunctions using compositions, this is the main player.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.blocks_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.lt_size_up_to_index_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.to_composition_as_set", "description": " To `c : composition n`, one can associate a `composition_as_set n` by registering the leftmost\npoint of each block, and adding a virtual point at the right of the last block.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.length_pos_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.length_split_wrt_composition_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.blocks_fun_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.single", "description": "The composition made of a single block of size `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.blocks_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.one_le_blocks_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.coe_inv_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.boundary_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.boundaries", "description": " The boundaries of a composition, i.e., the leftmost point of all the blocks. We include\na virtual point at the right of the last block, to make for a nice equiv with\n`composition_as_set n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.blocks_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.eq_single_iff_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.boundaries_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.nth_le_split_wrt_composition", "description": " The `i`-th sublist in the splitting of a list `l` along a composition `c`, is the slice of `l`\nbetween the indices `c.size_up_to i` and `c.size_up_to (i+1)`, i.e., the indices in the `i`-th\nblock of the composition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.ones_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.split_wrt_composition_aux", "description": "Auxiliary for `list.split_wrt_composition`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_take_map_length_split_wrt_composition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.map_length_split_wrt_composition_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.size_up_to_succ'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.join_split_wrt_composition_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.length_lt_card_boundaries", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.size_up_to_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.monotone_size_up_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.blocks_pos'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.blocks", "description": "List of the sizes of the blocks in a `composition_as_set`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.eq_ones_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.blocks_partial_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.length_pos_of_mem_split_wrt_composition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.boundary", "description": "Canonical increasing bijection from `fin c.boundaries.card` to `c.boundaries`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.length", "description": "Number of blocks in a `composition_as_set`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.size_up_to_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.of_fn_blocks_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.split_wrt_composition_aux_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.size_up_to_of_length_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.boundary_last", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.split_wrt_composition_join", "description": " If one joins a list of lists and then splits the join along the right composition, one gets\nback the original list of lists.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.ones_size_up_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.single_blocks_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.blocks_fun_mem_blocks", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.to_composition_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.eq_ones_iff_le_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.split_wrt_composition", "description": " Given a list of length `n` and a composition `[i\u2081, ..., i\u2096]` of `n`, split `l` into a list of\n`k` lists corresponding to the blocks of the composition, of respective lengths `i\u2081`, ..., `i\u2096`.\nThis makes sense mostly when `n = l.length`, but this is not necessary for the definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.to_composition", "description": " Associating a `composition n` to a `composition_as_set n`, by registering the sizes of the\nblocks as a list of positive integers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.length_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.to_composition_as_set_blocks", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.size_up_to_strict_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.ones_blocks", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.map_length_split_wrt_composition", "description": " When one splits a list along a composition `c`, the lengths of the sublists thus created are\ngiven by the block sizes in `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition", "description": "A composition of `n` is a list of positive integers summing to `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.blocks", "description": "A composition of `n` is a list of positive integers summing to `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.blocks_pos", "description": "A composition of `n` is a list of positive integers summing to `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.blocks_sum", "description": "A composition of `n` is a list of positive integers summing to `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.has_to_string", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.ones_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.eq_ones_iff_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition_as_set.to_composition_boundaries", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_indicator_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.strongly_measurable.strongly_measurable_at_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.integrable_indicator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.strongly_measurable_at_filter", "description": " If a function is continuous on an open set `s`, then it is strongly measurable at the filter\n`\ud835\udcdd x` for all `x \u2208 s` if either the source space or the target space is second-countable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.integrable_at_filter_ae", "description": "**Alias** of `measure_theory.measure.finite_at_filter.integrable_at_filter_of_tendsto_ae`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_strongly_measurable.strongly_measurable_at_filter_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.ae_strongly_measurable_of_is_compact", "description": " A function which is continuous on a compact set `s` is almost everywhere strongly measurable\nwith respect to `\u03bc.restrict s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.set_lintegral_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.integrable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_embedding.integrable_on_map_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_indicator_const_Lp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.mono_set_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.has_finite_integral_restrict_of_bounded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.ae_strongly_measurable_of_is_separable", "description": " A function which is continuous on a separable set `s` is almost everywhere strongly measurable\nwith respect to `\u03bc.restrict s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.mono_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integrable_on_Ioc_iff_integrable_on_Ioo'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_at_filter.inf_of_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.integrable_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integrable_on_Icc_iff_integrable_on_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_map_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_congr_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integrable_on_Ici_iff_integrable_on_Ioi'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strongly_measurable_at_filter", "description": " A function `f` is strongly measurable at a filter `l` w.r.t. a measure `\u03bc` if it is\nae strongly measurable w.r.t. `\u03bc.restrict s` for some `s \u2208 l`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strongly_measurable_at_filter.filter_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_at_filter", "description": " We say that a function `f` is *integrable at filter* `l` if it is integrable on some\nset `s \u2208 l`. Equivalently, it is eventually integrable on `s` in `l.small_sets`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.strongly_measurable_at_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.integrable_at_filter", "description": "**Alias** of `measure_theory.measure.finite_at_filter.integrable_at_filter_of_tendsto`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving.integrable_on_comp_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.integrable_of_forall_not_mem_eq_zero", "description": " If a function is integrable on a set `s` and vanishes everywhere on its complement,\nthen it is integrable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_finset_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_Lp_of_measure_ne_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.integrable_at_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integrable_on_Iic_iff_integrable_on_Iio'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_finite_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.restrict_to_measurable", "description": " If a function is integrable on a set `s` and nonzero there, then the measurable hull of `s` is\nwell behaved: the restriction of the measure to `to_measurable \u03bc s` coincides with its restriction\nto `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integrable_on_Icc_iff_integrable_on_Ico'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_congr_fun_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integrable_on_Icc_iff_integrable_on_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_finite_bUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.ae_strongly_measurable", "description": " A function which is continuous on a set `s` is almost everywhere strongly measurable with\nrespect to `\u03bc.restrict s` when either the source space or the target space is second-countable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.strongly_measurable_at_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_filter.integrable_at_filter", "description": " If `\u03bc` is a measure finite at filter `l` and `f` is a function such that its norm is bounded\nabove at `l`, then `f` is integrable at `l`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integrable_on_Iic_iff_integrable_on_Iio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.add_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on", "description": " A function is `integrable_on` a set `s` if it is almost everywhere strongly measurable on `s`\nand if the integral of its pointwise norm over `s` is less than infinity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_iff_integrable_of_support_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integrable_on_Ioc_iff_integrable_on_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integrable_on_Ici_iff_integrable_on_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_at_filter.of_inf_ae", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `measure_theory.integrable_at_filter.inf_ae_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.indicator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving.integrable_on_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_at_filter.inf_ae_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strongly_measurable_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integrable_on_Ico_iff_integrable_on_Ioo'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.integrable_at_nhds_within_of_is_separable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.of_ae_diff_eq_zero", "description": " If a function is integrable on a set `s`, and vanishes on `t \\ s`, then it is integrable on `t`\nif `t` is null-measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_filter.integrable_at_filter_of_tendsto_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_at_filter.inf_of_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_add_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_at_filter.filter_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_add_of_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_at_filter.eventually", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.lintegral_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integrable_on_Icc_iff_integrable_on_Ioo'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.left_of_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.finite_at_filter.integrable_at_filter_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.congr_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.strongly_measurable_at_filter_nhds_within", "description": "If a function is continuous on a measurable set `s`, then it is measurable at the filter\n `\ud835\udcdd[s] x` for all `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integrable_on_Icc_iff_integrable_on_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.ae_measurable", "description": " A function which is continuous on a set `s` is almost everywhere measurable with respect to\n`\u03bc.restrict s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.congr_set_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.integrable_at_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.indicator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.integrable_at_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.right_of_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.congr_fun_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_singleton_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integrable_on_Icc_iff_integrable_on_Ioc'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integrable_on_Ico_iff_integrable_on_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.of_forall_diff_eq_zero", "description": " If a function is integrable on a set `s`, and vanishes on `t \\ s`, then it is integrable on `t`\nif `t` is measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.strongly_measurable_at_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.mono_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.integrable_of_ae_not_mem_eq_zero", "description": " If a function is integrable on a set `s` and vanishes almost everywhere on its complement,\nthen it is integrable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strongly_measurable_at_filter.eventually", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equalizer_regular", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_epi", "description": "A regular epimorphism is a morphism which is the coequalizer of some parallel pair.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_epi.W", "description": "A regular epimorphism is a morphism which is the coequalizer of some parallel pair.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_epi.left", "description": "A regular epimorphism is a morphism which is the coequalizer of some parallel pair.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_epi.right", "description": "A regular epimorphism is a morphism which is the coequalizer of some parallel pair.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_epi.w", "description": "A regular epimorphism is a morphism which is the coequalizer of some parallel pair.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_epi.is_colimit", "description": "A regular epimorphism is a morphism which is the coequalizer of some parallel pair.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_mono_category", "description": "A regular mono category is a category in which every monomorphism is regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_mono_category.regular_mono_of_mono", "description": "A regular mono category is a category in which every monomorphism is regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_mono.mono", "description": "Every regular monomorphism is a monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_mono.lift'", "description": "If `f` is a regular mono, then any map `k : W \u27f6 Y` equalizing `regular_mono.left` and\n   `regular_mono.right` induces a morphism `l : W \u27f6 X` such that `l \u226b f = k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.strong_epi_of_regular_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_epi.epi", "description": "Every regular epimorphism is an epimorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_mono_of_mono", "description": "In a category in which every monomorphism is regular, we can express every monomorphism as\n   an equalizer. This is not an instance because it would create an instance loop.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_epi.of_split_epi", "description": "Every split epimorphism is a regular epimorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_epi.desc'", "description": "If `f` is a regular epi, then every morphism `k : X \u27f6 W` coequalizing `regular_epi.left` and\n   `regular_epi.right` induces `l : Y \u27f6 W` such that `f \u226b l = k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.strong_epi_category_of_regular_epi_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_of_is_pullback_snd_of_regular", "description": "The second leg of a pullback cone is a regular monomorphism if the right component is too.\n\nSee also `pullback.snd_of_mono` for the basic monomorphism version, and\n`regular_of_is_pullback_fst_of_regular` for the flipped version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_epi_category", "description": "A regular epi category is a category in which every epimorphism is regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_epi_category.regular_epi_of_epi", "description": "A regular epi category is a category in which every epimorphism is regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.strong_mono_of_regular_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_iso_of_regular_mono_of_epi", "description": "A regular monomorphism is an isomorphism if it is an epimorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_epi_of_epi", "description": "In a category in which every epimorphism is regular, we can express every epimorphism as\n   a coequalizer. This is not an instance because it would create an instance loop.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_epi.w_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_iso_of_regular_epi_of_mono", "description": "A regular epimorphism is an isomorphism if it is a monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.strong_mono_category_of_regular_mono_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_of_is_pushout_snd_of_regular", "description": "The second leg of a pushout cocone is a regular epimorphism if the right component is too.\n\nSee also `pushout.snd_of_epi` for the basic epimorphism version, and\n`regular_of_is_pushout_fst_of_regular` for the flipped version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_mono.w_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_mono_category_of_split_mono_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_epi_category_of_split_epi_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_mono.of_is_split_mono", "description": "Every split monomorphism is a regular monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_mono", "description": "A regular monomorphism is a morphism which is the equalizer of some parallel pair.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_mono.Z", "description": "A regular monomorphism is a morphism which is the equalizer of some parallel pair.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_mono.left", "description": "A regular monomorphism is a morphism which is the equalizer of some parallel pair.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_mono.right", "description": "A regular monomorphism is a morphism which is the equalizer of some parallel pair.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_mono.w", "description": "A regular monomorphism is a morphism which is the equalizer of some parallel pair.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_mono.is_limit", "description": "A regular monomorphism is a morphism which is the equalizer of some parallel pair.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.coequalizer_regular", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_of_is_pushout_fst_of_regular", "description": "The first leg of a pushout cocone is a regular epimorphism if the left component is too.\n\nSee also `pushout.fst_of_epi` for the basic epimorphism version, and\n`regular_of_is_pushout_snd_of_regular` for the flipped version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.regular_of_is_pullback_fst_of_regular", "description": "The first leg of a pullback cone is a regular monomorphism if the left component is too.\n\nSee also `pullback.fst_of_mono` for the basic monomorphism version, and\n`regular_of_is_pullback_snd_of_regular` for the flipped version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape_op_equiv_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape.hom_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_wide_pushout", "description": "`has_wide_pushout B objs arrows` means that `wide_span B objs arrows` has a colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape.equivalence_of_equiv", "description": "Wide pullback diagrams of equivalent index types are equivlent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape.mk_cone", "description": "Construct a cone over a wide cospan.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback", "description": "A choice of wide pullback.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape_op_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback.base", "description": "The unique map to the base from the pullback.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout.\u03b9", "description": "The `j`-th inclusion to the pushout.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape.struct", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape.ulift_equivalence", "description": "Lifting universe and morphism levels preserves wide pullback diagrams.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape_unop_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback.hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape.mk_cone_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape.diagram_iso_wide_span", "description": "Every diagram is naturally isomorphic (actually, equal) to a `wide_span`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape.wide_cospan_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape.hom.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback.eq_lift_of_comp_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout.desc", "description": "Descend a collection of morphisms to a morphism from the pushout.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape_op_equiv_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape.hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback.lift_\u03c0_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_wide_pullback", "description": "`has_wide_pullback B objs arrows` means that `wide_cospan B objs arrows` has a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_wide_pushouts", "description": "`has_wide_pushouts` represents a choice of wide pushout for every collection of morphisms", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout.head", "description": "The unique map from the head to the pushout.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape.hom_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape_op_equiv_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape_unop", "description": "The obvious functor `(wide_pushout_shape J)\u1d52\u1d56 \u2964 wide_pullback_shape J`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape.wide_span", "description": "Construct a functor out of the wide pushout shape given a J-indexed collection of arrows from a\nfixed object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback.lift_base_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape.wide_span_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape_op", "description": "The obvious functor `wide_pullback_shape J \u2964 (wide_pushout_shape J)\u1d52\u1d56`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape_op_equiv_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape_unop_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape_op", "description": "The obvious functor `wide_pushout_shape J \u2964 (wide_pullback_shape J)\u1d52\u1d56`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback.lift", "description": "Lift a collection of morphisms to a morphism to the pullback.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback.\u03c0_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape.wide_span_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape.mk_cocone", "description": "Construct a cocone over a wide span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape_unop_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_wide_pullbacks_shrink", "description": " If a category has wide pullbacks on a higher universe level it also has wide pullbacks\non a lower universe level.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape.wide_cospan", "description": "Construct a functor out of the wide pullback shape given a J-indexed collection of arrows to a\nfixed object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout.hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout.\u03b9_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape.struct", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape.diagram_iso_wide_cospan", "description": "Every diagram is naturally isomorphic (actually, equal) to a `wide_cospan`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape.mk_cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape.hom.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape_op_equiv_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape_op_equiv_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape.hom", "description": "The type of arrows for the shape indexing a wide psuhout.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape.hom.id", "description": "The type of arrows for the shape indexing a wide psuhout.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape.hom.init", "description": "The type of arrows for the shape indexing a wide psuhout.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout.\u03b9_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout.arrow_\u03b9_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout.hom_eq_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout.head_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape_op_map", "description": " The action on morphisms of the obvious functor\n`wide_pushout_shape_op : `wide_pushout_shape J \u2964 (wide_pullback_shape J)\u1d52\u1d56`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback.hom_eq_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout.arrow_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape_op_equiv", "description": "The duality equivalence `(wide_pushout_shape J)\u1d52\u1d56 \u224c wide_pullback_shape J`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape_op_unop", "description": " The inverse of the unit isomorphism of the equivalence\n`wide_pullback_shape_op_equiv : (wide_pullback_shape J)\u1d52\u1d56 \u224c wide_pushout_shape J`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape_unop_op", "description": " The counit isomorphism of the equivalence\n`wide_pullback_shape_op_equiv : (wide_pullback_shape J)\u1d52\u1d56 \u224c wide_pushout_shape J`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape_unop_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape.subsingleton_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback.\u03c0_arrow_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape.hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout.head_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape_op_equiv_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape.mk_cocone_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape.subsingleton_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape_op_map_2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback.lift_base", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape_op_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape_op_map", "description": "The action on morphisms of the obvious functor\n `wide_pullback_shape_op : wide_pullback_shape J \u2964 (wide_pushout_shape J)\u1d52\u1d56`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback.lift_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback.\u03c0", "description": "The `j`-th projection from the pullback.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape_unop", "description": "The obvious functor `(wide_pullback_shape J)\u1d52\u1d56 \u2964 wide_pushout_shape J`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape.hom", "description": "The type of arrows for the shape indexing a wide pullback.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape.hom.id", "description": "The type of arrows for the shape indexing a wide pullback.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape.hom.term", "description": "The type of arrows for the shape indexing a wide pullback.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape_op_unop", "description": " The inverse of the unit isomorphism of the equivalence\n`wide_pushout_shape_op_equiv : (wide_pushout_shape J)\u1d52\u1d56 \u224c wide_pullback_shape J`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape_op_equiv_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape_op_equiv", "description": "The duality equivalence `(wide_pullback_shape J)\u1d52\u1d56 \u224c wide_pushout_shape J`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout", "description": "A choice of wide pushout.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape_unop_op", "description": " The counit isomorphism of the equivalence\n`wide_pushout_shape_op_equiv : (wide_pushout_shape J)\u1d52\u1d56 \u224c wide_pullback_shape J`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape.mk_cocone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape", "description": "A wide pullback shape for any type `J` can be written simply as `option J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_wide_pullbacks", "description": "`has_wide_pullbacks` represents a choice of wide pullback for every collection of morphisms", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape_op_map_2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout_shape", "description": "A wide pushout shape for any type `J` can be written simply as `option J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pushout.eq_desc_of_comp_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.wide_pullback_shape.wide_cospan_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.some_add_some_of_Y_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.to_class_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.add_polynomial_slope", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.neg_Y", "description": " The $Y$-coordinate of the negation of an affine point in `W`.\n\nThis depends on `W`, and has argument order: $x_1$, $y_1$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.neg_some", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.XY_ideal_add_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.to_class_some", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.line_polynomial", "description": " The polynomial $L(X - x_1) + y_1$ associated to the line $Y = L(X - x_1) + y_1$,\nwith a slope of $L$ that passes through an affine point $(x_1, y_1)$.\n\nThis does not depend on `W`, and has argument order: $x_1$, $y_1$, $L$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.to_class_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.neg_add_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.add_polynomial_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.equation_add", "description": "The addition of two affine points in `W` on a sloped line lies in `W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.of_base_change_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.XY_ideal'", "description": "The non-zero fractional ideal $\\langle X - x, Y - y \\rangle$ of $F(W)$ for some $x, y \\in F$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.derivative_add_polynomial_slope", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.slope_of_Y_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.C_add_polynomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.eval_neg_polynomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.nonsingular_neg", "description": "The negation of a nonsingular affine point in `W` is nonsingular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.add_Y'", "description": " The $Y$-coordinate, before applying the final negation, of the addition of two affine points\n$(x_1, y_1)$ and $(x_2, y_2)$, where the line through them is not vertical and has a slope of $L$.\n\nThis depends on `W`, and has argument order: $x_1$, $x_2$, $y_1$, $L$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.coordinate_ring.C_add_polynomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.add_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.add_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.equation_neg_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.mk_XY_ideal'_mul_mk_XY_ideal'_of_Y_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.Y_eq_of_X_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.equation_neg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.nonsingular_neg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.base_change_add_Y'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point", "description": " A nonsingular rational point on a Weierstrass curve `W` over `R`. This is either the point at\ninfinity `weierstrass_curve.point.zero` or an affine point `weierstrass_curve.point.some` $(x, y)$\nsatisfying the equation $y^2 + a_1xy + a_3y = x^3 + a_2x^2 + a_4x + a_6$ of `W`. For an algebraic\nextension `S` of `R`, the type of nonsingular `S`-rational points on `W` is denoted `W\u27eeS\u27ef`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.zero", "description": " A nonsingular rational point on a Weierstrass curve `W` over `R`. This is either the point at\ninfinity `weierstrass_curve.point.zero` or an affine point `weierstrass_curve.point.some` $(x, y)$\nsatisfying the equation $y^2 + a_1xy + a_3y = x^3 + a_2x^2 + a_4x + a_6$ of `W`. For an algebraic\nextension `S` of `R`, the type of nonsingular `S`-rational points on `W` is denoted `W\u27eeS\u27ef`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.some", "description": " A nonsingular rational point on a Weierstrass curve `W` over `R`. This is either the point at\ninfinity `weierstrass_curve.point.zero` or an affine point `weierstrass_curve.point.some` $(x, y)$\nsatisfying the equation $y^2 + a_1xy + a_3y = x^3 + a_2x^2 + a_4x + a_6$ of `W`. For an algebraic\nextension `S` of `R`, the type of nonsingular `S`-rational points on `W` is denoted `W\u27eeS\u27ef`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.some_add_some_of_Y_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.some_add_self_of_Y_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.zero_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.XY_ideal_neg_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.neg_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "elliptic_curve.point.mk", "description": "An affine point on an elliptic curve `E` over `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.base_change_add_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.of_base_change", "description": "The group homomorphism from `W\u27eeF\u27ef` to `W\u27eeK\u27ef` induced by a base change from `F` to `K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.equation_add_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.base_change_neg_Y", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.of_base_change_fun", "description": "The function from `W\u27eeF\u27ef` to `W\u27eeK\u27ef` induced by a base change from `F` to `K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.mk_XY_ideal'_mul_mk_XY_ideal'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.nonsingular_add", "description": "The addition of two nonsingular affine points in `W` on a sloped line is nonsingular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.add_polynomial", "description": " The polynomial obtained by substituting the line $Y = L*(X - x_1) + y_1$, with a slope of $L$\nthat passes through an affine point $(x_1, y_1)$, into the polynomial $W(X, Y)$ associated to `W`.\nIf such a line intersects `W` at another point $(x_2, y_2)$, then the roots of this polynomial are\nprecisely $x_1$, $x_2$, and the $X$-coordinate of the addition of $(x_1, y_1)$ and $(x_2, y_2)$.\n\nThis depends on `W`, and has argument order: $x_1$, $y_1$, $L$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.base_change_slope", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.base_change_add_Y", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.add_X", "description": " The $X$-coordinate of the addition of two affine points $(x_1, y_1)$ and $(x_2, y_2)$ in `W`,\nwhere the line through them is not vertical and has a slope of $L$.\n\nThis depends on `W`, and has argument order: $x_1$, $x_2$, $L$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.slope_of_Y_ne_eq_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.add", "description": " The addition of two nonsingular rational points.\n\nGiven two nonsingular rational points `P` and `Q`, use `P + Q` instead of `add P Q`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.XY_ideal_eq\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.coordinate_ring.C_add_polynomial_slope", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.some_add_some_of_X_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.neg_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.to_class_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.XY_ideal_eq\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.slope_of_X_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.add_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.nonsingular_add_of_eval_derivative_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.neg_polynomial", "description": "The polynomial $-Y - a_1X - a_3$ associated to negation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.slope", "description": " The slope of the line through two affine points $(x_1, y_1)$ and $(x_2, y_2)$ in `W`.\nIf $x_1 \\ne x_2$, then this line is the secant of `W` through $(x_1, y_1)$ and $(x_2, y_2)$,\nand has slope $(y_1 - y_2) / (x_1 - x_2)$. Otherwise, if $y_1 \\ne -y_1 - a_1x_1 - a_3$,\nthen this line is the tangent of `W` at $(x_1, y_1) = (x_2, y_2)$, and has slope\n$(3x_1^2 + 2a_2x_1 + a_4 - a_1y_1) / (2y_1 + a_1x_1 + a_3)$. Otherwise, this line is vertical,\nand has undefined slope, in which case this function returns the value 0.\n\nThis depends on `W`, and has argument order: $x_1$, $x_2$, $y_1$, $y_2$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.XY_ideal'_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.some_add_some_of_X_ne'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.nonsingular_neg_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.base_change_neg_Y_of_base_change", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.some_add_self_of_Y_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.Y_eq_of_Y_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.add_Y", "description": " The $Y$-coordinate of the addition of two affine points $(x_1, y_1)$ and $(x_2, y_2)$ in `W`,\nwhere the line through them is not vertical and has a slope of $L$.\n\nThis depends on `W`, and has argument order: $x_1$, $x_2$, $y_1$, $L$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.to_class", "description": " The group homomorphism mapping an affine point $(x, y)$ of `W` to the class of the non-zero\nfractional ideal $\\langle X - x, Y - y \\rangle$ of $F(W)$ in the class group of $F[W]$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.add_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.has_involutive_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.base_change_add_Y'_of_base_change", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.base_change_slope_of_base_change", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.add_left_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.add_zero_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.XY_ideal_mul_XY_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.some_add_some_of_Y_ne'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.equation_add'", "description": " The addition of two affine points in `W` on a sloped line,\nbefore applying the final negation that maps $Y$ to $-Y - a_1X - a_3$, lies in `W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.nonsingular_add'", "description": " The addition of two nonsingular affine points in `W` on a sloped line,\nbefore applying the final negation that maps $Y$ to $-Y - a_1X - a_3$, is nonsingular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.to_class_fun", "description": " The set function mapping an affine point $(x, y)$ of `W` to the class of the non-zero fractional\nideal $\\langle X - x, Y - y \\rangle$ of $F(W)$ in the class group of $F[W]$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.some_add_self_of_Y_ne'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.equation_neg", "description": "The negation of an affine point in `W` lies in `W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.to_class_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.base_change_add_X_of_base_change", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.of_base_change_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.neg_Y_neg_Y", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.slope_of_Y_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.base_change_add_Y_of_base_change", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weierstrass_curve.point.neg", "description": " The negation of a nonsingular rational point.\n\nGiven a nonsingular rational point `P`, use `-P` instead of `neg P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_eq_edist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_le_Ico_sum_edist", "description": "The triangle (polygon) inequality for sequences of points; `finset.Ico` version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.tendsto_uniformly_iff", "description": "Expressing uniform convergence using `edist`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.controlled_of_uniform_embedding", "description": " If a map between pseudoemetric spaces is a uniform embedding then the edistance between `f x`\nand `f y` is controlled in terms of the distance between `x` and `y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_pi_const_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.ball_eq_empty_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.ball_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.cauchy_iff", "description": "\u03b5-\u03b4 characterization of Cauchy sequences on pseudoemetric spaces", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.uniform_continuous_on_iff", "description": "\u03b5-\u03b4 characterization of uniform continuity on a set for pseudoemetric spaces", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam_pair", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.inseparable_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.closed_ball_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_le_Ico_sum_of_edist_le", "description": " A version of `edist_le_Ico_sum_edist` with each intermediate distance replaced\nwith an upper estimate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.ball_subset_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ulift.edist_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.uniform_continuous_iff", "description": "\u03b5-\u03b4 characterization of uniform continuity on pseudoemetric spaces", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtype.emetric_space", "description": "Emetric space instance on subsets of emetric spaces", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.totally_bounded_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.emetric_space", "description": "Emetric space instance on the multiplicative opposite of an emetric space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pseudo_emetric_space_pi", "description": " The product of a finite number of pseudoemetric spaces, with the max distance, is still\na pseudoemetric space.\nThis construction would also work for infinite products, but it would not give rise\nto the product topology. Hence, we only formalize it in the good situation of finitely many\nspaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.is_open_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.tendsto_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric_space_pi", "description": " The product of a finite number of emetric spaces, with the max distance, is still\nan emetric space.\nThis construction would also work for infinite products, but it would not give rise\nto the product topology. Hence, we only formalize it in the good situation of finitely many\nspaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.edist_lt_top_setoid", "description": "Relation \u201ctwo points are at a finite edistance\u201d is an equivalence relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_le_range_sum_edist", "description": "The triangle (polygon) inequality for sequences of points; `finset.range` version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.ball_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.emetric_space", "description": "Emetric space instance on the additive opposite of an emetric space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.tendsto_locally_uniformly_iff", "description": "Expressing locally uniform convergence using `edist`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam", "description": "The diameter of a set in a pseudoemetric space, named `emetric.diam`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.separation_quotient.has_edist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.has_edist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_le_pi_edist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_mem_uniformity", "description": "Fixed size neighborhoods of the diagonal belong to the uniform structure", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam_Union_mem_option", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_to_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtype.edist_eq", "description": " The extended psuedodistance on a subset of a pseudoemetric space is the restriction of\nthe original pseudodistance, by definition", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.second_countable_of_sigma_compact", "description": " A sigma compact pseudo emetric space has second countable topology. This is not an instance\nto avoid a loop with `sigma_compact_space_of_locally_compact_second_countable`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.mem_nhds_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.pseudo_emetric_space_max", "description": " The product of two pseudoemetric spaces, with the max distance, is an extended\npseudometric spaces. We make sure that the uniform structure thus constructed is the one\ncorresponding to the product of uniform spaces, to avoid diamond problems.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.mem_nhds_within_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam_pi_le_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.subset_countable_closure_of_compact", "description": " A compact set in a pseudo emetric space is separable, i.e., it is a subset of the closure of a\ncountable set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam_image_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.pseudo_emetric_space", "description": "Pseudoemetric space instance on the additive opposite of a pseudoemetric space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_congr_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.nhds_within_basis_closed_eball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.tendsto_nhds_within_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_eq_zero", "description": "Characterize the equality of points by the vanishing of their extended distance", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.cauchy_seq_iff", "description": " In a pseudoemetric space, Cauchy sequences are characterized by the fact that, eventually,\nthe pseudoedistance between its elements is arbitrarily small", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ulift.pseudo_emetric_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_edist", "description": "`has_edist \u03b1` means that `\u03b1` is equipped with an extended distance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_edist.edist", "description": "`has_edist \u03b1` means that `\u03b1` is equipped with an extended distance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.complete_of_convergent_controlled_sequences", "description": " A very useful criterion to show that a space is complete is to show that all sequences\nwhich satisfy a bound of the form `edist (u n) (u m) < B N` for all `n m \u2265 N` are\nconverging. This is often applied for `B N = 2^{-N}`, i.e., with a very fast convergence to\n`0`, which makes it possible to use arguments of converging series, while this is impossible\nto do in general for arbitrary Cauchy sequences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.edist_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.tendsto_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam_empty", "description": "The diameter of the empty set vanishes", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.has_edist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniformity_edist", "description": "Reformulation of the uniform structure in terms of the extended distance", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam_pos_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.closed_ball", "description": "`emetric.closed_ball x \u03b5` is the set of all points `y` with `edist y x \u2264 \u03b5`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.uniform_embedding_iff", "description": "\u03b5-\u03b4 characterization of uniform embeddings on pseudoemetric spaces", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.mk_uniformity_basis_le", "description": " Given `f : \u03b2 \u2192 \u211d\u22650\u221e`, if `f` sends `{i | p i}` to a set of positive numbers\naccumulating to zero, then closed `f i`-neighborhoods of the diagonal form a basis of `\ud835\udce4 \u03b1`.\n\nFor specific bases see `uniformity_basis_edist_le` and `uniformity_basis_edist_le'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space_of_edist", "description": "Creating a uniform space from an extended distance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.uniform_embedding_iff'", "description": " A map between emetric spaces is a uniform embedding if and only if the edistance between `f x`\nand `f y` is controlled in terms of the distance between `x` and `y` and conversely.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.cauchy_seq_iff'", "description": "A variation around the emetric characterization of Cauchy sequences", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.mem_closed_ball_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam_singleton", "description": "The diameter of a singleton vanishes", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_to_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.mem_closed_ball'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniformity_pseudoedist", "description": "Reformulation of the uniform structure in terms of the extended distance", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pseudo_emetric_space", "description": " Extended (pseudo) metric spaces, with an extended distance `edist` possibly taking the\nvalue \u221e\n\nEach pseudo_emetric space induces a canonical `uniform_space` and hence a canonical\n`topological_space`.\nThis is enforced in the type class definition, by extending the `uniform_space` structure. When\ninstantiating a `pseudo_emetric_space` structure, the uniformity fields are not necessary, they\nwill be filled in by default. There is a default value for the uniformity, that can be substituted\nin cases of interest, for instance when instantiating a `pseudo_emetric_space` structure\non a product.\n\nContinuity of `edist` is proved in `topology.instances.ennreal`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pseudo_emetric_space.to_has_edist", "description": " Extended (pseudo) metric spaces, with an extended distance `edist` possibly taking the\nvalue \u221e\n\nEach pseudo_emetric space induces a canonical `uniform_space` and hence a canonical\n`topological_space`.\nThis is enforced in the type class definition, by extending the `uniform_space` structure. When\ninstantiating a `pseudo_emetric_space` structure, the uniformity fields are not necessary, they\nwill be filled in by default. There is a default value for the uniformity, that can be substituted\nin cases of interest, for instance when instantiating a `pseudo_emetric_space` structure\non a product.\n\nContinuity of `edist` is proved in `topology.instances.ennreal`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pseudo_emetric_space.edist_self", "description": " Extended (pseudo) metric spaces, with an extended distance `edist` possibly taking the\nvalue \u221e\n\nEach pseudo_emetric space induces a canonical `uniform_space` and hence a canonical\n`topological_space`.\nThis is enforced in the type class definition, by extending the `uniform_space` structure. When\ninstantiating a `pseudo_emetric_space` structure, the uniformity fields are not necessary, they\nwill be filled in by default. There is a default value for the uniformity, that can be substituted\nin cases of interest, for instance when instantiating a `pseudo_emetric_space` structure\non a product.\n\nContinuity of `edist` is proved in `topology.instances.ennreal`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pseudo_emetric_space.edist_comm", "description": " Extended (pseudo) metric spaces, with an extended distance `edist` possibly taking the\nvalue \u221e\n\nEach pseudo_emetric space induces a canonical `uniform_space` and hence a canonical\n`topological_space`.\nThis is enforced in the type class definition, by extending the `uniform_space` structure. When\ninstantiating a `pseudo_emetric_space` structure, the uniformity fields are not necessary, they\nwill be filled in by default. There is a default value for the uniformity, that can be substituted\nin cases of interest, for instance when instantiating a `pseudo_emetric_space` structure\non a product.\n\nContinuity of `edist` is proved in `topology.instances.ennreal`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pseudo_emetric_space.edist_triangle", "description": " Extended (pseudo) metric spaces, with an extended distance `edist` possibly taking the\nvalue \u221e\n\nEach pseudo_emetric space induces a canonical `uniform_space` and hence a canonical\n`topological_space`.\nThis is enforced in the type class definition, by extending the `uniform_space` structure. When\ninstantiating a `pseudo_emetric_space` structure, the uniformity fields are not necessary, they\nwill be filled in by default. There is a default value for the uniformity, that can be substituted\nin cases of interest, for instance when instantiating a `pseudo_emetric_space` structure\non a product.\n\nContinuity of `edist` is proved in `topology.instances.ennreal`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pseudo_emetric_space.to_uniform_space", "description": " Extended (pseudo) metric spaces, with an extended distance `edist` possibly taking the\nvalue \u221e\n\nEach pseudo_emetric space induces a canonical `uniform_space` and hence a canonical\n`topological_space`.\nThis is enforced in the type class definition, by extending the `uniform_space` structure. When\ninstantiating a `pseudo_emetric_space` structure, the uniformity fields are not necessary, they\nwill be filled in by default. There is a default value for the uniformity, that can be substituted\nin cases of interest, for instance when instantiating a `pseudo_emetric_space` structure\non a product.\n\nContinuity of `edist` is proved in `topology.instances.ennreal`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pseudo_emetric_space.uniformity_edist", "description": " Extended (pseudo) metric spaces, with an extended distance `edist` possibly taking the\nvalue \u221e\n\nEach pseudo_emetric space induces a canonical `uniform_space` and hence a canonical\n`topological_space`.\nThis is enforced in the type class definition, by extending the `uniform_space` structure. When\ninstantiating a `pseudo_emetric_space` structure, the uniformity fields are not necessary, they\nwill be filled in by default. There is a default value for the uniformity, that can be substituted\nin cases of interest, for instance when instantiating a `pseudo_emetric_space` structure\non a product.\n\nContinuity of `edist` is proved in `topology.instances.ennreal`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_uniformity_edist", "description": "Characterization of the elements of the uniformity in terms of the extended distance", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.separation_quotient.emetric_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.complete_of_cauchy_seq_tendsto", "description": "A sequentially complete pseudoemetric space is complete.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.tendsto_uniformly_on_iff", "description": "Expressing uniform convergence on a set using `edist`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.tendsto_nhds_within_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.ball_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.countable_closure_of_compact", "description": "A compact set in an emetric space is separable, i.e., it is the closure of a countable set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.mem_ball_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniformity_basis_edist_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.nhds_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.nhds_basis_closed_eball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.cauchy_seq_iff_nnreal", "description": " A variation of the emetric characterization of Cauchy sequences that deals with\n`\u211d\u22650` upper bounds.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_le_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam_triple", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.edist_le_diam_of_mem", "description": "If two points belong to some set, their edistance is bounded by the diameter of the set", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.closed_ball_subset_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.emetric_space_max", "description": " The product of two emetric spaces, with the max distance, is an extended\nmetric spaces. We make sure that the uniform structure thus constructed is the one\ncorresponding to the product of uniform spaces, to avoid diamond problems.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam_subsingleton", "description": "The diameter of a subsingleton vanishes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.pseudo_emetric_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.exists_ball_subset_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pseudo_emetric_space.induced", "description": "The extended pseudometric induced by a function taking values in a pseudoemetric space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.ball", "description": "`emetric.ball x \u03b5` is the set of all points `y` with `edist y x < \u03b5`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.ball_prod_same", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.mem_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_triangle_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_pi_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.mem_ball'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.ball_subset_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.mem_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam_union", "description": " The diameter of a union is controlled by the diameter of the sets, and the edistance\nbetween two points in the sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.ord_connected_set_of_ball_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.totally_bounded_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.edist_unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pseudo_emetric_space.replace_uniformity", "description": " Auxiliary function to replace the uniformity on a pseudoemetric space with\na uniformity which is equal to the original one, but maybe not defeq.\nThis is useful if one wants to construct a pseudoemetric space with a\nspecified uniformity. See Note [forgetful inheritance] explaining why having definitionally\nthe right uniformity is often important.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_of_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.emetric_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam_mono", "description": "The diameter is monotonous with respect to inclusion", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric_space.induced", "description": "The extended metric induced by an injective function taking values in a emetric space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.edist_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.is_closed_ball_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.nhds_basis_eball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.emetric_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ulift.edist_up_up", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_of_dual", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam_le", "description": " If the distance between any two points in a set is bounded by some constant, this constant\nbounds the diameter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_pi_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric_space.of_t0_pseudo_emetric_space", "description": "If a `pseudo_emetric_space` is a T\u2080 space, then it is an `emetric_space`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_separated", "description": "An emetric space is separated", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_triangle_left", "description": "Triangle inequality for the extended distance", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniformity_basis_edist_nnreal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.ord_connected_set_of_closed_ball_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.tendsto_locally_uniformly_on_iff", "description": "Expressing locally uniform convergence on a set using `edist`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.pos_of_mem_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.tendsto_nhds_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam_union'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.nhds_within_basis_eball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.second_countable_of_almost_dense_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.mk_uniformity_basis", "description": " Given `f : \u03b2 \u2192 \u211d\u22650\u221e`, if `f` sends `{i | p i}` to a set of positive numbers\naccumulating to zero, then `f i`-neighborhoods of the diagonal form a basis of `\ud835\udce4 \u03b1`.\n\nFor specific bases see `uniformity_basis_edist`, `uniformity_basis_edist'`,\n`uniformity_basis_edist_nnreal`, and `uniformity_basis_edist_inv_nat`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_triangle4", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.diam_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.mem_closed_ball_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric_space", "description": "We now define `emetric_space`, extending `pseudo_emetric_space`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric_space.to_pseudo_emetric_space", "description": "We now define `emetric_space`, extending `pseudo_emetric_space`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric_space.eq_of_edist_eq_zero", "description": "We now define `emetric_space`, extending `pseudo_emetric_space`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.pseudo_emetric_space", "description": "Pseudoemetric space instance on the multiplicative opposite of a pseudoemetric space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.closed_ball_prod_same", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.emetric_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.edist_le_of_diam_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_congr_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniformity_basis_edist'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniformity_basis_edist_inv_two_pow", "description": "", 