ite type, then `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b1` and `\u03b1` have the same cardinality.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.aleph_0_le_aleph'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.power_eq_two_power", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.aleph_idx.init", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.beth", "description": " Beth numbers are defined so that `beth 0 = \u2135\u2080`, `beth (succ o) = 2 ^ (beth o)`, and when `o` is\na limit ordinal, `beth o` is the supremum of `beth o'` for `o' < o`.\n\nAssuming the generalized continuum hypothesis, which is undecidable in ZFC, `beth o = aleph o` for\nevery `o`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.aleph", "description": "The `aleph` function gives the infinite cardinals listed by their\n ordinal index. `aleph 0 = \u2135\u2080`, `aleph 1 = succ \u2135\u2080` is the first\n uncountable cardinal, and so on.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.aleph_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.mul_eq_max_of_aleph_0_le_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.beth_normal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.add_lt_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.add_mk_eq_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.bit0_lt_bit0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.aleph_0_le_beth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.aleph_idx_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.aleph_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.aleph'_is_normal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.beth_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.powerlt_aleph_0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.add_right_inj_of_lt_aleph_0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.aleph_0_mul_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.bit1_le_bit0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.mk_multiset_of_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.mk_multiset_of_infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.bit0_le_bit1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.aleph'", "description": "The `aleph'` function gives the cardinals listed by their ordinal\n index, and is the inverse of `aleph_idx`.\n `aleph' n = n`, `aleph' \u03c9 = \u03c9`, `aleph' (\u03c9 + 1) = succ \u2135\u2080`, etc.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.mk_compl_eq_mk_compl_infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.mk_compl_eq_mk_compl_finite_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.aleph'_le_of_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.aleph_idx_aleph'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.mul_lt_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.eq_aleph_of_eq_card_ord", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.principal_add_ord", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.aleph_idx.initial_seg", "description": "The `aleph'` index function, which gives the ordinal index of a cardinal.\n (The `aleph'` part is because unlike `aleph` this counts also the\n finite stages. So `aleph_idx n = n`, `aleph_idx \u03c9 = \u03c9`,\n `aleph_idx \u2135\u2081 = \u03c9 + 1` and so on.)\n In this definition, we register additionally that this function is an initial segment,\n i.e., it is order preserving and its range is an initial segment of the ordinals.\n For the basic function version, see `aleph_idx`.\n For an upgraded version stating that the range is everything, see `aleph_idx.rel_iso`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.succ_aleph_0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.bit0_lt_aleph_0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.ord_aleph_is_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.nonempty_out_aleph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.mk_finsupp_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.eq_aleph'_of_eq_card_ord", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.mk_finsupp_lift_of_infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.zero_lt_bit1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.mul_eq_left_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.aleph'_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.one_le_bit1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.extend_function_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.aleph_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.mk_list_eq_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.mk_mul_aleph_0_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.aleph'_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.beth_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.aleph_to_part_enat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.power_self_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.aleph_le_beth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cardinal.exists_aleph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.homology_c_to_k.category_theory.is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.condition_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.\u03c0'_desc'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.hom_to_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.condition_\u03c0'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.homology_k", "description": "The kernel of `cokernel.desc f g w`. This is isomorphic to `homology f g w`.\n See `homology_iso_kernel_desc`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.\u03c0'_desc'_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.lift_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.map_eq_lift_desc'_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.map_\u03b9_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.homology_c_to_k.category_theory.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.map_eq_lift_desc'_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology_iso_kernel_desc", "description": "The homology associated to `f` and `g` is isomorphic to a kernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.desc'", "description": "Obtain a morphism from the homology, given a morphism from the kernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.map_eq_desc'_lift_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.\u03c0'_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.map_eq_desc'_lift_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.\u03c0'_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.condition_\u03b9_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.\u03b9", "description": "The canonical map from the homology of `f` and `g` to the cokernel of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.\u03c0'", "description": "The canonical map from the kernel of `g` to the homology of `f` and `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.lift", "description": "Obtain a moprhism to the homology, given a morphism to the kernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.lift_\u03b9_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.condition_\u03c0'_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.\u03c0'_eq_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.hom_from_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.homology_c_to_k", "description": "The canonical map from `homology_c` to `homology_k`.\n This is an isomorphism, and it is used in obtaining the API for `homology f g w`\n in the bottom of this file.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.homology_c", "description": "The cokernel of `kernel.lift g f w`. This is isomorphic to `homology f g w`.\n See `homology_iso_cokernel_lift`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.\u03c0'_eq_\u03c0_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.homology_c_to_k.category_theory.epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.homology_functor_iso", "description": "If `F` is an exact additive functor, then `F` commutes with `H\u1d62` (up to natural isomorphism).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.map_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.\u03c0'_map_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homology.\u03c0'_\u03b9_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.homology_iso", "description": "When `F` is an exact additive functor, `F(H\u1d62(X)) \u2245 H\u1d62(F(X))` for `X` a complex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.to_AddMon_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.to_CommMon_iso", "description": "Build an isomorphism in the category `CommMon` from a `mul_equiv` between `comm_monoid`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso.AddMon_iso_to_add_equiv", "description": "Build an `add_equiv` from an isomorphism in the category\n`AddMon`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.to_AddMon_iso_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CommMon.Mon.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CommMon.comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommMon.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddMon.of_hom", "description": "Typecheck a `add_monoid_hom` as a morphism in `AddMon`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommMon.forget_reflects_isos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CommMon.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.of_hom", "description": "Typecheck a `monoid_hom` as a morphism in `Mon`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommMon.Mon.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso.CommMon_iso_to_add_equiv", "description": "Build an `add_equiv` from an isomorphism in the category\n`AddCommMon`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.of.group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddMon.has_coe_to_sort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.to_CommMon_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CommMon.comm_monoid.to_monoid.category_theory.bundled_hom.parent_projection", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommMon.coe_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso.CommMon_iso_to_mul_equiv", "description": "Build a `mul_equiv` from an isomorphism in the category `CommMon`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.large_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.has_coe_to_sort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.of_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso.Mon_iso_to_mul_equiv", "description": "Build a `mul_equiv` from an isomorphism in the category `Mon`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommMon.large_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommMon.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddMon.of", "description": "Construct a bundled `Mon` from the underlying type and typeclass.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommMon.concrete_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommMon.of", "description": "Construct a bundled `AddCommMon` from the underlying type and typeclass.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CommMon.forget_reflects_isos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.bundled_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddMon.coe_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommMon.comm_monoid.to_monoid.category_theory.bundled_hom.parent_projection", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.to_AddCommMon_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.to_Mon_iso", "description": "Build an isomorphism in the category `Mon` from a `mul_equiv` between `monoid`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CommMon.large_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv_iso_Mon_iso", "description": " multiplicative equivalences between `monoid`s are the same as (isomorphic to) isomorphisms\nin `Mon`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.of", "description": "Construct a bundled `Mon` from the underlying type and typeclass.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.coe_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv_iso_CommMon_iso", "description": " multiplicative equivalences between `comm_monoid`s are the same as (isomorphic to) isomorphisms\nin `CommMon`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommMon", "description": "The category of additive commutative monoids and monoid morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv_iso_AddMon_iso", "description": "additive equivalences between `add_monoid`s are the same\nas (isomorphic to) isomorphisms in `AddMon`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddMon.assoc_add_monoid_hom", "description": "`add_monoid_hom` doesn't actually assume associativity. This alias is needed to make\nthe category theory machinery work.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv_iso_AddCommMon_iso", "description": "additive equivalences between `add_comm_monoid`s are\nthe same as (isomorphic to) isomorphisms in `AddCommMon`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon", "description": "The category of monoids and monoid morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CommMon.concrete_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.to_Mon_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddMon.forget_reflects_isos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.to_AddMon_iso", "description": "Build an isomorphism in the category `AddMon` from\nan `add_equiv` between `add_monoid`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddMon.of.add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.to_AddCommMon_iso_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddMon.add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.to_Mon_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.forget_reflects_isos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.to_CommMon_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddMon.bundled_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddMon", "description": "The category of additive monoids and monoid morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CommMon.has_coe_to_sort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.assoc_monoid_hom", "description": " `monoid_hom` doesn't actually assume associativity. This alias is needed to make the category\ntheory machinery work.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.to_AddCommMon_iso", "description": "Build an isomorphism in the category `AddCommMon`\nfrom an `add_equiv` between `add_comm_monoid`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddMon.large_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddMon.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CommMon", "description": "The category of commutative monoids and monoid morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddMon.concrete_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.concrete_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CommMon.of", "description": "Construct a bundled `CommMon` from the underlying type and typeclass.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommMon.has_forget_to_AddMon", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CommMon.has_forget_to_Mon", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CommMon.coe_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommMon.has_coe_to_sort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_eq_linear_combination", "description": " Viewing a module as an affine space modelled on itself, affine combinations are just linear\ncombinations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "centroid_mem_affine_span_of_nonempty", "description": " In the characteristic zero case, the centroid lies in the affine\nspan if the set is nonempty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_of_point_eq_of_sum_eq_zero", "description": " The weighted sum is independent of the base point when the sum of\nthe weights is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_subtype_eq_filter", "description": "A weighted sum over `s.subtype pred` equals one over `s.filter pred`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_const_smul", "description": "A constant multiplier of the weights in `weighted_vsub_of` may be moved outside the sum.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.centroid_weights_eq_const", "description": "`centroid_weights` equals a constant function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_centroid_weights_eq_one_of_cast_card_ne_zero", "description": " The weights in the centroid sum to 1, if the number of points,\nconverted to `k`, is not zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.eq_weighted_vsub_subset_iff_eq_weighted_vsub_subtype", "description": " Suppose an indexed family of points is given, along with a subset\nof the index type.  A vector can be expressed as `weighted_vsub` using\na `finset` lying within that subset and with sum of weights 0 if and\nonly if it can be expressed as `weighted_vsub` with sum of weights 0\nfor the corresponding indexed family whose index type is the subtype\ncorresponding to that subset.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_line_map_weights_apply_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_affine_combination_of_mem_affine_span", "description": " A point in the `affine_span` of an indexed family is an\n`affine_combination` with sum of weights 1. See also\n`eq_affine_combination_of_mem_affine_span_of_fintype`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.univ_fin2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_of_point", "description": " A weighted sum of the results of subtracting a base point from the\ngiven points, as a linear map on the weights.  The main cases of\ninterest are where the sum of the weights is 0, in which case the sum\nis independent of the choice of base point, and where the sum of the\nweights is 1, in which case the sum added to the base point is\nindependent of the choice of base point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_apply_const", "description": " The value of `weighted_vsub`, where the given points are equal and the sum of the weights\nis 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.centroid_weights_indicator_def", "description": "The definition of `centroid_weights_indicator`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_affine_combination_single_weights", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.attach_affine_combination_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_sdiff_sub", "description": "A weighted sum may be split into a subtraction of such sums over two subsets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_filter_of_ne", "description": " An affine combination over `s.filter pred` equals one over `s` if all the weights at indices\nin `s` not satisfying `pred` are zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.centroid_singleton", "description": "The centroid of a single point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_weighted_vsub_vsub_weights", "description": " A weighted subtraction with `weighted_vsub_vsub_weights` gives the result of subtracting the\nspecified points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_sdiff", "description": "A weighted sum may be split into such sums over two subsets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_vsub_weights_apply_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_of_point_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_apply_const", "description": "The value of `affine_combination`, where the given points are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_single_weights_apply_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_congr", "description": " `affine_combination` gives equal results for two families of weights and two families of\npoints that are equal on `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_line_map_weights", "description": "Weights for expressing `line_map` as an affine combination.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_centroid_weights_indicator", "description": "The sum of the weights for the centroid indexed by a `fintype`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_eq_weighted_vsub_of_point_of_sum_eq_zero", "description": " `weighted_vsub` gives the sum of the results of subtracting any\nbase point, when the sum of the weights is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_centroid_weights_eq_one_of_card_ne_zero", "description": " In the characteristic zero case, the weights in the centroid sum\nto 1 if the number of points is not zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_vsub_weights_apply_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.map_affine_combination", "description": "Affine maps commute with affine combinations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_span_eq_affine_span_line_map_units", "description": " Given a set of points, together with a chosen base point in this set, if we affinely transport\nall other members of the set along the line joining them to this base point, the affine span is\nunchanged.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_single_weights_apply_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.centroid_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.eq_weighted_vsub_of_point_subset_iff_eq_weighted_vsub_of_point_subtype", "description": " Suppose an indexed family of points is given, along with a subset\nof the index type.  A vector can be expressed as\n`weighted_vsub_of_point` using a `finset` lying within that subset and\nwith a given sum of weights if and only if it can be expressed as\n`weighted_vsub_of_point` with that sum of weights for the\ncorresponding indexed family whose index type is the subtype\ncorresponding to that subset.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_centroid_weights_eq_one_of_card_eq_add_one", "description": " In the characteristic zero case, the weights in the centroid sum\nto 1 if the number of points is `n + 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_smul_vsub_const_eq_weighted_vsub", "description": " A weighted sum of pairwise subtractions, where the point on the right is constant and the\nsum of the weights is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.centroid_pair_fin", "description": " The centroid of two points indexed by `fin 2`, expressed directly\nas adding a vector to the first point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_of_point_vadd_eq_of_sum_eq_one", "description": " The weighted sum, added to the base point, is independent of the\nbase point when the sum of the weights is 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.centroid_def", "description": "The definition of the centroid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_eq_of_weighted_vsub_eq_zero_of_eq_neg_one", "description": " If a weighted sum is zero and one of the weights is `-1`, the corresponding point is\nthe affine combination of the other points with the given weights.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.centroid_weights", "description": "The weights for the centroid of some points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_linear", "description": " The linear map corresponding to `affine_combination` is\n`weighted_vsub`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_affine_combination_single_weights", "description": "An affine combination with `affine_combination_single_weights` gives the specified point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_centroid_weights_indicator_eq_one_of_card_eq_add_one", "description": " In the characteristic zero case, the weights in the centroid\nindexed by a `fintype` sum to 1 if the number of points is `n + 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination", "description": " A weighted sum of the results of subtracting a default base point\nfrom the given points, added to that base point, as an affine map on\nthe weights.  This is intended to be used when the sum of the weights\nis 1, in which case it is an affine combination (barycenter) of the\npoints with the given weights; that condition is specified as a\nhypothesis on those lemmas that require it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_map", "description": " An affine combination, over the image of an embedding, equals an\naffine combination with the same points and weights over the original\n`finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_affine_combination_of_mem_affine_span_of_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_of_point_eq_of_weights_eq", "description": " Given a family of points, if we use a member of the family as a base point, the\n`weighted_vsub_of_point` does not depend on the value of the weights at this point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_smul_vsub_const_eq_affine_combination_vsub", "description": " A weighted sum of pairwise subtractions, where the point on the right is constant and the\nsum of the weights is 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_of_point_const_smul", "description": " A constant multiplier of the weights in `weighted_vsub_of_point` may be moved outside the\nsum.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_combination_mem_affine_span", "description": " An `affine_combination` with sum of weights 1 is in the\n`affine_span` of an indexed family, if the underlying ring is\nnontrivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.centroid", "description": " The centroid of some points.  Although defined for any `s`, this\nis intended to be used in the case where the number of points,\nconverted to `k`, is not zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_centroid_weights_eq_one_of_nonempty", "description": " In the characteristic zero case, the weights in the centroid sum\nto 1 if the set is nonempty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_indicator_subset", "description": " The weighted sum is unaffected by changing the weights to the\ncorresponding indicator function and adding points to the set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_of_point_map", "description": " A weighted sum, over the image of an embedding, equals a weighted\nsum with the same points and weights over the original\n`finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.centroid_weights_indicator", "description": " `centroid_weights` gives the weights for the centroid as a\nconstant function, which is suitable when summing over the points\nwhose centroid is being taken.  This function gives the weights in a\nform suitable for summing over a larger set of points, as an indicator\nfunction that is zero outside the set whose centroid is being taken.\nIn the case of a `fintype`, the sum may be over `univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_vsub_weights_apply_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_vsub_weights_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.centroid_eq_affine_combination_fintype", "description": "The centroid as an affine combination over a `fintype`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_of_point_sdiff", "description": "A weighted sum may be split into such sums over two subsets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_of_point_erase", "description": " The weighted sum is unaffected by removing the base point, if\npresent, from the set of points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_smul_const_vsub_eq_vsub_affine_combination", "description": " A weighted sum of pairwise subtractions, where the point on the left is constant and the\nsum of the weights is 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_affine_span_iff_eq_affine_combination", "description": " A point is in the `affine_span` of an indexed family if and only\nif it is an `affine_combination` with sum of weights 1, provided the\nunderlying ring is nontrivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_indicator_subset", "description": " An affine combination is unaffected by changing the weights to the\ncorresponding indicator function and adding points to the set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_eq_linear_combination", "description": " Viewing a module as an affine space modelled on itself, a `weighted_vsub` is just a linear\ncombination.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_affine_span_iff_eq_weighted_vsub_of_point_vadd", "description": " Given a family of points together with a chosen base point in that family, membership of the\naffine span of this family corresponds to an identity in terms of `weighted_vsub_of_point`, with\nweights that are not required to sum to 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.centroid_eq_of_inj_on_of_image_eq", "description": " Two indexed families of points that are injective on the given\n`finset`s and with the same points in the image of those `finset`s\nhave the same centroid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_line_map_weights_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "centroid_mem_affine_span_of_card_ne_zero", "description": " In the characteristic zero case, the centroid lies in the affine\nspan if the number of points is not zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_smul_vsub_eq_affine_combination_vsub", "description": " A weighted sum of pairwise subtractions, expressed as a subtraction of two `affine_combination`\nexpressions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_smul_const_vsub_eq_neg_weighted_vsub", "description": " A weighted sum of pairwise subtractions, where the point on the left is constant and the\nsum of the weights is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map.weighted_vsub_of_point", "description": "A weighted sum, as an affine map on the points involved.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_congr", "description": " `weighted_vsub` gives equal results for two families of weights and two families of points\nthat are equal on `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_of_point_indicator_subset", "description": " The weighted sum is unaffected by changing the weights to the\ncorresponding indicator function and adding points to the set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_centroid_weights_indicator_eq_one_of_nonempty", "description": " In the characteristic zero case, the weights in the centroid\nindexed by a `fintype` sum to 1 if the set is nonempty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_vector_span_iff_eq_weighted_vsub", "description": " A vector is in the `vector_span` of an indexed family if and only\nif it is a `weighted_vsub` with sum of weights 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.eq_affine_combination_subset_iff_eq_affine_combination_subtype", "description": " Suppose an indexed family of points is given, along with a subset\nof the index type.  A point can be expressed as an\n`affine_combination` using a `finset` lying within that subset and\nwith sum of weights 1 if and only if it can be expressed an\n`affine_combination` with sum of weights 1 for the corresponding\nindexed family whose index type is the subtype corresponding to that\nsubset.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_subtype_eq_filter", "description": "An affine combination over `s.subtype pred` equals one over `s.filter pred`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_map", "description": " A weighted subtraction, over the image of an embedding, equals a\nweighted subtraction with the same points and weights over the\noriginal `finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_of_point_congr", "description": " `weighted_vsub_of_point` gives equal results for two families of weights and two families of\npoints that are equal on `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_filter_of_ne", "description": " A weighted sum over `s.filter pred` equals one over `s` if all the weights at indices in `s`\nnot satisfying `pred` are zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_smul_vsub_eq_weighted_vsub_sub", "description": " A weighted sum of pairwise subtractions, expressed as a subtraction of two `weighted_vsub`\nexpressions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_centroid_weights_indicator_eq_one_of_card_ne_zero", "description": " In the characteristic zero case, the weights in the centroid\nindexed by a `fintype` sum to 1 if the number of points is not\nzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_weighted_vsub_vsub_weights", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_smul_const_vsub_eq_sub_weighted_vsub_of_point", "description": " A weighted sum of pairwise subtractions, where the point on the left is constant,\nexpressed as a subtraction involving a `weighted_vsub_of_point` expression.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_of_point_filter_of_ne", "description": " A weighted sum over `s.filter pred` equals one over `s` if all the weights at indices in `s`\nnot satisfying `pred` are zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "centroid_mem_affine_span_of_cast_card_ne_zero", "description": " The centroid lies in the affine span if the number of points,\nconverted to `k`, is not zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_of_point_insert", "description": " The weighted sum is unaffected by adding the base point, whether\nor not present, to the set of points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.centroid_eq_centroid_image_of_inj_on", "description": " An indexed family of points that is injective on the given\n`finset` has the same centroid as the image of that `finset`.  This is\nstated in terms of a set equal to the image to provide control of\ndefinitional equality for the index type used for the centroid of the\nimage.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.centroid_weights_apply", "description": "`centroid_weights` at any point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_empty", "description": "The `weighted_vsub` for an empty set is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_eq_weighted_vsub_of_point_vadd_of_sum_eq_one", "description": " `affine_combination` gives the sum with any base point, when the\nsum of the weights is 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_apply", "description": " Applying `affine_combination` with given weights.  This is for the\ncase where a result involving a default base point is OK (for example,\nwhen that base point will cancel out later); a more typical use case\nfor `affine_combination` would involve selecting a preferred base\npoint with\n`affine_combination_eq_weighted_vsub_of_point_vadd_of_sum_eq_one` and\nthen using `weighted_vsub_of_point_apply`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_sdiff_sub", "description": "A weighted sum may be split into a subtraction of affine combinations over two subsets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_smul_vsub_eq_weighted_vsub_of_point_sub", "description": " A weighted sum of pairwise subtractions, expressed as a subtraction of two\n`weighted_vsub_of_point` expressions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "centroid_mem_affine_span_of_card_eq_add_one", "description": " In the characteristic zero case, the centroid lies in the affine\nspan if the number of points is `n + 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_single_weights", "description": "Weights for expressing a single point as an affine combination.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_of_point_apply_const", "description": "The value of `weighted_vsub_of_point`, where the given points are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_vadd_affine_combination", "description": "Adding a `weighted_vsub` to an `affine_combination`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_affine_combination_line_map_weights", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_vsub", "description": "Subtracting two `affine_combination`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_vsub_weights", "description": "Weights for expressing the subtraction of two points as a `weighted_vsub`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_affine_combination_line_map_weights", "description": " An affine combination with `affine_combination_line_map_weights` gives the result of\n`line_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_line_map_weights_apply_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_of_eq_one_of_eq_zero", "description": " An `affine_combination` equals a point if that point is in the set\nand has weight 1 and the other points in the set have weight 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_apply", "description": " Applying `weighted_vsub` with given weights.  This is for the case\nwhere a result involving a default base point is OK (for example, when\nthat base point will cancel out later); a more typical use case for\n`weighted_vsub` would involve selecting a preferred base point with\n`weighted_vsub_eq_weighted_vsub_of_point_of_sum_eq_zero` and then\nusing `weighted_vsub_of_point_apply`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weighted_vsub_mem_vector_span", "description": " A `weighted_vsub` with sum of weights 0 is in the `vector_span` of\nan indexed family.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_of_point_sdiff_sub", "description": "A weighted sum may be split into a subtraction of such sums over two subsets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.attach_affine_combination_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.centroid_map", "description": " A centroid, over the image of an embedding, equals a centroid with\nthe same points and weights over the original `finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub", "description": " A weighted sum of the results of subtracting a default base point\nfrom the given points, as a linear map on the weights.  This is\nintended to be used when the sum of the weights is 0; that condition\nis specified as a hypothesis on those lemmas that require it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_smul_vsub_const_eq_weighted_vsub_of_point_sub", "description": " A weighted sum of pairwise subtractions, where the point on the right is constant,\nexpressed as a subtraction involving a `weighted_vsub_of_point` expression.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.weighted_vsub_of_point_subtype_eq_filter", "description": "A weighted sum over `s.subtype pred` equals one over `s.filter pred`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.affine_combination_line_map_weights_apply_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.centroid_pair", "description": " The centroid of two points, expressed directly as adding a vector\nto a point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.whiskering_left_obj_preimage_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal_functor_obj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal\u2082_counit_iso_hom_app_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension\u2081.map_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension\u2081.obj_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension\u2082.category_theory.is_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension\u2082_obj_obj_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.to_karoubi.category_theory.is_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension\u2082_comp_whiskering_left_to_karoubi_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal\u2082_functor_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal\u2082_functor_obj_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension\u2081.obj", "description": " The canonical extension of a functor `C \u2964 karoubi D` to a functor\n`karoubi C \u2964 karoubi D`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension\u2081.obj_obj_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension\u2081.obj_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension_obj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal_inverse_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal_inverse_obj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal\u2081_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension\u2082_comp_whiskering_left_to_karoubi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal\u2082_functor_map_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension\u2081_comp_whiskering_left_to_karoubi_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal_functor_obj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal\u2081.counit_iso_hom_app_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal\u2082_functor_obj_obj_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal\u2082_unit_iso_hom_app_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal\u2082_inverse_obj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal_functor_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal_counit_iso_hom_app_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension.category_theory.is_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension\u2082_obj_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal\u2081_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal\u2082_functor_obj_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension\u2081_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal\u2081_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal_inverse_obj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension\u2082_comp_whiskering_left_to_karoubi_iso", "description": " The natural isomorphism expressing that functors `karoubi C \u2964 karoubi D` obtained\nusing `functor_extension\u2082` actually extends the original functors `C \u2964 D`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal_functor_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal\u2081.counit_iso", "description": "The counit isomorphism of the equivalence `(C \u2964 karoubi D) \u224c (karoubi C \u2964 karoubi D)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal", "description": "The equivalence `(C \u2964 D) \u224c (karoubi C \u2964 D)` when `D` is idempotent complete.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.nat_trans_eq", "description": " A natural transformation between functors `karoubi C \u2964 D` is determined\nby its value on objects coming from `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension\u2081", "description": "The canonical functor `(C \u2964 karoubi D) \u2964 (karoubi C \u2964 karoubi D)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.obj.category_theory.is_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension\u2081_comp_whiskering_left_to_karoubi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension", "description": " The extension of functors functor `(C \u2964 D) \u2964 (karoubi C \u2964 D)`\nwhen `D` is idempotent compltete.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension\u2081_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal_counit_iso_inv_app_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension_obj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal\u2081", "description": "The equivalence of categories `(C \u2964 karoubi D) \u224c (karoubi C \u2964 karoubi D)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal\u2082_counit_iso_inv_app_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_universal\u2082_unit_iso_inv_app_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension\u2082_map_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.functor_extension\u2081.map", "description": " Extension of a natural transformation `\u03c6` between functors\n`C \u2964 karoubi D` to a natural transformation between the\nextension of these functors to `karoubi C \u2964 karoubi D`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name