 "galois_poly_separable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_field.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_field.equiv_zmod_p", "description": "A Galois field with exponent 1 is equivalent to `zmod`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_field.field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_field.is_galois", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_field.char_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_field.alg_equiv_of_card_eq", "description": "Uniqueness of finite fields:\n Any two finite fields of the same cardinality are (possibly non canonically) isomorphic", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_field.finrank", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_field.has_sub.sub.polynomial.is_splitting_field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_field.alg_equiv_galois_field", "description": "Any finite field is (possibly non canonically) isomorphic to some Galois field.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_field.splits_zmod_X_pow_sub_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_field.has_sub.sub.polynomial.is_splitting_field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_field.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_field.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_field", "description": " A finite field with `p ^ n` elements.\nEvery field with the same cardinality is (non-canonically)\nisomorphic to this field.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_field.ring_equiv_of_card_eq", "description": "Uniqueness of finite fields:\n Any two finite fields of the same cardinality are (possibly non canonically) isomorphic", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_field.splits_X_pow_card_sub_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_field.card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_field.is_splitting_field_of_card_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.has_besicovitch_covering", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.multiplicity", "description": " The maximum cardinality of a `1`-separated set in the ball of radius `2`. This is also the\noptimal number of families in the Besicovitch covering theorem.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.card_le_multiplicity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.multiplicity_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.satellite_config.center_and_rescale_center", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.satellite_config.center_and_rescale_radius", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.le_multiplicity_of_\u03b4_of_fin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.good_\u03c4", "description": " A number `\u03c4 > 1`, but chosen close enough to `1` so that the construction in the Besicovitch\ncovering theorem using this parameter `\u03c4` will give the smallest possible number of covering\nfamilies.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.card_le_multiplicity_of_\u03b4", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.exists_good_\u03b4", "description": " If `\u03b4` is small enough, a `(1-\u03b4)`-separated set in the ball of radius `2` also has cardinality\nat most `multiplicity E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.is_empty_satellite_config_multiplicity", "description": " In a normed vector space `E`, there can be no satellite configuration with `multiplicity E + 1`\npoints and the parameter `good_\u03c4 E`. This will ensure that in the inductive construction to get\nthe Besicovitch covering families, there will never be more than `multiplicity E` nonempty\nfamilies.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.satellite_config.exists_normalized_aux2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.satellite_config.exists_normalized_aux1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.satellite_config.exists_normalized", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.satellite_config.center_and_rescale", "description": " Rescaling a satellite configuration in a vector space, to put the basepoint at `0` and the base\nradius at `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.good_\u03b4_lt_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.card_le_of_separated", "description": " Any `1`-separated set in the ball of radius `2` has cardinality at most `5 ^ dim`. This is\nuseful to show that the supremum in the definition of `besicovitch.multiplicity E` is\nwell behaved.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.satellite_config.exists_normalized_aux3", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.one_lt_good_\u03c4", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "besicovitch.good_\u03b4", "description": " A small positive number such that any `1 - \u03b4`-separated set in the ball of radius `2` has\ncardinality at most `besicovitch.multiplicity E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prev_last_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cycle.fintype_nodup_cycle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prev", "description": "Given an element `x : \u03b1` of `l : list \u03b1` such that `x \u2208 l`, get the previous\nelement of `l`. This works from head to tail, (including a check for last element)\nso it will match on first hit, ignoring later duplicates.\n\n * `prev [1, 2, 3] 2 _ = 1`\n * `prev [1, 2, 3] 1 _ = 3`\n * `prev [1, 2, 3, 2, 4] 2 _ = 1`\n * `prev [1, 2, 3, 4, 2] 2 _ = 1`\n * `prev [1, 1, 2] 1 _ = 2`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.mem_of_next_or_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.next_or_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cycle.chain_iff_pairwise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cycle.mem_reverse_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.next_or", "description": "Return the `z` such that `x :: z :: _` appears in `xs`, or `default` if there is no such `z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cy