 "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cycle.chain_of_pairwise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cycle.prev_next", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cycle.nil", "description": "The unique empty cycle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.next", "description": "Given an element `x : \u03b1` of `l : list \u03b1` such that `x \u2208 l`, get the next\nelement of `l`. This works from head to tail, (including a check for last element)\nso it will match on first hit, ignoring later duplicates.\n\nFor example:\n * `next [1, 2, 3] 2 _ = 3`\n * `next [1, 2, 3] 3 _ = 1`\n * `next [1, 2, 3, 2, 4] 2 _ = 3`\n * `next [1, 2, 3, 2] 2 _ = 3`\n * `next [1, 1, 2, 3, 2] 1 _ = 1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cycle.map", "description": "The lift of `list.map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cycle.chain_range_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cycle.nontrivial.decidable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.next_reverse_eq_prev", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cycle.mem", "description": "For `x : \u03b1`, `s : cycle \u03b1`, `x \u2208 s` indicates that `x` occurs at least once in `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cycle", "description": "`cycle \u03b1` is the quotient of `list \u03b1` by cyclic permutation.\nDuplicates are allowed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cycle.prev_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cycle.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cycle.to_finset_to_multiset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cycle.nil_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.next_cons_cons_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cycle.reverse_reverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cycle.chain.nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cycle.has_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.next_or_eq_next_or_of_mem_of_ne", "description": "`next_or` does not depend on the default value, if the next value appears.", "p": "mathlib