distrib", "description": "A sequence of identically distributed L\u1d56 functions is p-uniformly integrable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ident_distrib.ae_strongly_measurable_snd", "description": "If `f` and `g` are identically distributed and `f` is a.e. strongly measurable, so is `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ident_distrib.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ident_distrib.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ident_distrib.ae_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ident_distrib.sub_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ident_distrib.of_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ident_distrib.integral_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ident_distrib.pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ident_distrib.variance_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ident_distrib.integrable_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ident_distrib.integrable_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ident_distrib.const_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ident_distrib.const_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ident_distrib.ae_strongly_measurable_fst", "description": " In a second countable topology, the first function in an identically distributed pair is a.e.\nstrongly measurable. So is the second function, but use `h.symm.ae_strongly_measurable_fst` as\n`h.ae_strongly_measurable_snd` has a different meaning.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ident_distrib.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ident_distrib.measure_preimage_eq", "description": "**Alias** of `probability_theory.ident_distrib.measure_mem_eq`.",