+ Q` (`plus P Q`) matches anything which match `P` or `Q`\n* `P * Q` (`comp P Q`) matches `x ++ y` if `x` matches `P` and `y` matches `Q`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.zero", "description": "This is the definition of regular expressions. The names used here is to mirror the definition\nof a Kleene algebra (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kleene_algebra).\n* `0` (`zero`) matches nothing\n* `1` (`epsilon`) matches only the empty string\n* `char a` matches only the string 'a'\n* `star P` matches any finite concatenation of strings which match `P`\n* `P + Q` (`plus P Q`) matches anything which match `P` or `Q`\n* `P * Q` (`comp P Q`) matches `x ++ y` if `x` matches `P` and `y` matches `Q`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.epsilon", "description": "This is the definition of regular expressions. The names used here is to mirror the definition\nof a Kleene algebra (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kleene_algebra).\n* `0` (`zero`) matches nothing\n* `1` (`epsilon`) matches only the empty string\n* `char a` matches only the string 'a'\n* `star P` matches any finite concatenation of strings which match `P`\n* `P + Q` (`plus P Q`) matches anything which match `P` or `Q`\n* `P * Q` (`comp P Q`) matches `x ++ y` if `x` matches `P` and `y` matches `Q`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.char", "description": "This is the definition of regular expressions. The names used here is to mirror the definition\nof a Kleene algebra (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kleene_algebra).\n* `0` (`zero`) matches nothing\n* `1` (`epsilon`) matches only the empty string\n* `char a` matches only the string 'a'\n* `star P` matches any finite concatenation of strings which match `P`\n* `P + Q` (`plus P Q`) matches anything which match `P` or `Q`\n* `P * Q` (`comp P Q`) matches `x ++ y` if `x` matches `P` and `y` matches `Q`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.plus", "description": "This is the definition of regular expressions. The names used here is to mirror the definition\nof a Kleene algebra (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kleene_algebra).\n* `0` (`zero`) matches nothing\n* `1` (`epsilon`) matches only the empty string\n* `char a` matches only the string 'a'\n* `star P` matches any finite concatenation of strings which match `P`\n* `P + Q` (`plus P Q`) matches anything which match `P` or `Q`\n* `P * Q` (`comp P Q`) matches `x ++ y` if `x` matches `P` and `y` matches `Q`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.comp", "description": "This is the definition of regular expressions. The names used here is to mirror the definition\nof a Kleene algebra (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kleene_algebra).\n* `0` (`zero`) matches nothing\n* `1` (`epsilon`) matches only the empty string\n* `char a` matches only the string 'a'\n* `star P` matches any finite concatenation of strings which match `P`\n* `P + Q` (`plus P Q`) matches anything which match `P` or `Q`\n* `P * Q` (`comp P Q`) matches `x ++ y` if `x` matches `P` and `y` matches `Q`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.star", "description": "This is the definition of regular expressions. The names used here is to mirror the definition\nof a Kleene algebra (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kleene_algebra).\n* `0` (`zero`) matches nothing\n* `1` (`epsilon`) matches only the empty string\n* `char a` matches only the string 'a'\n* `star P` matches any finite concatenation of strings which match `P`\n* `P + Q` (`plus P Q`) matches anything which match `P` or `Q`\n* `P * Q` (`comp P Q`) matches `x ++ y` if `x` matches `P` and `y` matches `Q`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.char_rmatch_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.plus_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.matches_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.zero_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.deriv_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.deriv", "description": "`P.deriv a` matches `x` if `P` matches `a :: x`, the Brzozowski derivative of `P` with respect\n to `a`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.one_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.matches_char", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.one_rmatch_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.rmatch", "description": "`P.rmatch x` is true if and only if `P` matches `x`. This is a computable definition equivalent\n to `matches`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.map_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.matches", "description": "`matches P` provides a language which contains all strings that `P` matches", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.matches_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.star_rmatch_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.match_epsilon", "description": "`match_epsilon P` is true if and only if `P` matches the empty string", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.deriv_char_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.matches_epsilon", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.deriv_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.deriv_char_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.zero_rmatch", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.matches_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.rmatch_iff_matches", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.deriv_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.matches_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.map_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.comp_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.deriv_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.mul_rmatch_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.matches.decidable_pred", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.nat.has_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.add_rmatch_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "regular_expression.matches_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.ae_differentiable_at", "description": " A real Lipschitz function into a finite dimensional real vector space is differentiable\nalmost everywhere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_locally_bounded_variation_on.exists_monotone_on_sub_monotone_on", "description": " If a real valued function has bounded variation on a set, then it is a difference of monotone\nfunctions there.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_bounded_variation_on.has_locally_bounded_variation_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.lower_continuous_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.union", "description": " If a set `s` is to the left of a set `t`, and both contain the boundary point `x`, then\nthe variation of `f` along `s \u222a t` is the sum of the variations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.ae_differentiable_within_at_of_mem", "description": " A real function into a finite dimensional real vector space which is Lipschitz on a set\nis differentiable almost everywhere in this set .", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.sum_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.comp_le_of_monotone_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "variation_on_from_to.eq_zero_iff_of_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_locally_bounded_variation_on", "description": " A function has locally bounded variation on a set `s` if, given any interval `[a, b]` with\nendpoints in `s`, then the function has finite variation on `s \u2229 [a, b]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone_on.has_locally_bounded_variation_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.subsingleton_Icc_of_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_locally_bounded_variation_on.ae_differentiable_within_at", "description": " A real function into a finite dimensional real vector space with bounded variation on a set\nis differentiable almost everywhere in this set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.sum_le_of_monotone_on_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "variation_on_from_to", "description": "The **signed** variation of `f` on the interval `Icc a b` intersected with the set `s`,\nsquashed to a real (therefore only really meaningful if the variation is finite)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "variation_on_from_to.nonneg_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "variation_on_from_to.nonpos_of_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.lower_semicontinuous", "description": "The map `\u03bb f, evariation_on f s` is lower semicontinuous for pointwise convergence *on `s`*.\nPointwise convergence on `s` is encoded here as uniform convergence on the family consisting of the\nsingletons of elements of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone_on.evariation_on_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "variation_on_from_to.eq_left_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.eq_of_edist_zero_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_locally_bounded_variation_on.ae_differentiable_within_at_of_mem_real", "description": " A bounded variation function into `\u211d` is differentiable almost everywhere. Superseded by\n`ae_differentiable_within_at_of_mem`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "variation_on_from_to.eq_neg_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "variation_on_from_to.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_bounded_variation_on.dist_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.eq_of_eq_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_locally_bounded_variation_on.ae_differentiable_within_at_of_mem_pi", "description": " A bounded variation function into a finite dimensional product vector space is differentiable\nalmost everywhere. Superseded by `ae_differentiable_within_at_of_mem`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.add_point", "description": " Consider a monotone function `u` parameterizing some points of a set `s`. Given `x \u2208 s`, then\none can find another monotone function `v` parameterizing the same points as `u`, with `x` added.\nIn particular, the variation of a function along `u` is bounded by its variation along `v`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.comp_has_bounded_variation_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.has_locally_bounded_variation_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on", "description": " The (extended real valued) variation of a function `f` on a set `s` inside a linear order is\nthe supremum of the sum of `edist (f (u (i+1))) (f (u i))` over all finite increasing\nsequences `u` in `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "variation_on_from_to.eq_of_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.edist_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "variation_on_from_to.sub_self_monotone_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.has_locally_bounded_variation_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "variation_on_from_to.antitone_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.sum_le_of_monotone_on_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.constant_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.comp_of_dual", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.nonempty_monotone_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with.comp_has_locally_bounded_variation_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.comp_inter_Icc_eq_of_monotone_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "variation_on_from_to.eq_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_bounded_variation_on", "description": "A function has bounded variation on a set `s` if its total variation there is finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.comp_evariation_on_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.comp_has_bounded_variation_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "variation_on_from_to.edist_zero_of_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.comp_le_of_antitone_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "variation_on_from_to.self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.lower_semicontinuous_uniform_on", "description": "The map `\u03bb f, evariation_on f s` is lower semicontinuous for uniform convergence on `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_bounded_variation_on.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.comp_has_locally_bounded_variation_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.add_le_union", "description": " The variation of a function on the union of two sets `s` and `t`, with `s` to the left of `t`,\nbounds the sum of the variations along `s` and `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.Icc_add_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_locally_bounded_variation_on.ae_differentiable_at", "description": " A real function into a finite dimensional real vector space with bounded variation\nis differentiable almost everywhere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.comp_eq_of_antitone_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "variation_on_from_to.comp_eq_of_monotone_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "variation_on_from_to.monotone_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "variation_on_from_to.eq_zero_iff_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_on_with.ae_differentiable_within_at", "description": " A real function into a finite dimensional real vector space which is Lipschitz on a set\nis differentiable almost everywhere in this set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "variation_on_from_to.eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "evariation_on.comp_eq_of_monotone_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_bounded_variation_on.sub_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_locally_bounded_variation_on.ae_differentiable_within_at_of_mem", "description": " A real function into a finite dimensional real vector space with bounded variation on a set\nis differentiable almost everywhere in this set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.lift_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes_rfl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.comap_mk_nhds_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes_iff_pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.tendsto_lift_nhds_within_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes.antisymm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.map_prod_map_mk_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.surjective_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_inseparable_iff_exists_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.specialization_monotone", "description": " A continuous function is monotone with respect to the specialization preorders on the domain and\nthe codomain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.mk_eq_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable_of_nhds_within_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable_iff_closure_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable.rfl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.mk", "description": "The natural map from a topological space to its separation quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.not_specializes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.comap_mk_nhds_set_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.image_mk_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes.prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.range_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes.mem_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.not_specializes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_specializes_iff_exists_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes_iff_forall_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable.specializes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.continuous_on_lift\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable_iff_mem_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtype_specializes_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.map_mk_nhds_within_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable.mem_closed_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.preimage_mk_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.preimage_image_mk_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.continuous_lift\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes.closure_subset", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `specializes_iff_closure_subset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable_iff_specializes_and", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable.mem_open_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specialization_preorder", "description": "Specialization forms a preorder on the topological space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.continuous_at_lift\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.is_closed_map_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_specializes_iff_exists_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inducing.inseparable_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inducing.specializes_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable.specializes'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.lift\u2082_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.continuous_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.continuous_on_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes_tfae", "description": " A collection of equivalent definitions of `x \u2933 y`. The public API is given by `iff` lemmas\nbelow.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes.mem_closure", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `specializes_iff_mem_closure`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable_setoid", "description": "A `setoid` version of `inseparable`, used to define the `separation_quotient`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes_of_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes_iff_closure_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes", "description": " `x` specializes to `y` (notation: `x \u2933 y`) if either of the following equivalent properties\nhold:\n\n* `\ud835\udcdd x \u2264 \ud835\udcdd y`; this property is used as the definition;\n* `pure x \u2264 \ud835\udcdd y`; in other words, any neighbourhood of `y` contains `x`;\n* `y \u2208 closure {x}`;\n* `closure {y} \u2286 closure {x}`;\n* for any closed set `s` we have `x \u2208 s \u2192 y \u2208 s`;\n* for any open set `s` we have `y \u2208 s \u2192 x \u2208 s`;\n* `y` is a cluster point of the filter `pure x = \ud835\udcdf {x}`.\n\nThis relation defines a `preorder` on `X`. If `X` is a T\u2080 space, then this preorder is a partial\norder. If `X` is a T\u2081 space, then this partial order is trivial : `x \u2933 y \u2194 x = y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.preimage_mk_frontier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes.pure_le_nhds", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `specializes_iff_pure`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable.of_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable.map_of_continuous_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes_of_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.continuous_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.inducing_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable_iff_forall_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes_iff_forall_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable.nhds_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.lift\u2082", "description": " Lift a map `f : X \u2192 Y \u2192 \u03b1` such that `inseparable a b \u2192 inseparable c d \u2192 f a c = f b d` to a\nmap `separation_quotient X \u2192 separation_quotient Y \u2192 \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable_iff_forall_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable", "description": " Two points `x` and `y` in a topological space are `inseparable` if any of the following\nequivalent properties hold:\n\n- `\ud835\udcdd x = \ud835\udcdd y`; we use this property as the definition;\n- for any open set `s`, `x \u2208 s \u2194 y \u2208 s`, see `inseparable_iff_open`;\n- for any closed set `s`, `x \u2208 s \u2194 y \u2208 s`, see `inseparable_iff_closed`;\n- `x \u2208 closure {y}` and `y \u2208 closure {x}`, see `inseparable_iff_mem_closure`;\n- `closure {x} = closure {y}`, see `inseparable_iff_closure_eq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.topological_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.not_inseparable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes_iff_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient", "description": " The quotient of a topological space by its `inseparable_setoid`. This quotient is guaranteed to\nbe a T\u2080 space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_basis.specializes_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.continuous_at_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.preimage_image_mk_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.lift_comp_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.tendsto_lift_nhds_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.continuous_within_at_lift\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.not_inseparable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes.nhds_le_nhds", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `specializes_iff_nhds`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtype_inseparable_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.tendsto_lift\u2082_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.map_mk_nhds_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.lift", "description": " Lift a map `f : X \u2192 \u03b1` such that `inseparable x y \u2192 f x = f y` to a map\n`separation_quotient X \u2192 \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.map_mk_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inseparable.prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes.mem_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.tendsto_lift\u2082_nhds_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.quotient_map_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.preimage_mk_interior", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.comap_mk_nhds_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.is_open_map_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes_iff_mem_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "separation_quotient.continuous_within_at_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "specializes.map_of_continuous_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03b5_app_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03b5_hom_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.unit_of_tensor_iso_unit_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03bc_naturality\u2082_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.associativity_app_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03bc_naturality\u1d63", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.unit_of_tensor_iso_unit", "description": "If `m \u2297 n \u2245 \ud835\udfd9_M`, then `F.obj m` is a left inverse of `F.obj n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03bc_inv_naturality\u2097", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equiv_of_tensor_iso_unit", "description": "If `m \u2297 n \u2245 \ud835\udfd9_M` and `n \u2297 m \u2245 \ud835\udfd9_M` (subject to some commuting constraints),\n then `F.obj m` and `F.obj n` forms a self-equivalence of `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.obj_\u03bc_inv_app_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.obj_\u03bc_app_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03b5_inv_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03bc_hom_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03b5_naturality_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03bc_hom_inv_app_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.obj_\u03b5_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.endofunctor_monoidal_category", "description": "The category of endofunctors of any category is a monoidal category,\nwith tensor product given by composition of functors\n(and horizontal composition of natural transformations).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03bc_naturality\u1d63_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.obj_\u03b5_app_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equiv_of_tensor_iso_unit_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03bc_naturality\u2097", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.tensoring_right_monoidal_to_lax_monoidal_functor_to_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03b5_inv_naturality_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.left_unitality_app_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03b5_inv_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.obj_\u03bc_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equiv_of_tensor_iso_unit_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.tensoring_right_monoidal", "description": "Tensoring on the right gives a monoidal functor from `C` into endofunctors of `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03bc_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03bc_naturality_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03bc_naturality\u2097_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03bc_inv_hom_app_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03bc_inv_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.obj_\u03bc_zero_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.obj_zero_map_\u03bc_app_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03bc_naturality\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03b5_inv_app_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.obj_\u03bc_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.obj_\u03b5_inv_app_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03bc_inv_naturality_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03bc_inv_naturality\u2097_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03bc_inv_naturality\u1d63_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03b5_inv_hom_app_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.right_unitality_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.left_unitality_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.associativity_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.tensoring_right_monoidal_to_lax_monoidal_functor_\u03bc_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.tensoring_right_monoidal_to_lax_monoidal_functor_\u03b5", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.obj_zero_map_\u03bc_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03b5_naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03b5_hom_inv_app_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.right_unitality_app_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equiv_of_tensor_iso_unit_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.obj_\u03b5_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equiv_of_tensor_iso_unit_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03bc_inv_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03bc_inv_naturality\u1d63", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.unit_of_tensor_iso_unit_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "print_sorry_in_cmd", "description": " The command\n```lean\n#print_sorry_in nm\n```\nprints all declarations that (transitively) occur in the value of declaration `nm` and depend on\n`sorry`. This command assumes that no `sorry` occurs in mathlib. To find `sorry` in mathlib, use\n``#eval print_sorry_in `nm ff`` instead.\nExample:\n```lean\ndef foo1 : false := sorry\ndef foo2 : false \u2227 false := \u27e8sorry, foo1\u27e9\ndef foo3 : false := foo2.left\ndef foo4 : true := trivial\ndef foo5 : true \u2227 false := \u27e8foo4, foo3\u27e9\n#print_sorry_in foo5\n```\nprints\n```lean\nfoo5 depends on foo3.\nfoo3 depends on foo2.\nfoo2 contains sorry and depends on foo1.\nfoo1 contains sorry.\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.command.print_sorry_in", "description": " The command\n```lean\n#print_sorry_in nm\n```\nprints all declarations that (transitively) occur in the value of declaration `nm` and depend on\n`sorry`. This command assumes that no `sorry` occurs in mathlib. To find `sorry` in mathlib, use\n``#eval print_sorry_in `nm ff`` instead.\nExample:\n```lean\ndef foo1 : false := sorry\ndef foo2 : false \u2227 false := \u27e8sorry, foo1\u27e9\ndef foo3 : false := foo2.left\ndef foo4 : true := trivial\ndef foo5 : true \u2227 false := \u27e8foo4, foo3\u27e9\n#print_sorry_in foo5\n```\nprints\n```lean\nfoo5 depends on foo3.\nfoo3 depends on foo2.\nfoo2 contains sorry and depends on foo1.\nfoo1 contains sorry.\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "print_sorry_in", "description": " Print all declarations that (transitively) occur in the value of declaration `nm` and depend on\n`sorry`. If `ignore_mathlib` is set true, then all declarations in `mathlib` are\nassumed to be `sorry`-free, which greatly reduces the search space. We could also exclude `core`,\nbut this doesn't speed up the search.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.find_all_exprs_aux", "description": " Auxiliary declaration for `tactic.find_all_exprs`.\n\nTraverse all declarations occurring in the declaration with the given name,\nexcluding declarations `n` such that `g n` is true (and all their descendants),\nrecording the structure of which declaration depends on which,\nand whether `f e` is true on any subexpression `e` of the declaration.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.find_all_exprs", "description": "`tactic.find_all_exprs env test exclude nm` searches for all declarations (transitively)\n occuring in `nm` that contain a subexpression `e` such that `test e` is true.\n All declarations `n` such that `exclude n` is true (and all their descendants) are ignored.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.find_all_expr_data", "description": "Auxiliary data type for `tactic.find_all_exprs`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.find_all_expr_data.matching_subexpr", "description": "Auxiliary data type for `tactic.find_all_exprs`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.find_all_expr_data.test_passed", "description": "Auxiliary data type for `tactic.find_all_exprs`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.find_all_expr_data.descendants", "description": "Auxiliary data type for `tactic.find_all_exprs`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.find_all_expr_data.name_map", "description": "Auxiliary data type for `tactic.find_all_exprs`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.find_all_expr_data.direct_descendants", "description": "Auxiliary data type for `tactic.find_all_exprs`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.groupoid.vertex_group_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.groupoid.vertex_group_npow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.groupoid.vertex_group_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.groupoid.vertex_group_isom_of_path", "description": "A path in the groupoid defines an isomorphism between its endpoints.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.groupoid.vertex_group_isom_of_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_vertex_group_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.groupoid.vertex_group_isom_of_map", "description": "An arrow in the groupoid defines, by conjugation, an isomorphism of groups between\nits endpoints.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.groupoid.vertex_group_isom_of_map_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.groupoid.vertex_group", "description": "The vertex group at `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_vertex_group", "description": "A functor defines a morphism of vertex group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.groupoid.vertex_group_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.groupoid.vertex_group_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.groupoid.vertex_group.inv_eq_inv", "description": "The inverse in the group is equal to the inverse given by `category_theory.inv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.groupoid.vertex_group_zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval.coe_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonempty_interval.coe_hom", "description": "Consider a nonempty interval `[a, b]` as the set `[a, b]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval.dual_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonempty_interval.is_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonempty_interval.snd_dual", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval.bot_ne_pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval.map", "description": "Pushforward of intervals.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval.coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval.lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonempty_interval.map\u2082_to_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonempty_interval.dual_pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonempty_interval.coe_ssubset_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonempty_interval.set.has_coe_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonempty_interval.preorder", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval.complete_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonempty_interval.mem_pure_self", "description":