"description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.continuous_at_arg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_eq_neg_pi_div_two_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.abs_arg_le_pi_div_two_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_mul_cos_add_sin_mul_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_of_im_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_mul_coe_angle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_eq_nhds_of_im_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.range_exp_mul_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.continuous_within_at_arg_of_re_neg_of_im_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_of_re_neg_of_im_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_neg_eq_arg_sub_pi_of_im_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.abs_mul_exp_arg_mul_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_neg_coe_angle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_mul_cos_add_sin_mul_I_coe_angle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_mul_cos_add_sin_mul_I_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.tendsto_arg_nhds_within_im_nonneg_of_re_neg_of_im_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_neg_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_lt_pi_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_cos_add_sin_mul_I_eq_to_Ioc_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_real_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_cos_add_sin_mul_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_div_coe_angle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.tendsto_arg_nhds_within_im_neg_of_re_neg_of_im_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_coe_angle_to_real_eq_arg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_eq_pi_div_two_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_eq_pi_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.range_arg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_coe_angle_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_neg_eq_arg_sub_pi_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_eq_nhds_of_re_neg_of_im_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.ext_abs_arg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_neg_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_coe_angle_eq_iff_eq_to_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_nonneg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_neg_eq_arg_add_pi_of_im_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg", "description": "`arg` returns values in the range (-\u03c0, \u03c0], such that for `x \u2260 0`,\n `sin (arg x) = x.im / x.abs` and `cos (arg x) = x.re / x.abs`,\n `arg 0` defaults to `0`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.continuous_at_arg_coe_angle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_of_real_of_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_conj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_of_re_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_neg_eq_arg_add_pi_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_of_real_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.tan_arg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_inv_coe_angle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.abs_arg_le_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_conj_coe_angle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.ext_abs_arg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.neg_pi_div_two_le_arg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_le_pi_div_two_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_eq_nhds_of_im_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_of_im_nonneg_of_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.abs_eq_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.abs_mul_cos_add_sin_mul_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_cos_add_sin_mul_I_coe_angle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.neg_pi_lt_arg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_eq_nhds_of_re_neg_of_im_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_cos_add_sin_mul_I_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_eq_arg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_eq_nhds_of_re_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.cos_arg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_neg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.arg_of_im_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.transport", "description": "Given `s : S \u03b1` for some structure `S` depending on a type `\u03b1`,\nand an equivalence `e : \u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2`,\ntry to produce an `S \u03b2`,\nby transporting data and axioms across `e` using `equiv_rw`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.tactic.transport", "description": "Given a goal `\u22a2 S \u03b2` for some type class `S`, and an equivalence `e : \u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2`.\n`transport using e` will look for a hypothesis `s : S \u03b1`,\nand attempt to close the goal by transporting `s` across the equivalence `e`.\n\n```lean\nexample {\u03b1 : Type} [ring \u03b1] {\u03b2 : Type} (e : \u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2) : ring \u03b2 :=\nby transport using e.\n```\n\nYou can specify the object to transport using `transport s using e`.\n\n`transport` works by attempting to copy each of the operations and axiom fields of `s`,\nrewriting them using `equiv_rw e` and defining a new structure using these rewritten fields.\n\nIf it fails to fill in all the new fields, `transport` will produce new subgoals.\nIt's probably best to think about which missing `simp` lemmas would have allowed `transport`\nto finish, rather than solving these goals by hand.\n(This may require looking at the implementation of `tranport` to understand its algorithm;\nthere are several examples of \"transport-by-hand\" at the end of `test/equiv_rw.lean`,\nwhich `transport` is an abstraction of.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.transport", "description": "Given a goal `\u22a2 S \u03b2` for some type class `S`, and an equivalence `e : \u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2`.\n`transport using e` will look for a hypothesis `s : S \u03b1`,\nand attempt to close the goal by transporting `s` across the equivalence `e`.\n\n```lean\nexample {\u03b1 : Type} [ring \u03b1] {\u03b2 : Type} (e : \u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2) : ring \u03b2 :=\nby transport using e.\n```\n\nYou can specify the object to transport using `transport s using e`.\n\n`transport` works by attempting to copy each of the operations and axiom fields of `s`,\nrewriting them using `equiv_rw e` and defining a new structure using these rewritten fields.\n\nIf it fails to fill in all the new fields, `transport` will produce new subgoals.\nIt's probably best to think about which missing `simp` lemmas would have allowed `transport`\nto finish, rather than solving these goals by hand.\n(This may require looking at the implementation of `tranport` to understand its algorithm;\nthere are several examples of \"transport-by-hand\" at the end of `test/equiv_rw.lean`,\nwhich `transport` is an abstraction of.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.comap_bracket_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.comap_map_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.bot_lie", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.map_bracket_le", "description": " Note that the inequality can be strict; e.g., the inclusion of an Abelian subalgebra of a\nsimple algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.has_bracket", "description": " Given a Lie module `M` over a Lie algebra `L`, the set of Lie ideals of `L` acts on the set\nof submodules of `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lie_le_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lie_eq_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lie_le_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lie_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lie_mem_lie", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.map_comap_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lie_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lie_ideal_oper_eq_linear_span'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.map_comap_bracket_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.mono_lie", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lie_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.map_bracket_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.map_comap_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.inf_lie", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.map_comap_incl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.comap_bracket_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lie_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.mono_lie_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lie_coe_mem_lie", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lie_ideal_oper_eq_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.le_comap_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lie_le_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.comap_bracket_incl_of_le", "description": " This is a very useful result; it allows us to use the fact that inclusion distributes over the\nLie bracket operation on ideals, subject to the conditions shown.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.sup_lie", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.mono_lie_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lie_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.map_bracket_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lie_ideal_oper_eq_linear_span", "description": " See also `lie_submodule.lie_ideal_oper_eq_linear_span'` and\n`lie_submodule.lie_ideal_oper_eq_tensor_map_range`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.map_comap_incl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.comap_bracket_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.comap_bracket_incl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.id_computable", "description": "A proof that the identity map on \u03b1 is computable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.inhabited_tm2_evals_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tm2_computable", "description": "A Turing machine + a proof it outputs f.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tm2_computable.to_tm2_computable_aux", "description": "A Turing machine + a proof it outputs f.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tm2_computable.outputs_fun", "description": "A Turing machine + a proof it outputs f.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.inhabited_evals_to_in_time", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.inhabited_tm2_computable_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.id_computer", "description": "A Turing machine computing the identity on \u03b1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.evals_to_in_time.refl", "description": "Reflexivity of `evals_to_in_time` in 0 steps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.fin_tm2.stmt", "description": "The type of statements (functions) corresponding to this TM.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tm2_outputs_in_time.to_tm2_outputs", "description": "The forgetful map, forgetting the upper bound on the number of steps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.fin_tm2.step", "description": "The step function corresponding to this TM.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.inhabited_tm2_outputs_in_time", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.halt_list", "description": "The final configuration corresponding to a list in the output alphabet.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.id_computable_in_poly_time", "description": "A proof that the identity map on \u03b1 is computable in polytime.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.evals_to_in_time.trans", "description": "Transitivity of `evals_to_in_time` in the sum of the numbers of steps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.inhabited_tm2_outputs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.tm2_outputs", "description": "A proof of tm outputting l' when given l.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.fin_tm2", "description": " A bundled TM2 (an equivalent of the classical Turing machine, defined starting from\nthe namespace `turing.TM2` in `turing_machine.lean`), with an input and output stack,\n a main function, an initial state and some finiteness guarantees.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.fin_tm2.K", "description": " A bundled TM2 (an equivalent of the classical Turing machine, defined starting from\nthe namespace `turing.TM2` in `turing_machine.lean`), with an input and output stack,\n a main function, an initial state and some finiteness guarantees.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "turing.fin_tm2.K_decidable_eq", "description": " A bundled TM2 (an equivalent of the classical Tu