uivalence", "description": "Whiskering by an equivalence gives an equivalence between categories of cones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.op_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cocones_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.whisker_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cocones_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.equivalence_of_reindexing", "description": "The categories of cones over `F` and `G` are equivalent if `F` and `G` are naturally isomorphic\n(possibly after changing the indexing category by an equivalence).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_of_cocone_left_op", "description": "Change a cocone on `F.left_op : J\u1d52\u1d56 \u2964 C` to a cocone on `F : J \u2964 C\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_of_cocone_unop_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.postcompose_equivalence_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.whiskering_map_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_of_cocone_left_op_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.cocones_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inhabited_cone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_left_op_of_cocone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.functoriality_map_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_morphism.w", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_morphism.w", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.precompose_whisker_left_map_cocone", "description": "For `F : J \u2964 C`, given a cocone `c : cocone F`, and a natural isomorphism `\u03b1 : H \u2245 H'` for functors\n`H H' : C \u2964 D`, the precomposition of the cocone `H.map_cocone` using the isomorphism `\u03b1` is\nisomorphic to the cocone `H'.map_cocone`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.precompose_equivalence_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_equivalence_op_cone_op_inverse_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.extend_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.equivalence_of_reindexing_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.precompose_equivalence", "description": "If `F` and `G` are naturally isomorphic functors, then they have equivalent categories of\ncocones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.precompose_whisker_left_map_cocone_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_of_cone_unop", "description": "Change a cone on `F.unop : J \u2964 C` into a cocone on `F : J\u1d52\u1d56 \u2964 C\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.ext_inv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.whiskering_equivalence_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inhabited_cocone_morphism", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.whiskering_map_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cone_postcompose_equivalence_functor_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cocone_map_cocone_inv", "description": "`map_cocone` is the left inverse to `map_cocone_inv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.postcompose_equivalence_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.whisker", "description": "Whisker a cocone by precomposition of a functor. See `whiskering` for a functorial\nversion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.postcompose_comp", "description": " Postcomposing a cone by the composite natural transformation `\u03b1 \u226b \u03b2` is the same as\npostcomposing by `\u03b1` and then by `\u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.whisker_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.cones_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.postcompose_id_hom_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.functoriality_equivalence_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.eta_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.precompose_equivalence_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.whiskering_equivalence_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cocones", "description": "Contravariantly associated to each functor `J \u2964 C`, we have the `C`-copresheaf consisting of\ncocones with a given cocone point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cocone_whisker_inv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_of_cone_right_op", "description": "Change a cone on `F.right_op : J \u2964 C\u1d52\u1d56` to a cocone on `F : J\u1d52\u1d56 \u2964 C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.whiskering_equivalence_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.functoriality", "description": "A functor `G : C \u2964 D` sends cones over `F` to cones over `F \u22d9 G` functorially.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_of_cone_right_op_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.extensions", "description": "A map from the vertex of a cocone naturally induces a cocone by composition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.postcompose_id_inv_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.precompose_obj_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.unop", "description": "Change a `cone F.op` into a `cocone F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.postcompose_equivalence_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.cones", "description": "`F.cones` is the functor assigning to an object `X` the type of\nnatural transformations from the constant functor with value `X` to `F`.\nAn object representing this functor is a limit of `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.eta_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.category_comp_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_morphism.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cones_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_equivalence_op_cone_op_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.postcompose_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone", "description": "A `c : cone F` is:\n* an object `c.X` and\n* a natural transformation `c.\u03c0 : c.X \u27f6 F` from the constant `c.X` functor to `F`.\n\n`cone F` is equivalent, via `cone.equiv` below, to `\u03a3 X, F.cones.obj X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.X", "description": "A `c : cone F` is:\n* an object `c.X` and\n* a natural transformation `c.\u03c0 : c.X \u27f6 F` from the constant `c.X` functor to `F`.\n\n`cone F` is equivalent, via `cone.equiv` below, to `\u03a3 X, F.cones.obj X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.\u03c0", "description": "A `c : cone F` is:\n* an object `c.X` and\n* a natural transformation `c.\u03c0 : c.X \u27f6 F` from the constant `c.X` functor to `F`.\n\n`cone F` is equivalent, via `cone.equiv` below, to `\u03a3 X, F.cones.obj X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.whisker_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.w", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.op", "description": "Change a `cone F` into a `cocone F.op`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.postcompose_id", "description": "Postcomposing by the identity does not change the cone up to isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cones_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cocone_precompose_equivalence_functor_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.extensions_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.unop_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_morphism.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cone_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_right_op_of_cone_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_unop_of_cocone", "description": "Change a cocone on `F : J\u1d52\u1d56 \u2964 C\u1d52\u1d56` into a cone on `F.unop : J \u2964 C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.eta", "description": "Eta rule for cocones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.extend_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_morphism.w_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.postcompose_whisker_left_map_cone_inv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.postcompose_equivalence", "description": "If `F` and `G` are naturally isomorphic functors, then they have equivalent categories of\ncones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.equiv_hom_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_morphism.w_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.extend", "description": "A map to the vertex of a cone induces a cone by composition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.cocone_iso_of_hom_iso", "description": "Given a cocone morphism whose object part is an isomorphism, produce an\nisomorphism of cocones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cone", "description": "The image of a cone in C under a functor G : C \u2964 D is a cone in D.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.functoriality_equivalence_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.precompose_id", "description": "Precomposing by the identity does not change the cocone up to isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.w_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cone_postcompose", "description": "`map_cone` commutes with `postcompose`. In particular, for `F : J \u2964 C`, given a cone `c : cone F`, a\nnatural transformation `\u03b1 : F \u27f6 G` and a functor `H : C \u2964 D`, we have two obvious ways of producing\na cone over `G \u22d9 H`, and they are both isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cocone_precompose_inv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.forget", "description": "Forget the cocone structure and obtain just the cocone point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.postcompose_whisker_left_map_cone_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.functoriality_full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.extend_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cocone_op", "description": "The opposite cone of the image of a cocone is the image of the opposite cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.functoriality_faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cocone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.precompose_map_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cone_postcompose_equivalence_functor", "description": "`map_cone` commutes with `postcompose_equivalence`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.functoriality_equivalence_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.unop_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.postcompose_obj_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cones", "description": "Functorially associated to each functor `J \u2964 C`, we have the `C`-presheaf consisting of\ncones with a given cone point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.unop_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_of_cocone_unop", "description": "Change a cocone on `F.unop : J \u2964 C` into a cone on `F : J\u1d52\u1d56 \u2964 C\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.reflects_cocone_isomorphism", "description": "If `F` reflects isomorphisms, then `cocones.functoriality F` reflects isomorphisms\nas well.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cocone_morphism", "description": " Given a cocone morphism `c \u27f6 c'`, construct a cocone morphism on the mapped cocones\nfunctorially.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.functoriality_equivalence_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.functoriality_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cocone_inv_map_cocone", "description": "`map_cocone` is the right inverse to `map_cocone_inv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.whiskering_equivalence_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_of_cone_unop_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.functoriality_full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.forget_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.whiskering_equivalence_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.precompose_whisker_left_map_cocone_inv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.precompose_equivalence_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.precompose_comp", "description": " Precomposing a cocone by the composite natural transformation `\u03b1 \u226b \u03b2` is the same as\nprecomposing by `\u03b2` and then by `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_of_cone_right_op_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_of_cone_left_op_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cocone_whisker", "description": "`map_cocone` commutes with `whisker`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.postcompose", "description": "Functorially postcompose a cone for `F` by a natural transformation `F \u27f6 G` to give a cone for `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_left_op_of_cone_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.precompose_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.category_comp_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.cones_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.functoriality_map_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.cocones", "description": "`F.cocones` is the functor assigning to an object `X` the type of\nnatural transformations from `F` to the constant functor with value `X`.\nAn object corepresenting this functor is a colimit of `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.reflects_cone_isomorphism", "description": "If `F` reflects isomorphisms, then `cones.functoriality F` reflects isomorphisms\nas well.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_of_cocone_right_op_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.whiskering_equivalence_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.w", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.forget_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.functoriality_equivalence", "description": "If `e : C \u224c D` is an equivalence of categories, then `functoriality F e.functor` induces an\nequivalence between cones over `F` and cones over `F \u22d9 e.functor`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.cocones_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_morphism", "description": " A cocone morphism between two cocones for the same diagram is a morphism of the cocone points\nwhich commutes with the cocone legs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_morphism.hom", "description": " A cocone morphism between two cocones for the same diagram is a morphism of the cocone points\nwhich commutes with the cocone legs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_morphism.w'", "description": " A cocone morphism between two cocones for the same diagram is a morphism of the cocone points\nwhich commutes with the cocone legs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cone_postcompose_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cocone_whisker_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.functoriality_obj_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.forget_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.equivalence_of_reindexing_functor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cocone_precompose_equivalence_functor_inv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.functoriality_obj_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_of_cocone_unop_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.postcompose_map_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.forget_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.ext", "description": "To give an isomorphism between cones, it suffices to give an\n isomorphism between their vertices which commutes with the cone\n maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cone_map_cone_inv", "description": "`map_cone` is the left inverse to `map_cone_inv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.equiv_inv_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.equivalence_of_reindexing_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_left_op_of_cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.functoriality_comp_precompose_inv_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.whiskering", "description": "Whiskering on the left by `E : K \u2964 J` gives a functor from `cone F` to `cone (E \u22d9 F)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cone_op", "description": "The opposite cocone of the image of a cone is the image of the opposite cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.postcompose_comp_hom_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cocone_precompose_equivalence_functor", "description": "`map_cocone` commutes with `precompose_equivalence`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.category", "description": "The category of cones on a given diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.whisker", "description": "Whisker a cone by precomposition of a functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.functoriality_comp_precompose_hom_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.equiv_hom_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inhabited_cone_morphism", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_left_op_of_cocone", "description": "Change a cocone on `F : J \u2964 C\u1d52\u1d56` to a cone on `F.left_op : J\u1d52\u1d56 \u2964 C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.eta_inv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cone_postcompose_equivalence_functor_inv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cone_inv", "description": " If `H` is an equivalence, we invert `H.map_cone` and get a cone for `F` from a cone\nfor `F \u22d9 H`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_morphism.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_of_cone_left_op", "description": "Change a cone on `F.left_op : J\u1d52\u1d56 \u2964 C` to a cocone on `F : J \u2964 C\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.ext", "description": "To give an isomorphism between cocones, it suffices to give an\n isomorphism between their vertices which commutes with the cocone\n maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.functoriality_equivalence_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_right_op_of_cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.category_id_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.postcompose_whisker_left_map_cone", "description": "For `F : J \u2964 C`, given a cone `c : cone F`, and a natural isomorphism `\u03b1 : H \u2245 H'` for functors\n`H H' : C \u2964 D`, the postcomposition of the cone `H.map_cone` using the isomorphism `\u03b1` is\nisomorphic to the cone `H'.map_cone`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cone_op_inv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.postcompose_equivalence_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.functoriality_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.op", "description": "Change a `cocone F` into a `cone F.op`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_right_op_of_cone", "description": "Change a cone on `F : J\u1d52\u1d56 \u2964 C` to a cocone on `F.right_op : J\u1d52\u1d56 \u2964 C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_equivalence_op_cone_op_inverse_map_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_right_op_of_cocone_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cone_morphism", "description": "Given a cone morphism `c \u27f6 c'`, construct a cone morphism on the mapped cones functorially.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_left_op_of_cone", "description": "Change a cone on `F : J \u2964 C\u1d52\u1d56` to a cocone on `F.left_op : J\u1d52\u1d56 \u2964 C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone", "description": "A `c : cocone F` is\n* an object `c.X` and\n* a natural transformation `c.\u03b9 : F \u27f6 c.X` from `F` to the constant `c.X` functor.\n\n`cocone F` is equivalent, via `cone.equiv` below, to `\u03a3 X, F.cocones.obj X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.X", "description": "A `c : cocone F` is\n* an object `c.X` and\n* a natural transformation `c.\u03b9 : F \u27f6 c.X` from `F` to the constant `c.X` functor.\n\n`cocone F` is equivalent, via `cone.equiv` below, to `\u03a3 X, F.cocones.obj X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.\u03b9", "description": "A `c : cocone F` is\n* an object `c.X` and\n* a natural transformation `c.\u03b9 : F \u27f6 c.X` from `F` to the constant `c.X` functor.\n\n`cocone F` is equivalent, via `cone.equiv` below, to `\u03a3 X, F.cocones.obj X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_morphism.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.unop_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.op_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.functoriality_equivalence_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.ext_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.functoriality_equivalence", "description": "If `e : C \u224c D` is an equivalence of categories, then `functoriality F e.functor` induces an\nequivalence between cocones over `F` and cocones over `F \u22d9 e.functor`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.equivalence_of_reindexing_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cone_inv_map_cone", "description": "`map_cone` is the right inverse to `map_cone_inv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_unop_of_cone_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cone_whisker_inv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_unop_of_cocone_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cocone_inv", "description": " If `H` is an equivalence, we invert `H.map_cone` and get a cone for `F` from a cone\nfor `F \u22d9 H`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.extend", "description": "A map from the vertex of a cocone induces a cocone by composition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_equivalence_op_cone_op_functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.category_id_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.extensions_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.inhabited_cocone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.w_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cocone_op_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.whiskering_equivalence", "description": "Whiskering by an equivalence gives an equivalence between categories of cones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_equivalence_op_cone_op", "description": "The category of cocones on `F`\nis equivalent to the opposite category of\nthe category of cones on the opposite of `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_unop_of_cone", "description": "Change a cone on `F : J\u1d52\u1d56 \u2964 C\u1d52\u1d56` into a cocone on `F.unop : J \u2964 C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_unop_of_cocone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cocone_op_inv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_unop_of_cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.whiskering_equivalence_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.equiv", "description": "The isomorphism between a cone on `F` and an element of the functor `F.cones`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.whiskering_equivalence_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_of_cocone_right_op_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.equiv", "description": "The isomorphism between a cocone on `F` and an element of the functor `F.cocones`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.op_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cocone_precompose_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.whiskering_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.functoriality_equivalence_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.equivalence_of_reindexing", "description": "The categories of cocones over `F` and `G` are equivalent if `F` and `G` are naturally isomorphic\n(possibly after changing the indexing category by an equivalence).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cone_postcompose_inv_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.eta", "description": "Eta rule for cones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.whiskering_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.postcompose_comp_inv_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_right_op_of_cocone", "description": "Change a cocone on `F : J\u1d52\u1d56 \u2964 C` to a cone on `F.right_op : J \u2964 C\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_equivalence_op_cone_op_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cocone", "description": "The image of a cocone in C under a functor G : C \u2964 D is a cocone in D.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone.unop", "description": "Change a `cocone F.op` into a `cone F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.functoriality_equivalence_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_right_op_of_cocone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.cone_iso_of_hom_iso", "description": "Given a cone morphism whose object part is an isomorphism, produce an\nisomorphism of cones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.forget", "description": "Forget the cone structure and obtain just the cone point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocones.ext_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cones.functoriality_faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_of_cone_left_op_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.extensions", "description": "A map to the vertex of a cone naturally induces a cone by composition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_morphism", "description": " A cone morphism between two cones for the same diagram is a morphism of the cone points which\ncommutes with the cone legs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_morphism.hom", "description": " A cone morphism between two cones for the same diagram is a morphism of the cone points which\ncommutes with the cone legs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_morphism.w'", "description": " A cone morphism between two cones for the same diagram is a morphism of the cone points which\ncommutes with the cone legs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_of_cone_unop_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_of_cocone_left_op_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_cocone_precompose", "description": "`map_cocone` commutes with `precompose`. In particular, for `F : J \u2964 C`, given a cocone\n`c : cocone F`, a natural transformation `\u03b1 : F \u27f6 G` and a functor `H : C \u2964 D`, we have two obvious\nways of producing a cocone over `G \u22d9 H`, and they are both isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone.equiv_inv_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "widget.tactic_view_action", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.tactic_view_action.out", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.tactic_view_action.filter", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.sf.of_eformat", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.tactic_view_term_goal", "description": "Component that displays the term-mode goal.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.sf.has_to_string", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.to_local_collection", "description": "Group consecutive locals according to whether they have the same type", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.show_type_component", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.view", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.tactic_render", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.mk", "description": "Make an interactive expression.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.sf.flatten", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.sf.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.action", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.action.on_mouse_enter", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.action.on_mouse_leave_all", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.action.on_click", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.action.on_tooltip_action", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.action.on_close_tooltip", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "subexpr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.tactic_view_goal", "description": "Component that displays the main (first) goal.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.filter_component", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.local_collection", "description": "A group of local constants in the context that should be rendered as one line.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.local_collection.key", "description": "A group of local constants in the context that should be rendered as one line.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.local_collection.locals", "description": "A group of local constants in the context that should be rendered as one line.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.local_collection.type", "description": "A group of local constants in the context that should be rendered as one line.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.filter_type", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.filter_type.none", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.filter_type.no_instances", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.filter_type.only_props", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.type_tooltip", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.filter_type.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.tactic_state_widget", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.local_collection.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.filter_local", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.sf.has_repr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.term_goal_widget", "description": "Widget used to display term-proof goals.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.tactic_view_component", "description": "Component that displays all goals, together with the `$n goals` message.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.sf.repr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.show_local_collection_component", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.implicit_arg_list", "description": "Render the implicit arguments for an expression in fancy, little pills.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.sf", "description": "eformat but without any of the formatting stuff like highlighting, groups etc.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.sf.tag_expr", "description": "eformat but without any of the formatting stuff like highlighting, groups etc.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.sf.compose", "description": "eformat but without any of the formatting stuff like highlighting, groups etc.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.interactive_expression.sf.of_string", "description": "eformat but without any of the formatting stuff like highlighting, groups etc.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_karoubi.inverse_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_karoubi.counit_iso_hom_app_f_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_karoubi.equivalence", "description": "The equivalence `karoubi C \u224c karoubi (karoubi C)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_karoubi.equivalence_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_karoubi.counit_iso", "description": "The counit isomorphism of the equivalence", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_karoubi.unit_iso", "description": "The unit isomorphism of the equivalence", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_karoubi.counit_iso_inv_app_f_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_karoubi.equivalence_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_karoubi.unit_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_karoubi.unit_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_karoubi.inverse_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_karoubi.inverse_obj_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_karoubi.equivalence.additive_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_karoubi.inverse", "description": "The canonical functor `karoubi (karoubi C) \u2964 karoubi C`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_karoubi.equivalence.additive_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_karoubi.inverse.category_theory.functor.additive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_karoubi.equivalence_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.idempotents.karoubi_karoubi.equivalence_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_R_or_C.re_clm_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_dimensional.is_R_or_C_to_real", "description": "An `is_R_or_C` field is finite-dimensional over `\u211d`, since it is spanned by `{1, I}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_dimensional.is_R_or_C.proper_space_submodule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_R_or_C.of_real_clm_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.of_real_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_R_or_C.conj_cle_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_dimensional.proper_is_R_or_C", "description": " A finite dimensional vector space over an `is_R_or_C` is a proper metric space.\n\nThis is not an instance because it would cause a search for `finite_dimensional ?x E` before\n`is_R_or_C ?x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "library_note.is_R_or_C instance", "description": " This instance generates a type-class problem with a metavariable `?m` that should satisfy\n`is_R_or_C ?m`. Since this can only be satisfied by `\u211d` or `\u2102`, this does not cause problems.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral.norm_integral_lt_of_norm_le_const_of_lt", "description": " If `f` is continuous on the circle `|z - c| = R`, `R > 0`, the `\u2016f z\u2016` is less than or equal to\n`C : \u211d` on this circle, and this norm is strictly less than `C` at some point `z` of the circle,\nthen `\u2016\u222e z in C(c, R), f z\u2016 < 2 * \u03c0 * R * C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral.norm_integral_le_of_norm_le_const'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_map_not_mem_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral.integral_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral.integral_const_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral.norm_two_pi_I_inv_smul_integral_le_of_norm_le_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral.integral_eq_zero_of_has_deriv_within_at'", "description": " If `f' : \u2102 \u2192 E` is a derivative of a complex differentiable function on the circle\n`metric.sphere c |R|`, then `\u222e z in C(c, R), f' z = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integrable_zero_radius", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral.integral_radius_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at_circle_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_map_ne_mem_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_map_eq_center_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral.integral_sub_inv_of_mem_ball", "description": "Integral $\\oint_{|z-c|=R} \\frac{dz}{z-w}=2\u03c0i$ whenever $|w-c|<R$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cauchy_power_series", "description": " The power series that is equal to\n$\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\oint_{|z-c|=R} \\left(\\frac{w-c}{z - c}\\right)^n \\frac{1}{z-c}f(z)\\,dz$ at\n`w - c`. The coefficients of this power series depend only on `f \u2218 circle_map c R`, and the power\nseries converges to `f w` if `f` is differentiable on the closed ball `metric.closed_ball c R` and\n`w` belongs to the corresponding open ball. For any circle integrable function `f`, this power\nseries converges to the Cauchy integral for `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral.integral_sub_inv_smul_sub_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.circle_integrable'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_map_mem_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral_def_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_two_pi_I_cauchy_power_series_integral", "description": " For any circle integrable function `f`, the power series `cauchy_power_series f c R` multiplied\nby `2\u03c0I` converges to the integral `\u222e z in C(c, R), (z - w)\u207b\u00b9 \u2022 f z` on the open disc\n`metric.ball c R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integrable.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral.integral_sub_center_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_circle_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_map_mem_sphere'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_map_zero_radius", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integrable_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integrable", "description": " We say that a function `f : \u2102 \u2192 E` is integrable on the circle with center `c` and radius `R` if\nthe function `f \u2218 circle_map c R` is integrable on `[0, 2\u03c0]`.\n\nNote that the actual function used in the definition of `circle_integral` is\n`(deriv (circle_map c R) \u03b8) \u2022 f (circle_map c R \u03b8)`. Integrability of this function is equivalent\nto integrability of `f \u2218 circle_map c R` whenever `R \u2260 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "image_circle_map_Ioc", "description": "The image of `(0, 2\u03c0]` under `circle_map c R` is the circle with center `c` and radius `|R|`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_circle_map_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integrable.out", "description": " The function we actually integrate over `[0, 2\u03c0]` in the definition of `circle_integral` is\nintegrable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_radius_cauchy_power_series", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integrable_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_map_ne_center", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_map", "description": " The exponential map $\u03b8 \u21a6 c + R e^{\u03b8i}$. The range of this map is the circle in `\u2102` with center\n`c` and radius `|R|`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cauchy_power_series_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "range_circle_map", "description": "The range of `circle_map c R` is the circle with center `c` and radius `|R|`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral.integral_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_map_mem_sphere", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_circle_map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_on_cauchy_integral", "description": " For any circle integrable function `f`, the power series `cauchy_power_series f c R`, `R > 0`,\nconverges to the Cauchy integral `(2 * \u03c0 * I : \u2102)\u207b\u00b9 \u2022 \u222e z in C(c, R), (z - w)\u207b\u00b9 \u2022 f z` on the open\ndisc `metric.ball c R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.circle_integrable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_map_sub_center", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral.integral_sub_zpow_of_ne", "description": " If `n \u2260 -1` is an integer number, then the integral of `(z - w) ^ n` over the circle equals\nzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integrable_sub_zpow_iff", "description": " The function `\u03bb z, (z - w) ^ n`, `n : \u2124`, is circle integrable on the circle with center `c` and\nradius `|R|` if and only if `R = 0` or `0 \u2264 n`, or `w` does not belong to this circle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "periodic_circle_map", "description": "`circle_map` is `2\u03c0`-periodic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_circle_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral.integral_undef", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_circle_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_cauchy_power_series_integral", "description": " For any circle integrable function `f`, the power series `cauchy_power_series f c R`, `R > 0`,\nconverges to the Cauchy integral `(2 * \u03c0 * I : \u2102)\u207b\u00b9 \u2022 \u222e z in C(c, R), (z - w)\u207b\u00b9 \u2022 f z` on the open\ndisc `metric.ball c R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral.integral_eq_zero_of_has_deriv_within_at", "description": " If `f' : \u2102 \u2192 E` is a derivative of a complex differentiable function on the circle\n`metric.sphere c R`, then `\u222e z in C(c, R), f' z = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_circle_map_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.countable.preimage_circle_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_circle_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral.integral_sub_zpow_of_undef", "description": " If `n < 0` and `|w - c| = |R|`, then `(z - w) ^ n` is not circle integrable on the circle with\ncenter `c` and radius `(|R|)`, so the integral `\u222e z in C(c, R), (z - w) ^ n` is equal to zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral", "description": "Definition for $\\oint_{|z-c|=R} f(z)\\,dz$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_circle_map_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral.integral_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integrable_sub_inv_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_cauchy_power_series_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral.norm_integral_le_of_norm_le_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integral.integral_smul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_integrable.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with_circle_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum_cauchy_power_series_eq_integral", "description": " For any circle integrable function `f`, the power series `cauchy_power_series f c R`, `R > 0`,\nconverges to the Cauchy integral `(2 * \u03c0 * I : \u2102)\u207b\u00b9 \u2022 \u222e z in C(c, R), (z - w)\u207b\u00b9 \u2022 f z` on the open\ndisc `metric.ball c R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.has_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.to_Top", "description": "The geometric realization functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.S1", "description": "The simplicial circle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.truncated.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.augmented.standard_simplex_obj_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.truncated.large_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.augmented.standard_simplex_obj_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.augmented.standard_simplex_map_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.augmented.standard_simplex_map_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.to_sSet", "description": "The functor associating the singular simplicial set to a topological space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.truncated", "description": "Truncated simplicial sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.horn_inclusion", "description": "The inclusion of the `i`-th horn of the `n`-th standard simplex into that standard simplex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.augmented.standard_simplex", "description": " The functor which sends `[n]` to the simplicial set `\u0394[n]` equipped by\nthe obvious augmentation towards the terminal object of the category of sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.large_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.boundary_inclusion", "description": "The inclusion of the boundary of the `n`-th standard simplex into that standard simplex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.truncated.has_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet_Top_adj", "description": "Geometric realization is left adjoint to the singular simplicial set construction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.augmented.standard_simplex_obj_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.truncated.has_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.augmented", "description": " The category of augmented simplicial sets, as a particular case of\naugmented simplicial objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.boundary", "description": " The boundary `\u2202\u0394[n]` of the `n`-th standard simplex consists of\nall `m`-simplices of `standard_simplex n` that are not surjective\n(when viewed as monotone function `m \u2192 n`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.to_Top_simplex", "description": "The geometric realization of the representable simplicial sets agree\n with the usual topological simplices.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.has_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.horn", "description": " `horn n i` (or `\u039b[n, i]`) is the `i`-th horn of the `n`-th standard simplex, where `i : n`.\nIt consists of all `m`-simplices `\u03b1` of `\u0394[n]`\nfor which the union of `{i}` and the range of `\u03b1` is not all of `n`\n(when viewing `\u03b1` as monotone function `m \u2192 n`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.as_order_hom", "description": " The `m`-simplices of the `n`-th standard simplex are\nthe monotone maps from `fin (m+1)` to `fin (n+1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet", "description": " The category of simplicial sets.\nThis is the category of contravariant functors from\n`simplex_category` to `Type u`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.sk", "description": "The skeleton functor on simplicial sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.standard_simplex", "description": " The `n`-th standard simplex `\u0394[n]` associated with a nonempty finite linear order `n`\nis the Yoneda embedding of `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_add_hom", "description": "`coe : \u2124 \u2192 \u03b1` as an `add_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.coe_cast_ring_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_ring_hom", "description": "`coe : \u2124 \u2192 \u03b1` as a `ring_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.has_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.to_nat_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.add_comm_group_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_nat_abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_int_cast'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.nat_mod_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_le_neg_one_or_one_le_cast_of_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.ext_int", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_nonpos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.nneg_mul_add_sq_of_abs_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_dual_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.ext_int", "description": "If two `monoid_hom`s agree on `-1` and the naturals then they are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.add_group_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.coe_nat_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.coe_int_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_strict_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_le_neg_one_of_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.commute_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_lex_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.add_group_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.of_nat_hom", "description": "Coercion `\u2115 \u2192 \u2124` as a `ring_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.int_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.eq_int_cast_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_add_hom_int", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_ite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lex.has_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_int'", "description": "If two `monoid_with_zero_hom`s agree on `-1` and the _positive_ naturals then they are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.int.subsingleton_ring_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.coe_cast_add_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_one_le_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.elim_int_cast_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lex.add_comm_group_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.coe_int", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_ring_hom_int", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_lex_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_dual_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_lt_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.ext_int", "description": "If two `monoid_with_zero_hom`s agree on `-1` and the naturals then they are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.coe_nat_succ_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.eq_int_cast'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_commute", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.ext_int", "description": " Two additive monoid homomorphisms `f`, `g` from `\u2124` to an additive monoid are equal\nif `f 1 = g 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lex.add_group_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.ext_mint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.has_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_of_tendsto_ennreal", "description": "A sequential limit of measurable `\u211d\u22650\u221e` valued functions is measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_of_tendsto_nnreal", "description": "A sequential limit of measurable `\u211d\u22650` valued functions is measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_of_tendsto_nnreal'", "description": "A limit (over a general filter) of measurable `\u211d\u22650` valued functions is measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_limit_of_tendsto_metrizable_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_of_tendsto_metrizable", "description": " A sequential limit of measurable functions valued in a (pseudo) metrizable space is\nmeasurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_measurable_of_tendsto_metrizable_ae'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_of_tendsto_metrizable'", "description": " A limit (over a general filter) of measurable functions valued in a (pseudo) metrizable space is\nmeasurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_measurable_of_unif_approx", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_of_tendsto_metrizable_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_of_tendsto_ennreal'", "description": "A limit (over a general filter) of measurable `\u211d\u22650\u221e` valued functions is measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_measurable_of_tendsto_metrizable_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.to_jordan_decomposition_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.subset_positive_null_set", "description": "A subset `v` of a null-set `w` has zero measure if `w` is a subset of a positive set `u`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.neg_pos_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.of_diff_eq_zero_of_symm_diff_eq_zero_negative", "description": " If the symmetric difference of two negative sets is a null-set, then so are the differences\nbetween the two sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.to_signed_measure_to_jordan_decomposition", "description": " **The Jordan decomposition theorem**: Given a signed measure `s`, there exists a pair of\nmutually singular measures `\u03bc` and `\u03bd` such that `s = \u03bc - \u03bd`. In this case, the measures `\u03bc`\nand `\u03bd` are given by `s.to_jordan_decomposition.pos_part` and\n`s.to_jordan_decomposition.neg_part` respectively.\n\nNote that we use `measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.to_signed_measure` to represent the\nsigned measure corresponding to\n`s.to_jordan_decomposition.pos_part - s.to_jordan_decomposition.neg_part`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.real_smul_neg_part_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.to_jordan_decomposition_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.total_variation", "description": "The total variation of a signed measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.to_jordan_decomposition_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.of_diff_eq_zero_of_symm_diff_eq_zero_positive", "description": " If the symmetric difference of two positive sets is a null-set, then so are the differences\nbetween the two sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.real_smul_pos_part_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition", "description": " A Jordan decomposition of a measurable space is a pair of mutually singular,\nfinite measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.pos_part", "description": " A Jordan decomposition of a measurable space is a pair of mutually singular,\nfinite measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.neg_part", "description": " A Jordan decomposition of a measurable space is a pair of mutually singular,\nfinite measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.pos_part_finite", "description": " A Jordan decomposition of a measurable space is a pair of mutually singular,\nfinite measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.neg_part_finite", "description": " A Jordan decomposition of a measurable space is a pair of mutually singular,\nfinite measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.mutually_singular", "description": " A Jordan decomposition of a measurable space is a pair of mutually singular,\nfinite measures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.has_involutive_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.to_signed_measure", "description": "The signed measure associated with a Jordan decomposition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.mutually_singular_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.to_jordan_decomposition", "description": " Given a signed measure `s`, `s.to_jordan_decomposition` is the Jordan decomposition `j`,\nsuch that `s = j.to_signed_measure`. This property is known as the Jordan decomposition\ntheorem, and is shown by\n`measure_theory.signed_measure.to_signed_measure_to_jordan_decomposition`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.exists_compl_positive_negative", "description": "A Jordan decomposition provides a Hahn decomposition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.subset_negative_null_set", "description": "A subset `v` of a null-set `w` has zero measure if `w` is a subset of a negative set `u`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.to_jordan_decomposition_equiv", "description": " `measure_theory.signed_measure.to_jordan_decomposition` and\n`measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.to_signed_measure` form a `equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.to_signed_measure_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.total_variation_mutually_singular_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.to_jordan_decomposition_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.total_variation_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.to_signed_measure_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.to_signed_measure_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.to_jordan_decomposition_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.of_inter_eq_of_symm_diff_eq_zero_positive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.real_smul_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.total_variation_absolutely_continuous_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.to_jordan_decomposition_smul_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.smul_pos_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.to_signed_measure_injective", "description": "The Jordan decomposition of a signed measure is unique.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.mutually_singular_ennreal_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.to_jordan_decomposition_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.real_smul_pos_part_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.real_smul_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.to_jordan_decomposition_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.absolutely_continuous_ennreal_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.smul_neg_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.of_inter_eq_of_symm_diff_eq_zero_negative", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.to_jordan_decomposition_to_signed_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.zero_neg_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.total_variation_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.real_smul_neg_part_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.real_smul_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.zero_pos_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.neg_neg_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.coe_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.jordan_decomposition.has_smul_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.signed_measure.null_of_total_variation_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.augmented.standard_simplex.shift_fun", "description": " When `[has_zero X]`, the shift of a map `f : fin n \u2192 X`\nis a map `fin (n+1) \u2192 X` which sends `0` to `0` and `i.succ` to `f i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.arrow.augmented_cech_nerve.extra_degeneracy", "description": "The augmented \u010cech nerve associated to a split epimorphism has an extra degeneracy.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.augmented.standard_simplex.shift", "description": " The shift of a morphism `f : [n] \u2192 \u0394` in `simplex_category` corresponds to\nthe monotone map which sends `0` to `0` and `i.succ` to `f.to_order_hom i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.arrow.augmented_cech_nerve.extra_degeneracy.s_comp_\u03c0_0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.augmented.extra_degeneracy.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.augmented.extra_degeneracy.s\u2080_comp_\u03b4\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.augmented.extra_degeneracy.s'_comp_\u03b5", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.augmented.extra_degeneracy.map", "description": " If `ed` is an extra degeneracy for `X : simplicial_object.augmented C` and\n`F : C \u2964 D` is a functor, then `ed.map F` is an extra degeneracy for the\naugmented simplical object in `D` obtained by applying `F` to `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.augmented.extra_degeneracy.s_comp_\u03b4\u2080_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.augmented.extra_degeneracy", "description": " The datum of an extra degeneracy is a technical condition on\naugmented simplicial objects. The morphisms `s'` and `s n` of the\nstructure formally behave like extra degeneracies `\u03c3 (-1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.augmented.extra_degeneracy.s'", "description": " The datum of an extra degeneracy is a technical condition on\naugmented simplicial objects. The morphisms `s'` and `s n` of the\nstructure formally behave like extra degeneracies `\u03c3 (-1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.augmented.extra_degeneracy.s", "description": " The datum of an extra degeneracy is a technical condition on\naugmented simplicial objects. The morphisms `s'` and `s n` of the\nstructure formally behave like extra degeneracies `\u03c3 (-1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.augmented.extra_degeneracy.s'_comp_\u03b5'", "description": " The datum of an extra degeneracy is a technical condition on\naugmented simplicial objects. The morphisms `s'` and `s n` of the\nstructure formally behave like extra degeneracies `\u03c3 (-1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.augmented.extra_degeneracy.s\u2080_comp_\u03b4\u2081'", "description": " The datum of an extra degeneracy is a technical condition on\naugmented simplicial objects. The morphisms `s'` and `s n` of the\nstructure formally behave like extra degeneracies `\u03c3 (-1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.augmented.extra_degeneracy.s_comp_\u03b4\u2080'", "description": " The datum of an extra degeneracy is a technical condition on\naugmented simplicial objects. The morphisms `s'` and `s n` of the\nstructure formally behave like extra degeneracies `\u03c3 (-1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.augmented.extra_degeneracy.s_comp_\u03b4'", "description": " The datum of an extra degeneracy is a technical condition on\naugmented simplicial objects. The morphisms `s'` and `s n` of the\nstructure formally behave like extra degeneracies `\u03c3 (-1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.augmented.extra_degeneracy.s_comp_\u03c3'", "description": " The datum of an extra degeneracy is a technical condition on\naugmented simplicial objects. The morphisms `s'` and `s n` of the\nstructure formally behave like extra degeneracies `\u03c3 (-1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.augmented.extra_degeneracy.s'_comp_\u03b5_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.augmented.extra_degeneracy.s\u2080_comp_\u03b4\u2081_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simplicial_object.augmented.extra_degeneracy.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.augmented.standard_simplex.shift_fun_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sSet.augmented.standard_simplex.shift_fun_0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.arrow.augmented_cech_nerve.extra_degeneracy.s_comp_\u03c0_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name"