": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.cond_distrib_ae_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measurable_cond_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.condexp_ae_eq_integral_cond_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.integral_cond_distrib_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ae_strongly_measurable_comp_snd_map_prod_mk_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_distrib.is_markov_kernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.integrable_comp_snd_map_prod_mk_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.integral_cond_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.norm_integral_cond_distrib_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.condexp_prod_ae_eq_integral_cond_distrib'", "description": " The conditional expectation of a function `f` of the product `(X, Y)` is almost everywhere equal\nto the integral of `y \u21a6 f(X, y)` against the `cond_distrib` kernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.ae_integrable_cond_distrib_map_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.comp_snd_map_prod_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.norm_integral_cond_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.integrable_to_real_cond_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_distrib", "description": " **Regular conditional probability distribution**: kernel associated with the conditional\nexpectation of `Y` given `X`.\nFor almost all `a`, `cond_distrib Y X \u03bc` evaluated at `X a` and a measurable set `s` is equal to\nthe conditional expectation `\u03bc\u27e6Y \u207b\u00b9' s | m\u03b2.comap X\u27e7 a`. It also satisfies the equality\n`\u03bc[(\u03bb a, f (X a, Y a)) | m\u03b2.comap X] =\u1d50[\u03bc] \u03bb a, \u222b y, f (X a, y) \u2202(cond_distrib Y X \u03bc (X a))` for\nall integrable functions `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.set_lintegral_cond_distrib_of_measurable_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.cond_distrib_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.set_lintegral_preimage_cond_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ae_strongly_measurable'_integral_cond_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cond_distrib_ae_eq_condexp", "description": " For almost every `a : \u03b1`, the `cond_distrib Y X \u03bc` kernel applied to `X a` and a measurable set\n`s` is equal to the conditional expectation of the indicator of `Y \u207b\u00b9' s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.condexp_prod_ae_eq_integral_cond_distrib", "description": " The conditional expectation of a function `f` of the product `(X, Y)` is almost everywhere equal\nto the integral of `y \u21a6 f(X, y)` against the `cond_distrib` kernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.comp_snd_map_prod_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.condexp_prod_ae_eq_integral_cond_distrib\u2080", "description": " The conditional expectation of a function `f` of the product `(X, Y)` is almost everywhere equal\nto the integral of `y \u21a6 f(X, y)` against the `cond_distrib` kernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.integral_norm_cond_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.integral_cond_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable.integral_cond_distrib_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.integral_norm_cond_distrib_map", "description": "", "p": 