tion": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.traversable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bicompl.bitraverse", "description": "The bitraverse function for `bicompl`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.bitraversable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.bitraverse", "description": "The bitraverse function for `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flip.bitraverse", "description": "The bitraverse function for `flip`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.bitraversable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "const.bitraverse", "description": "The bitraverse function for `const`. It throws away the second map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.bicompl.bitraversable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bitraversable.is_lawful_traversable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_lawful_bitraversable.flip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.is_lawful_bitraversable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.is_lawful_bitraversable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.bitraverse", "description": "The bitraverse function for `\u03b1 \u2295 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bicompr.bitraverse", "description": "The bitraverse function for `bicompr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.bicompr.bitraversable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.bicompr.is_lawful_bitraversable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.bicompl.is_lawful_bitraversable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_lawful_bitraversable.const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dite_dite_distrib_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Prop.forall", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dite_ite_distrib_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dite_dite_distrib_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ite_ite_distrib_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "heq.eq", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `heq_iff_eq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ite_dite_distrib_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq.heq", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `heq_iff_eq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ite_dite_distrib_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq.trans_ne", "description": "**Alias** of `ne_of_eq_of_ne`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Prop.exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ite_ite_distrib_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dite_ite_distrib_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne.trans_eq", "description": "**Alias** of `ne_of_ne_of_eq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.closed_unit", "description": " Auxiliary definition for `category_theory.monoidal_closed.functor_closed`.\nThe unit for the adjunction `(tensor_left F) \u22a3 (ihom F)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.monoidal_closed_closed'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.closed_ihom", "description": " Auxiliary definition for `category_theory.monoidal_closed.functor_closed`.\nThe internal hom functor `F \u27f6[C] -`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.ihom_ev_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.closed_counit", "description": " Auxiliary definition for `category_theory.monoidal_closed.functor_closed`.\nThe counit for the adjunction `(tensor_left F) \u22a3 (ihom F)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.closed_is_adj_adj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.monoidal_closed", "description": " If `C` is a monoidal closed category and `D` is groupoid, then the functor category `D \u2964 C`,\nwith the pointwise monoidal structure, is monoidal closed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.closed_counit_app_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.closed", "description": " If `C` is a monoidal closed category and `D` is groupoid, then every functor `F : D \u2964 C` is\nclosed in the functor category `F : D \u2964 C` with the pointwise monoidal structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.closed_ihom_obj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.closed_unit_app_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.ihom_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.closed_ihom_obj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.ihom_coev_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.closed_is_adj_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.closed_ihom_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable_on.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable_on_of_locally_integrable_restrict", "description": " If `f` is locally integrable with respect to `\u03bc.restrict s`, it is locally integrable on `s`.\n(See `locally_integrable_on_iff_locally_integrable_restrict` for an iff statement when `s` is\nclosed.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.mul_continuous_on_of_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable_on.integrable_on_is_compact", "description": "If a function is locally integrable on a compact set, then it is integrable on that set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.integrable_on_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.integrable_on_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable_on_iff", "description": " If `s` is either open, or closed, then `f` is locally integrable on `s` iff it is integrable on\nevery compact subset contained in `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.continuous_on_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable_map_homeomorph", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable.integrable_on_is_compact", "description": "If a function is locally integrable, then it is integrable on any compact set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.locally_integrable_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable_on", "description": " A function `f : X \u2192 E` is *locally integrable on s*, for `s \u2286 X`, if for every `x \u2208 s` there is\na neighbourhood of `x` within `s` on which `f` is integrable. (Note this is, in general, strictly\nweaker than local integrability with respect to `\u03bc.restrict s`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable_on.mul_continuous_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.locally_integrable_on", "description": " A function `f` continuous on a set `K` is locally integrable on this set with respect\nto any locally finite measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.locally_integrable", "description": "A continuous function `f` is locally integrable with respect to any locally finite measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable", "description": " A function `f : X \u2192 E` is *locally integrable* if it is integrable on a neighborhood of every\npoint. In particular, it is integrable on all compact sets,\nsee `locally_integrable.integrable_on_is_compact`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone.locally_integrable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone_on.integrable_on_of_measure_ne_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable_on.smul_continuous_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.integrable_on_compact", "description": " A function `f` continuous on a compact set `K` is integrable on this set with respect to any\nlocally finite measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone_on.integrable_on_is_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable_on.ae_strongly_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antione_on.integrable_on_is_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable_on.continuous_on_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.smul_continuous_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.locally_integrable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable_on.norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable.locally_integrable_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.continuous_on_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.integrable_of_has_compact_support", "description": "A continuous function with compact support is integrable on the whole space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.continuous_on_mul_of_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.integrable_on_uIcc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable.indicator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable_on_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.integrable_on_uIoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable_on.integrable_on_compact_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable_on.continuous_on_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on.mul_continuous_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable.ae_strongly_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.integrable_on_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable.integrable_on_nhds_is_compact", "description": " If a function is locally integrable, then it is integrable on an open neighborhood of any\ncompact set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.integrable_on_uIcc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable_on_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.locally_integrable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone_on.integrable_on_of_measure_ne_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.locally_integrable_on_iff_locally_integrable_restrict", "description": " If `s` is closed, being locally integrable on `s` wrt `\u03bc` is equivalent to being locally\nintegrable with respect to `\u03bc.restrict s`. For the one-way implication without assuming `s` closed,\nsee `locally_integrable_on_of_locally_integrable_restrict`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.max_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.ordered_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.distrib_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.ordered_cancel_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.division_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.linear_ordered_comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.ordered_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.has_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.ordered_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.ordered_add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.strict_ordered_comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.ordered_cancel_add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.strict_ordered_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.coe_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.const_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.const_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.strict_ordered_comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.const_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.ordered_comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.has_le.le.is_total", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.has_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.linear_order", "description": "If `\u03c6` is an ultrafilter then the ultraproduct is a linear order.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.const_lt_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.linear_ordered_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.division_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.ordered_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.const_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.semilattice_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.linear_ordered_field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.ordered_comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.abs_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.const_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.linear_ordered_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.strict_ordered_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.semifield", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.lt_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.const_abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.semilattice_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.ordered_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.coe_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.min_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.germ.linear_ordered_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linter.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "Linter that checks whether `has_coe_to_fun` instances comply with Note [function coercion].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "check_reducible_non_instances", "description": "Checks whether an instance contains a semireducible non-instance with a class as\ntype in its value. We add some restrictions to get not too many false positives:\n* We only consider classes with an `add` or `mul` field, since those classes are most likely to\n  occur as a field to another class, and be an extension of another class.\n* We only consider instances of type-valued classes and non-instances that are definitions.\n* We currently ignore declarations `foo` that have a `foo._main` declaration. We could look inside,\nor at the generated equation lemmas, but it's unlikely that there are many problematic instances\ndefined using the equation compiler.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linter.incorrect_type_class_argument", "description": "A linter object for `incorrect_type_class_argument`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "print_arguments", "description": " Pretty prints a list of arguments of a declaration. Assumes `l` is a list of argument positions\nand binders (or any other element that can be pretty printed).\n`l` can be obtained e.g. by applying `list.indexes_values` to a list obtained by\n`get_pi_binders`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linter.impossible_instance", "description": "A linter object for `impossible_instance`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "find_nondep", "description": "Finds all hypotheses that don't occur in the target or other hypotheses.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linter.fails_quickly", "description": "A linter object for `fails_quickly`.\nWe currently set the number of steps in the type-class search pretty high.\nSome instances take quite some time to fail, and we seem to run against the caching issue in\nhttps://leanprover.zulipchat.com/#narrow/stream/113488-general/topic/odd.20repeated.20type.20class.20search", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "library_note.lower instance priority", "description": "Certain instances always apply during type-class resolution. For example, the instance\n`add_comm_group.to_add_group {\u03b1} [add_comm_group \u03b1] : add_group \u03b1` applies to all type-class\nresolution problems of the form `add_group _`, and type-class inference will then do an\nexhaustive search to find a commutative group. These instances take a long time to fail.\nOther instances will only apply if the goal has a certain shape. For example\n`int.add_group : add_group \u2124` or\n`add_group.prod {\u03b1 \u03b2} [add_group \u03b1] [add_group \u03b2] : add_group (\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2)`. Usually these instances\nwill fail quickly, and when they apply, they are almost always the desired instance.\nFor this reason, we want the instances of the second type (that only apply in specific cases) to\nalways have higher priority than the instances of the first type (that always apply).\nSee also #1561.\n\nTherefore, if we create an instance that always applies, we set the priority of these instances to\n100 (or something similar, which is below the default value of 1000).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "find_nondep_aux", "description": "Auxilliary definition for `find_nondep`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linter.class_structure", "description": "A linter object for `class_structure`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linter.fintype_finite", "description": "A linter object for `fintype` vs `finite`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linter.check_reducibility", "description": "A linter that checks whether an instance contains a semireducible non-instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linter.has_coe_variable", "description": "A linter object for `has_coe_variable`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linter.has_nonempty_instance", "description": "A linter for missing `nonempty` instances.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linter.fintype_finite_fun", "description": " Checks whether a declaration is `Prop`-valued and takes a `fintype _`\nhypothesis that is unused elsewhere in the type.\nIn this case, that hypothesis can be replaced with `casesI nonempty_fintype _` in the proof.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linter.decidable_classical", "description": "A linter object for `decidable_classical`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linter.instance_priority", "description": " A linter object for checking instance priorities of instances that always apply.\nThis is in the default linter set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fails_quickly", "description": "Tests whether type-class inference search will end quickly on certain unsolvable\ntype-class problems. This is to detect loops or very slow searches, which are problematic\n(recall that normal type-class search often creates unsolvable subproblems, which have to fail\nquickly for type-class inference to perform well.\nWe create these type-class problems by taking an instance, and removing the last hypothesis that\ndoesn't appear in the goal (or a later hypothesis). Note: this argument is necessarily an\ninstance-implicit argument if it passes the `linter.incorrect_type_class_argument`.\nThis tactic succeeds if `mk_instance` succeeds quickly or fails quickly with the error\nmessage that it cannot find an instance. It fails if the tactic takes too long, or if any other\nerror message is raised (usually a maximum depth in the search).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linter.inhabited_nonempty", "description": "A linter object for `inhabited_nonempty`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linter.dangerous_instance", "description": "A linter object for `dangerous_instance`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "library_note.implicit instance arguments", "description": "There are places where typeclass arguments are specified with implicit `{}` brackets instead of\nthe usual `[]` brackets. This is done when the instances can be inferred because they are implicit\narguments to the type of one of the other arguments. When they can be inferred from these other\narguments,  it is faster to use this method than to use type class inference.\n\nFor example, when writing lemmas about `(f : \u03b1 \u2192+* \u03b2)`, it is faster to specify the fact that `\u03b1`\nand `\u03b2` are `semiring`s as `{r\u03b1 : semiring \u03b1} {r\u03b2 : semiring \u03b2}` rather than the usual\n`[semiring \u03b1] [semiring \u03b2]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p_zero_or_prime_power", "description": "In a local ring the characteristics is either zero or a prime power.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_div_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_within_const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at.const_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable.div_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at.mul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at.smul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at_mul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_mul_const_field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at.mul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.const_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at.const_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at_filter.const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.div_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_within_clm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_within_const_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.smul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.clm_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_within_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_within_smul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_within_div_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_at.div_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at.smul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_within_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_mul_const_field'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.mul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_const_mul_field'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at.clm_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at.clm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_on.div_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_within_clm_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_smul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.clm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_within_at.div_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_mul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at.clm_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_const_mul_field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at.const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at.div_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_clm_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_within_mul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at.clm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_clm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "deriv_const_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at.const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at.div_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.is_separable_contraction", "description": " A separable contraction of a polynomial `f` is a separable polynomial `g` such that\n`g(x^(q^m)) = f(x)` for some `m : \u2115`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.has_separable_contraction.degree", "description": "The separable degree of a polynomial is the degree of a given separable contraction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "irreducible.has_separable_contraction", "description": " Every irreducible polynomial can be contracted to a separable polynomial.\nhttps://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09H0", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.is_separable_contraction.dvd_degree'", "description": "The separable degree divides the degree, in function of the exponential characteristic of F.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.has_separable_contraction", "description": "The condition of having a separable contration.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.contraction_degree_eq_or_insep", "description": " If two expansions (along the positive characteristic) of two separable polynomials `g` and `g'`\nagree, then they have the same degree.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.has_separable_contraction.dvd_degree'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.has_separable_contraction.eq_degree", "description": "In exponential characteristic one, the separable degree equals the degree.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.has_separable_contraction.dvd_degree", "description": "The separable degree divides the degree.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.is_separable_contraction.degree_eq", "description": "The separable degree equals the degree of any separable contraction, i.e., it is unique.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.has_separable_contraction.contraction", "description": "A choice of a separable contraction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like.congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like.subsingleton_cod", "description": "This is not an instance to avoid slowing down every single `subsingleton` typeclass search.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like.coe_fn_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like.coe_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like.congr_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like.coe_eq_coe_fn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like.exists_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like.congr_arg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like.ext'_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like.ext'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like", "description": " The class `fun_like F \u03b1 \u03b2` expresses that terms of type `F` have an\ninjective coercion to functions from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2`.\n\nThis typeclass is used in the definition of the homomorphism typeclasses,\nsuch as `zero_hom_class`, `mul_hom_class`, `monoid_hom_class`, ....", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like.coe", "description": " The class `fun_like F \u03b1 \u03b2` expresses that terms of type `F` have an\ninjective coercion to functions from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2`.\n\nThis typeclass is used in the definition of the homomorphism typeclasses,\nsuch as `zero_hom_class`, `mul_hom_class`, `monoid_hom_class`, ....", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like.coe_injective'", "description": " The class `fun_like F \u03b1 \u03b2` expresses that terms of type `F` have an\ninjective coercion to functions from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2`.\n\nThis typeclass is used in the definition of the homomorphism typeclasses,\nsuch as `zero_hom_class`, `mul_hom_class`, `monoid_hom_class`, ....", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like.ne_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.lift_hom_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.pure_coherence", "description": "`pure_coherence` uses the coherence theorem for monoidal categories to prove the goal.\nIt can prove any equality made up only of associators, unitors, and identities.\n```lean\nexample {C : Type} [category C] [monoidal_category C] :\n  (\u03bb_ (\ud835\udfd9_ C)).hom = (\u03c1_ (\ud835\udfd9_ C)).hom :=\nby pure_coherence\n```\n\nUsers will typicall just use the `coherence` tactic, which can also cope with identities of the form\n`a \u226b f \u226b b \u226b g \u226b c = a' \u226b f \u226b b' \u226b g \u226b c'`\nwhere `a = a'`, `b = b'`, and `c = c'` can be proved using `pure_coherence`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.coherence.insert_id_rhs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.lift_hom_left_unitor_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.lift_hom", "description": "A typeclass carrying a choice of lift of a morphism from `C` to `free_monoidal_category C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.lift_hom.lift", "description": "A typeclass carrying a choice of lift of a morphism from `C` to `free_monoidal_category C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.monoidal_coherence", "description": "Coherence tactic for monoidal categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.tensor_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.coherence", "description": "Use the coherence theorem for monoidal categories to solve equations in a monoidal equation,\nwhere the two sides only differ by replacing strings of monoidal structural morphisms\n(that is, associators, unitors, and identities)\nwith different strings of structural morphisms with the same source and target.\n\nThat is, `coherence` can handle goals of the form\n`a \u226b f \u226b b \u226b g \u226b c = a' \u226b f \u226b b' \u226b g \u226b c'`\nwhere `a = a'`, `b = b'`, and `c = c'` can be proved using `pure_coherence`.\n\n(If you have very large equations on which `coherence` is unexpectedly failing,\nyou may need to increase the typeclass search depth,\nusing e.g. `set_option class.instance_max_depth 500`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.right_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.pure_coherence", "description": "`pure_coherence` uses the coherence theorem for monoidal categories to prove the goal.\nIt can prove any equality made up only of associators, unitors, and identities.\n```lean\nexample {C : Type} [category C] [monoidal_category C] :\n  (\u03bb_ (\ud835\udfd9_ C)).hom = (\u03c1_ (\ud835\udfd9_ C)).hom :=\nby pure_coherence\n```\n\nUsers will typicall just use the `coherence` tactic, which can also cope with identities of the form\n`a \u226b f \u226b b \u226b g \u226b c = a' \u226b f \u226b b' \u226b g \u226b c'`\nwhere `a = a'`, `b = b'`, and `c = c'` can be proved using `pure_coherence`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.coherence", "description": "Use the coherence theorem for monoidal categories to solve equations in a monoidal equation,\nwhere the two sides only differ by replacing strings of monoidal structural morphisms\n(that is, associators, unitors, and identities)\nwith different strings of structural morphisms with the same source and target.\n\nThat is, `coherence` can handle goals of the form\n`a \u226b f \u226b b \u226b g \u226b c = a' \u226b f \u226b b' \u226b g \u226b c'`\nwhere `a = a'`, `b = b'`, and `c = c'` can be proved using `pure_coherence`.\n\n(If you have very large equations on which `coherence` is unexpectedly failing,\nyou may need to increase the typeclass search depth,\nusing e.g. `set_option class.instance_max_depth 500`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence", "description": "A typeclass carrying a choice of monoidal structural isomorphism between two objects.\nUsed by the `\u2297\u226b` monoidal composition operator, and the `coherence` tactic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.hom", "description": "A typeclass carrying a choice of monoidal structural isomorphism between two objects.\nUsed by the `\u2297\u226b` monoidal composition operator, and the `coherence` tactic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.is_iso", "description": "A typeclass carrying a choice of monoidal structural isomorphism between two objects.\nUsed by the `\u2297\u226b` monoidal composition operator, and the `coherence` tactic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.assoc'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.lift_obj", "description": "A typeclass carrying a choice of lift of an object from `C` to `free_monoidal_category C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.lift_obj.lift", "description": "A typeclass carrying a choice of lift of an object from `C` to `free_monoidal_category C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.lift_obj_tensor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.tensor_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.assoc'_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.lift_obj_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.tactic.coherence", "description": "Use the coherence theorem for monoidal categories to solve equations in a monoidal equation,\nwhere the two sides only differ by replacing strings of monoidal structural morphisms\n(that is, associators, unitors, and identities)\nwith different strings of structural morphisms with the same source and target.\n\nThat is, `coherence` can handle goals of the form\n`a \u226b f \u226b b \u226b g \u226b c = a' \u226b f \u226b b' \u226b g \u226b c'`\nwhere `a = a'`, `b = b'`, and `c = c'` can be proved using `pure_coherence`.\n\n(If you have very large equations on which `coherence` is unexpectedly failing,\nyou may need to increase the typeclass search depth,\nusing e.g. `set_option class.instance_max_depth 500`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_comp_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.lift_hom_tensor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.right'_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.assoc_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.tensor_right_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_comp", "description": " Compose two morphisms in a monoidal category,\ninserting unitors and associators between as necessary.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.lift_hom_right_unitor_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.tensor_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.lift_hom_associator_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.left_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.refl_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.lift_hom_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_iso_comp", "description": " Compose two isomorphisms in a monoidal category,\ninserting unitors and associators between as necessary.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.lift_obj_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.tensor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.tensor_right'_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.lift_hom_left_unitor_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.coherence_loop", "description": "The main part of `coherence` tactic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.coherence.insert_id_lhs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.lift_hom_associator_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.coherence.liftable_prefixes", "description": "Internal tactic used in `coherence`.\n\nRewrites an equation `f = g` as `f\u2080 \u226b f\u2081 = g\u2080 \u226b g\u2081`,\nwhere `f\u2080` and `g\u2080` are maximal prefixes of `f` and `g` (possibly after reassociating)\nwhich are \"liftable\" (i.e. expressible as compositions of unitors and associators).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_iso", "description": " Construct an isomorphism between two objects in a monoidal category\nout of unitors and associators.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.mk_project_map_expr", "description": "Auxilliary definition of `monoidal_coherence`,\nbeing careful with namespaces to avoid shadowing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.left'_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.lift_hom_right_unitor_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_category.monoidal_coherence.right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.coherence.assoc_lift_hom", "description": "Auxiliary simp lemma for the `coherence` tactic:\nthis moves brackets to the left in order to expose a maximal prefix\nbuilt out of unitors and associators.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.is_empty_of_colorable_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.coloring.mem_color_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.coloring.to_colorable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.self_coloring", "description": "The \"tautological\" coloring of a graph, using the vertices of the graph as colors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.is_clique.card_le_chromatic_number", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.coloring.color_classes_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.coloring", "description": "An `\u03b1`-coloring of a simple graph `G` is a homomorphism of `G` into the complete graph on `\u03b1`.\nThis is also known as a proper coloring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.clique_free_of_chromatic_number_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.colorable.chromatic_number_mono_of_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.chromatic_number_eq_zero_of_isempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.recolor_of_equiv", "description": "Given an equivalence, there is an induced equivalence between colorings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.colorable_chromatic_number_of_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.coloring.color_classes", "description": "The set containing all color classes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.coloring.color_classes_independent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.colorable_of_chromatic_number_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.colorable.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.coloring.color_classes_is_partition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.chromatic_number_eq_card_of_forall_surj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.colorable.mono_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.colorable.of_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.colorable_iff_exists_bdd_nat_coloring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.coloring.valid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.coloring.color_class", "description": "The color class of a given color.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.complete_bipartite_graph.bicoloring", "description": " The bicoloring of a complete bipartite graph using whether a vertex\nis on the left or on the right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.chromatic_number_le_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.colorable_of_is_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.chromatic_number_bdd_below", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.chromatic_number_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.coloring.not_adj_of_mem_color_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.recolor_of_card_le", "description": " There is a noncomputable embedding of `\u03b1`-colorings to `\u03b2`-colorings if\n`\u03b2` has at least as large a cardinality as `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.is_empty_of_chromatic_number_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.chromatic_number_top_eq_zero_of_infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.coloring.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.coloring_of_is_empty", "description": "The coloring of an empty graph.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.recolor_of_embedding", "description": "Given an embedding, there is an induced embedding of colorings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.chromatic_number_le_one_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.colorable.to_coloring", "description": "Noncomputably get a coloring from colorability.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.chromatic_number_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.complete_bipartite_graph.chromatic_number", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.colorable.clique_free", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.is_clique.card_le_of_coloring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.colorable", "description": "Whether a graph can be colored by at most `n` colors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.colorable.chromatic_number_le_of_forall_imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.coloring.mk", "description": "Construct a term of `simple_graph.coloring` using a function that\nassigns vertices to colors and a proof that it is as proper coloring.\n\n(Note: this is a definitionally the constructor for `simple_graph.hom`,\nbut with a syntactically better proper coloring hypothesis.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.coloring.mem_color_classes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.chromatic_number_le_of_colorable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.coloring.card_color_classes_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.colorable_chromatic_number", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.chromatic_number", "description": " The chromatic number of a graph is the minimal number of colors needed to color it.\nIf `G` isn't colorable with finitely many colors, this will be 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.colorable_set_nonempty_of_colorable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.chromatic_number_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.colorable_of_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.is_clique.card_le_of_colorable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.colorable.chromatic_number_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_fderiv_apply_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fderiv_measurable_aux.is_open_A", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_deriv_measurable_aux.B_mem_nhds_within_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_fderiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_set_of_differentiable_at", "description": " The set of differentiability points of a function taking values in a complete space is\nBorel-measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_set_of_differentiable_within_at_Ioi", "description": " The set of right differentiability points of a function taking values in a complete space is\nBorel-measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strongly_measurable_deriv_within_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_deriv_within_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fderiv_measurable_aux.differentiable_set_eq_D", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_deriv_measurable_aux.le_of_mem_A", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fderiv_measurable_aux.B", "description": " The set `B f K r s \u03b5` is the set of points `x` around which there exists a continuous linear map\n`L` belonging to `K` (a given set of continuous linear maps) that approximates well the\nfunction `f` (up to an error `\u03b5`), simultaneously at scales `r` and `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_deriv_measurable_aux.A_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_deriv_measurable_aux.B", "description": " The set `B f K r s \u03b5` is the set of points `x` around which there exists a vector\n`L` belonging to `K` (a given set of vectors) such that `h \u2022 L` approximates well `f (x + h)`\n(up to an error `\u03b5`), simultaneously at scales `r` and `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_deriv_within_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_set_of_differentiable_within_at_Ici", "description": " The set of right differentiability points of a function taking values in a complete space is\nBorel-measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_deriv_measurable_aux.D_subset_differentiable_set", "description": "Harder inclusion: at a point in `D f K`, the function `f` has a derivative, in `K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_measurable_deriv_within_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fderiv_measurable_aux.is_open_B", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_deriv_measurable_aux.differentiable_set_eq_D", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_strongly_measurable_deriv_within_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fderiv_measurable_aux.norm_sub_le_of_mem_A", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fderiv_measurable_aux.A_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fderiv_measurable_aux.D_subset_differentiable_set", "description": "Harder inclusion: at a point in `D f K`, the function `f` has a derivative, in `K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_deriv_measurable_aux.A_mem_nhds_within_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_measurable_deriv_within_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_deriv_measurable_aux.measurable_set_B", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_strongly_measurable_deriv_within_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_deriv_measurable_aux.differentiable_set_subset_D", "description": "Easy inclusion: a differentiability point with derivative in `K` belongs to `D f K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_deriv_measurable_aux.norm_sub_le_of_mem_A", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_deriv_measurable_aux.A", "description": " The set `A f L r \u03b5` is the set of points `x` around which the function `f` is well approximated\nat scale `r` by the linear map `h \u21a6 h \u2022 L`, up to an error `\u03b5`. We tweak the definition to\nmake sure that this is open on the right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fderiv_measurable_aux.A", "description": " The set `A f L r \u03b5` is the set of points `x` around which the function `f` is well approximated\nat scale `r` by the linear map `L`, up to an error `\u03b5`. We tweak the definition to make sure that\nthis is an open set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fderiv_measurable_aux.D", "description": " The set `D f K` is a complicated set constructed using countable intersections and unions. Its\nmain use is that, when `K` is complete, it is exactly the set of points where `f` is differentiable,\nwith a derivative in `K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_deriv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_measurable_deriv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_deriv_measurable_aux.D", "description": " The set `D f K` is a complicated set constructed using countable intersections and unions. Its\nmain use is that, when `K` is complete, it is exactly the set of points where `f` is differentiable,\nwith a derivative in `K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_strongly_measurable_deriv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_deriv_measurable_aux.mem_A_of_differentiable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_set_of_differentiable_at_of_is_complete", "description": " The set of differentiability points of a function, with derivative in a given complete set,\nis Borel-measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.measurable_apply\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_set_of_differentiable_within_at_Ici_of_is_complete", "description": " The set of right differentiability points of a function, with derivative in a given complete\nset, is Borel-measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strongly_measurable_deriv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fderiv_measurable_aux.le_of_mem_A", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strongly_measurable_deriv_within_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fderiv_measurable_aux.differentiable_set_subset_D", "description": "Easy inclusion: a differentiability point with derivative in `K` belongs to `D f K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fderiv_measurable_aux.mem_A_of_differentiable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_R_or_C.conj_tsum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.dist_conj_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.summable_of_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.has_sum_iff", "description": "",