escription": " Core of a set `s : set \u03b2` w.r.t `r : rel \u03b1 \u03b2` is the set of `x : \u03b1` that are related *only*\nto elements of `s`. Other generalization of `function.preimage`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel", "description": "A relation on `\u03b1` and `\u03b2`, aka a set-valued function, aka a partial multifunction", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.image_core_gc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.preimage_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.inv", "description": "The inverse relation : `r.inv x y \u2194 r y x`. Note that this is *not* a groupoid inverse.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.preimage_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.core_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.core_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.preimage_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.graph", "description": "The graph of a function as a relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.core_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.core_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.mem_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.image_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.preimage", "description": "Preimage of a set under a relation `r`. Same as the image of `s` under `r.inv`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_eq_core", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.dom", "description": "Domain of a relation", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.comp_left_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.image_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.preimage_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.complete_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.comp", "description": "Composition of relation; note that it follows the `category_theory/` order of arguments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.image_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.inv_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.image_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.mem_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.core_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.preimage_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.restrict_domain", "description": "Restrict the domain of a relation to a subtype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.image_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.preimage_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.core_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_rev_eq_zero_of_oangle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": " If the oriented angle between two vectors is `\u03c0 / 2`, the inner product of those vectors\n(reversed) is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_eq_pi_iff_angle_eq_pi", "description": "The oriented angle between two vectors is `\u03c0` if and only if the unoriented angle is `\u03c0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.angle_eq_abs_oangle_to_real", "description": " The unoriented angle between two nonzero vectors is the absolute value of the oriented angle,\nconverted to a real.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.eq_zero_or_oangle_eq_iff_inner_eq_zero", "description": " One of two vectors is zero or the oriented angle between them is plus or minus `\u03c0 / 2` if\nand only if the inner product of those vectors is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_sub_left_swap", "description": " Subtracting the second vector passed to `oangle` from the first vector then swapping the\nvectors does not change the sign of the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.left_ne_zero_of_oangle_eq_pi", "description": "If the angle between two vectors is `\u03c0`, the first vector is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_neg_left_eq_neg_right", "description": "Negating the first vector produces the same angle as negating the second vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.right_ne_zero_of_oangle_eq_pi", "description": "If the angle between two vectors is `\u03c0`, the second vector is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_rev_eq_zero_of_oangle_eq_neg_pi_div_two", "description": " If the oriented angle between two vectors is `-\u03c0 / 2`, the inner product of those vectors\n(reversed) is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.right_ne_zero_of_oangle_sign_eq_neg_one", "description": "If the sign of the angle between two vectors is negative, the second vector is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.left_ne_zero_of_oangle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": "If the angle between two vectors is `\u03c0 / 2`, the first vector is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.two_zsmul_oangle_neg_right", "description": "Negating the second vector passed to `oangle` does not change twice the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_sub_right_swap", "description": " Subtracting the first vector passed to `oangle` from the second vector then swapping the\nvectors does not change the sign of the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.oangle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sub_left", "description": " Given three nonzero vectors, the angle between the first and the third minus the angle\nbetween the first and the second equals the angle between the second and the third.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_neg_neg", "description": "Negating both vectors passed to `oangle` does not change the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.two_zsmul_oangle_neg_self_left", "description": "Twice the angle between the negation of a vector and that vector is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_eq_of_angle_eq_of_sign_eq", "description": " If two unoriented angles are equal, and the signs of the corresponding oriented angles are\nequal, then the oriented angles are equal (even in degenerate cases).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.eq_iff_oangle_eq_zero_of_norm_eq", "description": "Two vectors with equal norms are equal if and only if they have zero angle between them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_sub_left_eq_neg", "description": " Subtracting the first vector passed to `oangle` from the second vector negates the sign of\nthe angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_eq_zero_iff_same_ray", "description": "The oriented angle between two vectors is zero if and only if they are on the same ray.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_eq_angle_or_eq_neg_angle", "description": "The oriented angle between two nonzero vectors is plus or minus the unoriented angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_neg_self_right", "description": "The angle between a nonzero vector and its negation is `\u03c0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_add_cyc3_neg_right", "description": " Given three nonzero vectors, adding the angles between them in cyclic order, with the second\nvector in each angle negated, results in \u03c0. If the vectors add to 0, this is a version of the\nsum of the angles of a triangle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_rev", "description": "Swapping the two vectors passed to `oangle` negates the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_neg_left", "description": "Negating the first vector passed to `oangle` adds `\u03c0` to the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_add_right", "description": " Adding the first vector passed to `oangle` to the second vector does not change the sign of\nthe angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_zero_left", "description": "If the first vector passed to `oangle` is 0, the result is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_smul_right_self_of_nonneg", "description": "The angle between a vector and a nonnegative multiple of that vector is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_add_oangle_rev", "description": "Adding the angles between two vectors in each order results in 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_zero_right", "description": "If the second vector passed to `oangle` is 0, the result is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_smul_add_smul_right", "description": " The sign of the angle between a vector, and a linear combination of that vector with a second\nvector, is the sign of the factor by which the second vector is multiplied in that combination\nmultiplied by the sign of the angle between the two vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.abs_oangle_sub_right_to_real_lt_pi_div_two", "description": "A base angle of an isosceles triangle is acute, oriented vector angle form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.left_ne_zero_of_oangle_eq_neg_pi_div_two", "description": "If the angle between two vectors is `-\u03c0 / 2`, the first vector is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.two_zsmul_oangle_right_of_span_eq", "description": " If the spans of two vectors are equal, twice angles with those vectors on the right are\nequal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.two_zsmul_oangle_smul_right_of_ne_zero", "description": " Multiplying the second vector passed to `oangle` by a nonzero real does not change twice the\nangle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_eq_angle_of_sign_eq_one", "description": "The oriented angle between two vectors equals the unoriented angle if the sign is positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_add_oangle_rev_neg_left", "description": " Adding the angles between two vectors in each order, with the first vector in each angle\nnegated, results in 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_smul_right_of_pos", "description": " Multiplying the second vector passed to `oangle` by a positive real does not change the\nangle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_neg_right", "description": "Negating the second vector passed to `oangle` negates the sign of the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_smul_right_of_neg", "description": " Multiplying the second vector passed to `oangle` by a negative real produces the same angle\nas negating that vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_sub_right", "description": " Subtracting the first vector passed to `oangle` from the second vector does not change the\nsign of the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_smul_add_right", "description": " Adding a multiple of the first vector passed to `oangle` to the second vector does not change\nthe sign of the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_smul_add_right_eq_zero_or_eq_pi_iff", "description": " Auxiliary lemma for the proof of `oangle_sign_smul_add_right`; not intended to be used\noutside of that proof.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_add_cyc3", "description": "Given three nonzero vectors, adding the angles between them in cyclic order results in 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_smul_sub_right", "description": " Subtracting the second vector passed to `oangle` from a multiple of the first vector negates\nthe sign of the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_sub_right_eq_neg", "description": " Subtracting the second vector passed to `oangle` from the first vector negates the sign of\nthe angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.two_zsmul_oangle_left_of_span_eq", "description": " If the spans of two vectors are equal, twice angles with those vectors on the left are\nequal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_self", "description": "If the two vectors passed to `oangle` are the same, the result is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_eq_zero_iff_oangle_rev_eq_zero", "description": " The oriented angle between two vectors is zero if and only if the angle with the vectors\nswapped is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.cos_oangle_eq_inner_div_norm_mul_norm", "description": " The cosine of the oriented angle between two nonzero vectors is the inner product divided by\nthe product of the norms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.right_ne_zero_of_oangle_ne_zero", "description": "If the angle between two vectors is nonzero, the second vector is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.angle_eq_iff_oangle_eq_of_sign_eq", "description": " If the signs of two oriented angles between nonzero vectors are equal, the oriented angles are\nequal if and only if the unoriented angles are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_smul_sub_left", "description": " Subtracting the first vector passed to `oangle` from a multiple of the second vector negates\nthe sign of the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.two_zsmul_oangle_smul_right_self", "description": "Twice the angle between a vector and a multiple of that vector is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.two_zsmul_oangle_smul_left_self", "description": "Twice the angle between a multiple of a vector and that vector is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.ne_of_oangle_sign_ne_zero", "description": "If the sign of the angle between two vectors is nonzero, the vectors are not equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_neg_orientation_eq_neg", "description": "Negating the orientation negates the value of `oangle`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.two_zsmul_oangle_smul_smul_self", "description": "Twice the angle between two multiples of a vector is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.two_zsmul_oangle_neg_left", "description": "Negating the first vector passed to `oangle` does not change twice the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.two_zsmul_oangle_smul_left_of_ne_zero", "description": " Multiplying the first vector passed to `oangle` by a nonzero real does not change twice the\nangle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.abs_oangle_sub_left_to_real_lt_pi_div_two", "description": "A base angle of an isosceles triangle is acute, oriented vector angle form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_smul_left_of_pos", "description": " Multiplying the first vector passed to `oangle` by a positive real does not change the\nangle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_eq_neg_angle_of_sign_eq_neg_one", "description": " The oriented angle between two vectors equals minus the unoriented angle if the sign is\nnegative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_eq_pi_iff_oangle_rev_eq_pi", "description": " The oriented angle between two vectors is `\u03c0` if and only if the angle with the vectors\nswapped is `\u03c0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_eq_zero_of_oangle_eq_neg_pi_div_two", "description": " If the oriented angle between two vectors is `-\u03c0 / 2`, the inner product of those vectors\nis zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.right_ne_zero_of_oangle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": "If the angle between two vectors is `\u03c0 / 2`, the second vector is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.right_ne_zero_of_oangle_sign_ne_zero", "description": "If the sign of the angle between two vectors is nonzero, the second vector is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_neg_left", "description": "Negating the first vector passed to `oangle` negates the sign of the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_add_left", "description": " Adding the second vector passed to `oangle` to the first vector does not change the sign of\nthe angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.cos_oangle_eq_cos_angle", "description": " The cosine of the oriented angle between two nonzero vectors equals that of the unoriented\nangle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_smul_add_smul_left", "description": " The sign of the angle between a linear combination of two vectors and the second vector is\nthe sign of the factor by which the first vector is multiplied in that combination multiplied by\nthe sign of the angle between the two vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.ne_of_oangle_eq_neg_pi_div_two", "description": "If the angle between two vectors is `-\u03c0 / 2`, the vectors are not equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_smul_right", "description": " Multiplying the second vector passed to `oangle` by a real multiplies the sign of the angle by\nthe sign of the real.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_add", "description": " Given three nonzero vectors, the angle between the first and the second plus the angle\nbetween the second and the third equals the angle between the first and the third.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_neg_self_left", "description": "The angle between the negation of a nonzero vector and that vector is `\u03c0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_map_complex", "description": " The oriented angle on an oriented real inner product space of dimension 2 can be evaluated in\nterms of a complex-number representation of the space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle", "description": " The oriented angle from `x` to `y`, modulo `2 * \u03c0`. If either vector is 0, this is 0.\nSee `inner_product_geometry.angle` for the corresponding unoriented angle definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.ne_of_oangle_sign_eq_neg_one", "description": "If the sign of the angle between two vectors is negative, the vectors are not equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.ne_of_oangle_ne_zero", "description": "If the angle between two vectors is nonzero, the vectors are not equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.left_ne_zero_of_oangle_sign_eq_one", "description": "If the sign of the angle between two vectors is positive, the first vector is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_smul_left_of_neg", "description": " Multiplying the first vector passed to `oangle` by a negative real produces the same angle\nas negating that vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.eq_iff_norm_eq_of_oangle_eq_zero", "description": "Two vectors with zero angle between them are equal if and only if they have equal norms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_eq_zero_or_eq_pi_iff_not_linear_independent", "description": " The oriented angle between two vectors is zero or `\u03c0` if and only if those two vectors are\nnot linearly independent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_map", "description": " The angle between two vectors, with respect to an orientation given by `orientation.map`\nwith a linear isometric equivalence, equals the angle between those two vectors, transformed by\nthe inverse of that equivalence, with respect to the original orientation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.ne_of_oangle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": "If the angle between two vectors is `\u03c0 / 2`, the vectors are not equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.eq_iff_norm_eq_and_oangle_eq_zero", "description": "Two vectors are equal if and only if they have equal norms and zero angle between them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.left_ne_zero_of_oangle_ne_zero", "description": "If the angle between two vectors is nonzero, the first vector is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.ne_of_oangle_eq_pi", "description": "If the angle between two vectors is `\u03c0`, the vectors are not equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.ne_of_oangle_sign_eq_one", "description": "If the sign of the angle between two vectors is positive, the vectors are not equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_eq_pi_iff_same_ray_neg", "description": " The oriented angle between two vectors is `\u03c0` if and only they are nonzero and the first is\non the same ray as the negation of the second.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_sub_smul_right", "description": " Subtracting a multiple of the first vector passed to `oangle` from the second vector does\nnot change the sign of the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.continuous_at_oangle", "description": "Oriented angles are continuous when the vectors involved are nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_smul_smul_self_of_nonneg", "description": "The angle between two nonnegative multiples of the same vector is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sub_right", "description": " Given three nonzero vectors, the angle between the first and the third minus the angle\nbetween the second and the third equals the angle between the first and the second.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_ne_zero_and_ne_pi_iff_linear_independent", "description": " The oriented angle between two vectors is not zero or `\u03c0` if and only if those two vectors\nare linearly independent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_smul_add_smul_smul_add_smul", "description": " The sign of the angle between two linear combinations of two vectors is the sign of the\ndeterminant of the factors in those combinations multiplied by the sign of the angle between the\ntwo vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.right_ne_zero_of_oangle_eq_neg_pi_div_two", "description": "If the angle between two vectors is `-\u03c0 / 2`, the second vector is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_eq_zero_of_oangle_eq_pi_div_two", "description": " If the oriented angle between two vectors is `\u03c0 / 2`, the inner product of those vectors\nis zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_neg_right", "description": "Negating the second vector passed to `oangle` adds `\u03c0` to the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.right_ne_zero_of_oangle_sign_eq_one", "description": "If the sign of the angle between two vectors is positive, the second vector is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_eq_norm_mul_norm_mul_cos_oangle", "description": " The inner product of two vectors is the product of the norms and the cosine of the oriented\nangle between the vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.two_zsmul_oangle_neg_self_right", "description": "Twice the angle between a vector and its negation is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_add_smul_left", "description": " Adding a multiple of the second vector passed to `oangle` to the first vector does not change\nthe sign of the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_sub_left", "description": " Subtracting the second vector passed to `oangle` from the first vector does not change the\nsign of the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_smul_left", "description": " Multiplying the first vector passed to `oangle` by a real multiplies the sign of the angle by\nthe sign of the real.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_add_cyc3_neg_left", "description": " Given three nonzero vectors, adding the angles between them in cyclic order, with the first\nvector in each angle negated, results in \u03c0. If the vectors add to 0, this is a version of the\nsum of the angles of a triangle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.eq_zero_or_angle_eq_zero_or_pi_of_sign_oangle_eq_zero", "description": " If the sign of the oriented angle between two vectors is zero, either one of the vectors is\nzero or the unoriented angle is 0 or \u03c0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.left_ne_zero_of_oangle_sign_eq_neg_one", "description": "If the sign of the angle between two vectors is negative, the first vector is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sign_sub_smul_left", "description": " Subtracting a multiple of the second vector passed to `oangle` from the first vector does\nnot change the sign of the angle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_eq_pi_sub_two_zsmul_oangle_sub_of_norm_eq", "description": " The angle at the apex of an isosceles triangle is `\u03c0` minus twice a base angle, oriented\nvector angle form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_add_swap", "description": " Given three nonzero vectors, the angle between the second and the third plus the angle\nbetween the first and the second equals the angle between the first and the third.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.two_zsmul_oangle_of_span_eq_of_span_eq", "description": " If the spans of two pairs of vectors are equal, twice angles between those vectors are\nequal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_sub_eq_oangle_sub_rev_of_norm_eq", "description": "Pons asinorum, oriented vector angle form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_eq_zero_iff_angle_eq_zero", "description": " The oriented angle between two nonzero vectors is zero if and only if the unoriented angle\nis zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.left_ne_zero_of_oangle_sign_ne_zero", "description": "If the sign of the angle between two vectors is nonzero, the first vector is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_eq_zero_or_eq_pi_iff_right_eq_smul", "description": " The oriented angle between two vectors is zero or `\u03c0` if and only if the first vector is zero\nor the second is a multiple of the first.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_add_oangle_rev_neg_right", "description": " Adding the angles between two vectors in each order, with the second vector in each angle\nnegated, results in 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.oangle_smul_left_self_of_nonneg", "description": "The angle between a nonnegative multiple of a vector and that vector is 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "counterexample.int_with_epsilon.lt_forget_epsilons_ceil", "description": " The ceil of `n + \u03b5` is `n + 1` but its image under `forget_epsilons` is `n`, whose ceil is\nitself.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.int_with_epsilon.forget_epsilons_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.int_with_epsilon.forget_epsilons", "description": "The ordered ring homomorphisms from `\u2124[\u03b5]` to `\u2124` that \"forgets\" the `\u03b5`s.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.int_with_epsilon.linear_ordered_comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.int_with_epsilon.forget_epsilons_floor_lt", "description": " The floor of `n - \u03b5` is `n - 1` but its image under `forget_epsilons` is `n`, whose floor is\nitself.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.int_with_epsilon.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.int_with_epsilon.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.int_with_epsilon.linear_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.int_with_epsilon.floor_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.int_with_epsilon.pos_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.int_with_epsilon", "description": "The integers with infinitesimals adjoined.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.int_with_epsilon.ordered_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.int_with_epsilon.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans.sum_app_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum", "description": "`sum C D` gives the direct sum of two categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.inl__obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.inr__obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.sum_obj_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.swap_obj_in