ces. (It is required that the\n sequences be nonempty to ensure productivity; in the case\n of an infinite sequence of `nil`, the first element is never\n generated.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq1", "description": "`seq1 \u03b1` is the type of nonempty sequences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.nth", "description": "Get the nth element of a sequence (if it exists)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.cons_injective2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq1.monad", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.mem_cons_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.unzip", "description": "Separate a sequence of pairs into two sequences", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.zip_with", "description": "Combine two sequences with a function", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.tail_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.split_at", "description": "Split a sequence at `n`, producing a finite initial segment\n and an infinite tail.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.coe_list", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.is_lawful_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.corec", "description": "Corecursor for `seq \u03b1` as a coinductive type. Iterates `f` to produce new elements\n of the sequence until `none` is obtained.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.corec_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.head_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.to_list", "description": "Convert a sequence which is known to terminate into a list", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.map_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.nil_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.coinduction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.append_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.enum_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.tail_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.destruct", "description": "Destructor for a sequence, resulting in either `none` (for `nil`) or\n `some (a, s)` (for `cons a s`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.not_mem_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.terminated_at_decidable", "description": "It is decidable whether a sequence terminates at a given position.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.coe_lazy_list", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.to_list_or_stream", "description": "Convert a sequence into either a list or a stream depending on whether\n it is finite or infinite. (Without decidability of the infiniteness predicate,\n this is not constructively possible.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.terminated_stable", "description": "If a sequence terminated at position `n`, it also terminated at `m \u2265 n `.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq1.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.zip", "description": "Pair two sequences into a sequence of pairs", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.append", "description": "Append two sequences. If `s\u2081` is infinite, then `s\u2081 ++ s\u2082 = s\u2081`,\n otherwise it puts `s\u2082` at the location of the `nil` in `s\u2081`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.mem", "description": "member definition for `seq`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq1.join", "description": "Flatten a nonempty sequence of nonempty sequences", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.of_mem_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.nats", "description": "The sequence of natural numbers some 0, some 1, ...", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq1.join_join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.enum", "description": "Enumerate a sequence by tagging each element with its index.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.destruct_eq_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.nth_cons_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.tail", "description": "Get the tail of a sequence (or `nil` if the sequence is `nil`)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq1.join_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.join_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.dropn_tail", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.mem_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.take", "description": "Take the first `n` elements of the sequence (producing a list)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.to_lazy_list", "description": "Translate a sequence into a `lazy_list`. Since `lazy_list` and `list`\n are isomorphic as non-meta types, this function is necessarily meta.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.map", "description": "Map a function over a sequence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.rec_on", "description": "Recursion principle for sequences, compare with `list.rec_on`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq1.map_join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.nil", "description": "The empty sequence", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.cons_left_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.cons", "description": "Prepend an element to a sequence", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.head_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.not_terminates_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.nth_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.join_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.destruct_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.drop", "description": "Remove the first `n` elements from the sequence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.mem_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.to_list'", "description": "Convert a sequence into a list, embedded in a computation to allow for\n the possibility of infinite sequences (in which case the computation\n never returns anything).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.map_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.nth_zip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.head_eq_destruct", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.omap", "description": "Functorial action of the functor `option (\u03b1 \u00d7 _)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.bisim_o", "description": "Bisimilarity relation over `option` of `seq1 \u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.of_lazy_list", "description": "Embed a `lazy_list \u03b1` as a sequence. Note that even though this\n is non-meta, it will produce infinite sequences if used with\n cyclic `lazy_list`s created by meta constructions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.nth_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.head_dropn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.destruct_eq_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq1.join_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.le_stable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq1.to_seq", "description": "Convert a `seq1` to a sequence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.join_cons_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.mem_append_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.map_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.join_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "stream.seq.mem_cons_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rdrop_concat_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rdrop", "description": "Drop `n` elements from the tail end of a list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rtake", "description": "Take `n` elements from the tail end of a list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rdrop_while", "description": " Drop elements from the tail end of a list that satisfy `p : \u03b1 \u2192 Prop`.\nImplemented naively via `list.reverse`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rtake_while_eq_self_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rdrop_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rdrop_while_last_not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rtake_while_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rtake_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rtake_concat_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rdrop_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.drop_while_eq_self_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rtake_eq_reverse_take_reverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rtake_while_concat_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rtake_while", "description": " Take elements from the tail end of a list that satisfy `p : \u03b1 \u2192 Prop`.\nImplemented naively via `list.reverse`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rtake_while_eq_nil_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rdrop_while_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rdrop_while_concat_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.mem_rtake_while_imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rdrop_while_prefix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.drop_while_idempotent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rtake_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rdrop_while_eq_self_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rtake_while_concat_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rdrop_while_concat_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rtake_while_idempotent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rdrop_eq_reverse_drop_reverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rdrop_while_eq_nil_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rtake_while_concat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rdrop_while_idempotent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rdrop_while_concat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rdrop_while_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rtake_while_suffix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_lt_of_left_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_eq_right_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_min_distrib_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_associative", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_lt_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_lt_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_eq_left_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_idem", "description": "An instance asserting that `min a a = a`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.map_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_left_commutative", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_le_of_left_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone_on.map_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_lt_of_right_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_lt_min_left_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone_on.map_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone_on.map_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_lt_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_max_of_le_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.map_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_lt_max_right_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_of_max_le_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max.right_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_lt_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lt_min_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_min_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_eq_right_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lt_max_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_idem", "description": "An instance asserting that `max a a = a`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_commutative", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_cases", "description": "For elements `a` and `b` of a linear order, either `min a b = a` and `a \u2264 b`,\n   or `min a b = b` and `b < a`.\n   Use cases on this lemma to automate linarith in inequalities", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_eq_left_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_left_commutative", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_commutative", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_max_distrib_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_choice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_lt_min_right_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_associative", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_right_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max.left_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_min_distrib_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_le_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone.map_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_choice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lt_max_of_lt_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_lt_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone_on.map_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_max_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone.map_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_max_distrib_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_max_of_le_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_cases", "description": "For elements `a` and `b` of a linear order, either `max a b = a` and `b \u2264 a`,\n   or `max a b = b` and `a < b`.\n   Use cases on this lemma to automate linarith in inequalities", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_le_of_right_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_le_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_lt_max_left_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_of_max_le_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_le_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lt_max_of_lt_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.reduce_reduced'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.gcd_a'_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.start_is_special", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.gcd_b_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.qp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.gcd_x", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type", "description": "A term of xgcd_type is a system of six naturals.  They should\nbe thought of as representing the matrix\n[[w, x], [y, z]] = [[wp + 1, x], [y, zp + 1]]\ntogether with the vector [a, b] = [ap + 1, bp + 1].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.wp", "description": "A term of xgcd_type is a system of six naturals.  They should\nbe thought of as representing the matrix\n[[w, x], [y, z]] = [[wp + 1, x], [y, zp + 1]]\ntogether with the vector [a, b] = [ap + 1, bp + 1].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.x", "description": "A term of xgcd_type is a system of six naturals.  They should\nbe thought of as representing the matrix\n[[w, x], [y, z]] = [[wp + 1, x], [y, zp + 1]]\ntogether with the vector [a, b] = [ap + 1, bp + 1].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.y", "description": "A term of xgcd_type is a system of six naturals.  They should\nbe thought of as representing the matrix\n[[w, x], [y, z]] = [[wp + 1, x], [y, zp + 1]]\ntogether with the vector [a, b] = [ap + 1, bp + 1].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.zp", "description": "A term of xgcd_type is a system of six naturals.  They should\nbe thought of as representing the matrix\n[[w, x], [y, z]] = [[wp + 1, x], [y, zp + 1]]\ntogether with the vector [a, b] = [ap + 1, bp + 1].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.ap", "description": "A term of xgcd_type is a system of six naturals.  They should\nbe thought of as representing the matrix\n[[w, x], [y, z]] = [[wp + 1, x], [y, zp + 1]]\ntogether with the vector [a, b] = [ap + 1, bp + 1].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.bp", "description": "A term of xgcd_type is a system of six naturals.  They should\nbe thought of as representing the matrix\n[[w, x], [y, z]] = [[wp + 1, x], [y, zp + 1]]\ntogether with the vector [a, b] = [ap + 1, bp + 1].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.finish_is_reduced", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.reduce_reduced", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.gcd_b'_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.is_reduced'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.reduce_a", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.gcd_rel_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.reduce", "description": "We can now define the full reduction function, which applies\nstep as long as possible, and then applies finish. Note that the\n\"have\" statement puts a fact in the local context, and the\nequation compiler uses this fact to help construct the full\ndefinition in terms of well-founded recursion.  The same fact\nneeds to be introduced in all the inductive proofs of properties\ngiven below.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.has_repr", "description": "The has_repr instance converts terms to strings in a way that\nreflects the matrix/vector interpretation as above.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.is_reduced", "description": "is_reduced holds if the two entries in the vector are the\nsame.  The reduction algorithm will produce a system with this\nproperty, whose product vector is the same as for the original\nsystem.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.flip_is_special", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.gcd_y", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.gcd_props", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.finish_v", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.reduce_special", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.v_eq_succ_vp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.q", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.gcd_w", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.flip_a", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.start", "description": "The following function provides the starting point for\nour algorithm.  We will apply an iterative reduction process\nto it, which will produce a system satisfying is_reduced.\nThe gcd can be read off from this final system.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.step", "description": "This is the main reduction step, which is used when u.r \u2260 0, or\nequivalently b does not divide a.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.start_v", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.b", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.flip_w", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.gcd_rel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.qp_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.is_special_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.gcd_z", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.is_special", "description": "is_special holds if the matrix has determinant one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.has_sizeof", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.gcd_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.flip_v", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.z", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.step_is_special", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.r", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.flip_b", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.reduce_v", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.succ\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.finish_is_special", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.gcd_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.gcd_det_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.step_v", "description": "The reduction step does not change the product vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.gcd_a'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.gcd_rel_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.is_special'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.gcd_b'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.vp", "description": "The map v gives the product of the matrix\n[[w, x], [y, z]] = [[wp + 1, x], [y, zp + 1]]\nand the vector [a, b] = [ap + 1, bp + 1].  The map\nvp gives [sp, tp] such that v = [sp + 1, tp + 1].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.finish", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.v", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.flip_z", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.gcd_a_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.reduce_special'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.flip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.rq_eq", "description": "Properties of division with remainder for a / b.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.w", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.gcd_rel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.is_reduced_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.flip_is_reduced", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.flip_y", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.flip_x", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.a", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.reduce_b", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.xgcd_type.step_wf", "description": "We will apply the above step recursively.  The following result\nis used to ensure that the process terminates.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.has_dist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.ball_eq_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.dist_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.dist_cast_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.proper_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.closed_embedding_coe_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.pairwise_one_le_dist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.preimage_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.uniform_embedding_coe_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cocompact_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cofinite_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.metric_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.closed_ball_eq_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.preimage_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.stopped_value_min_ae_eq_condexp", "description": " **Optional Sampling theorem**. If `\u03c4` is a bounded stopping time and `\u03c3` is another stopping\ntime, then the value of a martingale `f` at the stopping time `min \u03c4 \u03c3` is almost everywhere equal\nto the conditional expectation of `f` stopped at `\u03c4` with respect to the \u03c3-algebra generated\nby `\u03c3`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.stopped_value_ae_eq_condexp_of_le", "description": " If `\u03c4` and `\u03c3` are two stopping times with `\u03c3 \u2264 \u03c4` and `\u03c4` is bounded, then the value of a\nmartingale `f` at `\u03c3` is the conditional expectation of its value at `\u03c4` with respect to the\n\u03c3-algebra generated by `\u03c3`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.stopped_value_ae_eq_condexp_of_le_const", "description": " The value of a martingale `f` at a stopping time `\u03c4` bounded by `n` is the conditional\nexpectation of `f n` with respect to the \u03c3-algebra generated by `\u03c4`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.condexp_stopped_value_stopping_time_ae_eq_restrict_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.condexp_stopping_time_ae_eq_restrict_eq_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.stopped_value_ae_eq_condexp_of_le_const_of_countable_range", "description": " The value of a martingale `f` at a stopping time `\u03c4` bounded by `n` is the conditional\nexpectation of `f n` with respect to the \u03c3-algebra generated by `\u03c4`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "discrete_topology.second_countable_topology_of_countable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.stopped_value_ae_eq_condexp_of_le_of_countable_range", "description": " If `\u03c4` and `\u03c3` are two stopping times with `\u03c3 \u2264 \u03c4` and `\u03c4` is bounded, then the value of a\nmartingale `f` at `\u03c3` is the conditional expectation of its value at `\u03c4` with respect to the\n\u03c3-algebra generated by `\u03c3`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.condexp_stopping_time_ae_eq_restrict_eq_const_of_le_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.stopped_value_ae_eq_restrict_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.smul_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.pointwise_smul_to_add_subgroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.mem_inv_pointwise_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.mem_smul_pointwise_iff_exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.smul_mem_pointwise_smul_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.pointwise_smul_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.pointwise_smul_subset_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.smul_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.smul_mem_pointwise_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.mem_pointwise_smul_iff_inv_smul_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.pointwise_smul_le_pointwise_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.pointwise_mul_action", "description": " The action on a subring corresponding to applying the action to every element.\n\nThis is available as an instance in the `pointwise` locale.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.subset_pointwise_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.mem_pointwise_smul_iff_inv_smul_mem\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.pointwise_smul_to_subsemiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.le_pointwise_smul_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.mem_inv_pointwise_smul_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.pointwise_smul_le_pointwise_smul_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.smul_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.smul_mem_pointwise_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.coe_pointwise_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.pointwise_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subring.pointwise_smul_le_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.countable_spf_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.integral_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_integrable_functions", "description": " The subspace of integrable functions in the space of all bounded functions on a type.\nThis is a technical device, used to apply Hahn-Banach theorem to construct an extension of the\nintegral to all bounded functions.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.countable_discrete_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.discrete_copy.discrete_topology", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.neg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.norm_indicator_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.extension_to_bounded_functions", "description": " An arbitrary extension of the integral to all bounded functions, as a continuous linear map.\nIt is not at all canonical, and constructed using Hahn-Banach.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.additive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.integrable_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.le_bound", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.comp_ae_eq_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.to_functions_to_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_integrable_functions_integral_clm", "description": " The integral, as a continuous linear map on the subspace of integrable functions in the space\nof all bounded functions on a type. This is a technical device, that we will extend through\nHahn-Banach.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.apply_f_eq_continuous_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.sierpinski_pathological_family", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.C", "description": "A constant bounding the mass of any set for `f`.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure", "description": "A bounded signed finitely additive measure defined on *all* subsets of a type.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.to_fun", "description": "A bounded signed finitely additive measure defined on *all* subsets of a type.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.additive'", "description": "A bounded signed finitely additive measure defined on *all* subsets of a type.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.exists_bound", "description": "A bounded signed finitely additive measure defined on *all* subsets of a type.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.f", "description": " A family of bounded functions `f_x` from `\u211d` (seen with the discrete topology) to `\u211d` (in fact\ntaking values in `{0, 1}`), indexed by a real parameter `x`, corresponding to the characteristic\nfunctions of the different fibers of the Sierpinski pathological family", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.exists_linear_extension_to_bounded_functions", "description": " Given a measure, there exists a continuous linear form on the space of all bounded functions\n(not necessarily measurable) that coincides with the integral on bounded measurable functions.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.spf", "description": " A family of sets in `\u211d` which only miss countably many points, but such that any point is\ncontained in only countably many of them.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.discrete_part_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.restrict_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.continuous_part", "description": " The continuous part of a bounded additive measure, giving zero measure to every countable\nset.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.to_bounded_additive_measure", "description": " A functional in the dual space of bounded functions gives rise to a bounded additive measure,\nby applying the functional to the indicator functions.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.no_pettis_integral", "description": "The function `f Hcont : \u211d \u2192 (discrete_copy \u211d \u2192\u1d47 \u211d)` has no Pettis integral.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.discrete_support", "description": " A countable set outside of which the measure gives zero mass to countable sets. We are not\nclaiming this set is unique, but we make an arbitrary choice of such a set.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.norm_bound", "description": "The function `f Hcont : \u211d \u2192 (discrete_copy \u211d \u2192\u1d47 \u211d)` is uniformly bounded by `1` in norm.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.discrete_copy", "description": "A copy of a type, endowed with the discrete topology", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.to_functions_to_measure_continuous_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.countable_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.extension_to_bounded_functions_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.apply_countable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.exists_discrete_support_nonpos", "description": " There is a maximal countable set of positive measure, in the sense that any countable set\nnot intersecting it has nonpositive measure. Auxiliary lemma to prove `exists_discrete_support`.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.continuous_part_apply_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.discrete_copy.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.countable_compl_spf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.discrete_part", "description": " The discrete part of a bounded additive measure, obtained by restricting the measure to its\ncountable support.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.measurable_comp", "description": "The function `f Hcont : \u211d \u2192 (discrete_copy \u211d \u2192\u1d47 \u211d)` is scalarly measurable.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.continuous_part_apply_eq_zero_of_countable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.restrict", "description": "Restricting a bounded additive measure to a subset still gives a bounded additive measure.", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.continuous_part_eval_clm_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.abs_le_bound", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.eq_add_parts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.phillips_1940.bounded_additive_measure.exists_discrete_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "counterexample.discrete_copy.topological_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-counterexamples"}, {"name": "fintype.pi_finset_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.pi_finset_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.univ_pi_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.pi_finset_disjoint_of_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.mem_pi_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.pi_finset_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.fintype", "description": "A dependent product of fintypes, indexed by a fintype, is a fintype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.pi_finset_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.pi_finset_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.pi_finset", "description": " Given for all `a : \u03b1` a finset `t a` of `\u03b4 a`, then one can define the\nfinset `fintype.pi_finset t` of all functions taking values in `t a` for all `a`. This is the\nanalogue of `finset.pi` where the base finset is `univ` (but formally they are not the same, as\nthere is an additional condition `i \u2208 finset.univ` in the `finset.pi` definition).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.coe_pi_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.inducing_prod_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.prod_topology", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pi_fan_is_limit", "description": "The constructed fan is indeed a limit", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sigma_iso_sigma_hom_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pi_iso_pi_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.prod_iso_prod_inv_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.binary_cofan_is_colimit_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.prod_iso_prod_inv_fst_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.prod_snd", "description": "The second projection from the product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sigma_iso_sigma", "description": "The coproduct is homeomorphic to the disjoint union of the topological spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.embedding_prod_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pi_iso_pi_inv_\u03c0_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.prod_binary_fan", "description": "The explicit binary cofan of `X, Y` given by `X \u00d7 Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.prod_iso_prod_hom_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pi_fan_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.prod_binary_fan_is_limit", "description": "The constructed binary fan is indeed a limit", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.prod_iso_prod_inv_snd_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.prod_iso_prod_hom_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sigma_cofan", "description": "The explicit cofan of a family of topological spaces given by the sigma type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.prod_iso_prod_hom_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sigma_cofan_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sigma_iso_sigma_hom_\u03b9_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.induced_of_is_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.prod_iso_prod_hom_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pi_iso_pi", "description": "The product is homeomorphic to the product of the underlying spaces,\nequipped with the product topology.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.binary_cofan_is_colimit", "description": "The constructed binary coproduct cofan in `Top` is the coproduct.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.binary_cofan", "description": "The binary coproduct cofan in `Top`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.prod_fst", "description": "The first projection from the product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.prod_iso_prod_inv_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pi_iso_pi_inv_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sigma_iso_sigma_inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sigma_cofan_is_colimit", "description": "The constructed cofan is indeed a colimit", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sigma_cofan_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.limit_topology", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sigma_\u03b9", "description": "The inclusion to the coproduct as a bundled continous map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.prod_iso_prod_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.prod_iso_prod", "description": "The homeomorphism between `X \u2a2f Y` and the set-theoretic product of `X` and `Y`,\nequipped with the product topology.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pi_fan", "description": "The explicit fan of a family of topological spaces given by the pi type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.prod_iso_prod_inv_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.prod_iso_prod_inv_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pi_fan_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pi_iso_pi_inv_\u03c0_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sigma_iso_sigma_hom_\u03b9_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.range_prod_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.pi_\u03c0", "description": "The projection from the product as a bundled continous map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.add_hadamard", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.hadamard_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.hadamard_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.diagonal_hadamard_diagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.hadamard_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.hadamard_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.hadamard", "description": "`matrix.hadamard` defines the Hadamard product,\n   which is the pointwise product of two matrices of the same size.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.zero_hadamard", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.sum_hadamard_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.dot_product_vec_mul_hadamard", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.hadamard_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.smul_hadamard", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.one_hadamard", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.hadamard_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.hadamard_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_rule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_rule.orig_nm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_rule.func_nm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_rule.type", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_rule.loc_type", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_rule.args", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_rule.loc_args", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_rule.concl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_rule.insts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotonicity.not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.u_params", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.coinduction", "description": " Prepares coinduction proofs. This tactic constructs the coinduction invariant from\nthe quantifiers in the current goal.\n\nCurrent version: do not support mutual inductive rules", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.destruct", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.func", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotonicity.false", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.f\u2081_l", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotonicity.true", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotonicity.pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.func_g", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.pred", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotonicity.const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.coinductive_predicate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotonicity.or", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.compact_relation", "description": " compact_relation bs as_ps: Product a relation of the form:\n  R := \u03bb as, \u2203 bs, \u039b_i a_i = p_i[bs]\nThis relation is user visible, so we compact it by removing each `b_j` where a `p_i = b_j`, and\nhence `a_i = b_j`. We need to take care when there are `p_i` and `p_j` with `p_i = p_j = b_k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.rec'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotonicity.exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.construct", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.u_names", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.params", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.pd_name", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.type", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.intros", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.locals", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.f\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.f\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.u_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.coinduction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.f\u2082_l", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.corec_functional", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.pred_g", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotonicity.and", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotonicity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotonicity.imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.impl_locals", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.add_theorem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.add_coinductive_predicate.coind_pred.impl_params", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.dense_range_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.norm_sub_mod_part_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.zmod_repr_lt_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.dense_range_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.nth_hom_seq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.lim_nth_hom_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.dvd_appr_sub_appr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.sub_zmod_repr_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.nth_hom_seq_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.nth_hom_seq", "description": "`nth_hom_seq f_compat r` bundles `padic_int.nth_hom f r`\nas a Cauchy sequence of rationals with respect to the `p`-adic norm.\nThe `n`th value of the sequence is `((f n r).val : \u211a)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.exists_mem_range_of_norm_rat_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.lim_nth_hom_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.nth_hom_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.zmod_repr", "description": "`zmod_repr x` is the unique natural number smaller than `p`\nsatisfying `\u2016(x - zmod_repr x : \u2124_[p])\u2016 < 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.ext_of_to_zmod_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.lift_unique", "description": "One part of the universal property of `\u2124_[p]` as a projective limit.\nSee also `padic_int.lift_spec`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.lim_nth_hom_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.appr_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.zmod_congr_of_sub_mem_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.lift_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.mod_part_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.lim_nth_hom_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.nth_hom_seq_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.lift", "description": "`lift f_compat` is the limit of a sequence `f` of compatible ring homs `R \u2192+* zmod (p^k)`,\nwith the equality `lift f_compat r = padic_int.lim_nth_hom f_compat r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.to_zmod_pow_eq_iff_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.to_zmod_hom", "description": "`to_zmod_hom` is an auxiliary constructor for creating ring homs from `\u2124_[p]` to `zmod v`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.zmod_repr_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.zmod_congr_of_sub_mem_max_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.cast_to_zmod_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.is_cau_seq_nth_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.norm_sub_mod_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.to_zmod_spec", "description": "`z - (to_zmod z : \u2124_[p])` is contained in the maximal ideal of `\u2124_[p]`, for every `z : \u2124_[p]`.\n\nThe coercion from `zmod p` to `\u2124_[p]` is `zmod.has_coe_t`,\nwhich coerces `zmod p` into artibrary rings.\nThis is unfortunate, but a consequence of the fact that we allow `zmod p`\nto coerce to rings of arbitrary characteristic, instead of only rings of characteristic `p`.\nThis coercion is only a ring homomorphism if it coerces into a ring whose characteristic divides\n`p`. While this is not the case here we can still make use of the coercion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.zmod_cast_comp_to_zmod_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.appr", "description": " `appr n x` gives a value `v : \u2115` such that `x` and `\u2191v : \u2124_p` are congruent mod `p^n`.\nSee `appr_spec`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.zmod_congr_of_sub_mem_span_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.mod_part", "description": "`mod_part p r` is an integer that satisfies\n`\u2016(r - mod_part p r : \u211a_[p])\u2016 < 1` when `\u2016(r : \u211a_[p])\u2016 \u2264 1`,\nsee `padic_int.norm_sub_mod_part`.\nIt is the unique non-negative integer that is `< p` with this property.\n\n(Note that this definition assumes `r : \u211a`.\nSee `padic_int.zmod_repr` for a version that takes values in `\u2115`\nand works for arbitrary `x : \u2124_[p]`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.lim_nth_hom_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.lift_sub_val_mem_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.exists_mem_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.mod_part_lt_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.to_zmod_pow", "description": "A ring hom from `\u2124_[p]` to `zmod (p^n)`, with underlying function `padic_int.appr n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.appr_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.lift_spec", "description": "One part of the universal property of `\u2124_[p]` as a projective limit.\nSee also `padic_int.lift_unique`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.pow_dvd_nth_hom_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.ker_to_zmod_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.nth_hom", "description": "Given a family of ring homs `f : \u03a0 n : \u2115, R \u2192+* zmod (p ^ n)`,\n`nth_hom f r` is an integer-valued sequence\nwhose `n`th value is the unique integer `k` such that `0 \u2264 k < p ^ n`\nand `f n r = (k : zmod (p ^ n))`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.appr_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.to_zmod", "description": "`to_zmod` is a ring hom from `\u2124_[p]` to `zmod p`,\nwith the equality `to_zmod x = (zmod_repr x : zmod p)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.lim_nth_hom", "description": "`lim_nth_hom f_compat r` is the limit of a sequence `f` of compatible ring homs `R \u2192+* zmod (p^k)`.\nThis is itself a ring hom: see `padic_int.lift`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.ker_to_zmod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "padic_int.is_unit_denom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.snd_im_k_dual_number_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.im_i_snd_dual_number_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.snd_im_j_dual_number_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.im_k_snd_dual_number_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.im_k_fst_dual_number_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.snd_im_i_dual_number_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.fst_re_dual_number_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.snd_re_dual_number_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.fst_im_i_dual_number_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.dual_number_equiv", "description": " The dual quaternions can be equivalently represented as a quaternion with dual coefficients,\nor as a dual number with quaternion coefficients.\n\nSee also `matrix.dual_number_equiv` for a similar result.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.re_fst_dual_number_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.fst_im_k_dual_number_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.re_snd_dual_number_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.im_j_snd_dual_number_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.fst_im_j_dual_number_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.im_i_fst_dual_number_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.im_j_fst_dual_number_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth.of_is_localization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_etale.of_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth.mk_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth.of_split", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_unramified.lift_unique_of_ring_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth.localization_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth.of_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_etale.localization_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_etale.of_unramified_and_smooth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_unramified.localization_base", "description": " This actually does not need the localization instance, and is stated here again for\nconsistency. See `algebra.formally_unramified.of_comp` instead.\n\n The intended use is for copying proofs between `formally_{unramified, smooth, etale}`\n without the need to change anything (including removing redundant arguments).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth.base_change", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_unramified.of_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_etale.localization_base", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_unramified.subsingleton_kaehler_differential", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth.comp_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_etale.to_unramified", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_unramified.of_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth.mv_polynomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_unramified.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_unramified.of_is_localization", "description": "This holds in general for epimorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth.lift_of_surjective_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth.lift_of_surjective", "description": " For a formally smooth `R`-algebra `A` and a map `f : A \u2192\u2090[R] B \u29f8 I` with `I` nilpotent,\nthis is an arbitrary lift `A \u2192\u2090[R] B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_etale.base_change", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_unramified_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth.lift", "description": " For a formally smooth `R`-algebra `A` and a map `f : A \u2192\u2090[R] B \u29f8 I` with `I` square-zero,\nthis is an arbitrary lift `A \u2192\u2090[R] B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth.localization_base", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth.polynomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth.exists_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_etale.of_is_localization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_etale_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_unramified.lift_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_unramified.base_change", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_unramified.localization_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_etale.iff_unramified_and_smooth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_unramified.iff_subsingleton_kaehler_differential", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_etale.to_smooth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_unramified.lift_unique'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth.comp_lift_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_etale", "description": " An `R` algebra `A` is formally \u00e9tale if for every `R`-algebra, every square-zero ideal\n`I : ideal B` and `f : A \u2192\u2090[R] B \u29f8 I`, there exists exactly one lift `A \u2192\u2090[R] B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_etale.comp_bijective", "description": " An `R` algebra `A` is formally \u00e9tale if for every `R`-algebra, every square-zero ideal\n`I : ideal B` and `f : A \u2192\u2090[R] B \u29f8 I`, there exists exactly one lift `A \u2192\u2090[R] B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_unramified.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_etale.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth.iff_split_surjection", "description": " Let `P \u2192\u2090[R] A` be a surjection with kernel `J`, and `P` a formally smooth `R`-algebra,\nthen `A` is formally smooth over `R` iff the surjection `P \u29f8 J ^ 2 \u2192\u2090[R] A` has a section.\n\nGeometric intuition: we require that a first-order thickening of `Spec A` inside `Spec P` admits\na retraction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth", "description": " An `R` algebra `A` is formally smooth if for every `R`-algebra, every square-zero ideal\n`I : ideal B` and `f : A \u2192\u2090[R] B \u29f8 I`, there exists at least one lift `A \u2192\u2090[R] B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_smooth.comp_surjective", "description": " An `R` algebra `A` is formally smooth if for every `R`-algebra, every square-zero ideal\n`I : ideal B` and `f : A \u2192\u2090[R] B \u29f8 I`, there exists at least one lift `A \u2192\u2090[R] B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_unramified", "description": " An `R`-algebra `A` is formally unramified if for every `R`-algebra, every square-zero ideal\n`I : ideal B` and `f : A \u2192\u2090[R] B \u29f8 I`, there exists at most one lift `A \u2192\u2090[R] B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_unramified.comp_injective", "description": " An `R`-algebra `A` is formally unramified if for every `R`-algebra, every square-zero ideal\n`I : ideal B` and `f : A \u2192\u2090[R] B \u29f8 I`, there exists at most one lift `A \u2192\u2090[R] B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.formally_unramified.ext'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.int_smul_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action_with_zero.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.mul_action_with_zero", "description": " Pullback a `mul_action_with_zero` structure along an injective zero-preserving homomorphism.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action_with_zero", "description": "  An action of a monoid with zero `R` on a Type `M`, also with `0`, extends `mul_action` and\nis compatible with `0` (both in `R` and in `M`), with `1 \u2208 R`, and with associativity of\nmultiplication on the monoid `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action_with_zero.to_mul_action", "description": "  An action of a monoid with zero `R` on a Type `M`, also with `0`, extends `mul_action` and\nis compatible with `0` (both in `R` and in `M`), with `1 \u2208 R`, and with associativity of\nmultiplication on the monoid `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action_with_zero.smul_zero", "description": "  An action of a monoid with zero `R` on a Type `M`, also with `0`, extends `mul_action` and\nis compatible with `0` (both in `R` and in `M`), with `1 \u2208 R`, and with associativity of\nmultiplication on the monoid `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action_with_zero.zero_smul", "description": "  An action of a monoid with zero `R` on a Type `M`, also with `0`, extends `mul_action` and\nis compatible with `0` (both in `R` and in `M`), with `1 \u2208 R`, and with associativity of\nmultiplication on the monoid `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smul_with_zero.comp_hom", "description": "Compose a `smul_with_zero` with a `zero_hom`, with action `f r' \u2022 m`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero.to_opposite_mul_action_with_zero", "description": " Like `monoid_with_zero.to_mul_action_with_zero`, but multiplies on the right. See also\n`semiring.to_opposite_module`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smul_monoid_with_zero_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smul_with_zero", "description": "  `smul_with_zero` is a class consisting of a Type `R` with `0 \u2208 R` and a scalar multiplication\nof `R` on a Type `M` with `0`, such that the equality `r \u2022 m = 0` holds if at least one among `r`\nor `m` equals `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smul_with_zero.to_smul_zero_class", "description": "  `smul_with_zero` is a class consisting of a Type `R` with `0 \u2208 R` and a scalar multiplication\nof `R` on a Type `M` with `0`, such that the equality `r \u2022 m = 0` holds if at least one among `r`\nor `m` equals `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smul_with_zero.zero_smul", "description": "  `smul_with_zero` is a class consisting of a Type `R` with `0 \u2208 R` and a scalar multiplication\nof `R` on a Type `M` with `0`, such that the equality `r \u2022 m = 0` holds if at least one among `r`\nor `m` equals `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_ne_zero_of_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action_with_zero.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_ne_zero_of_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.smul_with_zero", "description": " Pullback a `smul_with_zero` structure along an injective zero-preserving homomorphism.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_zero_class.to_smul_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smul_inv\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.nat_smul_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.mul_action_with_zero", "description": " Pushforward a `mul_action_with_zero` structure along a surjective zero-preserving homomorphism.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smul_eq_zero_of_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.smul_with_zero", "description": " Pushforward a `smul_with_zero` structure along a surjective zero-preserving homomorphism.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_zero_class.to_opposite_smul_with_zero", "description": "Like `mul_zero_class.to_smul_with_zero`, but multiplies on the right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smul_eq_zero_of_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action_with_zero.to_smul_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smul_monoid_with_zero_hom", "description": "Scalar multiplication as a monoid homomorphism with zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action_with_zero.comp_hom", "description": "Compose a `mul_action_with_zero` with a `monoid_with_zero_hom`, with action `f r' \u2022 m`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero.to_mul_action_with_zero", "description": "See also `semiring.to_module`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.has_sum_deriv_of_summable_norm", "description": " If the terms in the sum `\u2211' (i : \u03b9), F i` are uniformly bounded on `U` by a\nsummable function, then the sum of `deriv F i` at a point in `U` is the derivative of the\nsum.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.cderiv_eq_deriv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.exists_cthickening_tendsto_uniformly_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.tendsto_uniformly_on_deriv_of_cthickening_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.norm_cderiv_sub_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.differentiable_on_tsum_of_summable_norm", "description": " If the terms in the sum `\u2211' (i : \u03b9), F i` are uniformly bounded on `U` by a\nsummable function, and each term in the sum is differentiable on `U`, then so is the sum.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_locally_uniformly_on.deriv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.cderiv", "description": " A circle integral which coincides with `deriv f z` whenever one can apply the Cauchy formula for\nthe derivative. It is useful in the proof that locally uniform limits of holomorphic functions are\nholomorphic, because it depends continuously on `f` for the uniform topology.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_locally_uniformly_on.differentiable_on", "description": " A locally uniform limit of holomorphic functions on an open domain of the complex plane is\nholomorphic (the derivatives converge locally uniformly to that of the limit, which is proved\nas `tendsto_locally_uniformly_on.deriv`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.norm_cderiv_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.tendsto_uniformly_on.cderiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.norm_cderiv_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.cderiv_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_right_id_hom_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_right_id_inv_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_left_obj_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.nat_trans_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.pre_left_obj_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_left_id_inv_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_left_id_hom_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_right_id_inv_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.post_obj_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.iso_mk_inv_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_left_obj_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_left_map_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.pre_right_obj_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_right_comp_hom_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.pre_right_obj_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_right_map_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_right_id_hom_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma_morphism.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_left_comp_inv_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_right_obj_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.snd", "description": "The functor sending an object `X` in the comma category to `X.right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_left_comp_hom_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.snd_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.post_obj_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.comp_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_right_comp_inv_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_left_id", "description": "The functor `comma L R \u2964 comma L R` induced by the identity natural transformation on `L` is\n   naturally isomorphic to the identity functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.pre_right_map_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.pre_left_obj_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_left_obj_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.pre_right_obj_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.eq_to_hom_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_left_comp", "description": "The functor `comma L\u2081 R \u2964 comma L\u2083 R` induced by the composition of two natural transformations\n   `l : L\u2081 \u27f6 L\u2082` and `l' : L\u2082 \u27f6 L\u2083` is naturally isomorphic to the composition of the two functors\n   induced by these natural transformations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_right", "description": "A natural transformation `R\u2081 \u27f6 R\u2082` induces a functor `comma L R\u2081 \u2964 comma L R\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_left_map_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_left_comp_hom_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma", "description": "The objects of the comma category are triples of an object `left : A`, an object\n  `right : B` and a morphism `hom : L.obj left \u27f6 R.obj right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.left", "description": "The objects of the comma category are triples of an object `left : A`, an object\n  `right : B` and a morphism `hom : L.obj left \u27f6 R.obj right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.right", "description": "The objects of the comma category are triples of an object `left : A`, an object\n  `right : B` and a morphism `hom : L.obj left \u27f6 R.obj right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.hom", "description": "The objects of the comma category are triples of an object `left : A`, an object\n  `right : B` and a morphism `hom : L.obj left \u27f6 R.obj right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.post", "description": "The functor `(L, R) \u2964 (L \u22d9 F, R \u22d9 F)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.fst", "description": "The functor sending an object `X` in the comma category to `X.left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma_morphism.w_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.pre_left", "description": "The functor `(F \u22d9 L, R) \u2964 (L, R)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.iso_mk_hom_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.comp_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.snd_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.id_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.iso_mk", "description": "Construct an isomorphism in the comma category given isomorphisms of the objects whose forward\ndirections give a commutative square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.pre_right", "description": "The functor `(F \u22d9 L, R) \u2964 (L, R)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.fst_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.pre_right_map_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.nat_trans", "description": "We can interpret the commutative square constituting a morphism in the comma category as a\n   natural transformation between the functors `fst \u22d9 L` and `snd \u22d9 R` from the comma category\n   to `T`, where the components are given by the morphism that constitutes an object of the comma\n   category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma_morphism.w", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.post_obj_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.iso_mk_hom_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.pre_left_map_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.post_map_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.fst_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma_morphism.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.pre_left_map_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_left", "description": "A natural transformation `L\u2081 \u27f6 L\u2082` induces a functor `comma L\u2082 R \u2964 comma L\u2081 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_left_id_hom_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_right_obj_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_right_obj_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma_morphism", "description": "A morphism between two objects in the comma category is a commutative square connecting the\n   morphisms coming from the two objects using morphisms in the image of the functors `L` and `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma_morphism.left", "description": "A morphism between two objects in the comma category is a commutative square connecting the\n   morphisms coming from the two objects using morphisms in the image of the functors `L` and `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma_morphism.right", "description": "A morphism between two objects in the comma category is a commutative square connecting the\n   morphisms coming from the two objects using morphisms in the image of the functors `L` and `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma_morphism.w'", "description": "A morphism between two objects in the comma category is a commutative square connecting the\n   morphisms coming from the two objects using morphisms in the image of the functors `L` and `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_right_id", "description": "The functor `comma L R \u2964 comma L R` induced by the identity natural transformation on `R` is\n   naturally isomorphic to the identity functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.iso_mk_inv_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_right_comp_inv_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_left_comp_inv_app_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.id_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_right_comp", "description": "The functor `comma L R\u2081 \u2964 comma L R\u2083` induced by the composition of the natural transformations\n   `r : R\u2081 \u27f6 R\u2082` and `r' : R\u2082 \u27f6 R\u2083` is naturally isomorphic to the composition of the functors\n   induced by these natural transformations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.pre_left_obj_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.post_map_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma_morphism.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_right_map_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_left_id_inv_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.map_right_comp_hom_app_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comma.eq_to_hom_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.from_iter", "description": "Iterations of a continuous function from a topological space `\u03b1`\n   to itself defines a semiflow by `\u2115` on `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fw_invariant_iff_is_invariant", "description": " If `\u03c4` is a `canonically_ordered_add_monoid` (e.g., `\u2115` or `\u211d\u22650`), then the notions\n`is_fw_invariant` and `is_invariant` are equivalent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.map_zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.to_homeomorph", "description": "The map `\u03d5 t` as a homeomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow", "description": "A flow on a topological space `\u03b1` by an a additive topological\n   monoid `\u03c4` is a continuous monoid action of `\u03c4` on `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.to_fun", "description": "A flow on a topological space `\u03b1` by an a additive topological\n   monoid `\u03c4` is a continuous monoid action of `\u03c4` on `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.cont'", "description": "A flow on a topological space `\u03b1` by an a additive topological\n   monoid `\u03c4` is a continuous monoid action of `\u03c4` on `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.map_add'", "description": "A flow on a topological space `\u03b1` by an a additive topological\n   monoid `\u03c4` is a continuous monoid action of `\u03c4` on `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.map_zero'", "description": "A flow on a topological space `\u03b1` by an a additive topological\n   monoid `\u03c4` is a continuous monoid action of `\u03c4` on `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.restrict", "description": "Restriction of a flow onto an invariant set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_invariant", "description": "A set `s \u2286 \u03b1` is invariant under `\u03d5 : \u03c4 \u2192 \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1` if\n   `\u03d5 t s \u2286 s` for all `t` in `\u03c4`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fw_invariant", "description": "A set `s \u2286 \u03b1` is forward-invariant under `\u03d5 : \u03c4 \u2192 \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1` if\n   `\u03d5 t s \u2286 s` for all `t \u2265 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.is_invariant_iff_image_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_invariant_iff_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_fw_invariant.is_invariant", "description": " If `\u03c4` is a `canonically_ordered_add_monoid` (e.g., `\u2115` or `\u211d\u22650`), then the notions\n`is_fw_invariant` and `is_invariant` are equivalent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_invariant.is_fw_invariant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.image_eq_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.flow", "description": "**Alias** of `flow.continuous`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.reverse", "description": "The time-reversal of a flow `\u03d5` by a (commutative, additive) group\n   is defined `\u03d5.reverse t x = \u03d5 (-t) x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_left_regular.pow", "description": "Any power of a left-regular element is left-regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_right_regular.pow_iff", "description": "An element `a` is right-regular if and only if a positive power of `a` is right-regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_left_regular.pow_iff", "description": "An element `a` is left-regular if and only if a positive power of `a` is left-regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_right_regular.pow", "description": "Any power of a right-regular element is right-regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_regular.pow", "description": "Any power of a regular element is regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_regular.pow_iff", "description": "An element `a` is regular if and only if a positive power of `a` is regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.one_lt_two_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_le_pow_of_le_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.one_le_two_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.one_le_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.one_lt_two_pow'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_left_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_lt_pow_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_dvd_of_le_of_pow_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.not_pos_pow_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_lt_pow_of_lt_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_le_iff_le_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_lt_iff_lt_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_le_pow_of_le_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_lt_iff_lt_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.one_lt_pow_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_dvd_pow_iff_pow_le_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strict_mono.nat_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_right_strict_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.one_lt_pow'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_right_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.one_lt_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.sq_sub_sq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.one_le_pow'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_left_strict_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_lt_pow_of_lt_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.dvd_of_pow_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.le_self_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.lt_pow_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_le_iff_le_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.mod_pow_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.lt_two_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_two_sub_pow_two", "description": "**Alias** of `nat.sq_sub_sq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.mul_lt_mul_pow_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.lt_of_pow_dvd_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_dvd_pow_iff_le_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_dvd_pow_iff_le_right", "description": "If `1 < x`, then `x^k` divides `x^l` if and only if `k` is at most `l`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.iso_mk_inv_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.pre_obj_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.eta_hom_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow", "description": "The category of `T`-structured arrows with domain `S : D` (here `T : C \u2964 D`),\nhas as its objects `D`-morphisms of the form `S \u27f6 T Y`, for some `Y : C`,\nand morphisms `C`-morphisms `Y \u27f6 Y'` making the obvious triangle commute.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.iso_mk_inv_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.w_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.mk_id_terminal", "description": "The identity costructured arrow is terminal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.hom_mk_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.proj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.w", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.to_costructured_arrow_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.iso_mk", "description": "To construct an isomorphism of structured arrows,\nwe need an isomorphism of the objects underlying the target,\nand to check that the triangle commutes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.eq_mk", "description": "Eta rule for costructured arrows. Prefer `costructured_arrow.eta`, as equality of objects tends\n   to cause problems.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.eta_inv_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.to_structured_arrow'", "description": "For a functor `F : C \u2964 D` and an object `d : D`, we obtain a contravariant functor from the\ncategory of costructured arrows `F.op.obj c \u27f6 op d` to the category of structured arrows\n`d \u27f6 F.obj c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.proj_faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.to_structured_arrow_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.epi_hom_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.map_map_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.iso_mk_inv_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.proj_faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.mk_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.eq_mk", "description": "Eta rule for structured arrows. Prefer `structured_arrow.eta`, since equality of objects tends\n   to cause problems.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.hom_mk", "description": "To construct a morphism of structured arrows,\nwe need a morphism of the objects underlying the target,\nand to check that the triangle commutes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.w", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.post_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.post", "description": "The functor `(F, S) \u2964 (F \u22d9 G, G(S))`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.map_obj_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.proj", "description": "The obvious projection functor from costructured arrows.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.map", "description": "A morphism between target objects `T \u27f6 T'`\ncovariantly induces a functor between costructured arrows,\n`costructured_arrow S T \u2964 costructured_arrow S T'`.\n\nIdeally this would be described as a 2-functor from `D`\n(promoted to a 2-category with equations as 2-morphisms)\nto `Cat`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.to_costructured_arrow'_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.map", "description": "A morphism between source objects `S \u27f6 S'`\ncontravariantly induces a functor between structured arrows,\n`structured_arrow S' T \u2964 structured_arrow S T`.\n\nIdeally this would be described as a 2-functor from `D`\n(promoted to a 2-category with equations as 2-morphisms)\nto `Cat`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.mono_of_mono_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.eta_inv_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.map_map_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.pre_obj_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.eta_hom_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.pre_obj_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.iso_mk_hom_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.pre_obj_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.to_costructured_arrow_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.proj_reflects_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.pre", "description": "The functor `(F \u22d9 G, S) \u2964 (G, S)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.pre_obj_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.eta_hom_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.proj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.mk_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.pre_map_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.hom_mk'", "description": "Given a structured arrow `X \u27f6 F(U)`, and an arrow `U \u27f6 Y`, we can construct a morphism of\nstructured arrow given by `(X \u27f6 F(U)) \u27f6 (X \u27f6 F(U) \u27f6 F(Y))`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.map_obj_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow", "description": "The category of `S`-costructured arrows with target `T : D` (here `S : C \u2964 D`),\nhas as its objects `D`-morphisms of the form `S Y \u27f6 T`, for some `Y : C`,\nand morphisms `C`-morphisms `Y \u27f6 Y'` making the obvious triangle commute.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.to_costructured_arrow'_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.mk_hom_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.to_structured_arrow", "description": "For a functor `F : C \u2964 D` and an object `d : D`, we obtain a contravariant functor from the\ncategory of costructured arrows `F.obj c \u27f6 d` to the category of structured arrows\n`op d \u27f6 F.op.obj c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.w_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.to_structured_arrow_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.iso_mk_inv_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.mk", "description": "Construct a structured arrow from a morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.iso_mk_hom_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.small_proj_preimage_of_locally_small", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.hom_mk", "description": "To construct a morphism of costructured arrows,\nwe need a morphism of the objects underlying the source,\nand to check that the triangle commutes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.iso_mk_hom_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.hom_mk_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.eta_inv_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.mk_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow_op_equivalence", "description": "For a functor `F : C \u2964 D` and an object `d : D`, the category of structured arrows `d \u27f6 F.obj c`\nis contravariantly equivalent to the category of costructured arrows `F.op.obj c \u27f6 op d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.pre", "description": "The functor `(S, F \u22d9 G) \u2964 (S, G)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.mono_of_mono_right", "description": "The converse of this is true with additional assumptions, see `mono_iff_mono_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.map_map_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.eta", "description": "Eta rule for structured arrows.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.epi_of_epi_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.eta_inv_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.pre_map_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.post_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.map_obj_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.iso_mk", "description": "To construct an isomorphism of costructured arrows,\nwe need an isomorphism of the objects underlying the source,\nand to check that the triangle commutes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.mk_hom_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.proj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.post_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.mk_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.post_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.map_map_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.to_costructured_arrow", "description": "For a functor `F : C \u2964 D` and an object `d : D`, we obtain a contravariant functor from the\ncategory of structured arrows `d \u27f6 F.obj c` to the category of costructured arrows\n`F.op.obj c \u27f6 (op d)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow_op_equivalence", "description": "For a functor `F : C \u2964 D` and an object `d : D`, the category of costructured arrows\n`F.obj c \u27f6 d` is contravariantly equivalent to the category of structured arrows\n`op d \u27f6 F.op.obj c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.map_obj_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.mono_hom_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.proj", "description": "The obvious projection functor from structured arrows.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.map_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.mono_hom_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.eta_hom_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.to_costructured_arrow'", "description": "For a functor `F : C \u2964 D` and an object `d : D`, we obtain a contravariant functor from the\ncategory of structured arrows `op d \u27f6 F.op.obj c` to the category of costructured arrows\n`F.obj c \u27f6 d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.proj_reflects_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.mk", "description": "Construct a costructured arrow from a morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.epi_of_epi_left", "description": "The converse of this is true with additional assumptions, see `epi_iff_epi_left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.mk_id_initial", "description": "The identity structured arrow is initial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.eta", "description": "Eta rule for costructured arrows.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.map_obj_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.small_proj_preimage_of_locally_small", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.pre_map_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.pre_map_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.iso_mk_hom_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.pre_obj_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.to_structured_arrow'_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.to_structured_arrow'_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.hom_mk_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.post", "description": "The functor `(S, F) \u2964 (G(S), F \u22d9 G)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.map_obj_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.hom_mk_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.map_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.structured_arrow.proj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.costructured_arrow.epi_hom_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.three_lt_four_mul_im_sq_of_mem_fdo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.lc_row0_extend_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.re_T_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.im_T_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.tendsto_abs_re_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.tendsto_norm_sq_coprime_pair", "description": "The function `(c,d) \u2192 |cz+d|^2` is proper, that is, preimages of bounded-above sets are finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.lc_row0_extend_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.fdo", "description": "The standard open fundamental domain of the action of `SL(2,\u2124)` on `\u210d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.abs_c_le_one", "description": "An auxiliary result en route to `modular_group.c_eq_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.bottom_row_coprime", "description": "The two numbers `c`, `d` in the \"bottom_row\" of `g=[[*,*],[c,d]]` in `SL(2, \u2124)` are coprime.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.exists_max_im", "description": "For `z : \u210d`, there is a `g : SL(2,\u2124)` maximizing `(g\u2022z).im`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.tendsto_lc_row0", "description": " The map `lc_row0` is proper, that is, preimages of cocompact sets are finite in\n`[[* , *], [c, d]]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.one_lt_norm_sq_T_zpow_smul", "description": "If `z \u2208 \ud835\udc9f\u1d52`, and `n : \u2124`, then `|z + n| > 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.coe_T_zpow_smul_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.exists_eq_T_zpow_of_c_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.lc_row0_extend", "description": " Linear map sending the matrix [a, b; c, d] to the matrix [ac\u2080 + bd\u2080, - ad\u2080 + bc\u2080; c, d], for\nsome fixed `(c\u2080, d\u2080)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.im_T_zpow_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.bottom_row_surj", "description": " Every pair `![c, d]` of coprime integers is the \"bottom_row\" of some element `g=[[*,*],[c,d]]`\nof `SL(2,\u2124)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.re_T_zpow_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.im_T_inv_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.g_eq_of_c_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.abs_two_mul_re_lt_one_of_mem_fdo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.exists_smul_mem_fd", "description": "Any `z : \u210d` can be moved to `\ud835\udc9f` by an element of `SL(2,\u2124)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.c_eq_zero", "description": "An auxiliary result en route to `modular_group.eq_smul_self_of_mem_fdo_mem_fdo`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.im_lt_im_S_smul", "description": "If `|z| < 1`, then applying `S` strictly decreases `im`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.fd", "description": "The standard (closed) fundamental domain of the action of `SL(2,\u2124)` on `\u210d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.eq_zero_of_mem_fdo_of_T_zpow_mem_fdo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.lc_row0_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.eq_smul_self_of_mem_fdo_mem_fdo", "description": " Second Main Fundamental Domain Lemma: if both `z` and `g \u2022 z` are in the open domain `\ud835\udc9f\u1d52`,\nwhere `z : \u210d` and `g : SL(2,\u2124)`, then `z = g \u2022 z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.norm_sq_S_smul_lt_one", "description": "If `1 < |z|`, then `|S \u2022 z| < 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.lc_row0", "description": "Given `coprime_pair` `p=(c,d)`, the matrix `[[a,b],[*,*]]` is sent to `a*c+b*d`.\n This is the linear map version of this operation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.re_T_inv_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.smul_eq_lc_row0_add", "description": "This replaces `(g\u2022z).re = a/c + *` in the standard theory with the following novel identity:\n `g \u2022 z = (a c + b d) / (c^2 + d^2) + (d z - c) / ((c^2 + d^2) (c z + d))`\n which does not need to be decomposed depending on whether `c = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "modular_group.exists_row_one_eq_and_min_re", "description": "Given `z : \u210d` and a bottom row `(c,d)`, among the `g : SL(2,\u2124)` with this bottom row, minimize\n `|(g\u2022z).re|`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.basis_fun_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.std_basis_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.basis_fun", "description": "The basis on `\u03b7 \u2192 R` where the `i`th basis vector is `function.update 0 i 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.proj_std_basis_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.std_basis_same", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.std_basis", "description": "The standard basis of the product of `\u03c6`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coe_std_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.proj_comp_std_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ker_std_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.infi_ker_proj_le_supr_range_std_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.supr_range_std_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.std_basis_eq_std_basis_matrix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.proj_std_basis_same", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.basis_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.std_basis_eq_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.basis_fun_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.disjoint_std_basis_std_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.basis_repr_std_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.basis_fun_equiv_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.supr_range_std_basis_le_infi_ker_proj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.std_basis_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.linear_independent_std_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.std_basis_eq_pi_diag", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.supr_range_std_basis_eq_infi_ker_proj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.basis", "description": " `pi.basis (s : \u2200 j, basis (\u03b9s j) R (Ms j))` is the `\u03a3 j, \u03b9s j`-indexed basis on `\u03a0 j, Ms j`\ngiven by `s j` on each component.\n\nFor the standard basis over `R` on the finite-dimensional space `\u03b7 \u2192 R` see `pi.basis_fun`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.basis_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.std_basis", "description": "The standard basis of `matrix m n R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.std_basis_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.lex.is_strict_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.is_trichotomous_lex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.to_lex_strict_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.lex_lt_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.lt_to_lex_update_self_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.lex.linear_order", "description": "`\u03a0\u2097 i, \u03b1 i` is a linear order if the original order is well-founded.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.lex.order_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.lex.no_max_order'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.to_lex_update_le_self_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.to_lex_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.lex.ordered_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.lex.densely_ordered", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.lex_lt_of_lt_of_preorder", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.of_lex_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.lex", "description": "The lexicographic relation on `\u03a0 i : \u03b9, \u03b2 i`, where `\u03b9` is ordered by `r`,\n and each `\u03b2 i` is ordered by `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.lex.ordered_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.to_lex_update_lt_self_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.lex_desc", "description": " If we swap two strictly decreasing values in a function, then the result is lexicographically\nsmaller than the original function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.lex.partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.lex.bounded_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.le_to_lex_update_self_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.lex.order_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.lex.no_max_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.lex.no_min_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.lex.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.lex.has_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.to_lex_monotone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.norm_extend_to_\ud835\udd5c'_apply_sq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.extend_to_\ud835\udd5c'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.extend_to_\ud835\udd5c_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.extend_to_\ud835\udd5c", "description": "Extend `fr : restrict_scalars \u211d \ud835\udd5c F \u2192\u2097[\u211d] \u211d` to `F \u2192\u2097[\ud835\udd5c] \ud835\udd5c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.norm_extend_to_\ud835\udd5c'_bound", "description": "The norm of the extension is bounded by `\u2016fr\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.extend_to_\ud835\udd5c'", "description": "Extend `fr : F \u2192L[\u211d] \u211d` to `F \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] \ud835\udd5c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.extend_to_\ud835\udd5c'", "description": " Extend `fr : F \u2192\u2097[\u211d] \u211d` to `F \u2192\u2097[\ud835\udd5c] \ud835\udd5c` in a way that will also be continuous and have its norm\nbounded by `\u2016fr\u2016` if `fr` is continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.extend_to_\ud835\udd5c_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.norm_extend_to_\ud835\udd5c'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.extend_to_\ud835\udd5c'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.extend_to_\ud835\udd5c'_apply_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.norm_extend_to_\ud835\udd5c", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.extend_to_\ud835\udd5c", "description": "Extend `fr : restrict_scalars \u211d \ud835\udd5c F \u2192L[\u211d] \u211d` to `F \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] \ud835\udd5c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.with_density_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.with_density.probability_theory.is_s_finite_kernel", "description": "For a s-finite kernel `\u03ba` and a function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 \u211d\u22650`, `with_density \u03ba f` is s-finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.is_s_finite_kernel.with_density", "description": " For a s-finite kernel `\u03ba` and a function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 \u211d\u22650\u221e` which is everywhere finite,\n`with_density \u03ba f` is s-finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.with_density_tsum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.integral_with_density", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.is_finite_kernel_with_density_of_bounded", "description": " If a kernel `\u03ba` is finite and a function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 \u211d\u22650\u221e` is bounded, then `with_density \u03ba f`\nis finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.with_density_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.with_density", "description": " Kernel with image `(\u03ba a).with_density (f a)` if `function.uncurry f` is measurable, and\nwith image 0 otherwise. If `function.uncurry f` is measurable, it satisfies\n`\u222b\u207b b, g b \u2202(with_density \u03ba f hf a) = \u222b\u207b b, f a b * g b \u2202(\u03ba a)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, 