ear_order.min_def", "description": " A conditionally complete linear order is a linear order in which\nevery nonempty subset which is bounded above has a supremum, and\nevery nonempty subset which is bounded below has an infimum.\nTypical examples are real numbers or natural numbers.\n\nTo differentiate the statements from the corresponding statements in (unconditional)\ncomplete linear orders, we prefix Inf and Sup by a c everywhere. The same statements should\nhold in both worlds, sometimes with additional assumptions of nonemptiness or\nboundedness.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_glb_cinfi_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cInf_pair", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_csupr_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_bot.conditionally_complete_lattice", "description": " Adding a bottom element to a conditionally complete lattice\ngives a conditionally complete lattice", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_top.supr_coe_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cInf_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.conditionally_complete_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_least.cInf_eq", "description": "A least element of a set is the infimum of this set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_top.Inf_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cInf_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cSup_eq_of_forall_le_of_forall_lt_exists_gt", "description": "Introduction rule to prove that `b` is the supremum of `s`: it suffices to check that `b`\nis larger than all elements of `s`, and that this is not the case of any `w<b`.\nSee `Sup_eq_of_forall_le_of_forall_lt_exists_gt` for a version in complete lattices.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cSup_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_mem_of_cSup_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cSup_le_cSup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_Icc_cInf_cSup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_between_of_forall_le", "description": " If all elements of a nonempty set `s` are less than or equal to all elements\nof a nonempty set `t`, then there exists an element between these sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Inf_eq_argmin_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_cSup_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.map_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_top.coe_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_top.has_Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_well_order.conditionally_complete_linear_order_bot", "description": "A well founded linear order is conditionally complete, with a bottom element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cInf_image2_eq_cSup_cInf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_glb_cInf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_lub.cSup_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conditionally_complete_linear_order.to_conditionally_complete_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.csupr_mem_Inter_Icc_of_antitone", "description": " Nested intervals lemma: if `f` is a monotone sequence, `g` is an antitone sequence, and\n`f n \u2264 g n` for all `n`, then `\u2a06 n, f n` belongs to all the intervals `[f n, g n]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_top.is_glb_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conditionally_complete_lattice_of_lattice_of_Inf", "description": "A version of `conditionally_complete_lattice_of_Inf` when we already know that `\u03b1` is a lattice.\n\nThis should only be used when it is both hard and unnecessary to provide `Sup` explicitly.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.u_cInf'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_cSup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cSup_image2_eq_cInf_cSup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Inf_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.map_cInf'", "description": "", "p": "mathli