l)\n - downward closed (any element less than an element of the ideal is in the ideal).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order.is_ideal.directed", "description": "A subset of a preorder `P` is an ideal if it is\n - nonempty\n - upward directed (any pair of elements in the ideal has an upper bound in the ideal)\n - downward closed (any element less than an element of the ideal is in the ideal).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order.ideal.inter_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order.ideal.coe_to_lower_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order.is_ideal.to_ideal", "description": " Create an element of type `order.ideal` from a set satisfying the predicate\n`order.is_ideal`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order.ideal.top_of_top_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order.ideal.principal", "description": "The smallest ideal containing a given element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order.ideal.mem_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order.ideal.has_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order.sequence_of_cofinals", "description": "Given a starting point, and a countable family of cofinal sets,\n this is an increasing sequence that intersects each cofinal set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order.cofinal", "description": "For a preorder `P`, `cofinal P` is the type of subsets of `P`\n containing arbitrarily large elements. They are the dense sets in\n the topology whose open sets are terminal segments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order.cofinal.carrier", "description": "For a preorder `P`, `cofinal P` is the type of subsets of `P`\n containing arbitrarily large elements. They are the dense sets in\n the topology whose open sets are terminal segments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order.cofinal.mem_gt", "description": "For a preorder `P`, `cofinal P` is the type of subsets of `P`\n containing arbitrarily large elements. They are the dense sets in\n the topology whose open sets are terminal segments.", "p":