raic_geometry.PresheafedSpace.colimit", "description": "Auxiliary definition for `PresheafedSpace.has_colimits`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.PresheafedSpace.colimit_cocone_is_colimit", "description": "Auxiliary definition for `PresheafedSpace.has_colimits`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.PresheafedSpace.colimit_cocone_\u03b9_app_base", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.PresheafedSpace.colimit_cocone_is_colimit.desc", "description": "Auxiliary definition for `PresheafedSpace.colimit_cocone_is_colimit`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.PresheafedSpace.forget.category_theory.limits.preserves_colimits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.PresheafedSpace.colimit_presheaf_obj_iso_componentwise_limit", "description": "The components of the colimit of a diagram of `PresheafedSpace C` is obtained\nvia taking componentwise limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.PresheafedSpace.colimit_presheaf_obj_iso_componentwise_limit_inv_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.PresheafedSpace.pushforward_diagram_to_colimit", "description": "Given a diagram of presheafed spaces,\nwe can push all the presheaves forward to the colimit `X` of the underlying topological spaces,\nobtaining a diagram in `(presheaf C X)\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.PresheafedSpace.componentwise_diagram", "description": "Given a diagram of `PresheafedSpace C`s, its colimit is computed by pushing the sheaves onto\nthe colimit of the underlying spaces, and taking componentwise limit.\nThis is the componentwise diagram for an open set `U` of the colimit of the underlying spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subrel.is_well_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_hom_class.map_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subrel", "description": "`subrel r p` is the inherited relation on a subset.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subrel.is_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subrel.is_irrefl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subrel_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_hom_class.map_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subrel.rel_embedding_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_embedding.cod_restrict_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_embedding.cod_restrict", "description": "Restrict the codomain of a relation embedding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subrel.is_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subrel.rel_embedding", "description": "The relation embedding from the inherited relation on a subset.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subrel.is_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_iso.range_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.types_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.hom_inv_id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor_to_types.hcomp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.types", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor_to_types.inv_hom_id_app_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.types_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_equiv_iso", "description": " Equivalences (between types in the same universe) are the same as (equivalent to) isomorphisms\nof types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.as_hom", "description": "`as_hom f` helps Lean type check a function as a morphism in the category `Type`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor_to_types.map_comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sort.split_epi_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.inv_hom_id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.to_iso", "description": "Any equivalence between types in the same universe gives\na categorical isomorphism between those types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.to_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.hom_of_element_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_equiv_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso.to_equiv_symm_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.surjective_of_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.types_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.types_comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_iso_iff_bijective", "description": "A morphism in `Type u` is an isomorphism if and only if it is bijective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_functor_trivial", "description": "The functor embedding `Type u` into `Type u` via `ulift` is isomorphic to the identity functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_trivial", "description": "The isomorphism between a `Type` which has been `ulift`ed to the same universe,\nand the original type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor_to_types.hom_inv_id_app_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective_of_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mono_iff_injective", "description": "A morphism in `Type` is a monomorphism if and only if it is injective.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/003C>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_iso_iso", "description": " Equivalences (between types in the same universe) are the same as (isomorphic to) isomorphisms\nof types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor_to_types.map_hom_map_inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.sections", "description": "The sections of a functor `J \u2964 Type` are\nthe choices of a point `u j : F.obj j` for each `j`,\nsuch that `F.map f (u j) = u j` for every morphism `f : j \u27f6 j'`.\n\nWe later use these to define limits in `Type` and in many concrete categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_equiv_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor_to_types.naturality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.epi_iff_surjective", "description": "A morphism in `Type` is an epimorphism if and only if it is surjective.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/003C>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.hom_of_element", "description": "Any term `x` of a type `X` corresponds to a morphism `punit \u27f6 X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_functor", "description": "The functor embedding `Type u` into `Type (max u v)`.\nWrite this as `ulift_functor.{5 2}` to get `Type 2 \u2964 Type 5`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor_to_types.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso.to_equiv_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor_to_types.map_id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.to_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.of_type_functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_functor_full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso.to_equiv_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.of_type_functor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor_to_types.map_inv_map_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso.to_equiv_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.iso.to_equiv", "description": "Any isomorphism between types gives an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.of_type_functor", "description": " `of_type_functor m` converts from Lean's `Type`-based `category` to `category_theory`. This\nallows us to use these functors in category theory.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_iso_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.types_id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv_iso_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_functor_faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.finite.to_finite_type", "description": "**Alias** of `ring_hom.finite_type.of_finite`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.support_gen_of_gen'", "description": " If a set `S` generates, as algebra, `add_monoid_algebra R M`, then the image of the union of\nthe supports of elements of `S` generates `add_monoid_algebra R M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.mem_adjoin_support", "description": "An element of `add_monoid_algebra R M` is in the subalgebra generated by its support.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module_polynomial_of_endo.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.mem_adjoin_support", "description": "An element of `monoid_algebra R M` is in the subalgebra generated by its support.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.finite_type.of_comp_finite_type", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.finite_type.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.fg_of_finite_type", "description": "If `add_monoid_algebra R M` is of finite type then `M` is finitely generated.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.finite_type.of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.finite_type.id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.mv_polynomial_aeval_of_surjective_of_closure", "description": " If a set `S` generates an additive monoid `M`, then the image of `M` generates, as algebra,\n`add_monoid_algebra R M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.finite.finite_type", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.mem_closure_of_mem_span_closure", "description": "If the image of an element `m : M` in `monoid_algebra R M` belongs the submodule generated by the\nclosure of some `S : set M` then `m \u2208 closure S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.finite_type.prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.finite_type_iff_group_fg", "description": " An additive group `G` is finitely generated if and only if `add_monoid_algebra R G` is of\nfinite type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.finite.finite_type", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.finite_type.self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.finite_type.of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.finite_type_iff_fg", "description": "A monoid `M` is finitely generated if and only if `monoid_algebra R M` is of finite type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.mem_closure_of_mem_span_closure", "description": "If the image of an element `m : M` in `add_monoid_algebra R M` belongs the submodule generated by\nthe closure of some `S : set M` then `m \u2208 closure S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.finite_type", "description": " An algebra over a commutative semiring is of `finite_type` if it is finitely generated\nover the base ring as algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.finite_type.out", "description": " An algebra over a commutative semiring is of `finite_type` if it is finitely generated\nover the base ring as algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.finite_type_of_fg", "description": " If an additive monoid `M` is finitely generated then `add_monoid_algebra R M` is of finite\ntype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.finite_type.iff_quotient_mv_polynomial", "description": " An algebra is finitely generated if and only if it is a quotient\nof a polynomial ring whose variables are indexed by a finset.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.finite_type_iff_fg", "description": " An additive monoid `M` is finitely generated if and only if `add_monoid_algebra R M` is of\nfinite type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.finite_type.iff_quotient_mv_polynomial''", "description": " An algebra is finitely generated if and only if it is a quotient of a polynomial ring in `n`\nvariables.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.finite_type.mv_polynomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.finite_type.polynomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.finite_type.iff_quotient_mv_polynomial'", "description": " An algebra is finitely generated if and only if it is a quotient\nof a polynomial ring whose variables are indexed by a fintype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.of'_mem_span", "description": " The image of an element `m : M` in `add_monoid_algebra R M` belongs the submodule generated by\n`S : set M` if and only if `m \u2208 S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.finite_type.of_comp_finite_type", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.finite_type_iff_group_fg", "description": "A group `G` is finitely generated if and only if `add_monoid_algebra R G` is of finite type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.finite_type.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.finite_type.id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.finite.finite_type", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.of_mem_span_of_iff", "description": " The image of an element `m : M` in `monoid_algebra R M` belongs the submodule generated by\n`S : set M` if and only if `m \u2208 S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.exists_finset_adjoin_eq_top", "description": " If `add_monoid_algebra R M` is of finite type, there there is a `G : finset M` such that its\nimage generates, as algera, `add_monoid_algebra R M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.support_gen_of_gen", "description": " If a set `S` generates, as algebra, `monoid_algebra R M`, then the set of supports of elements\nof `S` generates `monoid_algebra R M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module_polynomial_of_endo_smul_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.mv_polynomial_aeval_of_surjective_of_closure", "description": " If a set `S` generates a monoid `M`, then the image of `M` generates, as algebra,\n`monoid_algebra R M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.finite_type", "description": "A ring morphism `A \u2192+* B` is of `finite_type` if `B` is finitely generated as `A`-algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.fg_of_finite_type", "description": "If `monoid_algebra R M` is of finite type then `M` is finitely generated.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.finite_type.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.exists_finset_adjoin_eq_top", "description": " If `monoid_algebra R M` is of finite type, there there is a `G : finset M` such that its image\ngenerates, as algera, `monoid_algebra R M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.finite_type.of_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.finite_type.comp_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.support_gen_of_gen", "description": " If a set `S` generates, as algebra, `add_monoid_algebra R M`, then the set of supports of\nelements of `S` generates `add_monoid_algebra R M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.finite_type_of_fg", "description": "If a monoid `M` is finitely generated then `monoid_algebra R M` is of finite type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.finite_type.equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.finite.injective_of_surjective_endomorphism", "description": " A theorem/proof by Vasconcelos, given a finite module `M` over a commutative ring, any\nsurjective endomorphism of `M` is also injective. Based on,\nhttps://math.stackexchange.com/a/239419/31917,\nhttps://www.ams.org/journals/tran/1969-138-00/S0002-9947-1969-0238839-5/.\nThis is similar to `is_noetherian.injective_of_surjective_endomorphism` but only applies in the\ncommutative case, but does not use a Noetherian hypothesis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.finite_type.comp_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.finite_type.of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module_polynomial_of_endo", "description": " The structure of a module `M` over a ring `R` as a module over `R[X]` when given a\nchoice of how `X` acts by choosing a linear map `f : M \u2192\u2097[R] M`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.finite_type.is_noetherian_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.fg_iff_finite_type", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.finite_type.of_restrict_scalars_finite_type", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.finite_type", "description": " An algebra morphism `A \u2192\u2090[R] B` is of `finite_type` if it is of finite type as ring morphism.\nIn other words, if `B` is finitely generated as `A`-algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_algebra.support_gen_of_gen'", "description": " If a set `S` generates, as algebra, `monoid_algebra R M`, then the image of the union of the\nsupports of elements of `S` generates `monoid_algebra R M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.of_digits_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.of_digits_lt_base_pow_length'", "description": "an n-digit number in base b + 2 is less than (b + 2)^n", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.dvd_iff_dvd_of_digits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.le_digits_len_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_def'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.eleven_dvd_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.norm_digits.eval_aux", "description": "Helper function for the `norm_digits` tactic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.of_digits_zmodeq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_eq_nil_iff_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.norm_digits.digits_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_lt_base", "description": "The digits in the base b expansion of n are all less than b, if b \u2265 2", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_len_le_digits_len_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_lt_base'", "description": "The digits in the base b+2 expansion of n are all less than b+2", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq_nine_digits_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.of_digits_zmod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.of_digits_lt_base_pow_length", "description": "an n-digit number in base b is less than b^n if b > 1", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.of_digits_digits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_add_two_add_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.of_digits_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.of_digits_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.base_pow_length_digits_le'", "description": "Any non-zero natural number `m` is greater than\n(b+2)^((number of digits in the base (b+2) representation of m) - 1)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.eleven_dvd_of_palindrome", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_aux_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq_digits_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.lt_base_pow_length_digits", "description": "Any number m is less than b^(number of digits in the base b representation of m)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pow_length_le_mul_of_digits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.of_digits_eq_sum_map_with_index_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.lt_base_pow_length_digits'", "description": "Any number m is less than (b+2)^(number of digits in the base b + 2 representation of m)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.last_digit_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_aux_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.of_digits_eq_foldr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.nine_dvd_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.of_digits_neg_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.coe_of_digits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_aux_0", "description": "(Impl.) An auxiliary definition for `digits`, to help get the desired definitional unfolding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.of_digits", "description": "`of_digits b L` takes a list `L` of natural numbers, and interprets them\nas a number in semiring, as the little-endian digits in base `b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_ne_nil_iff_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.norm_digits.eval", "description": "A tactic for normalizing expressions of the form `nat.digits a b = l` where\n`a` and `b` are numerals.\n\n```lean\nexample : nat.digits 10 123 = [3,2,1] := by norm_num\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_one_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_of_digits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_eq_cons_digits_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_inj_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.base_pow_length_digits_le", "description": "Any non-zero natural number `m` is greater than\nb^((number of digits in the base b representation of m) - 1)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_zero_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_zero_of_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits.injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq_eleven_digits_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_aux", "description": "(Impl.) An auxiliary definition for `digits`, to help get the desired definitional unfolding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.dvd_iff_dvd_digits_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_two_eq_bits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.of_digits_one_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.coe_int_of_digits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.of_digits_modeq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.of_digits_eq_sum_map_with_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.three_dvd_iff", "description": "**Divisibility by 3 Rule**", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.zmodeq_of_digits_digits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_aux_1", "description": "(Impl.) An auxiliary definition for `digits`, to help get the desired definitional unfolding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits", "description": "`digits b n` gives the digits, in little-endian order,\nof a natural number `n` in a specified base `b`.\n\nIn any base, we have `of_digits b L = L.foldr (\u03bb x y, x + b * y) 0`.\n* For any `2 \u2264 b`, we have `l < b` for any `l \u2208 digits b n`,\n  and the last digit is not zero.\n  This uniquely specifies the behaviour of `digits b`.\n* For `b = 1`, we define `digits 1 n = list.replicate n 1`.\n* For `b = 0`, we define `digits 0 n = [n]`, except `digits 0 0 = []`.\n\nNote this differs from the existing `nat.to_digits` in core, which is used for printing numerals.\nIn particular, `nat.to_digits b 0 = [0]`, while `digits b 0 = []`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.of_digits_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_last", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_zero_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.of_digits_digits_append_digits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.norm_digits.digits_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.dvd_of_digits_sub_of_digits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.modeq_three_digits_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_zero_succ'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.of_digits_zmodeq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.digits_len", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.of_digits_modeq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.eq_one_of_roots_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.continuous_within_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.tendsto_norm_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.continuous_aeval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.exists_forall_norm_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.tendsto_abv_eval\u2082_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.continuous_eval\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.continuous_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.continuous_on_aeval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_bdd_of_roots_le", "description": " The coefficients of the monic polynomials of bounded degree with bounded roots are\nuniformely bounded.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.continuous_within_at_aeval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.continuous_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_le_of_roots_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.tendsto_abv_aeval_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.tendsto_abv_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.continuous_at_aeval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.prod_\u03b5", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.prod", "description": "The cartesian product of two monoidal functors is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_inverse", "description": "If a monoidal functor `F` is an equivalence of categories then its inverse is also monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.comm_tensor_left_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.comp_to_lax_monoidal_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor", "description": " A lax monoidal functor is a functor `F : C \u2964 D` between monoidal categories,\nequipped with morphisms `\u03b5 : \ud835\udfd9 _D \u27f6 F.obj (\ud835\udfd9_ C)` and `\u03bc X Y : F.obj X \u2297 F.obj Y \u27f6 F.obj (X \u2297 Y)`,\nsatisfying the appropriate coherences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.to_functor", "description": " A lax monoidal functor is a functor `F : C \u2964 D` between monoidal categories,\nequipped with morphisms `\u03b5 : \ud835\udfd9 _D \u27f6 F.obj (\ud835\udfd9_ C)` and `\u03bc X Y : F.obj X \u2297 F.obj Y \u27f6 F.obj (X \u2297 Y)`,\nsatisfying the appropriate coherences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.\u03b5", "description": " A lax monoidal functor is a functor `F : C \u2964 D` between monoidal categories,\nequipped with morphisms `\u03b5 : \ud835\udfd9 _D \u27f6 F.obj (\ud835\udfd9_ C)` and `\u03bc X Y : F.obj X \u2297 F.obj Y \u27f6 F.obj (X \u2297 Y)`,\nsatisfying the appropriate coherences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.\u03bc", "description": " A lax monoidal functor is a functor `F : C \u2964 D` between monoidal categories,\nequipped with morphisms `\u03b5 : \ud835\udfd9 _D \u27f6 F.obj (\ud835\udfd9_ C)` and `\u03bc X Y : F.obj X \u2297 F.obj Y \u27f6 F.obj (X \u2297 Y)`,\nsatisfying the appropriate coherences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.\u03bc_natural'", "description": " A lax monoidal functor is a functor `F : C \u2964 D` between monoidal categories,\nequipped with morphisms `\u03b5 : \ud835\udfd9 _D \u27f6 F.obj (\ud835\udfd9_ C)` and `\u03bc X Y : F.obj X \u2297 F.obj Y \u27f6 F.obj (X \u2297 Y)`,\nsatisfying the appropriate coherences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.associativity'", "description": " A lax monoidal functor is a functor `F : C \u2964 D` between monoidal categories,\nequipped with morphisms `\u03b5 : \ud835\udfd9 _D \u27f6 F.obj (\ud835\udfd9_ C)` and `\u03bc X Y : F.obj X \u2297 F.obj Y \u27f6 F.obj (X \u2297 Y)`,\nsatisfying the appropriate coherences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.left_unitality'", "description": " A lax monoidal functor is a functor `F : C \u2964 D` between monoidal categories,\nequipped with morphisms `\u03b5 : \ud835\udfd9 _D \u27f6 F.obj (\ud835\udfd9_ C)` and `\u03bc X Y : F.obj X \u2297 F.obj Y \u27f6 F.obj (X \u2297 Y)`,\nsatisfying the appropriate coherences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.right_unitality'", "description": " A lax monoidal functor is a functor `F : C \u2964 D` between monoidal categories,\nequipped with morphisms `\u03b5 : \ud835\udfd9 _D \u27f6 F.obj (\ud835\udfd9_ C)` and `\u03bc X Y : F.obj X \u2297 F.obj Y \u27f6 F.obj (X \u2297 Y)`,\nsatisfying the appropriate coherences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.id_\u03bc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.\u03bc_iso", "description": "The tensorator of a (strong) monoidal functor as an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.diag", "description": "The diagonal functor as a monoidal functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.id", "description": "The identity lax monoidal functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.right_unitality_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.prod_to_lax_monoidal_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.\u03bc_natural_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.prod'_\u03bc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.associativity_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.comm_tensor_left", "description": "Monoidal functors commute with left tensoring up to isomorphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.\u03bc_inv_hom_id_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_adjoint_to_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.right_unitality_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.id_\u03b5", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.diag_to_lax_monoidal_functor_\u03bc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_adjoint_\u03bc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.comp_\u03b5", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.comm_tensor_left_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.left_unitality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.\u03bc_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.comp_to_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.prod_\u03bc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.\u03bc_inv_hom_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.prod'", "description": "The cartesian product of two monoidal functors starting from the same monoidal category `C`\n   is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.id", "description": "The identity monoidal functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.id_to_lax_monoidal_functor_\u03b5", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.prod'_to_lax_monoidal_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.associativity_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.id_to_lax_monoidal_functor_\u03bc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.id_to_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.comp", "description": "The composition of two lax monoidal functors is again lax monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.prod", "description": "The cartesian product of two lax monoidal functors is lax monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor", "description": "A monoidal functor is a lax monoidal functor for which the tensorator and unitor as isomorphisms.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FFL>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.to_lax_monoidal_functor", "description": "A monoidal functor is a lax monoidal functor for which the tensorator and unitor as isomorphisms.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FFL>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.\u03b5_is_iso", "description": "A monoidal functor is a lax monoidal functor for which the tensorator and unitor as isomorphisms.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FFL>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.\u03bc_is_iso", "description": "A monoidal functor is a lax monoidal functor for which the tensorator and unitor as isomorphisms.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FFL>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.right_unitality", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.comm_tensor_right_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.prod_to_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_inverse_to_lax_monoidal_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.\u03bc_hom_inv_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.id_to_lax_monoidal_functor_to_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.left_unitality_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.prod'_to_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.comp_\u03bc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.comm_tensor_right", "description": "Monoidal functors commute with right tensoring up to isomorphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_adjoint_\u03b5", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.\u03b5_inv_hom_id_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.prod'", "description": "The cartesian product of two lax monoidal functors starting from the same monoidal category `C`\n   is lax monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.associativity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.comp", "description": "The composition of two monoidal functors is again monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.prod'_\u03b5", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.comm_tensor_right_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.map_tensor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.map_left_unitor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.\u03b5_inv_hom_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.\u03bc_nat_iso", "description": "The tensorator as a natural isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.associativity_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.diag_to_lax_monoidal_functor_\u03b5", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.map_right_unitor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.diag_to_lax_monoidal_functor_to_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.\u03bc_natural", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.\u03b5_hom_inv_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_adjoint", "description": "If we have a right adjoint functor `G` to a monoidal functor `F`, then `G` has a lax monoidal\nstructure as well.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.\u03b5_iso", "description": "The unit morphism of a (strong) monoidal functor as an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lax_monoidal_functor.left_unitality_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_functor.\u03b5_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fundamental_groupoid.to_top", "description": " Help the typechecker by converting a point in a groupoid back to a point in\nthe underlying topological space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.refl_trans_symm_aux", "description": "Auxilliary function for `refl_trans_symm`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.trans_assoc_reparam_aux_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.trans_refl_reparam_aux_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fundamental_groupoid.to_path", "description": " Help the typechecker by converting an arrow in the fundamental groupoid of\na topological space back to a path in that space (i.e., `path.homotopic.quotient`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.trans_refl_reparam_aux", "description": "Auxilliary function for `trans_refl_reparam`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fundamental_groupoid.comp_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.trans_refl_reparam_aux_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fundamental_groupoid.fundamental_groupoid_functor", "description": "The functor sending a topological space `X` to its fundamental groupoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.trans_assoc_reparam_aux_mem_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.refl_trans_symm", "description": "For any path `p` from `x\u2080` to `x\u2081`, we have a homotopy from the constant path based at `x\u2080` to\n `p.trans p.symm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.continuous_trans_assoc_reparam_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.trans_assoc_reparam_aux", "description": "Auxilliary function for `trans_assoc_reparam`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.refl_symm_trans", "description": "For any path `p` from `x\u2080` to `x\u2081`, we have a homotopy from the constant path based at `x\u2081` to\n `p.symm.trans p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fundamental_groupoid.id_eq_path_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.continuous_refl_trans_symm_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.trans_refl", "description": "For any path `p` from `x\u2080` to `x\u2081`, we have a homotopy from `p.trans (path.refl x\u2081)` to `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.continuous_trans_refl_reparam_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.trans_refl_reparam_aux_mem_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.trans_refl_reparam", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fundamental_groupoid", "description": "The fundamental groupoid of a space `X` is defined to be a type synonym for `X`, and we subsequently\nput a `category_theory.groupoid` structure on it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fundamental_groupoid.category_theory.groupoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.trans_assoc_reparam", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fundamental_groupoid.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.refl_trans_symm_aux_mem_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.trans_assoc", "description": "For paths `p q r`, we have a homotopy from `(p.trans q).trans r` to `p.trans (q.trans r)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.trans_assoc_reparam_aux_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "path.homotopy.refl_trans", "description": "For any path `p` from `x\u2080` to `x\u2081`, we have a homotopy from `(path.refl x\u2080).trans p` to `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fundamental_groupoid.map_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fundamental_groupoid.from_top", "description": " Help the typechecker by converting a point in a topological space to a\npoint in the fundamental groupoid of that space", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fundamental_groupoid.from_path", "description": " Help the typechecker by convering a path in a topological space to an arrow in the\nfundamental groupoid of that space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_monoid_morphism", "description": "Morphism of smooth monoids.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_monoid_morphism.to_monoid_hom", "description": "Morphism of smooth monoids.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_monoid_morphism.smooth_to_fun", "description": "Morphism of smooth monoids.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_within_at_finset_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_add_of_smooth", "description": "If the addition is smooth, then it is continuous. This is not an instance for technical reasons,\nsee note [Design choices about smooth algebraic structures].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_left_mul_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_within_at_finset_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_finsum_cond", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_at.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_finset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_at_finset_sum'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_finset_sum'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_right_mul_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_left_mul", "description": " Left multiplication by `g`. It is meant to mimic the usual notation in Lie groups.\nLemmas involving `smooth_left_mul` with the notation `\ud835\udc73` usually use `L` instead of `\ud835\udc73` in the\nnames.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_on_finset_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_finsum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_smooth_add.sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_add_monoid_morphism.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_add_monoid_morphism.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_finset_sum'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_within_at.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_on_finset_sum'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_at_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_smooth_add", "description": " Basic hypothesis to talk about a smooth (Lie) additive monoid or a smooth additive\nsemigroup. A smooth additive monoid over `\u03b1`, for example, is obtained by requiring both the\ninstances `add_monoid \u03b1` and `has_smooth_add \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_smooth_add.to_smooth_manifold_with_corners", "description": " Basic hypothesis to talk about a smooth (Lie) additive monoid or a smooth additive\nsemigroup. A smooth additive monoid over `\u03b1`, for example, is obtained by requiring both the\ninstances `add_monoid \u03b1` and `has_smooth_add \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_smooth_add.smooth_add", "description": " Basic hypothesis to talk about a smooth (Lie) additive monoid or a smooth additive\nsemigroup. A smooth additive monoid over `\u03b1`, for example, is obtained by requiring both the\ninstances `add_monoid \u03b1` and `has_smooth_add \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_at_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_on.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_within_at.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_smooth_mul", "description": " Basic hypothesis to talk about a smooth (Lie) monoid or a smooth semigroup.\nA smooth monoid over `G`, for example, is obtained by requiring both the instances `monoid G`\nand `has_smooth_mul I G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_smooth_mul.to_smooth_manifold_with_corners", "description": " Basic hypothesis to talk about a smooth (Lie) monoid or a smooth semigroup.\nA smooth monoid over `G`, for example, is obtained by requiring both the instances `monoid G`\nand `has_smooth_mul I G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_smooth_mul.smooth_mul", "description": " Basic hypothesis to talk about a smooth (Lie) monoid or a smooth semigroup.\nA smooth monoid over `G`, for example, is obtained by requiring both the instances `monoid G`\nand `has_smooth_mul I G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_within_at_finset_sum'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_within_at_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_smooth_add_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_finset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_on_finset_sum'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_within_at.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_monoid_morphism.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_right_mul", "description": " Right multiplication by `g`. It is meant to mimic the usual notation in Lie groups.\nLemmas involving `smooth_right_mul` with the notation `\ud835\udc79` usually use `R` instead of `\ud835\udc79` in the\nnames.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_smooth_mul.prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "L_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_finprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_within_at_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_at_finset_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_mul_of_smooth", "description": " If the multiplication is smooth, then it is continuous. This is not an instance for technical\nreasons, see note [Design choices about smooth algebraic structures].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_add_monoid_morphism.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_within_at_finset_sum'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_at_finset_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_finprod_cond", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_finprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "L_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_on.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_on_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_at.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_on.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_at.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_finsum_cond", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_at.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "R_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_at_finset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_on_finset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_within_at_finset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "R_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_finset_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_finset_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "library_note.Design choices about smooth algebraic structures", "description": "1. All smooth algebraic structures on `G` are `Prop`-valued classes that extend\n`smooth_manifold_with_corners I G`. This way we save users from adding both\n`[smooth_manifold_with_corners I G]` and `[has_smooth_mul I G]` to the assumptions. While many API\nlemmas hold true without the `smooth_manifold_with_corners I G` assumption, we're not aware of a\nmathematically interesting monoid on a topological manifold such that (a) the space is not a\n`smooth_manifold_with_corners`; (b) the multiplication is smooth at `(a, b)` in the charts\n`ext_chart_at I a`, `ext_chart_at I b`, `ext_chart_at I (a * b)`.\n\n2. Because of `model_prod` we can't assume, e.g., that a `lie_group` is modelled on `\ud835\udcd8(\ud835\udd5c, E)`. So,\nwe formulate the definitions and lemmas for any model.\n\n3. While smoothness of an operation implies its continuity, lemmas like\n`has_continuous_mul_of_smooth` can't be instances becausen otherwise Lean would have to search for\n`has_smooth_mul I G` with unknown `\ud835\udd5c`, `E`, `H`, and `I : model_with_corners \ud835\udd5c E H`. If users needs\n`[has_continuous_mul G]` in a proof about a smooth monoid, then they need to either add\n`[has_continuous_mul G]` as an assumption (worse) or use `haveI` in the proof (better).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_on_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_on.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_monoid_morphism.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_finprod_cond", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_within_at.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_at_finset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_finsum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_within_at_finset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_monoid_morphism.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_add_monoid_morphism", "description": "Morphism of additive smooth monoids.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_add_monoid_morphism.to_add_monoid_hom", "description": "Morphism of additive smooth monoids.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_add_monoid_morphism.smooth_to_fun", "description": "Morphism of additive smooth monoids.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_on_finset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_at_finset_sum'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_on_finset_prod'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slope_fun_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slope_same", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sub_div_sub_smul_slope_add_sub_div_sub_smul_slope", "description": " `slope f a c` is a linear combination of `slope f a b` and `slope f b c`. This version\nexplicitly provides coefficients. If `a \u2260 c`, then the sum of the coefficients is `1`, so it is\nactually an affine combination, see `line_map_slope_slope_sub_div_sub`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slope_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_of_slope_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.slope_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slope_def_module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slope_sub_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slope_fun_def_field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sub_smul_slope_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slope_def_field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map.slope_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "line_map_slope_slope_sub_div_sub", "description": " `slope f a c` is an affine combination of `slope f a b` and `slope f b c`. This version uses\n`line_map` to express this property.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slope_vadd_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "slope", "description": " `slope f a b = (b - a)\u207b\u00b9 \u2022 (f b -\u1d65 f a)` is the slope of a function `f` on the interval\n`[a, b]`. Note that `slope f a a = 0`, not the derivative of `f` at `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "line_map_slope_line_map_slope_line_map", "description": " `slope f a b` is an affine combination of `slope f a (line_map a b r)` and\n`slope f (line_map a b r) b`. We use `line_map` to express this property.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sub_smul_slope", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_neg_add_units_lift_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_units_lift_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_add_units_lift_symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.add_units_lift", "description": "Equivalence between continuous maps into the additive units of an additive monoid\nwith continuous addition and the additive units of the additive monoid of continuous maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_neg_add_units_lift_symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.units_of_forall_is_unit_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_inv_units_lift_symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.units_of_forall_is_unit", "description": " Construct a continuous map into the group of units of a normed ring from a function into the\nnormed ring and a proof that every element of the range is a unit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.can_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_units_lift_symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_inv_units_lift_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_ring.is_unit_unit_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_add_units_lift_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.units_lift", "description": " Equivalence between continuous maps into the units of a monoid with continuous multiplication\nand the units of the monoid of continuous maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.is_unit_iff_forall_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.is_unit_iff_forall_is_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.spectrum_eq_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cochain_complex.single\u2080.category_theory.faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.single\u2080_map_f_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cochain_complex.single\u2080_map_f_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cochain_complex.single\u2080_obj_X_d_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.single_obj_X_self_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cochain_complex.homology_functor_succ_single\u2080", "description": "Sending objects to cochain complexes supported at `0` then taking `(n+1)`-st homology\nis the same as the zero functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.from_single\u2080_equiv", "description": "Morphisms from a single object chain complex with `X` concentrated in degree 0\nto a `\u2115`-indexed chain complex `C` are the same as morphisms `f : X \u2192 C.X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.to_single\u2080_equiv_symm_apply_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cochain_complex.single\u2080.category_theory.full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.single_obj_X_self_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.to_single\u2080_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.single\u2080", "description": "`chain_complex.single\u2080 V` is the embedding of `V` into `chain_complex V \u2115`\nas chain complexes supported in degree 0.\n\nThis is naturally isomorphic to `single V _ 0`, but has better definitional properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.single_map_f_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.single\u2080_iso_single", "description": "`single\u2080` is the same as `single V _ 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.single\u2080.category_theory.faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cochain_complex.homology_functor_0_single\u2080", "description": "Sending objects to cochain complexes supported at `0` then taking `0`-th homology\nis the same as doing nothing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.single\u2080_obj_X_d_to", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.from_single\u2080_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cochain_complex.single\u2080_obj_X_d_from", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.single_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.single", "description": "The functor `V \u2964 homological_complex V c` creating a chain complex supported in a single degree.\n\nSee also `chain_complex.single\u2080 : V \u2964 chain_complex V \u2115`,\nwhich has better definitional properties,\nif you are working with `\u2115`-indexed complexes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cochain_complex.single\u2080", "description": "`cochain_complex.single\u2080 V` is the embedding of `V` into `cochain_complex V \u2115`\nas cochain complexes supported in degree 0.\n\nThis is naturally isomorphic to `single V _ 0`, but has better definitional properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.single_obj_X_self", "description": "The object in degree `j` of `(single V c h).obj A` is just `A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.single\u2080_obj_X_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.single_obj_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.to_single\u2080_equiv", "description": "Morphisms from a `\u2115`-indexed chain complex `C`\nto a single object chain complex with `X` concentrated in degree 0\nare the same as morphisms `f : C.X 0 \u27f6 X` such that `C.d 1 0 \u226b f = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.single\u2080_map_f_0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.single\u2080_obj_X_0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cochain_complex.single\u2080_map_f_0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cochain_complex.single\u2080_obj_X_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.single\u2080.category_theory.full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cochain_complex.single\u2080_obj_X_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.single.category_theory.full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.homology_functor_0_single\u2080", "description": "Sending objects to chain complexes supported at `0` then taking `0`-th homology\nis the same as doing nothing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.single.category_theory.faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.to_single\u2080_equiv_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.from_single\u2080_equiv_symm_apply_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.single\u2080_obj_X_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cochain_complex.from_single\u2080_equiv", "description": "Morphisms from a single object cochain complex with `X` concentrated in degree 0\nto a `\u2115`-indexed cochain complex `C`\nare the same as morphisms `f : X \u27f6 C.X 0` such that `f \u226b C.d 0 1 = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.single\u2080_obj_X_d_from", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.single_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cochain_complex.single\u2080_obj_X_0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cochain_complex.single\u2080_iso_single", "description": "`single\u2080` is the same as `single V _ 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "chain_complex.homology_functor_succ_single\u2080", "description": "Sending objects to chain complexes supported at `0` then taking `(n+1)`-st homology\nis the same as the zero functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.product_unique_iso",