"mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_coproducts", "description": "An abbreviation for `\u03a0 J, has_colimits_of_shape (discrete J) C`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pi.lift", "description": "A collection of morphisms `P \u27f6 f b` induces a morphism `P \u27f6 \u220f f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coproduct_is_coproduct", "description": "The cofan constructed of the inclusions from the coproduct is colimiting.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.sigma.\u03b9", "description": "The `b`-th inclusion into the sigma object over `f` has the form `f b \u27f6 \u2210 f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coproduct_unique_iso", "description": "A coproduct over a index type with exactly one term is just the object over that term.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_product_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.sigma.map", "description": "Construct a morphism between categorical coproducts (indexed by the same type)\nfrom a family of morphisms between the factors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fan.mk", "description": "A fan over `f : \u03b2 \u2192 C` consists of a collection of maps from an object `P` to every `f b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pi_comparison", "description": " The comparison morphism for the product of `f`. This is an iso iff `G` preserves the product\nof `f`, see `preserves_product.of_iso_comparison`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit_cocone_of_unique_is_colimit_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.\u03b9_comp_sigma_comparison", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mk_fan_limit_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_products_of_shape", "description": "An abbreviation for `has_limits_of_shape (discrete f)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit_cone_of_unique_cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fan.proj", "description": "Get the `j`th map in the fan", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coproduct_unique_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.product_unique_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_products", "description": "An abbreviation for `\u03a0 J, has_limits_of_shape (discrete J) C`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit_cocone_of_unique", "description": "The colimit cocone for the coproduct over an index type with exactly one term.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.sigma.reindex", "description": "Reindex a categorical coproduct via an equivalence of the index types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.coproduct_unique_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pi.map", "description": "Construct a morphism between categorical products (indexed by the same type)\nfrom a family of morphisms between the factors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pi_obj", "description": " `pi_obj f` computes the product of a family of elements `f`.\n(It is defined as an abbreviation for `limit (discrete.functor f)`,\nso for most facts about `pi_obj f`, you will just use general facts about limits.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.fan", "description": "A fan over `f : \u03b2 \u2192 C` consists of a collection of maps from an object `P` to every `f b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit_cone_of_unique", "description": "The limit cone for the product over an index type with exactly one term.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofan.mk_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_product", "description": "An abbreviation for `has_limit (discrete.functor f)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofan", "description": "A cofan over `f : \u03b2 \u2192 C` consists of a collection of maps from every `f b` to an object `P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.sigma.map_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.product_unique_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.mk_fan_limit", "description": "Make a fan `f` into a limit fan by providing `lift`, `fac`, and `uniq` --\n just a convenience lemma to avoid having to go through `discrete`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.sigma.desc", "description": "A collection of morphisms `f b \u27f6 P` induces a morphism `\u2210 f \u27f6 P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit_cocone_of_unique_cocone_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pi.reindex_hom_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofan.mk_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.sigma_obj", "description": " `sigma_obj f` computes the coproduct of a family of elements `f`.\n(It is defined as an abbreviation for `colimit (discrete.functor f)`,\nso for most facts about `sigma_obj f`, you will just use general facts about colimits.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cofan.mk", "description": "A cofan over `f : \u03b2 \u2192 C` consists of a collection of maps from every `f b` to an object `P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.indicator_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.indicator_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.indicator_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.indicator", "description": "Create an element of `\u03b9 \u2192\u2080 \u03b1` from a finset `s` and a function `f` defined on this finset.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.single_eq_indicator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.support_indicator_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.indicator_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof", "description": " This structure holds arguments of the Picard-Lipschitz (Cauchy-Lipschitz) theorem. It is part of\nthe internal API for convenience, so as not to constantly invoke choice. Unless you want to use one\nof the auxiliary lemmas, use `exists_forall_deriv_within_Icc_eq_of_lipschitz_of_continuous` instead\nof using this structure.\n\nThe similarly named `is_picard_lindelof` is a bundled `Prop` holding the long hypotheses of the\nPicard-Lindel\u00f6f theorem as named arguments. It is used as part of the public API.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.to_fun", "description": " This structure holds arguments of the Picard-Lipschitz (Cauchy-Lipschitz) theorem. It is part of\nthe internal API for convenience, so as not to constantly invoke choice. Unless you want to use one\nof the auxiliary lemmas, use `exists_forall_deriv_within_Icc_eq_of_lipschitz_of_continuous` instead\nof using this structure.\n\nThe similarly named `is_picard_lindelof` is a bundled `Prop` holding the long hypotheses of the\nPicard-Lindel\u00f6f theorem as named arguments. It is used as part of the public API.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.t_min", "description": " This structure holds arguments of the Picard-Lipschitz (Cauchy-Lipschitz) theorem. It is part of\nthe internal API for convenience, so as not to constantly invoke choice. Unless you want to use one\nof the auxiliary lemmas, use `exists_forall_deriv_within_Icc_eq_of_lipschitz_of_continuous` instead\nof using this structure.\n\nThe similarly named `is_picard_lindelof` is a bundled `Prop` holding the long hypotheses of the\nPicard-Lindel\u00f6f theorem as named arguments. It is used as part of the public API.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.t_max", "description": " This structure holds arguments of the Picard-Lipschitz (Cauchy-Lipschitz) theorem. It is part of\nthe internal API for convenience, so as not to constantly invoke choice. Unless you want to use one\nof the auxiliary lemmas, use `exists_forall_deriv_within_Icc_eq_of_lipschitz_of_continuous` instead\nof using this structure.\n\nThe similarly named `is_picard_lindelof` is a bundled `Prop` holding the long hypotheses of the\nPicard-Lindel\u00f6f theorem as named arguments. It is used as part of the public API.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.t\u2080", "description": " This structure holds arguments of the Picard-Lipschitz (Cauchy-Lipschitz) theorem. It is part of\nthe internal API for convenience, so as not to constantly invoke choice. Unless you want to use one\nof the auxiliary lemmas, use `exists_forall_deriv_within_Icc_eq_of_lipschitz_of_continuous` instead\nof using this structure.\n\nThe similarly named `is_picard_lindelof` is a bundled `Prop` holding the long hypotheses of the\nPicard-Lindel\u00f6f theorem as named arguments. It is used as part of the public API.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.x\u2080", "description": " This structure holds arguments of the Picard-Lipschitz (Cauchy-Lipschitz) theorem. It is part of\nthe internal API for convenience, so as not to constantly invoke choice. Unless you want to use one\nof the auxiliary lemmas, use `exists_forall_deriv_within_Icc_eq_of_lipschitz_of_continuous` instead\nof using this structure.\n\nThe similarly named `is_picard_lindelof` is a bundled `Prop` holding the long hypotheses of the\nPicard-Lindel\u00f6f theorem as named arguments. It is used as part of the public API.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.C", "description": " This structure holds arguments of the Picard-Lipschitz (Cauchy-Lipschitz) theorem. It is part of\nthe internal API for convenience, so as not to constantly invoke choice. Unless you want to use one\nof the auxiliary lemmas, use `exists_forall_deriv_within_Icc_eq_of_lipschitz_of_continuous` instead\nof using this structure.\n\nThe similarly named `is_picard_lindelof` is a bundled `Prop` holding the long hypotheses of the\nPicard-Lindel\u00f6f theorem as named arguments. It is used as part of the public API.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.R", "description": " This structure holds arguments of the Picard-Lipschitz (Cauchy-Lipschitz) theorem. It is part of\nthe internal API for convenience, so as not to constantly invoke choice. Unless you want to use one\nof the auxiliary lemmas, use `exists_forall_deriv_within_Icc_eq_of_lipschitz_of_continuous` instead\nof using this structure.\n\nThe similarly named `is_picard_lindelof` is a bundled `Prop` holding the long hypotheses of the\nPicard-Lindel\u00f6f theorem as named arguments. It is used as part of the public API.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.L", "description": " This structure holds arguments of the Picard-Lipschitz (Cauchy-Lipschitz) theorem. It is part of\nthe internal API for convenience, so as not to constantly invoke choice. Unless you want to use one\nof the auxiliary lemmas, use `exists_forall_deriv_within_Icc_eq_of_lipschitz_of_continuous` instead\nof using this structure.\n\nThe similarly named `is_picard_lindelof` is a bundled `Prop` holding the long hypotheses of the\nPicard-Lindel\u00f6f theorem as named arguments. It is used as part of the public API.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.is_pl", "description": " This structure holds arguments of the Picard-Lipschitz (Cauchy-Lipschitz) theorem. It is part of\nthe internal API for convenience, so as not to constantly invoke choice. Unless you want to use one\nof the auxiliary lemmas, use `exists_forall_deriv_within_Icc_eq_of_lipschitz_of_continuous` instead\nof using this structure.\n\nThe similarly named `is_picard_lindelof` is a bundled `Prop` holding the long hypotheses of the\nPicard-Lindel\u00f6f theorem as named arguments. It is used as part of the public API.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.nonempty_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space.to_continuous_map", "description": "Each curve in `picard_lindelof.fun_space` is continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.exists_fixed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.continuous_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.exists_contracting_iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space.norm_v_comp_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space.metric_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.t_dist_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space.lipschitz", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space.dist_apply_le_dist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space.map_t\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space.mem_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space.v_comp", "description": " Given a curve $\u03b3 \\colon [t_{\\min}, t_{\\max}] \u2192 E$, `v_comp` is the function\n$F(t)=v(\u03c0 t, \u03b3(\u03c0 t))$, where `\u03c0` is the projection $\u211d \u2192 [t_{\\min}, t_{\\max}]$. The integral of this\nfunction is the image of `\u03b3` under the contracting map we are going to define below.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space", "description": " The space of curves $\u03b3 \\colon [t_{\\min}, t_{\\max}] \\to E$ such that $\u03b3(t\u2080) = x\u2080$ and $\u03b3$ is\nLipschitz continuous with constant $C$. The map sending $\u03b3$ to\n$\\mathbf P\u03b3(t)=x\u2080 + \u222b_{t\u2080}^{t} v(\u03c4, \u03b3(\u03c4))\\,d\u03c4$ is a contracting map on this space, and its fixed\npoint is a solution of the ODE $\\dot x=v(t, x)$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space.to_fun", "description": " The space of curves $\u03b3 \\colon [t_{\\min}, t_{\\max}] \\to E$ such that $\u03b3(t\u2080) = x\u2080$ and $\u03b3$ is\nLipschitz continuous with constant $C$. The map sending $\u03b3$ to\n$\\mathbf P\u03b3(t)=x\u2080 + \u222b_{t\u2080}^{t} v(\u03c4, \u03b3(\u03c4))\\,d\u03c4$ is a contracting map on this space, and its fixed\npoint is a solution of the ODE $\\dot x=v(t, x)$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space.map_t\u2080'", "description": " The space of curves $\u03b3 \\colon [t_{\\min}, t_{\\max}] \\to E$ such that $\u03b3(t\u2080) = x\u2080$ and $\u03b3$ is\nLipschitz continuous with constant $C$. The map sending $\u03b3$ to\n$\\mathbf P\u03b3(t)=x\u2080 + \u222b_{t\u2080}^{t} v(\u03c4, \u03b3(\u03c4))\\,d\u03c4$ is a contracting map on this space, and its fixed\npoint is a solution of the ODE $\\dot x=v(t, x)$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space.lipschitz'", "description": " The space of curves $\u03b3 \\colon [t_{\\min}, t_{\\max}] \\to E$ such that $\u03b3(t\u2080) = x\u2080$ and $\u03b3$ is\nLipschitz continuous with constant $C$. The map sending $\u03b3$ to\n$\\mathbf P\u03b3(t)=x\u2080 + \u222b_{t\u2080}^{t} v(\u03c4, \u03b3(\u03c4))\\,d\u03c4$ is a contracting map on this space, and its fixed\npoint is a solution of the ODE $\\dot x=v(t, x)$.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.norm_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_is_picard_lindelof_const_of_cont_diff_on_nhds", "description": "A time-independent, locally continuously differentiable ODE satisfies the hypotheses of the\n Picard-Lindel\u00f6f theorem.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_forall_deriv_at_Ioo_eq_of_cont_diff", "description": "A time-independent, continuously differentiable ODE admits a solution in some open interval.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space.dist_iterate_next_apply_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_forall_deriv_within_Icc_eq_of_is_picard_lindelof", "description": "Picard-Lindel\u00f6f (Cauchy-Lipschitz) theorem.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space.next_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.lipschitz_on_with", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.dist_t\u2080_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space.range_to_continuous_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space.continuous_v_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space.uniform_inducing_to_continuous_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.t_min_le_t_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.proj_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space.dist_le_of_forall", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_picard_lindelof", "description": " `Prop` structure holding the hypotheses of the Picard-Lindel\u00f6f theorem.\n\nThe similarly named `picard_lindelof` structure is part of the internal API for convenience, so as\nnot to constantly invoke choice, but is not intended for public use.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_picard_lindelof.ht\u2080", "description": " `Prop` structure holding the hypotheses of the Picard-Lindel\u00f6f theorem.\n\nThe similarly named `picard_lindelof` structure is part of the internal API for convenience, so as\nnot to constantly invoke choice, but is not intended for public use.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_picard_lindelof.hR", "description": " `Prop` structure holding the hypotheses of the Picard-Lindel\u00f6f theorem.\n\nThe similarly named `picard_lindelof` structure is part of the internal API for convenience, so as\nnot to constantly invoke choice, but is not intended for public use.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_picard_lindelof.lipschitz", "description": " `Prop` structure holding the hypotheses of the Picard-Lindel\u00f6f theorem.\n\nThe similarly named `picard_lindelof` structure is part of the internal API for convenience, so as\nnot to constantly invoke choice, but is not intended for public use.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_picard_lindelof.cont", "description": " `Prop` structure holding the hypotheses of the Picard-Lindel\u00f6f theorem.\n\nThe similarly named `picard_lindelof` structure is part of the internal API for convenience, so as\nnot to constantly invoke choice, but is not intended for public use.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_picard_lindelof.norm_le", "description": " `Prop` structure holding the hypotheses of the Picard-Lindel\u00f6f theorem.\n\nThe similarly named `picard_lindelof` structure is part of the internal API for convenience, so as\nnot to constantly invoke choice, but is not intended for public use.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_picard_lindelof.C_mul_le_R", "description": " `Prop` structure holding the hypotheses of the Picard-Lindel\u00f6f theorem.\n\nThe similarly named `picard_lindelof` structure is part of the internal API for convenience, so as\nnot to constantly invoke choice, but is not intended for public use.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.fun_space.next", "description": " The Picard-Lindel\u00f6f operator. This is a contracting map on `picard_lindelof.fun_space v` such\nthat the fixed point of this map is the solution of the corresponding ODE.\n\nMore precisely, some iteration of this map is a contracting map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "picard_lindelof.t_dist", "description": "The maximum of distances from `t\u2080` to the endpoints of `[t_min, t_max]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_forall_deriv_at_Ioo_eq_of_cont_diff_on_nhds", "description": " A time-independent, locally continuously differentiable ODE admits a solution in some open\ninterval.", "p": "mathl