one if it exists.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.is_partition_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.sum_bUnion_boxes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "box_integral.prepartition.distortion_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_univ_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_univ_four", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.partial_prod", "description": "For `f = (a\u2081, ..., a\u2099)` in `\u03b1\u207f`, `partial_prod f` is `(1, a\u2081, a\u2081a\u2082, ..., a\u2081...a\u2099)` in `\u03b1\u207f\u207a\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_univ_six", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_Ioi_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_univ_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.partial_sum_left_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_univ_succ", "description": " A product of a function `f : fin (n + 1) \u2192 \u03b2` over all `fin (n + 1)`\nis the product of `f 0` plus the remaining product", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.neg_partial_sum_add_eq_contract_nth", "description": "Let `(g\u2080, g\u2081, ..., g\u2099)` be a tuple of elements in `G\u207f\u207a\u00b9`.\nThen if `k < j`, this says `-(g\u2080 + g\u2081 + ... + g\u2096\u208b\u2081) + (g\u2080 + g\u2081 + ... + g\u2096) = g\u2096`.\nIf `k = j`, it says `-(g\u2080 + g\u2081 + ... + g\u2096\u208b\u2081) + (g\u2080 + g\u2081 + ... + g\u2096\u208a\u2081) = g\u2096 + g\u2096\u208a\u2081`.\nIf `k > j`, it says `-(g\u2080 + g\u2081 + ... + g\u2096) + (g\u2080 + g\u2081 + ... + g\u2096\u208a\u2081) = g\u2096\u208a\u2081.`\nUseful for defining group cohomology.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_of_fn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_of_fn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_univ_four", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_congr'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_pow_mul_eq_add_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_univ_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_univ_succ_above", "description": " A product of a function `f : fin (n + 1) \u2192 \u03b2` over all `fin (n + 1)`\nis the product of `f x`, for some `x : fin (n + 1)` times the remaining product", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_univ_eight", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_congr'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_Ioi_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_univ_seven", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.partial_prod_left_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_univ_eight", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_univ_zero", "description": "A sum of a function `f : fin 0 \u2192 \u03b2` is `0` because `fin 0` is empty", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin_function_fin_equiv_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_trunc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_univ_three", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_univ_five", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.partial_sum", "description": "For `f = (a\u2081, ..., a\u2099)` in `\u03b1\u207f`, `partial_sum f` is\n`(0, a\u2081, a\u2081 + a\u2082, ..., a\u2081 + ... + a\u2099)` in `\u03b1\u207f\u207a\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_univ_three", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_Ioi_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_univ_zero", "description": "A product of a function `f : fin 0 \u2192 \u03b2` is `1` because `fin 0` is empty", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_univ_five", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_take_of_fn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.partial_sum_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_Ioi_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.alternating_sum_eq_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin_function_fin_equiv_symm_apply_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_univ_cast_succ", "description": "A sum of a function `f : fin (n + 1) \u2192 \u03b2` over all `fin (n + 1)` is the sum of\n`f (fin.last n)` plus the remaining sum", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_univ_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_univ_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin_function_fin_equiv", "description": "Equivalence between `fin n \u2192 fin m` and `fin (m ^ n)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_univ_cast_succ", "description": " A product of a function `f : fin (n + 1) \u2192 \u03b2` over all `fin (n + 1)`\nis the product of `f (fin.last n)` plus the remaining product", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.sum_of_fn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_take_of_fn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.partial_prod_succ'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_trunc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin_function_fin_equiv_apply_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.partial_sum_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.partial_prod_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_univ_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin_pi_fin_equiv", "description": "Equivalence between `\u03a0 i : fin m, fin (n i)` and `fin (\u220f i : fin m, n i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.partial_prod_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_univ_succ", "description": "A sum of a function `f : fin (n + 1) \u2192 \u03b2` over all `fin (n + 1)` is the sum of `f 0`\nplus the remaining product", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.inv_partial_prod_mul_eq_contract_nth", "description": " Let `(g\u2080, g\u2081, ..., g\u2099)` be a tuple of elements in `G\u207f\u207a\u00b9`.\nThen if `k < j`, this says `(g\u2080g\u2081...g\u2096\u208b\u2081)\u207b\u00b9 * g\u2080g\u2081...g\u2096 = g\u2096`.\nIf `k = j`, it says `(g\u2080g\u2081...g\u2096\u208b\u2081)\u207b\u00b9 * g\u2080g\u2081...g\u2096\u208a\u2081 = g\u2096g\u2096\u208a\u2081`.\nIf `k > j`, it says `(g\u2080g\u2081...g\u2096)\u207b\u00b9 * g\u2080g\u2081...g\u2096\u208a\u2081 = g\u2096\u208a\u2081.`\nUseful for defining group cohomology.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_univ_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.prod_univ_six", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin_pi_fin_equiv_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.alternating_prod_eq_finset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.partial_sum_succ'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.prod_of_fn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin_function_fin_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_univ_succ_above", "description": "A sum of a function `f : fin (n + 1) \u2192 \u03b2` over all `fin (n + 1)` is the sum of `f x`,\nfor some `x : fin (n + 1)` plus the remaining product", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_univ_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.sum_univ_seven", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin_pi_fin_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.partial_prod_right_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.partial_sum_right_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.prod_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.liftp_preservation_iff_uniform", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.id_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.Wrepr_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.fix.ind_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.liftp_preservation", "description": "does `abs` preserve `liftp`?", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.supp_preservation_iff_uniform", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.fix.rec_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.liftp_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.Wequiv.abs'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf", "description": "Quotients of polynomial functors.\n\nRoughly speaking, saying that `F` is a quotient of a polynomial functor means that for each `\u03b1`,\nelements of `F \u03b1` are represented by pairs `\u27e8a, f\u27e9`, where `a` is the shape of the object and\n`f` indexes the relevant elements of `\u03b1`, in a suitably natural manner.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.P", "description": "Quotients of polynomial functors.\n\nRoughly speaking, saying that `F` is a quotient of a polynomial functor means that for each `\u03b1`,\nelements of `F \u03b1` are represented by pairs `\u27e8a, f\u27e9`, where `a` is the shape of the object and\n`f` indexes the relevant elements of `\u03b1`, in a suitably natural manner.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.abs", "description": "Quotients of polynomial functors.\n\nRoughly speaking, saying that `F` is a quotient of a polynomial functor means that for each `\u03b1`,\nelements of `F \u03b1` are represented by pairs `\u27e8a, f\u27e9`, where `a` is the shape of the object and\n`f` indexes the relevant elements of `\u03b1`, in a suitably natural manner.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.repr", "description": "Quotients of polynomial functors.\n\nRoughly speaking, saying that `F` is a quotient of a polynomial functor means that for each `\u03b1`,\nelements of `F \u03b1` are represented by pairs `\u27e8a, f\u27e9`, where `a` is the shape of the object and\n`f` indexes the relevant elements of `\u03b1`, in a suitably natural manner.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.abs_repr", "description": "Quotients of polynomial functors.\n\nRoughly speaking, saying that `F` is a quotient of a polynomial functor means that for each `\u03b1`,\nelements of `F \u03b1` are represented by pairs `\u27e8a, f\u27e9`, where `a` is the shape of the object and\n`f` indexes the relevant elements of `\u03b1`, in a suitably natural manner.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.abs_map", "description": "Quotients of polynomial functors.\n\nRoughly speaking, saying that `F` is a quotient of a polynomial functor means that for each `\u03b1`,\nelements of `F \u03b1` are represented by pairs `\u27e8a, f\u27e9`, where `a` is the shape of the object and\n`f` indexes the relevant elements of `\u03b1`, in a suitably natural manner.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.supp_preservation_iff_liftp_preservation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.quotient_qpf", "description": " Given a qpf `F` and a well-behaved surjection `FG_abs` from F \u03b1 to\nfunctor G \u03b1, `G` is a qpf. We can consider `G` a quotient on `F` where\nelements `x y : F \u03b1` are in the same equivalence class if\n`FG_abs x = FG_abs y`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.supp_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.supp_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.liftr_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.cofix.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.fix.dest_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.is_uniform", "description": " A qpf is said to be uniform if every polynomial functor\nrepresenting a single value all have the same range.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.fix.rec_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.fix.rec", "description": "recursor of a type defined by a qpf", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.liftp_iff_of_is_uniform", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.Wequiv.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.W_setoid", "description": "Define the fixed point as the quotient of trees under the equivalence relation `Wequiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.cofix.bisim_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.Wrepr", "description": "maps every element of the W type to a canonical representative", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.cofix.dest", "description": "destructor for type defined by `cofix`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.fix.mk_dest", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.recF_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.corecF", "description": "does recursion on `q.P.M` using `g : \u03b1 \u2192 F \u03b1` rather than `g : \u03b1 \u2192 P \u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.fix.ind_rec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.is_precongr", "description": "A pre-congruence on q.P.M *viewed as an F-coalgebra*. Not necessarily symmetric.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.recF_eq_of_Wequiv", "description": "recF is insensitive to the representation", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.has_good_supp_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.Wequiv.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.liftp_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.cofix", "description": "coinductive type defined as the final coalgebra of a qpf", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.recF", "description": "does recursion on `q.P.W` using `g : F \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1` rather than `g : P \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.supp_preservation", "description": "does `abs` preserve `supp`?", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.supp_eq_of_is_uniform", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.corecF_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.comp_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.Mcongr", "description": "The maximal congruence on q.P.M", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.comp", "description": "composition of qpfs gives another qpf", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "qpf.cofix.bisim'", "description"