at.lcm_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.gcd_mul_left_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.coprime.mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.gcd_mul_right_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.gcd_mul_dvd_mul_gcd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.gcd_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.gcd_add_mul_right_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.coprime.coprime_div_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.gcd_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.gcd_eq_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.gcd_mul_gcd_of_coprime_of_mul_eq_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.gcd_gcd_self_right_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.gcd_gcd_self_left_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.lcm_dvd_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.coprime.coprime_dvd_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.gcd_self_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.coprime.coprime_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.dvd_gcd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.gcd_greatest", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.gcd_dvd_gcd_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.coprime.gcd_both", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.lcm_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.gcd_dvd_gcd_of_dvd_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.coprime_add_self_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.finite_of_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_field.algebra_base", "description": "If `K` is the fraction field of `A`, the `A`-algebra structure on `cyclotomic_field n K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_field.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension", "description": " Given an `A`-algebra `B` and `S : set \u2115+`, we define `is_cyclotomic_extension S A B` requiring\nthat there is a `n`-th primitive root of unity in `B` for all `n \u2208 S` and that `B` is generated\nover `A` by the roots of `X ^ n - 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.exists_prim_root", "description": " Given an `A`-algebra `B` and `S : set \u2115+`, we define `is_cyclotomic_extension S A B` requiring\nthat there is a `n`-th primitive root of unity in `B` for all `n \u2208 S` and that `B` is generated\nover `A` by the roots of `X ^ n - 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.adjoin_roots", "description": " Given an `A`-algebra `B` and `S : set \u2115+`, we define `is_cyclotomic_extension S A B` requiring\nthat there is a `n`-th primitive root of unity in `B` for all `n \u2208 S` and that `B` is generated\nover `A` by the roots of `X ^ n - 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_ring.eq_adjoin_primitive_root", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.iff_union_singleton_one", "description": "`is_cyclotomic_extension S A B` is equivalent to `is_cyclotomic_extension (S \u222a {1}) A B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_ring.algebra_base", "description": "The `A`-algebra structure on `cyclotomic_ring n A K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.splits_X_pow_sub_one", "description": "A cyclotomic extension splits `X ^ n - 1` if `n \u2208 S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_alg_closed_of_char_zero.is_cyclotomic_extension", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.adjoin_roots_cyclotomic_eq_adjoin_root_cyclotomic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_field.char_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.union_left", "description": " If `B` is a cyclotomic extension of `A` given by roots of unity of order in `T` and `S \u2286 T`,\nthen `adjoin A { b : B | \u2203 a : \u2115+, a \u2208 S \u2227 b ^ (a : \u2115) = 1 }` is a cyclotomic extension of `B`\ngiven by roots of unity of order in `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.iff_union_of_dvd", "description": " If `\u2200 s \u2208 S, n \u2223 s` and `S` is not empty, then `is_cyclotomic_extension S A B` if and only if\n`is_cyclotomic_extension (S \u222a {n}) A B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.adjoin_primitive_root_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.integral", "description": "A finite cyclotomic extension of an integral noetherian domain is integral", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_field.is_cyclotomic_extension", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_ring.no_zero_smul_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_primitive_root.adjoin_is_cyclotomic_extension", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.union_right", "description": " If `B` is a cyclotomic extension of `A` given by roots of unity of order in `S \u222a T`, then `B`\nis a cyclotomic extension of `adjoin A { b : B | \u2203 a : \u2115+, a \u2208 S \u2227 b ^ (a : \u2115) = 1 } ` given by\nroots of unity of order in `T`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_field.algebra'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.finite", "description": "If `S` is finite and `is_cyclotomic_extension S A B`, then `B` is a finite `A`-algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_ring", "description": " If `A` is a domain with fraction field `K` and `n : \u2115+`, we define `cyclotomic_ring n A K` as\nthe `A`-subalgebra of `cyclotomic_field n K` generated by the roots of `X ^ n - 1`. If `n`\nis nonzero in `A`, it has the instance `is_cyclotomic_extension {n} A (cyclotomic_ring n A K)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_field.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.singleton_one_of_algebra_map_bijective", "description": "If `function.surjective (algebra_map A B)`, then `is_cyclotomic_extension {1} A B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.trans", "description": "Transitivity of cyclotomic extensions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.splitting_field_cyclotomic", "description": "If `is_cyclotomic_extension {n} K L`, then `L` is the splitting field of `cyclotomic n K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.subsingleton_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.iff_singleton", "description": "A reformulation of `is_cyclotomic_extension` in the case `S` is a singleton.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_field.field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.adjoin_roots_cyclotomic_eq_adjoin_nth_roots", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_field.no_zero_smul_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.is_galois", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.of_union_of_dvd", "description": " If `\u2200 s \u2208 S, n \u2223 s` and `S` is not empty, then `is_cyclotomic_extension S A B` implies\n`is_cyclotomic_extension (S \u222a {n}) A B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.equiv", "description": " Given `(f : B \u2243\u2090[A] C)`, if `is_cyclotomic_extension S A B` then\n`is_cyclotomic_extension S A C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_ring.cyclotomic_field.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.empty", "description": "If `is_cyclotomic_extension \u2205 A B`, then the image of `A` in `B` equals `B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_field.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.splitting_field_X_pow_sub_one", "description": "If `is_cyclotomic_extension {n} K L`, then `L` is the splitting field of `X ^ n - 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.finite_dimensional", "description": "If `S` is finite and `is_cyclotomic_extension S K A`, then `finite_dimensional K A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.ne_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_ring.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_ring.cyclotomic_field.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_ring.cyclotomic_field.is_fraction_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_field", "description": " Given `n : \u2115+` and a field `K`, we define `cyclotomic_field n K` as the\nsplitting field of `cyclotomic n K`. If `n` is nonzero in `K`, it has\nthe instance `is_cyclotomic_extension {n} K (cyclotomic_field n K)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_ring.algebra_base_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.singleton_one", "description": "If `is_cyclotomic_extension {1} A B`, then the image of `A` in `B` equals `B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.iff_adjoin_eq_top", "description": "A reformulation of `is_cyclotomic_extension` that uses `\u22a4`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.splits_cyclotomic", "description": "A cyclotomic extension splits `cyclotomic n K` if `n \u2208 S` and `ne_zero (n : K)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.alg_equiv", "description": "Any two `n`-th cyclotomic extensions are isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_ring.is_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_alg_closed.is_cyclotomic_extension", "description": " Algebraically closed fields are `S`-cyclotomic extensions over themselves if\n`ne_zero ((a : \u2115) : K))` for all `a \u2208 S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_ring.adjoin_algebra_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.singleton_one_of_bot_eq_top", "description": "If `(\u22a5 : subalgebra A B) = \u22a4`, then `is_cyclotomic_extension {1} A B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.number_field", "description": "A cyclotomic finite extension of a number field is a number field.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclotomic_extension.singleton_zero_of_bot_eq_top", "description": "If `(\u22a5 : subalgebra A B) = \u22a4`, then `is_cyclotomic_extension \u2205 A B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_ring.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_ring.is_cyclotomic_extension", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cyclotomic_ring.cyclotomic_field.no_zero_smul_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.has_coe_to_fun", "description": " Helper instance for when there's too many metavariables to apply `fun_like.has_coe_to_fun`\ndirectly.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "distrib_mul_action.to_module_End", "description": " Each element of the monoid defines a module endomorphism.\n\nThis is a stronger version of `distrib_mul_action.to_add_monoid_End`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.restrict_scalars_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.module_End_self_op_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coe_copy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End", "description": " Linear endomorphisms of a module, with associated ring structure\n`module.End.semiring` and algebra structure `module.End.algebra`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ext_ring", "description": "If two `\u03c3`-linear maps from `R` are equal on `1`, then they are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.has_neg", "description": "The negation of a linear map is linear.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.comp_hom.to_linear_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_linear_map.is_linear_map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.comp_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.id_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "distrib_mul_action_hom.coe_to_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.has_sub", "description": "The subtraction of two linear maps is linear.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_linear", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_linear_map.is_linear_map_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.congr_arg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_linear_map.mk'", "description": "Convert an `is_linear_map` predicate to a `linear_map`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.module.End.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.one_eq_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ext_ring_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.mul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_map_class.distrib_mul_action_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.restrict_scalars", "description": " If `M` and `M\u2082` are both `R`-modules and `S`-modules and `R`-module structures\nare defined by an action of `R` on `S` (formally, we have two scalar towers), then any `S`-linear\nmap from `M` to `M\u2082` is `R`-linear.\n\nSee also `linear_map.map_smul_of_tower`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.smul_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "distrib_mul_action.to_module_End_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.one_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.mul_eq_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map", "description": " A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`. Elements of `linear_map \u03c3 M M\u2082` (available under the notation\n`M \u2192\u209b\u2097[\u03c3] M\u2082`) are bundled versions of such maps. For plain linear maps (i.e. for which\n`\u03c3 = ring_hom.id R`), the notation `M \u2192\u2097[R] M\u2082` is available. An unbundled version of plain linear\nmaps is available with the predicate `is_linear_map`, but it should be avoided most of the time.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_fun", "description": " A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`. Elements of `linear_map \u03c3 M M\u2082` (available under the notation\n`M \u2192\u209b\u2097[\u03c3] M\u2082`) are bundled versions of such maps. For plain linear maps (i.e. for which\n`\u03c3 = ring_hom.id R`), the notation `M \u2192\u2097[R] M\u2082` is available. An unbundled version of plain linear\nmaps is available with the predicate `is_linear_map`, but it should be avoided most of the time.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_add'", "description": " A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`. Elements of `linear_map \u03c3 M M\u2082` (available under the notation\n`M \u2192\u209b\u2097[\u03c3] M\u2082`) are bundled versions of such maps. For plain linear maps (i.e. for which\n`\u03c3 = ring_hom.id R`), the notation `M \u2192\u2097[R] M\u2082` is available. An unbundled version of plain linear\nmaps is available with the predicate `is_linear_map`, but it should be avoided most of the time.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_smul'", "description": " A map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`. Elements of `linear_map \u03c3 M M\u2082` (available under the notation\n`M \u2192\u209b\u2097[\u03c3] M\u2082`) are bundled versions of such maps. For plain linear maps (i.e. for which\n`\u03c3 = ring_hom.id R`), the notation `M \u2192\u2097[R] M\u2082` is available. An unbundled version of plain linear\nmaps is available with the predicate `is_linear_map`, but it should be avoided most of the time.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.apply_smul_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_add_monoid_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_smul_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_distrib_mul_action_hom", "description": "The `distrib_mul_action_hom` underlying a `linear_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_add_hom", "description": "The `add_hom` underlying a `linear_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.coe_to_rat_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.semilinear_map_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.coe_to_int_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.compatible_smul", "description": "A typeclass for `has_smul` structures which can be moved through a `linear_map`.\nThis typeclass is generated automatically from a `is_scalar_tower` instance, but exists so that\nwe can also add an instance for `add_comm_group.int_module`, allowing `z \u2022` to be moved even if\n`R` does not support negation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.compatible_smul.map_smul", "description": "A typeclass for `has_smul` structures which can be moved through a `linear_map`.\nThis typeclass is generated automatically from a `is_scalar_tower` instance, but exists so that\nwe can also add an instance for `add_comm_group.int_module`, allowing `z \u2022` to be moved even if\n`R` does not support negation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.comp_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.add_comm_group", "description": "The type of linear maps is an additive group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.comp_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coe_restrict_scalars", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coe_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.has_add", "description": "The sum of two linear maps is linear.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_scalar_tower.compatible_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_linear_map.map_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.module.End.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_smul_of_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.compatible_smul.units", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_rat_linear_map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.restrict_scalars_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.int_cast_apply", "description": "See also `module.End.int_cast_def`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "distrib_mul_action_hom.to_linear_map", "description": "A `distrib_mul_action_hom` between two modules is a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.restrict_scalars_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "image_smul_set\u209b\u2097", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "distrib_mul_action.to_linear_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_nat_linear_map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_linear_map.map_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_int_linear_map", "description": "Reinterpret an additive homomorphism as a `\u2124`-linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.zero_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "image_smul_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.apply_is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.module_End_self_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.to_semilinear_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.apply_module", "description": " The tautological action by `module.End R M` (aka `M \u2192\u2097[R] M`) on `M`.\n\nThis generalizes `function.End.apply_mul_action`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.nat_cast_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coe_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.smul_comm_class'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.has_zero", "description": "The constant 0 map is linear.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.apply_has_faithful_smul", "description": "`linear_map.apply_module` is faithful.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_map_class.map_smul_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map_class", "description": " `linear_map_class F R M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `R`-linear maps `M \u2192 M\u2082`.\n\nThis is an abbreviation for `semilinear_map_class F (ring_hom.id R) M M\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.cancel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.compatible_smul.int_module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.module_End_self_op", "description": " The canonical (semi)ring isomorphism from `R` to `module.End R\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 R` induced by the left\nmultiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_int_linear_map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.comp", "description": "Composition of two linear maps is a linear map", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.module_End_self_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.copy_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.module_End_self_op_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_map_class.add_monoid_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.to_semilinear_map", "description": "Interpret a `ring_hom` `f` as an `f`-semilinear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_nat_linear_map", "description": "Reinterpret an additive homomorphism as a `\u2115`-linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_add_monoid_hom", "description": "convert a linear map to an additive map", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.neg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_linear_map.map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_linear_map.mk'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.smul_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "distrib_mul_action_hom.to_linear_map_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.nat_cast_apply", "description": "See also `module.End.nat_cast_def`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_add_monoid_hom_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "distrib_mul_action.to_linear_map", "description": " Each element of the monoid defines a linear map.\n\nThis is a stronger version of `distrib_mul_action.to_add_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.int_cast_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_smul\u209b\u2097", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_map_class", "description": " `semilinear_map_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear maps `M \u2192 M\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_map_class F R M M\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_map_class.coe", "description": " `semilinear_map_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear maps `M \u2192 M\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_map_class F R M M\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_map_class.coe_injective'", "description": " `semilinear_map_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear maps `M \u2192 M\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_map_class F R M M\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_map_class.map_add", "description": " `semilinear_map_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear maps `M \u2192 M\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_map_class F R M M\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_map_class.map_smul\u209b\u2097", "description": " `semilinear_map_class F \u03c3 M M\u2082` asserts `F` is a type of bundled `\u03c3`-semilinear maps `M \u2192 M\u2082`.\n\nSee also `linear_map_class F R M M\u2082` for the case where `\u03c3` is the identity map on `R`.\n\nA map `f` between an `R`-module and an `S`-module over a ring homomorphism `\u03c3 : R \u2192+* S`\nis semilinear if it satisfies the two properties `f (x + y) = f x + f y` and\n`f (c \u2022 x) = (\u03c3 c) \u2022 f x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.sub_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semilinear_map_class.to_add_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.simps.apply", "description": "See Note [custom simps projection].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "distrib_mul_action_hom.linear_map.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.smul_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.to_module_End", "description": " Each element of the semiring defines a module endomorphism.\n\nThis is a stronger version of `distrib_mul_action.to_module_End`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_linear_map.is_linear_map_smul'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.congr_fun", "description": "If two linear maps are equal, they are equal at each point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_rat_linear_map", "description": "Reinterpret an additive homomorphism as a `\u211a`-linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.neg_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.comp_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ext_ring_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_linear_map", "description": " A map `f` between modules over a semiring is linear if it satisfies the two properties\n`f (x + y) = f x + f y` and `f (c \u2022 x) = c \u2022 f x`. The predicate `is_linear_map R f` asserts this\nproperty. A bundled version is available with `linear_map`, and should be favored over\n`is_linear_map` most of the time.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_linear_map.map_add", "description": " A map `f` between modules over a semiring is linear if it satisfies the two properties\n`f (x + y) = f x + f y` and `f (c \u2022 x) = c \u2022 f x`. The predicate `is_linear_map R f` asserts this\nproperty. A bundled version is available with `linear_map`, and should be favored over\n`is_linear_map` most of the time.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_linear_map.map_smul", "description": " A map `f` between modules over a semiring is linear if it satisfies the two properties\n`f (x + y) = f x + f y` and `f (c \u2022 x) = c \u2022 f x`. The predicate `is_linear_map R f` asserts this\nproperty. A bundled version is available with `linear_map`, and should be favored over\n`is_linear_map` most of the time.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.no_zero_smul_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.add_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "preimage_smul_set\u209b\u2097", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.default_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.inverse", "description": "If a function `g` is a left and right inverse of a linear map `f`, then `g` is linear itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.apply_smul_comm_class'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.module_End_self", "description": " The canonical (semi)ring isomorphism from `R\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56` to `module.End R R` induced by the right\nmultiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.add_comm_monoid", "description": "The type of linear maps is an additive monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.smul_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "distrib_mul_action_hom.to_linear_map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "preimage_smul_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.comp_hom.to_linear_map", "description": "`g : R \u2192+* S` is `R`-linear when the module structure on `S` is `module.comp_hom S g` .", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.id", "description": "Identity map as a `linear_map`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.comp_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.sub_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.cancel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.add_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.copy", "description": " Copy of a `linear_map` with a new `to_fun` equal to the old one. Useful to fix definitional\nequalities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.to_module_End_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.im_exp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.norm_exp", "description": " Note that this implies that exponentials of pure imaginary quaternions are unit quaternions\nsince in that case the RHS is `1` via `exp_zero` and `norm_one`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.re_exp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.has_sum_exp_series_of_imaginary", "description": " Auxiliary result; if the power series corresponding to `real.cos` and `real.sin` evaluated\nat `\u2016q\u2016` tend to `c` and `s`, then the exponential series tends to `c + (s / \u2016q\u2016)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.exp_eq", "description": "The closed form for the quaternion exponential on arbitrary quaternions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.exp_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.norm_sq_exp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quaternion.exp_of_re_eq_zero", "description": "The closed form for the quaternion exponential on imaginary quaternions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.has_bracket", "description": "The commutator of derivations is again a derivation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.commutator_coe_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.commutator_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.lie_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derivation.lie_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "user_attribute.set_untyped", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "user_attribute.get_param_untyped", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "attribute.register", "description": "Registers a new user-defined attribute. The argument must be the name of a definition of type\n  `user_attribute \u03b1 \u03b2`. Once registered, you may tag declarations with this attribute.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "attribute.get_instances", "description": " Get all of the declaration names that have the given attribute.\nEg. ``get_instances `simp`` returns a list with the names of all of the lemmas in the environment tagged with the `@[simp]` attribute.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "user_attribute.parse_reflect", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "register_attribute", "description": "Alias for attribute.register", "p": "core"}, {"name": "user_attribute.dflt_parser", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "user_attribute.dflt_cache_cfg", "description": "Close the current goal by filling it with the trivial `user_attribute_cache_cfg unit`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "user_attribute.get_cache", "description": "Returns the attribute cache for the given user attribute.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "attribute.fingerprint", "description": "Returns a hash of `get_instances`. You can use this to tell if your attribute instances have changed.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "user_attribute.set", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "user_attribute_cache_cfg", "description": " Configuration for a user attribute cache. For example, the `simp` attribute has a cache of type simp_lemmas.\n- `mk_cache` is a function where you are given all of the declarations tagged with your attribute and you return the new value for the cache.\n  That is, `mk_cache` makes the object you want to be cached.\n- `dependencies` is a list of other attributes whose caches need to be computed first.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "user_attribute_cache_cfg.mk_cache", "description": " Configuration for a user attribute cache. For example, the `simp` attribute has a cache of type simp_lemmas.\n- `mk_cache` is a function where you are given all of the declarations tagged with your attribute and you return the new value for the cache.\n  That is, `mk_cache` makes the object you want to be cached.\n- `dependencies` is a list of other attributes whose caches need to be computed first.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "user_attribute_cache_cfg.dependencies", "description": " Configuration for a user attribute cache. For example, the `simp` attribute has a cache of type simp_lemmas.\n- `mk_cache` is a function where you are given all of the declarations tagged with your attribute and you return the new value for the cache.\n  That is, `mk_cache` makes the object you want to be cached.\n- `dependencies` is a list of other attributes whose caches need to be computed first.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "get_attribute_cache_dyn", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "user_attribute", "description": "A __user attribute__ is an attribute defined by the user (ie, not built in to Lean).\n### Type parameters\n- `cache_ty` is the type of a cached VM object that is computed from all of the declarations in the environment tagged with this attribute.\n- `param_ty` is an argument for the attribute when it is used. For instance with `param_ty` being `\u2115` you could write `@[my_attribute 4]`.\n\n### Data\nA `user_attribute` consists of the following pieces of data:\n- `name` is the name of the attribute, eg ```simp```\n- `descr` is a plaintext description of the attribute for humans.\n- `after_set` is an optional handler that will be called after the attribute has been applied to a declaration.\n    Failing the tactic will fail the entire `attribute/def/...` command, i.e. the attribute will\n    not be applied after all.\n    Declaring an `after_set` handler without a `before_unset` handler will make the attribute\n    non-removable.\n- `before_unset` Optional handler that will be called before the attribute is removed from a declaration.\n- `cache_cfg` describes how to construct the user attribute's cache. See docstring for `user_attribute_cache_cfg`\n- `reflect_param` demands that `param_ty` can be reflected.\n    This means we have a function from `param_ty` to an expr.\n    See the docstring for `has_reflect`.\n- `parser` Parser that will be invoked after parsing the attribute's name. The parse result will be reflected\nand stored and can be retrieved with `user_attribute.get_param`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "user_attribute.name", "description": "A __user attribute__ is an attribute defined by the user (ie, not built in to Lean).\n### Type parameters\n- `cache_ty` is the type of a cached VM object that is computed from all of the declarations in the environment tagged with this attribute.\n- `param_ty` is an argument for the attribute when it is used. For instance with `param_ty` being `\u2115` you could write `@[my_attribute 4]`.\n\n### Data\nA `user_attribute` consists of the following pieces of data:\n- `name` is the name of the attribute, eg ```simp```\n- `descr` is a plaintext description of the attribute for humans.\n- `after_set` is an optional handler that will be called after the attribute has been applied to a declaration.\n    Failing the tactic will fail the entire `attribute/def/...` command, i.e. the attribute will\n    not be applied after all.\n    Declaring an `after_set` handler without a `before_unset` handler will make the attribute\n    non-removable.\n- `before_unset` Optional handler that will be called before the attribute is removed from a declaration.\n- `cache_cfg` describes how to construct the user attribute's cache. See docstring for `user_attribute_cache_cfg`\n- `reflect_param` demands that `param_ty` can be reflected.\n    This means we have a function from `param_ty` to an expr.\n    See the docstring for `has_reflect`.\n- `parser` Parser that will be invoked after parsing the attribute's name. The parse result will be reflected\nand stored and can be retrieved with `user_attribute.get_param`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "user_attribute.descr", "description": "A __user attribute__ is an attribute defined by the user (ie, not built in to Lean).\n### Type parameters\n- `cache_ty` is the type of a cached VM object that is computed from all of the declarations in the environment tagged with this attribute.\n- `param_ty` is an argument for the attribute when it is used. For instance with `param_ty` being `\u2115` you could write `@[my_attribute 4]`.\n\n### Data\nA `user_attribute` consists of the following pieces of data:\n- `name` is the name of the attribute, eg ```simp```\n- `descr` is a plaintext description of the attribute for humans.\n- `after_set` is an optional handler that will be called after the attribute has been applied to a declaration.\n    Failing the tactic will fail the entire `attribute/def/...` command, i.e. the attribute will\n    not be applied after all.\n    Declaring an `after_set` handler without a `before_unset` handler will make the attribute\n    non-removable.\n- `before_unset` Optional handler that will be called before the attribute is removed from a declaration.\n- `cache_cfg` describes how to construct the user attribute's cache. See docstring for `user_attribute_cache_cfg`\n- `reflect_param` demands that `param_ty` can be reflected.\n    This means we have a function from `param_ty` to an expr.\n    See the docstring for `has_reflect`.\n- `parser` Parser that will be invoked after parsing the attribute's name. The parse result will be reflected\nand stored and can be retrieved with `user_attribute.get_param`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "user_attribute.after_set", "description": "A __user attribute__ is an attribute defined by the user (ie, not built in to Lean).\n### Type parameters\n- `cache_ty` is the type of a cached VM object that is computed from all of the declarations in the environment tagged with this attribute.\n- `param_ty` is an argument for the attribute when it is used. For instance with `param_ty` being `\u2115` you could write `@[my_attribute 4]`.\n\n### Data\nA `user_attribute` consists of the following pieces of data:\n- `name` is the name of the attribute, eg ```simp```\n- `descr` is a plaintext description of the attribute for humans.\n- `after_set` is an optional handler that will be called after the attribute has been applied to a declaration.\n    Failing the tactic will fail the entire `attribute/def/...` command, i.e. the attribute will\n    not be applied after all.\n    Declaring an `after_set` handler without a `before_unset` handler will make the attribute\n    non-removable.\n- `before_unset` Optional handler that will be called before the attribute is removed from a declaration.\n- `cache_cfg` describes how to construct the user attribute's cache. See docstring for `user_attribute_cache_cfg`\n- `reflect_param` demands that `param_ty` can be reflected.\n    This means we have a function from `param_ty` to an expr.\n    See the docstring for `has_reflect`.\n- `parser` Parser that will be invoked after parsing the attribute's name. The parse result will be reflected\nand stored and can be retrieved with `user_attribute.get_param`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "user_attribute.before_unset", "description": "A __user attribute__ is an attribute defined by the user (ie, not built in to Lean).\n### Type parameters\n- `cache_ty` is the type of a cached VM object that is computed from all of the declarations in the environment tagged with this attribute.\n- `param_ty` is an argument for the attribute when it is used. For instance with `param_ty` being `\u2115` you could write `@[my_attribute 4]`.\n\n### Data\nA `user_attribute` consists of the following pieces of data:\n- `name` is the name of the attribute, eg ```simp```\n- `descr` is a plaintext description of the attribute for humans.\n- `after_set` is an optional handler that will be called after the attribute has been applied to a declaration.\n    Failing the tactic will fail the entire `attribute/def/...` command, i.e. the attribute will\n    not be applied after all.\n    Declaring an `after_set` handler without a `before_unset` handler will make the attribute\n    non-removable.\n- `before_unset` Optional handler that will be called before the attribute is removed from a declaration.\n- `cache_cfg` describes how to construct the user attribute's cache. See docstring for `user_attribute_cache_cfg`\n- `reflect_param` demands that `param_ty` can be reflected.\n    This means we have a function from `param_ty` to an expr.\n    See the docstring for `has_reflect`.\n- `parser` Parser that will be invoked after parsing the attribute's name. The parse result will be reflected\nand stored and can be retrieved with `user_attribute.get_param`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "user_attribute.cache_cfg", "description": "A __user attribute__ is an attribute defined by the user (ie, not built in to Lean).\n### Type parameters\n- `cache_ty` is the type of a cached VM object that is computed from all of the declarations in the environment tagged with this attribute.\n- `param_ty` is an argument for the attribute when it is used. For instance with `param_ty` being `\u2115` you could write `@[my_attribute 4]`.\n\n### Data\nA `user_attribute` consists of the following pieces of data:\n- `name` is the name of the attribute, eg ```simp```\n- `descr` is a plaintext description of the attribute for humans.\n- `after_set` is an optional handler that will be called after the attribute has been applied to a declaration.\n    Failing the tactic will fail the entire `attribute/def/...` command, i.e. the attribute will\n    not be applied after all.\n    Declaring an `after_set` handler without a `before_unset` handler will make the attribute\n    non-removable.\n- `before_unset` Optional handler that will be called before the attribute is removed from a declaration.\n- `cache_cfg` describes how to construct the user attribute's cache. See docstring for `user_attribute_cache_cfg`\n- `reflect_param` demands that `param_ty` can be reflected.\n    This means we have a function from `param_ty` to an expr.\n    See the docstring for `has_reflect`.\n- `parser` Parser that will be invoked after parsing the attribute's name. The parse result will be reflected\nand stored and can be retrieved with `user_attribute.get_param`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "user_attribute.reflect_param", "description": "A __user attribute__ is an attribute defined by the user (ie, not built in to Lean).\n### Type parameters\n- `cache_ty` is the type of a cached VM object that is computed from all of the declarations in the environment tagged with this attribute.\n- `param_ty` is an argument for the attribute when it is used. For instance with `param_ty` being `\u2115` you could write `@[my_attribute 4]`.\n\n### Data\nA `user_attribute` consists of the following pieces of data:\n- `name` is the name of the attribute, eg ```simp```\n- `descr` is a plaintext description of the attribute for humans.\n- `after_set` is an optional handler that will be called after the attribute has been applied to a declaration.\n    Failing the tactic will fail the entire `attribute/def/...` command, i.e. the attribute will\n    not be applied after all.\n    Declaring an `after_set` handler without a `before_unset` handler will make the attribute\n    non-removable.\n- `before_unset` Optional handler that will be called before the attribute is removed from a declaration.\n- `cache_cfg` describes how to construct the user attribute's cache. See docstring for `user_attribute_cache_cfg`\n- `reflect_param` demands that `param_ty` can be reflected.\n    This means we have a function from `param_ty` to an expr.\n    See the docstring for `has_reflect`.\n- `parser` Parser that will be invoked after parsing the attribute's name. The parse result will be reflected\nand stored and can be retrieved with `user_attribute.get_param`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "user_attribute.parser", "description": "A __user attribute__ is an attribute defined by the user (ie, not built in to Lean).\n### Type parameters\n- `cache_ty` is the type of a cached VM object that is computed from all of the declarations in the environment tagged with this attribute.\n- `param_ty` is an argument for the attribute when it is used. For instance with `param_ty` being `\u2115` you could write `@[my_attribute 4]`.\n\n### Data\nA `user_attribute` consists of the following pieces of data:\n- `name` is the name of the attribute, eg ```simp```\n- `descr` is a plaintext description of the attribute for humans.\n- `after_set` is an optional handler that will be called after the attribute has been applied to a declaration.\n    Failing the tactic will fail the entire `attribute/def/...` command, i.e. the attribute will\n    not be applied after all.\n    Declaring an `after_set` handler without a `before_unset` handler will make the attribute\n    non-removable.\n- `before_unset` Optional handler that will be called before the attribute is removed from a declaration.\n- `cache_cfg` describes how to construct the user attribute's cache. See docstring for `user_attribute_cache_cfg`\n- `reflect_param` demands that `param_ty` can be reflected.\n    This means we have a function from `param_ty` to an expr.\n    See the docstring for `has_reflect`.\n- `parser` Parser that will be invoked after parsing the attribute's name. The parse result will be reflected\nand stored and can be retrieved with `user_attribute.get_param`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "get_name_set_for_attr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "mk_name_set_attr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "user_attribute.get_param", "description": "Get the value of the parameter for the attribute on a given declatation. Will fail if the attribute does not exist.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even_equiv_even_neg_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_even.reverse_v", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.of_even_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_even.v", "description": "The embedding from the existing vector space", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_even.neg_v_mul_e0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_even.\u03b9_eq_v_add_smul_e0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even_to_neg", "description": "One direction of `clifford_algebra.even_equiv_even_neg`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.of_even", "description": "The embedding from the even subalgebra with an extra dimension into the original algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_even.involute_v", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_even.e0", "description": "The unit vector in the new dimension", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_even.v_sq_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_even.e0_mul_v_mul_e0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.to_even_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_even.e0_mul_e0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_even", "description": " Any clifford algebra is isomorphic to the even subalgebra of a clifford algebra with an extra\ndimension (that is, with vector space `M \u00d7 R`), with a quadratic form evaluating to `-1` on that new\nbasis vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even_to_neg_comp_even_to_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even_equiv_even_neg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even_equiv_even_neg", "description": " The even subalgebras of the algebras with quadratic form `Q` and `-Q` are isomorphic.\n\nStated another way, `\ud835\udc9e\u2113\u207a(p,q,r)` and `\ud835\udc9e\u2113\u207a(q,p,r)` are isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.coe_to_even_reverse_involute", "description": " The representation of the clifford conjugate (i.e. the reverse of the involute) in the even\nsubalgebra is just the reverse of the representation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_even.neg_e0_mul_v", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.even_to_neg_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_even.Q'", "description": "The quadratic form on the augmented vector space `M \u00d7 R` sending `v + r\u2022e0` to `Q v - r^2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_even_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_even_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_even.reverse_e0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_even.involute_e0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.to_even_comp_of_even", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_even.Q'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.to_even", "description": "The embedding from the smaller algebra into the new larger one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.of_even_comp_to_even", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.prime_degree_dvd_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.unique_gal_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.unique_gal_X_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.restrict_prod_injective", "description": "`polynomial.gal.restrict_prod` is actually a subgroup embedding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.apply_mul_semiring_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.gal_action_hom_injective", "description": "`gal p` embeds as a subgroup of permutations of the roots of `p` in `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.card_complex_roots_eq_card_real_add_card_not_gal_inv", "description": "The number of complex roots equals the number of real roots plus\n   the number of roots not fixed by complex conjugation (i.e. with some imaginary component).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.restrict", "description": "Restrict from a superfield automorphism into a member of `gal p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.card_of_separable", "description": " For a separable polynomial, its Galois group has cardinality\nequal to the dimension of its splitting field over `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.splits_\u211a_\u2102", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.splits_in_splitting_field_of_comp", "description": "`p` splits in the splitting field of `p \u2218 q`, for `q` non-constant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.gal_action", "description": "The action of `gal p` on the roots of `p` in `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.restrict_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.unique_gal_of_splits", "description": "If `p` splits in `F` then the `p.gal` is trivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.gal_action_hom_bijective_of_prime_degree'", "description": "An irreducible polynomial of prime degree with 1-3 non-real roots has full Galois group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.gal_action_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.map_roots", "description": " The function taking `roots p p.splitting_field` to `roots p E`. This is actually a bijection,\nsee `polynomial.gal.map_roots_bijective`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.unique_gal_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.gal_action_hom_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.restrict_comp_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.gal.has_coe_to_fun", "descrip