ib"}, {"name": "std_simplex", "description": " The standard simplex in the space of functions `\u03b9 \u2192 \ud835\udd5c` is the set of vectors with non-negative\ncoordinates with total sum `1`. This is the free object in the category of convex spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.affinity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.translate_preimage_left", "description": "The translation of a convex set is also convex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.add_smul_sub_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.translate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_iff_forall_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone.convex_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_iff_pairwise_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.convex_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.ord_connected", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `convex_iff_ord_connected`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.convex_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_iff_ord_connected", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_Iio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_convex_add_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_list_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.ord_connected.convex_of_chain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_uIcc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.linear_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "directed.convex_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.star_convex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "coe_convex_add_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_iff_div", "description": "Alternative definition of set convexity, using division.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.affine_image", "description": "The image of a convex set under an affine map is convex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_add_submonoid", "description": "The convex sets form an additive submonoid under pointwise addition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_multiset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.star_convex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone_on.convex_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.is_linear_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone.convex_gt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_halfspace_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_halfspace_gt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.mem_smul_of_zero_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.add_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "std_simplex_eq_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.subsingleton.convex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_Inter\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.segment_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_open_segment", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.is_linear_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_iff_open_segment_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone_on.convex_gt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.smul_mem_of_zero_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_segment", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_sInter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.mk_iso_hom_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.hom.comm_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.iso_app_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.mk_iso_inv_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.comp_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.shift_functor_add_hom_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.zero_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.has_zero_object", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.shift_functor_obj_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.iso_app", "description": "An isomorphism of differential objects gives an isomorphism of the underlying objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.hom.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.category_of_differential_objects", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.id_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.hom.comp", "description": "The composition of morphisms of differential objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.hom.comp_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.shift_functor_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.mk_iso", "description": " An isomorphism of differential objects can be constructed\nfrom an isomorphism of the underlying objects that commutes with the differentials.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_differential_object_obj_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.shift_functor_add", "description": "The shift functor on `differential_object C` is additive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.shift_zero_hom_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.concrete_category_of_differential_objects", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_differential_object_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_differential_object", "description": "A functor `F : C \u2964 D` which commutes with shift functors on `C` and `D` and preserves zero morphisms\ncan be lifted to a functor `differential_object C \u2964 differential_object D`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.hom.id_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.d_squared", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.eq_to_hom_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.iso_app_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.has_zero_morphisms", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.shift_functor_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.category_theory.has_forget\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object", "description": "A differential object in a category with zero morphisms and a shift is\nan object `X` equipped with\na morphism `d : X \u27f6 X\u27e61\u27e7`, such that `d^2 = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.X", "description": "A differential object in a category with zero morphisms and a shift is\nan object `X` equipped with\na morphism `d : X \u27f6 X\u27e61\u27e7`, such that `d^2 = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.d", "description": "A differential object in a category with zero morphisms and a shift is\nan object `X` equipped with\na morphism `d : X \u27f6 X\u27e61\u27e7`, such that `d^2 = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.d_squared'", "description": "A differential object in a category with zero morphisms and a shift is\nan object `X` equipped with\na morphism `d : X \u27f6 X\u27e61\u27e7`, such that `d^2 = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.shift_zero", "description": "The shift by zero is naturally isomorphic to the identity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.iso_app_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.shift_functor_add_inv_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.shift_functor", "description": "The shift functor on `differential_object C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.hom.id", "description": "The identity morphism of a differential object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.shift_zero_inv_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.forget_faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.hom.comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.forget", "description": "The forgetful functor taking a differential object to its underlying object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.iso_app_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.int.category_theory.has_shift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.iso_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.hom", "description": "A morphism of differential objects is a morphism commuting with the differentials.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.hom.f", "description": "A morphism of differential objects is a morphism commuting with the differentials.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.hom.comm'", "description": "A morphism of differential objects is a morphism commuting with the differentials.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_differential_object_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sheaf.obj_sup_iso_prod_eq_locus_hom_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition.pairwise_to_opens_le_cover.category_theory.functor.final", "description": "The diagram consisting of the `U i` and `U i \u2293 U j` is cofinal in the diagram\nof all opens contained in some `U i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sheaf.obj_sup_iso_prod_eq_locus_inv_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sheaf.inter_union_pullback_cone_lift", "description": " (Implementation).\nEvery cone over `F(U) \u27f6 F(U \u2293 V)` and `F(V) \u27f6 F(U \u2293 V)` factors through `F(U \u2294 V)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sheaf.inter_union_pullback_cone_lift_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sheaf.obj_sup_iso_prod_eq_locus_hom_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition.pairwise_to_opens_le_cover_obj", "description": "Implementation detail:\nthe object level of `pairwise_to_opens_le_cover : pairwise \u03b9 \u2964 opens_le_cover U`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sheaf.is_limit_pullback_cone", "description": "For a sheaf `F`, `F(U \u2294 V)` is the pullback of `F(U) \u27f6 F(U \u2293 V)` and `F(V) \u27f6 F(U \u2293 V)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sheaf.inter_union_pullback_cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition.pairwise_cocone_iso", "description": "The cocone `pairwise.cocone U` with cocone point `supr U` over `pairwise.diagram U` is isomorphic\nto the cocone `opens_le_cover_cocone U` (with the same cocone point)\nafter appropriate whiskering and postcomposition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.is_sheaf_pairwise_intersections", "description": "An alternative formulation of the sheaf condition\n(which we prove equivalent to the usual one below as\n`is_sheaf_iff_is_sheaf_pairwise_intersections`).\n\nA presheaf is a sheaf if `F` sends the cone `(pairwise.cocone U).op` to a limit cone.\n(Recall `pairwise.cocone U` has cone point `supr U`, mapping down to the `U i` and the `U i \u2293 U j`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sheaf.obj_sup_iso_prod_eq_locus", "description": "`F(U \u2294 V)` is isomorphic to the `eq_locus` of the two maps `F(U) \u00d7 F(V) \u27f6 F(U \u2293 V)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sheaf.inter_union_pullback_cone_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.is_sheaf_preserves_limit_pairwise_intersections", "description": "An alternative formulation of the sheaf condition\n(which we prove equivalent to the usual one below as\n`is_sheaf_iff_is_sheaf_preserves_limit_pairwise_intersections`).\n\nA presheaf is a sheaf if `F` preserves the limit of `pairwise.diagram U`.\n(Recall `pairwise.diagram U` is the diagram consisting of the pairwise intersections\n`U i \u2293 U j` mapping into the open sets `U i`. This diagram has limit `supr U`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition.pairwise_to_opens_le_cover_map_2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition.pairwise_to_opens_le_cover_map", "description": "Implementation detail:\nthe morphism level of `pairwise_to_opens_le_cover : pairwise \u03b9 \u2964 opens_le_cover U`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.is_sheaf_iff_is_sheaf_preserves_limit_pairwise_intersections", "description": "The sheaf condition in terms of an equalizer diagram is equivalent\nto the reformulation in terms of the presheaf preserving the limit of the diagram\nconsisting of the `U i` and `U i \u2293 U j`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.is_sheaf_opens_le_cover_iff_is_sheaf_pairwise_intersections", "description": "The sheaf condition\nin terms of a limit diagram over all `{ V : opens X // \u2203 i, V \u2264 U i }`\nis equivalent to the reformulation\nin terms of a limit diagram over `U i` and `U i \u2293 U j`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.is_sheaf_iff_is_sheaf_pairwise_intersections", "description": "The sheaf condition in terms of an equalizer diagram is equivalent\nto the reformulation in terms of a limit diagram over `U i` and `U i \u2293 U j`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sheaf.is_product_of_disjoint", "description": "If `U, V` are disjoint, then `F(U \u2294 V) = F(U) \u00d7 F(V)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition.pairwise_to_opens_le_cover", "description": "The category of single and double intersections of the `U i` maps into the category\nof open sets below some `U i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition.pairwise_diagram_iso", "description": "The diagram in `opens X` indexed by pairwise intersections from `U` is isomorphic\n(in fact, equal) to the diagram factored through `opens_le_cover U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition.pairwise_to_opens_le_cover_obj_2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sheaf.inter_union_pullback_cone_lift_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sheaf.obj_sup_iso_prod_eq_locus_inv_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sheaf.inter_union_pullback_cone", "description": " For a sheaf `F`, `F(U \u2294 V)` is the pullback of `F(U) \u27f6 F(U \u2293 V)` and `F(V) \u27f6 F(U \u2293 V)`.\nThis is the pullback cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.sheaf.inter_union_pullback_cone_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheaf_condition.category_theory.structured_arrow.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization_unit_is_iso'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_ring_hom_of_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.epi'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CommRing.is_local_ring_hom_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization_unit_is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_localization.epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_ring_hom_of_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.sat", "description": "Matches a single character satisfying the given predicate.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.eof", "description": "Matches the end of the input.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.one_of'", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.pure", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.run_string", "description": "Runs a parser on the given input.  The parser needs to match the complete input.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.foldl", "description": "Matches zero or more occurrences of `p`, and folds the result.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.many'", "description": "Matches zero or more occurrences of `p`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.any_char", "description": "Matches a single character. Fails only if there is no more input.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.alternative", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.digit", "description": "Matches a digit (0-9).", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.sep_by1", "description": "Matches one or more occurrences of `p`, separated by `sep`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.orelse", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.many", "description": "Matches zero or more occurrences of `p`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.bind", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.mk_error_msg", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.foldr", "description": "Matches zero or more occurrences of `p`, and folds the result.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.foldl_core", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.is_lawful_monad", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.monad", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.many1", "description": "Matches one or more occurrences of `p`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.fail", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.fix_core", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.eps", "description": "Matches the empty word.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.one_of", "description": "Matches one out of a list of characters.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.many_char1", "description": "Matches one or more occurences of the char parser `p` and implodes them into a string.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.sep_by", "description": "Matches zero or more occurrences of `p`, separated by `sep`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.monad_fail", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.decorate_errors", "description": "Overrides the expected token name, and does not consume input on failure.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.run", "description": "Runs a parser on the given input.  The parser needs to match the complete input.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.ch", "description": "Matches the given character.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.remaining", "description": "Number of remaining input characters.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.fix", "description": "Fixpoint combinator satisfying `fix F = F (fix F)`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.nat", "description": " Matches a natural number. Large numbers may cause performance issues, so\ndon't run this parser on untrusted input.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.failure", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parse_result", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parse_result.done", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parse_result.fail", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.str", "description": "Matches a string.  Does not consume input in case of failure.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.many_char", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.foldr_core", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.char_buf", "description": "Matches a whole char_buffer.  Does not consume input in case of failure.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser", "description": "The parser monad. If you are familiar with the Parsec library in Haskell, you will understand this.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "parser.decorate_error", "description": "Overrides the expected token name, and does not consume input on failure.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.encoding_\u0393", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.encoding_encode", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.sigma_imp", "description": " Applies `imp` to two elements of `(\u03a3 n, L.bounded_formula \u03b1 n)`,\nor returns `default` if not possible.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.list_decode", "description": "Decodes a list of symbols as a list of formulas.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.encodable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.list_encode", "description": "Encodes a bounded formula as a list of symbols.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.encoding_decode", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.list_encode_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.small", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.list_encode", "description": "Encodes a term as a list of variables and function symbols.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.countable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.sigma_all", "description": " Applies the `forall` quantifier to an element of `(\u03a3 n, L.bounded_formula \u03b1 n)`,\nor returns `default` if not possible.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.list_decode_encode_list", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.list_decode_encode_list", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.encoding_encode", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.card_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.list_encode_sigma_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.encoding", "description": "An encoding of bounded formulas as lists.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.card_sigma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.encoding_\u0393", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.list_decode", "description": "Decodes a list of variables and function symbols as a list of terms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.card_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.bounded_formula.encoding_decode", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.encoding", "description": "An encoding of terms as lists.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_nilpotent_neg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_reduced_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_nilpotent_mul_left_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.is_nilpotent_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_reduced_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_nilpotent.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zero_is_radical_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_radical", "description": "An element `y` in a monoid is radical if for any element `x`, `y` divides `x` whenever it\n divides a power of `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_nilpotent.mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_nilpotent.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_nilpotent.eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_reduced_of_no_zero_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.is_nilpotent_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_nilpotent_mul_right_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.is_nilpotent.mapq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.is_nilpotent_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_reduced", "description": "A structure that has zero and pow is reduced if it has no nonzero nilpotent elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_reduced.eq_zero", "description": "A structure that has zero and pow is reduced if it has no nonzero nilpotent elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilradical_le_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_reduced_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_nilradical", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_nilpotent", "description": " An element is said to be nilpotent if some natural-number-power of it equals zero.\n\nNote that we require only the bare minimum assumptions for the definition to make sense. Even\n`monoid_with_zero` is too strong since nilpotency is important in the study of rings that are only\npower-associative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_nilpotent_iff_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_reduced_iff_pow_one_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilpotent_iff_mem_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_radical_iff_pow_one_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_nilpotent.zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.ker_is_radical_iff_reduced_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_radical_iff_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilradical_eq_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilradical", "description": "The nilradical of a commutative semiring is the ideal of nilpotent elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nilradical_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.is_nilpotent_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "representation.is_proj_average_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_algebra.mul_average_left", "description": "`average k G` is invariant under left multiplication by elements of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "representation.lin_hom.invariants_equiv_Rep_hom", "description": " The invariants of the representation `lin_hom X.\u03c1 Y.\u03c1` correspond to the the representation\nhomomorphisms from `X` to `Y`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "representation.average_map_id", "description": "The `average_map` acts as the identity on the subspace of invariants.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "representation.lin_hom.invariants_equiv_Rep_hom_apply_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "representation.lin_hom.invariants_equiv_fdRep_hom", "description": " The invariants of the representation `lin_hom X.\u03c1 Y.\u03c1` correspond to the the representation\nhomomorphisms from `X` to `Y`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "representation.invariants", "description": "The subspace of invariants, consisting of the vectors fixed by all elements of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "representation.mem_invariants", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_algebra.mul_average_right", "description": "`average k G` is invariant under right multiplication by elements of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_algebra.average", "description": "The average of all elements of the group `G`, considered as an element of `monoid_algebra k G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "representation.average_map", "description": "The action of `average k G` gives a projection map onto the subspace of invariants.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "representation.invariants_eq_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "representation.lin_hom.mem_invariants_iff_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "representation.average_map_invariant", "description": "The `average_map` sends elements of `V` to the subspace of invariants.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "representation.lin_hom.invariants_equiv_Rep_hom_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.prod", "description": "The cartesian product of two continuous multilinear maps, as a continuous multilinear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.to_continuous_linear_map", "description": " If `f` is a continuous multilinear map, then `f.to_continuous_linear_map m i` is the continuous\nlinear map obtained by fixing all coordinates but `i` equal to those of `m`, and varying the\n`i`-th coordinate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.of_subsingleton_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.neg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.to_multilinear_map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.map_sum_finset", "description": " If `f` is continuous multilinear, then `f (\u03a3_{j\u2081 \u2208 A\u2081} g\u2081 j\u2081, ..., \u03a3_{j\u2099 \u2208 A\u2099} g\u2099 j\u2099)` is the\nsum of `f (g\u2081 (r 1), ..., g\u2099 (r n))` where `r` ranges over all functions with `r 1 \u2208 A\u2081`, ...,\n`r n \u2208 A\u2099`. This follows from multilinearity by expanding successively with respect to each\ncoordinate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.mk_pi_algebra_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.of_subsingleton_to_multilinear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map", "description": " Continuous multilinear maps over the ring `R`, from `\u03a0i, M\u2081 i` to `M\u2082` where `M\u2081 i` and `M\u2082`\nare modules over `R` with a topological structure. In applications, there will be compatibility\nconditions between the algebraic and the topological structures, but this is not needed for the\ndefinition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.to_multilinear_map", "description": " Continuous multilinear maps over the ring `R`, from `\u03a0i, M\u2081 i` to `M\u2082` where `M\u2081 i` and `M\u2082`\nare modules over `R` with a topological structure. In applications, there will be compatibility\nconditions between the algebraic and the topological structures, but this is not needed for the\ndefinition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.cont", "description": " Continuous multilinear maps over the ring `R`, from `\u03a0i, M\u2081 i` to `M\u2082` where `M\u2081 i` and `M\u2082`\nare modules over `R` with a topological structure. In applications, there will be compatibility\nconditions between the algebraic and the topological structures, but this is not needed for the\ndefinition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.apply_add_hom", "description": "Evaluation of a `continuous_multilinear_map` at a vector as an `add_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.has_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.to_multilinear_map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.map_smul_univ", "description": " Multiplicativity of a continuous multilinear map along all coordinates at the same time,\nwriting `f (\u03bb i, c i \u2022 m i)` as `(\u220f i, c i) \u2022 f m`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.cons_smul", "description": " In the specific case of continuous multilinear maps on spaces indexed by `fin (n+1)`, where one\ncan build an element of `\u03a0(i : fin (n+1)), M i` using `cons`, one can express directly the\nmultiplicativity of a multilinear map along the first variable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.to_multilinear_map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.mk_pi_algebra_fin_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.dom_dom_congr_equiv", "description": " An equivalence of the index set defines an equivalence between the spaces of continuous\nmultilinear maps. In case of normed spaces, this is a linear isometric equivalence, see\n`continuous.multilinear_map.dom_dom_congr\u2097\u1d62`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.coe_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.continuous_map_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.map_coord_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.cons_add", "description": " In the specific case of continuous multilinear maps on spaces indexed by `fin (n+1)`, where one\ncan build an element of `\u03a0(i : fin (n+1)), M i` using `cons`, one can express directly the\nadditivity of a multilinear map along the first variable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.is_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.map_piecewise_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.coe_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.const_of_is_empty_to_multilinear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.dom_dom_congr", "description": " An equivalence of the index set defines an equivalence between the spaces of continuous\nmultilinear maps. This is the forward map of this equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.cod_restrict_to_multilinear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.dom_dom_congr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.pi_linear_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.sub_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.smul_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.restrict_scalars", "description": " Reinterpret an `A`-multilinear map as an `R`-multilinear map, if `A` is an algebra over `R`\nand their actions on all involved modules agree with the action of `R` on `A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.pi_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.cod_restrict", "description": "Restrict the codomain of a continuous multilinear map to a submodule.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.dom_dom_congr_to_multilinear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.cod_restrict_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.pi", "description": " Combine a family of continuous multilinear maps with the same domain and codomains `M' i` into a\ncontinuous multilinear map taking values in the space of functions `\u03a0 i, M' i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.to_multilinear_map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.comp_continuous_linear_map", "description": " If `g` is continuous multilinear and `f` is a collection of continuous linear maps,\nthen `g (f\u2081 m\u2081, ..., f\u2099 m\u2099)` is again a continuous multilinear map, that we call\n`g.comp_continuous_linear_map f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.comp_continuous_multilinear_map_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.to_multilinear_map_linear", "description": " Linear map version of the map `to_multilinear_map` associating to a continuous multilinear map\nthe corresponding multilinear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.mk_pi_algebra_fin", "description": " The continuous multilinear map on `A^n`, where `A` is a normed algebra over `\ud835\udd5c`, associating to\n`m` the product of all the `m i`.\n\nSee also: `continuous_multilinear_map.mk_pi_algebra`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.map_sum", "description": " If `f` is continuous multilinear, then `f (\u03a3_{j\u2081} g\u2081 j\u2081, ..., \u03a3_{j\u2099} g\u2099 j\u2099)` is the sum of\n`f (g\u2081 (r 1), ..., g\u2099 (r n))` where `r` ranges over all functions `r`. This follows from\nmultilinearity by expanding successively with respect to each coordinate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.pi_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.dom_dom_congr_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.pi_equiv", "description": "`continuous_multilinear_map.pi` as an `equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.smul_right_to_multilinear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.pi_linear_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.comp_continuous_multilinear_map", "description": " Composing a continuous multilinear map with a continuous linear map gives again a\ncontinuous multilinear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.smul_right_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.add_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.simps.apply", "description": "See Note [custom simps projection]. We need to specify this projection explicitly in this case,\n because it is a composition of multiple projections.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.map_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.comp_continuous_linear_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.map_piecewise_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.const_of_is_empty", "description": "The constant map is multilinear when `\u03b9` is empty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.pi_linear_equiv", "description": "`continuous_multilinear_map.pi` as a `linear_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.sum_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.dom_dom_congr_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.map_add_univ", "description": " Additivity of a continuous multilinear map along all coordinates at the same time,\nwriting `f (m + m')` as the sum  of `f (s.piecewise m m')` over all sets `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.to_multilinear_map_linear_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.smul_right", "description": " Given a continuous `R`-multilinear map `f` taking values in `R`, `f.smul_right z` is the\ncontinuous multilinear map sending `m` to `f m \u2022 z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.module", "description": " The space of continuous multilinear maps over an algebra over `R` is a module over `R`, for the\npointwise addition and scalar multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.coe_restrict_scalars", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.of_subsingleton", "description": "The evaluation map from `\u03b9 \u2192 M\u2082` to `M\u2082` is multilinear at a given `i` when `\u03b9` is subsingleton.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.pi_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.mk_pi_algebra", "description": " The continuous multilinear map on `A^\u03b9`, where `A` is a normed commutative algebra\nover `\ud835\udd5c`, associating to `m` the product of all the `m i`.\n\nSee also `continuous_multilinear_map.mk_pi_algebra_fin`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.const_of_is_empty_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "expr_lens.to_tactic_string", "description": "Pretty print a lens.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "expr_lens.zoom", "description": " Zoom into `e : expr` given the context of an `expr_lens`, popping out an `expr` and a new\nzoomed `expr_lens`, if this is possible (`e` has to be an application).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "expr_lens.mk_congr_arg_using_dsimp", "description": " Sometimes `mk_congr_arg` fails, when the function is 'superficially dependent'.\nTry to `dsimp` the function first before building the `congr_arg` expression.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "expr_lens.dir", "description": " Inductive type with two constructors `F` and `A`,\nthat represent the function-part `f` and arg-part `a` of an application `f a`. They specify the\ndirections in which an `expr_lens` should zoom into an `expr`.\n\nThis type is used in the development of rewriting tactics such as `nth_rewrite` and\n`rewrite_search`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "expr_lens.dir.F", "description": " Inductive type with two constructors `F` and `A`,\nthat represent the function-part `f` and arg-part `a` of an application `f a`. They specify the\ndirections in which an `expr_lens` should zoom into an `expr`.\n\nThis type is used in the development of rewriting tactics such as `nth_rewrite` and\n`rewrite_search`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "expr_lens.dir.A", "description": " Inductive type with two constructors `F` and `A`,\nthat represent the function-part `f` and arg-part `a` of an application `f a`. They specify the\ndirections in which an `expr_lens` should zoom into an `expr`.\n\nThis type is used in the development of rewriting tactics such as `nth_rewrite` and\n`rewrite_search`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "expr_lens.to_dirs", "description": " Convert an `expr_lens` into a list of instructions needed to build it; repeatedly inspecting a\nfunction or its argument a finite number of times.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "expr_lens.dir.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "expr.app_map", "description": " `app_map F e` maps a function `F` which understands `expr_lens`es\nover the given `e : expr` in the natural way;\nthat is, make holes in `e` everywhere where that is possible\n(generating `expr_lens`es in the process),\nand at each stage call the function `F` passing\nboth the `expr_lens` generated and the `expr` which was removed to make the hole.\n\nAt each stage `F` returns a list of some type, and `app_map` collects these lists together and\nreturns a concatenation of them all.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "expr_lens", "description": " You're supposed to think of an `expr_lens` as a big set of nested applications with a single\nhole which needs to be filled, either in a function spot or argument spot. `expr_lens.fill` can\nfill this hole and turn your lens back into a real `expr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "expr_lens.app_fun", "description": " You're supposed to think of an `expr_lens` as a big set of nested applications with a single\nhole which needs to be filled, either in a function spot or argument spot. `expr_lens.fill` can\nfill this hole and turn your lens back into a real `expr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "expr_lens.app_arg", "description": " You're supposed to think of an `expr_lens` as a big set of nested applications with a single\nhole which needs to be filled, either in a function spot or argument spot. `expr_lens.fill` can\nfill this hole and turn your lens back into a real `expr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "expr_lens.entire", "description": " You're supposed to think of an `expr_lens` as a big set of nested applications with a single\nhole which needs to be filled, either in a function spot or argument spot. `expr_lens.fill` can\nfill this hole and turn your lens back into a real `expr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "expr_lens.dir.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "expr_lens.dir.has_to_string", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "expr_lens.dir.to_string", "description": "String representation of `dir`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "expr_lens.congr", "description": " Turn an `e : expr_lens` and a proof that `a = b` into a series of `congr_arg` or `congr_fun`\napplications showing that the expressions obtained from `e.fill a` and `e.fill b` are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "expr_lens.fill", "description": "Fill the function or argument hole in this lens with the given `expr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.category_theory.concrete_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.inhabited_graded_object", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.comap_eq_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.comap_eq_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object", "description": "A type synonym for `\u03b2 \u2192 C`, used for `\u03b2`-graded objects in a category `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object_with_shift", "description": "A type synonym for `\u03b2 \u2192 C`, used for `\u03b2`-graded objects in a category `C`\nwith a shift functor given by translation by `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.comap_equiv", "description": "The equivalence between \u03b2-graded objects and \u03b3-graded objects,\ngiven an equivalence between \u03b2 and \u03b3.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.has_zero_morphisms", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.shift_functor_obj_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.comap_equiv_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.eq_to_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.comap_eq", "description": "The natural isomorphism comparing between\npulling back along two propositionally equal functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.category_theory.has_forget\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.shift_functor_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.eval", "description": "The projection of a graded object to its `i`-th component.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.comap_eq_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.eval_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.category_of_graded_objects", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.has_shift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.comap_equiv_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.has_zero_object", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.comap_equiv_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.comap_eq_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.comap_equiv_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.total", "description": "The total object of a graded object is the coproduct of the graded components.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.eval_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.graded_object.total.category_theory.faithful", "description": "The `total` functor taking a graded object to the coproduct of its graded components is faithful.\nTo prove this, we need to know that the coprojections into the coproduct are monomorphisms,\nwhich follows from the fact we have zero morphisms and decidable equality for the grading.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.vars_sub_of_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.coeff_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.degree_of_sub_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.support_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.eval\u2082_hom_X", "description": " A ring homomorphism f : Z[X_1, X_2, ...] \u2192 R\nis determined by the evaluations f(X_1), f(X_2), ...", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.hom_equiv", "description": " Ring homomorphisms out of integer polynomials on a type `\u03c3` are the same as\nfunctions out of the type `\u03c3`,", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.vars_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.eval\u2082_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.C_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.coeff_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.vars_sub_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.support_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.eval\u2082_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.degrees_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.hom_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.total_degree_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.total_degree_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.degrees_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.C_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.bot_covering", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.discrete", "description": "The discrete Grothendieck topology, in which every sieve is covering.\n\nSee https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grothendieck_topology#The_discrete_and_indiscrete_topologies.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.map_Y\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow.from_middle", "description": "An arrow in bind has the form `A \u27f6 B \u27f6 X` where `A \u27f6 B` is an arrow in `T I` for some `I`.\nand `B \u27f6 X` is an arrow of `S`. This is the hom `B \u27f6 X`, as an arrow.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.map_g\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.covering_iff_covers_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.arrow_intersect", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.pullback_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.arrow_trans", "description": "The transitivity axiom in 'arrow' form: If `S` covers `f` and every arrow in `S` is covered by\n`R`, then `R` covers `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.dense", "description": "The dense Grothendieck topology.\n\nSee https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/dense+topology, or [MM92] Chapter III, Section 2, example (e).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.base_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.top_covering", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.discrete_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.covers", "description": "The sieve `S` on `X` `J`-covers an arrow `f` to `X` if `S.pullback f \u2208 J Y`.\nThis definition is an alternate way of presenting a Grothendieck topology.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.pullback_id", "description": "Pulling back along the identity is naturally isomorphic to the identity functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.map_f\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.dense_covering", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.preorder", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.trivial_covering", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.base", "description": "A relation of `S.pullback f` gives rise to a relation of `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.multifork", "description": " The natural multifork associated to `S : J.cover X` for a presheaf `P`.\nSaying that this multifork is a limit is essentially equivalent to the sheaf condition at the\ngiven object for the given covering sieve. See `sheaf.lean` for an equivalent sheaf condition\nusing this.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow.base_Y", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.map_Y\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.top_covers", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.base_Z", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.base_f\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.ext", "description": "An extensionality lemma in terms of the coercion to a pi-type.\nWe prove this explicitly rather than deriving it so that it is in terms of the coercion rather than\nthe projection `.sieves`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.base_Y\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow.to_middle", "description": "An arrow in bind has the form `A \u27f6 B \u27f6 X` where `A \u27f6 B` is an arrow in `T I` for some `I`.\nand `B \u27f6 X` is an arrow of `S`. This is the hom `A \u27f6 B`, as an arrow.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.index", "description": "To every `S : J.cover X` and presheaf `P`, associate a `multicospan_index`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.arrow_max", "description": "The maximality axiom in 'arrow' form: Any arrow `f` in `S` is covered by `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.base_g\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology", "description": "The definition of a Grothendieck topology: a set of sieves `J X` on each object `X` satisfying\nthree axioms:\n1. For every object `X`, the maximal sieve is in `J X`.\n2. If `S \u2208 J X` then its pullback along any `h : Y \u27f6 X` is in `J Y`.\n3. If `S \u2208 J X` and `R` is a sieve on `X`, then provided that the pullback of `R` along any arrow\n   `f : Y \u27f6 X` in `S` is in `J Y`, we have that `R` itself is in `J X`.\n\nA sieve `S` on `X` is referred to as `J`-covering, (or just covering), if `S \u2208 J X`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z4>, or [nlab], or [MM92][] Chapter III, Section 2,\nDefinition 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.sieves", "description": "The definition of a Grothendieck topology: a set of sieves `J X` on each object `X` satisfying\nthree axioms:\n1. For every object `X`, the maximal sieve is in `J X`.\n2. If `S \u2208 J X` then its pullback along any `h : Y \u27f6 X` is in `J Y`.\n3. If `S \u2208 J X` and `R` is a sieve on `X`, then provided that the pullback of `R` along any arrow\n   `f : Y \u27f6 X` in `S` is in `J Y`, we have that `R` itself is in `J X`.\n\nA sieve `S` on `X` is referred to as `J`-covering, (or just covering), if `S \u2208 J X`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z4>, or [nlab], or [MM92][] Chapter III, Section 2,\nDefinition 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.top_mem'", "description": "The definition of a Grothendieck topology: a set of sieves `J X` on each object `X` satisfying\nthree axioms:\n1. For every object `X`, the maximal sieve is in `J X`.\n2. If `S \u2208 J X` then its pullback along any `h : Y \u27f6 X` is in `J Y`.\n3. If `S \u2208 J X` and `R` is a sieve on `X`, then provided that the pullback of `R` along any arrow\n   `f : Y \u27f6 X` in `S` is in `J Y`, we have that `R` itself is in `J X`.\n\nA sieve `S` on `X` is referred to as `J`-covering, (or just covering), if `S \u2208 J X`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z4>, or [nlab], or [MM92][] Chapter III, Section 2,\nDefinition 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.pullback_stable'", "description": "The definition of a Grothendieck topology: a set of sieves `J X` on each object `X` satisfying\nthree axioms:\n1. For every object `X`, the maximal sieve is in `J X`.\n2. If `S \u2208 J X` then its pullback along any `h : Y \u27f6 X` is in `J Y`.\n3. If `S \u2208 J X` and `R` is a sieve on `X`, then provided that the pullback of `R` along any arrow\n   `f : Y \u27f6 X` in `S` is in `J Y`, we have that `R` itself is in `J X`.\n\nA sieve `S` on `X` is referred to as `J`-covering, (or just covering), if `S \u2208 J X`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z4>, or [nlab], or [MM92][] Chapter III, Section 2,\nDefinition 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.transitive'", "description": "The definition of a Grothendieck topology: a set of sieves `J X` on each object `X` satisfying\nthree axioms:\n1. For every object `X`, the maximal sieve is in `J X`.\n2. If `S \u2208 J X` then its pullback along any `h : Y \u27f6 X` is in `J Y`.\n3. If `S \u2208 J X` and `R` is a sieve on `X`, then provided that the pullback of `R` along any arrow\n   `f : Y \u27f6 X` in `S` is in `J Y`, we have that `R` itself is in `J X`.\n\nA sieve `S` on `X` is referred to as `J`-covering, (or just covering), if `S \u2208 J X`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z4>, or [nlab], or [MM92][] Chapter III, Section 2,\nDefinition 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.atomic", "description": "The atomic Grothendieck topology: a sieve is covering iff it is nonempty.\nFor the pullback stability condition, we need the right Ore condition to hold.\n\nSee https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/atomic+site, or [MM92] Chapter III, Section 2, example (f).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.base_g\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.coe_fun_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.pullback_comp", "description": "Pulling back with respect to a composition is the composition of the pullbacks.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.partial_order", "description": "See <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z6>", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.coe_pullback", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow.middle_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.snd", "description": " The second `arrow` associated to a `relation`.\nUsed in defining `index` in `plus.lean`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.arrow_stable", "description": "The stability axiom in 'arrow' form: If `S` covers `f` then `S` covers `g \u226b f` for any `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.fst_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.map_g\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow.map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.map", "description": "Map a `relation` along a refinement `S \u27f6 T`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.covers_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation", "description": "An auxiliary structure, used to define `S.index` in `plus.lean`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.Y\u2081", "description": "An auxiliary structure, used to define `S.index` in `plus.lean`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.Y\u2082", "description": "An auxiliary structure, used to define `S.index` in `plus.lean`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.Z", "description": "An auxiliary structure, used to define `S.index` in `plus.lean`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.g\u2081", "description": "An auxiliary structure, used to define `S.index` in `plus.lean`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.g\u2082", "description": "An auxiliary structure, used to define `S.index` in `plus.lean`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.f\u2081", "description": "An auxiliary structure, used to define `S.index` in `plus.lean`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.f\u2082", "description": "An auxiliary structure, used to define `S.index` in `plus.lean`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.h\u2081", "description": "An auxiliary structure, used to define `S.index` in `plus.lean`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.h\u2082", "description": "An auxiliary structure, used to define `S.index` in `plus.lean`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.w", "description": "An auxiliary structure, used to define `S.index` in `plus.lean`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.mem_sieves_iff_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.bind_covering", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.condition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.pullback_id", "description": "The isomorphism between `S` and the pullback of `S` w.r.t. the identity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.covering_of_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.transitive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.base_f\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.pullback", "description": "Pull back a cover along a morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.snd_Y", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.category_theory.sieve.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.semilattice_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow.to_middle_condition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.map_Z", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.trivial_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.right_ore_of_pullbacks", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow.base_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow.middle", "description": "An arrow in bind has the form `A \u27f6 B \u27f6 X` where `A \u27f6 B` is an arrow in `T I` for some `I`.\nand `B \u27f6 X` is an arrow of `S`. This is the object `B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.intersection_covering_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.right_ore_condition", "description": "A category satisfies the right Ore condition if any span can be completed to a commutative square.\nNB. Any category with pullbacks obviously satisfies the right Ore condition, see\n`right_ore_of_pullbacks`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.bind_to_base", "description": "The canonical moprhism from `S.bind T` to `T`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.snd_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover", "description": " `J.cover X` denotes the poset of covers of `X` with respect to the\nGrothendieck topology `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.bind", "description": "Combine a family of covers over a cover.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow.base", "description": "An arrow of `S.pullback f` gives rise to an arrow of `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow.from_middle_condition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow", "description": "An auxiliary structure, used to define `S.index` in `plus.lean`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow.Y", "description": "An auxiliary structure, used to define `S.index` in `plus.lean`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow.f", "description": "An auxiliary structure, used to define `S.index` in `plus.lean`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow.hf", "description": "An auxiliary structure, used to define `S.index` in `plus.lean`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.map_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.complete_lattice", "description": "Construct a complete lattice from the `Inf`, but make the trivial and discrete topologies\ndefinitionally equal to the bottom and top respectively.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.pullback_stable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.to_multiequalizer", "description": " The canonical map from `P.obj (op X)` to the multiequalizer associated to a covering sieve,\nassuming such a multiequalizer exists. This will be used in `sheaf.lean` to provide an equivalent\nsheaf condition in terms of multiequalizers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.pullback", "description": "Pull back a cover along a morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.intersection_covering", "description": "The intersection of two covering sieves is covering.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z5> (1), or [MM92] Chapter III,\nSection 2, Definition 1 (iv).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.base_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.trivial", "description": "The trivial Grothendieck topology, in which only the maximal sieve is covering. This topology is\nalso known as the indiscrete, coarse, or chaotic topology.\n\nSee [MM92] Chapter III, Section 2, example (a), or\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grothendieck_topology#The_discrete_and_indiscrete_topologies", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.pullback_comp", "description": " Pulling back along a composition is naturally isomorphic to\nthe composition of the pullbacks.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.has_Inf", "description": "See <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z7>", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.top_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.fst", "description": " The first `arrow` associated to a `relation`.\nUsed in defining `index` in `plus.lean`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow.to_middle_hom", "description": "An arrow in bind has the form `A \u27f6 B \u27f6 X` where `A \u27f6 B` is an arrow in `T I` for some `I`.\nand `B \u27f6 X` is an arrow of `S`. This is the hom `A \u27f6 B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.is_glb_Inf", "description": "See <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z7>", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.superset_covering", "description": "If `S` is a subset of `R`, and `S` is covering, then `R` is covering as well.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z5> (2), or discussion after [MM92] Chapter III,\nSection 2, Definition 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.le_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.fst_Y", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow.map", "description": "Map a `arrow` along a refinement `S \u27f6 T`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.map_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.base_Y\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.bot_covers", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow.from_middle_hom", "description": "An arrow in bind has the form `A \u27f6 B \u27f6 X` where `A \u27f6 B` is an arrow in `T I` for some `I`.\nand `B \u27f6 X` is an arrow of `S`. This is the hom `B \u27f6 X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.relation.map_f\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cover.arrow.map_Y", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.has_le", "description": "See <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00Z6>",