od_eq_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.Coprod_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.pi", "description": "The product of an indexed family of filters.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.pi_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.le_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.pi_le_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.Coprod", "description": "Coproduct of filters.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually.eval_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.Coprod_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.pi_inf_principal_univ_pi_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.mem_pi_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.ne_bot.Coprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.pi_inf_principal_pi_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.pi_inf_principal_univ_pi_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.mem_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.mem_sphere", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.cospherical_def", "description": "The definition of `cospherical`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.cospherical_empty", "description": "The empty set is cospherical.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.inner_vsub_vsub_of_mem_sphere_of_mem_sphere", "description": " Suppose that `p\u2081` and `p\u2082` lie in spheres `s\u2081` and `s\u2082`.  Then the vector between the centers\nof those spheres is orthogonal to that between `p\u2081` and `p\u2082`; this is a version of\n`inner_vsub_vsub_of_dist_eq_of_dist_eq` for bundled spheres.  (In two dimensions, this says that\nthe diagonals of a kite are orthogonal.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sbtw_of_collinear_of_dist_center_lt_radius", "description": " Given three collinear points, two on a sphere and one inside it, the one inside it is\nstrictly between the other two points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.cospherical_iff_exists_sphere", "description": "A set of points is cospherical if and only if they lie in some sphere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.cospherical_singleton", "description": "A single point is cospherical.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.concyclic", "description": " A set of points is concyclic if it is cospherical and coplanar. (Most results are stated\ndirectly in terms of `cospherical` instead of using `concyclic`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.concyclic.cospherical", "description": " A set of points is concyclic if it is cospherical and coplanar. (Most results are stated\ndirectly in terms of `cospherical` instead of using `concyclic`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.concyclic.coplanar", "description": " A set of points is concyclic if it is cospherical and coplanar. (Most results are stated\ndirectly in terms of `cospherical` instead of using `concyclic`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.inner_pos_of_dist_lt_radius", "description": " Given a point on a sphere and a point inside it, the inner product between the difference of\nthose points and the radius vector is positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.cospherical_pair", "description": "Two points are cospherical.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.cospherical.affine_independent_of_ne", "description": "The three points of a cospherical set are affinely independent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.inner_nonneg_of_dist_le_radius", "description": " Given a point on a sphere and a point not outside it, the inner product between the\ndifference of those points and the radius vector is nonnegative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.cospherical.subset", "description": "A subset of a cospherical set is cospherical.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.mem_sphere'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.dist_of_mem_subset_sphere", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.center_eq_iff_eq_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.cospherical.affine_independent_of_mem_of_ne", "description": "Any three points in a cospherical set are affinely independent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.concyclic_pair", "description": "Two points are concyclic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.wbtw_of_collinear_of_dist_center_le_radius", "description": " Given three collinear points, two on a sphere and one not outside it, the one not outside it\nis weakly between the other two points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.set.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.mk_center", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.dist_of_mem_subset_mk_sphere", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.concyclic.subset", "description": "A subset of a concyclic set is concyclic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.eq_of_mem_sphere_of_mem_sphere_of_mem_of_finrank_eq_two", "description": " Two spheres intersect in at most two points in a two-dimensional subspace containing their\ncenters; this is a version of `eq_of_dist_eq_of_dist_eq_of_mem_of_finrank_eq_two` for bundled\nspheres.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.has_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.dist_center_eq_dist_center_of_mem_sphere'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.subset_sphere", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.eq_of_mem_sphere_of_mem_sphere_of_finrank_eq_two", "description": " Two spheres intersect in at most two points in two-dimensional space; this is a version of\n`eq_of_dist_eq_of_dist_eq_of_finrank_eq_two` for bundled spheres.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.cospherical", "description": "The set of points in a sphere is cospherical.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.concyclic_singleton", "description": "A single point is concyclic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.center_ne_iff_ne_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.inner_pos_or_eq_of_dist_le_radius", "description": " Given a point on a sphere and a point not outside it, the inner product between the\ndifference of those points and the radius vector is positive unless the points are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.mk_center_radius", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.concyclic_empty", "description": "The empty set is concyclic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.mk_radius", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere", "description": " A `sphere P` bundles a `center` and `radius`. This definition does not require the radius to\nbe positive; that should be given as a hypothesis to lemmas that require it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.center", "description": " A `sphere P` bundles a `center` and `radius`. This definition does not require the radius to\nbe positive; that should be given as a hypothesis to lemmas that require it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.radius", "description": " A `sphere P` bundles a `center` and `radius`. This definition does not require the radius to\nbe positive; that should be given as a hypothesis to lemmas that require it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.ne_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.cospherical", "description": " A set of points is cospherical if they are equidistant from some\npoint.  In two dimensions, this is the same thing as being\nconcyclic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.coe_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.cospherical.affine_independent", "description": "Any three points in a cospherical set are affinely independent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.dist_center_eq_dist_center_of_mem_sphere", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sup_mem_sups", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.disj_sups_right_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nonempty.infs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sups_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.forall_infs_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.singleton_infs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.disj_sups_union_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sups_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.singleton_sups_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.infs_left_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.disj_sups_union_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.singleton_sups", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.decidable_pred_mem_lower_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sups_union_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.infs_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.disj_sups_subset_sups", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sups_union_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": 