ge_subset_infs_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.disj_sups_subset_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image_subset_infs_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.disj_sups_subset_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.subset_sups", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sups_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.disj_sups_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.infs_subset_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq.cmp_eq_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordering.swap_eq_iff_eq_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordering.compares.cmp_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordering.compares.of_swap", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `ordering.compares_swap`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cmp_to_dual", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lt_iff_lt_of_cmp_eq_cmp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cmp_le", "description": " Like `cmp`, but uses a `\u2264` on the type instead of `<`. Given two elements `x` and `y`, returns a\nthree-way comparison result `ordering`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordering.compares.le_total", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordering.compares.eq_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cmp_eq_lt_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordering.compares.eq_gt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cmp_le_of_dual", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordering.swap_or_else", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordering.compares.inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cmp_le_eq_cmp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordering.compares", "description": " `compares o a b` means that `a` and `b` have the ordering relation `o` between them, assuming\nthat the relation `a < b` is defined.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_iff_eq_of_cmp_eq_cmp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_lt.lt.cmp_eq_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_dual_compares_of_dual", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cmp_self_eq_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordering.swap_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cmp_eq_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_dual_compares_to_dual", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cmp_le_to_dual", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordering.compares_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cmp_compares", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordering.or_else_eq_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cmp_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cmp_eq_gt_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_lt.lt.cmp_eq_gt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cmp_eq_cmp_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_order_of_compares", "description": "Generate a linear order structure from a preorder and `cmp` function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cmp_le_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordering.compares.ne_gt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordering.compares.ne_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordering.compares.le_antisymm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_iff_le_of_cmp_eq_cmp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq.cmp_eq_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cmp_of_dual", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordering.compares.eq_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordering.compares.swap", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `ordering.compares_swap`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordering.compares_iff_of_compares_impl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coord_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.exists_extend", "description": " Any linear map `f : p \u2192\u2097[K] V'` defined on a subspace `p` can be extended to the whole\nspace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.ext_elem_iff", "description": "Two elements are equal iff their coordinates are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.fun_like", "description": "`b i` is the `i`th basis vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.repr_symm_single_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.mem_span_repr_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.constr", "description": " Construct a linear map given the value at the basis.\n\nThis definition is parameterized over an extra `semiring S`,\nsuch that `smul_comm_class R S M'` holds.\nIf `R` is commutative, you can set `S := R`; if `R` is not commutative,\nyou can recover an `add_equiv` by setting `S := \u2115`.\nSee library note [bundled maps over different rings].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.mk_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.sum_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.constr_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coe_mk_fin_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coe_sum_coords", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.repr_reindex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.restrict_scalars", "description": " Let `b` be a `S`-basis of `M`. Let `R` be a comm_ring such that `algebra R S` with no zero\nsmul divisors, then the submodule of `M` spanned by `b` over `R` admits `b` as a `R`-basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.linear_independent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.no_zero_smul_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.units_smul", "description": " Given a basis `v` and a map `w` such that for all `i`, `w i` is a unit, `smul_of_is_unit`\nprovides the basis corresponding to `w \u2022 v`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.prod_apply_inr_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.reindex_range_repr'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.constr_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.prod_apply_inl_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.mem_span_iff_repr_mem", "description": " Let `b` be a `S`-basis of `M`. Then `m : M` lies in the `R`-module spanned by `b` iff all the\ncoordinates of `m` on the basis `b` are in `R` (see `basis.mem_span` for the case `R = S`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.maximal", "description": "Any basis is a maximal linear independent set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.fin_two_prod", "description": "The basis of `R \u00d7 R` given by the two vectors `(1, 0)` and `(0, 1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.reindex_finset_range", "description": " `b.reindex_finset_range` is a basis indexed by `finset.univ.image b`,\nthe finite set of basis vectors themselves.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.equiv_fun", "description": "A module over `R` with a finite basis is linearly equivalent to functions from its basis to `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.equiv", "description": " If `b` is a basis for `M` and `b'` a basis for `M'`, and the index types are equivalent,\n`b.equiv b' e` is a linear equivalence `M \u2243\u2097[R] M'`, mapping `b i` to `b' (e i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.reindex_finset_range_repr_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_bot_of_rank_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.prod", "description": " `basis.prod` maps a `\u03b9`-indexed basis for `M` and a `\u03b9'`-indexed basis for `M'`\nto a `\u03b9 \u2295 \u03b9'`-index basis for `M \u00d7 M'`.\nFor the specific case of `R \u00d7 R`, see also `basis.fin_two_prod`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.card_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.mem_submodule_iff", "description": "If the submodule `P` has a basis, `x \u2208 P` iff it is a linear combination of basis vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.sum_coords_reindex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.map_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.sum_coords", "description": "The sum of the coordinates of an element `m : M` with respect to a basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coord", "description": " `b.coord i` is the linear function giving the `i`'th coordinate of a vector\nwith respect to the basis `b`.\n\n`b.coord i` is an element of the dual space. In particular, for\nfinite-dimensional spaces it is the `\u03b9`th basis vector of the dual space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.reindex_range_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.of_equiv_fun_repr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.is_unit_smul", "description": "A version of `smul_of_units` that uses `is_unit`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.mk_coord_apply", "description": " Given a basis, the `i`th element of the dual basis evaluates to the Kronecker delta on the\n`j`th element of the basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.extend_apply_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.of_vector_space_apply_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.repr_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.equiv_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.of_vector_space_index", "description": "A set used to index `basis.of_vector_space`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "atom_iff_nonzero_span", "description": " The atoms of the lattice of submodules of a module over a division ring are the\nsubmodules equal to the span of a nonzero element of the module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.exists_left_inverse_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.equiv'_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.prod_apply_inl_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.range_reindex", "description": "`simp` can prove this as `basis.coe_reindex` + `equiv_like.range_comp`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.repr_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.index_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_prod_linear_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.repr_symm_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.units_smul_span_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.smul_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.submodule.complemented_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.map_coeffs_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.mk_fin_cons", "description": " Let `b` be a basis for a submodule `N` of `M`. If `y : M` is linear independent of `N`\nand `y` and `N` together span the whole of `M`, then there is a basis for `M`\nwhose basis vectors are given by `fin.cons y b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.constr_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coord_repr_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.total_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.group_smul_span_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.sum_repr_mul_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.fin_two_prod_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.map", "description": "Apply the linear equivalence `f` to the basis vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.units_smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.mk_fin_cons_of_le", "description": " Let `b` be a basis for a submodule `N \u2264 O`. If `y \u2208 O` is linear independent of `N`\nand `y` and `N` together span the whole of `O`, then there is a basis for `O`\nwhose basis vectors are given by `fin.cons y b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.basis_singleton_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.exists_le_ker_of_lt_top", "description": " If `p < \u22a4` is a subspace of a vector space `V`, then there exists a nonzero linear map\n`f : V \u2192\u2097[K] K` such that `p \u2264 ker f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.reindex_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.mem_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.forall_coord_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.repr_total", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.map_coeffs", "description": " If `R` and `R'` are isomorphic rings that act identically on a module `M`,\nthen a basis for `M` as `R`-module is also a basis for `M` as `R'`-module.\n\nSee also `basis.algebra_map_coeffs` for the case where `f` is equal to `algebra_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.subset_extend", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.repr_sum_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis", "description": " A `basis \u03b9 R M` for a module `M` is the type of `\u03b9`-indexed `R`-bases of `M`.\n\nThe basis vectors are available as `coe_fn (b : basis \u03b9 R M) : \u03b9 \u2192 M`.\nTo turn a linear independent family of vectors spanning `M` into a basis, use `basis.mk`.\nThey are internally represented as linear equivs `M \u2243\u2097[R] (\u03b9 \u2192\u2080 R)`,\navailable as `basis.repr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.repr", "description": " A `basis \u03b9 R M` for a module `M` is the type of `\u03b9`-indexed `R`-bases of `M`.\n\nThe basis vectors are available as `coe_fn (b : basis \u03b9 R M) : \u03b9 \u2192 M`.\nTo turn a linear independent family of vectors spanning `M` into a basis, use `basis.mk`.\nThey are internally represented as linear equivs `M \u2243\u2097[R] (\u03b9 \u2192\u2080 R)`,\navailable as `basis.repr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.exists_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.span", "description": "A linear independent family of vectors is a basis for their span.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.of_vector_space", "description": "Each vector space has a basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.restrict_scalars_repr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coe_extend", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.singleton_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.prod_repr_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coe_mk_fin_cons_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.repr_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.equiv'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.equiv_fun_symm_apply", "description": " Given a basis `v` indexed by `\u03b9`, the canonical linear equivalence between `\u03b9 \u2192 R` and `M` maps\na function `x : \u03b9 \u2192 R` to the linear combination `\u2211_i x i \u2022 v i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.empty_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coe_reindex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.repr_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.ext_elem", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `basis.ext_elem_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.sum_coords_self_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.exists_is_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coe_sum_coords_of_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.repr_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.repr_apply_eq", "description": "An unbundled version of `repr_eq_iff`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.eq_of_apply_eq", "description": "Two bases are equal if their basis vectors are the same.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.prod_apply_inr_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.constr_apply_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.sum_extend", "description": "If `v` is a linear independent family of vectors, extend it to a basis indexed by a sum type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coord_units_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.span_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.constr_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coe_of_equiv_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.fintype_of_fintype", "description": "A module over a finite ring that admits a finite basis is finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.prod_repr_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.restrict_scalars_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.repr_self_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vector_space.card_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.constr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.mk_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.map_coeffs_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.equiv_fun_of_equiv_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coe_of_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.map_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.repr_units_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.singleton_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_atomistic", "description": "The lattice of submodules of a module over a division ring is atomistic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.mem_submodule_iff'", "description": " If the submodule `P` has a finite basis,\n`x \u2208 P` iff it is a linear combination of basis vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.equiv_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.of_vector_space_index.linear_independent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.dvd_coord_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.span_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.reindex", "description": "`b.reindex (e : \u03b9 \u2243 \u03b9')` is a basis indexed by `\u03b9'`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.sum_equiv_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.equiv_fun_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coe_sum_coords_eq_finsum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.repr_eq_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coe_fin_two_prod_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.of_equiv_fun", "description": " Define a basis by mapping each vector `x : M` to its coordinates `e x : \u03b9 \u2192 R`,\nas long as `\u03b9` is finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.eq_of_repr_eq_repr", "description": "Two bases are equal if they assign the same coordinates.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.group_smul", "description": " Given a basis `v` and a map `w` such that for all `i`, `w i` are elements of a group,\n`group_smul` provides the basis corresponding to `w \u2022 v`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.reindex_range_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.reindex_range_repr_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.equiv'", "description": " If `b` is a basis for `M` and `b'` a basis for `M'`,\nand `f`, `g` form a bijection between the basis vectors,\n`b.equiv' b' f g hf hg hgf hfg` is a linear equivalence `M \u2243\u2097[R] M'`, mapping `b i` to `f (b i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.induction_on_rank_aux", "description": " If `N` is a submodule with finite rank, do induction on adjoining a linear independent\nelement to a submodule.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.repr_reindex_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.equiv_fun_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.reindex_finset_range_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.singleton", "description": "`basis.singleton \u03b9 R` is the basis sending the unique element of `\u03b9` to `1 : R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonzero_span_atom", "description": " For a module over a division ring, the span of a nonzero element is an atom of the\nlattice of submodules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.range_extend", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.reindex_range", "description": "`b.reindex_range` is a basis indexed by `range b`, the basis vectors themselves.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.of_equiv_fun_equiv_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.constr_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.map_equiv_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.mk_coord_apply_ne", "description": " Given a basis, the `i`th element of the dual basis evaluates to 0 on the `j`th element of the\nbasis if `j \u2260 i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.extend", "description": "If `s` is a linear independent set of vectors, we can extend it to a basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coe_of_vector_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.ext", "description": "Two linear maps are equal if they are equal on basis vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coe_repr_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.reindex_finset_range_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.is_unit_smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.fin_two_prod_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.reindex_finset_range_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coe_map_coeffs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.reindex_range_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.exists_right_inverse_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.repr_support_subset_of_mem_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.apply_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.ext'", "description": "Two linear equivs are equal if they are equal on basis vectors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.mk_coord_apply_eq", "description": " Given a basis, the `i`th element of the dual basis evaluates to 1 on the `i`th element of the\nbasis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.range_of_vector_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.empty", "description": "If `M` is a subsingleton and `\u03b9` is empty, this is the unique `\u03b9`-indexed basis for `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.mk", "description": "A linear independent family of vectors spanning the whole module is a basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coord_equiv_fun_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.group_smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.reindex_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.constr_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.integral_comp_inv_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_comp_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_comp_div_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_linear_equiv.is_add_haar_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.comp_mul_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.comp_mul_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_comp_mul_right_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_continuous_linear_equiv.is_add_haar_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.integral_comp_smul", "description": " The integral of `f (R \u2022 x)` with respect to an additive Haar measure is a multiple of the\nintegral of `f`. The formula we give works even when `f` is not integrable or `R = 0`\nthanks to the convention that a non-integrable function has integral zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.comp_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.integral_comp_inv_smul_of_nonneg", "description": " The integral of `f (R\u207b\u00b9 \u2022 x)` with respect to an additive Haar measure is a multiple of the\nintegral of `f`. The formula we give works even when `f` is not integrable or `R = 0`\nthanks to the convention that a non-integrable function has integral zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.integral_comp_inv_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.comp_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.integral_comp_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.integral_comp_smul_of_nonneg", "description": " The integral of `f (R \u2022 x)` with respect to an additive Haar measure is a multiple of the\nintegral of `f`. The formula we give works even when `f` is not integrable or `R = 0`\nthanks to the convention that a non-integrable function has integral zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.integral_comp_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_comp_mul_left_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.integral_comp_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.integral_comp_inv_smul", "description": " The integral of `f (R\u207b\u00b9 \u2022 x)` with respect to an additive Haar measure is a multiple of the\nintegral of `f`. The formula we give works even when `f` is not integrable or `R = 0`\nthanks to the convention that a non-integrable function has integral zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.exists_finset_to_smooth_partition_of_unity_eventually_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.locally_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.sum_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.coe_to_smooth_partition_of_unity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.mem_support_ind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.mem_ext_chart_at_source_of_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.mem_chart_at_ind_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.to_smooth_partition_of_unity", "description": "Every `smooth_bump_covering` defines a smooth partition of unity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.sum_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.mem_chart_at_source_of_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.cont_mdiff_finsum_smul", "description": " If `f` is a smooth partition of unity on a set `s : set M` and `g : \u03b9 \u2192 M \u2192 F` is a family of\nfunctions such that `g i` is $C^n$ smooth at every point of the topological support of `f i`, then\nthe sum `\u03bb x, \u2211\u1da0 i, f i x \u2022 g i x` is smooth on the whole manifold.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity", "description": " We say that that a collection of functions form a smooth partition of unity on a set `s` if\n\n* all functions are infinitely smooth and nonnegative;\n* the family `\u03bb i, support (f i)` is locally finite;\n* for all `x \u2208 s` the sum `\u2211\u1da0 i, f i x` equals one;\n* for all `x`, the sum `\u2211\u1da0 i, f i x` is less than or equal to one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.to_fun", "description": " We say that that a collection of functions form a smooth partition of unity on a set `s` if\n\n* all functions are infinitely smooth and nonnegative;\n* the family `\u03bb i, support (f i)` is locally finite;\n* for all `x \u2208 s` the sum `\u2211\u1da0 i, f i x` equals one;\n* for all `x`, the sum `\u2211\u1da0 i, f i x` is less than or equal to one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.locally_finite'", "description": " We say that that a collection of functions form a smooth partition of unity on a set `s` if\n\n* all functions are infinitely smooth and nonnegative;\n* the family `\u03bb i, support (f i)` is locally finite;\n* for all `x \u2208 s` the sum `\u2211\u1da0 i, f i x` equals one;\n* for all `x`, the sum `\u2211\u1da0 i, f i x` is less than or equal to one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.nonneg'", "description": " We say that that a collection of functions form a smooth partition of unity on a set `s` if\n\n* all functions are infinitely smooth and nonnegative;\n* the family `\u03bb i, support (f i)` is locally finite;\n* for all `x \u2208 s` the sum `\u2211\u1da0 i, f i x` equals one;\n* for all `x`, the sum `\u2211\u1da0 i, f i x` is less than or equal to one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.sum_eq_one'", "description": " We say that that a collection of functions form a smooth partition of unity on a set `s` if\n\n* all functions are infinitely smooth and nonnegative;\n* the family `\u03bb i, support (f i)` is locally finite;\n* for all `x \u2208 s` the sum `\u2211\u1da0 i, f i x` equals one;\n* for all `x`, the sum `\u2211\u1da0 i, f i x` is less than or equal to one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.sum_le_one'", "description": " We say that that a collection of functions form a smooth partition of unity on a set `s` if\n\n* all functions are infinitely smooth and nonnegative;\n* the family `\u03bb i, support (f i)` is locally finite;\n* for all `x \u2208 s` the sum `\u2211\u1da0 i, f i x` equals one;\n* for all `x`, the sum `\u2211\u1da0 i, f i x` is less than or equal to one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.is_subordinate.cont_mdiff_finsum_smul", "description": " If `f` is a smooth partition of unity on a set `s : set M` subordinate to a family of open sets\n`U : \u03b9 \u2192 set M` and `g : \u03b9 \u2192 M \u2192 F` is a family of functions such that `g i` is $C^n$ smooth on\n`U i`, then the sum `\u03bb x, \u2211\u1da0 i, f i x \u2022 g i x` is $C^n$ smooth on the whole manifold.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.is_subordinate.to_bump_covering", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `smooth_bump_covering.is_subordinate_to_bump_covering`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.eventually_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.locally_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate", "description": " Let `M` be a smooth manifold with corners modelled on a finite dimensional real vector space.\nSuppose also that `M` is a Hausdorff `\u03c3`-compact topological space. Let `s` be a closed set\nin `M` and `U : M \u2192 set M` be a collection of sets such that `U x \u2208 \ud835\udcdd x` for every `x \u2208 s`.\nThen there exists a smooth bump covering of `s` that is subordinate to `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.is_subordinate", "description": " A smooth partition of unity `f i` is subordinate to a family of sets `U i` indexed by the same\ntype if for each `i` the closure of the support of `f i` is a subset of `U i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.to_smooth_partition_of_unity_eq_mul_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.fintype", "description": "The index type of a `smooth_bump_covering` of a compact manifold is finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_smooth_zero_one_of_closed", "description": " Given two disjoint closed sets in a Hausdorff \u03c3-compact finite dimensional manifold, there\nexists an infinitely smooth function that is equal to `0` on one of them and is equal to one on the\nother.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.is_subordinate", "description": "We say that `f : smooth_bump_covering \u03b9 I M s` is *subordinate* to a map `U : M \u2192 set M` if for each\nindex `i`, we have `tsupport (f i) \u2286 U (f i).c`. This notion is a bit more general than\nbeing subordinate to an open covering of `M`, because we make no assumption about the way `U x`\ndepends on `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering", "description": " We say that a collection of `smooth_bump_function`s is a `smooth_bump_covering` of a set `s` if\n\n* `(f i).c \u2208 s` for all `i`;\n* the family `\u03bb i, support (f i)` is locally finite;\n* for each point `x \u2208 s` there exists `i` such that `f i =\u1da0[\ud835\udcdd x] 1`;\n  in other words, `x` belongs to the interior of `{y | f i y = 1}`;\n\nIf `M` is a finite dimensional real manifold which is a `\u03c3`-compact Hausdorff topological space,\nthen for every covering `U : M \u2192 set M`, `\u2200 x, U x \u2208 \ud835\udcdd x`, there exists a `smooth_bump_covering`\nsubordinate to `U`, see `smooth_bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate`.\n\nThis covering can be used, e.g., to construct a partition of unity and to prove the weak\nWhitney embedding theorem.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.c", "description": " We say that a collection of `smooth_bump_function`s is a `smooth_bump_covering` of a set `s` if\n\n* `(f i).c \u2208 s` for all `i`;\n* the family `\u03bb i, support (f i)` is locally finite;\n* for each point `x \u2208 s` there exists `i` such that `f i =\u1da0[\ud835\udcdd x] 1`;\n  in other words, `x` belongs to the interior of `{y | f i y = 1}`;\n\nIf `M` is a finite dimensional real manifold which is a `\u03c3`-compact Hausdorff topological space,\nthen for every covering `U : M \u2192 set M`, `\u2200 x, U x \u2208 \ud835\udcdd x`, there exists a `smooth_bump_covering`\nsubordinate to `U`, see `smooth_bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate`.\n\nThis covering can be used, e.g., to construct a partition of unity and to prove the weak\nWhitney embedding theorem.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.to_fun", "description": " We say that a collection of `smooth_bump_function`s is a `smooth_bump_covering` of a set `s` if\n\n* `(f i).c \u2208 s` for all `i`;\n* the family `\u03bb i, support (f i)` is locally finite;\n* for each point `x \u2208 s` there exists `i` such that `f i =\u1da0[\ud835\udcdd x] 1`;\n  in other words, `x` belongs to the interior of `{y | f i y = 1}`;\n\nIf `M` is a finite dimensional real manifold which is a `\u03c3`-compact Hausdorff topological space,\nthen for every covering `U : M \u2192 set M`, `\u2200 x, U x \u2208 \ud835\udcdd x`, there exists a `smooth_bump_covering`\nsubordinate to `U`, see `smooth_bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate`.\n\nThis covering can be used, e.g., to construct a partition of unity and to prove the weak\nWhitney embedding theorem.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.c_mem'", "description": " We say that a collection of `smooth_bump_function`s is a `smooth_bump_covering` of a set `s` if\n\n* `(f i).c \u2208 s` for all `i`;\n* the family `\u03bb i, support (f i)` is locally finite;\n* for each point `x \u2208 s` there exists `i` such that `f i =\u1da0[\ud835\udcdd x] 1`;\n  in other words, `x` belongs to the interior of `{y | f i y = 1}`;\n\nIf `M` is a finite dimensional real manifold which is a `\u03c3`-compact Hausdorff topological space,\nthen for every covering `U : M \u2192 set M`, `\u2200 x, U x \u2208 \ud835\udcdd x`, there exists a `smooth_bump_covering`\nsubordinate to `U`, see `smooth_bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate`.\n\nThis covering can be used, e.g., to construct a partition of unity and to prove the weak\nWhitney embedding theorem.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.locally_finite'", "description": " We say that a collection of `smooth_bump_function`s is a `smooth_bump_covering` of a set `s` if\n\n* `(f i).c \u2208 s` for all `i`;\n* the family `\u03bb i, support (f i)` is locally finite;\n* for each point `x \u2208 s` there exists `i` such that `f i =\u1da0[\ud835\udcdd x] 1`;\n  in other words, `x` belongs to the interior of `{y | f i y = 1}`;\n\nIf `M` is a finite dimensional real manifold which is a `\u03c3`-compact Hausdorff topological space,\nthen for every covering `U : M \u2192 set M`, `\u2200 x, U x \u2208 \ud835\udcdd x`, there exists a `smooth_bump_covering`\nsubordinate to `U`, see `smooth_bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate`.\n\nThis covering can be used, e.g., to construct a partition of unity and to prove the weak\nWhitney embedding theorem.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.eventually_eq_one'", "description": " We say that a collection of `smooth_bump_function`s is a `smooth_bump_covering` of a set `s` if\n\n* `(f i).c \u2208 s` for all `i`;\n* the family `\u03bb i, support (f i)` is locally finite;\n* for each point `x \u2208 s` there exists `i` such that `f i =\u1da0[\ud835\udcdd x] 1`;\n  in other words, `x` belongs to the interior of `{y | f i y = 1}`;\n\nIf `M` is a finite dimensional real manifold which is a `\u03c3`-compact Hausdorff topological space,\nthen for every covering `U : M \u2192 set M`, `\u2200 x, U x \u2208 \ud835\udcdd x`, there exists a `smooth_bump_covering`\nsubordinate to `U`, see `smooth_bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate`.\n\nThis covering can be used, e.g., to construct a partition of unity and to prove the weak\nWhitney embedding theorem.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.to_smooth_partition_of_unity_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.smooth_to_partition_of_unity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.is_subordinate.to_smooth_partition_of_unity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.smooth_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_cont_mdiff_forall_mem_convex_of_local", "description": " Let `M` be a \u03c3-compact Hausdorff finite dimensional topological manifold. Let `t : M \u2192 set F`\nbe a family of convex sets. Suppose that for each point `x : M` there exists a neighborhood\n`U \u2208 \ud835\udcdd x` and a function `g : M \u2192 F` such that `g` is $C^n$ smooth on `U` and `g y \u2208 t y` for all\n`y \u2208 U`. Then there exists a $C^n$ smooth function `g : C^\u221e\u27eeI, M; \ud835\udcd8(\u211d, F), F\u27ef` such that `g x \u2208 t x`\nfor all `x`. See also `exists_smooth_forall_mem_convex_of_local` and\n`exists_smooth_forall_mem_convex_of_local_const`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.sum_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.exists_smooth_forall_closed_ball_subset", "description": " Let `M` be a smooth \u03c3-compact manifold with a metric. Let `K : \u03b9 \u2192 set M` be a locally finite\nfamily of closed sets, let `U : \u03b9 \u2192 set M` be a family of open sets such that `K i \u2286 U i` for all\n`i`. Then there exists a positive smooth function `\u03b4 : M \u2192 \u211d\u22650` such that for any `i` and `x \u2208 K i`,\nwe have `metric.closed_ball x (\u03b4 x) \u2286 U i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.is_subordinate.to_partition_of_unity", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `smooth_partition_of_unity.is_subordinate_to_partition_of_unity`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.mem_ext_chart_at_ind_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.to_smooth_partition_of_unity_to_partition_of_unity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.is_subordinate_to_bump_covering", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.single", "description": " A `smooth_partition_of_unity` that consists of a single function, uniformly equal to one,\ndefined as an example for `inhabited` instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.is_subordinate.smooth_finsum_smul", "description": " If `f` is a smooth partition of unity on a set `s : set M` subordinate to a family of open sets\n`U : \u03b9 \u2192 set M` and `g : \u03b9 \u2192 M \u2192 F` is a family of functions such that `g i` is smooth on `U i`,\nthen the sum `\u03bb x, \u2211\u1da0 i, f i x \u2022 g i x` is smooth on the whole manifold.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.support_to_smooth_partition_of_unity_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.smooth_finsum_smul", "description": " If `f` is a smooth partition of unity on a set `s : set M` and `g : \u03b9 \u2192 M \u2192 F` is a family of\nfunctions such that `g i` is smooth at every point of the topological support of `f i`, then the sum\n`\u03bb x, \u2211\u1da0 i, f i x \u2022 g i x` is smooth on the whole manifold.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.ind", "description": "Index of a bump function such that `fs i =\u1da0[\ud835\udcdd x] 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.point_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.exists_smooth_forall_closed_ball_subset", "description": " Let `M` be a smooth \u03c3-compact manifold with extended distance. Let `K : \u03b9 \u2192 set M` be a locally\nfinite family of closed sets, let `U : \u03b9 \u2192 set M` be a family of open sets such that `K i \u2286 U i` for\nall `i`. Then there exists a positive smooth function `\u03b4 : M \u2192 \u211d\u22650` such that for any `i` and\n`x \u2208 K i`, we have `emetric.closed_ball x (\u03b4 x) \u2286 U i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.finsum_smul_mem_convex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.is_subordinate.to_smooth_partition_of_unity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.to_smooth_partition_of_unity_zero_of_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.is_subordinate_to_partition_of_unity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.smooth_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.to_partition_of_unity", "description": "Reinterpret a smooth partition of unity as a continuous partition of unity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.sum_to_smooth_partition_of_unity_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.cont_mdiff_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.apply_ind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.to_smooth_partition_of_unity", "description": " A `bump_covering` such that all functions in this covering are smooth generates a smooth\npartition of unity.\n\nIn our formalization, not every `f : bump_covering \u03b9 M s` with smooth functions `f i` is a\n`smooth_bump_covering`; instead, a `smooth_bump_covering` is a covering by supports of\n`smooth_bump_function`s. So, we define `bump_covering.to_smooth_partition_of_unity`, then reuse it\nin `smooth_bump_covering.to_smooth_partition_of_unity`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.is_subordinate.support_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_smooth_forall_mem_convex_of_local", "description": " Let `M` be a \u03c3-compact Hausdorff finite dimensional topological manifold. Let `t : M \u2192 set F`\nbe a family of convex sets. Suppose that for each point `x : M` there exists a neighborhood\n`U \u2208 \ud835\udcdd x` and a function `g : M \u2192 F` such that `g` is smooth on `U` and `g y \u2208 t y` for all `y \u2208 U`.\nThen there exists a smooth function `g : C^\u221e\u27eeI, M; \ud835\udcd8(\u211d, F), F\u27ef` such that `g x \u2208 t x` for all `x`.\nSee also `exists_cont_mdiff_forall_mem_convex_of_local` and\n`exists_smooth_forall_mem_convex_of_local_const`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_partition_of_unity.exists_is_subordinate", "description": " If `X` is a paracompact normal topological space and `U` is an open covering of a closed set\n`s`, then there exists a `bump_covering \u03b9 X s` that is subordinate to `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_smooth_forall_mem_convex_of_local_const", "description": " Let `M` be a \u03c3-compact Hausdorff finite dimensional topological manifold. Let `t : M \u2192 set F` be\na family of convex sets. Suppose that for each point `x : M` there exists a vector `c : F` such that\nfor all `y` in a neighborhood of `x` we have `c \u2208 t y`. Then there exists a smooth function\n`g : C^\u221e\u27eeI, M; \ud835\udcd8(\u211d, F), F\u27ef` such that `g x \u2208 t x` for all `x`.  See also\n`exists_cont_mdiff_forall_mem_convex_of_local` and `exists_smooth_forall_mem_convex_of_local`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_covering.to_bump_covering", "description": " Reinterpret a `smooth_bump_covering` as a continuous `bump_covering`. Note that not every\n`f : bump_covering \u03b9 M s` with smooth functions `f i` is a `smooth_bump_covering`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.hom_mk", "description": "a constructor for morphisms of triangles", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.iso_mk", "description": "a constructor for isomorphisms of triangles", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism", "description": "A morphism of triangles `(X,Y,Z,f,g,h) \u27f6 (X',Y',Z',f',g',h')` in `C` is a triple of morphisms\n`a : X \u27f6 X'`, `b : Y \u27f6 Y'`, `c : Z \u27f6 Z'` such that\n`a \u226b f' = f \u226b b`, `b \u226b g' = g \u226b c`, and `a\u27e61\u27e7' \u226b h = h' \u226b c`.\nIn other words, we have a commutative diagram:\n```lean\n     f      g      h\n  X  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Y  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Z  \u2500\u2500\u2500> X\u27e61\u27e7\n  \u2502       \u2502       \u2502        \u2502\n  \u2502a      \u2502b      \u2502c       \u2502a\u27e61\u27e7'\n  V       V       V        V\n  X' \u2500\u2500\u2500> Y' \u2500\u2500\u2500> Z' \u2500\u2500\u2500> X'\u27e61\u27e7\n     f'     g'     h'\n```\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0144>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism.hom\u2081", "description": "A morphism of triangles `(X,Y,Z,f,g,h) \u27f6 (X',Y',Z',f',g',h')` in `C` is a triple of morphisms\n`a : X \u27f6 X'`, `b : Y \u27f6 Y'`, `c : Z \u27f6 Z'` such that\n`a \u226b f' = f \u226b b`, `b \u226b g' = g \u226b c`, and `a\u27e61\u27e7' \u226b h = h' \u226b c`.\nIn other words, we have a commutative diagram:\n```lean\n     f      g      h\n  X  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Y  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Z  \u2500\u2500\u2500> X\u27e61\u27e7\n  \u2502       \u2502       \u2502        \u2502\n  \u2502a      \u2502b      \u2502c       \u2502a\u27e61\u27e7'\n  V       V       V        V\n  X' \u2500\u2500\u2500> Y' \u2500\u2500\u2500> Z' \u2500\u2500\u2500> X'\u27e61\u27e7\n     f'     g'     h'\n```\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0144>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism.hom\u2082", "description": "A morphism of triangles `(X,Y,Z,f,g,h) \u27f6 (X',Y',Z',f',g',h')` in `C` is a triple of morphisms\n`a : X \u27f6 X'`, `b : Y \u27f6 Y'`, `c : Z \u27f6 Z'` such that\n`a \u226b f' = f \u226b b`, `b \u226b g' = g \u226b c`, and `a\u27e61\u27e7' \u226b h = h' \u226b c`.\nIn other words, we have a commutative diagram:\n```lean\n     f      g      h\n  X  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Y  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Z  \u2500\u2500\u2500> X\u27e61\u27e7\n  \u2502       \u2502       \u2502        \u2502\n  \u2502a      \u2502b      \u2502c       \u2502a\u27e61\u27e7'\n  V       V       V        V\n  X' \u2500\u2500\u2500> Y' \u2500\u2500\u2500> Z' \u2500\u2500\u2500> X'\u27e61\u27e7\n     f'     g'     h'\n```\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0144>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism.hom\u2083", "description": "A morphism of triangles `(X,Y,Z,f,g,h) \u27f6 (X',Y',Z',f',g',h')` in `C` is a triple of morphisms\n`a : X \u27f6 X'`, `b : Y \u27f6 Y'`, `c : Z \u27f6 Z'` such that\n`a \u226b f' = f \u226b b`, `b \u226b g' = g \u226b c`, and `a\u27e61\u27e7' \u226b h = h' \u226b c`.\nIn other words, we have a commutative diagram:\n```lean\n     f      g      h\n  X  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Y  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Z  \u2500\u2500\u2500> X\u27e61\u27e7\n  \u2502       \u2502       \u2502        \u2502\n  \u2502a      \u2502b      \u2502c       \u2502a\u27e61\u27e7'\n  V       V       V        V\n  X' \u2500\u2500\u2500> Y' \u2500\u2500\u2500> Z' \u2500\u2500\u2500> X'\u27e61\u27e7\n     f'     g'     h'\n```\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0144>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism.comm\u2081'", "description": "A morphism of triangles `(X,Y,Z,f,g,h) \u27f6 (X',Y',Z',f',g',h')` in `C` is a triple of morphisms\n`a : X \u27f6 X'`, `b : Y \u27f6 Y'`, `c : Z \u27f6 Z'` such that\n`a \u226b f' = f \u226b b`, `b \u226b g' = g \u226b c`, and `a\u27e61\u27e7' \u226b h = h' \u226b c`.\nIn other words, we have a commutative diagram:\n```lean\n     f      g      h\n  X  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Y  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Z  \u2500\u2500\u2500> X\u27e61\u27e7\n  \u2502       \u2502       \u2502        \u2502\n  \u2502a      \u2502b      \u2502c       \u2502a\u27e61\u27e7'\n  V       V       V        V\n  X' \u2500\u2500\u2500> Y' \u2500\u2500\u2500> Z' \u2500\u2500\u2500> X'\u27e61\u27e7\n     f'     g'     h'\n```\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0144>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism.comm\u2082'", "description": "A morphism of triangles `(X,Y,Z,f,g,h) \u27f6 (X',Y',Z',f',g',h')` in `C` is a triple of morphisms\n`a : X \u27f6 X'`, `b : Y \u27f6 Y'`, `c : Z \u27f6 Z'` such that\n`a \u226b f' = f \u226b b`, `b \u226b g' = g \u226b c`, and `a\u27e61\u27e7' \u226b h = h' \u226b c`.\nIn other words, we have a commutative diagram:\n```lean\n     f      g      h\n  X  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Y  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Z  \u2500\u2500\u2500> X\u27e61\u27e7\n  \u2502       \u2502       \u2502        \u2502\n  \u2502a      \u2502b      \u2502c       \u2502a\u27e61\u27e7'\n  V       V       V        V\n  X' \u2500\u2500\u2500> Y' \u2500\u2500\u2500> Z' \u2500\u2500\u2500> X'\u27e61\u27e7\n     f'     g'     h'\n```\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0144>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism.comm\u2083'", "description": "A morphism of triangles `(X,Y,Z,f,g,h) \u27f6 (X',Y',Z',f',g',h')` in `C` is a triple of morphisms\n`a : X \u27f6 X'`, `b : Y \u27f6 Y'`, `c : Z \u27f6 Z'` such that\n`a \u226b f' = f \u226b b`, `b \u226b g' = g \u226b c`, and `a\u27e61\u27e7' \u226b h = h' \u226b c`.\nIn other words, we have a commutative diagram:\n```lean\n     f      g      h\n  X  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Y  \u2500\u2500\u2500> Z  \u2500\u2500\u2500> X\u27e61\u27e7\n  \u2502       \u2502       \u2502        \u2502\n  \u2502a      \u2502b      \u2502c       \u2502a\u27e61\u27e7'\n  V       V       V        V\n  X' \u2500\u2500\u2500> Y' \u2500\u2500\u2500> Z' \u2500\u2500\u2500> X'\u27e61\u27e7\n     f'     g'     h'\n```\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0144>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism_id", "description": "The identity triangle morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.hom_mk_hom\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism_id_hom\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.contractible_triangle", "description": "For each object in `C`, there is a triangle of the form `(X,X,0,\ud835\udfd9 X,0,0)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism_id_hom\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism_id_hom\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism.comm\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism.comp", "description": "Composition of triangle morphisms gives a triangle morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism.comm\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_category_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.contractible_triangle_obj\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.contractible_triangle_obj\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.mk_mor\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism.comp_hom\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.contractible_triangle_obj\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.contractible_triangle_mor\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism.comm\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism.comm\u2083_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.contractible_triangle_mor\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_category", "description": "Triangles with triangle morphisms form a category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.mk_mor\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.iso_mk_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.contractible_triangle_mor\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism.comm\u2082_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.hom_mk_hom\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism.comm\u2081_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.mk_obj\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism.comp_hom\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism.comp_hom\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_morphism.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle", "description": "A triangle in `C` is a sextuple `(X,Y,Z,f,g,h)` where `X,Y,Z` are objects of `C`,\nand `f : X \u27f6 Y`, `g : Y \u27f6 Z`, `h : Z \u27f6 X\u27e61\u27e7` are morphisms in `C`.\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0144>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.obj\u2081", "description": "A triangle in `C` is a sextuple `(X,Y,Z,f,g,h)` where `X,Y,Z` are objects of `C`,\nand `f : X \u27f6 Y`, `g : Y \u27f6 Z`, `h : Z \u27f6 X\u27e61\u27e7` are morphisms in `C`.\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0144>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.obj\u2082", "description": "A triangle in `C` is a sextuple `(X,Y,Z,f,g,h)` where `X,Y,Z` are objects of `C`,\nand `f : X \u27f6 Y`, `g : Y \u27f6 Z`, `h : Z \u27f6 X\u27e61\u27e7` are morphisms in `C`.\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0144>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.obj\u2083", "description": "A triangle in `C` is a sextuple `(X,Y,Z,f,g,h)` where `X,Y,Z` are objects of `C`,\nand `f : X \u27f6 Y`, `g : Y \u27f6 Z`, `h : Z \u27f6 X\u27e61\u27e7` are morphisms in `C`.\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0144>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.mor\u2081", "description": "A triangle in `C` is a sextuple `(X,Y,Z,f,g,h)` where `X,Y,Z` are objects of `C`,\nand `f : X \u27f6 Y`, `g : Y \u27f6 Z`, `h : Z \u27f6 X\u27e61\u27e7` are morphisms in `C`.\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0144>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.mor\u2082", "description": "A triangle in `C` is a sextuple `(X,Y,Z,f,g,h)` where `X,Y,Z` are objects of `C`,\nand `f : X \u27f6 Y`, `g : Y \u27f6 Z`, `h : Z \u27f6 X\u27e61\u27e7` are morphisms in `C`.\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0144>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.mor\u2083", "description": "A triangle in `C` is a sextuple `(X,Y,Z,f,g,h)` where `X,Y,Z` are objects of `C`,\nand `f : X \u27f6 Y`, `g : Y \u27f6 Z`, `h : Z \u27f6 X\u27e61\u27e7` are morphisms in `C`.\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0144>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.iso_mk_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle_category_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.mk_obj\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.mk", "description": "A triangle `(X,Y,Z,f,g,h)` in `C` is defined by the morphisms `f : X \u27f6 Y`, `g : Y \u27f6 Z`\nand `h : Z \u27f6 X\u27e61\u27e7`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.mk_mor\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.mk_obj\u2083", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.pretriangulated.triangle.hom_mk_hom\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_cases", "description": "For an element `a` of a linear ordered ring, either `abs a = a` and `0 \u2264 a`,\n   or `abs a = -a` and `a < 0`.\n   Use cases on this lemma to automate linarith in inequalities", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dvd_abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_mul_abs_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_eq_iff_mul_self_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_dvd_abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_eq_neg_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_lt_iff_mul_self_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "self_dvd_abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_le_one_iff_mul_self_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_dvd_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_sub_sq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_le_iff_mul_self_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_hom", "description": "`abs` as a `monoid_with_zero_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_zero_add_max_neg_zero_eq_abs_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_mul_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.repr_gen_pow_is_integral", "description": " If `B : power_basis S A` is such that `is_integral R B.gen`, then\n`is_integral R (B.basis.repr (B.gen ^ n) i)` for all `i` if\n`minpoly S B.gen = (minpoly R B.gen).map (algebra_map R S)`. This is the case if `R` is a GCD domain\nand `S` is its fraction ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.repr_pow_is_integral", "description": " Let `B : power_basis S A` be such that `is_integral R B.gen`, and let `x : A` be and element\nwith integral coordinates in the base `B.basis`. Then `is_integral R ((B.basis.repr (x ^ n) i)` for\nall `i` and all `n` if `minpoly S B.gen = (minpoly R B.gen).map (algebra_map R S)`. This is the case\nif `R` is a GCD domain and `S` is its fraction ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.repr_mul_is_integral", "description": " Let `B : power_basis S A` be such that `is_integral R B.gen`, and let `x y : A` be elements with\nintegral coordinates in the base `B.basis`. Then `is_integral R ((B.basis.repr (x * y) i)` for all\n`i` if `minpoly S B.gen = (minpoly R B.gen).map (algebra_map R S)`. This is the case if `R` is a GCD\ndomain and `S` is its fraction ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.of_gen_mem_adjoin", "description": " The power basis given by `x` if `B.gen \u2208 adjoin K {x}`. See `power_basis.of_gen_mem_adjoin'`\nfor a version over a more general base ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.to_matrix_is_integral", "description": " Let `B B' : power_basis K S` be such that `is_integral R B.gen`, and let `P : R[X]` be such that\n`aeval B.gen P = B'.gen`. Then `is_integral R (B.basis.to_matrix B'.basis i j)` for all `i` and `j`\nif `minpoly K B.gen = (minpoly R B.gen).map (algebra_map R L)`. This is the case\nif `R` is a GCD domain and `K` is its fraction ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.adjoin.power_basis_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.adjoin.power_basis_aux", "description": " The elements `1, x, ..., x ^ (d - 1)` for a basis for the `K`-module `K[x]`,\nwhere `d` is the degree of the minimal polynomial of `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.of_gen_mem_adjoin_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "power_basis.of_gen_mem_adjoin_dim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.adjoin.power_basis_dim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.adjoin.power_basis", "description": " The power basis `1, x, ..., x ^ (d - 1)` for `K[x]`,\nwhere `d` is the degree of the minimal polynomial of `x`. See `algebra.adjoin.power_basis'` for\na version over a more general base ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_limsup_at_bot_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measure_zero_or_one_of_measurable_set_limsup_at_bot", "description": " **Kolmogorov's 0-1 law** : any event in the tail \u03c3-algebra of an independent sequence of\nsub-\u03c3-algebras has probability 0 or 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_supr_directed_limsup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measure_eq_zero_or_one_of_indep_set_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_bsupr_limsup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_bsupr_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measure_zero_or_one_of_measurable_set_limsup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_supr_limsup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_limsup_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_limsup_at_top_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measure_zero_or_one_of_measurable_set_limsup_at_top", "description": " **Kolmogorov's 0-1 law** : any event in the tail \u03c3-algebra of an independent sequence of\nsub-\u03c3-algebras has probability 0 or 1.\nThe tail \u03c3-algebra `limsup s at_top` is the same as `\u22c2 n, \u22c3 i \u2265 n, s i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measure_eq_zero_or_one_or_top_of_indep_set_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.fg_iff_mul_fg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.fg", "description": " An additive monoid is finitely generated if it is finitely generated as an additive submonoid of\nitself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.fg.out", "description": " An additive monoid is finitely generated if it is finitely generated as an additive submonoid of\nitself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.fg_of_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.rank_closure_finset_le_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.closure_finite_fg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.fg", "description": " An additive subgroup of `H` is finitely generated if it is the closure of a finite subset of\n`H`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.fg_iff", "description": "An equivalent expression of `add_group.fg` in terms of `set.finite` instead of\n`finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.fg_of_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.powers_fg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.closure_finite_fg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.multiples_fg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.fg_iff_submonoid_fg", "description": "A subgroup is finitely generated if and only if it is finitely generated as a submonoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.fg_iff_add_fg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.fg_iff_mul_fg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {