atrix.to_linear_equiv_right'_of_inv", "description": " If `M` and `M'` are each other's inverse matrices, they provide an equivalence between `n \u2192 A`\nand `m \u2192 A` corresponding to `M.vec_mul` and `M'.vec_mul`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_lin_of_inv", "description": " If `M` and `M` are each other's inverse matrices, `matrix.to_lin M` and `matrix.to_lin M'`\nform a linear equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.left_mul_matrix_mul_vec_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_lin_mul_apply", "description": "Shortcut lemma for `matrix.to_lin_mul` and `linear_map.comp_apply`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_matrix'_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_matrix_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_lin_eq_to_lin'", "description": " `matrix.to_lin'` is a particular case of `matrix.to_lin`, for the standard basis\n`pi.basis_fun R n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_lin'_submatrix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_lin_alg_equiv", "description": " Given a basis of a module `M\u2081` over a commutative ring `R`, we get an algebra\nequivalence between square matrices over `R` indexed by the basis and linear maps `M\u2081 \u2192\u2097 M\u2081`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_lin_alg_equiv'_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_lin_of_inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.range_mul_vec_lin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.mul_vec_lin_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_lin_alg_equiv'", "description": "A `matrix n n R` is algebra equivalent to a linear map `(n \u2192 R) \u2192\u2097[R] (n \u2192 R)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.left_mul_matrix_eq_repr_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_matrix_alg_equiv'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_matrix'", "description": "Linear maps `(n \u2192 R) \u2192\u2097[R] (m \u2192 R)` are linearly equivalent to `matrix m n R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_lin_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_lin_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_lin'_of_inv", "description": " If `M` and `M'` are each other's inverse matrices, they provide an equivalence between `m \u2192 A`\nand `n \u2192 A` corresponding to `M.mul_vec` and `M'.mul_vec`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv.alg_conj", "description": " A linear equivalence of two modules induces an equivalence of algebras of their\nendomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_matrix_alg_equiv'_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_matrix_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.to_matrix_lmul'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_linear_equiv_right'_of_inv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_lin_fin_two_prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.left_mul_matrix", "description": " `left_mul_matrix b x` is the matrix corresponding to the linear map `\u03bb y, x * y`.\n\n`left_mul_matrix_eq_repr_mul` gives a formula for the entries of `left_mul_matrix`.\n\nThis definition is useful for doing (more) explicit computations with `linear_map.mul_left`,\nsuch as the trace form or norm map for algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_lin'_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_equiv_matrix", "description": " A basis of a module induces an equivalence of algebras from the endomorphisms of the module to\nsquare matrices.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.mul_vec_lin_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.to_matrix_alg_equiv_transpose_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_lin'_of_inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_lin_to_matrix", "descrip