d: a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` with `gcd` (greatest common divisor) and\n`lcm` (least common multiple) operations, determined up to a unit. The type class focuses on `gcd`\nand we derive the corresponding `lcm` facts from `gcd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gcd_monoid.gcd_mul_lcm", "description": " GCD monoid: a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` with `gcd` (greatest common divisor) and\n`lcm` (least common multiple) operations, determined up to a unit. The type class focuses on `gcd`\nand we derive the corresponding `lcm` facts from `gcd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gcd_monoid.lcm_zero_left", "description": " GCD monoid: a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` with `gcd` (greatest common divisor) and\n`lcm` (least common multiple) operations, determined up to a unit. The type class focuses on `gcd`\nand we derive the corresponding `lcm` facts from `gcd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gcd_monoid.lcm_zero_right", "description": " GCD monoid: a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` with `gcd` (greatest common divisor) and\n`lcm` (least common multiple) operations, determined up to a unit. The type class focuses on `gcd`\nand we derive the corresponding `lcm` facts from `gcd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lcm_dvd_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gcd_eq_of_dvd_sub_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gcd_eq_of_dvd_sub_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normalize_eq_normalize", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lcm_units_coe_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lcm_dvd_lcm_mul_right_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gcd_one_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normalize_eq_normalize_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gcd_zero_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lcm_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gcd_mul_lcm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lcm_eq_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lcm_dvd_lcm_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gcd_mul_dvd_mul_gcd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normalized_gcd_monoid", "description": " Normalized GCD monoid: a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` with normalization and `gcd`\n(greatest common divisor) and `lcm` (least common multiple) operations. In this setting `gcd` and\n`lcm` form a bounded lattice on the associated elements where `gcd` is the infimum, `lcm` is the\nsupremum, `1` is bottom, and `0` is top. The type class focuses on `gcd` and we derive the\ncorresponding `lcm` facts from `gcd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normalized_gcd_monoid.to_normalization_monoid", "description": " Normalized GCD monoid: a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` with normalization and `gcd`\n(greatest common divisor) and `lcm` (least common multiple) operations. In this setting `gcd` and\n`lcm` form a bounded lattice on the associated elements where `gcd` is the infimum, `lcm` is the\nsupremum, `1` is bottom, and `0` is top. The type class focuses on `gcd` and we derive the\ncorresponding `lcm` facts from `gcd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normalized_gcd_monoid.to_gcd_monoid", "description": " Normalized GCD monoid: a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` with normalization and `gcd`\n(greatest common divisor) and `lcm` (least common multiple) operations. In this setting `gcd` and\n`lcm` form a bounded lattice on the associated elements where `gcd` is the infimum, `lcm` is the\nsupremum, `1` is bottom, and `0` is top. The type class focuses on `gcd` and we derive the\ncorresponding `lcm` facts from `gcd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normalized_gcd_monoid.normalize_gcd", "description": " Normalized GCD monoid: a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` with normalization and `gcd`\n(greatest common divisor) and `lcm` (least common multiple) operations. In this setting `gcd` and\n`lcm` form a bounded lattice on the associated elements where `gcd` is the infimum, `lcm` is the\nsupremum, `1` is bottom, and `0` is top. The type class focuses on `gcd` and we derive the\ncorresponding `lcm` facts from `gcd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normalized_gcd_monoid.normalize_lcm", "description": " Normalized GCD monoid: a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` with normalization and `gcd`\n(greatest common divisor) and `lcm` (least common multiple) operations. In this setting `gcd` and\n`lcm` form a bounded lattice on the associated elements where `gcd` is the infimum, `lcm` is the\nsupremum, `1` is bottom, and `0` is top. The type class focuses on `gcd` and we derive the\ncorresponding `lcm` facts from `gcd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gcd_dvd_gcd_mul_left_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gcd_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associated.gcd_eq_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gcd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lcm_dvd_lcm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gcd_monoid_of_lcm", "description": "Define `gcd_monoid` on a structure just from the `lcm` and its properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_eq_pow_of_mul_eq_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "associated_normalize_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gcd_zero_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pow_dvd_of_mul_eq_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gcd_one_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normalize_coe_units", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dvd_mul_gcd_of_dvd_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gcd_eq_normalize", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lcm_one_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dvd_gcd_mul_of_dvd_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normalization_monoid_of_monoid_hom_right_inverse", "description": "Define `normalization_monoid` on a structure from a `monoid_hom` inverse to `associates.mk`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normalization_monoid_of_unique_