081,c\u2082]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_complex.of_complex", "description": " Intermediate result for `clifford_algebra_complex.equiv`: `\u2102` can be converted to\n`clifford_algebra_complex.Q` above can be converted to.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_quaternion.to_quaternion_comp_of_quaternion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_quaternion.quaternion_basis_i", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_quaternion.of_quaternion_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_quaternion.equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_quaternion.Q", "description": " `Q c\u2081 c\u2082` is a quadratic form over `R \u00d7 R` such that `clifford_algebra (Q c\u2081 c\u2082)` is isomorphic\nas an `R`-algebra to `\u210d[R,c\u2081,c\u2082]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_quaternion.of_quaternion_star", "description": "The quaternion conjugate maps to the \"clifford conjugate\" (aka `star`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_complex.Q", "description": "The quadratic form sending elements to the negation of their square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_ring.equiv", "description": "The clifford algebra over a 0-dimensional vector space is isomorphic to its scalars.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_complex.to_complex", "description": " Intermediate result for `clifford_algebra_complex.equiv`: clifford algebras over\n`clifford_algebra_complex.Q` above can be converted to `\u2102`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_complex.to_complex_involute", "description": "`clifford_algebra.involute` is analogous to `complex.conj`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_complex.of_complex_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_quaternion.to_quaternion_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_ring.reverse_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_complex.Q_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_quaternion.equiv", "description": " The clifford algebra over `clifford_algebra_quaternion.Q c\u2081 c\u2082` is isomorphic as an `R`-algebra\nto `\u210d[R,c\u2081,c\u2082]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_quaternion.quaternion_basis_j", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_complex.clifford_algebra.comm_ring", "description": " The clifford algebra is commutative since it is isomorphic to the complex numbers.\n\nTODO: prove this is true for all `clifford_algebra`s over a 1-dimensional vector space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_dual_number.\u03b9_mul_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_quaternion.of_quaternion_to_quaternion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_dual_number.equiv_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_dual_number.equiv_symm_eps", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_complex.to_complex_comp_of_complex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_quaternion.of_quaternion_comp_to_quaternion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_complex.equiv", "description": " The clifford algebras over `clifford_algebra_complex.Q` is isomorphic as an `\u211d`-algebra to\n`\u2102`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_ring.clifford_algebra.comm_ring", "description": "Since the vector space is empty the ring is commutative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_complex.of_complex_comp_to_complex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_quaternion.quaternion_basis_k", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_complex.reverse_eq_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_complex.of_complex_conj", "description": "`complex.conj` is analogous to `clifford_algebra.involute`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_quaternion.to_quaternion_star", "description": "The \"clifford conjugate\" maps to the quaternion conjugate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_ring.involute_eq_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_complex.reverse_apply", "description": "`reverse` is a no-op over `clifford_algebra_complex.Q`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_complex.equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_complex.equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_complex.of_complex_to_complex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_ring.reverse_eq_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_complex.to_complex_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_complex.to_complex_of_complex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_ring.\u03b9_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_quaternion.of_quaternion", "description": "Map a quaternion into the clifford algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_dual_number.equiv", "description": " The clifford algebra over a 1-dimensional vector space with 0 quadratic form is isomorphic to\nthe dual numbers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra_quaternion.Q_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin_sum_equiv_of_finset", "description": " If `\u03b1` is a linearly ordered fintype, `s : finset \u03b1` has cardinality `m` and its complement has\ncardinality `n`, then `fin m \u2295 fin n \u2243 \u03b1`. The equivalence sends elements of `fin m` to\nelements of `s` and elements of `fin n` to elements of `s\u1d9c` while preserving order on each\n\"half\" of `fin m \u2295 fin n` (using `set.order_iso_of_fin`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin_sum_equiv_of_finset_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin_sum_equiv_of_finset_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mono_equiv_of_fin", "description": " Given a linearly ordered fintype `\u03b1` of cardinal `k`, the order isomorphism\n`mono_equiv_of_fin \u03b1 h` is the increasing bijection between `fin k` and `\u03b1`. Here, `h` is a proof\nthat the cardinality of `\u03b1` is `k`. We use this instead of an isomorphism `fin (card \u03b1) \u2243o \u03b1` to\navoid casting issues in further uses of this function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.untrop_sum'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trop_Inf_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.untrop_sum", "description": " Note we cannot use `i \u2208 s` instead of `i : s` here\nas it is simply not true on conditionally complete lattices!", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.trop_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.trop_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.trop_minimum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "untrop_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.trop_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.untrop_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trop_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.untrop_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "untrop_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trop_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "untrop_sum_eq_Inf_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.untrop_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.trop_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_zero_one_class", "description": "A typeclass for non-associative monoids with zero elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_zero_one_class.one", "description": "A typeclass for non-associative monoids with zero elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_zero_one_class.mul", "description": "A typeclass for non-associative monoids with zero elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_zero_one_class.one_mul", "description": "A typeclass for non-associative monoids with zero elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_zero_one_class.mul_one", "description": "A typeclass for non-associative monoids with zero elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_zero_one_class.zero", "description": "A typeclass for non-associative monoids with zero elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_zero_one_class.zero_mul", "description": "A typeclass for non-associative monoids with zero elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_zero_one_class.mul_zero", "description": "A typeclass for non-associative monoids with zero elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semigroup_with_zero", "description": " A type `S\u2080` is a \"semigroup with zero\u201d if it is a semigroup with zero element, and `0` is left\nand right absorbing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semigroup_with_zero.mul", "description": " A type `S\u2080` is a \"semigroup with zero\u201d if it is a semigroup with zero element, and `0` is left\nand right absorbing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semigroup_with_zero.mul_assoc", "description": " A type `S\u2080` is a \"semigroup with zero\u201d if it is a semigroup with zero element, and `0` is left\nand right absorbing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semigroup_with_zero.zero", "description": " A type `S\u2080` is a \"semigroup with zero\u201d if it is a semigroup with zero element, and `0` is left\nand right absorbing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semigroup_with_zero.zero_mul", "description": " A type `S\u2080` is a \"semigroup with zero\u201d if it is a semigroup with zero element, and `0` is left\nand right absorbing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semigroup_with_zero.mul_zero", "description": " A type `S\u2080` is a \"semigroup with zero\u201d if it is a semigroup with zero element, and `0` is left\nand right absorbing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_monoid_with_zero.to_monoid_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_left_cancel_mul_zero.to_is_cancel_mul_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ne_zero_comm", "description": " If `\u03b1` has no zero divisors, then for elements `a, b : \u03b1`, `a * b` is nonzero iff so is\n`b * a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ne_zero_iff", "description": " If `\u03b1` has no zero divisors, then the product of two elements is nonzero iff both of them\nare nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero", "description": "A type `M` is a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` if it is a commutative monoid with zero element,\n`0` is left and right absorbing,\n and left/right multiplication by a non-zero element is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero.mul", "description": "A type `M` is a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` if it is a commutative monoid with zero element,\n`0` is left and right absorbing,\n and left/right multiplication by a non-zero element is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero.mul_assoc", "description": "A type `M` is a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` if it is a commutative monoid with zero element,\n`0` is left and right absorbing,\n and left/right multiplication by a non-zero element is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero.one", "description": "A type `M` is a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` if it is a commutative monoid with zero element,\n`0` is left and right absorbing,\n and left/right multiplication by a non-zero element is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero.one_mul", "description": "A type `M` is a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` if it is a commutative monoid with zero element,\n`0` is left and right absorbing,\n and left/right multiplication by a non-zero element is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero.mul_one", "description": "A type `M` is a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` if it is a commutative monoid with zero element,\n`0` is left and right absorbing,\n and left/right multiplication by a non-zero element is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero.npow", "description": "A type `M` is a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` if it is a commutative monoid with zero element,\n`0` is left and right absorbing,\n and left/right multiplication by a non-zero element is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero.npow_zero'", "description": "A type `M` is a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` if it is a commutative monoid with zero element,\n`0` is left and right absorbing,\n and left/right multiplication by a non-zero element is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero.npow_succ'", "description": "A type `M` is a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` if it is a commutative monoid with zero element,\n`0` is left and right absorbing,\n and left/right multiplication by a non-zero element is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero.mul_comm", "description": "A type `M` is a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` if it is a commutative monoid with zero element,\n`0` is left and right absorbing,\n and left/right multiplication by a non-zero element is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero.zero", "description": "A type `M` is a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` if it is a commutative monoid with zero element,\n`0` is left and right absorbing,\n and left/right multiplication by a non-zero element is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero.zero_mul", "description": "A type `M` is a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` if it is a commutative monoid with zero element,\n`0` is left and right absorbing,\n and left/right multiplication by a non-zero element is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero.mul_zero", "description": "A type `M` is a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` if it is a commutative monoid with zero element,\n`0` is left and right absorbing,\n and left/right multiplication by a non-zero element is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero.mul_left_cancel_of_ne_zero", "description": "A type `M` is a `cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero` if it is a commutative monoid with zero element,\n`0` is left and right absorbing,\n and left/right multiplication by a non-zero element is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero.to_semigroup_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero.to_mul_zero_one_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_zero_class.to_has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_zero_class", "description": " Typeclass for expressing that a type `M\u2080` with multiplication and a zero satisfies\n`0 * a = 0` and `a * 0 = 0` for all `a : M\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_zero_class.mul", "description": " Typeclass for expressing that a type `M\u2080` with multiplication and a zero satisfies\n`0 * a = 0` and `a * 0 = 0` for all `a : M\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_zero_class.zero", "description": " Typeclass for expressing that a type `M\u2080` with multiplication and a zero satisfies\n`0 * a = 0` and `a * 0 = 0` for all `a : M\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_zero_class.zero_mul", "description": " Typeclass for expressing that a type `M\u2080` with multiplication and a zero satisfies\n`0 * a = 0` and `a * 0 = 0` for all `a : M\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_zero_class.mul_zero", "description": " Typeclass for expressing that a type `M\u2080` with multiplication and a zero satisfies\n`0 * a = 0` and `a * 0 = 0` for all `a : M\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_right_cancel_mul_zero.to_is_left_cancel_mul_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_monoid_with_zero.to_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_left_injective\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero.to_comm_monoid_