lib"}, {"name": "commensurable.commensurator'_mem_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commensurable.commensurator", "description": " For `H` a subgroup of `G`, this is the subgroup of all elements `g : G`\nsuch that `commensurable (g H g\u207b\u00b9) H`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commensurable.commensurable_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commensurable.quot_conj_equiv", "description": "Equivalence of `K/H \u2293 K` with `gKg\u207b\u00b9/gHg\u207b\u00b9 \u2293 gKg\u207b\u00b9`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commensurable.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commensurable.equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commensurable.commensurator'", "description": " For `H` a subgroup of `G`, this is the subgroup of all elements `g : conj_aut G`\nsuch that `commensurable (g \u2022 H) H`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commensurable.commensurable_conj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commensurable.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commensurable.comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commensurable.eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commensurable", "description": "Two subgroups `H K` of `G` are commensurable if `H \u2293 K` has finite index in both `H` and `K`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.surjective_units_map_of_local_ring_hom", "description": "If `f : R \u2192+* S` is a surjective local ring hom, then the induced units map is surjective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.eq_maximal_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field", "description": "The residue field of a local ring is the quotient of the ring by its maximal ideal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring", "description": " A semiring is local if it is nontrivial and `a` or `b` is a unit whenever `a + b = 1`.\nNote that `local_ring` is a predicate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.to_nontrivial", "description": " A semiring is local if it is nontrivial and `a` or `b` is a unit whenever `a + b = 1`.\nNote that `local_ring` is a predicate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.is_unit_or_is_unit_of_add_one", "description": " A semiring is local if it is nontrivial and `a` or `b` is a unit whenever `a + b = 1`.\nNote that `local_ring` is a predicate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.mem_maximal_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.is_unit_or_is_unit_one_sub_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.lift_comp_residue", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.map_id", "description": " Applying `residue_field.map` to the identity ring homomorphism gives the identity\nring homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.nonunits_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.local_hom_tfae", "description": "A ring homomorphism between local rings is a local ring hom iff it reflects units,\ni.e. any preimage of a unit is still a unit. https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07BJ", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.maximal_ideal_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.lift_residue_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.of_is_unit_or_is_unit_of_is_unit_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.is_field_iff_maximal_ideal_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.map_equiv_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_ring_hom_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit_map_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit_of_map_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.residue_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_ring_hom_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.of_surjective'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.maximal_ideal", "description": "The ideal of elements that are not units.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue.is_local_ring_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.map_equiv_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.of_unique_nonzero_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.map", "description": "The map on residue fields induced by a local homomorphism between local rings", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_ring_hom", "description": "A local ring homomorphism is a homomorphism `f` between local rings such that `a` in the domain\n is a unit if `f a` is a unit for any `a`. See `local_ring.local_hom_tfae` for other equivalent\n definitions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_ring_hom.map_nonunit", "description": "A local ring homomorphism is a homomorphism `f` between local rings such that `a` in the domain\n is a unit if `f a` is a unit for any `a`. See `local_ring.local_hom_tfae` for other equivalent\n definitions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.map_residue", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_irreducible_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.jacobson_eq_maximal_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.map_equiv.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.map_equiv", "description": "A ring isomorphism defines an isomorphism of residue fields.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.map_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.of_nonunits_add", "description": "A semiring is local if it is nontrivial and the set of nonunits is closed under the addition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_ring_hom_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.map_comp_residue", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_mem_nonunits_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.is_unit_or_is_unit_of_is_unit_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.of_unique_max_ideal", "description": "A semiring is local if it has a unique maximal ideal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.is_unit_of_mem_nonunits_one_sub_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.map_id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.of_is_unit_or_is_unit_one_sub_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.domain_local_ring", "description": "If `f : R \u2192+* S` is a local ring hom, then `R` is a local ring if `S` is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.lift", "description": "A local ring homomorphism into a field can be descended onto the residue field.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue", "description": "The quotient map from a local ring to its residue field.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.ker_eq_maximal_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.maximal_ideal.is_maximal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_equiv.local_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.local_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_ring_hom_of_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.le_maximal_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.mul_semiring_action", "description": "If `G` acts on `R` as a `mul_semiring_action`, then it also acts on `residue_field R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.maximal_ideal_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_nonunit", "description": "The image of the maximal ideal of the source is contained within the maximal ideal of the target.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.algebra_map_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.map_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.map_aut", "description": " The group homomorphism from `ring_aut R` to `ring_aut k` where `k`\nis the residue field of `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.is_local_ring_hom_residue", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.map_comp", "description": "The composite of two `residue_field.map`s is the `residue_field.map` of the composite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.residue_field.map_aut_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "local_ring.is_unit_one_sub_self_of_mem_nonunits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_mul_right_null", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_add_prod_neg", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (y + x, - x)` is measure-preserving.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.lintegral_lintegral_mul_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.absolutely_continuous_map_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_mul_measure_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_measure_preimage_mul_right_lt_top_of_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.absolutely_continuous_of_is_add_left_invariant", "description": " Any two nonzero left-invariant measures are absolutely continuous w.r.t. each\nother.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.absolutely_continuous_map_div_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_prod_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.quasi_measure_preserving_sub_left_of_right_invariant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_measure_preimage_add_right_lt_top_of_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.quasi_measure_preserving_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.shear_mul_right", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (x, xy)` as a `measurable_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_mul_prod_inv", "description": " The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (yx, x\u207b\u00b9)` is measure-preserving.\nThis is the function `S\u207b\u00b9RSR` in [Halmos, \u00a759],\nwhere `S` is the map `(x, y) \u21a6 (x, xy)` and `R` is `prod.swap`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_add_lintegral_eq", "description": "This is the computation performed in the proof of [Halmos, \u00a760 Th. A].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.quasi_measure_preserving_mul_left", "description": " A *right*-invariant measure is quasi-preserved by *left*-multiplication.\nThis should not be confused with `(measure_preserving_mul_left \u03bc g).quasi_measure_preserving`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.quasi_measure_preserving_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.lintegral_lintegral_add_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_prod_mul_swap_right", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (y, xy)` sends the measure `\u03bc \u00d7 \u03bd` to `\u03bd \u00d7 \u03bc`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_div_prod", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (x / y, y)` preserves the measure `\u03bc \u00d7 \u03bd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.quasi_measure_preserving_add_left", "description": "A *right*-invariant measure is quasi-preserved by *left*-addition.\nThis should not be confused with `(measure_preserving_add_left \u03bc g).quasi_measure_preserving`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.quasi_measure_preserving_mul_right", "description": " A *left*-invariant measure is quasi-preserved by *right*-multiplication.\nThis should not be confused with `(measure_preserving_mul_right \u03bc g).quasi_measure_preserving`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.quasi_measure_preserving_sub_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_eq_sub_vadd", "description": "Left invariant Borel measures on an additive measurable group are unique\n (up to a scalar).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_add_measure_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.inv_absolutely_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.absolutely_continuous_map_sub_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.quasi_measure_preserving_neg_of_right_invariant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_prod_sub_swap", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (y, x - y)` sends `\u03bc \u00d7 \u03bd` to `\u03bd \u00d7 \u03bc`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.absolutely_continuous_map_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_prod_div", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (x, y / x)` is measure-preserving.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_prod_inv_mul_swap", "description": " The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (y, y\u207b\u00b9x)` sends `\u03bc \u00d7 \u03bd` to `\u03bd \u00d7 \u03bc`.\nThis is the function `S\u207b\u00b9R` in [Halmos, \u00a759],\nwhere `S` is the map `(x, y) \u21a6 (x, xy)` and `R` is `prod.swap`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.quasi_measure_preserving_add_right", "description": "A *left*-invariant measure is quasi-preserved by *right*-addition.\nThis should not be confused with `(measure_preserving_add_right \u03bc g).quasi_measure_preserving`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.quasi_measure_preserving_div_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_prod_sub", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (x, y - x)` is measure-preserving.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.absolutely_continuous_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_prod_add_swap", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (y, y + x)` sends the measure `\u03bc \u00d7 \u03bd` to `\u03bd \u00d7 \u03bc`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_mul_prod_inv_right", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (xy, x\u207b\u00b9)` is measure-preserving.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_prod_add", "description": "The shear mapping `(x, y) \u21a6 (x, x + y)` preserves the measure `\u03bc \u00d7 \u03bd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_prod_neg_add", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (x, - x + y)` is measure-preserving.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_measure_preimage_add_right_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.absolutely_continuous_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measurable_measure_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.quasi_measure_preserving_sub_of_right_invariant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.quasi_measure_preserving_div_left_of_right_invariant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_mul_lintegral_eq", "description": "This is the computation performed in the proof of [Halmos, \u00a760 Th. A].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_prod_mul", "description": " The multiplicative shear mapping `(x, y) \u21a6 (x, xy)` preserves the measure `\u03bc \u00d7 \u03bd`.\nThis condition is part of the definition of a measurable group in [Halmos, \u00a759].\nThere, the map in this lemma is called `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.quasi_measure_preserving_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_prod_add_swap_right", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (y, x + y)` sends the measure `\u03bc \u00d7 \u03bd` to `\u03bd \u00d7 \u03bc`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.shear_div_right", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (x, y / x)` as a `measurable_equiv` with as inverse `(x, y) \u21a6 (x, yx)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_prod_mul_swap", "description": " The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (y, yx)` sends the measure `\u03bc \u00d7 \u03bd` to `\u03bd \u00d7 \u03bc`.\nThis is the map `SR` in [Halmos, \u00a759].\n`S` is the map `(x, y) \u21a6 (x, xy)` and `R` is `prod.swap`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_lintegral_div_measure", "description": "A technical lemma relating two different measures. This is basically [Halmos, \u00a760 Th. A].\n Note that if `f` is the characteristic function of a measurable set `t` this states that\n `\u03bc t = c * \u03bc s` for a constant `c` that does not depend on `\u03bc`.\n\n Note: There is a gap in the last step of the proof in [Halmos].\n In the last line, the equality `g(x\u207b\u00b9)\u03bd(sx\u207b\u00b9) = f(x)` holds if we can prove that\n `0 < \u03bd(sx\u207b\u00b9) < \u221e`. The first inequality follows from \u00a759, Th. D, but the second inequality is\n not justified. We prove this inequality for almost all `x` in\n `measure_theory.ae_measure_preimage_mul_right_lt_top_of_ne_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measurable_measure_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.absolutely_continuous_of_is_mul_left_invariant", "description": "Any two nonzero left-invariant measures are absolutely continuous w.r.t. each other.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_prod_inv_mul", "description": " The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (x, x\u207b\u00b9y)` is measure-preserving.\nThis is the function `S\u207b\u00b9` in [Halmos, \u00a759],\nwhere `S` is the map `(x, y) \u21a6 (x, xy)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.quasi_measure_preserving_div_of_right_invariant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.quasi_measure_preserving_inv_of_right_invariant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_prod_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_eq_div_smul", "description": "Left invariant Borel measures on a measurable group are unique (up to a scalar).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_mul_prod", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (xy, y)` preserves the measure `\u03bc \u00d7 \u03bd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.shear_sub_right", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (x, y - x)` as a `measurable_equiv` with as inverse `(x, y) \u21a6 (x, y + x)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.neg_absolutely_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_add_prod_neg_right", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (x + y, - x)` is measure-preserving.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.shear_add_right", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (x, x + y)` as a `measurable_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_lintegral_sub_measure", "description": "A technical lemma relating two different measures. This is basically\n[Halmos, \u00a760 Th. A]. Note that if `f` is the characteristic function of a measurable set `t` this\nstates that `\u03bc t = c * \u03bc s` for a constant `c` that does not depend on `\u03bc`.\n\nNote: There is a gap in the last step of the proof in [Halmos]. In the last line, the equality\n`g(-x) + \u03bd(s - x) = f(x)` holds if we can prove that `0 < \u03bd(s - x) < \u221e`. The first inequality\nfollows from \u00a759, Th. D, but the second inequality is not justified. We prove this inequality for\nalmost all `x` in `measure_theory.ae_measure_preimage_add_right_lt_top_of_ne_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_prod_div_swap", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (y, x / y)` sends `\u03bc \u00d7 \u03bd` to `\u03bd \u00d7 \u03bc`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_measure_preimage_mul_right_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_add_right_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_add_right_null", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_add_prod", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (x + y, y)` preserves the measure `\u03bc \u00d7 \u03bd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_prod_neg_add_swap", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (y, - y + x)` sends `\u03bc \u00d7 \u03bd` to `\u03bd \u00d7 \u03bc`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_preserving_sub_prod", "description": "The map `(x, y) \u21a6 (x - y, y)` preserves the measure `\u03bc \u00d7 \u03bd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.quasi_measure_preserving_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_neg_null", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_mul_right_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_inv_null", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.has_basis_nhds_zero", "description": " In a linearly ordered group with zero element adjoined, `U` is a neighbourhood of `0` if and\nonly if there exists a nonzero element `\u03b3\u2080` such that `Iio \u03b3\u2080 \u2286 U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.is_closed_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.has_continuous_inv\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.order_closed_topology", "description": " The topology on a linearly ordered group with zero element adjoined is compatible with the order\nstructure: the set `{p : \u0393\u2080 \u00d7 \u0393\u2080 | p.1 \u2264 p.2}` is closed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.has_basis_nhds_of_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.nhds_of_ne_zero", "description": " The neighbourhood filter of a nonzero element consists of all sets containing that\nelement.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.tendsto_units", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.Iio_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.tendsto_of_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.topological_space", "description": " The topology on a linearly ordered commutative group with a zero element adjoined.\nA subset U is open if 0 \u2209 U or if there is an invertible element \u03b3\u2080 such that {\u03b3 | \u03b3 < \u03b3\u2080} \u2286 U.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.has_continuous_mul", "description": " The topology on a linearly ordered group with zero element adjoined makes it a topological\nmonoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.t3_space", "description": "The topology on a linearly ordered group with zero element adjoined is T\u2083.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.is_open_Iio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.Iio_mem_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.has_basis_nhds_units", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.tendsto_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.singleton_mem_nhds_of_units", "description": " If `\u03b3` is an invertible element of a linearly ordered group with zero element adjoined, then\n`{\u03b3}` is a neighbourhood of `\u03b3`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.singleton_mem_nhds_of_ne_zero", "description": " If `\u03b3` is a nonzero element of a linearly ordered group with zero element adjoined, then `{\u03b3}`\nis a neighbourhood of `\u03b3`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.nhds_zero_of_units", "description": " If `\u03b3` is an invertible element of a linearly ordered group with zero element adjoined, then\n`Iio (\u03b3 : \u0393\u2080)` is a neighbourhood of `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.is_open_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.nhds_coe_units", "description": " The neighbourhood filter of an invertible element consists of all sets containing that\nelement.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "with_zero_topology.nhds_eq_update", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.fac_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.fac_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.has_lift", "description": "The assertion that a square has a `lift_struct`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.has_lift.exists_lift", "description": "The assertion that a square has a `lift_struct`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.lift_struct.op_equiv", "description": " Equivalences of `lift_struct` for a square and the corresponding square\nin the opposite category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.lift_struct.fac_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.flip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.subsingleton_lift_struct_of_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.lift", "description": " A choice of a diagonal morphism that is part of a `lift_struct` when\nthe square has a lift.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.map", "description": "**Alias** of `category_theory.functor.map_comm_sq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.op", "description": "The commutative square in the opposite category associated to a commutative square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.lift_struct.unop_equiv", "description": " Equivalences of `lift_struct` for a square in the oppositive category and\nthe corresponding square in the original category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map_comm_sq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.has_lift.iff_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.has_lift.iff_unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.lift_struct.op", "description": " A `lift_struct` for a commutative square gives a `lift_struct` for the\ncorresponding square in the opposite category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.fac_right_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.fac_left_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.lift_struct.unop", "description": " A `lift_struct` for a commutative square in the opposite category\ngives a `lift_struct` for the corresponding square in the original category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.lift_struct.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.of_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.lift_struct.fac_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.lift_struct", "description": " The datum of a lift in a commutative square, i.e. a up-right-diagonal\nmorphism which makes both triangles commute.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.lift_struct.l", "description": " The datum of a lift in a commutative square, i.e. a up-right-diagonal\nmorphism which makes both triangles commute.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.lift_struct.fac_left'", "description": " The datum of a lift in a commutative square, i.e. a up-right-diagonal\nmorphism which makes both triangles commute.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.lift_struct.fac_right'", "description": " The datum of a lift in a commutative square, i.e. a up-right-diagonal\nmorphism which makes both triangles commute.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.lift_struct.op_l", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.has_lift.mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.lift_struct.unop_l", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.lift_struct.op_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.w_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.unop", "description": "The commutative square associated to a commutative square in the opposite category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.subsingleton_lift_struct_of_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.has_lift.iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq", "description": " The proposition that a square\n```lean\n  W ---f---> X\n  |          |\n  g          h\n  |          |\n  v          v\n  Y ---i---> Z\n\n```\nis a commuting square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.w", "description": " The proposition that a square\n```lean\n  W ---f---> X\n  |          |\n  g          h\n  |          |\n  v          v\n  Y ---i---> Z\n\n```\nis a commuting square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.lift_struct.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comm_sq.lift_struct.op_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.palindrome.reverse_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.palindrome.of_reverse_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.palindrome.decidable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.palindrome", "description": "`palindrome l` asserts that `l` is a palindrome. This is defined inductively:\n\n* The empty list is a palindrome;\n* A list with one element is a palindrome;\n* Adding the same element to both ends of a palindrome results in a bigger palindrome.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.palindrome.nil", "description": "`palindrome l` asserts that `l` is a palindrome. This is defined inductively:\n\n* The empty list is a palindrome;\n* A list with one element is a palindrome;\n* Adding the same element to both ends of a palindrome results in a bigger palindrome.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.palindrome.singleton", "description": "`palindrome l` asserts that `l` is a palindrome. This is defined inductively:\n\n* The empty list is a palindrome;\n* A list with one element is a palindrome;\n* Adding the same element to both ends of a palindrome results in a bigger palindrome.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.palindrome.cons_concat", "description": "`palindrome l` asserts that `l` is a palindrome. This is defined inductively:\n\n* The empty list is a palindrome;\n* A list with one element is a palindrome;\n* Adding the same element to both ends of a palindrome results in a bigger palindrome.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.palindrome.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.palindrome.append_reverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.palindrome.iff_reverse_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.coe_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.image_to_enum_finset_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.map_to_enum_finset_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.to_embedding_coe_equiv_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.fst_coe_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.sum_eq_sum_to_enum_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.prod_to_enum_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.sum_to_enum_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.to_type", "description": " Auxiliary definition for the `has_coe_to_sort` instance. This prevents the `has_coe m \u03b1`\ninstance from inadverently applying to other sigma types. One should not use this definition\ndirectly.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.card_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.fintype_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.map_univ_coe_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.prod_eq_prod_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.coe_embedding_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.card_to_enum_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.coe_sort_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.to_enum_finset_filter_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.mem_of_mem_to_enum_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.to_enum_finset_subset_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.forall_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.coe_equiv_symm_apply_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.mem_to_enum_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.coe_equiv_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.mk_to_type", "description": " Constructor for terms of the coercion of `m` to a type.\nThis helps Lean pick up the correct instances.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.exists_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.coe_equiv", "description": " Another way to coerce a `multiset` to a type is to go through `m.to_enum_finset` and coerce\nthat `finset` to a type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.to_enum_finset_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.map_univ_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.coe_equiv_symm_apply_snd_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.coe_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.has_coe_to_sort", "description": " Create a type that has the same number of elements as the multiset.\nTerms of this type are triples `\u27e8x, \u27e8i, h\u27e9\u27e9` where `x : \u03b1`, `i : \u2115`, and `h : i < m.count x`.\nThis way repeated elements of a multiset appear multiple times with different values of `i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set_of.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.sum_eq_sum_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.to_enum_finset", "description": " Construct a finset whose elements enumerate the elements of the multiset `m`.\nThe `\u2115` component is used to differentiate between equal elements: if `x` appears `n` times\nthen `(x, 0)`, ..., and `(x, n-1)` appear in the `finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.map_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.has_coe_to_sort.has_coe", "description": " As a convenience, there is a coercion from `m : Type*` to `\u03b1` by projecting onto the first\ncomponent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.prod_eq_prod_to_enum_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.coe_embedding", "description": " The embedding from a multiset into `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u2115` where the second coordinate enumerates repeats.\n\nIf you are looking for the function `m \u2192 \u03b1`, that would be plain `coe`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "where.where_cmd", "description": "When working in a Lean file with namespaces, parameters, and variables, it can be confusing to\nidentify what the current \"parser context\" is. The command `#where` identifies and prints\ninformation about the current location, including the active namespace, open namespaces, and\ndeclared variables.\n\nIt is a bug for `#where` to incorrectly report this information (this was not formerly the case);\nplease file an issue on GitHub if you observe a failure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "where.build_str_includes", "description": "`#where` output helper which traces the includes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "where.build_str_end", "description": "`#where` output helper which traces the namespace end.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "where.sort_variable_list", "description": "Sort the variables by their priority as defined by `where.binder_priority`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "where.collect_implicit_names", "description": "Separate out the names of implicit variables (commonly instances with no name).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "where.build_str_variables", "description": "`#where` output helper which traces the variables.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "where.build_msg", "description": "`#where` output main function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "where.get_open_namespaces", "description": " `get_open_namespaces ns` returns a list of the open namespaces, given that we are currently in\nthe namespace `ns` (which we do not include).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "where.binder_priority", "description": "Assigns a priority to each binder for determining the order in which variables are traced.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "where.binder_less_important", "description": "The relation on binder priorities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "where.format_variable", "description": "Format an individual variable definition for printing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.command.#where", "description": "When working in a Lean file with namespaces, parameters, and variables, it can be confusing to\nidentify what the current \"parser context\" is. The command `#where` identifies and prints\ninformation about the current location, including the active namespace, open namespaces, and\ndeclared variables.\n\nIt is a bug for `#where` to incorrectly report this information (this was not formerly the case);\nplease file an issue on GitHub if you observe a failure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "where.compile_variable_list", "description": "Turn a list of triples of variable names, binder info, and types, into a pretty list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "where.collect_by", "description": " Returns the elements of `l` under the image of `p`, collecting together elements with the same\n`\u03b2` component, deleting duplicates.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "where.build_str_open_namespaces", "description": "`#where` output helper which traces the open namespaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "where.build_str_namespace", "description": "`#where` output helper which traces the current namespace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "where.select_for_which", "description": " Selects the elements of the given `list \u03b1` which under the image of `p : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u00d7 \u03b3` have `\u03b2`\ncomponent equal to `b'`. Returns the `\u03b3` components of the selected elements under the image of `p`,\nand the elements of the original `list \u03b1` which were not selected.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "in_tangent_coordinates_model_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_space.topological_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle_model_space_homeomorph_coe_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle.coe_chart_at_symm_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_fderiv_coord_change", "description": "Auxiliary lemma for tangent spaces: the derivative of a coordinate change between two charts is\n smooth on its source.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle.coord_change_model_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle.trivialization_at_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle.trivialization_at_base_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle_core_coord_change_model_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "in_tangent_coordinates", "description": " When `\u03d5 x` is a continuous linear map that changes vectors in charts around `f x` to vectors\nin charts around `g x`, `in_tangent_coordinates I I' f g \u03d5 x\u2080 x` is a coordinate change of\nthis continuous linear map that makes sense from charts around `f x\u2080` to charts around `g x\u2080`\nby composing it with appropriate coordinate changes.\nNote that the type of `\u03d5` is more accurately\n`\u03a0 x : N, tangent_space I (f x) \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] tangent_space I' (g x)`.\nWe are unfolding `tangent_space` in this type so that Lean recognizes that the type of `\u03d5` doesn't\nactually depend on `f` or `g`.\n\nThis is the underlying function of the trivializations of the hom of (pullbacks of) tangent spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle_core_base_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle_model_space_homeomorph", "description": " The canonical identification between the tangent bundle to the model space and the product,\nas a homeomorphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle.mem_chart_target_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle.coe_chart_at_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle.chart_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_space.topological_add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle.mem_chart_source_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "in_tangent_coordinates_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle_model_space_coe_chart_at_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle.trivialization_at_continuous_linear_map_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle.trivialization_at_symmL", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle.trivialization_at_eq_local_triv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_space.has_continuous_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle.trivialization_at_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_space", "description": " The tangent space at a point of the manifold `M`. It is just `E`. We could use instead\n`(tangent_bundle_core I M).to_topological_vector_bundle_core.fiber x`, but we use `E` to help the\nkernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_space.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle", "description": " The tangent bundle to a smooth manifold, as a Sigma type. Defined in terms of\n`bundle.total_space` to be able to put a suitable topology on it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle.smooth_vector_bundle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle_core", "description": "Let `M` be a smooth manifold with corners with model `I` on `(E, H)`.\nThen `vector_bundle_core I M` is the vector bundle core for the tangent bundle over `M`.\nIt is indexed by the atlas of `M`, with fiber `E` and its change of coordinates from the chart `i`\nto the chart `j` at point `x : M` is the derivative of the composite\n```lean\n  I.symm   i.symm    j     I\nE -----> H -----> M --> H --> E\n```\nwithin the set `range I \u2286 E` at `I (i x) : E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_space.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "in_coordinates_tangent_bundle_core_model_space", "description": "The map `in_coordinates` for the tangent bundle is trivial on the model spaces", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_space.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle.trivialization_at_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle.symmL_model_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle_core_coord_change", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle_model_space_homeomorph_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle_core_coord_change_achart", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle_core_index_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle_core.is_smooth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_space.fiber_bundle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle.continuous_linear_map_at_model_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_space.path_connected_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle.topological_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle.trivialization_at_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle.chart_at_to_local_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle_model_space_chart_at", "description": " In the tangent bundle to the model space, the charts are just the canonical identification\nbetween a product type and a sigma type, a.k.a. `equiv.sigma_equiv_prod`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_space.vector_bundle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tangent_bundle_model_space_coe_chart_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.coe_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.tsupport_subset_symm_image_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.nhds_within_range_basis", "description": " Given a smooth bump function `f : smooth_bump_function I c`, the closed ball of radius `f.R` is\nknown to include the support of `f`. These closed balls (in the model normed space `E`) intersected\nwith `set.range I` form a basis of `\ud835\udcdd[range I] (ext_chart_at I c c)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.nhds_basis_tsupport", "description": " The closures of supports of smooth bump functions centered at `c` form a basis of `\ud835\udcdd c`.\nIn other words, each of these closures is a neighborhood of `c` and each neighborhood of `c`\nincludes `tsupport f` for some `f : smooth_bump_function I c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.one_of_dist_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.eq_on_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.is_open_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.eventually_eq_of_mem_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.support_eq_symm_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.smooth", "description": "A smooth bump function is infinitely smooth.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.support_eq_inter_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.image_eq_inter_preimage_of_subset_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.support_subset_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.has_compact_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.tsupport_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.smooth_smul", "description": " If `f : smooth_bump_function I c` is a smooth bump function and `g : M \u2192 G` is a function smooth\non the source of the chart at `c`, then `f \u2022 g` is smooth on the whole manifold.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.to_fun", "description": " The function defined by `f : smooth_bump_function c`. Use automatic coercion to function\ninstead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.update_r", "description": "Replace `r` with another value in the interval `(0, f.R)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.R_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.is_closed_symm_image_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.nhds_basis_support", "description": " Given `s \u2208 \ud835\udcdd c`, the supports of smooth bump functions `f : smooth_bump_function I c` such that\n`tsupport f \u2286 s` form a basis of `\ud835\udcdd c`.  In other words, each of these supports is a\nneighborhood of `c` and each neighborhood of `c` includes `support f` for some `f :\nsmooth_bump_function I c` such that `tsupport f \u2286 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.eventually_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function", "description": " Given a smooth manifold modelled on a finite dimensional space `E`,\n`f : smooth_bump_function I M` is a smooth function on `M` such that in the extended chart `e` at\n`f.c`:\n\n* `f x = 1` in the closed ball of radius `f.r` centered at `f.c`;\n* `f x = 0` outside of the ball of radius `f.R` centered at `f.c`;\n* `0 \u2264 f x \u2264 1` for all `x`.\n\nThe structure contains data required to construct a function with these properties. The function is\navailable as `\u21d1f` or `f x`. Formal statements of the properties listed above involve some\n(pre)images under `ext_chart_at I f.c` and are given as lemmas in the `smooth_bump_function`\nnamespace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.to_cont_diff_bump", "description": " Given a smooth manifold modelled on a finite dimensional space `E`,\n`f : smooth_bump_function I M` is a smooth function on `M` such that in the extended chart `e` at\n`f.c`:\n\n* `f x = 1` in the closed ball of radius `f.r` centered at `f.c`;\n* `f x = 0` outside of the ball of radius `f.R` centered at `f.c`;\n* `0 \u2264 f x \u2264 1` for all `x`.\n\nThe structure contains data required to construct a function with these properties. The function is\navailable as `\u21d1f` or `f x`. Formal statements of the properties listed above involve some\n(pre)images under `ext_chart_at I f.c` and are given as lemmas in the `smooth_bump_function`\nnamespace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.closed_ball_subset", "description": " Given a smooth manifold modelled on a finite dimensional space `E`,\n`f : smooth_bump_function I M` is a smooth function on `M` such that in the extended chart `e` at\n`f.c`:\n\n* `f x = 1` in the closed ball of radius `f.r` centered at `f.c`;\n* `f x = 0` outside of the ball of radius `f.R` centered at `f.c`;\n* `0 \u2264 f x \u2264 1` for all `x`.\n\nThe structure contains data required to construct a function with these properties. The function is\navailable as `\u21d1f` or `f x`. Formal statements of the properties listed above involve some\n(pre)images under `ext_chart_at I f.c` and are given as lemmas in the `smooth_bump_function`\nnamespace.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.support_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.eventually_eq_one_of_dist_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.ball_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.nonempty_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.update_r_r", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.support_update_r", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.tsupport_subset_chart_at_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.c_mem_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.update_r_R", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.smooth_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.mem_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.tsupport_subset_ext_chart_at_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.exists_r_pos_lt_subset_ball", "description": " If `f` is a smooth bump function and `s` closed subset of the support of `f` (i.e., of the open\nball of radius `f.R`), then there exists `0 < r < f.R` such that `s` is a subset of the open ball of\nradius `r`. Formally, `s \u2286 e.source \u2229 e \u207b\u00b9' (ball (e c) r)`, where `e = ext_chart_at I c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.is_closed_image_of_is_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_bump_function.is_compact_symm_image_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_coeff.const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_coeff", "description": " The `n`-th Fourier coefficient of a function `add_circle T \u2192 E`, for `E` a complete normed\n`\u2102`-vector space, defined as the integral over `add_circle T` of `fourier (-n) t \u2022 f t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.scaled_exp_map_periodic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_coeff_eq_interval_integral", "description": " The Fourier coefficients of a function on `add_circle T` can be computed as an integral\nover `[a, a + T]`, for any real `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_coeff_on.const_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at_fourier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.haar_add_circle", "description": "Haar measure on the additive circle, normalised to have total measure 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.haar_add_circle.measure_theory.is_probability_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_Lp", "description": " The family of monomials `fourier n`, parametrized by `n : \u2124` and considered as\nelements of the `Lp` space of functions `add_circle T \u2192 \u2102`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_fourier_series_L2", "description": "The Fourier series of an `L2` function `f` sums to `f`, in the `L\u00b2` space of `add_circle T`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.continuous_to_circle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "coe_fourier_basis", "description": " The elements of the Hilbert basis `fourier_basis` are the functions `fourier_Lp 2`, i.e. the\nmonomials `fourier n` on the circle considered as elements of `L\u00b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.to_circle", "description": " The canonical map `\u03bb x, exp (2 \u03c0 i x / T)` from `\u211d / \u2124 \u2022 T` to the unit circle in `\u2102`.\nIf `T = 0` we understand this as the constant function 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier", "description": " The family of exponential monomials `\u03bb x, exp (2 \u03c0 i n x / T)`, parametrized by `n : \u2124` and\nconsidered as bundled continuous maps from `\u211d / \u2124 \u2022 T` to `\u2102`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_coeff_on.const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_subalgebra_separates_points", "description": " The subalgebra of `C(add_circle T, \u2102)` generated by `fourier n` for `n \u2208 \u2124`\nseparates points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_coeff_on_of_has_deriv_at", "description": "Express Fourier coefficients of `f` on an interval in terms of those of its derivative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.haar_add_circle.is_add_haar_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_coe_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_basis", "description": " We define `fourier_basis` to be a `\u2124`-indexed Hilbert basis for `Lp \u2102 2 haar_add_circle`,\nwhich by definition is an isometric isomorphism from `Lp \u2102 2 haar_add_circle` to `\u2113\u00b2(\u2124, \u2102)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.to_circle_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_fourier_series_of_summable", "description": " If the sequence of Fourier coefficients of `f` is summable, then the Fourier series converges\nuniformly to `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_coeff_on_eq_integral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_subalgebra_closure_eq_top", "description": "The subalgebra of `C(add_circle T, \u2102)` generated by `fourier n` for `n \u2208 \u2124` is dense.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "coe_fn_fourier_Lp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_antideriv_at_fourier_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_subalgebra", "description": "The subalgebra of `C(add_circle T, \u2102)` generated by `fourier n` for `n \u2208 \u2124` .", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.volume_eq_smul_haar_add_circle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_coeff.const_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_coeff_on", "description": " For a function on `\u211d`, the Fourier coefficients of `f` on `[a, b]` are defined as the\nFourier coefficients of the unique periodic function agreeing with `f` on `Ioc a b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.injective_to_circle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_subalgebra_coe", "description": " The subalgebra of `C(add_circle T, \u2102)` generated by `fourier n` for `n \u2208 \u2124` is in fact the\nlinear span of these functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "span_fourier_Lp_closure_eq_top", "description": " For each `1 \u2264 p < \u221e`, the linear span of the monomials `fourier n` is dense in\n`Lp \u2102 p haar_circle`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orthonormal_fourier", "description": "The monomials `fourier n` are an orthonormal set with respect to normalised Haar measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_pointwise_sum_fourier_series_of_summable", "description": " If the sequence of Fourier coefficients of `f` is summable, then the Fourier series of `f`\nconverges everywhere pointwise to `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_coeff_lift_Ioc_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_basis_repr", "description": " Under the isometric isomorphism `fourier_basis` from `Lp \u2102 2 haar_circle` to `\u2113\u00b2(\u2124, \u2102)`, the\n`i`-th coefficient is `fourier_coeff f i`, i.e., the integral over `add_circle T` of\n`\u03bb t, fourier (-i) t * f t` with respect to the Haar measure of total mass 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_eval_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_add_half_inv_index", "description": "For `n \u2260 0`, a translation by `T / 2 / n` negates the function `fourier n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsum_sq_fourier_coeff", "description": " **Parseval's identity**: for an `L\u00b2` function `f` on `add_circle T`, the sum of the squared\nnorms of the Fourier coefficients equals the `L\u00b2` norm of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "span_fourier_closure_eq_top", "description": "The linear span of the monomials `fourier n` is dense in `C(add_circle T, \u2102)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_subalgebra_conj_invariant", "description": " The subalgebra of `C(add_circle T, \u2102)` generated by `fourier n` for `n \u2208 \u2124` is invariant under\ncomplex conjugation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at_fourier_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_coeff_lift_Ico_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fourier_coeff_to_Lp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_cast_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.mul_X_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.C_dvd_iff_dvd_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.support_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.is_unit_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.smul_eq_C_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_bit0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_mul", "description": " Decomposes the coefficient of the product `p * q` as a sum\nover `nat.antidiagonal`. A version which sums over `range (n + 1)` can be obtained\nby using `finset.nat.sum_antidiagonal_eq_sum_range_succ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_X_pow_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_mul_X_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_C_mul_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_monomial_zero_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_X_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.mul_X_pow_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.support_binomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_mul_X_pow'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_mul_monomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_X_add_one_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.lsum", "description": "`polynomial.sum` as a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.constant_coeff_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_X_add_C_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.char_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_C_mul_X_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": 