 "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conj_act.of_mul_symm_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conj_act.of_conj_act", "description": "Reinterpret `g : conj_act G` as an element of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conj_act.smul_comm_class'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conj_act.of_conj_act_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conj_act.to_conj_act_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conj_act.units_mul_distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conj_act.units_smul_comm_class'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conj_act.to_conj_act_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conj_act.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conj_act.group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conj_act", "description": "A type alias for a group `G`. `conj_act G` acts on `G` by conjugation", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.generate_from_eq", "description": "**Dynkin's \u03c0-\u03bb theorem**:\nGiven a collection of sets closed under binary intersections, then the Dynkin system it\ngenerates is equal to the \u03c3-algebra it generates.\nThis result is known as the \u03c0-\u03bb theorem.\nA collection of sets closed under binary intersection is called a \u03c0-system (often requiring\nadditionnally that is is non-empty, but we drop this condition in the formalization).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.restrict_on", "description": "If `s` is in a Dynkin system `d`, we can form the new Dynkin system `{s \u2229 t | t \u2208 d}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_generate_pi_system_Union_elim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_Union_of_directed_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_pi_Union_Inter", "description": "If `\u03c0` is a family of \u03c0-systems, then `pi_Union_Inter \u03c0 S` is a \u03c0-system.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "generate_from_generate_pi_system_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_Union_Inter_mono_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_generate_pi_system_Union_elim'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_Ixx", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_Ixx_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.generate_has", "description": "The least Dynkin system containing a collection of basic sets.\n This inductive type gives the underlying collection of sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.generate_has.basic", "description": "The least Dynkin system containing a collection of basic sets.\n This inductive type gives the underlying collection of sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.generate_has.empty", "description": "The least Dynkin system containing a collection of basic sets.\n This inductive type gives the underlying collection of sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.generate_has.compl", "description": "The least Dynkin system containing a collection of basic sets.\n This inductive type gives the underlying collection of sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.generate_has.Union", "description": "The least Dynkin system containing a collection of basic sets.\n This inductive type gives the underlying collection of sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "generate_pi_system_subset_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_Union_of_monotone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_generate_from_pi_Union_Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.has_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_Ioo_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_Iio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.generate", "description": "The least Dynkin system containing a collection of basic sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "generate_pi_system_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_generate_pi_system_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_Union_Inter", "description": " From a set of indices `S : set \u03b9` and a family of sets of sets `\u03c0 : \u03b9 \u2192 set (set \u03b1)`,\ndefine the set of sets that can be written as `\u22c2 x \u2208 t, f x` for some finset `t \u2286 S` and sets\n`f x \u2208 \u03c0 x`. If `\u03c0` is a family of \u03c0-systems, then it is a \u03c0-system.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_Union_Inter_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_image_Iio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.generate_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "generate_from_pi_Union_Inter_singleton_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system.singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "generate_from_measurable_set_of_generate_pi_system", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.has_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_Ioc_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_generate_pi_system", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system.insert_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_Ico_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.generate_has_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.generate_has_subset_generate_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_pi_Union_Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_set_supr_of_mem_pi_Union_Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system", "description": "A Dynkin system is a collection of subsets of a type `\u03b1` that contains the empty set,\n is closed under complementation and under countable union of pairwise disjoint sets.\n The disjointness condition is the only difference with `\u03c3`-algebras.\n\n The main purpose of Dynkin systems is to provide a powerful induction rule for \u03c3-algebras\n generated by a collection of sets which is stable under intersection.\n\n A Dynkin system is also known as a \"\u03bb-system\" or a \"d-system\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.has", "description": "A Dynkin system is a collection of subsets of a type `\u03b1` that contains the empty set,\n is closed under complementation and under countable union of pairwise disjoint sets.\n The disjointness condition is the only difference with `\u03c3`-algebras.\n\n The main purpose of Dynkin systems is to provide a powerful induction rule for \u03c3-algebras\n generated by a collection of sets which is stable under intersection.\n\n A Dynkin system is also known as a \"\u03bb-system\" or a \"d-system\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.has_empty", "description": "A Dynkin system is a collection of subsets of a type `\u03b1` that contains the empty set,\n is closed under complementation and under countable union of pairwise disjoint sets.\n The disjointness condition is the only difference with `\u03c3`-algebras.\n\n The main purpose of Dynkin systems is to provide a powerful induction rule for \u03c3-algebras\n generated by a collection of sets which is stable under intersection.\n\n A Dynkin system is also known as a \"\u03bb-system\" or a \"d-system\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.has_compl", "description": "A Dynkin system is a collection of subsets of a type `\u03b1` that contains the empty set,\n is closed under complementation and under countable union of pairwise disjoint sets.\n The disjointness condition is the only difference with `\u03c3`-algebras.\n\n The main purpose of Dynkin systems is to provide a powerful induction rule for \u03c3-algebras\n generated by a collection of sets which is stable under intersection.\n\n A Dynkin system is also known as a \"\u03bb-system\" or a \"d-system\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.has_Union_nat", "description": "A Dynkin system is a collection of subsets of a type `\u03b1` that contains the empty set,\n is closed under complementation and under countable union of pairwise disjoint sets.\n The disjointness condition is the only difference with `\u03c3`-algebras.\n\n The main purpose of Dynkin systems is to provide a powerful induction rule for \u03c3-algebras\n generated by a collection of sets which is stable under intersection.\n\n A Dynkin system is also known as a \"\u03bb-system\" or a \"d-system\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.generate_has_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.has_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_Icc_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "generate_from_pi_Union_Inter_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_image_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_pi_Union_Inter_of_measurable_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.of_measurable_space_to_measurable_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.is_pi_system_measurable_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "generate_pi_system", "description": " Given a collection `S` of subsets of `\u03b1`, then `generate_pi_system S` is the smallest\n\u03c0-system containing `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "generate_pi_system.base", "description": " Given a collection `S` of subsets of `\u03b1`, then `generate_pi_system S` is the smallest\n\u03c0-system containing `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "generate_pi_system.inter", "description": " Given a collection `S` of subsets of `\u03b1`, then `generate_pi_system S` is the smallest\n\u03c0-system containing `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.of_measurable_space_le_of_measurable_space_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.has_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.has_compl_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system.insert_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "generate_pi_system_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.generate_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_Union_Inter_singleton_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_Union_Inter_mono_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system.comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.of_measurable_space", "description": "Every measurable space (\u03c3-algebra) forms a Dynkin system", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "generate_from_pi_Union_Inter_measurable_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system", "description": "A \u03c0-system is a collection of subsets of `\u03b1` that is closed under binary intersection of\n non-disjoint sets. Usually it is also required that the collection is nonempty, but we don't do\n that here.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.to_measurable_space", "description": "If a Dynkin system is closed under binary intersection, then it forms a `\u03c3`-algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "generate_pi_system_measurable_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.le_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.dynkin_system.has_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_pi_system_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_space.induction_on_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.commute.self_iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_succ_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.foldl_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.commute.iterate_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.foldr_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.commute.iterate_iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.commute.comp_iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_succ_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_pred_comp_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_succ'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.commute.iterate_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.commute.iterate_eq_of_map_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_cancel_of_add", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `function.iterate_add_eq_iterate`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_add_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate.rec", "description": "A recursor for the iterate of a function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.commute.iterate_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_add_eq_iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.semiconj.iterate_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.comp_iterate_pred_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.commute.iterate_iterate_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.left_inverse.iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.semiconj\u2082.iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.right_inverse.iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_fixed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate_commute", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.bijective.iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.semiconj.iterate_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.iterate.rec_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_equiv.affine_independent_iff", "description": "Affine equivalences preserve affine independence of families of points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.reindex_range_points", "description": "Reindexing a simplex produces one with the same set of points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent_iff_linear_independent_vsub", "description": " A family is affinely independent if and only if the differences\nfrom a base point in that family are linearly independent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.centroid_eq_of_range_eq", "description": "Two simplices with the same points have the same centroid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.reindex_refl", "description": "Reindexing by `equiv.refl` yields the original simplex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent_iff_indicator_eq_of_affine_combination_eq", "description": " A family is affinely independent if and only if any affine\ncombinations (with sum of weights 1) that evaluate to the same point\nhave equal `set.indicator`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_nontrivial_relation_sum_zero_of_not_affine_ind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent_iff_eq_of_fintype_affine_combination_eq", "description": " A finite family is affinely independent if and only if any affine\ncombinations (with sum of weights 1) that evaluate to the same point are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.mk_of_point", "description": "Construct a 0-simplex from a point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.face_centroid_eq_centroid", "description": " The centroid of a face of a simplex as the centroid of a subset of\nthe points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_combination_mem_affine_span_pair", "description": " Given an affinely independent family of points, an affine combination lies in the\nspan of two points given as affine combinations if and only if it is an affine combination\nwith weights those of one point plus a multiple of the difference between the weights of the\ntwo points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent.of_set_of_injective", "description": " If the range of an injective indexed family of points is affinely\nindependent, so is that family.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent", "description": " An indexed family is said to be affinely independent if no\nnontrivial weighted subtractions (where the sum of weights is 0) are\n0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent.not_mem_affine_span_diff", "description": " If a family is affinely independent, a point in the family is not\nin the affine span of the other points, if the underlying ring is\nnontrivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent_set_iff_linear_independent_vsub", "description": " A set is affinely independent if and only if the differences from\na base point in that set are linearly independent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.ext_iff", "description": "Two simplices are equal if and only if they have the same points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.reindex_points", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent_iff", "description": " Viewing a module as an affine space modelled on itself, we can characterise affine independence\nin terms of linear combinations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.mk_of_point_points", "description": "The point in a simplex constructed with `mk_of_point`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent_of_ne_of_mem_of_not_mem_of_mem", "description": " If distinct points `p\u2081` and `p\u2083` lie in `s` but `p\u2082` does not, the three points are affinely\nindependent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weighted_vsub_mem_vector_span_pair", "description": " Given an affinely independent family of points, a weighted subtraction lies in the\n`vector_span` of two points given as affine combinations if and only if it is a weighted\nsubtraction with weights a multiple of the difference between the weights of the two points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent.exists_mem_inter_of_exists_mem_inter_affine_span", "description": " If a family is affinely independent, and the spans of points\nindexed by two subsets of the index type have a point in common, those\nsubsets of the index type have an element in common, if the underlying\nring is nontrivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.reindex", "description": "Remap a simplex along an `equiv` of index types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent_of_subsingleton", "description": "A family with at most one point is affinely independent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_eq_of_affine_combination_mem_affine_span_pair", "description": " Given an affinely independent family of points, suppose that an affine combination lies in\nthe span of two points given as affine combinations, and suppose that, for two indices, the\ncoefficients in the first point in the span are zero and those in the second point in the span\nhave the same sign. Then the coefficients in the combination lying in the span have the same\nsign.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent_of_ne_of_mem_of_mem_of_not_mem", "description": " If distinct points `p\u2081` and `p\u2082` lie in `s` but `p\u2083` does not, the three points are affinely\nindependent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_set_iff_affine_independent_vadd_union_singleton", "description": " A set of nonzero vectors is linearly independent if and only if,\ngiven a point `p\u2081`, the vectors added to `p\u2081` and `p\u2081` itself are\naffinely independent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent_iff_of_fintype", "description": " A family indexed by a `fintype` is affinely independent if and\nonly if no nontrivial weighted subtractions over `finset.univ` (where\nthe sum of the weights is 0) are 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.reindex_symm_reindex", "description": "Reindexing by the inverse of an equivalence and that equivalence yields the original simplex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent.injective", "description": " An affinely independent family is injective, if the underlying\nring is nontrivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.face_points", "description": "The points of a face of a simplex are given by `mono_of_fin`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent.range", "description": " If an indexed family of points is affinely independent, so is the\ncorresponding set of points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_equiv.affine_independent_set_of_eq_iff", "description": "Affine equivalences preserve affine independence of subsets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.face_eq_mk_of_point", "description": " A single-point face equals the 0-simplex constructed with\n`mk_of_point`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent.subtype", "description": " If a family is affinely independent, so is any subfamily indexed\nby a subtype of the index type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.face", "description": " A face of a simplex is a simplex with the given subset of\npoints.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.reindex_reindex_symm", "description": "Reindexing by an equivalence and its inverse yields the original simplex.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent.map'", "description": " The image of a family of points in affine space, under an injective affine transformation, is\naffine-independent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map.affine_independent_iff", "description": "Injective affine maps preserve affine independence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.triangle", "description": "A `triangle k P` is a collection of three affinely independent points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent.affine_span_disjoint_of_disjoint", "description": " If a family is affinely independent, the spans of points indexed\nby disjoint subsets of the index type are disjoint, if the underlying\nring is nontrivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent.units_line_map", "description": " If we single out one member of an affine-independent family of points and affinely transport\nall others along the line joining them to this member, the resulting new family of points is affine-\nindependent.\n\nThis is the affine version of `linear_independent.units_smul`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent.mono", "description": "If a set of points is affinely independent, so is any subset.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.reindex_trans", "description": "Reindexing by the composition of two equivalences is the same as reindexing twice.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent.indicator_eq_of_affine_combination_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent_def", "description": "The definition of `affine_independent`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_subset_affine_independent_affine_span_eq_top", "description": " An affinely independent set of points can be extended to such a\nset that spans the whole space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent.mem_affine_span_iff", "description": " If a family is affinely independent, a point in the family is in\nthe span of some of the points given by a subset of the index type if\nand only if that point's index is in the subset, if the underlying\nring is nontrivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.face_points'", "description": "The points of a face of a simplex are given by `mono_of_fin`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.centroid_eq_iff", "description": " Over a characteristic-zero division ring, the centroids given by\ntwo subsets of the points of a simplex are equal if and only if those\nfaces are given by the same subset of points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent_of_ne_of_not_mem_of_mem_of_mem", "description": " If distinct points `p\u2082` and `p\u2083` lie in `s` but `p\u2081` does not, the three points are affinely\nindependent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.ext", "description": "Two simplices are equal if they have the same points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_affine_independent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.face_centroid_eq_iff", "description": " Over a characteristic-zero division ring, the centroids of two\nfaces of a simplex are equal if and only if those faces are given by\nthe same subset of points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex", "description": " A `simplex k P n` is a collection of `n + 1` affinely\nindependent points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.points", "description": " A `simplex k P n` is a collection of `n + 1` affinely\nindependent points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.independent", "description": " A `simplex k P n` is a collection of `n + 1` affinely\nindependent points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent.of_comp", "description": " If the image of a family of points in affine space under an affine transformation is affine-\nindependent, then the original family of points is also affine-independent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent.comp_embedding", "description": " If a family is affinely independent, so is any subfamily given by\ncomposition of an embedding into index type with the original\nfamily.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent.affine_independent_of_not_mem_span", "description": " If all but one point of a family are affinely independent, and that point does not lie in\nthe affine span of that family, the family is affinely independent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine.simplex.range_face_points", "description": "The set of points of a face.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sign_eq_of_affine_combination_mem_affine_span_single_line_map", "description": " Given an affinely independent family of points, suppose that an affine combination lies in\nthe span of one point of that family and a combination of another two points of that family given\nby `line_map` with coefficient between 0 and 1. Then the coefficients of those two points in the\ncombination lying in the span have the same sign.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_independent_of_ne", "description": "Two different points are affinely independent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_boolring_of_boolring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_mul.mul.is_idempotent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_boolring_symm_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_boolring_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "boolean_ring", "description": "A Boolean ring is a ring where multiplication is idempotent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "boolean_ring.to_ring", "description": "A Boolean ring is a ring where multiplication is idempotent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "boolean_ring.mul_self", "description": "A Boolean ring is a ring where multiplication is idempotent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_boolring_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_add_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sub_eq_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_boolring_symm_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "as_boolalg.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_boolalg_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "generalized_boolean_algebra.to_non_unital_comm_ring", "description": " Every generalized Boolean algebra has the structure of a non unital commutative ring with the\nfollowing data:\n\n* `a + b` unfolds to `a \u2206 b` (symmetric difference)\n* `a * b` unfolds to `a \u2293 b`\n* `-a` unfolds to `a`\n* `0` unfolds to `\u22a5`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_boolalg_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_lattice_hom.as_boolring_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_boolalg_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "as_boolring.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "boolean_ring.le_sup_inf_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_boolalg_sdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_lattice_hom.as_boolring_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_equiv.as_boolring_as_boolalg_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"n