an algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.as_boolalg", "description": " Turn a ring homomorphism from Boolean rings `\u03b1` to `\u03b2` into a bounded lattice homomorphism\nfrom `\u03b1` to `\u03b2` considered as Boolean algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.as_boolalg_as_boolring_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "boolean_algebra.to_boolean_ring", "description": " Every Boolean algebra has the structure of a Boolean ring with the following data:\n\n* `a + b` unfolds to `a \u2206 b` (symmetric difference)\n* `a * b` unfolds to `a \u2293 b`\n* `-a` unfolds to `a`\n* `0` unfolds to `\u22a5`\n* `1` unfolds to `\u22a4`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_boolalg_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.as_boolalg_to_lattice_hom_to_sup_hom_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_boolalg_symm_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_boolalg_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_eq_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.as_boolalg_as_boolring_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_boolring", "description": "The \"identity\" equivalence between `\u03b1` and `as_boolring \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_lattice_hom.as_boolring", "description": " Turn a bounded lattice homomorphism from Boolean algebras `\u03b1` to `\u03b2` into a ring homomorphism\nfrom `\u03b1` to `\u03b2` considered as Boolean rings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.as_boolalg_as_boolring", "description": " Order isomorphism between `\u03b1` considered as a Boolean ring considered as a Boolean algebra and\n`\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_lattice_hom.as_boolring_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_boolring_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bool.boolean_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_boolalg_symm_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_boolring_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_equiv.as_boolring_as_boolalg", "description": " Ring isomorphism between `\u03b1` considered as a Boolean algebra considered as a Boolean ring and\n`\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_boolring_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "neg_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_boolring_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_boolring", "description": "The \"identity\" equivalence between `as_boolring \u03b1` and `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "boolean_ring.to_comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "boolean_ring.to_boolean_algebra", "description": "The Boolean algebra structure on a Boolean ring.\n\nThe data is defined so that:\n* `a \u2294 b` unfolds to `a + b + a * b`\n* `a \u2293 b` unfolds to `a * b`\n* `a \u2264 b` unfolds to `a + b + a * b = b`\n* `\u22a5` unfolds to `0`\n* `\u22a4` unfolds to `1`\n* `a\u1d9c` unfolds to `1 + a`\n* `a \\ b` unfolds to `a * (1 + b)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_boolalg", "description": "The \"identity\" equivalence between `as_boolalg \u03b1` and `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_boolring_le_of_boolring_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_boolalg_of_boolalg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "as_boolring.boolean_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_boolring_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_boolalg_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "boolean_ring.sup_inf_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_boolalg_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_boolring_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_boolalg_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_boolalg_symm_diff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "punit.boolean_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_boolalg", "description": "The \"identity\" equivalence between `\u03b1` and `as_boolalg \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_boolring_to_boolring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "arithcc.register.le_of_lt_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.state_eq_rs_implies_write_eq_rs", "description": "Writing the same value to any register preserves `\u2243[t]/ac`.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.state_eq_rs.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.state_eq_rs.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.state_eq_rs", "description": "Machine states \u03b6\u2081 and \u03b6\u2082 are equal except for the accumulator and registers {x | x \u2265 t}.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.state_eq.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.expr.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.write", "description": "This is similar to the `a` function (3.9), but for registers only.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.outcome", "description": "The resulting machine state of running a target program from a given machine state (3.12).", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.expr", "description": "An expression in the source language is formed by constants, variables, and sums.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.expr.const", "description": "An expression in the source language is formed by constants, variables, and sums.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.expr.var", "description": "An expression in the source language is formed by constants, variables, and sums.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.expr.sum", "description": "An expression in the source language is formed by constants, variables, and sums.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.instruction.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.identifier", "description": "Variable identifier type in the source language.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.state_eq_implies_write_eq", "description": "Writing the same value to register `t` gives `\u2243[t + 1]` from `\u2243[t]`.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.state_eq.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.read", "description": "This is similar to the `c` function (3.8), but for registers only.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.register", "description": "Register name type in the target language.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.state.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.state_eq_state_eq_rs.trans", "description": "Transitivity of chaining `\u2243[t]` and `\u2243[t]/ac`.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.word", "description": "Value type shared by both source and target languages.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.state_eq", "description": "Machine states \u03b6\u2081 and \u03b6\u2082 are equal except for registers {x | x \u2265 t}.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.write_eq_implies_state_eq", "description": "`\u2243[t + 1]` with writing to register `t` implies `\u2243[t]`.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.state_eq_rs.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.instruction", "description": "Instructions of the target machine language (3.1--3.7).", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.instruction.li", "description": "Instructions of the target machine language (3.1--3.7).", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.instruction.load", "description": "Instructions of the target machine language (3.1--3.7).", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.instruction.sto", "description": "Instructions of the target machine language (3.1--3.7).", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.instruction.add", "description": "Instructions of the target machine language (3.1--3.7).", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.compiler_correctness", "description": " The main **compiler correctness theorem**.\n\nUnlike Theorem 1 in the paper, both `map` and the assumption on `t` are explicit.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.state", "description": " Machine state consists of the accumulator and a vector of registers.\n\nThe paper uses two functions `c` and `a` for accessing both the accumulator and registers.\nFor clarity, we make accessing the accumulator explicit and use `read`/`write` for registers.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.state.ac", "description": " Machine state consists of the accumulator and a vector of registers.\n\nThe paper uses two functions `c` and `a` for accessing both the accumulator and registers.\nFor clarity, we make accessing the accumulator explicit and use `read`/`write` for registers.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.state.rs", "description": " Machine state consists of the accumulator and a vector of registers.\n\nThe paper uses two functions `c` and `a` for accessing both the accumulator and registers.\nFor clarity, we make accessing the accumulator explicit and use `read`/`write` for registers.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.loc", "description": "Map a variable in the source expression to a machine register.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.value", "description": "The semantics of the source language (2.1).", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.state_eq.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.outcome_append", "description": "A lemma on the concatenation of two programs (3.13).", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.compile", "description": " The implementation of the compiler (4.2).\n\nThis definition explicitly takes a map from variables to registers.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.register.lt_succ_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "arithcc.step", "description": "The semantics of the target language (3.11).", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.lie_character_apply_of_mem_derived", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.lie_character_equiv_linear_dual_symm_apply_to_linear_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.lie_character_equiv_linear_dual_symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.lie_character", "description": "A character of a Lie algebra is a morphism to the scalars.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.lie_character_equiv_linear_dual", "description": "For an Abelian Lie algebra, characters are just linear forms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.lie_character_apply_lie", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.lie_character_equiv_linear_dual_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.non_unital_non_assoc_semiring", "description": " Pullback a `non_unital_non_assoc_semiring` instance along an injective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.comm_semiring", "description": " Pullback a `semiring` instance along an injective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.comm_ring", "description": " Pushforward a `comm_ring` instance along a surjective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.non_unital_non_assoc_ring", "description": " Pullback a `non_unital_non_assoc_ring` instance along an injective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.non_unital_comm_ring", "description": " Pushforward a `non_unital_comm_ring` instance along a surjective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.non_unital_non_assoc_semiring", "description": " Pushforward a `non_unital_non_assoc_semiring` instance along a surjective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.non_assoc_ring", "description": " Pullback a `non_assoc_ring` instance along an injective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.non_unital_comm_ring", "description": " Pullback a `comm_ring` instance along an injective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.non_unital_comm_semiring", "description": " Pullback a `non_unital_semiring` instance along an injective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.non_unital_semiring", "description": " Pushforward a `non_unital_semiring` instance along a surjective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.semiring", "description": " Pullback a `semiring` instance along an injective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.distrib", "description": " Pushforward a `distrib` instance along a surjective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.has_distrib_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.non_unital_ring", "description": " Pullback a `non_unital_ring` instance along an injective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.non_assoc_semiring", "description": " Pushforward a `non_assoc_semiring` instance along a surjective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.has_distrib_neg", "description": " A type endowed with `-` and `*` has distributive negation, if it admits an injective map that\npreserves `-` and `*` to a type which has distributive negation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.comm_ring", "description": " Pullback a `comm_ring` instance along an injective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.non_unital_semiring", "description": " Pullback a `non_unital_semiring` instance along an injective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.ring", "description": " Pullback a `ring` instance along an injective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.comm_semiring", "description": " Pushforward a `semiring` instance along a surjective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.distrib", "description": " Pullback a `distrib` instance along an injective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.ring", "description": " Pushforward a `ring` instance along a surjective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.non_assoc_semiring", "description": " Pullback a `non_assoc_semiring` instance along an injective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.non_unital_ring", "description": " Pushforward a `non_unital_ring` instance along a surjective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.non_unital_non_assoc_ring", "description": " Pushforward a `non_unital_non_assoc_ring` instance along a surjective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.has_distrib_neg", "description": " A type endowed with `-` and `*` has distributive negation, if it admits a surjective map that\npreserves `-` and `*` from a type which has distributive negation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.semiring", "description": " Pushforward a `semiring` instance along a surjective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.non_assoc_ring", "description": " Pushforward a `non_unital_ring` instance along a surjective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.non_unital_comm_semiring", "description": " Pushforward a `non_unital_semiring` instance along a surjective function.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.normalize_iso_app", "description": "Auxiliary definition for `normalize_iso`. Here we construct the isomorphism between\n   `n \u2297 X` and `normalize X n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.inclusion_obj", "description": "Auxiliary definition for `inclusion`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.normalize", "description": "Our normalization procedure works by first defining a functor `F C \u2964 (N C \u2964 N C)` (which turns\n   out to be very easy), and then obtain a functor `F C \u2964 N C` by plugging in the normal object\n   `\ud835\udfd9_ C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.normal_monoidal_object", "description": "We say an object in the free monoidal category is in normal form if it is of the form\n   `(((\ud835\udfd9_ C) \u2297 X\u2081) \u2297 X\u2082) \u2297 \u22ef`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.normal_monoidal_object.unit", "description": "We say an object in the free monoidal category is in normal form if it is of the form\n   `(((\ud835\udfd9_ C) \u2297 X\u2081) \u2297 X\u2082) \u2297 \u22ef`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.normal_monoidal_object.tensor", "description": "We say an object in the free monoidal category is in normal form if it is of the form\n   `(((\ud835\udfd9_ C) \u2297 X\u2081) \u2297 X\u2082) \u2297 \u22ef`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.subsingleton_hom", "description": "The monoidal coherence theorem.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.discrete_functor_map_eq_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.normalize_map_aux", "description": "Auxiliary definition for `normalize`. Here we prove that objects that are related by\n   associators and unitors map to the same normal form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.discrete_functor_obj_eq_as", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.normalize_iso_aux", "description": "Auxiliary definition for `normalize_iso`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.tensor_func", "description": "Given an object `X` of the free monoidal category and an object `n` in normal form, taking\n   the tensor product `n \u2297 X` in the free monoidal category is functorial in both `X` and `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.normalize_iso_app_tensor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.full_normalize_iso", "description": "The isomorphism between an object and its normal form is natural.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.category_theory.groupoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.normalize'", "description": "A variant of the normalization functor where we consider the result as an object in the free\n   monoidal category (rather than an object of the discrete subcategory of objects in normal\n   form).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.normalize_obj_unitor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.full_normalize", "description": "The normalization functor for the free monoidal category over `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.inclusion", "description": "The discrete subcategory of objects in normal form includes into the free monoidal category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.normalize_obj_tensor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.tensor_func_obj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.normalize_iso", "description": "The isomorphism between `n \u2297 X` and `normalize X n` is natural (in both `X` and `n`, but\n   naturality in `n` is trivial and was \"proved\" in `normalize_iso_aux`). This is the real heart\n   of our proof of the coherence theorem.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.tensor_func_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.normalize_obj", "description": "Auxiliary definition for `normalize`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.normalize_iso_app_unitor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.free_monoidal_category.inverse_aux", "description": "Auxiliary construction for showing that the free monoidal category is a groupoid. Do not use\n   this, use `is_iso.inv` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.odd_card_odd_degree_vertices_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart_card_eq_twice_card_edges", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart_edge_fiber_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart.edge_fiber", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.exists_ne_odd_degree_of_exists_odd_degree", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.even_card_odd_degree_vertices", "description": "The handshaking lemma.  See also `simple_graph.sum_degrees_eq_twice_card_edges`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.sum_degrees_eq_twice_card_edges", "description": " The degree-sum formula.  This is also known as the handshaking lemma, which might\nmore specifically refer to `simple_graph.even_card_odd_degree_vertices`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart_fst_fiber_card_eq_degree", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart_fst_fiber", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dart_card_eq_sum_degrees", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_homothety_image_subset_of_finite_subset_interior", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_center_homothety", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_self_homothety", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nndist_center_homothety", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_line_map_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nndist_left_line_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_midpoint_midpoint_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_line_map_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_right_line_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nndist_midpoint_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_left_midpoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_line_map_line_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nndist_midpoint_midpoint_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_map.of_map_midpoint", "description": " A continuous map between two normed affine spaces is an affine map provided that\nit sends midpoints to midpoints.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nndist_midpoint_midpoint_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nndist_self_homothety", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_homothety_center", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nndist_line_map_line_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_right_midpoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_midpoint_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antilipschitz_with_line_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_subspace.is_closed_direction_iff", "des