081", "description": " corecursor where the state of the computation can be sent downstream\nin the form of a recursive call", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.iselect_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.approx.truncate", "description": "`truncate a` turns `a` into a more limited approximation", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.approx.path", "description": "`path F` provides indices to access internal nodes in `corec F`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.approx.P_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.dest", "description": "unfold an M-type", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.head'_eq_head", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.corec", "description": "Corecursor for the M-type defined by `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.is_bisimulation", "description": " Bisimulation is the standard proof technique for equality between\ninfinite tree-like structures", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.is_bisimulation.head", "description": " Bisimulation is the standard proof technique for equality between\ninfinite tree-like structures", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.is_bisimulation.tail", "description": " Bisimulation is the standard proof technique for equality between\ninfinite tree-like structures", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.head_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.cases_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.iselect_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.approx.agree_children", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.cases", "description": "destructor for M-types", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.ext'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.children", "description": "return all the subtrees of the root of a tree `x : M F`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.approx.agree", "description": " Relation between two approximations of the cofix of a pfunctor\nthat state they both contain the same data until one of them is truncated", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.approx.agree.continue", "description": " Relation between two approximations of the cofix of a pfunctor\nthat state they both contain the same data until one of them is truncated", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.approx.agree.intro", "description": " Relation between two approximations of the cofix of a pfunctor\nthat state they both contain the same data until one of them is truncated", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.cases_on'", "description": " destructor for M-types, similar to `cases_on` but also\ngives access directly to the root and subtrees on an M-type", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.is_path_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.agree'_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M", "description": "For polynomial functor `F`, `M F` is its final coalgebra", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.cases_on_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.isubtree", "description": " follow a path through a value of `M F` and return the subtree\nfound at the end of the path if it is a valid path for that value and\nreturn a default tree", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.head", "description": " given a tree generated by `F`, `head` gives us the first piece of data\nit contains", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.approx.cofix_a.default", "description": "default inhabitant of `cofix_a`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.is_path", "description": "`is_path p x` tells us if `p` is a valid path through `x`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.is_path.nil", "description": "`is_path p x` tells us if `p` is a valid path through `x`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.is_path.cons", "description": "`is_path p x` tells us if `p` is a valid path through `x`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.corec_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.agree'", "description": " `agree' n` relates two trees of type `M F` that\nare the same up to dept `n`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.agree'.trivial", "description": " `agree' n` relates two trees of type `M F` that\nare the same up to dept `n`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.agree'.step", "description": " `agree' n` relates two trees of type `M F` that\nare the same up to dept `n`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.eq_of_bisim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.approx.s_mk", "description": "generates the approximations needed for `M.mk`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.bisim'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.ichildren", "description": " select a subtree using a `i : F.Idx` or return an arbitrary tree if\n`i` designates no subtree of `x`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.corec_on", "description": "corecursor for `M F` with swapped arguments", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.truncate_approx", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.corec'", "description": " corecursor where it is possible to return a fully formed value at any point\nof the computation", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.corec_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.approx.all_agree", "description": "Given an infinite series of approximations `approx`,\n`all_agree approx` states that they are all consistent with each other.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.approx.cofix_a.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.iselect_eq_default", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.approx.approx_eta", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.approx.truncate_eq_of_agree", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.bisim_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.dest_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.approx.cofix_a", "description": "`cofix_a F n` is an `n` level approximation of a M-type", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.approx.cofix_a.continue", "description": "`cofix_a F n` is an `n` level approximation of a M-type", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.approx.cofix_a.intro", "description": "`cofix_a F n` is an `n` level approximation of a M-type", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.approx_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.agree_iff_agree'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.bisim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.is_path_cons'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.cases_on", "description": "destructor for M-types", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.approx.head'", "description": "The label of the root of the tree for a non-trivial\napproximation of the cofix of a pfunctor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.mk", "description": "constructor for M-types", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.approx.s_corec", "description": " `s_corec f i n` creates an approximation of height `n`\nof the final coalgebra of `f`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.mk_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.cases_on_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.nth_of_bisim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.approx.P_corec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.iselect", "description": " similar to `isubtree` but returns the data at the end of the path instead\nof the whole subtree", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.children_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.head_eq_head'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pfunctor.M.head_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.mem_find_carrier_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.find", "description": " Choice of an element of a nonempty chain of partial refinements. If `i` belongs to one of\n`carrier v`, `v \u2208 c`, then `find c ne i` is one of these partial refinements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.closure_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.apply_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.chain_Sup_carrier", "description": " The carrier of the least upper bound of a non-empty chain of partial refinements\nis the union of their carriers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.find_apply_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_subset_Union_closed_subset", "description": " Shrinking lemma. A point-finite open cover of a closed subset of a normal space can be \"shrunk\"\nto a new closed cover so that each new closed set is contained in the corresponding original open\nset. See also `exists_subset_Union_closure_subset` for a stronger statement.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_subset_Union_closure_subset", "description": " Shrinking lemma. A point-finite open cover of a closed subset of a normal space can be \"shrunk\"\nto a new open cover so that the closure of each new open set is contained in the corresponding\noriginal open set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.exists_gt", "description": " If `s` is a closed set, `v` is a partial refinement, and `i` is an index such that\n`i \u2209 v.carrier`, then there exists a partial refinement that is strictly greater than `v`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.le_chain_Sup", "description": "`chain_Sup hu c hc ne hfin hU` is an upper bound of the chain `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.subset_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement", "description": " Auxiliary definition for the proof of `shrinking_lemma`. A partial refinement of a covering\n`\u22c3 i, u i` of a set `s` is a map `v : \u03b9 \u2192 set X` and a set `carrier : set \u03b9` such that\n\n* `s \u2286 \u22c3 i, v i`;\n* all `v i` are open;\n* if `i \u2208 carrier v`, then `closure (v i) \u2286 u i`;\n* if `i \u2209 carrier`, then `v i = u i`.\n\nThis type is equipped with the folowing partial order: `v \u2264 v'` if `v.carrier \u2286 v'.carrier`\nand `v i = v' i` for `i \u2208 v.carrier`. We will use Zorn's lemma to prove that this type has\na maximal element, then show that the maximal element must have `carrier = univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.to_fun", "description": " Auxiliary definition for the proof of `shrinking_lemma`. A partial refinement of a covering\n`\u22c3 i, u i` of a set `s` is a map `v : \u03b9 \u2192 set X` and a set `carrier : set \u03b9` such that\n\n* `s \u2286 \u22c3 i, v i`;\n* all `v i` are open;\n* if `i \u2208 carrier v`, then `closure (v i) \u2286 u i`;\n* if `i \u2209 carrier`, then `v i = u i`.\n\nThis type is equipped with the folowing partial order: `v \u2264 v'` if `v.carrier \u2286 v'.carrier`\nand `v i = v' i` for `i \u2208 v.carrier`. We will use Zorn's lemma to prove that this type has\na maximal element, then show that the maximal element must have `carrier = univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.carrier", "description": " Auxiliary definition for the proof of `shrinking_lemma`. A partial refinement of a covering\n`\u22c3 i, u i` of a set `s` is a map `v : \u03b9 \u2192 set X` and a set `carrier : set \u03b9` such that\n\n* `s \u2286 \u22c3 i, v i`;\n* all `v i` are open;\n* if `i \u2208 carrier v`, then `closure (v i) \u2286 u i`;\n* if `i \u2209 carrier`, then `v i = u i`.\n\nThis type is equipped with the folowing partial order: `v \u2264 v'` if `v.carrier \u2286 v'.carrier`\nand `v i = v' i` for `i \u2208 v.carrier`. We will use Zorn's lemma to prove that this type has\na maximal element, then show that the maximal element must have `carrier = univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.is_open'", "description": " Auxiliary definition for the proof of `shrinking_lemma`. A partial refinement of a covering\n`\u22c3 i, u i` of a set `s` is a map `v : \u03b9 \u2192 set X` and a set `carrier : set \u03b9` such that\n\n* `s \u2286 \u22c3 i, v i`;\n* all `v i` are open;\n* if `i \u2208 carrier v`, then `closure (v i) \u2286 u i`;\n* if `i \u2209 carrier`, then `v i = u i`.\n\nThis type is equipped with the folowing partial order: `v \u2264 v'` if `v.carrier \u2286 v'.carrier`\nand `v i = v' i` for `i \u2208 v.carrier`. We will use Zorn's lemma to prove that this type has\na maximal element, then show that the maximal element must have `carrier = univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.subset_Union'", "description": " Auxiliary definition for the proof of `shrinking_lemma`. A partial refinement of a covering\n`\u22c3 i, u i` of a set `s` is a map `v : \u03b9 \u2192 set X` and a set `carrier : set \u03b9` such that\n\n* `s \u2286 \u22c3 i, v i`;\n* all `v i` are open;\n* if `i \u2208 carrier v`, then `closure (v i) \u2286 u i`;\n* if `i \u2209 carrier`, then `v i = u i`.\n\nThis type is equipped with the folowing partial order: `v \u2264 v'` if `v.carrier \u2286 v'.carrier`\nand `v i = v' i` for `i \u2208 v.carrier`. We will use Zorn's lemma to prove that this type has\na maximal element, then show that the maximal element must have `carrier = univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.closure_subset'", "description": " Auxiliary definition for the proof of `shrinking_lemma`. A partial refinement of a covering\n`\u22c3 i, u i` of a set `s` is a map `v : \u03b9 \u2192 set X` and a set `carrier : set \u03b9` such that\n\n* `s \u2286 \u22c3 i, v i`;\n* all `v i` are open;\n* if `i \u2208 carrier v`, then `closure (v i) \u2286 u i`;\n* if `i \u2209 carrier`, then `v i = u i`.\n\nThis type is equipped with the folowing partial order: `v \u2264 v'` if `v.carrier \u2286 v'.carrier`\nand `v i = v' i` for `i \u2208 v.carrier`. We will use Zorn's lemma to prove that this type has\na maximal element, then show that the maximal element must have `carrier = univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.apply_eq'", "description": " Auxiliary definition for the proof of `shrinking_lemma`. A partial refinement of a covering\n`\u22c3 i, u i` of a set `s` is a map `v : \u03b9 \u2192 set X` and a set `carrier : set \u03b9` such that\n\n* `s \u2286 \u22c3 i, v i`;\n* all `v i` are open;\n* if `i \u2208 carrier v`, then `closure (v i) \u2286 u i`;\n* if `i \u2209 carrier`, then `v i = u i`.\n\nThis type is equipped with the folowing partial order: `v \u2264 v'` if `v.carrier \u2286 v'.carrier`\nand `v i = v' i` for `i \u2208 v.carrier`. We will use Zorn's lemma to prove that this type has\na maximal element, then show that the maximal element must have `carrier = univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.apply_eq_of_chain", "description": " If two partial refinements `v\u2081`, `v\u2082` belong to a chain (hence, they are comparable)\nand `i` belongs to the carriers of both partial refinements, then `v\u2081 i = v\u2082 i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.find_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.is_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.chain_Sup", "description": "Least upper bound of a nonempty chain of partial refinements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_Union_eq_closure_subset", "description": " Shrinking lemma. A point-finite open cover of a closed subset of a normal space can be \"shrunk\"\nto a new open cover so that the closure of each new open set is contained in the corresponding\noriginal open set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_Union_eq_closed_subset", "description": " Shrinking lemma. A point-finite open cover of a closed subset of a normal space can be \"shrunk\"\nto a new closed cover so that each of the new closed sets is contained in the corresponding\noriginal open set. See also `exists_Union_eq_closure_subset` for a stronger statement.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "shrinking_lemma.partial_refinement.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect.closure_nhds_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "acc_pt.nhds_inter", "description": " If `x` is an accumulation point of a set `C` and `U` is a neighborhood of `x`,\nthen `x` is an accumulation point of `U \u2229 C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect.small_diam_splitting", "description": " A refinement of `perfect.splitting` for metric spaces, where we also control\nthe diameter of the new perfect sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "preperfect.open_inter", "description": "The intersection of a preperfect set and an open set is preperfect", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "preperfect.perfect_closure", "description": " The closure of a preperfect set is perfect.\nFor a converse, see `preperfect_iff_perfect_closure`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "preperfect", "description": " A set `C` is preperfect if all of its points are accumulation points of itself.\nIf `C` is nonempty and `\u03b1` is a T1 space, this is equivalent to the closure of `C` being perfect.\nSee `preperfect_iff_perfect_closure`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "preperfect_iff_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_perfect_nonempty_of_is_closed_of_not_countable", "description": "Any uncountable closed set in a second countable space contains a nonempty perfect subset.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect.splitting", "description": " Given a perfect nonempty set in a T2.5 space, we can find two disjoint perfect subsets\nThis is the main inductive step in the proof of the Cantor-Bendixson Theorem", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.exists_nat_bool_injection_of_not_countable", "description": " Any closed uncountable subset of a Polish space admits a continuous injection\nfrom the Cantor space `\u2115 \u2192 bool`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "preperfect_iff_perfect_closure", "description": "In a T1 space, being preperfect is equivalent to having perfect closure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_countable_union_perfect_of_is_closed", "description": " The **Cantor-Bendixson Theorem**: Any closed subset of a second countable space\ncan be written as the union of a countable set and a perfect set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect", "description": " A set `C` is called perfect if it is closed and all of its\npoints are accumulation points of itself.\nNote that we do not require `C` to be nonempty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect.closed", "description": " A set `C` is called perfect if it is closed and all of its\npoints are accumulation points of itself.\nNote that we do not require `C` to be nonempty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect.acc", "description": " A set `C` is called perfect if it is closed and all of its\npoints are accumulation points of itself.\nNote that we do not require `C` to be nonempty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "perfect.exists_nat_bool_injection", "description": " Any nonempty perfect set in a complete metric space admits a continuous injection\nfrom the cantor space, `\u2115 \u2192 bool`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.card_chunk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.edge_density_chunk_uniform", "description": " Lower bound on the edge densities between parts of `szemeredi_regularity.increment`. This is the\nblanket lower bound used the uniform parts.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.star_subset_chunk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.card_le_m_add_one_of_mem_chunk_parts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.chunk", "description": "The portion of `szemeredi_regularity.increment` which partitions `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.bUnion_star_subset_nonuniform_witness", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.edge_density_chunk_not_uniform", "description": "Lower bound on the edge densities between non-uniform parts of `szemeredi_regularity.increment`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.card_bUnion_star_le_m_add_one_card_star_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.m_le_card_of_mem_chunk_parts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.card_eq_of_mem_parts_chunk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "szemeredi_regularity.star", "description": " The portion of `szemeredi_regularity.chunk` which is contained in the witness of non uniformity\nof `U` and `V`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_of_isometry", "description": " Two `clifford_algebra`s are equivalent as algebras if their quadratic forms are\nequivalent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.\u03b9_mul_\u03b9_add_swap", "description": "The symmetric product of vectors is a scalar", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.\u03b9_mul_\u03b9_mul_\u03b9", "description": "$aba$ is a vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.map_apply_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.to_clifford_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.induction", "description": " If `C` holds for the `algebra_map` of `r : R` into `clifford_algebra Q`, the `\u03b9` of `x : M`,\nand is preserved under addition and muliplication, then it holds for all of `clifford_algebra Q`.\n\nSee also the stronger `clifford_algebra.left_induction` and `clifford_algebra.right_induction`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra", "description": "The Clifford algebra of an `R`-module `M` equipped with a quadratic_form `Q`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.hom_ext", "description": "See note [partially-applied ext lemmas].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.\u03b9_mul_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.lift_comp_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.\u03b9_comp_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_of_isometry_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.inv_of_\u03b9_mul_\u03b9_mul_\u03b9", "description": "$a^{-1}ba$ is a vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.map_comp_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.lift_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.\u03b9_sq_scalar", "description": "As well as being linear, `\u03b9 Q` squares to the quadratic form", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.\u03b9_mul_\u03b9_mul_inv_of_\u03b9", "description": "$aba^{-1}$ is a vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.invertible_\u03b9_of_invertible", "description": "If the quadratic form of a vector is invertible, then so is that vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.lift", "description": "Given a linear map `f : M \u2192\u2097[R] A` into an `R`-algebra `A`, which satisfies the condition:\n`cond : \u2200 m : M, f m * f m = Q(m)`, this is the canonical lift of `f` to a morphism of `R`-algebras\nfrom `clifford_algebra Q` to `A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.\u03b9_range_map_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.lift_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_of_isometry_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.\u03b9_range_map_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.to_clifford", "description": " The canonical image of the `tensor_algebra` in the `clifford_algebra`, which maps\n`tensor_algebra.\u03b9 R x` to `clifford_algebra.\u03b9 Q x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.map_comp_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_of_isometry_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.lift_\u03b9_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.is_unit_\u03b9_of_is_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.rel", "description": " `rel` relates each `\u03b9 m * \u03b9 m`, for `m : M`, with `Q m`.\n\nThe Clifford algebra of `M` is defined as the quotient modulo this relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.rel.of", "description": " `rel` relates each `\u03b9 m * \u03b9 m`, for `m : M`, with `Q m`.\n\nThe Clifford algebra of `M` is defined as the quotient modulo this relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.\u03b9", "description": "The canonical linear map `M \u2192\u2097[R] clifford_algebra Q`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.comp_\u03b9_sq_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.inv_of_\u03b9", "description": "For a vector with invertible quadratic form, $v^{-1} = \\frac{v}{Q(v)}$", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.map", "description": " Any linear map that preserves the quadratic form lifts to an `alg_hom` between algebras.\n\nSee `clifford_algebra.equiv_of_isometry` for the case when `f` is a `quadratic_form.isometry`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.equiv_of_isometry_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.cokernel_\u03c0_cokernel_iso_range_quotient_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.kernel_iso_ker_hom_ker_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.kernel_iso_ker_inv_kernel_\u03b9_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.has_cokernels_Module", "description": "The category or R-modules has cokernels, given by the projection onto the quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.kernel_cone", "description": "The kernel cone induced by the concrete kernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.kernel_iso_ker_hom_ker_subtype_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.kernel_iso_ker_inv_kernel_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.kernel_is_limit", "description": "The kernel of a linear map is a kernel in the categorical sense.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.cokernel_\u03c0_cokernel_iso_range_quotient_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.cokernel_is_colimit", "description": "The projection onto the quotient is a cokernel in the categorical sense.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.cokernel_\u03c0_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.has_kernels_Module", "description": "The category of R-modules has kernels, given by the inclusion of the kernel submodule.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.range_mkq_cokernel_iso_range_quotient_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.cokernel_iso_range_quotient", "description": "The categorical cokernel of a morphism in `Module`\nagrees with the usual module-theoretical quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.kernel_iso_ker", "description": "The categorical kernel of a morphism in `Module`\nagrees with the usual module-theoretical kernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.cokernel_cocone", "description": "The cokernel cocone induced by the projection onto the quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Module.range_mkq_cokernel_iso_range_quotient_inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym_insert_equiv", "description": "If `a` does not belong to the finset `s`, then the `n`th symmetric power of `{a} \u222a s` is\n in 1-1 correspondence with the disjoint union of the `n - i`th symmetric powers of `s`,\n for `0 \u2264 i \u2264 n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.eq_empty_of_sym_eq_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mk_mem_sym2_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym2_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image_diag_union_image_off_diag", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym2_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.not_is_diag_mk_of_mem_off_diag", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nonempty.sym", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mem_sym_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym_filter_ne_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym_eq_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym2_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym2", "description": "Lifts a finset to `sym2 \u03b1`. `s.sym2` is the finset of all pairs with elements in `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mem_sym2_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym_insert_equiv_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym2_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.diag_mem_sym2_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym", "description": " Lifts a finset to `sym \u03b1 n`. `s.sym n` is the finset of all unordered tuples of cardinality `n`\nwith elements in `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym_fill_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym_insert_equiv_apply_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym2_eq_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym2_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nonempty.sym2", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `finset.sym2_nonempty`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.replicate_mem_sym", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.is_diag_mk_of_mem_diag", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sym_insert_equiv_apply_snd_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with_lipschitz_const_mul_edist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_lipschitz_add.C", "description": "The Lipschitz constant of an `add_monoid` `\u03b2` satisfying `has_lipschitz_add`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.has_lipschitz_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with_lipschitz_const_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_lipschitz_mul", "description": " Class `has_lipschitz_mul M` says that the multiplication `(*) : X \u00d7 X \u2192 X` is Lipschitz jointly\nin the two arguments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_lipschitz_mul.lipschitz_mul", "description": " Class `has_lipschitz_mul M` says that the multiplication `(*) : X \u00d7 X \u2192 X` is Lipschitz jointly\nin the two arguments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.has_lipschitz_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_lipschitz_add", "description": " Class `has_lipschitz_add M` says that the addition `(+) : X \u00d7 X \u2192 X` is Lipschitz jointly in\nthe two arguments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_lipschitz_add.lipschitz_add", "description": " Class `has_lipschitz_add M` says that the addition `(+) : X \u00d7 X \u2192 X` is Lipschitz jointly in\nthe two arguments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_bounded_smul.has_continuous_smul", "description": " The typeclass `has_bounded_smul` on a metric-space scalar action implies continuity of the\naction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_lipschitz_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_lipschitz_add.has_continuous_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with_lipschitz_const_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.has_lipschitz_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnreal.has_lipschitz_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.has_lipschitz_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.has_lipschitz_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_bounded_smul.op", "description": "If a scalar is central, then its right action is bounded when its left action is.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_lipschitz_mul.C", "description": "The Lipschitz constant of a monoid `\u03b2` satisfying `has_lipschitz_mul`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnreal.has_bounded_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.has_bounded_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lipschitz_with_lipschitz_const_add_edist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_pair_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_lipschitz_mul.has_continuous_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_bounded_smul", "description": " Mixin typeclass on a scalar action of a metric space `\u03b1` on a metric space `\u03b2` both with\ndistinguished points `0`, requiring compatibility of the action in the sense that\n`dist (x \u2022 y\u2081) (x \u2022 y\u2082) \u2264 dist x 0 * dist y\u2081 y\u2082` and\n`dist (x\u2081 \u2022 y) (x\u2082 \u2022 y) \u2264 dist x\u2081 x\u2082 * dist y 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_bounded_smul.dist_smul_pair'", "description": " Mixin typeclass on a scalar action of a metric space `\u03b1` on a metric space `\u03b2` both with\ndistinguished points `0`, requiring compatibility of the action in the sense that\n`dist (x \u2022 y\u2081) (x \u2022 y\u2082) \u2264 dist x 0 * dist y\u2081 y\u2082` and\n`dist (x\u2081 \u2022 y) (x\u2082 \u2022 y) \u2264 dist x\u2081 x\u2082 * dist y 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_bounded_smul.dist_pair_smul'", "description": " Mixin typeclass on a scalar action of a metric space `\u03b1` on a metric space `\u03b2` both with\ndistinguished points `0`, requiring compatibility of the action in the sense that\n`dist (x \u2022 y\u2081) (x \u2022 y\u2082) \u2264 dist x 0 * dist y\u2081 y\u2082` and\n`dist (x\u2081 \u2022 y) (x\u2082 \u2022 y) \u2264 dist x\u2081 x\u2082 * dist y 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dist_smul_pair", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.has_lipschitz_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.has_lipschitz_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.has_lipschitz_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_add_le_iff_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.degree_sum_eq_of_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_add_coeff_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_pow_of_nat_degree_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_add_le_iff_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_add_eq_left_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_C_mul_eq_of_mul_ne_zero", "description": " Although not explicitly stated, the assumptions of lemma `nat_degree_C_mul_eq_of_mul_ne_zero`\nforce the polynomial `p` to be non-zero, via `p.leading_coeff \u2260 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_sub_le_iff_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_mul_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_mul_C_eq_of_mul_ne_zero", "description": " Although not explicitly stated, the assumptions of lemma `nat_degree_mul_C_eq_of_mul_ne_zero`\nforce the polynomial `p` to be non-zero, via `p.leading_coeff \u2260 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_pos_of_eval\u2082_root", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.degree_pos_of_eval\u2082_root", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.degree_pos_of_root", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_mul_C_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coe_lt_degree", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_C_mul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_comp_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.leading_coeff_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_bit1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.degree_mul_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_sub_le_iff_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_add_eq_right_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_C_mul_eq_of_mul_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_sub_eq_left_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_C_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.eq_nat_degree_of_le_mem_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_mul_of_nat_degree_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_sum_eq_of_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_bit0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.degree_C_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_lt_coeff_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_mul_C_eq_of_mul_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_le_iff_coeff_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_sub_eq_neg_right_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_iterate_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Kuratowski_embedding.embedding_of_subset", "description": " A metric space can be embedded in `l^\u221e(\u211d)` via the distances to points in\na fixed countable set, if this set is dense. This map is given in `Kuratowski_embedding`,\nwithout density assumptions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Kuratowski_embedding.exists_isometric_embedding", "description": "Every separable metric space embeds isometrically in `\u2113_infty_\u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonempty_compacts.Kuratowski_embedding", "description": "Version of the Kuratowski embedding for nonempty compacts", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Kuratowski_embedding.embedding_of_subset_dist_le", "description": "The embedding map is always a semi-contraction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Kuratowski_embedding.embedding_of_subset_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Kuratowski_embedding.embedding_of_subset_isometry", "description": "When the reference set is dense, the embedding map is an isometry on its image.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Kuratowski_embedding", "description": "The Kuratowski embedding is an isometric embedding of a separable metric space in `\u2113^\u221e(\u211d)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Kuratowski_embedding.isometry", "description": "The Kuratowski embedding is an isometry.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.angle.exp_map_circle_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.angle.exp_map_circle_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.angle.exp_map_circle_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle.injective_arg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.angle.exp_map_circle_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle.arg_local_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle.arg_equiv_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.angle.coe_exp_map_circle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle.arg_local_equiv_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "surj_on_exp_map_circle_neg_pi_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle.arg_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle.arg_eq_arg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exp_map_circle_eq_exp_map_circle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exp_map_circle_two_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exp_map_circle_sub_two_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.angle.arg_exp_map_circle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "arg_exp_map_circle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_on_arg_exp_map_circle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle.arg_local_equiv", "description": " `complex.arg \u2218 coe` and `exp_map_circle` define a local equivalence between `circle and `\u211d` with\n`source = set.univ` and `target = set.Ioc (-\u03c0) \u03c0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle.arg_equiv", "description": "`complex.arg` and `exp_map_circle` define an equivalence between `circle and `(-\u03c0, \u03c0]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.angle.exp_map_circle", "description": "`exp_map_circle`, applied to a `real.angle`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle.arg_local_equiv_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle.arg_local_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "periodic_exp_map_circle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exp_map_circle_add_two_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_inverse_exp_map_circle_arg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exp_map_circle_arg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.via_embedding_apply_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.via_embedding_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.via_embedding_hom", "description": "`via_embedding` as a group homomorphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.via_embedding_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.via_embedding_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.via_embedding", "description": "Noncomputable version of `equiv.perm.via_fintype_embedding` that does not assume `fintype`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.atom", "description": "Represent a `csring_expr.atom` in Horner form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.of_csexpr", "description": "Brings expressions into Horner normal form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.cseval_atom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tree.get_or_zero", "description": " Returns an element indexed by `n`, or zero if `n` isn't a valid index.\nSee `tree.get`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.cseval_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.cseval_add_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.to_string", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.tactic.ring2", "description": " `ring2` solves equations in the language of rings.\n\nIt supports only the commutative semiring operations, i.e. it does not normalize subtraction or\ndivision.\n\n  This variant on the `ring` tactic uses kernel computation instead\n  of proof generation. In general, you should use `ring` instead of `ring2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.cseval_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.mul_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.has_to_string", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conv.interactive.ring2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.cseval_mul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.cseval_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.csring_expr.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.correctness", "description": " The main proof-by-reflection theorem. Given reflected csring expressions\n`r\u2081` and `r\u2082` plus a storage `t` of atoms, if both expressions go to the\nsame Horner normal form, then the original non-reflected expressions are\nequal. `H` follows from kernel reduction and is therefore `rfl`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.is_cs", "description": " True iff the `horner_expr` argument is a valid `csring_expr`.\nFor that to be the case, all its constants must be non-negative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.cseval", "description": "Evaluates a reflected `horner_expr` - see `csring_expr.eval`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.csring_expr.has_reflect", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.csring_expr", "description": " A reflected/meta representation of an expression in a commutative\nsemiring. This representation is a direct translation of such\nexpressions - see `horner_expr` for a normal form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.csring_expr.atom", "description": " A reflected/meta representation of an expression in a commutative\nsemiring. This representation is a direct translation of such\nexpressions - see `horner_expr` for a normal form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.csring_expr.const", "description": " A reflected/meta representation of an expression in a commutative\nsemiring. This representation is a direct translation of such\nexpressions - see `horner_expr` for a normal form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.csring_expr.add", "description": " A reflected/meta representation of an expression in a commutative\nsemiring. This representation is a direct translation of such\nexpressions - see `horner_expr` for a normal form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.csring_expr.mul", "description": " A reflected/meta representation of an expression in a commutative\nsemiring. This representation is a direct translation of such\nexpressions - see `horner_expr` for a normal form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.csring_expr.pow", "description": " A reflected/meta representation of an expression in a commutative\nsemiring. This representation is a direct translation of such\nexpressions - see `horner_expr` for a normal form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.cseval_horner'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.add_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.ring2", "description": " `ring2` solves equations in the language of rings.\n\nIt supports only the commutative semiring operations, i.e. it does not normalize subtraction or\ndivision.\n\n  This variant on the `ring` tactic uses kernel computation instead\n  of proof generation. In general, you should use `ring` instead of `ring2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.reflect_expr", "description": " Reflects a csring expression into a `csring_expr`, together\nwith a dlist of atoms, i.e. opaque variables over which the\nexpression is a polynomial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.horner'", "description": " Alternative constructor for (horner a x n b) which maintains canonical\nform by simplifying special cases of `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.csring_expr.eval", "description": " Evaluates a reflected `csring_expr` into an element of the\noriginal `comm_semiring` type `\u03b1`, retrieving opaque elements\n(atoms) from the tree `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tree.reflect'", "description": " `(reflect' t u \u03b1)` quasiquotes a tree `(t: tree expr)` of quoted\nvalues of type `\u03b1` at level `u` into an `expr` which reifies to a `tree \u03b1`\ncontaining the reifications of the `expr`s from the original `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.has_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.cseval_of_csexpr", "description": " For any given tree `t` of atoms and any reflected expression `r`,\nthe Horner form of `r` is a valid csring expression, and under `t`,\nthe Horner form evaluates to the same thing as `r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.add_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.mul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.csring_expr.replace", "description": " In the output of `reflect_expr`, `atom`s are initialized with incorrect indices.\nThe indices cannot be computed until the whole tree is built, so another pass over\nthe expressions is needed - this is what `replace` does. The computation (expressed\nin the state monad) fixes up `atom`s to match their positions in the atom tree.\nThe initial state is a list of all atom occurrences in the goal, left-to-right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr", "description": " An efficient representation of expressions in a commutative\nsemiring using the sparse Horner normal form. This type admits\nnon-optimal instantiations (e.g. `P` can be represented as `P+0+0`),\nso to get good performance out of it, care must be taken to maintain\nan optimal, *canonical* form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.const", "description": " An efficient representation of expressions in a commutative\nsemiring using the sparse Horner normal form. This type admits\nnon-optimal instantiations (e.g. `P` can be represented as `P+0+0`),\nso to get good performance out of it, care must be taken to maintain\nan optimal, *canonical* form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.ring2.horner_expr.horner", "description": " An efficient representation of expressions in a commutative\nsemiring using the sparse Horner normal form. This type admits\nnon-optimal instantiations (e.g. `P` can be represented as `P+0+0`),\nso to get good performance out of it, care must be taken to maintain\nan optimal, *canonical* form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_snd_fst_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.diagonal_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_iso_inv_snd_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_iso_inv_snd_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_iso", "description": "This iso witnesses the fact that\ngiven `f : X \u27f6 Y`, `i : U \u27f6 Y`, and `i\u2081 : V\u2081 \u27f6 X \u00d7[Y] U`, `i\u2082 : V\u2082 \u27f6 X \u00d7[Y] U`, the diagram\n\nV\u2081 \u00d7[X \u00d7[Y] U] V\u2082 \u27f6 V\u2081 \u00d7[U] V\u2082\n        |                 |\n        |                 |\n        \u2193                 \u2193\n        X         \u27f6  X \u00d7[Y] X\n\nis a pullback square.\nAlso see `pullback_fst_map_snd_is_pullback`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.diagonal.category_theory.is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_id_iso_hom_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_id_iso_inv_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_id_iso_inv_snd_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagonal_obj_pullback_fst_iso", "description": "The diagonal object of `X \u00d7[Z] Y \u27f6 X` is isomorphic to `\u0394_{Y/Z} \u00d7[Z] X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagonal_obj_pullback_fst_iso_hom_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_lift_map_is_pullback", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagonal_obj_pullback_fst_iso_inv_fst_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.diagonal_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.diagonal", "description": "The diagonal morphism `X \u27f6 \u0394_{X/Y}` for a morphism `f : X \u27f6 Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.fst.category_theory.is_split_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_fst_map_snd_is_pullback", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagonal_pullback_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagonal_obj_pullback_fst_iso_inv_snd_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_iso_inv_snd_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_id_iso_hom_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_iso_hom_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_iso_hom_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_iso_inv_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_fst_fst_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.diagonal_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_snd_snd_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagonal_obj_pullback_fst_iso_hom_fst_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagonal_obj_pullback_fst_iso_inv_fst_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagonal_obj_pullback_fst_iso_inv_snd_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_id_iso", "description": "This iso witnesses the fact that\ngiven `f : X \u27f6 T`, `g : Y \u27f6 T`, and `i : T \u27f6 S`, the diagram\n\nX \u00d7\u209c Y \u27f6 X \u00d7\u209b Y\n   |         |\n   |         |\n   \u2193         \u2193\n   T   \u27f6 T \u00d7\u209b T\n\nis a pullback square.\nAlso see `pullback_map_diagonal_is_pullback`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_id_iso_inv_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_map_eq_pullback_fst_fst_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_fst_fst_iso", "description": "Given the following diagram with `S \u27f6 S'` a monomorphism,\n\n    X  \u27f6 X'\n      \u2198      \u2198\n        S  \u27f6 S'\n      \u2197      \u2197\n    Y  \u27f6 Y'\n\nThis iso witnesses the fact that\n\n      X \u00d7[S] Y \u27f6 (X' \u00d7[S'] Y') \u00d7[Y'] Y\n          |                  |\n          |                  |\n          \u2193                  \u2193\n(X' \u00d7[S'] Y') \u00d7[X'] X \u27f6 X' \u00d7[S'] Y'\n\nis a pullback square. The diagonal map of this square is `pullback.map`.\nAlso see `pullback_lift_map_is_pullback`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.snd.category_theory.is_split_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_fst_fst_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_id_iso_inv_snd_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_snd_snd_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagonal_obj_pullback_fst_iso_inv_fst_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.diagonal_obj", "description": "The diagonal object of a morphism `f : X \u27f6 Y` is `\u0394_{X/Y} := pullback f f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagonal_obj_pullback_fst_iso_hom_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagonal_obj_pullback_fst_iso_hom_fst_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagonal_obj_pullback_fst_iso_hom_fst_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.diagonal.category_theory.is_split_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagonal_obj_pullback_fst_iso_hom_fst_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_iso_hom_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagonal_obj_pullback_fst_iso_inv_snd_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.diagonal_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.diagonal_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_iso_inv_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_id_iso_inv_snd_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_id_iso_hom_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagonal_obj_pullback_fst_iso_inv_fst_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_id_iso_inv_snd_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_iso_hom_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_iso_inv_snd_snd_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_id_iso_hom_fst_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_map_diagonal_is_pullback", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.diagonal_obj_pullback_fst_iso_inv_snd_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback_diagonal_map_snd_fst_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.pullback.diagonal_is_kernel_pair", "description": "The two projections `\u0394_{X/Y} \u27f6 X` form a kernel pair for `f : X \u27f6 Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exten