ption": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.swap_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept", "description": " The formal concepts of a relation. A concept of `r : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 Prop` is a pair of sets `s`, `t`\nsuch that `s` is the set of all elements that are `r`-related to all of `t` and `t` is the set of\nall elements that are `r`-related to all of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.to_prod", "description": " The formal concepts of a relation. A concept of `r : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 Prop` is a pair of sets `s`, `t`\nsuch that `s` is the set of all elements that are `r`-related to all of `t` and `t` is the set of\nall elements that are `r`-related to all of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.closure_fst", "description": " The formal concepts of a relation. A concept of `r : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 Prop` is a pair of sets `s`, `t`\nsuch that `s` is the set of all elements that are `r`-related to all of `t` and `t` is the set of\nall elements that are `r`-related to all of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.closure_snd", "description": " The formal concepts of a relation. A concept of `r : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 Prop` is a pair of sets `s`, `t`\nsuch that `s` is the set of all elements that are `r`-related to all of `t` and `t` is the set of\nall elements that are `r`-related to all of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.ext'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "intent_closure_extent_closure_intent_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "extent_closure_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.Inf_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.has_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.top_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "intent_closure_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.semilattice_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.sup_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_extent_closure_intent_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.bounded_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.strict_anti_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.fst_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gc_intent_closure_extent_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.sup_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.fst_subset_fst_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "intent_closure_Union\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "intent_closure_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "intent_closure_anti", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "extent_closure_anti", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.swap_equiv", "description": "The dual of a concept lattice is isomorphic to the concept lattice of the dual context.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "intent_closure_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.snd_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.top_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.swap_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "extent_closure", "description": " The extent closure of `t : set \u03b2` along a relation `r : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 Prop` is the set of all elements\nwhich `r` relates to all elements of `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.swap_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.fst_ssubset_fst_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concept.swap_le_swap_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "extent_closure_Union\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.has_limits.limit_cone_is_limit", "description": "Witness that the limit cone in `Algebra R` is a limit cone.\n(Internal use only; use the limits API.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.forget\u2082_Ring_preserves_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.forget\u2082_Module_preserves_limits_of_size", "description": "The forgetful functor from R-algebras to R-modules preserves all limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.limit_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.limit_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.has_limits.limit_cone", "description": "Construction of a limit cone in `Algebra R`.\n(Internal use only; use the limits API.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.limit_\u03c0_alg_hom", "description": "`limit.\u03c0 (F \u22d9 forget (Algebra R)) j` as a `alg_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.semiring_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.has_limits_of_size", "description": "The category of R-algebras has all limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.forget_preserves_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.algebra_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.sections_subalgebra", "description": "The flat sections of a functor into `Algebra R` form a submodule of all sections.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.forget_preserves_limits_of_size", "description": "The forgetful functor from R-algebras to types preserves all limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.forget\u2082_Ring_preserves_limits_of_size", "description": "The forgetful functor from R-algebras to rings preserves all limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.forget\u2082_Module_preserves_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Algebra.has_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_counit", "description": "The counit of a monoidal equivalence can be upgraded to a monoidal natural transformation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_iso.of_components", "description": "Construct a monoidal natural isomorphism from object level isomorphisms,\nand the monoidal naturality in the forward direction.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.tensor_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.category_monoidal_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.unit_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_counit_to_nat_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.comp_to_nat_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_unit", "description": "The unit of a monoidal equivalence can be upgraded to a monoidal natural transformation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.prod", "description": "The cartesian product of two monoidal natural transformations is monoidal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_unit.is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.comp_to_nat_trans_lax", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_iso.is_iso_of_is_iso_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_iso.of_components.inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.id_to_nat_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.hcomp_to_nat_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.vcomp_to_nat_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_unit_to_nat_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.hcomp", "description": "Horizontal composition of monoidal natural transformations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.vcomp", "description": "Vertical composition of monoidal natural transformations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.prod_to_nat_trans_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.id", "description": "The identity monoidal natural transformation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans", "description": "A monoidal natural transformation is a natural transformation between (lax) monoidal functors\nadditionally satisfying:\n`F.\u03bc X Y \u226b app (X \u2297 Y) = (app X \u2297 app Y) \u226b G.\u03bc X Y`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.to_nat_trans", "description": "A monoidal natural transformation is a natural transformation between (lax) monoidal functors\nadditionally satisfying:\n`F.\u03bc X Y \u226b app (X \u2297 Y) = (app X \u2297 app Y) \u226b G.\u03bc X Y`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.unit'", "description": "A monoidal natural transformation is a natural transformation between (lax) monoidal functors\nadditionally satisfying:\n`F.\u03bc X Y \u226b app (X \u2297 Y) = (app X \u2297 app Y) \u226b G.\u03bc X Y`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.tensor'", "description": "A monoidal natural transformation is a natural transformation between (lax) monoidal functors\nadditionally satisfying:\n`F.\u03bc X Y \u226b app (X \u2297 Y) = (app X \u2297 app Y) \u226b G.\u03bc X Y`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.category_lax_monoidal_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_nat_trans.tenso