oeff", "description": " `coeff x` is the additive group homomorphism `free_abelian_group X \u2192+ \u2124`\nthat sends `a` to the multiplicity of `x : X` in `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.equiv.of_is_free_group_equiv", "description": "Isomorphic free groups have equivalent bases (`is_free_group` variant`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.to_free_abelian_group_comp_to_finsupp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.equiv.of_free_abelian_group_equiv", "description": "Isomorphic free abelian groups (as additive groups) have equivalent bases.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.to_free_abelian_group", "description": "The group homomorphism `(X \u2192\u2080 \u2124) \u2192+ free_abelian_group X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.support_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.equiv.of_free_group_equiv", "description": "Isomorphic free groups have equivalent bases.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.support_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.to_free_abelian_group_comp_single_add_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.to_finsupp_comp_to_free_abelian_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.eq_nat_abs_iff_mul_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.nat_abs_lt_iff_mul_self_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.eq_zero_of_abs_lt_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.nat_abs_le_iff_mul_self_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.nat_abs_eq_iff_mul_self_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.dvd_div_of_mul_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.le_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.lt_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.sum_two_pow_lt_iff_lt", "description": "For subsets of \u2115, we can show that colex is equivalent to binary.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.singleton_le_iff_le", "description": "Colex is an extension of the base ordering on \u03b1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.colex_lt_of_ssubset", "description": " If `A \u2282 B`, then `A` is less than `B` in the colex order. Note the converse does not hold, as\n`\u2286` is not a linear order.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.hom_le_iff", "description": "Strictly monotone functions preserve the colex ordering.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.has_lt.lt.is_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.colex.has_le", "description": "We can define (\u2264) in the obvious way.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.hom_fin_lt_iff", "description": "A special case of `colex.hom_lt_iff` which is sometimes useful.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.finset.colex.bounded_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.forall_lt_of_colex_lt_of_forall_lt", "description": "If `A` is before `B` in colex, and everything in `B` is small, then everything in `A` is small.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.to_colex_rel_hom", "description": "The function from finsets to finsets with the colex order is a relation homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.colex.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.empty_to_colex_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.finset.colex.lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.sum_two_pow_lt", "description": "If everything in `A` is less than `k`, we can bound the sum of powers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.empty_to_colex_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.sum_two_pow_le_iff_lt", "description": "For subsets of \u2115, we can show that colex is equivalent to binary.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.lt_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.has_lt.lt.is_trichotomous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.decidable_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.colex", "description": "We define this type synonym to refer to the colexicographic ordering on finsets\nrather than the natural subset ordering.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.hom_fin_le_iff", "description": "A special case of `colex_hom` which is sometimes useful.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.lt_singleton_iff_mem_lt", "description": "`s.to_colex < {r}.to_colex` iff all elements of `s` are less than `r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.singleton_lt_iff_lt", "description": "Colex is an extension of the base ordering on \u03b1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.to_colex", "description": "A convenience constructor to turn a `finset \u03b1` into a `finset.colex \u03b1`, useful in order to\nuse the colex ordering rather than the subset ordering.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.finset.colex.order_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.to_colex_rel_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.colex.has_lt", "description": "`A` is less than `B` in the colex ordering if the largest thing that's not in both sets is in B.\nIn other words, `max (A \u2206 B) \u2208 B` (if the maximum exists).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.sdiff_lt_sdiff_iff_lt", "description": "Colex doesn't care if you remove the other set", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.sdiff_le_sdiff_iff_le", "description": "Colex doesn't care if you remove the other set", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.mem_le_of_singleton_le", "description": "If {r} is less than or equal to s in the colexicographical sense,\n then s contains an element greater than or equal to r.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.finset.colex.order_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.colex_le_of_subset", "description": " If `A \u2286 B`, then `A \u2264 B` in the colex order. Note the converse does not hold, as `\u2286` is not a\nlinear order.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.hom_lt_iff", "description": "Strictly monotone functions preserve the colex ordering.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.lt_trichotomy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.has_lt.lt.is_irrefl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.le_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "colex.finset.colex.linear_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imo1962_q4.formula", "description": " Someday, when there is a Grobner basis tactic, try to automate this proof. (A little tricky --\nthe ideals are not the same but their Jacobson radicals are.)", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q4.finding_zeros", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q4.solve_cos2_half", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q4.alt_formula", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q4.problem_equation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q4.cos_sum_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q4'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q4.alt_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q4.solve_cos3x_0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q4.solution_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q4.solve_cos2x_0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1962_q4", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "primorial_le_4_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "primorial_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "primorial", "description": "The primorial `n#` of `n` is the product of the primes less than or equal to `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "primorial_add_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "primorial_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "primorial_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "primorial_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.range_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.add_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.erase", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.filter_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.count_eq_one_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup", "description": "`nodup s` means that `s` has no duplicates, i.e. the multiplicity of\n any element is at most 1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.of_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.count_eq_of_nodup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup_decidable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.not_mem_erase", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup_iff_pairwise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup_iff_count_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.map_eq_map_of_bij_of_nodup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup_iff_ne_cons_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.le_iff_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup_iff_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.not_nodup_pair", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.coe_nodup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.inter_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.erase_eq_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.of_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.pmap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.sigma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.product", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.disjoint_of_nodup_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup_map_iff_inj_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.pairwise.forall", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup_attach", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.inj_on_of_nodup_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.pairwise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.map_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.mem_erase_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.mem_sub_of_nodup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.nodup.inter_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.sum_to_partition_of_unity_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate_of_locally_finite", "description": " If `X` is a normal topological space and `U i`, `i : \u03b9`, is a locally finite open covering of a\nclosed set `s`, then there exists a `bump_covering \u03b9 X s` that is subordinate to `U`. If `X` is a\nparacompact space, then the assumption `hf : locally_finite U` can be omitted, see\n`bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.exists_is_subordinate_of_locally_finite", "description": " If `X` is a normal topological space and `U` is a locally finite open covering of a closed set\n`s`, then there exists a `partition_of_unity \u03b9 X s` that is subordinate to `U`. If `X` is a\nparacompact space, then the assumption `hf : locally_finite U` can be omitted, see\n`bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.locally_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.sum_to_pou_fun_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.exists_pos", "description": " If `f` is a partition of unity on `s`, then for every `x \u2208 s` there exists an index `i` such\nthat `0 < f i x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate", "description": " If `X` is a paracompact normal topological space and `U` is an open covering of a closed set\n`s`, then there exists a `bump_covering \u03b9 X s` that is subordinate to `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.support_to_partition_of_unity_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.to_partition_of_unity_eq_mul_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.is_subordinate", "description": " A partition of unity `f i` is subordinate to a family of sets `U i` indexed by the same type if\nfor each `i` the closure of the support of `f i` is a subset of `U i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.exists_finset_to_pou_fun_eventually_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.eventually_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.is_subordinate.to_partition_of_unity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.to_pou_fun", "description": " Partition of unity defined by a `bump_covering`. We use this auxiliary definition to prove some\nproperties of the new family of functions before bundling it into a `partition_of_unity`. Do not use\nthis definition, use `bump_function.to_partition_of_unity` instead.\n\nThe partition of unity is given by the formula `g i x = f i x * \u220f\u1da0 j < i, (1 - f j x)`. In other\nwords, `g i x = \u220f\u1da0 j < i, (1 - f j x) - \u220f\u1da0 j \u2264 i, (1 - f j x)`, so\n`\u2211\u1da0 i, g i x = 1 - \u220f\u1da0 j, (1 - f j x)`. If `x \u2208 s`, then one of `f j x` equals one, hence the product\nof `1 - f j x` vanishes, and `\u2211\u1da0 i, g i x = 1`.\n\nIn order to avoid an assumption `linear_order \u03b9`, we use `well_ordering_rel` instead of `(<)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.to_pou_fun_eq_mul_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.sum_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.exists_is_subordinate", "description": " If `X` is a paracompact normal topological space and `U` is an open covering of a closed set\n`s`, then there exists a `partition_of_unity \u03b9 X s` that is subordinate to `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.to_partition_of_unity_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.is_subordinate", "description": " A collection of bump functions `f i` is subordinate to a family of sets `U i` indexed by the\nsame type if for each `i` the closure of the support of `f i` is a subset of `U i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.point_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering", "description": " A `bump_covering \u03b9 X s` is an indexed family of functions `f i`, `i : \u03b9`, such that\n\n* the supports of `f i` form a locally finite family of sets, i.e., for every point `x : X` there\n  exists a neighborhood `U \u220b x` such that all but finitely many functions `f i` are zero on `U`;\n* for all `i`, `x` we have `0 \u2264 f i x \u2264 1`;\n* each point `x \u2208 s` belongs to the interior of `{x | f i x = 1}` for some `i`.\n\nOne of the main use cases for a `bump_covering` is to define a `partition_of_unity`, see\n`bump_covering.to_partition_of_unity`, but some proofs can directly use a `bump_covering` instead of\na `partition_of_unity`.\n\nIf `X` is a normal paracompact space, then `bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate` guarantees that for\nevery open covering `U : set (set X)` of `s` there exists a `bump_covering` of `s` that is\nsubordinate to `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.to_fun", "description": " A `bump_covering \u03b9 X s` is an indexed family of functions `f i`, `i : \u03b9`, such that\n\n* the supports of `f i` form a locally finite family of sets, i.e., for every point `x : X` there\n  exists a neighborhood `U \u220b x` such that all but finitely many functions `f i` are zero on `U`;\n* for all `i`, `x` we have `0 \u2264 f i x \u2264 1`;\n* each point `x \u2208 s` belongs to the interior of `{x | f i x = 1}` for some `i`.\n\nOne of the main use cases for a `bump_covering` is to define a `partition_of_unity`, see\n`bump_covering.to_partition_of_unity`, but some proofs can directly use a `bump_covering` instead of\na `partition_of_unity`.\n\nIf `X` is a normal paracompact space, then `bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate` guarantees that for\nevery open covering `U : set (set X)` of `s` there exists a `bump_covering` of `s` that is\nsubordinate to `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.locally_finite'", "description": " A `bump_covering \u03b9 X s` is an indexed family of functions `f i`, `i : \u03b9`, such that\n\n* the supports of `f i` form a locally finite family of sets, i.e., for every point `x : X` there\n  exists a neighborhood `U \u220b x` such that all but finitely many functions `f i` are zero on `U`;\n* for all `i`, `x` we have `0 \u2264 f i x \u2264 1`;\n* each point `x \u2208 s` belongs to the interior of `{x | f i x = 1}` for some `i`.\n\nOne of the main use cases for a `bump_covering` is to define a `partition_of_unity`, see\n`bump_covering.to_partition_of_unity`, but some proofs can directly use a `bump_covering` instead of\na `partition_of_unity`.\n\nIf `X` is a normal paracompact space, then `bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate` guarantees that for\nevery open covering `U : set (set X)` of `s` there exists a `bump_covering` of `s` that is\nsubordinate to `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.nonneg'", "description": " A `bump_covering \u03b9 X s` is an indexed family of functions `f i`, `i : \u03b9`, such that\n\n* the supports of `f i` form a locally finite family of sets, i.e., for every point `x : X` there\n  exists a neighborhood `U \u220b x` such that all but finitely many functions `f i` are zero on `U`;\n* for all `i`, `x` we have `0 \u2264 f i x \u2264 1`;\n* each point `x \u2208 s` belongs to the interior of `{x | f i x = 1}` for some `i`.\n\nOne of the main use cases for a `bump_covering` is to define a `partition_of_unity`, see\n`bump_covering.to_partition_of_unity`, but some proofs can directly use a `bump_covering` instead of\na `partition_of_unity`.\n\nIf `X` is a normal paracompact space, then `bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate` guarantees that for\nevery open covering `U : set (set X)` of `s` there exists a `bump_covering` of `s` that is\nsubordinate to `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.le_one'", "description": " A `bump_covering \u03b9 X s` is an indexed family of functions `f i`, `i : \u03b9`, such that\n\n* the supports of `f i` form a locally finite family of sets, i.e., for every point `x : X` there\n  exists a neighborhood `U \u220b x` such that all but finitely many functions `f i` are zero on `U`;\n* for all `i`, `x` we have `0 \u2264 f i x \u2264 1`;\n* each point `x \u2208 s` belongs to the interior of `{x | f i x = 1}` for some `i`.\n\nOne of the main use cases for a `bump_covering` is to define a `partition_of_unity`, see\n`bump_covering.to_partition_of_unity`, but some proofs can directly use a `bump_covering` instead of\na `partition_of_unity`.\n\nIf `X` is a normal paracompact space, then `bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate` guarantees that for\nevery open covering `U : set (set X)` of `s` there exists a `bump_covering` of `s` that is\nsubordinate to `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.eventually_eq_one'", "description": " A `bump_covering \u03b9 X s` is an indexed family of functions `f i`, `i : \u03b9`, such that\n\n* the supports of `f i` form a locally finite family of sets, i.e., for every point `x : X` there\n  exists a neighborhood `U \u220b x` such that all but finitely many functions `f i` are zero on `U`;\n* for all `i`, `x` we have `0 \u2264 f i x \u2264 1`;\n* each point `x \u2208 s` belongs to the interior of `{x | f i x = 1}` for some `i`.\n\nOne of the main use cases for a `bump_covering` is to define a `partition_of_unity`, see\n`bump_covering.to_partition_of_unity`, but some proofs can directly use a `bump_covering` instead of\na `partition_of_unity`.\n\nIf `X` is a normal paracompact space, then `bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate` guarantees that for\nevery open covering `U : set (set X)` of `s` there exists a `bump_covering` of `s` that is\nsubordinate to `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.locally_finite_tsupport", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity", "description": " A continuous partition of unity on a set `s : set X` is a collection of continuous functions\n`f i` such that\n\n* the supports of `f i` form a locally finite family of sets, i.e., for every point `x : X` there\n  exists a neighborhood `U \u220b x` such that all but finitely many functions `f i` are zero on `U`;\n* the functions `f i` are nonnegative;\n* the sum `\u2211\u1da0 i, f i x` is equal to one for every `x \u2208 s` and is less than or equal to one\n  otherwise.\n\nIf `X` is a normal paracompact space, then `partition_of_unity.exists_is_subordinate` guarantees\nthat for every open covering `U : set (set X)` of `s` there exists a partition of unity that is\nsubordinate to `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.to_fun", "description": " A continuous partition of unity on a set `s : set X` is a collection of continuous functions\n`f i` such that\n\n* the supports of `f i` form a locally finite family of sets, i.e., for every point `x : X` there\n  exists a neighborhood `U \u220b x` such that all but finitely many functions `f i` are zero on `U`;\n* the functions `f i` are nonnegative;\n* the sum `\u2211\u1da0 i, f i x` is equal to one for every `x \u2208 s` and is less than or equal to one\n  otherwise.\n\nIf `X` is a normal paracompact space, then `partition_of_unity.exists_is_subordinate` guarantees\nthat for every open covering `U : set (set X)` of `s` there exists a partition of unity that is\nsubordinate to `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.locally_finite'", "description": " A continuous partition of unity on a set `s : set X` is a collection of continuous functions\n`f i` such that\n\n* the supports of `f i` form a locally finite family of sets, i.e., for every point `x : X` there\n  exists a neighborhood `U \u220b x` such that all but finitely many functions `f i` are zero on `U`;\n* the functions `f i` are nonnegative;\n* the sum `\u2211\u1da0 i, f i x` is equal to one for every `x \u2208 s` and is less than or equal to one\n  otherwise.\n\nIf `X` is a normal paracompact space, then `partition_of_unity.exists_is_subordinate` guarantees\nthat for every open covering `U : set (set X)` of `s` there exists a partition of unity that is\nsubordinate to `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.nonneg'", "description": " A continuous partition of unity on a set `s : set X` is a collection of continuous functions\n`f i` such that\n\n* the supports of `f i` form a locally finite family of sets, i.e., for every point `x : X` there\n  exists a neighborhood `U \u220b x` such that all but finitely many functions `f i` are zero on `U`;\n* the functions `f i` are nonnegative;\n* the sum `\u2211\u1da0 i, f i x` is equal to one for every `x \u2208 s` and is less than or equal to one\n  otherwise.\n\nIf `X` is a normal paracompact space, then `partition_of_unity.exists_is_subordinate` guarantees\nthat for every open covering `U : set (set X)` of `s` there exists a partition of unity that is\nsubordinate to `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.sum_eq_one'", "description": " A continuous partition of unity on a set `s : set X` is a collection of continuous functions\n`f i` such that\n\n* the supports of `f i` form a locally finite family of sets, i.e., for every point `x : X` there\n  exists a neighborhood `U \u220b x` such that all but finitely many functions `f i` are zero on `U`;\n* the functions `f i` are nonnegative;\n* the sum `\u2211\u1da0 i, f i x` is equal to one for every `x \u2208 s` and is less than or equal to one\n  otherwise.\n\nIf `X` is a normal paracompact space, then `partition_of_unity.exists_is_subordinate` guarantees\nthat for every open covering `U : set (set X)` of `s` there exists a partition of unity that is\nsubordinate to `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.sum_le_one'", "description": " A continuous partition of unity on a set `s : set X` is a collection of continuous functions\n`f i` such that\n\n* the supports of `f i` form a locally finite family of sets, i.e., for every point `x : X` there\n  exists a neighborhood `U \u220b x` such that all but finitely many functions `f i` are zero on `U`;\n* the functions `f i` are nonnegative;\n* the sum `\u2211\u1da0 i, f i x` is equal to one for every `x \u2208 s` and is less than or equal to one\n  otherwise.\n\nIf `X` is a normal paracompact space, then `partition_of_unity.exists_is_subordinate` guarantees\nthat for every open covering `U : set (set X)` of `s` there exists a partition of unity that is\nsubordinate to `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate_of_locally_finite_of_prop", "description": " If `X` is a normal topological space and `U i`, `i : \u03b9`, is a locally finite open covering of a\nclosed set `s`, then there exists a `bump_covering \u03b9 X s` that is subordinate to `U`. If `X` is a\nparacompact space, then the assumption `hf : locally_finite U` can be omitted, see\n`bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate`. This version assumes that `p : (X \u2192 \u211d) \u2192 Prop` is a predicate\nthat satisfies Urysohn's lemma, and provides a `bump_covering` such that each function of the\ncovering satisfies `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.to_partition_of_unity", "description": " The partition of unity defined by a `bump_covering`.\n\nThe partition of unity is given by the formula `g i x = f i x * \u220f\u1da0 j < i, (1 - f j x)`. In other\nwords, `g i x = \u220f\u1da0 j < i, (1 - f j x) - \u220f\u1da0 j \u2264 i, (1 - f j x)`, so\n`\u2211\u1da0 i, g i x = 1 - \u220f\u1da0 j, (1 - f j x)`. If `x \u2208 s`, then one of `f j x` equals one, hence the product\nof `1 - f j x` vanishes, and `\u2211\u1da0 i, g i x = 1`.\n\nIn order to avoid an assumption `linear_order \u03b9`, we use `well_ordering_rel` instead of `(<)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.continuous_to_pou_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.single", "description": " A `bump_covering` that consists of a single function, uniformly equal to one, defined as an\nexample for `inhabited` instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.locally_finite_tsupport", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.continuous_smul", "description": " If `f` is a partition of unity on `s : set X` and `g : X \u2192 E` is continuous at every point of\nthe topological support of some `f i`, then `\u03bb x, f i x \u2022 g x` is continuous on the whole space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.ind_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.exists_finset_nhd_support_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.coe_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.ind", "description": "Index of a bump function such that `fs i =\u1da0[\ud835\udcdd x] 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.is_subordinate.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.to_partition_of_unity_zero_of_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.locally_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.sum_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.support_to_pou_fun_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.continuous_finsum_smul", "description": " If `f` is a partition of unity on a set `s : set X` and `g : \u03b9 \u2192 X \u2192 E` is a family of functions\nsuch that each `g i` is continuous at every point of the topological support of `f i`, then the sum\n`\u03bb x, \u2211\u1da0 i, f i x \u2022 g i x` is continuous on the whole space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.exists_is_subordinate_of_prop", "description": " If `X` is a paracompact normal topological space and `U` is an open covering of a closed set\n`s`, then there exists a `bump_covering \u03b9 X s` that is subordinate to `U`. This version assumes that\n`p : (X \u2192 \u211d) \u2192 Prop` is a predicate that satisfies Urysohn's lemma, and provides a\n`bump_covering` such that each function of the covering satisfies `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.is_subordinate.continuous_finsum_smul", "description": " If `f` is a partition of unity that is subordinate to a family of open sets `U i` and\n`g : \u03b9 \u2192 X \u2192 E` is a family of functions such that each `g i` is continuous on `U i`, then the sum\n`\u03bb x, \u2211\u1da0 i, f i x \u2022 g i x` is a continuous function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.sum_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.to_pou_fun_zero_of_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partition_of_unity.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bump_covering.exists_finset_to_partition_of_unity_eventually_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_map.comp", "description": "The composition of smooth maps, as a smooth map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_map.coe_fn_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_map.cont_mdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_map.coe_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_map.id", "description": "The identity as a smooth map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_map.fst", "description": "The first projection of a product, as a smooth map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_map.prod_mk", "description": "Given two smooth maps `f` and `g`, this is the smooth map `x \u21a6 (f x, g x)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.has_coe_to_cont_mdiff_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_map.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_map.snd", "description": "The second projection of a product, as a smooth map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_map.continuous_map.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_map.smooth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_map.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_map.const", "description": "Constant map as a smooth map", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_map.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_map", "description": "Bundled `n` times continuously differentiable maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_map.continuous_map_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_mdiff_map.fun_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smooth_map", "description": "Bundled smooth maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable.iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_within_at.iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at.iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.comp", "description": "The chain rule for derivatives in the sense of strict differentiability.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_within_at.iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_at.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at_filter.iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at.iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at.comp", "description": "The chain rule.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at_filter.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fderiv.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fderiv_within_fderiv_within", "description": "A version of `fderiv_within.comp` that is useful to rewrite the composition of two derivatives\n into a single derivative. This version always applies, but creates a new side-goal `f x = y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_within_at.comp_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_at.comp_differentiable_within_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable.comp_differentiable_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fderiv_within.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_on.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fderiv.comp_fderiv_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_within_at.comp'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fderiv_within.comp\u2083", "description": "Ternary version of `fderiv_within.comp`, with equality assumptions of basepoints added, in\n order to apply more easily as a rewrite from right-to-left.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_on.iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at.comp_has_fderiv_within_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_within_at.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_within_at.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_at.iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.hyperplane_separation", "description": " This is a relative version of\n`convex_cone.hyperplane_separation_of_nonempty_of_is_closed_of_nmem`, which we recover by setting\n`f` to be the identity map. This is a geometric interpretation of the Farkas' lemma\nstated using proper cones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.is_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.mem_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.comap_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.map", "description": " The closure of image of a proper cone under a continuous `\u211d`-linear map is a proper cone. We\nuse continuous maps here so that the comap of f is also a map between proper cones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.mem_dual", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.coe_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.coe_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.pointed_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.mem_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.closure_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone", "description": " A proper cone is a convex cone `K` that is nonempty and closed. Proper cones have the nice\nproperty that the dual of the dual of a proper cone is itself. This makes them useful for defining\ncone programs and proving duality theorems.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.to_convex_cone", "description": " A proper cone is a convex cone `K` that is nonempty and closed. Proper cones have the nice\nproperty that the dual of the dual of a proper cone is itself. This makes them useful for defining\ncone programs and proving duality theorems.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.nonempty'", "description": " A proper cone is a convex cone `K` that is nonempty and closed. Proper cones have the nice\nproperty that the dual of the dual of a proper cone is itself. This makes them useful for defining\ncone programs and proving duality theorems.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.is_closed'", "description": " A proper cone is a convex cone `K` that is nonempty and closed. Proper cones have the nice\nproperty that the dual of the dual of a proper cone is itself. This makes them useful for defining\ncone programs and proving duality theorems.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.dual", "description": "The inner dual cone of a proper cone is a proper cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.hyperplane_separation_of_nmem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.mem_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.coe_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.pointed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.set_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.comap_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.to_convex_cone_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.mem_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.coe_dual", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.mem_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.convex_cone.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.ext'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_cone.closure", "description": " The closure of a convex cone inside a topological space as a convex cone. This\nconstruction is mainly used for defining maps between proper cones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.dual_dual", "description": "The dual of the dual of a proper cone is itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "proper_cone.comap", "description": "The preimage of a proper cone under a continuous `\u211d`-linear map is a proper cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_principal.mem_iff_generator_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "irreducible.coprime_or_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_coprime_of_prime_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_principal_ideal_ring", "description": "A ring is a principal ideal ring if all (left) ideals are principal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_principal_ideal_ring.principal", "description": "A ring is a principal ideal ring if all (left) ideals are principal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bot_is_principal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_ideal_ring.ne_zero_of_mem_factors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_principal", "description": "An `R`-submodule of `M` is principal if it is generated by one element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_principal.principal", "description": "An `R`-submodule of `M` is principal if it is generated by one element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_ideal_ring.irreducible_iff_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_ideal_ring.is_maximal_of_irreducible", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_ideal_ring.associates_irreducible_iff_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_principal.generator_submodule_image_dvd_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gcd_dvd_iff_exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_principal.span_singleton_generator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_principals_zorn", "description": " Any chain in the set of non-principal ideals has an upper bound which is non-principal.\n(Namely, the union of the chain is such an upper bound.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_principal.generator_map_dvd_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_ideal_ring.ring_hom_mem_submonoid_of_factors_subset_of_units_subset", "description": " If a `ring_hom` maps all units and all factors of an element `a` into a submonoid `s`, then it\nalso maps `a` into that submonoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_coprime_of_irreducible_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "top_is_principal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "irreducible.coprime_pow_of_not_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_principal.eq_bot_iff_generator_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dvd_or_coprime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_principal_ideal_ring_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_field.is_principal_ideal_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_principal_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_principal.generator", "description": "`generator I`, if `I` is a principal submodule, is an `x \u2208 M` such that `span R {x} = I`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_principal_ideal_ring.of_prime", "description": "If all prime ideals in a commutative ring are principal, so are all other ideals.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "irreducible.dvd_iff_not_coprime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_ideal_ring.to_unique_factorization_monoid", "description": "A principal ideal domain has unique factorization", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_principal.of_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_ring.is_principal_ideal_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gcd_is_unit_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_principals", "description": "`non_principals R` is the set of all ideals of `R` that are not principal ideals.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prime.coprime_iff_not_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_prime.to_maximal_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_principal_ideal_ring.of_surjective", "description": "The surjective image of a principal ideal ring is again a principal ideal ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_coprime_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_domain.to_principal_ideal_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_singleton_generator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_ideal_ring.factors", "description": "`factors a` is a multiset of irreducible elements whose product is `a`, up to units", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_gcd_eq_mul_add_mul", "description": "**B\u00e9zout's lemma**", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_principal.prime_generator_of_is_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_principals_eq_empty_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "span_gcd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_ideal_ring.is_noetherian_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_associated_pow_of_mul_eq_pow'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_principal.of_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "irreducible.coprime_iff_not_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mod_mem_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_ideal_ring.mem_submonoid_of_factors_subset_of_units_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_principal.mem_iff_eq_smul_generator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_principal.generator_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_ideal_ring.factors_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_principals_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.higher_faces_vanish.comp_H\u03c3_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.higher_faces_vanish.comp_\u03b4_eq_zero_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.higher_faces_vanish.of_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.higher_faces_vanish.of_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.higher_faces_vanish.induction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.higher_faces_vanish.comp_H\u03c3_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.higher_faces_vanish.comp_\u03b4_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_topology.dold_kan.higher_faces_vanish", "description": " A morphism `\u03c6 : Y \u27f6 X _[n+1]` satisfies `higher_faces_vanish q \u03c6`\nwhen the compositions `\u03c6 \u226b X.\u03b4 j` are `0` for `j \u2265 max 1 (n+2-q)`. When `q \u2264 n+1`,\nit basically means that the composition `\u03c6 \u226b X.\u03b4 j` are `0` for the `q` highest\npossible values of a nonzero `j`. Otherwise, when `q \u2265 n+2`, all the compositions\n`\u03c6 \u226b X.\u03b4 j` for nonzero `j` vanish. See also the lemma `comp_P_eq_self_iff` in\n`projections.lean` which states that `higher_faces_vanish q \u03c6` is equivalent to\nthe identity `\u03c6 \u226b (P q).f (n+1) = \u03c6`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.exists_ne", "description": " An injective function from a nontrivial type has an argument at\nwhich it does not take a given value.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nontrivial_iff_exists_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_pair_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nontrivial_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nontrivial_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nontrivial_psum_unique", "description": "An inhabited type is either nontrivial, or has a unique element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nontrivial_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nontrivial_iff_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "false_of_nontrivial_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nontrivial_prod_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "decidable.exists_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsingleton.le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtype.nontrivial_iff_exists_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nontrivial.to_nonempty", "description": "See Note [lower instance priority]\n\nNote that since this and `nonempty_of_inhabited` are the most \"obvious\" way to find a nonempty\ninstance if no direct instance can be found, we give this a higher priority than the usual `100`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_pair_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "option.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.nontrivial_at", "description": "A pi type is nontrivial if it's nonempty everywhere and nontrivial somewhere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sort.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bool.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_nontrivial_iff_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nontrivial_prod_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.nontrivial", "description": "Pushforward a `nontrivial` instance along an injective function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nontrivial", "description": " Predicate typeclass for expressing that a type is not reduced to a single element. In rings,\nthis is equivalent to `0 \u2260 1`. In vector spaces, this is equivalent to positive dimension.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nontrivial.exists_pair_ne", "description": " Predicate typeclass for expressing that a type is not reduced to a single element. In rings,\nthis is equivalent to `0 \u2260 1`. In vector spaces, this is equivalent to positive dimension.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsingleton_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsingleton_or_nontrivial", "description": "A type is either a subsingleton or nontrivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.nontrivial", "description": "Pullback a `nontrivial` instance along a surjective function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.nontrivial", "description": "As a convenience, provide an instance automatically if `(f default)` is nontrivial.\n\nIf a different index has the non-trivial type, then use `haveI := nontrivial_at that_index`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.char_p_iff_char_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_pow_char", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.char_is_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sub_pow_char", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.map_iterate_frobenius", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p_of_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.neg_one_pow_char_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frobenius_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frobenius_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.of_char_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.iterate_map_frobenius", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.add_pow_prime_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_pow_char_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.int_cast_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_pow_prime_pow_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.exists_add_pow_prime_pow_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sub_pow_char_of_commute", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.add_order_of_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.eq_self_iff_eq_zero_of_char_ne_two", "description": "Characteristic `\u2260 2` in a domain implies that `-a = a` iff `a = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frobenius_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sub_pow_char_pow_of_commute", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.cast_eq_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_add_pow_prime_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.ring_char_ne_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.map_frobenius", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.char_is_prime_of_two_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sub_pow_char_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.ring_char_ne_zero_of_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_inj_on_of_ring_char_ne_two", "description": " If two integers from `{0, 1, -1}` result in equal elements in a ring `R`\nthat is nontrivial and of characteristic not `2`, then they are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum_pow_char", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.add_pow_prime_pow_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p_of_prime_pow_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.neg_one_ne_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.exists_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_pow_char_pow_of_commute", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterate_frobenius", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.char_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_char.eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.map_frobenius", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_char.nat.cast_ring_char", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_pow_prime_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frobenius_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne_zero.of_not_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.two_ne_zero", "description": "We have `2 \u2260 0` in a nontrivial ring whose characteristic is not `2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.char_ne_zero_of_finite", "description": "The characteristic of a finite ring cannot be zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.nontrivial_of_char_ne_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_char.char_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_char.of_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_pow_char_of_commute", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.pow_prime_pow_mul_eq_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_char.dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.iterate_map_frobenius", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.exists_add_pow_prime_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.char_p", "description": "The characteristic of the product of two rings of the same characteristic\n is the same as the characteristic of the rings", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frobenius", "description": "The frobenius map that sends x to x^p", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_char.eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frobenius_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frobenius_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.char_ne_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p", "description": " The generator of the kernel of the unique homomorphism \u2115 \u2192 R for a semiring R.\n\n*Warning*: for a semiring `R`, `char_p R 0` and `char_zero R` need not coincide.\n* `char_p R 0` asks that only `0 : \u2115` maps to `0 : R` under the map `\u2115 \u2192 R`;\n* `char_zero R` requires an injection `\u2115 \u21aa R`.\n\nFor instance, endowing `{0, 1}` with addition given by `max` (i.e. `1` is absorbing), shows that\n`char_zero {0, 1}` does not hold and yet `char_p {0, 1} 0` does.\nThis example is formalized in `counterexamples/char_p_zero_ne_char_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.cast_eq_zero_iff", "description": " The generator of the kernel of the unique homomorphism \u2115 \u2192 R for a semiring R.\n\n*Warning*: for a semiring `R`, `char_p R 0` and `char_zero R` need not coincide.\n* `char_p R 0` asks that only `0 : \u2115` maps to `0 : R` under the map `\u2115 \u2192 R`;\n* `char_zero R` requires an injection `\u2115 \u21aa R`.\n\nFor instance, endowing `{0, 1}` with addition given by `max` (i.e. `1` is absorbing), shows that\n`char_zero {0, 1}` does not hold and yet `char_p {0, 1} 0` does.\nThis example is formalized in `counterexamples/char_p_zero_ne_char_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_char.spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frobenius_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.nat_cast_eq_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.neg_one_pow_char", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.map_iterate_frobenius", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.false_of_nontrivial_of_char_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.char_p_to_char_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.ring_char_of_prime_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_char", "description": "Noncomputable function that outputs the unique characteristic of a semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne_zero.not_char_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_square_of_char_two'", "description": " If `ring_char R = 2`, where `R` is a finite reduced commutative ring,\nthen every `a : R` is a square.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.int_cast_eq_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset_sum_pow_char", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.cast_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.char_is_prime_or_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list_sum_pow_char", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.lcm.char_p", "description": " The characteristic of the product of rings is the least common multiple of the\ncharacteristics of the two rings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frobenius_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.neg_one_ne_one_of_char_ne_two", "description": "Characteristic `\u2260 2` and nontrivial implies that `-1 \u2260 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.char_is_prime_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ulift.char_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frobenius_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_add_pow_prime_pow_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.cast_card_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_char.eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_scalar_tower.invertible_algebra_coe_nat", "description": " A natural number that is invertible when coerced to `R` is also invertible\nwhen coerced to any `R`-algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.coe_algebra_map_coeffs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.smul", "description": " `basis.smul (b : basis \u03b9 R S) (c : basis \u03b9 S A)` is the `R`-basis on `A`\nwhere the `(i, j)`th basis vector is `b i \u2022 c j`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.extend_scalars", "description": "Extend the scalars of an `alg_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.algebra_map_coeffs_repr_apply_support_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.smul_repr_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_scalar_tower.invertible.algebra_tower", "description": " Suppose that `R -> S -> A` is a tower of algebras.\nIf an element `r : R` is invertible in `S`, then it is invertible in `A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.algebra_map_coeffs_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.algebra_map_coeffs", "description": " If `R` and `A` have a bijective `algebra_map R A` and act identically on `M`,\nthen a basis for `M` as `R`-module is also a basis for `M` as `R'`-module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.smul_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom_equiv_sigma", "description": "`alg_hom`s from the top of a tower are equivalent to a pair of `alg_hom`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.algebra_map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_independent_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.algebra_map_coeffs_repr_apply_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.algebra_map_coeffs_repr_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.restrict_domain", "description": "Restrict the domain of an `alg_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.measure_ball_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_Ioi_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.eq_empty_of_measure_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.measure_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.measure_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_Iio_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.measure_closed_ball_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.is_open_pos_measure", "description": "A measure is said to be `is_open_pos_measure` if it is positive on nonempty open sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.is_open_pos_measure.open_pos", "description": "A measure is said to be `is_open_pos_measure` if it is positive on nonempty open sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.measure_ball_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.measure_pos_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.eq_on_Icc_of_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.is_open_pos_measure_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.absolutely_continuous.is_open_pos_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.measure_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_pos_of_nonempty_interior", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.eq_on_of_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_pos_of_mem_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.interior_eq_empty_of_null", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_Ioo_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.ae_eq_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.eq_on_Ioo_of_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.eq_on_Ioc_of_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_le.le.is_open_pos_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.measure_Ioo_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.eq_of_ae_eq", "description": "If two continuous functions are a.e. equal, then they are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "emetric.measure_closed_ball_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.eq_on_Ico_of_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.eq_on_open_of_ae_eq", "description": " If two functions are a.e. equal on an open set and are continuous on this set, then they are\nequal on this set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_seq_compact.is_compact", "description": "If `\ud835\udce4 \u03b2` is countably generated, then any sequentially compact set is compact.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient.sequential_space", "description": "The quotient of a sequential space is a sequential space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "seq_closure", "description": " The sequential closure of a set `s : set X` in a topological space `X` is the set of all `a : X`\nwhich arise as limit of sequences in `s`. Note that the sequential closure of a set is not\nguaranteed to be sequentially closed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_seq_compact.totally_bounded", "description": "A sequentially compact set in a uniform space is totally bounded.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_seq_closed_iff", "description": "A set is sequentially closed iff it is equal to its sequential closure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.seq_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_seq_closed_iff_is_closed", "description": "In a sequential space, a set is closed iff it's sequentially closed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frechet_urysohn_space", "description": " A topological space is called a *Fr\u00e9chet-Urysohn space*, if the sequential closure of any set\nis equal to its closure. Since one of the inclusions is trivial, we require only the non-trivial one\nin the definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frechet_urysohn_space.closure_subset_seq_closure", "description": " A topological space is called a *Fr\u00e9chet-Urysohn space*, if the sequential closure of any set\nis equal to its closure. Since one of the inclusions is trivial, we require only the non-trivial one\nin the definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_map.sequential_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_subseq_of_bounded", "description": " A version of Bolzano-Weistrass: in a proper metric space (eg. $\u211d^n$),\nevery bounded sequence has a converging subsequence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_seq_compact.exists_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "compact_space.tendsto_subseq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.is_compact_iff_is_seq_compact", "description": " A version of Bolzano-Weistrass: in a uniform space with countably generated uniformity filter\n(e.g., in a metric space), a set is compact if and only if it is sequentially compact.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.is_seq_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "seq_closure_eq_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.is_seq_closed", "description": "A set is sequentially closed if it is closed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frechet_urysohn_space.to_sequential_space", "description": "Every Fr\u00e9chet-Urysohn space is a sequential space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_seq_compact", "description": " A set `s` is sequentially compact if every sequence taking values in `s` has a\nconverging subsequence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.tendsto_subseq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "seq_compact_space", "description": " A space `X` is sequentially compact if every sequence in `X` has a\nconverging subsequence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "seq_compact_space.seq_compact_univ", "description": " A space `X` is sequentially compact if every sequence in `X` has a\nconverging subsequence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_nhds_iff_seq_tendsto", "description": " If the domain of a function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is a Fr\u00e9chet-Urysohn space, then convergence\nis equivalent to sequential convergence. See also `filter.tendsto_iff_seq_tendsto` for a version\nthat works for any pair of filters assuming that the filter in the domain is countably generated.\n\nThis property is equivalent to the definition of `frechet_urysohn_space`, see\n`frechet_urysohn_space.of_seq_tendsto_imp_tendsto`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_seq_closed.is_closed", "description": "In a sequential space, a sequentially closed set is closed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subset_seq_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "seq_compact_space.tendsto_subseq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_seq_closed.seq_closure_eq", "description": "The sequential closure of a sequentially closed set is the set itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "seq_closure_subset_closure", "description": " The sequential closure of a set is contained in the closure of that set.\nThe converse is not true.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sequential_space", "description": " A topological space is said to be a *sequential space* if any sequentially closed set in this\nspace is closed. This condition is weaker than being a Fr\u00e9chet-Urysohn space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sequential_space.is_closed_of_seq", "description": " A topological space is said to be a *sequential space* if any sequentially closed set in this\nspace is closed. This condition is weaker than being a Fr\u00e9chet-Urysohn space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_iff_seq_continuous", "description": " If the domain of a function is a sequential space, then continuity of this function is\nequivalent to its sequential continuity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_seq_closed", "description": " A set `s` is sequentially closed if for any converging sequence `x n` of elements of `s`, the\nlimit belongs to `s` as well. Note that the sequential closure of a set is not guaranteed to be\nsequentially closed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "seq_compact.lebesgue_number_lemma_of_metric", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.first_countable_topology.frechet_urysohn_space", "description": "Every first-countable space is a Fr\u00e9chet-Urysohn space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_seq_closed_of_seq_closure_eq", "description": "If a set is equal to its sequential closure, then it is sequentially closed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space.compact_space_iff_seq_compact_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_seq_compact.exists_tendsto_of_frequently_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_seq_closed.preimage", "description": " The preimage of a sequentially closed set under a sequentially continuous map is sequentially\nclosed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frechet_urysohn_space.of_seq_tendsto_imp_tendsto", "description": " An alternative construction for `frechet_urysohn_space`: if sequential convergence implies\nconvergence, then the space is a Fr\u00e9chet-Urysohn space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "seq_continuous", "description": "A function between topological spaces is sequentially continuous if it commutes with limit of\nconvergent sequences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_seq_compact.subseq_of_frequently_in", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_subseq_of_frequently_bounded", "description": " A version of **Bolzano-Weistrass**: in a proper metric space (eg. $\u211d^n$),\nevery bounded sequence has a converging subsequence. This version assumes only\nthat the sequence is frequently in some bounded set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.tendsto_subseq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_countable_topology.seq_compact_of_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_closure_iff_seq_limit", "description": " In a Fr\u00e9chet-Urysohn space, a point belongs to the closure of a set iff it is a limit\nof a sequence taking values in this set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "seq_continuous.continuous", "description": "A sequentially continuous function defined on a sequential space is continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "seq_compact_space_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_seq_compact.is_complete", "description": " A sequentially compact set in a uniform set with countably generated uniformity filter\nis complete.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covariants.to_unique_prods", "description": "  This instance asserts that if `A` has a multiplication, a linear order, and multiplication\nis 'very monotone', then `A` also has `unique_prods`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_prods", "description": "  Let `G` be a Type with multiplication.  `unique_prods G` asserts that any two non-empty\nfinite subsets of `G` have the `unique_mul` property, with respect to some element of their\nproduct `A * B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_prods.unique_mul_of_nonempty", "description": "  Let `G` be a Type with multiplication.  `unique_prods G` asserts that any two non-empty\nfinite subsets of `G` have the `unique_mul` property, with respect to some element of their\nproduct `A * B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_sums", "description": "  Let `G` be a Type with addition.  `unique_sums G` asserts that any two non-empty\nfinite subsets of `A` have the `unique_add` property, with respect to some element of their\nsum `A + B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_sums.unique_add_of_nonempty", "description": "  Let `G` be a Type with addition.  `unique_sums G` asserts that any two non-empty\nfinite subsets of `A` have the `unique_add` property, with respect to some element of their\nsum `A + B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covariants.to_unique_sums", "description": "This instance asserts that if `A` has an addition, a linear order, and addition\nis 'very monotone', then `A` also has `unique_sums`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_mul.mul_hom_map_iff", "description": "  `unique_mul` is preserved under embeddings that are multiplicative.\n\nSee `unique_mul.mul_hom_image_iff` for a version with swapped bundling.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.unique_sums", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_and_eq_of_le_of_le_of_mul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_mul.mul_hom_image_iff", "description": "  `unique_mul` is preserved under multiplicative maps that are injective.\n\nSee `unique_mul.mul_hom_map_iff` for a version with swapped bundling.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_add.exists_iff_exists_exists_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_add.set_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_mul.mul_hom_preimage", "description": "`unique_mul` is preserved by inverse images under injective, multiplicative maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_add.iff_exists_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_add.add_hom_preimage", "description": "`unique_add` is preserved by inverse images under injective, additive maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_mul.set_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_mul.mt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_add.add_hom_map_iff", "description": "`unique_add` is preserved under embeddings that are additive.\n\nSee `unique_add.add_hom_image_iff` for a version with swapped bundling.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_add.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_and_eq_of_le_of_le_of_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_mul", "description": "  Let `G` be a Type with multiplication, let `A B : finset G` be finite subsets and\nlet `a0 b0 : G` be two elements.  `unique_mul A B a0 b0` asserts `a0 * b0` can be written in at\nmost one way as a product of an element of `A` and an element of `B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_mul.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.unique_prods", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_mul.iff_exists_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_add", "description": "Let `G` be a Type with addition, let `A B : finset G` be finite subsets and\nlet `a0 b0 : G` be two elements.  `unique_add A B a0 b0` asserts `a0 + b0` can be written in at\nmost one way as a sum of an element from `A` and an element from `B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_add.add_hom_image_iff", "description": "`unique_add` is preserved under additive maps that are injective.\n\nSee `unique_add.add_hom_map_iff` for a version with swapped bundling.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_mul.exists_iff_exists_exists_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.mul_compl_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.subtype.has_sdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.coe_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.coe_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.subtype.has_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.coe_sdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection", "description": "A projection on a normed space `X` is said to be an L-projection if, for all `x` in `X`,\n$\\|x\\| = \\|P x\\| + \\|(1 - P) x\\|$.\n\nNote that we write `P \u2022 x` instead of `P x` for reasons described in the module docstring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.proj", "description": "A projection on a normed space `X` is said to be an L-projection if, for all `x` in `X`,\n$\\|x\\| = \\|P x\\| + \\|(1 - P) x\\|$.\n\nNote that we write `P \u2022 x` instead of `P x` for reasons described in the module docstring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.Lnorm", "description": "A projection on a normed space `X` is said to be an L-projection if, for all `x` in `X`,\n$\\|x\\| = \\|P x\\| + \\|(1 - P) x\\|$.\n\nNote that we write `P \u2022 x` instead of `P x` for reasons described in the module docstring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.subtype.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.Lcomplement", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.compl_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.subtype.boolean_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.subtype.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.subtype.has_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.le_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.coe_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.subtype.distrib_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.Lcomplement_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.subtype.partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.subtype.has_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.subtype.bounded_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.coe_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.distrib_lattice_lemma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Mprojection", "description": "A projection on a normed space `X` is said to be an M-projection if, for all `x` in `X`,\n$\\|x\\| = max(\\|P x\\|,\\|(1 - P) x\\|)$.\n\nNote that we write `P \u2022 x` instead of `P x` for reasons described in the module docstring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Mprojection.proj", "description": "A projection on a normed space `X` is said to be an M-projection if, for all `x` in `X`,\n$\\|x\\| = max(\\|P x\\|,\\|(1 - P) x\\|)$.\n\nNote that we write `P \u2022 x` instead of `P x` for reasons described in the module docstring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Mprojection.Mnorm", "description": "A projection on a normed space `X` is said to be an M-projection if, for all `x` in `X`,\n$\\|x\\| = max(\\|P x\\|,\\|(1 - P) x\\|)$.\n\nNote that we write `P \u2022 x` instead of `P x` for reasons described in the module docstring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.commute", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_Lprojection.coe_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.to_ordered_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.mul_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_add_mul_le_mul_add_mul'", "description": "Binary **rearrangement inequality**.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_add_mul_lt_mul_add_mul", "description": "Binary strict **rearrangement inequality**.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_add_mul_le_mul_add_mul", "description": "Binary **rearrangement inequality**.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.add", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.add_assoc", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.zero", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.zero_add", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.add_zero", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.nsmul", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.nsmul_zero'", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.nsmul_succ'", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.add_comm", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.le", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.lt", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.le_refl", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.le_trans", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.lt_iff_le_not_le", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.le_antisymm", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.add_le_add_left", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.bot", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.bot_le", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.exists_add_of_le", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.le_self_add", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, c