is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.npow", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.npow_zero'", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.npow_succ'", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.mul_comm", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.eq_zero_or_eq_zero_of_mul_eq_zero", "description": " A canonically ordered commutative semiring is an ordered, commutative semiring in which `a \u2264 b`\niff there exists `c` with `b = a + c`. This is satisfied by the natural numbers, for example, but\nnot the integers or other ordered groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tsub_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_add_mul_lt_mul_add_mul'", "description": "Binary **rearrangement inequality**.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.to_covariant_mul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.to_comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_tsub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.to_ordered_comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.to_no_zero_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_le_cancellable.tsub_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_le_cancellable.mul_tsub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_ordered_comm_semiring.to_canonically_ordered_add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.foldr_permutations_aux2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.mem_permutations_aux2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.map_permutations_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.map_permutations'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.map_permutations_aux2", "description": "The `f` argument to `permutations_aux2` when `r = []` can be eliminated.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.mem_foldr_permutations_aux2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.map_map_permutations'_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.permutations_aux2_snd_eq", "description": " An expository lemma to show how all of `ts`, `r`, and `f` can be eliminated from\n`permutations_aux2`.\n\n`(permutations_aux2 t [] [] ys id).2`, which appears on the RHS, is a list whose elements are\nproduced by inserting `t` into every non-terminal position of `ys` in order. As an example:\n```lean\n#eval permutations_aux2 1 [] [] [2, 3, 4] id\n-- [[1, 2, 3, 4], [2, 1, 3, 4], [2, 3, 1, 4]]\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.map_permutations_aux2'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.permutations_aux2_comp_append", "description": "The `ts` argument to `permutations_aux2` can be folded into the `f` argument.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.permutations_aux_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.mem_permutations_aux2'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.permutations_aux2_snd_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.permutations_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.permutations_aux_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.permutations_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.map_map_permutations_aux2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.length_foldr_permutations_aux2'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.permutations'_aux_eq_permutations_aux2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.permutations_aux_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.map_permutations", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.permutations_aux2_snd_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.permutations_aux2_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.length_permutations_aux2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.length_foldr_permutations_aux2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.permutations_aux2_append", "description": "The `r` argument to `permutations_aux2` is the same as appending.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.central_binom", "description": "The central binomial coefficient, `nat.choose (2 * n) n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.succ_dvd_central_binom", "description": "A crucial lemma to ensure that Catalan numbers can be defined via their explicit formula\n `catalan n = n.central_binom / (n + 1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.two_dvd_central_binom_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.two_dvd_central_binom_of_one_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.central_binom_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.two_le_central_binom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.four_pow_lt_mul_central_binom", "description": "An exponential lower bound on the central binomial coefficient.\nThis bound is of interest because it appears in\n[Tochiori's refinement of Erd\u0151s's proof of Bertrand's postulate](tochiori_bertrand).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.succ_mul_central_binom_succ", "description": "An inductive property of the central binomial coefficient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.central_binom_eq_two_mul_choose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.choose_le_central_binom", "description": "The central binomial coefficient is the largest binomial coefficient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.central_binom_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.central_binom_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.four_pow_le_two_mul_self_mul_central_binom", "description": "An exponential lower bound on the central binomial coefficient.\nThis bound is weaker than `nat.four_pow_lt_mul_central_binom`, but it is of historical interest\nbecause it appears in Erd\u0151s's proof of Bertrand's postulate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char", "description": " Define a structure for multiplicative characters.\nA multiplicative character from a commutative monoid `R` to a commutative monoid with zero `R'`\nis a homomorphism of (multiplicative) monoids that sends non-units to zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.to_monoid_hom", "description": " Define a structure for multiplicative characters.\nA multiplicative character from a commutative monoid `R` to a commutative monoid with zero `R'`\nis a homomorphism of (multiplicative) monoids that sends non-units to zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.map_nonunit'", "description": " Define a structure for multiplicative characters.\nA multiplicative character from a commutative monoid `R` to a commutative monoid with zero `R'`\nis a homomorphism of (multiplicative) monoids that sends non-units to zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.is_quadratic.pow_even", "description": "The `n`th power of a quadratic character is the trivial character, when `n` is even.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.of_unit_hom_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.trivial_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.of_unit_hom", "description": "Turn a homomorphism between unit groups into a `mul_char`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.is_quadratic.pow_char", "description": " The `p`th power of a quadratic character is itself, when `p` is the (prime) characteristic\nof the target ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.is_nontrivial", "description": "A multiplicative character is *nontrivial* if it takes a value `\u2260 1` on a unit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.ext", "description": " Extensionality. Since `mul_char`s always take the value zero on non-units, it is sufficient\nto compare the values on units.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.inv_apply_eq_inv", "description": "The inverse of a multiplicative character `\u03c7`, applied to `a`, is the inverse of `\u03c7 a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.is_quadratic.inv", "description": "The inverse of a quadratic character is itself. \u2192", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.to_unit_hom_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.map_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.has_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.map_nonunit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.inv_apply'", "description": " When the domain has a zero, then the inverse of a multiplicative character `\u03c7`,\napplied to `a`, is `\u03c7` applied to the inverse of `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.sum_one_eq_card_units", "description": " The sum over all values of the trivial multiplicative character on a finite ring is\nthe cardinality of its unit group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.of_unit_hom_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.mul_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.simps.apply", "description": "See note [custom simps projection]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.map_ring_char", "description": "If the domain is a ring `R`, then `\u03c7 (ring_char R) = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.mul", "description": "Multiplication of multiplicative characters. (This needs the target to be commutative.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.pow_apply'", "description": "If `n` is positive, then `(\u03c7 ^ n) a = (\u03c7 a) ^ n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.is_nontrivial.comp", "description": "Composition with an injective ring homomorphism preserves nontriviality.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.is_quadratic.pow_odd", "description": "The `n`th power of a quadratic character is itself, when `n` is odd.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.one_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.is_quadratic.comp", "description": "Composition with a ring homomorphism preserves the property of being a quadratic character.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.inv", "description": "The inverse of a multiplicative character. We define it as `inverse \u2218 \u03c7`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.comm_group", "description": "The commutative group structure on `mul_char R R'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.is_quadratic.eq_of_eq_coe", "description": " If two values of quadratic characters with target `\u2124` agree after coercion into a ring\nof characteristic not `2`, then they agree in `\u2124`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.equiv_to_unit_hom", "description": "The equivalence between multiplicative characters and homomorphisms of unit groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.map_zero", "description": "If the domain has a zero (and is nontrivial), then `\u03c7 0 = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.coe_equiv_to_unit_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.ext'", "description": "Extensionality. See `ext` below for the version that will actually be used.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.is_quadratic.sq_eq_one", "description": "The square of a quadratic character is the trivial character.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.coe_to_fun_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.is_nontrivial_iff", "description": "A multiplicative character is nontrivial iff it is not the trivial character.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.is_quadratic", "description": "A multiplicative character is *quadratic* if it takes only the values `0`, `1`, `-1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.trivial", "description": " The trivial multiplicative character. It takes the value `0` on non-units and\nthe value `1` on units.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.pow_apply_coe", "description": "If `a` is a unit and `n : \u2115`, then `(\u03c7 ^ n) a = (\u03c7 a) ^ n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.inv_apply", "description": " When the domain has a zero, then the inverse of a multiplicative character `\u03c7`,\napplied to `a`, is `\u03c7` applied to the inverse of `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.inv_apply_eq_inv'", "description": " The inverse of a multiplicative character `\u03c7`, applied to `a`, is the inverse of `\u03c7 a`.\nVariant when the target is a field", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.mul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.one_apply_coe", "description": "Evaluation of the trivial character", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.is_nontrivial.sum_eq_zero", "description": " The sum over all values of a nontrivial multiplicative character on a finite ring is zero\n(when the target is a domain).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.mul_char_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char_class", "description": "This is the corresponding extension of `monoid_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char_class.to_monoid_hom_class", "description": "This is the corresponding extension of `monoid_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char_class.map_nonunit", "description": "This is the corresponding extension of `monoid_hom_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.coe_to_unit_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.inv_mul", "description": "The product of a character with its inverse is the trivial character.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.equiv_unit_hom_symm_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.ring_hom_comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.to_unit_hom", "description": "Turn a `mul_char` into a homomorphism between the unit groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_char.ring_hom_comp", "description": "We can post-compose a multiplicative character with a ring homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_set_average", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_laverage_le_pos", "description": " **First moment method**. A measurable function is greater than its mean on a set of positive\nmeasure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.average_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.exists_not_mem_null_average_le", "description": " **First moment method**. The maximum of an integrable function is greater than its mean, while\navoiding a null set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_integral_le_pos", "description": " **First moment method**. An integrable function is greater than its integral on a set of\npositive measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_laverage_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.laverage_union_mem_segment", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_le_average_pos", "description": " **First moment method**. An integrable function is smaller than its mean on a set of positive\nmeasure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.exists_not_mem_null_lintegral_le", "description": " **First moment method**. The maximum of a measurable function is greater than its integral,\nwhile avoiding a null set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.average_zero_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.of_real_set_average", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_mul_set_laverage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_average_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_sub_set_average", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.lintegral_laverage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.exists_lintegral_le", "description": "**First moment method**. The maximum of a measurable function is greater than its integral.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.laverage_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure_smul_average", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.exists_le_set_laverage", "description": "**First moment method**. The minimum of a measurable function is smaller than its mean.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.laverage_union_mem_open_segment", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.exists_le_average", "description": "**First moment method**. The mini