cription": "A monoid object internal to a monoidal category.\n\nWhen the monoidal category is preadditive, this is also sometimes called an \"algebra object\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon_.one", "description": "A monoid object internal to a monoidal category.\n\nWhen the monoidal category is preadditive, this is also sometimes called an \"algebra object\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon_.mul", "description": "A monoid object internal to a monoidal category.\n\nWhen the monoidal category is preadditive, this is also sometimes called an \"algebra object\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon_.one_mul'", "description": "A monoid object internal to a monoidal category.\n\nWhen the monoidal category is preadditive, this is also sometimes called an \"algebra object\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon_.mul_one'", "description": "A monoid object internal to a monoidal category.\n\nWhen the monoidal category is preadditive, this is also sometimes called an \"algebra object\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon_.mul_assoc'", "description": "A monoid object internal to a monoidal category.\n\nWhen the monoidal category is preadditive, this is also sometimes called an \"algebra object\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.iterate_map_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.coe_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.iterate_map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.iterate_map_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_right_iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.iterate_map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.coe_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.iterate_map_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.End.coe_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.iterate_map_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_semiconj_by.function_semiconj_add_right_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.iterate_map_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_right_iterate_apply_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.iterate_map_zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_commute.function_commute_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_right_iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.iterate_map_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smul_iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zpow_iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.iterate_map_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.iterate_map_zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.iterate_map_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.iterate_map_zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.iterate_map_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.iterate_map_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semiconj_by.function_semiconj_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hom_coe_pow", "description": "An auxiliary lemma that can be used to prove `\u21d1(f ^ n) = (\u21d1f^[n])`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.iterate_map_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.iterate_map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.function_commute_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.iterate_map_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_left_iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zsmul_iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_left_iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pow_iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vadd_iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.iterate_map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_semiconj_by.function_semiconj_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_commute.function_commute_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.End.coe_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nsmul_iterate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.function_commute_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.iterate_map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.iterate_map_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.iterate_map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_right_iterate_apply_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "semiconj_by.function_semiconj_mul_right_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "universal_enveloping_algebra.lift_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "universal_enveloping_algebra", "description": "The universal enveloping algebra of a Lie algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "universal_enveloping_algebra.lift_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "universal_enveloping_algebra.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "universal_enveloping_algebra.mk_alg_hom", "description": " The quotient map from the tensor algebra to the universal enveloping algebra as a morphism of\nassociative algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "universal_enveloping_algebra.hom_ext", "description": "See note [partially-applied ext lemmas].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "universal_enveloping_algebra.\u03b9", "description": "The natural Lie algebra morphism from a Lie algebra to its universal enveloping algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "universal_enveloping_algebra.\u03b9_comp_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "universal_enveloping_algebra.ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "universal_enveloping_algebra.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "universal_enveloping_algebra.lift_\u03b9_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "universal_enveloping_algebra.lift", "description": " The universal property of the universal enveloping algebra: Lie algebra morphisms into\nassociative algebras lift to associative algebra morphisms from the universal enveloping algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "universal_enveloping_algebra.rel", "description": " The quotient by the ideal generated by this relation is the universal enveloping algebra.\n\nNote that we have avoided using the more natural expression:\n| lie_compat (x y : L) : rel (\u03b9\u209c \u2045x, y\u2046) \u2045\u03b9\u209c x, \u03b9\u209c y\u2046\nso that our construction needs only the semiring structure of the tensor algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "universal_enveloping_algebra.rel.lie_compat", "description": " The quotient by the ideal generated by this relation is the universal enveloping algebra.\n\nNote that we have avoided using the more natural expression:\n| lie_compat (x y : L) : rel (\u03b9\u209c \u2045x, y\u2046) \u2045\u03b9\u209c x, \u03b9\u209c y\u2046\nso that our construction needs only the semiring structure of the tensor algebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "well_founded.monotone_chain_condition'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_embedding.coe_nat_gt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_embedding.not_well_founded_of_decreasing_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.order_embedding_of_set_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotonic_sequence_limit", "description": " The constant value of an eventually-constant monotone sequence `a\u2080 \u2264 a\u2081 \u2264 a\u2082 \u2264 ...` in a\npartially-ordered type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.coe_order_embedding_of_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "well_founded.monotone_chain_condition", "description": "The \"monotone chain condition\" below is sometimes a convenient form of well foundedness.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_increasing_or_nonincreasing_subseq", "description": "This is the infinitary Erd\u0151s\u2013Szekeres theorem, and an important lemma in the usual proof of\n   Bolzano-Weierstrass for `\u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.subtype.order_iso_of_nat", "description": " `nat.subtype.of_nat` as an order isomorphism between `\u2115` and an infinite subset. See also\n`nat.nth` for a version where the subset may be finite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.order_embedding_of_set", "description": "An order embedding from `\u2115` to itself with a specified range", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotonic_sequence_limit_index", "description": " Given an eventually-constant monotone sequence `a\u2080 \u2264 a\u2081 \u2264 a\u2082 \u2264 ...` in a partially-ordered\ntype, `monotonic_sequence_limit_index a` is the least natural number `n` for which `a\u2099` reaches the\nconstant value. For sequences that are not eventually constant, `monotonic_sequence_limit_index a`\nis defined, but is a junk value.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_embedding.acc_iff_no_decreasing_seq", "description": "A value is accessible iff it isn't contained in any infinite decreasing sequence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_embedding.exists_not_acc_lt_of_not_acc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.order_embedding_of_set_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.subtype.order_iso_of_nat_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_embedding.coe_nat_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_embedding.well_founded_iff_no_descending_seq", "description": "A relation is well-founded iff it doesn't have any infinite decreasing sequence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_embedding.nat_lt", "description": "If `f` is a strictly `r`-increasing sequence, then this returns `f` as an order embedding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_embedding.not_acc_of_decreasing_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "well_founded.supr_eq_monotonic_sequence_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.exists_subseq_of_forall_mem_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_increasing_or_nonincreasing_subseq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_embedding.nat_gt", "description": "If `f` is a strictly `r`-decreasing sequence, then this returns `f` as an order embedding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.lower_central_series_last", "description": " Given a non-trivial nilpotent Lie module `M` with lower central series\n`M = C\u2080 \u2265 C\u2081 \u2265 \u22ef \u2265 C\u2096 = \u22a5`, this is the `k-1`th term in the lower central series (the last\nnon-trivial term).\n\nFor a trivial or non-nilpotent module, this is the bottom submodule, `\u22a5`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.is_nilpotent", "description": " We say a Lie algebra is nilpotent when it is nilpotent as a Lie module over itself via the\nadjoint representation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.lower_central_series_last_le_max_triv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.is_nilpotent_range_to_endomorphism_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.ucs_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.lcs_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.coe_lcs_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.ucs_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.coe_lower_central_series_ideal_le", "description": " Note that the below inequality can be strict. For example the ideal of strictly-upper-triangular\n2x2 matrices inside the Lie algebra of upper-triangular 2x2 matrices with `k = 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lower_central_series_eq_lcs_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.ucs", "description": " The upper (aka ascending) central series.\n\nSee also `lie_submodule.lcs`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lower_central_series_map_eq_lcs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.nilpotency_length", "description": " Given a nilpotent Lie module `M` with lower central series `M = C\u2080 \u2265 C\u2081 \u2265 \u22ef \u2265 C\u2096 = \u22a5`, this is\nthe natural number `k` (the number of inclusions).\n\nFor a non-nilpotent module, we use the junk value 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.lie_algebra_is_nilpotent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.trivial_iff_lower_central_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.nilpotent_of_nilpotent_quotient", "description": " If the quotient of a Lie module `M` by a Lie submodule on which the Lie algebra acts trivially\nis nilpotent then `M` is nilpotent.\n\nThis is essentially the Lie module equivalent of the fact that a central\nextension of nilpotent Lie algebras is nilpotent. See `lie_algebra.nilpotent_of_nilpotent_quotient`\nbelow for the corresponding result for Lie algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.lie_module_lcs_map_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.antitone_lower_central_series", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lcs_le_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.ucs_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.lower_central_series_map_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.ucs_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.lie_module_is_nilpotent_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.ucs_le_of_normalizer_eq_self", "description": " If a Lie module `M` contains a self-normalizing Lie submodule `N`, then all terms of the upper\ncentral series of `M` are contained in `N`.\n\nAn important instance of this situation arises from a Cartan subalgebra `H \u2286 L` with the roles of\n`L`, `M`, `N` played by `H`, `L`, `H`, respectively.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.is_nilpotent_range_ad_iff", "description": " Note that this result is not quite a special case of\n`lie_module.is_nilpotent_range_to_endomorphism_iff` which concerns nilpotency of the\n`(ad R L).range`-module `L`, whereas this result concerns nilpotency of the `(ad R L).range`-module\n`(ad R L).range`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.lower_central_series_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.ucs_eq_top_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.lower_central_series_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.nilpotent_of_nilpotent_quotient", "description": "A central extension of nilpotent Lie algebras is nilpotent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lcs_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lcs_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.infi_max_gen_zero_eigenspace_eq_top_of_nilpotent", "description": "See also `lie_algebra.zero_root_space_eq_top_of_nilpotent`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.is_nilpotent_iff", "description": "See also `lie_module.is_nilpotent_iff_exists_ucs_eq_top`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.nilpotent_endo_of_nilpotent_module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_equiv.nilpotent_iff_equiv_nilpotent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.ucs_comap_incl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.infi_max_gen_zero_eigenspace_eq_top_of_nilpotent", "description": " For a nilpotent Lie module, the weight space of the 0 weight is the whole module.\n\nThis result will be used downstream to show that weight spaces are Lie submodules, at which time\nit will be possible to state it in the language of weight spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.lcs_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.derived_series_le_lower_central_series", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.is_nilpotent_iff_exists_lcs_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.iterate_to_endomorphism_mem_lower_central_series", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.lie_algebra_is_nilpotent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.nontrivial_max_triv_of_is_nilpotent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.is_nilpotent_iff_exists_ucs_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.ad_nilpotent_of_nilpotent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.non_trivial_center_of_is_nilpotent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lcs_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.map_lower_central_series_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_subalgebra.is_nilpotent_ad_of_is_nilpotent_ad", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.nilpotency_length_eq_succ_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.trivial_is_nilpotent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.gc_lcs_ucs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_top.top.lie_algebra.is_nilpotent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.nontrivial_lower_central_series_last", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_hom.is_nilpotent_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.surjective.lie_module_is_nilpotent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.is_nilpotent_iff_exists_self_le_ucs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.ucs_eq_self_of_normalizer_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.lcs", "description": " Given a Lie module `M` over a Lie algebra `L` together with an ideal `I` of `L`, this is the\nlower central series of `M` as an `I`-module. The advantage of using this definition instead of\n`lie_module.lower_central_series R I M` is that its terms are Lie submodules of `M` as an\n`L`-module, rather than just as an `I`-module.\n\nSee also `lie_ideal.coe_lcs_eq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lcs", "description": " A generalisation of the lower central series. The zeroth term is a specified Lie submodule of\na Lie module. In the case when we specify the top ideal `\u22a4` of the Lie algebra, regarded as a Lie\nmodule over itself, we get the usual lower central series of a Lie algebra.\n\nIt can be more convenient to work with this generalisation when considering the lower central series\nof a Lie submodule, regarded as a Lie module in its own right, since it provides a type-theoretic\nexpression of the fact that the terms of the Lie submodule's lower central series are also Lie\nsubmodules of the enclosing Lie module.\n\nSee also `lie_module.lower_central_series_eq_lcs_comap` and\n`lie_module.lower_central_series_map_eq_lcs` below, as well as `lie_submodule.ucs`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.is_nilpotent_ad_of_is_nilpotent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.coe_lcs_range_to_endomorphism_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.is_solvable_of_is_nilpotent", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_submodule.lcs_add_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.is_nilpotent_of_top_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.is_nilpotent", "description": " A Lie module is nilpotent if its lower central series reaches 0 (in a finite number of\nsteps).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.is_nilpotent.nilpotent", "description": " A Lie module is nilpotent if its lower central series reaches 0 (in a finite number of\nsteps).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "coe_lower_central_series_ideal_quot_eq", "description": " Given an ideal `I` of a Lie algebra `L`, the lower central series of `L \u29f8 I` is the same\nwhether we regard `L \u29f8 I` as an `L` module or an `L \u29f8 I` module.\n\nTODO: This result obviously generalises but the generalisation requires the missing definition of\nmorphisms between Lie modules over different Lie algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.nilpotency_length_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.nilpotent_ad_of_nilpotent_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.lcs_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_ideal.map_lower_central_series_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_module.lower_central_series", "description": "The lower central series of Lie submodules of a Lie module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.edge_density_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.edge_density_empty_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.mul_edge_density_le_edge_density", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.card_interedges_add_card_interedges_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.mk_mem_interedges_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.card_interedges_finpartition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.edge_density", "description": "Edge density of a relation between two finsets of vertices.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.interedges_bUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.card_interedges_le_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.interedges_bUnion_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.interedges_disjoint_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.interedges_disjoint_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.interedges_bUnion_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_density", "description": "Density of edges of a graph between two finsets of vertices.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_density_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.interedges_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_density_empty_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.card_interedges_add_card_interedges_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.mem_interedges_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.mk_mem_interedges_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.interedges_bUnion_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_density_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.abs_edge_density_sub_edge_density_le_one_sub_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_density_add_edge_density_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.interedges_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_density_empty_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.interedges_empty_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.edge_density_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.edge_density_sub_edge_density_le_one_sub_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.interedges_disjoint_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.interedges_empty_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.abs_edge_density_sub_edge_density_le_two_mul_sub_sq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.mem_interedges_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.interedges_bUnion_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.edge_density_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.interedges_disjoint_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.mk_mem_interedges_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.card_interedges_finpartition_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.card_interedges_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.positivity_edge_density", "description": " Extension for the `positivity` tactic: `rel.edge_density` and `simple_graph.edge_density` are\nalways nonnegative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.card_interedges_div_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.card_interedges_finpartition_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.abs_edge_density_sub_edge_density_le_two_mul", "description": " If `s\u2082 \u2286 s\u2081`, `t\u2082 \u2286 t\u2081` and they take up all but a `\u03b4`-proportion, then the difference in edge\ndensities is at most `2 * \u03b4`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.interedges_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.card_interedges_le_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.swap_mem_interedges_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_density_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.swap_mem_interedges_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.interedges", "description": "Finset of edges of a relation between two finsets of vertices.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.edge_density_add_edge_density_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.interedges_bUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel.edge_density_empty_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.mk_mem_interedges_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.edge_density_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.interedges", "description": "Finset of edges of a relation between two finsets of vertices.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.sound", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.lift.is_lift", "description": "The original functor factors through the induced functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.comp_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.lift_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hom_rel.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.functor.category_theory.full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.lift_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.lift.is_lift_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.comp_closure", "description": "Generates the closure of a family of relations w.r.t. composition from left and right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.comp_closure.intro", "description": "Generates the closure of a family of relations w.r.t. composition from left and right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.lift_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.functor", "description": "The functor from a category to its quotient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.lift", "description": "The induced functor on the quotient category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.lift.is_lift_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.functor.category_theory.ess_surj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.comp", "description": "Composition in the quotient category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.comp_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.lift_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.hom", "description": "Hom-sets of the quotient category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "hom_rel", "description": "A `hom_rel` on `C` consists of a relation on every hom-set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.functor_map_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.lift_map_functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.induction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.functor_obj_as", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient", "description": "A type synonym for `C`, thought of as the objects of the quotient category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.as", "description": "A type synonym for `C`, thought of as the objects of the quotient category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.comp_closure.of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.congruence", "description": " A `hom_rel` is a congruence when it's an equivalence on every hom-set, and it can be composed\nfrom left and right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.congruence.is_equiv", "description": " A `hom_rel` is a congruence when it's an equivalence on every hom-set, and it can be composed\nfrom left and right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.congruence.comp_left", "description": " A `hom_rel` is a congruence when it's an equivalence on every hom-set, and it can be composed\nfrom left and right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.congruence.comp_right", "description": " A `hom_rel` is a congruence when it's an equivalence on every hom-set, and it can be composed\nfrom left and right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.quotient.comp_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.far_from_triangle_free.nonpos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.far_from_triangle_free.not_clique_free", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.far_from_triangle_free.clique_finset_nonempty'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.far_from_triangle_free.clique_finset_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.far_from_triangle_free", "description": " A simple graph is *`\u03b5`-triangle-free far* if one must remove at least `\u03b5 * (card \u03b1)^2` edges to\nmake it triangle-free.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.far_from_triangle_free_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.far_from_triangle_free.le_card_sub_card", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `simple_graph.far_from_triangle_free_iff`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.far_from_triangle_free.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.clique_free.not_far_from_triangle_free", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.next_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.refl_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.symm_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.refl", "description": "The complex shape where only differentials from each `X.i` to itself are allowed.\n\nThis is mostly only useful so we can describe the relation of \"related in `k` steps\" below.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.down_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.down'_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.next", "description": "An arbitary choice of index `j` such that `rel i j`, if such exists.\nReturns `i` otherwise.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.symm", "description": "The reverse of a `complex_shape`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.prev_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.up_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.up'_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.trans", "description": "The \"composition\" of two `complex_shape`s.\n\nWe need this to define \"related in k steps\" later.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.prev", "description": "An arbitary choice of index `i` such that `rel i j`, if such exists.\nReturns `j` otherwise.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape", "description": "A `c : complex_shape \u03b9` describes the shape of a chain complex,\nwith chain groups indexed by `\u03b9`.\nTypically `\u03b9` will be `\u2115`, `\u2124`, or `fin n`.\n\nThere is a relation `rel : \u03b9 \u2192 \u03b9 \u2192 Prop`,\nand we will only allow a non-zero differential from `i` to `j` when `rel i j`.\n\nThere are axioms which imply `{ j // c.rel i j }` and `{ i // c.rel i j }` are subsingletons.\nThis means that the shape consists of some union of lines, rays, intervals, and circles.\n\nBelow we define `c.next` and `c.prev` which provide these related elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.rel", "description": "A `c : complex_shape \u03b9` describes the shape of a chain complex,\nwith chain groups indexed by `\u03b9`.\nTypically `\u03b9` will be `\u2115`, `\u2124`, or `fin n`.\n\nThere is a relation `rel : \u03b9 \u2192 \u03b9 \u2192 Prop`,\nand we will only allow a non-zero differential from `i` to `j` when `rel i j`.\n\nThere are axioms which imply `{ j // c.rel i j }` and `{ i // c.rel i j }` are subsingletons.\nThis means that the shape consists of some union of lines, rays, intervals, and circles.\n\nBelow we define `c.next` and `c.prev` which provide these related elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.next_eq", "description": "A `c : complex_shape \u03b9` describes the shape of a chain complex,\nwith chain groups indexed by `\u03b9`.\nTypically `\u03b9` will be `\u2115`, `\u2124`, or `fin n`.\n\nThere is a relation `rel : \u03b9 \u2192 \u03b9 \u2192 Prop`,\nand we will only allow a non-zero differential from `i` to `j` when `rel i j`.\n\nThere are axioms which imply `{ j // c.rel i j }` and `{ i // c.rel i j }` are subsingletons.\nThis means that the shape consists of some union of lines, rays, intervals, and circles.\n\nBelow we define `c.next` and `c.prev` which provide these related elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.prev_eq", "description": "A `c : complex_shape \u03b9` describes the shape of a chain complex,\nwith chain groups indexed by `\u03b9`.\nTypically `\u03b9` will be `\u2115`, `\u2124`, or `fin n`.\n\nThere is a relation `rel : \u03b9 \u2192 \u03b9 \u2192 Prop`,\nand we will only allow a non-zero differential from `i` to `j` when `rel i j`.\n\nThere are axioms which imply `{ j // c.rel i j }` and `{ i // c.rel i j }` are subsingletons.\nThis means that the shape consists of some union of lines, rays, intervals, and circles.\n\nBelow we define `c.next` and `c.prev` which provide these related elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.down'_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.down_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.subsingleton_next", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.up", "description": "The `complex_shape` appropriate for cohomology, so `d : X i \u27f6 X j` only when `j = i + 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.down'", "description": "The `complex_shape` allowing differentials from `X (j+a)` to `X j`.\n(For example when `a = 1`, a homology theory indexed by `\u2115` or `\u2124`)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.subsingleton_prev", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.down", "description": "The `complex_shape` appropriate for homology, so `d : X i \u27f6 X j` only when `i = j + 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.symm_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex_shape.up'", "description": "The `complex_shape` allowing differentials from `X i` to `X (i+a)`.\n(For example when `a = 1`, a cohomology theory indexed by `\u2115` or `\u2124`)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.polynomial.is_open_map_comap_C", "description": "  The morphism `C\u207a : Spec R[x] \u2192 Spec R` is open.\nStacks Project \"Lemma 00FB\", first part.\n\nhttps://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00FB", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.polynomial.comap_C_mem_image_of_Df", "description": " If a point of `Spec R[x]` is not contained in the vanishing set of `f`, then its image in\n`Spec R` is contained in the open set where at least one of the coefficients of `f` is non-zero.\nThis lemma is a reformulation of `exists_C_coeff_not_mem`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.polynomial.is_open_image_of_Df", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.polynomial.image_of_Df", "description": " Given a polynomial `f \u2208 R[x]`, `image_of_Df` is the subset of `Spec R` where at least one\nof the coefficients of `f` does not vanish.  Lemma `image_of_Df_eq_comap_C_compl_zero_locus`\nproves that `image_of_Df` is the image of `(zero_locus {f})\u1d9c` under the morphism\n`comap C : Spec R[x] \u2192 Spec R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.polynomial.image_of_Df_eq_comap_C_compl_zero_locus", "description": " The open set `image_of_Df f` coincides with the image of `basic_open f` under the\nmorphism `C\u207a : Spec R[x] \u2192 Spec R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.chain.mem_map_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.seq_continuous'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous.of_bundled'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.of_fun", "description": " Construct a continuous function from a bare function, a continuous function, and a proof that\nthey are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.\u03c9Sup_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.chain.zip", "description": "`chain.zip` pairs up the elements of two chains that have the same index", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.of_mono", "description": "Construct a continuous function from a monotone function with a proof of continuity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.\u03c9Sup", "description": " The `\u03c9Sup` operator for continuous functions, which takes the pointwise countable supremum\nof the functions in the `\u03c9`-chain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.seq", "description": "`part.seq` as a continuous function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.bind", "description": "`part.bind` as a monotone function", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.comp", "description": "The composition of continuous functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.const_continuous'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.inf_continuous'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.coe_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.omega_complete_partial_order_\u03c9Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.omega_complete_partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.supr_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.chain.map", "description": "`map` function for `chain`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.bind_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.simps.apply", "description": "See Note [custom simps projection]. We need to specify this projection explicitly in this case,\n because it is a composition of multiple projections.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.omega_complete_partial_order_\u03c9Sup_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous'", "description": "`continuous' f` asserts that `f` is both monotone and continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.\u03c9Sup_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.order_hom.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part.\u03c9Sup_eq_some", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.\u03c9Sup_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.forall_forall_merge'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.map", "description": "`part.map` as a continuous function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.omega_complete_partial_order.flip\u2081_continuous'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous", "description": " A monotone function `f : \u03b1 \u2192o \u03b2` is continuous if it distributes over \u03c9Sup.\n\nIn order to distinguish it from the (more commonly used) continuity from topology\n(see topology/basic.lean), the present definition is often referred to as\n\"Scott-continuity\" (referring to Dana Scott). It corresponds to continuity\nin Scott topological spaces (not defined here).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.\u03c9Sup_zip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.congr_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.to_mono", "description": "The map from continuous functions to monotone functions is itself a monotone function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.\u03c9Sup_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.monotone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.order_hom.\u03c9Sup", "description": "The `\u03c9Sup` operator for monotone functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.omega_complete_partial_order.flip\u2082_continuous'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.order_hom.omega_complete_partial_order_\u03c9Sup_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.flip_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.\u03c9Sup_total", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.order_hom.omega_complete_partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.le_\u03c9Sup_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part.mem_chain_of_mem_\u03c9Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.apply_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.chain.zip_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.\u03c9Sup_apply_\u03c9Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.chain.map_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.subtype", "description": " A subset `p : \u03b1 \u2192 Prop` of the type closed under `\u03c9Sup` induces an\n`omega_complete_partial_order` on the subtype `{a : \u03b1 // p a}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.id_continuous'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part.eq_of_chain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.\u03c9Sup_le_\u03c9Sup_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.of_fun_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous.of_bundled", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.chain.mem_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.omega_complete_partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.chain.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.ite_continuous'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.coe_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order", "description": " An omega-complete partial order is a partial order with a supremum\noperation on increasing sequences indexed by natural numbers (which we\ncall `\u03c9Sup`). In this sense, it is strictly weaker than join complete\nsemi-lattices as only \u03c9-sized totally ordered sets have a supremum.\n\nSee the definition on page 114 of [gunter1992].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.to_partial_order", "description": " An omega-complete partial order is a partial order with a supremum\noperation on increasing sequences indexed by natural numbers (which we\ncall `\u03c9Sup`). In this sense, it is strictly weaker than join complete\nsemi-lattices as only \u03c9-sized totally ordered sets have a supremum.\n\nSee the definition on page 114 of [gunter1992].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.\u03c9Sup", "description": " An omega-complete partial order is a partial order with a supremum\noperation on increasing sequences indexed by natural numbers (which we\ncall `\u03c9Sup`). In this sense, it is strictly weaker than join complete\nsemi-lattices as only \u03c9-sized totally ordered sets have a supremum.\n\nSee the definition on page 114 of [gunter1992].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.le_\u03c9Sup", "description": " An omega-complete partial order is a partial order with a supremum\noperation on increasing sequences indexed by natural numbers (which we\ncall `\u03c9Sup`). In this sense, it is strictly weaker than join complete\nsemi-lattices as only \u03c9-sized totally ordered sets have a supremum.\n\nSee the definition on page 114 of [gunter1992].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.\u03c9Sup_le", "description": " An omega-complete partial order is a partial order with a supremum\noperation on increasing sequences indexed by natural numbers (which we\ncall `\u03c9Sup`). In this sense, it is strictly weaker than join complete\nsemi-lattices as only \u03c9-sized totally ordered sets have a supremum.\n\nSee the definition on page 114 of [gunter1992].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.bind_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.chain.map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.top_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part.\u03c9Sup", "description": "The (noncomputable) `\u03c9Sup` definition for the `\u03c9`-CPO structure on `part \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.seq_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.flip", "description": "A family of continuous functions yields a continuous family of functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.inf_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part.omega_complete_partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.const", "description": "`function.const` is a continuous function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.chain.has_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.Sup_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part.mem_\u03c9Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.map_continuous'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.to_mono_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.prod.apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.chain.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.bot_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.of_mono_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.\u03c9Sup_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.forall_forall_merge", "description": " When proving that a chain of applications is below a bound `z`, it suffices to consider the\nfunctions and values being selected from the same index in the chains.\n\nThis lemma is more specific than necessary, i.e. `c\u2080` only needs to be a\nchain of monotone functions, but it is only used with continuous functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.chain", "description": " A chain is a monotone sequence.\n\nSee the definition on page 114 of [gunter1992].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.lift", "description": " Transfer a `omega_complete_partial_order` on `\u03b2` to a `omega_complete_partial_order` on `\u03b1`\nusing a strictly monotone function `f : \u03b2 \u2192o \u03b1`, a definition of \u03c9Sup and a proof that `f` is\ncontinuous with regard to the provided `\u03c9Sup` and the \u03c9CPO on `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous'.to_bundled", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.chain.map_le_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.prod.apply", "description": "The application of continuous functions as a continuous function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.id", "description": "The identity as a continuous function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.chain.exists_of_mem_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.const_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom", "description": " A monotone function on `\u03c9`-continuous partial orders is said to be continuous\nif for every chain `c : chain \u03b1`, `f (\u2294 i, c i) = \u2294 i, f (c i)`.\nThis is just the bundled version of `order_hom.continuous`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.to_order_hom", "description": " A monotone function on `\u03c9`-continuous partial orders is said to be continuous\nif for every chain `c : chain \u03b1`, `f (\u2294 i, c i) = \u2294 i, f (c i)`.\nThis is just the bundled version of `order_hom.continuous`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.cont", "description": " A monotone function on `\u03c9`-continuous partial orders is said to be continuous\nif for every chain `c : chain \u03b1`, `f (\u2294 i, c i) = \u2294 i, f (c i)`.\nThis is just the bundled version of `order_hom.continuous`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.chain.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.sup_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.omega_complete_partial_order", "description": " Any complete lattice has an `\u03c9`-CPO structure where the countable supremum is a special case\nof arbitrary suprema.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.order_hom.\u03c9Sup_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.omega_complete_partial_order_\u03c9Sup_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous'.to_monotone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "part.\u03c9Sup_eq_none", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.\u03c9Sup_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.chain.has_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.bind", "description": "`part.bind` as a continuous function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.Sup_continuous'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous'_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.\u03c9Sup", "description": "The supremum of a chain in the product `\u03c9`-CPO.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.congr_arg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_complete_partial_order.continuous_hom.bind_continuous'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.omega_complete_partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.inductive_limit_dist", "description": "Predistance on the disjoint union `\u03a3 n, X n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.sigma.dist_same", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.glue_dist_glued_points", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.glue_dist", "description": "Define a predistance on `X \u2295 Y`, for which `\u03a6 p` and `\u03a8 p` are at distance `\u03b5`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.isometry_inl", "description": "The left injection of a space in a disjoint union is an isometry", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.sum.dist", "description": " Distance on a disjoint union. There are many (noncanonical) ways to put a distance compatible\nwith each factor.\nIf the two spaces are bounded, one can say for instance that each point in the first is at distance\n`diam X + diam Y + 1` of each point in the second.\nInstead, we choose a construction that works for unbounded spaces, but requires basepoints,\nchosen arbitrarily.\nWe embed isometrically each factor, set the basepoints at distance 1,\narbitrarily, and say that the distance from `a` to `b` is the sum of the distances of `a` and `b` to\ntheir respective basepoints, plus the distance 1 between the basepoints.\nSince there is an arbitrary choice in this construction, it is not an instance by default.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.to_glue_l", "description": "The canonical map from `X` to the space obtained by gluing isometric subsets in `X` and `Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.sum.one_dist_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.sigma.isometry_mk", "description": "The injection of a space in a disjoint union is an isometry", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.sigma.dist", "description": " Distance on a disjoint union. There are many (noncanonical) ways to put a distance compatible\nwith each factor.\nWe choose a construction that works for unbounded spaces, but requires basepoints,\nchosen arbitrarily.\nWe embed isometrically each factor, set the basepoints at distance 1, arbitrarily,\nand say that the distance from `a` to `b` is the sum of the distances of `a` and `b` to\ntheir respective basepoints, plus the distance 1 between the basepoints.\nSince there is an arbitrary choice in this construction, it is not an instance by default.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.to_inductive_limit_isometry", "description": "The map `to_inductive_limit n` mapping `X n` to the inductive limit is an isometry.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.sum.dist_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.sigma.metric_space", "description": " A metric space structure on the disjoint union `\u03a3 i, E i`.\nWe embed isometrically each factor, set the basepoints at distance 1, arbitrarily,\nand say that the distance from `a` to `b` is the sum of the distances of `a` and `b` to\ntheir respective basepoints, plus the distance 1 between the basepoints.\nSince there is an arbitrary choice in this construction, it is not an instance by default.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.to_glue_r", "description": "The canonical map from `Y` to the space obtained by gluing isometric subsets in `X` and `Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.sum.one_dist_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.glue_metric_approx", "description": " Given two maps `\u03a6` and `\u03a8` intro metric spaces `X` and `Y` such that the distances between\n`\u03a6 p` and `\u03a6 q`, and between `\u03a8 p` and `\u03a8 q`, coincide up to `2 \u03b5` where `\u03b5 > 0`, one can almost\nglue the two spaces `X` and `Y` along the images of `\u03a6` and `\u03a8`, so that `\u03a6 p` and `\u03a8 p` are\nat distance `\u03b5`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.sigma.one_le_dist_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.sigma.complete_space", "description": "A disjoint union of complete metric spaces is complete.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.sum.dist_eq_glue_dist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.inhabited_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.glue_space.metric_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.isometry_inr", "description": "The right injection of a space in a disjoint union is an isometry", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.to_glue_r_isometry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.inductive_limit.metric_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.inductive_limit.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.to_glue_l_isometry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.sigma.fst_eq_of_dist_lt_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.inductive_limit", "description": "The type giving the inductive limit in a metric space context.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.sigma.is_open_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.inductive_premetric", "description": "Premetric space structure on `\u03a3 n, X n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.to_inductive_limit", "description": "Mapping each `X n` to the inductive limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.inductive_limit_dist_eq_dist", "description": " The predistance on the disjoint union `\u03a3 n, X n` can be computed in any `X k` for large\nenough `k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.sigma.dist_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.glue_premetric", "description": " Given two isometric embeddings `\u03a6 : Z \u2192 X` and `\u03a8 : Z \u2192 Y`, we define a pseudo metric space\nstructure on `X \u2295 Y` by declaring that `\u03a6 x` and `\u03a8 x` are at distance `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.to_inductive_limit_commute", "description": "The maps `to_inductive_limit n` are compatible with the maps `f n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.glue_space", "description": " Given two isometric embeddings `\u03a6 : Z \u2192 X` and `\u03a8 : Z \u2192 Y`, we define a\nspace  `glue_space h\u03a6 h\u03a8` by identifying in `X \u2295 Y` the points `\u03a6 x` and `\u03a8 x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.metric_space_sum", "description": " The distance on the disjoint union indeed defines a metric space. All the distance properties\nfollow from our choice of the distance. The harder work is to show that the uniform structure\ndefined by the distance coincides with the disjoint union uniform structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.sigma.has_dist", "description": " A `has_dist` instance on the disjoint union `\u03a3 i, E i`.\nWe embed isometrically each factor, set the basepoints at distance 1, arbitrarily,\nand say that the distance from `a` to `b` is the sum of the distances of `a` and `b` to\ntheir respective basepoints, plus the distance 1 between the basepoints.\nSince there is an arbitrary choice in this construction, it is not an instance by default.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.inhabited_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.sigma.dist_triangle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.to_glue_commute", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans.app_hom", "description": " Application of a natural transformation at a fixed object,\nas group homomorphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans.app_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans.app_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans.app_zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans.app_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans.app_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans.app_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans.app_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_trans.app_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor_category_preadditive", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.gcd_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.is_primitive_classified_of_coprime_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.mul", "description": " A triple is still a triple if you multiply `x`, `y` and `z`\nby a constant `k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.coprime_classification'", "description": " by assuming `x` is odd and `z` is positive we get a slightly more precise classification of\nthe pythagorean triple `x ^ 2 + y ^ 2 = z ^ 2`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.is_classified", "description": " A Pythagorean triple `x, y, z` is \u201cclassified\u201d if there exist integers `k, m, n` such that\neither\n * `x = k * (m ^ 2 - n ^ 2)` and `y = k * (2 * m * n)`, or\n * `x = k * (2 * m * n)` and `y = k * (m ^ 2 - n ^ 2)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.mul_iff", "description": " `(k*x, k*y, k*z)` is a Pythagorean triple if and only if\n`(x, y, z)` is also a triple.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.classification", "description": "**Formula for Pythagorean Triples**", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.classified", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.coprime_of_coprime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_equiv_gen", "description": " A parameterization of the unit circle that is useful for classifying Pythagorean triples.\n(To be applied in the case where `K = \u211a`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.is_classified_of_normalize_is_primitive_classified", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.is_primitive_classified_of_coprime_of_odd_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple_comm", "description": " Pythagorean triples are interchangable, i.e `x * x + y * y = y * y + x * x = z * z`.\nThis comes from additive commutativity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.is_primitive_classified_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.zero", "description": "The zeroth Pythagorean triple is all zeros.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.is_primitive_classified", "description": "A primitive pythogorean triple `x, y, z` is a pythagorean triple with `x` and `y` coprime.\nSuch a triple is \u201cprimitively classified\u201d if there exist coprime integers `m, n` such that either\n* `x = m ^ 2 - n ^ 2` and `y = 2 * m * n`, or\n* `x = 2 * m * n` and `y = m ^ 2 - n ^ 2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.ne_zero_of_coprime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.normalize", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.sq_ne_two_mod_four", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.coprime_classification", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.is_classified_of_is_primitive_classified", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.is_primitive_classified_of_coprime_of_zero_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.mul_is_classified", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sq_ne_two_fin_zmod_four", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "circle_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.even_odd_of_coprime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple.is_primitive_classified_of_coprime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pythagorean_triple", "description": "Three integers `x`, `y`, and `z` form a Pythagorean triple if `x * x + y * y = z * z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.eval\u2082_one_cyclotomic_prime_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_eval_lt_add_one_pow_totient", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_nonneg", "description": "Cyclotomic polynomials are always nonnegative on inputs one or more.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.eval_one_cyclotomic_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_pos'", "description": " Cyclotomic polynomials are always positive on inputs larger than one.\nSimilar to `cyclotomic_pos` but with the condition on the input rather than index of the\ncyclotomic polynomial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.sub_one_pow_totient_le_cyclotomic_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.eval\u2082_one_cyclotomic_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.eval_one_cyclotomic_prime_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_eval_le_add_one_pow_totient", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.sub_one_lt_nat_abs_cyclotomic_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.sub_one_pow_totient_lt_cyclotomic_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.eval_one_cyclotomic_not_prime_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_pos_and_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.sub_one_pow_totient_lt_nat_abs_cyclotomic_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cyclotomic_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.multinomial_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.multinomial", "description": " The multinomial coefficient. Gives the number of strings consisting of symbols\nfrom `s`, where `c \u2208 s` appears with multiplicity `f c`.\n\nDefined as `(\u2211 i in s, f i)! / \u220f i in s, (f i)!`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.succ_mul_binomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.multinomial_update", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.multinomial_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.multinomial_univ_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.multinomial_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.multinomial_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.multinomial_insert_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.multinomial_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.binomial_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.multinomial", "description": "Alternative multinomial definition based on a finsupp, using the support\n for the big operations", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.multinomial_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.multinomial", "description": "Alternative definition of multinomial based on `multiset` delegating to the\n finsupp definition", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.multinomial_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_pow_of_commute", "description": "The multinomial theorem\n\nProof is by induction on the number of summands.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.binomial_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.binomial_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.multinomial_univ_three", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.multinomial_filter_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.binomial_eq_choose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.binomial_succ_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.eq", "description": "The `Kleisli` category of a `control.monad` is equivalent to the `kleisli` category of its\ncategory-theoretic version, provided the monad is lawful.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.eq_inverse_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.eq_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.of_type_monad_\u03bc_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.eq_functor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.of_type_monad", "description": "A lawful `control.monad` gives a category theory `monad` on the category of types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.of_type_monad_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.eq_inverse_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.eq_functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.eq_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.of_type_monad_\u03b7_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_nhds_of_Limsup_eq_Liminf", "description": " If the liminf and the limsup of a filter coincide, then this filter converges to\ntheir common value, at least if the filter is eventually bounded above and below.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.map_Liminf_of_continuous_at", "description": " A monotone function between complete linear ordered spaces sends a `filter.Liminf`\nto the `filter.liminf` of the image if it is continuous at the `Liminf`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_of_le_liminf_of_limsup_le", "description": " If a number `a` is less than or equal to the `liminf` of a function `f` at some filter\nand is greater than or equal to the `limsup` of `f`, then `f` tends to `a` along this filter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_le_nhds_class", "description": "Ad hoc typeclass stating that neighborhoods are eventually bounded above.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_le_nhds_class.is_bounded_le_nhds", "description": "Ad hoc typeclass stating that neighborhoods are eventually bounded above.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "limsup_eq_tendsto_sum_indicator_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_topology.to_bounded_le_nhds_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_top.to_bounded_le_nhds_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.limsup_eq", "description": "If a function has a limit, then its limsup coincides with its limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "supr_eq_of_forall_le_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Union_Iic_eq_Iio_of_lt_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Limsup_eq_of_le_nhds", "description": "If a filter is converging, its liminf coincides with its limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.bdd_below_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.bounded_ge_nhds_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.map_liminf_of_continuous_at", "description": " A continuous monotone function between complete linear ordered spaces sends a `filter.liminf`\nto the `filter.liminf` of the images.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.liminf_eq", "description": "If a function has a limit, then its liminf coincides with its limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cobounded_ge_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_ge_nhds_class", "description": "Ad hoc typeclass stating that neighborhoods are eventually bounded below.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_ge_nhds_class.is_bounded_ge_nhds", "description": "Ad hoc typeclass stating that neighborhoods are eventually bounded below.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_le_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.bounded_ge_nhds_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.bounded_le_nhds_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Union_Ici_eq_Ioi_of_lt_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_bot.to_bounded_ge_nhds_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.map_limsup_of_continuous_at", "description": " A continuous monotone function between complete linear ordered spaces sends a `filter.limsup`\nto the `filter.limsup` of the images.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.bdd_below_range_of_cofinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liminf_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.bounded_le_nhds_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.is_cobounded_under_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.is_cobounded_under_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.bdd_above_range_of_cofinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_liminf_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Liminf_eq_of_le_nhds", "description": "If a filter is converging, its limsup coincides with its limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone.map_Limsup_of_continuous_at", "description": " An antitone function between complete linear ordered spaces sends a `filter.Limsup`\nto the `filter.liminf` of the image if it is continuous at the `Limsup`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_of_no_upcrossings", "description": " Assume that, for any `a < b`, a sequence can not be infinitely many times below `a` and\nabove `b`. If it is also ultimately bounded above and below, then it has to converge. This even\nworks if `a` and `b` are restricted to a dense subset.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "limsup_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone.map_liminf_of_continuous_at", "description": " A continuous antitone function between complete linear ordered spaces sends a `filter.liminf`\nto the `filter.limsup` of the images.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.bdd_above_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_bounded_ge_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_of_liminf_eq_limsup", "description": " If the liminf and the limsup of a function coincide, then the limit of the function\nexists and has the same value", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_topology.to_bounded_ge_nhds_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.is_bounded_under_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infi_eq_of_forall_le_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone.map_Liminf_of_continuous_at", "description": " An antitone function between complete linear ordered spaces sends a `filter.Liminf`\nto the `filter.limsup` of the image if it is continuous at the `Liminf`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "limsup_eq_tendsto_sum_indicator_nat_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.bounded_ge_nhds_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.bounded_le_nhds_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.map_Limsup_of_continuous_at", "description": " A monotone function between complete linear ordered spaces sends a `filter.Limsup`\nto the `filter.limsup` of the image if it is continuous at the `Limsup`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cobounded_le_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone.map_limsup_of_continuous_at", "description": " A continuous antitone function between complete linear ordered spaces sends a `filter.limsup`\nto the `filter.liminf` of the images.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_le_limsup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Limsup_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Liminf_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.is_bounded_under_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.mul_n_is_poly.comp\u2082_i", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.mul_n_is_poly", "description": "Multiplication by `n` is a polynomial function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.witt_mul_n", "description": " `witt_mul_n p n` is the family of polynomials that computes\nthe coefficients of `x * n` in terms of the coefficients of the Witt vector `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.mul_n_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.mul_n_is_poly.comp_i", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.bind\u2081_witt_mul_n_witt_polynomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_group_with_zero_of_is_unit_or_eq_zero", "description": "Constructs a `comm_group_with_zero` structure on a `comm_monoid_with_zero`\n consisting only of units and 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.inverse", "description": " Introduce a function `inverse` on a monoid with zero `M\u2080`, which sends `x` to `x\u207b\u00b9` if `x` is\ninvertible and to `0` otherwise.  This definition is somewhat ad hoc, but one needs a fully (rather\nthan partially) defined inverse function for some purposes, including for calculus.\n\nNote that while this is in the `ring` namespace for brevity, it requires the weaker assumption\n`monoid_with_zero M\u2080` instead of `ring M\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_with_zero.eq_zero_or_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.mk0_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne.is_unit", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `is_unit_iff_ne_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_with_zero.no_zero_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.inverse_mul_cancel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "div_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_group_with_zero.to_division_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.mk0_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.inverse_non_unit", "description": "By definition, if `x` is not invertible then `inverse x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.inverse_mul_eq_iff_eq_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.inverse_unit", "description": "By definition, if `x` is invertible then `inverse x = x\u207b\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.exists0'", "description": " An alternative version of `units.exists0`. This one is useful if Lean cannot\nfigure out `p` when using `units.exists0` from right to left.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.exists0", "description": "In a group with zero, an existential over a unit can be rewritten in terms of `units.mk0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.exists_iff_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_group_with_zero.to_cancel_comm_monoid_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "div_ne_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.mk0_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group_with_zero_of_is_unit_or_eq_zero", "description": "Constructs a `group_with_zero` structure on a `monoid_with_zero`\n consisting only of units and 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "div_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.ne_zero", "description": "An element of the unit group of a nonzero monoid with zero represented as an element\n   of the monoid is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.inverse_eq_inv'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.inverse_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.coe_mk0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.mul_right_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_is_unit_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.mk0_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.mul_inverse_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.inverse_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit_iff_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.inv_mul'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.mul_left_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.mk0", "description": "Embed a non-zero element of a `group_with_zero` into the unit group.\n By combining this function with the operations on units,\n or the `/\u209a` operation, it is possible to write a division\n as a partial function with three arguments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.mul_inv'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit_ring_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.mk0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.eq_mul_inverse_iff_mul_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.mul_inverse_cancel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.inverse_eq_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.mul_right_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.mul_left_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.ring_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.inverse_mul_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.inverse_mul_cancel_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.mul_inverse_cancel_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_closed_unit_ball_eq_add_haar_unit_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_sphere_of_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "basis.parallelepiped_basis_fun", "description": "The parallelepiped formed from the standard basis for `\u03b9 \u2192 \u211d` is `[0,1]^\u03b9`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.is_unif_loc_doubling_measure_of_is_add_haar_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_preimage_continuous_linear_equiv", "description": " The preimage of a set `s` under a continuous linear equiv `f` has measure\nequal to `\u03bc s` times the absolute value of the inverse of the determinant of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_preimage_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.tendsto_add_haar_inter_smul_one_of_density_one_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.is_add_haar_measure_volume_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_affine_subspace", "description": "A strict affine subspace has measure zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_smul", "description": "Rescaling a set by a factor `r` multiplies its measure by `abs (r ^ dim)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.eventually_nonempty_inter_smul_of_density_one", "description": " Consider a point `x` at which a set `s` has density one, with respect to closed balls (i.e.,\na Lebesgue density point of `s`). Then `s` intersects the rescaled copies `{x} + r \u2022 t` of a given\nset `t` with positive measure, for any small enough `r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.measure", "description": " The Lebesgue measure associated to an alternating map. It gives measure `|\u03c9 v|` to the\nparallelepiped spanned by the vectors `v\u2081, ..., v\u2099`. Note that it is not always a Haar measure,\nas it can be zero, but it is always locally finite and translation invariant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_linear_map_add_haar_eq_smul_add_haar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.alternating_map.measure.is_add_left_invariant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.positive_compacts.Icc01", "description": "The interval `[0,1]` as a compact set with non-empty interior.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.tendsto_add_haar_inter_smul_one_of_density_one", "description": " Consider a point `x` at which a set `s` has density one, with respect to closed balls (i.e.,\na Lebesgue density point of `s`). Then `s` has also density one at `x` with respect to any\nmeasurable set `t`: the proportion of points in `s` belonging to a rescaled copy `{x} + r \u2022 t`\nof `t` tends to one as `r` tends to zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.tendsto_add_haar_inter_smul_zero_of_density_zero", "description": " Consider a point `x` at which a set `s` has density zero, with respect to closed balls. Then it\nalso has density zero with respect to any measurable set `t`: the proportion of points in `s`\nbelonging to a rescaled copy `{x} + r \u2022 t` of `t` tends to zero as `r` tends to zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.positive_compacts.pi_Icc01", "description": "The set `[0,1]^\u03b9` as a compact set with non-empty interior.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alternating_map.measure_parallelepiped", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_submodule", "description": "A strict vector subspace has measure zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.add_haar_measure_eq_volume_pi", "description": "The Haar measure equals the Lebesgue measure on `\u211d^\u03b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_smul_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_image_continuous_linear_equiv", "description": " The image of a set `s` under a continuous linear equiv `f` has measure\nequal to `\u03bc s` times the absolute value of the determinant of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_ball_mul_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_closed_ball_center", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_preimage_linear_map", "description": " The preimage of a set `s` under a linear map `f` with nonzero determinant has measure\nequal to `\u03bc s` times the absolute value of the inverse of the determinant of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.alternating_map.measure.measure_theory.is_locally_finite_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_closed_ball_eq_add_haar_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_parallelepiped", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_image_continuous_linear_map", "description": " The image of a set `s` under a continuous linear map `f` has measure\nequal to `\u03bc s` times the absolute value of the determinant of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.tendsto_add_haar_inter_smul_zero_of_density_zero_aux1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_add_haar_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_image_homothety", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_closed_ball'", "description": " The measure of a closed ball can be expressed in terms of the measure of the closed unit ball.\nUse instead `add_haar_closed_ball`, which uses the measure of the open unit ball as a standard\nform.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_closed_ball_mul_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_ball_center", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.null_measurable_set.const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_ball_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_singleton_add_smul_div_singleton_add_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.tendsto_add_haar_inter_smul_zero_of_density_zero_aux2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_sphere", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_eq_zero_of_disjoint_translates_aux", "description": " If a set is disjoint of its translates by infinitely many bounded vectors, then it has measure\nzero. This auxiliary lemma proves this assuming additionally that the set is bounded.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.add_haar_measure_eq_volume", "description": "The Haar measure equals the Lebesgue measure on `\u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_preimage_continuous_linear_map", "description": " The preimage of a set `s` under a continuous linear map `f` with nonzero determinant has measure\nequal to `\u03bc s` times the absolute value of the inverse of the determinant of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_preimage_linear_equiv", "description": " The preimage of a set `s` under a linear equiv `f` has measure\nequal to `\u03bc s` times the absolute value of the inverse of the determinant of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_closed_ball_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_eq_zero_of_disjoint_translates", "description": " If a set is disjoint of its translates by infinitely many bounded vectors, then it has measure\nzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.map_linear_map_add_haar_pi_eq_smul_add_haar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_image_linear_map", "description": " The image of a set `s` under a linear map `f` has measure\nequal to `\u03bc s` times the absolute value of the determinant of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_ball_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measure.add_haar_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom_class", "description": " `non_unital_alg_hom_class F R A B` asserts `F` is a type of bundled algebra homomorphisms\nfrom `A` to `B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom_class.coe", "description": " `non_unital_alg_hom_class F R A B` asserts `F` is a type of bundled algebra homomorphisms\nfrom `A` to `B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom_class.coe_injective'", "description": " `non_unital_alg_hom_class F R A B` asserts `F` is a type of bundled algebra homomorphisms\nfrom `A` to `B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom_class.map_smul", "description": " `non_unital_alg_hom_class F R A B` asserts `F` is a type of bundled algebra homomorphisms\nfrom `A` to `B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom_class.map_add", "description": " `non_unital_alg_hom_class F R A B` asserts `F` is a type of bundled algebra homomorphisms\nfrom `A` to `B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom_class.map_zero", "description": " `non_unital_alg_hom_class F R A B` asserts `F` is a type of bundled algebra homomorphisms\nfrom `A` to `B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom_class.map_mul", "description": " `non_unital_alg_hom_class F R A B` asserts `F` is a type of bundled algebra homomorphisms\nfrom `A` to `B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.coe_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.coe_mul_hom_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.to_mul_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.one_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.inr", "description": "The right injection into a product is a non-unital algebra homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.to_distrib_mul_action_hom_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.mul_hom.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.snd", "description": "The second projection of a product is a non-unital alg_hom.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.distrib_mul_action_hom.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom_class.non_unital_alg_hom_class.to_non_unital_ring_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.to_non_unital_alg_hom", "description": "A unital morphism of algebras is a `non_unital_alg_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.prod_equiv", "description": " Taking the product of two maps with the same domain is equivalent to taking the product of\ntheir codomains.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.to_non_unital_alg_hom_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.inr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.non_unital_alg_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.congr_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.inl_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.map_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom_class.to_mul_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.coe_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.coe_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.to_mul_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.fst_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.to_mul_hom_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.prod", "description": "The prod of two morphisms is a morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.coe_to_non_unital_alg_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom_class.non_unital_alg_hom.has_coe_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.fst", "description": "The first projection of a product is a non-unital alg_hom.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.prod_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.snd_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom_class.to_distrib_mul_action_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.coe_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom", "description": " A morphism respecting addition, multiplication, and scalar multiplication. When these arise from\nalgebra structures, this is the same as a not-necessarily-unital morphism of algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.to_fun", "description": " A morphism respecting addition, multiplication, and scalar multiplication. When these arise from\nalgebra structures, this is the same as a not-necessarily-unital morphism of algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.map_smul'", "description": " A morphism respecting addition, multiplication, and scalar multiplication. When these arise from\nalgebra structures, this is the same as a not-necessarily-unital morphism of algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.map_zero'", "description": " A morphism respecting addition, multiplication, and scalar multiplication. When these arise from\nalgebra structures, this is the same as a not-necessarily-unital morphism of algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.map_add'", "description": " A morphism respecting addition, multiplication, and scalar multiplication. When these arise from\nalgebra structures, this is the same as a not-necessarily-unital morphism of algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.map_mul'", "description": " A morphism respecting addition, multiplication, and scalar multiplication. When these arise from\nalgebra structures, this is the same as a not-necessarily-unital morphism of algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.prod_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.non_unital_alg_hom.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.non_unital_alg_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom_class.linear_map_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.coe_distrib_mul_action_hom_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.to_distrib_mul_action_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.coe_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "see Note [function coercion]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.prod_fst_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.fst_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.inl", "description": "The left injection into a product is a non-unital algebra homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.coe_to_mul_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.comp", "description": "The composition of morphisms is a morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.inverse", "description": "The inverse of a bijective morphism is a morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.snd_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.to_distrib_mul_action_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.map_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_alg_hom.coe_to_distrib_mul_action_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.sigma_hom.comp", "description": "Composition of sigma homomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.incl.category_theory.full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.sigma_hom.assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.nat_trans_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.map_id_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.incl_desc_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.map_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.desc_uniq", "description": "If `q` when restricted to each subcategory `C i` agrees with `F i`, then `q` is isomorphic to\n`desc F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.map_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.desc_map", "description": "(Implementation). An auxiliary definition to build the functor `desc`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.nat_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.sigma_hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.map_comp", "description": "The functor `sigma.map` applied to a composition is a composition of functors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.incl", "description": "The inclusion functor into the disjoint union of categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.desc_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.incl.category_theory.faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.functor.sigma", "description": "Assemble an `I`-indexed family of functors into a functor between the sigma types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.incl_comp_map_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.desc", "description": "Given a collection of functors `F i : C i \u2964 D`, we can produce a functor `(\u03a3 i, C i) \u2964 D`.\n\nThe produced functor `desc F` satisfies: `incl i \u22d9 desc F \u2245 F i`, i.e. restricted to just the\nsubcategory `C i`, `desc F` agrees with `F i`, and it is unique (up to natural isomorphism) with\nthis property.\n\nThis witnesses that the sigma-type is the coproduct in Cat.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.map", "description": "A function `J \u2192 I` induces a functor `\u03a3 j, C (g j) \u2964 \u03a3 i, C i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.incl_comp_map", "description": "The functor `sigma.map C g` restricted to the subcategory `C j` acts as the inclusion of `g j`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.incl_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.sigma_hom.comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.sigma_hom", "description": "The type of morphisms of a disjoint union of categories: for `X : C i` and `Y : C j`, a morphism\n`(i, X) \u27f6 (j, Y)` if `i = j` is just a morphism `X \u27f6 Y`, and if `i \u2260 j` there are no such morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.sigma_hom.mk", "description": "The type of morphisms of a disjoint union of categories: for `X : C i` and `Y : C j`, a morphism\n`(i, X) \u27f6 (j, Y)` if `i = j` is just a morphism `X \u27f6 Y`, and if `i \u2260 j` there are no such morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.nat_iso", "description": "If `q\u2081` and `q\u2082` when restricted to each subcategory `C i` agree, then `q\u2081` and `q\u2082` are isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.map_id", "description": "The functor `sigma.map` applied to the identity function is just the identity functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.nat_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.desc_uniq_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.sigma_hom.comp_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.sigma_hom.id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.desc_map_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.map_comp_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.incl_desc_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.desc_uniq_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.incl_desc", "description": "This shows that when `desc F` is restricted to just the subcategory `C i`, `desc F` agrees with\n`F i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.nat_trans.sigma", "description": "Assemble an `I`-indexed family of natural transformations into a single natural transformation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.incl_comp_map_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.sigma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.map_id_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.sigma_hom.sigma.category_theory.category_struct", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.sigma_hom.id", "description": "The identity morphism on an object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.map_comp_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.incl_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sigma.nat_trans", "description": "To build a natural transformation over the sigma category, it suffices to specify it restricted to\neach subcategory.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.frontier_set_of_le_re_and_im_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.frontier_set_of_re_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.interior_set_of_re_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.frontier_preimage_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open.re_prod_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.frontier_set_of_le_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.closure_preimage_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.frontier_set_of_le_re_and_le_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.interior_set_of_im_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.re_prod_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.closure_preimage_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.is_homeomorphic_trivial_fiber_bundle_im", "description": "`complex.im` turns `\u2102` into a trivial topological fiber bundle over `\u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.frontier_set_of_le_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.frontier_set_of_im_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.quotient_map_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.interior_set_of_le_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.closure_re_prod_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.closure_set_of_im_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.frontier_set_of_lt_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.quotient_map_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.interior_preimage_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.interior_re_prod_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.closure_set_of_re_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.closure_set_of_lt_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.is_open_map_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.is_homeomorphic_trivial_fiber_bundle_re", "description": "`complex.re` turns `\u2102` into a trivial topological fiber bundle over `\u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.interior_preimage_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.frontier_set_of_lt_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.closure_set_of_lt_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.interior_set_of_le_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "metric.bounded.re_prod_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.is_open_map_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.frontier_preimage_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.frontier_re_prod_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.frontier_set_of_im_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.frontier_set_of_re_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_colimit_of_reflects_iso", "description": "If `F` reflects isomorphisms and we can lift any colimit cocone to a colimit cocone,\nthen `F` creates colimits.\nIn particular here we don't need to assume that F reflects colimits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.reflects_colimits_of_creates_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_colimit_of_fully_faithful_of_lift", "description": "When `F` is fully faithful, and `has_colimit (K \u22d9 F)`, to show that `F` creates the colimit for `K`\nit suffices to exhibit a lift of the chosen colimit cocone for `K \u22d9 F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_limits_of_shape", "description": "`F` creates limits of shape `J` if `F` creates the limit of any diagram\n`K : J \u2964 C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_limits_of_shape.creates_limit", "description": "`F` creates limits of shape `J` if `F` creates the limit of any diagram\n`K : J \u2964 C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_colimits_of_size", "description": "`F` creates colimits if it creates colimits of shape `J` for any small `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_colimits_of_size.creates_colimits_of_shape", "description": "`F` creates colimits if it creates colimits of shape `J` for any small `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.id_lifts_cone", "description": "Any cone lifts through the identity functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_limits_of_size", "description": "`F` creates limits if it creates limits of shape `J` for any `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_limits_of_size.creates_limits_of_shape", "description": "`F` creates limits if it creates limits of shape `J` for any `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comp_creates_limits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comp_creates_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.has_limits_of_has_limits_creates_limits", "description": "If `F` creates limits, and `D` has all limits, then `C` has all limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lifts_to_colimit_of_creates", "description": "If F creates the colimit of K, any cocone lifts to a colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comp_creates_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_limit", "description": "Definition 3.3.1 of [Riehl].\nWe say that `F` creates limits of `K` if, given any limit cone `c` for `K \u22d9 F`\n(i.e. below) we can lift it to a cone \"above\", and further that `F` reflects\nlimits for `K`.\n\nIf `F` reflects isomorphisms, it suffices to show only that the lifted cone is\na limit - see `creates_limit_of_reflects_iso`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_limit.to_reflects_limit", "description": "Definition 3.3.1 of [Riehl].\nWe say that `F` creates limits of `K` if, given any limit cone `c` for `K \u22d9 F`\n(i.e. below) we can lift it to a cone \"above\", and further that `F` reflects\nlimits for `K`.\n\nIf `F` reflects isomorphisms, it suffices to show only that the lifted cone is\na limit - see `creates_limit_of_reflects_iso`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_limit.lifts", "description": "Definition 3.3.1 of [Riehl].\nWe say that `F` creates limits of `K` if, given any limit cone `c` for `K \u22d9 F`\n(i.e. below) we can lift it to a cone \"above\", and further that `F` reflects\nlimits for `K`.\n\nIf `F` reflects isomorphisms, it suffices to show only that the lifted cone is\na limit - see `creates_limit_of_reflects_iso`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_limits", "description": "`F` creates small limits if it creates limits of shape `J` for any small `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comp_creates_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.inhabited_liftable_cocone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_limit_of_iso_diagram", "description": "Transfer creation of limits along a natural isomorphism in the diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lifted_limit_maps_to_original", "description": "The lifted cone has an image isomorphic to the original cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_colimit_of_shape_of_creates_colimits_of_shape_and_has_colimits_of_shape", "description": "`F` preserves the colimit of shape `J` if it creates these colimits and `D` has them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_colimit_of_iso_diagram", "description": "Transfer creation of colimits along a natural isomorphism in the diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lifts_to_limit_of_creates", "description": "If F creates the limit of K, any cone lifts to a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_colimits_of_creates_colimits_and_has_colimits", "description": "`F` preserves limits if it creates limits and `D` has limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_limits_of_shape_of_nat_iso", "description": "If `F` creates limits of shape `J` and `F \u2245 G`, then `G` creates limits of shape `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.id_creates_limits", "description": "The identity functor creates all limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.has_colimits_of_has_colimits_creates_colimits", "description": "If `F` creates colimits, and `D` has all colimits, then `C` has all colimits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.reflects_limits_of_shape_of_creates_limits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.has_limit_of_created", "description": "If `F` creates the limit of `K` and `K \u22d9 F` has a limit, then `K` has a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_colimit_of_fully_faithful_of_lift'", "description": "When `F` is fully faithful, to show that `F` creates the colimit for `K` it suffices to exhibit a\nlift of a colimit cocone for `K \u22d9 F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.inhabited_liftable_cone", "description": "Satisfy the inhabited linter", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.reflects_limits_of_creates_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_limit_of_shape_of_creates_limits_of_shape_and_has_limits_of_shape", "description": "`F` preserves the limit of shape `J` if it creates these limits and `D` has them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_limits_of_creates_limits_and_has_limits", "description": "`F` preserves limits if it creates limits and `D` has limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.id_creates_colimits", "description": "The identity functor creates all colimits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.reflects_colimits_of_shape_of_creates_colimits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.id_lifts_cocone", "description": "Any cocone lifts through the identity functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lift_limit", "description": "`lift_limit t` is the cone for `K` given by lifting the limit `t` for `K \u22d9 F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_limit_of_reflects_iso", "description": "If `F` reflects isomorphisms and we can lift any limit cone to a limit cone,\nthen `F` creates limits.\nIn particular here we don't need to assume that F reflects limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comp_creates_colimits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lift_colimit", "description": "`lift_colimit t` is the cocone for `K` given by lifting the colimit `t` for `K \u22d9 F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_colimit_of_creates_colimit_and_has_colimit", "description": "`F` preserves the colimit of `K` if it creates the colimit and `K \u22d9 F` has the colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lifts_to_limit", "description": "A helper to show a functor creates limits. In particular, if we can show\nthat for any limit cone `c` for `K \u22d9 F`, there is a lift of it which is\na limit and `F` reflects isomorphisms, then `F` creates limits.\nUsually, `F` creating limits says that _any_ lift of `c` is a limit, but\nhere we only need to show that our particular lift of `c` is a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lifts_to_limit.to_liftable_cone", "description": "A helper to show a functor creates limits. In particular, if we can show\nthat for any limit cone `c` for `K \u22d9 F`, there is a lift of it which is\na limit and `F` reflects isomorphisms, then `F` creates limits.\nUsually, `F` creating limits says that _any_ lift of `c` is a limit, but\nhere we only need to show that our particular lift of `c` is a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lifts_to_limit.makes_limit", "description": "A helper to show a functor creates limits. In particular, if we can show\nthat for any limit cone `c` for `K \u22d9 F`, there is a lift of it which is\na limit and `F` reflects isomorphisms, then `F` creates limits.\nUsually, `F` creating limits says that _any_ lift of `c` is a limit, but\nhere we only need to show that our particular lift of `c` is a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_limit_of_nat_iso", "description": "If `F` creates the limit of `K` and `F \u2245 G`, then `G` creates the limit of `K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_colimits_of_shape", "description": "`F` creates colimits of shape `J` if `F` creates the colimit of any diagram\n`K : J \u2964 C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_colimits_of_shape.creates_colimit", "description": "`F` creates colimits of shape `J` if `F` creates the colimit of any diagram\n`K : J \u2964 C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_colimits_of_nat_iso", "description": "If `F` creates colimits and `F \u2245 G`, then `G` creates colimits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.inhabited_lifts_to_colimit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.has_colimits_of_shape_of_has_colimits_of_shape_creates_colimits_of_shape", "description": "If `F` creates colimits of shape `J`, and `D` has colimits of shape `J`, then\n`C` has colimits of shape `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_colimits_of_shape_of_nat_iso", "description": "If `F` creates colimits of shape `J` and `F \u2245 G`, then `G` creates colimits of shape `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_limits_of_nat_iso", "description": "If `F` creates limits and `F \u2245 G`, then `G` creates limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.has_colimit_of_created", "description": "If `F` creates the limit of `K` and `K \u22d9 F` has a limit, then `K` has a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comp_creates_colimit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.liftable_cone", "description": "Define the lift of a cone: For a cone `c` for `K \u22d9 F`, give a cone for `K`\nwhich is a lift of `c`, i.e. the image of it under `F` is (iso) to `c`.\n\nWe will then use this as part of the definition of creation of limits:\nevery limit cone has a lift.\n\nNote this definition is really only useful when `c` is a limit already.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.liftable_cone.lifted_cone", "description": "Define the lift of a cone: For a cone `c` for `K \u22d9 F`, give a cone for `K`\nwhich is a lift of `c`, i.e. the image of it under `F` is (iso) to `c`.\n\nWe will then use this as part of the definition of creation of limits:\nevery limit cone has a lift.\n\nNote this definition is really only useful when `c` is a limit already.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.liftable_cone.valid_lift", "description": "Define the lift of a cone: For a cone `c` for `K \u22d9 F`, give a cone for `K`\nwhich is a lift of `c`, i.e. the image of it under `F` is (iso) to `c`.\n\nWe will then use this as part of the definition of creation of limits:\nevery limit cone has a lift.\n\nNote this definition is really only useful when `c` is a limit already.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_colimit_of_fully_faithful_of_iso'", "description": "When `F` is fully faithful, to show that `F` creates the colimit for `K` it suffices to show that\na colimit point is in the essential image of `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.has_limits_of_shape_of_has_limits_of_shape_creates_limits_of_shape", "description": "If `F` creates limits of shape `J`, and `D` has limits of shape `J`, then\n`C` has limits of shape `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lifts_to_colimit", "description": "A helper to show a functor creates colimits. In particular, if we can show\nthat for any limit cocone `c` for `K \u22d9 F`, there is a lift of it which is\na limit and `F` reflects isomorphisms, then `F` creates colimits.\nUsually, `F` creating colimits says that _any_ lift of `c` is a colimit, but\nhere we only need to show that our particular lift of `c` is a colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lifts_to_colimit.to_liftable_cocone", "description": "A helper to show a functor creates colimits. In particular, if we can show\nthat for any limit cocone `c` for `K \u22d9 F`, there is a lift of it which is\na limit and `F` reflects isomorphisms, then `F` creates colimits.\nUsually, `F` creating colimits says that _any_ lift of `c` is a colimit, but\nhere we only need to show that our particular lift of `c` is a colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lifts_to_colimit.makes_colimit", "description": "A helper to show a functor creates colimits. In particular, if we can show\nthat for any limit cocone `c` for `K \u22d9 F`, there is a lift of it which is\na limit and `F` reflects isomorphisms, then `F` creates colimits.\nUsually, `F` creating colimits says that _any_ lift of `c` is a colimit, but\nhere we only need to show that our particular lift of `c` is a colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lifted_limit_is_limit", "description": "The lifted cone is a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_colimit", "description": "Dual of definition 3.3.1 of [Riehl].\nWe say that `F` creates colimits of `K` if, given any limit cocone `c` for\n`K \u22d9 F` (i.e. below) we can lift it to a cocone \"above\", and further that `F`\nreflects limits for `K`.\n\nIf `F` reflects isomorphisms, it suffices to show only that the lifted cocone is\na limit - see `creates_limit_of_reflects_iso`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_colimit.to_reflects_colimit", "description": "Dual of definition 3.3.1 of [Riehl].\nWe say that `F` creates colimits of `K` if, given any limit cocone `c` for\n`K \u22d9 F` (i.e. below) we can lift it to a cocone \"above\", and further that `F`\nreflects limits for `K`.\n\nIf `F` reflects isomorphisms, it suffices to show only that the lifted cocone is\na limit - see `creates_limit_of_reflects_iso`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_colimit.lifts", "description": "Dual of definition 3.3.1 of [Riehl].\nWe say that `F` creates colimits of `K` if, given any limit cocone `c` for\n`K \u22d9 F` (i.e. below) we can lift it to a cocone \"above\", and further that `F`\nreflects limits for `K`.\n\nIf `F` reflects isomorphisms, it suffices to show only that the lifted cocone is\na limit - see `creates_limit_of_reflects_iso`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_limit_of_fully_faithful_of_lift", "description": "When `F` is fully faithful, and `has_limit (K \u22d9 F)`, to show that `F` creates the limit for `K`\nit suffices to exhibit a lift of the chosen limit cone for `K \u22d9 F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lifted_colimit_maps_to_original", "description": "The lifted cocone has an image isomorphic to the original cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.inhabited_lifts_to_limit", "description": "Satisfy the inhabited linter", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_colimits", "description": "`F` creates small colimits if it creates colimits of shape `J` for any small `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_limit_of_fully_faithful_of_iso", "description": "When `F` is fully faithful, and `has_limit (K \u22d9 F)`, to show that `F` creates the limit for `K`\nit suffices to show that the chosen limit point is in the essential image of `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_limit_of_creates_limit_and_has_limit", "description": "`F` preserves the limit of `K` if it creates the limit and `K \u22d9 F` has the limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_colimit_of_nat_iso", "description": "If `F` creates the colimit of `K` and `F \u2245 G`, then `G` creates the colimit of `K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lifted_colimit_is_colimit", "description": "The lifted cocone is a colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_colimit_of_fully_faithful_of_iso", "description": "When `F` is fully faithful, and `has_colimit (K \u22d9 F)`, to show that `F` creates the colimit for `K`\nit suffices to show that the chosen colimit point is in the essential image of `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_limit_of_fully_faithful_of_lift'", "description": "When `F` is fully faithful, to show that `F` creates the limit for `K` it suffices to exhibit a lift\nof a limit cone for `K \u22d9 F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.liftable_cocone", "description": "Define the lift of a cocone: For a cocone `c` for `K \u22d9 F`, give a cocone for\n`K` which is a lift of `c`, i.e. the image of it under `F` is (iso) to `c`.\n\nWe will then use this as part of the definition of creation of colimits:\nevery limit cocone has a lift.\n\nNote this definition is really only useful when `c` is a colimit already.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.liftable_cocone.lifted_cocone", "description": "Define the lift of a cocone: For a cocone `c` for `K \u22d9 F`, give a cocone for\n`K` which is a lift of `c`, i.e. the image of it under `F` is (iso) to `c`.\n\nWe will then use this as part of the definition of creation of colimits:\nevery limit cocone has a lift.\n\nNote this definition is really only useful when `c` is a colimit already.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.liftable_cocone.valid_lift", "description": "Define the lift of a cocone: For a cocone `c` for `K \u22d9 F`, give a cocone for\n`K` which is a lift of `c`, i.e. the image of it under `F` is (iso) to `c`.\n\nWe will then use this as part of the definition of creation of colimits:\nevery limit cocone has a lift.\n\nNote this definition is really only useful when `c` is a colimit already.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.creates_limit_of_fully_faithful_of_iso'", "description": "When `F` is fully faithful, to show that `F` creates the limit for `K` it suffices to show that a\nlimit point is in the essential image of `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiples.is_add_submonoid", "description": "The set of natural number multiples of an element of\nan `add_monoid` `M` is an `add_submonoid` of `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_submonoid_Union_of_directed", "description": "The union of an indexed, directed, nonempty set\nof `add_submonoid`s of an `add_monoid` `M` is an `add_submonoid` of `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.subset_closure", "description": "A subset of an `add_monoid` is contained in the `add_submonoid` it generates.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.closure_subset", "description": "The submonoid generated by a set is contained in any submonoid that contains the set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.in_closure", "description": "The inductively defined membership predicate for the submonoid generated by a subset of a\n   monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.in_closure.basic", "description": "The inductively defined membership predicate for the submonoid generated by a subset of a\n   monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.in_closure.zero", "description": "The inductively defined membership predicate for the submonoid generated by a subset of a\n   monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.in_closure.add", "description": "The inductively defined membership predicate for the submonoid generated by a subset of a\n   monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "powers.one_mem", "description": "1 is in the set of natural number powers of an element of a monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "range.is_submonoid", "description": "The image of a monoid hom is a submonoid of the codomain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_submonoid.image", "description": "The image of a submonoid under a monoid hom is a submonoid of the codomain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.closure", "description": "The inductively defined `add_submonoid` genrated by a subset of an `add_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.in_closure", "description": "The inductively defined membership predicate for the `submonoid` generated by a subset of an\n   monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.in_closure.basic", "description": "The inductively defined membership predicate for the `submonoid` generated by a subset of an\n   monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.in_closure.one", "description": "The inductively defined membership predicate for the `submonoid` generated by a subset of an\n   monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.in_closure.mul", "description": "The inductively defined membership predicate for the `submonoid` generated by a subset of an\n   monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.is_submonoid_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.image_closure", "description": "The image under a monoid hom of the submonoid generated by a set equals the submonoid generated\n   by the image of the set under the monoid hom.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiples.self_mem", "description": "An element of an `add_monoid` is in the set of that element's natural number multiples.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.closure_subset", "description": "The `add_submonoid` generated by a set is contained in any `add_submonoid` that\ncontains the set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.closure.is_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiples.zero_mem", "description": "0 is in the set of natural number multiples of an element of an `add_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "powers.mul_mem", "description": "The set of natural number powers of an element of a monoid is closed under multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_submonoid.image", "description": "The image of an `add_submonoid` under an `add_monoid`\nhom is an `add_submonoid` of the codomain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_submonoid", "description": " `s` is a submonoid: a set containing 1 and closed under multiplication.\nNote that this structure is deprecated, and the bundled variant `submonoid M` should be\npreferred.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_submonoid.one_mem", "description": " `s` is a submonoid: a set containing 1 and closed under multiplication.\nNote that this structure is deprecated, and the bundled variant `submonoid M` should be\npreferred.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_submonoid.mul_mem", "description": " `s` is a submonoid: a set containing 1 and closed under multiplication.\nNote that this structure is deprecated, and the bundled variant `submonoid M` should be\npreferred.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.closure_mono", "description": "Given subsets `t` and `s` of a monoid `M`, if `s \u2286 t`, the submonoid of `M` generated by `s` is\n   contained in the submonoid generated by `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.mem_closure_union_iff", "description": "Given sets `s, t` of a commutative monoid `M`, `x \u2208 M` is in the submonoid of `M` generated by\n   `s \u222a t` iff there exists an element of the submonoid generated by `s` and an element of the\n   submonoid generated by `t` whose product is `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiples", "description": "The set of natural number multiples `0, x, 2x, ...` of an element `x` of an `add_monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_submonoid.power_subset", "description": "The set of natural number powers of an element of a submonoid is a subset of the submonoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_submonoid.finset_sum_mem", "description": "The sum of elements of an `add_submonoid` of an `add_comm_monoid` indexed by\na `finset` is an element of the `add_submonoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.closure_singleton", "description": "The submonoid generated by an element of a monoid equals the set of natural number powers of\n   the element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "univ.is_submonoid", "description": "A monoid is a submonoid of itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "univ.is_add_submonoid", "description": "An `add_monoid` is an `add_submonoid` of itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.of", "description": "Create a bundled additive submonoid from a set `s` and `[is_add_submonoid s]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_submonoid.smul_mem", "description": "An `add_submonoid` is closed under multiplication by naturals.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_submonoid.inter", "description": "The intersection of two `add_submonoid`s of an `add_monoid` `M` is\nan `add_submonoid` of M.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_submonoid.Inter", "description": "The intersection of an indexed set of submonoids of a monoid `M` is a submonoid of `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_submonoid", "description": " `s` is an additive submonoid: a set containing 0 and closed under addition.\nNote that this structure is deprecated, and the bundled variant `add_submonoid A` should be\npreferred.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_submonoid.zero_mem", "description": " `s` is an additive submonoid: a set containing 0 and closed under addition.\nNote that this structure is deprecated, and the bundled variant `add_submonoid A` should be\npreferred.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_submonoid.add_mem", "description": " `s` is an additive submonoid: a set containing 0 and closed under addition.\nNote that this structure is deprecated, and the bundled variant `add_submonoid A` should be\npreferred.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "powers.is_submonoid", "description": "The set of natural number powers of an element of a monoid `M` is a submonoid of `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "range.is_add_submonoid", "description": "The image of an `add_monoid` hom is an `add_submonoid`\nof the codomain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.is_add_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.is_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.closure_singleton", "description": "The `add_submonoid` generated by an element of an `add_monoid` equals the set of\nnatural number multiples of the element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "powers.self_mem", "description": "An element of a monoid is in the set of that element's natural number powers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.closure.is_add_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_submonoid.Inter", "description": "The intersection of an indexed set of `add_submonoid`s of an `add_monoid` `M` is\nan `add_submonoid` of `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "powers", "description": "The set of natural number powers `1, x, x\u00b2, ...` of an element `x` of a monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_submonoid.preimage", "description": "The preimage of an `add_submonoid` under an `add_monoid` hom is\nan `add_submonoid` of the domain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_submonoid.multiples_subset", "description": "The set of natural number multiples of an element\nof an `add_submonoid` is a subset of the `add_submonoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.exists_list_of_mem_closure", "description": " Given an element `a` of the submonoid of a monoid `M` generated by a set `s`, there exists\na list of elements of `s` whose product is `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.mem_closure_union_iff", "description": "Given sets `s, t` of a commutative `add_monoid M`, `x \u2208 M` is in the `add_submonoid`\nof `M` generated by `s \u222a t` iff there exists an element of the `add_submonoid` generated by `s`\nand an element of the `add_submonoid` generated by `t` whose sum is `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.of", "description": "Create a bundled submonoid from a set `s` and `[is_submonoid s]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_submonoid.inter", "description": "The intersection of two submonoids of a monoid `M` is a submonoid of `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.is_add_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.subset_closure", "description": "A subset of a monoid is contained in the submonoid it generates.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_submonoid_Union_of_directed", "description": "The union of an indexed, directed, nonempty set of submonoids of a monoid `M` is a submonoid\n   of `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.is_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_submonoid.multiset_prod_mem", "description": " The product of a multiset of elements of a submonoid of a `comm_monoid` is an element of\nthe submonoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_submonoid.finset_prod_mem", "description": " The product of elements of a submonoid of a `comm_monoid` indexed by a `finset` is an element\nof the submonoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.closure_mono", "description": "Given subsets `t` and `s` of an `add_monoid M`, if `s \u2286 t`, the `add_submonoid`\nof `M` generated by `s` is contained in the `add_submonoid` generated by `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_submonoid.pow_mem", "description": "Submonoids are closed under natural powers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_submonoid.list_sum_mem", "description": "The sum of a list of elements of an `add_submonoid` is an element of the\n`add_submonoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.image_closure", "description": "The image under an `add_monoid` hom of the `add_submonoid` generated by a set equals\nthe `add_submonoid` generated by the image of the set under the `add_monoid` hom.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_submonoid.list_prod_mem", "description": "The product of a list of elements of a submonoid is an element of the submonoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiples.add_mem", "description": "The set of natural number multiples of an element of an `add_monoid` is closed under addition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_submonoid.multiset_sum_mem", "description": "The sum of a multiset of elements of an `add_submonoid` of an `add_comm_monoid`\nis an element of the `add_submonoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.is_add_submonoid_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.exists_list_of_mem_closure", "description": "Given an element `a` of the `add_submonoid` of an `add_monoid M` generated by\na set `s`, there exists a list of elements of `s` whose sum is `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.closure", "description": "The inductively defined submonoid generated by a subset of a monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_submonoid.preimage", "description": "The preimage of a submonoid under a monoid hom is a submonoid of the domain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable_sub_inv_iff", "description": "The function `\u03bb x, (x - c)\u207b\u00b9` is integrable on `a..b` if and only if `a = b` or `c \u2209 [a, b]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_interval_integrable_of_tendsto_norm_at_top_of_deriv_is_O_punctured", "description": " If `f` is differentiable in a punctured neighborhood of `c`, `\u2016f x\u2016 \u2192 \u221e` as `x \u2192 c` (more\nformally, along the filter `\ud835\udcdd[\u2260] c`), and `f' = O(g)` along `\ud835\udcdd[\u2260] c`, where `f'` is the derivative\nof `f`, then `g` is not interval integrable on any nontrivial interval `a..b` such that\n`c \u2208 [a, b]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_interval_integrable_of_tendsto_norm_at_top_of_deriv_is_O_within_diff_singleton", "description": " If `a \u2260 b`, `c \u2208 [a, b]`, `f` is differentiable in the neighborhood of `c` within\n`[a, b] \\ {c}`, `\u2016f x\u2016 \u2192 \u221e` as `x \u2192 c` within `[a, b] \\ {c}`, and `f' = O(g)` along\n`\ud835\udcdd[[a, b] \\ {c}] c`, where `f'` is the derivative of `f`, then `g` is not interval integrable on\n`a..b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interval_integrable_inv_iff", "description": "The function `\u03bb x, x\u207b\u00b9` is integrable on `a..b` if and only if `a = b` or `0 \u2209 [a, b]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_interval_integrable_of_tendsto_norm_at_top_of_deriv_is_O_filter", "description": " If `f` is eventually differentiable along a nontrivial filter `l : filter \u211d` that is generated\nby convex sets, the norm of `f` tends to infinity along `l`, and `f' = O(g)` along `l`, where `f'`\nis the derivative of `f`, then `g` is not integrable on any interval `a..b` such that\n`[a, b] \u2208 l`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_interval_integrable_of_sub_inv_is_O_punctured", "description": " If `f` grows in the punctured neighborhood of `c : \u211d` at least as fast as `1 / (x - c)`,\nthen it is not interval integrable on any nontrivial interval `a..b`, `c \u2208 [a, b]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.uniform_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.arrow_congrSL_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.strong_topology.t2_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.strong_topology.has_basis_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.strong_topology.topological_add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.strong_uniformity", "description": " The uniform structure associated with `continuous_linear_map.strong_topology`. We make sure\nthat this has nice definitional properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.t2_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.has_continuous_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.precomp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.arrow_congrSL_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.arrow_congrSL_to_linear_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.strong_topology.has_continuous_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.postcomp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.precomp_coe_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.precomp", "description": " Pre-composition by a *fixed* continuous linear map as a continuous linear map.\nNote that in non-normed space it is not always true that composition is continuous\nin both variables, so we have to fix one of them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.strong_topology.embedding_coe_fn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.strong_topology", "description": " Given `E` and `F` two topological vector spaces and `\ud835\udd16 : set (set E)`, then\n`strong_topology \u03c3 F \ud835\udd16` is the \"topology of uniform convergence on the elements of `\ud835\udd16`\" on\n`E \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] F`.\n\nIf the continuous linear image of any element of `\ud835\udd16` is bounded, this makes `E \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] F` a\ntopological vector space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.has_basis_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.postcomp", "description": " Post-composition by a *fixed* continuous linear map as a continuous linear map.\nNote that in non-normed space it is not always true that composition is continuous\nin both variables, so we have to fix one of them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.uniform_add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.topological_add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.strong_topology.has_basis_nhds_zero_of_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.postcomp_coe_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.strong_uniformity.uniform_embedding_coe_fn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.arrow_congrSL_to_linear_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.strong_uniformity.uniform_add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.arrow_congr", "description": " A pair of continuous linear equivalences generates an continuous linear equivalence between\nthe spaces of continuous linear maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.topological_space", "description": " The topology of bounded convergence on `E \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] F`. This coincides with the topology induced by\nthe operator norm when `E` and `F` are normed spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.strong_uniformity_topology_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_equiv.arrow_congrSL", "description": " A pair of continuous (semi)linear equivalences generates a (semi)linear equivalence between the\nspaces of continuous (semi)linear maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_linear_map.has_basis_nhds_zero_of_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.equiv_quotient", "description": " The obvious equivalence between the quotient associated to an indexed partition and\nthe indexing type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.partition.le", "description": "Defining `\u2264` on partitions as the `\u2264` defined on their induced equivalence relations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.exists_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.setoid_of_disjoint_union", "description": "Makes an equivalence relation from a set of disjoints sets covering \u03b1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.classes_eqv_classes", "description": "Equivalence classes partition the type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.eq_of_mem_classes", "description": "If x \u2208 \u03b1 is in 2 equivalence classes, the equivalence classes are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.proj", "description": "The projection onto the quotient associated to an indexed partition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.is_partition.pairwise_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.eqv_class_mem", "description": "The equivalence classes of the equivalence relation defined by a set of sets\n   partitioning \u03b1 are elements of the set of sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.nonempty_of_mem_partition", "description": "A partition of `\u03b1` does not contain the empty set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.classes", "description": "Makes the equivalence classes of an equivalence relation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.equiv_quotient_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.is_partition", "description": " A collection `c : set (set \u03b1)` of sets is a partition of `\u03b1` into pairwise\ndisjoint sets if `\u2205 \u2209 c` and each element `a : \u03b1` belongs to a unique set `b \u2208 c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.mem_iff_index_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.mk'", "description": "The non-constructive constructor for `indexed_partition`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.exists_of_mem_partition", "description": "All elements of a partition of \u03b1 are the equivalence class of some y \u2208 \u03b1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.classes_inj", "description": "Two equivalence relations are equal iff their equivalence classes are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.eq_of_mem_eqv_class", "description": "If x \u2208 \u03b1 is in 2 elements of a set of sets partitioning \u03b1, those 2 sets are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.partition.order_iso", "description": "The order-preserving bijection between equivalence relations on a type `\u03b1`, and\n partitions of `\u03b1` into subsets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.rel_iff_exists_classes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition", "description": " Constructive information associated with a partition of a type `\u03b1` indexed by another type `\u03b9`,\n`s : \u03b9 \u2192 set \u03b1`.\n\n`indexed_partition.index` sends an element to its index, while `indexed_partition.some` sends\nan index to an element of the corresponding set.\n\nThis type is primarily useful for definitional control of `s` - if this is not needed, then\n`setoid.ker index` by itself may be sufficient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.eq_of_mem", "description": " Constructive information associated with a partition of a type `\u03b1` indexed by another type `\u03b9`,\n`s : \u03b9 \u2192 set \u03b1`.\n\n`indexed_partition.index` sends an element to its index, while `indexed_partition.some` sends\nan index to an element of the corresponding set.\n\nThis type is primarily useful for definitional control of `s` - if this is not needed, then\n`setoid.ker index` by itself may be sufficient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.some", "description": " Constructive information associated with a partition of a type `\u03b1` indexed by another type `\u03b9`,\n`s : \u03b9 \u2192 set \u03b1`.\n\n`indexed_partition.index` sends an element to its index, while `indexed_partition.some` sends\nan index to an element of the corresponding set.\n\nThis type is primarily useful for definitional control of `s` - if this is not needed, then\n`setoid.ker index` by itself may be sufficient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.some_mem", "description": " Constructive information associated with a partition of a type `\u03b1` indexed by another type `\u03b9`,\n`s : \u03b9 \u2192 set \u03b1`.\n\n`indexed_partition.index` sends an element to its index, while `indexed_partition.some` sends\nan index to an element of the corresponding set.\n\nThis type is primarily useful for definitional control of `s` - if this is not needed, then\n`setoid.ker index` by itself may be sufficient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.index", "description": " Constructive information associated with a partition of a type `\u03b1` indexed by another type `\u03b9`,\n`s : \u03b9 \u2192 set \u03b1`.\n\n`indexed_partition.index` sends an element to its index, while `indexed_partition.some` sends\nan index to an element of the corresponding set.\n\nThis type is primarily useful for definitional control of `s` - if this is not needed, then\n`setoid.ker index` by itself may be sufficient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.mem_index", "description": " Constructive information associated with a partition of a type `\u03b1` indexed by another type `\u03b9`,\n`s : \u03b9 \u2192 set \u03b1`.\n\n`indexed_partition.index` sends an element to its index, while `indexed_partition.some` sends\nan index to an element of the corresponding set.\n\nThis type is primarily useful for definitional control of `s` - if this is not needed, then\n`setoid.ker index` by itself may be sufficient.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.mk_classes", "description": "Makes an equivalence relation from a set of sets partitioning \u03b1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.eqv_class_mem'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.sUnion_classes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.classes_ker_subset_fiber_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.empty_not_mem_classes", "description": "The empty set is not an equivalence class.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.is_partition.finpartition", "description": "A finite setoid partition furnishes a finpartition", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.finite_classes_ker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.card_classes_ker_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.classes_mk_classes", "description": "The equivalence classes of the equivalence relation defined by a partition of \u03b1 equal\n   the original partition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.eqv_classes_disjoint", "description": "Distinct elements of a set of sets partitioning \u03b1 are disjoint.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.out_proj", "description": "This lemma is analogous to `quotient.mk_out'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.mem_classes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.proj_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.inhabited", "description": "On a unique index set there is the obvious trivial partition", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.class_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.quotient.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.proj_out", "description": "This lemma is analogous to `quotient.out_eq'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.proj_fiber", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.partition.partial_order", "description": "Defining a partial order on partitions as the partial order on their induced\n   equivalence relations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.quotient", "description": "The quotient associated to an indexed partition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.equiv_quotient_index_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.equiv_quotient_symm_proj_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.index_some", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.is_partition.sUnion_eq_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.out", "description": " A map choosing a representative for each element of the quotient associated to an indexed\npartition. This is a computable version of `quotient.out'` using `indexed_partition.some`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finpartition.is_partition_parts", "description": "A finpartition gives rise to a setoid partition", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.setoid", "description": " The equivalence relation associated to an indexed partition. Two\nelements are equivalent if they belong to the same set of the partition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.is_partition_classes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.partition.complete_lattice", "description": "A complete lattice instance for partitions; there is more infrastructure for the\n   equivalent complete lattice on equivalence relations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.mk_classes_classes", "description": "The equivalence relation made from the equivalence classes of an equivalence\n   relation r equals r.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.eq_eqv_class_of_mem", "description": "The elements of a set of sets partitioning \u03b1 are the equivalence classes of the\n   equivalence relation defined by the set of sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.proj_some_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.index_out'", "description": "The indices of `quotient.out'` and `indexed_partition.out` are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.is_partition.finpartition_parts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.eqv_classes_of_disjoint_union", "description": "A set of disjoint sets covering \u03b1 partition \u03b1 (classical).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "setoid.eq_iff_classes_eq", "description": "Two equivalence relations are equal iff all their equivalence classes are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "indexed_partition.some_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.antidiagonal", "description": " The antidiagonal of `s : \u03b1 \u2192\u2080 \u2115` is the finset of all pairs `(t\u2081, t\u2082) : (\u03b1 \u2192\u2080 \u2115) \u00d7 (\u03b1 \u2192\u2080 \u2115)`\nsuch that `t\u2081 + t\u2082 = s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.antidiagonal_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.antidiagonal_filter_snd_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.antidiagonal_filter_fst_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.antidiagonal'", "description": " The `finsupp` counterpart of `multiset.antidiagonal`: the antidiagonal of\n`s : \u03b1 \u2192\u2080 \u2115` consists of all pairs `(t\u2081, t\u2082) : (\u03b1 \u2192\u2080 \u2115) \u00d7 (\u03b1 \u2192\u2080 \u2115)` such that `t\u2081 + t\u2082 = s`.\nThe finitely supported function `antidiagonal s` is equal to the multiplicities of these pairs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.sum_antidiagonal_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.swap_mem_antidiagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.mem_antidiagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.prod_antidiagonal_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_field.trace_pow_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.trace_pow_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.charpoly_pow_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_field.matrix.charpoly_pow_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.subring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.subsemiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_p.subring'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "get_localized", "description": "Get all commands in the given locale and return them as a list of strings", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localized_attr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "print_localized_commands", "description": "Print all commands in a given locale", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localized_cmd", "description": "Add a new command to a locale and execute it right now.\n The new command is added as a declaration to the environment with name `_localized_decl.<number>`.\n This declaration has attribute `_localized` and as value a name-string pair.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "open_locale_cmd", "description": "Execute all commands in the given locale", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.command.localized notation", "description": "This consists of two user-commands which allow you to declare notation and commands localized to a\nlocale.\n\n* Declare notation which is localized to a locale using:\n```lean\nlocalized \"infix (name := my_add) ` \u22b9 `:60 := my_add\" in my.add\n```\n\n* After this command it will be available in the same section/namespace/file, just as if you wrote\n  `local infix (name := my_add) ` \u22b9 `:60 := my_add`\n\n* You can open it in other places. The following command will declare the notation again as local\n  notation in that section/namespace/file:\n```lean\nopen_locale my.add\n```\n\n* More generally, the following will declare all localized notation in the specified locales.\n```lean\nopen_locale locale1 locale2 ...\n```\n\n* You can also declare other localized commands, like local attributes\n```lean\nlocalized \"attribute [simp] le_refl\" in le\n```\n\n* To see all localized commands in a given locale, run:\n```lean\nrun_cmd print_localized_commands [`my.add].\n```\n\n* To see a list of all locales with localized commands, run:\n```lean\nrun_cmd do\n  m \u2190 localized_attr.get_cache,\n  tactic.trace m.keys -- change to `tactic.trace m.to_list` to list all the commands in each locale\n```\n\n* Warning: You have to give full names of all declarations used in localized notation,\n  so that the localized notation also works when the appropriate namespaces are not opened.\n\n* Note: In mathlib, you should always provide names for localized notations using the\n  `(name := ...)` parameter. This prevents issues if the localized notation overrides\n  an existing notation when it gets opened.\n\n* Warning: Due to limitations in the implementation, you cannot use `_` in localized notations.\n  (Otherwise `open_locale foo` will fail if `foo` is already opened or partially opened.)\n  Instead, you should use the `hole!` notation as a drop-in replacement. For example:\n```lean\n-- BAD\n-- localized \"infix (name := my_add) ` \u22b9[` R `] ` := my_add _ R\" in foo\n-- GOOD\nlocalized \"infix (name := my_add) ` \u22b9[` R `] ` := my_add hole! R\" in foo\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.units_inv_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.units_sq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.is_unit_iff_abs_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.units_pow_eq_pow_mod_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.sq_eq_one_of_sq_lt_four", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.units_coe_mul_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.units_mul_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.is_unit_sq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.units_pow_two", "description": "**Alias** of `int.units_sq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.neg_one_pow_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.sq_eq_one_of_sq_le_three", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_X_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_coeff_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_add_of_nat_degree_lt_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_nat_degree_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.mono_map_nat_degree_eq", "description": " Let `\u03c6 : R[x] \u2192 S[x]` be an additive map, `k : \u2115` a bound, and `fu : \u2115 \u2192 \u2115` a\n\"sufficiently monotone\" map.  Assume also that\n* `\u03c6` maps to `0` all monomials of degree less than `k`,\n* `\u03c6` maps each monomial `m` in `R[x]` to a polynomial `\u03c6 m` of degree `fu (deg m)`.\nThen, `\u03c6` maps each polynomial `p` in `R[x]` to a polynomial of degree `fu (deg p)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_nat_degree_lt_or_erase_lead_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.self_sub_C_mul_X_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.card_support_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_not_mem_erase_lead_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead", "description": " `erase_lead f` for a polynomial `f` is the polynomial obtained by\nsubtracting from `f` the leading term of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_add_of_nat_degree_lt_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.induction_with_nat_degree_le", "description": " An induction lemma for polynomials. It takes a natural number `N` as a parameter, that is\nrequired to be at least as big as the `nat_degree` of the polynomial.  This is useful to prove\nresults where you want to change each term in a polynomial to something else depending on the\n`nat_degree` of the polynomial itself and not on the specific `nat_degree` of each term.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_add_monomial_nat_degree_leading_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_card_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.card_support_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.self_sub_monomial_nat_degree_leading_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.map_nat_degree_eq_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.card_support_eq_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_monomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_degree_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_support_card_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_coeff_nat_degree", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_nat_degree_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_C_mul_X_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.ne_nat_degree_of_mem_erase_lead_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.map_nat_degree_eq_nat_degree", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_card_support'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_add_C_mul_X_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.card_support_eq_three", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.erase_lead_nat_degree_le_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.card_support_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.lt_nat_degree_of_mem_erase_lead_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "punit.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "punit.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "punit.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "punit_eq_star", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "punit_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.interval_cases.get_bounds", "description": "Inspect the local hypotheses for upper and lower bounds on a variable `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interval_cases.gives_lower_bound", "description": "If `e` easily implies `(%%n \u2265 %%b)`\nfor some explicit `b`,\nreturn that proof.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interval_cases.update_bounds", "description": "Inspect a given expression, using it to update a set of upper and lower bounds on `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interval_cases.combine_lower_bounds", "description": "Combine two lower bounds.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interval_cases.initial_upper_bound", "description": "Attempt to find an upper bound for the variable `n`, by evaluating `le_top n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.tactic.interval_cases", "description": "`interval_cases n` searches for upper and lower bounds on a variable `n`,\nand if bounds are found,\nsplits into separate cases for each possible value of `n`.\n\nAs an example, in\n```lean\nexample (n : \u2115) (w\u2081 : n \u2265 3) (w\u2082 : n < 5) : n = 3 \u2228 n = 4 :=\nbegin\n  interval_cases n,\n  all_goals {simp}\nend\n```\nafter `interval_cases n`, the goals are `3 = 3 \u2228 3 = 4` and `4 = 3 \u2228 4 = 4`.\n\nYou can also explicitly specify a lower and upper bound to use,\nas `interval_cases using hl hu`.\nThe hypotheses should be in the form `hl : a \u2264 n` and `hu : n < b`,\nin which case `interval_cases` calls `fin_cases` on the resulting fact `n \u2208 set.Ico a b`.\n\nYou can also explicitly specify a name to use for the hypothesis added,\nas `interval_cases n with hn` or `interval_cases n using hl hu with hn`.\n\nIn particular, `interval_cases n`\n1) inspects hypotheses looking for lower and upper bounds of the form `a \u2264 n` and `n < b`\n   (although in `\u2115`, `\u2124`, and `\u2115+` bounds of the form `a < n` and `n \u2264 b` are also allowed),\n   and also makes use of lower and upper bounds found via `le_top` and `bot_le`\n   (so for example if `n : \u2115`, then the bound `0 \u2264 n` is found automatically), then\n2) calls `fin_cases` on the synthesised hypothesis `n \u2208 set.Ico a b`,\n   assuming an appropriate `fintype` instance can be found for the type of `n`.\n\nThe variable `n` can belong to any type `\u03b1`, with the following restrictions:\n* only bounds on which `expr.to_rat` succeeds will be considered \"explicit\" (TODO: generalise this?)\n* an instance of `decidable_eq \u03b1` is available,\n* an explicit lower bound can be found amongst the hypotheses, or from `bot_le n`,\n* an explicit upper bound can be found amongst the hypotheses, or from `le_top n`,\n* if multiple bounds are located, an instance of `linear_order \u03b1` is available, and\n* an instance of `fintype set.Ico l u` is available for the relevant bounds.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interval_cases.combine_upper_bounds", "description": "Combine two upper bounds.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.interval_cases", "description": "`interval_cases n` searches for upper and lower bounds on a variable `n`,\nand if bounds are found,\nsplits into separate cases for each possible value of `n`.\n\nAs an example, in\n```lean\nexample (n : \u2115) (w\u2081 : n \u2265 3) (w\u2082 : n < 5) : n = 3 \u2228 n = 4 :=\nbegin\n  interval_cases n,\n  all_goals {simp}\nend\n```\nafter `interval_cases n`, the goals are `3 = 3 \u2228 3 = 4` and `4 = 3 \u2228 4 = 4`.\n\nYou can also explicitly specify a lower and upper bound to use,\nas `interval_cases using hl hu`.\nThe hypotheses should be in the form `hl : a \u2264 n` and `hu : n < b`,\nin which case `interval_cases` calls `fin_cases` on the resulting fact `n \u2208 set.Ico a b`.\n\nYou can specify a name `h` for the new hypothesis,\nas `interval_cases n with h` or `interval_cases n using hl hu with h`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interval_cases_using", "description": " Call `fin_cases` on membership of the finset built from\nan `Ico` interval corresponding to a lower and an upper bound.\n\nHere `hl` should be an expression of the form `a \u2264 n`, for some explicit `a`, and\n`hu` should be of the form `n < b`, for some explicit `b`.\n\nBy default `interval_cases_using` automatically generates a name for the new hypothesis. The name\ncan be specified via the optional argument `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interval_cases.gives_upper_bound", "description": "If `e` easily implies `(%%n < %%b)`\nfor some explicit `b`,\nreturn that proof.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interval_cases.mem_set_elems", "description": "Each element of `s` is a member of `set_elems s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interval_cases.set_elems", "description": "The finset of elements of a set `s` for which we have `fintype s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interval_cases.initial_lower_bound", "description": "Attempt to find a lower bound for the variable `n`, by evaluating `bot_le n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Pi.uniform_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Pi.uniformity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Pi.separated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Pi.uniform_continuous_proj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_continuous_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Pi.complete", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit_of_has_terminal_of_preserves_limit", "description": "If `G` preserves the terminal object and `C` has a terminal object, then the image of the terminal\nobject is terminal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit_map_cocone_empty_cocone_equiv", "description": "The map of an empty cocone is a colimit iff the mapped object is initial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_initial.of_iso_comparison", "description": "If the initial comparison map for `G` is an isomorphism, then `G` preserves initial objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial.is_initial_obj", "description": "The property of preserving initial objects expressed in terms of `is_initial`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_terminal_of_iso", "description": "If there is any isomorphism `G.obj \u22a4 \u2245 \u22a4`, then `G` preserves terminal objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_initial.iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit_map_cone_empty_cone_equiv", "description": "The map of an empty cone is a limit iff the mapped object is terminal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial_comparison.category_theory.is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal.is_terminal_of_obj", "description": "The property of reflecting terminal objects expressed in terms of `is_terminal`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_terminal_of_has_terminal_of_preserves_limit", "description": "If `C` has a terminal object and `G` preserves terminal objects, then `D` has a terminal object\nalso.\nNote this property is somewhat unique to (co)limits of the empty diagram: for general `J`, if `C`\nhas limits of shape `J` and `G` preserves them, then `D` does not necessarily have limits of shape\n`J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_initial_of_iso", "description": "If there is any isomorphism `\u22a5 \u2245 G.obj \u22a5 `, then `G` preserves initial objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_limits_of_shape_pempty_of_preserves_terminal", "description": "Preserving the terminal object implies preserving all limits of the empty diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial.is_initial_of_obj", "description": "The property of reflecting initial objects expressed in terms of `is_initial`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_terminal.iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal.is_terminal_obj", "description": "The property of preserving terminal objects expressed in terms of `is_terminal`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_terminal_of_is_iso", "description": "If there is any isomorphism `G.obj \u22a4 \u27f6 \u22a4`, then `G` preserves terminal objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit_of_has_initial_of_preserves_colimit", "description": "If `G` preserves the initial object and `C` has a initial object, then the image of the initial\nobject is initial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_terminal.of_iso_comparison", "description": "If the terminal comparison map for `G` is an isomorphism, then `G` preserves terminal objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_terminal.iso", "description": "If `G` preserves terminal objects, then the terminal comparison map for `G` is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_initial_of_is_iso", "description": "If there is any isomorphism `\u22a5 \u27f6 G.obj \u22a5`, then `G` preserves initial objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_colimits_of_shape_pempty_of_preserves_initial", "description": "Preserving the initial object implies preserving all colimits of the empty diagram.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_initial_of_has_initial_of_preserves_colimit", "description": "If `C` has a initial object and `G` preserves initial objects, then `D` has a initial object\nalso.\nNote this property is somewhat unique to colimits of the empty diagram: for general `J`, if `C`\nhas colimits of shape `J` and `G` preserves them, then `D` does not necessarily have colimits of\nshape `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_initial.iso", "description": "If `G` preserves initial objects, then the initial comparison map for `G` is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.terminal_comparison.category_theory.is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_mul_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.right_cancel_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_mul_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.is_right_cancel_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.has_involutive_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative", "description": " If `\u03b1` carries some additive structure, then `multiplicative \u03b1` carries the corresponding\nmultiplicative structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_add_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.add_zero_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_add_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.has_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.to_additive''_symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.is_cancel_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.to_additive'_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.to_additive'", "description": "Reinterpret `\u03b1 \u2192* multiplicative \u03b2` as `additive \u03b1 \u2192+ \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.is_right_cancel_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_multiplicative''_symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiplicative.right_cancel_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.is_left_cancel_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "additive.add_comm_semigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_mul_to_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.to_additive", "description": "Reinterpret `\u03b1 \u2192* \u03b2` as `additive \u03b1 \u2192+ additive \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_mul_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.to_multiplicative", "description": "Reinterpret `\u03b1 \u2192+ \u03b2` as `multiplicative \u03b1 \u2192* multiplicative \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_mul_mul