easure_theory.set_lintegral_nnnorm_condexp_ind_smul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.norm_condexp_L2_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.inner_condexp_L2_left_eq_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.inner_condexp_L2_eq_inner_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_smul_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.lintegral_nnnorm_condexp_L2_indicator_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L2_comp_continuous_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L2_indicator_eq_to_span_singleton_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integral_condexp_L2_eq", "description": "`condexp_L2` verifies the equality of integrals defining the conditional expectation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_smul", "description": "Conditional expectation of the indicator of a measurable set with finite measure, in L2.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_smul_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_on_condexp_L2_of_measure_ne_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_condexp_ind_smul", "description": " If the measure `\u03bc.trim hm` is sigma-finite, then the conditional expectation of a measurable set\nwith finite measure is integrable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_limit_preimage_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_limit_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_maps_to_of_is_compact_absorbing_of_is_open_of_omega_limit_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_limit_subset_closure_fw_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_limit_eq_bInter_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_limit_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.omega_limit_omega_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_limit_eq_Inter_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.omega_limit_image_eq", "description": "the \u03c9-limit of a forward image of `s` is the same as the \u03c9-limit of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_limit_eq_Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.is_invariant_omega_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "maps_to_omega_limit'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_limit_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_limit", "description": "The \u03c9-limit of a set `s` under `\u03d5` with respect to a filter `f` is\n   \u22c2 u \u2208 f, cl (\u03d5 u s).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_closure_subset_of_is_compact_absorbing_of_is_open_of_omega_limit_subset'", "description": " A set is eventually carried into any open neighbourhood of its \u03c9-limit:\nif `c` is a compact set such that `closure {\u03d5 t x | t \u2208 v, x \u2208 s} \u2286 c` for some `v \u2208 f`\nand `n` is an open neighbourhood of `\u03c9 f \u03d5 s`, then for some `u \u2208 f` we have\n`closure {\u03d5 t x | t \u2208 u, x \u2208 s} \u2286 n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_closure_subset_of_is_open_of_omega_limit_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonempty_omega_limit_of_is_compact_absorbing", "description": "The \u03c9-limit of a nonempty set w.r.t. a nontrivial filter is nonempty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_limit_mono_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_limit_Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_limit_mono_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_limit_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_omega_limit_iff_frequently", "description": "An element `y` is in the \u03c9-limit set of `s` w.r.t. `f` if the\n   preimages of an arbitrary neighbourhood of `y` frequently\n   (w.r.t. `f`) intersects of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_maps_to_of_is_open_of_omega_limit_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonempty_omega_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flow.omega_limit_image_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "maps_to_omega_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_omega_limit_iff_frequently\u2082", "description": "An element `y` is in the \u03c9-limit set of `s` w.r.t. `f` if the\n   forward images of `s` frequently (w.r.t. `f`) intersect arbitrary\n   neighbourhoods of `y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_closure_subset_of_is_compact_absorbing_of_is_open_of_omega_limit_subset", "description": " A set is eventually carried into any open neighbourhood of its \u03c9-limit:\nif `c` is a compact set such that `closure {\u03d5 t x | t \u2208 v, x \u2208 s} \u2286 c` for some `v \u2208 f`\nand `n` is an open neighbourhood of `\u03c9 f \u03d5 s`, then for some `u \u2208 f` we have\n`closure {\u03d5 t x | t \u2208 u, x \u2208 s} \u2286 n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_omega_limit_singleton_iff_map_cluster_point", "description": "An element `y` is in the \u03c9-limit of `x` w.r.t. `f` if the forward\n   images of `x` frequently (w.r.t. `f`) falls within an arbitrary\n   neighbourhood of `y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_limit_subset_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed_omega_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega_limit_image_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.is_algebraic.cardinal_mk_le_sigma_polynomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.is_algebraic.cardinal_mk_le_max", "description": "The cardinality of an algebraic extension is at most the maximum of the cardinality\nof the base ring or `\u2135\u2080`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_alg_closed.ring_equiv_of_cardinal_eq_of_char_eq", "description": " Two uncountable algebraically closed fields are isomorphic\nif they have the same cardinality and the same characteristic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_alg_closed.equiv_of_transcendence_basis", "description": " setting `R` to be `zmod (ring_char R)` this result shows that if two algebraically\nclosed fields have equipotent transcendence bases and the same characteristic then they are\nisomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_alg_closed.cardinal_eq_cardinal_transcendence_basis_of_aleph_0_lt", "description": " If `K` is an uncountable algebraically closed field, then its\ncardinality is the same as that of a transcendence basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_alg_closed.ring_equiv_of_cardinal_eq_of_char_zero", "description": " Two uncountable algebraically closed fields of characteristic zero are isomorphic\nif they have the same cardinality.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_alg_closed.cardinal_le_max_transcendence_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_alg_closed.is_alg_closure_of_transcendence_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.top_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.finset_inf_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.coe_to_nat_submodule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.to_add_submonoid_to_nat_submodule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_sup_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.to_nat_submodule", "description": "An additive submonoid is equivalent to a \u2115-submodule.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.has_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.to_add_subgroup_to_int_submodule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.top_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.eq_zero_of_coe_mem_of_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.sum_mem_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.to_int_submodule", "description": "An additive subgroup is equivalent to a \u2124-submodule.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.top_to_add_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.add_mem_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_supr_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_Sup_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.eq_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.bot_equiv_punit_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.infi_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.order_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.restrict_scalars_eq_top_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.sum_mem_bsupr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.bot_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.bot_to_add_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.eq_bot_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.complete_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_finset_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.inhabited'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_sup_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.disjoint_def'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.has_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.restrict_scalars_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.disjoint_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.eq_top_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.restrict_scalars_eq_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.order_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.restrict_scalars_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.ne_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.to_nat_submodule_to_add_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.top_equiv", "description": " The top submodule is linearly equivalent to the module.\n\nThis is the module version of `add_submonoid.top_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.to_nat_submodule_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.sub_mem_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.bot_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.nonzero_mem_of_bot_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.top_equiv_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.unique_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.inf_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.has_top", "description": "The universal set is the top element of the lattice of submodules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.exists_mem_ne_zero_of_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.to_int_submodule_to_add_subgroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.Inf_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.has_bot", "description": "The set `{0}` is the bottom element of the lattice of submodules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.to_int_submodule_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.coe_to_int_submodule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.bot_equiv_punit", "description": "The bottom submodule is linearly equivalent to punit as an `R`-module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.to_opposite", "description": " A ring homomorphism `f : R \u2192+* S` such that `f x` commutes with `f y` for all `x, y` defines\na ring homomorphism to `S\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.op_symm_apply_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.op_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.to_opposite_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.to_opposite", "description": " A non-unital ring homomorphism `f : R \u2192\u2099+* S` such that `f x` commutes with `f y` for all `x, y`\ndefines a non-unital ring homomorphism to `S\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.non_unital_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.op", "description": " A non-unital ring hom `\u03b1 \u2192\u2099+* \u03b2` can equivalently be viewed as a non-unital ring hom\n`\u03b1\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u2192+* \u03b2\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`. This is the action of the (fully faithful) `\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`-functor on morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.op", "description": " A ring hom `\u03b1 \u2192+* \u03b2` can equivalently be viewed as a ring hom `\u03b1\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u2192+* \u03b2\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`. This is the\naction of the (fully faithful) `\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`-functor on morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.from_opposite_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.unop", "description": "The 'unopposite' of a ring hom `\u03b1\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u2192+* \u03b2\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`. Inverse to `ring_hom.op`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.no_zero_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.from_opposite", "description": " A non-unital ring homomorphism `f : R \u2192\u2099* S` such that `f x` commutes with `f y` for all `x, y`\ndefines a non-unital ring homomorphism from `R\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.non_unital_comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.non_unital_non_assoc_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.mul_zero_one_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.semigroup_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.non_assoc_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.non_unital_comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.mul_zero_one_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.non_unital_comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.non_assoc_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.is_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.non_assoc_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.unop", "description": " The 'unopposite' of a non-unital ring hom `\u03b1\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56 \u2192\u2099+* \u03b2\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`. Inverse to\n`non_unital_ring_hom.op`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.non_unital_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.to_opposite_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.op_symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.non_unital_non_assoc_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.non_unital_non_assoc_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.non_assoc_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.no_zero_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.non_unital_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.from_opposite_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.group_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "non_unital_ring_hom.op_apply_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.non_unital_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.is_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.monoid_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.mul_zero_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.group_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.semigroup_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.non_unital_non_assoc_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.from_opposite", "description": " A ring homomorphism `f : R \u2192+* S` such that `f x` commutes with `f y` for all `x, y` defines\na ring homomorphism from `R\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.non_unital_comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_opposite.mul_zero_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.monoid_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_tower_to_alg_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.to_finsupp_iso_alg_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_tower_of_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.adjoin_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.eval\u2082_int_cast_ring_hom_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coe_aeval_eq_eval_ring_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_eq_zero_of_dvd_aeval_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.not_is_unit_X_sub_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.is_root_of_aeval_algebra_map_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_zero_eq_aeval_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_fn_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.alg_hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_bit1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_eq_sum_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_algebra_map_apply_eq_algebra_map_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_eq_sum_range'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.to_finsupp_iso_alg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.eval_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_tower_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_tower_comp_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.eval_mul_X_sub_C", "description": "The evaluation map is not generally multiplicative when the coefficient ring is noncommutative,\nbut nevertheless any polynomial of the form `p * (X - monomial 0 r)` is sent to zero\nwhen evaluated at `r`.\n\nThis is the key step in our proof of the Cayley-Hamilton theorem.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_tower", "description": "Version of `aeval` for defining algebra homs out of `R[X]` over a smaller base ring\n than `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.eval\u2082_algebra_map_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_bit0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_endomorphism", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.of_finsupp_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_zero_eq_aeval_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.subalgebra.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_X_left_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.adjoin_singleton_eq_range_aeval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_tower_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.ring_hom_eval\u2082_cast_int_ring_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_monomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_tower_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_subalgebra_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_tower_comp_to_alg_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_alg_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.dvd_term_of_is_root_of_dvd_terms", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.C_eq_algebra_map", "description": "When we have `[comm_semiring R]`, the function `C` is the same as `algebra_map R R[X]`.\n\n(But note that `C` is defined when `R` is not necessarily commutative, in which case\n`algebra_map` is not available.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_X_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.map_aeval_eq_aeval_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coe_aeval_eq_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval", "description": " Given a valuation `x` of the variable in an `R`-algebra `A`, `aeval R A x` is\nthe unique `R`-algebra homomorphism from `R[X]` to `A` sending `X` to `x`.\n\nThis is a stronger variant of the linear map `polynomial.leval`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_tower_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_alg_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.alg_hom_ext'", "description": "Extensionality lemma for algebra maps out of `A'[X]` over a smaller base ring than `A'`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_X_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.to_finsupp_iso_alg", "description": " Algebra isomorphism between `R[X]` and `add_monoid_algebra R \u2115`. This is just an\nimplementation detail, but it can be useful to transfer results from `finsupp` to polynomials.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.alg_hom_eval\u2082_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_alg_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.is_root_of_eval\u2082_map_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.to_finsupp_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.aeval_tower_comp_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.dvd_term_of_dvd_eval_of_dvd_terms", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.algebra_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.algebra_of_algebra", "description": "Note that this instance also provides `algebra R R[X]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.solve1", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.iterate_exactly", "description": "`iterate_exactly n t` : execute t n times", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.failed", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.add_lemmas_from_facts_core", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.definev", "description": "Add the hypothesis (h : t := v) in the current goal if v has type t.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.set_goals", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.ematch_using", "description": "Produce new facts using heuristic lemma instantiation based on E-matching.\nThis tactic tries to match patterns from the given lemmas with terms in\nthe main goal.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.get_config", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.trace_state", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.ematch_core", "description": "Produce new facts using heuristic lemma instantiation based on E-matching.\nThis tactic tries to match patterns from lemmas in the main goal with terms\nin the main goal. The set of lemmas is populated with theorems\ntagged with the attribute specified at smt_config.em_attr, and lemmas\nadded using tactics such as `smt_tactic.add_lemmas`.\nThe current set of lemmas can be retrieved using the tactic `smt_tactic.get_lemmas`.\n\nRemark: the given predicate is applied to every new instance. The instance\nis only added to the state if the predicate returns tt.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.add_lemmas_from_facts", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.add_ematch_lhs_lemma_from_decl", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.add_ematch_lemma_from_decl", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "simp_attr.pre_smt", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.seq", "description": "LCF-style AND_THEN tactic. It applies tac1, and if succeed applies tac2 to each subgoal produced by tac1", "p": "core"}, {"name": "using_smt", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.intron", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.trace", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.write", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "ematch_lhs", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.swap", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.when_tracing", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.monad_fail", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_state.to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_goal", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.when", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.slift", "description": "This lift operation will restart the SMT state.\nIt is useful for using tactics that change the set of hypotheses.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.classical", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.pose", "description": "Add (h : t := pr) to the current goal", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.intros", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.add_ematch_lemma_core", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_state.has_append", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.close", "description": "Try to close main goal by using equalities implied by the congruence\nclosure module.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.proof_for", "description": "Return a proof for e, if 'e' is a known fact in the main goal.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.add_ematch_lhs_lemma", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.focus1", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.mk_ematch_eqn_lemmas_for_core", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.alternative", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.get_facts", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.ematch", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.has_andthen", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.to_expr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.add_ematch_eqn_lemmas_for", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_state.mk", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.all_goals", "description": "Apply the given tactic to all goals.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_state", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.define", "description": "Add a new goal for t, and the hypothesis (h : t := ?M) in the current goal.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "ematch", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.slift_aux", "description": "See slift", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.add_ematch_lemma", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.get_refuted_facts", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.assertv", "description": "Add the hypothesis (h : t) in the current goal if v has type t.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.add_lemmas", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.fail", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.try", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.to_em_state", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.monad_state", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.note", "description": "Add (h : t) to the current goal, given a proof (pr : t)", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_config", "description": "Configuration for the smt_state object.\n\n- em_attr: is the attribute name for the hinst_lemmas\n  that are used for ematching", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_config.cc_cfg", "description": "Configuration for the smt_state object.\n\n- em_attr: is the attribute name for the hinst_lemmas\n  that are used for ematching", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_config.em_cfg", "description": "Configuration for the smt_state object.\n\n- em_attr: is the attribute name for the hinst_lemmas\n  that are used for ematching", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_config.pre_cfg", "description": "Configuration for the smt_state object.\n\n- em_attr: is the attribute name for the hinst_lemmas\n  that are used for ematching", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_config.em_attr", "description": "Configuration for the smt_state object.\n\n- em_attr: is the attribute name for the hinst_lemmas\n  that are used for ematching", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.assert", "description": "Add a new goal for t, and the hypothesis (h : t) in the current goal.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.get_lemmas", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.has_monad_lift", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.get_goals", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.iterate_at_most", "description": "`iterate_at_most n t`: repeat the given tactic at most n times or until t fails", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.iterate", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.eblast", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.intro_lst", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.monad", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.read", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_pre_config", "description": "Configuration for the smt tactic preprocessor. The preprocessor\nis applied whenever a new hypothesis is introduced.\n\n- simp_attr: is the attribute name for the simplification lemmas\n  that are used during the preprocessing step.\n\n- max_steps: it is the maximum number of steps performed by the simplifier.\n\n- zeta: if tt, then zeta reduction (i.e., unfolding let-expressions)\n  is used during preprocessing.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_pre_config.simp_attr", "description": "Configuration for the smt tactic preprocessor. The preprocessor\nis applied whenever a new hypothesis is introduced.\n\n- simp_attr: is the attribute name for the simplification lemmas\n  that are used during the preprocessing step.\n\n- max_steps: it is the maximum number of steps performed by the simplifier.\n\n- zeta: if tt, then zeta reduction (i.e., unfolding let-expressions)\n  is used during preprocessing.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_pre_config.max_steps", "description": "Configuration for the smt tactic preprocessor. The preprocessor\nis applied whenever a new hypothesis is introduced.\n\n- simp_attr: is the attribute name for the simplification lemmas\n  that are used during the preprocessing step.\n\n- max_steps: it is the maximum number of steps performed by the simplifier.\n\n- zeta: if tt, then zeta reduction (i.e., unfolding let-expressions)\n  is used during preprocessing.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_pre_config.zeta", "description": "Configuration for the smt tactic preprocessor. The preprocessor\nis applied whenever a new hypothesis is introduced.\n\n- simp_attr: is the attribute name for the simplification lemmas\n  that are used during the preprocessing step.\n\n- max_steps: it is the maximum number of steps performed by the simplifier.\n\n- zeta: if tt, then zeta reduction (i.e., unfolding let-expressions)\n  is used during preprocessing.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.to_cc_state", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.by_contradiction", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.by_cases", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.induction", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "using_smt_with", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic_to_smt_tactic", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.set_lemmas", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.destruct", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.add_ematch_eqn_lemmas_for_core", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_config.set_classical", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.refutation_for", "description": "Return a refutation for e (i.e., a proof for (not e)), if 'e' has been refuted in the main goal.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.add_ematch_lemma_from_decl_core", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.num_goals", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_tactic.preprocess", "description": "Preprocess the given term using the same simplifications rules used when\nwe introduce a new hypothesis. The result is pair containing the resulting\nterm and a proof that it is equal to the given one.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "smt_state.classical", "description": "Return tt iff classical excluded middle was enabled at  smt_state.mk", "p": "core"}, {"name": "finset.nat.antidiagonal_succ_succ'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.map_swap_antidiagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.sigma_antidiagonal_equiv_prod", "description": "The disjoint union of antidiagonals `\u03a3 (n : \u2115), antidiagonal n` is equivalent to the product\n   `\u2115 \u00d7 \u2115`. This is such an equivalence, obtained by mapping `(n, (k, l))` to `(k, l)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.filter_snd_eq_antidiagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.antidiagonal.snd_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.mem_antidiagonal", "description": "A pair (i, j) is contained in the antidiagonal of `n` if and only if `i + j = n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.filter_fst_eq_antidiagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.sigma_antidiagonal_equiv_prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.sigma_antidiagonal_equiv_prod_symm_apply_snd_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.sigma_antidiagonal_equiv_prod_symm_apply_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.antidiagonal_zero", "description": "The antidiagonal of `0` is the list `[(0, 0)]`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.antidiagonal.fst_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.antidiagonal_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.antidiagonal_congr", "description": "A point in the antidiagonal is determined by its first co-ordinate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.antidiagonal", "description": "The antidiagonal of a natural number `n` is\n   the finset of pairs `(i, j)` such that `i + j = n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.antidiagonal_succ'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.card_antidiagonal", "description": "The cardinality of the antidiagonal of `n` is `n + 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.independent.linear_independent", "description": " If a family of submodules is `independent`, then a choice of nonzero vector from each submodule\nforms a linearly independent family.\n\nSee also `complete_lattice.independent.linear_independent'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dfinsupp_sum_add_hom_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.lsum_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.map_range.linear_map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.lmk_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.add_comm_monoid_of_linear_map", "description": " Typeclass inference can't find `dfinsupp.add_comm_monoid` without help for this case.\nThis instance allows it to be found where it is needed on the LHS of the colon in\n`dfinsupp.module_of_linear_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.lhom_ext", "description": "Two `R`-linear maps from `\u03a0\u2080 i, M i` which agree on each `single i x` agree everywhere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.coprod_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.map_range_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.independent.dfinsupp_sum_add_hom_injective", "description": " The canonical map out of a direct sum of a family of additive subgroups is injective when the\nadditive subgroups are `complete_lattice.independent`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_supr_iff_exists_dfinsupp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.independent_of_dfinsupp_sum_add_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.lapply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.coprod_map", "description": " Given a family of linear maps `f i : M i  \u2192\u2097[R] N`, we can form a linear map\n`(\u03a0\u2080 i, M i) \u2192\u2097[R] N` which sends `x : \u03a0\u2080 i, M i` to the sum over `i` of `f i` applied to `x i`.\nThis is the map coming from the universal property of `\u03a0\u2080 i, M i` as the coproduct of the `M i`.\nSee also `linear_map.coprod` for the binary product version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.map_range.linear_map", "description": "`dfinsupp.map_range` as an `linear_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.map_range.linear_equiv_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.independent_iff_forall_dfinsupp", "description": " Independence of a family of submodules can be expressed as a quantifier over `dfinsupp`s.\n\nThis is an intermediate result used to prove\n`complete_lattice.independent_of_dfinsupp_lsum_injective` and\n`complete_lattice.independent.dfinsupp_lsum_injective`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.independent_iff_dfinsupp_lsum_injective", "description": " A family of submodules over an additive group are independent if and only iff `dfinsupp.lsum`\napplied with `submodule.subtype` is injective.\n\nNote that this is not generally true for `[semiring R]`; see\n`complete_lattice.independent.dfinsupp_lsum_injective` for details.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.sum_map_range_index.linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.map_range.linear_equiv", "description": "`dfinsupp.map_range.linear_map` as an `linear_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.lsingle_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.independent_of_dfinsupp_sum_add_hom_injective'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.lsingle", "description": "`dfinsupp.single` as a `linear_map`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.lapply", "description": "Interpret `\u03bb (f : \u03a0\u2080 i, M i), f i` as a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_bsupr_iff_exists_dfinsupp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.lsum_single", "description": " While `simp` can prove this, it is often convenient to avoid unfolding `lsum` into `sum_add_hom`\nwith `dfinsupp.lsum_apply_apply`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.lhom_ext'", "description": " Two `R`-linear maps from `\u03a0\u2080 i, M i` which agree on each `single i x` agree everywhere.\n\nSee note [partially-applied ext lemmas].\nAfter apply this lemma, if `M = R` then it suffices to verify `\u03c6 (single a 1) = \u03c8 (single a 1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.map_range.linear_map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.map_range.linear_equiv_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_supr_finset_iff_exists_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.lmk", "description": "`dfinsupp.mk` as a `linear_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.module_of_linear_map", "description": " Typeclass inference can't find `dfinsupp.module` without help for this case.\nThis is needed to define `dfinsupp.lsum` below.\n\nThe cause seems to be an inability to unify the `\u03a0 i, add_comm_monoid (M i \u2192\u2097[R] N)` instance that\nwe have with the `\u03a0 i, has_zero (M i \u2192\u2097[R] N)` instance which appears as a parameter to the\n`dfinsupp` type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.lsum_comp_map_range_to_span_singleton", "description": "Combining `dfinsupp.lsum` with `linear_map.to_span_singleton` is the same as `finsupp.total`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.lsum_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.basis", "description": " The direct sum of free modules is free.\n\nNote that while this is stated for `dfinsupp` not `direct_sum`, the types are defeq.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.bsupr_eq_range_dfinsupp_lsum", "description": " The bounded supremum of a family of commutative additive submonoids is equal to the range of\n`dfinsupp.sum_add_hom` composed with `dfinsupp.filter_add_monoid_hom`; that is, every element in the\nbounded `supr` can be produced from taking a finite number of non-zero elements from the `S i` that\nsatisfy `p i`, coercing them to `\u03b3`, and summing them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.independent_iff_dfinsupp_sum_add_hom_injective", "description": " A family of additive subgroups over an additive group are independent if and only if\n`dfinsupp.sum_add_hom` applied with `add_subgroup.subtype` is injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.independent_iff_linear_independent_of_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.lsum", "description": " The `dfinsupp` version of `finsupp.lsum`.\n\nSee note [bundled maps over different rings] for why separate `R` and `S` semirings are used.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.independent_of_dfinsupp_lsum_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_lattice.independent.dfinsupp_lsum_injective", "description": " The canonical map out of a direct sum of a family of submodules is injective when the submodules\nare `complete_lattice.independent`.\n\nNote that this is not generally true for `[semiring R]`, for instance when `A` is the\n`\u2115`-submodules of the positive and negative integers.\n\nSee `counterexamples/direct_sum_is_internal.lean` for a proof of this fact.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.dfinsupp_sum_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.supr_eq_range_dfinsupp_lsum", "description": " The supremum of a family of submodules is equal to the range of `dfinsupp.lsum`; that is\nevery element in the `supr` can be produced from taking a finite number of non-zero elements\nof `p i`, coercing them to `N`, and summing them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.map_range.linear_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.map_range.linear_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_supr_iff_exists_dfinsupp'", "description": "A variant of `submodule.mem_supr_iff_exists_dfinsupp` with the RHS fully unfolded.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dfinsupp.map_range.linear_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_action.minimal_period_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action.minimal_period_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action.orbit_zpowers_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action.zpowers_quotient_stabilizer_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_action.orbit_zmultiples_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_action.orbit_zmultiples_equiv_symm_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_order_eq_card_zmultiples'", "description": "See also `add_order_eq_card_zmultiples`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_action.minimal_period_eq_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_action.orbit_zmultiples_equiv", "description": "The orbit `(\u2124 \u2022 a) +\u1d65 b` is a cycle of order `minimal_period ((+\u1d65) a) b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action.orbit_zpowers_equiv", "description": "The orbit `(a ^ \u2124) \u2022 b` is a cycle of order `minimal_period ((\u2022) a) b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.quotient_zmultiples_equiv_zmod", "description": "`\u2124` modulo multiples of `a : \u2124` is `zmod a.nat_abs`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_eq_card_zpowers'", "description": "See also `order_eq_card_zpowers`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_of_fin_order.finite_zpowers", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.quotient_span_equiv_zmod", "description": "`\u2124` modulo the ideal generated by `a : \u2124` is `zmod a.nat_abs`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action.zpowers_quotient_stabilizer_equiv", "description": "The quotient `(a ^ \u2124) \u29f8 (stabilizer b)` is cyclic of order `minimal_period ((\u2022) a) b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.quotient_zmultiples_nat_equiv_zmod", "description": "`\u2124` modulo multiples of `n : \u2115` is `zmod n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action.minimal_period_eq_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_action.orbit_zpowers_equiv_symm_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.quotient_span_nat_equiv_zmod", "description": "`\u2124` modulo the ideal generated by `n : \u2115` is `zmod n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_action.zmultiples_quotient_stabilizer_equiv", "description": "The quotient `(\u2124 \u2219 a) \u29f8 (stabilizer b)` is cyclic of order `minimal_period ((+\u1d65) a) b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_action.zmultiples_quotient_stabilizer_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_of_fin_add_order.finite_zmultiples", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.ppred", "description": "Partial predecessor operation. Returns `ppred n = some m`\n if `n = m + 1`, otherwise `none`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.psub", "description": "Partial subtraction operation. Returns `psub m n = some k`\n if `m = n + k`, otherwise `none`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.psub'", "description": "Same as `psub`, but with a more efficient implementation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.ppred_eq_none", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.psub'_eq_psub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pred_eq_ppred", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.ppred_eq_some", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.sub_eq_psub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.psub_eq_some", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.psub_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.ppred_eq_pred", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.psub_eq_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.psub_eq_none", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.beck_algebra_cofork_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.beck_algebra_cofork_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.free_coequalizer.bottom_map.category_theory.is_reflexive_pair", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.beck_coequalizer", "description": "The Beck cofork is a coequalizer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.free_coequalizer.\u03c0_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.free_coequalizer.bottom_map", "description": "The bottom map in the coequalizer diagram we will construct.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.beck_cofork_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.beck_cofork_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.free_coequalizer.top_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.free_coequalizer.top_map", "description": "The top map in the coequalizer diagram we will construct.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.beck_cofork", "description": "This is the Beck cofork. It is a split coequalizer, in particular a coequalizer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.beck_algebra_cofork", "description": "Construct the Beck cofork in the category of algebras. This cofork is reflexive as well as a\ncoequalizer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.free_coequalizer.bottom_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.beck_coequalizer_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.free_coequalizer.\u03c0", "description": "The cofork map in the coequalizer diagram we will construct.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.beck_split_coequalizer", "description": "The Beck cofork is a split coequalizer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.free_coequalizer.condition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monad.beck_algebra_coequalizer", "description": "The cofork constructed is a colimit. This shows that any algebra is a (reflexive) coequalizer of\nfree algebras.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.single_obj.groupoid", "description": "Groupoid structure on `single_obj \u03b1`.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0019>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.single_obj.difference_functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.single_obj.star", "description": "Abbreviation that allows writing `category_theory.single_obj.star` rather than\n`quiver.single_obj.star`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.single_obj.category_struct", "description": "One and `flip (*)` become `id` and `comp` for morphisms of the single object category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.to_functor", "description": " Reinterpret a monoid homomorphism `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` as a functor `(single_obj \u03b1) \u2964 (single_obj \u03b2)`.\nSee also `category_theory.single_obj.map_hom` for an equivalence between these types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.to_Cat", "description": "The fully faithful functor from `Mon` to `Cat`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.single_obj.map_hom", "description": " There is a 1-1 correspondence between monoid homomorphisms `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` and functors between the\n    corresponding single-object categories. It means that `single_obj` is a fully faithful\n    functor.\n\nSee <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/001F> --\nalthough we do not characterize when the functor is full or faithful.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.single_obj.id_as_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.single_obj.map_hom_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.to_Cat_full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.to_Aut", "description": "The units in a monoid are (multiplicatively) equivalent to\nthe automorphisms of `star` when we think of the monoid as a single-object category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.single_obj.difference_functor", "description": "Given a function `f : C \u2192 G` from a category to a group, we get a functor\n   `C \u2964 G` sending any morphism `x \u27f6 y` to `f y * (f x)\u207b\u00b9`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.id_to_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.to_Aut_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.single_obj.comp_as_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.to_Aut_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Mon.to_Cat_faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.single_obj.to_End", "description": "The endomorphisms monoid of the only object in `single_obj \u03b1` is equivalent to the original\n    monoid \u03b1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.comp_to_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.single_obj.to_End_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.single_obj", "description": "Abbreviation that allows writing `category_theory.single_obj` rather than `quiver.single_obj`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.single_obj.map_hom_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.single_obj.category", "description": "Monoid laws become category laws for the single object category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.single_obj.inv_as_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.single_obj.difference_functor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix'_comp_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.nondegenerate_to_bilin_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix'_to_bilin'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_bilin_to_matrix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_skew_adjoint_matrices_submodule'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.nondegenerate.to_matrix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.nondegenerate_to_bilin'_of_det_ne_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.mul_to_matrix'_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_bilin_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.is_adjoint_pair_equiv'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.nondegenerate_to_bilin'_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_bilin'_aux_std_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_bilin'_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.nondegenerate_to_matrix'_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "self_adjoint_matrices_submodule'", "description": " The submodule of self-adjoint matrices with respect to the bilinear form corresponding to\nthe matrix `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.nondegenerate_to_matrix_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_bilin'_to_matrix'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.nondegenerate_of_det_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.nondegenerate_to_bilin'_iff_nondegenerate_to_bilin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix'_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.mul_to_matrix_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix'_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilinear_form.to_matrix_aux_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix_comp_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_adjoint_pair_to_bilin'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skew_adjoint_matrices_submodule'", "description": " The submodule of skew-adjoint matrices with respect to the bilinear form corresponding to\nthe matrix `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.nondegenerate.to_matrix'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix_comp_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix", "description": " `bilin_form.to_matrix b` is the equivalence between `R`-bilinear forms on `M` and\n`n`-by-`n` matrices with entries in `R`, if `b` is an `R`-basis for `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_bilin'_aux_to_matrix_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_bilin'", "description": "The linear equivalence between `n \u00d7 n` matrices and bilinear forms on `n \u2192 R`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix'_comp_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix_aux_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.nondegenerate.to_bilin'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.nondegenerate.to_bilin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_bilin_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_adjoint_pair_to_bilin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pair_self_adjoint_matrices_submodule'", "description": " The submodule of pair-self-adjoint matrices with respect to bilinear forms corresponding to\ngiven matrices `J`, `J\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix_aux", "description": " The linear map from bilinear forms to `matrix n n R` given an `n`-indexed basis.\n\nThis is an auxiliary definition for the equivalence `matrix.to_bilin_form'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_bilin", "description": " `bilin_form.to_matrix b` is the equivalence between `R`-bilinear forms on `M` and\n`n`-by-`n` matrices with entries in `R`, if `b` is an `R`-basis for `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_bilin_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.nondegenerate_iff_det_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_pair_self_adjoint_matrices_submodule'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_bilin'_std_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix_aux_std_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix'", "description": "The linear equivalence between bilinear forms on `n \u2192 R` and `n \u00d7 n` matrices", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix'_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_self_adjoint_matrices_submodule'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.nondegenerate_to_bilin'_iff_det_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_bilin'_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix_basis_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_bilin'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix_mul_basis_to_matrix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.mul_to_matrix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.to_matrix_to_bilin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_bilin'_aux_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_bilin'_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_bilin_basis_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bilin_form.mul_to_matrix'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.to_bilin'_aux", "description": " The map from `matrix n n R` to bilinear forms on `n \u2192 R`.\n\nThis is an auxiliary definition for the equivalence `matrix.to_bilin_form'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.exists_ideal_over_prime_of_is_integral'", "description": " `comap (algebra_map R S)` is a surjection from the prime spec of `R` to prime spec of `S`.\n`hP : (algebra_map R S).ker \u2264 P` is a slight generalization of the extension being injective", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.exists_ideal_over_prime_of_is_integral", "description": " More general going-up theorem than `exists_ideal_over_prime_of_is_integral'`.\nTODO: Version of going-up theorem with arbitrary length chains (by induction on this)?\n  Not sure how best to write an ascending chain in Lean", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_maximal_of_is_integral_of_is_maximal_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_integral_closure.comap_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_maximal_of_is_integral_of_is_maximal_comap'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_integral_closure.comap_lt_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.comap_eq_of_scalar_tower_quotient", "description": " If there is an injective map `R/p \u2192 S/P` such that following diagram commutes:\n```lean\nR   \u2192 S\n\u2193     \u2193\nR/p \u2192 S/P\n```\nthen `P` lies over `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.eq_bot_of_comap_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.coeff_zero_mem_comap_of_root_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.injective_quotient_le_comap_map", "description": " Let `P` be an ideal in `R[x]`.  The map\n`R[x]/P \u2192 (R / (P \u2229 R))[x] / (P / (P \u2229 R))`\nis injective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_maximal_comap_of_is_integral_of_is_maximal'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.comap_ne_bot_of_integral_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient_mk_maps_eq", "description": "The identity in this lemma asserts that the \"obvious\" square\n```lean\n    R    \u2192 (R / (P \u2229 R))\n    \u2193          \u2193\nR[x] / P \u2192 (R / (P \u2229 R))[x] / (P / (P \u2229 R))\n```\ncommutes.  It is used, for instance, in the proof of `quotient_mk_comp_C_is_integral_of_jacobson`,\nin the file `ring_theory/jacobson`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.exists_coeff_ne_zero_mem_comap_of_root_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_integral_closure.is_maximal_of_is_maximal_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.comap_lt_comap_of_root_mem_sdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.exists_coeff_mem_comap_sdiff_comap_of_root_mem_sdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.algebra_quotient_map_quotient", "description": "`R / p` has a canonical map to `S / pS`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient_map_quotient.is_noetherian", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.algebra_map_quotient_map_quotient", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.tower_quotient_map_quotient", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.exists_ideal_over_maximal_of_is_integral", "description": " `comap (algebra_map R S)` is a surjection from the max spec of `S` to max spec of `R`.\n`hP : (algebra_map R S).ker \u2264 P` is a slight generalization of the extension being injective", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.exists_nonzero_mem_of_ne_bot", "description": "This technical lemma asserts the existence of a polynomial `p` in an ideal `P \u2282 R[x]`\nthat is non-zero in the quotient `R / (P \u2229 R) [x]`.  The assumptions are equivalent to\n`P \u2260 0` and `P \u2229 R = (0)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.integral_closure.is_maximal_of_is_maximal_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.integral_closure.eq_bot_of_comap_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.exists_coeff_ne_zero_mem_comap_of_non_zero_divisor_root_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_of_one_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_integral_closure.eq_bot_of_comap_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.comap_ne_bot_of_root_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.algebra_quotient_of_le_comap", "description": "If `P` lies over `p`, then `R / p` has a canonical map to `S / P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.mk_smul_mk_quotient_map_quotient", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.coeff_zero_mem_comap_of_root_mem_of_eval_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_maximal_comap_of_is_integral_of_is_maximal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.integral_closure.comap_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.comap_lt_comap_of_integral_mem_sdiff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.integral_closure.comap_lt_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.comap_ne_bot_of_algebraic_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable.nat_bodd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partrec.of_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable.sum_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable.vector_tail", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable.vector_to_list", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partrec\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable.list_nth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable.snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partrec.vector_m_of_fn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable.encode", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.rfind_min'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable.unpair", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable.encode_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.of_eq_tot", "description": 