iption": "An `add_comm_group_with_one` is an `add_group_with_one` satisfying `a + b = b + a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group_with_one.int_cast", "description": "An `add_comm_group_with_one` is an `add_group_with_one` satisfying `a + b = b + a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group_with_one.nat_cast", "description": "An `add_comm_group_with_one` is an `add_group_with_one` satisfying `a + b = b + a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group_with_one.one", "description": "An `add_comm_group_with_one` is an `add_group_with_one` satisfying `a + b = b + a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group_with_one.nat_cast_zero", "description": "An `add_comm_group_with_one` is an `add_group_with_one` satisfying `a + b = b + a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group_with_one.nat_cast_succ", "description": "An `add_comm_group_with_one` is an `add_group_with_one` satisfying `a + b = b + a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group_with_one.int_cast_of_nat", "description": "An `add_comm_group_with_one` is an `add_group_with_one` satisfying `a + b = b + a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group_with_one.int_cast_neg_succ_of_nat", "description": "An `add_comm_group_with_one` is an `add_group_with_one` satisfying `a + b = b + a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group_with_one.to_add_comm_monoid_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.int_cast", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.add", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.add_assoc", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.zero", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.zero_add", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.add_zero", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.nsmul", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.nsmul_zero'", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.nsmul_succ'", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.neg", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.sub", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.sub_eq_add_neg", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.zsmul", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.zsmul_zero'", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.zsmul_succ'", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.zsmul_neg'", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.add_left_neg", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.nat_cast", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.one", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.nat_cast_zero", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.nat_cast_succ", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.int_cast_of_nat", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.int_cast_neg_succ_of_nat", "description": "An `add_group_with_one` is an `add_group` with a `1`.\nIt also contains data for the unique homomorphisms `\u2115 \u2192 R` and `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_def", "description": "Default value for `add_group_with_one.int_cast`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.to_add_monoid_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.to_add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group_with_one.to_has_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group_with_one.to_add_group_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group_with_one.to_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_int_cast", "description": "Type class for the canonical homomorphism `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_int_cast.int_cast", "description": "Type class for the canonical homomorphism `\u2124 \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.cast_of_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.log", "description": " `log` as an arithmetic function `\u2115 \u2192 \u211d`. Note this is in the `nat.arithmetic_function`\nnamespace to indicate that it is bundled as an `arithmetic_function` rather than being the usual\nreal logarithm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.von_mangoldt_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.von_mangoldt_pos_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.von_mangoldt", "description": "The `von_mangoldt` function is the function on natural numbers that returns `log p` if the input can\nbe expressed as `p^k` for a prime `p`.\nIn the case when `n` is a prime power, `min_fac` will give the appropriate prime, as it is the\nsmallest prime factor.\n\nIn the `arithmetic_function` locale, we have the notation `\u039b` for this function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.von_mangoldt_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.von_mangoldt_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.von_mangoldt_ne_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.von_mangoldt_mul_zeta", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.von_mangoldt_apply_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.log_mul_moebius_eq_von_mangoldt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.von_mangoldt_le_log", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.moebius_mul_log_eq_von_mangoldt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.von_mangoldt_apply_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.zeta_mul_von_mangoldt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.log_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.von_mangoldt_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.von_mangoldt_apply_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.arithmetic_function.sum_moebius_mul_log_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.lift_to_diagram_limit_obj", "description": " An auxiliary definition to be used in the proof of the fact that\n`J.diagram_functor D X` preserves limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.sheafification.category_theory.limits.preserves_finite_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.diagram_functor.category_theory.limits.preserves_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.plus_functor.category_theory.limits.preserves_finite_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cone_comp_evaluation_of_cone_comp_diagram_functor_comp_evaluation_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.lift_to_plus_obj_limit_obj", "description": " An auxiliary definition to be used in the proof that `J.plus_functor D` commutes\nwith finite limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presheaf_to_Sheaf.limits.preserves_finite_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.sheafification.category_theory.limits.preserves_limits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.presheaf_to_Sheaf.limits.preserves_limits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.diagram_functor.category_theory.limits.preserves_limits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cone_comp_evaluation_of_cone_comp_diagram_functor_comp_evaluation_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.plus_functor.category_theory.limits.preserves_limits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.cone_comp_evaluation_of_cone_comp_diagram_functor_comp_evaluation", "description": " An auxiliary definition to be used in the proof of the fact that\n`J.diagram_functor D X` preserves limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.diagram_functor.category_theory.limits.preserves_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.grothendieck_topology.lift_to_plus_obj_limit_obj_fac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.restricted_yoneda_map_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.extend_along_yoneda_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.extend_along_yoneda_iso_Kan_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor_to_representables", "description": "A functor to the presheaf category in which everything in the image is representable (witnessed\nby the fact that it factors through the yoneda embedding).\n`cocone_of_representable` gives a cocone for this functor which is a colimit and has point `P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.restricted_yoneda", "description": "The functor taking `(E : \u2130) (c : C\u1d52\u1d56)` to the homset `(A.obj C \u27f6 E)`. It is shown in `L_adjunction`\nthat this functor has a left adjoint (provided `E` has colimits) given by taking colimits over\ncategories of elements.\nIn the case where `\u2130 = C\u1d52\u1d56 \u2964 Type u` and `A = yoneda`, this functor is isomorphic to the identity.\n\nDefined as in [MM92], Chapter I, Section 5, Theorem 2.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.extend_along_yoneda_iso_Kan_app_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.extend_along_yoneda_iso_Kan", "description": "Verify that `extend_along_yoneda` is indeed the left Kan extension along the yoneda embedding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.is_extension_along_yoneda", "description": "`extend_along_yoneda A` is an extension of `A` to the presheaf category along the yoneda embedding.\n`unique_extension_along_yoneda` shows it is unique among functors preserving colimits with this\nproperty (up to isomorphism).\n\nThe first part of [MM92], Chapter I, Section 5, Corollary 4.\nSee Property 1 of <https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension#properties>.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_left_adjoint_of_preserves_colimits", "description": "If `L` preserves colimits and `\u2130` has them, then it is a left adjoint. Note this is a (partial)\nconverse to `left_adjoint_preserves_colimits`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.restrict_yoneda_hom_equiv", "description": "(Implementation). The equivalence of homsets which helps construct the left adjoint to\n`colimit_adj.restricted_yoneda`.\nIt is shown in `restrict_yoneda_hom_equiv_natural` that this is a natural bijection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.extend_along_yoneda_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.restricted_yoneda_yoneda", "description": "The functor `restricted_yoneda` is isomorphic to the identity functor when evaluated at the yoneda\nembedding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.extend_along_yoneda.category_theory.limits.preserves_colimits", "description": "See Property 2 of https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension#properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.unique_extension_along_yoneda", "description": "Show that `extend_along_yoneda` is the unique colimit-preserving functor which extends `A` to\nthe presheaf category.\n\nThe second part of [MM92], Chapter I, Section 5, Corollary 4.\nSee Property 3 of https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension#properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cocone_of_representable_\u03b9_app", "description": "An explicit formula for the legs of the cocone `cocone_of_representable`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.yoneda_adjunction", "description": "Show `extend_along_yoneda` is left adjoint to `restricted_yoneda`.\n\nThe construction of [MM92], Chapter I, Section 5, Theorem 2.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nat_iso_of_nat_iso_on_representables", "description": "Given two functors L\u2081 and L\u2082 which preserve colimits, if they agree when restricted to the\nrepresentable presheaves then they agree everywhere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.restricted_yoneda_obj_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comp_yoneda_iso_yoneda_comp_Lan", "description": "`F \u22d9 yoneda` is naturally isomorphic to `yoneda \u22d9 Lan F.op`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.extend_of_comp_yoneda_iso_Lan_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.extend_of_comp_yoneda_iso_Lan_inv_app_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.is_initial", "description": "Show that `elements.initial A` is initial in the category of elements for the `yoneda` functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.elements.initial", "description": "The initial object in the category of elements for a representable functor. In `is_initial` it is\nshown that this is initial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.restricted_yoneda_obj_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comp_yoneda_iso_yoneda_comp_Lan_inv_app_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.extend_along_yoneda", "description": "The left adjoint to the functor `restricted_yoneda` (shown in `yoneda_adjunction`). It is also an\nextension of `A` along the yoneda embedding (shown in `is_extension_along_yoneda`), in particular\nit is the left Kan extension of `A` through the yoneda embedding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cocone_of_representable_naturality", "description": "The legs of the cocone `cocone_of_representable` are natural in the choice of presheaf.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.extend_along_yoneda_iso_Kan_app", "description": "Show that the images of `X` after `extend_along_yoneda` and `Lan yoneda` are indeed isomorphic.\nThis follows from `category_theory.category_of_elements.costructured_arrow_yoneda_equivalence`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.extend_along_yoneda_iso_Kan_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.extend_along_yoneda_iso_Kan_app_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.extend_along_yoneda_yoneda", "description": "Since `extend_along_yoneda A` is adjoint to `restricted_yoneda A`, if we use `A = yoneda`\nthen `restricted_yoneda A` is isomorphic to the identity, and so `extend_along_yoneda A` is as well.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_of_representable", "description": "The cocone with point `P` given by `the_cocone` is a colimit: that is, we have exhibited an\narbitrary presheaf `P` as a colimit of representables.\n\nThe result of [MM92], Chapter I, Section 5, Corollary 3.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.extend_of_comp_yoneda_iso_Lan", "description": "extending `F \u22d9 yoneda` along the yoneda embedding is isomorphic to `Lan F.op`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cocone_of_representable", "description": "This is a cocone with point `P` for the functor `functor_to_representables P`. It is shown in\n`colimit_of_representable P` that this cocone is a colimit: that is, we have exhibited an arbitrary\npresheaf `P` as a colimit of representables.\n\nThe construction of [MM92], Chapter I, Section 5, Corollary 3.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.comp_yoneda_iso_yoneda_comp_Lan_hom_app_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_left_adjoint_of_preserves_colimits_aux", "description": "If `L` preserves colimits and `\u2130` has them, then it is a left adjoint. This is a special case of\n`is_left_adjoint_of_preserves_colimits` used to prove that.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.cocone_of_representable_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.colimit_adj.restrict_yoneda_hom_equiv_natural", "description": "(Implementation). Show that the bijection in `restrict_yoneda_hom_equiv` is natural (on the right).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.smul_mem_pointwise_smul_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_coe_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.singleton_mul_subgroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.mem_inv_pointwise_smul_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.closure_induction''", "description": " An induction principle for closure membership. If `p` holds for `1` and all elements of\n`k` and their inverse, and is preserved under multiplication, then `p` holds for all elements of\nthe closure of `k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.pointwise_smul_le_pointwise_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.add_normal", "description": "The carrier of `H \u2294 N` is just `\u2191H + \u2191N` (pointwise set addition)\nwhen `N` is normal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.coe_pointwise_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.closure_mul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.inf_mul_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.smul_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.smul_normal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.mem_smul_pointwise_iff_exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.conj_smul_subgroup_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.closure_induction''", "description": "An induction principle for additive closure membership. If `p` holds for `0` and all\nelements of `k` and their negation, and is preserved under addition, then `p` holds for all\nelements of the additive closure of `k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.normal.conj_act", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.inv_subset_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.mem_inv_pointwise_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.mul_inf_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.pointwise_smul_le_pointwise_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.supr_induction", "description": " An induction principle for elements of `\u2a06 i, S i`.\nIf `C` holds for `0` and all elements of `S i` for all `i`, and is preserved under addition,\nthen it holds for all elements of the supremum of `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.equiv_smul_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.smul_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.sup_eq_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.normal_add", "description": "The carrier of `N \u2294 H` is just `\u2191N + \u2191H` (pointwise set addition)\nwhen `N` is normal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.smul_mem_pointwise_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.inf_add_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.pointwise_smul_to_add_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.pointwise_smul_le_pointwise_smul_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.sup_eq_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.mem_inv_pointwise_smul_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.add_inf_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.mem_pointwise_smul_iff_inv_smul_mem\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.pointwise_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.smul_mem_pointwise_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.smul_mem_pointwise_smul_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.sup_normal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.mem_smul_pointwise_iff_exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.smul_mem_pointwise_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.pointwise_smul_to_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.supr_induction'", "description": "A dependent version of `subgroup.supr_induction`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.conj_smul_le_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.closure_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.closure_induction_right", "description": "For additive subgroups generated by a single element, see the simpler\n`zsmul_induction_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.equiv_smul", "description": "Applying a `mul_distrib_mul_action` results in an isomorphic subgroup", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.smul_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.subset_pointwise_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.le_pointwise_smul_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.pointwise_smul_le_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.supr_induction", "description": " An induction principle for elements of `\u2a06 i, S i`.\nIf `C` holds for `1` and all elements of `S i` for all `i`, and is preserved under multiplication,\nthen it holds for all elements of the supremum of `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.pointwise_smul_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.pointwise_smul_le_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.pointwise_smul_subset_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.closure_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.closure_induction_right", "description": "For subgroups generated by a single element, see the simpler `zpow_induction_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.closure_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.le_pointwise_smul_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.smul_opposite_image_mul_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.pointwise_mul_action", "description": " The action on a subgroup corresponding to applying the action to every element.\n\nThis is available as an instance in the `pointwise` locale.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.le_pointwise_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.normal_mul", "description": "The carrier of `N \u2294 H` is just `\u2191N * \u2191H` (pointwise set product) when `N` is normal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.mem_pointwise_smul_iff_inv_smul_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.pointwise_smul_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.pointwise_smul_le_pointwise_smul_iff\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.smul_mem_pointwise_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.mem_pointwise_smul_iff_inv_smul_mem\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.mul_normal", "description": "The carrier of `H \u2294 N` is just `\u2191H * \u2191N` (pointwise set product) when `N` is normal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.mem_pointwise_smul_iff_inv_smul_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.smul_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.mem_inv_pointwise_smul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.pointwise_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.closure_to_add_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.supr_induction'", "description": "A dependent version of `add_subgroup.supr_induction`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.closure_induction_left", "description": "For additive subgroups generated by a single element, see the simpler\n`zsmul_induction_left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.pointwise_mul_action", "description": " The action on an additive subgroup corresponding to applying the action to every element.\n\nThis is available as an instance in the `pointwise` locale.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.equiv_smul_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.closure_to_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.neg_subset_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.coe_pointwise_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.subgroup_mul_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.closure_induction_left", "description": "For subgroups generated by a single element, see the simpler `zpow_induction_left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "neg_coe_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.vadd_opposite_image_add_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.coe_to_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.subtype", "description": "Embedding of a `subtype`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.sigma_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.sectr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtype.imp_embedding", "description": " A subtype `{x // p x}` can be injectively sent to into a subtype `{x // q x}`,\nif `p x \u2192 q x` for all `x : \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.option_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.sectr", "description": "Fixing an element `a : \u03b1` gives an embedding `\u03b2 \u21aa \u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.refl_to_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.sectl_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.to_embedding_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.mk_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.coe_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.Pi_congr_right_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.coe_option_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.of_is_empty", "description": "There is always an embedding from an empty type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.of_surjective", "description": "A right inverse `surj_inv` of a surjective function as an `embedding`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.apply_eq_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.sigma_mk_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.coe_eq_to_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.trans", "description": "Composition of `f : \u03b1 \u21aa \u03b2` and `g : \u03b2 \u21aa \u03b3`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.trans_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.some", "description": "Embedding into `option \u03b1` using `some`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.punit", "description": "Choosing an element `b : \u03b2` gives an embedding of `punit` into `\u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.coe_sum_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.embedding_congr_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding", "description": "`\u03b1 \u21aa \u03b2` is a bundled injective function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.to_fun", "description": "`\u03b1 \u21aa \u03b2` is a bundled injective function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.inj'", "description": "`\u03b1 \u21aa \u03b2` is a bundled injective function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.inl", "description": "The embedding of `\u03b1` into the sum `\u03b1 \u2295 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.swap_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtype_or_left_embedding_apply_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.equiv_symm_to_embedding_trans_to_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.inl_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.arrow_congr_right_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.arrow_congr_right", "description": " An embedding `e : \u03b1 \u21aa \u03b2` defines an embedding `(\u03b3 \u2192 \u03b1) \u21aa (\u03b3 \u2192 \u03b2)` that sends each `f`\nto `e \u2218 f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.sigma_map", "description": " If `f : \u03b1 \u21aa \u03b1'` is an embedding and `g : \u03a0 a, \u03b2 \u03b1 \u21aa \u03b2' (f \u03b1)` is a family\nof embeddings, then `sigma.map f g` is an embedding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.some_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.embedding_congr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.coe_quotient_out", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.refl", "description": "The identity map as a `function.embedding`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.pprod_map", "description": "If `e\u2081` and `e\u2082` are embeddings, then so is `\u03bb \u27e8a, b\u27e9, \u27e8e\u2081 a, e\u2082 b\u27e9 : pprod \u03b1 \u03b3 \u2192 pprod \u03b2 \u03b4`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.equiv_to_embedding_trans_symm_to_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.subtype_map", "description": "Restrict both domain and codomain of an embedding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.inr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.as_embedding_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.congr", "description": "Transfer an embedding along a pair of equivalences.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.coe_fn_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtype_or_left_embedding", "description": " A subtype `{x // p x \u2228 q x}` over a disjunction of `p q : \u03b1 \u2192 Prop` can be injectively split\ninto a sum of subtypes `{x // p x} \u2295 {x // q x}` such that `\u00ac p x` is sent to the right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtype.imp_embedding_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.prod_map", "description": "If `e\u2081` and `e\u2082` are embeddings, then so is `prod.map e\u2081 e\u2082 : (a, b) \u21a6 (e\u2081 a, e\u2082 b)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.coe_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.sectl", "description": "Fixing an element `b : \u03b2` gives an embedding `\u03b1 \u21aa \u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.embedding_congr", "description": " If `\u03b1\u2081 \u2243 \u03b1\u2082` and `\u03b2\u2081 \u2243 \u03b2\u2082`, then the type of embeddings `\u03b1\u2081 \u21aa \u03b2\u2081`\nis equivalent to the type of embeddings `\u03b1\u2082 \u21aa \u03b2\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.quotient_out", "description": "`quotient.out` as an embedding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.to_embedding", "description": " Convert an `\u03b1 \u2243 \u03b2` to `\u03b1 \u21aa \u03b2`.\n\nThis is also available as a coercion `equiv.coe_embedding`.\nThe explicit `equiv.to_embedding` version is preferred though, since the coercion can have issues\ninferring the type of the resulting embedding. For example:\n\n```lean\n-- Works:\nexample (s : finset (fin 3)) (f : equiv.perm (fin 3)) : s.map f.to_embedding = s.map f := by simp\n-- Error, `f` has type `fin 3 \u2243 fin 3` but is expected to have type `fin 3 \u21aa ?m_1 : Type ?`\nexample (s : finset (fin 3)) (f : equiv.perm (fin 3)) : s.map f = s.map f.to_embedding := by simp\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.embedding_congr_apply_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.refl_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.embedding_congr_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.embedding_congr_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.subtype_injective_equiv_embedding", "description": "The type of embeddings `\u03b1 \u21aa \u03b2` is equivalent to\n   the subtype of all injective functions `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subtype_or_left_embedding_apply_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.coe_prod_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.option_map", "description": "A version of `option.map` for `function.embedding`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.equiv_of_surjective", "description": "Convert a surjective `embedding` to an `equiv`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.sigma_mk", "description": "`sigma.mk` as an `function.embedding`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.coe_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.swap_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.coe_option", "description": "Embedding into `option \u03b1` using `coe`. Usually the correct synctatical form for `simp`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.inr", "description": "The embedding of `\u03b2` into the sum `\u03b1 \u2295 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.set_value", "description": " Change the value of an embedding `f` at one point. If the prescribed image\nis already occupied by some `f a'`, then swap the values at these two points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.coe_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.set_value_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.arrow_congr_left", "description": " An embedding `e : \u03b1 \u21aa \u03b2` defines an embedding `(\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b3) \u21aa (\u03b2 \u2192 \u03b3)` for any inhabited type `\u03b3`.\nThis embedding sends each `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b3` to a function `g : \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b3` such that `g \u2218 e = f` and\n`g y = default` whenever `y \u2209 range e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.injective.can_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.sum_map", "description": "If `e\u2081` and `e\u2082` are embeddings, then so is `sum.map e\u2081 e\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.congr_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.trans_to_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.Pi_congr_right", "description": " Define an embedding `(\u03a0 a : \u03b1, \u03b2 a) \u21aa (\u03a0 a : \u03b1, \u03b3 a)` from a family of embeddings\n`e : \u03a0 a, (\u03b2 a \u21aa \u03b3 a)`. This embedding sends `f` to `\u03bb a, e a (f a)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.as_embedding", "description": " Given an equivalence to a subtype, produce an embedding to the elements of the corresponding\nset.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.add_empty_constants_symm_is_expansion_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.of_is_empty_on_function", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.map_constants_inclusion_is_expansion_on", "description": "", 