o sum-languages induced by maps on the two factors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.is_expansion_on_reduct", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lequiv.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.injective.is_expansion_on_default", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.coe_con", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.of_is_empty_on_relation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.card_with_constants", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.sum_inl_on_function", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.sum_elim_is_expansion_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.add_constants", "description": "Adds constants to a language map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.injective", "description": "A language homomorphism is injective when all the maps between symbol types are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.injective.on_function", "description": "A language homomorphism is injective when all the maps between symbol types are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.injective.on_relation", "description": "A language homomorphism is injective when all the maps between symbol types are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.constants_on.Structure", "description": "Gives a `constants_on \u03b1` structure to a type by assigning each constant a value.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.map_constants_comp_sum_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.sum_inl_on_relation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.sum_inr_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.constants_on_map_is_expansion_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.funext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.card_constants_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lequiv.add_empty_constants_to_Lhom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lhom.unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Lequiv.symm_to_Lhom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.left_U_subset_right_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.lim_of_nmem_U", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_continuous_zero_one_of_closed", "description": " Urysohns lemma: if `s` and `t` are two disjoint closed sets in a normal topological space `X`,\nthen there exists a continuous function `f : X \u2192 \u211d` such that\n\n* `f` equals zero on `s`;\n* `f` equals one on `t`;\n* `0 \u2264 f x \u2264 1` for all `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.lim_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.lim_mem_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.left_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.approx_le_lim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.right_U", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU", "description": " An auxiliary type for the proof of Urysohn's lemma: a pair of a closed set `C` and its\nopen neighborhood `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.C", "description": " An auxiliary type for the proof of Urysohn's lemma: a pair of a closed set `C` and its\nopen neighborhood `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.U", "description": " An auxiliary type for the proof of Urysohn's lemma: a pair of a closed set `C` and its\nopen neighborhood `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.closed_C", "description": " An auxiliary type for the proof of Urysohn's lemma: a pair of a closed set `C` and its\nopen neighborhood `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.open_U", "description": " An auxiliary type for the proof of Urysohn's lemma: a pair of a closed set `C` and its\nopen neighborhood `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.subset", "description": " An auxiliary type for the proof of Urysohn's lemma: a pair of a closed set `C` and its\nopen neighborhood `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.lim", "description": " A continuous function `f : X \u2192 \u211d` such that\n\n* `0 \u2264 f x \u2264 1` for all `x`;\n* `f` equals zero on `c.C` and equals one outside of `c.U`;", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.approx_mem_Icc_right_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.approx_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.left_U_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.left", "description": " Due to `normal_exists_closure_subset`, for each `c : CU X` there exists an open set `u`\nsuch chat `c.C \u2286 u` and `closure u \u2286 c.U`. `c.left` is the pair `(c.C, u)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.approx_le_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.approx_of_nmem_U", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.approx_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.tendsto_approx_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.right", "description": " Due to `normal_exists_closure_subset`, for each `c : CU X` there exists an open set `u`\nsuch chat `c.C \u2286 u` and `closure u \u2286 c.U`. `c.right` is the pair `(closure u, c.U)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.approx_of_mem_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.lim_eq_midpoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.approx", "description": " `n`-th approximation to a continuous function `f : X \u2192 \u211d` such that `f = 0` on `c.C` and `f = 1`\noutside of `c.U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.approx_le_approx_of_U_sub_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.lim_of_mem_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.subset_right_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.approx_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.continuous_lim", "description": "Continuity of `urysohns.CU.lim`. See module docstring for a sketch of the proofs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.bdd_above_range_approx", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "urysohns.CU.lim_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "directed.finset_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.exists_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.add_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.zero_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.pure_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.sub_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.lift.of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.lift_add_group_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.pure_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.of_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.lift_add_group_hom", "description": " If `g : free_abelian_group X` and `A` is an abelian group then `lift_add_group_hom g`\nis the additive group homomorphism sending a function `X \u2192 A` to the term of type `A`\ncorresponding to the evaluation of the induced map `free_abelian_group X \u2192 A` at `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.seq_add_group_hom", "description": " If `f : free_abelian_group (\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2)`, then `f <*>` is an additive morphism\n`free_abelian_group \u03b1 \u2192+ free_abelian_group \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.map", "description": "The additive group homomorphism `free_abelian_group \u03b1 \u2192+ free_abelian_group \u03b2` induced from a\n map `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.lift", "description": "The map `free_abelian_group \u03b1 \u2192+ A` induced by a map of types `\u03b1 \u2192 A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.has_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.seq_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.of_mul_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.neg_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.map_of_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.lift.map_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.non_unital_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.map_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.is_lawful_monad", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.seq_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.lift_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.mul_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.zero_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.neg_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group", "description": "The free abelian group on a type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.add_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.induction_on'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.seq_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.of_mul_hom", "description": "`free_abelian_group.of` is a `monoid_hom` when `\u03b1` is a `monoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.map_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.lift_monoid_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.map_id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.induction_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.of_mul_hom_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.lift.unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.equiv_of_equiv", "description": "Isomorphic types have isomorphic free abelian groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.lift_neg'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.lift_monoid_symm_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.lift.ext", "description": "See note [partially-applied ext lemmas].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.of_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.of", "description": "The canonical map from \u03b1 to `free_abelian_group \u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.is_comm_applicative", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.one_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.monad", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.map_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.pempty_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.non_unital_non_assoc_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.punit_equiv", "description": "The free abelian group on a type with one term is isomorphic to `\u2124`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.lift.add'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.lift_monoid_coe_add_monoid_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.map_comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.seq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.sub_bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.map_pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.map_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_abelian_group.lift_monoid", "description": "If `f` preserves multiplication, then so does `lift f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.tendsto_ae_condexp", "description": " Part c of the **L\u00b9 martingale convergnce theorem**: Given a integrable function `g` which\nis measurable with respect to `\u2a06 n, \u2131 n` where `\u2131` is a filtration, the martingale defined by\n`\ud835\udd3c[g | \u2131 n]` converges almost everywhere to `g`.\n\nThis martingale also converges to `g` in L\u00b9 and this result is provided by\n`measure_theory.integrable.tendsto_snorm_condexp`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.tendsto_ae_condexp", "description": " **L\u00e9vy's upward theorem**, almost everywhere version: given a function `g` and a filtration\n`\u2131`, the sequence defined by `\ud835\udd3c[g | \u2131 n]` converges almost everywhere to `\ud835\udd3c[g | \u2a06 n, \u2131 n]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.not_frequently_of_upcrossings_lt_top", "description": " If a stochastic process has bounded upcrossing from below `a` to above `b`,\nthen it does not frequently visit both below `a` and above `b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale.tendsto_snorm_one_limit_process", "description": " Part a of the **L\u00b9 martingale convergence theorem**: a uniformly integrable submartingale\nadapted to the filtration `\u2131` converges a.e. and in L\u00b9 to an integrable function which is\nmeasurable with respect to the \u03c3-algebra `\u2a06 n, \u2131 n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale.upcrossings_ae_lt_top'", "description": "An L\u00b9-bounded submartingale has bounded upcrossings almost everywhere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale.exists_ae_tendsto_of_bdd", "description": "An L\u00b9-bounded submartingale converges almost everywhere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.ae_eq_condexp_limit_process", "description": " Part b of the **L\u00b9 martingale convergence theorem**: if `f` is a uniformly integrable martingale\nadapted to the filtration `\u2131`, then for all `n`, `f n` is almost everywhere equal to the conditional\nexpectation of its limiting process wrt. `\u2131 n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale.eq_condexp_of_tendsto_snorm", "description": " If a martingale `f` adapted to `\u2131` converges in L\u00b9 to `g`, then for all `n`, `f n` is almost\neverywhere equal to `\ud835\udd3c[g | \u2131 n]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale.ae_tendsto_limit_process_of_uniform_integrable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.tendsto_snorm_condexp", "description": " **L\u00e9vy's upward theorem**, L\u00b9 version: given a function `g` and a filtration `\u2131`, the\nsequence defined by `\ud835\udd3c[g | \u2131 n]` converges in L\u00b9 to `\ud835\udd3c[g | \u2a06 n, \u2131 n]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale.upcrossings_ae_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale.exists_ae_trim_tendsto_of_bdd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.tendsto_of_uncrossing_lt_top", "description": " A realization of a stochastic process with bounded upcrossings and bounded liminfs is\nconvergent.\n\nWe use the spelling `< \u221e` instead of the standard `\u2260 \u221e` in the assumptions since it is not as easy\nto change `<` to `\u2260` under binders.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale.ae_tendsto_limit_process", "description": " **Almost everywhere martingale convergence theorem**: An L\u00b9-bounded submartingale converges\nalmost everywhere to a `\u2a06 n, \u2131 n`-measurable function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.upcrossings_eq_top_of_frequently_lt", "description": " A stochastic process that frequently visits below `a` and above `b` have infinite\nupcrossings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.submartingale.mem_\u2112p_limit_process", "description": "The limiting process of an L\u1d56-bounded submartingale is L\u1d56.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable.tendsto_snorm_condexp", "description": " Part c of the **L\u00b9 martingale convergnce theorem**: Given a integrable function `g` which\nis measurable with respect to `\u2a06 n, \u2131 n` where `\u2131` is a filtration, the martingale defined by\n`\ud835\udd3c[g | \u2131 n]` converges in L\u00b9 to `g`.\n\nThis martingale also converges to `g` almost everywhere and this result is provided by\n`measure_theory.integrable.tendsto_ae_condexp`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.nim_add_nim_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.grundy_value_eq_mex_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.is_empty_nim_zero_left_moves", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.move_right_nim_heq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.unique_nim_one_right_moves", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.to_left_moves_nim_one_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.grundy_value_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.grundy_value_eq_mex_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.move_left_nim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.nim_one_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.to_left_moves_nim", "description": "Turns an ordinal less than `o` into a left move for `nim o` and viceversa.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.grundy_value_eq_iff_equiv_nim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.grundy_value_nim_add_nim", "description": " The Grundy value of the sum of two nim games with natural numbers of piles equals their bitwise\nxor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.to_right_moves_nim_symm_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.grundy_value", "description": "The Grundy value of an impartial game, the ordinal which corresponds to the game of nim that the\ngame is equivalent to", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.move_left_nim_heq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.unique_nim_one_left_moves", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.nim_zero_relabelling", "description": "`nim 0` has exactly the same moves as `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.left_moves_nim_rec_on", "description": "A recursion principle for left moves of a nim game.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.nim_one_move_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.grundy_value_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.nim_one_relabelling", "description": "`nim 1` has exactly the same moves as `star`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.left_moves_nim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.nim_add_fuzzy_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.right_moves_nim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.is_empty_nim_zero_right_moves", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.nim", "description": "The definition of single-heap nim, which can be viewed as a pile of stones where each player can\n take a positive number of stones from it on their turn.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.nim_one_move_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.to_right_moves_nim", "description": "Turns an ordinal less than `o` into a right move for `nim o` and viceversa.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.move_right_nim'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.nim_zero_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.move_left_nim'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.neg_nim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.grundy_value_eq_iff_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.nim_equiv_iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.move_right_nim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.grundy_value_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.grundy_value_iff_equiv_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.grundy_value_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.nim_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.nim_fuzzy_zero_of_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.equiv_nim_grundy_value", "description": "The Sprague-Grundy theorem which states that every impartial game is equivalent to a game of\nnim, namely the game of nim corresponding to the games Grundy value", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.to_left_moves_nim_symm_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.nim_birthday", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.default_nim_one_right_moves_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.default_nim_one_left_moves_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.to_right_moves_nim_one_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.nim_impartial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.nim_grundy_value", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.nim_add_equiv_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pgame.right_moves_nim_rec_on", "description": "A recursion principle for right moves of a nim game.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_locally_homeomorph_on.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_locally_homeomorph_on.mk", "description": " Proves that `f` satisfies `is_locally_homeomorph_on f s`. The condition `h` is weaker than the\ndefinition of `is_locally_homeomorph_on f s`, since it only requires `e : local_homeomorph X Y` to\nagree with `f` on its source `e.source`, as opposed to on the whole space `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_locally_homeomorph_on", "description": " A function `f : X \u2192 Y` satisfies `is_locally_homeomorph_on f s` if each `x \u2208 s` is contained in\nthe source of some `e : local_homeomorph X Y` with `f = e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_locally_homeomorph_on.continuous_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_locally_homeomorph.is_open_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_locally_homeomorph.continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_locally_homeomorph", "description": "A function `f : X \u2192 Y` satisfies `is_locally_homeomorph f` if each `x : x` is contained in\n the source of some `e : local_homeomorph X Y` with `f = e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_locally_homeomorph.mk", "description": " Proves that `f` satisfies `is_locally_homeomorph f`. The condition `h` is weaker than the\ndefinition of `is_locally_homeomorph f`, since it only requires `e : local_homeomorph X Y` to\nagree with `f` on its source `e.source`, as opposed to on the whole space `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_locally_homeomorph_on.continuous_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_locally_homeomorph.map_nhds_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_locally_homeomorph.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_locally_homeomorph_on.map_nhds_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_locally_homeomorph_iff_is_locally_homeomorph_on_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_locally_homeomorph.is_locally_homeomorph_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_lower_set.null_frontier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_antichain.volume_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.ord_connected.null_frontier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_upper_set.null_frontier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.ord_connected.null_measurable_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.transfer_nat_trans_self_symm_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.transfer_nat_trans_self_symm_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.transfer_nat_trans_self_symm_iso", "description": "If `f` is an isomorphism, then the un-transferred natural transformation is an isomorphism.\nThe converse is given in `transfer_nat_trans_self_symm_of_iso`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.transfer_nat_trans_self_symm_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.unit_transfer_nat_trans_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.transfer_nat_trans_self_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.transfer_nat_trans_self_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.transfer_nat_trans_self_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.transfer_nat_trans_self_adjunction_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.transfer_nat_trans", "description": "Suppose we have a square of functors (where the top and bottom are adjunctions `L\u2081 \u22a3 R\u2081` and\n`L\u2082 \u22a3 R\u2082` respectively).\n\n      C \u2194 D\n    G \u2193   \u2193 H\n      E \u2194 F\n\nThen we have a bijection between natural transformations `G \u22d9 L\u2082 \u27f6 L\u2081 \u22d9 H` and\n`R\u2081 \u22d9 G \u27f6 H \u22d9 R\u2082`.\nThis can be seen as a bijection of the 2-cells:\n\n         L\u2081                  R\u2081\n      C --\u2192 D             C \u2190-- D\n    G \u2193  \u2197  \u2193 H         G \u2193  \u2198  \u2193 H\n      E --\u2192 F             E \u2190-- F\n         L\u2082                  R\u2082\n\nNote that if one of the transformations is an iso, it does not imply the other is an iso.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.transfer_nat_trans_self_adjunction_id_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.transfer_nat_trans_self", "description": "Given two adjunctions `L\u2081 \u22a3 R\u2081` and `L\u2082 \u22a3 R\u2082` both between categories `C`, `D`, there is a\nbijection between natural transformations `L\u2082 \u27f6 L\u2081` and natural transformations `R\u2081 \u27f6 R\u2082`.\nThis is defined as a special case of `transfer_nat_trans`, where the two \"vertical\" functors are\nidentity.\nTODO: Generalise to when the two vertical functors are equivalences rather than being exactly `\ud835\udfed`.\n\nFurthermore, this bijection preserves (and reflects) isomorphisms, i.e. a transformation is an iso\niff its image under the bijection is an iso, see eg `category_theory.transfer_nat_trans_self_iso`.\nThis is in contrast to the general case `transfer_nat_trans` which does not in general have this\nproperty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.unit_transfer_nat_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.transfer_nat_trans_self_counit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.transfer_nat_trans_self_of_iso", "description": "If `f` is a natural transformation whose transferred natural transformation is an isomorphism,\nthen `f` is an isomorphism.\nThe converse is given in `transfer_nat_trans_self_iso`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.transfer_nat_trans_self_symm_of_iso", "description": "If `f` is a natural transformation whose un-transferred natural transformation is an isomorphism,\nthen `f` is an isomorphism.\nThe converse is given in `transfer_nat_trans_self_symm_iso`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.transfer_nat_trans_counit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.transfer_nat_trans_self_iso", "description": "If `f` is an isomorphism, then the transferred natural transformation is an isomorphism.\nThe converse is given in `transfer_nat_trans_self_of_iso`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_extr.fderiv_eq_zero", "description": "**Fermat's Theorem**: the derivative of a function at a local extremum equals zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_pos_tangent_cone_at_of_segment_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_max.has_deriv_at_eq_zero", "description": "**Fermat's Theorem**: the derivative of a function at a local maximum equals zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_max_on.has_fderiv_within_at_eq_zero", "description": " If `f` has a local max on `s` at `a`, `f'` is a derivative of `f` at `a` within `s`, and\nboth `y` and `-y` belong to the positive tangent cone of `s` at `a`, then `f' y \u2264 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_deriv_eq_zero", "description": "**Rolle's Theorem** `deriv` version", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_max.deriv_eq_zero", "description": "**Fermat's Theorem**: the derivative of a function at a local maximum equals zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_extr.has_deriv_at_eq_zero", "description": "**Fermat's Theorem**: the derivative of a function at a local extremum equals zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_min.fderiv_eq_zero", "description": "**Fermat's Theorem**: the derivative of a function at a local minimum equals zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.card_root_set_le_derivative", "description": " The number of real roots of a polynomial is at most the number of roots of its derivative plus\none.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.card_roots_to_finset_le_card_roots_derivative_diff_roots_succ", "description": " The number of roots of a real polynomial `p` is at most the number of roots of its derivative\nthat are not roots of `p` plus one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_min_on.fderiv_within_nonneg", "description": " If `f` has a local min on `s` at `a` and `y` belongs to the positive tangent cone\nof `s` at `a`, then `0 \u2264 f' y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_max_on.fderiv_within_nonpos", "description": " If `f` has a local max on `s` at `a` and `y` belongs to the positive tangent cone\nof `s` at `a`, then `f' y \u2264 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.card_roots_to_finset_le_derivative", "description": " The number of roots of a real polynomial is at most the number of roots of its derivative plus\none.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_Ioo_extr_on_Icc", "description": " A continuous function on a closed interval with `f a = f b` takes either its maximum\nor its minimum value at a point in the interior of the interval.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_extr.has_fderiv_at_eq_zero", "description": "**Fermat's Theorem**: the derivative of a function at a local extremum equals zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_local_extr_Ioo", "description": " A continuous function on a closed interval with `f a = f b` has a local extremum at some\npoint of the corresponding open interval.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_extr.deriv_eq_zero", "description": "**Fermat's Theorem**: the derivative of a function at a local extremum equals zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_has_deriv_at_eq_zero", "description": "**Rolle's Theorem** `has_deriv_at` version", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_max.has_fderiv_at_eq_zero", "description": "**Fermat's Theorem**: the derivative of a function at a local maximum equals zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.card_roots_le_derivative", "description": " The number of roots of a real polynomial (counted with multiplicities) is at most the number of\nroots of its derivative (counted with multiplicities) plus one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_min_on.has_fderiv_within_at_nonneg", "description": " If `f` has a local min on `s` at `a`, `f'` is the derivative of `f` at `a` within `s`, and\n`y` belongs to the positive tangent cone of `s` at `a`, then `0 \u2264 f' y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_max_on.fderiv_within_eq_zero", "description": " If `f` has a local max on `s` at `a` and both `y` and `-y` belong to the positive tangent cone\nof `s` at `a`, then `f' y = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pos_tangent_cone_at", "description": " \"Positive\" tangent cone to `s` at `x`; the only difference from `tangent_cone_at`\nis that we require `c n \u2192 \u221e` instead of `\u2016c n\u2016 \u2192 \u221e`. One can think about `pos_tangent_cone_at`\nas `tangent_cone_at nnreal` but we have no theory of normed semifields yet.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_max.fderiv_eq_zero", "description": "**Fermat's Theorem**: the derivative of a function at a local maximum equals zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_deriv_eq_zero'", "description": " **Rolle's Theorem**, a version for a function on an open interval: if `f` has the same limit\n`l` at `\ud835\udcdd[>] a` and `\ud835\udcdd[<] b`, then `deriv f c = 0` for some `c \u2208 (a, b)`. This version\ndoes not require differentiability of `f` because we define `deriv f c = 0` whenever `f` is not\ndifferentiable at `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_min.has_fderiv_at_eq_zero", "description": "**Fermat's Theorem**: the derivative of a function at a local minimum equals zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_has_deriv_at_eq_zero'", "description": " **Rolle's Theorem**, a version for a function on an open interval: if `f` has derivative `f'`\non `(a, b)` and has the same limit `l` at `\ud835\udcdd[>] a` and `\ud835\udcdd[<] b`, then `f' c = 0`\nfor some `c \u2208 (a, b)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_pos_tangent_cone_at_of_segment_subset'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_min.has_deriv_at_eq_zero", "description": "**Fermat's Theorem**: the derivative of a function at a local minimum equals zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_min_on.has_fderiv_within_at_eq_zero", "description": " If `f` has a local max on `s` at `a`, `f'` is a derivative of `f` at `a` within `s`, and\nboth `y` and `-y` belong to the positive tangent cone of `s` at `a`, then `f' y \u2264 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_max_on.has_fderiv_within_at_nonpos", "description": " If `f` has a local max on `s` at `a`, `f'` is the derivative of `f` at `a` within `s`, and\n`y` belongs to the positive tangent cone of `s` at `a`, then `f' y \u2264 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_min_on.fderiv_within_eq_zero", "description": " If `f` has a local min on `s` at `a` and both `y` and `-y` belong to the positive tangent cone\nof `s` at `a`, then `f' y = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pos_tangent_cone_at_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pos_tangent_cone_at_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_local_min.deriv_eq_zero", "description": "**Fermat's Theorem**: the derivative of a function at a local minimum equals zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.map_absolutely_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.is_uniform.pdf_to_real_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.of_real_to_real_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.quasi_measure_preserving_has_pdf'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.to_quasi_measure_preserving", "description": "A random variable that `has_pdf` is quasi-measure preserving.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.is_uniform.has_pdf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.is_uniform", "description": " A random variable `X` has uniform distribution if it has a probability density function `f`\nwith support `s` such that `f = (\u03bc s)\u207b\u00b9 1\u209b` a.e. where `1\u209b` is the indicator function for `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.integral_fun_mul_eq_integral", "description": " **The Law of the Unconscious Statistician**: Given a random variable `X` and a measurable\nfunction `f`, `f \u2218 X` is a random variable with expectation `\u222b x, f x * pdf X \u2202\u03bc`\nwhere `\u03bc` is a measure on the codomain of `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.has_pdf", "description": " A random variable `X : \u03a9 \u2192 E` is said to `has_pdf` with respect to the measure `\u2119` on `\u03a9` and\n`\u03bc` on `E` if there exists a measurable function `f` such that the push-forward measure of `\u2119`\nalong `X` equals `\u03bc.with_density f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.has_pdf.pdf'", "description": " A random variable `X : \u03a9 \u2192 E` is said to `has_pdf` with respect to the measure `\u2119` on `\u03a9` and\n`\u03bc` on `E` if there exists a measurable function `f` such that the push-forward measure of `\u2119`\nalong `X` equals `\u03bc.with_density f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.has_pdf.measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.map_eq_set_lintegral_pdf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.is_uniform.is_probability_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf_eq_zero_of_not_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.quasi_measure_preserving_has_pdf", "description": " A random variable that `has_pdf` transformed under a `quasi_measure_preserving`\nmap also `has_pdf` if `(map g (map X \u2119)).have_lebesgue_decomposition \u03bc`.\n\n`quasi_measure_preserving_has_pdf'` is more useful in the case we are working with a\nprobability measure and a real-valued random variable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.has_pdf_of_pdf_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.is_uniform.mul_pdf_integrable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf", "description": " If `X` is a random variable that `has_pdf X \u2119 \u03bc`, then `pdf X` is the measurable function `f`\nsuch that the push-forward measure of `\u2119` along `X` equals `\u03bc.with_density f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.has_pdf_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.has_finite_integral_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.is_uniform.measure_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.real.has_pdf_iff_of_measurable", "description": " A real-valued random variable `X` `has_pdf X \u2119 \u03bb` (where `\u03bb` is the Lebesgue measure) if and\nonly if the push-forward measure of `\u2119` along `X` is absolutely continuous with respect to `\u03bb`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.map_eq_with_density_pdf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.real.has_pdf_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.have_lebesgue_decomposition_of_has_pdf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.integral_mul_eq_integral", "description": " If `X` is a real-valued random variable that has pdf `f`, then the expectation of `X` equals\n`\u222b x, x * f x \u2202\u03bb` where `\u03bb` is the Lebesgue measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measurable_of_pdf_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf_undef", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.ae_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.integrable_iff_integrable_mul_pdf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.is_uniform.integral_eq", "description": " A real uniform random variable `X` with support `s` has expectation\n`(\u03bb s)\u207b\u00b9 * \u222b x in s, x \u2202\u03bb` where `\u03bb` is the Lebesgue measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.has_pdf_iff_of_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.pdf.lintegral_eq_measure_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.measurable_pdf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.ring_topology", "description": " The ring topology on `localization M` coinduced from the natural homomorphism sending `x : R`\nto the equivalence class of `(x, 1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.topological_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "localization.topological_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_has_deriv_within_at_eq_of_lt_of_gt", "description": "**Darboux's theorem**: if `a \u2264 b` and `f' b < m < f' a`, then `f' c = m` for some `c \u2208 (a, b)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.ord_connected.image_deriv", "description": " **Darboux's theorem**: the image of an `ord_connected` set under `f'` is an `ord_connected`\nset, `deriv` version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.ord_connected.image_has_deriv_within_at", "description": " **Darboux's theorem**: the image of an `ord_connected` set under `f'` is an `ord_connected`\nset, `has_deriv_within_at` version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_has_deriv_within_at_eq_of_gt_of_lt", "description": " **Darboux's theorem**: if `a \u2264 b` and `f' a < m < f' b`, then `f' c = m` for some\n`c \u2208 (a, b)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_has_deriv_within_at_eq_of_ge_of_le", "description": " **Darboux's theorem**: if `a \u2264 b` and `f' a \u2264 m \u2264 f' b`, then `f' c = m` for some\n`c \u2208 [a, b]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.ord_connected.image_deriv_within", "description": " **Darboux's theorem**: the image of an `ord_connected` set under `f'` is an `ord_connected`\nset, `deriv_within` version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_has_deriv_within_at_eq_of_le_of_ge", "description": " **Darboux's theorem**: if `a \u2264 b` and `f' b \u2264 m \u2264 f' a`, then `f' c = m` for some\n`c \u2208 [a, b]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.image_deriv", "description": " **Darboux's theorem**: the image of a convex set under `f'` is a convex set,\n`deriv` version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.image_deriv_within", "description": " **Darboux's theorem**: the image of a convex set under `f'` is a convex set,\n`deriv_within` version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_within_at_forall_lt_or_forall_gt_of_forall_ne", "description": " If the derivative of a function is never equal to `m`, then either\nit is always greater than `m`, or it is always less than `m`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex.image_has_deriv_within_at", "description": " **Darboux's theorem**: the image of a convex set under `f'` is a convex set,\n`has_deriv_within_at` version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_tensor_product'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_one", "description": "The trace of the identity endomorphism is the dimension of the free module", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_comp_comm'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_transpose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_eq_contract_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_id", "description": "The trace of the identity endomorphism is the dimension of the free module", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_aux_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_comp_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_prod_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_eq_matrix_trace", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_eq_contract_of_basis", "description": "The trace of a linear map correspond to the contraction pairing under the isomorphism\n`End(M) \u2243 M* \u2297 M`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_conj'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_conj", "description": "The trace of an endomorphism is invariant under conjugation", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_mul_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_transpose'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_eq_contract_of_basis'", "description": "The trace of a linear map correspond to the contraction pairing under the isomorphism\n`End(M) \u2243 M* \u2297 M`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_eq_contract'", "description": " When `M` is finite free, the trace of a linear map correspond to the contraction pairing under\nthe isomorphism `End(M) \u2243 M* \u2297 M`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace", "description": "Trace of an endomorphism independent of basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_tensor_product", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_eq_matrix_trace_of_finset", "description": "Auxiliary lemma for `trace_eq_matrix_trace`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_eq_contract", "description": " When `M` is finite free, the trace of a linear map correspond to the contraction pairing under\nthe isomorphism `End(M) \u2243 M* \u2297 M`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_aux", "description": "The trace of an endomorphism given a basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_aux_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_proj.trace", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.trace_prod_map'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.alg_hom_ext'", "description": " Two `alg_hom`s out of a direct sum are equal if they agree on the generators.\n\nSee note [partially-applied ext lemmas].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.galgebra", "description": " A graded version of `algebra`. An instance of `direct_sum.galgebra R A` endows `(\u2a01 i, A i)`\nwith an `R`-algebra structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.galgebra.to_fun", "description": " A graded version of `algebra`. An instance of `direct_sum.galgebra R A` endows `(\u2a01 i, A i)`\nwith an `R`-algebra structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.galgebra.map_one", "description": " A graded version of `algebra`. An instance of `direct_sum.galgebra R A` endows `(\u2a01 i, A i)`\nwith an `R`-algebra structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.galgebra.map_mul", "description": " A graded version of `algebra`. An instance of `direct_sum.galgebra R A` endows `(\u2a01 i, A i)`\nwith an `R`-algebra structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.galgebra.commutes", "description": " A graded version of `algebra`. An instance of `direct_sum.galgebra R A` endows `(\u2a01 i, A i)`\nwith an `R`-algebra structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.galgebra.smul_def", "description": " A graded version of `algebra`. An instance of `direct_sum.galgebra R A` endows `(\u2a01 i, A i)`\nwith an `R`-algebra structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.to_algebra", "description": " A family of `linear_map`s preserving `direct_sum.ghas_one.one` and `direct_sum.ghas_mul.mul`\ndescribes an `alg_hom` on `\u2a01 i, A i`. This is a stronger version of `direct_sum.to_semiring`.\n\nOf particular interest is the case when `A i` are bundled subojects, `f` is the family of\ncoercions such as `submodule.subtype (A i)`, and the `[gmonoid A]` structure originates from\n`direct_sum.gmonoid.of_add_submodules`, in which case the proofs about `ghas_one` and `ghas_mul`\ncan be discharged by `rfl`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "direct_sum.algebra_map_to_add_monoid_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"