"p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_max_chain.bot_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "flag.mem_coe_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_chain_univ_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_chain.directed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.subsingleton.is_chain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "super_chain", "description": "`super_chain s t` means that `t` is a chain that strictly includes `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_chain.symm", "description": "This can be used to turn `is_chain (\u2265)` into `is_chain (\u2264)` and vice-versa.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal.mono_from", "description": "Any morphism from a terminal object is mono.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial.hom_ext", "description": "Any two morphisms from an initial object are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_of_diagram_initial_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial.unique_up_to_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.terminal.comp_from", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal.comp_from", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal.unique_up_to_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial_unop_of_terminal", "description": "A terminal object in the opposite category is initial in the original category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial_iso_is_initial", "description": "The (unique) isomorphism between the chosen initial object and any other initial object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial.of_iso", "description": "Transport a term of type `is_initial` across an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_of_diagram_terminal_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial_is_initial", "description": "An initial object is initial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.as_empty_cocone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal.is_split_mono_from", "description": "Any morphism from a terminal object is split mono.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_\u03c0_terminal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal.of_unique", "description": "An object `Y` is terminal if for every `X` there is a unique morphism `X \u27f6 Y`\n   (as an instance).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit_of_diagram_terminal", "description": " From a functor `F : J \u2964 C`, given a terminal object of `J` and that the morphisms in the\ndiagram are isomorphisms, show the cone `cone_of_diagram_terminal` is a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.as_empty_cocone", "description": "Construct a cocone for the empty diagram given an object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.terminal.from", "description": "The map from an object to the terminal object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial.unique_up_to_iso", "description": "If `I` and `I'` are initial, they are isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal.from", "description": "Give the morphism to a terminal object from any other.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial.is_split_epi_to", "description": "Any morphism to an initial object is split epi.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_\u03b9_terminal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial.to", "description": "Give the morphism from an initial object to any other.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_terminal_change_diagram", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.\u03b9_colimit_const_initial_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_of_diagram_terminal", "description": " From a functor `F : J \u2964 C`, given a terminal object of `J`, construct a cone for `J`,\nprovided that the morphisms in the diagram are isomorphisms.\nIn `limit_of_diagram_terminal` we show it is a limit cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_initial_op_of_has_terminal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.\u03b9_colimit_const_initial_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit_of_diagram_initial", "description": " From a functor `F : J \u2964 C`, given an initial object of `J` and that the morphisms in the\ndiagram are isomorphisms, show the cone `cocone_of_diagram_initial` is a colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal.hom_ext", "description": "Any two morphisms to a terminal object are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_initial_of_has_terminal_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit_of_terminal", "description": " For a functor `F : J \u2964 C`, if `J` has a terminal object and all the morphisms in the diagram\nare isomorphisms, then the image of the terminal object is isomorphic to the limit of `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal_equiv_unique", "description": "An object `Y` is terminal iff for every `X` there is a unique morphism `X \u27f6 Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_of_diagram_terminal_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_of_diagram_initial", "description": " From a functor `F : J \u2964 C`, given an initial object of `J`, construct a cone for `J`.\nIn `limit_of_diagram_initial` we show it is a limit cone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_terminal_of_unique", "description": " We can more explicitly show that a category has a terminal object by specifying the object,\nand showing there is a unique morphism to it from any other object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.obj.has_limit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial.of_unique", "description": "An object `X` is initial if for every `Y` there is a unique morphism `X \u27f6 Y`\n   (as an instance).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_initial_of_unique", "description": " We can more explicitly show that a category has an initial object by specifying the object,\nand showing there is a unique morphism from it to any other object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit_of_terminal", "description": " For a functor `F : J \u2964 C`, if `J` has a terminal object then the image of it is isomorphic\nto the colimit of `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_terminal_of_has_initial_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit_const_initial_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.terminal_iso_is_terminal", "description": "The (unique) isomorphism between the chosen terminal object and any other terminal object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial.to_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial.unique_up_to_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial.mono_from", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.unique_from_initial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.as_empty_cone_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_\u03c0_of_is_terminal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial_mono_class", "description": " A category is a `initial_mono_class` if the canonical morphism of an initial object is a\nmonomorphism.  In practice, this is most useful when given an arbitrary morphism out of the chosen\ninitial object, see `initial.mono_from`.\nGiven a terminal object, this is equivalent to the assumption that the unique morphism from initial\nto terminal is a monomorphism, which is the second of Freyd's axioms for an AT category.\n\nTODO: This is a condition satisfied by categories with zero objects and morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial_mono_class.is_initial_mono_from", "description": " A category is a `initial_mono_class` if the canonical morphism of an initial object is a\nmonomorphism.  In practice, this is most useful when given an arbitrary morphism out of the chosen\ninitial object, see `initial.mono_from`.\nGiven a terminal object, this is equivalent to the assumption that the unique morphism from initial\nto terminal is a monomorphism, which is the second of Freyd's axioms for an AT category.\n\nTODO: This is a condition satisfied by categories with zero objects and morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_of_diagram_terminal", "description": " From a functor `F : J \u2964 C`, given a terminal object of `J`, construct a cocone for `J`.\nIn `colimit_of_diagram_terminal` we show it is a colimit cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial.mono_from", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial.is_split_epi_to", "description": "Any morphism to an initial object is split epi.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial.epi_to", "description": "Any morphism to an initial object is epi.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit_of_diagram_terminal", "description": " From a functor `F : J \u2964 C`, given a terminal object of `J`, show the cocone\n`cocone_of_diagram_terminal` is a colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_terminal_op_of_has_initial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.terminal_unop_of_initial", "description": "An initial object in the opposite category is terminal in the original category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_of_diagram_initial_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit_empty_cocone_equiv", "description": "Replacing an empty cocone in `is_colimit` by another with the same cocone point\n   is an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_terminal_change_universe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal", "description": "`X` is terminal if the cone it induces on the empty diagram is limiting.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_of_diagram_initial", "description": " From a functor `F : J \u2964 C`, given an initial object of `J`, construct a cocone for `J`,\nprovided that the morphisms in the diagram are isomorphisms.\nIn `colimit_of_diagram_initial` we show it is a colimit cocone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit_of_diagram_initial", "description": " From a functor `F : J \u2964 C`, given an initial object of `J`, show the cone\n`cone_of_diagram_initial` is a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_\u03c0_initial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.terminal_op_of_initial", "description": "An initial object is terminal in the opposite category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.as_empty_cocone_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial_bot", "description": "If `\u03b1` is a preorder with bot, then `\u22a5` is an initial object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial.has_initial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_of_diagram_terminal_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.as_empty_cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial.to", "description": "The map to an object from the initial object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit_const_terminal_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_\u03c0_of_is_initial", "description": "If `j` is initial in the index category, then the map `limit.\u03c0 F j` is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial_mono_class.of_initial", "description": " To show a category is a `initial_mono_class` it suffices to show every morphism out of the\ninitial object is a monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial.to_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_\u03b9_initial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cocone_of_diagram_initial_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.terminal_comparison", "description": "The comparison morphism from the image of a terminal object to the terminal object in the target\ncategory.\nThis is an isomorphism iff `G` preserves terminal objects, see\n`category_theory.limits.preserves_terminal.of_iso_comparison`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_of_diagram_terminal_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.terminal", "description": "An arbitrary choice of terminal object, if one exists.\nYou can use the notation `\u22a4_ C`.\nThis object is characterized by having a unique morphism from any object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal.unique_up_to_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_initial", "description": "A category has an initial object if it has a colimit over the empty diagram.\nUse `has_initial_of_unique` to construct instances.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_initial_change_diagram", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial", "description": "An arbitrary choice of initial object, if one exists.\nYou can use the notation `\u22a5_ C`.\nThis object is characterized by having a unique morphism to any object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal.unique_up_to_iso", "description": "If `T` and `T'` are terminal, they are isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.terminal.is_split_mono_from", "description": "Any morphism from a terminal object is split mono.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit_change_empty_cocone", "description": "Being initial is independent of the empty diagram, its universe, and the cocone over it,\n   as long as the cocone points are isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit_const_terminal_inv_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_terminal", "description": "A category has a terminal object if it has a limit over the empty diagram.\nUse `has_terminal_of_unique` to construct instances.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_initial_change_universe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal_top", "description": "If `\u03b1` is a preorder with top, then `\u22a4` is a terminal object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial.to_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial_mono_class.of_is_initial", "description": " To show a category is a `initial_mono_class` it suffices to give an initial object such that\nevery morphism out of it is a monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_\u03b9_of_is_terminal", "description": "If `j` is terminal in the index category, then the map `colimit.\u03b9 F j` is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit_of_initial", "description": " For a functor `F : J \u2964 C`, if `J` has an initial object then the image of it is isomorphic\nto the limit of `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit_of_initial", "description": " For a functor `F : J \u2964 C`, if `J` has an initial object and all the morphisms in the diagram\nare isomorphisms, then the image of the initial object is isomorphic to the colimit of `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.colimit_const_initial", "description": "The colimit of the constant `\u22a5_ C` functor is `\u22a5_ C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial", "description": "`X` is initial if the cocone it induces on the empty diagram is colimiting.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.as_empty_cone", "description": "Construct a cone for the empty diagram given an object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit_const_terminal", "description": "The limit of the constant `\u22a4_ C` functor is `\u22a4_ C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.limit_const_terminal_inv_\u03c0_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit_empty_cone_equiv", "description": "Replacing an empty cone in `is_limit` by another with the same cone point\n   is an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial_op_of_terminal", "description": "A terminal object is initial in the opposite category.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.obj.has_colimit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial_mono_class.of_terminal", "description": " To show a category is a `initial_mono_class` it suffices to show the unique morphism from the\ninitial object to a terminal object is a monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.unique_to_terminal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal.of_iso", "description": "Transport a term of type `is_terminal` across an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_initial_equiv_unique", "description": "An object `X` is initial iff for every `Y` there is a unique morphism `X \u27f6 Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal.has_terminal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit_change_empty_cone", "description": "Being terminal is independent of the empty diagram, its universe, and the cone over it,\n   as long as the cone points are isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial_mono_class.of_is_terminal", "description": " To show a category is a `initial_mono_class` it suffices to show the unique morphism from an\ninitial object to a terminal object is a monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_iso_\u03b9_of_is_initial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_terminal.from_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.initial_comparison", "description": "The comparison morphism from the initial object in the target category to the image of the initial\nobject.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.terminal_is_terminal", "description": "A terminal object is terminal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cone_of_diagram_initial_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ulift.normed_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.is_bounded_under.smul_tendsto_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph_unit_ball_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.normed_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnnorm_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ulift.normed_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frontier_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.restrict_scalars.normed_space_orig", "description": "The action of the original normed_field on `restrict_scalars \ud835\udd5c \ud835\udd5c' E`.\nThis is not an instance as it would be contrary to the purpose of `restrict_scalars`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_closed_ball'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.zmultiples.discrete_topology", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_algebra_rat", "description": " Any normed characteristic-zero division ring that is a normed_algebra over the reals is also a\nnormed algebra over the rationals.\n\nPhrased another way, if `\ud835\udd5c` is a normed algebra over the reals, then `algebra_rat` respects that\nnorm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "punit.normed_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_algebra", "description": " A normed algebra `\ud835\udd5c'` over `\ud835\udd5c` is normed module that is also an algebra.\n\nSee the implementation notes for `algebra` for a discussion about non-unital algebras. Following\nthe strategy there, a non-unital *normed* algebra can be written as:\n```lean\nvariables [normed_field \ud835\udd5c] [non_unital_semi_normed_ring \ud835\udd5c']\nvariables [normed_module \ud835\udd5c \ud835\udd5c'] [smul_comm_class \ud835\udd5c \ud835\udd5c' \ud835\udd5c'] [is_scalar_tower \ud835\udd5c \ud835\udd5c' \ud835\udd5c']\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_algebra.to_algebra", "description": " A normed algebra `\ud835\udd5c'` over `\ud835\udd5c` is normed module that is also an algebra.\n\nSee the implementation notes for `algebra` for a discussion about non-unital algebras. Following\nthe strategy there, a non-unital *normed* algebra can be written as:\n```lean\nvariables [normed_field \ud835\udd5c] [non_unital_semi_normed_ring \ud835\udd5c']\nvariables [normed_module \ud835\udd5c \ud835\udd5c'] [smul_comm_class \ud835\udd5c \ud835\udd5c' \ud835\udd5c'] [is_scalar_tower \ud835\udd5c \ud835\udd5c' \ud835\udd5c']\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_algebra.norm_smul_le", "description": " A normed algebra `\ud835\udd5c'` over `\ud835\udd5c` is normed module that is also an algebra.\n\nSee the implementation notes for `algebra` for a discussion about non-unital algebras. Following\nthe strategy there, a non-unital *normed* algebra can be written as:\n```lean\nvariables [normed_field \ud835\udd5c] [non_unital_semi_normed_ring \ud835\udd5c']\nvariables [normed_module \ud835\udd5c \ud835\udd5c'] [smul_comm_class \ud835\udd5c \ud835\udd5c' \ud835\udd5c'] [is_scalar_tower \ud835\udd5c \ud835\udd5c' \ud835\udd5c']\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnnorm_algebra_map'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rescale_to_shell_semi_normed_zpow", "description": " If there is a scalar `c` with `\u2016c\u2016>1`, then any element with nonzero norm can be\nmoved by scalar multiplication to any shell of width `\u2016c\u2016`. Also recap information on the norm of\nthe rescaling element that shows up in applications.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_sphere", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.normed_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.seminormed_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frontier_sphere", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph_unit_ball", "description": " A (semi) normed real vector space is homeomorphic to the unit ball in the same space.\nThis homeomorphism sends `x : E` to `(1 + \u2016x\u2016\u00b2)^(- \u00bd) \u2022 x`.\n\nIn many cases the actual implementation is not important, so we don't mark the projection lemmas\n`homeomorph_unit_ball_apply_coe` and `homeomorph_unit_ball_symm_apply` as `@[simp]`.\n\nSee also `cont_diff_homeomorph_unit_ball` and `cont_diff_on_homeomorph_unit_ball_symm` for\nsmoothness properties that hold when `E` is an inner-product space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.induced", "description": " A linear map from a `module` to a `normed_space` induces a `normed_space` structure on the\ndomain, using the `seminormed_add_comm_group.induced` norm.\n\nSee note [reducible non-instances]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.normed_space", "description": "The product of two normed spaces is a normed space, with the sup norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_smul_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "closure_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_algebra.id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rescale_to_shell_semi_normed", "description": " If there is a scalar `c` with `\u2016c\u2016>1`, then any element with nonzero norm can be\nmoved by scalar multiplication to any shell of width `\u2016c\u2016`. Also recap information on the norm of\nthe rescaling element that shows up in applications.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frontier_closed_ball'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "range_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.unbounded_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_algebra_map_nnreal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.noncompact_space", "description": " A normed vector space over a nontrivially normed field is a noncompact space. This cannot be\nan instance because in order to apply it, Lean would have to search for `normed_space \ud835\udd5c E` with\nunknown `\ud835\udd5c`. We register this as an instance in two cases: `\ud835\udd5c = E` and `\ud835\udd5c = \u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nontrivially_normed_field.noncompact_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "range_nnnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frontier_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph_unit_ball_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnnorm_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real_normed_space.noncompact_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.punctured_nhds_module_ne_bot", "description": " If `E` is a nontrivial topological module over `\u211d`, then `E` has no isolated points.\nThis is a particular case of `module.punctured_nhds_ne_bot`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.restrict_scalars", "description": " Warning: This declaration should be used judiciously.\nPlease consider using `is_scalar_tower` and/or `restrict_scalars \ud835\udd5c \ud835\udd5c' E` instead.\n\nThis definition allows the `restrict_scalars.normed_space` instance to be put directly on `E`\nrather on `restrict_scalars \ud835\udd5c \ud835\udd5c' E`. This would be a very bad instance; both because `\ud835\udd5c'` cannot be\ninferred, and because it is likely to create instance diamonds.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_norm_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_algebra_map'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_field.to_has_bounded_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "coe_homeomorph_unit_ball_apply_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_nhds_norm_smul_sub_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.exists_lt_norm", "description": " If `E` is a nontrivial normed space over a nontrivially normed field `\ud835\udd5c`, then `E` is unbounded:\nfor any `c : \u211d`, there exists a vector `x : E` with norm strictly greater than `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.has_bounded_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space", "description": " A normed space over a normed field is a vector space endowed with a norm which satisfies the\nequality `\u2016c \u2022 x\u2016 = \u2016c\u2016 \u2016x\u2016`. We require only `\u2016c \u2022 x\u2016 \u2264 \u2016c\u2016 \u2016x\u2016` in the definition, then prove\n`\u2016c \u2022 x\u2016 = \u2016c\u2016 \u2016x\u2016` in `norm_smul`.\n\nNote that since this requires `seminormed_add_comm_group` and not `normed_add_comm_group`, this\ntypeclass can be used for \"semi normed spaces\" too, just as `module` can be used for\n\"semi modules\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.to_module", "description": " A normed space over a normed field is a vector space endowed with a norm which satisfies the\nequality `\u2016c \u2022 x\u2016 = \u2016c\u2016 \u2016x\u2016`. We require only `\u2016c \u2022 x\u2016 \u2264 \u2016c\u2016 \u2016x\u2016` in the definition, then prove\n`\u2016c \u2022 x\u2016 = \u2016c\u2016 \u2016x\u2016` in `norm_smul`.\n\nNote that since this requires `seminormed_add_comm_group` and not `normed_add_comm_group`, this\ntypeclass can be used for \"semi normed spaces\" too, just as `module` can be used for\n\"semi modules\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.norm_smul_le", "description": " A normed space over a normed field is a vector space endowed with a norm which satisfies the\nequality `\u2016c \u2022 x\u2016 = \u2016c\u2016 \u2016x\u2016`. We require only `\u2016c \u2022 x\u2016 \u2264 \u2016c\u2016 \u2016x\u2016` in the definition, then prove\n`\u2016c \u2022 x\u2016 = \u2016c\u2016 \u2016x\u2016` in `norm_smul`.\n\nNote that since this requires `seminormed_add_comm_group` and not `normed_add_comm_group`, this\ntypeclass can be used for \"semi normed spaces\" too, just as `module` can be used for\n\"semi modules\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_algebra.to_normed_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.normed_algebra", "description": "The product of two normed algebras is a normed algebra, with the sup norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnnorm_algebra_map_nnreal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.normed_algebra", "description": "The product of finitely many normed algebras is a normed algebra, with the sup norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra_map_isometry", "description": "In a normed algebra, the inclusion of the base field in the extended field is an isometry.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rescale_to_shell", "description": " If there is a scalar `c` with `\u2016c\u2016>1`, then any element can be moved by scalar multiplication to\nany shell of width `\u2016c\u2016`. Also recap information on the norm of the rescaling element that shows\nup in applications.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rescale_to_shell_zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interior_sphere'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.to_normed_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_norm_smul_mem_closed_unit_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_field.to_normed_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.zero_smul_is_bounded_under_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.to_module'", "description": " While this may appear identical to `normed_space.to_module`, it contains an implicit argument\ninvolving `normed_add_comm_group.to_seminormed_add_comm_group` that typeclass inference has trouble\ninferring.\n\nSpecifically, the following instance cannot be found without this `normed_space.to_module'`:\n```lean\nexample\n  (\ud835\udd5c \u03b9 : Type*) (E : \u03b9 \u2192 Type*)\n  [normed_field \ud835\udd5c] [\u03a0 i, normed_add_comm_group (E i)] [\u03a0 i, normed_space \ud835\udd5c (E i)] :\n  \u03a0 i, module \ud835\udd5c (E i) := by apply_instance\n```\n\n[This Zulip thread](https://leanprover.zulipchat.com/#narrow/stream/113488-general/topic/Typeclass.20resolution.20under.20binders/near/245151099)\ngives some more context.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.normed_space", "description": "A subspace of a normed space is also a normed space, with the restriction of the norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "frontier_sphere'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "restrict_scalars.normed_space", "description": " If `E` is a normed space over `\ud835\udd5c'` and `\ud835\udd5c` is a normed algebra over `\ud835\udd5c'`, then\n`restrict_scalars.module` is additionally a `normed_space`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.normed_space", "description": "The product of finitely many normed spaces is a normed space, with the sup norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_algebra.induced", "description": " A non-unital algebra homomorphism from an `algebra` to a `normed_algebra` induces a\n`normed_algebra` structure on the domain, using the `semi_normed_ring.induced` norm.\n\nSee note [reducible non-instances]", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_opposite.normed_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_algebra.to_normed_space'", "description": " While this may appear identical to `normed_algebra.to_normed_space`, it contains an implicit\nargument involving `normed_ring.to_semi_normed_ring` that typeclass inference has trouble inferring.\n\nSpecifically, the following instance cannot be found without this `normed_space.to_module'`:\n```lean\nexample\n  (\ud835\udd5c \u03b9 : Type*) (E : \u03b9 \u2192 Type*)\n  [normed_field \ud835\udd5c] [\u03a0 i, normed_ring (E i)] [\u03a0 i, normed_algebra \ud835\udd5c (E i)] :\n  \u03a0 i, module \ud835\udd5c (E i) := by apply_instance\n```\n\nSee `normed_space.to_module'` for a similar situation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_map.continuous_lift_prod_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.continuous_map_of_unique", "description": "If `\u03b1` has a single element, then `\u03b2` is homeomorphic to `C(\u03b1, \u03b2)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous_curry", "description": "The currying process is a continuous map between function spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.curry_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.curry", "description": "The curried form of a continuous map `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b3` as a continuous map `\u03b1 \u2192 C(\u03b2, \u03b3)`.\n   If `a \u00d7 \u03b2` is locally compact, this is continuous. If `\u03b1` and `\u03b2` are both locally\n   compact, then this is a homeomorphism, see `homeomorph.curry`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quotient_map.continuous_lift_prod_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous_comp", "description": "C(\u03b1, -) is a functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.is_open_gen", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous_of_continuous_uncurry", "description": "To show continuity of a map `\u03b1 \u2192 C(\u03b2, \u03b3)`, it suffices to show that its uncurried form\n   `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b3` is continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous_comp_left", "description": "C(-, \u03b3) is a functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.image_coev", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous_const'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous_uncurry_of_continuous", "description": "The uncurried form of a continuous map `\u03b1 \u2192 C(\u03b2, \u03b3)` is a continuous map `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b3`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous_restrict", "description": " For any subset `s` of `\u03b1`, the restriction of continuous functions to `s` is continuous as a\nfunction from `C(\u03b1, \u03b2)` to `C(s, \u03b2)` with their respective compact-open topologies.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous_comp'", "description": "Composition is a continuous map from `C(\u03b1, \u03b2) \u00d7 C(\u03b2, \u03b3)` to `C(\u03b1, \u03b3)`, provided that `\u03b2` is\n locally compact. This is Prop. 9 of Chap. X, \u00a73, \u2116. 4 of Bourbaki's *Topologie G\u00e9n\u00e9rale*.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.t2_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coev", "description": " The coevaluation map `\u03b2 \u2192 C(\u03b1, \u03b2 \u00d7 \u03b1)` sending a point `x : \u03b2` to the continuous function\non `\u03b1` sending `y` to `(x, y)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.compact_open_eq_Inf_induced", "description": " The compact-open topology on `C(\u03b1, \u03b2)` is equal to the infimum of the compact-open topologies\non `C(s, \u03b2)` for `s` a compact subset of `\u03b1`.  The key point of the proof is that the union of the\ncompact subsets of `\u03b1` is equal to the union of compact subsets of the compact subsets of `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.gen_empty_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.uncurry_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.nhds_compact_open_eq_Inf_nhds_induced", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous_coev", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous_eval_const'", "description": "See also `continuous_map.continuous_eval_const`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.tendsto_compact_open_iff_forall", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.compact_open_le_induced", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.gen_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.tendsto_compact_open_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.compact_open.gen", "description": "A generating set for the compact-open topology (when `s` is compact and `u` is open).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.const'", "description": "The family of constant maps: `\u03b2 \u2192 C(\u03b1, \u03b2)` as a continuous map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.compact_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.curry'", "description": "Auxiliary definition, see `continuous_map.curry` and `homeomorph.curry`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.gen_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.continuous_map_of_unique_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous.comp'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.coe_const'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.gen_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.continuous_map_of_unique_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.uncurry", "description": "The uncurried form of a continuous map `\u03b1 \u2192 C(\u03b2, \u03b3)` as a continuous map `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b3` (if `\u03b2` is\n   locally compact). If `\u03b1` is also locally compact, then this is a homeomorphism between the two\n   function spaces, see `homeomorph.curry`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous_eval'", "description": " The evaluation map `C(\u03b1, \u03b2) \u00d7 \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is continuous if `\u03b1` is locally compact.\n\nSee also `continuous_map.continuous_eval`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous_uncurry", "description": "The uncurrying process is a continuous map between function spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous_curry'", "description": "If a map `\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b3` is continuous, then its curried form `\u03b1 \u2192 C(\u03b2, \u03b3)` is continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.exists_tendsto_compact_open_iff_forall", "description": " A family `F` of functions in `C(\u03b1, \u03b2)` converges in the compact-open topology, if and only if\nit converges in the compact-open topology on each compact subset of `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous_coe'", "description": "See also `continuous_map.continuous_coe`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homeomorph.curry", "description": "Currying as a homeomorphism between the function spaces `C(\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b2, \u03b3)` and `C(\u03b1, C(\u03b2, \u03b3))`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.gen_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_change_of_variables_sum", "description": " `comp_change_of_variables m M N` is a bijection between `comp_partial_sum_source m M N`\nand `comp_partial_sum_target m M N`, yielding equal sums for functions that correspond to each\nother under the bijection. As `comp_change_of_variables m M N` is a dependent function, stating\nthat it is a bijection is not directly possible, but the consequence on sums can be stated\nmore easily.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.length_gather", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_partial_sum", "description": " Composing the partial sums of two multilinear series coincides with the sum over all\ncompositions in `comp_partial_sum_target 0 N N`. This is precisely the motivation for the\ndefinition of `comp_partial_sum_target`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_coeff_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_continuous_linear_map_apply_composition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.apply_composition", "description": " Given a formal multilinear series `p`, a composition `c` of `n` and the index `i` of a\nblock of `c`, we may define a function on `fin n \u2192 E` by picking the variables in the `i`-th block\nof `n`, and applying the corresponding coefficient of `p` to these variables. This function is\ncalled `p.apply_composition c v i` for `v : fin n \u2192 E` and `i : fin c.length`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_coeff_zero''", "description": " The `0`-th coefficient of `q.comp p` is `q 0`. When `p` goes from `E` to `E`, this can be\nexpressed as a direct equality", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.length_sigma_composition_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_change_of_variables_length", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_along_composition_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_partial_sum_source", "description": " Source set in the change of variables to compute the composition of partial sums of formal\npower series.\nSee also `comp_partial_sum`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_coeff_zero", "description": " The `0`-th coefficient of `q.comp p` is `q 0`. Since these maps are multilinear maps in zero\nvariables, but on different spaces, we can not state this directly, so we state it when applied to\narbitrary vectors (which have to be the zero vector).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.mem_comp_partial_sum_target_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.apply_composition_update", "description": " Technical lemma stating how `p.apply_composition` commutes with updating variables. This\nwill be the key point to show that functions constructed from `apply_composition` retain\nmultilinearity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "analytic_at.comp", "description": " If two functions `g` and `f` are analytic respectively at `f x` and `x`, then `g \u2218 f` is\nanalytic at `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp", "description": " Formal composition of two formal multilinear series. The `n`-th coefficient in the composition\nis defined to be the sum of `q.comp_along_composition p c` over all compositions of\n`n`. In other words, this term (as a multilinear function applied to `v_0, ..., v_{n-1}`) is\n`\u2211'_{k} \u2211'_{i\u2081 + ... + i\u2096 = n} q\u2096 (p_{i_1} (...), ..., p_{i_k} (...))`, where one puts all variables\n`v_0, ..., v_{n-1}` in increasing order in the dots.\n\nIn general, the composition `q \u2218 p` only makes sense when the constant coefficient of `p` vanishes.\nWe give a general formula but which ignores the value of `p 0` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.le_comp_radius_of_summable", "description": " Bounding below the radius of the composition of two formal multilinear series assuming\nsummability over all compositions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.id", "description": " The identity formal multilinear series, with all coefficients equal to `0` except for `n = 1`\nwhere it is (the continuous multilinear version of) the identity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.remove_zero_comp_of_pos", "description": "Only `0`-th coefficient of `q.comp p` depends on `q 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_summable_nnreal", "description": " If two formal multilinear series have positive radius of convergence, then the terms appearing\nin the definition of their composition are also summable (when multiplied by a suitable positive\ngeometric term).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_partial_sum_target_tendsto_at_top", "description": " The auxiliary set corresponding to the composition of partial sums asymptotically contains\nall possible compositions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.remove_zero_apply_composition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_partial_sum_target_subset_image_comp_partial_sum_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.apply_composition_ones", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.comp_along_composition", "description": " Given a formal multilinear series `p`, a composition `c` of `n` and a continuous multilinear\nmap `f` in `c.length` variables, one may form a continuous multilinear map in `n` variables by\napplying the right coefficient of `p` to each block of the composition, and then applying `f` to\nthe resulting vector. It is called `f.comp_along_composition p c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fpower_series_at.comp", "description": " If two functions `g` and `f` have power series `q` and `p` respectively at `f x` and `x`, then\n`g \u2218 f` admits the power series `q.comp p` at `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_along_composition", "description": " Given two formal multilinear series `q` and `p` and a composition `c` of `n`, one may\nform a continuous multilinear map in `n` variables by applying the right coefficient of `p` to each\nblock of the composition, and then applying `q c.length` to the resulting vector. It is\ncalled `q.comp_along_composition p c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_along_composition_norm", "description": " The norm of `q.comp_along_composition p c` is controlled by the product of\nthe norms of the relevant bits of `q` and `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_partial_sum_target", "description": " Target set in the change of variables to compute the composition of partial sums of formal\npower series, here given a a finset.\nSee also `comp_partial_sum`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_partial_sum_target_set", "description": " Target set in the change of variables to compute the composition of partial sums of formal\npower series, here given a a set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.apply_composition_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.sigma_composition_eq_iff", "description": " Rewriting equality in the dependent type `\u03a3 (a : composition n), composition a.length)` in\nnon-dependent terms with lists, requiring that the blocks coincide.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.sigma_equiv_sigma_pi", "description": "Natural equivalence between `(\u03a3 (a : composition n), composition a.length)` and\n`(\u03a3 (c : composition n), \u03a0 (i : fin c.length), composition (c.blocks_fun i))`, that shows up as a\nchange of variables in the proof that composition of formal multilinear series is associative.\n\nConsider a composition `a` of `n` and a composition `b` of `a.length`. Then `b` indicates how to\ngroup together some blocks of `a`, giving altogether `b.length` blocks of blocks. These blocks of\nblocks can be called `d\u2080, ..., d_{a.length - 1}`, and one obtains a composition `c` of `n` by\nsaying that each `d\u1d62` is one single block. The map `\u27e8a, b\u27e9 \u2192 \u27e8c, (d\u2080, ..., d_{a.length - 1})\u27e9` is\nthe direct map in the equiv.\n\nConversely, if one starts from `c` and the `d\u1d62`s, one can join the `d\u1d62`s to obtain a composition\n`a` of `n`, and register the lengths of the `d\u1d62`s in a composition `b` of `a.length`. This is the\ninverse map of the equiv.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.sigma_composition_aux", "description": " An auxiliary function used in the definition of `sigma_equiv_sigma_pi` below, associating to\ntwo compositions `a` of `n` and `b` of `a.length`, and an index `i` bounded by the length of\n`a.gather b`, the subcomposition of `a` made of those blocks belonging to the `i`-th block of\n`a.gather b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_coeff_one", "description": " The first coefficient of a composition of formal multilinear series is the composition of the\nfirst coefficients seen as continuous linear maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.mem_comp_partial_sum_source_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.size_up_to_size_up_to_add", "description": " Auxiliary lemma to prove that the composition of formal multilinear series is associative.\n\nConsider a composition `a` of `n` and a composition `b` of `a.length`. Grouping together some\nblocks of `a` according to `b` as in `a.gather b`, one can compute the total size of the blocks\nof `a` up to an index `size_up_to b i + j` (where the `j` corresponds to a set of blocks of `a`\nthat do not fill a whole block of `a.gather b`). The first part corresponds to a sum of blocks\nin `a.gather b`, and the second one to a sum of blocks in the next block of\n`sigma_composition_aux a b`. This is the content of this lemma.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_multilinear_map.comp_along_composition_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.id_apply_one", "description": "The first coefficient of `id \ud835\udd5c E` is the identity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.id_apply_ne_one", "description": "For `n \u2260 1`, the `n`-th coefficient of `id \ud835\udd5c E` is zero, by definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.sigma_pi_composition_eq_iff", "description": " Rewriting equality in the dependent type\n`\u03a3 (c : composition n), \u03a0 (i : fin c.length), composition (c.blocks_fun i)` in\nnon-dependent terms with lists, requiring that the lists of blocks coincide.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_along_composition_nnnorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_along_composition_bound", "description": " The norm of `f.comp_along_composition p c` is controlled by the product of\nthe norms of the relevant bits of `f` and `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_change_of_variables_blocks_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.id_apply_one'", "description": " The `n`th coefficient of `id \ud835\udd5c E` is the identity when `n = 1`. We state this in a dependent\nway, as it will often appear in this form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_remove_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "formal_multilinear_series.comp_change_of_variables", "description": " Change of variables appearing to compute the composition of partial sums of formal\npower series", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.gather", "description": " When `a` is a composition of `n` and `b` is a composition of `a.length`, `a.gather b` is the\ncomposition of `n` obtained by gathering all the blocks of `a` corresponding to a block of `b`.\nFor instance, if `a = [6, 5, 3, 5, 2]` and `b = [2, 3]`, one should gather together\nthe first two blocks of `a` and its last three blocks, giving `a.gather b = [11, 10]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "composition.blocks_fun_sigma_composition_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.fin_succ_equiv_support'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.map_alg_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.sum_to_iter_Xl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.sum_alg_equiv", "description": "The algebra isomorphism between multivariable polynomials in a sum of two types,\nand multivariable polynomials in one of the types,\nwith coefficents in multivariable polynomials in the other type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.support_fin_succ_equiv_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_empty_alg_equiv_symm_apply_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.iter_to_sum", "description": "The function from multivariable polynomials in one type,\nwith coefficents in multivariable polynomials in another type,\nto multivariable polynomials in the sum of the two types.\n\nSee `sum_ring_equiv` for the ring isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.sum_to_iter_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.fin_succ_equiv_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.fin_succ_equiv", "description": "The algebra isomorphism between multivariable polynomials in `fin (n + 1)` and\npolynomials over multivariable polynomials in `fin n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_empty_alg_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.degree_fin_succ_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.map_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.degree_of_coeff_fin_succ_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.fin_succ_equiv_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.sum_to_iter", "description": "The function from multivariable polynomials in a sum of two types,\nto multivariable polynomials in one of the types,\nwith coefficents in multivariable polynomials in the other type.\n\nSee `sum_ring_equiv` for the ring isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.mv_polynomial_equiv_mv_polynomial_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.sum_to_iter_Xr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.mv_polynomial_equiv_mv_polynomial_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_empty_ring_equiv_symm_apply_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.punit_alg_equiv", "description": "The ring isomorphism between multivariable polynomials in a single variable and\npolynomials over the ground ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.iter_to_sum_C_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.map_alg_equiv_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.map_alg_equiv_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.map_equiv", "description": "If `e : A \u2243+* B` is an isomorphism of rings, then so is `map e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.option_equiv_left_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_empty_ring_equiv_symm_apply_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.iter_to_sum_C_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.fin_succ_equiv_coeff_coeff", "description": "The coefficient of `m` in the `i`-th coefficient of `fin_succ_equiv R n f` equals the\n   coefficient of `finsupp.cons i m` in `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.punit_alg_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.option_equiv_left", "description": "The algebra isomorphism between multivariable polynomials in `option S\u2081` and\npolynomials with coefficients in `mv_polynomial S\u2081 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.support_coeff_fin_succ_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.fin_succ_equiv_X_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.option_equiv_left_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.sum_ring_equiv", "description": "The ring isomorphism between multivariable polynomials in a sum of two types,\nand multivariable polynomials in one of the types,\nwith coefficents in multivariable polynomials in the other type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.punit_alg_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.nat_degree_fin_succ_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_empty_alg_equiv_symm_apply_support", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.map_alg_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_empty_ring_equiv", "description": " The ring isomorphism between multivariable polynomials in no variables\nand the ground ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.map_equiv_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.fin_succ_equiv_X_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.map_alg_equiv", "description": "If `e : A \u2243\u2090[R] B` is an isomorphism of `R`-algebras, then so is `map e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.mv_polynomial_equiv_mv_polynomial", "description": "A helper function for `sum_ring_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.iter_to_sum_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.fin_succ_equiv_comp_C_eq_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.map_equiv_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_empty_ring_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.coeff_eval_eq_eval_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.map_equiv_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.option_equiv_right", "description": "The algebra isomorphism between multivariable polynomials in `option S\u2081` and\nmultivariable polynomials with coefficients in polynomials.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.fin_succ_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_empty_alg_equiv", "description": " The algebra isomorphism between multivariable polynomials in no variables\nand the ground ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.eval_eq_eval_mv_eval'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.one_le_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.add_monoid_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.unique_ring_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_nat'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_commute", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_dvd.dvd.nat_cast", "description": "**Alias** of `nat.coe_nat_dvd`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.coe_nat_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lex.add_comm_monoid_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_ring_hom_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lex.has_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_add_monoid_hom", "description": "`coe : \u2115 \u2192 \u03b1` as an `add_monoid_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.has_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.ext_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.add_comm_monoid_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eq_nat_cast'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_lt_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.eq_nat_cast'", "description": "This is primed to match `eq_int_cast'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_order_embedding", "description": "`coe : \u2115 \u2192 \u03b1` as an `order_embedding`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_add_one_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_with_zero_hom.ext_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_lex_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.coe_cast_add_monoid_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.nat_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.coe_cast_ring_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_order_embedding_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.commute_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_ring_hom", "description": "`coe : \u2115 \u2192 \u03b1` as a `ring_hom`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ext_nat''", "description": "If two `monoid_with_zero_hom`s agree on the positive naturals they are equal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.elim_nat_cast_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.mono_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.strict_mono_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_nat_cast'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_lex_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne_zero.nat_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne_zero.nat_of_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_dual_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.abs_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.has_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lex.add_monoid_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.add_monoid_with_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_dual_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.coe_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_tsub", "description": " A version of `nat.cast_sub` that works for `\u211d\u22650` and `\u211a\u22650`. Note that this proof doesn't work\nfor `\u2115\u221e` and `\u211d\u22650\u221e`, so we use type-specific lemmas for these types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.one_lt_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.star_module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.finrank_real_complex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.equiv_real_prod_lm", "description": "The natural `linear_equiv` from `\u2102` to `\u211d \u00d7 \u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_dimensional.complex_to_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.conj_ae_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.coe_basis_one_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.real_complex_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.lift", "description": " A universal property of the complex numbers, providing a unique `\u2102 \u2192\u2090[\u211d] A` for every element\nof `A` which squares to `-1`.\n\nThis can be used to embed the complex numbers in the `quaternion`s.\n\nThis isomorphism is named to match the very similar `zsqrtd.lift`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.finrank_real_complex_fact", "description": " `fact` version of the dimension of `\u2102` over `\u211d`, locally useful in the definition of the\ncircle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smul_comm_class.complex_to_real", "description": " The scalar action of `\u211d` on a `\u2102`-module `E` induced by `module.complex_to_real` commutes with\nanother scalar action of `M` on `E` whenever the action of `\u2102` commutes with the action of `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real_part_add_I_smul_imaginary_part", "description": " The standard decomposition of `\u211c a + complex.I \u2022 \u2111 a = a` of an element of a star module over\n`\u2102` into a linear combination of self adjoint elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.finite_dimensional", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.equiv_real_prod_add_hom", "description": "The natural `add_equiv` from `\u2102` to `\u211d \u00d7 \u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imaginary_part", "description": " The imaginary part `\u2111 a` of an element `a` of a star module over `\u2102`, as a linear map into the\nself adjoint elements. In a general star module, we have a decomposition into the `self_adjoint`\nand `skew_adjoint` parts, but in a star module over `\u2102` we have\n`real_part_add_I_smul_imaginary_part`, which allows us to decompose into a linear combination of\n`self_adjoint`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.equiv_real_prod_add_hom_symm_apply_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.complex_to_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.is_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.coe_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.lift_aux_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.of_real_am", "description": "`\u211d`-algebra morphism version of the canonical embedding of `\u211d` in `\u2102`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.real_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imaginary_part_I_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imaginary_part_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_module.complex_to_real", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.re_lm", "description": "Linear map version of the real part function, from `\u2102` to `\u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skew_adjoint.neg_I_smul", "description": " Create a `self_adjoint` element from a `skew_adjoint` element by multiplying by the scalar\n`-complex.I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real_part", "description": " The real part `\u211c a` of an element `a` of a star module over `\u2102`, as a linear map. This is just\n`self_adjoint_part \u211d`, but we provide it as a separate definition in order to link it with lemmas\nconcerning the `imaginary_part`, which doesn't exist in star modules over other rings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.smul_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.equiv_real_prod_lm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skew_adjoint.neg_I_smul_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.im_lm_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.coe_basis_one_I_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.equiv_real_prod_add_hom_symm_apply_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.coe_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.smul_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.equiv_real_prod_add_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.real_alg_hom_eq_id_or_conj", "description": "The identity and the complex conjugation are the only two `\u211d`-algebra homomorphisms of `\u2102`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.distrib_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.equiv_real_prod_lm_symm_apply_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.lift_aux", "description": " There is an alg_hom from `\u2102` to any `\u211d`-algebra with an element that squares to `-1`.\n\nSee `complex.lift` for this as an equiv.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real_part_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.lift_aux_neg_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.ordered_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.basis_one_I", "description": "`\u2102` has a basis over `\u211d` given by `1` and `I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.lift_aux_apply_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.lift_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finrank_real_of_complex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.im_lm", "description": "Linear map version of the imaginary part function, from `\u2102` to `\u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.conj_ae", "description": "`\u211d`-algebra isomorphism version of the complex conjugation function from `\u2102` to `\u2102`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.map_coe_real_complex", "description": " We need this lemma since `complex.coe_algebra_map` diverts the simp-normal form away from\n`alg_hom.commutes`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.equiv_real_prod_lm_symm_apply_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.of_real_am_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.to_matrix_conj_ae", "description": "The matrix representation of `conj_ae`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rank_real_of_complex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.smul_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.rank_real_complex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skew_adjoint.I_smul_neg_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.re_lm_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real_part_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.lift_aux_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.alg_hom_ext", "description": "Two `\u211d`-algebra homomorphisms from \u2102 are equal if they agree on `complex.I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real_part_I_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.lift_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.rank_real_complex'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imaginary_part_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.reindex_reindex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.zero_tprod_coeff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.lift_tprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.subsingleton_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product", "description": "`pi_tensor_product R s` with `R` a commutative semiring and `s : \u03b9 \u2192 Type*` is the tensor\n product of all the `s i`'s. This is denoted by `\u2a02[R] i, s i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.lift_aux", "description": " Auxiliary function to constructing a linear map `(\u2a02[R] i, s i) \u2192 E` given a\n`multilinear map R s E` with the property that its composition with the canonical\n`multilinear_map R s (\u2a02[R] i, s i)` is the given multilinear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.tmul_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.induction_on'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.smul_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.smul_tprod_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.add_tprod_coeff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.subsingleton_equiv_apply_tprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.has_smul'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.lift_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.smul_comm_class'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.lift_reindex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.reindex_tprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.lift", "description": " Constructing a linear map `(\u2a02[R] i, s i) \u2192 E` given a `multilinear_map R s E` with the\nproperty that its composition with the canonical `multilinear_map R s E` is\nthe given multilinear map `\u03c6`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.eqv", "description": " The relation on `free_add_monoid (R \u00d7 \u03a0 i, s i)` that generates a congruence whose quotient is\nthe tensor product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.eqv.of_zero", "description": " The relation on `free_add_monoid (R \u00d7 \u03a0 i, s i)` that generates a congruence whose quotient is\nthe tensor product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.eqv.of_zero_scalar", "description": " The relation on `free_add_monoid (R \u00d7 \u03a0 i, s i)` that generates a congruence whose quotient is\nthe tensor product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.eqv.of_add", "description": " The relation on `free_add_monoid (R \u00d7 \u03a0 i, s i)` that generates a congruence whose quotient is\nthe tensor product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.eqv.of_add_scalar", "description": " The relation on `free_add_monoid (R \u00d7 \u03a0 i, s i)` that generates a congruence whose quotient is\nthe tensor product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.eqv.of_smul", "description": " The relation on `free_add_monoid (R \u00d7 \u03a0 i, s i)` that generates a congruence whose quotient is\nthe tensor product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.eqv.add_comm", "description": " The relation on `free_add_monoid (R \u00d7 \u03a0 i, s i)` that generates a congruence whose quotient is\nthe tensor product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.zero_tprod_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.tprod_coeff_eq_smul_tprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.lift.unique'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.lift_comp_reindex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.lift_aux_tprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.smul_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.lift_add_hom", "description": " Construct an `add_monoid_hom` from `(\u2a02[R] i, s i)` to some space `F` from a function\n`\u03c6 : (R \u00d7 \u03a0 i, s i) \u2192 F` with the appropriate properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.module'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.smul_tprod_coeff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.tprod_coeff", "description": " `tprod_coeff R r f` with `r : R` and `f : \u03a0 i, s i` is the tensor product of the vectors `f i`\nover all `i : \u03b9`, multiplied by the coefficient `r`. Note that this is meant as an auxiliary\ndefinition for this file alone, and that one should use `tprod` defined below for most purposes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.is_empty_equiv_apply_tprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.lift.unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.tmul_equiv", "description": " Equivalence between a `tensor_product` of `pi_tensor_product`s and a single\n`pi_tensor_product` indexed by a `sum` type.\n\nFor simplicity, this is defined only for homogeneously- (rather than dependently-) typed components.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.induction_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.is_empty_equiv", "description": "The tensor product over an empty index type `\u03b9` is isomorphic to the base ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.tprod", "description": "The canonical `multilinear_map R s (\u2a02[R] i, s i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.is_scalar_tower'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.distrib_mul_action'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.reindex", "description": " Re-index the components of the tensor power by `e`.\n\nFor simplicity, this is defined only for homogeneously- (rather than dependently-) typed components.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.subsingleton_equiv", "description": "The tensor product over an single index is isomorphic to the module", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.lift_aux_tprod_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.is_empty_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.reindex_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.add_tprod_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.reindex_comp_tprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.lift_aux.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.reindex_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.smul_tprod_coeff_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.tmul_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.reindex_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi_tensor_product.lift.tprod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.has_faithful_smul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.add_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.is_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.smul_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.smul_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.has_faithful_smul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.smul_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.vadd_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.vadd_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.has_faithful_vadd_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.smul_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.vadd_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.vadd_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.has_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.smul_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.is_central_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.vadd_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sum.has_faithful_vadd_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_vec.has_to_string", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.predictor_type.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_vec.of_expr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature.repr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature.has_to_tactic_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_vec.union", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.predictor", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_vec.of_thm", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_vec.has_to_tactic_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_stats.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature.has_to_string", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.predictor_type", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.predictor_type.knn", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.predictor_type.mepo", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.predictor_type.bayes", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_stats.cosine_similarity", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_vec.of_proof", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_vec.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_vec.to_list", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature.const", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature.arg", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_stats.dotp", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_cfg", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_cfg.ignore_tc", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_cfg.ignore_pi_domain", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_cfg.ignore_type_args", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_cfg.ignore_decidable", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_cfg.ignore_conns", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_stats.features", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_stats.of_feature_vecs", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_vec.of_exprs", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_stats.has_to_tactic_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature.to_string", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_vec", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_vec.isect", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_stats", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_vec.has_repr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.predictor.predict", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_stats.norm", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "environment.mk_predictor", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_stats.has_to_string", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_vec.has_inter", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature.has_repr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_vec.has_union", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_stats.features_with_idf", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_stats.has_repr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature_stats.idf", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.predictor_cfg", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.predictor_cfg.to_feature_cfg", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.predictor_cfg.type", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "feature_search.feature.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "quadratic_form.isometry_sum_squares", "description": " The isometry between a weighted sum of squares on the complex numbers and the\nsum of squares, i.e. `weighted_sum_squares` with weights 1 or 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_form.complex_equivalent", "description": "All nondegenerate quadratic forms on the complex numbers are equivalent.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_form.isometry_sum_squares_units", "description": " The isometry between a weighted sum of squares on the complex numbers and the\nsum of squares, i.e. `weighted_sum_squares` with weight `\u03bb i : \u03b9, 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quadratic_form.equivalent_sum_squares", "description": " A nondegenerate quadratic form on the complex numbers is equivalent to\nthe sum of squares, i.e. `weighted_sum_squares` with weight `\u03bb i : \u03b9, 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.eval\u2082_hom_bind\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2081_rename", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.mem_vars_bind\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.map_bind\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2081_comp_bind\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2081", "description": "`bind\u2081` is the \"left hand side\" bind operation on `mv_polynomial`, operating on the variable type.\nGiven a polynomial `p : mv_polynomial \u03c3 R` and a map `f : \u03c3 \u2192 mv_polynomial \u03c4 R` taking variables\nin `p` to polynomials in the variable type `\u03c4`, `bind\u2081 f p` replaces each variable in `p` with\nits value under `f`, producing a new polynomial in `\u03c4`. The coefficient type remains the same.\nThis operation is an algebra hom.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2081_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.aeval_eq_bind\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.eval\u2082_hom_C_eq_bind\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2082_monomial_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_lawful_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.eval\u2082_hom_bind\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.eval\u2082_hom_C_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2082_C_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2082_C_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.map_comp_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.join\u2081", "description": "`join\u2081` is the monadic join operation corresponding to `mv_polynomial.bind\u2081`. Given a polynomial `p`\nwith coefficients in `R` whose variables are polynomials in `\u03c3` with coefficients in `R`,\n`join\u2081 p` collapses `p` to a polynomial with variables in `\u03c3` and coefficients in `R`.\nThis operation is an algebra hom.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.join\u2082", "description": "`join\u2082` is the monadic join operation corresponding to `mv_polynomial.bind\u2082`. Given a polynomial `p`\nwith variables in `\u03c3` whose coefficients are polynomials in `\u03c3` with coefficients in `R`,\n`join\u2082 p` collapses `p` to a polynomial with variables in `\u03c3` and coefficients in `R`.\nThis operation is a ring hom.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.join\u2082_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.aeval_bind\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2082_monomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2081_bind\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2082", "description": "`bind\u2082` is the \"right hand side\" bind operation on `mv_polynomial`,\noperating on the coefficient type.\nGiven a polynomial `p : mv_polynomial \u03c3 R` and\na map `f : R \u2192 mv_polynomial \u03c3 S` taking coefficients in `p` to polynomials over a new ring `S`,\n`bind\u2082 f p` replaces each coefficient in `p` with its value under `f`,\nproducing a new polynomial over `S`.\nThe variable type remains the same. This operation is a ring hom.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2081_X_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.eval\u2082_hom_id_X_eq_join\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2082_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2081_comp_rename", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.join\u2081_rename", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.eval\u2082_hom_comp_bind\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.eval\u2082_hom_C_id_eq_join\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.aeval_bind\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.eval\u2082_hom_comp_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2082_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.rename_bind\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.hom_bind\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.vars_bind\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.monad", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2081_X_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.aeval_comp_bind\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2082_X_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.aeval_id_rename", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2081_C_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2082_comp_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2082_bind\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.map_bind\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.eval\u2082_hom_eq_bind\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2082_comp_bind\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.bind\u2081_monomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.is_lawful_monad", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.rename_comp_bind\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.aeval_id_eq_join\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.join\u2082_comp_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.extend_cofan_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.extend_cofan_\u03b9_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.has_finite_coproducts_of_has_binary_and_initial", "description": "If `C` has an initial object and binary coproducts, then it has finite coproducts.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_finite_coproducts_of_preserves_binary_and_initial", "description": "If `F` preserves the initial object and binary coproducts then it preserves finite products.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_fin_of_preserves_binary_and_initial", "description": "If `F` preserves the initial object and binary coproducts, then it preserves products indexed by\n`fin n` for any `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_shape_fin_of_preserves_binary_and_initial", "description": "If `F` preserves the initial object and binary coproducts, then it preserves colimits of shape\n`discrete (fin n)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_fin_of_preserves_binary_and_terminal", "description": "If `F` preserves the terminal object and binary products, then it preserves products indexed by\n`fin n` for any `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.has_finite_products_of_has_binary_and_terminal", "description": "If `C` has a terminal object and binary products, then it has finite products.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_finite_products_of_preserves_binary_and_terminal", "description": "If `F` preserves the terminal object and binary products then it preserves finite products.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.extend_cofan_is_colimit", "description": "Show that if the two given cofans in `extend_cofan` are colimits,\nthen the constructed cofan is also a colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.extend_fan", "description": "Given `n+1` objects of `C`, a fan for the last `n` with point `c\u2081.X` and a binary fan on `c\u2081.X` and\n`f 0`, we can build a fan for all `n+1`.\n\nIn `extend_fan_is_limit` we show that if the two given fans are limits, then this fan is also a\nlimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.extend_fan_\u03c0_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.extend_fan_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.extend_fan_is_limit", "description": "Show that if the two given fans in `extend_fan` are limits, then the constructed fan is also a\nlimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_shape_fin_of_preserves_binary_and_terminal", "description": "If `F` preserves the terminal object and binary products, then it preserves limits of shape\n`discrete (fin n)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.extend_cofan", "description": "Given `n+1` objects of `C`, a cofan for the last `n` with point `c\u2081.X`\nand a binary cofan on `c\u2081.X` and `f 0`, we can build a cofan for all `n+1`.\n\nIn `extend_cofan_is_colimit` we show that if the two given cofans are colimits,\nthen this cofan is also a colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.nat_cast_right_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.nat_abs_min_of_le_div_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.mul_inv_eq_gcd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_nat_cast'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.lift_comp_cast_add_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.coe_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.nat_cast_self'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.le_div_two_iff_mul_two_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.nontrivial'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_min_nat_abs_nat_cast_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.add_order_of_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.chinese_remainder", "description": " The **Chinese remainder theorem**. For a pair of coprime natural numbers, `m` and `n`,\n  the rings `zmod (m * n)` and `zmod m \u00d7 zmod n` are isomorphic.\n\nSee `ideal.quotient_inf_ring_equiv_pi_quotient` for the Chinese remainder theorem for ideals in any\nring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.coe_unit_of_coprime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.nat_cast_to_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.subsingleton_ring_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.units_equiv_coprime", "description": " Equivalence between the units of `zmod n` and\nthe subtype of terms `x : zmod n` for which `x.val` is comprime to `n`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_min_abs_mem_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_pow'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.fst_zmod_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.is_domain", "description": "`zmod p` is an integral domain when `p` is prime.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_id'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.snd_zmod_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.ext_zmod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.mul_inv_of_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.unit_of_coprime", "description": "`unit_of_coprime` makes an element of `(zmod n)\u02e3` given\n a natural number `x` and a proof that `x` is coprime to `n`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_mul'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.nat_cast_zmod_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.ker_int_cast_add_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_coe_unit_coprime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.nat_cast_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.char_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.ring_hom_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.ring_equiv_congr", "description": "The identity between `zmod m` and `zmod n` when `m = n`, as a ring isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.coe_mul_inv_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_sub_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_min_abs_neg_of_ne_half", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_min_abs_def_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_min_abs_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.neg_eq_self_mod_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_min_abs_mul_two_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.nat_coe_zmod_eq_zero_iff_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.has_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.injective_val_min_abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.lift_cast_add_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.inv", "description": " The inversion on `zmod n`.\nIt is setup in such a way that `a * a\u207b\u00b9` is equal to `gcd a.val n`.\nIn particular, if `a` is coprime to `n`, and hence a unit, `a * a\u207b\u00b9 = 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_int_cast'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.neg_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.coe_add_eq_ite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.subsingleton_units", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.int_cast_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.add_order_of_coe", "description": "  This lemma works in the case in which `zmod n` is not infinite, i.e. `n \u2260 0`.  The version\nwhere `a \u2260 0` is `add_order_of_coe'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.ker_int_cast_ring_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_min_abs_nonneg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.lift", "description": "The map from `zmod n` induced by `f : \u2124 \u2192+ A` that maps `n` to `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.int_cast_zmod_cast", "description": " So-named because the outer coercion is `int.cast` into `zmod`. For `int.cast` into an arbitrary\nring, see `zmod.int_cast_cast`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_eq_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_sub'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.nat_cast_nat_abs_val_min_abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.ne_neg_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_min_abs", "description": "`val_min_abs x` returns the integer in the same equivalence class as `x` that is closest to `0`,\n The result will be in the interval `(-n/2, n/2]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.nat_cast_comp_val", "description": "The coercions are respectively `nat.cast` and `zmod.cast`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.int_coe_eq_int_coe_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_add'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.int_cast_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.nat_abs_val_min_abs_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.int_coe_zmod_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.int_coe_eq_int_coe_iff_dvd_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_neg_one", "description": "`-1 : zmod n` lifts to `n - 1 : R`. This avoids the characteristic assumption in `cast_neg`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.int_cast_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.neg_val'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_mul'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.lift_symm_apply_coe_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.lift_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_int_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.ring_hom_right_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.lift_comp_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.inv_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.nat_coe_eq_nat_coe_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_min_abs_nat_abs_eq_min", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val", "description": " `val a` is a natural number defined as:\n  - for `a : zmod 0` it is the absolute value of `a`\n  - for `a : zmod n` with `0 < n` it is the least natural number in the equivalence class\n\nSee `zmod.val_min_abs` for a variant that takes values in the integers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_min_abs_nat_cast_of_half_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.int_cast_comp_cast", "description": "The coercions are respectively `int.cast`, `zmod.cast`, and `zmod.cast`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.field", "description": "Field structure on `zmod p` if `p` is prime.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.le_div_two_iff_lt_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.coe_val_min_abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_cast_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.add_order_of_coe'", "description": " This lemma works in the case in which `a \u2260 0`.  The version where\n`zmod n` is not infinite, i.e. `n \u2260 0`, is `add_order_of_coe`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.neg_eq_self_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.ring_char_zmod_n", "description": "We have that `ring_char (zmod n) = n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_one'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_neg_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.int_coe_zmod_eq_zero_iff_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_eq_ite_val_min_abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.int_coe_eq_int_coe_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.nat_cast_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.ring_equiv", "description": " The unique ring isomorphism between `zmod n` and a ring `R`\nof characteristic `n` and cardinality `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_neg'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_one'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_one_eq_one_mod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.prime_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.lift_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_nat_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.subsingleton_ring_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.nat_coe_eq_nat_coe_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.int_cast_right_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.cast_hom", "description": " The canonical ring homomorphism from `zmod n` to a ring of characteristic `n`.\n\nSee also `zmod.lift` (in `data.zmod.quotient`) for a generalized version working in `add_group`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.nat_cast_zmod_val", "description": " So-named because the coercion is `nat.cast` into `zmod`. For `nat.cast` into an arbitrary ring,\nsee `zmod.nat_cast_val`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.nat_abs_mod_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.ring_hom_map_cast", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.inv_mul_of_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.inv_coe_unit", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.nat_abs_val_min_abs_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_min_abs_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_min_abs_def_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_min_abs_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.val_min_abs_nat_ca