"filter.tendsto_prod_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.prod_le_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.prod_ne_bot'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.prod_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.coprod_ne_bot_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.prod_map_map_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_const_principal_coprod_map_id_principal", "description": " Characterization of the coproduct of the `filter.map`s of two principal filters `\ud835\udcdf {a}` and\n`\ud835\udcdf {i}`, the first under the constant function `\u03bb a, b` and the second under the identity function.\nTogether with the next lemma, `map_prod_map_const_id_principal_coprod_principal`, this provides an\nexample showing that the inequality in the lemma `map_prod_map_coprod_le` can be strict.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.eventually_le.prod_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map_prod_map_const_id_principal_coprod_principal", "description": " Characterization of the `filter.map` of the coproduct of two principal filters `\ud835\udcdf {a}` and\n`\ud835\udcdf {i}`, under the `prod.map` of two functions, respectively the constant function `\u03bb a, b` and the\nidentity function.  Together with the previous lemma,\n`map_const_principal_coprod_map_id_principal`, this provides an example showing that the inequality\nin the lemma `map_prod_map_coprod_le` can be strict.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto_prod_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.prod_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.prod_principal_principal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.sup_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.bot_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.prod_mem_prod_iff", "description": "", "p": "m