ategory_theory.injective", "description": "An object `J` is injective iff every morphism into `J` can be obtained by extending a monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective.factors", "description": "An object `J` is injective iff every morphism into `J` can be obtained by extending a monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective.opposite.unop.injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective.d", "description": "When `C` has enough injective,\n`injective.d f : Y \u27f6 syzygies f` is the composition\n`cokernel.\u03c0 f \u226b \u03b9 (cokernel f)`.\n\n(When `C` is abelian, we have `exact f (injective.d f)`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective.category_theory.limits.biproduct.injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective.injective_under", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equivalence.enough_injectives_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective.\u03b9", "description": "The monomorphism `injective.\u03b9 : X \u27f6 injective.under X`\nfrom the arbitrarily chosen injective object under `X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective.opposite.op.category_theory.projective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective.enough_injectives_of_enough_projectives_op", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective.of_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective.zero_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective.under", "description": "`injective.under X` provides an arbitrarily chosen injective object equipped with\nan monomorphism `injective.\u03b9 : X \u27f6 injective.under X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective.category_theory.limits.biprod.injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective_presentation", "description": "An injective presentation of an object `X` consists of a monomorphism `f : X \u27f6 J`\nto some injective object `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective_presentation.J", "description": "An injective presentation of an object `X` consists of a monomorphism `f : X \u27f6 J`\nto some injective object `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective_presentation.injective", "description": "An injective presentation of an object `X` consists of a monomorphism `f : X \u27f6 J`\nto some injective object `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective_presentation.f", "description": "An injective presentation of an object `X` consists of a monomorphism `f : X \u27f6 J`\nto some injective object `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective_presentation.mono", "description": "An injective presentation of an object `X` consists of a monomorphism `f : X \u27f6 J`\nto some injective object `J`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective.injective_iff_preserves_epimorphisms_yoneda_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective.factor_thru", "description": "Let `J` be injective and `g` a morphism into `J`, then `g` can be factored through any monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.injective_of_map_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.map_injective_presentation", "description": " Given an adjunction `F \u22a3 G` such that `F` preserves monos, `G` maps an injective presentation\nof `X` to an injective presentation of `G(X)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective.\u03b9_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective.syzygies.injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.injective.exact.desc", "description": "Given 