: "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_subset_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_distrib_subset_right", "description": "The other direction does not hold because of the `u`-`u` cross terms on the RHS.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_nonempty_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_right_identity", "description": " If `b` is a right identity for `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b1`, then `{b}` is a right identity for\n`finset.image\u2082 f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.forall_image\u2082_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image_image\u2082_right_anticomm", "description": "Symmetric statement to `finset.image_image\u2082_antidistrib_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_image\u2082_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_image\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_image\u2082_image\u2082_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.subset_image\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_dvd_card_image\u2082_left", "description": " If each partial application of `f` is injective, and images of `t` under those partial\napplications are disjoint (but not necessarily distinct!), then the size of `s` divides the size of\n`finset.image\u2082 f s t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_image2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_subset_iff_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mem_image\u2082_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_inter_subset_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_singleton_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image_image\u2082_antidistrib_left", "description": "Symmetric statement to `finset.image\u2082_image_left_anticomm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_union_inter_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_mk_eq_product", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_insert_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image_subset_image\u2082_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nonempty.of_image\u2082_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_insert_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_union_inter_subset_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image_uncurry_product", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image_subset_image\u2082_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image_image\u2082_distrib_left", "description": "Symmetric statement to `finset.image\u2082_image_left_comm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image_image\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.bUnion_image_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image_image\u2082_distrib_right", "description": "Symmetric statement to `finset.image_image\u2082_right_comm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_image_left_comm", "description": "Symmetric statement to `finset.image_image\u2082_distrib_left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_le_card_image\u2082_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_singleton_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_congr'", "description": "A common special case of `image\u2082_congr`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image_image\u2082_antidistrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_inter_subset_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_image\u2082_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_inter_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image_image\u2082_antidistrib_right", "description": "Symmetric statement to `finset.image_image\u2082_right_anticomm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.coe_image\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_right_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_image\u2082_singleton_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_left_identity", "description": " If `a` is a left identity for `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b2`, then `{a}` is a left identity for\n`finset.image\u2082 f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nonempty.of_image\u2082_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_inter_union_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image_image\u2082_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_subset_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_image_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_dvd_card_image\u2082_right", "description": " If each partial application of `f` is injective, and images of `s` under those partial\napplications are disjoint (but not necessarily distinct!), then the size of `t` divides the size of\n`finset.image\u2082 f s t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_left_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_curry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_image_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_union_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_image\u2082_singleton_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_empty_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_image_left_anticomm", "description": "Symmetric statement to `finset.image_image\u2082_antidistrib_left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_le_card_image\u2082_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_union_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_singleton_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_inter_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nonempty.image\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_singleton_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image_image\u2082_right_comm", "description": "Symmetric statement to `finset.image_image\u2082_distrib_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mem_image\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.image\u2082_inter_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.correct.w_ne_one", "description": "The width of any cube in the partition cannot be 1.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.bottom_mem_side", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube", "description": " A (hyper)-cube (in standard orientation) is a vector `b` consisting of the bottom-left point\nof the cube, a width `w` and a proof that `w > 0`. We use functions from `fin n` to denote vectors.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.b", "description": " A (hyper)-cube (in standard orientation) is a vector `b` consisting of the bottom-left point\nof the cube, a width `w` and a proof that `w > 0`. We use functions from `fin n` to denote vectors.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.w", "description": " A (hyper)-cube (in standard orientation) is a vector `b` consisting of the bottom-left point\nof the cube, a width `w` and a proof that `w > 0`. We use functions from `fin n` to denote vectors.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.hw", "description": " A (hyper)-cube (in standard orientation) is a vector `b` consisting of the bottom-left point\nof the cube, a width `w` and a proof that `w > 0`. We use functions from `fin n` to denote vectors.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.bottom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.valley", "description": "A valley is a square on which cubes in the family of cubes are placed, so that the cubes\n completely cover the valley and none of those cubes is partially outside the square.\n We also require that no cube on it has the same size as the valley (so that there are at least\n two cubes on the valley).\n This is the main concept in the formalization.\n We prove that the smallest cube on a valley has another valley on the top of it, which\n gives an infinite sequence of cubes in the partition, which contradicts the finiteness.\n A valley is characterized by a cube `c` (which is not a cube in the family cs) by considering\n the bottom face of `c`.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.correct.nontrivial_fin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.correct.shift_up_bottom_subset_bottoms", "description": "The top of a cube (which is the bottom of the cube shifted up by its width) must be covered by\n bottoms of (other) cubes in the family.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.tail_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.correct.zero_le_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.b_mem_bottom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.nonempty_bcubes", "description": "There is a cube in the valley", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.b_mem_to_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.univ_pi_side", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.tail_shift_up", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.mi_not_on_boundary'", "description": "The same result that `mi` cannot lie on the boundary of the valley written as inequalities.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.not_correct", "description": "The infinite sequence of cubes contradicts the finiteness of the family.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.side", "description": "The j-th side of a cube is the half-open interval `[b j, b j + w)`", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.b_mem_side", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.on_boundary", "description": "A cube which lies on the boundary of a valley in dimension `j`", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.w_lt_w", "description": "Every cube in the valley must be smaller than it", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.sequence_of_cubes", "description": "We get a sequence of cubes whose size is decreasing", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.side_tail", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.t_le_t", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.head_shift_up", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.xm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.Ico_lemma", "description": "Given three intervals `I, J, K` such that `J \u2282 I`,\n neither endpoint of `J` coincides with an endpoint of `I`, `\u00ac (K \u2286 J)` and\n `K` does not lie completely to the left nor completely to the right of `J`.\n Then `I \u2229 K \\ J` is nonempty.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.correct.to_set_subset_unit_cube", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.correct.zero_le_b", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.correct", "description": "A finite family of (at least 2) cubes partitioning the unit cube with different sizes", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.correct.pairwise_disjoint", "description": "A finite family of (at least 2) cubes partitioning the unit cube with different sizes", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.correct.Union_eq", "description": "A finite family of (at least 2) cubes partitioning the unit cube with different sizes", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.correct.injective", "description": "A finite family of (at least 2) cubes partitioning the unit cube with different sizes", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.correct.three_le", "description": "A finite family of (at least 2) cubes partitioning the unit cube with different sizes", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.mi_strict_minimal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.shift_up", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.hw'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.correct.side_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.mi", "description": "We let `mi` be the (index for the) smallest cube in the valley `c`", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.nontrivial_bcubes", "description": "There are at least two cubes in a valley", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.mi_not_on_boundary", "description": "`mi` cannot lie on the boundary of the valley. Otherwise, the cube adjacent to it in the `j`-th\n direction will intersect one of the neighbouring cubes on the same boundary as `mi`.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.bcubes", "description": "the cubes which lie in the valley `c`", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.mi_minimal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.smallest_on_boundary", "description": "If `mi` lies on the boundary of the valley in dimension j, then this lemma expresses that all\n other cubes on the same boundary extend further from the boundary.\n More precisely, there is a j-th coordinate `x : \u211d` in the valley, but not in `mi`,\n such that every cube that shares a (particular) j-th coordinate with `mi` also contains j-th\n coordinate `x`", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.unit_cube", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.side_unit_cube", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.b_le_b", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.strict_anti_sequence_of_cubes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.to_set_disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.correct.b_add_w_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.tail", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.mi_xm_ne_one", "description": "The top of `mi` cannot be 1, since there is a larger cube in the valley", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.valley_unit_cube", "description": "The bottom of the unit cube is a valley", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.decreasing_sequence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.to_set_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.b_ne_xm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.to_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.exists_mi", "description": "There is a smallest cube in the valley", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.mi_mem_bcubes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.b_lt_xm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.injective_sequence_of_cubes", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cube.side_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.valley_mi", "description": "The top of `mi` gives rise to a new valley, since the neighbouring cubes extend further upward\n than `mi`.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.cannot_cube_a_cube", "description": "**Dissection of Cubes**: A cube cannot be cubed.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.82.correct.zero_le_of_mem_side", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.prod_adic_completions.topological_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.finite_integral_adeles.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.finite_integral_adeles.coe.alg_hom", "description": "The inclusion of `R_hat` in `K_hat` as an algebra homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.prod_adic_completions.algebra'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.finite_integral_adeles.coe.add_monoid_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.prod_adic_completions.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.finite_integral_adeles.coe.ring_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.prod_adic_completions.is_finite_adele.zero", "description": "The tuple `(0)_v` is a finite ad\u00e8le.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.finite_integral_adeles.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.finite_integral_adeles.topological_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.mem_finite_adele_ring_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.prod_adic_completions", "description": "The product of all `adic_completion`, where `v` runs over the maximal ideals of `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.prod_adic_completions.is_finite_adele.neg", "description": "The negative of a finite ad\u00e8le is a finite ad\u00e8le.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.prod_adic_completions.is_finite_adele.one", "description": "The tuple `(1)_v` is a finite ad\u00e8le.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.finite_integral_adeles.coe.add_monoid_hom", "description": "The inclusion of `R_hat` in `K_hat` as a homomorphism of additive monoids.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.prod_adic_completions.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.prod_adic_completions.is_finite_adele.add", "description": "The sum of two finite ad\u00e8les is a finite ad\u00e8le.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.finite_integral_adeles", "description": "The product of all `adic_completion_integers`, where `v` runs over the maximal ideals of `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.prod_adic_completions.is_finite_adele", "description": "An element `x : K_hat R K` is a finite ad\u00e8le if for all but finitely many height one ideals\n `v`, the component `x v` is a `v`-adic integer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.prod_adic_completions.topological_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.prod_adic_completions.is_scalar_tower_completions", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.prod_adic_completions.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.prod_adic_completions.is_finite_adele.mul", "description": "The product of two finite ad\u00e8les is a finite ad\u00e8le.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.prod_adic_completions.non_unital_non_assoc_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.finite_integral_adeles.coe.ring_hom", "description": "The inclusion of `R_hat` in `K_hat` as a ring homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.finite_adele_ring", "description": " The finite ad\u00e8le ring of `R` is the restricted product over all maximal ideals `v` of `R`\nof `adic_completion` with respect to `adic_completion_integers`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.finite_integral_adeles.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.prod_adic_completions.algebra_completions", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.finite_integral_adeles.coe_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.prod_adic_completions.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.finite_integral_adeles.dedekind_domain.prod_adic_completions.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dedekind_domain.finite_integral_adeles.coe.alg_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.ergodic_zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.ergodic_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.ergodic_zsmul_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.ae_empty_or_univ_of_forall_vadd_ae_eq_self", "description": " If a null-measurable subset of the circle is almost invariant under rotation by a family of\nrational angles with denominators tending to infinity, then it must be almost empty or almost full.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.ergodic_nsmul_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.as_small.up_obj_down", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_hom", "description": "`ulift_hom.{w} C` is an alias for `C`, which is endowed with a category instance\n whose morphisms are obtained by applying `ulift.{w}` to the morphisms from `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_hom.obj_up", "description": "The obvious function `C \u2192 ulift_hom C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.as_small.small_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.obj_up_obj_down", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.as_small.down", "description": "One half of the equivalence between `C` and `as_small C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift.up_functor_obj_down", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.as_small.down_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.as_small.equiv", "description": "The equivalence between `C` and `as_small C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_hom.obj_down", "description": "The obvious function `ulift_hom C \u2192 C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift.down_functor", "description": "The functorial version of `ulift.down`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.as_small.up_map_down", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_hom.up_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.as_small.equiv_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_hom.equiv", "description": "The equivalence between `C` and `ulift_hom C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift.equivalence_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.as_small.equiv_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.as_small.down_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_hom.down", "description": "One half of the quivalence between `C` and `ulift_hom C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift.down_functor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift.up_functor", "description": "The functorial version of `ulift.up`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift.equivalence_counit_iso_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.obj_down_obj_up", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.as_small.equiv_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift.equivalence_unit_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.as_small", "description": "`as_small C` is a small category equivalent to `C`.\n More specifically, if `C : Type u` is endowed with `category.{v} C`, then\n `as_small.{w} C : Type (max w v u)` is endowed with an instance of a small category.\n\n The objects and morphisms of `as_small C` are defined by applying `ulift` to the\n objects and morphisms of `C`.\n\n Note: We require a category instance for this definition in order to have direct\n access to the universe level `v`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_hom.down_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_hom_ulift_category.equiv", "description": "The equivalence between `C` and `ulift_hom (ulift C)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.as_small.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_hom.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.as_small.up", "description": "One half of the equivalence between `C` and `as_small C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift.up_functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.as_small.equiv_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_hom.up", "description": "One half of the quivalence between `C` and `ulift_hom C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_hom.down_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift.equivalence_counit_iso_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift.down_functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift.equivalence_unit_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift.equivalence_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift.equivalence", "description": "The categorical equivalence between `C` and `ulift C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.ulift_hom.up_map_down", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.has_forget_to_FinPartOrd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.dual_equiv", "description": "The equivalence between `FinBddDistLat` and itself induced by `order_dual` both ways.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.iso.mk_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.dual_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.dual_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.iso.mk", "description": " Constructs an equivalence between finite distributive lattices from an order isomorphism\nbetween them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.distrib_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.bounded_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.dual", "description": "`order_dual` as a functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.concrete_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.large_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat_dual_comp_forget_to_BddDistLat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.iso.mk_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.has_forget_to_BddDistLat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.dual_equiv_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.of", "description": "Construct a bundled `FinBddDistLat` from a `nonempty` `bounded_order` `distrib_lattice`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat", "description": "The category of finite distributive lattices with bounded lattice morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.to_BddDistLat", "description": "The category of finite distributive lattices with bounded lattice morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.is_fintype", "description": "The category of finite distributive lattices with bounded lattice morphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.dual_equiv_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.has_coe_to_sort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "FinBddDistLat.of'", "description": "Construct a bundled `FinBddDistLat` from a `nonempty` `bounded_order` `distrib_lattice`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum_to_CompHaus.ess_surj", "description": "The functor Compactum_to_CompHaus is essentially surjective.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.free", "description": "The \"free\" Compactum functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum", "description": "The type `Compactum` of Compacta, defined as algebras for the ultrafilter monad.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CompHaus.forget_creates_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Profinite.forget_creates_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.of_topological_space", "description": "Given any compact Hausdorff space, we construct a Compactum.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.forget.faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.hom_of_continuous", "description": "Any continuous map between Compacta is a morphism of compacta.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.adj", "description": "The adjunction between `free` and `forget`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.le_nhds_of_str_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum_to_CompHaus_comp_forget", "description": " The forgetful functors of `Compactum` and `CompHaus` are compatible via\n`Compactum_to_CompHaus`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.category_theory.limits.has_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.continuous_of_hom", "description": "Any morphism of compacta is continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.forget", "description": "The forgetful functor to Type*", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum_to_CompHaus.iso_of_topological_space", "description": "This definition is used to prove essential surjectivity of Compactum_to_CompHaus.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum_to_CompHaus.is_equivalence", "description": "The functor Compactum_to_CompHaus is an equivalence of categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.incl", "description": "The inclusion of `X` into `ultrafilter X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.is_closed_cl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.str", "description": "The structure map for a compactum, essentially sending an ultrafilter to its limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.forget.creates_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.str_hom_commute", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.t2_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum_to_CompHaus.faithful", "description": "The functor Compactum_to_CompHaus is faithful.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.Lim_eq_str", "description": "The structure map of a compactum actually computes limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum_to_CompHaus.full", "description": "The functor Compactum_to_CompHaus is full.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.str_eq_of_le_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.quiver.hom.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.join_distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.join", "description": "The monadic join.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.category_theory.concrete_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.topological_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.has_coe_to_sort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum_to_CompHaus", "description": "The functor functor from Compactum to CompHaus.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.is_closed_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.compact_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.str_incl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Compactum.cl_eq_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.le_iff_mem_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.gc_homogeneous_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.basic_open_mul_le_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.gc_ideal", "description": "`zero_locus` and `vanishing_ideal` form a galois connection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.union_zero_locus", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.is_closed_zero_locus", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.mem_zero_locus", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.vanishing_ideal_anti_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.ideal_le_vanishing_ideal_zero_locus", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_empty_of_one_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_sup_homogeneous_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.mem_coe_basic_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zariski_topology", "description": " The Zariski topology on the prime spectrum of a commutative ring is defined via the closed sets\nof the topology: they are exactly those sets that are the zero locus of a subset of the ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.basic_open_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_anti_mono_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_mul_homogeneous_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.subset_zero_locus_iff_le_vanishing_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.mem_basic_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.vanishing_ideal", "description": " The vanishing ideal of a set `t` of points of the projective spectrum of a commutative ring `R`\nis the intersection of all the relevant homogeneous prime ideals in the set `t`.\n\nAn element `f` of `A` can be thought of as a dependent function on the projective spectrum of `\ud835\udc9c`.\nAt a point `x` (a homogeneous prime ideal) the function (i.e., element) `f` takes values in the\nquotient ring `A` modulo the prime ideal `x`. In this manner, `vanishing_ideal t` is exactly the\nideal of `A` consisting of all \"functions\" that vanish on all of `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.vanishing_ideal_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_singleton_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.basic_open_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.vanishing_ideal_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.homogeneous_ideal_le_vanishing_ideal_zero_locus", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_mul_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.is_open_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum", "description": " The projective spectrum of a graded commutative ring is the subtype of all homogenous ideals\nthat are prime and do not contain the irrelevant ideal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.as_homogeneous_ideal", "description": " The projective spectrum of a graded commutative ring is the subtype of all homogenous ideals\nthat are prime and do not contain the irrelevant ideal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.is_prime", "description": " The projective spectrum of a graded commutative ring is the subtype of all homogenous ideals\nthat are prime and do not contain the irrelevant ideal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.not_irrelevant_le", "description": " The projective spectrum of a graded commutative ring is the subtype of all homogenous ideals\nthat are prime and do not contain the irrelevant ideal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_sup_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.basic_open_eq_zero_locus_compl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.vanishing_ideal_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.basic_open_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.gc_set", "description": "`zero_locus` and `vanishing_ideal` form a galois connection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.basic_open_mul_le_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_anti_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.subset_zero_locus_iff_subset_vanishing_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.is_topological_basis_basic_opens", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_singleton_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.is_closed_iff_zero_locus", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.basic_open_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_bUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_supr_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_singleton_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_anti_mono_homogeneous_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.basic_open", "description": "`basic_open r` is the open subset containing all prime ideals not containing `r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_vanishing_ideal_eq_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.basic_open_eq_union_of_projection", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.as_ideal_le_as_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.as_ideal_lt_as_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus", "description": " The zero locus of a set `s` of elements of a commutative ring `A` is the set of all relevant\nhomogeneous prime ideals of the ring that contain the set `s`.\n\nAn element `f` of `A` can be thought of as a dependent function on the projective spectrum of `\ud835\udc9c`.\nAt a point `x` (a homogeneous prime ideal) the function (i.e., element) `f` takes values in the\nquotient ring `A` modulo the prime ideal `x`. In this manner, `zero_locus s` is exactly the subset\nof `projective_spectrum \ud835\udc9c` where all \"functions\" in `s` vanish simultaneously.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.coe_vanishing_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.vanishing_ideal_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.mem_compl_zero_locus_iff_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.subset_vanishing_ideal_zero_locus", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.is_open_basic_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.vanishing_ideal_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.sup_vanishing_ideal_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.subset_zero_locus_vanishing_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.Top", "description": "The underlying topology of `Proj` is the projective spectrum of graded ring `A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_singleton_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.mem_vanishing_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "projective_spectrum.zero_locus_supr_homogeneous_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.is_pell_pell_zd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.pell_zd", "description": "The Pell sequence can also be viewed as an element of `\u2124\u221ad`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.xy_succ_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.xn_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.y_mul_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.eq_pell", "description": " Every solution to **Pell's equation** is recursively obtained from the initial solution\n`(1,0)` using the recursion `pell`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.xn_modeq_x2n_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.yn"