l.is_pell_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.yn_succ_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.yn_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.ysq_dvd_yy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.eq_pell_lem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.pell_zd_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.xz_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.dz_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.yz_succ_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.xn_modeq_x2n_add_lem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.yn_modeq_a_sub_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.eq_pell_zd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.pell", "description": " The Pell sequences, i.e. the sequence of integer solutions to `x ^ 2 - d * y ^ 2 = 1`, where\n`d = a ^ 2 - 1`, defined together in mutual recursion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.xn", "description": "The Pell `x` sequence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.x_sub_y_dvd_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.pell_zd_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.eq_of_xn_modeq_lem3", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pell.pell_zd_succ_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.measurable_equiv_Ico", "description": "The isomorphism `add_circle T \u2243 Ico a (a + T)` whose inverse is the natural quotient map,\n as an equivalence of measurable spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unit_add_circle.interval_integral_preimage", "description": " The integral of an almost-everywhere strongly measurable function over `unit_add_circle` is\nequal to the integral over an interval (t, t + 1] in `\u211d` of its lift to `\u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic.tendsto_at_bot_interval_integral_of_pos'", "description": " If `g : \u211d \u2192 \u211d` is periodic with period `T > 0` and `\u2200 x, 0 < g x`, then `t \u21a6 \u222b x in 0..t, g x`\ntends to `-\u221e` as `t` tends to `-\u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.measure_theory.measure_space.volume.is_unif_loc_doubling_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.measure_space", "description": " Equip the \"additive circle\" `\u211d \u29f8 (\u2124 \u2219 T)` with, as a standard measure, the Haar measure of total\nmass `T`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.lintegral_preimage", "description": " The lower integral of a function over `add_circle T` is equal to the lower integral over an\ninterval (t, t + T] in `\u211d` of its lift to `\u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_fundamental_domain_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic.interval_integral_add_zsmul_eq", "description": " If `f` is an integrable periodic function with period `T`, and `n` is an integer, then its\nintegral over `[t, t + n \u2022 T]` is `n` times its integral over `[t, t + T]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.measure_preserving_mk", "description": " The covering map from `\u211d` to the \"additive circle\" `\u211d \u29f8 (\u2124 \u2219 T)` is measure-preserving,\nconsidered with respect to the standard measure (defined to be the Haar measure of total mass `T`)\non the additive circle, and with respect to the restriction of Lebsegue measure on `\u211d` to an\ninterval (t, t + T].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.volume_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.measure_theory.measure_space.volume.measure_theory.measure.is_add_haar_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_fundamental_domain_Ioc'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic.interval_integral_add_eq_add", "description": " If `f` is an integrable periodic function with period `T`, then its integral over `[t, s + T]`\nis the sum of its integrals over the intervals `[t, s]` and `[t, t + T]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic.integral_le_Sup_add_zsmul_of_pos", "description": " If `g : \u211d \u2192 \u211d` is periodic with period `T > 0`, then for any `t : \u211d`, the function\n`t \u21a6 \u222b x in 0..t, g x` is bounded above by `t \u21a6 X + \u230at/T\u230b \u2022 Y` for appropriate constants `X` and\n`Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.measurable_mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unit_add_circle.is_finite_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.interval_integral_preimage", "description": " The integral of an almost-everywhere strongly measurable function over `add_circle T` is equal\nto the integral over an interval (t, t + T] in `\u211d` of its lift to `\u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.borel_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unit_add_circle.integral_preimage", "description": " The integral of an almost-everywhere strongly measurable function over `unit_add_circle` is\nequal to the integral over an interval (t, t + 1] in `\u211d` of its lift to `\u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic.tendsto_at_bot_interval_integral_of_pos", "description": " If `g : \u211d \u2192 \u211d` is periodic with period `T > 0` and `0 < \u222b x in 0..T, g x`, then\n`t \u21a6 \u222b x in 0..t, g x` tends to `-\u221e` as `t` tends to `-\u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unit_add_circle.lintegral_preimage", "description": " The integral of a measurable function over `unit_add_circle` is equal to the integral over an\ninterval (t, t + 1] in `\u211d` of its lift to `\u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unit_add_circle.measure_preserving_mk", "description": " The covering map from `\u211d` to the \"unit additive circle\" `\u211d \u29f8 \u2124` is measure-preserving,\nconsidered with respect to the standard measure (defined to be the Haar measure of total mass 1)\non the additive circle, and with respect to the restriction of Lebsegue measure on `\u211d` to an\ninterval (t, t + 1].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic.Inf_add_zsmul_le_integral_of_pos", "description": " If `g : \u211d \u2192 \u211d` is periodic with period `T > 0`, then for any `t : \u211d`, the function\n`t \u21a6 \u222b x in 0..t, g x` is bounded below by `t \u21a6 X + \u230at/T\u230b \u2022 Y` for appropriate constants `X` and\n`Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unit_add_circle.measure_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.measurable_equiv_Ioc", "description": "The isomorphism `add_circle T \u2243 Ioc a (a + T)` whose inverse is the natural quotient map,\n as an equivalence of measurable spaces.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.measure_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic.interval_integral_add_eq", "description": " If `f` is a periodic function with period `T`, then its integral over `[t, t + T]` does not\ndepend on `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.measurable_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unit_add_circle.measure_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.integral_preimage", "description": " The integral of an almost-everywhere strongly measurable function over `add_circle T` is equal\nto the integral over an interval (t, t + T] in `\u211d` of its lift to `\u211d`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_circle.is_finite_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic.tendsto_at_top_interval_integral_of_pos", "description": " If `g : \u211d \u2192 \u211d` is periodic with period `T > 0` and `0 < \u222b x in 0..T, g x`, then\n`t \u21a6 \u222b x in 0..t, g x` tends to `\u221e` as `t` tends to `\u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic.interval_integral_add_eq_of_pos", "description": "An auxiliary lemma for a more general `function.periodic.interval_integral_add_eq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.periodic.tendsto_at_top_interval_integral_of_pos'", "description": " If `g : \u211d \u2192 \u211d` is periodic with period `T > 0` and `\u2200 x, 0 < g x`, then `t \u21a6 \u222b x in 0..t, g x`\ntends to `\u221e` as `t` tends to `\u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise_of_forall", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise.imp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise_join", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise_middle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise_reverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise_and_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise_pmap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pw_filter_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise.filter_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise.sublist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pw_filter_sublist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.rel_of_pairwise_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise_iff_nth_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise.iff_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise_append", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise.forall_of_forall", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pw_filter_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise.pw_filter", "description": "**Alias** of the reverse direction of `list.pw_filter_eq_self`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pw_filter_cons_of_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise.and_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise.tail", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise.filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise_of_reflexive_of_forall_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwise.forall_of_forall_of_flip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.pairwis