le.id_sequence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "traversable.pure_traverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "traversable.pure_transformation_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "traversable.traverse_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "traversable.traverse_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "traversable.traverse_map'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "traversable.map_traverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "traversable.comp_sequence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "traversable.naturality'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "traversable.map_eq_traverse_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "traversable.naturality_pf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "traversable.traverse_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "traversable.map_traverse'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "traversable.traverse_eq_map_id'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "traversable.pure_transformation", "description": " The natural applicative transformation from the identity functor\nto `F`, defined by `pure : \u03a0 {\u03b1}, \u03b1 \u2192 F \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.of_injective_finite_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite.set.finite_of_finite_image", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.coe_order_iso_of_fin_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sorted_last_eq_max'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sorted_zero_eq_min'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sort_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.length_sort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sorted_last_eq_max'_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sort_nodup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.max'_eq_sorted_last", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mem_sort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sort_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.order_emb_of_fin_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.range_order_emb_of_fin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.order_emb_of_fin_unique", "description": " Any increasing map `f` from `fin k` to a finset of cardinality `k` has to coincide with\nthe increasing bijection `order_emb_of_fin s h`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.order_iso_of_fin_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.has_repr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sort_sorted_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sorted_zero_eq_min'_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sort_sorted", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.order_emb_of_fin", "description": " Given a finset `s` of cardinality `k` in a linear order `\u03b1`, the map `order_emb_of_fin s h` is\nthe increasing bijection between `fin k` and `s` as an order embedding into `\u03b1`. Here, `h` is a\nproof that the cardinality of `s` is `k`. We use this instead of an embedding `fin s.card \u21aao \u03b1` to\navoid casting issues in further uses of this function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sort_to_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.order_emb_of_fin_last", "description": "The bijection `order_emb_of_fin s h` sends `k-1` to the maximum of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.min'_eq_sorted_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.order_emb_of_card_le_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.order_emb_of_fin_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.order_emb_of_fin_singleton", "description": "`order_emb_of_fin {a} h` sends any argument to `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.order_iso_of_fin", "description": " Given a finset `s` of cardinality `k` in a linear order `\u03b1`, the map `order_iso_of_fin s h`\nis the increasing bijection between `fin k` and `s` as an `order_iso`. Here, `h` is a proof that\nthe cardinality of `s` is `k`. We use this instead of an iso `fin s.card \u2243o s` to avoid\ncasting issues in further uses of this function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.order_emb_of_fin_unique'", "description": " An order embedding `f` from `fin k` to a finset of cardinality `k` has to coincide with\nthe increasing bijection `order_emb_of_fin s h`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.order_emb_of_fin_zero", "description": "The bijection `order_emb_of_fin s h` sends `0` to the minimum of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.order_emb_of_fin_eq_order_emb_of_fin_iff", "description": " Two parametrizations `order_emb_of_fin` of the same set take the same value on `i` and `j` if\nand only if `i = j`. Since they can be defined on a priori not defeq types `fin k` and `fin l`\n(although necessarily `k = l`), the conclusion is rather written `(i : \u2115) = (j : \u2115)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sort", "description": "`sort s` constructs a sorted list from the unordered set `s`.\n (Uses merge sort algorithm.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.order_emb_of_card_le", "description": " Given a finset `s` of size at least `k` in a linear order `\u03b1`, the map `order_emb_of_card_le`\nis an order embedding from `fin k` to `\u03b1` whose image is contained in `s`. Specifically, it maps\n`fin k` to an initial segment of `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sort_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sort_perm_to_list", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "id.is_comm_applicative", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.applicative_id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "applicative.map_seq_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.add_const.is_lawful_applicative", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.is_lawful_applicative", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comp.seq_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.seq_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.const.applicative", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.is_comm_applicative", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.map_pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.seq_pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.const.is_lawful_applicative", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "applicative.pure_seq_eq_map'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "applicative.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.applicative_comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.comp.pure_seq_eq_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "functor.add_const.applicative", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.stable_iff_exists_pow_smul_eq_of_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.stable.inter_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.submodule_closure_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration", "description": " An `I`-filtration on the module `M` is a sequence of decreasing submodules `N i` such that\n`I \u2022 (N i) \u2264 N (i + 1)`. Note that we do not require the filtration to start from `\u22a4`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.N", "description": " An `I`-filtration on the module `M` is a sequence of decreasing submodules `N i` such that\n`I \u2022 (N i) \u2264 N (i + 1)`. Note that we do not require the filtration to start from `\u22a4`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.mono", "description": " An `I`-filtration on the module `M` is a sequence of decreasing submodules `N i` such that\n`I \u2022 (N i) \u2264 N (i + 1)`. Note that we do not require the filtration to start from `\u22a4`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.smul_le", "description": " An `I`-filtration on the module `M` is a sequence of decreasing submodules `N i` such that\n`I \u2022 (N i) \u2264 N (i + 1)`. Note that we do not require the filtration to start from `\u22a4`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.has_inf", "description": "The `inf` of two `I.filtration`s is an `I.filtration`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.sup_N", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.submodule_fg_iff_stable", "description": " If the components of a filtration are finitely generated, then the filtration is stable iff\nits associated submodule of is finitely generated.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.infi_pow_smul_eq_bot_of_local_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.inf_submodule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.stable_filtration", "description": "The trivial stable `I`-filtration of `N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.has_sup", "description": "The `sup` of two `I.filtration`s is an `I.filtration`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.bot_N", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.stable", "description": "An `I` filtration is stable if `I \u2022 F.N n = F.N (n+1)` for large enough `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.submodule_eq_span_le_iff_stable_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.stable.inter_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.submodule", "description": "The `R[IX]`-submodule of `M[X]` associated with an `I`-filtration.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.stable.of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.top_N", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.Sup_N", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.complete_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.mem_submodule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.trivial_filtration_N", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.trivial_filtration", "description": "The trivial `I`-filtration of `N`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.stable_filtration_N", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.Inf_N", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.has_Sup", "description": "The `Sup` of a family of `I.filtration`s is an `I.filtration`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.has_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.antitone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.stable.exists_pow_smul_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.pow_smul_le_pow_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.inf_N", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.submodule_inf_hom", "description": "`ideal.filtration.submodule` as an `inf_hom`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.stable.exists_forall_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.submodule_span_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.stable.bounded_difference", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.exists_pow_inf_eq_pow_smul", "description": "**Artin-Rees lemma**", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.has_Inf", "description": "The `Inf` of a family of `I.filtration`s is an `I.filtration`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.stable_filtration_stable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_infi_smul_pow_eq_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.pow_smul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.infi_pow_eq_bot_of_is_domain", "description": "**Krull's intersection theorem** for noetherian domains.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.has_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.stable.exists_pow_smul_eq_of_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.supr_N", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.filtration.infi_N", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.infi_pow_eq_bot_of_local_ring", "description": "**Krull's intersection theorem** for noetherian local rings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_coequalizers_of_has_pushouts_and_binary_coproducts.construct_coequalizer", "description": "Define the equalizing object", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_coequalizers_of_has_pushouts_and_binary_coproducts.coequalizer_cocone_is_colimit", "description": "Show the equalizing cocone is a colimit", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_equalizers_of_has_pullbacks_and_binary_products.equalizer_cone_is_limit", "description": "Show the equalizing cone is a limit", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_equalizers_of_has_pullbacks_and_binary_products.equalizer_cone", "description": "Define the equalizing cone", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_equalizers_of_has_pullbacks_and_binary_products.pullback_fst", "description": "Define the equalizing morphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_coequalizers_of_has_pushouts_and_binary_coproducts.coequalizer_cocone", "description": "Define the equalizing cocone", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_coequalizers_of_has_pushouts_and_binary_coproducts.pushout_inl", "description": "Define the equalizing morphism", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_equalizers_of_has_pullbacks_and_binary_products.construct_equalizer", "description": "Define the equalizing object", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_coequalizers_of_has_pushouts_and_binary_coproducts.pushout_inl_eq_pushout_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_equalizers_of_has_pullbacks_and_binary_products.pullback_fst_eq_pullback_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_coequalizers_of_preserves_pushouts_and_binary_coproducts", "description": "A functor that preserves pushouts and binary coproducts also presrves coequalizers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_equalizers_of_preserves_pullbacks_and_binary_products", "description": "A functor that preserves pullbacks and binary products also presrves equalizers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_coequalizers_of_has_pushouts_and_binary_coproducts", "description": "Any category with pullbacks and binary products, has equalizers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_equalizers_of_has_pullbacks_and_binary_products", "description": "Any category with pullbacks and binary products, has equalizers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.Ici_bot", "description": "Order isomorphism between `Ici (\u22a5 : \u03b1)` and `\u03b1` when `\u03b1` has a bottom element", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.preimage_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.preimage_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.image_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.image_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.image_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.image_Iic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.Iic_top", "description": "Order isomorphism between `Iic (\u22a4 : \u03b1)` and `\u03b1` when `\u03b1` has a top element", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.image_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.image_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.preimage_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.preimage_Iio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.preimage_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.image_Iio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.preimage_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.preimage_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.preimage_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_iso.image_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.mk_lt_zero_pf_aux", "description": "`mk_lt_zero_pf_aux c pf npf coeff` assumes that `pf` is a proof of `t1 R1 0` and `npf` is a proof\nof `t2 R2 0`. It uses `mk_single_comp_zero_pf` to prove `t1 + coeff*t2 R 0`, and returns `R`\nalong with this proof.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.mk_neg_eq_zero_pf", "description": "If `e` is a proof that `t = 0`, `mk_neg_eq_zero_pf e` returns a proof that `-t = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.add_neg_eq_pfs", "description": "`add_neg_eq_pfs l` inspects the list of proofs `l` for proofs of the form `t = 0`. For each such\nproof, it adds a proof of `-t = 0` to the list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.ineq_const_nm", "description": "If our goal is to add together two inequalities `t1 R1 0` and `t2 R2 0`,\n`ineq_const_nm R1 R2` produces the strength of the inequality in the sum `R`,\nalong with the name of a lemma to apply in order to conclude `t1 + t2 R 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.ineq_prf_tp", "description": "If `prf` is a proof of `t R s`, `ineq_prf_tp prf` returns the type of `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.prove_eq_zero_using", "description": "`prove_eq_zero_using tac e` tries to use `tac` to construct a proof of `e = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.mul_expr", "description": "`mul_expr n e` creates a `pexpr` representing `n*e`.\nWhen elaborated, the coefficient will be a native numeral of the same type as `e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.prove_false_by_linarith", "description": "`prove_false_by_linarith` is the main workhorse of `linarith`.\nGiven a list `l` of proofs of `t\u1d62 R\u1d62 0`,\nit tries to derive a contradiction from `l` and use this to produce a proof of `false`.\n\nAn oracle is used to search for a certificate of unsatisfiability.\nIn the current implementation, this is the Fourier Motzkin elimination routine in\n`elimination.lean`, but other oracles could easily be swapped in.\n\nThe returned certificate is a map `m` from hypothesis indices to natural number coefficients.\nIf our set of hypotheses has the form  `{t\u1d62 R\u1d62 0}`,\nthen the elimination process should have guaranteed that\n1.\\ `\u2211 (m i)*t\u1d62 = 0`,\nwith at least one `i` such that `m i > 0` and `R\u1d62` is `<`.\n\nWe have also that\n2.\\ `\u2211 (m i)*t\u1d62 < 0`,\nsince for each `i`, `(m i)*t\u1d62 \u2264 0` and at least one is strictly negative.\nSo we conclude a contradiction `0 < 0`.\n\nIt remains to produce proofs of (1) and (2). (1) is verified by calling the `discharger` tactic\nof the `linarith_config` object, which is typically `ring`. We prove (2) by folding over the\nset of hypotheses.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.mk_neg_one_lt_zero_pf", "description": "`mk_neg_one_lt_zero_pf tp` returns a proof of `-1 < 0`,\nwhere the numerals are natively of type `tp`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.term_of_ineq_prf", "description": "If `prf` is a proof of `t R s`, `term_of_ineq_prf prf` returns `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.add_exprs", "description": "`add_exprs l` creates a `pexpr` representing the sum of the elements of `l`, associated left.\nIf `l` is empty, it will be the `pexpr` 0. Otherwise, it does not include 0 in the sum.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linarith.mk_lt_zero_pf", "description": "`mk_lt_zero_pf coeffs pfs` takes a list of proofs of the form `t\u1d62 R\u1d62 0`,\npaired with coefficients `c\u1d62`.\nIt produces a proof that `\u2211c\u1d62 * t\u1d62 R 0`, where `R` is as strong as possible.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "level.occurs", "description": "Return tt iff the first level occurs in the second", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.lt", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.lex_lt", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level", "description": "A type universe term. eg `max u v`. Reflect a C++ level object. The VM replaces it with the C++ implementation.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.zero", "description": "A type universe term. eg `max u v`. Reflect a C++ level object. The VM replaces it with the C++ implementation.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.succ", "description": "A type universe term. eg `max u v`. Reflect a C++ level object. The VM replaces it with the C++ implementation.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.max", "description": "A type universe term. eg `max u v`. Reflect a C++ level object. The VM replaces it with the C++ implementation.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.imax", "description": "A type universe term. eg `max u v`. Reflect a C++ level object. The VM replaces it with the C++ implementation.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.param", "description": "A type universe term. eg `max u v`. Reflect a C++ level object. The VM replaces it with the C++ implementation.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.mvar", "description": "A type universe term. eg `max u v`. Reflect a C++ level object. The VM replaces it with the C++ implementation.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.of_nat", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.to_format", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.to_string", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.instantiate", "description": "Replace a parameter named n with l in the first level if the list contains the pair (n, l)", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.fold", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.has_decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.has_param", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.has_to_string", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.normalize", "description": "Return the given level expression normal form", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "level.eqv", "description": "Return tt iff lhs and rhs denote the same level.\n  The check is done by normalization.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "set.image_multiset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_fintype_sum_pi", "description": "A special case of `set.image_finset_sum_pi` for `finset.univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.multiset_sum_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.mem_finset_sum", "description": "The n-ary version of `set.mem_add`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_multiset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.mem_finset_prod", "description": "The n-ary version of `set.mem_mul`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_finset_sum_pi", "description": "The n-ary version of `set.add_image_prod`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.multiset_prod_subset_multiset_prod", "description": "An n-ary version of `set.mul_subset_mul`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_list_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.mem_fintype_prod", "description": "A version of `set.mem_finset_prod` with a simpler RHS for products over a fintype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.list_sum_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finset_prod_mem_finset_prod", "description": "An n-ary version of `set.mul_mem_mul`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.multiset_prod_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finset_prod_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finset_prod_subset_finset_prod", "description": "An n-ary version of `set.mul_subset_mul`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.list_sum_mem_list_sum", "description": "An n-ary version of `set.add_mem_add`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.multiset_sum_mem_multiset_sum", "description": "An n-ary version of `set.add_mem_add`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.list_sum_subset_list_sum", "description": "An n-ary version of `set.add_subset_add`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.list_prod_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finset_sum_subset_finset_sum", "description": "An n-ary version of `set.add_subset_add`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.mem_fintype_sum", "description": "A version of `set.mem_finset_sum` with a simpler RHS for sums over a fintype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.list_prod_subset_list_prod", "description": "An n-ary version of `set.mul_subset_mul`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.list_prod_mem_list_prod", "description": "An n-ary version of `set.mul_mem_mul`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.multiset_prod_mem_multiset_prod", "description": "An n-ary version of `set.mul_mem_mul`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finset_sum_mem_finset_sum", "description": "An n-ary version of `set.add_mem_add`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finset_sum_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_finset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_fintype_prod_pi", "description": "A special case of `set.image_finset_prod_pi` for `finset.univ`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_list_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.multiset_sum_subset_multiset_sum", "description": "An n-ary version of `set.add_subset_add`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.image_finset_prod_pi", "description": "The n-ary version of `set.image_mul_prod`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_unit_speed_on.Icc_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_constant_speed_on_with_iff_variation_on_from_to_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_unit_speed_on", "description": "`f` has unit speed on `s` if it is linearly parameterized by `l = 1` on `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_unit_speed_on_Icc_zero", "description": "If both `f` and `f \u2218 \u03c6` have unit speed (on `Icc 0 t` and `Icc 0 s` respectively)\nand `\u03c6` monotonically maps `Icc 0 s` onto `Icc 0 t`, then `\u03c6` is the identity on `Icc 0 s`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_constant_speed_on_with", "description": "`f` has constant speed `l` on `s` if the variation of `f` on `s \u2229 Icc x y` is equal to\n`l * (y - x)` for any `x y` in `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "natural_parameterization", "description": "The natural parameterization of `f` on `s`, which, if `f` has locally bounded variation on `s`,\n* has unit speed on `s`\n  (by `natural_parameterization_has_unit_speed`).\n* composed with `variation_on_from_to f s a`, is at distance zero from `f`\n  (by `natural_parameterization_edist_zero`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_unit_speed", "description": "If both `f` and `f \u2218 \u03c6` have unit speed (on `t` and `s` respectively) and `\u03c6`\nmonotonically maps `s` onto `t`, then `\u03c6` is just a translation (on `s`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_unit_speed_on.union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_unit_speed_natural_parameterization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_constant_speed_on_with_iff_ordered", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_constant_speed_on_with_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_constant_speed_on_with.has_locally_bounded_variation_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_constant_speed_on_with.union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_constant_speed_on_with.Icc_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_constant_speed_on_with.ratio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "edist_natural_parameterization_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_constant_speed_on_with_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03b9_preserves_colimits_iso_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_colimit_nat_iso", "description": " If `C, D` has all colimits of shape `J`, and `G` preserves them, then `preserves_colimit_iso`\nis functorial wrt `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_limits_iso_hom_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lift_comp_preserves_limits_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_limit_nat_iso_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_colimits_iso_inv_comp_desc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03b9_preserves_colimits_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_limits_iso_inv_\u03c0_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_limits_iso_inv_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_colimits_iso_inv_comp_desc_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03b9_preserves_colimits_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_colimit_iso", "description": "If `G` preserves colimits, we have an isomorphism from the image of the colimit of a functor `F`\nto the colimit of the functor `F \u22d9 G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_desc_map_cocone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lift_comp_preserves_limits_iso_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_limit_nat_iso", "description": " If `C, D` has all limits of shape `J`, and `G` preserves them, then `preserves_limit_iso` is\nfunctorial wrt `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_limit_nat_iso_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_limits_iso_hom_\u03c0_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_limit_iso", "description": "If `G` preserves limits, we have an isomorphism from the image of the limit of a functor `F`\nto the limit of the functor `F \u22d9 G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.\u03b9_preserves_colimits_iso_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_lift_map_cone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_colimit_nat_iso_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preserves_colimit_nat_iso_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable_pred", "description": "A computable predicate is one whose indicator function is computable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.part_iff\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable_pred.computable_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.head", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "re_pred", "description": "A recursively enumerable predicate is one which is the domain of a computable partial function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable_pred.rice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.tail", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable_pred.computable_iff_re_compl_re'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.of_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.idv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partrec.merge'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partrec.dom_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.vec_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable_pred.halting_problem_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.comp'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable_pred.halting_problem_not_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.to_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.vec", "description": "Analogous to `nat.partrec'` for `\u2115`-valued functions, a predicate for partial recursive\n vector-valued functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.rfind_opt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'", "description": "A simplified basis for `partrec`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.prim", "description": "A simplified basis for `partrec`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.comp", "description": "A simplified basis for `partrec`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.rfind", "description": "A simplified basis for `partrec`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable_pred.not", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partrec.cond", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable_pred.rice\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.part_iff\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "re_pred.of_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.part_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partrec.merge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.of_prim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable_pred.computable_iff_re_compl_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable_pred.of_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable_pred.to_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "partrec.sum_cases", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec.merge'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.vec.prim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.comp\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "computable_pred.halting_problem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.partrec'.of_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.star", "description": "The constant functor sending everything to `punit.star`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.from_punit", "description": "The functor from `discrete punit` sending everything to the given object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.star_map_down_down", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.equiv_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.equiv_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.equiv_functor_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.punit_ext_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.punit_ext'", "description": "Any two functors to `discrete punit` are *equal*.\nYou probably want to use `punit_ext` instead of this.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.equiv_punit_iff_unique", "description": "A category being equivalent to `punit` is equivalent to it having a unique morphism between\n any two objects. (In fact, such a category is also a groupoid; see `groupoid.of_hom_unique`)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.equiv_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.punit_ext_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.equiv", "description": "Functors from `discrete punit` are equivalent to the category itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.punit_ext", "description": "Any two functors to `discrete punit` are isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.equiv_functor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.is_s_finite_kernel.piecewise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.kernel_sum_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.coe_add_hom", "description": "Coercion to a function as an additive monoid homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.piecewise_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.is_s_finite_kernel_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.is_s_finite_kernel", "description": "A kernel is s-finite if it can be written as the sum of countably many finite kernels.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.is_s_finite_kernel.tsum_finite", "description": "A kernel is s-finite if it can be written as the sum of countably many finite kernels.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.sum_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.coe_fn_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.integral_deterministic'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.set_lintegral_deterministic'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.is_markov_kernel_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.set_integral_deterministic'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.piecewise_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.is_finite_kernel.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.is_s_finite_kernel.finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.is_s_finite_kernel.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.of_fun_of_countable", "description": " In a countable space with measurable singletons, every function `\u03b1 \u2192 measure \u03b2` defines a\nkernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.sum", "description": "Sum of an indexed family of kernels.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.set_lintegral_piecewise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.is_finite_kernel.bound_ne_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.lintegral_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.ext_fun_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.is_finite_kernel.piecewise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.comap_right", "description": " Kernel with value `(\u03ba a).comap f`, for a measurable embedding `f`. That is, for a measurable set\n`t : set \u03b2`, `comap_right \u03ba hf a t = \u03ba a (f '' t)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.is_s_finite_kernel.restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.is_finite_kernel.restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.comap_right_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.is_finite_kernel.is_s_finite_kernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.comap_right_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.coe_finset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.is_finite_kernel.comap_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.is_markov_kernel_deterministic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.const_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.ext_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.sum_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.is_s_finite_kernel.comap_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.piecewise", "description": " `piecewise hs \u03ba \u03b7` is the kernel equal to `\u03ba` on the measurable set `s` and to `\u03b7` on its\ncomplement.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.integral_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.is_finite_kernel", "description": "A kernel is finite if every measure in its image is finite, with a uniform bound.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.is_finite_kernel.exists_univ_le", "description": "A kernel is finite if every measure in its image is finite, with a uniform bound.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.ext_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.is_markov_kernel.comap_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.set_lintegral_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.sum_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.set_integral_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.sum_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.restrict_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.set_integral_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.finset_sum_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.set_integral_deterministic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.lintegral_deterministic'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.coe_fn_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.lintegral_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.is_markov_kernel.is_finite_kernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.is_finite_kernel.bound_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.deterministic", "description": "Kernel which to `a` associates the dirac measure at `f a`. This is a Markov kernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.restrict_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel", "description": " A kernel from a measurable space `\u03b1` to another measurable space `\u03b2` is a measurable function\n`\u03ba : \u03b1 \u2192 measure \u03b2`. The measurable space structure on `measure \u03b2` is given by\n`measure_theory.measure.measurable_space`. A map `\u03ba : \u03b1 \u2192 measure \u03b2` is measurable iff\n`\u2200 s : set \u03b2, measurable_set s \u2192 measurable (\u03bb a, \u03ba a s)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.restrict", "description": "Kernel given by the restriction of the measures in the image of a kernel to a set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.seq", "description": " A sequence of finite kernels such that `\u03ba = kernel.sum (seq \u03ba)`. See `is_finite_kernel_seq`\nand `kernel_sum_seq`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.measure_sum_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.set_lintegral_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.is_markov_kernel", "description": "A kernel is a Markov kernel if every measure in its image is a probability measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.is_markov_kernel.is_probability_measure", "description": "A kernel is a Markov kernel if every measure in its image is a probability measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.sum_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.is_markov_kernel.is_probability_measure'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.const", "description": "Constant kernel, which always returns the same measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.is_finite_kernel_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.is_finite_kernel_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.is_finite_kernel.bound", "description": " A constant `C : \u211d\u22650\u221e` such that `C < \u221e` (`is_finite_kernel.bound_lt_top \u03ba`) and for all\n`a : \u03b1` and `s : set \u03b2`, `\u03ba a s \u2264 C` (`measure_le_bound \u03ba a s`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.restrict_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.is_finite_kernel.is_finite_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.lintegral_piecewise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.integral_deterministic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.integral_piecewise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.sum_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.measurable_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.lintegral_deterministic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.finset_sum_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.deterministic_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.is_s_finite_kernel_sum_of_denumerable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.set_lintegral_deterministic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.is_markov_kernel.piecewise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.set_integral_piecewise", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.measure_le_bound", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.kernel.deterministic_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.is_finite_kernel_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_L1", "description": " Conditional expectation of the indicator of a set, as a function in L1. Its value for sets\nwhich are not both measurable and of finite measure is not used: we set it to 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_L1_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_condexp_L1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L1_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L1_measure_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_L1_fin_smul'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_L1_fin_ae_eq_condexp_ind_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_disjoint_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L1_congr_ae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable'_condexp_L1_clm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L1_clm_of_ae_strongly_measurable'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.norm_condexp_ind_apply_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L1_clm_indicator_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L1_clm_indicator_const_Lp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.norm_condexp_ind_L1_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_L1_fin_disjoint_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_condexp_ind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_ae_eq_condexp_ind_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.continuous_condexp_ind_L1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_disjoint_union_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L1_of_ae_strongly_measurable'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind", "description": "Conditional expectation of the indicator of a set, as a linear map from `G` to L1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable'_condexp_ind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_strongly_measurable'_condexp_L1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_L1_of_not_measurable_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_condexp_L1_clm", "description": " The integral of the conditional expectation `condexp_L1_clm` over an `m`-measurable set is equal\nto the integral of `f` on that set. See also `set_integral_condexp`, the similar statement for\n`condexp`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_condexp_L1", "description": " The integral of the conditional expectation `condexp_L1` over an `m`-measurable set is equal to\nthe integral of `f` on that set. See also `set_integral_condexp`, the similar statement for\n`condexp`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L1_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L1_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_of_measurable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L1_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.norm_condexp_ind_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.norm_condexp_ind_L1_fin_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.set_integral_condexp_L1_clm_of_measure_ne_top", "description": "Auxiliary lemma used in the proof of `set_integral_condexp_L1_clm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_L1_fin_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_L1_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L1_clm", "description": "Conditional expectation of a function as a linear map from `\u03b1 \u2192\u2081[\u03bc] F'` to itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_L1_disjoint_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_L1_fin", "description": " Conditional expectation of the indicator of a measurable set with finite measure,\nas a function in L1.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L1_undef", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_L1_smul'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L1_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L1_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L1_clm_Lp_meas", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L1_clm_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_L1_of_measurable_set_of_measure_ne_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.dominated_fin_meas_additive_condexp_ind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_smul'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_L1_of_measure_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L1_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_L1", "description": " Conditional expectation of a function, in L1. Its value is 0 if the function is not\nintegrable. The function-valued `condexp` should be used instead in most cases.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ind_L1_fin_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_norm.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "Helper instance for when there's too many metavariables to apply `fun_like.has_coe_to_fun`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_norm.to_add_group_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_norm.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm.to_add_group_seminorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_norm.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_norm.ring_norm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_ring_seminorm", "description": "The norm of a `non_unital_semi_normed_ring` as a `ring_seminorm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "Helper instance for when there's too many metavariables to apply `fun_like.has_coe_to_fun`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_norm.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm.mul_ring_seminorm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_ring_norm_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_norm.has_one", "description": " The trivial norm on a ring `R` is the `mul_ring_norm` taking value `0` at `0` and `1` at every\nother element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_norm.mul_ring_norm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_norm.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_norm", "description": "A function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` is a norm on a (nonunital) ring if it is a seminorm and `f x = 0`\n implies `x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_norm.to_fun", "description": "A function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` is a norm on a (nonunital) ring if it is a seminorm and `f x = 0`\n implies `x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_norm.map_zero'", "description": "A function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` is a norm on a (nonunital) ring if it is a seminorm and `f x = 0`\n implies `x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_norm.add_le'", "description": "A function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` is a norm on a (nonunital) ring if it is a seminorm and `f x = 0`\n implies `x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_norm.neg'", "description": "A function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` is a norm on a (nonunital) ring if it is a seminorm and `f x = 0`\n implies `x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_norm.mul_le'", "description": "A function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` is a norm on a (nonunital) ring if it is a seminorm and `f x = 0`\n implies `x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_norm.eq_zero_of_map_eq_zero'", "description": "A function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` is a norm on a (nonunital) ring if it is a seminorm and `f x = 0`\n implies `x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_norm.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "Helper instance for when there's too many metavariables to apply `fun_like.has_coe_to_fun`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_norm.to_mul_ring_seminorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_norm.to_add_group_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_norm", "description": " A multiplicative norm on a ring `R` is a multiplicative ring seminorm such that `f x = 0`\nimplies `x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_norm.to_fun", "description": " A multiplicative norm on a ring `R` is a multiplicative ring seminorm such that `f x = 0`\nimplies `x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_norm.map_zero'", "description": " A multiplicative norm on a ring `R` is a multiplicative ring seminorm such that `f x = 0`\nimplies `x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_norm.add_le'", "description": " A multiplicative norm on a ring `R` is a multiplicative ring seminorm such that `f x = 0`\nimplies `x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_norm.neg'", "description": " A multiplicative norm on a ring `R` is a multiplicative ring seminorm such that `f x = 0`\nimplies `x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_norm.map_one'", "description": " A multiplicative norm on a ring `R` is a multiplicative ring seminorm such that `f x = 0`\nimplies `x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_norm.map_mul'", "description": " A multiplicative norm on a ring `R` is a multiplicative ring seminorm such that `f x = 0`\nimplies `x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_norm.eq_zero_of_map_eq_zero'", "description": " A multiplicative norm on a ring `R` is a multiplicative ring seminorm such that `f x = 0`\nimplies `x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_norm.apply_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_norm.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm.ne_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm", "description": "A seminorm on a ring `R` is a function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` that preserves zero, takes nonnegative\n values, is subadditive and submultiplicative and such that `f (-x) = f x` for all `x \u2208 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm.to_fun", "description": "A seminorm on a ring `R` is a function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` that preserves zero, takes nonnegative\n values, is subadditive and submultiplicative and such that `f (-x) = f x` for all `x \u2208 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm.map_zero'", "description": "A seminorm on a ring `R` is a function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` that preserves zero, takes nonnegative\n values, is subadditive and submultiplicative and such that `f (-x) = f x` for all `x \u2208 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm.add_le'", "description": "A seminorm on a ring `R` is a function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` that preserves zero, takes nonnegative\n values, is subadditive and submultiplicative and such that `f (-x) = f x` for all `x \u2208 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm.neg'", "description": "A seminorm on a ring `R` is a function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` that preserves zero, takes nonnegative\n values, is subadditive and submultiplicative and such that `f (-x) = f x` for all `x \u2208 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm.mul_le'", "description": "A seminorm on a ring `R` is a function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` that preserves zero, takes nonnegative\n values, is subadditive and submultiplicative and such that `f (-x) = f x` for all `x \u2208 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_ring_norm", "description": "The norm of a normed_ring as a ring_norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm.seminorm_one_eq_one_iff_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm.apply_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm.eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_norm.apply_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm", "description": " A multiplicative seminorm on a ring `R` is a function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` that preserves zero and\nmultiplication, takes nonnegative values, is subadditive and such that `f (-x) = f x` for all `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm.to_fun", "description": " A multiplicative seminorm on a ring `R` is a function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` that preserves zero and\nmultiplication, takes nonnegative values, is subadditive and such that `f (-x) = f x` for all `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm.map_zero'", "description": " A multiplicative seminorm on a ring `R` is a function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` that preserves zero and\nmultiplication, takes nonnegative values, is subadditive and such that `f (-x) = f x` for all `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm.add_le'", "description": " A multiplicative seminorm on a ring `R` is a function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` that preserves zero and\nmultiplication, takes nonnegative values, is subadditive and such that `f (-x) = f x` for all `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm.neg'", "description": " A multiplicative seminorm on a ring `R` is a function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` that preserves zero and\nmultiplication, takes nonnegative values, is subadditive and such that `f (-x) = f x` for all `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm.map_one'", "description": " A multiplicative seminorm on a ring `R` is a function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` that preserves zero and\nmultiplication, takes nonnegative values, is subadditive and such that `f (-x) = f x` for all `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm.map_mul'", "description": " A multiplicative seminorm on a ring `R` is a function `f : R \u2192 \u211d` that preserves zero and\nmultiplication, takes nonnegative values, is subadditive and such that `f (-x) = f x` for all `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_norm.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm.has_one", "description": " The trivial seminorm on a ring `R` is the `mul_ring_seminorm` taking value `0` at `0` and `1` at\nevery other element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_norm.to_ring_seminorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm.to_monoid_with_zero_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_norm.has_one", "description": "The trivial norm on a ring `R` is the `ring_norm` taking value `0` at `0` and `1` at every\n other element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm.to_add_group_seminorm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm.to_ring_norm", "description": "A nonzero ring seminorm on a field `K` is a ring norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm.apply_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_ring_seminorm.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm.has_one", "description": " The trivial seminorm on a ring `R` is the `ring_seminorm` taking value `0` at `0` and `1` at\nevery other element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm.ring_seminorm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_seminorm.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "Helper instance for when there's too many metavariables to apply `fun_like.has_coe_to_fun`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid.path_nonempty_of_hom", "description": " If there exists a morphism `a \u2192 b` in a free groupoid, then there also exists a zigzag\nfrom `a` to `b` in the generating quiver.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid", "description": "A groupoid `G` is free when we have the following data:\n- a quiver on `is_free_groupoid.generators G` (a type synonym for `G`)\n- a function `of` taking a generating arrow to a morphism in `G`\n- such that a functor from `G` to any group `X` is uniquely determined\n  by assigning labels in `X` to the generating arrows.\n\n  This definition is nonstandard. Normally one would require that functors `G \u2964 X`\n  to any _groupoid_ `X` are given by graph homomorphisms from `generators`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid.quiver_generators", "description": "A groupoid `G` is free when we have the following data:\n- a quiver on `is_free_groupoid.generators G` (a type synonym for `G`)\n- a function `of` taking a generating arrow to a morphism in `G`\n- such that a functor from `G` to any group `X` is uniquely determined\n  by assigning labels in `X` to the generating arrows.\n\n  This definition is nonstandard. Normally one would require that functors `G \u2964 X`\n  to any _groupoid_ `X` are given by graph homomorphisms from `generators`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid.of", "description": "A groupoid `G` is free when we have the following data:\n- a quiver on `is_free_groupoid.generators G` (a type synonym for `G`)\n- a function `of` taking a generating arrow to a morphism in `G`\n- such that a functor from `G` to any group `X` is uniquely determined\n  by assigning labels in `X` to the generating arrows.\n\n  This definition is nonstandard. Normally one would require that functors `G \u2964 X`\n  to any _groupoid_ `X` are given by graph homomorphisms from `generators`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid.unique_lift", "description": "A groupoid `G` is free when we have the following data:\n- a quiver on `is_free_groupoid.generators G` (a type synonym for `G`)\n- a function `of` taking a generating arrow to a morphism in `G`\n- such that a functor from `G` to any group `X` is uniquely determined\n  by assigning labels in `X` to the generating arrows.\n\n  This definition is nonstandard. Normally one would require that functors `G \u2964 X`\n  to any _groupoid_ `X` are given by graph homomorphisms from `generators`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid.spanning_tree.tree_hom_eq", "description": "Any path to `a` gives `tree_hom T a`, since paths in the tree are unique.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid.ext_functor", "description": " Two functors from a free groupoid to a group are equal when they agree on the generating\nquiver.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid.generators_connected", "description": "Given a connected free groupoid, its generating quiver is rooted-connected.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid.spanning_tree.tree_hom", "description": "For every vertex `a`, there is a canonical hom from the root, given by the path in the tree.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid.generators", "description": " `is_free_groupoid.generators G` is a type synonym for `G`. We think of this as\nthe vertices of the generating quiver of `G` when `G` is free. We can't use `G` directly,\nsince `G` already has a quiver instance from being a groupoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid.spanning_tree.functor_of_monoid_hom", "description": "Since a hom gives a loop, any homomorphism from the vertex group at the root\n   extends to a functor on the whole groupoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid.spanning_tree.loop_of_hom", "description": "Any hom in `G` can be made into a loop, by conjugating with `tree_hom`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid.spanning_tree.End_is_free", "description": "Given a free groupoid and an arborescence of its generating quiver, the vertex\n   group at the root is freely generated by loops coming from generating arrows\n   in the complement of the tree.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup_is_free_of_is_free", "description": "The Nielsen-Schreier theorem: a subgroup of a free group is free.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid.spanning_tree.loop_of_hom_eq_id", "description": "Turning an edge in the spanning tree into a loop gives the indentity loop.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid.spanning_tree.functor_of_monoid_hom_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid.spanning_tree.tree_hom_root", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid.action_groupoid_is_free", "description": " An action groupoid over a free group is free. More generally, one could show that the groupoid\nof elements over a free groupoid is free, but this version is easier to prove and suffices for our\npurposes.\n\nAnalogous to the fact that a covering space of a graph is a graph. (A free groupoid is like a graph,\nand a groupoid of elements is like a covering space.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid.spanning_tree.hom_of_path", "description": "A path in the tree gives a hom, by composition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid.spanning_tree.functor_of_monoid_hom_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_free_groupoid.End_is_free_of_connected_free", "description": " A vertex group in a free connected groupoid is free. With some work one could drop the\nconnectedness assumption, by looking at connected components.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.to_measure_uniform_of_fintype_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.to_outer_measure_uniform_of_finset_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.to_outer_measure_uniform_of_fintype_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.uniform_of_finset_apply_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.mem_support_uniform_of_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.uniform_of_finset_apply_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.support_of_multiset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.uniform_of_finset_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.mem_support_of_multiset_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.of_multiset_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.support_uniform_of_fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.uniform_of_finset", "description": "Uniform distribution taking the same non-zero probability on the nonempty finset `s`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.support_uniform_of_finset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.mem_support_uniform_of_finset_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.uniform_of_fintype", "description": "The uniform pmf taking the same uniform value on all of the fintype `\u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.to_measure_of_multiset_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.of_multiset_apply_of_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.uniform_of_fintype_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.to_outer_measure_of_multiset_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.to_measure_uniform_of_finset_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pmf.of_multiset", "description": "Given a non-empty multiset `s` we construct the `pmf` which sends `a` to the fraction of\n elements in `s` that are `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.lifting.id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.is_localization.of_equivalence_target", "description": " If `L : C \u2964 D` is a localization for `W : morphism_property C`, then it is also\nthe case of a functor obtained by post-composing `L` with an equivalence of categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.lifting.of_isos_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.Q_comp_equivalence_from_model_functor_iso", "description": " Via the equivalence of categories `equivalence_from_model L W : W.localization \u224c D`,\none may identify the functors `W.Q` and `L`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.whiskering_left_functor.category_theory.is_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.whiskering_left_functor'_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.is_localization.for_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.lift_nat_iso", "description": " Given a localization functor `L : C \u2964 D` for `W : morphism_property C`,\nif `(F\u2081' F\u2082' : D \u2964 E)` are functors which lifts functors `(F\u2081 F\u2082 : C \u2964 E)`,\na natural isomorphism `\u03c4 : F\u2081 \u27f6 F\u2082` lifts to a natural isomorphism `F\u2081' \u27f6 F\u2082'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.lift_nat_trans", "description": " Given a localization functor `L : C \u2964 D` for `W : morphism_property C`,\nif `(F\u2081' F\u2082' : D \u2964 E)` are functors which lifts functors `(F\u2081 F\u2082 : C \u2964 E)`,\na natural transformation `\u03c4 : F\u2081 \u27f6 F\u2082` uniquely lifts to a natural transformation `F\u2081' \u27f6 F\u2082'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.fac_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.whiskering_left_functor'_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.lift", "description": " Given a localization functor `L : C \u2964 D` for `W : morphism_property C` and\na functor `F : C \u2964 E` which inverts `W`, this is a choice of functor\n`D \u2964 E` which lifts `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.Q_is_localization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.strict_universal_property_fixed_target", "description": " This universal property states that a functor `L : C \u2964 D` inverts morphisms\nin `W` and the all functors `D \u2964 E` (for a fixed category `E`) uniquely factors\nthrough `L`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.strict_universal_property_fixed_target.inverts", "description": " This universal property states that a functor `L : C \u2964 D` inverts morphisms\nin `W` and the all functors `D \u2964 E` (for a fixed category `E`) uniquely factors\nthrough `L`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.strict_universal_property_fixed_target.lift", "description": " This universal property states that a functor `L : C \u2964 D` inverts morphisms\nin `W` and the all functors `D \u2964 E` (for a fixed category `E`) uniquely factors\nthrough `L`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.strict_universal_property_fixed_target.fac", "description": " This universal property states that a functor `L : C \u2964 D` inverts morphisms\nin `W` and the all functors `D \u2964 E` (for a fixed category `E`) uniquely factors\nthrough `L`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.strict_universal_property_fixed_target.uniq", "description": " This universal property states that a functor `L : C \u2964 D` inverts morphisms\nin `W` and the all functors `D \u2964 E` (for a fixed category `E`) uniquely factors\nthrough `L`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.ess_surj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.comp_equivalence_from_model_inverse_iso", "description": " Via the equivalence of categories `equivalence_from_model L W : W.localization \u224c D`,\none may identify the functors `L` and `W.Q`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.whiskering_left_functor'", "description": " The functor `(D \u2964 E) \u2964 (C \u2964 E)` given by the composition with a localization\nfunctor `L : C \u2964 D` with respect to `W : morphism_property C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.functor_equivalence", "description": " The equivalence of categories `(D \u2964 E) \u224c (W.functors_inverting E)` induced by\nthe composition with a localization functor `L : C \u2964 D` with respect to\n`W : morphism_property C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.comp_lift_nat_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.lifting_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.construction.lift.category_theory.is_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.strict_universal_property_fixed_target_id_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.lifting.comp_right_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.fac", "description": " The canonical isomorphism `L \u22d9 lift F hF L \u2245 F` for any functor `F : C \u2964 E`\nwhich inverts `W`, when `L : C \u2964 D` is a localization functor for `W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.lift_nat_iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.whiskering_left_functor", "description": " The functor `(D \u2964 E) \u2964 W.functors_inverting E` induced by the composition\nwith a localization functor `L : C \u2964 D` with respect to `W : morphism_property C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.lifting.id_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.strict_universal_property_fixed_target_id", "description": " When `W` consists of isomorphisms, the identity satisfies the universal property\nof the localization.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.lifting.comp_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.lifting_construction_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.iso_of_hom_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.is_localization.mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.lifting", "description": " When `L : C \u2964 D` is a localization functor for `W : morphism_property C` and\n`F : C \u2964 E` is a functor, we shall say that `F' : D \u2964 E` lifts `F` if the obvious diagram\nis commutative up to an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.lifting.iso", "description": " When `L : C \u2964 D` is a localization functor for `W : morphism_property C` and\n`F : C \u2964 E` is a functor, we shall say that `F' : D \u2964 E` lifts `F` if the obvious diagram\nis commutative up to an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.strict_universal_property_fixed_target_Q_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.nat_trans_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.whiskering_left_functor'.category_theory.full", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.lift_nat_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.strict_universal_property_fixed_target.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.is_localization.of_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.lift_nat_trans_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.inverts", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.is_localization", "description": " The predicate expressing that, up to equivalence, a functor `L : C \u2964 D`\nidentifies the category `D` with the localized category of `C` with respect\nto `W : morphism_property C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.is_localization.inverts", "description": " The predicate expressing that, up to equivalence, a functor `L : C \u2964 D`\nidentifies the category `D` with the localized category of `C` with respect\nto `W : morphism_property C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.is_localization.nonempty_is_equivalence", "description": " The predicate expressing that, up to equivalence, a functor `L : C \u2964 D`\nidentifies the category `D` with the localized category of `C` with respect\nto `W : morphism_property C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.whiskering_left_functor'.category_theory.faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.comp_lift_nat_trans_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.iso_of_hom_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.strict_universal_property_fixed_target_Q", "description": " The localized category `W.localization` that was constructed satisfies\nthe universal property of the localization.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.lift_nat_trans_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.lifting.of_isos", "description": " Given a localization functor `L : C \u2964 D` for `W : morphism_property C`,\nif `F\u2081' : D \u2964 E` lifts a functor `F\u2081 : C \u2964 D`, then a functor `F\u2082'` which\nis isomorphic to `F\u2081'` also lifts a functor `F\u2082` that is isomorphic to `F\u2081`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.equivalence_from_model", "description": " A chosen equivalence of categories `W.localization \u2245 D` for a functor\n`L : C \u2964 D` which satisfies `L.is_localization W`. This shall be used in\norder to deduce properties of `L` from properties of `W.Q`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.fac_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.localization.iso_of_hom", "description": " The isomorphism `L.obj X \u2245 L.obj Y` that is deduced from a morphism `f : X \u27f6 Y` which\nbelongs to `W`, when `L.is_localization W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exp_char_one_of_char_zero", "description": "The exponential characteristic is one if the characteristic is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exp_char", "description": "The definition of the exponential characteristic of a semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exp_char.zero", "description": "The definition of the exponential characteristic of a semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exp_char.prime", "description": "The definition of the exponential characteristic of a semiring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_zero_of_exp_char_one'", "description": "The characteristic is zero if the exponential characteristic is one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_zero_of_exp_char_one", "description": "The exponential characteristic is one if the characteristic is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_prime_of_ne_zero", "description": "A helper lemma: the characteristic is prime if it is non-zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exp_char_is_prime_or_one", "description": "The exponential characteristic is a prime number or one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_eq_exp_char_iff", "description": "The characteristic equals the exponential characteristic iff the former is prime.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exp_char_one_iff_char_zero", "description": "The exponential characteristic is one iff the characteristic is zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldl_prod_map_\u03b9", "description": "This lemma demonstrates the origin of the `foldl` name.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldl_reverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldr'_aux_foldr'_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldr_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldr_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldr_reverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldl_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldr", "description": " Fold a bilinear map along the generators of a term of the clifford algebra, with the rule\ngiven by `foldr Q f hf n (\u03b9 Q m * x) = f m (foldr Q f hf n x)`.\n\nFor example, `foldr f hf n (r \u2022 \u03b9 R u + \u03b9 R v * \u03b9 R w) = r \u2022 f u n + f v (f w n)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldl", "description": " Fold a bilinear map along the generators of a term of the clifford algebra, with the rule\ngiven by `foldl Q f hf n (\u03b9 Q m * x) = f m (foldl Q f hf n x)`.\n\nFor example, `foldl f hf n (r \u2022 \u03b9 R u + \u03b9 R v * \u03b9 R w) = r \u2022 f u n + f v (f w n)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldr_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldr_prod_map_\u03b9", "description": "This lemma demonstrates the origin of the `foldr` name.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldr'_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.left_induction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldr'_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldl_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldr'_\u03b9_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldr_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldr'_aux", "description": "Auxiliary definition for `clifford_algebra.foldr'`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.right_induction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldr'", "description": " Fold a bilinear map along the generators of a term of the clifford algebra, with the rule\ngiven by `foldr' Q f hf n (\u03b9 Q m * x) = f m (x, foldr' Q f hf n x)`.\nNote this is like `clifford_algebra.foldr`, but with an extra `x` argument.\nImplement the recursion scheme `F[n0](m * x) = f(m, (x, F[n0](x)))`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldl_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldr'_aux_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "clifford_algebra.foldl_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.has_basis_uniformity_of_basis_aux\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.uniform_equiv_Pi_comm", "description": " The natural bijection between `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03a0 i, \u03b4 i` and `\u03a0 i, \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b4 i`, upgraded to a uniform\nisomorphism between `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] (\u03a0 i, \u03b4 i)` and `\u03a0 i, \u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b4 i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.uniform_equiv_Pi_comm", "description": " The natural bijection between `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03a0 i, \u03b4 i` and `\u03a0 i, \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b4 i`, upgraded to a uniform\nisomorphism between `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 (\u03a0 i, \u03b4 i)` and `\u03a0 i, \u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b4 i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.uniform_continuous_eval_of_mem", "description": " If `x : \u03b1` is in some `S \u2208 \ud835\udd16`, then evaluation at `x` is uniformly continuous on\n`\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.uniform_continuous_restrict", "description": " If `S \u2208 \ud835\udd16`, then the restriction to `S` is a uniformly continuous map from `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2` to\n`\u21a5S \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.topological_space_eq", "description": " The topology of `\ud835\udd16`-convergence is the infimum, for `S \u2208 \ud835\udd16`, of topology induced by the map\nof `S.restrict : (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2) \u2192 (\u21a5S \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2)` of restriction to `S`, where `\u21a5S \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2` is endowed with\nthe topology of uniform convergence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.mono", "description": " Let `u\u2081`, `u\u2082` be two uniform structures on `\u03b3` and `\ud835\udd16\u2081 \ud835\udd16\u2082 : set (set \u03b1)`. If `u\u2081 \u2264 u\u2082` and\n`\ud835\udd16\u2082 \u2286 \ud835\udd16\u2081` then `\ud835\udcb1(\u03b1, \u03b3, \ud835\udd16\u2081, u\u2081) \u2264 \ud835\udcb1(\u03b1, \u03b3, \ud835\udd16\u2082, u\u2082)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.uniform_core", "description": "Core of the uniform structure of uniform convergence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.is_basis_gen", "description": " If `\ud835\udcd5` is a filter on `\u03b2 \u00d7 \u03b2`, then the set of all `uniform_convergence.gen \u03b1 \u03b2 V` for\n`V \u2208 \ud835\udcd5` is a filter basis on `(\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2) \u00d7 (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2)`. This will only be applied to `\ud835\udcd5 = \ud835\udce4 \u03b2` when\n`\u03b2` is equipped with a `uniform_space` structure, but it is useful to define it for any filter in\norder to be able to state that it has a lower adjoint (see `uniform_convergence.gc`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.of_fun", "description": "Reinterpret `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` as an element of `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.has_basis_uniformity_of_basis", "description": " The uniformity of `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2` admits the family `{(f, g) | \u2200 x, (f x, g x) \u2208 V}` for `V \u2208 \ud835\udcd1` as\na filter basis, for any basis `\ud835\udcd1` of `\ud835\udce4 \u03b2` (in the case `\ud835\udcd1 = (\ud835\udce4 \u03b2).as_basis` this is true by\ndefinition).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.gen", "description": " Basis sets for the uniformity of `\ud835\udd16`-convergence: for `S : set \u03b1` and `V : set (\u03b2 \u00d7 \u03b2)`,\n`gen \ud835\udd16 S V` is the set of pairs `(f, g)` of functions `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2` such that\n`\u2200 x \u2208 S, (f x, g x) \u2208 V`. Note that the family `\ud835\udd16 : set (set \u03b1)` is only used to specify which\ntype alias of `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` to use here.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.has_basis_uniformity", "description": " By definition, the uniformity of `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2` admits the family `{(f, g) | \u2200 x, (f x, g x) \u2208 V}`\nfor `V \u2208 \ud835\udce4 \u03b2` as a filter basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.comap_eq", "description": " If `u` is a uniform structures on `\u03b2` and `f : \u03b3 \u2192 \u03b2`, then\n`\ud835\udcb1(\u03b1, \u03b3, \ud835\udd16, comap f u) = comap (\u03bb g, f \u2218 g) \ud835\udcb1(\u03b1, \u03b3, \ud835\udd16, u\u2081)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.is_basis_gen", "description": " If `\ud835\udd16 : set (set \u03b1)` is nonempty and directed and `\ud835\udcd1` is a filter basis on `\u03b2 \u00d7 \u03b2`, then the\nfamily `uniform_on_fun.gen \ud835\udd16 S V` for `S \u2208 \ud835\udd16` and `V \u2208 \ud835\udcd1` is a filter basis on\n`(\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2) \u00d7 (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2)`.\nWe will show in `has_basis_uniformity_of_basis` that, if `\ud835\udcd1` is a basis for `\ud835\udce4 \u03b2`, then the\ncorresponding filter is the uniformity of `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.postcomp_uniform_inducing", "description": " Post-composition by a uniform inducing is a uniform inducing for the\nuniform structures of `\ud835\udd16`-convergence.\n\nMore precisely, if `f : \u03b3 \u2192 \u03b2` is a uniform inducing, then\n`(\u03bb g, f \u2218 g) : (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b3) \u2192 (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2)` is a uniform inducing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.uniform_space", "description": " Uniform structure of uniform convergence, declared as an instance on `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2`.\nWe will denote it `\ud835\udcb0(\u03b1, \u03b2, u\u03b2)` in the rest of this file.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.comap_eq", "description": " If `u` is a uniform structures on `\u03b2` and `f : \u03b3 \u2192 \u03b2`, then\n`\ud835\udcb0(\u03b1, \u03b3, comap f u) = comap (\u03bb g, f \u2218 g) \ud835\udcb0(\u03b1, \u03b3, u\u2081)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.uniform_equiv_prod_arrow", "description": " The natural bijection between `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u00d7 \u03b3` and `(\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2) \u00d7 (\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b3)`, upgraded to a uniform\nisomorphism between `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2 \u00d7 \u03b3` and `(\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2) \u00d7 (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b3)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.precomp_uniform_continuous", "description": " Pre-composition by a any function is uniformly continuous for the uniform structures of\nuniform convergence.\n\nMore precisely, for any `f : \u03b3 \u2192 \u03b1`, the function `(\u03bb g, g \u2218 f) : (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2) \u2192 (\u03b3 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2)` is uniformly\ncontinuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.to_fun", "description": "Reinterpret `f : \u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2` as an element of `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.t2_space", "description": "The topology of uniform convergence is T\u2082.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.tendsto_iff_tendsto_uniformly_on", "description": " Convergence in the topology of `\ud835\udd16`-convergence means uniform convergence on `S` (in the sense\nof `tendsto_uniformly_on`) for all `S \u2208 \ud835\udd16`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.has_basis_nhds_of_basis", "description": " For `f : \u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2`, `\ud835\udcdd f` admits the family `{g | \u2200 x, (f x, g x) \u2208 V}` for `V \u2208 \ud835\udcd1` as a filter\nbasis, for any basis `\ud835\udcd1` of `\ud835\udce4 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.has_basis_uniformity", "description": " If `\ud835\udd16 : set (set \u03b1)` is nonempty and directed, then the uniformity of `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2` admits the\nfamily `{(f, g) | \u2200 x \u2208 S, (f x, g x) \u2208 V}` for `S \u2208 \ud835\udd16` and `V \u2208 \ud835\udce4 \u03b2` as a filter basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.of_fun", "description": "Reinterpret `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` as an element of `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.infi_eq", "description": " If `u` is a family of uniform structures on `\u03b3`, then\n`\ud835\udcb0(\u03b1, \u03b3, (\u2a05 i, u i)) = \u2a05 i, \ud835\udcb0(\u03b1, \u03b3, u i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.precomp_uniform_continuous", "description": " Let `f : \u03b3 \u2192 \u03b1`, `\ud835\udd16 : set (set \u03b1)`, `\ud835\udd17 : set (set \u03b3)`, and assume that `\u2200 T \u2208 \ud835\udd17, f '' T \u2208 \ud835\udd16`.\nThen, the function `(\u03bb g, g \u2218 f) : (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2) \u2192 (\u03b3 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd17] \u03b2)` is uniformly continuous.\n\nNote that one can easily see that assuming `\u2200 T \u2208 \ud835\udd17, \u2203 S \u2208 \ud835\udd16, f '' T \u2286 S` would work too, but\nwe will get this for free when we prove that `\ud835\udcb1(\u03b1, \u03b2, \ud835\udd16, u\u03b2) = \ud835\udcb1(\u03b1, \u03b2, \ud835\udd16', u\u03b2)` where `\ud835\udd16'` is the\n***noncovering*** bornology generated by `\ud835\udd16`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.uniform_continuous_eval", "description": "Evaluation at a fixed point is uniformly continuous on `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.has_basis_nhds_of_basis", "description": " For `f : \u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2`, where `\ud835\udd16 : set (set \u03b1)` is nonempty and directed, `\ud835\udcdd f` admits the\nfamily `{g | \u2200 x \u2208 S, (f x, g x) \u2208 V}` for `S \u2208 \ud835\udd16` and `V \u2208 \ud835\udcd1` as a filter basis, for any basis\n`\ud835\udcd1` of `\ud835\udce4 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.congr_left", "description": " Turn a bijection `\u03b3 \u2243 \u03b1` into a uniform isomorphism\n`(\u03b3 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2) \u2243\u1d64 (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2)` by pre-composing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.uniform_space", "description": " Uniform structure of `\ud835\udd16`-convergence, i.e uniform convergence on the elements of `\ud835\udd16`,\ndeclared as an instance on `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2`. It is defined as the infimum, for `S \u2208 \ud835\udd16`, of the pullback\nby `S.restrict`, the map of restriction to `S`, of the uniform structure `\ud835\udcb0(s, \u03b2, u\u03b2)` on\n`\u21a5S \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2`. We will denote it `\ud835\udcb1(\u03b1, \u03b2, \ud835\udd16, u\u03b2)`, where `u\u03b2` is the uniform structure on `\u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.mono", "description": " If `u\u2081` and `u\u2082` are two uniform structures on `\u03b3` and `u\u2081 \u2264 u\u2082`, then\n`\ud835\udcb0(\u03b1, \u03b3, u\u2081) \u2264 \ud835\udcb0(\u03b1, \u03b3, u\u2082)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.postcomp_uniform_continuous", "description": " Post-composition by a uniformly continuous function is uniformly continuous on `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2`.\n\nMore precisely, if `f : \u03b3 \u2192 \u03b2` is uniformly continuous, then `(\u03bb g, f \u2218 g) : (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b3) \u2192 (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2)`\nis uniformly continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.congr_left", "description": " Turn a bijection `e : \u03b3 \u2243 \u03b1` such that we have both `\u2200 T \u2208 \ud835\udd17, e '' T \u2208 \ud835\udd16` and\n`\u2200 S \u2208 \ud835\udd16, e \u207b\u00b9' S \u2208 \ud835\udd17` into a uniform isomorphism `(\u03b3 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd17] \u03b2) \u2243\u1d64 (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2)` by pre-composing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.t2_space_of_covering", "description": "If `\ud835\udd16` covers `\u03b1`, then the topology of `\ud835\udd16`-convergence is T\u2082.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.gen_mono", "description": "`uniform_on_fun.gen` is antitone in the first argument and monotone in the second.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.tendsto_iff_tendsto_uniformly", "description": " The topology of uniform convergence indeed gives the same notion of convergence as\n`tendsto_uniformly`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.has_basis_uniformity_of_basis", "description": " If `\ud835\udd16 : set (set \u03b1)` is nonempty and directed and `\ud835\udcd1` is a filter basis of `\ud835\udce4 \u03b2`, then the\nuniformity of `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2` admits the family `{(f, g) | \u2200 x \u2208 S, (f x, g x) \u2208 V}` for `S \u2208 \ud835\udd16` and\n`V \u2208 \ud835\udcd1` as a filter basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.to_fun", "description": "Reinterpret `f : \u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2` as an element of `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.gc", "description": " The function `uniform_convergence.filter \u03b1 \u03b2 : filter (\u03b2 \u00d7 \u03b2) \u2192 filter ((\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2) \u00d7 (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2))`\nhas a lower adjoint `l` (in the sense of `galois_connection`). The exact definition of `l` is not\ninteresting; we will only use that it exists (in `uniform_convergence.mono` and\n`uniform_convergence.infi_eq`) and that\n`l (filter.map (prod.map f f) \ud835\udcd5) = filter.map (prod.map ((\u2218) f) ((\u2218) f)) (l \ud835\udcd5)` for each\n`\ud835\udcd5 : filter (\u03b3 \u00d7 \u03b3)` and `f : \u03b3 \u2192 \u03b1` (in `uniform_convergence.comap_eq`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.gen_eq_preimage_restrict", "description": " For `S : set \u03b1` and `V : set (\u03b2 \u00d7 \u03b2)`, we have\n`uniform_on_fun.gen \ud835\udd16 S V = (S.restrict \u00d7 S.restrict) \u207b\u00b9' (uniform_fun.gen S \u03b2 V)`.\nThis is the crucial fact for proving that the family `uniform_on_fun.gen S V` for `S \u2208 \ud835\udd16` and\n`V \u2208 \ud835\udce4 \u03b2` is indeed a basis for the uniformity `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2` endowed with `\ud835\udcb1(\u03b1, \u03b2, \ud835\udd16, u\u03b2)`\nthe uniform structure of `\ud835\udd16`-convergence, as defined in `uniform_on_fun.uniform_space`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.uniform_continuous_to_fun", "description": " If `\ud835\udd16` covers `\u03b1`, the natural map `uniform_on_fun.to_fun` from `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2` to `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is\nuniformly continuous.\n\nIn other words, if `\ud835\udd16` covers `\u03b1`, then the uniform structure of `\ud835\udd16`-convergence is finer than\nthat of pointwise convergence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.uniform_equiv_prod_arrow", "description": " The natural bijection between `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u00d7 \u03b3` and `(\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2) \u00d7 (\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b3)`, upgraded to a uniform\nisomorphism between `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2 \u00d7 \u03b3` and `(\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2) \u00d7 (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b3)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.filter", "description": " For `\ud835\udcd5 : filter (\u03b2 \u00d7 \u03b2)`, this is the filter generated by the filter basis\n`uniform_convergence.basis \u03b1 \u03b2 \ud835\udcd5`. For `\ud835\udcd5 = \ud835\udce4 \u03b2`, this will be the uniformity of uniform\nconvergence on `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.has_basis_nhds", "description": " For `f : \u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2`, `\ud835\udcdd f` admits the family `{g | \u2200 x, (f x, g x) \u2208 V}` for `V \u2208 \ud835\udce4 \u03b2` as a\nfilter basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.infi_eq", "description": " If `u` is a family of uniform structures on `\u03b3`, then\n`\ud835\udcb1(\u03b1, \u03b3, \ud835\udd16, (\u2a05 i, u i)) = \u2a05 i, \ud835\udcb1(\u03b1, \u03b3, \ud835\udd16, u i)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.basis", "description": " For `\ud835\udcd5 : filter (\u03b2 \u00d7 \u03b2)`, this is the set of all `uniform_convergence.gen \u03b1 \u03b2 V` for\n`V \u2208 \ud835\udcd5` as a bundled `filter_basis` over `(\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2) \u00d7 (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2)`. This will only be applied to\n`\ud835\udcd5 = \ud835\udce4 \u03b2` when `\u03b2` is equipped with a `uniform_space` structure, but it is useful to define it for\nany filter in order to be able to state that it has a lower adjoint\n(see `uniform_convergence.gc`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.postcomp_uniform_inducing", "description": " Post-composition by a uniform inducing is a uniform inducing for the\nuniform structures of uniform convergence.\n\nMore precisely, if `f : \u03b3 \u2192 \u03b2` is a uniform inducing, then `(\u03bb g, f \u2218 g) : (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b3) \u2192 (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2)` is\na uniform inducing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.gen", "description": " Basis sets for the uniformity of uniform convergence: `gen \u03b1 \u03b2 V` is the set of pairs `(f, g)`\nof functions `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2` such that `\u2200 x, (f x, g x) \u2208 V`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun", "description": " The type of functions from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2` equipped with the uniform structure and topology of\nuniform convergence. We denote it `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.inf_eq", "description": " If `u\u2081` and `u\u2082` are two uniform structures on `\u03b3`, then\n`\ud835\udcb1(\u03b1, \u03b3, \ud835\udd16, u\u2081 \u2293 u\u2082) = \ud835\udcb1(\u03b1, \u03b3, \ud835\udd16, u\u2081) \u2293 \ud835\udcb1(\u03b1, \u03b3, \ud835\udd16, u\u2082)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.postcomp_uniform_continuous", "description": " Post-composition by a uniformly continuous function is uniformly continuous for the\nuniform structures of `\ud835\udd16`-convergence.\n\nMore precisely, if `f : \u03b3 \u2192 \u03b2` is uniformly continuous, then\n`(\u03bb g, f \u2218 g) : (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b3) \u2192 (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2)` is uniformly continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.has_basis_nhds", "description": " For `f : \u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2`, where `\ud835\udd16 : set (set \u03b1)` is nonempty and directed, `\ud835\udcdd f` admits the\nfamily `{g | \u2200 x \u2208 S, (f x, g x) \u2208 V}` for `S \u2208 \ud835\udd16` and `V \u2208 \ud835\udce4 \u03b2` as a filter basis.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun", "description": " The type of functions from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2` equipped with the uniform structure and topology of\nuniform convergence on some family `\ud835\udd16` of subsets of `\u03b1`. We denote it `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.congr_right", "description": " Turn a uniform isomorphism `\u03b3 \u2243\u1d64 \u03b2` into a uniform isomorphism `(\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b3) \u2243\u1d64 (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2)`\nby post-composing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.topological_space", "description": " Topology of `\ud835\udd16`-convergence, i.e uniform convergence on the elements of `\ud835\udd16`, declared as an\ninstance on `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64[\ud835\udd16] \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.uniform_continuous_to_fun", "description": " The natural map `uniform_fun.to_fun` from `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2` to `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is uniformly continuous.\n\nIn other words, the uniform structure of uniform convergence is finer than that of pointwise\nconvergence, aka the product uniform structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_on_fun.has_basis_uniformity_of_basis_aux\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.topological_space", "description": "Topology of uniform convergence, declared as an instance on `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.inf_eq", "description": " If `u\u2081` and `u\u2082` are two uniform structures on `\u03b3`, then\n`\ud835\udcb0(\u03b1, \u03b3, u\u2081 \u2293 u\u2082) = \ud835\udcb0(\u03b1, \u03b3, u\u2081) \u2293 \ud835\udcb0(\u03b1, \u03b3, u\u2082)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_fun.congr_right", "description": " Turn a uniform isomorphism `\u03b3 \u2243\u1d64 \u03b2` into a uniform isomorphism `(\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b3) \u2243\u1d64 (\u03b1 \u2192\u1d64 \u03b2)` by\npost-composing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_search.config", "description": "Configuration options for a rewrite search.\n`max_iterations` controls how many vertices are expanded in the graph search.\n`explain` generates Lean code to replace the call to `rewrite_search`.\n`explain_using_conv` changes the nature of the explanation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_search.config.to_cfg", "description": "Configuration options for a rewrite search.\n`max_iterations` controls how many vertices are expanded in the graph search.\n`explain` generates Lean code to replace the call to `rewrite_search`.\n`explain_using_conv` changes the nature of the explanation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_search.config.max_iterations", "description": "Configuration options for a rewrite search.\n`max_iterations` controls how many vertices are expanded in the graph search.\n`explain` generates Lean code to replace the call to `rewrite_search`.\n`explain_using_conv` changes the nature of the explanation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_search.config.explain_using_conv", "description": "Configuration options for a rewrite search.\n`max_iterations` controls how many vertices are expanded in the graph search.\n`explain` generates Lean code to replace the call to `rewrite_search`.\n`explain_using_conv` changes the nature of the explanation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_search.side", "description": "`side` represents the side of an equation, either the left or the right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_search.side.L", "description": "`side` represents the side of an equation, either the left or the right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_search.side.R", "description": "`side` represents the side of an equation, either the left or the right.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_search.how", "description": "A `how` contains information needed by the explainer to generate code for a rewrite.\n`rule_index` denotes which rule in the static list of rules is used.\n`location` describes which match of that rule was used, to work with `nth_rewrite`.\n`addr` is a list of \"left\" and \"right\" describing which subexpression is rewritten.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_search.how.rule_index", "description": "A `how` contains information needed by the explainer to generate code for a rewrite.\n`rule_index` denotes which rule in the static list of rules is used.\n`location` describes which match of that rule was used, to work with `nth_rewrite`.\n`addr` is a list of \"left\" and \"right\" describing which subexpression is rewritten.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_search.how.location", "description": "A `how` contains information needed by the explainer to generate code for a rewrite.\n`rule_index` denotes which rule in the static list of rules is used.\n`location` describes which match of that rule was used, to work with `nth_rewrite`.\n`addr` is a list of \"left\" and \"right\" describing which subexpression is rewritten.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_search.how.addr", "description": "A `how` contains information needed by the explainer to generate code for a rewrite.\n`rule_index` denotes which rule in the static list of rules is used.\n`location` describes which match of that rule was used, to work with `nth_rewrite`.\n`addr` is a list of \"left\" and \"right\" describing which subexpression is rewritten.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_search.side.to_string", "description": "Convert a side to a human-readable string.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_search.side.to_xhs", "description": "Convert a side to the string \"lhs\" or \"rhs\", for use in tactic name generation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_search.how.to_string", "description": "Convert a `how` to a human-readable string.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_search.side.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_search.how.has_to_format", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_search.side.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_search.proof_unit", "description": "`proof_unit` represents a sequence of steps that can be applied to one side of the\nequation to prove a particular expression.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_search.proof_unit.proof", "description": "`proof_unit` represents a sequence of steps that can be applied to one side of the\nequation to prove a particular expression.", "p": 