p `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` between uniform spaces is called *uniform inducing* if the uniformity filter\non `\u03b1` is the pullback of the uniformity filter on `\u03b2` under `prod.map f f`. If `\u03b1` is a separated\nspace, then this implies that `f` is injective, hence it is a `uniform_embedding`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_inducing.comap_uniformity", "description": " A map `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` between uniform spaces is called *uniform inducing* if the uniformity filter\non `\u03b1` is the pullback of the uniformity filter on `\u03b2` under `prod.map f f`. If `\u03b1` is a separated\nspace, then this implies that `f` is injective, hence it is a `uniform_embedding`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniformly_extend_of_ind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.uniform_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_inducing.cauchy_map_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_embedding_of_spaced_out", "description": " If a map `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` sends any two distinct points to point that are **not** related by a fixed\n`s \u2208 \ud835\udce4 \u03b2`, then `f` is a uniform embedding with respect to the discrete uniformity on `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_inducing.comap_uniform_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_space_coe_iff_is_complete", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_embedding", "description": " A map `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` between uniform spaces is a *uniform embedding* if it is uniform inducing and\ninjective. If `\u03b1` is a separated space, then the latter assumption follows from the former.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_embedding.to_uniform_inducing", "description": " A map `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` between uniform spaces is a *uniform embedding* if it is uniform inducing and\ninjective. If `\u03b1` is a separated space, then the latter assumption follows from the former.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_embedding.inj", "description": " A map `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` between uniform spaces is a *uniform embedding* if it is uniform inducing and\ninjective. If `\u03b1` is a separated space, then the latter assumption follows from the former.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_embedding.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_inducing.basis_uniformity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_inducing_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_inducing.inducing", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_embedding_subtype_emb", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_space_iff_is_complete_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_inducing.uniform_continuous_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniformly_extend_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_inducing.uniform_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniformly_extend_spec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_closed.complete_space_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_embedding_set_inclusion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "embedding.to_uniform_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_space_extension", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complete_space_congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_inducing.mk'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comap_uniformity_of_spaced_out", "description": " If a map `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` sends any two distinct points to point that are **not** related by a fixed\n`s \u2208 \ud835\udce4 \u03b2`, then `f` is uniform inducing with respect to the discrete uniformity on `\u03b1`:\nthe preimage of `\ud835\udce4 \u03b2` under `prod.map f f` is the principal filter generated by the diagonal in\n`\u03b1 \u00d7 \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_embedding_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_inducing.is_complete_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_continuous_uniformly_extend", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "embedding.comap_uniform_space", "description": " Pull back a uniform space structure by an embedding, adjusting the new uniform structure to\nmake sure that its topology is defeq to the original one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_embedding_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_embedding_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_basis.uniform_embedding_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_inducing.uniform_embedding", "description": " If the domain of a `uniform_inducing` map `f` is a `separated_space`, then `f` is injective,\nhence it is a `uniform_embedding`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "totally_bounded_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_inducing_of_compose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_embedding_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_complete_image_iff", "description": "A set is complete iff its image under a uniform inducing map is complete.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_inducing.prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_inducing_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.has_basis.uniform_inducing_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ulift.complete_space", "description": "The lift of a complete space to another universe is still complete.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_complete.complete_space_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_inducing.dense_inducing", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_embedding_iff_uniform_inducing", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ulift.module'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ulift.mul_distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ulift.smul_zero_class", "description": "", "p"