 of a function.\nThis definition is meta because it creates an infinite list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lazy_list.iota", "description": "The infinite lazy list `[i, i+1, i+2, ...]`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lazy_list.join", "description": "The monadic join operation for lazy lists.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lazy_list.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lazy_list.nth", "description": "The nth element of a lazy list as an option (like `list.nth`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lazy_list", "description": "Lazy list.\nAll elements (except the first) are computed lazily.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lazy_list.nil", "description": "Lazy list.\nAll elements (except the first) are computed lazily.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lazy_list.cons", "description": "Lazy list.\nAll elements (except the first) are computed lazily.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lazy_list.append", "description": "Appends two lazy lists.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lazy_list.singleton", "description": "The singleton lazy list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lazy_list.of_list", "description": "Constructs a lazy list from a list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lazy_list.map", "description": "Maps a function over a lazy list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lazy_list.filter", "description": "The lazy list of all elements satisfying the predicate.\nIf the lazy list is infinite and none of the elements satisfy the predicate,\nthen this function will not terminate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lazy_list.approx", "description": "The list containing the first `n` elements of a lazy list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lazy_list.zip", "description": "Zips two lazy lists.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lazy_list.head", "description": "Returns the first element of the lazy list,\nor `default` if the lazy list is empty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lazy_list.map\u2082", "description": "Maps a binary function over two lazy list.\nLike `lazy_list.zip`, the result is only as long as the smaller inp