`add_submonoid` of an `add_comm_monoid` indexed by a `finset`\nis in the `add_submonoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_mem_class.mul_mem_add_closure", "description": " The product of two elements of the additive closure of a submonoid `M` is an element of the\nadditive closure of `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.mem_closure_pair", "description": " An element is in the closure of a two-element set if it is a linear combination of those two\nelements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid_class.coe_multiset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.log_pow_int_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.list_sum_mem", "description": "Sum of a list of elements in an `add_submonoid` is in the `add_submonoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.sum_mem", "description": "Sum of elements in an `add_submonoid` of an `add_comm_monoid` indexed by a `finset`\nis in the `add_submonoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.mem_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.mem_closure_singleton", "description": " The `add_submonoid` generated by an element of an `add_monoid` equals the set of\nnatural number multiples of the element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid_class.coe_list_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.multiples_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list_sum_mem", "description": "Sum of a list of elements in an `add_submonoid` is in the `add_submonoid`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.exists_list_of_mem_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.coe_finset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.powers_eq_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.coe_list_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.mem_sup_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.supr_induction", "description": " An induction principle for elements of `\u2a06 i, S i`.\nIf `C` holds for `0` and all elements of `S i` for all `i`, and is preserved under addition,\nthen it holds for all elements of the supremum of `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.prod_mem", "description": "Product of elements of a submonoid of a `comm_monoid` indexed by a `finset` is in the\n   submonoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.coe_multiset_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.coe_multiset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.mem_supr_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.supr_induction'", "description": "A dependent version of `add_submonoid.supr_induction`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "of_add_image_multiples_eq_powers_of_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid_class.coe_list_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.mem_supr_of_directed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.pow_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.mem_multiples_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.induction_of_closure_eq_top_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.pow_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.mem_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.closure_induction_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.mem_closure_singleton_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.mem_Sup_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.powers_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.multiples_eq_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod_mem", "description": "Product of elements of a submonoid of a `comm_monoid` indexed by a `finset` is in the\n   submonoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.mem_powers_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid_class.coe_finset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "free_add_monoid.mrange_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.closure_singleton_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smul_comm_class.of_mclosure_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.coe_Sup_of_directed_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.log", "description": "Logarithms from powers to natural numbers.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit_map_cocone_cofork_equiv'", "description": "The map of a cokernel cofork is a colimit iff\nthe cokernel cofork consisting of the mapped morphisms is a colimit.\nThis essentially lets us commute `cokernel_cofork.of_\u03c0` with `functor.map_cocone`.\n\nThis is a variant of `is_colimit_map_cocone_cofork_equiv` for equalizers,\nwhich we can't use directly between `G.map 0 = 0` does not hold definitionally.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.category_theory.functor.map.has_cokernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_cokernel.of_iso_comparison", "description": "If the cokernel comparison map for `G` at `f` is an isomorphism, then `G` preserves the\ncokernel of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit_of_has_kernel_of_preserves_limit", "description": "If `G` preserves kernels and `C` has them, then the fork constructed of the mapped morphisms of\na kernel fork is a limit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_cokernel.iso", "description": "If `G` preserves the cokernel of `f`, then the cokernel comparison map for `G` at `f` is\nan isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_map_comp_preserves_kernel_iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_cokernel.iso_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_cokernel_iso_comp_cokernel_map_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_cokernel_iso_comp_cokernel_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit_map_cone_fork_equiv'", "description": "The map of a kernel fork is a limit iff\nthe kernel fork consisting of the mapped morphisms is a limit.\nThis essentially lets us commute `kernel_fork.of_\u03b9` with `functor.map_cone`.\n\nThis is a variant of `is_limit_map_cone_fork_equiv` for equalizers,\nwhich we can't use directly between `G.map 0 = 0` does not hold definitionally.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_map_comp_preserves_kernel_iso_inv_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_limit_fork_map_of_is_limit'", "description": "The property of preserving kernels expressed in terms of kernel forks.\n\nThis is a variant of `is_limit_fork_map_of_is_limit` for equalizers,\nwhich we can't use directly between `G.map 0 = 0` does not hold definitionally.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit_cofork_map_of_is_colimit'", "description": "The property of preserving cokernels expressed in terms of cokernel coforks.\n\nThis is a variant of `is_colimit_cofork_map_of_is_colimit` for equalizers,\nwhich we can't use directly between `G.map 0 = 0` does not hold definitionally.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_kernel.of_iso_comparison", "description": "If the kernel comparison map for `G` at `f` is an isomorphism, then `G` preserves the\nkernel of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_kernel.iso_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.kernel_comparison.category_theory.is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.category_theory.functor.map.has_kernel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.is_colimit_of_has_cokernel_of_preserves_colimit", "description": "If `G` preserves cokernels and `C` has them, then the cofork constructed of the mapped morphisms of\na cokernel cofork is a colimit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.preserves_kernel.iso", "description": "If `G` preserves the kernel of `f`, then the kernel comparison map for `G` at `f` is\nan isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.cokernel_comparison.category_theory.is_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_torsion_by_set_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_torsion'_powers_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.is_torsion_by_set.mk_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_gc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by_set_is_internal", "description": "If the `p i` are pairwise coprime, a `\u2a05 i, p i`-torsion module is the internal direct sum of\nits `p i`-torsion submodules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion", "description": "The torsion submodule, containing all elements `x` of `M` such that  `a \u2022 x = 0` for some\n non-zero-divisor `a` in `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quot_torsion_of_equiv_span_singleton_apply_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_torsion_by_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion'", "description": " The `S`-torsion submodule, containing all elements `x` of `M` such that `a \u2022 x = 0` for some\n`a` in `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion'_torsion'_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by_set.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by_singleton_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion'_is_torsion'", "description": "The `S`-torsion submodule is a `S`-torsion module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by_set_carrier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.is_torsion_by_set_iff_is_torsion_by_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.supr_torsion_by_eq_torsion_by_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.supr_torsion_by_ideal_eq_torsion_by_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.is_torsion'", "description": "A `S`-torsion module is a module where every element is `a`-torsion for some `a` in `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.is_torsion_iff_is_torsion_int", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by_set.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.is_torsion'_iff_torsion'_eq_top", "description": "A `S`-torsion module is a module whose `S`-torsion submodule is the full space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by_is_internal", "description": "If the `q i` are pairwise coprime, a `\u220f i, q i`-torsion module is the internal direct sum of\nits `q i`-torsion submodules.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.is_torsion_by_set.module", "description": "A `(R \u29f8 I)`-module is a `R`-module which `is_torsion_by_set R M I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion'_carrier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_torsion_of_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by_span_singleton_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient_torsion.torsion_eq_bot", "description": "Quotienting by the torsion submodule gives a torsion-free module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quotient.torsion_by_eq_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.is_torsion_by_span_singleton_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.pow_p_order_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.torsion_of_eq_bot_iff_of_no_zero_smul_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.is_torsion_by_set.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by_set_is_torsion_by_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by", "description": "The `a`-torsion submodule for `a` in `R`, containing all elements `x` of `M` such that\n `a \u2022 x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.is_torsion_iff_is_torsion_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.torsion_of_carrier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.is_torsion_by_set_iff_torsion_by_set_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by_le_torsion_by_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.sup_indep_torsion_by_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.has_quotient.quotient.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.p_order", "description": "In a `p ^ \u221e`-torsion module (that is, a module where all elements are cancelled by scalar\nmultiplication by some power of `p`), the smallest `n` such that `p ^ n \u2022 x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion'.distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_torsion_eq_top", "description": " The torsion submodule of the torsion submodule (viewed as a module) is the full\ntorsion module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_torsion_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by_set", "description": "The submodule containing all elements `x` of `M` such that `a \u2022 x = 0` for all `a` in `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.is_torsion_by", "description": "A `a`-torsion module is a module where every element is `a`-torsion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.exists_is_torsion_by", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_is_torsion", "description": "The torsion submodule is always a torsion module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by_set.mk_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.is_torsion_by_set.has_smul", "description": "can't be an instance because hM can't be inferred", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.torsion_of_eq_top_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.coe_torsion_eq_annihilator_ne_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.is_torsion", "description": "A torsion module is a module where every element is `a`-torsion for some non-zero-divisor `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.is_torsion_by_iff_torsion_by_eq_top", "description": "A `a`-torsion module is a module whose `a`-torsion submodule is the full space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by_set_eq_torsion_by_span", "description": "Torsion by a set is torsion by the ideal generated by it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.smul_coe_torsion_by", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.sup_indep_torsion_by", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.torsion_of_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by_set_torsion_by_set_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion'.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.annihilator_top_inter_non_zero_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion'.has_smul_smul_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.smul_torsion_by", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.is_torsion_by_singleton_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.complete_lattice.independent.linear_independent'", "description": " See also `complete_lattice.independent.linear_independent` which provides the same conclusion\nbut requires the stronger hypothesis `no_zero_smul_divisors R M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.quot_torsion_of_equiv_span_singleton", "description": "The span of `x` in `M` is isomorphic to `R` quotiented by the torsion ideal of `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion'.smul_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.no_zero_smul_divisors_iff_torsion_eq_bot", "description": "A module over a domain has `no_zero_smul_divisors` iff its torsion submodule is trivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.is_torsion_by_set", "description": "A module where every element is `a`-torsion for all `a` in `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by_set_le_torsion_by_set_of_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_torsion'_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.torsion_of", "description": "The torsion ideal of `x`, containing all `a` such that `a \u2022 x = 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by.mk_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by.module", "description": "The `a`-torsion submodule as a `(R \u29f8 R\u2219a)`-module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient_torsion.no_zero_smul_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.is_torsion_by_set_annihilator_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by_torsion_by_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by_is_torsion_by", "description": "The `a`-torsion submodule is a `a`-torsion module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.torsion_by_carrier", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.mul_right", "description": " If `G` is a group with measurable multiplication, then right multiplication by `g : G` is a\nmeasurable automorphism of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.coe_smul\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_embedding_const_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.coe_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.symm_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.to_equiv_mul_left\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.inv", "description": "Inversion as a measurable automorphism of a group or group with zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.symm_smul\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.symm_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.to_equiv_mul_right\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.symm_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.vadd", "description": "If an additive group `G` acts on `\u03b1` by measurable maps, then each element `c : G`\ndefines a measurable automorphism of `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.coe_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.symm_mul_right\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.symm_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.coe_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.smul_to_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_embedding_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.div_right", "description": "`equiv.div_right` as a `measurable_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_embedding_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.smul", "description": " If a group `G` acts on `\u03b1` by measurable maps, then each element `c : G` defines a measurable\nautomorphism of `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_embedding_mul_left\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.inv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.to_equiv_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_embedding_const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.coe_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.symm_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.coe_mul_left\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.symm_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_embedding_const_smul\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_embedding_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.inv_to_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.div_left", "description": "`equiv.div_left` as a `measurable_equiv`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.vadd_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.mul_right\u2080", "description": " If `G\u2080` is a group with zero with measurable multiplication, then right multiplication by a\nnonzero element `g : G\u2080` is a measurable automorphism of `G\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.symm_mul_left\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.symm_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_embedding_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.sub_left", "description": "`equiv.sub_left` as a `measurable_equiv`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.symm_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.add_right", "description": "If `G` is an additive group with measurable addition, then addition of `g : G`\non the right is a measurable automorphism of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.mul_left", "description": " If `G` is a group with measurable multiplication, then left multiplication by `g : G` is a\nmeasurable automorphism of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.coe_mul_right\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.vadd_to_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.neg", "description": "Negation as a measurable automorphism of an additive group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.to_equiv_add_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_embedding_mul_right\u2080", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.smul\u2080", "description": " If a group with zero `G\u2080` acts on `\u03b1` by measurable maps, then each nonzero element `c : G\u2080`\ndefines a measurable automorphism of `\u03b1`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.mul_left\u2080", "description": " If `G\u2080` is a group with zero with measurable multiplication, then left multiplication by a\nnonzero element `g : G\u2080` is a measurable automorphism of `G\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.add_left", "description": "If `G` is an additive group with measurable addition, then addition of `g : G`\non the left is a measurable automorphism of `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.to_equiv_add_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.sub_right", "description": "`equiv.sub_right` as a `measurable_equiv`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.neg_to_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.to_equiv_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable_equiv.neg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with", "description": "The type of homotopies between `f\u2080 f\u2081 : C(X, Y)`, where the intermediate maps satisfy the predicate\n`P : C(X, Y) \u2192 Prop`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.to_homotopy", "description": "The type of homotopies between `f\u2080 f\u2081 : C(X, Y)`, where the intermediate maps satisfy the predicate\n`P : C(X, Y) \u2192 Prop`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.prop'", "description": "The type of homotopies between `f\u2080 f\u2081 : C(X, Y)`, where the intermediate maps satisfy the predicate\n`P : C(X, Y) \u2192 Prop`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.coe_to_continuous_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.refl_to_homotopy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.symm_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.eq_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.simps.apply", "description": " See Note [custom simps projection]. We need to specify this projection explicitly in this case,\nbecause it is a composition of multiple projections.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel", "description": "A `homotopy_rel f\u2080 f\u2081 S` is a homotopy between `f\u2080` and `f\u2081` which is fixed on the points in `S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopic_with.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.congr_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopic_rel.equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.symm", "description": "Given a `homotopy_with f\u2080 f\u2081 P`, we can define a `homotopy_with f\u2081 f\u2080 P` by reversing the homotopy.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.trans_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.trans", "description": "Given `homotopy f\u2080 f\u2081` and `homotopy f\u2081 f\u2082`, we can define a `homotopy f\u2080 f\u2082` by putting the first\nhomotopy on `[0, 1/2]` and the second on `[1/2, 1]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.coe_to_continuous_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopic_rel.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.apply_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.refl_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopic_rel.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.refl", "description": "Given a continuous function `f`, and a proof `h : P f`, we can define a `homotopy_with f f P` by\n`F (t, x) = f x`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.curry", "description": "Currying a homotopy to a continuous function fron `I` to `C(X, Y)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopic.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.extend_apply_of_one_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopic", "description": "Given continuous maps `f\u2080` and `f\u2081`, we say `f\u2080` and `f\u2081` are homotopic if there exists a\n`homotopy f\u2080 f\u2081`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.extend_apply_of_le_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.continuous_map.homotopy_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopic.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.fst_eq_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopic_rel", "description": "Given continuous maps `f\u2080` and `f\u2081`, we say `f\u2080` and `f\u2081` are homotopic relative to a set `S` if\nthere exists a `homotopy_rel f\u2080 f\u2081 S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.symm", "description": "Given a `homotopy f\u2080 f\u2081`, we can define a `homotopy f\u2081 f\u2080` by reversing the homotopy.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.refl", "description": "Given a map `f : C(X, Y)` and a set `S`, we can define a `homotopy_rel f f S` by setting\n`F (t, x) = f x` for all `t`. This is defined using `homotopy_with.refl`, but with the proof\nfilled in.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.extend_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.eq_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.apply_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.cast_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.continuous", "description": "Deprecated. Use `map_continuous` instead.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.symm_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_like.to_continuous_map_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.hcomp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.apply_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopic_with.trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopic_rel.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopic_with", "description": "Given continuous maps `f\u2080` and `f\u2081`, we say `f\u2080` and `f\u2081` are homotopic with respect to the\npredicate `P` if there exists a `homotopy_with f\u2080 f\u2081 P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.refl", "description": "Given a continuous function `f`, we can define a `homotopy f f` by `F (t, x) = f x`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.extend_apply_of_mem_I", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.symm_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.has_coe_to_fun", "description": " Helper instance for when there's too many metavariables to apply `fun_like.has_coe_to_fun`\ndirectly.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopic.refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.refl_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy", "description": " `continuous_map.homotopy f\u2080 f\u2081` is the type of homotopies from `f\u2080` to `f\u2081`.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : homotopy f\u2080 f\u2081)`,\nyou should parametrize over `{F : Type*} [homotopy_like F f\u2080 f\u2081] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `continuous_map.homotopy_like`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.to_continuous_map", "description": " `continuous_map.homotopy f\u2080 f\u2081` is the type of homotopies from `f\u2080` to `f\u2081`.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : homotopy f\u2080 f\u2081)`,\nyou should parametrize over `{F : Type*} [homotopy_like F f\u2080 f\u2081] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `continuous_map.homotopy_like`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.map_zero_left'", "description": " `continuous_map.homotopy f\u2080 f\u2081` is the type of homotopies from `f\u2080` to `f\u2081`.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : homotopy f\u2080 f\u2081)`,\nyou should parametrize over `{F : Type*} [homotopy_like F f\u2080 f\u2081] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `continuous_map.homotopy_like`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.map_one_left'", "description": " `continuous_map.homotopy f\u2080 f\u2081` is the type of homotopies from `f\u2080` to `f\u2081`.\n\nWhen possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : homotopy f\u2080 f\u2081)`,\nyou should parametrize over `{F : Type*} [homotopy_like F f\u2080 f\u2081] (f : F)`.\n\nWhen you extend this structure, make sure to extend `continuous_map.homotopy_like`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.cast", "description": "Casting a `homotopy_rel f\u2080 f\u2081 S` to a `homotopy_rel g\u2080 g\u2081 S` where `f\u2080 = g\u2080` and `f\u2081 = g\u2081`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.refl_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.refl_to_homotopy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_like", "description": " `continuous_map.homotopy_like F f\u2080 f\u2081` states that `F` is a type of homotopies between `f\u2080` and\n`f\u2081`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `continuous_map.homotopy`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_like.coe", "description": " `continuous_map.homotopy_like F f\u2080 f\u2081` states that `F` is a type of homotopies between `f\u2080` and\n`f\u2081`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `continuous_map.homotopy`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_like.coe_injective'", "description": " `continuous_map.homotopy_like F f\u2080 f\u2081` states that `F` is a type of homotopies between `f\u2080` and\n`f\u2081`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `continuous_map.homotopy`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_like.map_continuous", "description": " `continuous_map.homotopy_like F f\u2080 f\u2081` states that `F` is a type of homotopies between `f\u2080` and\n`f\u2081`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `continuous_map.homotopy`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_like.map_zero_left", "description": " `continuous_map.homotopy_like F f\u2080 f\u2081` states that `F` is a type of homotopies between `f\u2080` and\n`f\u2081`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `continuous_map.homotopy`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_like.map_one_left", "description": " `continuous_map.homotopy_like F f\u2080 f\u2081` states that `F` is a type of homotopies between `f\u2080` and\n`f\u2081`.\n\nYou should extend this class when you extend `continuous_map.homotopy`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.cast_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.trans", "description": "Given `homotopy_with f\u2080 f\u2081 P` and `homotopy_with f\u2081 f\u2082 P`, we can define a `homotopy_with f\u2080 f\u2082 P`\nby putting the first homotopy on `[0, 1/2]` and the second on `[1/2, 1]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.prop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopic_with.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.coe_fn_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.cast", "description": "Casting a `homotopy f\u2080 f\u2081` to a `homotopy g\u2080 g\u2081` where `f\u2080 = g\u2080` and `f\u2081 = g\u2081`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.extend_prop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.apply_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.congr_arg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopic.equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.trans_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.hcomp", "description": "If we have a `homotopy f\u2080 f\u2081` and a `homotopy g\u2080 g\u2081`, then we can compose them and get a\n`homotopy (g\u2080.comp f\u2080) (g\u2081.comp f\u2081)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.symm", "description": "Given a `homotopy_rel f\u2080 f\u2081 S`, we can define a `homotopy_rel f\u2081 f\u2080 S` by reversing the homotopy.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.trans_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.cast_to_homotopy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.simps.apply", "description": " See Note [custom simps projection]. We need to specify this projection explicitly in this case,\nbecause it is a composition of multiple projections.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.curry_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.extend", "description": "Continuously extending a curried homotopy to a function from `\u211d` to `C(X, Y)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.symm_to_homotopy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.trans", "description": "Given `homotopy_rel f\u2080 f\u2081 S` and `homotopy_rel f\u2081 f\u2082 S`, we can define a `homotopy_rel f\u2080 f\u2082 S`\nby putting the first homotopy on `[0, 1/2]` and the second on `[1/2, 1]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.coe_to_homotopy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_rel.symm_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.cast", "description": "Casting a `homotopy_with f\u2080 f\u2081 P` to a `homotopy_with g\u2080 g\u2081 P` where `f\u2080 = g\u2080` and `f\u2081 = g\u2081`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopic.hcomp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.cast_to_homotopy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.symm_to_homotopy", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.symm_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy.symm_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.homotopy_with.cast_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.dimension_le_one.is_integral_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.dimension_le_one.not_lt_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain", "description": "A Dedekind domain is an integral domain that is Noetherian, integrally closed, and\nhas Krull dimension at most one.\n\nThis is definition 3.2 of [Neukirch1992].\n\nThe integral closure condition is independent of the choice of field of fractions:\nuse `is_dedekind_domain_iff` to prove `is_dedekind_domain` for a given `fraction_map`.\n\nThis is the default implementation, but there are equivalent definitions,\n`is_dedekind_domain_dvr` and `is_dedekind_domain_inv`.\nTODO: Prove that these are actually equivalent definitions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.is_noetherian_ring", "description": "A Dedekind domain is an integral domain that is Noetherian, integrally closed, and\nhas Krull dimension at most one.\n\nThis is definition 3.2 of [Neukirch1992].\n\nThe integral closure condition is independent of the choice of field of fractions:\nuse `is_dedekind_domain_iff` to prove `is_dedekind_domain` for a given `fraction_map`.\n\nThis is the default implementation, but there are equivalent definitions,\n`is_dedekind_domain_dvr` and `is_dedekind_domain_inv`.\nTODO: Prove that these are actually equivalent definitions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.dimension_le_one", "description": "A Dedekind domain is an integral domain that is Noetherian, integrally closed, and\nhas Krull dimension at most one.\n\nThis is definition 3.2 of [Neukirch1992].\n\nThe integral closure condition is independent of the choice of field of fractions:\nuse `is_dedekind_domain_iff` to prove `is_dedekind_domain` for a given `fraction_map`.\n\nThis is the default implementation, but there are equivalent definitions,\n`is_dedekind_domain_dvr` and `is_dedekind_domain_inv`.\nTODO: Prove that these are actually equivalent definitions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain.is_integrally_closed", "description": "A Dedekind domain is an integral domain that is Noetherian, integrally closed, and\nhas Krull dimension at most one.\n\nThis is definition 3.2 of [Neukirch1992].\n\nThe integral closure condition is independent of the choice of field of fractions:\nuse `is_dedekind_domain_iff` to prove `is_dedekind_domain` for a given `fraction_map`.\n\nThis is the default implementation, but there are equivalent definitions,\n`is_dedekind_domain_dvr` and `is_dedekind_domain_inv`.\nTODO: Prove that these are actually equivalent definitions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_dedekind_domain_iff", "description": " An integral domain is a Dedekind domain iff and only if it is\nNoetherian, has dimension \u2264 1, and is integrally closed in a given fraction field.\nIn particular, this definition does not depend on the choice of this fraction field.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.dimension_le_one.principal_ideal_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_principal_ideal_ring.is_dedekind_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.dimension_le_one", "description": "A ring `R` has Krull dimension at most one if all nonzero prime ideals are maximal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.dimension_le_one.integral_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring.dimension_le_one.eq_bot_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_neg_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_inv_inv'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_zero_sub_max_neg_zero_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_div_div_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_div_div_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_div_div_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_sub_sub_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_zero_sub_eq_self", "description": "**Alias** of `max_zero_sub_max_neg_zero_eq_self`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_sub_sub_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_max_sub_max_le_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_inv_inv'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_div_div_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_one_div_max_inv_one_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_sub_sub_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_sub_max_le_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_min_sub_min_le_max", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "abs_max_sub_max_le_abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "max_neg_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "min_sub_sub_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_eq_of_eq_mul_det_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_units_conj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_eq_of_forall_row_eq_smul_add_pred", "description": "If you add multiples of previous rows to the next row, the determinant doesn't change.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_update_column_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_zero_of_row_eq", "description": "If a matrix has a repeated row, the determinant will be zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_from_blocks_zero\u2082\u2081", "description": " The determinant of a 2\u00d72 block matrix with the lower-left block equal to zero is the product of\nthe determinants of the diagonal blocks. For the generalization to any number of blocks, see\n`matrix.det_of_upper_triangular`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_transpose", "description": "Transposing a matrix preserves the determinant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_succ_column", "description": "Laplacian expansion of the determinant of an `n+1 \u00d7 n+1` matrix along column `j`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_submatrix_equiv_self", "description": "Permuting rows and columns with the same equivalence has no effect.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.map_det", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_update_column_smul'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_block_diagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_eq_of_forall_row_eq_smul_add_const_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_permutation", "description": "The determinant of a permutation matrix equals its sign.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_fin_two", "description": "Determinant of 2x2 matrix", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.map_det", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_conj_transpose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_from_blocks_zero\u2081\u2082", "description": " The determinant of a 2\u00d72 block matrix with the upper-right block equal to zero is the product of\nthe determinants of the diagonal blocks. For the generalization to any number of blocks, see\n`matrix.det_of_lower_triangular`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_succ_row", "description": "Laplacian expansion of the determinant of an `n+1 \u00d7 n+1` matrix along row `i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_units_conj'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det", "description": "The determinant of a matrix given by the Leibniz formula.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_fin_one", "description": "Determinant of 1x1 matrix", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.coe_det_monoid_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_diagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_equiv.map_det", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_mul_comm", "description": "On square matrices, `mul_comm` applies under `det`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_reindex_self", "description": " Reindexing both indices along the same equivalence preserves the determinant.\n\nFor the `simp` version of this lemma, see `det_submatrix_equiv_self`; this one is unsuitable because\n`matrix.reindex_apply` unfolds `reindex` first.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_succ_row_zero", "description": "Laplacian expansion of the determinant of an `n+1 \u00d7 n+1` matrix along row 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_eq_one_of_card_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_mul_left_comm", "description": "On square matrices, `mul_left_comm` applies under `det`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_update_column_add_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_mul_column", "description": " Multiplying each column by a fixed `v j` multiplies the determinant by\nthe product of the `v`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_mul_row", "description": " Multiplying each row by a fixed `v i` multiplies the determinant by\nthe product of the `v`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_fin_two_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_update_row_add_smul_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_eq_zero_of_row_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.coe_det_is_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_eq_of_eq_det_one_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_succ_column_zero", "description": "Laplacian expansion of the determinant of an `n+1 \u00d7 n+1` matrix along column 0.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_zero_of_column_eq", "description": "If a matrix has a repeated column, the determinant will be zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_eq_zero_of_column_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_fin_zero", "description": "Determinant of 0x0 matrix", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_mul_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_update_row_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_update_column_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_update_row_smul'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_fin_one_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_eq_elem_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_smul_of_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_row_alternating", "description": "`det` is an `alternating_map` in the rows of the matrix.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_eq_elem_of_card_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_is_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_update_row_add_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_eq_of_forall_row_eq_smul_add_const", "description": "If you add multiples of row `B k` to other rows, the determinant doesn't change.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_fin_three", "description": "Determinant of 3x3 matrix", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_eq_of_forall_col_eq_smul_add_pred", "description": "If you add multiples of previous columns to the next columns, the determinant doesn't change.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_update_column_add_smul_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_neg_eq_smul", "description": " A variant of `matrix.det_neg` with scalar multiplication by `units \u2124` instead of multiplication\nby `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_equiv.map_det", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_monoid_hom", "description": "The determinant of a matrix, as a monoid homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_eq_of_forall_row_eq_smul_add_pred_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_unique", "description": " If `n` has only one element, the determinant of an `n` by `n` matrix is just that element.\nAlthough `unique` implies `decidable_eq` and `fintype`, the instances might\nnot be syntactically equal. Thus, we need to fill in the args explicitly.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_update_row_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_mul_right_comm", "description": "On square matrices, `mul_right_comm` applies under `det`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.det_permute", "description": "Permuting the columns changes the sign of the determinant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.is_ultrahomogeneous", "description": " A structure `M` is ultrahomogeneous if every embedding of a finitely generated substructure\ninto `M` extends to an automorphism of `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.equiv.age_eq_age", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.embedding.age_subset_age", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.Structure.fg.mem_age_of_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.amalgamation", "description": "A class `K` has the amalgamation property when for any pair of embeddings of a structure `M` in\n `K` into other structures in `K`, those two structures can be embedded into a fourth structure in\n `K` such that the resulting square of embeddings commutes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.age.is_equiv_invariant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.joint_embedding", "description": "A class `K` has the joint embedding property when for every `M`, `N` in `K`, there is another\n structure in `K` into which both `M` and `N` embed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.is_fraisse_limit.is_fraisse", "description": "If a class has a Fra\u00efss\u00e9 limit, it must be Fra\u00efss\u00e9.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.age", "description": "The age of a structure `M` is the class of finitely-generated structures that embed into it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.is_fraisse", "description": " A Fra\u00efss\u00e9 class is a nonempty, isomorphism-invariant, essentially countable class of structures\nsatisfying the hereditary, joint embedding, and amalgamation properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.is_fraisse.is_nonempty", "description": " A Fra\u00efss\u00e9 class is a nonempty, isomorphism-invariant, essentially countable class of structures\nsatisfying the hereditary, joint embedding, and amalgamation properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.is_fraisse.fg", "description": " A Fra\u00efss\u00e9 class is a nonempty, isomorphism-invariant, essentially countable class of structures\nsatisfying the hereditary, joint embedding, and amalgamation properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.is_fraisse.is_equiv_invariant", "description": " A Fra\u00efss\u00e9 class is a nonempty, isomorphism-invariant, essentially countable class of structures\nsatisfying the hereditary, joint embedding, and amalgamation properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.is_fraisse.is_essentially_countable", "description": " A Fra\u00efss\u00e9 class is a nonempty, isomorphism-invariant, essentially countable class of structures\nsatisfying the hereditary, joint embedding, and amalgamation properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.is_fraisse.hereditary", "description": " A Fra\u00efss\u00e9 class is a nonempty, isomorphism-invariant, essentially countable class of structures\nsatisfying the hereditary, joint embedding, and amalgamation properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.is_fraisse.joint_embedding", "description": " A Fra\u00efss\u00e9 class is a nonempty, isomorphism-invariant, essentially countable class of structures\nsatisfying the hereditary, joint embedding, and amalgamation properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.is_fraisse.amalgamation", "description": " A Fra\u00efss\u00e9 class is a nonempty, isomorphism-invariant, essentially countable class of structures\nsatisfying the hereditary, joint embedding, and amalgamation properties.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.is_ultrahomogeneous.age_is_fraisse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.hereditary.is_equiv_invariant_of_fg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.age.joint_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.age.hereditary", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.age.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.exists_cg_is_age_of", "description": "Sufficient conditions for a class to be the age of a countably-generated structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.is_ultrahomogeneous.amalgamation_age", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.age.countable_quotient", "description": " The age of a countable structure is essentially countable (has countably many isomorphism\nclasses).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.age_direct_limit", "description": "The age of a direct limit of structures is the union of the ages of the structures.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.exists_countable_is_age_of_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.hereditary", "description": "A class `K` has the hereditary property when all finitely-generated structures that embed into\n structures in `K` are also in `K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.is_fraisse_limit", "description": " A structure `M` is a Fra\u00efss\u00e9 limit for a class `K` if it is countably generated,\nultrahomogeneous, and has age `K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.is_fraisse_limit.ultrahomogeneous", "description": " A structure `M` is a Fra\u00efss\u00e9 limit for a class `K` if it is countably generated,\nultrahomogeneous, and has age `K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.is_fraisse_limit.age", "description": " A structure `M` is a Fra\u00efss\u00e9 limit for a class `K` if it is countably generated,\nultrahomogeneous, and has age `K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.op_norm_zero_iff", "description": "For normed groups, an operator is zero iff its norm vanishes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.to_add_monoid_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.mk_normed_add_group_hom_norm_le'", "description": " If a bounded group homomorphism map is constructed from a group homomorphism\nvia the constructor `mk_normed_add_group_hom`, then its norm is bounded by the bound\ngiven to the constructor or zero if this bound is negative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.has_nat_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.ker.lift_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.incl_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.le_op_norm", "description": "The fundamental property of the operator norm: `\u2016f x\u2016 \u2264 \u2016f\u2016 * \u2016x\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.neg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_ker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.equalizer.\u03b9", "description": "The inclusion of `f.equalizer g` as a `normed_add_group_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.norm_comp_le_of_le'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.equalizer.lift_equiv", "description": "The lifting property of the equalizer as an equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.is_closed_ker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.op_norm_le_of_lipschitz", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.isometry_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.norm_id", "description": "If a normed space is non-trivial, then the norm of the identity equals `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.incl", "description": "The inclusion of an `add_subgroup`, as bounded group homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.comp_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.op_norm_eq_of_bounds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.op_norm_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.lipschitz", "description": "continuous linear maps are Lipschitz continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.bounds_bdd_below", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.op_norm_zero", "description": "The norm of the `0` operator is `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.mem_ker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.equalizer.lift_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.norm_noninc_of_isometry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.sub_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.comp", "description": "The composition of continuous normed group homs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.antilipschitz_of_norm_ge", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.norm_noninc.zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.op_norm_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.surjective_on_with.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.norm_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.to_fun_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.ker.lift", "description": "Given a normed group hom `f : V\u2081 \u2192 V\u2082` satisfying `g.comp f = 0` for some `g : V\u2082 \u2192 V\u2083`,\n   the corestriction of `f` to the kernel of `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.has_neg", "description": "Opposite of a normed group hom.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.le_of_op_norm_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.has_op_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.equalizer.lift_equiv_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.ker", "description": " The kernel of a bounded group homomorphism. Naturally endowed with a\n`seminormed_add_comm_group` instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.surjective_on_with.exists_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.equalizer.map_norm_noninc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.equalizer.comp_\u03b9_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.smul_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.mem_range_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.mk_normed_add_group_hom_norm_le'", "description": "**Alias** of `normed_add_group_hom.mk_normed_add_group_hom_norm_le'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.norm_id_of_nontrivial_seminorm", "description": " If there is an element with norm different from `0`, then the norm of the identity equals `1`.\n(Since we are working with seminorms supposing that the space is non-trivial is not enough.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.equalizer.map", "description": " Given `\u03c6 : normed_add_group_hom V\u2081 V\u2082` and `\u03c8 : normed_add_group_hom W\u2081 W\u2082` such that\n`\u03c8.comp f\u2081 = f\u2082.comp \u03c6` and `\u03c8.comp g\u2081 = g\u2082.comp \u03c6`, the induced morphism\n`normed_add_group_hom (f\u2081.equalizer g\u2081) (f\u2082.equalizer g\u2082)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.range", "description": " The image of a bounded group homomorphism. Naturally endowed with a\n`seminormed_add_comm_group` instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.ker.incl_comp_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.mk_normed_add_group_hom_norm_le", "description": "**Alias** of `normed_add_group_hom.mk_normed_add_group_hom_norm_le`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.norm_comp_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.bounds_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.norm_noninc", "description": "A `normed_add_group_hom` is *norm-nonincreasing* if `\u2016f v\u2016 \u2264 \u2016v\u2016` for all `v`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.nsmul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.surjective_on_with.surj_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_fn_add_hom", "description": "Coercion of a `normed_add_group_hom` is an `add_monoid_hom`. Similar to `add_monoid_hom.coe_fn`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.incl_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.comp_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "library_note.addition on function coercions", "description": "Terms containing `@has_add.add (has_coe_to_fun.F ...) pi.has_add`\nseem to cause leanchecker to [crash due to an out-of-memory\ncondition](https://github.com/leanprover-community/lean/issues/543).\nAs a workaround, we add a type annotation: `(f + g : V\u2081 \u2192 V\u2082)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.norm_noninc.id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_pos_bound_of_bound", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.equalizer.map_comp_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.has_sub", "description": "Subtraction of normed group homs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.to_normed_add_comm_group", "description": "Normed group homomorphisms themselves form a normed group with respect to\n   the operator norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_mk_normed_add_group_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.equalizer.\u03b9_comp_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.norm_id_le", "description": " The norm of the identity is at most `1`. It is in fact `1`, except when the norm of every\nelement vanishes, where it is `0`. (Since we are working with seminorms this can happen even if the\nspace is non-trivial.) It means that one can not do better than an inequality in general.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.equalizer.\u03b9_norm_noninc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.isometry_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.add_monoid_hom_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.equalizer", "description": "The equalizer of two morphisms `f g : normed_add_group_hom V W`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.is_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.mk_normed_add_group_hom", "description": " Associate to a group homomorphism a bounded group homomorphism under a norm control condition.\n\nSee `add_monoid_hom.mk_normed_add_group_hom'` for a version that uses `\u211d\u22650` for the bound.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.ratio_le_op_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_mk_normed_add_group_hom'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.le_op_norm_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_fn_add_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.norm_noninc.norm_noninc_iff_norm_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.distrib_mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.has_int_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom", "description": "A morphism of seminormed abelian groups is a bounded group homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.to_fun", "description": "A morphism of seminormed abelian groups is a bounded group homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.map_add'", "description": "A morphism of seminormed abelian groups is a bounded group homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.bound'", "description": "A morphism of seminormed abelian groups is a bounded group homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.norm_incl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.surjective_on_with", "description": " A normed group hom is surjective on the subgroup `K` with constant `C` if every element\n`x` of `K` has a preimage whose norm is bounded above by `C*\u2016x\u2016`. This is a more\nabstract version of `f` having a right inverse defined on `K` with operator norm\nat most `C`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.range_comp_incl_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.to_add_monoid_hom", "description": "The group homomorphism underlying a bounded group homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.norm_noninc.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_inj_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.equalizer.lift_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.equalizer.\u03b9_comp_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.mem_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.op_norm_add_le", "description": "The operator norm satisfies the triangle inequality.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.uniform_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.comp_hom", "description": "Composition of normed groups hom as an additive group morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.norm_noninc.neg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_to_add_monoid_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.equalizer.comm_sq\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.equalizer.lift", "description": " If `\u03c6 : normed_add_group_hom V\u2081 V` is such that `f.comp \u03c6 = g.comp \u03c6`, the induced morphism\n`normed_add_group_hom V\u2081 (f.equalizer g)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.equalizer.norm_lift_le", "description": "If `\u03c6` satisfies `\u2016\u03c6\u2016 \u2264 C`, then the same is true for the lifted morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.norm_eq_of_isometry", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.mk_normed_add_group_hom_norm_le", "description": " If a bounded group homomorphism map is constructed from a group homomorphism via the constructor\n`mk_normed_add_group_hom`, then its norm is bounded by the bound given to the constructor if it is\nnonnegative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.ker_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.comp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.comp_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_hom.mk_normed_add_group_hom'", "description": " Associate to a group homomorphism a bounded group homomorphism under a norm control condition.\n\nSee `add_monoid_hom.mk_normed_add_group_hom` for a version that uses `\u211d` for the bound.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.zsmul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.to_seminormed_add_comm_group", "description": "Normed group homomorphisms themselves form a seminormed group with respect to\n   the operator norm.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.coe_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.op_norm_le_bound", "description": "If one controls the norm of every `f x`, then one controls the norm of `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.equalizer.norm_map_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.id", "description": "The identity as a continuous normed group hom.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.bound", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.has_add", "description": "Addition of normed group homs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.norm_comp_le_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.equalizer.lift_norm_noninc", "description": "The lifting of a norm nonincreasing morphism is norm nonincreasing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.sum_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.op_norm", "description": "The operator norm of a seminormed group homomorphism is the inf of all its bounds.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.add_comm_group", "description": "Homs between two given normed groups form a commutative additive group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.zero_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.add_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.equalizer.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.mk_to_add_monoid_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_add_group_hom.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.elim", "description": "The canonical map from `W_type \u03b2` into any type `\u03b3` given a map `(\u03a3 a : \u03b1, \u03b2 a \u2192 \u03b3) \u2192 \u03b3`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.equiv_sigma", "description": "The canonical bijection with the sigma type, showing that `W_type` is a fixed point of\n the polynomial functor `X \u21a6 \u03a3 a : \u03b1, \u03b2 a \u2192 X`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.depth", "description": "The depth of a finitely branching tree.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.depth_lt_depth_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.of_sigma", "description": "The canonical map from the sigma type into a `W_type`. Given a node `a : \u03b1`, and\n its children as a function `\u03b2 a \u2192 W_type \u03b2`, return the corresponding tree.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.to_sigma", "description": "The canonical map to the corresponding sigma type, returning the label of a node as an\n element `a` of `\u03b1`, and the children of the node as a function `\u03b2 a \u2192 W_type \u03b2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.elim_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.infinite_of_nonempty_of_is_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.to_sigma_of_sigma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.equiv_sigma_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.encodable", "description": " `W_type` is encodable when `\u03b1` is an encodable fintype and for every `a : \u03b1`, `\u03b2 a` is\nencodable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.depth_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.of_sigma_to_sigma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type", "description": "Given `\u03b2 : \u03b1 \u2192 Type*`, `W_type \u03b2` is the type of finitely branching trees where nodes are labeled by\nelements of `\u03b1` and the children of a node labeled `a` are indexed by elements of `\u03b2 a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.mk", "description": "Given `\u03b2 : \u03b1 \u2192 Type*`, `W_type \u03b2` is the type of finitely branching trees where nodes are labeled by\nelements of `\u03b1` and the children of a node labeled `a` are indexed by elements of `\u03b2 a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.equiv_sigma_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.is_empty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.compl\u2081\u2082_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_sub\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.mk\u2082'", "description": " Create a bilinear map from a function that is linear in each component.\nSee `mk\u2082` for the special case where both arguments come from modules over the same ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.lcomp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.flip", "description": " Given a linear map from `M` to linear maps from `N` to `P`, i.e., a bilinear map from `M \u00d7 N` to\n`P`, change the order of variables and get a linear map from `N` to linear maps from `M` to `P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.compl\u2082_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_neg\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.flip_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ext\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.lcomp\u209b\u2097_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.lflip_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.congr_fun\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.compr\u2082_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.lsmul", "description": "Scalar multiplication as a bilinear map `R \u2192 M \u2192 M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_smul\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.lcomp_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_add\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.flip_flip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.compl\u2081\u2082", "description": " Composing linear maps `Q \u2192 M` and `Q' \u2192 N` with a bilinear map `M \u2192 N \u2192 P` to\nform a bilinear map `Q \u2192 Q' \u2192 P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_zero\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.compr\u2082", "description": " Composing a linear map `P \u2192 Q` and a bilinear map `M \u2192 N \u2192 P` to\nform a bilinear map `M \u2192 N \u2192 Q`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.mk\u2082'\u209b\u2097_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.mk\u2082", "description": " Create a bilinear map from a function that is linear in each component.\n\nThis is a shorthand for `mk\u2082'` for the common case when `R = S`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.mk\u2082'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ker_lsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_sum\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.compl\u2082", "description": " Composing a linear map `Q \u2192 N` and a bilinear map `M \u2192 N \u2192 P` to\nform a bilinear map `M \u2192 Q \u2192 P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.compl\u2081\u2082_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.llcomp_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.lsmul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.dom_restrict\u2081\u2082_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.llcomp", "description": "Composing a linear map `M \u2192 N` and a linear map `N \u2192 P` to form a linear map `M \u2192 P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.dom_restrict\u2081\u2082", "description": "Restricting a bilinear map in both components", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.mk\u2082'\u209b\u2097", "description": " Create a bilinear map from a function that is semilinear in each component.\nSee `mk\u2082'` and `mk\u2082` for the linear case.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.llcomp_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.mk\u2082_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.compl\u2082_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.map_smul\u209b\u2097\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.dom_restrict\u2082", "description": "Restricting a bilinear map in the second entry", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.compl\u2081\u2082_id_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.lflip", "description": " Given a linear map from `M` to linear maps from `N` to `P`, i.e., a bilinear map `M \u2192 N \u2192 P`,\nchange the order of variables and get a linear map from `N` to linear maps from `M` to `P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.lcomp\u209b\u2097", "description": " Composing a semilinear map `M \u2192 N` and a semilinear map `N \u2192 P` to form a semilinear map\n`M \u2192 P` is itself a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.flip_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.lcomp", "description": "Composing a linear map `M \u2192 N` and a linear map `N \u2192 P` to form a linear map `M \u2192 P`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.lsmul_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.dom_restrict\u2082_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.elim_eqs", "description": "Find and return the sequence of steps for eliminating\n   all equality constraints in the current state.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.add_ee", "description": "Add a new step to the sequence of equality elimination steps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.ee_commit", "description": "If `t1` succeeds and returns a value, 'commit' to that choice and\n   run `t3` with the returned value as argument. Do not backtrack\n   to try `t2` even if `t3` fails. If `t1` fails outright, run `t2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.find_min_coeff_core", "description": " If list has a nonzero element, return the minimum element\n(by absolute value) with its index. Otherwise, return none.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.get_eqs", "description": "Get the current list of equality constraints.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.eqelim", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.factor", "description": "Divide a term by an integer if the integer divides\n   the constant component of the term. It is assumed that\n   the integer also divides all coefficients of the term.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.set_ees", "description": "Update the sequence of equality elimiation steps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.find_ees", "description": " Given a linear constrain clause, return a list of steps for eliminating its equality\nconstraints.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.run", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.elim_eq", "description": "Find an appropriate equality elimination step for the\n   current state and apply it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.ee_state", "description": "The state of equality elimination proof search. `eqs` is the list of\n   equality constraints, and each `t \u2208 eqs` represents the constraint `0 = t`.\n   Similarly, `les` is the list of inequality constraints, and each `t \u2208 eqs`\n   represents the constraint `0 < t`. `ees` is the sequence of equality\n   elimination steps that have been used so far to obtain the current set of\n   constraints. The list `ees` grows over time until `eqs` becomes empty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.ee_state.eqs", "description": "The state of equality elimination proof search. `eqs` is the list of\n   equality constraints, and each `t \u2208 eqs` represents the constraint `0 = t`.\n   Similarly, `les` is the list of inequality constraints, and each `t \u2208 eqs`\n   represents the constraint `0 < t`. `ees` is the sequence of equality\n   elimination steps that have been used so far to obtain the current set of\n   constraints. The list `ees` grows over time until `eqs` becomes empty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.ee_state.les", "description": "The state of equality elimination proof search. `eqs` is the list of\n   equality constraints, and each `t \u2208 eqs` represents the constraint `0 = t`.\n   Similarly, `les` is the list of inequality constraints, and each `t \u2208 eqs`\n   represents the constraint `0 < t`. `ees` is the sequence of equality\n   elimination steps that have been used so far to obtain the current set of\n   constraints. The list `ees` grows over time until `eqs` becomes empty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.ee_state.ees", "description": "The state of equality elimination proof search. `eqs` is the list of\n   equality constraints, and each `t \u2208 eqs` represents the constraint `0 = t`.\n   Similarly, `les` is the list of inequality constraints, and each `t \u2208 eqs`\n   represents the constraint `0 < t`. `ees` is the sequence of equality\n   elimination steps that have been used so far to obtain the current set of\n   constraints. The list `ees` grows over time until `eqs` becomes empty.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.get_les", "description": "Get the current list of inequality constraints.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.set_eqs", "description": "Update the list of equality constraints.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.abort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.gcd", "description": "GCD of all elements of the list.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.get_gcd", "description": "GCD of all coefficients in a term.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.get_ees", "description": "Get the current sequence of equality elimiation steps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.set_les", "description": "Update the list of inequality constraints.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.ee_state.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.find_min_coeff", "description": "Find and return the smallest coefficient (by absolute value) in a term,\n   along with the coefficient's variable index and the term itself.\n   If the coefficient is negative, negate both the coefficient and the term\n   before returning them.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.head_eq", "description": "Return the first equality constraint in the current list of\n   equality constraints. The returned constraint is 'popped' and\n   no longer available in the state.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.prod_antidiagonal_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.sum_antidiagonal_succ'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.prod_antidiagonal_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.sum_antidiagonal_eq_sum_range_succ", "description": "This lemma matches more generally than\n`finset.nat.sum_antidiagonal_eq_sum_range_succ_mk` when using `rw \u2190`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.sum_antidiagonal_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.prod_antidiagonal_eq_prod_range_succ", "description": " This lemma matches more generally than `finset.nat.prod_antidiagonal_eq_prod_range_succ_mk` when\nusing `rw \u2190`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.prod_antidiagonal_eq_prod_range_succ_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.sum_antidiagonal_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.sum_antidiagonal_subst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.sum_antidiagonal_eq_sum_range_succ_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.prod_antidiagonal_subst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.nat.prod_antidiagonal_succ'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "theorems_100.disc_eq_region_between", "description": "A disc of radius `r` can be represented as the region between the two curves\n `\u03bb x, - sqrt (r ^ 2 - x ^ 2)` and `\u03bb x, sqrt (r ^ 2 - x ^ 2)`.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.area_disc", "description": "**Area of a Circle**: The area of a disc with radius `r` is `\u03c0 * r ^ 2`.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.disc", "description": "A disc of radius `r` is defined as the collection of points `(p.1, p.2)` in `\u211d \u00d7 \u211d` such that\n `p.1 ^ 2 + p.2 ^ 2 < r ^ 2`.\n Note that this definition is not equivalent to `metric.ball (0 : \u211d \u00d7 \u211d) r`. This was done\n intentionally because `dist` in `\u211d \u00d7 \u211d` is defined as the uniform norm, making the `metric.ball`\n in `\u211d \u00d7 \u211d` a square, not a disc.\n See the module docstring for an explanation of why we don't define the disc in Euclidean space.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "theorems_100.measurable_set_disc", "description": "The disc is a `measurable_set`.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "nat.prime.sum_proper_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.map_div_right_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.snd_mem_divisors_of_mem_antidiagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.mem_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.sum_proper_divisors_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.sum_proper_divisors_eq_one_iff_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.proper_divisors.not_self_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prime.proper_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.divisors", "description": "`divisors n` is the `finset` of divisors of `n`. As a special case, `divisors 0 = \u2205`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prod_divisors_antidiagonal'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.divisors_antidiagonal", "description": "`divisors_antidiagonal n` is the `finset` of pairs `(x,y)` such that `x * y = n`.\n As a special case, `divisors_antidiagonal 0 = \u2205`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.sum_proper_divisors_prime_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.insert_self_proper_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.proper_divisors_subset_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prime.sum_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.divisors_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.divisors_antidiagonal_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.filter_dvd_eq_proper_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.proper_divisors", "description": "`proper_divisors n` is the `finset` of divisors of `n`, other than `n`.\n As a special case, `proper_divisors 0 = \u2205`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.perfect", "description": "`n : \u2115` is perfect if and only the sum of the proper divisors of `n` is `n` and `n`\n is positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.divisors_subset_proper_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.divisors_subset_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.divisors_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.image_div_divisors_eq_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.eq_proper_divisors_of_subset_of_sum_eq_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.one_mem_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.image_fst_divisors_antidiagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.divisors_prime_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.mem_proper_divisors_prime_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.proper_divisors_eq_singleton_one_iff_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.divisors_antidiagonal_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.mem_divisors_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prime_divisors_eq_to_filter_divisors_prime", "description": "The factors of `n` are the prime divisors", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prod_proper_divisors_prime_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cons_self_proper_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.proper_divisors_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prime.prod_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.dvd_of_mem_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.one_mem_proper_divisors_iff_one_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prod_divisors_antidiagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.map_swap_divisors_antidiagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.proper_divisors_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.sum_div_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.proper_divisors_prime_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.sum_divisors_eq_sum_proper_divisors_add_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prime.prod_proper_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.sum_divisors_prime_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.perfect_iff_sum_divisors_eq_two_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.mem_proper_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.filter_dvd_eq_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.mem_divisors_prime_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pos_of_mem_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.image_snd_divisors_antidiagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.perfect_iff_sum_proper_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.pos_of_mem_proper_divisors", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prime.divisors"