, {"name": "add_nsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "neg_one_zsmul_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_commute.self_zsmul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pow_monoid_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pow_bit1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_zpow'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_div_zpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ite_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pow_mul_pow_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.mul_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "one_div_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.homogeneous_hull_eq_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.homogeneous_core_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.to_ideal_homogeneous_core_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.homogeneous_hull_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.homogeneous_hull.gc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.eq_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.eq_top_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.to_ideal", "description": "Converting a homogeneous ideal to an ideal", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.to_ideal_irrelevant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.coe_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.has_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_homogeneous.to_ideal_homogeneous_core_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.to_ideal_infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.le_to_ideal_homogeneous_hull", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.to_ideal_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_homogeneous.iff_exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.homogeneous_hull_to_ideal_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.to_ideal_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.homogeneous_hull.gi", "description": " `ideal.homogeneous_hull \ud835\udc9c` and `to_ideal : homogeneous_ideal \ud835\udc9c \u2192 ideal A` form a galois\ninsertion", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.homogeneous_hull_eq_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_homogeneous_core_of_is_homogeneous_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.coe_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.mem_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.homogeneous_core'_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.irrelevant", "description": "For a graded ring `\u2a01\u1d62 \ud835\udc9c\u1d62` graded by a `canonically_ordered_add_monoid \u03b9`, the irrelevant ideal\nrefers to `\u2a01_{i>0} \ud835\udc9c\u1d62`, or equivalently `{a | a\u2080 = 0}`. This definition is used in `Proj`\nconstruction where `\u03b9` is always `\u2115` so the irrelevant ideal is simply elements with `0` as\n0-th coordinate.\n\n# Future work\nHere in the definition, `\u03b9` is assumed to be `canonically_ordered_add_monoid`. However, the notion\nof irrelevant ideal makes sense in a more general setting by defining it as the ideal of elements\nwith `0` as i-th coordinate for all `i \u2264 0`, i.e. `{a | \u2200 (i : \u03b9), i \u2264 0 \u2192 a\u1d62 = 0}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_homogeneous_iff_subset_Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.has_Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_homogeneous.infi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.homogeneous_core'_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_homogeneous_iff_forall_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.to_ideal_homogeneous_core_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.homogeneous_hull", "description": "For any `I : ideal A`, not necessarily homogeneous, `I.homogeneous_hull \ud835\udc9c` is\nthe smallest homogeneous ideal containing `I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.to_ideal_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_homogeneous_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.has_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_homogeneous.bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.set_like", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.has_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_homogeneous", "description": "An `I : ideal A` is homogeneous if for every `r \u2208 I`, all homogeneous components\n  of `r` are in `I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_homogeneous.top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.to_ideal_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.homogeneous_core.gi", "description": "`to_ideal : homogeneous_ideal \ud835\udc9c \u2192 ideal A` and `ideal.homogeneous_core \ud835\udc9c` forms a galois\ncoinsertion", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_homogeneous.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.to_ideal_Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.is_homogeneous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.has_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.homogeneous_core", "description": "For any `I : ideal A`, not necessarily homogeneous, `I.homogeneous_core' \ud835\udc9c`\nis the largest homogeneous ideal of `A` contained in `I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_homogeneous.iff_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.coe_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.to_ideal_infi\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_homogeneous.Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.coe_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.has_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.to_ideal_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.homogeneous_core.gc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_homogeneous.supr\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.homogeneous_core'", "description": " For any `I : ideal A`, not necessarily homogeneous, `I.homogeneous_core' \ud835\udc9c`\nis the largest homogeneous ideal of `A` contained in `I`, as an ideal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.has_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_homogeneous.inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.homogeneous_core'_eq_Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.to_ideal_homogeneous_hull_eq_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_homogeneous.supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.to_ideal_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.to_ideal_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_homogeneous.sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal", "description": "For any `semiring A`, we collect the homogeneous ideals of `A` into a type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.to_submodule", "description": "For any `semiring A`, we collect the homogeneous ideals of `A` into a type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.is_homogeneous'", "description": "For any `semiring A`, we collect the homogeneous ideals of `A` into a type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.homogeneous_core_eq_Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.to_ideal_supr\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.complete_lattice", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_homogeneous.Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_homogeneous.infi\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.has_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_homogeneous.to_ideal_homogeneous_hull_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.partial_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mul_homogeneous_element_mem_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.mem_irrelevant_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.to_ideal_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homogeneous_ideal.to_ideal_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "card_class_group_eq_one_iff", "description": "The class number is `1` iff the ring of integers is a principal ideal domain.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.coe_mk0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.mk", "description": "Send a nonzero fractional ideal to the corresponding class in the class group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.mk_eq_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.map_canonical_equiv_mk0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.canonical_equiv_mk0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.mk0_eq_mk0_iff_exists_fraction_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "principal_ideals.normal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.mk_eq_mk_of_coe_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.equiv_mk0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.equiv", "description": "The definition of the class group does not depend on the choice of field of fractions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_principal_ideals_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.mk0", "description": "Send a nonzero ideal to the corresponding class in the class group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_principal_ideal", "description": "`to_principal_ideal R K x` sends `x \u2260 0 : K` to the fractional `R`-ideal generated by `x`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.mk_mk0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group", "description": " The ideal class group of `R` is the group of invertible fractional ideals\nmodulo the principal ideals.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.mk0_eq_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.mk0_eq_mk0_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.fintype", "description": " The class group of principal ideal domain is finite (in fact a singleton).\n\nSee `class_group.fintype_of_admissible` for a finiteness proof that works for rings of integers\nof global fields.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_principal_ideal_eq_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.mk_eq_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.equiv_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.mk_canonical_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.mk0_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "card_class_group_eq_one", "description": "The class number of a principal ideal domain is `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "coe_to_principal_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fractional_ideal.mk0", "description": "Send a nonzero integral ideal to an invertible fractional ideal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.induction", "description": " Induction principle for the class group: to show something holds for all `x : class_group R`,\nwe can choose a fraction field `K` and show it holds for the equivalence class of each\n`I : fractional_ideal R\u2070 K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.mk_eq_one_of_coe_ideal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "class_group.comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.continuous_functions.map", "description": " A homomorphism of topological rings can be postcomposed with functions from a source space `X`;\nthis is a ring homomorphism (with respect to the pointwise ring operations on functions).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf_to_Types", "description": "The presheaf of dependently typed functions on `X`, with fibres given by a type family `T`.\nThere is no requirement that the functions are continuous, here.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf_to_Top_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.continuous_functions.pullback", "description": "Pulling back functions into a topological ring along a continuous map is a ring homomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf_to_Type", "description": "The presheaf of functions on `X` with values in a type `T`.\nThere is no requirement that the functions are continuous, here.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf_to_Top", "description": " The presheaf of continuous functions on `X` with values in fixed target topological space\n`T`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf_to_Types_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf_to_TopCommRing", "description": "The presheaf (of commutative rings), consisting of functions on an open set `U \u2286 X` with\nvalues in some topological commutative ring `T`.\n\nFor example, we could construct the presheaf of continuous complex valued functions of `X` as\n```lean\npresheaf_to_TopCommRing X (TopCommRing.of \u2102)\n```\n(this requires `import topology.instances.complex`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf_to_Type_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf_to_Type_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.continuous_functions", "description": " The (bundled) commutative ring of continuous functions from a topological space\nto a topological commutative ring, with pointwise multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.CommRing_yoneda", "description": " An upgraded version of the Yoneda embedding, observing that the continuous maps\nfrom `X : Top` to `R : TopCommRing` form a commutative ring, functorial in both `X` and `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf_to_Types_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.frequently_even", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.frequently_mod_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.frequently_odd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.frequently_modeq", "description": "Infinitely many natural numbers are equal to `d` mod `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.skip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.failed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.repeat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.trace", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.findp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.first", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.dsimp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv_result", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv_result.val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv_result.rhs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv_result.proof", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.change", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.apply_propext_lemmas", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.apply_lemmas_core", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.orelse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.to_tactic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.conversion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.apply_propext_simp_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.apply_lemmas", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.trace_lhs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.match_pattern", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.funext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.find_pattern", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.lhs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.alternative", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.congr_core", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.apply_propext_lemmas_core", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.monad", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.apply_simp_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.whnf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.find", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.top_down", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.bind", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.bottom_up", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.pure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.fail", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.lift_tactic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.mk_match_expr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "old_conv.match_expr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_alt.is_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.separating_left_congr_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.span_singleton_sup_orthogonal_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_alt", "description": "The proposition that a sesquilinear form is alternating", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.separating_left_iff_ker_eq_bot", "description": "A bilinear form is left-separating if and only if it has a trivial kernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_adjoint_pair_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_adjoint_pair", "description": " Given a pair of modules equipped with bilinear forms, this is the condition for a pair of\nmaps between them to be mutually adjoint.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_refl.ortho_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_symm_iff_eq_flip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_pair_self_adjoint", "description": " The condition for an endomorphism to be \"self-adjoint\" with respect to a pair of bilinear forms\non the underlying module. In the case that these two forms are identical, this is the usual concept\nof self adjointness. In the case that one of the forms is the negation of the other, this is the\nusual concept of skew adjointness.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.nondegenerate_restrict_of_disjoint_orthogonal", "description": " The restriction of a reflexive bilinear form `B` onto a submodule `W` is\nnondegenerate if `W` has trivial intersection with its orthogonal complement,\nthat is `disjoint W (W.orthogonal_bilin B)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_skew_adjoint", "description": " An endomorphism of a module is skew-adjoint with respect to a bilinear form if its negation\nserves as an adjoint.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.mem_skew_adjoint_submodule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_adjoint_pair.sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_refl.ker_flip_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.separating_left.ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_adjoint_pair_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_ortho_zero_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_refl.dom_restrict_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_adjoint_pair.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.linear_independent_of_is_Ortho", "description": "A set of orthogonal vectors `v` with respect to some sesquilinear form `B` is linearly\n independent if for all `i`, `B (v i) (v i) \u2260 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_ortho_flip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.mem_is_pair_self_adjoint_submodule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_symm.dom_restrict_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_symm", "description": "The proposition that a sesquilinear form is symmetric", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_pair_self_adjoint_submodule", "description": "The set of pair-self-adjoint endomorphisms are a submodule of the type of all endomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ortho_smul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_Ortho", "description": " A set of vectors `v` is orthogonal with respect to some bilinear form `B` if and only\nif for all `i \u2260 j`, `B (v i) (v j) = 0`. For orthogonality between two elements, use\n`bilin_form.is_ortho`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_adjoint_pair.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_alt.self_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_self_adjoint", "description": " An endomorphism of a module is self-adjoint with respect to a bilinear form if it serves as an\nadjoint for itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.flip_nondegenerate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.skew_adjoint_submodule", "description": " The set of skew-adjoint endomorphisms of a module with bilinear form is a submodule. (In fact\nit is a Lie subalgebra.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_Ortho_flip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.span_singleton_inf_orthogonal_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_refl", "description": "The proposition that a sesquilinear form is reflexive", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.separating_left_iff_linear_nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_Ortho.not_is_ortho_basis_self_of_separating_right", "description": " An orthogonal basis with respect to a right-separating bilinear form has no self-orthogonal\nelements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.orthogonal_bilin_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.separating_right_iff_linear_flip_nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.orthogonal_span_singleton_eq_to_lin_ker", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_symm.ortho_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_adjoint_pair.comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.separating_left.congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_skew_adjoint_iff_neg_self_adjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_refl.flip_is_refl_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mem_orthogonal_bilin_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_adjoint_pair_iff_comp_eq_compl\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.orthogonal_bilin", "description": " The orthogonal complement of a submodule `N` with respect to some bilinear form is the set of\nelements `x` which are orthogonal to all elements of `N`; i.e., for all `y` in `N`, `B x y = 0`.\n\nNote that for general (neither symmetric nor antisymmetric) bilinear forms this definition has a\nchirality; in addition to this \"left\" orthogonal complement one could define a \"right\" orthogonal\ncomplement for which, for all `y` in `N`, `B y x = 0`.  This variant definition is not currently\nprovided in mathlib.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.flip_separating_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_refl.nondegenerate_of_separating_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.separating_right", "description": " A bilinear form is called right-separating if\nthe only element that is right-orthogonal to every other element is `0`; i.e.,\nfor every nonzero `y` in `M\u2082`, there exists `x` in `M\u2081` with `B x y \u2260 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_symm.is_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ortho_smul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.nondegenerate", "description": "A bilinear form is called non-degenerate if it is left-separating and right-separating.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_ortho", "description": "The proposition that two elements of a sesquilinear form space are orthogonal", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_refl.ker_eq_bot_iff_ker_flip_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_compl_span_singleton_orthogonal", "description": "Given a bilinear form `B` and some `x` such that `B x x \u2260 0`, the span of the singleton of `x`\n is complement to its orthogonal complement.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_ortho_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_ortho_zero_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.self_adjoint_submodule", "description": " The set of self-adjoint endomorphisms of a module with bilinear form is a submodule. (In fact\nit is a Jordan subalgebra.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_alt.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_Ortho.separating_left_of_not_is_ortho_basis_self", "description": " Given an orthogonal basis with respect to a bilinear form, the bilinear form is left-separating\nif the basis has no elements which are self-orthogonal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.separating_right_iff_flip_ker_eq_bot", "description": "A bilinear form is right-separating if and only if its flip has a trivial kernel.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_Ortho.separating_right_iff_not_is_ortho_basis_self", "description": " Given an orthogonal basis with respect to a bilinear form, the bilinear form is right-separating\nif the basis has no elements which are self-orthogonal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_adjoint_pair.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_refl.nondegenerate_of_separating_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.separating_left", "description": " A bilinear form is called left-separating if\nthe only element that is left-orthogonal to every other element is `0`; i.e.,\nfor every nonzero `x` in `M\u2081`, there exists `y` in `M\u2082` with `B x y \u2260 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_Ortho_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.mem_self_adjoint_submodule", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.not_separating_left_zero", "description": "In a non-trivial module, zero is not non-degenerate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_alt_iff_eq_neg_flip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.flip_separating_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.le_orthogonal_bilin_orthogonal_bilin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_pair_self_adjoint_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_alt.ortho_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_Ortho.not_is_ortho_basis_self_of_separating_left", "description": " An orthogonal basis with respect to a left-separating bilinear form has no self-orthogonal\nelements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_refl.eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_symm.eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.is_Ortho.nondegenerate_of_not_is_ortho_basis_self", "description": " Given an orthogonal basis with respect to a bilinear form, the bilinear form is nondegenerate\nif the basis has no elements which are self-orthogonal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_cyclic", "description": "A group is called *cyclic* if it is generated by a single element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_cyclic.exists_generator", "description": "A group is called *cyclic* if it is generated by a single element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_cyclic.exists_add_monoid_generator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_simple_add_group.is_add_cyclic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclic.exponent_eq_zero_of_infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclic.of_exponent_eq_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infinite.order_of_eq_zero_of_forall_mem_zpowers", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_cyclic.image_range_order_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclic_of_prime_card", "description": "A finite group of prime order is cyclic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclic.card_order_of_eq_totient", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclic_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_group_of_cycle_center_quotient", "description": "A group is commutative if the quotient by the center is cyclic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_cyclic_of_order_of_eq_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_simple_add_group_of_prime_card", "description": "A finite group of prime order is simple.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_cyclic.card_pow_eq_one_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclic.image_range_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_cyclic.exponent_eq_zero_of_infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclic.iff_exponent_eq_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_cyclic.card_order_of_eq_totient", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bot.is_add_cyclic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.is_cyclic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_cyclic_of_prime_card", "description": "A finite group of prime order is cyclic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclic_of_order_of_eq_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclic.exists_monoid_generator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_order_of_eq_card_of_forall_mem_zmultiples", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_cyclic.exponent_eq_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclic.image_range_order_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_add_hom.map_add_cyclic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_simple_add_group.prime_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_group.is_simple_iff_is_cyclic_and_prime_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_simple_group_of_prime_card", "description": "A finite group of prime order is simple.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid_hom.map_cyclic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commutative_of_add_cyclic_center_quotient", "description": "A group is commutative if the quotient by\n  the center is cyclic. Also see `add_comm_group_of_cycle_center_quotient`\n  for the `add_comm_group` instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclic", "description": "A group is called *cyclic* if it is generated by a single element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclic.exists_generator", "description": "A group is called *cyclic* if it is generated by a single element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commutative_of_cyclic_center_quotient", "description": "A group is commutative if the quotient by the center is cyclic.\n Also see `comm_group_of_cycle_center_quotient` for the `comm_group` instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_cyclic.add_comm_group", "description": "A cyclic group is always commutative. This is not an `instance` because often we have\n  a better proof of `add_comm_group`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_simple_group.prime_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bot.is_cyclic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_cyclic.iff_exponent_eq_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.is_simple_iff_is_add_cyclic_and_prime_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclic.comm_group", "description": " A cyclic group is always commutative. This is not an `instance` because often we have a better\nproof of `comm_group`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclic.exponent_eq_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.is_add_cyclic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_of_eq_card_of_forall_mem_zpowers", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_simple_group.is_cyclic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_cyclic.of_exponent_eq_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_cyclic.image_range_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "card_order_of_eq_totient_aux\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infinite.add_order_of_eq_zero_of_forall_mem_zmultiples", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commutative_of_add_cycle_center_quotient", "description": "A group is commutative if the quotient by\n  the center is cyclic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclic_of_card_pow_eq_one_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_cyclic_of_card_pow_eq_one_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_cyclic.card_pow_eq_one_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_cyclic_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contravariant_mul_lt_of_covariant_mul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_left_cancel_semigroup.contravariant_add_le_of_contravariant_add_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contravariant_swap_add_lt_of_contravariant_add_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covariant_add_lt_of_contravariant_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone.covariant_of_const'", "description": "Dual of `monotone.covariant_of_const'`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covariant.monotone_of_const", "description": "The partial application of a constant to a covariant operator is monotone.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contravariant_lt_of_contravariant_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "antitone.covariant_of_const", "description": "Dual of `monotone.covariant_of_const`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contravariant_flip_mul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_right_cancel_semigroup.contravariant_swap_add_le_of_contravariant_swap_add_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covariant_swap_add_le_of_covariant_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_cancel_semigroup.contravariant_mul_le_of_contravariant_mul_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.covariant_iff_contravariant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covariant_flip_mul_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group.covconv_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_act_of_rel_of_rel_act", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group.covariant_iff_contravariant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covariant_le_of_covariant_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.covconv_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contravariant_flip_add_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contravariant.flip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covariant_le_iff_contravariant_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group.covconv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_cancel_semigroup.contravariant_swap_mul_le_of_contravariant_swap_mul_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "act_rel_act_of_rel_of_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contravariant_swap_mul_lt_of_contravariant_mul_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covariant_flip_add_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.covariant_of_const'", "description": " Same as `monotone.covariant_of_const`, but with the constant on the other side of\nthe operator.  E.g., `\u2200 (m : \u2115), monotone f \u2192 monotone (\u03bb n, f (n + m))`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covariant_class", "description": "  Given an action `\u03bc` of a Type `M` on a Type `N` and a relation `r` on `N`, informally, the\n`covariant_class` says that \"the action `\u03bc` preserves the relation `r`.\"\n\nMore precisely, the `covariant_class` is a class taking two Types `M N`, together with an \"action\"\n`\u03bc : M \u2192 N \u2192 N` and a relation `r : N \u2192 N \u2192 Prop`.  Its unique field `elim` is the assertion that\nfor all `m \u2208 M` and all elements `n\u2081, n\u2082 \u2208 N`, if the relation `r` holds for the pair\n`(n\u2081, n\u2082)`, then, the relation `r` also holds for the pair `(\u03bc m n\u2081, \u03bc m n\u2082)`,\nobtained from `(n\u2081, n\u2082)` by acting upon it by `m`.\n\nIf `m : M` and `h : r n\u2081 n\u2082`, then `covariant_class.elim m h : r (\u03bc m n\u2081) (\u03bc m n\u2082)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covariant_class.elim", "description": "  Given an action `\u03bc` of a Type `M` on a Type `N` and a relation `r` on `N`, informally, the\n`covariant_class` says that \"the action `\u03bc` preserves the relation `r`.\"\n\nMore precisely, the `covariant_class` is a class taking two Types `M N`, together with an \"action\"\n`\u03bc : M \u2192 N \u2192 N` and a relation `r : N \u2192 N \u2192 Prop`.  Its unique field `elim` is the assertion that\nfor all `m \u2208 M` and all elements `n\u2081, n\u2082 \u2208 N`, if the relation `r` holds for the pair\n`(n\u2081, n\u2082)`, then, the relation `r` also holds for the pair `(\u03bc m n\u2081, \u03bc m n\u2082)`,\nobtained from `(n\u2081, n\u2082)` by acting upon it by `m`.\n\nIf `m : M` and `h : r n\u2081 n\u2082`, then `covariant_class.elim m h : r (\u03bc m n\u2081) (\u03bc m n\u2082)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covariant_swap_mul_lt_of_covariant_mul_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "act_rel_of_act_rel_of_rel_act_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covariant", "description": " `covariant` is useful to formulate succintly statements about the interactions between an\naction of a Type on another one and a relation on the acted-upon Type.\n\nSee the `covariant_class` doc-string for its meaning.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covariant.flip", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covariant_mul_lt_of_contravariant_mul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_act_of_act_rel_act_of_rel_act", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contravariant_add_lt_of_covariant_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "group.covariant_swap_iff_contravariant_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covariant_lt_iff_contravariant_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_iff_cov", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.covariant_swap_iff_contravariant_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "left_cancel_semigroup.covariant_mul_lt_of_covariant_mul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monotone.covariant_of_const", "description": " A monotone function remains monotone when composed with the partial application\nof a covariant operator. E.g., `\u2200 (m : \u2115), monotone f \u2192 monotone (\u03bb n, f (m + n))`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contravariant", "description": " `contravariant` is useful to formulate succintly statements about the interactions between an\naction of a Type on another one and a relation on the acted-upon Type.\n\nSee the `contravariant_class` doc-string for its meaning.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covariant_swap_add_lt_of_covariant_add_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_group.covconv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contravariant_class", "description": "  Given an action `\u03bc` of a Type `M` on a Type `N` and a relation `r` on `N`, informally, the\n`contravariant_class` says that \"if the result of the action `\u03bc` on a pair satisfies the\nrelation `r`, then the initial pair satisfied the relation `r`.\"\n\nMore precisely, the `contravariant_class` is a class taking two Types `M N`, together with an\n\"action\" `\u03bc : M \u2192 N \u2192 N` and a relation `r : N \u2192 N \u2192 Prop`.  Its unique field `elim` is the\nassertion that for all `m \u2208 M` and all elements `n\u2081, n\u2082 \u2208 N`, if the relation `r` holds for the\npair `(\u03bc m n\u2081, \u03bc m n\u2082)` obtained from `(n\u2081, n\u2082)` by acting upon it by `m`, then, the relation\n`r` also holds for the pair `(n\u2081, n\u2082)`.\n\nIf `m : M` and `h : r (\u03bc m n\u2081) (\u03bc m n\u2082)`, then `contravariant_class.elim m h : r n\u2081 n\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contravariant_class.elim", "description": "  Given an action `\u03bc` of a Type `M` on a Type `N` and a relation `r` on `N`, informally, the\n`contravariant_class` says that \"if the result of the action `\u03bc` on a pair satisfies the\nrelation `r`, then the initial pair satisfied the relation `r`.\"\n\nMore precisely, the `contravariant_class` is a class taking two Types `M N`, together with an\n\"action\" `\u03bc : M \u2192 N \u2192 N` and a relation `r : N \u2192 N \u2192 Prop`.  Its unique field `elim` is the\nassertion that for all `m \u2208 M` and all elements `n\u2081, n\u2082 \u2208 N`, if the relation `r` holds for the\npair `(\u03bc m n\u2081, \u03bc m n\u2082)` obtained from `(n\u2081, n\u2082)` by acting upon it by `m`, then, the relation\n`r` also holds for the pair `(n\u2081, n\u2082)`.\n\nIf `m : M` and `h : r (\u03bc m n\u2081) (\u03bc m n\u2082)`, then `contravariant_class.elim m h : r n\u2081 n\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "act_rel_of_rel_of_act_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_left_cancel_semigroup.covariant_add_lt_of_covariant_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "right_cancel_semigroup.covariant_swap_mul_lt_of_covariant_swap_mul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "act_rel_act_of_rel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contravariant_swap_mul_le_of_contravariant_mul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rel_of_act_rel_act", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_right_cancel_semigroup.covariant_swap_add_lt_of_covariant_swap_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "contravariant_swap_add_le_of_contravariant_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "covariant_swap_mul_le_of_covariant_mul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.card_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.relindex_inf_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.index_comap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.index_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.dvd_index_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.sq_mem_of_index_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.finite_index_of_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.relindex_dvd_index_of_normal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.relindex_top_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.index_map_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.index_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.index_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.finite_index_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.relindex_dvd_of_le_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.relindex_top_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.relindex_bot_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.finite_index_of_finite_quotient", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.index_eq_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.index_ne_zero_of_finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.index_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.relindex_dvd_index_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.relindex_bot_left_eq_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.index_eq_two_iff", "description": "/-- An additive subgroup has index two if and only if there exists `a` such that for\nall `b`, exactly one of `b + a` and `b` belong to `H`. -/", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.relindex_le_of_le_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.relindex_bot_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.relindex_dvd_index_of_normal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.relindex_dvd_index_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.index_bot_eq_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.two_smul_mem_of_index_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.finite_quotient_of_finite_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.relindex_add_subgroup_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.inf_relindex_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.relindex_eq_zero_of_le_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.has_top.top.finite_index", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.one_lt_index_of_ne_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.index_infi_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.finite_index", "description": "Typeclass for finite index subgroups.", "p": "ma