s contained in the submonoid\nof unitary elements.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zsqrtd.distrib", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zsqrtd.norm_eq_mul_conj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zsqrtd.of_int_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zsqrtd.ordered_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zsqrtd.has_mul", "description": "Multiplication in `\u2124\u221ad`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zsqrtd.has_star", "description": "Conjugation in `\u2124\u221ad`. The conjugate of `a + b \u221ad` is `a - b \u221ad`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zsqrtd.add_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zsqrtd.coe_int_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zsqrtd.coe_int_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zsqrtd.decidable_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zsqrtd.lift", "description": " The unique `ring_hom` from `\u2124\u221ad` to a ring `R`, constructed by replacing `\u221ad` with the provided\nroot. Conversely, this associates to every mapping `\u2124\u221ad \u2192+* R` a value of `\u221ad` in `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zsqrtd.norm", "description": "The norm of an element of `\u2124[\u221ad]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zsqrtd.d_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zsqrtd.nonneg_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zsqrtd.norm_eq_of_associated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zsqrtd.sq_le_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zsqrtd.smul_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zsqrtd.is_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_convergent.comp_rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_comp_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_convergent_zero_of_is_O", "description": " If `f` is a locally integrable real-valued function which is `O(x ^ (-b))` at `0`, then for any\n`b < s`, its Mellin transform converges on some right neighbourhood of `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_convergent.comp_mul_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_O_rpow_zero_log_smul", "description": "If `f` is `O(x ^ (-a))` as `x \u2192 0`, then `log \u2022 f` is `O(x ^ (-b))` for every `a < b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_comp_rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_convergent.const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_comp_mul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_convergent", "description": "Predicate on `f` and `s` asserting that the Mellin integral is well-defined.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_differentiable_at_of_is_O_rpow", "description": " Suppose `f` is locally integrable on `(0, \u221e)`, is `O(x ^ (-a))` as `x \u2192 \u221e`, and is\n`O(x ^ (-b))` as `x \u2192 0`. Then its Mellin transform is differentiable on the domain `b < re s < a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_O_rpow_top_log_smul", "description": "If `f` is `O(x ^ (-a))` as `x \u2192 +\u221e`, then `log \u2022 f` is `O(x ^ (-b))` for every `b < a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_mellin", "description": " Predicate standing for \"the Mellin transform of `f` is defined at `s` and equal to `m`\". This\nshortens some arguments.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_div_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_convergent_of_is_O_scalar", "description": " If `f` is a locally integrable real-valued function on `Ioi 0` which is `O(x ^ (-a))` at `\u221e`\nand `O(x ^ (-b))` at `0`, then its Mellin transform integral converges for `b < s < a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_convergent_of_is_O_rpow_exp", "description": " If `f` is locally integrable, decays exponentially at infinity, and is `O(x ^ (-b))` at 0, then\nits Mellin transform converges for `b < s.re`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_mellin_cpow_Ioc", "description": "The Mellin transform of a power function restricted to `Ioc 0 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_cpow_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_differentiable_at_of_is_O_rpow_exp", "description": " If `f` is locally integrable, decays exponentially at infinity, and is `O(x ^ (-b))` at 0, then\nits Mellin transform is holomorphic on `b < s.re`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin", "description": " The Mellin transform of a function `f` (for a complex exponent `s`), defined as the integral of\n`t ^ (s - 1) \u2022 f` over `Ioi 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_mellin_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.cpow_mul_of_real_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_convergent.div_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_has_deriv_of_is_O_rpow", "description": " Suppose `f` is locally integrable on `(0, \u221e)`, is `O(x ^ (-a))` as `x \u2192 \u221e`, and is\n`O(x ^ (-b))` as `x \u2192 0`. Then its Mellin transform is differentiable on the domain `b < re s < a`,\nwith derivative equal to the Mellin transform of `log \u2022 f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_mellin_one_Ioc", "description": "The Mellin transform of the indicator function of `Ioc 0 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_convergent_top_of_is_O", "description": " If `f` is a locally integrable real-valued function which is `O(x ^ (-a))` at `\u221e`, then for any\n`s < a`, its Mellin transform converges on some neighbourhood of `+\u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_comp_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_mellin_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_convergent_iff_norm", "description": " Auxiliary lemma to reduce convergence statements from vector-valued functions to real\nscalar-valued functions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_convergent.cpow_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mellin_convergent_of_is_O_rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.pairwise_disjoint.bUnion_finset", "descri