"", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.dist_le_two_norm", "description": "Distance between the images of any two points is at most twice the norm of the function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.apply_le_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.norm_le_of_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.uniform_continuity", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.isometry_equiv_bounded_of_compact", "description": "When `\u03b1` is compact, and `\u03b2` is a metric space, the bounded continuous maps `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d47 \u03b2` are\nisometric to `C(\u03b1, \u03b2)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.summable_of_locally_summable_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.norm_lt_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.add_equiv_bounded_of_compact", "description": "When `\u03b1` is compact, the bounded continuous maps `\u03b1 \u2192\u1d47 \ud835\udd5c` are\nadditively equivalent to `C(\u03b1, \ud835\udd5c)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bounded_continuous_function.dist_mk_of_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.has_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.eval_clm", "description": "The evaluation at a point, as a continuous linear map from `C(\u03b1, \ud835\udd5c)` to `\ud835\udd5c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.continuous_eval_const", "description": "See also `continuous_map.continuous_eval_const`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.dist_lt_iff_of_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.normed_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.norm_le", "description": "The norm of a function is controlled by the supremum of the pointwise norms", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_map.linear_isometry_bounded_of_compact", "description": "When `\u03b1` is compact and `\ud835\udd5c` is 