{"name": "asymptotics.is_Theta.eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.is_Theta.is_bounded_under_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.is_Theta.trans_is_O", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.is_Theta.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.is_Theta_norm_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.is_O.trans_is_Theta", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.is_Theta_const_smul_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.is_Theta.is_O_congr_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.is_Theta", "description": " We say that `f` is `\u0398(g)` along a filter `l` (notation: `f =\u0398[l] g`) if `f =O[l] g` and\n`g =O[l] f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.is_Theta.of_const_mul_left", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `asymptotics.is_Theta_const_mul_left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.is_Theta.trans_eventually_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.is_Theta.tendsto_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.is_Theta.symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.is_Theta.of_const_smul_right", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `asymptotics.is_Theta_const_smul_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Sheaf.adjunction_to_types", "description": " A variant of the adjunction between sheaf categories, in the case where the right adjoint\nis the forgetful functor to sheaves of types.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Sheaf.compose_and_sheafify_from_types", "description": "This is the functor sending a sheaf of types `X` to the sheafification of `X \u22d9 G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Sheaf.adjunction_to_types_counit_app_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Sheaf.compose_and_sheafify", "description": " This is the functor sending a sheaf `X : Sheaf J E` to the sheafification\nof `X \u22d9 G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Sheaf.adjunction_counit_app_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Sheaf.category_theory.Sheaf_forget.category_theory.is_right_adjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Sheaf.adjunction", "description": " An adjunction `adj : G \u22a3 F` with `F : D \u2964 E` and `G : E \u2964 D` induces an adjunction\nbetween `Sheaf J D` and `Sheaf J E`, in contexts where one can sheafify `D`-valued presheaves,\nand `F` preserves the correct limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Sheaf.category_theory.Sheaf_compose.category_theory.is_right_adjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Sheaf.adjunction_to_types_unit_app_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Sheaf.compose_equiv_symm_apply_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Sheaf.adjunction_unit_app_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Sheaf_forget", "description": " The forgetful functor from `Sheaf J D` to sheaves of types, for a concrete category `D`\nwhose forgetful functor preserves the correct limits.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Sheaf.compose_equiv", "description": "An auxiliary definition to be used in defining `category_theory.Sheaf.adjunction` below.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.Sheaf.compose_equiv_apply_val", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.skolem\u2081_Structure", "description": " The structure assigning each function symbol of `L.skolem\u2081` to a skolem function generated with\nchoice.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.skolem\u2081_reduct_is_elementary", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.card_functions_sum_skolem\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.elementary_skolem\u2081_reduct", "description": "Any `L.sum L.skolem\u2081`-substructure is an elementary `L`-substructure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.skolem\u2081_functions", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.skolem\u2081", "description": " A language consisting of Skolem functions for another language.\nCalled `skolem\u2081` because it is the first step in building a Skolemization of a language.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.elementary_skolem\u2081_reduct.small", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.skolem\u2081_relations", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.card_functions_sum_skolem\u2081_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.exists_elementary_substructure_card_eq", "description": "The Downward L\u00f6wenheim\u2013Skolem theorem :\n If `s` is a set in an `L`-structure `M` and `\u03ba` an infinite cardinal such that\n `max (# s, L.card) \u2264 \u03ba` and `\u03ba \u2264 # M`, then `M` has an elementary substructure containing `s` of\n cardinality `\u03ba`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.substructure.coe_sort_elementary_skolem\u2081_reduct", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.exists_small_elementary_substructure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixed_points_submonoid_supr", "description": "Fixed points of supr of submonoids is intersection", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixing_submonoid_union", "description": "Fixing submonoid of union is intersection", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixing_add_submonoid", "description": "The additive submonoid fixing a set under an `add_action`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixed_points_subgroup_sup", "description": "Fixed points of sup of subgroups is intersection", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_fixing_submonoid_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixing_subgroup", "description": "The subgroup fixing a set under a `mul_action`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixing_submonoid_antitone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixing_submonoid_Union", "description": "Fixing submonoid of Union is intersection", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixing_add_subgroup", "description": "The additive subgroup fixing a set under an `add_action`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixing_subgroup_antitone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixing_submonoid_fixed_points_gc", "description": "The Galois connection between fixing submonoids and fixed points of a monoid action", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_fixing_subgroup_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixing_subgroup_union", "description": "Fixing subgroup of union is intersection", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixed_points_antitone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixing_subgroup_Union", "description": "Fixing subgroup of Union is intersection", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixing_submonoid", "description": "The submonoid fixing a set under a `mul_action`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixing_subgroup_fixed_points_gc", "description": "The Galois connection between fixing subgroups and fixed points of a group action", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixed_points_submonoid_sup", "description": "Fixed points of sup of submonoids is intersection", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixed_points_subgroup_antitone", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixed_points_subgroup_supr", "description": "Fixed points of supr of subgroups is intersection", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.pullback_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.category_theory.limits.has_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.pushout", "description": " When `C` has pushouts, a morphism `f : X \u27f6 Y` induces a functor `under X \u2964 under Y`,\nby pushing a morphism forward along `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.creates_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.map_pullback_adj", "description": "`over.map f` is left adjoint to `over.pullback f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.has_limit_of_has_limit_comp_forget", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.category_theory.limits.has_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.category_theory.limits.has_colimits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.pullback_is_right_adjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.pullback_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.category_theory.limits.has_limits_of_shape", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.pushout_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.epi_left_of_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.pullback_id", "description": "pullback (\ud835\udfd9 A) : over A \u2964 over A is the identity functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.pullback_comp", "description": "pullback commutes with composition (up to natural isomorphism).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.mono_right_of_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.mono_iff_mono_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.epi_iff_epi_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.has_colimit_of_has_colimit_comp_forget", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.under.pushout_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.pullback", "description": " When `C` has pullbacks, a morphism `f : X \u27f6 Y` induces a functor `over Y \u2964 over X`,\nby pulling back a morphism along `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.creates_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra", "description": "The exterior algebra of an `R`-module `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.\u03b9_add_mul_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.\u03b9_inv", "description": " The left-inverse of `\u03b9`.\n\nAs an implementation detail, we implement this using `triv_sq_zero_ext` which has a suitable\nalgebra structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.invertible_algebra_map_equiv_symm_apply_inv_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.is_unit_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.algebra_map_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.to_exterior_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.\u03b9", "description": "The canonical linear map `M \u2192\u2097[R] exterior_algebra R M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.to_triv_sq_zero_ext", "description": " The canonical map from `exterior_algebra R M` into `triv_sq_zero_ext R M` that sends\n`exterior_algebra.\u03b9` to `triv_sq_zero_ext.inr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.induction", "description": " If `C` holds for the `algebra_map` of `r : R` into `exterior_algebra R M`, the `\u03b9` of `x : M`,\nand is preserved under addition and muliplication, then it holds for all of `exterior_algebra R M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.lift_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.comp_\u03b9_sq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.lift", "description": "Given a linear map `f : M \u2192\u2097[R] A` into an `R`-algebra `A`, which satisfies the condition:\n`cond : \u2200 m : M, f m * f m = 0`, this is the canonical lift of `f` to a morphism of `R`-algebras\nfrom `exterior_algebra R M` to `A`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.\u03b9_multi_succ_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.to_triv_sq_zero_ext_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.\u03b9_left_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.lift_comp_\u03b9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.\u03b9_eq_algebra_map_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tensor_algebra.to_exterior", "description": " The canonical image of the `tensor_algebra` in the `exterior_algebra`, which maps\n`tensor_algebra.\u03b9 R x` to `exterior_algebra.\u03b9 R x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.\u03b9_sq_zero", "description": "As well as being linear, `\u03b9 m` squares to zero", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.\u03b9_multi_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.\u03b9_range_disjoint_one", "description": "The generators of the exterior algebra are disjoint from its scalars.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.\u03b9_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.\u03b9_comp_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.\u03b9_multi_succ_curry_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.\u03b9_mul_prod_list", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.algebra_map_left_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.\u03b9_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.lift_\u03b9_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.invertible_algebra_map_equiv_apply_inv_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.\u03b9_multi_zero_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.lift_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.algebra_map_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.\u03b9_ne_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.invertible_algebra_map_equiv", "description": "Invertibility in the exterior algebra is the same as invertibility of the base ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.\u03b9_multi", "description": " The product of `n` terms of the form `\u03b9 R m` is an alternating map.\n\nThis is a special case of `multilinear_map.mk_pi_algebra_fin`, and the exterior algebra version of\n`tensor_algebra.tprod`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.algebra_map_eq_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.algebra_map_inv", "description": "The left-inverse of `algebra_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exterior_algebra.hom_ext", "description": "See note [partially-applied ext lemmas].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.nonempty_of_probability_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.measure_theory.measure.has_coe", "description": "A probability measure can be interpreted as a measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.finite_measure.normalize_test_against_nn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.to_finite_measure_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.to_finite_measure_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure", "description": " Probability measures are defined as the subtype of measures that have the property of being\nprobability measures (i.e., their total mass is one).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.coe_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.tendsto_iff_forall_lintegral_tendsto", "description": " A characterization of weak convergence of probability measures by the condition that the\nintegrals of every continuous bounded nonnegative function converge to the integral of the function\nagainst the limit measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.eq_of_forall_measure_apply_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.to_weak_dual_bcnn_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.tendsto_nhds_iff_to_finite_measures_tendsto_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.coe_to_weak_dual_bcnn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.mass_to_finite_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.to_finite_measure_nonzero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.to_weak_dual_bcnn", "description": " Probability measures yield elements of the `weak_dual` of bounded continuous nonnegative\nfunctions via `measure_theory.finite_measure.test_against_nn`, i.e., integration.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.finite_measure.normalize_eq_of_nonzero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.apply_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.finite_measure.normalize", "description": " Normalize a finite measure so that it becomes a probability measure, i.e., divide by the\ntotal mass.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.eq_of_forall_apply_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.coe_fn_comp_to_finite_measure_eq_coe_fn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.finite_measure.self_eq_mass_mul_normalize", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.finite_measure.self_eq_mass_smul_normalize", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.finite_measure.tendsto_normalize_iff_tendsto", "description": " The weak convergence of finite measures to a nonzero limit can be characterized by the weak\nconvergence of both their normalized versions (probability measures) and their total masses.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.finite_measure.average_eq_integral_normalize", "description": " Averaging with respect to a finite measure is the same as integraing against\n`measure_theory.finite_measure.normalize`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.tendsto_iff_forall_integral_tendsto", "description": " The characterization of weak convergence of probability measures by the usual (defining)\ncondition that the integrals of every continuous bounded function converge to the integral of the\nfunction against the limit measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.to_finite_measure", "description": "A probability measure can be interpreted as a finite measure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.to_weak_dual_bcnn_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.test_against_nn_lipschitz", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.finite_measure.tendsto_test_against_nn_of_tendsto_normalize_test_against_nn_of_tendsto_mass", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.coe_comp_to_finite_measure_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.finite_measure.tendsto_of_tendsto_normalize_test_against_nn_of_tendsto_mass", "description": " If the normalized versions of finite measures converge weakly and their total masses\nalso converge, then the finite measures themselves converge weakly.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.finite_measure.tendsto_normalize_of_tendsto", "description": " If finite measures themselves converge weakly to a nonzero limit measure, then their\nnormalized versions also converge weakly.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.coe_fn_univ_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.topological_space", "description": " The topology of weak convergence on `measure_theory.probability_measure \u03a9`. This is inherited\n(induced) from the topology of weak convergence of finite measures via the inclusion\n`measure_theory.probability_measure.to_finite_measure`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.finite_measure.tendsto_normalize_test_against_nn_of_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.continuous_test_against_nn_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.measure_theory.is_probability_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.finite_measure.test_against_nn_eq_mass_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.val_eq_to_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.coe_fn_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.coe_fn_eq_to_nnreal_coe_fn_to_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.finite_measure.coe_normalize_eq_of_nonzero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.probability_measure.ennreal_coe_fn_eq_coe_fn_to_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.finite_measure.normalize_eq_inv_mass_smul_of_nonzero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_measure.to_finite_measure_normalize_eq_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.ord_connected_component", "description": " Order-connected component of a point `x` in a set `s`. It is defined as the set of `y` such that\n`set.uIcc x y \u2286 s`. Note that it is empty if and only if `x \u2209 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.mem_ord_connected_component_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.ord_connected_component_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.dual_ord_connected_component", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.self_mem_ord_connected_component", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.ord_separating_set", "description": " Given two sets `s t : set \u03b1`, the set `set.order_separating_set s t` is the set of points that\nbelong both to some `set.ord_connected_component t\u1d9c x`, `x \u2208 s`, and to some\n`set.ord_connected_component s\u1d9c x`, `x \u2208 t`. In the case of two disjoint closed sets, this is the\nunion of all open intervals $(a, b)$ such that their endpoints belong to different sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.ord_connected_proj_mem_ord_connected_component", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.ord_connected_component_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.ord_connected_proj", "description": " Projection from `s : set \u03b1` to `\u03b1` sending each order connected component of `s` to a single\npoint of this component.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.ord_connected_component_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.disjoint_left_ord_separating_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.mem_ord_connected_component_ord_connected_proj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.ord_separating_set_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.eq_of_mem_ord_connected_section_of_uIcc_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.mem_ord_connected_component_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.ord_connected_section", "description": " A set that intersects each order connected component of a set by a single point. Defined as the\nrange of `set.ord_connected_proj s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.ord_connected_section_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {