, "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite.smul_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite.add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite.of_vadd_set", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `set.finite_smul_set`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite.smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.infinite.of_smul_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite.vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite.of_smul_set", "description": "**Alias** of the forward direction of `set.finite_smul_set`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.infinite_smul_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.infinite.of_vadd_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite.neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite_smul_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.finite_vadd_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.is_sqrt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.prove_sqrt", "description": "Given `n` provides `(a, \u22a2 nat.sqrt n = a)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_num.eval_sqrt", "description": "A `norm_num` plugin for `sqrt n` when `n` is a numeral.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.neg_cancel_leads", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_cancel_leads_lt_of_nat_degree_le_nat_degree", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.cancel_leads", "description": "`cancel_leads p q` is formed by multiplying `p` and `q` by monomials so that they\n have the same leading term, and then subtracting.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_cancel_leads_lt_of_nat_degree_le_nat_degree_of_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.dvd_cancel_leads_of_dvd_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.inclusion_in_double_dual_norm_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.norm_le_dual_bound", "description": "If one controls the norm of every `f x`, then one controls the norm of `x`.\n   Compare `continuous_linear_map.op_norm_le_bound`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.mem_polar_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.polar_ball_subset_closed_ball_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.polar_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.smul_mem_polar", "description": " If `x'` is a dual element such that the norms `\u2016x' z\u2016` are bounded for `z \u2208 s`, then a\nsmall scalar multiple of `x'` is in `polar \ud835\udd5c s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.dual_pairing_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.eq_zero_iff_forall_dual_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.dual.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.dual", "description": "The topological dual of a seminormed space `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.bounded_polar_of_mem_nhds_zero", "description": " Given a neighborhood `s` of the origin in a normed space `E`, the dual norms\nof all elements of the polar `polar \ud835\udd5c s` are bounded by a constant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.eq_iff_forall_dual_eq", "description": "See also `geometric_hahn_banach_point_point`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.dual_pairing_separating_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.dual_pairing", "description": "The dual pairing as a bilinear form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.dual.normed_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.continuous_linear_map_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.polar_closed_ball", "description": " The `polar` of closed ball in a normed space `E` is the closed ball of the dual with\ninverse radius.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.dual_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.eq_zero_of_forall_dual_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.polar", "description": " Given a subset `s` in a normed space `E` (over a field `\ud835\udd5c`), the polar\n`polar \ud835\udd5c s` is the subset of `dual \ud835\udd5c E` consisting of those functionals which\nevaluate to something of norm at most one at all points `z \u2208 s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.dual.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.polar_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.dual.finite_dimensional", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.inclusion_in_double_dual_li", "description": "The inclusion of a normed space in its double dual is an isometry onto its image.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.inclusion_in_double_dual_norm_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.double_dual_bound", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.dual.seminormed_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.is_closed_polar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.dual.normed_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.inclusion_in_double_dual", "description": "The inclusion of a normed space in its double (topological) dual, considered\n  as a bounded linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "normed_space.closed_ball_inv_subset_polar_closed_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ordered_ring.to_ordered_add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conjugate_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ordered_ring.to_ordered_add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conjugate_nonneg'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ordered_ring.to_has_exists_add_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ordered_ring.of_nonneg_iff'", "description": " When `R` is a non-unital ring, to construct a `star_ordered_ring` instance it suffices to\nshow that the nonnegative elements are precisely those elements of the form `star s * s`\nfor `s : R`.\n\nThis is provided for convenience because it holds in many common scenarios (e.g.,`\u211d`, `\u2102`, or\nany C\u22c6-algebra), and obviates the hassle of `add_submonoid.closure_induction` when creating those\ninstances.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_mul_self_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ordered_ring.nonneg_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conjugate_le_conjugate'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ordered_ring.of_nonneg_iff", "description": " When `R` is a non-unital ring, to construct a `star_ordered_ring` instance it suffices to\nshow that the nonnegative elements are precisely those elements in the `add_submonoid` generated\nby `star s * s` for `s : R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ordered_ring.of_le_iff", "description": " To construct a `star_ordered_ring` instance it suffices to show that `x \u2264 y` if and only if\n`y = x + star s * s` for some `s : R`.\n\nThis is provided for convenience because it holds in some common scenarios (e.g.,`\u211d\u22650`, `C(X, \u211d\u22650)`)\nand obviates the hassle of `add_submonoid.closure_induction` when creating those instances.\n\nIf you are working with a `non_unital_ring` and not a `non_unital_semiring`, see\n`star_ordered_ring.of_nonneg_iff` for a more convenient version.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ordered_ring", "description": "An ordered `*`-ring is a ring which is both an `ordered_add_comm_group` and a `*`-ring,\nand the nonnegative elements constitute precisely the `add_submonoid` generated by\nelements of the form `star s * s`.\n\nIf you are working with a `non_unital_ring` and not a `non_unital_semiring`, it may be more\nconvenient do declare instances using `star_ordered_ring.of_nonneg_iff'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ordered_ring.to_star_ring", "description": "An ordered `*`-ring is a ring which is both an `ordered_add_comm_group` and a `*`-ring,\nand the nonnegative elements constitute precisely the `add_submonoid` generated by\nelements of the form `star s * s`.\n\nIf you are working with a `non_unital_ring` and not a `non_unital_semiring`, it may be more\nconvenient do declare instances using `star_ordered_ring.of_nonneg_iff'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ordered_ring.add_le_add_left", "description": "An ordered `*`-ring is a ring which is both an `ordered_add_comm_group` and a `*`-ring,\nand the nonnegative elements constitute precisely the `add_submonoid` generated by\nelements of the form `star s * s`.\n\nIf you are working with a `non_unital_ring` and not a `non_unital_semiring`, it may be more\nconvenient do declare instances using `star_ordered_ring.of_nonneg_iff'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_ordered_ring.le_iff", "description": "An ordered `*`-ring is a ring which is both an `ordered_add_comm_group` and a `*`-ring,\nand the nonnegative elements constitute precisely the `add_submonoid` generated by\nelements of the form `star s * s`.\n\nIf you are working with a `non_unital_ring` and not a `non_unital_semiring`, it may be more\nconvenient do declare instances using `star_ordered_ring.of_nonneg_iff'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conjugate_le_conjugate", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_mul_self_nonneg'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.apply_cfg.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc_entry.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "interactive.loc.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pos.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smt_pre_config.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "reducibility_hints.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "environment.projection_info.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rbmap.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.unfold_proj_config.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bin_tree.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vm_decl_kind.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rsimp.config.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ulift.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.simp_config.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.transparency.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.rewrite_cfg.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.new_goals.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rbnode.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unsigned.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "format.color.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.delta_config.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subsingleton_info.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rbnode.color.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.dsimp_config.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "smt_config.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "congr_arg_kind.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unification_constraint.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unification_hint.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pprod.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_info.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.dunfold_config.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cc_config.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "string.iterator.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "doc_category.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ematch_config.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.inhabited_instance", "description": "Tries to derive an `inhabited` instance for inductives and structures.\n\nFor example:\n```lean\n@[derive inhabited]\nstructure foo :=\n(a : \u2115 := 42)\n(b : list \u2115)\n```\nHere, `@[derive inhabited]` adds the instance `foo.inhabited`, which is defined as\n`\u27e8\u27e842, default\u27e9\u27e9`.  For inductives, the default value is the first constructor.\n\nIf the structure/inductive has a type parameter `\u03b1`, then the generated instance will have an\nargument `inhabited \u03b1`, even if it is not used.  (This is due to the implementation using\n`instance_derive_handler`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rbtree.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "param_info.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "plift.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "string_imp.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ordering.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.unfold_config.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.simp_intros_config.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "string.iterator_imp.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "vm_obj_kind.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_id_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_comp_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.inclusion_top_iso", "description": "The inclusion of the top open subset (i.e. the whole space) is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_id_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.functor_obj_map_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_comp_obj_unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map.functor_obj_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.bot_le", "description": "The inclusion `\u22a5 \u27f6 U` as a morphism in the category of open sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_comp_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_iso_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.to_Top_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map.adjunction", "description": "An open map `f : X \u27f6 Y` induces an adjunction between `opens X` and `opens Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_id_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.op_map_comp_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_iso_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.functor_map_eq_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.inf_le_left", "description": "The inclusion `U \u2293 V \u27f6 U` as a morphism in the category of open sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.inclusion_top_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_id", "description": "The functor `opens X \u2964 opens X` given by taking preimages under the identity function\nis naturally isomorphic to the identity functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.adjunction_counit_map_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_map_iso_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.le_map_top", "description": "The inclusion `U \u27f6 (map f).obj \u22a4` as a morphism in the category of open sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.inf_le_left_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.opens_hom_has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.open_embedding_obj_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map.functor_full_of_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map.functor_faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.inf_le_right", "description": "The inclusion `U \u2293 V \u27f6 V` as a morphism in the category of open sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.inf_le_left_apply_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map.functor_map_down_down", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.le_supr", "description": "The inclusion `U i \u27f6 supr U` as a morphism in the category of open sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_comp_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_map_iso_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.open_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_iso_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_map_iso_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.le_supr_apply_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_open_map.functor", "description": "An open map `f : X \u27f6 Y` induces a functor `opens X \u2964 opens Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_comp_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_functor_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_id_obj'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_id_obj_unop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.inclusion", "description": "The inclusion map from an open subset to the whole space, as a morphism in `Top`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_supr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_comp_obj'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.inclusion_map_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_id_hom_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.adjunction_counit_app_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.op_map_id_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.inclusion_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.le_top", "description": "The inclusion `U \u27f6 \u22a4` as a morphism in the category of open sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.to_Top", "description": "The functor from open sets in `X` to `Top`,\nrealising each open set as a topological space itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_comp_inv_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map", "description": "`opens.map f` gives the functor from open sets in Y to open set in X,\n   given by taking preimages under f.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_functor_eq'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_map_iso_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_iso", "description": "If two continuous maps `f g : X \u27f6 Y` are equal,\nthen the functors `opens Y \u2964 opens X` they induce are isomorphic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_map_iso", "description": " A homeomorphism of spaces gives an equivalence of categories of open sets.\n\nTODO: define `order_iso.equivalence`, use it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "topological_space.opens.map_comp", "description": "The natural isomorphism between taking preimages under `f \u226b g`, and the composite\nof taking preimages under `g`, then preimages under `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.coord_change_homeomorph_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.preimage_subset_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.coe_mem_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.preimage_homeomorph_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pretrivialization.coe_fst'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.symm", "description": " A fiberwise inverse to `e'`. The function `F \u2192 E x` that induces a local inverse\n`B \u00d7 F \u2192 total_space F E` of `e'` on `e'.base_set`. It is defined to be `0` outside\n`e'.base_set`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.is_image_preimage_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.coord_change_same", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pretrivialization.symm_apply_mk_proj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pretrivialization.symm_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.disjoint_union", "description": " Given two bundle trivializations `e`, `e'` over disjoint sets, `e.disjoint_union e' H` is the\nbundle trivialization over the union of the base sets that agrees with `e` and `e'` over their\nbase sets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.coe_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pretrivialization.preimage_symm_proj_base_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.image_preimage_eq_prod_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.preimage_singleton_homeomorph", "description": "Each fiber of a trivialization is homeomorphic to the specified fiber.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.continuous_at_of_comp_right", "description": " Read off the continuity of a function `f : Z \u2192 X` at `z : Z` by transferring via a\ntrivialization of `Z` containing `z`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.map_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.frontier_preimage", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pretrivialization.trans_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pretrivialization.preimage_symm_proj_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.piecewise", "description": " Given two bundle trivializations `e`, `e'` of `proj : Z \u2192 B` and a set `s : set B` such that\nthe base sets of `e` and `e'` intersect `frontier s` on the same set and `e p = e' p` whenever\n`proj p \u2208 e.base_set \u2229 frontier s`, `e.piecewise e' s Hs Heq` is the bundle trivialization over\n`set.ite s e.base_set e'.base_set` that is equal to `e` on `proj \u207b\u00b9 s` and is equal to `e'`\notherwise.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.mk_coord_change", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.coord_change", "description": " Coordinate transformation in the fiber induced by a pair of bundle trivializations. See also\n`trivialization.coord_change_homeomorph` for a version bundled as `F \u2243\u209c F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.apply_mk_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pretrivialization.set_symm", "description": "Composition of inverse and coercion from the subtype of the target.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.coord_change_apply_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.trans_fiber_homeomorph", "description": " If `e` is a `trivialization` of `proj : Z \u2192 B` with fiber `F` and `h` is a homeomorphism\n`F \u2243\u209c F'`, then `e.trans_fiber_homeomorph h` is the trivialization of `proj` with the fiber `F'`\nthat sends `p : Z` to `((e p).1, h (e p).2)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.source_inter_preimage_target_inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pretrivialization.mem_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.coord_change_same_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pretrivialization.apply_symm_apply'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pretrivialization.symm_trans_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.mk_mem_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.mk_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.trans_fiber_homeomorph_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pretrivialization.proj_surj_on_base_set", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.coe_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.symm_trans_source_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.symm_apply_mk_proj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pretrivialization.symm_trans_source_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pretrivialization.eq_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization", "description": "A structure extending local homeomorphisms, defining a local trivialization of a projection\n`proj : Z \u2192 B` with fiber `F`, as a local homeomorphism between `Z` and `B \u00d7 F` defined between two\nsets of the form `proj \u207b\u00b9' base_set` and `base_set \u00d7 F`, acting trivially on the first coordinate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.to_local_homeomorph", "description": "A structure extending local homeomorphisms, defining a local trivialization of a projection\n`proj : Z \u2192 B` with fiber `F`, as a local homeomorphism between `Z` and `B \u00d7 F` defined between two\nsets of the form `proj \u207b\u00b9' base_set` and `base_set \u00d7 F`, acting trivially on the first coordinate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.base_set", "description": "A structure extending local homeomorphisms, defining a local trivialization of a projection\n`proj : Z \u2192 B` with fiber `F`, as a local homeomorphism between `Z` and `B \u00d7 F` defined between two\nsets of the form `proj \u207b\u00b9' base_set` and `base_set \u00d7 F`, acting trivially on the first coordinate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.open_base_set", "description": "A structure extending local homeomorphisms, defining a local trivialization of a projection\n`proj : Z \u2192 B` with fiber `F`, as a local homeomorphism between `Z` and `B \u00d7 F` defined between two\nsets of the form `proj \u207b\u00b9' base_set` and `base_set \u00d7 F`, acting trivially on the first coordinate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.source_eq", "description": "A structure extending local homeomorphisms, defining a local trivialization of a projection\n`proj : Z \u2192 B` with fiber `F`, as a local homeomorphism between `Z` and `B \u00d7 F` defined between two\nsets of the form `proj \u207b\u00b9' base_set` and `base_set \u00d7 F`, acting trivially on the first coordinate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.target_eq", "description": "A structure extending local homeomorphisms, defining a local trivialization of a projection\n`proj : Z \u2192 B` with fiber `F`, as a local homeomorphism between `Z` and `B \u00d7 F` defined between two\nsets of the form `proj \u207b\u00b9' base_set` and `base_set \u00d7 F`, acting trivially on the first coordinate.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.proj_to_fun", "description": "A structure extending local homeomorphisms, defining a local trivialization of a projection\n`proj : Z \u2192 B` with fiber `F`, as a local homeomorphism between `Z` and `B \u00d7 F` defined between two\nsets of the form