ired by [Neukirch], proposition 6.1", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_norm_localization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_norm_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.abs_norm_dvd_abs_norm_of_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_norm_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.nat_abs_det_basis_change", "description": " Let `b` be a basis for `S` over `\u2124` and `bI` a basis for `I` over `\u2124` of the same dimension.\nThen an alternative way to compute the norm of `I` is given by taking the determinant of `bI`\nover `b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_norm_mul_of_field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.finite_set_of_abs_norm_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_norm_eq_bot_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_norm", "description": " `ideal.span_norm R (I : ideal S)` is the ideal generated by mapping `algebra.norm R` over `I`.\n\nSee also `ideal.rel_norm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.abs_norm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.mem_prime_of_mul_mem_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.norm_mem_span_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.rel_norm_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.abs_norm_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.abs_norm_span_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.card_quot", "description": " The cardinality of `(M \u29f8 S)`, if `(M \u29f8 S)` is finite, and `0` otherwise.\nThis is used to define the absolute ideal norm `ideal.abs_norm`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.abs_norm_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.card_quot_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.abs_norm", "description": "The absolute norm of the ideal `I : ideal R` is the cardinality of the quotient `R \u29f8 I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.prime_of_irreducible_abs_norm_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "card_quot_mul", "description": "Multiplicativity of the ideal norm in number rings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.card_quot_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "card_quot_pow_of_prime", "description": "Multiplicity of the ideal norm, for powers of prime ideals.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.card_quot_eq_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.rel_norm_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.map_rel_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.rel_norm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_singleton_abs_norm_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.abs_norm_ne_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.nat_abs_det_equiv", "description": " Let `e : S \u2243 I` be an additive isomorphism (therefore a `\u2124`-linear equiv).\nThen an alternative way to compute the norm of `I` is given by taking the determinant of `e`.\nSee `nat_abs_det_basis_change` for a more familiar formulation of this result.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.abs_norm_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.exists_mul_add_mem_pow_succ", "description": " If `a \u2208 P^i \\ P^(i+1)` and `c \u2208 P^i`, then `a * d + e = c` for `e \u2208 P^(i+1)`.\n`ideal.mul_add_mem_pow_succ_unique` shows the choice of `d` is unique, up to `P`.\nInspired by [Neukirch], proposition 6.1", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_norm_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.abs_norm_dvd_norm_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_norm_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.abs_norm_span_insert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.is_prime_of_irreducible_abs_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.abs_norm_eq_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.rel_norm_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.span_norm_mul_of_bot_or_top", "description": " This condition `eq_bot_or_top` is equivalent to being a field.\nHowever, `span_norm_mul_of_field` is harder to apply since we'd need to upgrade a `comm_ring R`\ninstance to a `field R` instance.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.free.add_monoid_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.rank_vec_mul_vec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.finite.add_monoid_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.free.linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finite_dimensional.finrank_linear_map", "description": "The finrank of `M \u2192\u2097[R] N` is `(finrank R M) * (finrank R N)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.finite.linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_commute.neg_add_cancel", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "neg_add_cancel_comm_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.right_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.units_inv_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_commute.neg_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_commute.add_add_add_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_inv_cancel_comm_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_commute.neg_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_commute.refl", "description": "Any element commutes with itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_commute", "description": "Two elements additively commute if `a + b = b + a`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.units_coe_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.semiconj_by", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.left_of_mul", "description": "If the product of two commuting elements is a unit, then the left multiplier is a unit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.one_left", "description": "", "p": "mat