name": "biheyting_hom", "description": " The type of bi-Heyting homomorphisms from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2`. Bounded lattice homomorphisms that\npreserve Heyting implication and difference.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "biheyting_hom.to_lattice_hom", "description": " The type of bi-Heyting homomorphisms from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2`. Bounded lattice homomorphisms that\npreserve Heyting implication and difference.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "biheyting_hom.map_himp'", "description": " The type of bi-Heyting homomorphisms from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2`. Bounded lattice homomorphisms that\npreserve Heyting implication and difference.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "biheyting_hom.map_sdiff'", "description": " The type of bi-Heyting homomorphisms from `\u03b1` to `\u03b2`. Bounded lattice homomorphisms that\npreserve Heyting implication and difference.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "coheyting_hom.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "coheyting_hom.id_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "heyting_hom.id", "description": "`id` as a `heyting_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "coheyting_hom.comp_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "heyting_hom.id_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "biheyting_hom.coe_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.from_Spec.mem_carrier_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.to_Spec.carrier_ne_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.from_Spec.carrier.zero_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.to_Spec.preimage_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.from_Spec.mem_carrier_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.from_Spec.carrier.denom_not_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.from_Spec.to_fun", "description": "The function `Spec A\u2070_f \u2192 Proj|D(f)` by sending `q` to `{a | a\u1d62\u1d50/f\u2071 \u2208 q}`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.from_Spec.carrier.as_ideal.prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.to_Spec.mem_carrier.clear_denominator", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.to_Spec", "description": "The continuous function between the basic open set `D(f)` in `Proj` to the corresponding basic\nopen set in `Spec A\u2070_f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.to_Spec.carrier", "description": "For any `x` in `Proj| (pbo f)`, the corresponding ideal in `Spec A\u2070_f`. This fact that this ideal\nis prime is proven in `Top_component.forward.to_fun`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.from_Spec.carrier.smul_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.to_Spec.mem_carrier.clear_denominator'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.from_Spec.carrier.as_homogeneous_ideal", "description": "For a prime ideal `q` in `A\u2070_f`, the set `{a | a\u1d62\u1d50/f\u2071 \u2208 q}` as a homogeneous ideal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.to_Spec.mem_carrier_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.from_Spec.carrier.relevant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.from_Spec.carrier", "description": "The function from `Spec A\u2070_f` to `Proj|D(f)` is defined by `q \u21a6 {a | a\u1d62\u1d50/f\u2071 \u2208 q}`, i.e. sending\n`q` a prime ideal in `A\u2070_f` to the homogeneous prime relevant ideal containing only and all the\nelements `a : A` such that for every `i`, the degree 0 element formed by dividing the `m`-th power\nof the `i`-th projection of `a` by the `i`-th power of the degree-`m` homogeneous element `f`,\nlies in `q`.\n\nThe set `{a | a\u1d62\u1d50/f\u2071 \u2208 q}`\n* is an ideal, as proved in `carrier.as_ideal`;\n* is homogeneous, as proved in `carrier.as_homogeneous_ideal`;\n* is prime, as proved in `carrier.as_ideal.prime`;\n* is relevant, as proved in `carrier.relevant`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.from_Spec.carrier.as_ideal.homogeneous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.from_Spec.carrier.as_ideal.ne_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.from_Spec.carrier.as_ideal", "description": "For a prime ideal `q` in `A\u2070_f`, the set `{a | a\u1d62\u1d50/f\u2071 \u2208 q}` as an ideal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.to_Spec.disjoint", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.to_Spec.to_fun", "description": "The function between the basic open set `D(f)` in `Proj` to the corresponding basic open set in\n`Spec A\u2070_f`. This is bundled into a continuous map in `Top_component.forward`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj_iso_Spec_Top_component.from_Spec.carrier.add_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.convergent_succ", "description": "The `(n+1)`th convergent of `\u03be` is the `n`th convergent of `1/(fract \u03be)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.contfrac_legendre.ass", "description": "Define the technical condition to be used as assumption in the inductive proof.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.exists_int_int_abs_mul_sub_le", "description": " *Dirichlet's approximation theorem:*\nFor any real number `\u03be` and positive natural `n`, there are integers `j` and `k`,\nwith `0 < k \u2264 n` and `|k*\u03be - j| \u2264 1/(n+1)`.\n\nSee also `real.exists_nat_abs_mul_sub_round_le`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.exists_continued_fraction_convergent_eq_rat", "description": " The main result, *Legendre's Theorem* on rational approximation:\nif `\u03be` is a real number and  `q` is a rational number such that `|\u03be - q| < 1/(2*q.denom^2)`,\nthen `q` is a convergent of the continued fraction expansion of `\u03be`.\nThis is the version using `generalized_contined_fraction.convergents`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.exists_rat_abs_sub_lt_and_lt_of_irrational", "description": " Given any rational approximation `q` to the irrational real number `\u03be`, there is\na good rational approximation `q'` such that `|\u03be - q'| < |\u03be - q|`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.exists_rat_eq_convergent'", "description": "The technical version of *Legendre's Theorem*.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.infinite_rat_abs_sub_lt_one_div_denom_sq_of_irrational", "description": " If `\u03be` is an irrational real number, then there are infinitely many good\nrational approximations to `\u03be`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.convergent_of_zero", "description": "All convergents of `0` are zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.convergent_zero", "description": "The zeroth convergent of `\u03be` is `\u230a\u03be\u230b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.continued_fraction_convergent_eq_convergent", "description": " The `n`th convergent of the `generalized_continued_fraction.of \u03be`\nagrees with `\u03be.convergent n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.convergent", "description": " We give a direct recursive definition of the convergents of the continued fraction\nexpansion of a real number `\u03be`. The main reason for that is that we want to have the\nconvergents as rational numbers; the versions\n`(generalized_continued_fraction.of \u03be).convergents` and\n`(generalized_continued_fraction.of \u03be).convergents'` always give something of the\nsame type as `\u03be`. We can then also use dot notation `\u03be.convergent n`.\nAnother minor reason is that this demonstrates that the proof\nof Legendre's theorem does not need anything beyond this definition.\nWe provide a proof that this definition agrees with the other one;\nsee `real.continued_fraction_convergent_eq_convergent`.\n(Note that we use the fact that `1/0 = 0` here to make it work for rational `\u03be`.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rat.denom_le_and_le_num_le_of_sub_lt_one_div_denom_sq", "description": " If `\u03be` is rational, then the good rational approximations to `\u03be` have bounded\nnumerator and denominator.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.exists_nat_abs_mul_sub_round_le", "description": " *Dirichlet's approximation theorem:*\nFor any real number `\u03be` and positive natural `n`, there is a natural number `k`,\nwith `0 < k \u2264 n` such that `|k*\u03be - round(k*\u03be)| \u2264 1/(n+1)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.infinite_rat_abs_sub_lt_one_div_denom_sq_iff_irrational", "description": " The set of good rational approximations to a real number `\u03be` is infinite if and only if\n`\u03be` is irrational.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.exists_rat_eq_convergent", "description": " The main result, *Legendre's Theorem* on rational approximation:\nif `\u03be` is a real number and  `q` is a rational number such that `|\u03be - q| < 1/(2*q.denom^2)`,\nthen `q` is a convergent of the continued fraction expansion of `\u03be`.\nThis version uses `real.convergent`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rat.finite_rat_abs_sub_lt_one_div_denom_sq", "description": "A rational number has only finitely many good rational approximations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.exists_rat_abs_sub_le_and_denom_le", "description": " *Dirichlet's approximation theorem:*\nFor any real number `\u03be` and positive natural `n`, there is a fraction `q`\nsuch that `q.denom \u2264 n` and `|\u03be - q| \u2264 1/((n+1)*q.denom)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.convergent_of_int", "description": "If `\u03be` is an integer, all its convergents equal `\u03be`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_equicontinuous_of_equicontinuous_at_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_equicontinuous_of_equicontinuous_at_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equicontinuous_of_equicontinuous_at_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equicontinuous_of_equicontinuous_at_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.image", "description": "the image of a morphism in AddCommGroup is just the bundling of `add_monoid_hom.range f`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.image.\u03b9.category_theory.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.image_iso_range", "description": "The categorical image of a morphism in `AddCommGroup`\nagrees with the usual group-theoretical range.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.is_image", "description": " the factorisation of any morphism in AddCommGroup through a mono has the universal property of\nthe image.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.image.lift", "description": "the universal property for the image factorisation", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.image.\u03b9", "description": "the inclusion of `image f` into the target", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.mono_factorisation", "description": "the factorisation of any morphism in AddCommGroup through a mono.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.image.lift_fac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.factor_thru_image", "description": "the corestriction map to the image", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "AddCommGroup.image.fac", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.nodup_of_fn", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.map_nth_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.fin_range_succ_eq_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.of_fn_eq_pmap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.map_fin_range_perm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.nodup_of_fn_of_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.of_fn_comp_perm", "description": " The list obtained from a permutation of a tuple `f` is permutation equivalent to\nthe list obtained from `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.of_fn_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.of_fn_eq_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.map_coe_fin_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rat.sqrt_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rat.exists_mul_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rat.sqrt_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rat.sqrt", "description": " Square root function on rational numbers, defined by taking the (integer) square root of the\nnumerator and the square root (on natural numbers) of the denominator.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quot_adjoin_equiv_quot_map_apply_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quot_adjoin_equiv_quot_map", "description": "The canonical morphism of rings from `R<x> \u29f8 (I*R<x>)` to `S \u29f8 (I*S)` is an isomorphism\n   when `I` and `(conductor R x) \u2229 R` are coprime.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod_mem_ideal_map_of_mem_conductor", "description": "This technical lemma tell us that if `C` is the conductor of `R<x>` and `I` is an ideal of `R`\n then `p * (I * S) \u2286 I * R<x>` for any `p` in `C \u2229 R`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conductor_eq_of_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kummer_dedekind.multiplicity_factors_map_eq_multiplicity", "description": "The second half of the **Kummer-Dedekind Theorem** in the monogenic case, stating that the\n   bijection `factors_equiv'` defined in the first half preserves multiplicities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kummer_dedekind.normalized_factors_ideal_map_eq_normalized_factors_min_poly_mk_map", "description": "The **Kummer-Dedekind Theorem**.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_conductor_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comap_map_eq_map_adjoin_of_coprime_conductor", "description": "A technical result telling us that `(I * S) \u2229 R<x> = I * R<x>` for any ideal `I` of `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conductor_subset_adjoin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kummer_dedekind.ideal.irreducible_map_of_irreducible_minpoly", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "kummer_dedekind.normalized_factors_map_equiv_normalized_factors_min_poly_mk", "description": "The first half of the **Kummer-Dedekind Theorem** in the monogenic case, stating that the prime\n   factors of `I*S` are in bijection with those of the minimal polynomial of the generator of `S`\n   over `R`, taken `mod I`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conductor_eq_top_of_power_basis", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conductor", "description": "Let `S / R` be a ring extension and `x : S`, then the conductor of `R<x>` is the\n   biggest ideal of `S` contained in `R<x>`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "conductor_eq_top_of_adjoin_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functorial.map_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functorial_comp", "description": "`G \u2218 F` is a functorial if both `F` and `G` are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functorial", "description": "A unbundled functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functorial.map", "description": "A unbundled functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functorial.map_id'", "description": "A unbundled functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functorial.map_comp'", "description": "A unbundled functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.of", "description": "Bundle a functorial function as a functor.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.map", "description": "If `F : C \u2192 D` (just a function) has `[functorial F]`,\nwe can write `map F f : F X \u27f6 F Y` for the action of `F` on a morphism `f : X \u27f6 Y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.obj.functorial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.map_functorial_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.map_as_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functorial_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functorial.map_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.le_inf_support_multiset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.le_inf_support_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.le_inf_support_finset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.sup_support_mul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.le_inf_support_list_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.le_inf_support_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.sup_support_list_prod_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.le_inf_support_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.sup_support_multiset_prod_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.sup_support_pow_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.sup_support_finset_prod_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.sup_support_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_off_diag", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.to_finset_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.infinite_of_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.infinite_of_right", "description": "Non-dependent version of `pi.infinite_of_exists_right` and `pi.infinite_of_right`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fintype.card_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.infinite_of_right", "description": "See `pi.infinite_of_exists_right` for the case that only one `\u03c0 i` is infinite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.univ_product_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "infinite_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pi.infinite_of_exists_right", "description": "If at least one `\u03c0 i` is infinite and the rest nonempty, the pi type of all `\u03c0` is infinite.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.infinite_of_left", "description": "Non-dependent version of `pi.infinite_of_left`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.ring_of_integers.char_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.ring_of_integers.is_integrally_closed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.ring_of_integers_algebra", "description": " Given an algebra between two fields, create an algebra between their two rings of integers.\n\nFor now, this is not an instance by default as it creates an equal-but-not-defeq diamond with\n`algebra.id` when `K = L`. This is caused by `x = \u27e8x, x.prop\u27e9` not being defeq on subtypes. This\nwill likely change in Lean 4.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.integral_basis", "description": "A basis of `K` over `\u211a` that is also a basis of `\ud835\udcde K` over `\u2124`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.is_integral_of_mem_ring_of_integers", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.is_algebraic", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.ring_of_integers.is_noetherian", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.ring_of_integers.rank", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.ring_of_integers.is_localization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.ring_of_integers", "description": " The ring of integers (or number ring) corresponding to a number field\nis the integral closure of \u2124 in the number field.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.ring_of_integers.is_dedekind_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.ring_of_integers.basis", "description": "A \u2124-basis of the ring of integers of `K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.ring_of_integers.is_integral_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.ring_of_integers.is_integral_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field", "description": " A number field is a field which has characteristic zero and is finite\ndimensional over \u211a.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.to_char_zero", "description": " A number field is a field which has characteristic zero and is finite\ndimensional over \u211a.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.to_finite_dimensional", "description": " A number field is a field which has characteristic zero and is finite\ndimensional over \u211a.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "adjoin_root.number_field", "description": " The quotient of `\u211a[X]` by the ideal generated by an irreducible polynomial of `\u211a[X]`\nis a number field.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.ring_of_integers.is_fraction_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rat.number_field", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.mem_ring_of_integers", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rat.ring_of_integers_equiv", "description": "The ring of integers of `\u211a` as a number field is just `\u2124`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.integral_basis_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.ring_of_integers.module.free", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.not_is_field", "description": "`\u2124` with its usual ring structure is not a field.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.ring_of_integers.not_is_field", "description": "The ring of integers of a number field is not a field.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.ring_of_integers.map_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "number_field.ring_of_integers.equiv", "description": "The ring of integers of `K` are equivalent to any integral closure of `\u2124` in `K`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_subspace.pointwise_add_action", "description": " The additive action on an affine subspace corresponding to applying the action to every element.\n\nThis is available as an instance in the `pointwise` locale.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_subspace.pointwise_vadd_direction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_subspace.pointwise_vadd_span", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_subspace.coe_pointwise_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_subspace.map_pointwise_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_subspace.pointwise_vadd_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "affine_subspace.vadd_mem_pointwise_vadd_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_swap.eval", "description": "A `norm_num` plugin for normalizing `equiv.swap a b c`\nwhere `a b c` are numerals of `\u2115`, `\u2124`, `\u211a` or `fin n`.\n\n```lean\nexample : equiv.swap 1 2 1 = 2 := by norm_num\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.to_character_space_apply_eq_zero_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.character_space.comp_continuous_map_id", "description": "`weak_dual.character_space.comp_continuous_map` sends the identity to the identity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.character_space.exists_apply_eq_zero", "description": " If `a : A` is not a unit, then some character takes the value zero at `a`. This is equivlaent\nto `gelfand_transform \u2102 A a` takes the value zero at some character.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.character_space.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gelfand_star_transform_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.character_space.comp_continuous_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.character_space.mem_spectrum_iff_exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.character_space.comp_continuous_map_comp", "description": "`weak_dual.character_space.comp_continuous_map` is functorial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gelfand_star_transform", "description": " The Gelfand transform as a `star_alg_equiv` between a commutative unital C\u22c6-algebra over `\u2102`\nand the continuous functions on its `character_space`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.character_space.comp_continuous_map", "description": " The functorial map taking `\u03c8 : A \u2192\u22c6\u2090[\u2102] B` to a continuous function\n`character_space \u2102 B \u2192 character_space \u2102 A` obtained by pre-composition with `\u03c8`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gelfand_transform_map_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gelfand_transform_bijective", "description": "The Gelfand transform is bijective when the algebra is a C\u22c6-algebra over `\u2102`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gelfand_transform_isometry", "description": "The Gelfand transform is an isometry when the algebra is a C\u22c6-algebra over `\u2102`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "gelfand_star_transform_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ideal.to_character_space", "description": " Every maximal ideal in a commutative complex Banach algebra gives rise to a character on that\nalgebra. In particular, the character, which may be identified as an algebra homomorphism due to\n`weak_dual.character_space.equiv_alg_hom`, is given by the composition of the quotient map and\nthe Gelfand-Mazur isomorphism `normed_ring.alg_equiv_complex_of_complete`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "spectrum.gelfand_transform_eq", "description": "The Gelfand transform is spectrum-preserving.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.card_uIcc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.card_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.card_fintype_uIcc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.uIcc_eq_finset_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.map_subtype_embedding_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.Ioc_eq_finset_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.card_fintype_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.card_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.card_fintype_Ioo", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.card_fintype_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.Ico_eq_finset_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.map_subtype_embedding_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.Icc_eq_finset_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.map_subtype_embedding_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.locally_finite_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.card_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.card_Ico", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.Ioo_eq_finset_subtype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.map_subtype_embedding_uIcc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.map_subtype_embedding_Ioc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pnat.card_fintype_Icc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.topological_closure_minimal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "division_ring.has_continuous_const_smul_rat", "description": "The action induced by `algebra_rat` is continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.topological_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.topological_closure", "description": "The closure of a subalgebra in a topological algebra as a subalgebra.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.elemental_algebra", "description": "The topological closure of the subalgebra generated by a single element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.comm_ring_topological_closure", "description": " If a subalgebra of a topological algebra is commutative, then so is its topological closure.\nSee note [reducible non-instances].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.topological_closure_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra_map_clm_coe_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_algebra_map_iff_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.self_mem_elemental_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.is_closed_topological_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.topological_closure_comap_homeomorph", "description": "This is really a statement about topological algebra isomorphisms,\nbut we don't have those, so we use the clunky approach of talking about\nan algebra homomorphism, and a separate homeomorphism,\nalong with a witness that as functions they are the same.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra_map_clm", "description": "The inclusion of the base ring in a topological algebra as a continuous linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.has_continuous_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra_map_clm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra_map_clm_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra_map_clm_to_linear_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_continuous_smul_of_algebra_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.comm_semiring_topological_closure", "description": "If a subalgebra of a topological algebra is commutative, then so is its topological closure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.elemental_algebra.comm_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.le_topological_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.char.step", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.char.of_fintype.step", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.char.err_static", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.prog", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.from_one.bounded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.from_one.of_fintype", "description": "Parse a string of digits as a numeral while casting it to target type `\u03b1`,\nwhich has a `[fintype \u03b1]` constraint. The parser ensures that the numeral parsed in\nis within the cardinality of the type `\u03b1`. The parsing starts\nat \"1\", so `\"1\"` is parsed in as `nat.cast 0`. Providing `\"0\"` to the parser causes a failure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.from_one.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.char", "description": "Parse a character as a numeral while casting it to target type `\u03b1`,\nThe parser ensures that the character parsed in is within the bounds set by `fromc` and `toc`,\nand subtracts the value of `fromc` from the parsed in character.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.char.of_fintype.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.from_one.prog", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.char.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.from_one.of_fintype.prog", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.char.of_fintype", "description": "Parse a character as a numeral while casting it to target type `\u03b1`,\nwhich has a `[fintype \u03b1]` constraint.\nThe parser ensures that the character parsed in is greater or equal to `fromc` and\nand subtracts the value of `fromc` from the parsed in character. There is also a check\nthat the resulting value is within the cardinality of the type `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.of_fintype", "description": "Parse a string of digits as a numeral while casting it to target type `\u03b1`,\nwhich has a `[fintype \u03b1]` constraint. The parser ensures that the numeral parsed in\nis within the cardinality of the type `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.char.of_fintype.err_static", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.from_one.of_fintype.bounded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.of_fintype.prog", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.int", "description": "Matches an integer, like `43` or `-2`.\nLarge numbers may cause performance issues, so don't run this parser on untrusted input.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.from_one.of_fintype.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.of_fintype.mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.rat", "description": "Matches an rational number, like `43/1` or `-2/3`.\nRequires that the negation is in the numerator,\nand that both a numerator and denominator are provided (e.g. will not match `43`).\nLarge numbers may cause performance issues, so don't run this parser on untrusted input.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.char.bounded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.bounded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.from_one", "description": "Parse a string of digits as a numeral while casting it to target type `\u03b1`. The parsing starts\nat \"1\", so `\"1\"` is parsed in as `nat.cast 0`. Providing `\"0\"` to the parser causes a failure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral", "description": "Parse a string of digits as a numeral while casting it to target type `\u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.of_fintype.bounded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "parser.numeral.char.of_fintype.bounded", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.second_inter_vsub_mem_affine_span", "description": " If the vector passed to `second_inter` is given by a subtraction involving the point in\n`second_inter`, the result lies in the span of the two points.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.wbtw_second_inter", "description": " If the vector passed to `second_inter` is given by a subtraction involving the point in\n`second_inter`, and the second point is not outside the sphere, the second point is weakly\nbetween the first point and the result of `second_inter`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.second_inter_eq_line_map", "description": " If the vector passed to `second_inter` is given by a subtraction involving the point in\n`second_inter`, the result of `second_inter` may be expressed using `line_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.second_inter_eq_self_iff", "description": " The point given by `second_inter` equals the original point if and only if the line is\northogonal to the radius vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.second_inter", "description": " The second intersection of a sphere with a line through a point on that sphere; that point\nif it is the only point of intersection of the line with the sphere. The intended use of this\ndefinition is when `p \u2208 s`; the definition does not use `s.radius`, so in general it returns\nthe second intersection with the sphere through `p` and with center `s.center`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.second_inter_smul", "description": "`second_inter` is unchanged by multiplying the vector by a nonzero real.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.second_inter_mem", "description": "The point given by `second_inter` lies on the sphere.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.sbtw_second_inter", "description": " If the vector passed to `second_inter` is given by a subtraction involving the point in\n`second_inter`, and the second point is inside the sphere, the second point is strictly between\nthe first point and the result of `second_inter`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.second_inter_second_inter", "description": "Applying `second_inter` twice returns the original point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.second_inter_zero", "description": "If the vector is zero, `second_inter` gives the original point.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.second_inter_neg", "description": "`second_inter` is unchanged by negating the vector.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.second_inter_collinear", "description": " If the vector passed to `second_inter` is given by a subtraction involving the point in\n`second_inter`, the three points are collinear.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.second_inter_dist", "description": " The distance between `second_inter` and the center equals the distance between the original\npoint and the center.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.sphere.eq_or_eq_second_inter_of_mem_mk'_span_singleton_iff_mem", "description": "A point on a line through a point on a sphere equals that point or `second_inter`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "transfer.compute_transfer", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "transfer.analyse_decls", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "transfer.has_to_tactic_format_rule_data", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "transfer.has_to_tactic_format_rel_data", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.transfer", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_quasi_separated.of_quasi_separated_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quasi_separated_space_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quasi_separated_space", "description": " A topological space is quasi-separated if the intersections of any pairs of compact open\nsubsets are still compact.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quasi_separated_space.inter_is_compact", "description": " A topological space is quasi-separated if the intersections of any pairs of compact open\nsubsets are still compact.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_quasi_separated_iff_quasi_separated_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_quasi_separated.of_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_quasi_separated_univ_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_quasi_separated", "description": " A subset `s` of a topological space is quasi-separated if the intersections of any pairs of\ncompact open subsets of `s` are still compact.\n\nNote that this is equivalent to `s` being a `quasi_separated_space` only when `s` is open.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "open_embedding.is_quasi_separated_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "t2_space.to_quasi_separated_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quasi_separated_space.of_open_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "noetherian_space.to_quasi_separated_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_quasi_separated_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_quasi_separated.image_of_embedding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rotation_of_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rotation_of_rotation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.re_apply_eq_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rotation_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rotation_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rotation", "description": " An element of the unit circle defines a `linear_isometry_equiv` from `\u2102` to itself, by\nrotation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_equiv_det_rotation", "description": "The determinant of `rotation` (as a linear equiv) is equal to `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.im_apply_eq_im_or_neg_of_re_apply_eq_re", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.im_apply_eq_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_complex_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rotation_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "det_rotation", "description": "The determinant of `rotation` (as a linear map) is equal to `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rotation_ne_conj_lie", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry_complex", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rotation_of", "description": " Takes an element of `\u2102 \u2243\u2097\u1d62[\u211d] \u2102` and checks if it is a rotation, returns an element of the\nunit circle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rotation_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "to_matrix_rotation", "description": " The matrix representation of `rotation a` is equal to the conformal matrix\n`!![re a, -im a; im a, re a]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_isometry.re_apply_eq_re_of_add_conj_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "jacobi_theta", "description": "Jacobi's theta function `\u2211' (n : \u2124), exp (\u03c0 * I * n ^ 2 * \u03c4)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_jacobi_theta_sub_one_le", "description": "An explicit upper bound for `\u2016jacobi_theta \u03c4 - 1\u2016`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "jacobi_theta_T_sq_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "jacobi_theta_eq_tsum_nat", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "differentiable_at_jacobi_theta", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "jacobi_theta_S_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_O_at_im_infty_jacobi_theta_sub_one", "description": "The norm of `jacobi_theta \u03c4 - 1` decays exponentially as `im \u03c4 \u2192 \u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_summable_bound_exp_mul_sq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_exp_mul_sq_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_sum_nat_jacobi_theta", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "summable_exp_mul_sq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at_jacobi_theta", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "jacobi_theta_two_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.log_two_lt_d9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.log_two_gt_d9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.exp_neg_one_lt_d9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.log_two_near_10", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.exp_one_lt_d9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.exp_neg_one_gt_d9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.exp_one_near_10", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.exp_one_near_20", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.exp_one_gt_d9", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.right_adjoint_of_costructured_arrow_terminals_aux", "description": "Implementation: If each costructured arrow category on `G` has a terminal object, an equivalence\nwhich is helpful for constructing a right adjoint to `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.right_adjoint_of_costructured_arrow_terminals_aux_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_right_adjoint_of_structured_arrow_initials", "description": "If each structured arrow category on `G` has an initial object, `G` is a right adjoint.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.left_adjoint_of_structured_arrow_initials", "description": "If each structured arrow category on `G` has an initial object, construct a left adjoint to `G`. It\nis shown that it is a left adjoint in `adjunction_of_structured_arrow_initials`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.right_adjoint_of_costructured_arrow_terminals_aux_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.left_adjoint_of_structured_arrow_initials_aux_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction_of_costructured_arrow_terminals", "description": "If each costructured arrow category on `G` has a terminal object, we have a constructed right\nadjoint to `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nonempty_is_right_adjoint_iff_has_initial_structured_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.nonempty_is_left_adjoint_iff_has_terminal_costructured_arrow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mk_terminal_of_right_adjoint", "description": " Given a right adjoint to `F`, we can construct a terminal object in each costructured arrow\ncategory on `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction_of_structured_arrow_initials", "description": "If each structured arrow category on `G` has an initial object, we have a constructed left adjoint\nto `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.left_adjoint_of_structured_arrow_initials_aux_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_left_adjoint_of_costructured_arrow_terminals", "description": "If each costructured arrow category on `G` has an terminal object, `G` is a left adjoint.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.mk_initial_of_left_adjoint", "description": " Given a left adjoint to `G`, we can construct an initial object in each structured arrow\ncategory on `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.right_adjoint_of_costructured_arrow_terminals", "description": "If each costructured arrow category on `G` has a terminal object, construct a right adjoint to `G`.\nIt is shown that it is a right adjoint in `adjunction_of_structured_arrow_initials`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.left_adjoint_of_structured_arrow_initials_aux", "description": "Implementation: If each structured arrow category on `G` has an initial object, an equivalence\nwhich is helpful for constructing a left adjoint to `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at_exp", "description": " The exponential map in `\ud835\udd42 = \u211d` or `\ud835\udd42 = \u2102` has strict derivative `exp \ud835\udd42 x` at any point\n`x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at_exp_zero_of_radius_pos", "description": " The exponential in a Banach-algebra `\ud835\udd38` over a normed field `\ud835\udd42` has Fr\u00e9chet-derivative\n`1 : \ud835\udd38 \u2192L[\ud835\udd42] \ud835\udd38` at zero, as long as it converges on a neighborhood of zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at_exp_smul_const_of_mem_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at_exp_smul_const_of_mem_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at_exp", "description": "The exponential map in `\ud835\udd42 = \u211d` or `\ud835\udd42 = \u2102` has derivative `exp \ud835\udd42 x` at any point `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at_exp_smul_const_of_mem_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at_exp", "description": " The exponential map in a commutative Banach-algebra `\ud835\udd38` over `\ud835\udd42 = \u211d` or `\ud835\udd42 = \u2102` has strict\nFr\u00e9chet-derivative `exp \ud835\udd42 x \u2022 1 : \ud835\udd38 \u2192L[\ud835\udd42] \ud835\udd38` at any point `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at_exp_smul_const'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at_exp_smul_const'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.exp_eq_exp_\u211d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.exp_eq_exp_\u2102", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at_exp_zero", "description": " The exponential in a Banach-algebra `\ud835\udd38` over `\ud835\udd42 = \u211d` or `\ud835\udd42 = \u2102` has Fr\u00e9chet-derivative\n`1 : \ud835\udd38 \u2192L[\ud835\udd42] \ud835\udd38` at zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at_exp_of_mem_ball", "description": " The exponential map in a complete normed field `\ud835\udd42` of characteristic zero has derivative\n`exp \ud835\udd42 x` at any point `x` in the disk of convergence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at_exp_zero_of_radius_pos", "description": " The exponential map in a complete normed field `\ud835\udd42` of characteristic zero has strict derivative\n`1` at zero, as long as it converges on a neighborhood of zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at_exp_of_mem_ball", "description": " The exponential map in a commutative Banach-algebra `\ud835\udd38` over a normed field `\ud835\udd42` of\ncharacteristic zero has Fr\u00e9chet-derivative `exp \ud835\udd42 x \u2022 1 : \ud835\udd38 \u2192L[\ud835\udd42] \ud835\udd38` at any point `x` in the\ndisk of convergence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at_exp_smul_const_of_mem_ball'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at_exp_smul_const'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at_exp_zero", "description": " The exponential in a Banach-algebra `\ud835\udd38` over `\ud835\udd42 = \u211d` or `\ud835\udd42 = \u2102` has strict Fr\u00e9chet-derivative\n`1 : \ud835\udd38 \u2192L[\ud835\udd42] \ud835\udd38` at zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at_exp_smul_const_of_mem_ball'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at_exp_smul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at_exp_smul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at_exp_zero", "description": "The exponential map in `\ud835\udd42 = \u211d` or `\ud835\udd42 = \u2102` has strict derivative `1` at zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at_exp", "description": " The exponential map in a commutative Banach-algebra `\ud835\udd38` over `\ud835\udd42 = \u211d` or `\ud835\udd42 = \u2102` has\nFr\u00e9chet-derivative `exp \ud835\udd42 x \u2022 1 : \ud835\udd38 \u2192L[\ud835\udd42] \ud835\udd38` at any point `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at_exp_zero_of_radius_pos", "description": " The exponential in a Banach-algebra `\ud835\udd38` over a normed field `\ud835\udd42` has strict Fr\u00e9chet-derivative\n`1 : \ud835\udd38 \u2192L[\ud835\udd42] \ud835\udd38` at zero, as long as it converges on a neighborhood of zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at_exp_smul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at_exp_zero", "description": "The exponential map in `\ud835\udd42 = \u211d` or `\ud835\udd42 = \u2102` has derivative `1` at zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at_exp_smul_const_of_mem_ball'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at_exp_smul_const'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at_exp_smul_const_of_mem_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at_exp_zero_of_radius_pos", "description": " The exponential map in a complete normed field `\ud835\udd42` of characteristic zero has derivative\n`1` at zero, as long as it converges on a neighborhood of zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_fderiv_at_exp_of_mem_ball", "description": " The exponential map in a commutative Banach-algebra `\ud835\udd38` over a normed field `\ud835\udd42` of\ncharacteristic zero has strict Fr\u00e9chet-derivative `exp \ud835\udd42 x \u2022 1 : \ud835\udd38 \u2192L[\ud835\udd42] \ud835\udd38` at any point `x` in\nthe disk of convergence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_fderiv_at_exp_smul_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_deriv_at_exp_smul_const_of_mem_ball'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_strict_deriv_at_exp_of_mem_ball", "description": " The exponential map in a complete normed field `\ud835\udd42` of characteristic zero has strict derivative\n`exp \ud835\udd42 x` at any point `x` in the disk of convergence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unif_loc_doubling_measure.ae_tendsto_measure_inter_div", "description": " A version of *Lebesgue's density theorem* for a sequence of closed balls whose centers are\nnot required to be fixed.\n\nSee also `besicovitch.ae_tendsto_measure_inter_div`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unif_loc_doubling_measure.tendsto_closed_ball_filter_at", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unif_loc_doubling_measure.closed_ball_mem_vitali_family_of_dist_le_mul", "description": " In the Vitali family `is_unif_loc_doubling_measure.vitali_family K`, the sets based at `x`\ncontain all balls `closed_ball y r` when `dist x y \u2264 K * r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unif_loc_doubling_measure.vitali_family", "description": " A Vitali family in a space with a uniformly locally doubling measure, designed so that the sets\nat `x` contain all `closed_ball y r` when `dist x y \u2264 K * r`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unif_loc_doubling_measure.ae_tendsto_average", "description": " A version of *Lebesgue differentiation theorem* for a sequence of closed balls whose\ncenters are not required to be fixed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unif_loc_doubling_measure.ae_tendsto_average_norm_sub", "description": " A version of *Lebesgue differentiation theorem* for a sequence of closed balls whose\ncenters are not required to be fixed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.mk_constructor_arg_names", "description": "Return a list of names of the form [p.i, ..., p.{i+n}] where n is\n  the number of fields of the constructor c", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.mk_brec_on_rec_value", "description": "Construct brec_on \"recursive value\". F_name is the name of the brec_on \"dictionary\".\n  Type of the F_name hypothesis should be of the form (below (C ...)) where C is a constructor.\n  The result is the \"recursive value\" for the (i+1)-th recursive value of the constructor C.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.constructor_num_fields", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.is_type_app_of", "description": "Return tt iff e's type is of the form `(I_name ...)`", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.mk_constructors_arg_names", "description": "Given an inductive datatype I with k constructors and where constructor i has n_i fields,\n  return the list [[p.1, ..., p.n_1], [p.{n_1 + 1}, ..., p.{n_1 + n_2}], ..., [..., p.{n_1 + ... + n_k}]]", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.mk_constructor_fresh_names", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.mk_constructors_fresh_names", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "sym.E1", "description": "Over `fin n+1`, the multisets of size `k+1` containing `0` are equivalent to those of size `k`,\nas demonstrated by respectively erasing or appending `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym.card_sym_eq_choose", "description": " The *stars and bars* lemma: the cardinality of `sym \u03b1 k` is equal to\n`nat.choose (card \u03b1 + k - 1) k`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym2.card_subtype_not_diag", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym2.card", "description": "Type **stars and bars** for the case `n = 2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym2.two_mul_card_image_off_diag", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym2.card_subtype_diag", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym.card_sym_fin_eq_multichoose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_sym2", "description": "Finset **stars and bars** for the case `n = 2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym2.card_image_diag", "description": "The `diag` of `s : finset \u03b1` is sent on a finset of `sym2 \u03b1` of card `s.card`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym.card_sym_eq_multichoose", "description": "For any fintype `\u03b1` of cardinality `n`, `card (sym \u03b1 k) = multichoose (card \u03b1) k`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym2.card_image_off_diag", "description": " The `off_diag` of `s : finset \u03b1` is sent on a finset of `sym2 \u03b1` of card `s.off_diag.card / 2`.\nThis is because every element `\u27e6(x, y)\u27e7` of `sym2 \u03b1` not on the diagonal comes from exactly two\npairs: `(x, y)` and `(y, x)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sym.E2", "description": "The multisets of size `k` over `fin n+2` not containing `0`\nare equivalent to those of size `k` over `fin n+1`,\nas demonstrated by respectively decrementing or incrementing every element of the multiset.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.bohr_mollerup.ge_log_gamma_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.doubling_Gamma_add_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strict_concave_on.congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.Gamma_mul_add_mul_le_rpow_Gamma_mul_rpow_Gamma", "description": " Log-convexity of the Gamma function on the positive reals (stated in multiplicative form),\nproved using the H\u00f6lder inequality applied to Euler's integral.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.log_doubling_Gamma_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.bohr_mollerup.tendsto_log_gamma_seq_of_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.doubling_Gamma", "description": "Auxiliary definition for the doubling formula (we'll show this is equal to `Gamma s`)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.bohr_mollerup.f_add_nat_le", "description": "Linear upper bound for `f (x + n)` on unit interval", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.bohr_mollerup.tendsto_log_gamma_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.Gamma_three_div_two_lt_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.Gamma_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.bohr_mollerup.le_log_gamma_seq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concave_on.congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.doubling_Gamma_eq_Gamma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.eq_Gamma_of_log_convex", "description": " The **Bohr-Mollerup theorem**: the Gamma function is the *unique* log-convex, positive-valued\nfunction on the positive reals which satisfies `f 1 = 1` and `f (x + 1) = x * f x` for all `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_on.congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.bohr_mollerup.f_add_nat_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.Gamma_mul_Gamma_add_half_of_pos", "description": " Legendre's doubling formula for the Gamma function, for positive real arguments. Note that\nwe shall later prove this for all `s` as `real.Gamma_mul_Gamma_add_half` (superseding this result)\nbut this result is needed as an intermediate step.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.doubling_Gamma_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strict_convex_on.add_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.bohr_mollerup.tendsto_log_Gamma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.Gamma_strict_mono_on_Ici", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strict_concave_on.add_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.bohr_mollerup.log_gamma_seq_add_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.convex_on_Gamma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.convex_on_log_Gamma", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "convex_on.add_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.bohr_mollerup.f_nat_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "concave_on.add_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.bohr_mollerup.f_add_nat_ge", "description": "Linear lower bound for `f (x + n)` on unit interval", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.bohr_mollerup.log_gamma_seq", "description": " The function `n \u21a6 x log n + log n! - (log x + ... + log (x + n))`, which we will show tends to\n`log (Gamma x)` as `n \u2192 \u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "strict_convex_on.congr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.doubling_Gamma_log_convex_Ioi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.le_next_fixed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.is_greatest_gfp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.lfp_le_fixed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.lfp", "description": "Least fixed point of a monotone function", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.prev_fixed_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.lfp_induction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.is_greatest_gfp_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.lfp_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixed_points.function.fixed_points.semilattice_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.next_fixed", "description": " Next fixed point of a monotone map. If `f` is a monotone self-map of a complete lattice and\n`x` is a point such that `x \u2264 f x`, then `f.next_fixed x hx` is the least fixed point of `f`\nthat is greater than or equal to `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixed_points.function.fixed_points.complete_semilattice_Inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.gfp_induction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.gfp_const_inf_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.le_map_sup_fixed_points", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.map_le_gfp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.le_gfp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.le_map_Sup_subset_fixed_points", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixed_points.function.fixed_points.complete_lattice", "description": "**Knaster-Tarski Theorem**: The fixed points of `f` form a complete lattice.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.map_le_lfp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.lfp_lfp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.gfp_gfp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.next_fixed_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.map_gfp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.is_fixed_pt_lfp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.gfp_le_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.le_prev_fixed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixed_points.function.fixed_points.semilattice_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.gfp_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.prev_fixed", "description": " Previous fixed point of a monotone map. If `f` is a monotone self-map of a complete lattice and\n`x` is a point such that `f x \u2264 x`, then `f.prev_fixed x hx` is the greatest fixed point of `f`\nthat is less than or equal to `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.map_Inf_subset_fixed_points_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.map_inf_fixed_points_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.is_least_lfp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.gfp", "description": "Greatest fixed point of a monotone function", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.map_lfp_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.is_fixed_pt_gfp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.le_lfp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.lfp_le_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fixed_points.function.fixed_points.complete_semilattice_Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.le_prev_fixed_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.map_lfp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.is_least_lfp_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.next_fixed_le_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_hom.map_gfp_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_countable_complex", "description": "The complex numbers are not countable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mk_univ_complex", "description": "The cardinality of the complex numbers, as a set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mk_complex", "description": "The cardinality of the complex numbers, as a type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne_zero.succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "two_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "four_ne_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne_zero.coe_trans", "description": ""