cription": "The chosen retraction of a split monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_iso.of_epi_section'", "description": "Every split epi whose section is epi is an iso.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map.is_split_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_iso_of_epi_of_is_split_mono", "description": "A split mono which is epi is an iso.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.split_epi.id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_split_mono", "description": "`is_split_mono f` is the assertion that `f` admits a retraction", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_split_mono.exists_split_mono", "description": "`is_split_mono f` is the assertion that `f` admits a retraction", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_split_mono_of_mono", "description": "In a category in which every monomorphism is split, every monomorphism splits. This is not an\n   instance because it would create an instance loop.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_split_epi.id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_split_mono.id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.op_mono_of_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_split_mono.mono", "description": "Every split mono is a mono.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.op_epi_of_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_split_epi.epi", "description": "Every split epi is an epi.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_split_mono.of_iso", "description": "Every iso is a split mono.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_split_epi.mk'", "description": "A constructor for `is_split_epi f` taking a `split_epi f` as an argument", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.split_mono", "description": "A split monomorphism is a morphism `f : X \u27f6 Y` with a given retraction `retraction f : Y \u27f6 X`\nsuch that `f \u226b retraction f = \ud835\udfd9 X`.\n\nEvery split monomorphism is a monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.split_mono.retraction", "description": "A split monomorphism is a morphism `f : X \u27f6 Y` with a given retraction `retraction f : Y \u27f6 X`\nsuch that `f \u226b retraction f = \ud835\udfd9 X`.\n\nEvery split monomorphism is a monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.split_mono.id'", "description": "A split monomorphism is a morphism `f : X \u27f6 Y` with a given retraction `retraction f : Y \u27f6 X`\nsuch that `f \u226b retraction f = \ud835\udfd9 X`.\n\nEvery split monomorphism is a monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.split_mono.id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.retraction_is_split_epi", "description": "The retraction of a split monomorphism is itself a split epimorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.split_epi.ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_split_mono.mk'", "description": "A constructor for `is_split_mono f` taking a `split_mono f` as an argument", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.split_mono.split_epi", "description": "The retraction of a split monomorphism has an obvious section.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.split_epi", "description": "A split epimorphism is a morphism `f : X \u27f6 Y` with a given section `section_ f : Y \u27f6 X`\nsuch that `section_ f \u226b f = \ud835\udfd9 Y`.\n(Note that `section` is a reserved keyword, so we append an underscore.)\n\nEvery split epimorphism is an epimorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.split_epi.section_", "description": "A split epimorphism is a morphism `f : X \u27f6 Y` with a given section `section_ f : Y \u27f6 X`\nsuch that `section_ f \u226b f = \ud835\udfd9 Y`.\n(Note that `section` is a reserved keyword, so we append an underscore.)\n\nEvery split epimorphism is an epimorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.split_epi.id'", "description": "A split epimorphism is a morphism `f : X \u27f6 Y` with a given section `section_ f : Y \u27f6 X`\nsuch that `section_ f \u226b f = \ud835\udfd9 Y`.\n(Note that `section` is a reserved keyword, so we append an underscore.)\n\nEvery split epimorphism is an epimorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.split_epi.map_section_", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_split_epi_of_epi", "description": "In a category in which every epimorphism is split, every epimorphism splits. This is not an\n   instance because it would create an instance loop.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_split_epi", "description": "`is_split_epi f` is the assertion that `f` admits a section", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_split_epi.exists_split_epi", "description": "`is_split_epi f` is the assertion that `f` admits a section", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_iso_of_mono_of_is_split_epi", "description": "A split epi which is mono is an iso.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.section_is_split_mono", "description": "The section of a split epimorphism is itself a split monomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.functor.map.is_split_epi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.split_epi.map", "description": "Split epimorphisms are also absolute epimorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_split_mono.id_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.split_mono.map", "description": "Split monomorphisms are also absolute monomorphisms.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.split_mono.map_retraction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.is_split_epi.id_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.groupoid.of_trunc_split_mono", "description": "A category where every morphism has a `trunc` retraction is computably a groupo