ow_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "integrable_one_add_norm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "sqrt_one_add_norm_sq_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minpoly.min", "description": " The defining property of the minimal polynomial of an element `x`:\nit is the monic polynomial with smallest degree that has `x` as its root.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minpoly.eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minpoly.monic", "description": "A minimal polynomial is monic.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minpoly.aeval_ne_zero_of_dvd_not_unit_minpoly", "description": "If `a` strictly divides the minimal polynomial of `x`, then `x` cannot be a root for `a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minpoly.nat_degree_pos", "description": "The degree of a minimal polynomial, as a natural number, is positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minpoly.minpoly_alg_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minpoly.minpoly_alg_equiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minpoly.ne_one", "description": "A minimal polynomial is not `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minpoly.ne_zero", "description": "A minimal polynomial is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minpoly.irreducible", "description": "A minimal polynomial is irreducible.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minpoly.map_ne_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minpoly.aeval", "description": "An element is a root of its minimal polynomial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minpoly", "description": "Suppose `x : B`, where `B` is an `A`-algebra.\n\nThe minimal polynomial `minpoly A x` of `x`\nis a monic polynomial with coefficients in `A` of smallest degree that has `x` as its root,\nif such exists (`is_integral A x`) or zero otherwise.\n\nFor example, if `V` is a `\ud835\udd5c`-vector space for some field `\ud835\udd5c` and `f : V \u2192\u2097[\ud835\udd5c] V` then\nthe minimal polynomial of `f` is `minpoly \ud835\udd5c f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minpoly.subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minpoly.unique'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minpoly.eq_X_sub_C_of_algebra_map_inj", "description": " If `B/A` is an injective ring extension, and `a` is an element of `A`,\nthen the minimal polynomial of `algebra_map A B a` is `X - C a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minpoly.degree_pos", "description": "The degree of a minimal polynomial is positive.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minpoly.mem_range_of_degree_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "minpoly.not_is_unit", "description": "A minimal polynomial is not a unit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.quotient_structure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.prestructure", "description": "A prestructure is a first-order structure with a `setoid` equivalence relation on it,\n such that quotienting by that equivalence relation is still a structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.prestructure.to_structure", "description": "A prestructure is a first-order structure with a `setoid` equivalence relation on it,\n such that quotienting by that equivalence relation is still a structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.prestructure.fun_equiv", "description": "A prestructure is a first-order structure with a `setoid` equivalence relation on it,\n such that quotienting by that equivalence relation is still a structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.prestructure.rel_equiv", "description": "A prestructure is a first-order structure with a `setoid` equivalence relation on it,\n such that quotienting by that equivalence relation is still a structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.fun_map_quotient_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.rel_map_quotient_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "first_order.language.term.realize_quotient_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name":