ion": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mkq_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.mk_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient_rel_r_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.range_liftq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.has_quotient.quotient.has_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quot_equiv_of_eq_bot_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.mul_action'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.liftq", "description": " The map from the quotient of `M` by a submodule `p` to `M\u2082` induced by a linear map `f : M \u2192 M\u2082`\nvanishing on `p`, as a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient_bot.infinite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.ker_mkq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.is_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.distrib_mul_action'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.equiv", "description": " If `P` is a submodule of `M` and `Q` a submodule of `N`,\nand `f : M \u2243\u2097 N` maps `P` to `Q`, then `M \u29f8 P` is equivalent to `N \u29f8 Q`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quot_equiv_of_eq_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.nontrivial_of_lt_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.mk_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.le_comap_mkq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.equiv_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mapq_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.ker_liftq_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.ker_le_range_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.comap_mkq.rel_iso", "description": " The correspondence theorem for modules: there is an order isomorphism between submodules of the\nquotient of `M` by `p`, and submodules of `M` larger than `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient_top.unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.comap_liftq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.smul_zero_class'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.restrict_scalars_equiv_symm_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.liftq_span_singleton", "description": "Special case of `liftq` when `p` is the span of `x`. In this case, the condition on `f` simply\nbecomes vanishing at `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient_rel", "description": " The equivalence relation associated to a submodule `p`, defined by `x \u2248 y` iff `-x + y \u2208 p`.\n\nNote this is equivalent to `y - x \u2208 p`, but defined this way to be be defeq to the `add_subgroup`\nversion, where commutativity can't be assumed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mapq_comp", "description": " Given submodules `p \u2286 M`, `p\u2082 \u2286 M\u2082`, `p\u2083 \u2286 M\u2083` and maps `f : M \u2192 M\u2082`, `g : M\u2082 \u2192 M\u2083` inducing\n`mapq f : M \u29f8 p \u2192 M\u2082 \u29f8 p\u2082` and `mapq g : M\u2082 \u29f8 p\u2082 \u2192 M\u2083 \u29f8 p\u2083` then\n`mapq (g \u2218 f) = (mapq g) \u2218 (mapq f)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.has_quotient", "description": "The quotient of a module `M` by a submodule `p \u2286 M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.comap_mkq_embedding_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.liftq_mkq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.mk", "description": " Map associating to an element of `M` the corresponding element of `M/p`,\nwhen `p` is a submodule of `M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quot_hom_ext", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quot_equiv_of_eq", "description": "Quotienting by equal submodules gives linearly equivalent quotients.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.mk_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mapq_id", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mkq", "description": "The map from a module `M` to the quotient of `M` by a submodule `p` as a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mkq_map_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.mkq_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.quotient.restrict_scalars_equiv_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_separated.open_cover_tfae", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_separated_of_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_separated_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_separated_space_of_is_affine", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_separated.affine_open_cover_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_localization_basic_open_of_qcqs", "description": " If `U` is qcqs, then `\u0393(X, D(f)) \u2243 \u0393(X, U)_f` for every `f : \u0393(X, U)`.\nThis is known as the **Qcqs lemma** in [R. Vakil, *The rising sea*][RisingSea].", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_separated_eq_diagonal_is_quasi_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.category_theory.limits.pullback.snd.quasi_separated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_separated_eq_affine_property", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_separated.is_local_at_target", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_separated_space_of_quasi_separated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_separated_of_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.category_theory.limits.pullback.fst.quasi_separated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.exists_eq_pow_mul_of_is_affine_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_separated_eq_affine_property_diagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_separated_stable_under_composition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_separated_space_iff_quasi_separated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_separated_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_compact_affine_property_iff_quasi_separated_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_compact_affine_property_diagonal_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_separated_space_iff_affine", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.is_affine_open.is_quasi_separated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_separated_stable_under_base_change", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.exists_eq_pow_mul_of_is_compact_of_quasi_separated_space_aux", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_separated_respects_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_separated", "description": "A morphism is `quasi_separated` if diagonal map is quasi-compact.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.quasi_separated.diagonal_quasi_compact", "description": "A morphism is `quasi_separated` if diagonal map is quasi-compact.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebr