 E\u2082` is `inducing`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.base_set_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fiber_bundle.prod.topological_space", "description": " Equip the total space of the fiberwise product of two fiber bundles `E\u2081`, `E\u2082` with\nthe induced topology from the diagonal embedding into `total_space E\u2081 \u00d7 total_space E\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bundle.trivial.bundle.total_space.topological_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.prod.left_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fiber_bundle.pullback", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.prod.right_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fiber_bundle.prod", "description": "The product of two fiber bundles is a fiber bundle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pullback.continuous_lift", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bundle.trivial.fiber_bundle", "description": "Fiber bundle instance on the trivial bundle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bundle.pullback.topological_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pullback_topology", "description": "Definition of `pullback.total_space.topological_space`, which we make irreducible.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bundle.trivial.trivialization", "description": "Local trivialization for trivial bundle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.pullback", "description": "A fiber bundle trivialization can be pulled back to a trivialization on the pullback bundle.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pullback.total_space.topological_space", "description": " The topology on the total space of a pullback bundle is the coarsest topology for which both\nthe projections to the base and the map to the original bundle are continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.prod.continuous_inv_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bundle.trivial.eq_trivialization", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pullback.continuous_proj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.prod.inv_fun'", "description": " Given trivializations `e\u2081`, `e\u2082` for fiber bundles `E\u2081`, `E\u2082` over a base `B`, the inverse\nfunction for the construction `trivialization.prod`, the induced\ntrivialization for the fiberwise product of `E\u2081` and `E\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "bundle.trivial.trivialization_source", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.prod.continuous_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.prod.to_fun'", "description": " Given trivializations `e\u2081`, `e\u2082` for fiber bundles `E\u2081`, `E\u2082` over a base `B`, the forward\nfunction for the construction `trivialization.prod`, the induced\ntrivialization for the fiberwise product of `E\u2081` and `E\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "trivialization.prod", "description": " Given trivializations `e\u2081`, `e\u2082` for bundle types `E\u2081`, `E\u2082` over a base `B`, the induced\ntrivialization for the fiberwise product of `E\u2081` and `E\u2082`, whose base set is\n`e\u2081.base_set \u2229 e\u2082.base_set`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.general_linear_group.to_linear", "description": " An element of the matrix general linear group on `(n) [fintype n]` can be considered as an\nelement of the endomorphism general linear group on `n \u2192 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.special_linear_group.matrix.GL_pos.has_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.general_linear_group.ext", "description": "Not marked `@[ext]` as the `ext` tactic already solves this.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.GL_pos", "description": " This is the subgroup of `nxn` matrices with entries over a\nlinear ordered ring and positive determinant.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.general_linear_group.mk''", "description": "Given a matrix with unit determinant we get an element of `GL n R`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.GL_pos.has_distrib_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.GL_pos.has_neg", "description": " Formal operation of negation on general linear group on even cardinality `n` given by negating\neach element.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.special_linear_group.coe_to_GL_det", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.special_linear_group.coe_GL_pos_coe_GL_coe_matrix", "description": " Coercing a `special_linear_group` via `GL_pos` and `GL` is the same as coercing striaght to a\nmatrix.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.special_linear_group.to_GL_pos", "description": "`special_linear_group n R` embeds into `GL_pos n R`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.GL_pos.coe_neg_GL", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.GL_pos.coe_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.general_linear_group.to_linear_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.general_linear_group.coe_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.special_linear_group.has_coe_to_general_linear_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.special_linear_group.coe_GL_pos_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.special_linear_group.coe_to_GL_pos_to_GL_det", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.coe_plane_conformal_matrix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.special_linear_group.coe_eq_to_GL_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.general_linear_group.to_lin", "description": "The `GL n R` and `general_linear_group R n` groups are multiplicatively equivalent", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.GL_pos.coe_neg_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.general_linear_group.mk'", "description": "Given a matrix with invertible determinant we get an element of `GL n R`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.general_linear_group.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "This instance is here for convenience, but is not the simp-normal form.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.general_linear_group", "description": " `GL n R` is the group of `n` by `n` `R`-matrices with unit determinant.\nDefined as a subtype of matrices", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.general_linear_group.coe_to_linear", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.general_linear_group.coe_inv_det_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.general_linear_group.ext_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.general_linear_group.mk_of_det_ne_zero", "description": "Given a matrix with non-zero determinant over a field, we get an element of `GL n K`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.GL_pos.det_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.general_linear_group.det", "description": "The determinant of a unit matrix is itself a unit.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.general_linear_group.coe_det_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.mem_GL_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.special_linear_group.to_GL_pos_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.plane_conformal_matrix", "description": " The matrix [a, -b; b, a] (inspired by multiplication by a complex number); it is an element of\n$GL_2(R)$ if `a ^ 2 + b ^ 2` is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.general_linear_group.coe_fn_eq_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.general_linear_group.coe_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.general_linear_group.coe_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.Ico_filter_coprime_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_prime_pow_succ", "description": "When `p` is prime, then the totient of `p ^ (n + 1)` is `p ^ n * (p - 1)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_eq_mul_prod_factors", "description": "Euler's product formula for the totient function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_eq_div_factors_mul", "description": "Euler's product formula for the totient function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_eq_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_mul_prod_factors", "description": "Euler's product formula for the totient function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.sum_totient", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_super_multiplicative", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_eq_prod_factorization", "description": "Euler's product formula for the totient function.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_even", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.card_units_zmod_lt_sub_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.sum_totient'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.filter_coprime_Ico_eq_totient", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_prime_pow", "description": "When `p` is prime, then the totient of `p ^ n` is `p ^ (n - 1) * (p - 1)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.prime_iff_card_units", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_div_of_dvd", "description": "For `d \u2223 n`, the totient of `n/d` equals the number of values `k < n` such that `gcd n k = d`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_eq_card_lt_and_coprime", "description": "A characterisation of `nat.totient` that avoids `finset`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_gcd_mul_totient_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_mul_of_prime_of_not_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.card_units_eq_totient", "description": " Note this takes an explicit `fintype ((zmod n)\u02e3)` argument to avoid trouble with instance\ndiamonds.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_dvd_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_eq_card_coprime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient", "description": " Euler's totient function. This counts the number of naturals strictly less than `n` which are\ncoprime with `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_mul_of_prime_of_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_eq_iff_prime", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.totient_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.distrib_mul_action", "description": " If a monoid `M` distributively continuously acts on `\ud835\udd5c` and this action commutes with\nmultiplication on `\ud835\udd5c`, then it acts distributively on `weak_dual \ud835\udd5c E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_bilin.module'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_bilin.eval_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_bilin.continuous_of_continuous_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_bilin.embedding", "description": "The coercion `(\u03bb x y, B x y) : E \u2192 (F \u2192 \ud835\udd5c)` is an embedding.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_bilin.coe_fn_continuous", "description": "The coercion `(\u03bb x y, B x y) : E \u2192 (F \u2192 \ud835\udd5c)` is continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.continuous_of_continuous_eval", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_bilin.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_bilin.has_continuous_add", "description": "Addition in `weak_space B` is continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_bilin.topological_add_group", "description": " `weak_space B` is a `topological_add_group`, meaning that addition and negation are\ncontinuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_space.has_continuous_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_iff_forall_eval_tendsto_top_dual_pairing", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_space.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.eval_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.has_continuous_smul", "description": " If a monoid `M` distributively continuously acts on `\ud835\udd5c` and this action commutes with\nmultiplication on `\ud835\udd5c`, then it continuously acts on `weak_dual \ud835\udd5c E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.module'", "description": " If `\ud835\udd5c` is a topological module over a semiring `R` and scalar multiplication commutes with the\nmultiplication on `\ud835\udd5c`, then `weak_dual \ud835\udd5c E` is a module over `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_bilin.topological_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_bilin.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.has_coe_to_fun", "description": " Helper instance for when there's too many metavariables to apply `fun_like.has_coe_to_fun`\ndirectly.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "top_dual_pairing", "description": "The canonical pairing of a vector space and its topological dual.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_space.add_comm_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_space.map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_space.topological_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_bilin.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_bilin.has_continuous_smul", "description": "Scalar multiplication by `\ud835\udd5c` on `weak_bilin B` is continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.coe_fn_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_bilin.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.has_continuous_const_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual", "description": " The weak star topology is the topology coarsest topology on `E \u2192L[\ud835\udd5c] \ud835\udd5c` such that all\nfunctionals `\u03bb v, top_dual_pairing \ud835\udd5c E v x` are continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dual_pairing_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_space.coe_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_bilin.tendsto_iff_forall_eval_tendsto", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.mul_action", "description": " If a monoid `M` distributively continuously acts on `\ud835\udd5c` and this action commutes with\nmultiplication on `\ud835\udd5c`, then it acts on `weak_dual \ud835\udd5c E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.weak_dual.continuous_linear_map_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_bilin", "description": "The space `E` equipped with the weak topology induced by the bilinear form `B`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.has_continuous_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.t2_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_space", "description": " The weak topology is the topology coarsest topology on `E` such that all\nfunctionals `\u03bb x, top_dual_pairing \ud835\udd5c E v x` are continuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_dual.topological_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "weak_space.map", "description": " A continuous linear map from `E` to `F` is still continuous when `E` and `F` are equipped with\ntheir weak topologies.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.is_torsion.not_torsion_free", "description": "A nontrivial additive torsion group is not torsion-free.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_torsion_free.add_subgroup", "description": "Subgroups of additive torsion-free groups are additively torsion-free.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_monoid.add_torsion.is_torsion", "description": "Additive torsion submonoids are additively torsion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.is_torsion_free", "description": "A predicate on a monoid saying that only 1 is of finite order.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.is_torsion.torsion_add_equiv_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_torsion.of_surjective", "description": "The image of a surjective torsion group homomorphism is torsion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_is_torsion.of_surjective", "description": "The image of a surjective additive torsion group homomorphism is torsion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_torsion_of_finite", "description": "Finite groups are torsion groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_torsion.not_torsion_free", "description": "A nontrivial torsion group is not torsion-free.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_monoid.torsion.is_torsion", "description": "Torsion submonoids are torsion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_torsion.exponent_exists", "description": "The group exponent exists for any bounded additive torsion group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_torsion.add_group", "description": "Torsion additive monoids are really additive groups", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.is_torsion.torsion_add_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.is_torsion.module_of_torsion", "description": "A module whose scalars are additively torsion is additively torsion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_group.primary_component", "description": "The `p`-primary component is the subgroup of elements with order prime-power of `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_torsion.extension_closed", "description": "Torsion groups are closed under extensions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_monoid.primary_component.disjoint", "description": "The `p`- and `q`-primary components are disjoint for `p \u2260 q`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_group.torsion", "description": "The torsion subgroup of an abelian group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_is_torsion.extension_closed", "description": "Additive torsion groups are closed under extensions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_add_torsion_of_finite", "description": "Finite additive groups are additive torsion groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.is_torsion.module_of_finite", "description": "A module with a finite ring of scalars is additively torsion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_monoid.primary_component.exists_order_of_eq_prime_nsmul", "description": "Elements of the `p`-primary component have additive order `p^n` for some `n`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.torsion", "description": "The torsion subgroup of an additive abelian group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_torsion.subgroup", "description": "Subgroups of torsion groups are torsion groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_torsion.quotient_iff", "description": "The image of a quotient is torsion iff the group is torsion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_is_torsion_free.quotient_torsion", "description": "Quotienting a group by its additive torsion subgroup yields an additive torsion free group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "torsion.of_torsion", "description": "Torsion submonoids of a torsion submonoid are isomorphic to the submonoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.not_is_torsion_free_iff", "description": "A nontrivial monoid is not torsion-free if any nontrivial element has finite order.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.is_torsion.torsion_add_equiv", "description": "An additive torsion monoid is isomorphic to its torsion submonoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.is_torsion.torsion_eq_top", "description": "The additive torsion submonoid of an additive torsion monoid is `\u22a4`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_monoid.primary_component.disjoint", "description": "The `p`- and `q`-primary components are disjoint for `p \u2260 q`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_monoid.primary_component", "description": "The `p`-primary component is the submonoid of elements with order prime-power of `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_monoid.torsion", "description": "The torsion submonoid of a commutative monoid.\n\n(Note that by `monoid.is_torsion.group` torsion monoids are truthfully groups.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_torsion.exponent_exists", "description": "The group exponent exists for any bounded torsion group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_torsion_free.quotient_torsion", "description": "Quotienting a group by its torsion subgroup yields a torsion free group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_is_torsion.quotient_iff", "description": "The image of a quotient is additively torsion iff the group is torsion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.is_torsion_free", "description": "A predicate on an additive monoid saying that only 0 is of finite order.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.is_torsion", "description": "A predicate on a monoid saying that all elements are of finite order.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_monoid.add_torsion", "description": "The torsion submonoid of an additive commutative monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.is_torsion.torsion_mul_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_monoid.torsion.of_torsion", "description": "Additive torsion submonoids of an additive torsion submonoid are isomorphic to the submonoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_group.torsion_eq_torsion_submonoid", "description": "The torsion submonoid of an abelian group equals the torsion subgroup as a submonoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_torsion_free.prod", "description": "Direct products of torsion free groups are torsion free.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exponent_exists.is_torsion", "description": "If a group exponent exists, the group is torsion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.is_torsion.torsion_eq_top", "description": "The torsion submonoid of a torsion monoid is `\u22a4`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.not_is_torsion_iff", "description": "An additive monoid is not a torsion monoid if it has an element of infinite order.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.not_is_torsion_iff", "description": "A monoid is not a torsion monoid if it has an element of infinite order.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_monoid.primary_component", "description": "The `p`-primary component is the submonoid of elements with additive order prime-power of `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.is_torsion.torsion_mul_equiv", "description": "A torsion monoid is isomorphic to its torsion submonoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.add_torsion_eq_add_torsion_submonoid", "description": "The additive torsion submonoid of an abelian group equals the torsion subgroup as a submonoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_torsion_free.not_torsion", "description": "A nontrivial torsion-free group is not torsion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_group.primary_component.is_p_group", "description": "The `p`-primary component is a `p` group.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_torsion.add_subgroup", "description": "Subgroups of additive torsion groups are additive torsion groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.primary_component", "description": "The `p`-primary component is the subgroup of elements with additive order prime-power of `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_group.primary_component_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_torsion_free.subgroup", "description": "Subgroups of torsion-free groups are torsion-free.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_monoid.primary_component.exists_order_of_eq_prime_pow", "description": "Elements of the `p`-primary component have order `p^n` for some `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.is_torsion_free.not_torsion", "description": "A nontrivial torsion-free additive group is not torsion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_monoid.primary_component_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_group.primary_component_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_torsion.group", "description": "Torsion monoids are really groups.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.not_is_torsion_free_iff", "description": "An additive monoid is not torsion free if any nontrivial element has finite order.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monoid.is_torsion.torsion_mul_equiv_symm_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exponent_exists.is_add_torsion", "description": "If a group exponent exists, the group is additively torsion.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_comm_monoid.primary_component_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.is_torsion_free.prod", "description": "Direct products of additive torsion free groups are torsion free.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid.is_torsion", "description": "A predicate on an additive monoid saying that all elements are of finite order.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.pi", "description": " Given a finitely supported function `f : \u03b9 \u2192\u2080 finset \u03b1`, one can define the finset\n`f.pi` of all finitely supported functions whose value at `i` is in `f i` for all `i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.mem_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mem_finsupp_iff_of_support_subset", "description": "When `t` is supported on `s`, `f \u2208 s.finsupp t` precisely means that `f` is pointwise in `t`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.card_finsupp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.mem_finsupp_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.finsupp", "description": "Finitely supported product of finsets.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finsupp.card_pi", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjoint_triangle_lift", "description": "The adjoint triangle theorem: Suppose `U : B \u2964 C` has a left adjoint `F` such that each counit\n`\u03b5_X : FUX \u27f6 X` is a regular epimorphism. Then if a category `A` has coequalizers of reflexive\npairs, then a functor `R : A \u2964 B` has a left adjoint if the composite `R \u22d9 U` does.\n\nNote the converse is true (with weaker assumptions), by `adjunction.comp`.\nSee https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/adjoint+triangle+theorem", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monadic_adjoint_triangle_lift", "description": "If `R \u22d9 U` has a left adjoint, the domain of `R` has reflexive coequalizers and `U` is a monadic\nfunctor, then `R` has a left adjoint.\nThis is a special case of `adjoint_triangle_lift` which is often more useful in practice.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lift_adjoint.construct_left_adjoint", "description": "Construct the left adjoint to `R`, with object map `construct_left_adjoint_obj`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjoint_square_lift", "description": "Suppose we have a commutative square of functors\n\n      Q\n    A \u2192 B\n  U \u2193   \u2193 V\n    C \u2192 D\n      R\n\nwhere `U` has a left adjoint, `A` has reflexive coequalizers and `V` has a left adjoint such that\neach component of the counit is a regular epi.\nThen `Q` has a left adjoint if `R` has a left adjoint.\n\nSee https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/adjoint+lifting+theorem", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monadic_adjoint_square_lift", "description": "Suppose we have a commutative square of functors\n\n      Q\n    A \u2192 B\n  U \u2193   \u2193 V\n    C \u2192 D\n      R\n\nwhere `U` has a left adjoint, `A` has reflexive coequalizers and `V` is monadic.\nThen `Q` has a left adjoint if `R` has a left adjoint.\n\nSee https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/adjoint+lifting+theorem", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lift_adjoint.construct_left_adjoint_equiv", "description": "The homset equivalence which helps show that `R` is a right adjoint.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lift_adjoint.other_map", "description": "(Implementation)\nTo construct the left adjoint, we use the coequalizer of `F' U \u03b5_Y` with the composite\n\n`F' U F U X \u27f6 F' U F U R F U' X \u27f6 F' U R F' U X \u27f6 F' U X`\n\nwhere the first morphism is `F' U F \u03b9_UX`, the second is `F' U \u03b5_RF'UX`, and the third is `\u03b4_F'UX`.\nWe will show that this coequalizer exists and that it forms the object map for a left adjoint to\n`R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lift_adjoint.counit_coequalises", "description": "To show that `\u03b5_X` is a coequalizer for `(FU\u03b5_X, \u03b5_FUX)`, it suffices to assume it's always a\ncoequalizer of something (i.e. a regular epi).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lift_adjoint.other_map.category_theory.is_reflexive_pair", "description": "`(F'U\u03b5_X, other_map X)` is a reflexive pair: in particular if `A` has reflexive coequalizers then\nit has a coequalizer.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lift_adjoint.construct_left_adjoint_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lift_adjoint.construct_left_adjoint_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.lift_adjoint.construct_left_adjoint_obj", "description": "Construct the object part of the desired left adjoint as the coequalizer of `F'U\u03b5_Y` with\n`other_map`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_le.countable_Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "countable_Inter_filter_principal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "countable_bInter_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_eq.countable_Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_le.countable_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_eq.countable_bUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "countable_Inter_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_le.countable_bUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.countable_generate", "description": "`filter.countable_generate g` is the greatest `countable_Inter_filter` containing `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.comap.countable_Inter_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.mem_of_countable_Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_countable_ball", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.countable_Inter_of_countable_Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "countable_sInter_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.countable_generate.countable_Inter_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_eq.countable_Union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.map.countable_Inter_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.of_countable_Inter", "description": " Construct a filter with countable intersection property. This constructor deduces\n`filter.univ_sets` and `filter.inter_sets` from the countable intersection property.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "countable_Inter_filter_sup", "description": "Supremum of two `countable_Inter_filter`s is a `countable_Inter_filter`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.le_countable_generate_iff_of_countable_Inter_filter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.countable_generate_is_greatest", "description": "`countable_generate g` is the greatest `countable_Inter_filter` containing `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "countable_Inter_filter", "description": " A filter `l` has the countable intersection property if for any countable collection\nof sets `s \u2208 l` their intersection belongs to `l` as well.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "countable_Inter_filter.countable_sInter_mem'", "description": " A filter `l` has the countable intersection property if for any countable collection\nof sets `s \u2208 l` their intersection belongs to `l` as well.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_countable_forall", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_eq.countable_bInter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.mem_countable_generate_iff", "description": " A set is in the `countable_Inter_filter` generated by `g` if and only if\nit contains a countable intersection of elements of `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "countable_Inter_filter_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_le.countable_bInter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.countable_generate_sets", "description": " `filter.countable_generate_sets g` is the (sets of the)\ngreatest `countable_Inter_filter` containing `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.countable_generate_sets.basic", "description": " `filter.countable_generate_sets g` is the (sets of the)\ngreatest `countable_Inter_filter` containing `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.countable_generate_sets.univ", "description": " `filter.countable_generate_sets g` is the (sets of the)\ngreatest `countable_Inter_filter` containing `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.countable_generate_sets.superset", "description": " `filter.countable_generate_sets g` is the (sets of the)\ngreatest `countable_Inter_filter` containing `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.countable_generate_sets.Inter", "description": " `filter.countable_generate_sets g` is the (sets of the)\ngreatest `countable_Inter_filter` containing `g`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "countable_Inter_filter_inf", "description": " Infimum of two `countable_Inter_filter`s is a `countable_Inter_filter`. This is useful, e.g.,\nto automatically get an instance for `residual \u03b1 \u2293 \ud835\udcdf s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "countable_Inter_filter_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale_part", "description": " Any `\u2115`-indexed stochastic process can be written as the sum of a martingale and a predictable\nprocess. This is the martingale. See `predictable_part` for the predictable process.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.adapted_martingale_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale_part_bdd_difference", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.predictable_part_add_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale_part_add_predictable_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.predictable_part_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale_martingale_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale_part_eq_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.predictable_part_bdd_difference", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.adapted_predictable_part'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.predictable_part", "description": " Any `\u2115`-indexed stochastic process can be written as the sum of a martingale and a predictable\nprocess. This is the predictable process. See `martingale_part` for the martingale.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.adapted_predictable_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.integrable_martingale_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.martingale_part_add_ae_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.standard_one_dim_isocrystal.frobenius_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.standard_one_dim_isocrystal", "description": "Type synonym for `K(p, k)` to carry the standard 1-dimensional isocrystal structure\nof slope `m : \u2124`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.inv_pair\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.standard_one_dim_isocrystal.isocrystal", "description": "The standard one-dimensional isocrystal of slope `m : \u2124` is an isocrystal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.isocrystal_classification", "description": " A one-dimensional isocrystal over an algebraically closed field\nadmits an isomorphism to one of the standard (indexed by `m : \u2124`) one-dimensional isocrystals.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.inv_pair\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.isocrystal", "description": "An isocrystal is a vector space over the field `K(p, k)` additionally equipped with a\nFrobenius-linear automorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.isocrystal.to_module", "description": "An isocrystal is a vector space over the field `K(p, k)` additionally equipped with a\nFrobenius-linear automorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.isocrystal.frob", "description": "An isocrystal is a vector space over the field `K(p, k)` additionally equipped with a\nFrobenius-linear automorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.fraction_ring.module", "description": "A helper instance for type class inference.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.isocrystal.frobenius", "description": "Project the Frobenius automorphism from an isocrystal. Denoted by `\u03a6(p, k)` when V can be inferred.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.standard_one_dim_isocrystal.add_comm_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.fraction_ring.frobenius", "description": "The Frobenius automorphism of `k` induces an automorphism of `K`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.isocrystal_hom", "description": "A homomorphism between isocrystals respects the Frobenius map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.isocrystal_hom.to_linear_map", "description": "A homomorphism between isocrystals respects the Frobenius map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.isocrystal_hom.frob_equivariant", "description": "A homomorphism between isocrystals respects the Frobenius map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.isocrystal_equiv", "description": "An isomorphism between isocrystals respects the Frobenius map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.isocrystal_equiv.to_linear_equiv", "description": "An isomorphism between isocrystals respects the Frobenius map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.isocrystal_equiv.frob_equivariant", "description": "An isomorphism between isocrystals respects the Frobenius map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.fraction_ring.frobenius_ring_hom", "description": "The Frobenius automorphism of `k` induces an endomorphism of `K`. For notation purposes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "witt_vector.standard_one_dim_isocrystal.module", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.with_bot.one_le_iff_zero_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.with_bot.add_eq_one_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.with_bot.add_one_le_of_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.with_bot.coe_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.with_bot.add_eq_three_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.with_bot.lt_one_iff_le_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.with_bot.add_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.with_bot.add_eq_two_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.with_bot.lt_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.prove_unsat_ef", "description": "Given a (([],les) : clause), return the expr of a term (t : clause.unsat ([],les)).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.prove_neg", "description": "Return expr of proof that given int is negative", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.forall_mem_replicate_zero_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.prove_unsats", "description": "Given a (cs : list clause), return the expr of a term (t : clauses.unsat cs)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.prove_forall_mem_eq_zero", "description": "Return expr of proof that elements of (replicate is.length 0) are all 0", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.prove_unsat_lin_comb", "description": "Return expr of proof that the combination of linear constraints\n   represented by ks and ts is unsatisfiable", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "omega.prove_unsat", "description": "Given a (c : clause), return the expr of a term (t : clause.unsat c)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.mul_divisors_filter_prime_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_prime_pow.min_fac_pow_factorization_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_prime_pow_iff_min_fac_pow_factorization_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_prime_pow_iff_unique_prime_dvd", "description": " An equivalent definition for prime powers: `n` is a prime power iff there is a unique prime\ndividing it.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_ord_compl_eq_one_iff_is_prime_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_prime_pow.exists_ord_compl_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_prime_pow_iff_factorization_eq_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.coprime.is_prime_pow_dvd_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_prime_pow_pow_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_prime_pow_iff_card_support_factorization_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_prime_pow_of_min_fac_pow_factorization_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.gcd_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.gcd_dedup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.gcd_ndinsert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.gcd", "description": "Greatest common divisor of a multiset", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.gcd_ndunion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.lcm_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.lcm_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.extract_gcd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.lcm_ndunion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.lcm_dedup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.gcd_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.gcd_dvd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.dvd_gcd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.gcd_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.normalize_lcm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.lcm_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.lcm_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.gcd_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.extract_gcd'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.lcm_union", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.normalize_gcd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.gcd_singleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.dvd_lcm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.lcm_ndinsert", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.gcd_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.lcm_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.lcm", "description": "Least common multiple of a multiset", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.gcd_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.lcm_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.gcd_map_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.lcm_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "scope_trace", "description": "This function has a native implementation that displays in the given position all trace messages used in f.\n  The arguments line and col are filled by the elaborator.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "try_for", "description": "This function has a native implementation where\nthe thunk is interrupted if it takes more than 'max' \"heartbeats\" to compute it.\nThe heartbeat is approx. the maximum number of memory allocations (in thousands) performed by 'f ()'.\nThis is a deterministic way of interrupting long running tasks.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "trace", "description": "This function has a native implementation that displays the given string in the regular output stream.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "trace_call_stack", "description": "This function has a native implementation that shows the VM call stack.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "unchecked_cast", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "undefined_core", "description": "Throws an exception when it is evaluated.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "try_for_time", "description": "This function has a native implementation where\nthe thunk is interrupted if it takes more than `max` milliseconds to compute it.\nThis is useful due to the variance in the number of heartbeats used by tactics.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "trace_val", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "id_tag", "description": "For tactics to tag the proofs they construct.\nThe tag is `unit` but is intended to be encoded by a constant, e.g.\ndef tagged_proof.ring : unit := ()", "p": "core"}, {"name": "timeit", "description": "This function has a native implementation that tracks time.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "undefined", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "star_linear_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "self_adjoint_part", "description": "The self-adjoint part of an element of a star module, as a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_nat_cast_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_linear_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skew_adjoint_part", "description": "The skew-adjoint part of an element of a star module, as a linear map.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_module.self_adjoint_part_add_skew_adjoint_part", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_int_cast_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_rat_cast_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_rat_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skew_adjoint.submodule", "description": "The skew-adjoint elements of a star module, as a submodule.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra_map_star_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "self_adjoint.submodule", "description": "The self-adjoint elements of a star module, as a submodule.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "self_adjoint_part_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_inv_nat_cast_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_inv_int_cast_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "skew_adjoint_part_apply_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_module.decompose_prod_adjoint", "description": " The decomposition of elements of a star module into their self- and skew-adjoint parts,\nas a linear equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_module.decompose_prod_adjoint_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_linear_equiv", "description": " If `A` is a module over a commutative `R` with compatible actions,\nthen `star` is a semilinear equivalence.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "star_module.decompose_prod_adjoint_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.coe_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.coe_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.vadd_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.vadd_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.smul_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.has_smul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.is_scalar_tower", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.mul_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.vadd_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.has_vadd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.smul_comm_class", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.smul_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.is_central_scalar", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "function.embedding.add_action", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cgf_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_fun.cgf_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.central_moment_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.mgf_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measure_ge_le_exp_mul_mgf", "description": "**Chernoff bound** on the upper tail of a real random variable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cgf_undef", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.central_moment_one'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cgf", "description": "Cumulant generating function of a real random variable `X`: `\u03bb t, log \u03bc[exp(t*X)]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cgf_const'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cgf_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cgf_zero_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_fun.integrable_exp_mul_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.mgf_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.moment_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.mgf_undef", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.mgf", "description": "Moment generating function of a real random variable `X`: `\u03bb t, \u03bc[exp(t*X)]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.mgf_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.mgf_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_fun.mgf_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.mgf_const'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.Indep_fun.integrable_exp_mul_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.mgf_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.central_moment_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cgf_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.mgf_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.mgf_zero_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cgf_zero_measure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.central_moment_two_eq_variance", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_fun.mgf_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_fun.exp_mul", "description": "This is a trivial application of `indep_fun.comp` but it will come up frequently.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_fun.mgf_add'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.mgf_pos'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.indep_fun.cgf_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.mgf_zero_fun", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.cgf_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measure_ge_le_exp_cgf", "description": "**Chernoff bound** on the upper tail of a real random variable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ae_strongly_measurable_exp_mul_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.moment", "description": "Moment of a real random variable, `\u03bc[X ^ p]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measure_le_le_exp_cgf", "description": "**Chernoff bound** on the lower tail of a real random variable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.ae_strongly_measurable_exp_mul_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.measure_le_le_exp_mul_mgf", "description": "**Chernoff bound** on the lower tail of a real random variable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "probability_theory.central_moment", "description": "Central moment of a real random variable, `\u03bc[(X - \u03bc[X]) ^ p]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.at_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.sq_one", "description": "The square of the symbol is 1 if `p \u2224 a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.mod_four_ne_three_of_sq_eq_neg_sq'", "description": "If two nonzero squares are negatives of each other in `zmod p`, then `p % 4 \u2260 3`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.eq_one_iff", "description": "When `p \u2224 a`, then `legendre_sym p a = 1` iff `a` is a square mod `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.mul", "description": "The Legendre symbol is multiplicative in `a` for `p` fixed.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.euler_criterion", "description": "Euler's Criterion: a nonzero `a : zmod p` is a square if and only if `x ^ (p / 2) = 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.eq_neg_one_iff", "description": "`legendre_sym p a = -1` iff `a` is a nonsquare mod `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.eq_neg_one_iff_not_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.eq_one_of_sq_sub_mul_sq_eq_zero", "description": " The Legendre symbol `legendre_sym p a = 1` if there is a solution in `\u2124/p\u2124`\nof the equation `x^2 - a*y^2 = 0` with `y \u2260 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.mod_four_ne_three_of_sq_eq_neg_sq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.eq_pow", "description": "We have the congruence `legendre_sym p a \u2261 a ^ (p / 2) mod p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym", "description": " The Legendre symbol of `a : \u2124` and a prime `p`, `legendre_sym p a`,\nis an integer defined as\n\n* `0` if `a` is `0` modulo `p`;\n* `1` if `a` is a nonzero square modulo `p`\n* `-1` otherwise.\n\nNote the order of the arguments! The advantage of the order chosen here is\nthat `legendre_sym p` is a multiplicative function `\u2124 \u2192 \u2124`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.mod", "description": "The Legendre symbol depends only on `a` mod `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.at_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.eq_neg_one_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.prime_dvd_of_eq_neg_one", "description": "If `legendre_sym p a = -1` and `p` divides `x^2 - a*y^2`, then `p` must divide `x` and `y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.mod_four_ne_three_of_sq_eq_neg_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.sq_one'", "description": "The Legendre symbol of `a^2` at `p` is 1 if `p \u2224 a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.eq_one_of_sq_sub_mul_sq_eq_zero'", "description": " The Legendre symbol `legendre_sym p a = 1` if there is a solution in `\u2124/p\u2124`\nof the equation `x^2 - a*y^2 = 0` with `x \u2260 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.pow_div_two_eq_neg_one_or_one", "description": "If `a : zmod p` is nonzero, then `a^(p/2)` is either `1` or `-1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.card_sqrts", "description": "The number of square roots of `a` modulo `p` is determined by the Legendre symbol.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.exists_sq_eq_neg_one_iff", "description": "`-1` is a square in `zmod p` iff `p` is not congruent to `3` mod `4`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.eq_zero_iff", "description": "The Legendre symbol of `p` and `a` is zero iff `p \u2223 a`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.eq_one_or_neg_one", "description": "If `p \u2224 a`, then `legendre_sym p a` is `1` or `-1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.eq_zero_mod_of_eq_neg_one", "description": " If `legendre_sym p a = -1`, then the only solution of `x^2 - a*y^2 = 0` in `\u2124/p\u2124`\nis the trivial one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "zmod.euler_criterion_units", "description": "Euler's Criterion: A unit `x` of `zmod p` is a square if and only if `x ^ (p / 2) = 1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.hom", "description": "The Legendre symbol is a homomorphism of monoids with zero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.eq_one_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "legendre_sym.at_neg_one", "description": "`legendre_sym p (-1)` is given by `\u03c7\u2084 p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_idempotent_of_compact_t2_of_continuous_mul_left", "description": " Any nonempty compact Hausdorff semigroup where right-multiplication is continuous contains\nan idempotent, i.e. an `m` such that `m * m = m`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_idempotent_of_compact_t2_of_continuous_add_left", "description": "Any nonempty compact Hausdorff additive semigroup where right-addition is continuous\ncontains an idempotent, i.e. an `m` such that `m + m = m`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_idempotent_in_compact_add_subsemigroup", "description": "A version of\n`exists_idempotent_of_compact_t2_of_continuous_add_left` where the idempotent lies in some specified\nnonempty compact additive subsemigroup.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "exists_idempotent_in_compact_subsemigroup", "description": " A version of `exists_idempotent_of_compact_t2_of_continuous_mul_left` where the idempotent lies\nin some specified nonempty compact subsemigroup.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "units.is_smul_regular", "description": "Any element in `R\u02e3` is `M`-regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.of_mul_eq_one", "description": "An element of `R` admitting a left inverse is `M`-regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.smul_iff", "description": " An element is `M`-regular if and only if multiplying it on the left by an `M`-regular element\nis `M`-regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.mul_iff", "description": "A product is `M`-regular if and only if the factors are.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.of_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_left_regular.is_smul_regular", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.zero", "description": "The element `0` is `M`-regular when `M` is trivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.not_zero", "description": "The `0` element is not `M`-regular, on a non-trivial module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_unit.is_smul_regular", "description": "A unit is `M`-regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.of_smul", "description": " If an element `b` becomes `M`-regular after multiplying it on the left by an `M`-regular\nelement, then `b` is `M`-regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.is_right_regular", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular", "description": " An `M`-regular element is an element `c` such that multiplication on the left by `c` is an\ninjective map `M \u2192 M`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_right_regular.is_smul_regular", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.pow_iff", "description": "An element `a` is `M`-regular if and only if a positive power of `a` is `M`-regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.mul_iff_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.subsingleton", "description": "The element `0` is `M`-regular if and only if `M` is trivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.of_smul_eq_one", "description": "An element of `S` admitting a left inverse in `R` is `M`-regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular_of_group", "description": " An element of a group acting on a Type is regular. This relies on the availability\nof the inverse given by groups, since there is no `left_cancel_smul` typeclass.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.not_zero_iff", "description": "The `0` element is not `M`-regular, on a non-trivial module.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.zero_iff_subsingleton", "description": "The element `0` is `M`-regular if and only if `M` is trivial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.smul", "description": "The product of `M`-regular elements is `M`-regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.is_left_regular", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_right_regular_iff", "description": "Right-regular multiplication on `R` is equivalent to `R\u1d50\u1d52\u1d56`-regularity of `R` itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.one", "description": "One is `M`-regular always.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.pow", "description": "Any power of an `M`-regular element is `M`-regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_smul_regular.mul_and_mul_iff", "description": " Two elements `a` and `b` are `M`-regular if and only if both products `a * b` and `b * a`\nare `M`-regular.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_left_regular_iff", "description": "Left-regular multiplication on `R` is equivalent to `R`-regularity of `R` itself.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.projective_spectrum.structure_sheaf.section_subring.neg_mem'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.section_in_basic_open", "description": "Given a point `x` corresponding to a homogeneous prime ideal, there is a (dependent) function\nsuch that, for any `f` in the homogeneous localization at `x`, it returns the obvious section in the\nbasic open set `D(f.denom)`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.germ_comp_stalk_to_fiber_ring_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj.to_LocallyRingedSpace", "description": "`Proj` of a graded ring as a `LocallyRingedSpace`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.projective_spectrum.structure_sheaf.is_fraction", "description": "The predicate saying that a dependent function on an open `U` is realised as a fixed fraction\n`r / s` of *same grading* in each of the stalks (which are localizations at various prime ideals).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.homogeneous_localization_to_stalk", "description": "Given any point `x` and `f` in the homogeneous localization at `x`, there is an element in the\nstalk at `x` obtained by `section_in_basic_open`. This is the inverse of `stalk_to_fiber_ring_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.stalk_to_fiber_ring_hom_germ'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.stalk_to_fiber_ring_hom_germ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.open_to_localization", "description": " The ring homomorphism that takes a section of the structure sheaf of `Proj` on the open set `U`,\nimplemented as a subtype of dependent functions to localizations at homogeneous prime ideals, and\nevaluates the section on the point corresponding to a given homogeneous prime ideal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.projective_spectrum.structure_sheaf.structure_sheaf_in_Type", "description": "The structure sheaf (valued in `Type`, not yet `CommRing`) is the subsheaf consisting of\nfunctions satisfying `is_locally_fraction`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.projective_spectrum.structure_sheaf.section_subring.zero_mem'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.projective_spectrum.structure_sheaf.comm_ring_structure_sheaf_in_Type_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.stalk_to_fiber_ring_hom", "description": " The ring homomorphism from the stalk of the structure sheaf of `Proj` at a point corresponding\nto a homogeneous prime ideal `x` to the *homogeneous localization* at `x`,\nformed by gluing the `open_to_localization` maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.projective_spectrum.structure_sheaf.section_subring.mul_mem'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.projective_spectrum.structure_sheaf.structure_presheaf_in_CommRing", "description": "The structure presheaf, valued in `CommRing`, constructed by dressing up the `Type` valued\nstructure presheaf.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.projective_spectrum.Proj.structure_sheaf", "description": "The structure sheaf on `Proj` \ud835\udc9c, valued in `CommRing`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.res_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.projective_spectrum.structure_sheaf.section_subring.one_mem'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.projective_spectrum.structure_sheaf.structure_presheaf_comp_forget", "description": "Some glue, verifying that that structure presheaf valued in `CommRing` agrees with the `Type`\nvalued structure presheaf.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.projective_spectrum.structure_sheaf.structure_presheaf_in_CommRing_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj.to_SheafedSpace", "description": "`Proj` of a graded ring as a `SheafedSpace`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.homogeneous_localization.mem_basic_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.projective_spectrum.structure_sheaf.section_subring.add_mem'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.projective_spectrum.structure_sheaf.structure_presheaf_in_CommRing_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.projective_spectrum.structure_sheaf.is_locally_fraction", "description": "We will define the structure sheaf as the subsheaf of all dependent functions in\n`\u03a0 x : U, homogeneous_localization \ud835\udc9c x` consisting of those functions which can locally be expressed\nas a ratio of `A` of same grading.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.projective_spectrum.structure_sheaf.is_fraction_prelocal", "description": "The predicate `is_fraction` is \"prelocal\", in the sense that if it holds on `U` it holds on any open\nsubset `V` of `U`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.Proj.stalk_iso'", "description": "Using `homogeneous_localization_to_stalk`, we construct a ring isomorphism between stalk at `x`\nand homogeneous localization at `x` for any point `x` in `Proj`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebraic_geometry.projective_spectrum.structure_sheaf.sections_subring", "description": "The functions satisfying `is_locally_fraction` form a subring of all dependent functions\n`\u03a0 x : U, homogeneous_localization \ud835\udc9c x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "solvable_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derived_series_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup_solvable_of_solvable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "solvable_of_ker_le_range", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derived_series", "description": "The derived series of the group `G`, obtained by starting from the subgroup `\u22a4` and repeatedly\n taking the commutator of the previous subgroup with itself for `n` times.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_solvable_of_subsingleton", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derived_series_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "solvable_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_derived_series_le_derived_series", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "solvable_of_solvable_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_simple_group.derived_series_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.fin_5_not_solvable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_simple_group.comm_iff_is_solvable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derived_series_normal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derived_series_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_solvable_of_top_eq_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "derived_series_le_map_derived_series", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_solvable_of_mem_derived_series", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.perm.not_solvable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "solvable_quotient_of_solvable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "map_derived_series_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_solvable_of_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_solvable_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_solvable", "description": "A group `G` is solvable if its derived series is eventually trivial. We use this definition\n because it's the most convenient one to work with.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_solvable.solvable", "description": "A group `G` is solvable if its derived series is eventually trivial. We use this definition\n because it's the most convenient one to work with.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "comm_group.is_solvable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_o_exp_neg_mul_rpow_at_top", "description": "`exp (-a * x) = o(x ^ s)` as `x \u2192 \u221e`, for any positive `a` and real `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_rpow_div_mul_add", "description": " The function `x ^ (a / (b * x + c))` tends to `1` at `+\u221e`, for any real numbers `a`, `b`, and\n`c` such that `b` is nonzero.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_log_div_rpow_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.is_Theta_cpow_const_rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_log_mul_rpow_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.is_Theta_cpow_rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_o_rpow_exp_pos_mul_at_top", "description": "`x ^ s = o(exp(b * x))` as `x \u2192 \u221e` for any real `s` and positive `b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_rpow_mul_exp_neg_mul_at_top_nhds_0", "description": "The function `x ^ s * exp (-b * x)` tends to `0` at `+\u221e`, for any real `s` and `b > 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_o_log_rpow_rpow_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_o_rpow_exp_at_top", "description": "`x ^ s = o(exp x)` as `x \u2192 \u221e` for any real `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.is_Theta_exp_arg_mul_im", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_o_abs_log_rpow_rpow_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.tendsto_rpow_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_o_zpow_exp_pos_mul_at_top", "description": "`x ^ k = o(exp(b * x))` as `x \u2192 \u221e` for any integer `k` and positive `b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.is_o.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_exp_div_rpow_at_top", "description": "The function `exp(x) / x ^ s` tends to `+\u221e` at `+\u221e`, for any real number `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_rpow_div", "description": "The function `x ^ (1 / x)` tends to `1` at `+\u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_o_log_rpow_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.is_O.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_rpow_neg_div", "description": "The function `x ^ (-1 / x)` tends to `1` at `+\u221e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_exp_mul_div_rpow_at_top", "description": "The function `exp (b * x) / x ^ s` tends to `+\u221e` at `+\u221e`, for any real `s` and `b > 0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nnreal.tendsto_rpow_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_rpow_neg_at_top", "description": "The function `x ^ (-y)` tends to `0` at `+\u221e` for any positive real `y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_rpow_at_top", "description": "The function `x ^ y` tends to `+\u221e` at `+\u221e` for any positive real `y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_o_pow_exp_pos_mul_at_top", "description": "`x ^ k = o(exp(b * x))` as `x \u2192 \u221e` for any natural `k` and positive `b`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "asymptotics.is_O_with.rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_o_log_rpow_nhds_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.is_O_cpow_rpow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.dgo_equiv_homological_complex_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.dgo_to_homological_complex", "description": "The functor from differential graded objects to homological complexes.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.homological_complex_to_dgo_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.eq_to_hom_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.homological_complex_to_dgo_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.dgo_to_homological_complex_obj_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.eq_to_hom_d_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.d_eq_to_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.homological_complex_to_dgo_obj_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.eq_to_hom_f'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.dgo_equiv_homological_complex_counit_iso_hom_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.d_eq_to_hom_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.eq_to_hom_f'_assoc", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.dgo_equiv_homological_complex_unit_iso", "description": "The unit isomorphism for `dgo_equiv_homological_complex`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.dgo_to_homological_complex_obj_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.dgo_equiv_homological_complex", "description": "The category of differential graded objects in `V` is equivalent\nto the category of homological complexes in `V`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.X_eq_to_hom_refl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.dgo_equiv_homological_complex_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.dgo_to_homological_complex_map_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.dgo_equiv_homological_complex_unit_iso_inv_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.dgo_equiv_homological_complex_unit_iso_2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.dgo_equiv_homological_complex_counit_iso_2", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.dgo_equiv_homological_complex_counit_iso", "description": "The counit isomorphism for `dgo_equiv_homological_complex`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.differential_object.X_eq_to_hom", "description": " Since `eq_to_hom` only preserves the fact that `X.X i = X.X j` but not `i = j`, this definition\nis used to aid the simplifier.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.homological_complex_to_dgo", "description": "The functor from homological complexes to differential graded objects.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.dgo_equiv_homological_complex_unit_iso_hom_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "homological_complex.dgo_equiv_homological_complex_counit_iso_inv_app_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.log_div_sqrt_antitone_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.log_div_self_antitone_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.log_div_self_rpow_antitone_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.log_mul_self_monotone_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.div_X", "description": "`div_X p` returns a polynomial `q` such that `q * X + C (p.coeff 0) = p`.\n It can be used in a semiring where the usual division algorithm is not possible", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.coeff_div_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.div_X_mul_X_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.div_X_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.degree_pos_induction_on", "description": "  A property holds for all polynomials of positive `degree` with coefficients in a semiring `R`\nif it holds for\n* `a * X`, with `a \u2208 R`,\n* `p * X`, with `p \u2208 R[X]`,\n* `p + a`, with `a \u2208 R`, `p \u2208 R[X]`,\nwith appropriate restrictions on each term.\n\nSee `nat_degree_ne_zero_induction_on` for a similar statement involving no explicit multiplication.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.div_X_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_ne_zero_induction_on", "description": "  A property holds for all polynomials of non-zero `nat_degree` with coefficients in a\nsemiring `R` if it holds for\n* `p + a`, with `a \u2208 R`, `p \u2208 R[X]`,\n* `p + q`, with `p, q \u2208 R[X]`,\n* monomials with nonzero coefficient and non-zero exponent,\nwith appropriate restrictions on each term.\nNote that multiplication is \"hidden\" in the assumption on monomials, so there is no explicit\nmultiplication in the statement.\nSee `degree_pos_induction_on` for a similar statement involving more explicit multiplications.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.degree_div_X_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.rec_on_horner", "description": "An induction principle for polynomials, valued in Sort* instead of Prop.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.div_X_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_of_forall_one_lt_div_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_of_forall_pos_sub_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_of_forall_lt_one_mul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_iff_forall_pos_le_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_of_forall_neg_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_iff_forall_neg_add_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_iff_forall_lt_one_mul_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "le_iff_forall_one_lt_le_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.inverse_associator_is_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.associator", "description": "The associator functor `(C \u2295 D) \u2295 E \u2964 C \u2295 (D \u2295 E)` for sums of categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.inverse_associator_obj_inr_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.inverse_associator_map_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.associator_map_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.associator_map_inl_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.associator_obj_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.associator_is_equivalence", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.inverse_associator", "description": "The inverse associator functor `C \u2295 (D \u2295 E) \u2964 (C \u2295 D) \u2295 E` for sums of categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.inverse_associator_map_inr_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.inverse_associator_obj_inr_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.inverse_associator_map_inr_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.associativity", "description": "The equivalence of categories expressing associativity of sums of categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.associator_obj_inl_inr", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.inverse_associator_obj_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.associator_obj_inl_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.sum.associator_map_inl_inl", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quiver.push", "description": "The `quiver` instance obtained by pushing arrows of `V` along the map `\u03c3 : V \u2192 W`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quiver.push.quiver", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quiver.push.of_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quiver.push.lift_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quiver.push.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quiver.push.of", "description": "The prefunctor induced by pushing arrows via `\u03c3`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quiver.push.lift_unique", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quiver.push_quiver", "description": "The quiver structure obtained by pushing arrows of `V` along the map `\u03c3 : V \u2192 W`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quiver.push_quiver.arrow", "description": "The quiver structure obtained by pushing arrows of `V` along the map `\u03c3 : V \u2192 W`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quiver.push.lift_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "quiver.push.lift", "description": " Given a function `\u03c4 : W \u2192 W'` and a prefunctor `\u03c6 : V \u2964q W'`, one can extend `\u03c4` to be\na prefunctor `W \u2964q W'` if `\u03c4` and `\u03c3` factorize `\u03c6` at the level of objects, where `W` is given\nthe pushforward quiver structure `push \u03c3`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.right_angle_rotation_trans_right_angle_rotation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.kahler_apply_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.area_form", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.right_angle_rotation_trans_neg_orientation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.kahler_comp_right_angle_rotation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.kahler_comp_linear_isometry_equiv", "description": " The bilinear map `kahler` is invariant under pullback by a positively-oriented isometric\nautomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.kahler_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.kahler_ne_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.area_form_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.kahler_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_right_angle_rotation_aux\u2081_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.eq_zero_or_eq_zero_of_kahler_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.kahler", "description": " A complex-valued real-bilinear map on an oriented real inner product space of dimension 2. Its\nreal part is the inner product and its imaginary part is `orientation.area_form`.\n\nOn `\u2102` with the standard orientation, `kahler w z = conj w * z`; see `complex.kahler`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.right_angle_rotation_map'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.right_angle_rotation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.kahler_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.right_angle_rotation", "description": " An isometric automorphism of an oriented real inner product space of dimension 2 (usual notation\n`J`). This automorphism squares to -1.  We will define rotations in such a way that this\nautomorphism is equal to rotation by 90 degrees.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.basis_right_angle_rotation", "description": " For a nonzero vector `x` in an oriented two-dimensional real inner product space `E`,\n`![x, J x]` forms an (orthogonal) basis for `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_mul_inner_add_area_form_mul_area_form'", "description": " For vectors `a x y : E`, the identity `\u27eaa, x\u27eb * \u27eaa, y\u27eb + \u03c9 a x * \u03c9 a y = \u2016a\u2016 ^ 2 * \u27eax, y\u27eb`. (See\n`orientation.inner_mul_inner_add_area_form_mul_area_form` for the \"applied\" form.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.kahler_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.area_form_right_angle_rotation_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_right_angle_rotation_swap'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.area_form_right_angle_rotation_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_right_angle_rotation_aux\u2081_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_comp_right_angle_rotation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_mul_area_form_sub'", "description": " For vectors `a x y : E`, the identity `\u27eaa, x\u27eb * \u03c9 a y - \u03c9 a x * \u27eaa, y\u27eb = \u2016a\u2016 ^ 2 * \u03c9 x y`. (See\n`orientation.inner_mul_area_form_sub` for the \"applied\" form.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.area_form'", "description": "Continuous linear map version of `orientation.area_form`, useful for calculus.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.right_angle_rotation_aux\u2082", "description": " Auxiliary construction for `orientation.right_angle_rotation`, rotation by 90 degrees in an\noriented real inner product space of dimension 2.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.right_angle_rotation_map_complex", "description": " The rotation by 90 degrees on an oriented real inner product space of dimension 2 can be\nevaluated in terms of a complex-number representation of the space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.kahler_apply_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.coe_basis_right_angle_rotation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.norm_sq_kahler", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.nonneg_inner_and_area_form_eq_zero_iff_same_ray", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.area_form_apply_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_sq_add_area_form_sq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.kahler_map_complex", "description": " The Kahler form on an oriented real inner product space of dimension 2 can be evaluated in terms\nof a complex-number representation of the space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.area_form_map_complex", "description": " The area form on an oriented real inner product space of dimension 2 can be evaluated in terms\nof a complex-number representation of the space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.kahler_neg_orientation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.abs_area_form_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.linear_isometry_equiv_comp_right_angle_rotation'", "description": "`J` commutes with any positively-oriented isometric automorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.kahler_right_angle_rotation_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.kahler_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.linear_isometry_equiv_comp_right_angle_rotation", "description": "`J` commutes with any positively-oriented isometric automorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.area_form_comp_right_angle_rotation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_right_angle_rotation_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.norm_kahler", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_mul_area_form_sub", "description": "For vectors `a x y : E`, the identity `\u27eaa, x\u27eb * \u03c9 a y - \u03c9 a x * \u27eaa, y\u27eb = \u2016a\u2016 ^ 2 * \u03c9 x y`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.area_form_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.right_angle_rotation_right_angle_rotation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_mul_inner_add_area_form_mul_area_form", "description": "For vectors `a x y : E`, the identity `\u27eaa, x\u27eb * \u27eaa, y\u27eb + \u03c9 a x * \u03c9 a y = \u2016a\u2016 ^ 2 * \u27eax, y\u27eb`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.right_angle_rotation_neg_orientation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.area_form_to_volume_form", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.right_angle_rotation_aux\u2081_right_angle_rotation_aux\u2081", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.area_form'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.right_angle_rotation_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "complex.kahler", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_right_angle_rotation_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.right_angle_rotation_symm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_right_angle_rotation_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.area_form_comp_linear_isometry_equiv", "description": "The area form is invariant under pullback by a positively-oriented isometric automorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.area_form", "description": " An antisymmetric bilinear form on an oriented real inner product space of dimension 2 (usual\nnotation `\u03c9`).  When evaluated on two vectors, it gives the oriented area of the parallelogram they\nspan.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.area_form_neg_orientation", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.abs_area_form_of_orthogonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.inner_right_angle_rotation_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.right_angle_rotation_aux\u2081", "description": " Auxiliary construction for `orientation.right_angle_rotation`, rotation by 90 degrees in an\noriented real inner product space of dimension 2.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.kahler_right_angle_rotation_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.area_form_swap", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "orientation.abs_kahler", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imp_congr_ctx_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "propext", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "eq_false_intro", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "forall_congr_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "imp_congr_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "eq_true_intro", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "iff.to_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "iff_eq_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "iterated_deriv_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_deriv", "description": "The `n`-th iterated derivative of a function from `\ud835\udd5c` to `F`, as a function from `\ud835\udd5c` to `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_within_eq_equiv_comp", "description": " Write the iterated Fr\u00e9chet derivative as the composition of a continuous linear equiv and the\niterated derivative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_deriv_within_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_deriv_within_succ", "description": " The `n+1`-th iterated derivative within a set with unique derivatives can be obtained by\ndifferentiating the `n`-th iterated derivative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_deriv_within_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_deriv_within_succ'", "description": " The `n+1`-th iterated derivative within a set with unique derivatives can be obtained by\ntaking the `n`-th derivative of the derivative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_iff_iterated_deriv", "description": " The property of being `C^n`, initially defined in terms of the Fr\u00e9chet derivative, can be\nreformulated in terms of the one-dimensional derivative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.continuous_on_iterated_deriv_within", "description": " On a set with unique derivatives, a `C^n` function has derivatives up to `n` which are\ncontinuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_deriv_within_eq_iterated_fderiv_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_deriv_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff.differentiable_iterated_deriv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_of_continuous_on_differentiable_on_deriv", "description": " If the first `n` derivatives within a set of a function are continuous, and its first `n-1`\nderivatives are differentiable, then the function is `C^n`. This is not an equivalence in general,\nbut this is an equivalence when the set has unique derivatives, see\n`cont_diff_on_iff_continuous_on_differentiable_on_deriv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_deriv_succ'", "description": " The `n+1`-th iterated derivative can be obtained by taking the `n`-th derivative of the\nderivative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_deriv_within_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_eq_equiv_comp", "description": " Write the iterated Fr\u00e9chet derivative as the composition of a continuous linear equiv and the\niterated derivative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_iterated_fderiv_eq_norm_iterated_deriv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_iff_continuous_on_differentiable_on_deriv", "description": " The property of being `C^n`, initially defined in terms of the Fr\u00e9chet derivative, can be\nreformulated in terms of the one-dimensional derivative on sets with unique derivatives.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on_of_differentiable_on_deriv", "description": " To check that a function is `n` times continuously differentiable, it suffices to check that its\nfirst `n` derivatives are differentiable. This is slightly too strong as the condition we\nrequire on the `n`-th derivative is differentiability instead of continuity, but it has the\nadvantage of avoiding the discussion of continuity in the proof (and for `n = \u221e` this is optimal).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_of_differentiable_iterated_deriv", "description": " To check that a function is `n` times continuously differentiable, it suffices to check that its\nfirst `n` derivatives are differentiable. This is slightly too strong as the condition we\nrequire on the `n`-th derivative is differentiability instead of continuity, but it has the\nadvantage of avoiding the discussion of continuity in the proof (and for `n = \u221e` this is optimal).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_within_apply_eq_iterated_deriv_within_mul_prod", "description": " The `n`-th Fr\u00e9chet derivative applied to a vector `(m 0, ..., m (n-1))` is the derivative\nmultiplied by the product of the `m i`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_deriv_within_eq_iterate", "description": " The `n`-th iterated derivative within a set with unique derivatives can be obtained by\niterating `n` times the differentiation operation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_deriv_eq_iterated_fderiv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_fderiv_apply_eq_iterated_deriv_mul_prod", "description": " The `n`-th Fr\u00e9chet derivative applied to a vector `(m 0, ..., m (n-1))` is the derivative\nmultiplied by the product of the `m i`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_on.differentiable_on_iterated_deriv_within", "description": " On a set with unique derivatives, a `C^n` function has derivatives less than `n` which are\ndifferentiable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "norm_iterated_fderiv_within_eq_norm_iterated_deriv_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_deriv_succ", "description": " The `n+1`-th iterated derivative can be obtained by differentiating the `n`-th\niterated derivative.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_deriv_eq_iterate", "description": " The `n`-th iterated derivative can be obtained by iterating `n` times the\ndifferentiation operation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_deriv_within", "description": " The `n`-th iterated derivative of a function from `\ud835\udd5c` to `F` within a set `s`, as a function\nfrom `\ud835\udd5c` to `F`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff.continuous_iterated_deriv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_deriv_within_eq_equiv_comp", "description": " Write the iterated derivative as the composition of a continuous linear equiv and the iterated\nFr\u00e9chet derivative", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "iterated_deriv_eq_equiv_comp", "description": " Write the iterated derivative as the composition of a continuous linear equiv and the iterated\nFr\u00e9chet derivative", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cont_diff_within_at.differentiable_within_at_iterated_deriv_within", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_measurable.const_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.has_measurable_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_measurable_inf\u2082.to_has_measurable_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable.const_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable.sup'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.has_measurable_sup\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_measurable_inf\u2082", "description": " We say that a type `has_measurable_inf\u2082` if `uncurry (\u2294)` is a measurable functions.\nFor a typeclass assuming measurability of `((\u2294) c)` and `(\u2294 c)` see `has_measurable_inf`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_measurable_inf\u2082.measurable_inf", "description": " We say that a type `has_measurable_inf\u2082` if `uncurry (\u2294)` is a measurable functions.\nFor a typeclass assuming measurability of `((\u2294) c)` and `(\u2294 c)` see `has_measurable_inf`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_measurable_inf", "description": " We say that a type `has_measurable_inf` if `((\u2293) c)` and `(\u2293 c)` are measurable functions.\nFor a typeclass assuming measurability of `uncurry (\u2293)` see `has_measurable_inf\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_measurable_inf.measurable_const_inf", "description": " We say that a type `has_measurable_inf` if `((\u2293) c)` and `(\u2293 c)` are measurable functions.\nFor a typeclass assuming measurability of `uncurry (\u2293)` see `has_measurable_inf\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_measurable_inf.measurable_inf_const", "description": " We say that a type `has_measurable_inf` if `((\u2293) c)` and `(\u2293 c)` are measurable functions.\nFor a typeclass assuming measurability of `uncurry (\u2293)` see `has_measurable_inf\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_measurable.inf_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_measurable.sup_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable.inf_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.measurable_sup'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable.const_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_measurable_sup", "description": " We say that a type `has_measurable_sup` if `((\u2294) c)` and `(\u2294 c)` are measurable functions.\nFor a typeclass assuming measurability of `uncurry (\u2294)` see `has_measurable_sup\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_measurable_sup.measurable_const_sup", "description": " We say that a type `has_measurable_sup` if `((\u2294) c)` and `(\u2294 c)` are measurable functions.\nFor a typeclass assuming measurability of `uncurry (\u2294)` see `has_measurable_sup\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_measurable_sup.measurable_sup_const", "description": " We say that a type `has_measurable_sup` if `((\u2294) c)` and `(\u2294 c)` are measurable functions.\nFor a typeclass assuming measurability of `uncurry (\u2294)` see `has_measurable_sup\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_measurable.const_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.measurable_range_sup'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_measurable.inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_measurable.inf'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.measurable_range_sup''", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_measurable_sup\u2082.to_has_measurable_sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable.inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable.inf'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_measurable_sup\u2082", "description": " We say that a type `has_measurable_sup\u2082` if `uncurry (\u2294)` is a measurable functions.\nFor a typeclass assuming measurability of `((\u2294) c)` and `(\u2294 c)` see `has_measurable_sup`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_measurable_sup\u2082.measurable_sup", "description": " We say that a type `has_measurable_sup\u2082` if `uncurry (\u2294)` is a measurable functions.\nFor a typeclass assuming measurability of `((\u2294) c)` and `(\u2294 c)` see `has_measurable_sup`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.has_measurable_inf\u2082", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_measurable.sup'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable.sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measurable.sup_const", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_measurable.sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "order_dual.has_measurable_inf", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_floor_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_fract", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_ceil_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_floor_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_ceil_right'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_floor_at_bot", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_fract_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_ceil_left'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_fract_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.comp_fract''", "description": "A special case of `continuous_on.comp_fract`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on_floor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_floor_at_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_ceil_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_floor_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "c