{"name": "simple_graph.box_prod_comm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.box_prod", "description": " Box product of simple graphs. It relates `(a\u2081, b)` and `(a\u2082, b)` if `G` relates `a\u2081` and `a\u2082`,\nand `(a, b\u2081)` and `(a, b\u2082)` if `H` relates `b\u2081` and `b\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.connected.box_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.box_prod_degree", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.preconnected.of_box_prod_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.box_prod_right_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.box_prod_assoc", "description": "The box product is associative up to isomorphism. `equiv.prod_assoc` as a graph isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.preconnected.of_box_prod_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.connected.of_box_prod_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.walk.of_box_prod_left_box_prod_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.box_prod_adj_right", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.box_prod_adj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fin.vne_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fin.has_lt", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fin.has_le", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fin.eq_of_veq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fin.ne_of_vne", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fin.veq_of_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fin", "description": "`fin n` is the subtype of `\u2115` consisting of natural numbers strictly smaller than `n`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fin.val", "description": "`fin n` is the subtype of `\u2115` consisting of natural numbers strictly smaller than `n`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fin.property", "description": "`fin n` is the subtype of `\u2115` consisting of natural numbers strictly smaller than `n`.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fin.lt", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fin.decidable_lt", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fin.decidable_eq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fin.decidable_le", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fin.elim0", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fin.le", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "category_theory.adjunction.gc", "description": "An adjunction between preorder categories induces a galois connection.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "galois_connection.adjunction", "description": "A galois connection between preorders induces an adjunction between the associated categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_sUnion_interior_of_closed", "description": " Baire theorem: if countably many closed sets cover the whole space, then their interiors\nare dense. Formulated here with `\u22c3\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_Inter_of_G\u03b4", "description": " Baire theorem: a countable intersection of dense G\u03b4 sets is dense. Formulated here with\nan index set which is an encodable type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "baire_category_theorem_locally_compact", "description": "The second theorem states that locally compact spaces are Baire.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "baire_space", "description": " The property `baire_space \u03b1` means that the topological space `\u03b1` has the Baire property:\nany countable intersection of open dense subsets is dense.\nFormulated here when the source space is \u2115 (and subsumed below by `dense_Inter_of_open` working\nwith any encodable source space).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "baire_space.baire_property", "description": " The property `baire_space \u03b1` means that the topological space `\u03b1` has the Baire property:\nany countable intersection of open dense subsets is dense.\nFormulated here when the source space is \u2115 (and subsumed below by `dense_Inter_of_open` working\nwith any encodable source space).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_G\u03b4.dense_sUnion_interior_of_closed", "description": " If a countable family of closed sets cover a dense `G\u03b4` set, then the union of their interiors\nis dense. Formulated here with `\u22c3\u2080`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_bInter_of_open", "description": " Baire theorem: a countable intersection of dense open sets is dense. Formulated here with\nan index set which is a countable set in any type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_Union_interior_of_closed", "description": " Baire theorem: if countably many closed sets cover the whole space, then their interiors\nare dense. Formulated here with an index set which is an encodable type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_Inter_of_open", "description": " Baire theorem: a countable intersection of dense open sets is dense. Formulated here with\nan index set which is an encodable type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_Inter_of_open_nat", "description": "Definition of a Baire space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_of_mem_residual", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nonempty_interior_of_Union_of_closed", "description": " One of the most useful consequences of Baire theorem: if a countable union of closed sets\ncovers the space, then one of the sets has nonempty interior.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_sInter_of_open", "description": "Baire theorem: a countable intersection of dense open sets is dense. Formulated here with \u22c2\u2080.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense.inter_of_G\u03b4", "description": "Baire theorem: the intersection of two dense G\u03b4 sets is dense.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "eventually_residual", "description": "A property holds on a residual (comeagre) set if and only if it holds on some dense `G\u03b4` set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_G\u03b4.dense_bUnion_interior_of_closed", "description": " If a countable family of closed sets cover a dense `G\u03b4` set, then the union of their interiors\nis dense. Formulated here with a union over a countable set in any type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mem_residual", "description": "A set is residual (comeagre) if and only if it includes a dense `G\u03b4` set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_sInter_of_G\u03b4", "description": "Baire theorem: a countable intersection of dense G\u03b4 sets is dense. Formulated here with \u22c2\u2080.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_bInter_of_G\u03b4", "description": " Baire theorem: a countable intersection of dense G\u03b4 sets is dense. Formulated here with\nan index set which is a countable set in any type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "baire_category_theorem_emetric_complete", "description": " Baire theorems asserts that various topological spaces have the Baire property.\nTwo versions of these theorems are given.\nThe first states that complete pseudo_emetric spaces are Baire.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_G\u03b4.dense_Union_interior_of_closed", "description": " If a countable family of closed sets cover a dense `G\u03b4` set, then the union of their interiors\nis dense. Formulated here with `\u22c3`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "dense_bUnion_interior_of_closed", "description": " Baire theorem: if countably many closed sets cover the whole space, then their interiors\nare dense. Formulated here with an index set which is a countable set in any type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_noetherian_ring_of_fg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.fg_def", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.is_noetherian_ring_range", "description": "The image of a Noetherian R-algebra under an R-algebra map is a Noetherian ring.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.fg_of_fg_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.induction_on_adjoin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "algebra.fg_trans", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.fg_of_submodule_fg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subalgebra.fg_top", "description": 