ame": "canonically_linear_ordered_semifield.zpow_succ'", "description": " A canonically linear ordered field is a linear ordered field in which `a \u2264 b` iff there exists\n`c` with `b = a + c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_linear_ordered_semifield.zpow_neg'", "description": " A canonically linear ordered field is a linear ordered field in which `a \u2264 b` iff there exists\n`c` with `b = a + c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_linear_ordered_semifield.inv_zero", "description": " A canonically linear ordered field is a linear ordered field in which `a \u2264 b` iff there exists\n`c` with `b = a + c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_linear_ordered_semifield.mul_inv_cancel", "description": " A canonically linear ordered field is a linear ordered field in which `a \u2264 b` iff there exists\n`c` with `b = a + c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_linear_ordered_semifield.to_linear_ordered_semifield", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_linear_ordered_semifield.to_linear_ordered_comm_group_with_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_linear_ordered_semifield.to_canonically_linear_ordered_add_monoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "canonically_linear_ordered_semifield.to_canonically_ordered_comm_semiring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.dickson_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.dickson", "description": " `dickson` is the `n`the (generalised) Dickson polynomial of the `k`-th kind associated to the\nelement `a \u2208 R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.map_dickson", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.chebyshev_T_eq_dickson_one_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.dickson_one_one_comp_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.dickson_of_two_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.dickson_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.dickson_two_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.dickson_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.dickson_one_one_zmod_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.dickson_one_one_eval_add_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.dickson_one_one_mul", "description": " The `(m * n)`-th Dickson polynomial of the first kind is the composition of the `m`-th and\n`n`-th.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.dickson_one_one_char_p", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.dickson_one_one_eq_chebyshev_T", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.dickson_add_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ne_zero.char_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_ne_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_zero_of_inj_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_add_one_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_zero", "description": " Typeclass for monoids with characteristic zero.\n  (This is usually stated on fields but it makes sense for any additive monoid with 1.)\n\n*Warning*: for a semiring `R`, `char_zero R` and `char_p R 0` need not coincide.\n* `char_zero R` requires an injection `\u2115 \u21aa R`;\n* `char_p R 0` asks that only `0 : \u2115` maps to `0 : R` under the map `\u2115 \u2192 R`.\n\nFor instance, endowing `{0, 1}` with addition given by `max` (i.e. `1` is absorbing), shows that\n`char_zero {0, 1}` does not hold and yet `char_p {0, 1} 0` does.\nThis example is formalized in `counterexamples/char_p_zero_ne_char_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_zero.cast_injective", "description": " Typeclass for monoids with characteristic zero.\n  (This is usually stated on fields but it makes sense for any additive monoid with 1.)\n\n*Warning*: for a semiring `R`, `char_zero R` and `char_p R 0` need not coincide.\n* `char_zero R` requires an injection `\u2115 \u21aa R`;\n* `char_p R 0` asks that only `0 : \u2115` maps to `0 : R` under the map `\u2115 \u2192 R`.\n\nFor instance, endowing `{0, 1}` with addition given by `max` (i.e. `1` is absorbing), shows that\n`char_zero {0, 1}` does not hold and yet `char_p {0, 1} 0` does.\nThis example is formalized in `counterexamples/char_p_zero_ne_char_zero`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_eq_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.cast_ne_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multilinear_map.dom_coprod'_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multilinear_map.dom_coprod'", "description": " A more bundled version of `multilinear_map.dom_coprod` that maps\n`((\u03b9\u2081 \u2192 N) \u2192 N\u2081) \u2297 ((\u03b9\u2082 \u2192 N) \u2192 N\u2082)` to `(\u03b9\u2081 \u2295 \u03b9\u2082 \u2192 N) \u2192 N\u2081 \u2297 N\u2082`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multilinear_map.dom_coprod_dom_dom_congr_sum_congr", "description": " When passed an `equiv.sum_congr`, `multilinear_map.dom_dom_congr` distributes over\n`multilinear_map.dom_coprod`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multilinear_map.dom_coprod", "description": " Given two multilinear maps `(\u03b9\u2081 \u2192 N) \u2192 N\u2081` and `(\u03b9\u2082 \u2192 N) \u2192 N\u2082`, this produces the map\n`(\u03b9\u2081 \u2295 \u03b9\u2082 \u2192 N) \u2192 N\u2081 \u2297 N\u2082` by taking the coproduct of the domain and the tensor product\nof the codomain.\n\nThis can be thought of as combining `equiv.sum_arrow_equiv_prod_arrow.symm` with\n`tensor_product.map`, noting that the two operations can't be separated as the intermediate result\nis not a `multilinear_map`.\n\nWhile this can be generalized to work for dependent `\u03a0 i : \u03b9\u2081, N'\u2081 i` instead of `\u03b9\u2081 \u2192 N`, doing so\nintroduces `sum.elim N'\u2081 N'\u2082` types in the result which are difficult to work with and not defeq\nto the simple case defined here. See [this zulip thread](\nhttps://leanprover.zulipchat.com/#narrow/stream/217875-Is-there.20code.20for.20X.3F/topic/Instances.20on.20.60sum.2Eelim.20A.20B.20i.60/near/218484619).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multilinear_map.dom_coprod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imo1987_q1.main\u2080", "description": "Main statement for permutations of `fin n`, a version that works for `n = 0`.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1987_q1.fiber.fintype", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1987_q1.card_fixed_points", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1987_q1.fixed_points_equiv", "description": " The set of pairs `(x : \u03b1, \u03c3 : perm \u03b1)` such that `\u03c3 x = x` is equivalent to the set of pairs\n`(x : \u03b1, \u03c3 : perm {x}\u1d9c)`.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1987_q1.main_fintype", "description": "Main statement for any `(\u03b1 : Type*) [fintype \u03b1]`.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1987_q1.main", "description": "Main statement for permutations of `fin n`.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1987_q1.mem_fiber", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1987_q1.p", "description": "`p \u03b1 k` is the number of permutations of `\u03b1` with exactly `k` fixed points.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1987_q1.fiber", "description": " Given `\u03b1 : Type*` and `k : \u2115`, `fiber \u03b1 k` is the set of permutations of `\u03b1` with exactly `k`\nfixed points.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1987_q1.fixed_points_equiv'", "description": " The set of triples `(k \u2264 card \u03b1, \u03c3 \u2208 fiber \u03b1 k, x \u2208 fixed_points \u03c3)` is equivalent\nto the set of pairs `(x : \u03b1, \u03c3 : perm \u03b1)` such that `\u03c3 x = x`. The equivalence sends\n`(k, \u03c3, x)` to `(x, \u03c3)` and `(x, \u03c3)` to `(card (fixed_points \u03c3), \u03c3, x)`.\n\nIt is easy to see that the cardinality of the LHS is given by\n`\u2211 k : fin (card \u03b1 + 1), k * p \u03b1 k`.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "finset.sum_powerset_apply_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.choose_middle_le_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_pow", "description": "The **binomial theorem**", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_powerset_neg_one_pow_card_of_nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.sum_range_choose", "description": "The sum of entries in a row of Pascal's triangle", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.alternating_sum_range_choose", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.alternating_sum_range_choose_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.add_pow", "description": "A version of the **binomial theorem** for commuting elements in noncommutative semirings.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "finset.sum_powerset_neg_one_pow_card", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commute.add_pow'", "description": " A version of `commute.add_pow` that avoids \u2115-subtraction by summing over the antidiagonal and\nalso with the binomial coefficient applied via scalar action of \u2115.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.sum_range_choose_halfway", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.four_pow_le_two_mul_add_one_mul_central_binom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.nat_abs_eq_iff_associated", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_restrict_ae_eq_restrict", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ae_eq_restrict_of_measurable_space_eq_on", "description": " If the restriction to a `m`-measurable set `s` of a \u03c3-algebra `m` is equal to the restriction\nto `s` of another \u03c3-algebra `m\u2082` (hypothesis `hs`), then `\u03bc[f | m] =\u1d50[\u03bc.restrict s] \u03bc[f | m\u2082]`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_ae_eq_restrict_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_indicator_aux", "description": "Auxiliary lemma for `condexp_indicator`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.condexp_indicator", "description": " The conditional expectation of the indicator of a function over an `m`-measurable set with\nrespect to the \u03c3-algebra `m` is a.e. equal to the indicator of the conditional expectation.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.protect_proj_tac", "description": "Tactic that is executed when a structure is marked with the `protect_proj` attribute", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.attribute.protect_proj", "description": "Attribute to protect the projections of a structure.\nIf a structure `foo` is marked with the `protect_proj` user attribute, then\nall of the projections become protected, meaning they must always be referred to by\ntheir full name `foo.bar`, even when the `foo` namespace is open.\n\n`protect_proj without bar baz` will protect all projections except for `bar` and `baz`.\n\n```lean\n@[protect_proj without baz bar] structure foo : Type :=\n(bar : unit) (baz : unit) (qux : unit)\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.attribute.protected", "description": "Attribute to protect a declaration.\nIf a declaration `foo.bar` is marked protected, then it must be referred to\nby its full name `foo.bar`, even when the `foo` namespace is open.\n\nProtectedness is a built in parser feature that is independent of this attribute.\nA declaration may be protected even if it does not have the `@[protected]` attribute.\nThis provides a convenient way to protect many declarations at once.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.protected_attr", "description": "Attribute to protect a declaration.\nIf a declaration `foo.bar` is marked protected, then it must be referred to\nby its full name `foo.bar`, even when the `foo` namespace is open.\n\nProtectedness is a built in parser feature that is independent of this attribute.\nA declaration may be protected even if it does not have the `@[protected]` attribute.\nThis provides a convenient way to protect many declarations at once.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.protect_proj_attr", "description": "Attribute to protect the projections of a structure.\nIf a structure `foo` is marked with the `protect_proj` user attribute, then\nall of the projections become protected, meaning they must always be referred to by\ntheir full name `foo.bar`, even when the `foo` namespace is open.\n\n`protect_proj without bar baz` will protect all projections except for `bar` and `baz`.\n\n```lean\n@[protect_proj without baz bar] structure foo : Type :=\n(bar : unit) (baz : unit) (qux : unit)\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "monad.filter", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "monad.foldl", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "mjoin", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "monad.sequence'", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "monad.whenb", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "monad.join", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "list.mfirst", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "list.mfilter", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "monad.sequence", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "monad.cond", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "monad.mapm", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "when", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "list.mmap", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "list.mfoldl", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "monad.unlessb", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "mwhen", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "monad.mapm'", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "mcond", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "list.mfoldr", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "list.mmap'", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "polynomial.hasse_deriv_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.hasse_deriv_apply_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.hasse_deriv_coeff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.hasse_deriv_zero'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.factorial_smul_hasse_deriv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.hasse_deriv_eq_zero_of_lt_nat_degree", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.hasse_deriv_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.hasse_deriv_comp", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.hasse_deriv_monomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_hasse_deriv_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.hasse_deriv_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.hasse_deriv_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.hasse_deriv", "description": " The `k`th Hasse derivative of a polynomial `\u2211 a_i X^i` is `\u2211 (i.choose k) a_i X^(i-k)`.\nIt satisfies `k! * (hasse_deriv k f) = derivative^[k] f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.hasse_deriv_one'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.nat_degree_hasse_deriv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.hasse_deriv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "polynomial.hasse_deriv_C", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rat.star_ordered_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rat.star_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rat.has_trivial_star", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "surj_on_Iio_of_monotone_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "surj_on_Ioi_of_monotone_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "surj_on_Ioo_of_monotone_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "surj_on_Icc_of_monotone_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "surj_on_Ici_of_monotone_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "surj_on_Iic_of_monotone_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "surj_on_Ico_of_monotone_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "surj_on_Ioc_of_monotone_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.commutator_ring.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commutator_ring", "description": " Type synonym for turning a `lie_ring` into a `non_unital_non_assoc_semiring`.\n\nA `lie_ring` can be regarded as a `non_unital_non_assoc_semiring` by turning its\n`has_bracket` (denoted `\u2045, \u2046`) into a `has_mul` (denoted `*`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_hom.to_non_unital_alg_hom_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "commutator_ring.non_unital_non_assoc_semiring", "description": " A `lie_ring` can be regarded as a `non_unital_non_assoc_semiring` by turning its\n`has_bracket` (denoted `\u2045, \u2046`) into a `has_mul` (denoted `*`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.is_scalar_tower", "description": " Regarding the `lie_ring` of a `lie_algebra` as a `non_unital_non_assoc_semiring`, we can\nreinterpret the `smul_lie` law as an `is_scalar_tower`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.commutator_ring.nonempty", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_hom.to_non_unital_alg_hom", "description": " Regarding the `lie_ring` of a `lie_algebra` as a `non_unital_non_assoc_semiring`, we can\nregard a `lie_hom` as a `non_unital_alg_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_hom.to_non_unital_alg_hom_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.smul_comm_class", "description": " Regarding the `lie_ring` of a `lie_algebra` as a `non_unital_non_assoc_semiring`, we can\nreinterpret the `lie_smul` law as an `smul_comm_class`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.commutator_ring.lie_algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "lie_algebra.commutator_ring.lie_ring", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.abstract_if_success", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.chain_core", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.trace_output", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.chain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.tactic_script_unit_has_to_string", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.chain_single", "description": "`chain_many tac` recursively tries `tac` on all goals, working depth-first on generated subgoals,\nuntil it no longer succeeds on any goal. `chain_many` automatically makes auxiliary definitions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.chain_iter", "description": "`chain_many tac` recursively tries `tac` on all goals, working depth-first on generated subgoals,\nuntil it no longer succeeds on any goal. `chain_many` automatically makes auxiliary definitions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.chain_many", "description": "`chain_many tac` recursively tries `tac` on all goals, working depth-first on generated subgoals,\nuntil it no longer succeeds on any goal. `chain_many` automatically makes auxiliary definitions.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.range_list_nthd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.range_list_nth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.range_list_nth_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.can_lift", "description": " If each element of a list can be lifted to some type, then the whole list can be lifted to this\ntype.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.range_list_inth", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.range_list_map_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set.range_list_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rbnode.mem_of_mem_exact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rbnode.find.induction", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rbnode.find_eq_find_of_eqv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rbnode.eqv_of_find_some", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rbnode.find_correct_exact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rbnode.find_correct", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.cardinal_mk_le_of_le", "description": "`#(W_type \u03b2)` is the least cardinal `\u03ba` such that `sum (\u03bb a : \u03b1, \u03ba ^ #(\u03b2 a)) \u2264 \u03ba`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.cardinal_mk_le_max_aleph_0_of_finite", "description": "If, for any `a : \u03b1`, `\u03b2 a` is finite, then the cardinality of `W_type \u03b2`\n is at most the maximum of the cardinality of `\u03b1` and `\u2135\u2080`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "W_type.cardinal_mk_eq_sum", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Scott", "description": " A Scott topological space is defined on preorders\nsuch that their open sets, seen as a function `\u03b1 \u2192 Prop`,\npreserves the joins of \u03c9-chains", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Scott.is_\u03c9Sup", "description": "`x` is an `\u03c9`-Sup of a chain `c` if it is the least upper bound of the range of `c`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Scott.is_open.inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_below_is_open", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_of_Scott_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_\u03c9Sup_\u03c9Sup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Scott.is_open", "description": " The characteristic function of open sets is monotone and preserves\nthe limits of chains.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Scott.is_open_sUnion", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Scott.is_\u03c9Sup_iff_is_lub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Scott.topological_space", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Scott_continuous_of_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Scott.is_open_univ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "not_below", "description": " `not_below` is an open set in `Scott \u03b1` used\nto prove the monotonicity of continuous functions", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.is_integral_stable_under_base_change", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.is_integral_respects_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ring_hom.is_integral_stable_under_composition", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.mem_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "image.is_subfield", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "range.is_subfield", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_subfield", "description": " `is_subfield (S : set F)` is the predicate saying that a given subset of a field is\nthe set underlying a subfield. This structure is deprecated; use the bundled variant\n`subfield F` to model subfields of a field.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_subfield.to_is_subring", "description": " `is_subfield (S : set F)` is the predicate saying that a given subset of a field is\nthe set underlying a subfield. This structure is deprecated; use the bundled variant\n`subfield F` to model subfields of a field.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_subfield.inv_mem", "description": " `is_subfield (S : set F)` is the predicate saying that a given subset of a field is\nthe set underlying a subfield. This structure is deprecated; use the bundled variant\n`subfield F` to model subfields of a field.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_subfield_Union_of_directed", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_subfield.Inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.closure_mono", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_subfield.inter", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_subfield.div_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.closure_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.closure.is_submonoid", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.subset_closure", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.ring_closure_subset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.closure", "description": "`field.closure s` is the minimal subfield that includes `s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.closure_subset_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.closure.is_subfield", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "preimage.is_subfield", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_subfield.pow_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "univ.is_subfield", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.prod_equiv_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.snd", "description": "Second projection as `alg_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.algebra_map_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.prod_fst_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.fst", "description": "First projection as `alg_hom`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.prod", "description": "The `pi.prod` of two morphisms is a morphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.coe_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "prod.algebra", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.fst_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.prod_equiv_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.snd_prod", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.prod_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "alg_hom.prod_equiv", "description": " Taking the product of two maps with the same domain is equivalent to taking the product of\ntheir codomains.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.unique_embedding_equiv_result", "description": "Embeddings from a single-member type are equivalent to members of the target type.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sum_embedding_equiv_sigma_embedding_restricted", "description": " A combination of the above results, allowing us to turn one embedding over a sum type\ninto two dependent embeddings, the second of which avoids any members of the range\nof the first. This is helpful for constructing larger embeddings out of smaller ones.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.sum_embedding_equiv_prod_embedding_disjoint", "description": "Embeddings from a sum type are equivalent to two separate embeddings with disjoint ranges.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.prod_embedding_disjoint_equiv_sigma_embedding_restricted", "description": " Pairs of embeddings with disjoint ranges are equivalent to a dependent sum of embeddings,\nin which the second embedding cannot take values in the range of the first.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "equiv.cod_restrict", "description": " Embeddings whose range lies within a set are equivalent to embeddings to that set.\nThis is `function.embedding.cod_restrict` as an equiv.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimits_of_shape_of_has_filtered_colimits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_filtered_colimits_of_size", "description": "Class for having all filtered colimits of a given size.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_filtered_colimits_of_size.has_colimits_of_shape", "description": "Class for having all filtered colimits of a given size.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limits_of_shape_of_has_cofiltered_limits", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_cofiltered_limits_of_size", "description": "Class for having all cofiltered limits of a given size.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_cofiltered_limits_of_size.has_limits_of_shape", "description": "Class for having all cofiltered limits of a given size.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.multiplicative_additive", "description": "`multiplicative (additive H)` is just `H`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.to_additive'", "description": "Reinterpret `G \u2243* multiplicative H` as `additive G \u2243+ H` as.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.to_multiplicative'", "description": "Reinterpret `additive G \u2243+ H` as `G \u2243* multiplicative H`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.to_multiplicative''", "description": "Reinterpret `G \u2243+ additive H` as `multiplicative G \u2243* H`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.to_multiplicative", "description": "Reinterpret `G \u2243+ H` as `multiplicative G \u2243* multiplicative H`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_equiv.additive_multiplicative", "description": "`additive (multiplicative G)` is just `G`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.to_additive", "description": "Reinterpret `G \u2243* H` as `additive G \u2243+ additive H`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mul_equiv.to_additive''", "description": "Reinterpret `multiplicative G \u2243* H` as `G \u2243+ additive H` as.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set_like.fintype", "description": " TODO: It should be possible to obtain a computable version of this for most\nset_like objects. If we add those instances, we should remove this one.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "set_like.finite", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_abs_nhds_within_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tendsto_zero_iff_abs_tendsto_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at.abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_ordered_add_comm_group.topological_add_group", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_at.abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "filter.tendsto.abs", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bundled", "description": " `bundled` is a type bundled with a type class instance for that type. Only\nthe type class is exposed as a parameter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bundled.\u03b1", "description": " `bundled` is a type bundled with a type class instance for that type. Only\nthe type class is exposed as a parameter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bundled.str", "description": " `bundled` is a type bundled with a type class instance for that type. Only\nthe type class is exposed as a parameter.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bundled.coe_mk", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bundled.has_coe_to_sort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bundled.of", "description": "A generic function for lifting a type equipped with an instance to a bundled object.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.bundled.map", "description": "Map over the bundled structure", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imo1994_q1.tedious", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo1994_q1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "category_theory.preadditive.dold_kan.equivalence_unit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preadditive.dold_kan.N_obj_X_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preadditive.dold_kan.N_map_f_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preadditive.dold_kan.N", "description": " The functor `karoubi (simplicial_object C) \u2964 karoubi (chain_complex C \u2115)` of\nthe Dold-Kan equivalence for additive categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preadditive.dold_kan.equivalence_counit_iso", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preadditive.dold_kan.\u0393_obj_X_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preadditive.dold_kan.equivalence_functor", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preadditive.dold_kan.\u0393_obj_p_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preadditive.dold_kan.\u0393", "description": " The inverse functor `karoubi (chain_complex C \u2115) \u2964 karoubi (simplicial_object C)` of\nthe Dold-Kan equivalence for additive categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preadditive.dold_kan.equivalence", "description": " The Dold-Kan equivalence `karoubi (simplicial_object C) \u224c karoubi (chain_complex C \u2115)`\nfor additive categories.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preadditive.dold_kan.N_obj_X_d", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preadditive.dold_kan.equivalence_inverse", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preadditive.dold_kan.\u0393_obj_X_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preadditive.dold_kan.N_obj_p_f", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.preadditive.dold_kan.\u0393_map_f_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.uniform_continuous_on_of_continuous", "description": " Heine-Cantor: a continuous function on a compact set of a uniform space is uniformly\ncontinuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "unique_uniformity_of_compact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nhds_set_diagonal_eq_uniformity", "description": " On a compact uniform space, the topology determines the uniform structure, entourages are\nexactly the neighborhoods of the diagonal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "compact_space.uniform_continuous_of_continuous", "description": " Heine-Cantor: a continuous function on a compact uniform space is uniformly\ncontinuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.tendsto_uniformly", "description": " A continuous family of functions `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b3` tends uniformly to its value at `x` if `\u03b1` is\nlocally compact and `\u03b2` is compact.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_compact_support.uniform_continuous_of_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_on.tendsto_uniformly", "description": " A family of functions `\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b3` tends uniformly to its value at `x` if `\u03b1` is locally compact,\n`\u03b2` is compact and `f` is continuous on `U \u00d7 (univ : set \u03b2)` for some neighborhood `U` of `x`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_compact_mul_support.is_one_at_infty", "description": "If `f` has compact multiplicative support, then `f` tends to 1 at infinity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_compact.uniform_continuous_at_of_continuous_at", "description": " If `s` is compact and `f` is continuous at all points of `s`, then `f` is\n\"uniformly continuous at the set `s`\", i.e. `f x` is close to `f y` whenever `x \u2208 s` and `y` is\nclose to `x` (even if `y` is not itself in `s`, so this is a stronger assertion than\n`uniform_continuous_on s`).", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "compact_space_uniformity", "description": " On a compact uniform space, the topology determines the uniform structure, entourages are\nexactly the neighborhoods of the diagonal.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "uniform_space_of_compact_t2", "description": "The unique uniform structure inducing a given compact topological structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "compact_space.uniform_equicontinuous_of_equicontinuous", "description": " An equicontinuous family of functions defined on a compact uniform space is automatically\nuniformly equicontinuous.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_compact_mul_support.uniform_continuous_of_continuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous.uniform_continuous_of_tendsto_cocompact", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_compact_support.is_zero_at_infty", "description": "If `f` has compact support, then `f` tends to zero at infinity.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.left.exists_add_of_mem_support_single_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.no_zero_divisors.of_right_ordered", "description": "  If `R` is a semiring with no non-trivial zero-divisors and `A` is a right-ordered add left\ncancel semigroup, then `add_monoid_algebra R A` also contains no non-zero zero-divisors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.right.exists_add_of_mem_support_single_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.mul_apply_add_eq_mul_of_forall_ne", "description": "  The coefficient of a monomial in a product `f * g` that can be reached in at most one way\nas a product of monomials in the supports of `f` and `g` is a product.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_monoid_algebra.no_zero_divisors.of_left_ordered", "description": "  If `R` is a semiring with no non-trivial zero-divisors and `A` is a left-ordered add right\ncancel semigroup, then `add_monoid_algebra R A` also contains no non-zero zero-divisors.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dist_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dist_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.connected.dist_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.reachable.dist_eq_zero_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.reachable.pos_dist_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dist_eq_zero_of_not_reachable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dist_eq_zero_iff_eq_or_not_reachable", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dist", "description": " The distance between two vertices is the length of the shortest walk between them.\nIf no such walk exists, this uses the junk value of `0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.reachable.exists_walk_of_dist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.nonempty_of_pos_dist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.connected.pos_dist_of_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.connected.dist_triangle", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.dist_self", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "simple_graph.connected.exists_walk_of_dist", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_finite_products", "description": "A category has finite products if there is a chosen limit for every diagram\nwith shape `discrete J`, where we have `[finite J]`.\n\nWe require this condition only for `J = fin n` in the definition, then deduce a version for any\n`J : Type*` as a corollary of this definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_finite_products.out", "description": "A category has finite products if there is a chosen limit for every diagram\nwith shape `discrete J`, where we have `[finite J]`.\n\nWe require this condition only for `J = fin n` in the definition, then deduce a version for any\n`J : Type*` as a corollary of this definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_finite_products_of_has_products", "description": "If a category has all products then in particular it has finite products.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_finite_products_of_has_finite_limits", "description": "If `C` has finite limits then it has finite products.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_finite_coproducts", "description": "A category has finite coproducts if there is a chosen colimit for every diagram\nwith shape `discrete J`, where we have `[fintype J]`.\n\nWe require this condition only for `J = fin n` in the definition, then deduce a version for any\n`J : Type*` as a corollary of this definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_finite_coproducts.out", "description": "A category has finite coproducts if there is a chosen colimit for every diagram\nwith shape `discrete J`, where we have `[fintype J]`.\n\nWe require this condition only for `J = fin n` in the definition, then deduce a version for any\n`J : Type*` as a corollary of this definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_finite_coproducts_of_has_finite_colimits", "description": "If `C` has finite colimits then it has finite coproducts.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_limits_of_shape_discrete", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_colimits_of_shape_discrete", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.limits.has_finite_coproducts_of_has_coproducts", "description": "If a category has all coproducts then in particular it has finite coproducts.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.antidiagonal_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.antidiagonal_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.prod_map_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.mem_antidiagonal", "description": "A pair `(t\u2081, t\u2082)` of multisets is contained in `antidiagonal s`\n   if and only if `t\u2081 + t\u2082 = s`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.antidiagonal_map_fst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.antidiagonal", "description": "The antidiagonal of a multiset `s` consists of all pairs `(t\u2081, t\u2082)`\n   such that `t\u2081 + t\u2082 = s`. These pairs are counted with multiplicities.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.antidiagonal_map_snd", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.antidiagonal_coe'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.card_antidiagonal", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.antidiagonal_eq_map_powerset", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "multiset.antidiagonal_coe", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic_doc.tactic.cancel_denoms", "description": "`cancel_denoms` attempts to remove numerals from the denominators of fractions.\nIt works on propositions that are field-valued inequalities.\n\n```lean\nvariables {\u03b1 : Type} [linear_ordered_field \u03b1] (a b c : \u03b1)\n\nexample (h : a / 5 + b / 4 < c) : 4*a + 5*b < 20*c :=\nbegin\n  cancel_denoms at h,\n  exact h\nend\n\nexample (h : a > 0) : a / 5 > 0 :=\nbegin\n  cancel_denoms,\n  exact h\nend\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_factors.cancel_factors_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_factors.neg_subst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_factors.derive_div", "description": "Given `e`, a term with rational divison, produces a natural number `n` and a proof of `e = e' / n`,\nwhere `e'` has no divison. Assumes \"well-behaved\" division.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.interactive.cancel_denoms", "description": "`cancel_denoms` attempts to remove numerals from the denominators of fractions.\nIt works on propositions that are field-valued inequalities.\n\n```lean\nvariables {\u03b1 : Type} [linear_ordered_field \u03b1] (a b c : \u03b1)\n\nexample (h : a / 5 + b / 4 < c) : 4*a + 5*b < 20*c :=\nbegin\n  cancel_denoms at h,\n  exact h\nend\n\nexample (h : a > 0) : a / 5 > 0 :=\nbegin\n  cancel_denoms,\n  exact h\nend\n```", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_factors.cancel_factors_lt", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_factors.cancel_denominators_in_type", "description": "`cancel_denominators_in_type h` assumes that `h` is of the form `lhs R rhs`,\nwhere `R \u2208 {<, \u2264, =, \u2265, >}`.\nIt produces an expression `h'` of the form `lhs' R rhs'` and a proof that `h = h'`.\nNumeric denominators have been canceled in `lhs'` and `rhs'`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_factors.sub_subst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_factors.add_subst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_factors.mul_subst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_factors.mk_prod_prf", "description": "`mk_prod_prf n tr e` produces a proof of `n*e = e'`, where numeric denominators have been\ncanceled in `e'`, distributing `n` proportionally according to `tr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_factors.derive", "description": "Given `e`, a term with rational division, produces a natural number `n` and a proof of `n*e = e'`,\nwhere `e'` has no division. Assumes \"well-behaved\" division.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_factors.find_comp_lemma", "description": "`find_comp_lemma e` arranges `e` in the form `lhs R rhs`, where `R \u2208 {<, \u2264, =}`, and returns\n`lhs`, `rhs`, and the `cancel_factors` lemma corresponding to `R`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_factors.div_subst", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_factors.cancel_factors_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_factors.cancel_factors_eq_div", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "cancel_factors.find_cancel_factor", "description": "`find_cancel_factor e` produces a natural number `n`, such that multiplying `e` by `n` will\nbe able to cancel all the numeric denominators in `e`. The returned `tree` describes how to\ndistribute the value `n` over products inside `e`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ae_measurable_with_density_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_ordered_semifield", "description": "A linear ordered semifield is a field with a linear order respecting the operations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_ordered_semifield.add", "description": "A linear ordered semifield is a field with a linear order respecting the operations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_ordered_semifield.add_assoc", "description": "A linear ordered semifield is a field with a linear order respecting the operations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_ordered_semifield.zero", "description": "A linear ordered semifield is a field with a linear order respecting the operations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_ordered_semifield.zero_add", "description": "A linear ordered semifield is a field with a linear order respecting the operations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_ordered_semifield.add_zero", "description": "A linear ordered semifield is a field with a linear order respecting the operations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_ordered_semifield.nsmul", "description": "A linear ordered semifield is a field with a linear order respecting the operations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_ordered_semifield.nsmul_zero'", "description": "A linear ordered semifield is a field with a linear order respecting the operations.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"n