"}, {"name": "matrix.circulant_mul_comm", "description": "Multiplication of circulant matrices commutes when the elements do.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.circulant_neg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.circulant_single_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.fin.circulant_is_symm_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.circulant_single", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.fin.circulant_mul_comm", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.fin.transpose_circulant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.circulant_add", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.fin.circulant_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.fin.circulant_mul", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.fin.circulant_is_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.circulant_inj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.circulant", "description": "Given the condition `[has_sub n]` and a vector `v : n \u2192 \u03b1`,\n   we define `circulant v` to be the circulant matrix generated by `v` of type `matrix n n \u03b1`.\n   The `(i,j)`th entry is defined to be `v (i - j)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.circulant_col_zero_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.map_circulant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.fin.circulant_ite", "description": " Note we use `\u2191i = 0` instead of `i = 0` as `fin 0` has no `0`.\nThis means that we cannot state this with `pi.single` as we did with `matrix.circulant_single`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.circulant_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.conj_transpose_circulant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.circulant_is_symm_iff", "description": "A circulant of `v` is symmetric iff `v` equals its reverse.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.circulant_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.fin.circulant_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.fin.conj_transpose_circulant", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.circulant_sub", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.circulant_smul", "description": "`k \u2022 circulant v` is another circulant matrix `circulant (k \u2022 v)`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.circulant_mul", "description": "The product of two circulant matrices `circulant v` and `circulant w` is\n   the circulant matrix generated by `mul_vec (circulant v) w`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.circulant_is_symm_apply", "description": "If `circulant v` is symmetric, `\u2200 i j : I, v (- i) = v i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.circulant_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "widget.tc", "description": "A component that implicitly depends on tactic_state. For efficiency we always assume that the tactic_state is unchanged between component renderings.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.tc.to_html", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.tc.to_component", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.tc.of_component", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.tc.map_action", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.tc.has_coe_to_fun", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.tc.stateless", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.tc.mk_simple", "description": " Make a tactic component from some init, update, views which are expecting a tactic.\nThe tactic_state never mutates.", "p": "core"}, {"name": "widget.tc.map_props", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "tactic.auto_cases.auto_cases_tac", "description": "Structure representing a tactic which can be used by `tactic.auto_cases`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.auto_cases.auto_cases_tac.name", "description": "Structure representing a tactic which can be used by `tactic.auto_cases`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.auto_cases.auto_cases_tac.\u03b1", "description": "Structure representing a tactic which can be used by `tactic.auto_cases`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.auto_cases.auto_cases_tac.tac", "description": "Structure representing a tactic which can be used by `tactic.auto_cases`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.auto_cases_at", "description": "Applies `cases` or `induction` on the local_hypothesis `hyp : expr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.auto_cases.tac_cases", "description": "The `auto_cases_tac` for `tactic.cases`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.auto_cases", "description": "Applies `cases` or `induction` on certain hypotheses.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.auto_cases.find_tac", "description": "Find an `auto_cases_tac` which matches the given `type : expr`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "tactic.auto_cases.tac_induction", "description": "The `auto_cases_tac` for `tactic.induction`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "imo2006_q5.int.add_eq_add_of_nat_abs_eq_of_nat_abs_eq", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo2006_q5.int.nat_abs_eq_of_chain_dvd", "description": " If every entry in a cyclic list of integers divides the next, then they all have the same\nabsolute value.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo2006_q5.polynomial.iterate_comp_sub_X_ne", "description": "", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo2006_q5.imo2006_q5'", "description": "We solve the problem for the specific case k = 2 first.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo2006_q5", "description": "The general problem follows easily from the k = 2 case.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "imo2006_q5.polynomial.is_periodic_pt_eval_two", "description": "The main lemma in the proof: if $P^k(t)=t$, then $P(P(t))=t$.", "p": "mathlib-archive"}, {"name": "matrix.is_integral", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.minpoly_to_matrix'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "charpoly_left_mul_matrix", "description": " The characteristic polynomial of the map `\u03bb x, a * x` is the minimal polynomial of `a`.\n\nIn combination with `det_eq_sign_charpoly_coeff` or `trace_eq_neg_charpoly_coeff`\nand a bit of rewriting, this will allow us to conclude the\nfield norm resp. trace of `x` is the product resp. sum of `x`'s conjugates.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.minpoly_to_matrix", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.minpoly_dvd_charpoly", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.minpoly_to_lin", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.minpoly_to_lin'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_dvd_card_solutions", "description": " The **Chevalley\u2013Warning theorem**, unary version.\nLet `f` be a multivariate polynomial in finitely many variables (`X s`, `s : \u03c3`)\nover a finite field of characteristic `p`.\nAssume that the total degree of `f` is less than the cardinality of `\u03c3`.\nThen the number of solutions of `f` is divisible by `p`.\nSee `char_dvd_card_solutions_of_sum_lt` for a version that takes a family of polynomials `f i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "mv_polynomial.sum_eval_eq_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_dvd_card_solutions_of_sum_lt", "description": " The **Chevalley\u2013Warning theorem**, finitary version.\nLet `(f i)` be a finite family of multivariate polynomials\nin finitely many variables (`X s`, `s : \u03c3`) over a finite field of characteristic `p`.\nAssume that the sum of the total degrees of the `f i` is less than the cardinality of `\u03c3`.\nThen the number of common solutions of the `f i` is divisible by `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_dvd_card_solutions_of_fintype_sum_lt", "description": " The **Chevalley\u2013Warning theorem**, fintype version.\nLet `(f i)` be a finite family of multivariate polynomials\nin finitely many variables (`X s`, `s : \u03c3`) over a finite field of characteristic `p`.\nAssume that the sum of the total degrees of the `f i` is less than the cardinality of `\u03c3`.\nThen the number of common solutions of the `f i` is divisible by `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "char_dvd_card_solutions_of_add_lt", "description": " The **Chevalley\u2013Warning theorem**, binary version.\nLet `f\u2081`, `f\u2082` be two multivariate polynomials in finitely many variables (`X s`, `s : \u03c3`) over a\nfinite field of characteristic `p`.\nAssume that the sum of the total degrees of `f\u2081` and `f\u2082` is less than the cardinality of `\u03c3`.\nThen the number of common solutions of the `f\u2081` and `f\u2082` is divisible by `p`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville", "description": "A Liouville number is a real number `x` such that for every natural number `n`, there exist\n`a, b \u2208 \u2124` with `1 < b` such that `0 < |x - a/b| < 1/b\u207f`.\nIn the implementation, the condition `x \u2260 a/b` replaces the traditional equivalent `0 < |x - a/b|`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville.exists_one_le_pow_mul_dist", "description": " Let `Z, N` be types, let `R` be a metric space, let `\u03b1 : R` be a point and let\n`j : Z \u2192 N \u2192 R` be a function.  We aim to estimate how close we can get to `\u03b1`, while staying\nin the image of `j`.  The points `j z a` of `R` in the image of `j` come with a \"cost\" equal to\n`d a`.  As we get closer to `\u03b1` while staying in the image of `j`, we are interested in bounding\nthe quantity `d a * dist \u03b1 (j z a)` from below by a strictly positive amount `1 / A`: the intuition\nis that approximating well `\u03b1` with the points in the image of `j` should come at a high cost.  The\nhypotheses on the function `f : R \u2192 R` provide us with sufficient conditions to ensure our goal.\nThe first hypothesis is that `f` is Lipschitz at `\u03b1`: this yields a bound on the distance.\nThe second hypothesis is specific to the Liouville argument and provides the missing bound\ninvolving the cost function `d`.\n\nThis lemma collects the properties used in the proof of `exists_pos_real_of_irrational_root`.\nIt is stated in more general form than needed: in the intended application, `Z = \u2124`, `N = \u2115`,\n`R = \u211d`, `d a = (a + 1) ^ f.nat_degree`, `j z a  = z / (a + 1)`, `f \u2208 \u2124[x]`, `\u03b1` is an irrational\nroot of `f`, `\u03b5` is small, `M` is a bound on the Lipschitz constant of `f` near `\u03b1`, `n` is\nthe degree of the polynomial `f`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville.exists_pos_real_of_irrational_root", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville.transcendental", "description": "**Liouville's Theorem**", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "liouville.irrational", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.subobject_iso_subobject_op", "description": "In an abelian category, the subobjects and quotient objects of an object `X` are\n   order-isomorphic via taking kernels and cokernels.\n   Implemented here using subobjects in the opposite category,\n   since mathlib does not have a notion of quotient objects at the time of writing.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.well_powered_opposite", "description": "A well-powered abelian category is also well-copowered.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.subobject_iso_subobject_op_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.abelian.subobject_iso_subobject_op_symm_apply", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.all_iff_forall", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.any_iff_exists_prop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.any_of_mem", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.all_iff_forall_prop", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.all_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.any_nil", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.all_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.any_iff_exists", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "list.any_cons", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.range_of_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.range_rec", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.zero_union_range_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.range_cases_on", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "nat.range_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.aeval_apply_of_has_eigenvector", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.ker_aeval_ring_hom'_unit_polynomial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.eigenvalues.fintype", "description": "An endomorphism of a finite-dimensional vector space has finitely many eigenvalues.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.has_eigenvalue_of_is_root", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.has_eigenvalue_iff_is_root", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.eigenspace_aeval_polynomial_degree_1", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "module.End.is_root_of_has_eigenvalue", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.finite_dimensional'", "description": " Linear maps over a `k`-algebra are finite dimensional (over `k`) if both the source and\ntarget are, as they form a subspace of all `k`-linear maps.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_map.finite_dimensional", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "matrix.finite_dimensional", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ptendsto_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ptendsto'_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rtendsto_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "rtendsto'_nhds", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pcontinuous_iff'", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "pcontinuous", "description": "Continuity of a partial function", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "open_dom_of_pcontinuous", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "continuous_within_at_iff_ptendsto_res", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "euclidean_geometry.mul_dist_add_mul_dist_eq_mul_dist_of_cospherical", "description": "**Ptolemy\u2019s Theorem**.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "ennreal.ae_measurable_of_exist_almost_disjoint_supersets", "description": " If a function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u211d\u22650\u221e` is such that the level sets `{f < p}` and `{q < f}` have measurable\nsupersets which are disjoint up to measure zero when `p` and `q` are finite numbers satisfying\n`p < q`, then `f` is almost-everywhere measurable.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "measure_theory.ae_measurable_of_exist_almost_disjoint_supersets", "description": " If a function `f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2` is such that the level sets `{f < p}` and `{q < f}` have measurable\nsupersets which are disjoint up to measure zero when `p < q`, then `f` is almost-everywhere\nmeasurable. It is even enough to have this for `p` and `q` in a countable dense set.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.coe_center", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.center.smul_comm_class_right", "description": "The center of a monoid acts commutatively on that monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.decidable_mem_center", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.center", "description": "The center of a monoid `M` is the set of elements that commute with everything in `M`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.mem_center_iff", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.center_to_add_subsemigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.center_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_submonoid.center", "description": "The center of a monoid `M` is the set of elements that commute with everything in\n`M`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.coe_center", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.center.smul_comm_class_left", "description": "The center of a monoid acts commutatively on that monoid.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submonoid.center_to_subsemigroup", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"na