` is simple when it has exactly two normal `add_subgroup`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_simple_add_group.subgroup.is_simple_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_simple_group.is_simple_group_of_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "subgroup.normal.eq_bot_or_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_simple_group", "description": "A `group` is simple when it has exactly two normal `subgroup`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_simple_group.exists_pair_ne", "description": "A `group` is simple when it has exactly two normal `subgroup`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_simple_group.eq_bot_or_eq_top_of_normal", "description": "A `group` is simple when it has exactly two normal `subgroup`s.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "add_subgroup.normal.eq_bot_or_eq_top", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_simple_group.subgroup.is_simple_order", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "is_simple_add_group.to_nontrivial", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.wallis.W_le", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.wallis.W_eq_factorial_ratio", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.tendsto_prod_pi_div_two", "description": "Wallis' product formula for `\u03c0 / 2`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.wallis.tendsto_W_nhds_pi_div_two", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.wallis.W_eq_integral_sin_pow_div_integral_sin_pow", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.wallis.W_succ", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.wallis.le_W", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.wallis.W", "description": "The product of the first `k` terms in Wallis' formula for `\u03c0`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "real.wallis.W_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_of_nonneg", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_of_pos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_of_le_one", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_of_nonpos", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "inv_of_lt_zero", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.parallel_pair_connected", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.wide_pushout_shape_connected", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.parallel_pair_inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.prod_preserves_connected_limits.\u03b3\u2081", "description": "(Impl). The obvious natural transformation from (X \u00d7 K -) to X", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.wide_pullback_shape_connected", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.prod_preserves_connected_limits", "description": "The functor `(X \u00d7 -)` preserves any connected limit.\nNote that this functor does not preserve the two most obvious disconnected limits - that is,\n`(X \u00d7 -)` does not preserve products or terminal object, eg `(X \u2a2f A) \u2a2f (X \u2a2f B)` is not isomorphic to\n`X \u2a2f (A \u2a2f B)` and `X \u2a2f 1` is not isomorphic to `1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.prod_preserves_connected_limits.forget_cone_X", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.prod_preserves_connected_limits.\u03b3\u2082", "description": "(Impl). The obvious natural transformation from (X \u00d7 K -) to K.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.prod_preserves_connected_limits.\u03b3\u2082_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.prod_preserves_connected_limits.forget_cone_\u03c0", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.prod_preserves_connected_limits.forget_cone", "description": " (Impl).\nGiven a cone for (X \u00d7 K -), produce a cone for K using the natural transformation `\u03b3\u2082`", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.prod_preserves_connected_limits.\u03b3\u2081_app", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_has_finite_products.tensor_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_has_finite_coproducts.left_unitor_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.symmetric_of_has_finite_products_braiding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_has_finite_coproducts.right_unitor_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.symmetric_of_has_finite_coproducts", "description": "The monoidal structure coming from finite coproducts is symmetric.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_has_finite_coproducts.left_unitor_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_has_finite_coproducts.tensor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_has_finite_products.right_unitor_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_has_finite_coproducts.associator_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_has_finite_products.associator_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_has_finite_coproducts.tensor_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_has_finite_coproducts", "description": "A category with an initial object and binary coproducts has a natural monoidal structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.symmetric_of_has_finite_coproducts_braiding", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_has_finite_products.right_unitor_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.symmetric_of_has_finite_products", "description": "The monoidal structure coming from finite products is symmetric.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_has_finite_products.left_unitor_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_has_finite_coproducts.right_unitor_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_has_finite_products.left_unitor_inv", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_has_finite_products", "description": "A category with a terminal object and binary products has a natural monoidal structure.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.monoidal_of_has_finite_products.tensor_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_recurrence.to_init", "description": "The function that maps a solution `u` of `E` to its first\n `E.order` terms as a `linear_equiv`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_recurrence.mk_sol", "description": "A solution of a `linear_recurrence` which satisfies certain initial conditions.\n We will prove this is the only such solution.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_recurrence.geom_sol_iff_root_char_poly", "description": "The geometric sequence `q^n` is a solution of `E` iff\n `q` is a root of `E`'s characteristic polynomial.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_recurrence", "description": "A \"linear recurrence relation\" over a commutative semiring is given by its\n order `n` and `n` coefficients.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_recurrence.order", "description": "A \"linear recurrence relation\" over a commutative semiring is given by its\n order `n` and `n` coefficients.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_recurrence.coeffs", "description": "A \"linear recurrence relation\" over a commutative semiring is given by its\n order `n` and `n` coefficients.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_recurrence.sol_space", "description": "The space of solutions of `E`, as a `submodule` over `\u03b1` of the module `\u2115 \u2192 \u03b1`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_recurrence.inhabited", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_recurrence.eq_mk_of_is_sol_of_eq_init", "description": "If `u` is a solution to `E` and `init` designates its first `E.order` values,\n then `\u2200 n, u n = E.mk_sol init n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_recurrence.is_sol_mk_sol", "description": "`E.mk_sol` indeed gives solutions to `E`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_recurrence.sol_eq_of_eq_init", "description": "Two solutions are equal iff they are equal on `range E.order`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_recurrence.is_solution", "description": "We say that a sequence `u` is solution of `linear_recurrence order coeffs` when we have\n `u (n + order) = \u2211 i : fin order, coeffs i * u (n + i)` for any `n`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_recurrence.sol_space_rank", "description": "The dimension of `E.sol_space` is `E.order`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_recurrence.mk_sol_eq_init", "description": "`E.mk_sol init`'s first `E.order` terms are `init`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_recurrence.eq_mk_of_is_sol_of_eq_init'", "description": "If `u` is a solution to `E` and `init` designates its first `E.order` values,\n then `u = E.mk_sol init`. This proves that `E.mk_sol init` is the only solution\n of `E` whose first `E.order` values are given by `init`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_recurrence.char_poly", "description": " The characteristic polynomial of `E` is\n`X ^ E.order - \u2211 i : fin E.order, (E.coeffs i) * X ^ i`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_recurrence.is_sol_iff_mem_sol_space", "description": "Defining property of the solution space : `u` is a solution\n iff it belongs to the solution space.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "linear_recurrence.tuple_succ", "description": "`E.tuple_succ` maps `![s\u2080, s\u2081, ..., s\u2099]` to `![s\u2081, ..., s\u2099, \u2211 (E.coeffs i) * s\u1d62]`,\n where `n := E.order`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "field.to_euclidean_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "int.euclidean_domain", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "has_seq_left", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "has_seq_left.seq_left", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "applicative", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "applicative.to_functor", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "applicative.to_has_pure", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "applicative.to_has_seq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "applicative.to_has_seq_left", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "applicative.to_has_seq_right", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "has_seq_right", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "has_seq_right.seq_right", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "has_seq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "has_seq.seq", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "has_pure", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "has_pure.pure", "description": "", "p": "core"}, {"name": "fun_like.finite", "description": " All `fun_like`s are finite if their domain and codomain are.\n\nCan't be an instance because it can cause infinite loops.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like.finite'", "description": " All `fun_like`s are finite if their domain and codomain are.\n\nNon-dependent version of `fun_like.finite` that might be easier to infer.\nCan't be an instance because it can cause infinite loops.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like.fintype", "description": " All `fun_like`s are finite if their domain and codomain are.\n\nThis is not an instance because specific `fun_like` types might have a better-suited definition.\n\nSee also `fun_like.finite`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "fun_like.fintype'", "description": " All `fun_like`s are finite if their domain and codomain are.\n\nNon-dependent version of `fun_like.fintype` that might be easier to infer.\nThis is not an instance because specific `fun_like` types might have a better-suited definition.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.smul_sup_le_of_le_smul_of_le_jacobson_bot", "description": " *Nakayama's Lemma** - Statement (4) in\n[Stacks 00DV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00DV).\nSee also `smul_sup_eq_smul_sup_of_le_smul_of_le_jacobson` for a generalisation\nto the `jacobson` of any ideal", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.eq_bot_of_le_smul_of_le_jacobson_bot", "description": " *Nakayama's Lemma** - Statement (2) in\n[Stacks 00DV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00DV).\nSee also `eq_smul_of_le_smul_of_le_jacobson` for a generalisation\nto the `jacobson` of any ideal", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.smul_sup_eq_smul_sup_of_le_smul_of_le_jacobson", "description": " *Nakayama's Lemma** - A slightly more general version of (4) in\n[Stacks 00DV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00DV).\nSee also `smul_sup_eq_of_le_smul_of_le_jacobson_bot` for the special case when `J = \u22a5`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "submodule.eq_smul_of_le_smul_of_le_jacobson", "description": " *Nakayama's Lemma** - A slightly more general version of (2) in\n[Stacks 00DV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00DV).\nSee also `eq_bot_of_le_smul_of_le_jacobson_bot` for the special case when `J = \u22a5`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.over.forget.is_left_adjoint", "description": "Note that the binary products assumption is necessary: the existence of a right adjoint to\n`over.forget X` is equivalent to the existence of each binary product `X \u2a2f -`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.star_obj_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.star_obj_hom", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.star", "description": "The functor from `C` to `over X` which sends `Y : C` to `\u03c0\u2081 : X \u2a2f Y \u27f6 X`, sometimes denoted `X*`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.forget_adj_star", "description": "The functor `over.forget X : over X \u2964 C` has a right adjoint given by `star X`.\n\nNote that the binary products assumption is necessary: the existence of a right adjoint to\n`over.forget X` is equivalent to the existence of each binary product `X \u2a2f -`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "category_theory.star_map_left", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_to_fiber_injective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheafify", "description": "The sheafification of a `Type` valued presheaf, defined as the functions into the stalks which\nare locally equal to germs.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheafify.is_germ", "description": "The prelocal predicate on functions into the stalks, asserting that the function is equal to a germ.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheafify_stalk_iso", "description": "The isomorphism betweeen a stalk of the sheafification and the original stalk.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_to_fiber_surjective", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.stalk_to_fiber", "description": "The natural morphism from the stalk of the sheafification to the original stalk.\nIn `sheafify_stalk_iso` we show this is an isomorphism.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.to_sheafify", "description": "The morphism from a presheaf to its sheafification,\nsending each section to its germs.\n(This forms the unit of the adjunction.)", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top.presheaf.sheafify.is_locally_germ", "description": "The local predicate on functions into the stalks,\nasserting that the function is locally equal to a germ.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top_to_Locale_obj", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top_to_Locale", "description": "The forgetful functor from `Top` to `Locale` which forgets that the space has \"enough points\".", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Top_to_Locale_map", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Locale.large_category", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Locale.has_coe_to_sort", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Locale.of", "description": "Construct a bundled `Locale` from a `frame`.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Locale", "description": "The category of locales.", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "CompHaus_to_Locale.faithful", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, {"name": "Locale.coe_of", "description": "", "p": "mathlib"}, 